    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm should be designed for that future from the beginning.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Therefore an excellent Nazm program should not merely execute efficiently.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "It should also be **efficient to communicate, understand, generate, modify, validate and repair by both humans and AI systems**.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "That is a fundamental language requirement.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 6A. Best-in-Class Compiler and Decentralized/Web3 Constitution")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The goals below extend the original ninety-nine goals without changing their authority class. They are ambitions, not status claims. They exist because “best of the best” must be translated into engineering dimensions, and because decentralized execution introduces requirements ordinary native software does not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G100 — Best-in-Class by Evidence, Not Slogan")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm should pursue the strongest practical combination of:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "clarity")
    strs_push(l, "safety")
    strs_push(l, "performance")
    strs_push(l, "compile latency")
    strs_push(l, "memory efficiency")
    strs_push(l, "portability")
    strs_push(l, "reliability")
    strs_push(l, "determinism")
    strs_push(l, "security")
    strs_push(l, "verification")
    strs_push(l, "interoperability")
    strs_push(l, "AI efficiency")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "No universal score may hide trade-offs. Every “best” claim names a comparator, workload, machine/profile and evidence class.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G101 — One Semantic Core, Multiple Backends")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm should support several execution environments without forking program meaning.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Potential backend families:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "LLVM/native")
    strs_push(l, "Cranelift/JIT or dev AOT if justified")
    strs_push(l, "WebAssembly")
    strs_push(l, "EVM-oriented contract backend")
    strs_push(l, "sBPF/SVM-oriented backend")
    strs_push(l, "future accelerator backends")
    strs_push(l, "future verified/restricted backends")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Backends translate settled semantics. They do not invent new source-language meaning.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G102 — Backend Contract Precision")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Every backend boundary should consume an explicit representation whose semantics, ABI assumptions, failure behaviour and target inputs are known. Backend caches should key the **actual transformation input** where possible rather than a fragile approximation of upstream dependencies.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G103 — WebAssembly as a First-Class Portable Target")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm should eventually target WebAssembly for:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- browser components;")
    strs_push(l, "- sandboxed server plugins;")
    strs_push(l, "- edge runtimes;")
    strs_push(l, "- portable extensions;")
    strs_push(l, "- WASM-oriented smart-contract environments.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The source language must not become browser-specific. Host authority belongs in imported capabilities/interfaces.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G104 — Web3 as a Restriction Profile, Never a Dialect")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A future Web3 profile must use the same Nazm semantics and may only:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- refuse nondeterministic or unavailable operations;")
    strs_push(l, "- restrict allocation/control flow/resource use;")
    strs_push(l, "- grant chain-specific capabilities;")
    strs_push(l, "- impose additional verification obligations;")
    strs_push(l, "- choose a contract backend and ABI.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "It must never reinterpret ordinary arithmetic, ownership, evaluation order or error semantics merely because code is on-chain.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G105 — Deterministic Consensus Execution")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A contract-capable profile should make consensus determinism statically checkable where possible.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Disallowed ambient sources should include, unless supplied by an explicit deterministic host capability:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "wall clock")
    strs_push(l, "process environment")
    strs_push(l, "filesystem")
    strs_push(l, "arbitrary network")
    strs_push(l, "ambient randomness")
    strs_push(l, "thread scheduling observation")
    strs_push(l, "unspecified platform state")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Target-provided time, randomness, oracle or block metadata must be explicit inputs/capabilities with defined semantics.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G106 — Metered and Explainable Resource Cost")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Web3 execution introduces gas/compute/storage budgets. Nazm should eventually explain and, where possible, statically bound:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "compute")
    strs_push(l, "storage reads")
    strs_push(l, "storage writes")
    strs_push(l, "memory")
    strs_push(l, "allocations")
    strs_push(l, "external calls")
    strs_push(l, "cryptographic host calls")
    strs_push(l, "event/log output")
    strs_push(l, "loop bounds")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Where a static upper bound is impossible, the compiler should distinguish that from an unknown implementation detail.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G107 — Persistent State as Explicit Authority")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Persistent contract state must not look like an ordinary hidden global variable.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler should eventually know:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- what state a function may read;")
    strs_push(l, "- what state it may mutate;")
    strs_push(l, "- who authorizes the mutation;")
    strs_push(l, "- which layout/version is stored;")
    strs_push(l, "- which external calls can observe intermediate state.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G108 — Digital Asset / Resource Safety")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm should research an asset/resource semantic kind suitable for tokens, capabilities, ownership certificates and other scarce values.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Potential guarantees:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "no accidental duplication")
    strs_push(l, "no silent discard where conservation is required")
    strs_push(l, "explicit transfer")
    strs_push(l, "explicit authorized destruction")
    strs_push(l, "well-defined storage ownership")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "This must compose with, not replace, ordinary Nazm ownership semantics.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G109 — Financial Numeric Correctness")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Smart contracts and financial systems require arithmetic beyond a single signed machine integer. Nazm should eventually support or standardize:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "fixed-width signed/unsigned integers")
    strs_push(l, "large integers such as 128/256-bit where targets require them")
    strs_push(l, "fixed-point decimal/rational representations with explicit scale")
    strs_push(l, "checked conversion")
    strs_push(l, "explicit rounding rules")
    strs_push(l, "no implicit floating-point money semantics")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Numeric semantics must be target-independent unless a profile explicitly exposes a target-specific primitive.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G110 — Typed Cryptographic and Address Primitives")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Addresses, hashes, signatures and public keys should not all degrade into unstructured byte arrays at API boundaries.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm should prefer typed library/profile primitives with explicit algorithms and lengths while keeping cryptographic implementations in audited libraries or target host functions rather than making every algorithm a language keyword.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G111 — Contract Interface / ABI Generation")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "From one typed source definition the toolchain should eventually be able to generate target artefacts such as:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "contract ABI")
    strs_push(l, "client bindings")
    strs_push(l, "event schemas")
    strs_push(l, "storage/interface metadata")
    strs_push(l, "source maps")
    strs_push(l, "interface fingerprints")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Duplicated handwritten ABI descriptions are a correctness risk.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G112 — Storage Layout and Upgrade Safety")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Persistent-state layout can outlive a compiler version. Nazm should eventually make contract storage layout explicit, inspectable and version-aware.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An upgrade should be able to answer:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "Is the old state readable?")
    strs_push(l, "Which fields moved or changed?")
    strs_push(l, "Is migration required?")
    strs_push(l, "Did an interface or storage compatibility contract break?")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G113 — External-Call and Reentrancy Awareness")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler should eventually model external contract/program calls as effects with explicit authority and state-ordering consequences.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Where a target admits reentrant execution, tooling should be able to identify dangerous patterns such as:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "state read")
    strs_push(l, "external call")
    strs_push(l, "state write based on stale assumption")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The goal is analysis and explicitness, not pretending all reentrancy can be universally prohibited.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G114 — Signer and Authorization Semantics")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Contract APIs should make authorization requirements visible in types, capabilities or contracts.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler should eventually help answer:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "Who may invoke this transition?")
    strs_push(l, "Which signer/authority is required?")
    strs_push(l, "Which state may that authority modify?")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Authentication policy remains application logic; authority flow should not remain invisible.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G115 — Chain-Neutral Core, Typed Host Adapters")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "EVM storage, WASM host imports, account-oriented state and future chain models differ. Nazm should isolate these differences behind typed backend/profile adapters.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Core language semantics should not acquire a keyword merely because one chain exposes a particular syscall or account convention.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G116 — EVM Backend Goal")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm should be architecturally capable of targeting EVM-compatible environments.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Possible implementation routes may evolve:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm semantic contract model")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "contract IR")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "Yul/other verified intermediate route")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "EVM bytecode")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "or a direct backend later if evidence justifies it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The goal is semantic correctness and tooling quality, not owning every low-level assembler immediately.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G117 — WASM Contract Backend Goal")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "For chains and runtimes that execute WebAssembly, Nazm should reuse the ordinary WASM backend where possible and isolate chain-specific host functions in the Web3 profile/standard library.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "One WASM code generator should not be duplicated into a “blockchain WASM” compiler unless the execution semantics genuinely differ.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G118 — sBPF/SVM-Style Backend Goal")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm should be capable of targeting account-oriented BPF-derived contract environments where the program code and mutable account state are separate.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler should aim to understand signer, writable/read-only state, account ownership/type constraints and cross-program calls sufficiently to produce useful static diagnostics.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G119 — Move and Resource-Oriented Interoperability")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm should study Move-style resource semantics as evidence, not promise binary compatibility prematurely.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Interop or a compatible backend is acceptable only when Nazm's asset/resource guarantees can be mapped without weakening either language's safety assumptions.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G120 — On-Chain / Off-Chain Semantic Continuity")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Where feasible, shared domain logic should be reusable between off-chain native/server code and on-chain code.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The contract profile may refuse operations, but a pure function valid in both profiles should mean the same thing in both.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "This reduces duplicated business logic and makes differential testing possible.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G121 — Contract Testing as Compiler Tooling")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Future Web3 tooling should support:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "unit tests")
    strs_push(l, "state-transition/property tests")
    strs_push(l, "fuzzing")
    strs_push(l, "mutation testing")
    strs_push(l, "scenario simulation")
    strs_push(l, "contract differential tests")
    strs_push(l, "upgrade compatibility tests")
    strs_push(l, "resource-budget tests")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Testing must run against the semantics of the target backend, not only an optimistic mock.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G122 — Smart-Contract Security Analysis")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A mature Web3 profile should make the compiler/toolchain capable of analysing classes such as:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- arithmetic/rounding mistakes;")
    strs_push(l, "- missing authorization;")
    strs_push(l, "- invalid state transitions;")
    strs_push(l, "- asset duplication/loss;")
    strs_push(l, "- unsafe external-call ordering;")
    strs_push(l, "- storage-layout incompatibility;")
    strs_push(l, "- unexpected capability use;")
    strs_push(l, "- unbounded resource behaviour where the profile forbids it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "No compiler can prove application business logic correct by default. That limitation must remain explicit.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G123 — Formal Contract Verification Path")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Web3 and Critical profiles should share as much contract/proof infrastructure as semantics permit.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Future constructs may express:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "requires")
    strs_push(l, "ensures")
    strs_push(l, "invariant")
    strs_push(l, "resource invariant")
    strs_push(l, "state-transition invariant")
    strs_push(l, "asset conservation invariant")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "and lower either to runtime checks, static analysis or proof obligations according to profile.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G124 — Reproducible Contract Builds")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "On-chain deployment magnifies compiler provenance risk. Nazm should eventually support reproducible contract artefacts with:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "source digest")
    strs_push(l, "compiler identity")
    strs_push(l, "profile/backend identity")
    strs_push(l, "target configuration")
    strs_push(l, "ABI/storage metadata")
    strs_push(l, "dependency provenance")
    strs_push(l, "reproducible build instructions")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A contract address or bytecode hash is not a substitute for knowing how it was produced.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G125 — Audit Artifact Generation")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler should eventually be able to emit a compact audit bundle describing:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "public entry points")
    strs_push(l, "authorities")
    strs_push(l, "state reads/writes")
    strs_push(l, "external calls")
    strs_push(l, "effects")
    strs_push(l, "resource estimates")
    strs_push(l, "storage layout")
    strs_push(l, "unsafe/foreign boundaries")
    strs_push(l, "contracts/invariants")
    strs_push(l, "compiler and dependency provenance")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The bundle is evidence input for auditors, not an automatic certification.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G126 — Cross-Chain Architecture Without Semantic Fragmentation")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Supporting several chains must not produce several subtly incompatible Nazm dialects.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "If a target requires a fundamentally different semantic rule, the project must either:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "1. express it as a profile restriction/capability;")
    strs_push(l, "2. isolate it in an explicit foreign/host boundary; or")
    strs_push(l, "3. decline that target.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "“Target support” is not worth corrupting language coherence.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G127 — Multi-Objective Optimizer")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm's optimizer should eventually support explicit goals such as:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "latency")
    strs_push(l, "throughput")
    strs_push(l, "code size")
    strs_push(l, "energy")
    strs_push(l, "memory")
    strs_push(l, "compile time")
    strs_push(l, "gas/compute units")
    strs_push(l, "critical predictability")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "No one optimization profile is best for firmware, cloud services, HPC and contracts. The semantics remain one; optimization objectives differ.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G128 — Best-in-Class Development Loop")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler should optimize the full edit→check→test→build loop, not only generated machine code.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Target properties include:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- instant incremental semantic feedback where possible;")
    strs_push(l, "- deterministic structured diagnostics;")
    strs_push(l, "- precise affected-test selection;")
    strs_push(l, "- content-addressed reuse where it earns its cost;")
    strs_push(l, "- fast dev backend/JIT where justified;")
    strs_push(l, "- aggressive release optimization separately.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G129 — Best-in-Class Semantic Observability")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A future programmer or agent should be able to ask the compiler not only “did it compile?” but:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "what changed semantically?")
    strs_push(l, "what did this allocate?")
    strs_push(l, "what can this call?")
    strs_push(l, "what can it mutate?")
    strs_push(l, "what authority does it require?")
    strs_push(l, "what state does it touch?")
    strs_push(l, "what may block?")
    strs_push(l, "what may fail?")
    strs_push(l, "what resource budget remains?")
    strs_push(l, "what tests and callers are affected?")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler's semantic model should become a product interface.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## G130 — Universal Capability Without Universal Runtime")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm's long-term ambition may span:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "CLI and applications")
    strs_push(l, "servers and distributed systems")
    strs_push(l, "OS/runtime components")
    strs_push(l, "embedded and bare metal")
    strs_push(l, "cybersecurity")
    strs_push(l, "AI/HPC and accelerators")
    strs_push(l, "WASM plugins")
    strs_push(l, "decentralized/Web3 contracts")
    strs_push(l, "critical/high-assurance subsets")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "This does **not** imply one runtime, allocator, scheduler, standard-library surface or backend is appropriate everywhere.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The universal part is the semantic foundation and toolchain discipline.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 7. What \"Super Fast\" Means")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm must never use \"fast\" as one number.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Performance contains multiple independent dimensions.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## P1 — Scalar CPU Performance")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Compare equivalent algorithms against:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "C")
    strs_push(l, "Rust")
    strs_push(l, "Zig")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Goal:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "be competitive with leading native systems implementations.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Do not promise universal superiority.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## P2 — Memory Efficiency")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Measure:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- peak RSS;")
    strs_push(l, "- heap allocation;")
    strs_push(l, "- allocation count;")
    strs_push(l, "- stack consumption;")
    strs_push(l, "- fragmentation;")
    strs_push(l, "- metadata;")
    strs_push(l, "- task overhead.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## P3 — Startup Latency")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Important for:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- CLI;")
    strs_push(l, "- serverless;")
    strs_push(l, "- utilities;")
    strs_push(l, "- embedded startup.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Native programs should not automatically inherit heavy-runtime startup.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## P4 — Tail Latency")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Measure:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "p50")
    strs_push(l, "p95")
    strs_push(l, "p99")
    strs_push(l, "p99.9")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Average latency alone is insufficient.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## P5 — Throughput")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Measure under:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- single core;")
    strs_push(l, "- multiple cores;")
    strs_push(l, "- high concurrency;")
    strs_push(l, "- I/O load.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## P6 — Compilation Speed")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Measure:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "clean check")
    strs_push(l, "incremental check")
    strs_push(l, "clean build")
    strs_push(l, "incremental build")
    strs_push(l, "optimized build")
    strs_push(l, "self-host build")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## P7 — Compiler Memory")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A compiler that requires enormous RAM is not universally usable.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Peak memory must be tracked as a regression metric.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## P8 — Concurrency Density")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Eventually measure:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- bytes/task;")
    strs_push(l, "- spawn latency;")
    strs_push(l, "- scheduling latency;")
    strs_push(l, "- context switch;")
    strs_push(l, "- channel send;")
    strs_push(l, "- cancellation;")
    strs_push(l, "- task completion.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## P9 — Scaling")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Measure throughput against core count.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Avoid claims based only on maximum throughput.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Look for:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "1")
    strs_push(l, "2")
    strs_push(l, "4")
    strs_push(l, "8")
    strs_push(l, "16")
    strs_push(l, "32...")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "cores.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## P10 — SIMD")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Measure auto/manual vectorization.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Compiler must explain failed vectorization where practical.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## P11 — Accelerator Performance")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Future GPU/NPU comparisons must include:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- transfer cost;")
    strs_push(l, "- kernel launch;")
    strs_push(l, "- occupancy;")
    strs_push(l, "- throughput;")
    strs_push(l, "- synchronization.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Never compare GPU kernel time while hiding host/device transfer.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## P12 — Energy Efficiency")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "For embedded, mobile and data-center systems, operations-per-joule can matter as much as operations-per-second.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Future benchmark architecture should permit energy measurement.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## P13 — AI Token Performance")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Measure:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- source tokens;")
    strs_push(l, "- context tokens;")
    strs_push(l, "- task-completion tokens;")
    strs_push(l, "- patch tokens;")
    strs_push(l, "- repair iterations;")
    strs_push(l, "- semantic context size;")
    strs_push(l, "- tool-output tokens.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Performance in the AI era includes communication cost.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 8. Performance Claim Rule")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "No marketing performance statement may become an architecture fact without:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "benchmark source")
    strs_push(l, "hardware specification")
    strs_push(l, "OS")
    strs_push(l, "compiler versions")
    strs_push(l, "flags")
    strs_push(l, "dataset")
    strs_push(l, "measurement method")
    strs_push(l, "variance")
    strs_push(l, "comparison implementation")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Examples of prohibited unsupported statements:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm is faster than C.")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm is 10x faster than Rust.")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm has zero overhead.")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm uses less memory than every language.")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm always uses fewer AI tokens.")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Acceptable:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> On benchmark X, commit Y, target Z, Nazm measured N under documented conditions.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 9. What \"Error-Free\" Means")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm cannot guarantee the absence of all software errors.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Logical errors, incorrect requirements, hardware faults and compiler defects can still exist.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Therefore \"error-free\" must be decomposed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Compiler-preventable target classes")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm should aim to eliminate or strongly reduce:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "syntax ambiguity")
    strs_push(l, "type mismatch")
    strs_push(l, "uninitialized access")
    strs_push(l, "dangling references")
    strs_push(l, "use-after-free")
    strs_push(l, "double free")
    strs_push(l, "invalid aliasing")
    strs_push(l, "data races")
    strs_push(l, "unchecked resource lifetime")
    strs_push(l, "unhandled important failure")
    strs_push(l, "unsafe narrowing")
    strs_push(l, "unintended overflow")
    strs_push(l, "out-of-bounds access")
    strs_push(l, "capability violation")
    strs_push(l, "known-invalid information flow")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Statically reducible but not universally eliminable")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "deadlock")
    strs_push(l, "livelock")
    strs_push(l, "starvation")
    strs_push(l, "resource exhaustion")
    strs_push(l, "algorithmic complexity attacks")
    strs_push(l, "timing bugs")
    strs_push(l, "distributed race conditions")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Cannot generally be solved by language safety")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "wrong business requirement")
    strs_push(l, "incorrect algorithm")
    strs_push(l, "malicious specification")
    strs_push(l, "hardware defect")
    strs_push(l, "cosmic radiation")
    strs_push(l, "incorrect external system")
    strs_push(l, "compromised compiler/toolchain")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm architecture must never market language safety as universal correctness.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 10. Domain Profiles")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "One semantic language.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Different permitted capabilities.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## General Profile")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Target:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- applications;")
    strs_push(l, "- CLI;")
    strs_push(l, "- servers;")
    strs_push(l, "- services;")
    strs_push(l, "- developer tooling.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Allows broad stdlib and runtime features.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Systems Profile")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Target:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- OS components;")
    strs_push(l, "- runtimes;")
    strs_push(l, "- databases;")
    strs_push(l, "- storage engines;")
    strs_push(l, "- networking;")
    strs_push(l, "- security tools.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Requires stronger control over:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- allocation;")
    strs_push(l, "- layout;")
    strs_push(l, "- ABI;")
    strs_push(l, "- FFI;")
    strs_push(l, "- atomics;")
    strs_push(l, "- unsafe code.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Embedded Profile")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Target:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- MCU;")
    strs_push(l, "- robotics;")
    strs_push(l, "- firmware;")
    strs_push(l, "- IoT;")
    strs_push(l, "- controllers.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Needs:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "no_std capability")
    strs_push(l, "optional/no heap")
    strs_push(l, "static allocation")
    strs_push(l, "MMIO")
    strs_push(l, "interrupts")
    strs_push(l, "volatile")
    strs_push(l, "cross compilation")
    strs_push(l, "small binaries")
    strs_push(l, "deterministic startup")
