    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 54. Historical Lesson Summary")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm should learn:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from C:** respect the machine.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from C++:** abstraction can remain native, but complexity accumulates.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from Python:** humans matter.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from Java:** portability and managed safety can transform software deployment.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from Erlang:** failure isolation matters as much as successful execution.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from Go:** simplicity, build speed and tooling are language features.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from Rust:** systems safety does not require mandatory GC.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from Zig:** invisible behaviour deserves suspicion.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from SPARK:** high assurance requires restrictions and evidence.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from Haskell:** visible effects improve reasoning.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from CUDA:** hardware parallelism sometimes requires new execution models.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from Julia:** high-level scientific productivity and low-level performance should not require two codebases.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from Swift:** native safety and approachable syntax can coexist.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from Kotlin:** interoperability and pragmatism accelerate adoption.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from ML/OCaml:** algebraic data, exhaustive matching and inference can compress complex symbolic programs without surrendering static meaning.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from TypeScript:** semantic tooling and incremental adoption can be adoption features as important as syntax.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from WebAssembly:** portable sandboxing can be a compilation target rather than a separate source language.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from Solidity/EVM:** consensus execution makes determinism, storage layout, ABI and resource cost part of correctness.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from Move:** scarce digital assets need resource semantics stronger than ordinary copy/discard conventions.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from account-oriented chains:** explicit state-access authority can improve security and parallel scheduling.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**from the AI era:** context and reasoning tokens are part of software-development cost.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm must synthesize lessons, not syntax.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 55. Ultimate Nazm Equation")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "C machine access")
    strs_push(l, "+")
    strs_push(l, "C++ zero-cost abstraction ambition")
    strs_push(l, "+")
    strs_push(l, "Python readability/productivity ambition")
    strs_push(l, "+")
    strs_push(l, "Go tooling/concurrency simplicity")
    strs_push(l, "+")
    strs_push(l, "Rust static safety")
    strs_push(l, "+")
    strs_push(l, "Erlang failure isolation")
    strs_push(l, "+")
    strs_push(l, "Zig cost transparency")
    strs_push(l, "+")
    strs_push(l, "SPARK assurance discipline")
    strs_push(l, "+")
    strs_push(l, "Haskell effect reasoning")
    strs_push(l, "+")
    strs_push(l, "CUDA heterogeneous compute")
    strs_push(l, "+")
    strs_push(l, "Julia scientific performance/productivity")
    strs_push(l, "+")
    strs_push(l, "WebAssembly portable sandboxing")
    strs_push(l, "+")
    strs_push(l, "Move-style resource-safety lessons")
    strs_push(l, "+")
    strs_push(l, "EVM smart-contract determinism and ABI lessons")
    strs_push(l, "+")
    strs_push(l, "account-oriented decentralized execution lessons")
    strs_push(l, "+")
    strs_push(l, "modern AI semantic tooling")
    strs_push(l, "+")
    strs_push(l, "AI-era token efficiency")
    strs_push(l, "-----------------------------------------")
    strs_push(l, "            NAZM")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "This equation is conceptual.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "It does not mean literal feature equivalence.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 56. The Hardest Research Question")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The most important question is not:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> How do we add all these features?")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "It is:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **What is the smallest semantic system from which most of these properties can emerge without contradiction?**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Current candidate answer revolves around:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "ownership")
    strs_push(l, "regions")
    strs_push(l, "effects")
    strs_push(l, "capabilities")
    strs_push(l, "tasks")
    strs_push(l, "messages")
    strs_push(l, "contracts")
    strs_push(l, "profiles")
    strs_push(l, "semantic identity")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "This hypothesis must be tested.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 57. Definition of Futuristic")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "\"Futuristic\" does not mean unusual syntax.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm becomes futuristic if it meaningfully improves unresolved problems such as:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- human + AI collaborative programming;")
    strs_push(l, "- safe systems development;")
    strs_push(l, "- predictable high-level performance;")
    strs_push(l, "- semantic incremental compilation;")
    strs_push(l, "- heterogeneous hardware;")
    strs_push(l, "- provenance-aware security;")
    strs_push(l, "- evidence-producing builds;")
    strs_push(l, "- verified self-host development;")
    strs_push(l, "- token-efficient agent workflows.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 58. Definition of Machine-Native")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Machine-native means:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- hardware-aware when necessary;")
    strs_push(l, "- native code generation;")
    strs_push(l, "- direct ABI interoperability;")
    strs_push(l, "- no mandatory virtual machine;")
    strs_push(l, "- explicit memory/layout controls;")
    strs_push(l, "- SIMD/accelerator capability;")
    strs_push(l, "- small-runtime possibility.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 59. Definition of AI-Native")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "AI-native means:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- stable semantic APIs;")
    strs_push(l, "- machine-readable diagnostics;")
    strs_push(l, "- semantic identities;")
    strs_push(l, "- deterministic tools;")
    strs_push(l, "- safe automatic edits;")
    strs_push(l, "- change-impact information;")
    strs_push(l, "- compiler-verifiable agent workflows;")
    strs_push(l, "- minimum-sufficient-context delivery;")
    strs_push(l, "- semantic delta protocols.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "It does NOT require embedding AI inference inside every compiled program.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 60. Definition of Human-Readable")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Human-readable means:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- local reasoning;")
    strs_push(l, "- predictable grammar;")
    strs_push(l, "- limited implicit behaviour;")
    strs_push(l, "- clarity at use sites;")
    strs_push(l, "- explainable costs;")
    strs_push(l, "- excellent diagnostics;")
    strs_push(l, "- progressive disclosure;")
    strs_push(l, "- consistent formatting.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 61. Definition of Token-Efficient")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Token-efficient means:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- low unnecessary redundancy;")
    strs_push(l, "- high semantic density;")
    strs_push(l, "- regular grammar;")
    strs_push(l, "- concise but meaningful naming;")
    strs_push(l, "- compiler-backed inference;")
    strs_push(l, "- structured diagnostics;")
    strs_push(l, "- semantic context retrieval;")
    strs_push(l, "- minimal patches;")
    strs_push(l, "- low repair iteration count;")
    strs_push(l, "- efficient intent-to-verified-code flow.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "It does NOT mean:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- code golf;")
    strs_push(l, "- cryptic symbols;")
    strs_push(l, "- tokenizer-specific hacks;")
    strs_push(l, "- sacrificing human comprehension for shorter source.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 62. Definition of Safe")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Safe means specific guarantees.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Every guarantee must name its scope.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Examples:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "memory safe")
    strs_push(l, "data-race safe")
    strs_push(l, "bounds safe")
    strs_push(l, "type safe")
    strs_push(l, "capability safe")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Never use \"safe\" without specifying what safety property is guaranteed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 63. Definition of Reliable")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Reliable includes:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "safety")
    strs_push(l, "determinism")
    strs_push(l, "failure containment")
    strs_push(l, "resource control")
    strs_push(l, "testing")
    strs_push(l, "verification")
    strs_push(l, "reproducibility")
    strs_push(l, "observability")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Reliability is broader than memory safety.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 64. Long-Term Maturity Stages")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Stage A — Correct language core")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Semantics and compiler correctness.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Stage B — Self-hosted language")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm builds Nazm.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Stage C — Safe systems language")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Ownership/resource semantics mature.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Stage D — Concurrency-native language")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Structured concurrency and data-race safety mature.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Stage E — Semantic tooling language")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Incremental/AI-native compiler interfaces mature.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Stage F — Token-efficient agent-development platform")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Semantic context packets, delta protocols, structured edits and AI task metrics mature.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Stage G — High-performance general language")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Native performance and optimization mature.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Stage H — Embedded/systems platform")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Bare-metal and architecture controls mature.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Stage I — Heterogeneous compute language")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "SIMD/GPU/accelerator model matures.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Stage J — Portable / decentralized execution platform")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "WebAssembly and at least one evidence-backed Web3 contract backend mature under deterministic, capability-restricted and resource-metered profile semantics.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Stage K — High-assurance profile")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Formalized restricted semantics mature. Critical and Web3 verification infrastructure may share contracts/proof machinery where their semantic obligations overlap.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "These stages may overlap, but evidence must remain independent.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 65. Current Development Discipline")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "This goal file must never instruct an agent to implement everything immediately.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "At every stage:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "specify")
    strs_push(l, "→ implement minimum coherent slice")
    strs_push(l, "→ test")
    strs_push(l, "→ measure")
    strs_push(l, "→ attack")
    strs_push(l, "→ document")
    strs_push(l, "→ expand")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Never:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "add twenty features")
    strs_push(l, "→ hope architecture emerges.")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 66. Instructions to Claude Code and Future Agents")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "When using this document:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "1. Treat it as long-term direction.")
    strs_push(l, "2. Do not mark goals implemented because they appear here.")
    strs_push(l, "3. Cross-reference the capability matrix for current truth.")
    strs_push(l, "4. Cross-reference specifications for semantics.")
    strs_push(l, "5. Cross-reference tests for evidence.")
    strs_push(l, "6. Cross-reference benchmarks for performance claims.")
    strs_push(l, "7. Put speculative concepts in the research register.")
    strs_push(l, "8. Do not implement future phases without dependency justification.")
    strs_push(l, "9. Preserve current verified behaviour while evolving architecture.")
    strs_push(l, "10. Challenge this document when evidence contradicts it.")
    strs_push(l, "11. Treat token efficiency as a measurable performance property.")
    strs_push(l, "12. Do not optimize syntax for a single tokenizer.")
    strs_push(l, "13. Prefer semantic compression over cryptic brevity.")
    strs_push(l, "14. Prefer minimum sufficient semantic context for agents.")
    strs_push(l, "15. Prefer structured edits over whole-file rewrites where safe.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 67. Mandatory Agent Question Before Major Work")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Before a significant implementation, an agent should be able to answer:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "Which barrier are we solving?")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Why now?")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What prerequisite is already satisfied?")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Which semantic invariant changes?")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What existing verified behaviour can regress?")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What runtime cost changes?")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What token/context cost changes?")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What evidence will prove success?")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What result would cause us to reject this design?")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "If these answers are missing, implementation is premature.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 68. Goal File / Status File Separation")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "This file should change rarely.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`NAZM_LANGUAGE_GOALS.md` answers:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> Where are we ultimately going?")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A capability matrix answers:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> What exists today?")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A roadmap answers:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> What comes next?")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A specification answers:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> What exactly does the language mean?")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A research register answers:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> What are we still uncertain about?")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A benchmark report answers:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> How does it actually perform?")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An AI/token benchmark report answers:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> How efficiently can agents understand and produce verified changes?")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A release report answers:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> What exactly did we verify?")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Never collapse these into one document.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 69. AI-Era Development Model")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm should explicitly anticipate a future development workflow:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "Human")
    strs_push(l, "  ↓")
    strs_push(l, "problem selection")
    strs_push(l, "architecture")
    strs_push(l, "constraints")
    strs_push(l, "trade-offs")
    strs_push(l, "risk decisions")
    strs_push(l, "approval")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "AI agents")
    strs_push(l, "  ↓")
    strs_push(l, "implementation")
    strs_push(l, "tests")
    strs_push(l, "refactoring")
    strs_push(l, "migration")
    strs_push(l, "routine debugging")
    strs_push(l, "documentation")
    strs_push(l, "repetitive optimization")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Compiler + verification toolchain")
    strs_push(l, "  ↓")
    strs_push(l, "semantic checks")
    strs_push(l, "safety checks")
    strs_push(l, "tests")
    strs_push(l, "mutation")
    strs_push(l, "fuzzing")
    strs_push(l, "bootstrap")
    strs_push(l, "reproducibility")
    strs_push(l, "provenance")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Human")
    strs_push(l, "  ↓")
    strs_push(l, "governance")
    strs_push(l, "approval")
    strs_push(l, "release")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "This model does not remove humans from programming.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "It moves humans toward intent, architecture, governance and high-value decisions while automation takes more implementation burden.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 70. Intent-to-Verified-Software Efficiency")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The ultimate AI-era optimization target is not:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "fewest source tokens")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "It is:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "fewest total resources needed to move from")
    strs_push(l, "human intent")
    strs_push(l, "to")
    strs_push(l, "verified implementation")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Resources include:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "human attention")
    strs_push(l, "AI input tokens")
    strs_push(l, "AI output tokens")
    strs_push(l, "tool tokens")
    strs_push(l, "compiler work")
    strs_push(l, "repair iterations")
    strs_push(l, "test runs")
    strs_push(l, "review effort")
    strs_push(l, "runtime compute")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm should seek **Intent → Verified Software Efficiency**.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "This may become one of the defining performance dimensions of the language.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "# 71. Final North Star")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm should allow a developer to express intent at a high level without forcing them to surrender knowledge or control of the machine.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler should understand enough semantics to protect the programmer from major classes of failure, optimize aggressively, expose meaningful costs, support concurrent and heterogeneous execution, communicate precise program meaning to humans, IDEs and AI agents, and provide compact semantic context for automated development.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "For portable sandboxed and decentralized execution, the same semantics should be lowerable through WebAssembly and contract-oriented backends while profiles restrict ambient authority, enforce determinism, expose persistent state and make metered resource cost visible.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "For Web3, smart-contract features must remain a restriction/profile/backend concern rather than contaminating ordinary Nazm with chain-specific meaning. Asset/resource safety, authorization, ABI/storage generation and contract verification should reuse the general ownership, effects, capabilities, contracts and provenance architecture wherever sound.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "For critical domains, the same semantic foundation should be restrictable into profiles that prioritize analyzability, determinism and evidence.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "For low-level domains, the programmer must still be able to reach the hardware.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "For high-level domains, those details should disappear when irrelevant.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "For AI-assisted development, program meaning must be available through deterministic semantic interfaces rather than guessed from source text.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "For token efficiency, the language must minimize unnecessary ceremony while avoiding cryptic syntax, and the toolchain must minimize the amount of context an agent needs to complete a verified change.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "For performance, claims must come from measurements.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "For safety, claims must name guarantees.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "For reliability, claims must come with evidence.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "For future evolution, experimental ideas must remain removable until proved.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The ultimate objective is not:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> one language with every feature.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "It is:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **one coherent semantic foundation that removes as many historical programming barriers as possible while preserving human clarity, machine efficiency, safety, determinism, evidence, control, portable/decentralized execution, and AI-era token efficiency.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "That is the long-term Nazm goal.")
    str_join(l, str_from_byte(10)) + str_from_byte(10)
}

fn dd_doc1() -> Str {
    let l = strs_new()
    strs_push(l, "# Architecture")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Status: design record. Partly implemented — see below.** This documents decisions made")
    strs_push(l, "before writing the compiler, and the reasoning that would otherwise be lost. Where a")
    strs_push(l, "decision rests on a claim that has not been checked, it says so.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Current state — Nazm 1.0 (Gate 1, 2026-10-07)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Read this first. Everything after it is the design record: §1–§6 are the design written before")
    strs_push(l, "the compiler, and each §7.n is the dated record of one milestone's decisions. They are kept, not")
    strs_push(l, "rewritten, and a later section or a marked correction governs an earlier one. Where they disagree")
    strs_push(l, "with this overview or with [`capability-matrix.md`](capability-matrix.md) about what exists")
    strs_push(l, "today, the matrix decides.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The pipeline.** One front end, two ways to run what it accepts:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Stage | Crate | What it owns |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Source | `nazm-span` | files, `FileId`-carrying spans, the source map |")
    strs_push(l, "| Syntax | `nazm-syntax` | lexer, error-tolerant parser, the lossless CST and the AST |")
    strs_push(l, "| Meaning | `nazm-sema`, `nazm-core` | one resolution, types, generics, traits, effects, capabilities, provenance, contracts — the checker, and the interpreter `nazm run` uses |")
    strs_push(l, "| Modules and reuse | `nazm-iface`, `nazm-cache`, `nazm-package` | persisted interfaces (`nazm.interface/13`), keyed semantic and object caches, packages, locks and local registries |")
    strs_push(l, "| Core IR | `nazm-cir` | what each position of a checked program means, decided once (`nazm.core-ir/3`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| MIR | `nazm-mir` | every copy, move and drop explicit and validated; monomorphisation for the native path |")
    strs_push(l, "| LIR | `nazm-lir` | the instruction-level IR both native backends translate (`nazm.lir/2`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Code generation | `nazm-lir` (LLVM text, compiled by `clang`), `nazm-codegen-clif` (Cranelift, in process) | machine code; neither backend falls back to the other |")
    strs_push(l, "| Runtime | `nazm-runtime` | LLVM IR for the task scheduler, channels, reclamation and the outside-world built-ins, generated into every native program (runtime ABI 15) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Tooling | `nazm-service`, `nazm-cli`, `nazm-mcp`, `nazm-docs`, `nazm-repo`, `nazm-formal` | the language service, the command line, the MCP server, documentation and repository maps, bounded formal checks |")
    strs_push(l, "| Measurement | `nazm-bench`, `nazm-agent-bench`, `nazm-tokens`, `xtask` | benchmarks, the agent benchmark, token-cost counting, the repository's gates, contained runner and release tooling |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm run` interprets the checked program's Core IR; `nazm build` lowers it through MIR and LIR to")
    strs_push(l, "native code, and the two are held to the same results by differential tests. `compiler/*.nz` is a")
    strs_push(l, "second compiler, written in Nazm for a declared subset of the language (`bootstrap.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is stable.** The language surface `spec.md` classifies STABLE 1.0, the schemas, commands")
    strs_push(l, "and package formats `stability.md` classifies STABLE 1.x, and nothing else. The crates' Rust APIs")
    strs_push(l, "are not a public interface; `publish = false` holds every one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What remains design, not code.** §2's HIR level, §4's automatic layout selection (one opt-in")
    strs_push(l, "layout exists, N68), §5's parameter conventions beyond `let` and its region calculus, effect")
    strs_push(l, "handlers and user-defined effects. `limitations.md` is the current list.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Corrected 2026-09-21.** This line read \"Nothing below §7 exists in code\", and that was")
    strs_push(l, "the single most-copied false sentence in the repository — the workspace router and three")
    strs_push(l, "other documents paraphrased it. What is now implemented: one IR crate (§2 level 7 by name,")
    strs_push(l, "though not by definition — see §7), the LLVM-text backend (§2 level 8), a task and channel")
    strs_push(l, "runtime emitted into every compiled program, and the differential-testing discipline of §6.")
    strs_push(l, "What remains design: §2 levels 2-6, §4 entirely, and every part of §5 except the reduced")
    strs_push(l, "concurrency model. [`capability-matrix.md`](capability-matrix.md) is the authority on which")
    strs_push(l, "is which, area by area, with evidence.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 1. Does Nazm need a new compiler design?")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The question that started the project. Answered layer by layer:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Layer | Verdict | Why |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Lexer / parser / CST | **New** | Error-tolerant, incremental, IDE-grade. Nothing reusable |")
    strs_push(l, "| Name resolution, type + effect inference | **New** | No existing engine does effect rows plus MVS parameter conventions |")
    strs_push(l, "| Core IR | **New** | Must carry effects and be content-hashable |")
    strs_push(l, "| MIR (ownership / regions / taint) | **New — narrow the novelty** | Rust's MIR already carries exclusivity and [region inference](https://rustc-dev-guide.rust-lang.org/borrow-check.html). What is new is the *combination* — conventions, regions, effect rows, provenance in one IR — and reusing the region solve for arena and layout decisions |")
    strs_push(l, "| Monomorphisation + layout selection | **New within the §4 boundary** | Prior art exists for the transformation. Whole-program automatic selection is a **proposed research direction**, pending a literature review that has not been done |")
    strs_push(l, "| LIR (low-level SSA) | **New, thin, deliberately boring** | Just the contract both backends read |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Machine code generation** | **REUSE — Cranelift + LLVM** | Instruction selection, register allocation, scheduling, and target coverage are decades of work with no novelty available |")
    strs_push(l, "| Linker | **Reuse** | `object` crate + system linker |")
    strs_push(l, "| Incremental framework | **Reuse `salsa` + own persistence** | salsa's durability story is weak; do not depend on it for disk |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**New front end, new IR, new middle end, reused back end.** But the shape is closer to")
    strs_push(l, "rust-analyzer plus a content-addressed cache than to a batch compiler like gcc.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Four corrections to the obvious version of that")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**\"Rust is slow because of LLVM\" is roughly one-third true.** LLVM is 30–50% of a rustc")
    strs_push(l, "debug build; the rest is trait solving, monomorphisation, borrow checking, linking.")
    strs_push(l, "Swapping in Cranelift buys 20–40% on debug builds, not an order of magnitude. The fast")
    strs_push(l, "loop comes from four tiers:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Tier | What | Role |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| 0 | `nazm check` — no codegen, function-granular incremental | ~95% of what an agent needs. A **front-end** achievement, not a backend one |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1 | Interpret / cranelift-jit | run tests and scripts, no object files |")
    strs_push(l, "| 2 | Cranelift AOT | dev binaries |")
    strs_push(l, "| 3 | LLVM | release only |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Do not monomorphise in dev builds.** Monomorphisation is what *generates* the LLVM work.")
    strs_push(l, "Dictionary passing for tiers 0–2, monomorphise only for release (Swift's model). A bigger")
    strs_push(l, "dev-build win than the backend swap, and it composes with it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Cranelift's payoff is that one component does four jobs** — comptime evaluator, REPL,")
    strs_push(l, "test runner, hot reload — not \"faster debug builds\". Its AArch64 backend is production")
    strs_push(l, "grade (Wasmtime runs on it), so macOS-arm64 development is fine.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Do not link against LLVM in year one.** Emit LLVM IR as *text* and shell out to")
    strs_push(l, "`clang`/`opt`. Costs perhaps 10–20% of release build time, and release builds are rare.")
    strs_push(l, "Keeps `nazm` a small Cranelift-only binary with the LLVM toolchain an optional download.")
    strs_push(l, "Also practical: the development machine had 18GB free of 460GB when this was written.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Two backends is two sets of semantics bugs")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "UB, floating point, overflow, atomics, unwinding, ABI. A bug reproducing only under")
    strs_push(l, "`--release` is the worst class there is. Mandatory once codegen exists:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- LIR stays narrow and prose-specified; backends translate, they do not optimise")
    strs_push(l, "- a **LIR reference interpreter** is the semantic oracle")
    strs_push(l, "- differential fuzzing in CI from the start")
    strs_push(l, "- release is **always** LLVM, so divergence never reaches a user")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Differential testing catches divergence, not bugs shared by all implementations. See §6")
    strs_push(l, "for what must be specified before backends can be compared at all.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Not MLIR, in v1")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "It offers real things — pass infrastructure, a dialect system, affine and vector dialects.")
    strs_push(l, "It costs a C++ build dependency in a Rust project, immature Rust bindings, coupling to")
    strs_push(l, "LLVM's release cadence, and decisively: it is not a content-addressed incremental database")
    strs_push(l, "and cannot be made into one. Revisit only if Nazm pivots toward tensor/accelerator codegen.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 2. IR levels")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| # | Level | Form | Content-addressed | Consumers |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| 0 | Source | UTF-8 `.nz` in git | file hash | humans, agents, git |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1 | CST | lossless green tree, error-tolerant | interned | formatter, LSP, structured edits |")
    strs_push(l, "| 2 | HIR | name-resolved, path-based `DefId` (never positional) | no | inference, IDE |")
    strs_push(l, "| 3 | **Core** | typed, effect rows explicit, traits→dictionaries, ANF | **yes** | comptime, REPL, cache keys, oracle |")
    strs_push(l, "| 4 | Core′ | after comptime partial evaluation | derived | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| 5 | MIR | CFG over *places*: moves, projections, drops, regions, effect ops | cached | exclusivity, region/escape, taint |")
    strs_push(l, "| 6 | Mono MIR | monomorphised, devirtualised, layout-selected | cached | layout pass, whole-program opts |")
    strs_push(l, "| 7 | LIR | SSA, concrete layouts, ABI-explicit | cached | the single backend contract + oracle interpreter |")
    strs_push(l, "| 8 | Machine | Cranelift IR (dev) or LLVM IR text (release) | by LIR hash | — |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The commitment that is hardest to reverse:** field access stays a symbolic")
    strs_push(l, "`project(place, field_id)` through level 6. Offsets appear only at level 7. Bake offsets")
    strs_push(l, "into the front end — as most compilers do — and layout selection becomes unrecoverable.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 3. Source of truth, and what Unison teaches")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Source of truth is plain UTF-8 `.nz` files in git.** Non-negotiable. grep works,")
    strs_push(l, "`git diff` works, code review works, every editor works, and — decisively for this project")
    strs_push(l, "— LLMs have seen text.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "[Unison](https://www.unison-lang.org/docs/the-big-idea/) shipped content-addressed code to")
    strs_push(l, "1.0 in November 2025. What hurt its adoption was not content addressing; it was replacing")
    strs_push(l, "the *file* as the unit of code, which broke every existing tool at once in exchange for")
    strs_push(l, "benefits users could not feel on day one. For Nazm that trade would be worse, because text")
    strs_push(l, "source is the transfer-learning surface and it is the largest lever the project has.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Content addressing applies to derived artifacts only.** After name resolution and type")
    strs_push(l, "checking, each top-level definition is normalised (names erased to de Bruijn indices,")
    strs_push(l, "dependencies replaced by their hashes) and hashed → a Merkle DAG. That hash keys")
    strs_push(l, "type-check results, MIR, monomorphised instances, LIR, object code, test results, docs.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The payoff that motivates it: **definition-hash equality.** If an agent rewrites a function")
    strs_push(l, "and the normalised Core hash is unchanged, the compiler knows the edit produced an")
    strs_push(l, "identical definition and can say so. This detects **one class** of no-op edit — normalised")
    strs_push(l, "Core alpha-equivalence — and not all behaviour-preserving rewrites. Definition hashing is")
    strs_push(l, "Unison's idea; the contribution here is the agent-facing use of it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Cache-key correctness")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Determinism aids reproducibility but does not make incorrect cache hits impossible.** The")
    strs_push(l, "key must cover:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "compiler identity · schema version · transitive dependency hashes · target triple and CPU")
    strs_push(l, "features · optimisation flags · ABI · every compile-time input the result depends on")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Anything omitted is a silent miscompile waiting to happen.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Comptime execution through a JIT needs a sandbox**: no filesystem, network, or clock by")
    strs_push(l, "default, with resource and time limits and an explicit capability to widen. Zig and Rust")
    strs_push(l, "restrict const-eval for exactly this reason.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 4. The layout-selection boundary")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Symbolic projections are necessary but not sufficient. Before any automatic layout change,")
    strs_push(l, "the spec must define behaviour for: **address identity, escaping references, FFI,")
    strs_push(l, "serialization, atomics, separately compiled modules.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Conservative start: **explicitly eligible collections whose elements cannot expose a stable")
    strs_push(l, "address**, opt-in at the type level, compiler chooses within that envelope. Widen only with")
    strs_push(l, "evidence.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Prior art exists: published [AoS-to-SoA compiler work](https://arxiv.org/html/2502.16517v1),")
    strs_push(l, "ISPC, Julia's `StructArrays`, explicit SoA in Jai and Odin. Whole-program automatic")
    strs_push(l, "selection with a sound semantic boundary is **Nazm's proposed research direction** — stated")
    strs_push(l, "that way because no literature review has been done, so \"nobody has done this\" is not a")
    strs_push(l, "claim this project is entitled to make. The survey is a Phase 1 deliverable.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Benchmarking rule:** layout wins are measured against **both idiomatic Rust and")
    strs_push(l, "hand-written SoA Rust**. Beating only idiomatic Rust measures a different representation,")
    strs_push(l, "not a better compiler.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 5. Type system")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Mutable value semantics, not lifetimes")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Everything is a value; no references in the type system, only *projections* that provably")
    strs_push(l, "cannot escape. Ownership lives in parameter conventions — `let` (read-only projection),")
    strs_push(l, "`inout` (exclusive mutable), `sink` (consumed), `set` (initialised) — inferable at call")
    strs_push(l, "sites and checked **intraprocedurally**. No lifetime variables, no annotations, no")
    strs_push(l, "non-local error messages.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Honest costs:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Expressiveness.** Cyclic and shared-observer structures need arena indices rather than")
    strs_push(l, "  pointers. Good Rust does this anyway, but it is a real restriction.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Silent copies.** MVS says \"pass by value\" and relies on elision. Two separate")
    strs_push(l, "  diagnostics, because **a no-codegen check cannot know what the backend did**:")
    strs_push(l, "  `nazm check` reports *potential* copies (front end, conservative, incremental, in-editor);")
    strs_push(l, "  `nazm build --remarks` reports *surviving* copies (backend optimisation remarks, accurate,")
    strs_push(l, "  post-codegen).")
    strs_push(l, "- **Maturity.** [Hylo](https://hylo-lang.org/) is a research language with no large")
    strs_push(l, "  production codebase, and **adopting the terminology does not supply the rules.** Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "  needs its own specification of copying, borrowing, closure capture, and concurrency")
    strs_push(l, "  interaction. This is risk #2 after training data.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The hedge:** the IR carries a full region/borrow calculus even though the surface has")
    strs_push(l, "none. If MVS proves insufficient, the underlying reference model can be exposed without")
    strs_push(l, "re-founding the language. Never design a surface whose semantics the IR cannot express a")
    strs_push(l, "superset of.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Effects, capabilities, provenance are three problems, not one")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "They share row-unification machinery. They answer different questions:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Effects** — what operations can this function perform?")
    strs_push(l, "- **Capabilities** — what authority does this code hold?")
    strs_push(l, "- **Information flow** — where can this data reach?")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An earlier draft called provenance \"nearly free once effects exist\". That was overclaiming.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Effects** are a row on every function type in Core: `fn(A) -> B / {io, alloc, panic | r}`.")
    strs_push(l, "Inference is unification over rows with a row variable for polymorphism; the check at each")
    strs_push(l, "call site is a subset test. Polymorphism is what prevents function colouring:")
    strs_push(l, "`fn map[T,U,e](xs: List[T], f: fn(T)->U / e) -> List[U] / e` serves pure and effectful")
    strs_push(l, "callers from one definition.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Purity is a prerequisite, not a licence.** An empty row does **not** by itself authorise")
    strs_push(l, "dropping, reordering, memoizing, or parallelising a call:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn forever() -> Int / {} { loop {} }")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "forever()           // dropping this unused call changes the program")
    strs_push(l, "print(\"finished\")   // from never printing to printing")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Each transformation must additionally establish its own conditions — termination,")
    strs_push(l, "exceptions, dependencies, ownership, observable behaviour.")
    strs_push(l, "[LLVM](https://llvm.org/docs/LangRef.html) separates memory effects, termination/progress")
    strs_push(l, "(`willreturn`, `mustprogress`), and speculatability precisely because they are not")
    strs_push(l, "interchangeable. Nazm's effect row must do the same rather than collapse them into one bit.")
    strs_push(l, "**Open spec question: is divergence an effect?** See `spec.md` §Open.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Provenance** is a lattice-valued qualifier (`Untrusted(source)`, `Secret`, `PII`) on the")
    strs_push(l, "same row machinery, plus a flow-sensitive MIR pass for precision. The rule is")
    strs_push(l, "**position-sensitive**, which is what separates taint checking people use from taint")
    strs_push(l, "checking people disable:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "db.query(\"SELECT * FROM items WHERE id = $1\", [req.body.id])   // legal: bound parameter")
    strs_push(l, "db.query(\"SELECT * FROM items WHERE id = \" + req.body.id)      // error: query construction")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Same shape for HTML text vs markup, shell argv vs shell string. Still to specify: implicit")
    strs_push(l, "flows (branching on a secret), sanitizers, aliasing, declassification (capability-gated),")
    strs_push(l, "the FFI boundary.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Concurrency")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "M:N green threads, work-stealing scheduler, growable stacks (copy-and-grow, not segmented),")
    strs_push(l, "blocking-looking code with no `async`/`await`, reactor on kqueue/epoll/io_uring, FFI")
    strs_push(l, "blocking handoff detected by an effect annotation on the extern declaration.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Structured concurrency is mandatory:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "scope { s =>")
    strs_push(l, "    s.spawn { mutate(x) }")
    strs_push(l, "    mutate(x)              // compile error")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The borrow region is `[spawn point, scope end]`**, and parent *or sibling* access to that")
    strs_push(l, "place anywhere in the region is rejected — the same discipline as Rust's `thread::scope`.")
    strs_push(l, "An earlier draft justified this by saying the parent is \"provably blocked at the scope's")
    strs_push(l, "end\", which is wrong: the parent runs before the join.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Channels transfer ownership (`send` takes `sink T`), so nothing aliased crosses one. That")
    strs_push(l, "does **not** cover captured variables, globals/statics, or foreign pointers; each needs its")
    strs_push(l, "own rule.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Cancellation is ambient in the scope rather than a `ctx` threaded through every signature —")
    strs_push(l, "it is a scoped effect handler. Detached tasks require an explicit `daemon` capability.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deadlock-freedom is not claimed.** Ownership prevents data races, not lock-ordering")
    strs_push(l, "mistakes or channel cycles. Ship a lock-order lint and a debug-build detector.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The task-count target is withdrawn.** \"1M live tasks under 2GB\" was arithmetically")
    strs_push(l, "impossible — 1M × 4KB is 4.1GB of stack alone, and macOS arm64 uses 16KB pages, though only")
    strs_push(l, "*if* each stack is a separate page-granular resident allocation; a pooling allocator packing")
    strs_push(l, "small stacks into shared pages would not pay that. Which is why it is replaced by a")
    strs_push(l, "benchmark that states its terms: task states distinguished (created / parked / runnable /")
    strs_push(l, "running), allocation strategy stated, lazy commit explicit, **RSS measured rather than")
    strs_push(l, "virtual reservation**, page size recorded per platform.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 6. Differential testing: what must be specified first")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm test --backend=all` compares only **specified** semantics. Before any backend")
    strs_push(l, "comparison the spec must fix integer overflow, floating-point semantics, panic and unwind")
    strs_push(l, "behaviour, and what counts as an observable output. Undefined behaviour cannot be")
    strs_push(l, "differentially tested — only differentially *discovered*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Deterministic sequential programs first. Concurrent programs legitimately produce different")
    strs_push(l, "schedules, so those compare **permitted outcomes and invariants**, never identical traces.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Cadence | Checks |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Pull request | Conformance, golden diagnostics, bounded differential cases, `cargo xtask check`, `cargo lint` |")
    strs_push(l, "| Scheduled | Longer fuzzing, broader targets, reproducibility matrix |")
    strs_push(l, "| Release | Full supported matrix, plus review of every outstanding discrepancy |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7. Crate layout")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Crates are created when their responsibility exists.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Corrected 2026-09-20.** This section read \"Phase 2 is `nazm-bench` and `xtask` only —")
    strs_push(l, "there is no compiler yet, deliberately\", and that is no longer the case: the Phase 4")
    strs_push(l, "front-end crates exist and a `.nz` program executes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Corrected again 2026-09-21.** The sentence that followed — \"everything from `nazm-hir`")
    strs_push(l, "downward is still design\" — has itself rotted, which is worth leaving visible: a correction")
    strs_push(l, "is not permanent either. `nazm-lir` exists, the backend exists, and a runtime is emitted")
    strs_push(l, "into every compiled program. What is still design is everything *between* the AST and")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-lir`: `nazm-hir`, `nazm-ty`, `nazm-db`, `nazm-mir`, `nazm-mono`. See")
    strs_push(l, "[`roadmap.md`](../user/roadmap.md) for ordering and [`capability-matrix.md`](capability-matrix.md)")
    strs_push(l, "for what each one's absence currently costs.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Corrected 2026-09-30 (N39).** One level between the AST and `nazm-lir` now exists: Core IR,")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-cir`, the one lowering of a checked program that the interpreter runs and `nazm-lir`")
    strs_push(l, "lowers (§7.41). It earned its crate the way §3 of `master-architecture.md` requires — by taking")
    strs_push(l, "a responsibility away from two places that each held it: deciding, from the tree, what a")
    strs_push(l, "program's positions, `?`s, blocks and transfers mean. `nazm-hir`, `nazm-ty`, `nazm-db`,")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-mir` and `nazm-mono` are still design.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Corrected 2026-10-01 (N40).** `nazm-mir` exists: MIR, the one lowering from Core IR for the")
    strs_push(l, "native backend (§7.42), which took from `nazm-lir` its temporaries, its partly-built slots and its")
    strs_push(l, "`?` completion, and from the emitter every cleanup decision it used to make per exit. The instance")
    strs_push(l, "planner moved into it, so monomorphisation — the table's `nazm-mono` — is MIR lowering's first")
    strs_push(l, "step rather than a crate of its own. `nazm-hir`, `nazm-ty` and `nazm-db` are still design.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Phase | Crates | State |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| 2 | `nazm-bench` · `xtask` | **exists** |")
    strs_push(l, "| 4 | `nazm-span` · `nazm-diag` · `nazm-syntax` · `nazm-sema` · `nazm-iface` · `nazm-core` · `nazm-cli` | **exists** (`nazm-core` is the checker, the one lowering to Core IR, and the evaluator over Core IR; `nazm-sema` and `nazm-iface` are not on this diagram at all — see §7.2 and §7.3) |")
    strs_push(l, "| 4 | **`nazm-cir`** | **exists** (N39) — Core IR, level 3 by responsibility: typed, resolved, explicit control, effects as function metadata. A tree of structured regions, not ANF, and no traits to lower. §7.41 |")
    strs_push(l, "| 4 | `nazm-hir` · `nazm-ty` · `nazm-mcp` | planned |")
    strs_push(l, "| 6 | **`nazm-mir`** | **exists** (N40) — MIR, level 6 by responsibility: each concrete function as a typed CFG with every copy, move, drop, scope join and failure edge explicit, validated. Not SSA, and no borrow checking. §7.42 |")
    strs_push(l, "| 6 | `nazm-db` · `nazm-lsp` | planned |")
    strs_push(l, "| 7 | **`nazm-lir`** | **exists** — since N40 it reads validated MIR and holds layout, symbols and LLVM text emission; the structured tree that was once named for this level is gone. See the note below |")
    strs_push(l, "| 7 | **`nazm-codegen-clif`** | **exists** (N41) — the Cranelift backend behind `nazm-lir`'s `Backend`: every MIR function body to Cranelift IR to one object per unit, in process. §7.43 |")
    strs_push(l, "| 7 | `nazm-link` · `nazm-driver` | planned — clang links, and `nazm-cli` drives |")
    strs_push(l, "| 7 | `nazm-test` | **exists as a subcommand**, `nazm test`, not as a crate |")
    strs_push(l, "| 8 | `nazm-rt` | planned |")
    strs_push(l, "| 9 | `nazm-mono` | planned — and nothing is polymorphic, so there is nothing to monomorphise yet |")
    strs_push(l, "| 9 | `nazm-codegen-llvm` | **exists inside `nazm-lir`**, as LLVM IR emitted in text |")
    strs_push(l, "| 10 | `nazm-pkg` · `nazm-std-build` | planned |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "One deliberate departure from this table is already recorded: [`roadmap.md`](../user/roadmap.md)")
    strs_push(l, "M1 brings `nazm-lir` and `nazm-codegen-llvm` forward, and does **not** create the levels")
    strs_push(l, "between them and the AST. Five empty pass-through crates would match the diagram and carry")
    strs_push(l, "no information.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A name is not a level.** `nazm-lir` is named for level 7 and owns a real responsibility —")
    strs_push(l, "it records which operations can fail and where the source said so, which the AST does not")
    strs_push(l, "carry. Its *form* is not what the table above describes: `While`, `If` and `Scope` nest,")
    strs_push(l, "locals are slot indices, and nothing is in SSA form. Reading the crate list as a progress")
    strs_push(l, "bar against this diagram is what produced four contradictory status claims in September")
    strs_push(l, "2026. The rule that replaced it is in")
    strs_push(l, "[`master-architecture.md`](master-architecture.md) §3: **an IR level earns its existence by")
    strs_push(l, "owning a semantic responsibility no existing level owns**, and matching the diagram is not")
    strs_push(l, "such a reason.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Roles, in dependency order: `span` (files, byte spans — depends on nothing; the `FileId`")
    strs_push(l, "this list promised **exists** since N1, and a `Span` is a file and a range inside it) ·")
    strs_push(l, "`sema` (types, built-in identity, module identity, durable keys, unit interfaces,")
    strs_push(l, "resolution — not a row in the table above, and §7.2 says why) · `iface` (a module's")
    strs_push(l, "interface as persisted, and its fingerprint — §7.3) · `diag` (stable error codes, fixits, JSON schema, renderer) · `syntax`")
    strs_push(l, "(lexer, parser, CST, typed AST, canonical formatter, CST-preserving edits) · `hir` (`DefId`")
    strs_push(l, "graph, modules, name resolution) · `ty` (types, effect rows, provenance, inference) · `core`")
    strs_push(l, "(the checker, the one lowering to Core IR, the reference interpreter) · `cir` (Core IR: its")
    strs_push(l, "invariants, its printed form, per-function digests — §7.41; Merkle hashing over definitions is")
    strs_push(l, "not built) · `db` (salsa queries +")
    strs_push(l, "on-disk store) · `mir` (exclusivity, regions, taint, drop elaboration, effect lowering) ·")
    strs_push(l, "`mono` (monomorphisation, devirtualisation, layout selection) · `lir` (backend contract +")
    strs_push(l, "oracle interpreter) · `codegen-clif` / `codegen-llvm` · `link` · `rt` (scheduler, stacks,")
    strs_push(l, "channels, reactor, allocator — the one crate allowed `unsafe`) · `std-build` · `driver` ·")
    strs_push(l, "`pkg` · `test` · `lsp` · `mcp` · `bench` · `cli` · `xtask`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`unsafe_code` is `forbid` at the workspace level today. It becomes `deny` with a per-crate")
    strs_push(l, "allowance for `nazm-rt` and the FFI crates when those exist — stack switching and allocators")
    strs_push(l, "cannot be written without it. `xtask` enforces that the allowance stays narrow.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.1 Where source identity and resolution live — settled by N1, 2026-09-21")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "§7's table lists crates by the level they would occupy. That was the wrong question to ask")
    strs_push(l, "next, and `master-architecture.md` §3 says why: **a layer earns its existence by owning a")
    strs_push(l, "semantic responsibility no existing layer owns.** The table would have put `nazm-hir` next")
    strs_push(l, "because it is the next row. The tree gave a better reason: name and signature resolution")
    strs_push(l, "was performed *twice* — once in `nazm_core::check`, whose answer `nazm-core/src/lib.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "discarded, and again in `nazm-lir/src/lower.rs`, which rebuilt an equivalent scope stack,")
    strs_push(l, "slot allocator and name-keyed signature table because `xtask/src/rules.rs` forbids the")
    strs_push(l, "backend depending on the interpreter's crate.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**No new crate was created.** The shared vocabulary went to `nazm-syntax`, which both")
    strs_push(l, "consumers already depend on:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| What | Where it lives now | Why there |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `FileId`, `Span { file, start, end }`, `SourceMap` | `nazm-span` | it already owned positions; a span naming its file is the same responsibility done properly |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Type`, `Intrinsic` | `nazm-syntax` | the language's types and built-in signatures are surface vocabulary, and the backend needs them without reaching the interpreter |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Resolution` — definitions, signatures, call targets, slots | `nazm-syntax` | the one type both consumers read; the **algorithm** stays in `nazm_core::check`, which produces it while checking |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "That last row is the part worth stating plainly, because it is where a new crate would have")
    strs_push(l, "been easy to justify and wrong. `Resolution` is a **value**, not a pass. The resolver did")
    strs_push(l, "not move; the second one was deleted. A `nazm-hir` crate holding a copy of the checker's")
    strs_push(l, "answer would have been the pass-through this section was written to prevent — and the")
    strs_push(l, "acceptance test for such a crate, *after it exists, one of the two resolvers is gone*, is")
    strs_push(l, "met here without one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A resolution is not an IR.** It holds no expressions and no control flow. Levels 2–6 of")
    strs_push(l, "§2 remain absent, and `capability-matrix.md` areas 8 and 9 stay MISSING.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What N1 did **not** settle: there is still no compilation unit — every file is parsed")
    strs_push(l, "separately but checked together — and every id in a `Resolution` is session-local, so it is")
    strs_push(l, "not a cache key and not a definition identity that survives a process. `spec.md` *Open*")
    strs_push(l, "carries both, and `research-register.md` R2 and R3 depend on them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.2 Modules, interfaces, and the crate N2 created — settled by N2, 2026-09-22")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N1 left two things open and this milestone closed one of them: **what a compilation unit")
    strs_push(l, "is.** `spec.md` owns the answer — one module, and today one module is one file — and this")
    strs_push(l, "section owns where each part of it lives.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The passes, and what each may see")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "load          the driver follows `use`, reads each file once by canonical path,")
    strs_push(l, "              and produces a SourceMap *and* a ModuleGraph. The last time a path")
    strs_push(l, "              is consulted.")
    strs_push(l, "                  ↓")
    strs_push(l, "parse         each file on its own text")
    strs_push(l, "                  ↓")
    strs_push(l, "declare_unit  per module: its declarations, their signatures, which are `pub`.")
    strs_push(l, "              Reads no other module — which is why the stage needs no ordering")
    strs_push(l, "              and an import cycle has none to violate.")
    strs_push(l, "                  ↓  UnitInterface per module")
    strs_push(l, "check_unit    per module: bodies, against its own definitions and the")
    strs_push(l, "              *interfaces* of the modules it directly imports.")
    strs_push(l, "                  ↓  one Resolution")
    strs_push(l, "lower / eval  read it. Neither resolves a name; neither knows the rule.")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`check(program, graph)` is a loop over the two stages and holds no resolution of its own,")
    strs_push(l, "so a compilation of many modules and a compilation of one take the same path.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Where each thing lives")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| What | Where | Why there |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `ModuleId`, `ModuleGraph`, `Dependency` | `nazm-sema` | the semantic unit and the edges between units; built by the driver, read by everything after |")
    strs_push(l, "| `UnitInterface`, `Export`, `Visibility` | `nazm-sema` | what one unit offers another. No bodies, no private definitions, no hashes |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Resolution`, `FnDef { module, visibility, decl }`, `FnId` | `nazm-sema` | one answer, read by the evaluator and the backend |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Type`, `Intrinsic` | `nazm-sema` | moved from `nazm-syntax`; see below |")
    strs_push(l, "| the module graph's **construction** | `crates/nazm-service/src/load.rs` (in `nazm-cli` until N16) | resolving a path reads the filesystem, which is an effect, and the front end performs none |")
    strs_push(l, "| `declare_unit`, `check_unit`, `Env` | `nazm-core` | resolution is a pass, and the pass did not move |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Why a crate this time, when N1 declined one")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "§7.1 declined `nazm-hir` because it would have held a copy of the checker's answer. This")
    strs_push(l, "crate is a different case, and the evidence is in the source rather than in this diagram:")
    strs_push(l, "**`nazm-syntax`'s lexer, parser, formatter and AST referred to `types`, `intrinsic` and")
    strs_push(l, "`resolve` exactly zero times.** They sat there because N1 needed a place both consumers")
    strs_push(l, "could reach, which was the right call for three types and the wrong one for eight.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-sema` depends on `nazm-span` and nothing else — deliberately not on `nazm-syntax`,")
    strs_push(l, "so the vocabulary a checker records its decisions in cannot begin describing the tree those")
    strs_push(l, "decisions were read off. The AST carries `Function::pub_span`, which records **that `pub`")
    strs_push(l, "was written and where**; what it *means* is `Visibility`, in `nazm-sema`, so visibility is")
    strs_push(l, "decided in one place.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "It is not on §7's table, and that is the point rather than an omission. It owns a")
    strs_push(l, "responsibility no row owns: `nazm-hir` on that list is a graph of definitions *with")
    strs_push(l, "bodies*, and this holds no body at all.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Definition identity")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`FnId` is the definition identity, and it stays flat rather than becoming")
    strs_push(l, "`DefId { module, index }`. A flat index already distinguishes every definition in the")
    strs_push(l, "compilation; qualifying it by module would add a second indirection and no discriminating")
    strs_push(l, "power. What N2 needed was an **owner**, and that is `FnDef::module`, so \"which unit owns")
    strs_push(l, "this definition\" has an answer without changing what identifies one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "It remains session-local, in the same sense as `FileId` and `ModuleId`. Nothing here is a")
    strs_push(l, "cache key or survives a process; `research-register.md` R2 and R3 are unchanged by this.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The same architecture, in the compiler written in Nazm — N2.1, 2026-09-22")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Worth recording because it is a second implementation of these semantics, in a language")
    strs_push(l, "with no structs, no nested arrays and no map type, and it came out with the same shape:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "module.nz    load_modules  →  the merged text, and beside it: where each module's text")
    strs_push(l, "                              begins, and which module each `use` names")
    strs_push(l, "analyse.nz   collect_signatures  →  each definition's owner and `pub` bit")
    strs_push(l, "             check_imports       →  every module's visible imports, before any body,")
    strs_push(l, "                                    with N0207/N0208 raised at the `use`")
    strs_push(l, "             check_all           →  bodies, resolving each call in the asking module and")
    strs_push(l, "                                    **recording** what it resolved to")
    strs_push(l, "emit.nz                          →  reads that record; looks up no name")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Parallel `Ints`/`Strs` columns stand in for the structs `nazm-sema` has, and a linear scan")
    strs_push(l, "stands in for a `HashMap`. What is not a substitution is the division of responsibility:")
    strs_push(l, "the parser records that `pub` was written, the module layer records relationships, the")
    strs_push(l, "checker decides what a name means, and emission consumes the decision. The last edge is the")
    strs_push(l, "one that had teeth — emission used to turn a *name* into an LLVM symbol, which was correct")
    strs_push(l, "under one namespace and a miscompile under modules.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What is still whole-program")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Written at N2, and superseded by §7.5 on 2026-09-22. Kept because it is the statement N5")
    strs_push(l, "had to make false.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> Lowering and code generation. `nazm_lir::lower` takes the whole `Program` and one")
    strs_push(l, "> `Resolution`, emits one LLVM module, and numbers its functions `@nz.fN` — which is why two")
    strs_push(l, "> modules' private `helper` needed no backend change at all. There are no per-module object")
    strs_push(l, "> files, no linker symbols and no cached interfaces, and `capability-matrix.md` says so")
    strs_push(l, "> rather than implying separate compilation from the existence of a unit.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What remains whole-program after N5 is two *analyses* — signature admissibility and the")
    strs_push(l, "recursion refusal — and not generation. §7.5 says why both stay.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.3 Durable identity and persistent interfaces — settled by N3, 2026-09-22")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N2 gave a definition an owner and a module an identity, and both were **session-local**:")
    strs_push(l, "indices into one compilation in one process. That is the right shape for a compilation and")
    strs_push(l, "the wrong one for anything that outlives it. N3 adds a second layer beside it, and the two")
    strs_push(l, "coexist on purpose.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Two layers, not a rename")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Answers | Shape | Lives |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `FileId` | which source did this span come from, **here** | index into a `SourceMap` | one process |")
    strs_push(l, "| `ModuleId` | which loaded module owns this, **here** | index into a `ModuleGraph` | one process |")
    strs_push(l, "| `FnId` | which declaration does this reference mean, **here** | index into a `Resolution` | one process |")
    strs_push(l, "| **`ModuleKey`** | which logical module is this | normalised source-root-relative path | across processes |")
    strs_push(l, "| **`DefKey`** | which logical definition is this | `ModuleKey` + kind + name | across processes |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The session ids are not deprecated and were not renamed. They are dense, cheap and exact")
    strs_push(l, "within a compilation, which is what the checker and the backend need; a durable key is a")
    strs_push(l, "string, computed once per module, which is what a file on disk needs. `spec.md` owns what")
    strs_push(l, "the durable ones *mean*; this section owns where they live.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`ModuleGraph::key(ModuleId)` and `Resolution::def_key(FnId)` are the mapping, and both")
    strs_push(l, "return `Option` — a module outside the source root or reached under two names through a")
    strs_push(l, "symbolic link has **no** durable key, and is refused one rather than given a guess.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The serialization boundary, again")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`Span` taught this: a semantic type and a wire representation are different")
    strs_push(l, "responsibilities, and putting the second inside the first makes every use of the first")
    strs_push(l, "lossy. So `nazm-sema` still depends on `nazm-span` and nothing else — **no serde** — and a")
    strs_push(l, "separate crate owns what a module publishes:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "nazm-sema    semantic, session-local, and durable *identities*      → span")
    strs_push(l, "nazm-iface   the persisted form of a module's interface, and its")
    strs_push(l, "             fingerprint                                            → sema, span, serde, blake3")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-iface` converts explicitly. `UnitInterface` (in-memory, holds `FnId` and `Span`)")
    strs_push(l, "becomes `PersistentUnitInterface` (durable keys, canonical type names, no spans) by a")
    strs_push(l, "function that takes the module's `ModuleKey` and fails without one. Nothing derives")
    strs_push(l, "`Serialize` on a session-local type, because the crate that holds them cannot: `cargo xtask")
    strs_push(l, "check`'s **sema purity** gate fails if `nazm-sema` gains a serde dependency, in the same way")
    strs_push(l, "and for the same reason as the span-identity gate.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Three fingerprints, kept apart")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Over | Used for |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **`InterfaceHash`** | the canonical bytes of a module's persisted interface | deciding whether a module's *dependents* must be re-checked |")
    strs_push(l, "| Implementation fingerprint | a module's own bodies | deciding whether a module's *own* output can be reused — **not built in N3** |")
    strs_push(l, "| `BuildKey` | compiler identity, target, flags, dependency hashes | reusing a generated artefact — **not built in N3** |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Collapsing them is the mistake worth naming: an `InterfaceHash` used as a codegen cache key")
    strs_push(l, "would reuse an object file after a body change, because a body is deliberately not in it.")
    strs_push(l, "N3 builds the first and states the other two so the first cannot be quietly promoted.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Invalidation, as a consequence rather than an engine")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The fingerprint exists so that this holds, and it is tested:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "B's private body changes   → B's InterfaceHash unchanged → A need not be re-checked")
    strs_push(l, "B's exported signature      → B's InterfaceHash changes   → A must be re-checked")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Propagation stops where it stops being true: re-checking A produces A's interface, and if")
    strs_push(l, "*that* is unchanged, A's own importers are unaffected. That is the intended model and it is")
    strs_push(l, "written down here; **no scheduler, cache or query engine implements it**, and")
    strs_push(l, "`capability-matrix.md` says incremental compilation is absent.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What the self-hosted compiler does with all this")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nothing, deliberately. Persistent interfaces are toolchain architecture, not language")
    strs_push(l, "semantics: no Nazm program can observe a `ModuleKey`, and the bootstrap chain neither writes")
    strs_push(l, "nor reads an interface file. What the two implementations must agree on is the *rule* — and")
    strs_push(l, "they do, by both declining durable identity exactly where they could disagree. If a later")
    strs_push(l, "milestone gives the Nazm-written compiler an incremental path, it needs `realpath` first;")
    strs_push(l, "`spec.md` records why.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.4 Semantic reuse, and the keys that make it sound — settled by N4, 2026-09-22")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N3 built identity and an interface fingerprint and reused nothing. N4 is the first")
    strs_push(l, "milestone that *skips work*, which makes it the first one where being wrong is a")
    strs_push(l, "correctness bug rather than a slow build.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What is reused, precisely")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The second stage of checking one module: its bodies.** Not reading the file, not parsing")
    strs_push(l, "it, not reading its declarations. Every module is read, parsed and declared from source on")
    strs_push(l, "every run, which is what makes a skipped module invisible — the interface every other")
    strs_push(l, "module's key depends on, and the compilation's own facts including whether there is a")
    strs_push(l, "`main`, are recomputed rather than recalled.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "So the claim is **incremental semantic checking**, and it is not incremental compilation.")
    strs_push(l, "Lowering and code generation still take the whole program (area 10); `nazm run` and `nazm")
    strs_push(l, "build` reuse nothing, because both need the resolution that only checking a body produces.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### A declared source root came first")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`spec.md` owns the rule. The reason it had to be settled before anything was stored: under")
    strs_push(l, "a derived root a module's key depends on which file the compilation began at, so two")
    strs_push(l, "compilations of one project disagree about what their modules are. That is sound — the keys")
    strs_push(l, "differ, so nothing wrong is found — and it is useless, because nothing is ever shared.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.root` is a marker with no content, and the emptiness is enforced. A configuration")
    strs_push(l, "file is justified when it owns a responsibility; this one owns exactly one fact, and a")
    strs_push(l, "manifest is what it must not be allowed to become.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Three fingerprints, and three keys")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N3's table stands; N4 adds the middle row of the second.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Over | Answers |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `InterfaceHash` | a module's published interface | must its **dependents** be re-checked |")
    strs_push(l, "| **`CheckKey`** | everything semantic checking of a module reads | may its **own check** be skipped |")
    strs_push(l, "| `CodegenKey` | that, plus implementation, target, CPU features, backend, optimisation level, ABI | may its **object code** be reused — **not built** |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`CheckKey` is the checker's identity, the module's `ModuleKey`, its `SourceFingerprint`,")
    strs_push(l, "and the `(ModuleKey, InterfaceHash)` of each direct import. It is deliberately **not** a")
    strs_push(l, "`CodegenKey`: it carries no target and reaches a body only through the module's own source")
    strs_push(l, "fingerprint, so an object file keyed on one would be handed back for a different machine.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**`SourceFingerprint` normalises nothing** — not newlines, not whitespace, not comments, not")
    strs_push(l, "a BOM. A comment edit re-checks its own module and stops there, because the module then")
    strs_push(l, "publishes the same interface. Normalising would mean deciding that two byte sequences check")
    strs_push(l, "identically, and every such decision is somewhere the compiler and the normaliser can come")
    strs_push(l, "to disagree.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is deliberately excluded**, each checked against the implementation rather than")
    strs_push(l, "assumed: the target triple, CPU features and ABI (no rule in `crates/nazm-core/src/check/`")
    strs_push(l, "consults any of them, and `Int` is 64-bit in every configuration); the optimisation level")
    strs_push(l, "and backend (`nazm build`'s subset refusals live after checking); the interpreter's")
    strs_push(l, "iteration and depth budgets; the checkout directory and the working directory; the cache's")
    strs_push(l, "own location; and whether the compilation is a program, because `N0204` is a fact about a")
    strs_push(l, "compilation and is recomputed every run. The first row is right *today*, and a rule that")
    strs_push(l, "became target-sensitive would have to join the key on the day it was added.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Compiler identity: derived where it can be, declared where it cannot")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A result produced under one set of checking rules must not be reused by a compiler with")
    strs_push(l, "another. Nothing affordable computes \"do these two binaries check identically\" — a digest of")
    strs_push(l, "the compiler's source changes when a comment does, and a digest of the binary changes with")
    strs_push(l, "the optimisation level of the build that produced it. So `CheckerIdentity` derives the")
    strs_push(l, "built-in table with its signatures, the type set, both schemas and the crate version, and")
    strs_push(l, "names the rest as `SEMANTIC_EPOCH`, a counter bumped by hand.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The maintenance rule is one sentence — *bump the epoch in the commit that changes what the")
    strs_push(l, "checker accepts or refuses* — and it is made hard to forget rather than merely written down.")
    strs_push(l, "`cargo xtask check`'s **cache soundness** gate fails when the set of diagnostic codes")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-core`'s checker can raise stops matching the list the identity is built from, and")
    strs_push(l, "nearly every new rule brings a code. What it does not catch is a tightened rule reusing an")
    strs_push(l, "existing code, or a parser that starts accepting a construct the checker then sees; that is")
    strs_push(l, "what the epoch is for, and saying so is better than claiming an automatic identity this")
    strs_push(l, "does not have.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The algorithm, and why it needs no ordering")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "stage 1   every module's declarations, from source            → its UnitInterface")
    strs_push(l, "          an interface depends on that module alone,")
    strs_push(l, "          so every InterfaceHash exists at once — cycles included")
    strs_push(l, "stage 2   per module: CheckKey → look it up")
    strs_push(l, "          hit  → its bodies are not checked")
    strs_push(l, "          miss → check, and if it produced no diagnostic at all, publish")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "There is no scheduler and no dependency order, because there is nothing to order. The one")
    strs_push(l, "thing that would have needed one — a module's interface — was already local as of N2, which")
    strs_push(l, "is the property that makes an import cycle legal and the same property that makes this")
    strs_push(l, "work.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Invalidation, now implemented rather than described")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "B's private body changes  → B's SourceFingerprint moves → B re-checked")
    strs_push(l, "                          → B's InterfaceHash does not  → A's CheckKey holds → A reused")
    strs_push(l, "B's exported signature    → B's InterfaceHash moves     → A's CheckKey moves → A re-checked")
    strs_push(l, "                          → if A's own interface holds, A's importers are unaffected")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Propagation is interface-driven, not reachability-driven: it stops where a re-checked")
    strs_push(l, "module's interface turns out to be unchanged. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/incremental.rs` runs")
    strs_push(l, "all three cases of `A → B → C` and requires the middle one to stop at B.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The cache is never authority")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Source under this compiler decides what a program means; an entry is derived data.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "* **only a clean check is written.** A module with a diagnostic in either stage publishes")
    strs_push(l, "  nothing, so no entry is a cached refusal and no hit can suppress an error;")
    strs_push(l, "* **reading validates.** The file name is a digest, and a digest match is evidence rather")
    strs_push(l, "  than proof, so the entry repeats the inputs it was keyed on, the key is recomputed from")
    strs_push(l, "  them, and the interface is revalidated through the reader that owns that format. A")
    strs_push(l, "  truncated, edited, mis-filed or foreign entry is a **miss** — never a hit and never a")
    strs_push(l, "  compilation error;")
    strs_push(l, "* **publication is atomic.** Write, `fsync`, `rename`. An interrupted compiler leaves a")
    strs_push(l, "  `.part` file that nothing looks for;")
    strs_push(l, "* **entries are immutable**, because they are addressed by everything they depend on. Two")
    strs_push(l, "  compilers racing to publish one result compute the same bytes, so the second rename lands")
    strs_push(l, "  the same file and no lock is needed;")
    strs_push(l, "* **deleting the store changes nothing** but the work done.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Where it lives, and where it declines")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`.nazm/check/` under the source root, overridable with `NAZM_CACHE_DIR`. Beside the tree")
    strs_push(l, "because it is derived data about that tree: deleting the checkout deletes it, a second")
    strs_push(l, "checkout does not inherit it, and no compiler writes to a home directory. The location is")
    strs_push(l, "not part of any identity — the same entry computed anywhere is the same bytes under the")
    strs_push(l, "same name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Since R1.5 (D12, §7.113)* one kind of entry does live in the user's home directory: the native")
    strs_push(l, "objects of the runtime and of the standard library, which are the same for every project. A")
    strs_push(l, "project's own check results and objects are still kept here, and nothing else changed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A module with no durable identity — outside the source root, or given two names by a")
    strs_push(l, "symbolic link — is checked from source every time and publishes nothing. That is N3's")
    strs_push(l, "principle applied rather than re-decided: decline where the two implementations could")
    strs_push(l, "disagree, and never let a limit on an optimisation become a refusal to compile.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Lifecycle: there isn't one, and that is the design")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The store may be deleted at any moment, whole or in part, by anything. An entry nothing")
    strs_push(l, "asks for is never read, so a store full of results for source that no longer exists costs")
    strs_push(l, "disk and nothing else. **There is no pruning, no eviction, no size bound and no expiry**,")
    strs_push(l, "because each of those is a thing that deletes files, and a compiler that deletes files")
    strs_push(l, "under a directory a person chose needs a much better reason than tidiness. A size policy is")
    strs_push(l, "a later decision with its own argument; until then `rm -rf .nazm` is the whole interface,")
    strs_push(l, "and it is safe by construction.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The one file the compiler removes is the temporary it just failed to write. Nothing scans")
    strs_push(l, "the directory, nothing removes another process's leftovers, and nothing outside the store")
    strs_push(l, "is touched.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What the self-hosted compiler does with all this")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nothing, deliberately, as with N3. A cache is toolchain architecture: no Nazm program can")
    strs_push(l, "observe a `CheckKey`, the bootstrap chain neither reads nor writes an entry, and porting a")
    strs_push(l, "store into the Nazm-written compiler for symmetry would be building a second thing to keep")
    strs_push(l, "correct. What the two implementations must agree on is the language, and that is what")
    strs_push(l, "`bootstrap.md` measures.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.5 Separate code generation and internal linking — settled by N5, 2026-09-22")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N2 gave the language a compilation unit and N4 made checking per-unit. Emission stayed")
    strs_push(l, "whole-program: one LLVM module, functions named `@nz.f<N>` by their position in one")
    strs_push(l, "numbering. N5 makes generation per-unit too.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "checked compilation")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓ global backend admissibility")
    strs_push(l, "lower each module            → one Unit per Nazm module")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "emit each unit               → one LLVM module each, plus runtime and entry")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓ clang -c, once per artefact")
    strs_push(l, "objects")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓ linker")
    strs_push(l, "one executable")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### A symbol is a spelling of a definition's identity")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`@nz.f<N>` could not survive this: the number depends on how many functions were collected")
    strs_push(l, "before it, so a module's symbols would change when an unrelated module gained a function.")
    strs_push(l, "So a symbol is derived from the `DefKey` N3 already settled:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "DefKey (nazm-sema)   which definition is this — backend-independent")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "NativeSymbol (nazm-lir)   what the linker calls it")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Each part is encoded byte by byte: alphanumerics stand for themselves and everything else,")
    strs_push(l, "**including `_`, becomes `_XX`**. Because `_` is itself escaped it never appears literally,")
    strs_push(l, "so the encoding is injective and `.` is free to separate fields. A symbol is therefore")
    strs_push(l, "unique **by construction** — no digest, no truncation, no collision probability. That")
    strs_push(l, "guarantee is available because the inputs are small, and it is why this scheme is preferred")
    strs_push(l, "to hashing. *v1 (Q1-B-06):* the one input that is not always small is a generic instance's type")
    strs_push(l, "arguments, whose spelling nesting can make exponential; past 512 bytes an instance is named")
    strs_push(l, "`….d.<BLAKE3 hex>` instead of `….g.<spelling>`, unique by collision resistance, since `.` cannot")
    strs_push(l, "occur in a spelling and `d.` and `g.` therefore never meet.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "@nz.m.lib_2Futil_2Enz.parse       lib/util.nz :: parse")
    strs_push(l, "@nz.m.a_2Enz.helper               a.nz :: helper")
    strs_push(l, "@nz.m.b_2Enz.helper               and b.nz's, which is a different definition")
    strs_push(l, "@nz.u.2.helper                    a module with no durable identity: compilation-local")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The kind is deliberately absent, which is the opposite of what `DefKey` does and right for")
    strs_push(l, "the same reason: a durable identity that did not say what it identified would have to be")
    strs_push(l, "*reinterpreted* when a second kind arrived, while a native symbol is regenerated on every")
    strs_push(l, "build and read back by nothing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A body edit cannot rename a symbol**, because a body is not an input to one. That is what")
    strs_push(l, "makes a future native cache able to distinguish \"B changed\" from \"what A calls changed\".")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `pub` chooses linkage, never spelling")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Source-level `pub` says which **Nazm modules** may name a definition. It is not an ELF")
    strs_push(l, "export, not a C ABI, not a shared-library symbol and not a stability promise, and N5 must")
    strs_push(l, "not quietly turn it into one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Linkage | Why |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| a private definition | `internal` | nothing outside its module can name it, so nothing outside its object can refer to it — and LLVM may still inline, specialise and delete it |")
    strs_push(l, "| an exported definition | `hidden` | the linker must bind it; the finished image exports it anyway never |")
    strs_push(l, "| the root module's `main` | `hidden` | the entry wrapper is a separate artefact. The one place linkage does not follow visibility, and it is about where a process starts |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The symbol string is the same either way. `cargo xtask check`'s **native identity** gate")
    strs_push(l, "fails if visibility reaches the naming, if a session-local `FnId` reaches a symbol, if a")
    strs_push(l, "positional symbol returns, or if LLVM spelling reaches `nazm-sema`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What stays whole-program, and why that is not a defect")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Two analyses run once over the whole compilation, before any module is lowered:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "* **signature admissibility** — whether this backend can represent a function's types. A")
    strs_push(l, "  caller in another module has to know before it can emit the call;")
    strs_push(l, "* **the recursion refusal** — `A::f → B::g → A::f` is a cycle no single module can see.")
    strs_push(l, "  Per-module code generation is not a reason to stop looking for one, and weakening the")
    strs_push(l, "  policy to make lowering local would have traded a language rule for an implementation")
    strs_push(l, "  convenience.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Import cycles are unaffected and remain legal: a linker has no opinion about the order")
    strs_push(l, "objects were produced in, which is exactly why separate generation needs no topological")
    strs_push(l, "order. An import cycle and a call cycle are different things and only the second is refused.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Runtime ownership")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Every definition that must exist **exactly once per program** lives in one artefact: the")
    strs_push(l, "thread-local failure state, `@nz.fail`, `@nz.report`, and each helper set the program")
    strs_push(l, "reaches. Which sets those are is the union of what the modules reached — the one")
    strs_push(l, "whole-program fact emission needs, and the thing a future runtime-artefact cache would key")
    strs_push(l, "on.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The platform entry is a third kind of artefact. Nazm's `main` is an ordinary definition")
    strs_push(l, "with an ordinary symbol; `@main` is a C entry point with a C signature, in its own file.")
    strs_push(l, "Keeping them apart is what makes the separation between language identity and operating-")
    strs_push(l, "system identity visible rather than implied — and it is what stops an imported module's")
    strs_push(l, "`main` from ever becoming a process entry.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Constants needed no qualification at all. `private` linkage makes them local labels rather")
    strs_push(l, "than symbol-table entries, so two units may both number theirs `@.s0` with no collision;")
    strs_push(l, "that was established by linking two such objects rather than reasoned about. Declarations")
    strs_push(l, "go into **every** unit unconditionally: a `declare` costs nothing, emits no reference when")
    strs_push(l, "unused, and deciding per unit which are needed is a class of bug for no benefit.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What an object actually depends on — measured")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The question a native cache will have to answer, settled here with evidence rather than")
    strs_push(l, "carried forward as an assumption. `a.nz`'s artefact says exactly two things about `b.nz`:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "declare i64 @nz.m.b_2Enz.twice(i64)")
    strs_push(l, "%1 = call i64 @nz.m.b_2Enz.twice(i64 %0)")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| B changes | A's object |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| a body, exported or private | **byte-identical** |")
    strs_push(l, "| a private definition added or removed | **byte-identical** |")
    strs_push(l, "| an export A does not call, added | **byte-identical** |")
    strs_push(l, "| the signature of a definition A calls | changes — it is written into A's declaration |")
    strs_push(l, "| a rename, which is a new `DefKey` | changes |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "So A's object depends on B's **symbol identity and ABI signature** and on nothing else,")
    strs_push(l, "because there is no cross-module optimisation: each unit is assembled with no other unit's")
    strs_push(l, "IR in scope. N4's report assumed a dependent object would need its dependency's")
    strs_push(l, "implementation; on this architecture it does not, and a future `CodegenKey` for A may")
    strs_push(l, "therefore use B's interface rather than B's bodies.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**One thing does depend on bodies**: the recursion refusal, which is whole-program. A body")
    strs_push(l, "edit cannot change any object's contents and can change whether the program is admissible")
    strs_push(l, "at all.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What N5 is not")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Not a cache. Every module is regenerated on every build; there is no `CodegenKey`, no object")
    strs_push(l, "store and no reuse. `capability-matrix.md` says so, and the clean-build cost is measured in")
    strs_push(l, "`performance.md` rather than presented as a speed improvement — it is roughly twice as slow")
    strs_push(l, "for a small program, almost entirely because there are now several `clang` processes where")
    strs_push(l, "there was one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **Superseded in part by N6, 2026-09-22.** This section says \"a future native cache\" in")
    strs_push(l, "> three places; it exists, and §7.6 is it. The last paragraph above describes what was true")
    strs_push(l, "> only between N5 and N6.")
    strs_push(l, ">")
    strs_push(l, "> The measured dependency table is what N6 was built on and is unchanged. One sentence in")
    strs_push(l, "> it was written as a prediction and is worth correcting: a key for A's object does **not**")
    strs_push(l, "> use B's interface. It uses the bytes of A's own emitted unit, which already contain the")
    strs_push(l, "> part of B's interface that A depends on and nothing else — so the key needed no semantic")
    strs_push(l, "> input at all, which is less than this section expected.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.6 Native object reuse — settled by N6, 2026-09-22")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The claim, stated narrowly")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> If the exact LLVM text a unit would be compiled from, the configuration the object")
    strs_push(l, "> compiler resolves for the run, and the object compiler itself are all the ones a previous")
    strs_push(l, "> build recorded, the recorded object is linked instead of being compiled again.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Per-unit object reuse exists. **Incremental native compilation does not**, and the")
    strs_push(l, "difference is worth stating in the same breath: lowering and emission run on every build,")
    strs_push(l, "the final link runs on every build, there is no executable cache, no link-result cache and")
    strs_push(l, "no incremental linker. What is skipped is `clang -c`, which N5 measured as the expensive")
    strs_push(l, "part.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Keyed on the backend's input, not on a model of the front end")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The obvious design is a second dependency graph: this module's source fingerprint, each")
    strs_push(l, "dependency's exported signatures, an emitter epoch, the target. Every one of those is an")
    strs_push(l, "*approximation* of what the object compiler reads, and every approximation has the same")
    strs_push(l, "failure — something reaches the object that nobody remembered to add.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The emitted IR is not an approximation. It **is** the input. So")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "ObjectKey = BLAKE3(")
    strs_push(l, "    \"nazm.object-key/1\"")
    strs_push(l, "  ‖ LlvmInput       = BLAKE3(\"nazm.llvm-input/1\"      ‖ the exact bytes written for clang)")
    strs_push(l, "  ‖ BackendIdentity = BLAKE3(\"nazm.backend-tool/1\"    ‖ driver ‖ its own version report)")
    strs_push(l, "  ‖ CodegenConfig   = BLAKE3(\"nazm.codegen-config/1\"  ‖ the arguments the driver resolved)")
    strs_push(l, ")")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "with the same length-prefixed framing every digest in `nazm-cache` uses, so no field")
    strs_push(l, "boundary can move. N5's measured table then falls out rather than being encoded:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Edit | The caller's emitted unit | Its object |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| a dependency's body | unchanged | **reused** |")
    strs_push(l, "| an export it never calls | unchanged | **reused** |")
    strs_push(l, "| the signature of something it calls | the `declare` moves | recompiled |")
    strs_push(l, "| a comment that moves no emitted position | unchanged | **reused** |")
    strs_push(l, "| a comment above a fallible operation | the failure message's position moves | recompiled |")
    strs_push(l, "| the emitter, emitting the same text | unchanged | **reused** |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "None of those rows is a rule anywhere in the compiler.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What is deliberately not in the key")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Left out | Why it cannot affect the object |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `ModuleKey` | two units with identical IR are identical inputs. Module identity already reaches the IR as a native symbol; adding it again would only refuse valid reuse |")
    strs_push(l, "| a dependency's `InterfaceHash` | the part of an interface an object depends on is in its own `declare` lines. Including the whole thing would invalidate a caller when an export it never mentions changes — over-invalidation, and a mutation tests for it |")
    strs_push(l, "| the module's source fingerprint | an edit that does not reach the IR does not reach the object |")
    strs_push(l, "| the input path, the output path, the working directory | measured: identical object bytes under three spellings of the first two and from two directories for the third |")
    strs_push(l, "| the linker, its version, its options | a linker does not produce an object. That belongs to a `LinkKey`, which does not exist |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Asking the compiler what it is going to do")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm build` passes three arguments. The driver resolves about two hundred, and almost none")
    strs_push(l, "of the ones that decide the object are among the three: the triple with its deployment")
    strs_push(l, "version, `-target-cpu` and thirty `-target-feature` flags, the relocation model, the ABI,")
    strs_push(l, "the resource directory. A configuration built from what was *asked for* would leave every")
    strs_push(l, "one of them out, so two machines with one clang version and different processors would")
    strs_push(l, "share entries they must not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "So one `clang -###` per build reads what the compiler says it will actually run — the")
    strs_push(l, "version banner and the resolved command line — and only the arguments naming **this")
    strs_push(l, "invocation's own files** are removed from it: the job's directory, `-main-file-name`, `-o`,")
    strs_push(l, "the input and output paths, and the debug and coverage compilation directories. Each was")
    strs_push(l, "measured not to change a byte of the object. Everything else is kept, including arguments")
    strs_push(l, "this compiler has never heard of, because an argument wrongly kept costs a miss and an")
    strs_push(l, "argument wrongly removed is a wrong hit.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The identity is the report, not the executable.** Hashing the driver's own bytes was")
    strs_push(l, "considered and rejected with numbers: `/usr/bin/clang` on this machine is a 200 KB shim")
    strs_push(l, "with 78 hard links in front of a 124 MB executable, so it would identify the wrong file,")
    strs_push(l, "and reading and digesting the right one costs about 200 ms — more than the entire 158 ms")
    strs_push(l, "warm build it would be protecting. The stated limit is therefore that two builds of a")
    strs_push(l, "compiler reporting one version and behaving differently are indistinguishable, and that is")
    strs_push(l, "when `.nazm/native` should be deleted.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### A controlled environment rather than a hashed one")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Measured on 2026-09-22:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Variable | Effect on the object of a pure LLVM input |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `CCC_OVERRIDE_OPTIONS=+-O2` | an `-O0` invocation produced the `-O2` object, byte for byte |")
    strs_push(l, "| `SDKROOT` | moved `LC_BUILD_VERSION`'s `minos` from 27.0 to 27.2 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET` | moved it to whatever was asked for |")
    strs_push(l, "| the working directory | none |")
    strs_push(l, "| the input and output paths | none |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Hashing the environment would answer the first three with a set nobody can finish")
    strs_push(l, "enumerating and a key that moves when an unrelated variable does. The invocation is made")
    strs_push(l, "hermetic instead: the child's environment is built from nothing and ten named variables are")
    strs_push(l, "put into it — `PATH` and `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` so the driver can be found and started,")
    strs_push(l, "`TMPDIR` for a crash report, and `DEVELOPER_DIR`, `SDKROOT` and the deployment targets")
    strs_push(l, "because a platform build legitimately needs them. Everything passed through is still")
    strs_push(l, "covered, because the probe runs in the same environment as the compilations it describes:")
    strs_push(l, "a deployment target arrives in the key as `-triple arm64-apple-macosx12.0.0`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### A generated artefact names a module by its durable identity")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A preflight correction, and the thing that makes an object reusable between checkouts at")
    strs_push(l, "all. Two strings used to reach a native artefact as the path the command line spelled: the")
    strs_push(l, "`source_filename` and the location inside every runtime failure message. So")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "nazm build app.nz              lib/util.nz:3:5")
    strs_push(l, "nazm build /tmp/a/app.nz       /tmp/a/lib/util.nz:3:5")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "were two programs, byte for byte, differing in nothing a reader of the source could see.")
    strs_push(l, "They are named by the module's `ModuleKey` now — the same name the symbols carry and the")
    strs_push(l, "same name a check entry is filed under. A module with no durable identity keeps the name")
    strs_push(l, "the loader gave it, consistently with everything else about such a module.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The store")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`.nazm/` became a derived-data root with one subdirectory per kind: `check/` for")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.check/1`, `native/` for `nazm.object/1`. `NAZM_CACHE_DIR` moves the root rather than")
    strs_push(l, "one store.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An entry is **one file** — a line of JSON, a newline, then the object's exact bytes — so")
    strs_push(l, "there is no window in which a reader can see half of a two-file entry as complete. Six")
    strs_push(l, "things must hold before it is a hit: the header parses, its schema is known, every digest")
    strs_push(l, "is in canonical form, the inputs it records reproduce the key it is filed under, that key is")
    strs_push(l, "the one asked for, and the object's length and digest are the ones it claims. A file name is")
    strs_push(l, "how an entry is found and never why it is believed. Every failure is a miss.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Entries are immutable because the key covers every input, so two compilers racing on one key")
    strs_push(l, "both write and one rename lands second, with identical bytes either way. No lock, no index,")
    strs_push(l, "no sweep.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Why a warm store cannot skip anything it must not")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A key is a digest of an artefact. So the artefact must exist before the key does, which")
    strs_push(l, "means everything required to produce it has already run: the files were read, parsed and")
    strs_push(l, "checked; global backend admissibility ran; lowering ran; emission ran. The whole-program")
    strs_push(l, "recursion refusal is one of those, and a fully warm store is never reached before it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "That is not a rule this code follows. It is the shape of the pipeline, and it is why N6")
    strs_push(l, "needed no \"run the analyses first\" guard:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "checked compilation → admissibility → lower → emit → hash → look up → compile misses → link")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What still runs on every build")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Reading, parsing, checking, admissibility, lowering, emission, fingerprinting, the store")
    strs_push(l, "lookups, one `clang -###` and one link. `performance.md` measures which of those matter: on")
    strs_push(l, "the five-module compiler a warm build is 157.6 ms against 665.4 ms with the cache off, and")
    strs_push(l, "what remains is dominated by the two external processes — the probe and the link — plus")
    strs_push(l, "about 36 ms of `nazm`'s own startup.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What N6 is not")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "No executable cache, no `LinkKey`, no incremental linker, no persistent LIR or LLVM, no")
    strs_push(l, "remote or distributed cache, no LTO. The link runs every time and the report says so in a")
    strs_push(l, "field that is always `true`, because a report that omitted it would read as though something")
    strs_push(l, "had been saved there.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.7 Memory: what values mean, and when storage goes — settled by N7, 2026-09-22")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/spec.md`'s *memory constitution* is the law. This is the evidence it was derived")
    strs_push(l, "from, the implementation, and the parts that are deliberately not done.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **Two of those parts were done by N8, 2026-09-22.** *\"`Str` and `Chan` storage is not")
    strs_push(l, "> reclaimed\"* was true when this section was written and the paragraphs below give the")
    strs_push(l, "> reason it was. §7.8 is the answer to that reason and §7.9 is the shape it left the")
    strs_push(l, "> backend in; everything else here still stands, including the audit, the counts and the")
    strs_push(l, "> argument for a non-atomic count on a sequence.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The audit came first, and it moved the design twice")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Read out of the two implementations rather than out of the documentation:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Interpreter | Native | Aliasing observable | Crosses a task |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Int`, `Bool` | `i64`, `bool` | `i64`, `i1` | — | yes |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Str` | `Vec<u8>`, **deep-copied on every read** | `{ ptr, i64 }`, **bytes shared** | no — it is immutable | yes |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Ints`, `Strs` | `Arc<Mutex<Vec<…>>>` | pointer to a header | **yes** | no, `N0321` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Chan` | `Arc<Channel>` | pointer to a runtime header | yes | yes, by design |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The second row is the whole argument for the constitution's `Str` rule. The two")
    strs_push(l, "implementations have *always* disagreed about whether a `Str` is copied, and no test has")
    strs_push(l, "ever caught them, because the specification says the difference is unobservable. That is")
    strs_push(l, "not a bug to fix; it is the licence a shared-immutable value gives an implementation, and")
    strs_push(l, "it was already being used.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Two findings changed what the milestone could do:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A `Str` has four provenances and does not say which.** Its bytes may live in a `private`")
    strs_push(l, "constant (a literal), in the process's `argv`, in a `malloc`'d buffer — or *in the middle")
    strs_push(l, "of any of those*, because `str_slice` is specified not to allocate and is emitted as a")
    strs_push(l, "`getelementptr`. `free(s.ptr)` is therefore wrong for three of the four. Reclaiming `Str`")
    strs_push(l, "needs a representation that records its provenance, which is a change to the hottest type")
    strs_push(l, "in the language and is not this milestone.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The specification's `Str` value semantics are currently paid for with the leak.** A")
    strs_push(l, "`Str` read out of a `Strs` keeps its bytes after the sequence is overwritten — measured,")
    strs_push(l, "both implementations, `63` — and natively that is true only because nothing is ever freed.")
    strs_push(l, "Any scheme that reclaims `Str` has to buy that guarantee some other way.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What the real workload does, counted")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/*.nz`, 5,272 lines, 197 functions:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| parameters | `Ints` 108, `Str` 68, `Int` 68, `Strs` 60 |")
    strs_push(l, "| returns | `Int` 153, `Str` 28, `Bool` 15, **`Strs` 1**, `Ints` 0 |")
    strs_push(l, "| sequences created | 176 |")
    strs_push(l, "| **`let b = a;` aliasing a sequence** | **0** |")
    strs_push(l, "| sequence mutations | 746 — 588 through the binding that created it, 49 through a parameter |")
    strs_push(l, "| `scope`, `spawn`, `chan_*` actually used | **none**; every occurrence is a comment or a string in the code that compiles them |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A compiler that passes sequences in constantly, returns one exactly once, and aliases none")
    strs_push(l, "is the shape *borrowed parameters, transfer on return* was made for. It is also why the")
    strs_push(l, "reference counting below costs it nothing: the traffic is at bindings, and it has none.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The leak, before")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Workload | Live set | Peak RSS |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| 5,000 short-lived sequences | ~400 B | 4.38 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| 20,000 | ~400 B | 12.28 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| 80,000 | ~400 B | 43.52 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Linear in **work done**, constant in **live data**. Eleven allocation sites, **zero**")
    strs_push(l, "deallocation sites: `@free` appeared nowhere in the emitted runtime.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The models that were considered, and why this one")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Why not |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Unique ownership with explicit moves | 168 sequence parameters would each need a move or a borrow concept at the surface; the borrow is the common case, so this is the model below with ceremony added |")
    strs_push(l, "| Copy-on-write value semantics | `let b = a; ints_push(a, 1)` is specified to be visible through `b`, and measured to be. Changing it is a language break, and §4 of this milestone forbade doing that to make reclamation easier |")
    strs_push(l, "| Regions or arenas | The compiler already *is* one arena freed at exit — which is exactly why its peak is what it is. It answers nothing for a program that does not exit |")
    strs_push(l, "| A tracing collector | Excluded at constitution level, and unnecessary: see cycles |")
    strs_push(l, "| Reference counting on the handle | **Selected.** It matches the semantics the language already has, needs no annotation, and costs nothing where nothing is aliased |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The implementation")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The header grows from 24 bytes to 32: `{ i64 len, i64 cap, ptr data, i64 rc }`. Only")
    strs_push(l, "`malloc`'s size changed; every existing offset is where it was.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "@nz.arr_new      allocate, rc = 1          @nz.seq_new      that, and count it")
    strs_push(l, "@nz.arr_retain   rc += 1")
    strs_push(l, "@nz.arr_release  rc -= 1, free at zero     @nz.seq_release  that, and count the free")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not an atomic**, and that is a consequence rather than an optimisation: `N0321` refuses")
    strs_push(l, "to let a sequence cross into a task, so no two threads can hold one handle. The comment in")
    strs_push(l, "the runtime says what would have to change in the same commit if that rule were relaxed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The emitter tracks, per function, which SSA values hold a reference nobody has taken over.")
    strs_push(l, "`ints_new` and a call that returned a handle create one; reading a variable does not — that")
    strs_push(l, "is rule 2, and it is why passing a sequence emits no instruction at all. A binding takes")
    strs_push(l, "one over, a `return` carries one out, a discard releases one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Cleanup is on the exit edges, not at the closing brace.** There are exactly three ways")
    strs_push(l, "out of a generated function — the tail value, each `return`, and the shared `nz.unwind`")
    strs_push(l, "block every failure branches to — and all three release the frame. Handle slots are")
    strs_push(l, "initialised to null in `entry`, and releasing null is a no-op, so a path that never reached")
    strs_push(l, "a declaration needs no special case. Parameter slots are excluded, which *is* rule 2:")
    strs_push(l, "releasing a borrowed parameter would destroy storage the caller still holds.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A `phi` merging two branches that arrived at ownership differently —")
    strs_push(l, "`if c { ints_new() } else { xs }` — is normalised inside each branch, before its jump,")
    strs_push(l, "because after the `phi` there is no branch left to attribute a retain to.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The scope machinery's list of task ids uses the same allocator and is now released when")
    strs_push(l, "the scope is joined, on every way out. It is deliberately **not** counted: it is not a")
    strs_push(l, "value any program can name, and a report about a program's sequences that included one")
    strs_push(l, "would be answering a different question.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The interpreter models the rule rather than inheriting it")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`Arc` already reclaims at the right moment, and *\"the host does the right thing\"* is not")
    strs_push(l, "evidence. So sequence storage is wrapped in a type whose construction and `Drop` bump the")
    strs_push(l, "same two counters a compiled program reports, and every case in")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/memory.rs` asserts the two implementations produce the same value")
    strs_push(l, "**and** the same three numbers.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Measured")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Before | After |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| 5,000 short-lived sequences | 4.38 MiB | **1.78 MiB** |")
    strs_push(l, "| 20,000 | 12.28 MiB | **1.88 MiB** |")
    strs_push(l, "| 80,000 | 43.52 MiB | **1.86 MiB** |")
    strs_push(l, "| one 2,000,000-element sequence, genuinely live | 19.08 MiB | 19.08 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| string-heavy loop, no sequences | 23.77 MiB | 23.78 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| the self-hosted compiler on `emit.nz` | 46.81 MiB | 42.59 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Flat in work where it was linear, and unchanged where the memory is live or is a `Str` —")
    strs_push(l, "which is what a correct reclamation of exactly one kind of value should look like.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What this does not do")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **`Str` and `Chan` storage is not reclaimed** — *until N8, which is §7.8*. The reasons")
    strs_push(l, "  are above and were good ones; the answer to them is a wider value, not a cleverer guess.")
    strs_push(l, "- **`exit_with` reclaims nothing and reports nothing.** Found by measuring: the")
    strs_push(l, "  self-hosted compiler ends that way, so the entry wrapper is never reached. It is correct")
    strs_push(l, "  — a process that has ended returned everything — and there is a test so that nobody")
    strs_push(l, "  later spends real time on the largest workload here \"fixing\" it.")
    strs_push(l, "- **A failure still leaks the temporary it was holding.** A `Val::Transferred` on a guard's")
    strs_push(l, "  failing path cannot be followed by a release, and that path ends the program. Stated")
    strs_push(l, "  rather than papered over.")
    strs_push(l, "- No destructors, no RAII, no user-visible ordering.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.8 What owns a string's bytes — settled by N8, 2026-09-22")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "§7.7 stopped at `Ints` and `Strs` and named the obstacle exactly: **a `Str` has four")
    strs_push(l, "provenances and does not say which.** Its bytes may live in a `private` constant, in the")
    strs_push(l, "process's `argv`, in a `malloc`'d buffer — or *in the middle of any of those*, because")
    strs_push(l, "`str_slice` is specified not to allocate and is emitted as a `getelementptr`. Given")
    strs_push(l, "`{ pointer, length }`, `free(s.ptr)` is wrong in three cases out of four and there is no")
    strs_push(l, "sound way to tell them apart.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Every way of telling them apart *from the pointer* is a heuristic — a range test, a length")
    strs_push(l, "test, a rule about which built-in produced it — and every one of them is wrong on a")
    strs_push(l, "program somebody will write. So the value says.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The representation")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A `Str` is `{ pointer, length, owner }`, 24 bytes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Field | What it is |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `pointer` | the first byte of this **view**. Valid to read `length` bytes from |")
    strs_push(l, "| `length` | bytes, not characters. An embedded zero is data; nothing here is NUL-terminated |")
    strs_push(l, "| `owner` | the **allocation whose lifetime keeps `pointer` valid**, or null when nothing has to |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`owner` is not language-visible. No Nazm expression can read it, `docs/user/spec.md` still")
    strs_push(l, "specifies a `Str` as its bytes, and the type `nazm capabilities` reports is unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Every** expression that produces a `Str`, and what it owns. The four origins become")
    strs_push(l, "three answers and one of them is free:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Producer | Class | `owner` | What the expression holds |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| a literal | immortal | `null` | nothing — a retain is one comparison |")
    strs_push(l, "| `arg(i)` | external | `null` | nothing — the bytes are the operating system's |")
    strs_push(l, "| `str_concat`, `str_join`, `int_to_str`, `str_from_byte`, `read_file` | owned heap | the backing that call allocated | **one reference**, born with the allocation |")
    strs_push(l, "| `str_slice` | view | **the same owner as its source** | **one reference**, taken inside the built-in — see below |")
    strs_push(l, "| `strs_get` | view | the stored element's owner | **one reference**, taken inside the built-in |")
    strs_push(l, "| `strs_pop` | view | the stored element's owner | **one reference**, *transferred* — the sequence gives up its own, so nothing is retained and nothing released |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`str_slice` and `strs_get` take their reference **inside** the built-in rather than leaving")
    strs_push(l, "it to whoever binds the result, and the reason is the order. A built-in's arguments are")
    strs_push(l, "released as temporaries the moment it returns, so `str_slice(str_concat(a, b), 1, 2)` and")
    strs_push(l, "`strs_get(one(), 0)` would otherwise free the storage their own results point into before")
    strs_push(l, "anything could claim it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Null being a valid owner is what makes *immortal* and *external* cost nothing and need no")
    strs_push(l, "tag: they are simply strings that own nothing, and `@nz.str_retain(null)` is a branch.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A backing is `{ i64 rc, i64 length, bytes… }` and the view's `pointer` is `owner + 16` or")
    strs_push(l, "anywhere after it. **That separation is the whole idea**: the bytes a value names and the")
    strs_push(l, "allocation that protects them are different addresses, so a slice moves one and keeps the")
    strs_push(l, "other. `make()` below returns a value pointing into the middle of a buffer whose only")
    strs_push(l, "binding died on the way out, and it is ordinary:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn make() -> Str {")
    strs_push(l, "    let s = str_concat(\"ab\", \"cd\");")
    strs_push(l, "    str_slice(s, 1, 3)")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Why this count is atomic and a sequence's is not")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Neither is a judgement about how likely sharing is. Each follows from a rule the language")
    strs_push(l, "already had.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`N0321` refuses to let a sequence cross into a task, so no two threads can hold one handle,")
    strs_push(l, "so no two threads can touch one count: an ordinary `add`. A `Str` **may** cross, by")
    strs_push(l, "immutable sharing, and a task can slice what it was handed and bind the slice — so two")
    strs_push(l, "sibling tasks really do adjust one backing's count. Atomic, therefore, with the decrement")
    strs_push(l, "released and an acquiring fence before the free, which is the standard pairing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The same argument makes a channel's count atomic: a `Chan` exists to cross.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A consequence worth stating: if `N0321` were relaxed, the sequence count would have to")
    strs_push(l, "become atomic **in the same commit**, and `crates/nazm-lir/src/emit.rs` says so where the")
    strs_push(l, "count is written.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Containers own what they hold")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A `Strs` element is a 24-byte descriptor, and the sequence holds a reference to each")
    strs_push(l, "element's backing. That is four rules, and the order in two of them is the correctness:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `strs_push(xs, s)` | takes a reference of its own. The caller's `s` is untouched and still valid |")
    strs_push(l, "| `strs_get(xs, i)` | hands back a reference of its own. This is what makes *\"a `Str` already read out of a sequence is unaffected by changing the sequence\"* — promised since sequences existed — true by construction rather than true because nothing was freed |")
    strs_push(l, "| `strs_set(xs, i, s)` | takes the new reference **before** releasing the old, so replacing an element with a view of the same backing cannot drop the count to zero in between |")
    strs_push(l, "| a `Strs` dying | releases every element's backing, **then** the array, then the header. Freeing only the descriptors would turn a leaked string into a leaked string inside a sequence |")
    strs_push(l, "| `strs_pop(xs)` | **transfers**: the sequence gives up its reference and the expression takes that same one over. No retain, no release |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Channels: what permits destruction")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A channel header carries a count like everything else, and at zero its condition variable")
    strs_push(l, "and mutex are destroyed — `pthread_cond_destroy`, `pthread_mutex_destroy`, which release")
    strs_push(l, "what the platform allocated behind an opaque handle — and then its ring and header are")
    strs_push(l, "freed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Closing is not destroying.** `chan_close` changes what the channel does and touches no")
    strs_push(l, "storage; a closed channel with live references still answers, and still drains. The two")
    strs_push(l, "events are kept apart on purpose.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The safety argument is structural rather than hopeful. A reference is a binding holding the")
    strs_push(l, "handle, a value on its way out of a `return`, or the argument block of a task that has not")
    strs_push(l, "been joined. A thread blocked inside `chan_send` or `chan_recv` **reached it from a frame")
    strs_push(l, "that holds the handle** — a built-in borrows its argument and the caller keeps its reference")
    strs_push(l, "across the call — so a waiter implies a live reference, and therefore no reference implies")
    strs_push(l, "no waiter. That is why `rc == 0` is a sufficient condition and no second one is needed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The destroy results are not checked**, and that is a decision rather than an oversight.")
    strs_push(l, "`pthread_mutex_destroy` returns `EBUSY` for a mutex that is still locked or waited on, which")
    strs_push(l, "is exactly the state the argument above rules out — so a branch on it would be a path no")
    strs_push(l, "test can reach and no diagnostic can name, in a helper that has no source position to report")
    strs_push(l, "at. If the argument were ever wrong, refusing to free would convert a use-after-free into a")
    strs_push(l, "leak, which is the safer failure; the reason not to write it is that an unreachable")
    strs_push(l, "recovery path is itself a place for a defect to live.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What crosses into a task, and who holds it")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A `spawn` argument is **held for the task**, not borrowed from the statement that started")
    strs_push(l, "it: the reference is taken at the spawn site, on the thread that already has one, and given")
    strs_push(l, "back by the task's trampoline when the call returns — on both the succeeding and the failing")
    strs_push(l, "path, because they meet. Without that,")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "scope { spawn worker(s); s = other(); }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "releases the bytes the task is still reading, and the window is not theoretical: the scope's")
    strs_push(l, "body runs concurrently with the task by construction.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Four leaks that were nobody's feature")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Found by looking for `malloc` with no matching `free` rather than by a test failing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| a `spawn`'s argument block | one `malloc` per task, never freed. Freed at the join, after `pthread_join` and after its diagnostic has been read out |")
    strs_push(l, "| `@nz.cstr`'s terminated path copy | one per file operation, never freed. Freed once `fopen` has returned |")
    strs_push(l, "| a partly-built channel | four allocations, and a failure after the second left the first behind. One label per stage now, each freeing exactly what has been taken |")
    strs_push(l, "| a task that never started | its arguments and its block, on the one path where the program is already out of resources |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Two defects in N7's own instrument")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The counters were not atomic.** `@nz.seq_allocated` was an ordinary load-add-store, and a")
    strs_push(l, "*task* can create a sequence — `N0321` stops a handle crossing, not a task allocating — so a")
    strs_push(l, "concurrent program could under-report what it had allocated. A counter that is wrong in the")
    strs_push(l, "direction of \"less was allocated\" is the worst direction for a leak check.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The report was emitted only into programs that used a sequence.** A string-heavy program")
    strs_push(l, "printed nothing at all, which reads as *nothing to say* and meant *the instrument was not")
    strs_push(l, "built in*. Six counters and the report are unconditional now: six words of data, and every")
    strs_push(l, "program can be asked.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.9 One classification, and where cleanup goes — settled by N8, 2026-09-22")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N7 emitted cleanup for two types by testing `Ty::is_handle()` at each site. N8 makes four")
    strs_push(l, "types reclaimable, and repeating that test would have put `if type == Ints { … }` in seven")
    strs_push(l, "places across three files.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`Ty::owns()` answers, once, what a value of a type owns: nothing, a sequence of `Int`, a")
    strs_push(l, "sequence of `Str`, a string backing, or a channel. Every retain, every release, every frame")
    strs_push(l, "slot, every container and every task boundary dispatches on that one answer. Adding a type")
    strs_push(l, "to the language means answering it and nothing else.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "It is deliberately **not** a destructor system. Nazm has no user-defined destruction, no")
    strs_push(l, "ordering a program can observe, and nothing a program can write runs at reclamation. Each")
    strs_push(l, "variant names a runtime helper that already exists; none of them is a hook.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Cleanup is on the **exit edges** of a generated function, as in N7 and for the same reason:")
    strs_push(l, "the tail value, each `Stmt::Return`, and the shared `nz.unwind` block a failure takes.")
    strs_push(l, "Parameter slots are excluded, and that exclusion *is* rule 2 — a callee borrows, so")
    strs_push(l, "releasing a parameter would destroy storage its caller still holds. Every owning slot is")
    strs_push(l, "zeroed at entry, and a zeroed slot releases to nothing, so a path that never reached a")
    strs_push(l, "declaration costs one comparison.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The two compilers, held together by derivation")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/emit.nz` emits the same model. It did not, for a milestone: N7 taught the Rust")
    strs_push(l, "emitter to reclaim and the Nazm-written one went on emitting a header with no reference")
    strs_push(l, "count at all, and every behavioural test passed throughout — **a program that never frees")
    strs_push(l, "computes the same answers as one that does.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Two hand-kept transcriptions of a memory model is the arrangement that produced that, so")
    strs_push(l, "there is now one. Every line of the Nazm emitter's `runtime`, `task_runtime` and")
    strs_push(l, "`channel_runtime` is a line of `crates/nazm-runtime/src/core.rs`'s runtime constants (in `emit.rs` until N43, in `nazm-lir` until N53) with")
    strs_push(l, "`hidden` changed to `internal`, and `cargo xtask check`'s **`runtime parity`** gate performs")
    strs_push(l, "the derivation again and refuses a difference by line number.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What a textual gate cannot check is where each emitter *decides* to retain and release.")
    strs_push(l, "`the_nazm_written_compiler_emits_the_same_memory_semantics` is for that: eight programs")
    strs_push(l, "built by both compilers, run under `NAZM_MEMORY_REPORT`, required to print the same line —")
    strs_push(l, "and then required to print `live=0` in all three classes, because a report that matched")
    strs_push(l, "because both leaked would pass the first comparison and mean nothing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Where a binding hides a missing reference")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "One mutation survived the first run, and what it found is worth keeping. Removing")
    strs_push(l, "`strs_get`'s own reference to the string it hands back broke nothing: `let s = strs_get(xs,")
    strs_push(l, "0);` retains what it stores whether or not the built-in already did, and so does a `return`,")
    strs_push(l, "and so does storing it back into a sequence. Every shape in the suite had a binding standing")
    strs_push(l, "in for the missing reference.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The shape that has none is a sequence with **no binding** — `strs_get(one(), 0)`, where the")
    strs_push(l, "sequence is the result of a call. A built-in's arguments are released the moment it returns,")
    strs_push(l, "so the order decides it: with the reference taken inside the built-in, the retain precedes")
    strs_push(l, "the release; without it, the sequence and every string in it are freed first and the")
    strs_push(l, "binding's retain then touches storage that is gone.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The general lesson, and it applies to every rule in this section: **a compensating")
    strs_push(l, "mechanism makes a defect invisible without making it absent.** Reference counting is full of")
    strs_push(l, "them, because almost every value passes through a binding eventually. The test that finds")
    strs_push(l, "one has to be the shape where nothing else is holding the value.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What this still does not do")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Nothing about future types.** Leak freedom here is a claim about six built-in types —")
    strs_push(l, "  and, since N9, about records composed of them (§7.10) — and rests on the cycle argument")
    strs_push(l, "  in `docs/user/spec.md`: `Ints` holds `Int`, `Strs` holds `Str`,")
    strs_push(l, "  `Str` is a leaf, and a channel holds `Int`, so no value can refer to one that refers back.")
    strs_push(l, "  The first recursive user-defined type ends that, and the constitution says in advance what")
    strs_push(l, "  admitting one requires.")
    strs_push(l, "- **`exit_with` reclaims nothing and reports nothing.** Unchanged from §7.7, and correct: a")
    strs_push(l, "  process that has ended returned everything.")
    strs_push(l, "- **A failure still leaks the temporary it was holding** — *closed by N9; see §7.10*. A")
    strs_push(l, "  `Val::Transferred` on a guard's failing path still cannot be followed by a release, and")
    strs_push(l, "  that path ends the program. What N9 added is the release of everything the expression")
    strs_push(l, "  *was* holding when the failure left, which is the larger half of what this bullet meant.")
    strs_push(l, "- **No sanitizer result is claimed.** The language-level counters are the evidence here.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.10 Records: composition instead of cases — settled by N9, 2026-09-23")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N9 adds the first user-defined type. The question it exists to answer is not whether")
    strs_push(l, "records compile — it is whether the memory constitution N7 and N8 built can describe a type")
    strs_push(l, "whose ownership behaviour is **composed from arbitrary field types** rather than written")
    strs_push(l, "out in compiler branches.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The answer is in what did *not* change. `Owns` gained one variant, `Owns::Record`, and no")
    strs_push(l, "consumer gained a case: every retain, every release, every frame slot, every container and")
    strs_push(l, "every task boundary still dispatches on the one answer `Ty::owns()` gives. The four")
    strs_push(l, "properties a record has are all derived:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Derived as |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| needs cleanup | some field does, recursively |")
    strs_push(l, "| may cross into a task | every field may, recursively — and the failing path is reported |")
    strs_push(l, "| copy | retain each owning field, by that field's rule |")
    strs_push(l, "| destroy | release each owning field, by that field's rule |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A record adds no new **kind** of value. It is a composition of the four that existed, which")
    strs_push(l, "is also why `spec.md`'s cycle argument survives: a composition of leaves is a leaf, and a")
    strs_push(l, "containment cycle has no finite layout and is refused (`N0336`) before anything is lowered.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Semantic identity, and where a field's position is decided")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A record's durable identity is a `DefKey` with `DefKind::Record` — the second kind that")
    strs_push(l, "enum has ever had, and no key written before N9 changed meaning, which is what N3 designed")
    strs_push(l, "it for. `Type::Record(RecordId)` carries a session-local index and **not** a field list:")
    strs_push(l, "two records with identical fields are different types, so a type that held its shape would")
    strs_push(l, "compare equal where the language says unequal.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "§4 has required since before there was a backend that *field access remains symbolic until")
    strs_push(l, "the low-level layout boundary*. N9 is the first feature where that costs anything, and the")
    strs_push(l, "boundary is one function:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "checker          FieldRef { record, field }      a field's identity, as a declaration index")
    strs_push(l, "  ↓")
    strs_push(l, "nazm-lir::lower  RecordLayout::of_declaration    the only place a position is decided")
    strs_push(l, "  ↓")
    strs_push(l, "emitter          extractvalue %rec, <position>")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nothing above `lower` knows a position, and nothing anywhere knows a byte offset — the LLVM")
    strs_push(l, "struct is named and its offsets are the target's business. A future AoS/SoA pass changes")
    strs_push(l, "`record_layouts` and nothing else.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Why the layout is canonical by field name")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`spec.md` makes declaration order non-semantic: construction is named, and moving two field")
    strs_push(l, "declarations is not a change to the type. Laying fields out in **name order** makes that")
    strs_push(l, "true of the object file as well.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The alternative — declaration order — would have produced an ABI difference from an edit")
    strs_push(l, "the compiler itself calls meaningless: the fingerprint would not move, the semantic cache")
    strs_push(l, "would reuse, and the object would differ. A compiler and a linker disagreeing about whether")
    strs_push(l, "anything happened is the worst kind of disagreement, because each is right.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### A projection borrows when its base does")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Reading a field out of a record held in a **slot** takes no reference. The slot keeps the")
    strs_push(l, "field's storage alive, nothing in one expression can change it — assignment is a statement")
    strs_push(l, "— and rule 2 says a borrowed reference costs nothing. Reading one out of an owned")
    strs_push(l, "**temporary** must take a reference first, before the temporary is dropped; that ordering is")
    strs_push(l, "the whole of why `make().name` is valid.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Retaining unconditionally was the first implementation and it was wrong in a way only a")
    strs_push(l, "failure could show: `ints_get(h.values, 0)` took a reference, the built-in failed, and the")
    strs_push(l, "release that would have balanced it was on the path the program did not take.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### A failure now releases what it was holding")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "§7.9 listed, under *what this still does not do*: **\"A failure still leaks the temporary it")
    strs_push(l, "was holding.\"** N8 knew about it and left it; N9 closes it, because a record projection made")
    strs_push(l, "the shape ordinary enough to test.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The shared `nz.unwind` block releases the frame's **slots**, which is right for everything a")
    strs_push(l, "binding holds and says nothing about a value in a register.")
    strs_push(l, "`str_concat(str_concat(a, b), int_to_str(1 / z))` has the inner result in hand when the")
    strs_push(l, "division fails, and the call that would have consumed it is on a path control never takes.")
    strs_push(l, "Both emitters now release the outstanding set at each failure site — the only place that")
    strs_push(l, "knows it, because which temporaries are live is a property of the program point rather than")
    strs_push(l, "of the block they all eventually reach.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The first attempt was unsound and `clang` said so: *Instruction does not dominate all uses*.")
    strs_push(l, "A value created in a `then` block does not dominate the `else` block, so the set is scoped")
    strs_push(l, "to the branch that created it. The refusal came from an assembler rather than from a wrong")
    strs_push(l, "program, which is the failure mode this backend is built to have.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### A construction is assembled in a slot when it owns anything")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`Holder(name: int_to_str(1), n: 1 / z)` allocates a string and then fails. A value held only")
    strs_push(l, "in a register is not reachable from the frame's cleanup, so a construction with an owning")
    strs_push(l, "field is assembled into a hidden local instead. The \"which fields are initialised\"")
    strs_push(l, "bookkeeping is the **zeroed slot itself**: an unwritten field is null, releasing null is a")
    strs_push(l, "no-op in every release helper, and there is no separate flag to keep in agreement with the")
    strs_push(l, "value. A record whose fields own nothing gets no slot and pays for none of it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### One helper per record per direction")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A record released in forty places emits forty calls, not forty copies of its field walk —")
    strs_push(l, "and a nested record's helper calls the inner record's, which puts the recursion in the")
    strs_push(l, "**emitted program**, where there is a stack, rather than in the compiler. The self-hosted")
    strs_push(l, "emitter has no recursion at all, so this is not a convenience there; it is the mechanism.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### A premature free is not a counting error")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "One mutation survived the first run: releasing the old field **before** taking the new one.")
    strs_push(l, "Both orders end with the same two numbers, so the reclamation counters — the instrument")
    strs_push(l, "every other rule in §7.7–§7.9 is checked with — cannot see it. The existing")
    strs_push(l, "same-allocation case used `str_slice`, which takes its own reference inside the built-in")
    strs_push(l, "and so survived the wrong order by accident.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The shape that observes it is `h.name = h.name` — a projection out of a borrowed record,")
    strs_push(l, "which holds no reference of its own — followed by three hundred small allocations, so the")
    strs_push(l, "block the wrong order freed is handed back out. The program then stops with a signal rather")
    strs_push(l, "than returning a wrong answer.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "This is §7.9's lesson in a form that section did not cover. There, the compensating")
    strs_push(l, "mechanism was a binding. Here it was an allocator that had not yet reused the block, and")
    strs_push(l, "the general rule is the same: **the test that finds a defect has to be the shape where")
    strs_push(l, "nothing is compensating for it.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The self-hosted compiler")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/lex.nz`, `parse.nz`, `analyse.nz` and `emit.nz` all learned records: the keyword")
    strs_push(l, "and `.`, declarations and named construction and projection-path assignment, the record")
    strs_push(l, "table and its three declaration stages, and named LLVM aggregates with generated helpers.")
    strs_push(l, "There is **no divergence to record** — the reference and the Nazm-written compiler accept")
    strs_push(l, "and reject the same record language, and `compiler/conformance/records.nz` plus")
    strs_push(l, "`modules/exported-record` are checked by C2, C3 and the reference.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Two differences are inherited rather than introduced. The self-hosted emitter names a record")
    strs_push(l, "`%nz.t<index>` exactly as it names a function `@nz.f<index>`, which is sound because it")
    strs_push(l, "emits one module for a whole program and is the same limitation N5 removed for the reference")
    strs_push(l, "compiler and not for this one. And its `owns` answer for a record is a precomputed bit per")
    strs_push(l, "record rather than a walk, because a Nazm function cannot recurse.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "It also **uses** one. `Place { line, column }` in `compiler/emit.nz` replaced `line_of` and")
    strs_push(l, "`column_of`, which were two functions because a function returns one value: the first")
    strs_push(l, "scanned forward counting newlines, the second scanned backward looking for one, and every")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostic paid for both. A column falls out of the forward scan for nothing. That is the")
    strs_push(l, "whole of the dogfood evidence and it is deliberately one record — see")
    strs_push(l, "`research-register.md` R1 for why a wider migration would not have been honest.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What this still does not do")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **No variants, no generics, no traits, no methods, no pattern matching.** N9 is product")
    strs_push(l, "  types. Sum types are the next distinct semantic problem — §7.11 is where N10 answered it.")
    strs_push(l, "- **No layout promise.** A record's field offsets, size and calling convention are")
    strs_push(l, "  compiler-private. `pub` says which Nazm modules may name the type.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Nothing about a record inside a sequence.** `Ints` holds `Int` and `Strs` holds `Str`;")
    strs_push(l, "  there is no container that can hold a record, which is also why the cycle argument still")
    strs_push(l, "  holds. A generic container is what would end it.")
    strs_push(l, "- **No sanitizer result is claimed**, and the one defect class the counters cannot see —")
    strs_push(l, "  a premature free — is covered by exactly one test shape rather than by an instrument.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.11 Enums: a composition chosen at runtime — settled by N10, 2026-09-23")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N9 answered whether ownership can be *composed* from field types. N10 asks the next")
    strs_push(l, "question, and it is a different one: can that composition be **selected at runtime**? A")
    strs_push(l, "record owns every field it declares. An enum owns the fields of its active variant, and")
    strs_push(l, "which variant that is is a value the program carries.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The answer is again in what did not change. `Owns` gained one variant, `Owns::Enum`, and no")
    strs_push(l, "consumer gained a case. What changed is where the answer is computed:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Record | Enum |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| needs cleanup | some field does, recursively | some field of **some** variant does |")
    strs_push(l, "| may cross into a task | every field may | every field of **every** variant may |")
    strs_push(l, "| copy | retain each owning field | branch on the discriminant, then retain the **active** variant's |")
    strs_push(l, "| destroy | release each owning field | branch, then release the active variant's |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The first two rows are static questions about a type and are computed in the checker. The")
    strs_push(l, "last two are runtime questions about a value, and they are computed **in the emitted")
    strs_push(l, "program** — one generated helper per enum, a `switch`, and one call per site. That is the")
    strs_push(l, "whole difference, and it is why adding a sum type added no arm to either compiler's")
    strs_push(l, "dispatch.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### An enum adds no new kind of value either")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`spec.md`'s cycle argument holds for the same reason it held for records: an enum is a")
    strs_push(l, "choice between compositions of existing kinds, and a choice between leaves is a leaf. The")
    strs_push(l, "containment graph is now one graph over records and enums together — a record field may be")
    strs_push(l, "an enum and a payload may be a record — and a cycle anywhere in it is refused (`N0336`)")
    strs_push(l, "before anything is lowered. A walk that knew only about records would have run forever on")
    strs_push(l, "`struct A { b: B } enum B { V(a: A) }`, which is why `needs_cleanup`, `task_safety`,")
    strs_push(l, "`layout_cycle` and `depth` left `Records` for `UserTypes`. What they share is the graph;")
    strs_push(l, "what a record and an enum *do* with their fields is written out at each derivation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Semantic identity, and where a discriminant is decided")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An enum's durable identity is a `DefKey` with `DefKind::Enum` — the third kind, and the")
    strs_push(l, "second time a key written by an earlier build kept its meaning, which is what the field")
    strs_push(l, "exists for. A **variant** has no key of its own: `spec.md` makes its durable meaning the")
    strs_push(l, "enum's identity and its name, and no persistent consumer has needed a composed one, so none")
    strs_push(l, "was invented.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "In one session a variant is a `VariantRef { enumeration, variant }` and a payload field a")
    strs_push(l, "`PayloadRef { enumeration, variant, field }`, both naming **declaration indices**. Nothing")
    strs_push(l, "above the backend knows a discriminant, and nothing anywhere knows a byte offset.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-lir::lower`'s `enum_layouts` is the only place a tag is decided, from the canonical")
    strs_push(l, "variant-name order, exactly as `RecordLayout::of_declaration` is the only place a field")
    strs_push(l, "position is decided.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Why the tag is canonical by variant name")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The same argument the field order rests on. `spec.md` makes variant declaration order")
    strs_push(l, "non-semantic, so deriving the discriminant from the **names** makes that true of the object")
    strs_push(l, "file as well: moving two variant declarations changes no byte. Taking the parser's order")
    strs_push(l, "because it was there would have created an ABI difference from an edit with no meaning —")
    strs_push(l, "the compiler right that nothing changed, and the linker disagreeing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The representation, and what it costs")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`{ i64, %V0, %V1, … }`: a discriminant followed by **one slot per variant**, in canonical")
    strs_push(l, "order, each slot that variant's payload struct. A value is built from `zeroinitializer` and")
    strs_push(l, "the active slot filled, so every byte is defined and copying the aggregate is defined; the")
    strs_push(l, "inactive slots hold zeros, which no operation reads.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "This is larger than the union it stands for — an enum of three `Str` payloads is")
    strs_push(l, "8 + 24 × 3 bytes where an ideal tagged union is 8 + 24 — and `performance.md` measures it.")
    strs_push(l, "It was chosen over a sized payload area with typed loads and stores through it for two")
    strs_push(l, "reasons. That form needs the compiler to compute each variant's size exactly right, and an")
    strs_push(l, "arithmetic mistake there is a buffer overflow rather than a compile error. And this form")
    strs_push(l, "needs no memory at all: a variant is built with `insertvalue` and a payload read with")
    strs_push(l, "`extractvalue`, entirely in registers. `spec.md` promises nothing about an enum's size or")
    strs_push(l, "layout, so the representation can change without the language moving.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The discriminant is written first, and that was a defect")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A variant that owns something is assembled in a hidden local, for the reason a record is: an")
    strs_push(l, "initialiser that fails after an earlier one produced a heap string must not leak it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The first implementation wrote the discriminant **last**, on the reasonable-sounding theory")
    strs_push(l, "that a partially built value should not claim a variant. It is the other way round. Cleanup")
    strs_push(l, "finds the fields to release by dispatching on the tag, so a tag written last leaves the slot")
    strs_push(l, "saying *variant 0* while variant 3's payload is the one being filled — and a failure")
    strs_push(l, "releases variant 0's fields, finds null in each, does nothing, and leaks everything the")
    strs_push(l, "initialisers produced. On the one path the program was already failing on.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Both emitters now zero the slot, write the tag, and then fill the payload. Cleanup at any")
    strs_push(l, "point in between dispatches on a **valid** tag and releases exactly the fields that exist:")
    strs_push(l, "the ones already stored, properly, and the ones not yet stored as null. The zeroed payload")
    strs_push(l, "*is* the \"which fields are initialised\" bookkeeping, exactly as it is for a record.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Writing the emitter a second time is what found it.** The Nazm-written backend was being")
    strs_push(l, "written against the same design, and the question \"which variant does the frame think this")
    strs_push(l, "is\" only has to be asked once for the answer to be obviously wrong. `memory.rs` carries the")
    strs_push(l, "shape that observes it, with the owning variant deliberately **not** tag 0 — with the")
    strs_push(l, "variants the other way round the defect is invisible.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `match` is `if` with N arms, plus one thing")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The block structure is `conditional`'s: a `switch` on the discriminant, one block per arm,")
    strs_push(l, "a `phi` at the join, and each arm brought to the same ownership state **inside its own")
    strs_push(l, "block and before its jump** — the only place a retain can go, because after the `phi` there")
    strs_push(l, "is no arm left to attribute it to.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The one addition is that the value being matched lives in a hidden slot the frame releases.")
    strs_push(l, "That is what makes a failure inside any arm give it back by the ordinary path, and what lets")
    strs_push(l, "each arm read its payload out of something that dominates it. The release happens **after**")
    strs_push(l, "the `phi`, which is the ordering the whole milestone turns on: every arm has already taken")
    strs_push(l, "its own reference to whatever it hands to the join, so a payload returned from an arm holds")
    strs_push(l, "one by the time the value it came out of is let go.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A pattern binding lowers to an ordinary `Stmt::Let` over an `Expr::Payload`. Not a")
    strs_push(l, "convenience: a binding *is* a local that takes a reference to what it names, and `Stmt::Let`")
    strs_push(l, "is the one path that already gets take-before-release right when the same slot is reached")
    strs_push(l, "again on the next turn of a loop.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The switch's default")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Checking establishes that every variant has exactly one arm, so the default is unreachable")
    strs_push(l, "for any value a safe program can build. It is written as a branch to the first arm rather")
    strs_push(l, "than as `unreachable`: the block has to exist for the instruction to be well formed, and a")
    strs_push(l, "`switch` whose default is poison would turn a compiler mistake into undefined behaviour")
    strs_push(l, "instead of a wrong answer. `spec.md` is explicit that no runtime trap stands in for the")
    strs_push(l, "checker's coverage.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The self-hosted compiler")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The Nazm-written compiler implements the same language, and its data model is one flag on")
    strs_push(l, "the table N9 already had: **an enum is a record whose fields are its variants, and a variant")
    strs_push(l, "is a record whose fields are its payload.** `rkind` says which of the three an entry is.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "That is not a trick to save an array. Every derivation N9 wrote over records is the one N10")
    strs_push(l, "needs over enums — *needs cleanup* is some field of some variant, which is the same walk; a")
    strs_push(l, "containment cycle through a variant is the same cycle; and the task-safety path comes out as")
    strs_push(l, "`work.Values.items`, naming the variant on the way, because a variant genuinely is a step in")
    strs_push(l, "that path. What differs is how a value is built and eliminated, and those are written out at")
    strs_push(l, "those two places.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Its parser needed one new decision and one new mark: `IDENT . IDENT (` is a variant rather")
    strs_push(l, "than a projection, and a `match` suspends its scrutinee at the `{` exactly as an `if`")
    strs_push(l, "suspends its condition, after which each arm's body is an ordinary pending expression — so")
    strs_push(l, "an `if` inside an arm needs no machinery of its own. Its emitter carries two bits where it")
    strs_push(l, "had one: `rowns` says *2* for an enum and *1* for a record, so every site that already asked")
    strs_push(l, "`owns` keeps asking exactly that, and an enum's helper switches on the tag and then calls the")
    strs_push(l, "**variant's** helper — which is a record's, because a payload is record-shaped.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Parity is compared on **codes rather than spans**. The self-hosted parser records one span")
    strs_push(l, "per arm, so a diagnostic about a payload field inside a pattern points at the arm where the")
    strs_push(l, "reference points at the field. Where each compiler points is not what N2.1 is about; what")
    strs_push(l, "each decides is.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "#### And it uses one")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`enum Owning { Nothing, Sequence, Strings, Backing, Channel, Record(at: Int), Enum(at: Int) }`")
    strs_push(l, "in `compiler/emit.nz`. It was a small integer — `0` nothing, `3` a string backing, `5` a")
    strs_push(l, "record — that every caller compared against a number, and the two cases carrying an index")
    strs_push(l, "recomputed it from the type at each site. N10 added a seventh and every one of those")
    strs_push(l, "comparisons had to be found by hand.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "As an enum the dispatch is exhaustive, so adding a kind stops the retain and release paths")
    strs_push(l, "compiling until both have answered; and the index a record or an enum needs travels **in")
    strs_push(l, "the value that says it needs one**, so the two cannot disagree. The sites that only want")
    strs_push(l, "*does this own anything* go through one `owns_anything`, which is the same `match` answered")
    strs_push(l, "once rather than at each of them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "It is one enum rather than a migration, and the reason is the same one N9 gave for one")
    strs_push(l, "record: the compiler's node kinds, token kinds and type codes are integers stored in `Ints`,")
    strs_push(l, "and there is no container that can hold an enum. `Owning` is the case where the value is")
    strs_push(l, "returned and never stored, which is exactly the case a container is not needed for.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "#### A record crossing a task boundary, which N9 got wrong")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Making that `match` exhaustive found a defect, and it was N9's rather than N10's. The")
    strs_push(l, "self-hosted emitter's trampoline released four kinds of value and not a record's. Worse, the")
    strs_push(l, "argument block's offsets were arithmetic — twenty-four bytes for a `Str` and eight for")
    strs_push(l, "everything else, which was true of every type the language had when it was written. A record")
    strs_push(l, "is neither: `struct M { text: Str }` is twenty-four bytes and was given eight, so the store")
    strs_push(l, "ran past its slot and the task read the next argument's bytes as its own.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "So a record passed to a task produced a **wrong answer** and leaked its fields, in the")
    strs_push(l, "self-hosted compiler only, since N9. The block is a named LLVM type now — `{ i64 handle,")
    strs_push(l, "ptr message, i64 length, … arguments }`, which is what the reference emitter always had —")
    strs_push(l, "so LLVM computes the offsets and the arithmetic that could not survive a new type is gone.")
    strs_push(l, "`the_nazm_written_compiler_emits_the_same_memory_semantics` carries the case.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Two things this says. The first is that the reference emitter was right and the second")
    strs_push(l, "implementation was the one that drifted, which is the usual direction and the reason the")
    strs_push(l, "differential test exists. The second is that N9's evidence did not reach it: records crossed")
    strs_push(l, "module boundaries, were returned on both edges and were copied in loops, and **no test")
    strs_push(l, "passed one to a task through the self-hosted compiler.** The gap was in the corpus, not in")
    strs_push(l, "the design.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Leaving an expression that never finishes, which was wrong in four places")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The surviving mutation of the milestone is the one worth writing down, because what it")
    strs_push(l, "found was not the defect it described.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`a-variant-slot-keeps-what-the-last-round-left-in-it` removes the store that zeroes a")
    strs_push(l, "variant's assembly slot before the value is built, and the suite still passed. Working out")
    strs_push(l, "*why* it passed is what found three real defects — and then showed that the mutation itself")
    strs_push(l, "had become inert, because the slot is zero on every path that reaches it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The real rule is **4a** in `spec.md`, and it was satisfied on one of four paths. A")
    strs_push(l, "half-evaluated expression holds things: arguments already produced, fields already stored")
    strs_push(l, "into a record's or a variant's slot, and the value a `match` is holding while an arm runs.")
    strs_push(l, "There are four ways to leave it part way through, and only the first gave any of them back:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Leaving by | Register temporaries | The frame's slots |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| a failure | released — N9, `release_temporaries` | released — the shared unwind block |")
    strs_push(l, "| `return` | **leaked** | released — `release_frame` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `break` | **leaked** | **leaked**, because the next turn stores over the slot |")
    strs_push(l, "| `continue` | **leaked** | **leaked**, the same way |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Three shapes, all of them expressible since N8 and none of them in the corpus:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "while i < 3 { i = i + 1;")
    strs_push(l, "    let v = pick(int_to_str(i), if i == 1 { continue; } else { i });   // the argument")
    strs_push(l, "    let r = R(a: int_to_str(i), b: if i == 1 { continue; } else { i }); // the record")
    strs_push(l, "    total = total + match E.Text(value: int_to_str(i)) {                // the scrutinee")
    strs_push(l, "        E.Absent() => 0,")
    strs_push(l, "        E.Text(value: s) => if i == 1 { continue; } else { str_len(s) },")
    strs_push(l, "    };")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Each leaked one string per abandoned round, in **both** backends and in the compiler")
    strs_push(l, "written in Nazm, since N8. The interpreter was right in every one of them, which is the")
    strs_push(l, "usual direction and why `memory.rs` runs the same program through both.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The fix is the one N9 already wrote for failures, on the other three paths. `transfer`")
    strs_push(l, "releases the temporaries this loop produced and the slots it is part way through filling;")
    strs_push(l, "`Stmt::Return` releases the temporaries, because the slots are the frame's and it is about")
    strs_push(l, "to release those anyway. Two depths make it exact rather than approximate — `Targets`")
    strs_push(l, "records how many temporaries were outstanding and how many slots were in flight when the")
    strs_push(l, "loop started, the same distinction `scope_depth` already drew for tasks. Releasing more")
    strs_push(l, "than that is not a leak but a **premature free**: a string produced before the loop and")
    strs_push(l, "read after it is still wanted. That one is invisible to the counters for the same reason")
    strs_push(l, "§7.10's survivor was — the premature release frees, and the ordinary release afterwards")
    strs_push(l, "finds freed memory and counts nothing, so both numbers come out equal — so")
    strs_push(l, "`a_transfer_gives_back_only_what_the_loop_it_leaves_was_holding` reads the string's")
    strs_push(l, "**bytes** after thirty allocations have had every chance to reuse them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The Nazm-written emitter needed the same fix and a smaller version of it: a post-order")
    strs_push(l, "stack machine has no half-filled construction slot — the initialisers are complete before")
    strs_push(l, "the node is reached — so only the temporaries and the `match` slots are at stake there.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Two things this says, and they are the same two N9's task-block defect said. The first is")
    strs_push(l, "that the rule was right and the implementation satisfied it on the path a test happened to")
    strs_push(l, "take. The second is that **a mutation that survives is a question, not a verdict**: this")
    strs_push(l, "one was answered by three defects and a fourth finding, that the mutation no longer")
    strs_push(l, "describes a defect at all, and it was replaced by four that do.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### A transfer in a value position, in the compiler written in Nazm — N10.1")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The paragraph above says the Nazm-written emitter needed only a smaller fix. That was true of")
    strs_push(l, "what the transfer *gives back* and said nothing about what it *produces*, and the shape the")
    strs_push(l, "table above opens with did not compile at all:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "let v = pick(int_to_str(i), if i == 1 { continue; } else { i });")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The reference represents completion once, as a type: the checker's `Completion { Value(T),")
    strs_push(l, "Unit, Diverges }` and the emitter's `Val { Of { value, ty }, Transferred }`, and nothing")
    strs_push(l, "consumes an operand without matching on it. The compiler written in Nazm had neither half.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **The checker** kept one integer per node, and `unknown` meant three things — a statement,")
    strs_push(l, "  an error already reported, and a branch that leaves. A two-branch `if` took its")
    strs_push(l, "  then-branch's type, so the `if` above had *no value*. The call's argument list was then")
    strs_push(l, "  built from that type, and `llvm_type(unknown)` is `\"void\"`: `call i64 @nz.f0({ ptr, i64,")
    strs_push(l, "  ptr } %19, void %24)`, which clang refuses. Records and variants took their field types")
    strs_push(l, "  from the declaration instead, so the same shape there compiled — correctly, by accident,")
    strs_push(l, "  because the else-branch's value happened to be left on the stack exactly where the")
    strs_push(l, "  constructor looked.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The emitter** is a post-order scan, and it opened every join whether or not a branch")
    strs_push(l, "  reached it. A construct whose branches all left therefore handed its parent an empty")
    strs_push(l, "  stack, and the parent popped a value somebody else had pushed: `N0405` inside the")
    strs_push(l, "  compiler, or a real value in the wrong operand.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The repair is one bit per node in each half. `ndiv` in `compiler/analyse.nz` records that a")
    strs_push(l, "node **never completes** — the reference's `Diverges`, kept beside the type rather than in")
    strs_push(l, "it, because a type code is also what a slot and an operand are given. An `if` or a `match`")
    strs_push(l, "is typed by the branches that complete; a value position with no expectation of its own")
    strs_push(l, "sees a diverging value as `Int`, which is the reference's `value_type(e, None)`; and what")
    strs_push(l, "follows a child that leaves is refused as `N0313`, which this checker had never reported.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "In the emitter, **whether the block being written is live is the one answer**, and it is")
    strs_push(l, "asked in one place, `unreachable_here`. A node reached while it is not was never evaluated,")
    strs_push(l, "so nothing is emitted for it — no call with an argument missing, no store of a value nobody")
    strs_push(l, "produced, no arithmetic on half its operands — and what its operands left on the stack is")
    strs_push(l, "discarded down to the depth recorded where its subtree began, because the transfer already")
    strs_push(l, "gave back what they held. Nothing reopens a block except a construct whose dispatch really")
    strs_push(l, "was emitted (`opened`), and a join is opened only if some branch reached it (`joined`). A")
    strs_push(l, "`phi` is built from the incomings that arrived (`nin`, and `emit_phi` shared by `if` and")
    strs_push(l, "`match`), so a branch that transferred contributes nothing rather than a stand-in.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Two things were found by the audit that followed, and both are transfer rules the reference")
    strs_push(l, "had and this compiler did not. **A `break`, a `continue` or a `return` out of a `scope` did")
    strs_push(l, "not join it**, since N7: a task that failed inside a scope a `break` left was never waited")
    strs_push(l, "for, so the program printed a value where the reference stopped with the task's diagnostic.")
    strs_push(l, "`join_from` is the reference's `join_through`, and `unwind` uses it too. And **`==` on two")
    strs_push(l, "strings kept its operands**, in both native backends and with no transfer involved: a")
    strs_push(l, "temporary compared was never reclaimed. Rule 2 says a comparison borrows, as a call does.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Why not the enum N10 made available.** `enum EmitCompletion { Value(value: Int, ty: Int),")
    strs_push(l, "Transferred }` is the shape the reference has, and it does not fit here for the reason N10G")
    strs_push(l, "gave: the emitter's operand stack is an `Ints`, and no container can hold an enum. A")
    strs_push(l, "post-order scan also never has a completion *in hand* to return — the node that would return")
    strs_push(l, "it is not the node that consumes it. The live flag is the same fact stated at the only place")
    strs_push(l, "this design can ask it, and there is one of it rather than one per consumer.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### No value, as a third completion — N10.2")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N10.1's bit said *never completes* and left *completes with no value* inside the type code,")
    strs_push(l, "as `unknown` — which also meant \"already reported\". N10.2 replaced the bit with the")
    strs_push(l, "reference's three states: `ncomp` in `compiler/analyse.nz` holds `c_value`, `c_unit` or")
    strs_push(l, "`c_diverges` for every node, and nothing reconstructs one from another or from the type.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Node | Completion |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `break`, `continue`, `return` | `Diverges` |")
    strs_push(l, "| an expression statement | its expression's, if that diverges; otherwise `Unit` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `let`, assignment, `while`, `scope`, `spawn` | `Unit` |")
    strs_push(l, "| a block | `Diverges` if a statement is still leaving when the statements end (a tail after it is `N0313`); otherwise its tail's; with no tail, `Unit` |")
    strs_push(l, "| an `if` with no `else` | `Unit`, whatever its branch does: the condition may be false |")
    strs_push(l, "| an `if` with one | the join below |")
    strs_push(l, "| a `match` | its arms folded: one that leaves defers, one with no value makes the whole `Unit` |")
    strs_push(l, "| every other expression | `Value` |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The `if` join is the reference's, in the reference's order — the order is the rule, because")
    strs_push(l, "the first line decides the `Unit` and `Diverges` pairs:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| then | else | result | diagnostic |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Diverges` | anything | the else branch's completion and type | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| anything | `Diverges` | the then branch's | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Value(A)` | `Value(A)` | `Value(A)` | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Value(A)` | `Value(B)` | `Value(A)` | `N0302` at the else branch's value |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Value(A)` | `Unit`, or the reverse | `Value(A)` | `N0302` at the whole `if` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Unit` | `Unit` | `Unit` | — |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An expected outer type changes none of it: the reference passes one into the branches for")
    strs_push(l, "recovery only, so `f(if c { 1 } else { \"x\" })` is `N0302` whatever `f` takes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**`N0300` is decided in one place.** `value_child` says which children of a node must")
    strs_push(l, "produce a value — every operand, argument and initialiser, the value of a `let`, an")
    strs_push(l, "assignment and a `return`, and the condition of an `if` and a `while`; the scrutinee asks")
    strs_push(l, "the same question where it is finished — and `needs_value` refuses a `Unit` there at the")
    strs_push(l, "child's span, before the node's own rule reads the child's type. `Diverges` is not refused:")
    strs_push(l, "it never produces the contradictory value. After the report the value is read as the")
    strs_push(l, "reference reads it, `expected.unwrap_or(Int)`, so the consequences the reference reports —")
    strs_push(l, "`N0304` for a comparison with a `Str`, `N0342` for a scrutinee — are reported here too, and")
    strs_push(l, "the ones it does not are not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Two checks the Nazm checker had never made came with it: a body is held to its signature")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0300` at the tail, or at the body when it produces nothing) and so is each `return`.")
    strs_push(l, "And a `match` whose scrutinee is not an enum discards what its arms reported, because the")
    strs_push(l, "reference returns after `N0342` without checking them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The emitter changed in one place**, as a consequence. A `match` statement whose arms are a")
    strs_push(l, "value and nothing is `Unit` — the reference accepts it — so the value arm's value has no")
    strs_push(l, "`phi` to go to. `discard_branch_value` drops it inside the arm's own block and releases it if")
    strs_push(l, "it was a temporary, which is what an expression statement does with a value. Before N10.2")
    strs_push(l, "that `match` had its value arm's type and never reached this question; it reached a")
    strs_push(l, "different one, the emitter's stack.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What this still does not do")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **No generics** — *superseded by N11, §7.12*: a generic enum is expressible now, and")
    strs_push(l, "  `Option` and `Result` are still not built in — *and since N12, §7.13, they are ordinary")
    strs_push(l, "  enums of the core prelude rather than built into the checker*.")
    strs_push(l, "- **No wildcard arm**, no guards, no or-patterns, no literal or record patterns, no `let`")
    strs_push(l, "  destructuring. N10 is variant selection with named payload bindings.")
    strs_push(l, "- **No space promise.** The representation is one slot per variant, which is larger than a")
    strs_push(l, "  union; `performance.md` says by how much, and nothing here claims otherwise.")
    strs_push(l, "- **No stable ABI.** Discriminant values, payload layout, size and calling convention are")
    strs_push(l, "  compiler-private and may change between builds.")
    strs_push(l, "- **A bare block is still not an expression in the self-hosted parser**, so an arm body")
    strs_push(l, "  there may be `n + 1` but not `{ let n = …; n }`. That limitation is N2's and is unchanged;")
    strs_push(l, "  N10 only made it reachable in one more position — *closed by N12.1, §7.14, in both")
    strs_push(l, "  compilers*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.12 Generics: parametric checking, concrete code — settled by N11, 2026-09-23")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N9 asked whether ownership composes from field types, and N10 whether that composition can")
    strs_push(l, "be chosen at runtime. N11 asks whether it survives **substitution**: whether a definition")
    strs_push(l, "checked once, with its parameters unknown, can be given concrete types later without any")
    strs_push(l, "law in §7.7–§7.11 learning that it happened. `docs/user/spec.md`, *Generics*, is the language;")
    strs_push(l, "this section is how both compilers implement it and why.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The type representation")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`Type` stays one small `Copy` value. It gained two variants, and nothing else:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Type::Param(TypeParam { owner, index })` | a type parameter: its owner — `Function(FnId)`, `Record(RecordId)`, `Enum(EnumId)` or `Builtin(Intrinsic)` — and its **position** in the owner's list |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Type::Vec(VecId)` | `Vec[T]`, an interned element type |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An **applied** record or enum — `Pair[Int, Str]` — is not a new variant. It is an entry of")
    strs_push(l, "the record or enum table of its own, whose `instance` is `Some(Instance { template, args })`")
    strs_push(l, "and whose fields are the definition's with the parameters substituted, done once, when the")
    strs_push(l, "application is interned (`crates/nazm-sema/src/generic.rs`). So `Type::Record(id)` still")
    strs_push(l, "names one entry with concrete fields, and every consumer that reads fields — copy and")
    strs_push(l, "cleanup derivation, task safety, layout, construction, projection, the emitters' helpers —")
    strs_push(l, "was written, tested and mutation-tested against exactly that, and did not change. This is")
    strs_push(l, "the decision the milestone turned on: a new `Type::Applied` would have given every one of")
    strs_push(l, "those consumers a case to get wrong.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Interning is what keeps `==` the language's type equality.** One definition applied to one")
    strs_push(l, "argument list is one entry — `apply_record`/`apply_enum` look it up before creating it — so")
    strs_push(l, "two modules writing `Pair[Int, Str]` for the same `Pair` get the same `Type`, and")
    strs_push(l, "`a.nz::Box[Int]` and `b.nz::Box[Int]` do not, because their templates differ. Nothing")
    strs_push(l, "compares shapes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Completion is deferred and iterative.** A field may name a generic type declared later or")
    strs_push(l, "in another module, which has no fields yet while stage 0b is resolving them. So an")
    strs_push(l, "application is interned at once and **completed** later, from a worklist, when")
    strs_push(l, "`UserTypes::settle` runs; completing substitutes, which may intern more, which join the same")
    strs_push(l, "worklist. No completion recurses into another. A definition that would expand without bound —")
    strs_push(l, "`Strange[T] { next: Vec[Strange[Vec[T]]] }` — is refused by the ownership rule below before")
    strs_push(l, "it matters, and cannot keep the checker busy regardless: an application nested deeper than")
    strs_push(l, "`HARD_NESTING` (256) is interned and never completed, and there is a total")
    strs_push(l, "`INSTANCE_BUDGET` (100,000). Those are the last line, not the rule.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Checking a generic definition, once")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`declare_unit` reserves a function's id before resolving its signature, because the")
    strs_push(l, "parameters' types name their owner. The body is checked **once** with `T` a `Type::Param`,")
    strs_push(l, "and every rule that asks a type what it supports gets the answer an unknown type deserves:")
    strs_push(l, "`==` refuses it (`N0304`), a projection refuses it (`N0335`), a `match` refuses it, and task")
    strs_push(l, "safety says no — `may_cross_into_a_task` excludes parameters, so a generic body cannot")
    strs_push(l, "launder a `Vec` into a task through a `T`. What a `T` may do is what every value may do:")
    strs_push(l, "be bound, copied by its own law, passed, returned, stored, pushed and popped.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Calling one, and inference")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`check_generic_call` is the whole rule. Each parameter is `solved` from an argument by")
    strs_push(l, "`unify`, which is structural through applications and `Vec` and nothing else, or taken from")
    strs_push(l, "the written type arguments when there are exactly as many as the callee declares. An")
    strs_push(l, "argument whose declared type is already known — it mentions no parameter, or every one was")
    strs_push(l, "written — is checked against it as a monomorphic argument is. **The expected result type is")
    strs_push(l, "never consulted**, so `fn make[T]() -> T` needs `make[Int]()` (`N0354`), and a conflict")
    strs_push(l, "between two arguments is its own diagnostic (`N0355`) rather than the second argument read")
    strs_push(l, "against what the first happened to say. One mistake is one error: a parameter an argument")
    strs_push(l, "already failed on is *excused* from `N0354`. What the call settled is recorded on its site,")
    strs_push(l, "for the planner below.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What an importer reads: `nazm.interface/4`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-iface/src/wire.rs`. A type is an untagged `PersistentType` — a built-in's name,")
    strs_push(l, "`{ param }` (a **position**), `{ vec }`, or `{ def, args }` — and every generic definition")
    strs_push(l, "and export carries `generics`, its arity. **No parameter name appears anywhere**, so")
    strs_push(l, "alpha-renaming changes no byte and no `InterfaceHash`")
    strs_push(l, "(`a_generic_interface_carries_positions_and_no_parameter_names`), while reordering,")
    strs_push(l, "adding a parameter or changing a public generic signature, field or variant does")
    strs_push(l, "(`the_generic_invalidation_table_is_what_the_fingerprint_actually_does`). A body edit")
    strs_push(l, "changes nothing an importer reads. Reading validates every parameter position against its")
    strs_push(l, "owner's arity and every application against its definition's, bounds nesting at 64, and")
    strs_push(l, "refuses bytes that do not re-serialise to themselves (`NotCanonical`); rehydrating defers")
    strs_push(l, "and settles like stage 0b does. A dependent type-checks `Box[Int]`, `Maybe[Str]` and")
    strs_push(l, "`identity[Int]` against the deserialised interface **with the dependency's source deleted**.")
    strs_push(l, "`SEMANTIC_EPOCH` is 4: `[` and `]` stopped being unknown characters, a generic body is held")
    strs_push(l, "to old codes under new rules, and the interface a fingerprint is taken over changed shape —")
    strs_push(l, "the reasons are in `crates/nazm-cache/src/identity.rs`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Native code: parametric semantics, concrete LLVM")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm check` and `nazm run` are parametric — the interpreter runs a generic body once for")
    strs_push(l, "every type. `nazm build` **monomorphises**: one native function per generic function and")
    strs_push(l, "concrete argument list the program reaches. That is a property of this backend, not of the")
    strs_push(l, "language (`docs/user/spec.md`, *What a program cannot observe*), and the reason is concrete:")
    strs_push(l, "LLVM needs a layout and a copy/drop sequence per value, and an instance knows both at")
    strs_push(l, "compile time for free. Dictionary passing — a runtime description of `T`'s size and helpers")
    strs_push(l, "— would let one body serve every type and is the natural design for a future development")
    strs_push(l, "tier that trades code quality for build speed — the Cranelift tier of §1; nothing in the")
    strs_push(l, "semantic layers assumes monomorphisation, so it remains possible.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Instance identity** is a `GenericInstanceKey { def: FnId, args: Vec<Type> }` inside one")
    strs_push(l, "compilation and, durably, the definition's `DefKey` plus each argument's **canonical type")
    strs_push(l, "key** (`crates/nazm-lir/src/symbol.rs`, `type_key`): a built-in is its name, a definition is")
    strs_push(l, "`R.m.<module key>.<name>` or `E.…` (each component encoded), an application appends its")
    strs_push(l, "arguments' keys in parentheses, a `Vec` is `Vec(…)`, and a module with no durable key is")
    strs_push(l, "`u.<index>`. The key contains no `RecordId`, `TypeId`, span or absolute path. An instance's")
    strs_push(l, "symbol is `nz.m.<module>.<name>.g.<encode(keys, \",\")>`, so `identity[Int]` and")
    strs_push(l, "`identity[Str]` are different symbols by construction and the same instance requested from")
    strs_push(l, "two modules is one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Planning** (`crates/nazm-lir/src/instance.rs`) is global and deterministic. The")
    strs_push(l, "expanding-cycle rule runs first: nodes are (function, parameter position), a call passing a")
    strs_push(l, "type built from the caller's parameter to a callee's parameter adds an edge — *expanding*")
    strs_push(l, "when the argument is more than the parameter itself — and an expanding edge inside a")
    strs_push(l, "strongly connected component is polymorphic recursion, refused with the call that expands")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0357`). Then a breadth-first worklist starts from the calls non-generic functions make")
    strs_push(l, "and adds every call each instance's body makes under its substitution; everything an")
    strs_push(l, "instance's body mentions is interned then, so the table is complete before a layout is")
    strs_push(l, "written. `MAX_INSTANCES` (10,000) and `MAX_INSTANCE_NESTING` (64) are stated bounds")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0358`). The planned list is sorted by symbol. Ordinary recursion through a generic")
    strs_push(l, "function is recursion, and the definition-level recursion check refuses it as it refuses any")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0101`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Artefacts.** Each instance is lowered, from its definition's own nodes, into a unit of its")
    strs_push(l, "own — artefacts `g0`, `g1`, … — never into a caller's. A caller declares the instance by")
    strs_push(l, "symbol and signature; a declaration now carries the types its signature names into the")
    strs_push(l, "caller's unit, which the conformance corpus found missing (`<enum>` in a declaration of")
    strs_push(l, "`or_else[Str]`). A private function a generic body calls gets hidden linkage, because the")
    strs_push(l, "instance that calls it is another object. The object cache needed nothing new: an")
    strs_push(l, "instance's key is its exact bytes, as every unit's is. Measured")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-cli/tests/native_cache.rs`): a new instantiation compiles the caller, the new")
    strs_push(l, "instance and whatever runtime it newly reaches; a **generic body edit recompiles exactly its")
    strs_push(l, "instances and no caller**, not even its own module's unit; renaming a parameter recompiles")
    strs_push(l, "nothing. `nazm.build-report/1` gained `native.instances { units, compiled, reused }` — a")
    strs_push(l, "compatible addition under its contract.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `Vec[T]`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The sequence header every `Ints` already has — `{ len, cap, data, rc }` from")
    strs_push(l, "`@nz.seq_new` — so a `Vec` is allocated, counted, grown and reclaimed by the runtime that")
    strs_push(l, "already does all four. What is `T`'s is the element's layout, asked of LLVM by the address of")
    strs_push(l, "element 1 of an array at null (no semantic stage knows a byte size, §7.10), and what an")
    strs_push(l, "element owns, by `T`'s own law: push takes its own reference, get returns its own copy, set")
    strs_push(l, "takes the new reference before releasing the old, pop transfers. One release helper per")
    strs_push(l, "owning element type, `nz.vrel.<key>`, releases each element before the buffer; a `Vec` of")
    strs_push(l, "non-owning elements is released as an `Ints` is. Growth relocates bytes with `realloc` and")
    strs_push(l, "changes no count: every value this language has is movable by its bytes. `arr_grow`'s size")
    strs_push(l, "arithmetic is overflow-checked (`umul`) since N11.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Ownership cycles, over definitions")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`UserTypes::ownership_cycles`. The graph's nodes are **definitions** — an application is")
    strs_push(l, "not a declaration and is answered by the one it applies — and an edge runs from a record or")
    strs_push(l, "enum to every definition its fields or payloads mention, labelled **inline** or **counted**")
    strs_push(l, "by the path. How a generic definition uses each parameter — inline, counted, both, or not at")
    strs_push(l, "all — is found first by a fixpoint (`parameter_uses`), and an application's argument")
    strs_push(l, "inherits that use composed with how the application is reached. So `Tag[T] { n: Int }` owns")
    strs_push(l, "nothing of its argument and `Box[T] { v: T }` owns it inline. An all-inline cycle is")
    strs_push(l, "`N0336`, as before; any cycle with a counted edge is `N0359`, with the path. Two passes —")
    strs_push(l, "inline first, then everything, avoiding what the first reported — so one cycle is one")
    strs_push(l, "error.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The compiler written in Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/*.nz` implements all of it within its own subset, and did not mirror the")
    strs_push(l, "reference's structure where its own was simpler:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **One table.** The record table since N9 already held records, enums and variants; N11")
    strs_push(l, "  adds two more kinds, `rk_vec` and `rk_param`, and an application is an entry of kind")
    strs_push(l, "  record or enum with `tpl` naming its definition. A type is still one `Int`: `100 + r` a")
    strs_push(l, "  record, enum or variant, `1_000_000 + r` a `Vec`, `2_000_000 + r` a parameter. The arrays")
    strs_push(l, "  travel as one `struct Table` of handles — the first record in the compiler used as a")
    strs_push(l, "  bundle of shared state.")
    strs_push(l, "- **No recursion anywhere**, which the native backend requires of the compiler compiling")
    strs_push(l, "  itself. Substitution is a post-order walk with an explicit stack; `apply` only enqueues,")
    strs_push(l, "  and the stages that hand a type on call `settle_now` — because `apply → settle → complete")
    strs_push(l, "  → substitute → apply` is a call cycle `nazm build` refuses, and was, the first time.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Written types carry their offsets.** A type with arguments is written into a node's text")
    strs_push(l, "  as `Pair@10[Int@15,Vec@20[Str@24]@27]@28`, and a return type always carries its offset, so")
    strs_push(l, "  the checker reports at the reference's spans; `selfhost.rs`'s dumper writes the same text")
    strs_push(l, "  from the reference's `TypeName`.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Instances are node ranges.** The emitter plans instances with a worklist before emitting")
    strs_push(l, "  anything, records each one's substituted `ntype`/`nrec` and callee instances, and emits a")
    strs_push(l, "  generic function's subtree once per instance with those arrays patched — one LLVM module,")
    strs_push(l, "  as always; the per-instance objects are the reference's decomposition, not a language")
    strs_push(l, "  requirement. Instance symbols are `@nz.g<n>`, numbered by the worklist, which is a")
    strs_push(l, "  function of the program alone. The same N0357/N0358/N0101 refusals apply.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`the_nazm_checker_agrees_with_the_reference_on_generics` compares code **and** span over 42")
    strs_push(l, "programs; the memory test builds five generic programs with both compilers and compares the")
    strs_push(l, "reclamation reports; the bootstrap compiles a generic corpus and refuses a refusal corpus")
    strs_push(l, "with C2, C3 and the reference.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The dogfood.** The diagnostics were four parallel arrays — code, start, end, message —")
    strs_push(l, "threaded through every stage as four parameters and kept the same length by care. They are")
    strs_push(l, "a `Vec[Diag]` now: 19 parameter lists and 127 argument lists lost three parameters each, and")
    strs_push(l, "a stage that pushed a code without a message would not compile. Measured on the compiler")
    strs_push(l, "compiling itself: the same result, 26 KB less IR, about 3 MB less peak RSS and no")
    strs_push(l, "measurable change in time (`performance.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What this still does not do")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **No traits, constraints, methods or `impl`**, so a generic body can do only what every")
    strs_push(l, "  type can, and no `Option`/`Result` in the standard sense — `enum Maybe[T]` is a user")
    strs_push(l, "  declaration. No higher kinds, const generics, defaults, variance, specialisation or")
    strs_push(l, "  overloading. *(Superseded in part by §7.13: `Result` and `Option` now exist, as ordinary")
    strs_push(l, "  generic enums of the core prelude, and N12 needed no generic machinery N11 did not have.)*")
    strs_push(l, "- **No spawn of a generic function**, and no generic `main`.")
    strs_push(l, "- **No indexing syntax**; `vec_get`/`vec_set` are calls.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Monomorphisation only.** Code size grows with the number of instances; `performance.md`")
    strs_push(l, "  measures 1, 10 and 100.")
    strs_push(l, "- **No space promise for an enum in a `Vec`**: an enum is still one slot per variant, and a")
    strs_push(l, "  `Vec[Enum]` multiplies it by the length.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.13 Typed errors: a prelude module and one operator — settled by N12, 2026-09-24")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/spec.md`, *Typed error values*, is the language. This is where it lives. The design")
    strs_push(l, "question was not how to represent `Result` — N9, N10 and N11 already could — but how one")
    strs_push(l, "definition becomes **the** `Result` in every module without a package system, a structural")
    strs_push(l, "test or a name test. The answer is one module whose identity the toolchain fixes, imported")
    strs_push(l, "by every other.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The core source boundary")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`library/core/prelude.nz` is ordinary `.nz` source declaring `pub enum Result[T, E]` and")
    strs_push(l, "`pub enum Option[T]`. Nothing in any crate describes those enums: `nazm-sema/src/prelude.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "holds the file's **bytes** (`include_str!`, so a compilation needs no installation")
    strs_push(l, "directory — a packaging decision) and the name it is shown under, and the checker reads them")
    strs_push(l, "as source like any other file.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Loading.** `nazm-service/src/load.rs` (in `nazm-cli` until N16) appends the prelude after every project file; the")
    strs_push(l, "  `&str` entry points (`nazm_core::one_file`) do the same. It is therefore the **last**")
    strs_push(l, "  module and the last `FileId`: no project module's id and no span in one moves.")
    strs_push(l, "  `ModuleGraph::attach_prelude` adds it and an ordinary import edge from every other module,")
    strs_push(l, "  with a synthetic span because nothing was written.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Identity.** `ModuleKey::prelude()` is `@core/prelude`. `ModuleKey::relative` refuses a")
    strs_push(l, "  first component `@core`, so the key is disjoint from every project key by construction,")
    strs_push(l, "  and `ModuleKey::parse` accepts it back from a persisted interface.")
    strs_push(l, "  `ModuleGraph::prelude()` finds the module **by key** — never by position — so a")
    strs_push(l, "  compilation assembled by hand, or from persisted interfaces, has one exactly when it")
    strs_push(l, "  contains that key.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Visibility and collision.** Because the prelude is an import, `type_environment` puts")
    strs_push(l, "  its exported types in every module's type namespace by the existing rule. The one special")
    strs_push(l, "  case is the collision: a project type named like a prelude type is `N0363` at the")
    strs_push(l, "  declaration rather than `N0208` at an import line that does not exist.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `?`: resolved once, lowered as a `match`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Syntax.** `TokenKind::Question`, `Expr::Propagate { operand, op_span, span }`, parsed in")
    strs_push(l, "  the postfix loop beside projection.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Checking.** `Checker::check_propagate`. The canonical `Result` is found once per unit —")
    strs_push(l, "  `Enums::declared(prelude, \"Result\")`, a `DefKey` lookup — and a type is a `Result` iff")
    strs_push(l, "  `definition_of(t)` is that enum. The operand's and the function's `Result`s must share")
    strs_push(l, "  their second argument by `Type` equality, which interning makes nominal. The decision is")
    strs_push(l, "  recorded as a `Propagation { operand, ok, err, into, into_err }` keyed by the `?`'s span;")
    strs_push(l, "  nothing downstream asks whether a type is called `Result`.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Completion.** None of its own: the operand's `Value(T)` is the result, and the `Err` arm")
    strs_push(l, "  is a `return`, which N10.1 already made a transfer from any value position.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Interpreter.** `Interpreter::propagate`: the operand once, then `Flow::Fell(payload)` or")
    strs_push(l, "  `Flow::Return(Err)` in the function's own `Result` — the same `Flow::Return` a written")
    strs_push(l, "  `return` produces, so it leaves loops and scopes, joining tasks, exactly as one does.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Native.** `lower_propagate` builds the LIR `Expr::Match` the operator means: the operand")
    strs_push(l, "  into a hidden local the frame releases, an `Ok` arm binding the payload with `Stmt::Let`")
    strs_push(l, "  and yielding it, and an `Err` arm binding the error and `Stmt::Return`ing a `Variant` of")
    strs_push(l, "  the function's `Result`. **There is no new LIR node**, and the emitter did not change: the")
    strs_push(l, "  scope joins, temporaries and frame cleanup on the error path are `Stmt::Return`'s, and the")
    strs_push(l, "  retain-before-release order is `Stmt::Let`'s. No landing pad, no `invoke`, no personality")
    strs_push(l, "  function — there is nothing to unwind, because this is a branch.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Interfaces and caches")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **`nazm.interface/4` is sufficient.** A signature mentioning `Result[Int, E]` persists as")
    strs_push(l, "  an application of `@core/prelude::enum Result`, which `/4` already represented; the")
    strs_push(l, "  prelude's own interface is an ordinary `/4` interface; and every module's `dependencies`")
    strs_push(l, "  now lists `@core/prelude`, which is data `/4` already had a field for. Nothing changed")
    strs_push(l, "  shape, so the schema did not move.")
    strs_push(l, "- **One identity across interfaces.** An interface carries every type its shapes mention,")
    strs_push(l, "  so B's carries the prelude's `Result`. N3–N11 rehydrated each interface's types")
    strs_push(l, "  separately, which made two rehydrated interfaces disagree about a shared definition —")
    strs_push(l, "  harmless until a third module's type mattered, and decisive for `?`. N12 adds")
    strs_push(l, "  `PersistentUnitInterface::rehydrate_into` with a `Rehydrated` table keyed by `DefKey`: a")
    strs_push(l, "  definition met in two interfaces is one definition, and one first met as a mention is")
    strs_push(l, "  adopted by its own module when that module's interface arrives, in either order.")
    strs_push(l, "- **`CheckKey`.** Unchanged in shape: the prelude is an import, so its `(ModuleKey,")
    strs_push(l, "  InterfaceHash)` is in every module's dependency list already. It is not also hashed into")
    strs_push(l, "  `CheckerIdentity`, which describes the checker, not the program. `SEMANTIC_EPOCH` moved")
    strs_push(l, "  4 → 5 for the rule changes the code set cannot show (`nazm-cache/src/identity.rs`).")
    strs_push(l, "- **Objects.** `ObjectKey` is untouched — any difference `?` makes is in the LLVM bytes.")
    strs_push(l, "  A module that declares no function now has **no unit**, so the prelude never produces an")
    strs_push(l, "  object; its enums' helpers are emitted in the units that use them, as every enum's are.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The compiler written in Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Loading.** `emit FILE CORE` and `check FILE CORE`: the prelude is named on the command")
    strs_push(l, "  line, because it is the toolchain's source and not the program's. `attach_core` appends")
    strs_push(l, "  it as the last module and gives every module an edge to it. This compiler's modules are")
    strs_push(l, "  session indices, so \"the last module\" was its identity for the prelude — *replaced by N12.1,")
    strs_push(l, "  §7.14: the module keyed `@core/prelude`, found by key*. Every stage of the bootstrap reads the same file,")
    strs_push(l, "  and `bootstrap.sh` records its digest.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Checking.** `n_propagate`, finished in `check_all`: the canonical `Result` is the entry")
    strs_push(l, "  the prelude module declares under that name; the node records the operand's `Ok` variant")
    strs_push(l, "  entry in `nrec` — substituted per instance like an arm's — and a hidden slot in `nslot`.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Emission.** `emit_propagate`, at the node: store the operand into its slot, one test of")
    strs_push(l, "  the discriminant, and on the error path retain the error, build the function's `Result`,")
    strs_push(l, "  and leave by `n_return`'s exact sequence; on the success path retain the payload and")
    strs_push(l, "  release the operand.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The dogfood")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The front end — lexing, parsing and twelve checking passes over one shared `Vec[Diag]` —")
    strs_push(l, "was written out twice, in `check.nz` and in `emit.nz`'s `main`, and each copy ended by")
    strs_push(l, "asking `vec_len(diags) > 0`. It is now **one stage**, `check_program(…) ->")
    strs_push(l, "Result[Checked, Vec[Diag]]`, where `Checked` is a record of the tables emission reads.")
    strs_push(l, "Inside it every pass still collects into the one `Vec[Diag]` and keeps going — recovery is")
    strs_push(l, "untouched, and a program with three mistakes still reports three. `check.nz` lost its copy")
    strs_push(l, "(171 → 64 lines), and `emit.nz` became `emit_program(…) -> Result[Str, Vec[Diag]]`, whose")
    strs_push(l, "first line is `check_program(…)?`, with `main` taking the result apart once. Measured in")
    strs_push(l, "`performance.md`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What this still does not do")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **No `?` on `Option`**, no conversion between error types, no `Error` trait, no methods")
    strs_push(l, "  on `Result`: each needs a protocol, and traits do not exist.")
    strs_push(l, "- **No `main` returning `Result`**: mapping a typed error to a process status is a separate")
    strs_push(l, "  contract.")
    strs_push(l, "- **No niche layout**: `Option[Str]` and `Result[A, B]` are enums, one slot per variant.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Every module depends on the whole prelude**, not on the names it uses. With two")
    strs_push(l, "  declarations that over-invalidates nothing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.14 One block in every position, and the prelude by its key — settled by N12.1, 2026-09-24")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N12.1 adds nothing to the language. It closes two places where an implementation said less")
    strs_push(l, "than the language does: the native backends refused a block used as a value anywhere but a")
    strs_push(l, "function body and an `if` branch, and the compiler written in Nazm recognised the core")
    strs_push(l, "prelude by its position.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The block law, unchanged")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/spec.md`, *One block, and completion decided by checking*: a block is statements and an optional tail, and it")
    strs_push(l, "completes `Value(T)`, `Unit` or `Diverges`. A `match` folds its arms as an `if` folds its")
    strs_push(l, "branches — an arm that diverges defers to the others, a `Unit` arm makes the whole `match`")
    strs_push(l, "`Unit`, and two `Value` arms must agree. The parser has always accepted `{` as an operand,")
    strs_push(l, "the checker has always checked it with `check_block`, and the interpreter has always run")
    strs_push(l, "it. What changed is that `nazm build` and the Nazm-written compiler compile it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Reference backend")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **One lowering for a value block.** `lower_block` — statements, then the tail, `result:")
    strs_push(l, "  None` when the statements transfer — is now reached from a function body, an `if` branch,")
    strs_push(l, "  a `match` arm written as a block, and a bare block in any value position. A block arm is")
    strs_push(l, "  the pattern's bindings followed by the block's own statements, in one `Block`. There is")
    strs_push(l, "  no second block lowering and no arm-specific completion rule.")
    strs_push(l, "- **`Expr::Block(Box<Block>)`** is the one LIR generalisation a value position needed: a")
    strs_push(l, "  block inside an argument or an initialiser has nowhere else to go, and hoisting its")
    strs_push(l, "  statements out would move their effects before the arguments to their left. It is")
    strs_push(l, "  emitted by the same `Emitter::block` the branches use. Its bindings need no scope: slots")
    strs_push(l, "  are unique per function, so a block local is frame storage exactly as an `if` branch's is.")
    strs_push(l, "- **`Stmt::Match`**, the statement form, pairs with `Stmt::If` for the same reason: an arm")
    strs_push(l, "  that only assigns completes `Unit`, which a value `Block` cannot represent — its `None`")
    strs_push(l, "  means *never arrives*. `lower_effect` is the one place an expression in statement")
    strs_push(l, "  position is lowered: an `if`, a `match` or a block keeps its statement form, anything else")
    strs_push(l, "  is a `Stmt::Discard`. The emitter shares the scrutinee dispatch (`dispatch`) and the")
    strs_push(l, "  release at the join (`release_matched`) between the value and the statement `match`.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Joins.** Unchanged, and now reached by block arms: an arm whose block transfers is")
    strs_push(l, "  emitted into its own terminator and is not a predecessor of the join; the `phi` lists only")
    strs_push(l, "  the arms that arrive; a `match` no arm reaches opens no join and has no value.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Ownership at a block's end")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A block does not release its locals when it ends. They are frame slots, released when the")
    strs_push(l, "function leaves or when their `let` runs again, which is what N7 already specified for a")
    strs_push(l, "branch. So the take-before-release question is the consumer's, and it is the one every")
    strs_push(l, "value already answers: a tail read from a local is **borrowed**, and whatever takes it over")
    strs_push(l, "— a `let`, an argument, a field, the `phi` of a `match` in each arm's own block before its")
    strs_push(l, "jump — takes its own reference. A `Vec` tail is the same handle, not a copy. A pattern")
    strs_push(l, "binding took its own reference from the scrutinee when it was bound, so the scrutinee's")
    strs_push(l, "release at the join cannot reach a payload an arm handed on.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The compiler written in Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Parsing.** `{` in operand position suspends the expression exactly as an `if` does and")
    strs_push(l, "  opens a `frame_blockexpr`; when it closes, the block is the operand, wrapped in a")
    strs_push(l, "  `blockexpr` node — the reference AST's `Expr::Block`, and the encoding `selfhost.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "  already fixed for it. A statement that starts with `{` is block-like and needs no `;`.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Checking.** `blockexpr` completes and types exactly as its block does. The block's")
    strs_push(l, "  `Value`/`Unit`/`Diverges` is the existing `c_value`/`c_unit`/`c_diverges`; nothing is")
    strs_push(l, "  inferred from which node came last.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Emission.** Structure only, like `block`: the tail's value is already on the stack, and")
    strs_push(l, "  the joins, `phi` incomings and `live` state are the existing ones.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The prelude's identity.** A module's entry in `mpath` is its **key**: a project file's")
    strs_push(l, "  normalised path, or `@core/prelude`, which `attach_core` gives the prelude. `core_module`")
    strs_push(l, "  finds the module with that key, once, in `check_program`, and both consumers — the")
    strs_push(l, "  collision rule in `check_type_imports` and `?`'s `Result` in `check_all` — take that one")
    strs_push(l, "  answer. A project path whose first component is `@core` is re-keyed out of the namespace,")
    strs_push(l, "  so no project module can hold the key; like the reference, such a file still compiles.")
    strs_push(l, "  The loader still places the prelude last, and nothing reads that.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The dogfood")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`record_owned` — which declaration a module owns under a name — answered `-1` for none. The")
    strs_push(l, "same `-1` is what `definition_of` answers for any type that is not a record, so each of its")
    strs_push(l, "four consumers carried an `if found >= 0` guard, one of them in front of the comparison that")
    strs_push(l, "decides whether a type is the core `Result`. It returns `Option[Int]` now, and each consumer")
    strs_push(l, "takes it apart with `match`: the type lookup falls through to imports on `None`, the")
    strs_push(l, "duplicate and collision checks report from the `Some` arm, and `applies_core_result` answers")
    strs_push(l, "`false` for a compilation with no prelude rather than comparing with anything.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What this still does not do")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **No equality on enums**, so the compiler's integer tags stay integers: `kind ==")
    strs_push(l, "  n_block()` cannot become a `match` without a comparison the language does not have.")
    strs_push(l, "- **A block does not end a lifetime.** Locals are released with the frame; nothing here")
    strs_push(l, "  shortens that.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The self-hosted compiler still emits one LLVM module**, and still has no durable keys")
    strs_push(l, "  beyond the prelude's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N13 answered the first of these: enums compare now, and `analyse.nz`'s completion states")
    strs_push(l, "are one (§7.15).*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.15 Equality: a derived capability, and a helper per compared type — settled by N13, 2026-09-25")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/spec.md`, *Equality is derived*, is the law. This is how the two compilers implement")
    strs_push(l, "it, and the decisions that are implementation rather than language.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### One derivation, beside the others, and independent of them")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`UserTypes::equality(t) -> Result<(), NoEquality>` in `crates/nazm-sema/src/udt.rs` is the")
    strs_push(l, "whole rule. It sits beside `needs_cleanup` and `task_safety` because it is the same kind of")
    strs_push(l, "answer — a property of a type derived from what it contains — and walks the same")
    strs_push(l, "containment graph through `contained`, which for a record is its fields and for an enum every")
    strs_push(l, "payload field of every variant. What it does **not** do is consult either of them: a `Str`")
    strs_push(l, "needs cleanup and compares; a `Chan` may cross into a task and does not compare; `Vec[Int]`")
    strs_push(l, "does neither. Leaves: `Int`, `Bool` and `Str` have equality; `Ints`, `Strs`, `Vec`, `Chan`")
    strs_push(l, "and `Param` do not. The walk is iterative, depth-first over declaration order so the")
    strs_push(l, "reported path is the one a reader finds first, and keeps a visited set, so it ends even on a")
    strs_push(l, "program whose containment cycle is being refused in the same run. It is not memoised:")
    strs_push(l, "answers are asked once per `==`, and each is linear in the definitions reachable from the")
    strs_push(l, "type, which no measurement has shown to matter.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The checker's `check_binary` is the one consumer: `lt == rt && types.equality(lt).is_ok()`.")
    strs_push(l, "Type equality is id equality, so the nominal rule is the representation's — two records of")
    strs_push(l, "one shape are two `RecordId`s — and an applied type is its interned instance, whose fields")
    strs_push(l, "are already substituted: `Box[Int]` is answered over `value: Int`, `Box[T]` over")
    strs_push(l, "`value: T`, and nothing in the rule knows generics exist. `Option` and `Result` are")
    strs_push(l, "instances of prelude enums and are answered the same way; no code names them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The refusal stays `N0304`. The derived path (`NoEquality::path`) makes its message say which")
    strs_push(l, "component is responsible, `inner.values` or `work.Held.items`, in the task-safety path's")
    strs_push(l, "spelling.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Persisted interfaces carry nothing new")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An interface already carries each exported record's and enum's fields and variants, with")
    strs_push(l, "their types, under durable identity — which is exactly the input the derivation reads. So an")
    strs_push(l, "importer that has only the interface derives equality for the imported type exactly as the")
    strs_push(l, "declaring module does (`a_dependent_derives_equality_from_a_deserialised_interface_with_the_dependency_deleted`),")
    strs_push(l, "and no `equality_capable` fact is written that could disagree with the shape it summarises.")
    strs_push(l, "The schema stays `nazm.interface/4`, and an unchanged public type has the same bytes and the")
    strs_push(l, "same `InterfaceHash` it had before N13; the pinned-interface tests are unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The checker's own identity moves instead: `SEMANTIC_EPOCH` 5 → 6, because the conditions")
    strs_push(l, "under which `N0304` is raised changed and the code set did not. `CheckerIdentity::at_epoch`")
    strs_push(l, "lets a test stand in for the epoch-5 checker, and an entry that build would have filed is a")
    strs_push(l, "miss (`an_entry_from_the_checker_before_derived_equality_is_never_read`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The interpreter: the language's relation, not the host's")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`eval.rs`'s `equal(a, b) -> Option<bool>` is `==`, written out: `Int` and `Bool` by value,")
    strs_push(l, "`Str` by `bytes()`, a record over its fields, an enum by variant and then over that variant's")
    strs_push(l, "fields. An enum value carries only its active payload, so there is nothing inactive to read.")
    strs_push(l, "No definition id is compared — checking already guaranteed one type — and `Value`'s own")
    strs_push(l, "`PartialEq`, which compares sequences by identity so the rest of `Value` can derive things,")
    strs_push(l, "is not what `==` evaluates. `!=` is `!equal`, computed once.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Native code: a helper per compared type")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A record or enum comparison lowers to `Expr::Compare` exactly as a `Str` one does, and the")
    strs_push(l, "emitter calls `@nz.eq.<type>(T %a, T %b) -> i1`, generated on first use in the unit:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **A record** extracts each field in **layout order** — canonical, by field name — compares")
    strs_push(l, "  it (`icmp`, the `Str` length-then-`memcmp` branch, or the field type's own helper), and")
    strs_push(l, "  branches to `false` at the first difference. Comparing is pure, so the order cannot be")
    strs_push(l, "  observed; canonical order makes the helper's bytes independent of how the declaration was")
    strs_push(l, "  written, and a program whose fields, variants and payload fields are written in another")
    strs_push(l, "  order emits byte-identical IR (`declaration_order_changes_no_byte_of_the_program`).")
    strs_push(l, "- **An enum** compares discriminants and branches to `false` if they differ, before any slot")
    strs_push(l, "  is read. Equal ones `switch` to the variant's arm, which extracts that variant's slot — tag")
    strs_push(l, "  plus one — from both operands and compares its payload fields; a zero-payload variant has")
    strs_push(l, "  no arm and reaches `true` through the default. An inactive slot is never extracted.")
    strs_push(l, "- **`!=`** is the helper's answer and an `xor i1 …, true`. There is no second helper.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Helpers are `internal`, named from the type's `NativeTypeName` — the durable identity with")
    strs_push(l, "its canonical type arguments, so `Box[Int]` and `Box[Str]` get two and a comparison written")
    strs_push(l, "twice gets one — and duplicated in each unit that compares the type. No symbol is exported,")
    strs_push(l, "so no ABI is promised and the object cache needs nothing new: a changed comparison is changed")
    strs_push(l, "LLVM, which is a changed `ObjectKey`. The recursion over a nested type is calls between")
    strs_push(l, "helpers, in the emitted program, as retain and release already are.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Ownership** is the `Str` comparison's, generalised: both operands are evaluated, left then")
    strs_push(l, "right; the helper borrows them and retains nothing; after the answer exists each operand that")
    strs_push(l, "is a temporary is released once (`drop_temporary`). A bound operand is untouched. An operand")
    strs_push(l, "that transfers leaves before the helper is called, and what the other side built is released")
    strs_push(l, "by the unwinding that already exists.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The compiler written in Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`analyse.nz` has the same derivation, `equality_blocker`, over the same table: an enum's")
    strs_push(l, "fields are its variants and a variant's are its payload, so one walk covers both kinds, as")
    strs_push(l, "`task_unsafe_path` already did. `emit.nz` emits the same helper shape, `@nz.eq<entry>`,")
    strs_push(l, "generated after every function for each entry a comparison reached, each adding the entries")
    strs_push(l, "its own fields compare. The two compilers' helpers are not textually identical — the")
    strs_push(l, "self-hosted one delegates a variant's payload to the variant entry's helper — and nothing")
    strs_push(l, "requires them to be: both are compared on answers and on reclamation, not on text.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The dogfood")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`analyse.nz`'s completion was `c_value() = 0`, `c_unit() = 1`, `c_diverges() = 2` stored in")
    strs_push(l, "an `Ints`, with a fourth value, `-1`, meaning \"no arm yet\" in a `match`'s fold. It is")
    strs_push(l, "`enum Completion { Value, Unit, Diverges }` in a `Vec[Completion]` now, the fold is an")
    strs_push(l, "`Option[Completion]`, and its twenty comparisons are `Completion == Completion`. An integer")
    strs_push(l, "that is not a completion can no longer be stored as one — which is also why nine historical")
    strs_push(l, "mutations that compared a completion with `99` had to be rewritten: the state they")
    strs_push(l, "simulated is no longer expressible.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What this still does not do")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **No abstraction over equality.** `fn same[T](a: T, b: T)` is refused and has to be: there")
    strs_push(l, "  is no way to say \"`T` has equality\", and N13 added none.")
    strs_push(l, "- **No sequence or channel equality**, and so none for anything that contains one.")
    strs_push(l, "- **No ordering, hashing or custom equality** on a user type.")
    strs_push(l, "- **An enum is still one slot per variant**, so an equality helper for a wide enum extracts")
    strs_push(l, "  from an aggregate larger than a tagged union would be; the helper reads only one slot.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.16 A requirement on a type parameter: one set, read by one derivation — settled by N14, 2026-09-25")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/spec.md`, *A type parameter may require equality*, is the law. N13 found the wall:")
    strs_push(l, "a concrete `Box[Int]` compares and a generic body over `Box[T]` cannot say it wants one")
    strs_push(l, "that does. N14 is the smallest mechanism that lets it say so.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Why a built-in requirement and not a trait")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Three shapes were compared. A **trait-shaped bound** (`T: Eq`) reads as the first half of a")
    strs_push(l, "trait system — it invites `impl Eq for`, which would contradict N13's rule that equality is")
    strs_push(l, "derived and cannot be written — and would need a namespace in which user traits could later")
    strs_push(l, "live, decided now for no program. **Another spelling** (`T: ==`, `requires equality(T)`)")
    strs_push(l, "avoids a name but is either an operator in a type position or a second clause form. A")
    strs_push(l, "**built-in capability requirement**, `T: Equality`, is one name in one position: it reuses")
    strs_push(l, "the `:` a field already uses for \"has this type\", names the capability rather than a")
    strs_push(l, "declaration, and commits to nothing a future constraint system would have to undo — a trait")
    strs_push(l, "system could later make `Equality` one of its members, or not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Representation: an assumption environment of one set")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`Generics::equality: BTreeSet<TypeParam>` holds every parameter whose declaration requires")
    strs_push(l, "equality, keyed by the parameter's identity — its owner and position — never by its name.")
    strs_push(l, "That set *is* the assumption environment. A parameter only appears inside its own")
    strs_push(l, "declaration, so one set for the compilation answers \"what may this body assume\" for every")
    strs_push(l, "body at once, and no environment has to be threaded through checking.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`UserTypes::equality` — N13's single derivation — reads it in exactly one place: the leaf")
    strs_push(l, "rule for `Type::Param(p)` is `requires_equality(p)`. Everything else follows from the walk")
    strs_push(l, "that already existed: `Box[T]` is an interned instance whose field is `T`, so it derives")
    strs_push(l, "equality exactly when `T` does; `Result[T, E]` needs both; `Vec[T]` is a leaf with none. No")
    strs_push(l, "bounded-parameter case is written in the operator, in record or enum logic, or in the core")
    strs_push(l, "prelude, and termination is the walk's (a visited set over definitions).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Checking")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "* **Declaration** (`declare_unit`): `declared_requirements` records `T: Equality` for a")
    strs_push(l, "  function's parameter, refuses an unknown name (`N0365`) and a requirement on a record's or")
    strs_push(l, "  enum's parameter (`N0101`, not supported yet: every instance of such a type would have to")
    strs_push(l, "  be checked wherever it is written).")
    strs_push(l, "* **The body**: unchanged code. `check_binary` already asks `equality(lt)`; a required `T`")
    strs_push(l, "  now answers yes. The body is checked once.")
    strs_push(l, "* **A call** (`check_generic_call`): after the type arguments are settled — written or")
    strs_push(l, "  inferred, by the unchanged N11 rules — each argument of a required parameter is asked")
    strs_push(l, "  `equality(arg)`. A concrete argument answers by what it contains; a caller's own")
    strs_push(l, "  parameter by *its* requirement, which is what makes forwarding work exactly when the")
    strs_push(l, "  caller requires the same. `N0364` is reported at the callee for a written argument and at")
    strs_push(l, "  the argument an inferred one came from, with N13's blocking path.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Interfaces and caches")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.interface/5` adds `requires_equality` — ascending positions, absent when empty — to")
    strs_push(l, "each exported function; the reader validates it and rehydration re-records it, so an")
    strs_push(l, "importer checked against the interface alone is held to the requirement. A `/4` file could")
    strs_push(l, "not say it, and a `/4` reader handed a `/5` file could not honour it, so the major moved.")
    strs_push(l, "Because the field is by position, renaming a parameter changes no byte; because it is in the")
    strs_push(l, "interface, adding or removing a public requirement moves its `InterfaceHash`, which reaches")
    strs_push(l, "every importer's `CheckKey` through its dependencies — the existing invalidation path, with")
    strs_push(l, "nothing added. A private function's requirement is not in any interface and rechecks only")
    strs_push(l, "its own module. `SEMANTIC_EPOCH` moved 6 → 7 for the module's own body: `==` on a required")
    strs_push(l, "parameter moved from refused to accepted under the existing `N0304`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Native code: nothing")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Native generics are monomorphised, so by the time a body is lowered every parameter is a")
    strs_push(l, "concrete type and `==` on it is N13's comparison — an `icmp`, the `Str` comparison, or a")
    strs_push(l, "concrete helper. The requirement is not in the IR, the object key or the program: the")
    strs_push(l, "instance of `same[T: Equality]` at `Int` is instruction for instruction a hand-written")
    strs_push(l, "`same_int` (`a_requirement_leaves_no_trace_in_the_program`). The interpreter is parametric")
    strs_push(l, "and compares values, so it has nothing to do either.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The compiler written in Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The parser writes a requirement into the parameter list's text after the parameter's")
    strs_push(l, "position — `[T@5=Equality@8]` — where every existing reader of that text stops, so only the")
    strs_push(l, "checker's `requirement_of` sees it. The table gains a `req` column, `1` for a parameter")
    strs_push(l, "whose declaration requires equality; `has_no_equality` reads it for a parameter, which puts")
    strs_push(l, "the assumption environment in the same one place as the reference's; `check_generic_call`")
    strs_push(l, "checks each argument by `equality_blocker`, at the reference's spans. The emitter needed no")
    strs_push(l, "change.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What this still does not do")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Only equality.** No other capability can be required, and nothing lets a program declare")
    strs_push(l, "  one.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Only functions.** A record's or enum's parameter cannot carry a requirement.")
    strs_push(l, "- **No user-defined behaviour behind a bound.** `==` is N13's everywhere; a bound only proves")
    strs_push(l, "  an operand is in its domain.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.17 The lossless concrete syntax tree — settled by N15, 2026-09-25")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Why it exists.** The abstract tree is what a program means, and it forgets exactly what")
    strs_push(l, "an editing tool needs: whitespace, comments, parentheses, punctuation, and the whole body of")
    strs_push(l, "a function with a syntax error in it. Until N15 comments reached nothing but the formatter,")
    strs_push(l, "as a side list of spans, and one malformed statement discarded the rest of its function. The")
    strs_push(l, "concrete tree is the file as written. It owns what no other layer owns — the source")
    strs_push(l, "structure, every byte of trivia, the structure of malformed regions, and stable node")
    strs_push(l, "boundaries — and nothing else: no name is resolved in it and no type is in it, and nothing")
    strs_push(l, "downstream of the parser reads it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**One scan, one parser, two trees.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "UTF-8 bytes ─ lex_lossless_in ─▶ [Lexeme]  (every byte: token | whitespace | comment | invalid)")
    strs_push(l, "                                    │")
    strs_push(l, "                         tokens, borrowed in order")
    strs_push(l, "                                    │")
    strs_push(l, "                           parser.rs (one grammar)")
    strs_push(l, "                            ├──▶ Program (AST)      → checker, evaluator, backend")
    strs_push(l, "                            └──▶ events ─▶ Cst      → tools; nothing in the compiler")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The lexer produces one lossless stream; the token list the parser reads, and the comment")
    strs_push(l, "list the formatter reads, are views of it, so nothing scans a file twice")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-syntax/src/lexer.rs`). The parser (`parser.rs`) builds both trees from the")
    strs_push(l, "same decisions: every consumed token passes through one `bump`, which records it for the")
    strs_push(l, "concrete tree, and every construct records where it began and wraps its concrete node at the")
    strs_push(l, "point it builds its abstract one. **`parser.rs` is where concrete syntax becomes abstract")
    strs_push(l, "syntax** — not a pass over the concrete tree. This is the transitional shape the directive")
    strs_push(l, "allowed, stated as such: a later milestone may make the abstract tree a projection of the")
    strs_push(l, "concrete one, and nothing here depends on it not being. What makes it one grammar rather")
    strs_push(l, "than two is that neither tree can be built without the other's decisions, and")
    strs_push(l, "`the_abstract_and_concrete_trees_agree_on_every_construct` checks, over every clean file in")
    strs_push(l, "the repository, that each construct the checker sees has a concrete node over the same bytes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The tree** (`crates/nazm-syntax/src/cst.rs`) is a `cstree` 0.14 green tree with a red")
    strs_push(l, "layer, wrapped: the workspace sees `Cst`, `CstNode`, `Leaf` and `SyntaxKind`, never a")
    strs_push(l, "`cstree` type. `SyntaxKind` is one vocabulary — a leaf kind per lexer token (by an")
    strs_push(l, "exhaustive mapping, so a new token does not compile without one), three trivia kinds, a node")
    strs_push(l, "kind per grammar construct, and `Error`. **No kind has a fixed spelling**: `cstree` would")
    strs_push(l, "store such a token without its text and print it back from the kind, which is reconstruction")
    strs_push(l, "from canonical spelling; every leaf is interned from the bytes it was scanned from instead.")
    strs_push(l, "The end of the file is not a leaf.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Trivia placement** is decided once, after parsing, from an event log: trivia before a token")
    strs_push(l, "is emitted immediately before it, after every node that closed before it and before every")
    strs_push(l, "node that opens at it. So no node begins or ends with trivia, and a comment between two")
    strs_push(l, "statements belongs to the block around them. Deciding it during parsing put trivia inside")
    strs_push(l, "whatever construct was being attempted when it was seen — including ones that then failed —")
    strs_push(l, "which the invariant tests caught on the first run.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Error structure.** A malformed region is an `Error` node over the bytes it covers: the")
    strs_push(l, "leaves of the construct that failed and the tokens skipped after it. A character the lexer")
    strs_push(l, "refuses is an `Invalid` leaf owning its bytes. There is no synthetic token; a missing `;` is")
    strs_push(l, "a diagnostic, not a zero-width leaf.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Recovery boundaries.** Inside a block, a statement that fails is skipped to the nearest")
    strs_push(l, "place a statement can start — past a `;`, before the block's own `}`, or before a keyword")
    strs_push(l, "that can only begin a statement (`let`, `while`, `return`, `break`, `continue`, `scope`,")
    strs_push(l, "`spawn`) — counting braces from those the failed statement left open, so a `match` it")
    strs_push(l, "opened does not end the block. `if` and `match` are not boundaries: they begin expressions,")
    strs_push(l, "and the tail of a malformed statement is full of them. Reaching `fn`, `pub` or the end of")
    strs_push(l, "the file abandons the block, which is the missing `}` already reported. Every path consumes")
    strs_push(l, "a token or ends the block. At the top level, recovery is what it was: skip to the next item.")
    strs_push(l, "**The abstract tree keeps its contract**: a body that recovered is complete in the concrete")
    strs_push(l, "tree and absent from the abstract one, exactly as a failed body was, so the checker never")
    strs_push(l, "sees a statement list with a hole in it and the signature still serves every caller.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Cascades.** A later independent mistake in the same function is its own diagnostic. When")
    strs_push(l, "the item's delimiters do not balance, which block a later statement belongs to is what the")
    strs_push(l, "mistake made ambiguous, so after its first recovery the item's further syntax diagnostics")
    strs_push(l, "are withheld until the next item begins. Measured against the pre-N15 parser on 4,240")
    strs_push(l, "single-token deletions and duplications of real programs: the first diagnostic and the")
    strs_push(l, "abstract tree identical in every case, no diagnostic lost, one case with one more.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it costs**, measured in process (`performance.md`): the whole compiler written in Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "(606 KB) parses in 28.9 ms against 14.3 ms, with 29.2 MB peak heap against 15.8 MB, and a")
    strs_push(l, "retained tree of 2.7 MB. Every parse builds the tree, the compiler's included; it is built")
    strs_push(l, "and dropped when only the abstract tree is wanted. Removing that cost would mean a parse")
    strs_push(l, "path that builds only one tree, which is a second path; it has not been taken.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Still future work.** Full-file parsing only: no incremental relexing, no subtree reuse, no")
    strs_push(l, "persisted green nodes. Recovery is local at statements inside blocks; errors inside an")
    strs_push(l, "item's signature, a record, an enum or a `use` still skip to the next item. The formatter")
    strs_push(l, "still lays out from tokens — it reads comments from the same scan the tree is built from,")
    strs_push(l, "but not through the tree. No language server, no structured-edit command. The compiler")
    strs_push(l, "written in Nazm has no concrete tree and does not recover; bootstrap parity is about the")
    strs_push(l, "language it accepts, not about this.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.18 The language service and `nazm lsp` — settled by N16, 2026-09-25")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Why `nazm-service` exists.** An editor asks the same questions `nazm check` answers —")
    strs_push(l, "which files, what is wrong, what a name refers to — about text that is not on disk yet, in a")
    strs_push(l, "process that stays alive. Two things needed a home that was not the CLI binary: the loader")
    strs_push(l, "and root discovery, so that the command line and the editor share one module graph rather")
    strs_push(l, "than each having one; and a long-lived owner of open buffers. `crates/nazm-service` holds")
    strs_push(l, "both. It depends on `nazm-span`, `nazm-diag` and `nazm-core` only (`xtask/src/rules.rs`), so")
    strs_push(l, "it can reach the compiler's answers and cannot reach the parser or `nazm-sema` to compute")
    strs_push(l, "its own.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "editor ──stdio── nazm lsp (nazm-cli/src/lsp.rs)       framing, message types, UTF-16")
    strs_push(l, "                     │  byte offsets and paths only")
    strs_push(l, "                     ▼")
    strs_push(l, "              LanguageService (nazm-service)           buffers, versions, one analysis each")
    strs_push(l, "                     │")
    strs_push(l, "        load::load_from(…, Overlaid) ── the loader every command uses")
    strs_push(l, "        nazm_core::analyse           ── the parse and check every command runs")
    strs_push(l, "        Resolution                   ── what each name was resolved to, by identity")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Who owns what.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Concern | Owner |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| open buffers and their versions | `LanguageService` |")
    strs_push(l, "| which files a compilation has, identity of a path, cycles, prelude | `nazm-service/src/load.rs`, reading through a `Sources` — `Disk` for commands, `Overlaid` (buffer first, then disk) for the service |")
    strs_push(l, "| the source root | `nazm-service/src/root.rs`, `decide`, called exactly as `nazm check` calls it; `nazm lsp --source-root` is `nazm check --source-root` |")
    strs_push(l, "| what a program means | `nazm_core::analyse`, which `on_checked_map` is now a wrapper over |")
    strs_push(l, "| where a position is | the document's concrete tree (N15), by the rule below |")
    strs_push(l, "| what a name refers to | `Resolution`: calls by `FnId`, locals by slot of a function, constructions, variants, fields, payload fields |")
    strs_push(l, "| which occurrences an entity has | `ReferenceIndex` (N17, §7.19), derived from `Resolution` and nothing else |")
    strs_push(l, "| byte offset ↔ LSP position | `LineIndex` in `nazm-cli/src/lsp.rs`, and nowhere else |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Where the concrete tree stops.** It answers exactly one question: which token a byte")
    strs_push(l, "offset is on. The rule is fixed — the identifier whose bytes contain the offset, or whose")
    strs_push(l, "last byte is just before it; anything else, including whitespace, comments, punctuation,")
    strs_push(l, "keywords, literals and the end of the file, is on no name. What that identifier *means* is")
    strs_push(l, "read from the resolution, keyed by its span. A name the resolution has no entry for — inside")
    strs_push(l, "a body that did not parse, a type annotation, a built-in — has no definition. **The service")
    strs_push(l, "never resolves a name itself:** no table from names to definitions exists in it, and a unit")
    strs_push(l, "test and the `one resolver` gate keep it that way. N16 needed one addition to the resolution")
    strs_push(l, "for this — each local binding records where its name is written (`LocalDef::span`), so a use")
    strs_push(l, "goes to its definition by slot rather than by spelling.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Current versions.** Every open, change and close bumps a generation and re-analyses every")
    strs_push(l, "open document before returning. A query is answered only from an analysis whose generation")
    strs_push(l, "is current and whose version is the one asked about; diagnostics are published with the")
    strs_push(l, "version they were computed for, and every document's complete set is published every time —")
    strs_push(l, "an empty set included, which is how an editor clears errors. A broken buffer is analysed like")
    strs_push(l, "any other: its diagnostics are current, and a query into its broken body has no answer. The")
    strs_push(l, "previous, clean analysis is not kept.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is deliberately not incremental.** Every open document is loaded, lexed, parsed and")
    strs_push(l, "checked in full as the root of its own compilation on every change. No reparse of a changed")
    strs_push(l, "region, no maintained module graph, no reuse of semantic work between versions, no")
    strs_push(l, "persistent cache read or written: an unsaved buffer is not state `nazm-cache` may record. What")
    strs_push(l, "is reused is the process and the buffers. Measured on the whole compiler written in Nazm, a")
    strs_push(l, "warm edit is about 80 ms on one CPU (`performance.md`) — the evidence that incremental")
    strs_push(l, "reparse is not yet needed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Protocol surface.** Full-document synchronisation, `publishDiagnostics`, definition and")
    strs_push(l, "hover, positions in UTF-16 — and, since N17, references (§7.19), since N18 prepare-rename")
    strs_push(l, "and rename (§7.20), since N19 completion (§7.21), since N20 signature help (§7.22), since")
    strs_push(l, "N21 structure completion and constructor signature help (§7.23), since N22 document and")
    strs_push(l, "workspace symbols (§7.24), since N23 `semanticTokens/full` (§7.25), since N24 quick")
    strs_push(l, "fixes over `textDocument/codeAction` (§7.26), since N25 call hierarchy (§7.27), and since")
    strs_push(l, "N26 completion at a structured hole with `.` as the one trigger character (§7.28). Nothing")
    strs_push(l, "else is advertised. The core prelude has no file, so a")
    strs_push(l, "definition in it has no location. Diagnostics keep their Nazm codes and messages; the")
    strs_push(l, "protocol message is an adapter's rendering of a `nazm.diagnostic/1` object's primary span,")
    strs_push(l, "not a new schema.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.19 The reference index and `textDocument/references` — settled by N17, 2026-09-25")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a reference is.** A source occurrence that the current analysis resolved to a")
    strs_push(l, "specific entity — exactly the spans `Resolution` recorded an answer for. Not an identifier")
    strs_push(l, "with a matching spelling, not a mention in a comment or a string, not a name the checker")
    strs_push(l, "could not resolve, and not a token the concrete tree merely knows is a name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "CST             → which token a position is on        (N15, the service's cursor rule)")
    strs_push(l, "Resolution      → which entity that occurrence is      (the checker, and only the checker)")
    strs_push(l, "ReferenceIndex  → which occurrences an entity has      (N17: Resolution read backwards)")
    strs_push(l, "LSP adapter     → UTF-16 ranges and `includeDeclaration` (nazm-cli/src/lsp.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the index owns.** `nazm_sema::ReferenceIndex` (`crates/nazm-sema/src/references.rs`)")
    strs_push(l, "is built once per analysis by `ReferenceIndex::of(&Resolution)` and dropped with it. It holds")
    strs_push(l, "every indexed occurrence — declaration or use — with its entity, and for each entity its")
    strs_push(l, "declaration and its uses, apart. It is derived from two things the resolution already has:")
    strs_push(l, "the definition tables (functions and their locals, records and their fields, enums, their")
    strs_push(l, "variants and their payload fields), read by position; and the use answers the checker")
    strs_push(l, "recorded, read by span (`Resolution::each_use`, crate-private). **It resolves nothing**: it")
    strs_push(l, "never reads a name to decide what anything means, holds no scope, and a unit test keeps every")
    strs_push(l, "spelling-keyed search out of the file. A declaration is not a use of itself: the span where a")
    strs_push(l, "`let` introduces its binding, which the checker records for the backend, is the binding's")
    strs_push(l, "declaration and is not in its uses.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Identity.** `ReferenceTarget` is resolution's own identity and nothing stronger:")
    strs_push(l, "`Function(FnId)`, `Local(LocalRef)`, `Record(RecordId)`, `Variant(VariantRef)`,")
    strs_push(l, "`Field(FieldRef)`, `PayloadField(PayloadRef)`. Every one is **session-local** — valid in one")
    strs_push(l, "compilation — and none is persisted: `nazm.interface/5` and `SEMANTIC_EPOCH` 7 are unchanged,")
    strs_push(l, "because an interface describes what an importer needs, not where anybody uses it. A durable")
    strs_push(l, "identity exists for top-level definitions (`DefKey`) and is not needed here; a local has only")
    strs_push(l, "its slot, and stable local identity across edits is not claimed. One adjustment is made, and")
    strs_push(l, "it is not a resolution: a use through an applied type (`Box[Int]`) is taken to the definition")
    strs_push(l, "it applies, by the type table's own `Instance` record, so a generic record's field has one set")
    strs_push(l, "of uses however many instances reach it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What `Resolution` gained.** Two narrow things, both recorded where the checker already knew")
    strs_push(l, "them. A variable use now records **which function's** slot it is (`LocalRef { function, slot")
    strs_push(l, "}`; `Resolution::var` still returns the slot the backend reads, and `Resolution::local` the")
    strs_push(l, "pair), so a use is not placed by working out which body a span is in. And a record")
    strs_push(l, "construction's initialiser label records **which field** it names — the checker looked the")
    strs_push(l, "field up there and discarded the answer — so a field's uses include the constructions that set")
    strs_push(l, "it. Neither changes what any program means, and the backend and interpreter read neither.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Definition and references are one lookup.** The service takes the occurrence under a")
    strs_push(l, "position to its entity through the index; definition is that entity's declaration, references")
    strs_push(l, "are its uses. They cannot disagree about what a name means, because neither decides it. One")
    strs_push(l, "consequence, deliberate: definition on a *declaration* now answers with that declaration (N16")
    strs_push(l, "answered it for a `let` and not for a function), and definition on a construction label now")
    strs_push(l, "answers with the field.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Which program a query covers.** The current snapshot: every compilation the service holds —")
    strs_push(l, "one rooted at each open document, loaded exactly as `nazm check <that document>` would load it")
    strs_push(l, "— that contains the file declaring the entity, with the same text. Identity does not cross")
    strs_push(l, "compilations, so an entity is carried from one to another by **where it is declared**: the")
    strs_push(l, "same bytes of the same file, analysed from the same text, are the same declaration in each,")
    strs_push(l, "and each compilation's own index answers what its uses are. Uses are merged by file and span,")
    strs_push(l, "so one found by two compilations is listed once, and ordered by file path, then start, then")
    strs_push(l, "end. A file that no open document's compilation loads is in no program being analysed and is")
    strs_push(l, "not searched: there is no scan of the disk and no persistent symbol index.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Current means current.** The index is part of an analysis snapshot: replaced on every open,")
    strs_push(l, "change and close with the analysis it was read from, never kept across generations, and")
    strs_push(l, "answered only for the version asked about. A body that did not parse has no resolution, so its")
    strs_push(l, "names are no one's references — the concrete tree knowing a name is there does not make it")
    strs_push(l, "one. `retained()` and `indexed()` are functions of what is open now.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What has no references.** A built-in (it declares nothing), a type parameter, and anything")
    strs_push(l, "in a body that did not parse. Until N18 a type name in an annotation or a generic argument, and")
    strs_push(l, "the enum name in `E.V(…)`, had none either; they are occurrences now (§7.20). A core-prelude")
    strs_push(l, "entity has uses in files and no declaration an editor can open, and the prelude's own uses are")
    strs_push(l, "not navigable.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is deliberately not here.** Rename, prepare-rename, any edit, call hierarchy, a")
    strs_push(l, "general semantic graph, a persistent index, incremental invalidation (the index is rebuilt")
    strs_push(l, "with its analysis), and MCP. The only edges are *occurrence → entity* and its reverse.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.20 Type-name identity, safe rename and stale-safe edit plans — settled by N18, 2026-09-25")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Four layers, each owning one thing, and the rule that binds them:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "Resolution      the entity each occurrence is                  (the checker)")
    strs_push(l, "ReferenceIndex  entity → occurrences                            (§7.19, Resolution read backwards)")
    strs_push(l, "RenamePlan      a complete, validated edit set + preconditions  (nazm-service/src/rename.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "LSP adapter     prepareRename, rename, versioned WorkspaceEdit  (nazm-cli/src/lsp.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **Rename never resolves by spelling and never uses a text search to complete a semantic")
    strs_push(l, "> occurrence set.** An entity whose occurrences are not all recorded is not renamed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Type names now have identity (N18A).** Every user-defined type's name is resolved at one of")
    strs_push(l, "two places in the checker — `resolve_written_inner`, for a type written in full (a parameter,")
    strs_push(l, "a return, a record field's or a payload field's type, a type argument at any depth, a call's")
    strs_push(l, "explicit type argument), and `Checker::resolve_type`, for a construction's head and the enum")
    strs_push(l, "before the `.` of a variant construction or a pattern. Both now record the answer they already")
    strs_push(l, "reached (`Resolution::record_type_name`, `TypeNode` by span), so a written type is an")
    strs_push(l, "occurrence of the record or enum it names, and `ReferenceTarget` gains `Enum(EnumId)`. In")
    strs_push(l, "`State.Ready()` the qualifier is the enum and `Ready` the variant — two occurrences, two")
    strs_push(l, "entities. A built-in type and a type parameter are not recorded: neither is a definition a")
    strs_push(l, "program wrote. Definition and references answer on written types and qualifiers through the")
    strs_push(l, "same lookup as everything else — N16's type-annotation gap, closed as a consequence.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Coverage is explicit, and gated.** `ReferenceTarget::rename_coverage` states, per kind, that")
    strs_push(l, "every position the grammar gives it is recorded; it is an exhaustive `match`, so a new kind")
    strs_push(l, "cannot be added without answering. A new *position* for an existing kind is held by a corpus")
    strs_push(l, "gate (`every_name_token_of_the_corpus_is_indexed_or_is_not_an_entity`): every identifier token")
    strs_push(l, "of every clean compilation of the repository's own source is either indexed or one of a short,")
    strs_push(l, "syntactically recognised list of non-entities — a built-in type or call, a type parameter, `_`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Kind | Declaration | Uses recorded | Rename |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| function | its name | every call, `spawn` included | complete |")
    strs_push(l, "| local | parameter, `let`, pattern binding | every mention and assignment | complete |")
    strs_push(l, "| record | its name | constructions; every written type (parameter, return, field, payload, type argument at any depth) | complete |")
    strs_push(l, "| enum | its name | every written type; the qualifier of every variant construction and pattern | complete |")
    strs_push(l, "| variant | its name | the name after `.` in every construction and pattern | complete |")
    strs_push(l, "| field | its name | projections, assignment paths, construction labels | complete |")
    strs_push(l, "| payload field | its name | construction labels, pattern labels | complete |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The safe scope.** A plan's occurrence universe must be provably complete, and two scopes are,")
    strs_push(l, "from the language's own rules: a **local**, written only inside its function's body; and a")
    strs_push(l, "**private** top-level entity with what it owns (a private record's fields, a private enum's")
    strs_push(l, "variants and payload fields), which only its own module can name — resolution binds another")
    strs_push(l, "module's names only to an import's exports, and `N0337` refuses a public item that would expose")
    strs_push(l, "a private type, so no value of one reaches another module. Both put every occurrence in the")
    strs_push(l, "declaring file, which a clean analysis resolved in full. An **exported** entity is refused: any")
    strs_push(l, "file under any source root may import its module, the service knows only the programs rooted at")
    strs_push(l, "open documents, and a directory an editor opened is not a project. No manifest is invented to")
    strs_push(l, "make it one. A **core-prelude** entity is refused as toolchain-owned; a built-in or a type")
    strs_push(l, "parameter is not an entity.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The plan.** `LanguageService::rename(path, version, offset, new_name)` returns a `RenamePlan` —")
    strs_push(l, "the entity's kind, old and new names, the service generation, and for each file edited its")
    strs_push(l, "path, the open document's version (or none), the **exact text** the plan was computed from, and")
    strs_push(l, "the edits, each `start..end` with the bytes it expects and its replacement, ordered and")
    strs_push(l, "disjoint. The exact text rather than `nazm-cache`'s `SourceFingerprint`: the service may not")
    strs_push(l, "depend on the cache (`rules.rs`), and the bytes themselves, which it already holds, are a")
    strs_push(l, "stronger precondition than a digest of them. `plan_is_current` holds only while the generation,")
    strs_push(l, "every version and every text are unchanged. The service writes nothing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Validation.** The new name must be one identifier by the lexer every compilation uses (not a")
    strs_push(l, "keyword, not `_`, not empty, not punctuation). The program must be clean before: a resolution")
    strs_push(l, "with errors is not a complete account of uses. Then the candidate — the buffers with the edits")
    strs_push(l, "applied in memory — is loaded and checked by the same loader and checker, once for every open")
    strs_push(l, "compilation containing the edited file, and must have no diagnostics, which is where every")
    strs_push(l, "collision (two definitions, a built-in's name, one scope's two bindings) is found — the rename")
    strs_push(l, "engine decides none of them. And its occurrences must group into entities exactly as the old")
    strs_push(l, "program's did, with the old offsets moved past the edits: same groups, same kinds, ids ignored.")
    strs_push(l, "So a rename that captures a use into another binding, merges or splits entities, or loses a")
    strs_push(l, "resolution is refused though it checks. A top-level rename changes the entity's `DefKey` and")
    strs_push(l, "may change its module's `InterfaceHash`; that is what renaming means, and neither is compared.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The protocol cannot carry the plan's precondition, so the adapter refuses what it cannot")
    strs_push(l, "protect.** LSP can tie an edit to an open document's **version**; a `null` version means \"the")
    strs_push(l, "disk is the master\", with no check of what the disk holds, and there is no content precondition")
    strs_push(l, "for any file. So `rename` answers only with versioned `documentChanges` (never `changes`), only")
    strs_push(l, "to a client that declares `workspaceEdit.documentChanges`, and only when every file the plan")
    strs_push(l, "edits is an open document; otherwise it is refused with `RequestFailed` and the reason. Every")
    strs_push(l, "rename N18 allows edits only its declaring file, which is the document asked about, so the")
    strs_push(l, "closed-file refusal is the rule's guarantee rather than a case that arises today.")
    strs_push(l, "`prepareRename` returns the token's range and spelling, or `null`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** Rename of an exported or prelude entity, any other code action, an edit command")
    strs_push(l, "(`nazm rename --apply` was not needed and does not exist), a general edit engine, and any")
    strs_push(l, "schema: rename is standard protocol traffic.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.21 Scope at a position, and completion — settled by N19, 2026-09-25")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **Completion does not resolve names. It enumerates the semantic candidates the checker")
    strs_push(l, "> recorded as available.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "Checker          decides what is visible where — its frames, its lookups, its environments")
    strs_push(l, "ScopeTrace       records those decisions as the checker makes them   (nazm-sema/src/scope.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "CST              says which kind of name a position expects           (the node around the token)")
    strs_push(l, "LanguageService  intersects the two, for the current document only    (nazm-service/src/completion.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "LSP adapter      renders ordered CompletionItems, UTF-16 at the edge  (nazm-cli/src/lsp.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the checker records.** `Resolution::scopes()` is a `ScopeTrace`, written at the points")
    strs_push(l, "the checker already acts: every scope it pushes — a function's parameters (`f.span`), every")
    strs_push(l, "block (`b.span`: a body, an `if` branch, a `while` body, `scope { … }`, a block expression) and")
    strs_push(l, "every match arm (`arm.span`) — with its parent; every binding it defines, with **the byte it")
    strs_push(l, "becomes visible from** and **the binding its own lookup found under that name** at that")
    strs_push(l, "moment, which it now hides; each definition's type parameters over the definition, with the")
    strs_push(l, "type name each hides (again the checker's lookup); and each module's environment as the checker")
    strs_push(l, "built it — built-ins (`Intrinsic::ALL`), own and directly imported functions, own and directly")
    strs_push(l, "imported types, the built-in types (`Type::ALL`, `Vec`) — **less every name it refused** as an")
    strs_push(l, "ambiguous import or a collision with a local definition.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Scope | Opens | Closes | What enters it, visible from |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| function | its declaration | its end | each parameter, after its name |")
    strs_push(l, "| block | `{` | `}` | each `let`, after the end of its statement — never in its own initializer |")
    strs_push(l, "| match arm | the pattern | the arm's end | each pattern binding, after its name; never a sibling arm |")
    strs_push(l, "| module | — | — | every function and type in the module's environment, in any order (declarations are collected before bodies) |")
    strs_push(l, "| type parameters | a function, record or enum | its end | its type parameters, in type positions only |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Reading it back resolves nothing.** `ScopeTrace::visible_at(module, file, offset)` finds the")
    strs_push(l, "innermost frame around the position and walks its parents; a binding is visible if it was")
    strs_push(l, "introduced at or before the position; one is hidden if a visible binding recorded that it")
    strs_push(l, "hides it; a binding the checker refused as a same-scope duplicate names nothing, and neither")
    strs_push(l, "does the one it collided with. No name is compared with another anywhere in the file, which a")
    strs_push(l, "unit test holds. The answer is three lists by namespace — values (locals), callables (functions")
    strs_push(l, "and built-ins) and types — because the language keeps them apart: a record and a function may")
    strs_push(l, "share a spelling, and there are no function values.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**When the scope is complete.** The checker saw a recovered tree wherever N15 recovered, and a")
    strs_push(l, "recovered statement may have been a declaration it never saw. So a position's **locals** are")
    strs_push(l, "offered only when the function around it parsed without recovery, and a module's **functions")
    strs_push(l, "and types** only when no file of the compilation needed recovery (`Analysis::syntax_errors`).")
    strs_push(l, "Otherwise there is no answer (`NoCompletion::RecoveredSyntax`) rather than a list that could")
    strs_push(l, "be missing a name. A type error, an undefined name or a refused duplicate is not a recovery:")
    strs_push(l, "the checker's scope is still its own, and completion answers from it. A stale version is never")
    strs_push(l, "answered, and the last clean analysis is never consulted.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The service.** `LanguageService::scope_at(path, version, offset)` answers at any position, not")
    strs_push(l, "only on a name. `LanguageService::completion(path, version, offset)` completes the identifier")
    strs_push(l, "under the cursor: the node around it chooses the context — `NameRef` or an assignment's root")
    strs_push(l, "is a **value**, `CallExpr`'s head a **call**, `Type` a **type** — and the candidates are that")
    strs_push(l, "namespace's, filtered by exact byte prefix of what is written up to the cursor, ordered by")
    strs_push(l, "name then identity, each with the hover-style detail the resolution already has and its")
    strs_push(l, "declaration's location. An accepted completion replaces the whole identifier. It is one")
    strs_push(l, "document's compilation: another open program's names never enter it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not here.** Completion of a field after `.`, a variant after `E.`, a construction")
    strs_push(l, "or payload label, a pattern, an import path; auto-import; trigger characters; ranking; fuzzy")
    strs_push(l, "matching; signature help. Nothing is persisted: the trace lives and dies with its analysis.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.22 The call at a position, and signature help — settled by N20, 2026-09-26")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **N20 does not perform call resolution. It reports call resolution that already happened.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "CST              which call's argument list holds the position, which argument   (the tree's nesting)")
    strs_push(l, "Checker          which callee the call resolved to, the signature its arguments   (nazm-core/src/check/)")
    strs_push(l, "                 were checked against, what a generic call settled")
    strs_push(l, "CheckedCall      records those as the checker decides them                         (nazm-sema/src/resolve.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "LanguageService  joins the two, for the current document only                     (nazm-service/src/signature.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "LSP adapter      renders one SignatureHelp, UTF-16 at the edge                     (nazm-cli/src/lsp.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the checker records.** `Resolution::checked_call(callee_span)` is a `CheckedCall`, written")
    strs_push(l, "wherever the checker checks a call or a `spawn` against a callee it resolved — whether or not")
    strs_push(l, "the arguments then fitted: the `Callee` (`Function(FnId)` or `Builtin(Intrinsic)`), the call's")
    strs_push(l, "and each parsed argument's span, and the parameter and return types **exactly as the module's")
    strs_push(l, "environment gave them** — a function's own signature, an import's from the interface it was")
    strs_push(l, "checked against, a built-in's from `Intrinsic::ALL`. For a generic callee it adds an")
    strs_push(l, "`Instantiation`: whether the type arguments were written, each one the checker settled (`None`")
    strs_push(l, "where it settled none, which it has reported), and the parameters and result with the settled")
    strs_push(l, "arguments in place, computed by `UserTypes::substituted` — which reads the type table and adds")
    strs_push(l, "nothing to it, so recording changes no type id and nothing a backend emits. A call whose")
    strs_push(l, "callee did not resolve is not recorded. Keyed by the callee's span, like `Resolution::callee`,")
    strs_push(l, "and session-local; it is not a call graph and nothing about compilation reads it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Which call, which argument.** The service walks down the one path of tree nodes containing")
    strs_push(l, "the position and keeps the last call or `spawn` whose argument list holds it — strictly after")
    strs_push(l, "its `(` and no later than its `)`. On the callee, before the `(`, and after the `)` the")
    strs_push(l, "position is in no call. The active argument is the number of that `ArgList`'s **own** `,`")
    strs_push(l, "tokens ending at or before the position: a comma of a nested call, a construction, a")
    strs_push(l, "parenthesised expression or a type argument list belongs to another node, and one in a string")
    strs_push(l, "or a comment is not a comma token. Then the call is looked up by its callee's span; no record")
    strs_push(l, "means no answer (`NoCall::NotChecked`) — a callee that did not resolve, whatever it is spelled.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Position | Answer |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| on the callee, or before `(` | none |")
    strs_push(l, "| just after `(`, before the first argument | argument 0 |")
    strs_push(l, "| inside an argument, or just before the `,` after it | that argument |")
    strs_push(l, "| just after a `,` | the next argument |")
    strs_push(l, "| inside a nested call's argument list | the nested call |")
    strs_push(l, "| just before `)` | the last argument (or 0 when there are none) |")
    strs_push(l, "| after `)` | none — not the nearest call |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**When there is an answer.** One document at its current version, from its own compilation;")
    strs_push(l, "never an earlier clean one. None when any file of the compilation needed syntax recovery")
    strs_push(l, "(`NoCall::RecoveredSyntax`, the rule N19 applies to module names): a lost declaration could")
    strs_push(l, "have changed what the call resolved to. Too few arguments, too many and wrong argument types")
    strs_push(l, "do not stop it — the checker still resolved the callee. The active *parameter* is the active")
    strs_push(l, "argument when the callee has a parameter there, and none otherwise: for a callee with no")
    strs_push(l, "parameters, and for an argument past the last one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**One signature, one spelling.** `Signature` is structured — callee, name, type parameters with")
    strs_push(l, "whether each requires `Equality`, parameters with their declared names and types, result — and")
    strs_push(l, "`Signature::render` is the only place a signature becomes text: hover, completion's detail and")
    strs_push(l, "signature help all call it, so they cannot disagree. A function's parameter names are its first")
    strs_push(l, "slots, which the checker bound; a built-in's are not named by the inventory, so it shows types")
    strs_push(l, "only (`fn str_len(Str) -> Int`). Rendered with a call's instantiation, the settled arguments")
    strs_push(l, "replace the parameters: `fn identity[T](x: T) -> T` is shown at `identity(1)` as")
    strs_push(l, "`fn identity[Int](x: Int) -> Int`; the declared form, with `[T: Equality]`, is what hover shows.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The protocol.** One `SignatureInformation`, parameters as offsets into the label in UTF-16,")
    strs_push(l, "`activeSignature` 0; triggered by `(` and `,`, with no retrigger characters. Past the last")
    strs_push(l, "parameter of an over-long call the answer is `null`, because the protocol reads an absent active")
    strs_push(l, "parameter as the first; a callee with no parameters has its signature and no active parameter.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not here.** Signature help for a record construction or a variant construction")
    strs_push(l, "(neither is a call; each would be a label contract of its own); documentation; overloads, which")
    strs_push(l, "the language does not have; call hierarchy. Nothing is persisted: the records live and die with")
    strs_push(l, "their analysis.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.23 Structure at a position — settled by N21, 2026-09-26")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **N21's language-service and LSP layers never resolve fields, variants, records, enums or")
    strs_push(l, "> types by spelling.** Structure queries consume semantic identities recorded by the checker.")
    strs_push(l, "> The one incomplete-source exception is `E.name` before `(` exists: after `E` fails as a value,")
    strs_push(l, "> the checker itself consults its existing module type environment and may record a non-generic")
    strs_push(l, "> enum as a tooling anchor. This is the canonical checker environment, not a second resolver.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "CST              which structured site the position is in:                (the node around the name)")
    strs_push(l, "                 a field after `.`, a variant after `E.`, a label")
    strs_push(l, "Checker          which record, enum or variant that site belongs to,      (nazm-core/src/check/)")
    strs_push(l, "                 and every field's and variant's identity")
    strs_push(l, "StructureSite    joins the two, for the current document                  (nazm-service/src/structure.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "Completion       enumerates that record's fields, enum's variants or")
    strs_push(l, "                 variant's payload fields")
    strs_push(l, "Constructor help renders the construction's record or variant shape")
    strs_push(l, "LSP adapter      byte spans to UTF-16                                     (nazm-cli/src/lsp.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What was already there.** Every name the checker resolved inside a structure is already in the")
    strs_push(l, "resolution, keyed by its span: a projection's or an initialiser's field (`FieldRef`), a")
    strs_push(l, "construction's record (`construction`), a variant construction's or pattern's variant")
    strs_push(l, "(`VariantRef`), a payload label (`PayloadRef`). A record or enum identity of an applied generic")
    strs_push(l, "is its **instance**, whose fields and payloads the type table substituted once, when the")
    strs_push(l, "instance was made. So a site whose name resolved needs nothing new: `Pair[Int, Str]`'s `first`")
    strs_push(l, "is `first: Int` because the instance says so.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What was added to the checker.** One narrow fact, `Resolution::looked_up_on(span)`: the type")
    strs_push(l, "a member name **that did not resolve** was looked for on — the record an unknown field was")
    strs_push(l, "looked for on (`check_projection`), the enum an unknown variant was looked for in")
    strs_push(l, "(`find_variant`, for constructions and patterns alike), and, for `E.name` written before its")
    strs_push(l, "`(` exists, the enum `E` names in the module's types when `E` is no value and the enum is not")
    strs_push(l, "generic. It is written only where a lookup failed, so a program that checks holds **none** —")
    strs_push(l, "there is no per-expression type table, no copy of any definition, and no index. The")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostics are unchanged: the last case records what the checker's own environment says and")
    strs_push(l, "reports exactly what it reported before.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The sites.** `LanguageService::structure_at(path, version, offset)` finds the node around the")
    strs_push(l, "identifier and answers only where the name is a member position:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Site | Anchor | Candidates |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| a projection's or an assignment place's field, after `.` | the field's record, or the record it was looked for on | the record's fields |")
    strs_push(l, "| a variant construction's or pattern's variant, after `E.` | the variant's enum, or the enum it was looked for in | the enum's variants |")
    strs_push(l, "| `E.name` with no `(` yet | the enum `E` names, when not generic | the enum's variants |")
    strs_push(l, "| a record construction's label | the construction's record | its fields, less those given elsewhere |")
    strs_push(l, "| a variant construction's or pattern's payload label | the variant | its payload fields, less those given elsewhere |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A label given elsewhere is excluded **by the identity the checker recorded for it**; a label")
    strs_push(l, "that did not resolve excludes nothing, and the label under the cursor is never counted as")
    strs_push(l, "given — it is the one being replaced. A pattern's binding (`code: c`'s `c`) is a local, not a")
    strs_push(l, "label, and is N19's. Candidates keep their identities (`Candidate::Entity(Field | Variant |")
    strs_push(l, "PayloadField)`) and come in the definition's **canonical** order — fields and payloads by")
    strs_push(l, "`in_layout_order`, variants by `in_tag_order`, both sorted by name, the order the backend")
    strs_push(l, "already uses — because declaration order means nothing in this language, and a tool that showed")
    strs_push(l, "it would make an edit with no meaning observable. Details are the field's type (`value: Int`)")
    strs_push(l, "or the variant's payload shape (`Done(code: Int)`), from the instance.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Constructor signature help** is not function signature help: a construction has no callee")
    strs_push(l, "and runs no function, so it is its own `Constructor::Record | Variant`, never a `Callee` or a")
    strs_push(l, "`CheckedCall`. `LanguageService::help_at` finds the innermost call and the innermost")
    strs_push(l, "construction by the same rule — strictly after the `(`, no later than the `)` — and answers the")
    strs_push(l, "one whose parentheses open later: a call written in an initialiser is answered as the call, a")
    strs_push(l, "construction written as an argument as the construction. The label is the instance's name and")
    strs_push(l, "its fields in canonical order — `Point(label: Str, x: Int)`, `Box[Int](value: Int)`,")
    strs_push(l, "`Maybe[Int].Some(value: Int)` — rendered by the same list renderer as a function's parameters.")
    strs_push(l, "The active parameter is **the field whose initialiser holds the position, by its label's")
    strs_push(l, "identity**, at its canonical position; initialisers are named and in any order, so how many")
    strs_push(l, "precede it says nothing. Between initialisers, and on a label that did not resolve, no field is")
    strs_push(l, "active; the protocol then gets the label without parameters, because an absent index would")
    strs_push(l, "mark the first. `call_at` and `signature_help` are N20's, unchanged: they answer the innermost")
    strs_push(l, "call.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**When there is an answer.** One document at its current version, from its own compilation;")
    strs_push(l, "never an earlier one. A candidate list comes from a definition and its anchor from the")
    strs_push(l, "checker's reading of the site's function and of the module's names, and both are complete when")
    strs_push(l, "every other file of the compilation parsed without recovery and every recovery in the document")
    strs_push(l, "lies inside the body of a function other than the one the position is in — a recovered")
    strs_push(l, "statement there can neither lose a declaration the module's names need nor change a local this")
    strs_push(l, "site reads. A recovery at the top level, in a declaration, in the site's own function or in")
    strs_push(l, "another file refuses (`RecoveredSyntax`); a site the checker anchored nowhere refuses")
    strs_push(l, "(`Unanchored`) whatever it is spelled.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not here.** Completion with nothing written after `.` or `(` (the source does not")
    strs_push(l, "parse, so nothing anchors it) and therefore no `.` trigger character; methods, which the")
    strs_push(l, "language does not have; import paths, auto-import, ranking; documentation. Nothing is")
    strs_push(l, "persisted.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.24 Document and workspace symbols — settled by N22, 2026-09-26")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **A symbol is a declaration the current analysis declared. Symbols are never reconstructed")
    strs_push(l, "> by scanning identifier spellings, and workspace symbols do not establish a complete Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "> project boundary and therefore do not close N18's exported-rename limitation.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "Checker          which declarations exist, and what each is:          (nazm-sema definition tables)")
    strs_push(l, "                 FnId, RecordId + field, EnumId + variant + payload field")
    strs_push(l, "Parsed items     where each is written: the item the table's `decl`   (nazm-syntax Program, via Analysis)")
    strs_push(l, "                 index names, and the child whose name span matches")
    strs_push(l, "Symbol view      source-backed declarations, nested, derived on demand (nazm-service/src/symbols.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "LanguageService  which files are analysed now: every file of every")
    strs_push(l, "                 compilation rooted at an open document")
    strs_push(l, "DocumentSymbol   one file's declarations, in source order")
    strs_push(l, "WorkspaceSymbol  every analysed file's, once each, filtered by a substring")
    strs_push(l, "LSP adapter      protocol kinds, nesting or its flat form, UTF-16        (nazm-cli/src/lsp.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What was already there.** Everything. The checker's definition tables hold every declared")
    strs_push(l, "function, record, enum, variant, field and payload field with its identity (the same")
    strs_push(l, "`ReferenceTarget` references and rename use) and its `name_span`; each function, record and")
    strs_push(l, "enum also carries `decl`, its index in the parsed `Program` the resolution was produced from, so")
    strs_push(l, "its item — and the item's span, the whole declaration — is one index away. A field, variant or")
    strs_push(l, "payload field is found inside its parent's item by its name span: a position, never a spelling.")
    strs_push(l, "N22 added no checker fact, no table and no index. An applied generic's instance is not a")
    strs_push(l, "declaration and is skipped, as the reference index skips it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a symbol is, exactly.** It exists when the checker declared something:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Source | Symbol? |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| a function, record or enum the checker declared, private or `pub` | yes, with its visibility kept as metadata |")
    strs_push(l, "| a function whose body did not parse (the parser keeps its signature) | yes; its range ends where the parser's item does |")
    strs_push(l, "| a body with type errors | yes: existence is not a clean body |")
    strs_push(l, "| an item the parser could not read | no — nothing was declared, and an outline of text is not this contract |")
    strs_push(l, "| a second function, type, variant or field the checker refused as a duplicate | no; the first keeps its symbol |")
    strs_push(l, "| a function that collides with an import | yes, in its own file; the import's is in the dependency's |")
    strs_push(l, "| locals, parameters, pattern bindings, type parameters | no: an outline is structure, and scope is N19's |")
    strs_push(l, "| built-ins, intrinsics, the core prelude's `Option` and `Result` | no: there is no file an editor can open |")
    strs_push(l, "| a definition rehydrated from a persisted interface | no: its spans are synthetic and its `decl` is none |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The language service never checks against a persisted interface — it reads source or reports")
    strs_push(l, "the module missing — so the last row is guarded twice rather than reachable: a synthetic span")
    strs_push(l, "is never a symbol, and an item must sit at `decl` with the same name span.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Range and selection.** A symbol's range is the parsed item's span (from `pub` or the keyword")
    strs_push(l, "to the closing brace; a field's `name: Type`; a variant's name to its `)`); its selection is the")
    strs_push(l, "table's `name_span` — the span definition goes to from any use, and the span the reference")
    strs_push(l, "index records the declaration at, so the two cannot disagree. A symbol's range holds its")
    strs_push(l, "selection and a parent's range holds each child's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Order.** A document's symbols are in **source order** — the order the author wrote them —")
    strs_push(l, "at every level. That is deliberately not N21's canonical order: declaration order means nothing")
    strs_push(l, "to what a record or enum *is*, which is why candidates and constructor help are canonical, but")
    strs_push(l, "an outline presents the file, and moving two fields does move them in it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The workspace universe.** `LanguageService::workspace_symbols(query)` covers every file of")
    strs_push(l, "every compilation the service holds at the current generation: each open document's")
    strs_push(l, "compilation, loaded exactly as `nazm check <it>` would load it, with everything it imports.")
    strs_push(l, "That is the union of the open roots and their loaded dependency graphs — **not** a directory:")
    strs_push(l, "there is no filesystem walk, no manifest, no persistent index and no watcher, and a `.nz` file no")
    strs_push(l, "open document's compilation loads is never read. Unlike completion, definition and signature")
    strs_push(l, "help, which belong to the one requesting compilation, it deliberately spans every open root,")
    strs_push(l, "and it does not apply import visibility: the question is what exists, not what one file may")
    strs_push(l, "name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**One declaration, however many compilations load it.** Identity does not cross")
    strs_push(l, "compilations, so a declaration is carried across them as N17 carries an entity: the same file")
    strs_push(l, "(by identity path), the same kind, the same name span. `DefKey` is not used: its module key is")
    strs_push(l, "measured from each compilation's source root, so one file can have two keys in two")
    strs_push(l, "compilations, and one reached through a symbolic link has none. Deduplication is by that")
    strs_push(l, "position and never by spelling: two modules' `helper`, a record and a function both called")
    strs_push(l, "`Box`, two records' `value` and two enums' `Ready` are all distinct.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The query.** A case-sensitive substring of the declared name; the empty query is everything.")
    strs_push(l, "It filters a universe already built — it loads, resolves and discovers nothing — and there is")
    strs_push(l, "no fuzzy matching, case folding, ranking or truncation. Results are ordered by name, then file,")
    strs_push(l, "then where the name is, then kind. Fields, variants and payload fields are included, each with")
    strs_push(l, "the name of what it is declared in (`Point`, `State`, `State.Done`), read from its parent.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**When there is an answer.** Document symbols are of one document at its current version,")
    strs_push(l, "from its own compilation, and a superseded version has none (`NotCurrent`); workspace symbols")
    strs_push(l, "are of the current generation only. Both see unsaved buffers at once, and closing a buffer makes")
    strs_push(l, "the disk authoritative for it again. Neither refuses because of a recovery: a symbol is what")
    strs_push(l, "the checker declared, and a recovery can only remove declarations, never invent one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Over the protocol.** `textDocument/documentSymbol` returns nested `DocumentSymbol`s to a client")
    strs_push(l, "that declares `hierarchicalDocumentSymbolSupport` and flat `SymbolInformation`s, each naming its")
    strs_push(l, "container, to one that does not. `workspace/symbol` returns `WorkspaceSymbol`s located at the")
    strs_push(l, "declared name; `resolveProvider` is `false` and there is no `workspaceSymbol/resolve`. Kinds:")
    strs_push(l, "function → Function, record → Struct, enum → Enum, variant → EnumMember, field and payload field")
    strs_push(l, "→ Field.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not here.** Locals in an outline, a syntax outline of text that did not declare")
    strs_push(l, "anything, qualified-name queries, fuzzy search, a project index, symbol tags, semantic tokens,")
    strs_push(l, "call hierarchy and any agent-facing export. Nothing is persisted.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.25 Semantic identifiers and semantic tokens — settled by N23, 2026-09-26")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **N23 never classifies an unresolved identifier by syntactic position or spelling. N23")
    strs_push(l, "> semantic tokens are a semantic-identifier layer, not a replacement for lexical syntax")
    strs_push(l, "> highlighting.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "Checker / Resolution  what each name at each span is                    (nazm-core/src/check/)")
    strs_push(l, "ReferenceIndex        entity occurrences, declarations apart (N17)      (nazm-sema/src/references.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "Resolution            built-in calls; written built-in and type-")
    strs_push(l, "                      parameter names (new, N23)                        (nazm-sema/src/resolve.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "SemanticIdentifier    identity + class + role + exact span, per span     (nazm-service/src/semantic.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "LanguageService       one current document's identifiers, source order")
    strs_push(l, "LSP adapter           static legend, UTF-16, relative encoding           (nazm-cli/src/lsp.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The rule.** The document's concrete tree lists its identifier tokens; each is classified by")
    strs_push(l, "what the compiler recorded at exactly its span, and by nothing else:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Fact at the span | Class | Role |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| an entity in the reference index | its kind; a local is a **parameter** when its slot is one of its function's parameter slots, which the checker allocates first | declaration when the index records the entity declared at this span |")
    strs_push(l, "| a call to a built-in (`Callee::Builtin`) | intrinsic | reference |")
    strs_push(l, "| `WrittenType::Builtin` | built-in type | reference |")
    strs_push(l, "| `WrittenType::Param` / `ParamDeclaration` | type parameter | reference / declaration |")
    strs_push(l, "| nothing | not an identifier | — |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "So an unknown call head is not a function, an unknown member after `.` is not a field, and a")
    strs_push(l, "word in a comment or a string, a keyword or a name in a body that did not parse is nothing.")
    strs_push(l, "Keywords, comments, strings, numbers, operators and punctuation are an editor grammar's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What was already there.** Every program entity: functions, locals (parameters among them),")
    strs_push(l, "records, enums, variants, fields and payload fields, declarations and uses, each by the")
    strs_push(l, "identity references and rename use — N17's index, read by span. Built-in calls, in the")
    strs_push(l, "resolution's call map. Parameterhood needed nothing new: `LocalDef` slots are allocated")
    strs_push(l, "parameters first, and a slot below the function's parameter count is a parameter.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What was added to the checker.** One narrow record, `Resolution::written_type(span)`: the")
    strs_push(l, "written type names the checker resolved to **something no program declares** — a built-in type")
    strs_push(l, "(as the `Type` resolution decided, `Int` as `Type::Int`, the `Vec` of `Vec[Int]` as its vector")
    strs_push(l, "type) or a type parameter (as its `TypeParam`: owner and position) — and each type parameter's")
    strs_push(l, "declaration in its `[…]`. It is written at the two points that already decided these names")
    strs_push(l, "(`resolve_written_inner` and the declaration of a definition's parameters), kept apart from the")
    strs_push(l, "reference index because neither is an entity, and measured in `performance.md`. A function the")
    strs_push(l, "checker refuses for redefining a built-in never has its body checked under an id, so the")
    strs_push(l, "parameter uses resolved in its signature are forgotten rather than left under the id the next")
    strs_push(l, "function receives; a refused *duplicate* is checked as the first definition, as it always has")
    strs_push(l, "been, and its names are classified as the checker made them — its parameters as bindings of the")
    strs_push(l, "first function after that function's own.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Roles and modifiers.** A declaration is marked `declaration`; a use is not; nothing is both.")
    strs_push(l, "`defaultLibrary` marks exactly what is compiler-owned — intrinsics and built-in types — and")
    strs_push(l, "never a source declaration, the core prelude's included: `Option` is an enum like any other.")
    strs_push(l, "There is no `definition`, `readonly` or `modification`: an assignment is a reference.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The legend**, fixed at compile time and pinned by a test: token types `type`, `struct`,")
    strs_push(l, "`enum`, `typeParameter`, `parameter`, `variable`, `property`, `enumMember`, `function`, in that")
    strs_push(l, "order; modifiers `declaration`, `defaultLibrary`. Function → function, intrinsic → function +")
    strs_push(l, "defaultLibrary, parameter → parameter, local → variable, record → struct, enum → enum, variant →")
    strs_push(l, "enumMember, field and payload field → property, type parameter → typeParameter, built-in type →")
    strs_push(l, "type + defaultLibrary. Two display kinds are one LSP type; their identities are not merged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Encoding.** One identifier token is one span, so no span is classified twice, and tokens come")
    strs_push(l, "in source order. The adapter converts each span to a line and UTF-16 columns with the one")
    strs_push(l, "`LineIndex`, and encodes relatively — lines since the previous token, start column relative to")
    strs_push(l, "the previous token on the same line and absolute on a new one, length in UTF-16 units. It")
    strs_push(l, "**refuses** (an error response, never a token array) an identifier list that is out of order,")
    strs_push(l, "overlapping, empty or spanning lines.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**When there is an answer.** One document at its current version, from its own compilation;")
    strs_push(l, "another open program never changes it, and a superseded version has none (`NotCurrent`).")
    strs_push(l, "Unsaved buffers take effect at once and closing one restores the disk. Unlike completion, a")
    strs_push(l, "recovery does not refuse the whole view: what the checker resolved is classified and what it")
    strs_push(l, "did not is omitted, and nothing from an earlier version is ever served.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not here.** `semanticTokens/range` and `semanticTokens/full/delta` (no")
    strs_push(l, "`resultId`, no previous token array, no cache); lexical tokens; read/write distinctions; a")
    strs_push(l, "workspace-wide token query. Nothing is persisted.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.26 Quick fixes from current diagnostics — settled by N24, 2026-09-26")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **N24 does not derive repairs from diagnostic codes, messages, spelling or syntax. It only")
    strs_push(l, "> presents fixes already attached to current compiler diagnostics. Returning a")
    strs_push(l, "> `WorkspaceEdit` is not applying it; the client must send the resulting `didChange` before")
    strs_push(l, "> server state changes.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "Compiler diagnostic   owns its fixes                                     (nazm-diag Fix)")
    strs_push(l, "Fix                   one span (one file), replacement, applicability,")
    strs_push(l, "                      precondition, description")
    strs_push(l, "LanguageService       current diagnostic · current version and generation ·")
    strs_push(l, "                      open document · exact bytes at the span           (nazm-service/src/fixes.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "FixPlan               the fix as one validated, versioned edit")
    strs_push(l, "LSP adapter           quick fix · versioned documentChanges · UTF-16     (nazm-cli/src/lsp.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a fix is.** `nazm_diag::Fix { span, replacement, description, applicability,")
    strs_push(l, "precondition }`: one span, so one edit to one file. `Applicability` is `Automatic` or")
    strs_push(l, "`NeedsReview`, and the precondition is always present. It carries no expected text; the bytes")
    strs_push(l, "at its span in the analysed source are what it expects, and both consumers record them when")
    strs_push(l, "they take the fix.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The plan.** `LanguageService::fix_plans(path, version, start, end)` reads the diagnostics of")
    strs_push(l, "the document's current analysis, keeps those in the document whose primary span the range")
    strs_push(l, "touches (half-open overlap; a cursor touches a span it is inside or at either end of; an empty")
    strs_push(l, "span, a range containing it), and makes one `FixPlan` per fix: the diagnostic, which fix of how")
    strs_push(l, "many, the applicability, description and precondition, the generation, and one N18")
    strs_push(l, "`FileEdit` — path, open version, exact text, and the edit with its expected bytes. The fix's")
    strs_push(l, "span decides the edit, the diagnostic's span only relevance: `mut` goes on the `let`, not on")
    strs_push(l, "the assignment. A fix whose file is not an open document has no plan — there is no version to")
    strs_push(l, "protect it — and neither does one whose span is not a range of the text. One fix has one edit,")
    strs_push(l, "so a plan cannot hold overlapping edits; two fixes of one diagnostic are two plans, which may")
    strs_push(l, "overlap as alternatives, and nothing combines them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Freshness.** `fix_plan_is_current` holds a plan to its generation, to its file being open at")
    strs_push(l, "its version with exactly its text, and to its bytes still being the ones it replaces — through")
    strs_push(l, "`file_is_current`, the one freshness law a rename's plan answers to as well. Version and bytes")
    strs_push(l, "protect different boundaries and both are kept: the bytes, what the server analysed; the")
    strs_push(l, "version, what the client applies to.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Over the protocol.** `codeAction` returns `CodeAction`s of kind `quickfix`, one per plan, each")
    strs_push(l, "with the current diagnostic converted exactly as published and its edit as versioned")
    strs_push(l, "`documentChanges` — the same conversion, and the same refusal, a rename uses: a client that does")
    strs_push(l, "not accept versioned changes, or a file not open, gets no action rather than a weaker edit. An")
    strs_push(l, "automatic fix is `isPreferred` when it is its diagnostic's only fix; a needs-review fix never")
    strs_push(l, "is, and its title carries its precondition. The diagnostics a client sends are not consulted:")
    strs_push(l, "a stale copy cannot resurrect a fix and a fabricated one cannot produce one. `only` asking for")
    strs_push(l, "anything but quick fixes gets an empty list. No refactors, source actions, fix-all, commands,")
    strs_push(l, "`data` or `codeAction/resolve`; nothing is cached between requests.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**`nazm fix` beside it.** The command collects the same fixes and applies the automatic ones to")
    strs_push(l, "disk right to left, skipping overlaps, stale bytes, spans that name no range, and a result that")
    strs_push(l, "would not parse, with each of its seven skip reasons now reached by its own test. It writes and")
    strs_push(l, "can roll back; the server writes nothing and cannot — it relies on each fix being tested to")
    strs_push(l, "parse and to remove its diagnostic, on the bytes being checked, and on the version.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not here.** Edits to files that are not open (N18's gap stands), fix-all,")
    strs_push(l, "refactors, and any fix the compiler does not attach.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.27 Call hierarchy from checked calls — settled by N25, 2026-09-26")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **N25 call hierarchy is a view of the current bound compilation. It does not establish a")
    strs_push(l, "> complete project boundary and does not prove that all possible callers are loaded. An edge")
    strs_push(l, "> exists only because the checker recorded a call from one source function to another; none")
    strs_push(l, "> is inferred from names, references, syntax or text.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "N17  occurrence -> function identity                      (ReferenceIndex)")
    strs_push(l, "N20  checked call -> callee identity                      (CheckedCall, by callee name span)")
    strs_push(l, "     the body being checked -> the calls it made          (FnDef::call_sites, the same point)")
    strs_push(l, "N22  function identity -> source declaration and name     (symbols::function_symbol)")
    strs_push(l, "N25  current source function")
    strs_push(l, "       -> direct checked-call edges, grouped by the function at the other end")
    strs_push(l, "       -> source-backed hierarchy items                    (nazm-service/src/hierarchy.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "LanguageService   binds an item to one current compilation and generation (Locator)")
    strs_push(l, "LSP adapter       opaque locator in item data · UTF-16 · the three standard methods")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Items.** A hierarchy item is a function the checker declared from an item this compilation")
    strs_push(l, "parsed, with the declaration and name ranges of its outline symbol: the outline and the")
    strs_push(l, "hierarchy read both from one function, `function_symbol`, so there is no second location")
    strs_push(l, "table. A built-in or intrinsic has no declaration, the core prelude declares no function, and")
    strs_push(l, "the service loads every module from source, so a function known only from a persisted")
    strs_push(l, "interface does not occur in its compilations; the item builder refuses anything without a")
    strs_push(l, "parsed item in a file an editor can open, and an edge to it is left out rather than given a")
    strs_push(l, "place that does not exist. Records, variants, fields, locals and parameters are never items.")
    strs_push(l, "Generic instantiations are one item: instantiation is call metadata, not identity.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Preparing.** `prepare_call_hierarchy(path, version, offset)` reads the entity the reference")
    strs_push(l, "index records at the name under the cursor — a function's declaration or any call of it — and")
    strs_push(l, "nothing else. It never looks a function up by its spelling; a record called `Box` is not the")
    strs_push(l, "function `Box`. Nazm has no function values, so every non-declaration occurrence of a function")
    strs_push(l, "is a call or a spawn; preparation answers *which function*, and edges answer *which checked")
    strs_push(l, "calls*, separately.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Edges.** Each is read from two facts the checker already keeps, both recorded at the same")
    strs_push(l, "point under the same resolved callee: a `CheckedCall` at the callee's name span (N20), and the")
    strs_push(l, "same span in the `call_sites` of the body the checker was checking. So the caller is read, not")
    strs_push(l, "derived from where a span sits; no per-call state was added. Incoming calls scan every body's")
    strs_push(l, "call sites and keep those whose checked call resolved to the item — O(calls in the")
    strs_push(l, "compilation), with a request-local map from caller to spans that is dropped with the answer.")
    strs_push(l, "Outgoing calls read the item's own call sites — O(its calls). A call site with no checked call")
    strs_push(l, "is no edge (a refused generic `spawn` resolves its name and checks no call), a reference is not")
    strs_push(l, "a call, and a construction is not a call to the checker and is not one here. Calls nested in")
    strs_push(l, "another call's arguments, or inside `if`, `while`, `match` or a block, belong to the function")
    strs_push(l, "whose body holds them. A `spawn f(…)` is a checked call of `f`. A recursive call is an edge to")
    strs_push(l, "itself; mutual recursion is an edge each way; nothing is transitive — one level per request.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Grouping and order.** Edges are grouped by the function at the other end, by identity, never")
    strs_push(l, "by name: two modules' `helper` are two callers. Each edge's ranges are the callee's name at each")
    strs_push(l, "call — the span N17 and N20 key the call by, without type arguments — in source order, each")
    strs_push(l, "once. Edges are ordered by the other end's declaring file, then where its name is, then name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Which program.** An item belongs to the compilation rooted at the document it was prepared")
    strs_push(l, "from, at the generation it was prepared at: callers are the calls known in that compilation —")
    strs_push(l, "the root and everything it imports — and no other. A shared file prepared through two open")
    strs_push(l, "roots gives two items at the same place with different callers; neither is a claim about the")
    strs_push(l, "project, and nothing reads a directory. So N25 does not lift N18's refusal to rename an")
    strs_push(l, "exported definition.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Across requests.** An item carries a `Locator`: the root document's identity path, its")
    strs_push(l, "version, the service generation, and the declaring file and name bytes — a position, never a")
    strs_push(l, "session-local `FnId` or a spelling. Incoming and outgoing calls are answered only while the")
    strs_push(l, "generation, the root's presence and version all still hold, and then from that root's own")
    strs_push(l, "current analysis, where the function is found at exactly those bytes. After any change —")
    strs_push(l, "unrelated ones included — or once the root is closed, the item has no answer and is never")
    strs_push(l, "rebound to another root; it must be prepared again. Nothing is kept between requests: no item")
    strs_push(l, "table and no graph.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Over the protocol.** `callHierarchyProvider` is advertised. An item's `range` is the whole")
    strs_push(l, "declaration and `selectionRange` its name, kind `Function`, detail the shared signature")
    strs_push(l, "renderer's, and `data` the locator's six fields and nothing more — opaque, and not a Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "machine schema. Missing, forged or stale data is answered `null`. Byte ranges become UTF-16")
    strs_push(l, "only in the adapter, through one line index per file text per response.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not here.** A persistent or whole-program call graph, transitive closure,")
    strs_push(l, "filesystem discovery of callers, and any claim that every caller in a project is known.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.28 Completion at a structured hole — settled by N26, 2026-09-27")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **N26 does not infer a receiver, record, enum, variant or construction from spelling.")
    strs_push(l, "> Incomplete-source completion is available only where the canonical compiler can establish")
    strs_push(l, "> one semantic anchor.** `point.`, `State.`, `Point(` and `State.Done(` remain invalid")
    strs_push(l, "> programs; `nazm check` reports them exactly as before.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "Lossless CST / parser     the exact hole: a `.` or `(` token ending at the cursor")
    strs_push(l, "                          (a probe parse: nazm-syntax parse_both_at / parse_map_at)")
    strs_push(l, "Canonical checker         the anchor, at decision points it already has   (nazm-core probe)")
    strs_push(l, "N21 candidate machinery   real FieldRef / VariantRef / PayloadRef candidates (structure::candidates)")
    strs_push(l, "LanguageService           current version · the probe · zero-width completion (incomplete.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "LSP                       \".\" trigger · UTF-16")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Why a probe, not a record in every analysis.** An unfinished statement makes the parser")
    strs_push(l, "drop its function's body, so the ordinary analysis has no receiver, local or scope there — and")
    strs_push(l, "which `.` or `(` is being completed is decided by the editor's cursor, which only the request")
    strs_push(l, "knows; a `.` elsewhere is just broken code. So a completion request at a hole re-parses and")
    strs_push(l, "re-checks the compilation's current sources — the same `SourceMap` and module graph the")
    strs_push(l, "document's analysis loaded, overlays included, never the disk — with the parser told the")
    strs_push(l, "cursor's byte offset (`nazm_core::probe`). Nothing is inserted into any text. At exactly that")
    strs_push(l, "offset, right after the `.` or `(`, the parser reads a zero-width, empty name, which no source")
    strs_push(l, "can spell, and takes the `;` or `)` the unfinished statement leaves unwritten as written, until")
    strs_push(l, "that statement ends; a pattern's hole with no `=>` gets a zero-width body. Everything else is")
    strs_push(l, "parsed and reported as ever. The ordinary parse never takes this path: a parse with no hole")
    strs_push(l, "offset is unchanged, and a probe parse at an offset that is no hole is the ordinary parse")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-syntax/tests/holes.rs`, over the corpus).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The anchor.** The checker decides, at points it already had:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Hole | Anchor |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `receiver.` | the type an unknown member was looked for on (N21's record) — a record's fields |")
    strs_push(l, "| `E.`, `E` naming an enum and no value | the enum, when not generic (N21's rule; a value named `E` wins, as for any `E.x`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `E[T, …].` | the applied enum an unknown variant was looked for in |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Name(` | only when the module has no function `Name`: the record its types name, resolved and applied as a construction's head is |")
    strs_push(l, "| `E.V(`, construction or pattern | the variant |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The one new checker behaviour is the `Name(` row, and it runs only in a probe: the probe's")
    strs_push(l, "`Resolution` carries the hole's callee, and only when that call finds no function does the")
    strs_push(l, "checker resolve the name as a construction head and record the construction. In a probe, a")
    strs_push(l, "type name the module refused as an ambiguous import anchors nothing. An ordinary compilation")
    strs_push(l, "records nothing new: **clean-program N26 state is zero**, and an incomplete program's ordinary")
    strs_push(l, "analysis is unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A bare `(`.** Without a label, `Name(` is a call to the grammar, and the probe reads it as")
    strs_push(l, "one. A function `Name` makes it that call — signature help's — whether or not a record is also")
    strs_push(l, "called `Name`; only where no function is does a record anchor its labels. A generic record needs")
    strs_push(l, "its type arguments written, as a construction does.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Completeness.** N21's rule, applied unchanged to the probe's own parse, in which the hole is")
    strs_push(l, "not a recovery: no other file recovered, and every other recovery in the document is inside the")
    strs_push(l, "body of another function. Another mistake in the hole's function, at the top level or in a")
    strs_push(l, "dependency, leaves no answer.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Candidates.** `structure::candidates`, the function N21's completion uses: the anchor's")
    strs_push(l, "members in canonical order, identities, substituted details. Only the range differs: empty, at")
    strs_push(l, "the cursor — the `.` or `(` is not replaced — where a name being written is replaced whole.")
    strs_push(l, "Declarations are the definitions' name spans in the same files. The probe's diagnostics are never")
    strs_push(l, "published and its analysis is dropped with the response; nothing is cached.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Over the protocol.** `completionProvider.triggerCharacters` is `[\".\"]`: not `(`, which")
    strs_push(l, "signature help owns, nor `,` or `:`. The client's trigger is never read: whether a position is a")
    strs_push(l, "hole is decided from the current source, so a `.` in a string or a comment, or a trigger reported")
    strs_push(l, "where there is no `.`, completes nothing, and invoked and triggered requests answer alike.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not here.** Completion after a comma or at an empty label slot later in a list,")
    strs_push(l, "methods, ordinary call arguments, `(` as a trigger, ranking, snippets, and any reading of source")
    strs_push(l, "that would make an unfinished construct valid.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.29 Semantic context packet v1 and read-only MCP — settled by N27, 2026-09-27")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **MCP does not create semantic facts. It serialises a protocol-independent packet derived")
    strs_push(l, "> from the compiler's current root compilation.** A packet reports what the compiler already")
    strs_push(l, "> knows — never effects, capabilities, tests or changes it does not have, which are marked")
    strs_push(l, "> unsupported rather than empty.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "N17  references, and every use inside a declaration      (ReferenceIndex)")
    strs_push(l, "N18  written names of program records and enums          (Resolution::type_name)")
    strs_push(l, "N20  the one function signature renderer                 (Signature)")
    strs_push(l, "N21  canonical fields, variants and payloads             (structure::members)")
    strs_push(l, "N22  declaration and name ranges, exact source           (symbols::declared_in)")
    strs_push(l, "N25  direct callers and callees                          (incoming_calls / outgoing_calls)")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "ContextPacket, nazm.context/1                            (nazm-service/src/context.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "nazm context --json                                      (nazm-cli/src/context.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "nazm-mcp: one read-only stdio tool                       (nazm-mcp, rmcp)")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The target.** A function, record or enum the checker declared from source, found through the")
    strs_push(l, "entity the reference index records at a byte offset — its declaration or any use. A local, a")
    strs_push(l, "parameter, a field, a variant, an intrinsic or a built-in type is not a target; neither is a")
    strs_push(l, "position on no name. Nothing is looked up by spelling, so a record and a function called `Box`, or")
    strs_push(l, "two modules' `helper`, are always distinct.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a packet holds.** The target's durable identity (`module::kind name`, the `DefKey` the")
    strs_push(l, "interface already persists; null where a module has no durable key — never a session-local id),")
    strs_push(l, "kind, name, and a function's signature or a record's fields or an enum's variants and payloads,")
    strs_push(l, "by the existing renderers; its exact source, sliced from the declaration range N22 uses —")
    strs_push(l, "comments and all. Then compact links, each an identity, kind, name and declaration place:")
    strs_push(l, "**dependencies**, every entity used inside the declaration other than its own locals and itself,")
    strs_push(l, "grouped by identity with every occurrence; **related types**, the records and enums whose names")
    strs_push(l, "the checker recorded as written there — as a type, a construction's head or a variant's enum —")
    strs_push(l, "directly, not a closure; **references**, every use of the target, the declaration excluded;")
    strs_push(l, "**callers** and **callees**, call hierarchy's direct edges for a function and `not_applicable` for a")
    strs_push(l, "record or enum; and **diagnostics** whose primary span is inside the declaration, by code, span and")
    strs_push(l, "fix count. `availability` marks effects, capabilities, tests, semantic changes and semantic deltas")
    strs_push(l, "`unsupported`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Source links only.** Context packet v1 exposes source-linked program dependencies only: every")
    strs_push(l, "dependency, related type, caller and callee carries a declaration in a file of the compilation, and")
    strs_push(l, "`link.declaration` is never null. Compiler-owned, built-in, interface-only or toolchain definitions")
    strs_push(l, "without a navigable declaration — the core prelude's `Option` and `Result`, an intrinsic, `Int` —")
    strs_push(l, "may affect checking but are omitted from the link sections, rather than linked with no place. (A")
    strs_push(l, "link's `identity.definition` may still be null where its module has no durable key; its place is")
    strs_push(l, "given all the same.) Related types come from N18's record of the written names of program records")
    strs_push(l, "and enums; N23's `Resolution::written_type`, which records built-in types and type parameters, is")
    strs_push(l, "not read, since neither is a definition with a source.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Minimum context.** The target's source is the only source text in a packet; everything else is a")
    strs_push(l, "place to ask about next. That is a strategy for compact context — not a claim that a packet is")
    strs_push(l, "sufficient for every task, or minimal in any proven sense.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Which program.** The compilation rooted at one chosen file — its imports, and nothing else; no")
    strs_push(l, "directory is read and no project boundary is claimed. A compilation that needed syntax recovery, or")
    strs_push(l, "could not load a module, has no packet: what was lost could be a use, a caller or a declaration.")
    strs_push(l, "Type errors do not stop one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Determinism.** Paths are relative to the source root, every list has an explicit order (links by")
    strs_push(l, "kind, declaring file and place, then identity; references and diagnostics by position), and")
    strs_push(l, "nothing session-local — generation, numeric id, host path, time — is serialised; one compact")
    strs_push(l, "serialisation. The same sources and question give the same bytes, from any checkout.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The CLI and the MCP server.** `nazm context` and `nazm-mcp` each open the root from disk, build")
    strs_push(l, "the packet and drop everything: no packet, analysis or graph outlives a request. `nazm-mcp` is its")
    strs_push(l, "own crate and binary on the official Rust SDK (`rmcp`), stdio only, with one tool,")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.semantic_context` (`file`, `byte_offset`), whose output schema is `schema/nazm.context-3.json`")
    strs_push(l, "and whose result carries the packet once, as structured content, with an empty `content`;")
    strs_push(l, "it advertises tools and nothing else, and answers resources, prompts and completions as methods it")
    strs_push(l, "does not have. The root is fixed at startup; each call reads the disk as it is then, so an agent's")
    strs_push(l, "edit is seen at once and a broken file never gets an earlier packet. The `file` argument is only")
    strs_push(l, "compared with the compilation's own files by identity, so no other path — `/etc/passwd`, a file")
    strs_push(l, "nothing imports — is ever opened. It does not see an editor's unsaved buffers.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not here.** Semantic deltas, test mapping, effects and capabilities, history,")
    strs_push(l, "edit tools, HTTP transports, a persistent index or daemon, and any claim that every caller or")
    strs_push(l, "importer in a project is known.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.30 Semantic snapshot manifest and semantic delta v1 — settled by N28, 2026-09-27")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **N28 reports changes in the semantic surfaces Nazm currently records. It is not a proof of")
    strs_push(l, "> behavioural equivalence.** Effects, capabilities and tests are unsupported, not unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "N17  every use of an entity, by where it is             (ReferenceIndex)")
    strs_push(l, "N18  written names of program records and enums         (Resolution::type_name)")
    strs_push(l, "N20  the one function signature renderer                (Signature)")
    strs_push(l, "N21  canonical fields, variants and payloads            (structure::members)")
    strs_push(l, "N22  top-level declarations and their exact ranges      (symbols::declared_in)")
    strs_push(l, "N25  the one checked-call edge rule                     (hierarchy::callee)")
    strs_push(l, "N27  identity, shape and source-link rules              (context::{identity_of, shape, Paths})")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "SemanticSnapshot, nazm.snapshot/1                       (nazm-service/src/snapshot.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "        +  a baseline snapshot, as data")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "SemanticDelta, nazm.delta/1                             (nazm-service/src/delta.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "nazm snapshot --json · nazm delta --baseline --json     (nazm-cli/src/snapshot.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "nazm-mcp: nazm.semantic_snapshot · nazm.semantic_delta  (nazm-mcp)")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Which definitions.** Every function, record and enum the checker declared from a file of the")
    strs_push(l, "root's compilation — the root and what it imports, no directory read — that has a durable")
    strs_push(l, "definition key. `DefKey` is the only identity: no `FnId`, `RecordId` or `EnumId` is serialised, and")
    strs_push(l, "nothing is matched by path or name. A definition in a module outside the source root has no key; it")
    strs_push(l, "is left out and counted in `untracked`. A key the compilation gave two declarations would be no")
    strs_push(l, "identity for either and is counted the same way (the checker refuses a second declaration, so this")
    strs_push(l, "is a guard, not a case that occurs today). Built-ins and the core prelude's definitions are not the")
    strs_push(l, "root's definitions.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a snapshot holds.** The root's identity — its module key and the compiler (`nazm <version>`)")
    strs_push(l, "— then per definition its key, kind, declaration place (for navigation, not compared) and one BLAKE3")
    strs_push(l, "digest per section, over a length-prefixed framing that names schema and section:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Section | Canonical data digested |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `source` | the declaration's exact bytes |")
    strs_push(l, "| `shape` | kind, visibility, and the rendered signature, or the fields, or the variants and payloads |")
    strs_push(l, "| `dependencies` | every source-linked entity used inside (N27's rule), by kind and identity, with a count |")
    strs_push(l, "| `related_types` | the records and enums written by name inside, by identity, with a count |")
    strs_push(l, "| `references` | every use of it, by the identity of the definition the use is in, with a count |")
    strs_push(l, "| `callers`, `callees` | a function's direct checked calls in and out, by the identity at the other end, with a count; null for a record or an enum |")
    strs_push(l, "| `diagnostics` | code, severity, fix count and declaration-relative range of each diagnostic inside it — never its message |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Relationship digests take identities and counts, never byte offsets, so a line added above a")
    strs_push(l, "definition changes nothing below it; a reference or call is attributed to the declaration whose")
    strs_push(l, "range contains it, found by binary search over each file's declarations. No complete packet is")
    strs_push(l, "stored per definition — a snapshot is a manifest. `unsupported` lists effects, capabilities, tests,")
    strs_push(l, "semantic history and behavioural equivalence.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a digest proves.** Equal digests mean the canonical bytes above were equal, and nothing")
    strs_push(l, "more. `fn answer() -> Int { 1 }` and `{ 2 }` agree in every section but `source`. A digest is not")
    strs_push(l, "the program's meaning.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Root identity and determinism.** The root is its module key, relative to the source root, so")
    strs_push(l, "the same project in another directory has the same identity and the same bytes; no absolute path,")
    strs_push(l, "generation, numeric id, time or random value is digested or written. Definitions are ordered by")
    strs_push(l, "identity; every map is ordered. The same sources and compiler give byte-identical snapshots across")
    strs_push(l, "calls, processes and checkouts. Two different projects whose root modules have the same key share")
    strs_push(l, "a root identity; a delta between them is still exact about which keys differ.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The delta.** A baseline is data: parsed as JSON and validated before anything is compared. It is")
    strs_push(l, "refused — never compared as well as it can be — for another schema, an unavailable snapshot, any")
    strs_push(l, "field `nazm.snapshot/1` does not define or a missing one, an identity not in canonical `DefKey`")
    strs_push(l, "spelling or not of its entry's kind, a duplicate identity, a digest that is not 64 lowercase")
    strs_push(l, "hexadecimal digits, callers or callees present on a record or absent on a function, another root")
    strs_push(l, "module, or another compiler. Otherwise the current snapshot is derived and compared by key:")
    strs_push(l, "`added`, `removed` (with its baseline place), `changed` with a record of which sections differ —")
    strs_push(l, "`callers` and `callees` null for a type, not false — and an `unchanged` count. A rename is its old")
    strs_push(l, "key removed and its new key added; nothing is inferred. A comment, a reformatting or a different")
    strs_push(l, "literal is `source` alone.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**No state.** Snapshot and delta are derived per request from one analysis and dropped with it:")
    strs_push(l, "no snapshot cache, dependency graph, call graph or history outlives a call. Nothing needs, or asks,")
    strs_push(l, "git.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The CLI and the MCP server.** `nazm snapshot --root FILE --json` prints a snapshot; `nazm delta")
    strs_push(l, "--root FILE --baseline FILE --json` reads a snapshot file the caller kept and prints the delta — a")
    strs_push(l, "file that is not JSON is a malformed baseline. `nazm-mcp` adds `nazm.semantic_snapshot` (no")
    strs_push(l, "arguments) and `nazm.semantic_delta` (`baseline`, a `nazm.snapshot/1` object), with the two schemas")
    strs_push(l, "as output schemas and each result carried once, as structured content. The server keeps no")
    strs_push(l, "previous snapshot: the client keeps the baseline and hands it back. A baseline is never a path,")
    strs_push(l, "so no file a client names is read. Each call reads the disk as it is then, so an edit is seen at")
    strs_push(l, "once and a broken one gets no snapshot or delta, never an earlier one. `nazm.semantic_context` is")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not here.** Rename inference, test impact, effect and capability deltas, semantic")
    strs_push(l, "history, a persistent snapshot cache or index, git integration, patch application, and any claim")
    strs_push(l, "that equal digests mean equal behaviour.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.31 Minimal semantic patch plan v1 — settled by N29, 2026-09-27")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **N29 plans edits but never applies them.** A patch is a proposal bound to exact semantic and")
    strs_push(l, "> source state, not permission to mutate files.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "N18  rename: entity at a position, declaration + uses, scope rule,      (rename.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "     new-name lexing, candidate re-parsed, re-checked, same partition")
    strs_push(l, "N24  the fix a current diagnostic carries, as one validated edit          (fixes.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "N28  the root's snapshot and identity                                     (snapshot.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "SemanticPatch, nazm.patch/1                                               (nazm-service/src/patch.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "nazm patch rename|fix --json                                              (nazm-cli/src/patch.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "nazm-mcp: nazm.semantic_patch, read-only                                  (nazm-mcp)")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Two operations, and no others.** `rename` is N18's validated plan: the entity the reference")
    strs_push(l, "index records at the position, its declaration and every use, nothing found by spelling, the new")
    strs_push(l, "name lexed as one identifier, and the candidate program re-parsed and re-checked — clean, its")
    strs_push(l, "occurrences grouped into entities exactly as before. Every category N18 renames: function,")
    strs_push(l, "local, record, enum, variant, field, payload field. `diagnostic_fix` is N24's projection of a")
    strs_push(l, "`Fix` a current diagnostic owns — selected by the file, a byte its primary span touches, and the")
    strs_push(l, "fix's index among those at that byte, in the order the compiler attached them — never by a code, a")
    strs_push(l, "message or a spelling, so a position with no diagnostic has no fix whatever a client believes.")
    strs_push(l, "Its applicability (`automatic` or `needs_review`) and precondition are carried as structured")
    strs_push(l, "fields, exactly as the compiler wrote them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Exported rename remains refused because one root compilation is not a complete importer")
    strs_push(l, "universe.** A snapshot of that compilation describes it; it does not make every module that may")
    strs_push(l, "import an exported name known. N18's refusal is unchanged and reported as `exported`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N29 does not alter LSP closed-file safety.** The disk plan reads the root and analyses it;")
    strs_push(l, "when the edit is in another file of that compilation, the request's own service opens that file")
    strs_push(l, "from the text the analysis read — no second read — and N18 or N24 plan against it as against an")
    strs_push(l, "open document. The plan may therefore describe a file no editor has open, protected by the")
    strs_push(l, "freshness below. `textDocument/rename` and `textDocument/codeAction` still edit open documents")
    strs_push(l, "only.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Three freshness layers.** `baseline.snapshot` is BLAKE3 of the root's canonical")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.snapshot/1` bytes (N28) — the semantic state of the whole compilation; `files[].digest` is")
    strs_push(l, "BLAKE3 of each edited file's exact bytes; `edits[].expected` is the exact bytes each edit replaces.")
    strs_push(l, "None implies another — a comment in another definition of the file moves the file and the")
    strs_push(l, "snapshot but not the edit's bytes, an edit in another file moves only the snapshot, and a line")
    strs_push(l, "above the target moves the expected bytes out from under the range — so all three are kept, and a")
    strs_push(l, "future applier refuses unless all three hold. `root` is N28's `RootIdentity`: the durable")
    strs_push(l, "compilation namespace, not proof of project lineage.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Minimal and canonical.** One edit per renamed occurrence, each the name's bytes; a fix's one")
    strs_push(l, "span. No file text is carried. Files are ordered by root-relative path, edits by start then end;")
    strs_push(l, "a duplicate, an overlap, two insertions at one point, or an edit that changes nothing refuse the")
    strs_push(l, "whole patch. Serialisation order is not application order — right-to-left application is the")
    strs_push(l, "applier's concern. No session id, generation, host path or time is written: the same sources and")
    strs_push(l, "request give the same bytes from any checkout.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Targets.** A top-level function, record or enum, and a member of one, carries its durable key")
    strs_push(l, "(`module::kind name`, with the member); `durable` says so. A local has no durable key and is not")
    strs_push(l, "given one: it is named by its declaration's place and the durable key of the function it is in.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a patch is not.** Not applied, by any command or tool; not cached — each request analyses")
    strs_push(l, "the disk and drops everything; not a refactoring framework; not a text replacement a client")
    strs_push(l, "supplies. A fix of a syntax diagnostic has no patch: the compilation that carries it needed")
    strs_push(l, "recovery, so N28 has no snapshot to bind it to, and it is refused as `incomplete_compilation`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The CLI and the MCP server.** `nazm patch rename --root --file --byte --new-name --json` and")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm patch fix --root --file --byte --fix --json` print exactly `nazm.patch/1`. `nazm-mcp` adds")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.semantic_patch`, whose input is a typed request tagged by `operation` (`rename` or")
    strs_push(l, "`diagnostic_fix`), its schema the SDK's derivation of that type — no root field and no unknown")
    strs_push(l, "argument is accepted — and whose result is the patch once, as structured content.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not here.** Patch application or any write, MCP write tools, exported rename,")
    strs_push(l, "project-wide importer discovery, multi-file renames (N18's scope rule keeps a private entity's")
    strs_push(l, "occurrences in its declaring file), fix-all, refactors, git.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.32 Compact diagnostics and progressive disclosure — settled by N30, 2026-09-28")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **Compact diagnostics never infer structured semantics from diagnostic prose.** A compiler")
    strs_push(l, "> `Fix` and an N29 semantic patch are distinct capabilities.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "compiler Diagnostic                                         (nazm-diag)")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "nazm.diagnostic/1, unchanged                                (Diagnostic::published)")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "compact summary index, nazm.diagnostic-index/1              (nazm-service/src/diagnostics.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "one selected detail, nazm.diagnostic-detail/1")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "optional N29 patch planning                                 (a nazm.semantic_patch selector)")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is indexed.** Every diagnostic of the root's compilation as the service analyses it —")
    strs_push(l, "the analysis N27–N29 read, from disk, the root and what it imports and no other file. It is a")
    strs_push(l, "module's analysis, as the language server's is, so a missing `main` (`N0204`) is not among them.")
    strs_push(l, "Syntax diagnostics are: the index needs no semantic snapshot.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The compact entry.** `id`, `code`, `severity`, `primary` (root-relative file and UTF-8 byte")
    strs_push(l, "range, translated from the compiler's span by the same source map every answer uses — never the")
    strs_push(l, "published concatenation offset), `owner`, and `fixes` counted by applicability. No message, help,")
    strs_push(l, "label text, fix description or precondition. The index adds counts — total, `error` (the one")
    strs_push(l, "severity the compiler has), diagnostics with fixes, automatic and needs-review fixes — and builds")
    strs_push(l, "no patch.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Facts.** The compiler's `Diagnostic` carries no typed expected/actual/entity facts today, so")
    strs_push(l, "none are exposed: detail says `facts: \"unavailable\"`, and no field is reconstructed from a")
    strs_push(l, "sentence. A structural test keeps the module from reading a diagnostic's message, help,")
    strs_push(l, "description or precondition.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Identity.** Entries are ordered by primary file, start, end and code, then by their secondary")
    strs_push(l, "and fix places, then by the compiler's own deterministic order. An id is `code@file:start-end#n`,")
    strs_push(l, "`n` counting earlier entries with the same code and primary place; two diagnostics the compiler's")
    strs_push(l, "structure cannot tell apart are told apart by that ordinal and nothing else. Message and help")
    strs_push(l, "never reach an id.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**State.** Two fields, each with one meaning. `state.source`, always present: BLAKE3 over the")
    strs_push(l, "root's identity (module key and compiler) and every loaded source file's root-relative path and")
    strs_push(l, "exact bytes, in load order, length-prefixed — no absolute path, generation or time. `state.snapshot`:")
    strs_push(l, "BLAKE3 of the root's `nazm.snapshot/1` (N28), or null where the compilation has none — after")
    strs_push(l, "syntax recovery or a missing module; N28's completeness rule is not weakened. A detail request")
    strs_push(l, "names the index's `state.source`; any other value is `stale_state`, and an id is resolved only")
    strs_push(l, "within the state it came from, so an old id never selects another diagnostic now at its place.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Owners.** The durable function, record or enum whose declaration, by N22's outline, contains the")
    strs_push(l, "primary span — only in a compilation that needed no syntax recovery and loaded every module.")
    strs_push(l, "Otherwise, and for anything outside every declaration (a refused duplicate, an import), none.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Detail.** The diagnostic exactly as `nazm.diagnostic/1` publishes it — canonical prose,")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged, spans as that schema defines them — with the same spans in their own files, the owner,")
    strs_push(l, "`facts`, `compiler_fixes`, `semantic_patches`, and for each fix its applicability and the")
    strs_push(l, "`diagnostic_fix` selector (`file`, `byte_offset`, `fix`) N29 plans it from, or null. A fix is a")
    strs_push(l, "semantic patch only where N29 would plan it: a compilation with a snapshot, and N24 planning the")
    strs_push(l, "edit. The check reads N24's plans for that one diagnostic and builds no patch; a syntax")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostic's fix is a compiler fix and no patch.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The CLI and the MCP server.** `nazm diagnostics --root FILE --json` prints the index; `--detail ID")
    strs_push(l, "--state DIGEST` one detail. `nazm-mcp` adds `nazm.diagnostics` (no arguments) and")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.diagnostic_detail` (`id`, `state`, typed). Each result once, as structured content. Every call")
    strs_push(l, "reads the disk; nothing — index, detail, history — is kept. They are disk tools: an editor's")
    strs_push(l, "unsaved buffers are the language server's, whose diagnostics are unchanged. `nazm check --json`")
    strs_push(l, "is unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not here.** Typed facts for any diagnostic, other verbosity levels, diagnostic")
    strs_push(l, "history, AI-written explanations, message parsing, patch application, and build or test output.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.33 Token-efficient command and test summaries — settled by N31, 2026-09-28")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **Summary is an additive view, not a replacement for existing detailed machine output.**")
    strs_push(l, "> **Absence of diagnostics does not imply command success.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "nazm check / build / test, as they run today               (nazm-cli)")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓  the command's own outcome, and its diagnostics or case verdicts")
    strs_push(l, "compact summary                                             (nazm-service/src/summary.rs, nazm-cli/src/test.rs)")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓  counts, and only the diagnostics and cases that matter")
    strs_push(l, "nazm.command-summary/1 · nazm.test-summary/1")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓  on demand")
    strs_push(l, "existing detail: --json, nazm.test/1, nazm diagnostics --detail")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a command summary is.** `--summary-json` on `nazm check` and `nazm build` prints one")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.command-summary/1` object on stdout and no diagnostic on stderr. It carries the command's")
    strs_push(l, "status — `success`, `rejected`, `unreadable`, `refused`, `toolchain_failed`, one per exit path the")
    strs_push(l, "command has, set where the command returns — and its exit status, unchanged; counts; and a")
    strs_push(l, "reference to every diagnostic the command reported: code, severity, place, fix counts, no prose.")
    strs_push(l, "A build adds the artifact path as it prints it. No timing is included, so the same sources give the")
    strs_push(l, "same summary.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**References and N30.** The command's diagnostics are its own — `nazm check`'s program check,")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm build`'s check and lowering — not N30's module analysis, so a missing `main` (`N0204`) and a")
    strs_push(l, "backend's refusal of a construct (`N0101`) are kept. Each is matched to N30's index by structure")
    strs_push(l, "alone (code, primary, secondary and fix places, the n-th of equals to the n-th): a match carries")
    strs_push(l, "N30's `id` with `scope: \"index\"`, and the summary carries N30's `state.source`, so `nazm diagnostics")
    strs_push(l, "--detail` answers it; anything else is `scope: \"command\"` with no id — never a fake one. N30's")
    strs_push(l, "shared structure orders them. If a file changed between the command's read and the summary's, no")
    strs_push(l, "reference is linked and `state` is null. No N28 snapshot is needed, so syntax diagnostics are")
    strs_push(l, "references like any other.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a test summary is.** `nazm test --summary-json` runs the cases exactly as `nazm test` does")
    strs_push(l, "and prints one `nazm.test-summary/1`: its status (`passed`, `failed`, `no_cases`, `unreadable`,")
    strs_push(l, "`toolchain_failed`, one per exit path), exit status, whether the native leg ran, counts — cases,")
    strs_push(l, "passed and failed each counted from the case's own verdict, and files without an expectation —")
    strs_push(l, "and every case that did not pass, by `nazm.test/1`'s name and file, with how each leg ended:")
    strs_push(l, "`matched`, `mismatched`, `not_run`, `build_failed`, `could_not_build`, `could_not_run`. Each is read")
    strs_push(l, "from what the runner did — which process it started, whether it could, whether it succeeded —")
    strs_push(l, "never from output text, so a runtime error or a compile error in a case is a `mismatched` leg and no")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostic is made of it. No passed name, no output, no truncation; cases in the order they ran.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Every outcome is exercised.** Each status and each leg has a regression test that reaches its")
    strs_push(l, "production branch through the real binary. The runner starts each leg with this executable, or with")
    strs_push(l, "the one `NAZM_TEST_DRIVER` names — a test seam, not an interface — so a test can hand it a driver")
    strs_push(l, "that does not exist, one that removes itself after the program has run, or one whose build succeeds")
    strs_push(l, "and writes nothing; `nazm build` finds `clang` on the process's own PATH, so a test gives that one")
    strs_push(l, "process a `clang` that refuses, one that will not link, or none. Nothing machine-wide is changed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Flags and channels.** `--summary-json` conflicts with `--json`, and with `--cache-report` and")
    strs_push(l, "`--build-report`: an ambiguous combination is refused by the argument parser (exit 2; 5 since Q1-C1 froze the exit")
    strs_push(l, "contract). Human output,")
    strs_push(l, "`--json`, `nazm.test/1`, `nazm.check-report/1` and `nazm.build-report/1` are unchanged. A build's")
    strs_push(l, "toolchain failure may still write its own message to stderr.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**MCP.** One tool, `nazm.command_summary`, with a typed `operation` whose only value is `check`:")
    strs_push(l, "the root's check from the disk as it is now, run without the check cache, so nothing is written.")
    strs_push(l, "Building writes an executable and testing runs programs, which may write files; neither is")
    strs_push(l, "read-only, so neither is offered.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not here.** Test-detail retrieval, test impact, failure explanations, a build-log")
    strs_push(l, "store, timing, remote CI, and any MCP tool that builds, tests or runs a command.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.34 Machine-addressable documentation and selective retrieval — settled by N32, 2026-09-28")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "canonical documents under docs/                       (the authorities)")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "structural section index                              (crates/nazm-docs)")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "stable ids + authority classes")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "selective exact retrieval                             nazm.docs-index/1 · nazm.docs-section/1")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "nazm docs  ·  nazm-mcp nazm.docs_index / nazm.docs_section  (read-only)")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The index is not a second source of documentation truth.** The documents are. `nazm-docs`")
    strs_push(l, "reads them, as they are on disk at each request, into sections, and answers with their bytes;")
    strs_push(l, "it holds no copy of any rule, title or example. Its manifest is fourteen rows — a document's id,")
    strs_push(l, "its path, its authority and which reader it takes — in the order of `master-architecture.md`")
    strs_push(l, "§5's authority table, with `mcp.md` beside `diagnostics.md` and the grammar beside the guide.")
    strs_push(l, "Nothing is found by walking a directory: `README.md`, `releases/` (frozen evidence) and")
    strs_push(l, "`research/` (a draft protocol) are outside it, and so is every user project's documentation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Goals, roadmaps, architecture, evidence and normative specification retain distinct")
    strs_push(l, "authority classes.** Every document, and so every section, carries one of eleven: `goal`")
    strs_push(l, "(`NAZM_LANGUAGE_GOALS.md` — aspiration, never evidence of what exists), `law`")
    strs_push(l, "(`master-architecture.md`), `architecture`, `normative` (`spec.md`), `grammar`, `guide`,")
    strs_push(l, "`interface` (`diagnostics.md`, `mcp.md`), `evidence` (`capability-matrix.md`, `performance.md`,")
    strs_push(l, "`bootstrap.md`), `planning` (`roadmap.md`), `research` and `operational` (`runbook.md`). The")
    strs_push(l, "class is the document's, from §5; nothing classifies a section by its words, and a section's")
    strs_push(l, "`kind` is structural only — `document`, `heading` or `production`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Retrieval never paraphrases canonical text.** A section's body is exact bytes of its file:")
    strs_push(l, "a heading's line through the byte before the next heading of any level. That is its **direct**")
    strs_push(l, "text — a parent never carries its subsections, which are listed as children — so a document's")
    strs_push(l, "sections, in order, are the document. A grammar production's body is its attached comments")
    strs_push(l, "and the production through `;`, with the production's text and its `@example`s beside it,")
    strs_push(l, "exactly.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Identity.** `document:local`, and a document's root — its title and the text before its")
    strs_push(l, "first subheading — is `document`. The local part is an explicit anchor, `<!-- id: name -->` on")
    strs_push(l, "the line under a heading, which survives rewording and moving; else the heading's own label")
    strs_push(l, "where the document numbers its sections (`architecture:7.33`, `capabilities:2a`, `goals:G78`,")
    strs_push(l, "`roadmap:N31`, `research:R1`), which survives rewording; else the heading's text as a segment")
    strs_push(l, "under its parent (`spec:generics/identity`), which does not. Never a line, an offset, an")
    strs_push(l, "ordinal, a hash, a random value or a commit. `spec.md` gained forty-three anchors, one under each")
    strs_push(l, "of its `##` and `###` headings, and no other change; no other document was edited for this. A")
    strs_push(l, "production is `grammar:name`. Two sections with one id are refused, never numbered apart — which")
    strs_push(l, "is also the one mechanical G79 audit this milestone makes: no anchor, and so no rule id an anchor")
    strs_push(l, "carries, is defined twice.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Structure is read, not guessed.** ATX headings outside fenced code (backticks or tildes, at any")
    strs_push(l, "indentation) and outside HTML comments; a `#` line inside a fence is code. Setext and HTML")
    strs_push(l, "headings, which the corpus does not use, are refused rather than mis-sectioned. The grammar is")
    strs_push(l, "read as productions — a comment separated from every rule by a blank line, after the header, is")
    strs_push(l, "refused — and a production's `references` are the nonterminals it names: a grammar reference,")
    strs_push(l, "not a semantic dependency.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Links are explicit or absent.** A Markdown link into the corpus resolves to a section id — a")
    strs_push(l, "`#fragment` by the anchor a reader's browser gives the heading — and one that resolves to nothing")
    strs_push(l, "makes the corpus unavailable, never quietly partial. A link outside the corpus or to the web is")
    strs_push(l, "kept as written. A guide section between the generator's markers titled `` `name` `` is")
    strs_push(l, "`generated_from` `grammar:name`. Nothing links sections because their words are alike.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Freshness.** The corpus `state` is BLAKE3 over a domain tag and, in manifest order, each")
    strs_push(l, "document's id, repository-relative path and bytes; a section's digest is BLAKE3 over another tag,")
    strs_push(l, "its document, its id and its body — so moving an anchored section changes its parent and not its")
    strs_push(l, "digest. No absolute path, time, process or commit enters either, and a copy of the repository")
    strs_push(l, "elsewhere gives the same bytes. A section asked for with a state that is not the current one is")
    strs_push(l, "`stale_state`; an unknown id is `not_found` — never the nearest one. The MCP tool requires the")
    strs_push(l, "state, as N30's detail does; the command line takes it optionally.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Surfaces.** `nazm docs --index [--document ID]` and `nazm docs --section ID [--state S]`, with")
    strs_push(l, "`--json` one object on stdout and nothing on stderr, and `--root` for another checkout; without a")
    strs_push(l, "root, the repository the binary was built from, used to find files and never written into an")
    strs_push(l, "answer. `nazm-mcp` adds `nazm.docs_index` and `nazm.docs_section`, whose arguments are a document")
    strs_push(l, "id, or a section id and a state — never a path — over the repository given as `--docs`, fixed at")
    strs_push(l, "startup. Both read at every call and keep nothing. `cargo xtask check` has a `docs corpus` gate")
    strs_push(l, "that loads the corpus with the same reader.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not here.** Semantic, fuzzy or full-text search, embeddings, summaries,")
    strs_push(l, "documentation history, Git, fine-grained normative rule ids below section level, an installed")
    strs_push(l, "copy of the documentation, and any user project's documents.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.35 Repository context map and minimum task context — settled by N33, 2026-09-29")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "nazm-cli (nazm repo)  ·  nazm-mcp (nazm.repository_map, nazm.task_context)")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "nazm-repo — the repository map and the task planner          nazm.repository-map/1 · nazm.task-context/1")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓                  ↓                     ↓                          ↓")
    strs_push(l, "nazm-service           nazm-docs            Cargo manifests          the mutation catalogue")
    strs_push(l, "(N17 · N22 · N25 ·     (N32 ids, authority,  (packages, targets,      (profiles, killers,")
    strs_push(l, " N27 · N28 · N30)       sections, links)      dependencies, docs)      where a mutant lands)")
    strs_push(l, "        ↓")
    strs_push(l, "nazm-core")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not another source of truth: an index and a planner over the ones that exist.** `nazm-repo`")
    strs_push(l, "decides no meaning, reads no Markdown and scans no import: every entity and relationship is read")
    strs_push(l, "from the authority that owns it — Cargo manifests for packages, targets and their dependencies;")
    strs_push(l, "the compiler, through the language service, for which files a compilation loads, its durable")
    strs_push(l, "definitions (N28's, with N22's name ranges, a new service accessor and no new checker state),")
    strs_push(l, "their links, callers and diagnostics (N17, N25, N27, N30); `nazm-docs` for documents, sections,")
    strs_push(l, "authority and links (N32); the mutation catalogue for which tests observe which paths and which")
    strs_push(l, "test kills which mutant. The layering is the diagram: nothing below `nazm-repo` knows it exists.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Repository entity law.** An entity is something with a durable identity in one of those")
    strs_push(l, "authorities, named `kind:authority-id`: `package:nazm-docs`, `target:nazm-docs:test:corpus`,")
    strs_push(l, "`sources:compiler`, `root:compiler:emit.nz`, `module:compiler:analyse.nz`,")
    strs_push(l, "`def:compiler:analyse.nz::fn check_program` (N3's durable key under a source root),")
    strs_push(l, "`doc:spec:generics` (N32's id), `schema:nazm.context/1` (the constant the file declares),")
    strs_push(l, "`profile:checker`, and — in a task context — `mutation:NAME`, `test:PKG:KIND:TARGET::PATH` (a")
    strs_push(l, "catalogue killer) and `diagnostic:SOURCES:ROOT:ID` (N30's id within its compilation). Never an")
    strs_push(l, "absolute path, a line, an offset, a random value, a time or a commit; a path appears only as a")
    strs_push(l, "location. What has no durable identity is named as omitted, not invented: Rust items (the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler owns no Rust semantics — packages and targets are what is mapped), locals, the core")
    strs_push(l, "prelude's definitions, untracked definitions, the definitions of a compilation that needed syntax")
    strs_push(l, "recovery, and tests the catalogue does not name. The one place the Nazm side is written down is")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-repo`'s manifest: three source roots, `compiler` (its four drivers are roots, its other")
    strs_push(l, "files modules), `examples` and `examples-bad`, each with the sections that are its authority. A")
    strs_push(l, "package declares its own, as `[package.metadata.nazm] docs = [...]` in its manifest.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The map** (`nazm.repository-map/1`) says what exists and how it relates, never what it says:")
    strs_push(l, "each entity's kind, parent, location, a compilation's completeness and diagnostic count,")
    strs_push(l, "structural relationships — `depends_on` and `dev_depends_on` (Cargo), `documented_by` (a")
    strs_push(l, "package's metadata or a source root's row), `includes` (a module a compilation loaded),")
    strs_push(l, "`observed_by` and `covers` (a profile's targets and owned package or source root) — and where to")
    strs_push(l, "retrieve more, as the schema and arguments of an existing answer: `nazm.snapshot/1` and")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.diagnostic-index/1` of a root, `nazm.docs-index/1` of a document. Sections, mutations,")
    strs_push(l, "catalogue tests and diagnostics are counted as delegated to the answer that enumerates them. A")
    strs_push(l, "class table gives each kind's authority; a document carries its own. Canonical order is kind,")
    strs_push(l, "then id in byte order; relationships by kind and target.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Validation.** A map is published only if every id is unique and well-formed, every parent and")
    strs_push(l, "relationship target exists (an N32 section by the corpus), every kind, relationship, retrieval")
    strs_push(l, "and authority is known, and the order is canonical — `nazm_repo::validate`, run on every map")
    strs_push(l, "built. Anything else, or any unreadable input, broken documentation link, unresolved catalogue")
    strs_push(l, "target, duplicate package or schema, missing root, or compilation that loads a file outside its")
    strs_push(l, "source root, is `unavailable` with every problem: never a partial map.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Minimum-context closure.** A task (`nazm.task-context/1`) takes one to eight seeds — entity")
    strs_push(l, "ids, never paths or queries — and an intent. One relationship step from each seed, never more:")
    strs_push(l, "nothing is followed from an item that is not a seed, so a cycle is one visit, and each")
    strs_push(l, "relationship is cut at sixteen members, counted in `bounded`. From a definition: `understand` —")
    strs_push(l, "its exact source and shape, the records and enums it names (`signature_type`), every other")
    strs_push(l, "durable definition it uses by shape (`direct_dependency`), its source root's sections; `edit`,")
    strs_push(l, "the default because it is the widest — that, plus what uses it in **every** compilation of the")
    strs_push(l, "manifest that loads its module (`direct_caller` for a function, from N25; `direct_reference` for")
    strs_push(l, "a type, each use placed in its durable owner), and its tests; `diagnose` — the seed, the")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostics it owns, what it names; `test` — the seed and its tests. Tests are related only by")
    strs_push(l, "the catalogue: the verified killers of each mutation whose `find` lands inside the seed's")
    strs_push(l, "declaration (`killer_test`), and the targets of the profile owning its file (`profile_target`) —")
    strs_push(l, "never by a name that looks related, and a killed mutant is evidence the test observes that")
    strs_push(l, "defect, not that the code is right. A section brings the sections its text links to, the")
    strs_push(l, "production a guide rule is generated from and the productions a production names; an edit adds")
    strs_push(l, "the sections that link to it, pointed at without their text. A diagnostic brings its owner with")
    strs_push(l, "its exact source. A package brings its declared sections and dependencies, and for an edit its")
    strs_push(l, "dependents, owned targets, killers and profile targets.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Why each item is there.** Every item carries its `reason`, the seed it came `via`, its priority")
    strs_push(l, "`class`, its `authority` and a `retrieval` — the arguments of `nazm context`, `nazm docs")
    strs_push(l, "--section` or `nazm diagnostics --detail` that give it again. What was known and not selected is")
    strs_push(l, "counted in `excluded` (callers for an `understand`, dependencies with no durable key). No score:")
    strs_push(l, "the classes are `seed`, `correctness`, `authority` (normative, grammar, law, interface,")
    strs_push(l, "architecture, evidence sections, in that order), `edit_safety`, `test`, `supporting` (guide and")
    strs_push(l, "operational sections, children), `context` (planning, research, goal) — a goal or a plan never")
    strs_push(l, "outranks the specification or the evidence. Within a class, by that authority order and then id.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Budget.** `max_entities`, `max_source_bytes` (definition source included) and `max_doc_bytes`")
    strs_push(l, "(section text included) — structural, not tokens. The seeds are mandatory: a budget they do not")
    strs_push(l, "fit is `insufficient_budget` with what they need, never a context without its seed. Then items in")
    strs_push(l, "priority order until one does not fit: it (with the dimension it exceeded) and everything after")
    strs_push(l, "it (`priority`) are listed in `omitted`, and the answer is `partial`. A fan-out cut also makes it")
    strs_push(l, "`partial`. The same request and state give the same bytes, so the same budget chooses the same")
    strs_push(l, "items.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Source and documentation inclusion.** Source only as a definition's exact declaration (N27's")
    strs_push(l, "range) — for a seed, a diagnostic's owner and a mutated definition; every other definition by its")
    strs_push(l, "shape, and never a whole file. Documentation only as N32 sections, never a whole document.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Freshness and partial compilation.** The repository `state` is BLAKE3 over a tag, the compiler,")
    strs_push(l, "the manifest, N32's corpus state, every Cargo manifest and the targets Cargo would find, the")
    strs_push(l, "catalogue, every schema and every `.nz` file directly in a source root — paths and bytes; a task")
    strs_push(l, "with another state is `stale_state`. A compilation that needed syntax recovery keeps its modules")
    strs_push(l, "and loses its definitions: a definition only such a compilation loads is `incomplete_compilation`,")
    strs_push(l, "never last-clean facts.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Security boundary.** A seed is compared with the repository's own identities and never opened:")
    strs_push(l, "`/etc/passwd`, `../x.nz` and a part with a `/` are `invalid_request`; an unknown well-formed id is")
    strs_push(l, "`not_found`, never the nearest. There is no listing, globbing, search or read of a caller-named")
    strs_push(l, "path. The CLI takes `--root`; the MCP tools read the repository fixed at startup (`--docs`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Surfaces.** `nazm repo --map` and `nazm repo --task [--intent I] --seed ID… [--state S]")
    strs_push(l, "[--max-entities N] [--max-source-bytes N] [--max-doc-bytes N]`; with `--json`, one object on")
    strs_push(l, "stdout, nothing on stderr, exit 0 with a map or a context and 1 with a refusal; conflicting modes")
    strs_push(l, "refused by the parser. `nazm-mcp` adds `nazm.repository_map` and `nazm.task_context`, whose")
    strs_push(l, "`state` is required. Both derive every answer from the disk at the call and keep nothing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not here.** Rust semantics, search of any kind, embeddings, relevance scores,")
    strs_push(l, "transitive closure, Git, history, a persistent index, a daemon, network access, package")
    strs_push(l, "resolution, tokens, snapshot or delta machinery of its own (N28's), a second documentation")
    strs_push(l, "reader (N32's), a second context packet (N27's) — and any claim of project-wide completeness:")
    strs_push(l, "callers are those of the manifest's compilations, and an exported definition's users elsewhere")
    strs_push(l, "are not known.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.36 Tokenizer-independent context measurement — settled by N34, 2026-09-29")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "nazm repo --task … --json            (selection: entities, source bytes, doc bytes — N33)")
    strs_push(l, "        │  exact bytes, piped")
    strs_push(l, "        ▼")
    strs_push(l, "nazm-tokens measure                  nazm.token-cost/1        (a tool beside the compiler)")
    strs_push(l, "        │")
    strs_push(l, "        ├── tiktoken-rs 0.12.1       openai-bpe/cl100k_base, openai-bpe/o200k_base")
    strs_push(l, "        └── tokenizers 0.23.1        sentencepiece-bpe/mistral-7b-v0.1, sentencepiece-unigram/t5-small")
    strs_push(l, "                                     tools/tokenizers/*.tokenizer.json, pinned by BLAKE3")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Tokenizer independence.** No tokenizer reaches the language. `nazm-tokens` depends on no")
    strs_push(l, "internal crate, and no crate depends on it: the layering table lists it nowhere, and the")
    strs_push(l, "`tokenizer reach` gate refuses any other crate that depends on `tiktoken-rs` or `tokenizers`.")
    strs_push(l, "Parsing, checking, `DefKey` and `ModuleKey`, diagnostics, code generation, the bootstrap, the")
    strs_push(l, "documentation index and the planner's selection are what they were: `nazm` and `nazm-mcp` are")
    strs_push(l, "built without a tokenizer anywhere in their graphs.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The byte-budget law.** N33's budgets — entities, bytes of definition source, bytes of section")
    strs_push(l, "text — stay the canonical ones, because they are the same under every tokenizer. A context is")
    strs_push(l, "selected first, from bytes and structure; it is counted afterwards, by any number of tokenizers,")
    strs_push(l, "and no count, identity or tokenizer-specific rank changes what was selected. N34's benchmark shows")
    strs_push(l, "why: one selection of `check_program`'s context is 1.63–1.66× as many tokens under one tokenizer")
    strs_push(l, "as under another, so a token")
    strs_push(l, "budget would be a budget for one tokenizer.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Tokenizer identity.** A count is evidence only under the exact implementation and vocabulary.")
    strs_push(l, "Each tokenizer's identity is its id (`family-slug/name`), family, algorithm, library and version,")
    strs_push(l, "source and revision, licence, normalisation, special-token policy, and a BLAKE3 digest of its asset")
    strs_push(l, "— for the Hugging Face files the file's bytes, for the OpenAI vocabularies every rank's bytes as")
    strs_push(l, "the library decodes them — pinned in the crate and checked at every load. A missing, altered or")
    strs_push(l, "malformed asset is refused by name; an id no tokenizer has is `unsupported`, never another")
    strs_push(l, "tokenizer. Changing a version or an asset changes the identity.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Three families.** `openai_bpe` (byte-level BPE over a regex pre-split, no normalisation;")
    strs_push(l, "`cl100k_base` and `o200k_base` are one family, two vocabularies), `sentencepiece_bpe` (Mistral")
    strs_push(l, "7B v0.1: merges over metaspace pieces with byte fallback) and `sentencepiece_unigram` (T5-small:")
    strs_push(l, "the most probable segmentation under per-piece scores, after the model's own NFKC-style")
    strs_push(l, "normalisation and whitespace split). The two SentencePiece models are different algorithms, not")
    strs_push(l, "two vocabularies of one: the files say `BPE` with 58,980 merges and a list of scored pieces, and the")
    strs_push(l, "tests hold both.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The special-token law.** A count is of content: the exact text encoded as ordinary text.")
    strs_push(l, "OpenAI's special-token strings count as text; the SentencePiece templates' `<s>` and `</s>` are")
    strs_push(l, "not added, and are reported beside the count as `framing_tokens`. Chat roles, system framing and")
    strs_push(l, "vendor protocol overhead are not measured.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The normalisation law.** Nothing is normalised before counting: the bytes measured are the")
    strs_push(l, "bytes that would be sent, and a composed and a decomposed accent are two inputs. T5 normalises;")
    strs_push(l, "that is its behaviour, recorded in its identity, and its unknown pieces are counted as")
    strs_push(l, "`unknown_tokens` — a smaller count that lost the text is reported as such.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Offline and pinned.** The assets are in `tools/tokenizers/` with their provenance; the")
    strs_push(l, "libraries are pinned exactly, with no HTTP, hub or download feature, and the crate has no network")
    strs_push(l, "code. The container the gate runs in has no network.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The multi-tokenizer benchmark law.** The seven N33 tasks, with N33's naive baselines unchanged")
    strs_push(l, "— they are defined once, in `crates/nazm-repo/tests/scenarios/`, for both benchmarks — are counted")
    strs_push(l, "under every tokenizer, each separately; reductions are integer basis points; the spread is the")
    strs_push(l, "largest minus the smallest reduction across tokenizers; the per-tokenizer median, worst and best")
    strs_push(l, "exclude only the fixed-overhead stress case, which is reported in full beside them. Every N33")
    strs_push(l, "mechanical check runs in the same pass.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Surfaces.** `nazm-tokens list` and `nazm-tokens measure [--tokenizer ID]…`, the text on")
    strs_push(l, "standard input and never a path argument, one `nazm.token-cost/1` object on stdout. To measure a")
    strs_push(l, "task context: `nazm repo --task … --json | nazm-tokens measure`. There is no MCP tool: a server")
    strs_push(l, "that answers from the disk has no text of its own to measure, and would have to link a tokenizer.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not here.** Token budgets, token-ranked selection, a compact transport,")
    strs_push(l, "tokenizer-driven identity changes, chat-template accounting, model calls, and a persistent count")
    strs_push(l, "cache.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.37 Agent task token, cost and correctness benchmark — settled by N35, 2026-09-29")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "suite::build()        the N33 scenarios' baselines and `nazm repo --task` contexts, digested;")
    strs_push(l, "        │             truths read from the authorities; witnesses in both contexts")
    strs_push(l, "        ▼")
    strs_push(l, "run::plan()           task × arm × trial, arms alternating by trial, one independent request each")
    strs_push(l, "        │  budget check before every attempt, ≤ 2 retries of transport failures only")
    strs_push(l, "        ▼")
    strs_push(l, "Provider              openai (Chat Completions) · anthropic (Messages) · fake (tests)")
    strs_push(l, "        │  curl, credential on standard input — the only network access in the workspace")
    strs_push(l, "        ▼")
    strs_push(l, "journal.jsonl         nazm.agent-benchmark/1 records, raw usage beside normalised usage")
    strs_push(l, "        │  oracle::score() offline, fact by fact; price list applied, never in identity")
    strs_push(l, "        ▼")
    strs_push(l, "report::build()       per task, category and provider: correctness first, then tokens and cost")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The evaluation boundary.** `nazm-agent-bench` is evaluation tooling. No crate depends on it —")
    strs_push(l, "the layering table lists it nowhere — and it is the only crate allowed to depend on")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-tokens`; the `tokenizer reach` gate refuses any other. It reads the planner and the")
    strs_push(l, "authorities through `nazm-repo`, `nazm-service` and `nazm-docs`; nothing it learns flows back. A")
    strs_push(l, "model's answer is never compiler truth: it enters no specification, no semantic database and no")
    strs_push(l, "capability evidence other than this benchmark's own results.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The context-arm law.** Each task has two contexts and the requests differ only in them. The")
    strs_push(l, "baseline is the N33 scenario's naive texts — the whole files the facts are in, the whole")
    strs_push(l, "documents, the catalogue entries a search would show — each under a `==> label <==` line naming")
    strs_push(l, "what it is. The N33 context is `nazm repo --task`'s output for the scenario's request, byte for")
    strs_push(l, "byte, never trimmed. The system text, the layout, the task's wording, the answer contract, the")
    strs_push(l, "model, its parameters and the output budget are one value for both arms. Every context is")
    strs_push(l, "addressed by the BLAKE3 of its bytes, and a task whose two contexts have one digest is refused.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The oracle law.** Every truth is read from an authority — the service's packets, a")
    strs_push(l, "documentation section, the mutation catalogue parsed independently — never from either context,")
    strs_push(l, "and a truth that rests on a section's statement is checked against the section's text, so a")
    strs_push(l, "reworded section stops the suite. Answers are JSON; each field is scored by an explicit,")
    strs_push(l, "mechanical normalisation: a definition as `file::name`, a test by its function name, a target by")
    strs_push(l, "its name, a citation as `document:id`, a scalar against a listed set of spellings. A fact is")
    strs_push(l, "correct or missing. A claim the truths do not contain is *hallucinated* when the supplied context")
    strs_push(l, "does not support it either, and a *wrong repository fact* when it does; a real section cited")
    strs_push(l, "beyond the required ones is recorded and neither credited nor counted. Solved is every fact")
    strs_push(l, "correct, no false claim, a valid object and no refusal. Every task's witnesses occur in both")
    strs_push(l, "contexts, so a refusal is always a failure here. No reasoning is requested or scored.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The usage and cost law.** Usage is the provider's report, kept raw and normalised into total")
    strs_push(l, "input (cached parts included), uncached input, cache reads, cache writes, output and, where")
    strs_push(l, "reported, the reasoning part of output; `total_tokens` is input plus output and nothing else.")
    strs_push(l, "Prices are dated entries of `tools/agent-bench/pricing.toml`, with their source, applied to")
    strs_push(l, "usage and never part of an identity: a result can be priced again. Money is integer pico-USD — a")
    strs_push(l, "price in micro-USD per million tokens is pico-USD per token — so every cost is an exact product.")
    strs_push(l, "Local `o200k_base` counts of the context and of the fixed rest are recorded beside the")
    strs_push(l, "provider's; where the provider can count without generating, its counts of the request with and")
    strs_push(l, "without the context are recorded too, so the fixed prompt is never credited to a context.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Benchmark identity.** A request's identity is its task, arm, trial, provider, requested model,")
    strs_push(l, "every request parameter, the prompt version and template digest, the suite version and the")
    strs_push(l, "context digest. A benchmark's identity is the suite digest, the prompt, the mode, the trial")
    strs_push(l, "count, the provider, the model and the parameters. A reply from a model other than the one")
    strs_push(l, "requested is recorded as `model_drift` and stops the run; it is never compared.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The budget and retry law.** A run needs an explicit cap. Before every attempt, retries")
    strs_push(l, "included, the attempt's worst case — every input token uncached at the provider's bound over the")
    strs_push(l, "local count, and the whole output budget — is added to everything the evidence directory's")
    strs_push(l, "ledger has charged, and the attempt is refused if the sum passes the cap. A transport failure is")
    strs_push(l, "retried at most twice; a reply never is. A request with no reply is a `runner_error`: not scored,")
    strs_push(l, "never incorrect. A dry run computes the plan, the context sizes and the worst case with no")
    strs_push(l, "provider, credential or network.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The resume law.** The journal is appended and synced one record at a time. A resumed run skips")
    strs_push(l, "every request whose identity has a record, and repeats a runner error only when asked to. A pilot")
    strs_push(l, "is its own benchmark identity and never evidence; the report reads authoritative records only.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The network boundary.** Only `nazm-agent-bench run` reaches a network, through `curl`, with the")
    strs_push(l, "headers — the credential among them — on `curl`'s standard input and the body in a temporary")
    strs_push(l, "file, never on a command line. The credential comes from the environment or an owner-only file,")
    strs_push(l, "is never serialised, and is removed from any error text kept. Every contained workload, and so")
    strs_push(l, "every test and mutation killer, still runs with no network; the tests drive the runner with a")
    strs_push(l, "fake provider and the adapters with recorded responses.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not here.** Tool-using agents, multi-turn repair, automatic routing between raw")
    strs_push(l, "source and structured context, prompt tuning per arm, and any provider framework beyond the two")
    strs_push(l, "adapters the benchmark uses.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.38 Typed effects — settled by N36, 2026-09-29")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "parse        fn f() -> Int ! { io } { … }        EffectDecl: names and spans, as written")
    strs_push(l, "  │")
    strs_push(l, "declare      crate::effects::declared            N0367 unknown · N0368 duplicate (fix) → FnDef.declared_effects")
    strs_push(l, "  │                                               Export.effects → nazm.interface/6 (by name, id order; absent = undeclared)")
    strs_push(l, "check        record_site per call and spawn      Callee::Builtin | Callee::Function, spawned")
    strs_push(l, "  │")
    strs_push(l, "settle       crate::effects::analyse             direct effects + callees', Jacobi rounds to the least fixed point")
    strs_push(l, "  │                                               FnDef.inferred_effects, FnDef.effect_reasons")
    strs_push(l, "contract     inferred ⊆ declared?                N0366 at the first missing effect's site, shortest witness, fix for review")
    strs_push(l, "  │")
    strs_push(l, "tools        signature · hover · nazm.context/2 · nazm.snapshot/2 · nazm.delta/2")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Effect authority.** `nazm_sema::Effect` is the compiler's: two variants, each with a stable")
    strs_push(l, "`id` that is never reused or reordered, a name, and nothing else. A built-in's effect is")
    strs_push(l, "`Effect::of_intrinsic`, an exhaustive `match` on the built-in's identity, so a built-in added")
    strs_push(l, "without being classified does not compile; the call graph the checker already records — each")
    strs_push(l, "call site's resolved callee, and whether it is a `spawn` — is the only input. Nothing reads a")
    strs_push(l, "spelling: a name resolves to an effect only inside an effect set, in a namespace of its own.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Canonical sets.** `EffectSet` is a bit per id: order-free and duplicate-free by construction,")
    strs_push(l, "iterated, printed (`{ io, spawn }`, the formatter's spelling) and persisted in id order, so no")
    strs_push(l, "map iteration can reach a set, a diagnostic or a digest. Purity is the empty set; no other flag")
    strs_push(l, "exists. The only relation between sets is `is_within`; there is no effect subtyping beyond it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Propagation.** After `check_unit` has checked every body of a module, `effects::analyse` builds,")
    strs_push(l, "per function, its direct effects — each built-in's, each `spawn`'s — and its edges to the module's")
    strs_push(l, "undeclared functions. A declared callee contributes its set, a constant; an imported callee")
    strs_push(l, "contributes the importer's view of its export — the declared set, or **every** effect when it")
    strs_push(l, "declares none; a callee whose body did not parse contributes nothing, since it is already an")
    strs_push(l, "error. Then rounds: each reads only the previous round's sets, so visiting order cannot change a")
    strs_push(l, "result, and the lattice is finite, so at most functions × effects rounds settle it — cycles")
    strs_push(l, "included. The first reason each effect was added is kept; the callee had it a round earlier, so a")
    strs_push(l, "chain of reasons is acyclic, and rounds being breadth-first it is a shortest one. No provenance")
    strs_push(l, "graph is kept: one reason per effect per function.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The contract and its witness.** A declared set whose body requires more is `N0366`: one")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostic per function, at the first site requiring the first missing effect in id order, with a")
    strs_push(l, "secondary label per hop of the witness through the module's inferred functions to the built-in, the")
    strs_push(l, "`spawn`, the contract or the undeclared import where it ends, and a fix for review that declares")
    strs_push(l, "the union. A declaration naming an unknown effect is treated as unwritten after its `N0367`, so a")
    strs_push(l, "single mistake is a single error.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The module boundary.** `Export.effects` is the declared set, and only it is persisted:")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.interface/6` writes it by name in id order, `[]` for `! {}`, absent for no declaration, and")
    strs_push(l, "reads it back validated — an unknown name or a non-canonical order is refused. This is forced by")
    strs_push(l, "the cache design and is the right rule anyway: a module's interface hash is taken over its")
    strs_push(l, "**declarations** before any body is checked (N4), so a body-inferred set could not be in it")
    strs_push(l, "without a body change reaching importers unnoticed. A contract in the interface means an effect")
    strs_push(l, "change is an interface change, so every importer's key moves; a body change within its contract")
    strs_push(l, "moves nothing an importer depends on. `SEMANTIC_EPOCH` is 8: the checker refuses what it accepted")
    strs_push(l, "before.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Tooling.** The signature renderer appends a declared set (and a built-in's own effect), so hover,")
    strs_push(l, "completion, signature help and packets show `fn f() -> Int ! { io }`; hover adds an undeclared")
    strs_push(l, "function's inferred set on a line of its own, since it is not a declaration. `nazm.context/2`")
    strs_push(l, "gives a function's `effects` — declared, required, published and one reason per effect, with the")
    strs_push(l, "call's range and the built-in or callee's identity — where `/1` had the section `unsupported`.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.snapshot/2` digests an `effects` section per function (declared or not, and required), and")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.delta/2` reports it, so an effect-only change is never reported as unchanged. `DefKey` is")
    strs_push(l, "untouched: an effect change changes a definition's shape, not which definition it is, so rename,")
    strs_push(l, "references, call hierarchy and semantic tokens are unaffected. `nazm.diagnostic-detail/1`'s typed")
    strs_push(l, "facts stay `unavailable`: the effect facts are in the packet.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**No runtime.** Nothing reaches lowering. `nazm build` emits the same IR for a program with its")
    strs_push(l, "effects declared and without them; the interpreter never reads a set. When Core IR and MIR exist,")
    strs_push(l, "a function's checked set is on its `FnDef` for lowering to carry, which is where a later profile")
    strs_push(l, "(no `io`, no `spawn`) or an optimisation that needs to know a call is effect-free would read it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not here.** Handlers, effect variables and polymorphism, user-defined effects,")
    strs_push(l, "`alloc`, `native`/`unsafe`/`foreign` (no FFI exists to exercise them), divergence and panic as")
    strs_push(l, "effects, capabilities and authority (§7.39 since N37), profiles that forbid effects, completion of effect names,")
    strs_push(l, "and the Nazm-written compiler reading effect sets — its lexer and parser do not, and no source it")
    strs_push(l, "reads writes one (`examples/effects/` is outside the folders its agreement tests read).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.39 Capabilities and authority — settled by N37, 2026-09-30")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "types        Type::Cap(CapabilityKind)            IoCap, SpawnCap: built-in names, Type::ALL, no equality leaf")
    strs_push(l, "  │")
    strs_push(l, "check        record_site per call and spawn      CallSite.held = kinds of the capability bindings a name reaches")
    strs_push(l, "  │           construction of a capability        N0370 (record form and call form)")
    strs_push(l, "  │           main's parameters                   N0371 unless every one is a capability")
    strs_push(l, "settle       crate::effects::analyse             effects to the least fixed point (§7.38), unchanged")
    strs_push(l, "  │")
    strs_push(l, "authority    crate::effects::authority           per function with a declared set, per site, in body order:")
    strs_push(l, "  │                                               built-in → CapabilityKind::of_intrinsic")
    strs_push(l, "  │                                               spawn → to_start_a_task")
    strs_push(l, "  │                                               undeclared callee → for_effects(its effects; every effect if imported)")
    strs_push(l, "  │                                               required ∖ held → N0369 once per kind, witness, no fix")
    strs_push(l, "contract     inferred ⊆ declared?                N0366, after the function's N0369s")
    strs_push(l, "  │")
    strs_push(l, "runtime      interpreter: Value::Cap(kind) for main's parameters · native: an i64 0 per root in the entry wrapper")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Effect versus authority.** An effect (§7.38) is what a function does; a capability is what allows")
    strs_push(l, "it to. `nazm_sema::CapabilityKind` is the compiler's: two variants with stable ids, each the")
    strs_push(l, "authority for one effect today (`CapabilityKind::for_effect`, exhaustive, returning a")
    strs_push(l, "`CapabilitySet` so a finer mapping is a table change). A built-in's required authority is")
    strs_push(l, "`CapabilityKind::of_intrinsic`, a second exhaustive table on the built-in's identity — written out")
    strs_push(l, "rather than derived from `Effect::of_intrinsic`, since what a built-in does and what allows it are")
    strs_push(l, "two questions, and a unit test holds the two consistent. `spawn`'s is `to_start_a_task`: authority")
    strs_push(l, "to **create** a task, kept apart from whatever the task itself does.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Identity and namespace.** A capability's type is `Type::Cap(kind)`: a built-in type, in")
    strs_push(l, "`Type::ALL`, parsed by `Type::from_name` and refused as a declaration by the existing")
    strs_push(l, "`BUILTIN_TYPE_REDEFINED`. Kind and resource are separate by construction: the kind is the whole of a")
    strs_push(l, "v1 capability, and a resource-specific one would be `Cap` with an argument, not a new mechanism.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Possession is lexical.** The checker's scope stack already holds every binding's type, so")
    strs_push(l, "`record_site` records, on each `CallSite`, the kinds of the capability-typed bindings a name reaches")
    strs_push(l, "there — innermost first, a shadowed binding reaching nothing. That set is the only authority input:")
    strs_push(l, "no function carries a flag, and nothing about a function's name, module or effect declaration adds")
    strs_push(l, "to it. A record containing a capability holds nothing until it is bound; a type parameter holds")
    strs_push(l, "nothing whatever instantiates it, which is parametricity rather than a special case.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The check.** After the effect fixed point, `effects::authority` runs for each function with a")
    strs_push(l, "declared set — the ones that have left the bridge — over its call sites in body order. What each")
    strs_push(l, "site needs is decided from resolution only: a built-in's table entry, a `spawn`'s `SpawnCap`, and for")
    strs_push(l, "a callee with no declared set the authority for its effects — its inferred set in this module,")
    strs_push(l, "every effect across one. A declared callee needs nothing at the call: its authority is its")
    strs_push(l, "parameters, and ordinary type checking has already made the caller supply them. What is missing is")
    strs_push(l, "`N0369`, once per kind per function at the first site needing it, with the chain through the")
    strs_push(l, "module's undeclared functions (the §7.38 reasons, followed for the effect the kind authorises) and")
    strs_push(l, "no fix. Authority diagnostics precede the function's `N0366`, so a body wrong in both is reported")
    strs_push(l, "in one order every time.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Unforgeability and the root.** No expression produces a capability: the record form and the call")
    strs_push(l, "form are `N0370`, there is no literal, conversion or default, and no built-in returns one. The root")
    strs_push(l, "is `main`, whose parameters must all be capabilities (`N0371`) and are supplied by the runtime —")
    strs_push(l, "`Interpreter::run_main` binds `Value::Cap(kind)` to each, and `emit_entry` passes an `i64 0` per")
    strs_push(l, "root. `lower` accepts a `main` whose parameters are all capabilities and still refuses any other.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Spawn.** Starting a task needs a `SpawnCap` at the `spawn`. The task's authority is whatever the")
    strs_push(l, "`spawn` passes as arguments — capabilities cross into a task because they are values, not sequences")
    strs_push(l, "— and, for a task function with no declared set, what its effects need, which the spawner must")
    strs_push(l, "hold. A task never inherits its spawner's scope.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The interface.** A capability parameter is a parameter: `nazm.interface/6` writes it as")
    strs_push(l, "`\"IoCap\"`, the built-in form every built-in type has, so authority crosses a module with no body")
    strs_push(l, "inspected and no new field. `/6` is kept deliberately: no field was added and none changed meaning,")
    strs_push(l, "an absent `effects` still means *declares none* — the rule that an importer with a contract must")
    strs_push(l, "then hold every authority is the checker's, covered by `SEMANTIC_EPOCH` 9 — and an older reader")
    strs_push(l, "refuses `IoCap` as an unknown type rather than misreading it. A capability-only change changes the")
    strs_push(l, "export's parameter list, so the interface fingerprint, every importer's key, the snapshot's `shape`")
    strs_push(l, "digest and the delta move; `DefKey` does not, so the definition is changed, not replaced.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The compatibility bridge.** A function with no declared set is ambient: it has no authority of")
    strs_push(l, "its own and exercises its caller's. Its only root is a `main` with no set, which is handed all of it.")
    strs_push(l, "The bound is enforced at the one place the bridge meets explicit code — a call or `spawn` of an")
    strs_push(l, "ambient function from a function with a declared set needs the callee's authority held — so explicit")
    strs_push(l, "code cannot reach ambient authority, and an undeclared import is every authority. Before N37 every")
    strs_push(l, "source in the repository was ambient; each still is, unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The enforcement boundary.** Static only. `Ty::of(Type::Cap(_))` is `Ty::Int`: a word that is")
    strs_push(l, "always 0 and that nothing reads — a word rather than a zero-sized `{}` because every storage, copy")
    strs_push(l, "and sequence path already handles a word, where a zero-byte element would reach a zero-byte")
    strs_push(l, "allocation. A capability parameter's function lowers to exactly the IR of the same function taking")
    strs_push(l, "an `Int`. There is no runtime check, no sandbox and no operating-system boundary; erasure permits")
    strs_push(l, "no forgery because forgery is refused before anything runs.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Tooling.** Nothing new: a capability is a built-in type to hover, signature help, completion")
    strs_push(l, "(offered in type positions as a built-in type, never in a call head as a constructor), semantic")
    strs_push(l, "tokens and packets. `nazm.context/2`, `nazm.snapshot/2` and `nazm.delta/2` are unchanged — a")
    strs_push(l, "function's authority is its parameter list, which they already carry, and whether it is ambient is")
    strs_push(l, "whether `effects.declared` is null. No machine schema was added.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not here.** Attenuation and resource-specific kinds (nothing narrower exists to")
    strs_push(l, "derive), revocation, linear or affine capabilities, lifetimes, capability polymorphism,")
    strs_push(l, "user-defined capabilities, channels as authority, restriction profiles, foreign and unsafe")
    strs_push(l, "authority, runtime enforcement, retiring the bridge, and the Nazm-written compiler reading")
    strs_push(l, "capabilities — no source it reads declares one (`examples/capabilities/` is outside its")
    strs_push(l, "agreement tests' folders).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.40 Provenance and information flow — settled by N38, 2026-09-30")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "check_unit      each module's bodies, as before")
    strs_push(l, "  │")
    strs_push(l, "facts           crate::provenance::facts          one walk per body over resolution (vars, callees):")
    strs_push(l, "  │                                                 FunctionFacts { calls, result, sinks } as Flows")
    strs_push(l, "  │                                                 Flow = origins + why spans + params + call indices")
    strs_push(l, "  │             Reuse::checked_clean(m, facts)    kept in nazm.check/2 beside the interface")
    strs_push(l, "  │             Reuse::facts(m)                   a reused module's, rehydrated by durable name")
    strs_push(l, "solve           crate::provenance::solve          every module's facts, every run:")
    strs_push(l, "  │                                                 worklist 1: origins + passed-on params (least fixed point)")
    strs_push(l, "  │                                                 worklist 2: params reaching write_file's path")
    strs_push(l, "  │                                                 fixed point 3: origins each param is handed")
    strs_push(l, "restrict        explicit functions only           N0372 at the sink or the call, one witness chain")
    strs_push(l, "  │")
    strs_push(l, "tools           FnDef.provenance → nazm.context/3 · nazm.snapshot/3 · nazm.delta/3")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Provenance authority.** `nazm_sema::Origin` is the compiler's: four variants with stable ids —")
    strs_push(l, "`argument`, `file`, `authority`, `unknown` — and the absence of all four is local. A built-in's flow")
    strs_push(l, "is `Origin::of_intrinsic`, an exhaustive table on its identity: a source of one origin, a function")
    strs_push(l, "of its arguments, a read out of shared storage (`unknown`), a fresh handle, or the one sink. No")
    strs_push(l, "source syntax names an origin, so none can be forged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Summary representation.** A body is reduced once to `FunctionFacts`: its call sites (callee,")
    strs_push(l, "place, each argument's `Flow`), its result's `Flow` and its sinks. A `Flow` is a set of origins with")
    strs_push(l, "the first span each was met at, the enclosing function's parameters and indices of its own calls —")
    strs_push(l, "bounded by the body, whatever joins it. Solving turns each into a `Summary`: result origins,")
    strs_push(l, "passed-on parameters, parameters reaching a sink, and the origins each parameter is handed. There")
    strs_push(l, "is no symbolic execution and no per-operation identity; a function returning a constant has an")
    strs_push(l, "empty summary.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The join law and the walk.** `Flow::join` is a set union and reports whether it grew. Bindings")
    strs_push(l, "are flow-insensitive slots: a walk joins every assignment into its slot and re-walks only if a slot")
    strs_push(l, "grew after the same walk read it, which is exactly when another walk could differ — so a body")
    strs_push(l, "settles in one walk unless a loop or a later assignment feeds an earlier read. Conditions are walked")
    strs_push(l, "for their calls and contribute nothing to values.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Fixed points.** Three, over the settled facts of every module. Summaries grow from empty; a")
    strs_push(l, "worklist re-queues the callers of a function whose summary grew, seeded callees-last-first, and")
    strs_push(l, "empties because origins and parameter positions are finite — recursion, mutual recursion and import")
    strs_push(l, "cycles need no special case, and source order changes how soon, never what. Reaching a sink is a")
    strs_push(l, "second worklist over the settled values; what parameters are handed is a third. Call values inside")
    strs_push(l, "one function are their own small fixed point, since a loop can feed a call's result into its own")
    strs_push(l, "argument.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Module persistence.** Facts name callees by module key and name, and places by byte range in the")
    strs_push(l, "module's own file, as `nazm_iface::PersistentFacts`. They are a function of exactly what a module's")
    strs_push(l, "`CheckKey` covers — its source and its imports' declarations — so they sit in the check entry, whose")
    strs_push(l, "schema moved to `nazm.check/2`, and no key changed. A reused module's facts are rehydrated strictly;")
    strs_push(l, "anything that does not fit this compilation is no facts, and a module without facts is solved as the")
    strs_push(l, "worst case — every origin `unknown`, every parameter passed on and reaching the sink — never as")
    strs_push(l, "local. `nazm.interface/6` did not move: the interface is declarations, and facts are not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Incremental invalidation.** None is needed, and that is the design: conclusions are never cached.")
    strs_push(l, "The whole program is solved every run from every module's facts, fresh or kept, so a callee's body")
    strs_push(l, "edit that changes its summary reaches a caller whose own entry was reused, in the same run. What a")
    strs_push(l, "cache hit saves is the body check and the walk; the solve is a few milliseconds over the facts.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Diagnostic witnesses.** `N0372` is raised only in functions with a declared effect set, at the")
    strs_push(l, "`write_file` or at the call that hands a restricted value to a parameter that reaches one. Its")
    strs_push(l, "labels are one deterministic chain: through callee results (`g returns data from …`) and")
    strs_push(l, "pass-through calls to the span where the origin entered, and, for a call, through the callee's")
    strs_push(l, "calls to its `write_file`. Diagnostics are sorted by span within a function, after its N0369s and")
    strs_push(l, "N0366.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Runtime erasure.** Nothing reaches lowering: `nazm-lir` reads no provenance, and the IR of every")
    strs_push(l, "example and of `compiler/emit.nz` is byte-identical under N37 and N38. The interpreter never reads a")
    strs_push(l, "summary. There is no runtime tag, table or object.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Security limitations.** Explicit data flow only: implicit flow through conditions, timing and")
    strs_push(l, "every side channel are outside it. Records, variants and `Result` are tracked whole; sequences,")
    strs_push(l, "`Vec`s and channels are `unknown` on every read, because aliasing hides their writers. One sink.")
    strs_push(l, "Ambient functions' own writes are not checked. No declassification, sanitiser, user label or")
    strs_push(l, "policy exists. This is explicit information-flow provenance and a single restricted flow — not")
    strs_push(l, "non-interference, confidentiality enforcement or a sandbox.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.41 Core IR: the constitution — N39, 2026-09-30")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the representation, so that the structs follow the law and not the other way")
    strs_push(l, "round. `crates/nazm-cir` holds the representation; this section is what it is allowed to be.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "source ─ parse ─ AST ─ check ─ Resolution ─┐")
    strs_push(l, "                                           ├─ nazm-core::lower (only after checking succeeded)")
    strs_push(l, "                                           ▼")
    strs_push(l, "                                  Core IR  (crates/nazm-cir, nazm.core-ir/1)")
    strs_push(l, "                                   │     │")
    strs_push(l, "                interpreter ───────┘     └─── nazm-lir::lower ─ LIR ─ LLVM text ─ clang")
    strs_push(l, "                (nazm-core::eval)              (reads no syntax tree and no position map)")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What Core IR represents.** The checked meaning of each function body, once: every value typed,")
    strs_push(l, "every name replaced by what it resolved to, every control transfer explicit, every piece of")
    strs_push(l, "surface sugar gone. It is the one lowering from a checked program; the interpreter and the native")
    strs_push(l, "backend both start from it, and neither reads the syntax tree or the checker's position maps")
    strs_push(l, "(the span-keyed answers: callee, binding, field, variant, payload, propagation, construction,")
    strs_push(l, "type arguments, checked call).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it deliberately omits.** Syntax: spellings, parentheses, statement-versus-expression")
    strs_push(l, "position, `?`, the shape an `if` or a block was written in. Layout: field offsets, discriminants,")
    strs_push(l, "aggregate shapes, symbols, linkage — the backend's, below the layout boundary of §2. Ownership")
    strs_push(l, "operations: no retain, release, move or drop instruction exists; what Core IR carries is the")
    strs_push(l, "semantic fact they are derived from, which locals a region owns until its exit (below).")
    strs_push(l, "Provenance: it stays a checker fact (below). Level 3 of §2 is also described as ANF with traits")
    strs_push(l, "as dictionaries; v1 is neither — it is a typed tree, and the language has no traits.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**When it is constructed.** Only from a program that checked with no diagnostics, by")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-core`'s lowering, which is private to that crate and reached only through its checked entry")
    strs_push(l, "points. A parse or check failure produces no Core IR. The language service, completion, the")
    strs_push(l, "repository map and every other tool that reads incomplete source never construct it. A failure")
    strs_push(l, "inside lowering after a clean check is a compiler defect, reported as one; there is no fallback")
    strs_push(l, "to any other lowering.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Invariants every consumer may assume.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "1. *Typed.* Every expression carries the type the checker established for it, read from the")
    strs_push(l, "   checker's facts — a binding's type, a checked call's result, a record field's or payload's")
    strs_push(l, "   declared type, the enum a variant constructs — and composed structurally, never inferred.")
    strs_push(l, "   The one other state is *never*: an `if`, `match` or block every path of which transfers")
    strs_push(l, "   control produces no value, and says so.")
    strs_push(l, "2. *Resolved.* A call names a function by its definition identity and a built-in by")
    strs_push(l, "   `Intrinsic`; a record, enum, field, variant and payload field are identities (declaration")
    strs_push(l, "   indices within a definition, as resolution spells them). No spelling is identity anywhere; a")
    strs_push(l, "   name kept for display is labelled display.")
    strs_push(l, "3. *Explicit control.* Structured regions, not basic blocks (why: below). A loop has a")
    strs_push(l, "   function-unique `LoopId`, and every `break` and `continue` names the loop it leaves or")
    strs_push(l, "   restarts — a `break` in a loop's condition names the enclosing loop, as the language has")
    strs_push(l, "   always meant. `return` carries its value. Each region states whether it falls through or")
    strs_push(l, "   transfers, and a value region has a tail exactly when it falls through. `if` without `else`")
    strs_push(l, "   exists only as a statement; `?` is a `match` whose error arm returns.")
    strs_push(l, "4. *Deterministic.* Functions in declaration order, locals in slot order, constants in first-use")
    strs_push(l, "   order, loops in source order, arms and initialisers in written order. The printed form of a")
    strs_push(l, "   program is a function of the checked program; no map iteration order reaches it.")
    strs_push(l, "5. *Source-linked, not source-identified.* Each node carries the span a diagnostic about it")
    strs_push(l, "   points at; a compiler-made node (the `match` a `?` becomes, its two bindings) is marked as")
    strs_push(l, "   such and carries the span of the source it came from. Spans are metadata: no digest includes")
    strs_push(l, "   one.")
    strs_push(l, "6. *Backend-neutral.* Nothing in it names LLVM, a slot index the emitter chose, a native type or")
    strs_push(l, "   a runtime entry point.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**IDs.** A function is its `FnId`, the checker's session-local definition identity — a Core IR")
    strs_push(l, "function exists for each and at the same index. A local is a `LocalId`: the checker's slots,")
    strs_push(l, "parameters first, then Core IR's own temporaries. A loop is a `LoopId`, a constant a `ConstId`,")
    strs_push(l, "both per function. None is a `DefKey`: those are durable names for definitions, and an IR entity")
    strs_push(l, "that lives for one compilation does not get one. The printed form names definitions and types by")
    strs_push(l, "their durable keys, so it reads the same from any checkout.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The printed form, `nazm.core-ir/3` (R3, 2026-10-15).** `/3` prints what a lowering written")
    strs_push(l, "outside this workspace (R3's `toolchain/pipeline/`) needs and could only recover from uses under")
    strs_push(l, "`/2`. Every `/2` field stays where it was. A function type is spelled `fn(Int) -> Str ! { io }`,")
    strs_push(l, "with an effect parameter written `$effects`, and an array type `[Int; 4]`. `/2` wrote `?` for")
    strs_push(l, "both, and the digests still do, so no digest moved. Each function gains `pub`, `closure`,")
    strs_push(l, "`captures` (the locals holding them) and `attributes`: `export`, `section`, `interrupt`, `task`")
    strs_push(l, "(`priority`, `period`) and `on_failure`. At the root, beside `functions`, are `modules` in load")
    strs_push(l, "order, each with its name, `root`, `prelude` and `imports`, and `types`. `types.records` and")
    strs_push(l, "`types.enums` are the checker's tables in its id order, generic definitions and applied instances")
    strs_push(l, "alike. Each entry has its `type` (the spelling used everywhere else), `display` (as a message")
    strs_push(l, "shows it), `definition`, `module`, `pub`, `type_args`, its fields or variants with their names")
    strs_push(l, "and types in declaration order, and `canonical` orders. Then come `statics`, each with its key,")
    strs_push(l, "`type`, `cell`, starting `value` and `section`; `impls`, each impl's trait, `self` type and, per")
    strs_push(l, "method, the function a call reaches, its `type_args` and whether it is the trait's `default`; and")
    strs_push(l, "`derived_hash`. Every one of these is a fact the checker settled, printed rather than decided.")
    strs_push(l, "A function's `Atomic` constant, whose `value` is `static NAME` as its module spells it, also")
    strs_push(l, "carries `static`: that static's durable key, the `def` of its `statics` entry. Two modules may each")
    strs_push(l, "declare a `static COUNT`, and only the key says which cell a use reaches. The field was added")
    strs_push(l, "within `/3` (R4's finding, 2026-10-15): every existing field keeps its place and meaning, the")
    strs_push(l, "schema is debug/internal, and a reader of the earlier output loses nothing it had. No digest moved.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Why regions and not basic blocks.** Both consumers are structured: the interpreter walks a tree,")
    strs_push(l, "and LIR is a structured tree the emitter turns into LLVM blocks, placing releases by region. A CFG")
    strs_push(l, "here would force a re-structuring pass downstream — a second analysis of control flow, which is")
    strs_push(l, "what this milestone removes — and would lose the region-ownership facts. Explicit loop targets and")
    strs_push(l, "explicit completion give every consumer what blocks would, without it. There is no SSA and no phi:")
    strs_push(l, "locals are mutable slots, `let` binds one, assignment writes one. A MIR may choose blocks.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Generics.** Core IR is generic, as checking is: a generic function's body is lowered once, its")
    strs_push(l, "types mentioning its own parameters, and each call records its type arguments. The interpreter")
    strs_push(l, "runs it parametrically; the native backend instantiates it by substitution, as before. There is")
    strs_push(l, "no second generic system and no monomorphisation above the backend.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Runtime primitives.** `Intrinsic`, the built-in table the checker reads — explicit, typed,")
    strs_push(l, "enumerated. `Vec[T]` operations carry their element type. Channels, `spawn` and `scope` are Core IR")
    strs_push(l, "operations; nothing is lowered to a thread or a runtime call here.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Equality.** A comparison states its operand type and which law applies — integer, boolean,")
    strs_push(l, "bytes, or the derived structural equality of a named record or enum — or, in a generic body,")
    strs_push(l, "that the parameter's instance decides. No consumer discovers it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Effects and authority.** Each function carries its declared effect set, the set its body")
    strs_push(l, "requires, and whether it is pure; its parameters' types say which capabilities it holds, since")
    strs_push(l, "a capability is an ordinary typed value. Nothing re-infers either, and neither becomes a global")
    strs_push(l, "permission flag.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The provenance boundary.** Provenance is decided before Core IR and stays in the checker's")
    strs_push(l, "summaries (`FnDef::provenance`, `nazm.check/2`). Core IR carries none — nothing below it reads")
    strs_push(l, "provenance, and a per-node origin set would be the bulk §7.40 avoided. No Core IR digest covers it;")
    strs_push(l, "the check artefact owns it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Memory management.** No retain or release is in Core IR. What survives is the semantic ownership")
    strs_push(l, "level: every region lists the locals bound in it, which the language releases at its exit, and a")
    strs_push(l, "`match` owns its scrutinee. The interpreter drops at exactly those points; LIR places native")
    strs_push(l, "retains and releases from the same regions and from each type's ownership law. That boundary is")
    strs_push(l, "the one a MIR will lower across.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Digests.** Two per function, BLAKE3 over a canonical encoding that names every definition and")
    strs_push(l, "type durably and omits every span, display name and session-local number:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- *semantic*: the signature, the effect contract (declared and required), purity, and the body;")
    strs_push(l, "- *body*: what code generation reads — parameter, local and result types and the body — and no")
    strs_push(l, "  effect metadata.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An effect-only change moves the first and not the second; a capability-parameter change moves")
    strs_push(l, "both, because Core IR is typed and a capability is a type, even though the native backend erases")
    strs_push(l, "it (machine-code identity is the object cache's key, the emitted IR's bytes, §7.9); a")
    strs_push(l, "provenance-only change moves neither. A digest is not an identity: two functions with equal")
    strs_push(l, "digests are two definitions.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Incremental boundary.** Core IR is built per module from the current run's full check and is")
    strs_push(l, "never persisted in v1; each function's digests exist for the caches that will key on them. Nothing")
    strs_push(l, "is reused across runs at this level yet, so nothing can be reused wrongly.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Backend boundary.** Below Core IR a consumer may read the checker's semantic tables —")
    strs_push(l, "definitions, signatures, visibility, the call graph, the user-type table — and nothing that answers")
    strs_push(l, "a question about a source position. `cargo xtask check` enforces it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.42 MIR: the constitution — N40, 2026-09-30")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the representation, like §7.41. `crates/nazm-mir` holds MIR; this section is what")
    strs_push(l, "it is allowed to be.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "Core IR (nazm-cir) ─ nazm-mir::lower (instances, CFG, cleanup) ─ MIR (nazm.mir/1) ─ verify")
    strs_push(l, "                                                                    │")
    strs_push(l, "                          interpreter stays on Core IR              └─ nazm-lir: layout, symbols,")
    strs_push(l, "                          (a tree walker; §7.41)                       LLVM text ─ clang")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What MIR represents.** Each *concrete* function the native program contains — every")
    strs_push(l, "non-generic definition and every generic instance a program needs — as an explicit control-flow")
    strs_push(l, "graph whose ownership and cleanup obligations are written out. A backend reading MIR makes no")
    strs_push(l, "language decision: which loop a `break` leaves, what a `?` does, which values die on an edge,")
    strs_push(l, "which scopes must be joined before a `return`, whether a construction that failed half-way must")
    strs_push(l, "release what it took — all are statements and terminators in MIR.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it deliberately omits.** Syntax and everything Core IR already omits. Layout (field")
    strs_push(l, "positions, discriminants, sizes), symbols, mangling, linkage, object files, registers, stack")
    strs_push(l, "slots, calling conventions, relocations: the backend's, below MIR. Provenance: none (below).")
    strs_push(l, "Effects are function-level metadata only; nothing in MIR re-infers or checks them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**When Core IR becomes MIR.** Only for `nazm build`, after the program checked cleanly and Core IR")
    strs_push(l, "was built and verified. MIR lowering plans the generic instances (moved here from `nazm-lir`,")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged: the same planner and bounds), then lowers each concrete function once. The")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter does not use MIR (below). A MIR the validator rejects after a clean check is a")
    strs_push(l, "compiler defect, `N0900`, and nothing is emitted.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Front-end, MIR and backend concerns.** Front end: names, types, exhaustiveness, effects,")
    strs_push(l, "capabilities, provenance, which region owns which binding (§7.41). MIR: instantiation, the CFG,")
    strs_push(l, "evaluation into temporaries in the language's order, the move/copy/drop of every managed value,")
    strs_push(l, "scope joins and failure edges. Backend: layout, symbols and linkage, how a primitive is")
    strs_push(l, "implemented, how a drop of a given type is expanded into runtime calls, instruction selection.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Invariants later passes may assume.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "1. *Typed.* Every local has a concrete type — a checker type with no parameter left, or the")
    strs_push(l, "   internal task-list type a `scope` holds. Every rvalue's result type is the destination's; no")
    strs_push(l, "   pass infers one.")
    strs_push(l, "2. *Resolved.* A call names a MIR function (`FuncId`); a primitive is an `Intrinsic`, with its")
    strs_push(l, "   element type for `Vec[T]`; records, fields, enums, variants and payload fields are the")
    strs_push(l, "   checker's identities (definition id plus declaration index). No string is an identity; names")
    strs_push(l, "   are display.")
    strs_push(l, "3. *Blocks and terminators.* Basic blocks, `BlockId(0)` the entry. Each block has exactly one")
    strs_push(l, "   terminator and nothing after it; statements do not transfer control except along an explicit")
    strs_push(l, "   *failure edge* (below). Terminators: `goto`, `branch` on a `Bool`, `switch` over an enum's")
    strs_push(l, "   variants (one arm per variant, no default), `return`, `unwind` (the failure exit), `exit` (the")
    strs_push(l, "   process ends: `exit_with`). No fall-through between blocks exists.")
    strs_push(l, "4. *Locals.* `LocalId`s are per function: parameters first, then the checker's bindings, then")
    strs_push(l, "   MIR's temporaries in creation order. They are ephemeral — never a `DefKey`, never persisted.")
    strs_push(l, "5. *Deterministic.* Functions: non-generic definitions in `FnId` order, then instances in")
    strs_push(l, "   canonical-key order. Blocks, locals and temporaries are numbered in creation order by a")
    strs_push(l, "   deterministic walk of Core IR; no map iteration reaches MIR.")
    strs_push(l, "6. *Source-linked.* Each statement and terminator carries the span a failure or diagnostic about")
    strs_push(l, "   it names. Compiler-made operations — drops, joins, the shared unwind block — carry a synthetic")
    strs_push(l, "   span and say so; no source position is fabricated.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Ownership law.** A value of a *managed* type (`Str`, `Ints`, `Strs`, `Chan`, `Vec[T]`, and a")
    strs_push(l, "record or enum any field of which is managed, transitively) is owned by exactly one local at a")
    strs_push(l, "time. `copy l` takes a new reference (retain); `move l` transfers the one `l` holds and leaves `l`")
    strs_push(l, "empty; `drop l` gives it back and leaves `l` empty. An operand that reads a local *borrows* it:")
    strs_push(l, "calls, primitives and comparisons borrow their arguments, and a callee never releases a")
    strs_push(l, "parameter. Every result an rvalue produces is owned by its destination — a call's result, a")
    strs_push(l, "primitive's (a string literal and `arg` are owned too: their storage is immortal and their")
    strs_push(l, "release is a no-op), a projected field or payload (retained). A record or enum is built only")
    strs_push(l, "complete, from moved temporaries: there is no partially initialised aggregate in MIR, so")
    strs_push(l, "cleanup can never reach an uninitialised field. The empty state is the representation's zero,")
    strs_push(l, "and releasing it is a no-op, which is what makes `drop` of an already-moved local safe.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Cleanup law.** Every edge that leaves a region drops what the region owns: the locals bound in")
    strs_push(l, "it so far, in reverse binding order, and every temporary still live. `return` drops everything")
    strs_push(l, "but the returned temporary, which it moves out; `break` and `continue` drop only what lies inside")
    strs_push(l, "the loop they leave, and join only the scopes opened inside it; `?` is a `match` whose error arm")
    strs_push(l, "returns (Core IR), and is cleaned like any `return`; a region's normal end drops its own. A")
    strs_push(l, "`scope` is opened by an allocation and closed by a join on **every** exit, innermost first; the")
    strs_push(l, "closing brace's join is followed by a failure check, as the language requires. Destruction order")
    strs_push(l, "is not observable (Nazm has no destructors) and is fixed anyway: reverse binding order.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Failure edges and traps.** An operation that can fail — checked arithmetic, a call (the callee")
    strs_push(l, "may have failed), a primitive, opening a scope, spawning, the failure check after a join —")
    strs_push(l, "carries an explicit edge to a cleanup block. That block joins every open scope, innermost first,")
    strs_push(l, "and goes to the function's shared unwind block, which drops every managed local (null-safe) and")
    strs_push(l, "ends in `unwind`. A trap is this edge and nothing else; a `Result` is ordinary data and ordinary")
    strs_push(l, "control flow, and never an unwind. `exit_with` ends the process with no cleanup, as it always")
    strs_push(l, "has.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Validator.** `nazm_mir::verify` checks, for every function: block targets and switch arms")
    strs_push(l, "exist; exactly one terminator per block; locals and constants exist and their types agree with")
    strs_push(l, "every operation (call signatures, primitive signatures, field and payload identities, record and")
    strs_push(l, "variant completeness, branch conditions); failure edges exist exactly on fallible operations;")
    strs_push(l, "payload reads occur only in the arm of a `switch` on the same local and variant; and, by a")
    strs_push(l, "forward dataflow over managed locals (`empty`, `owned`, `maybe`): no read of an empty local, no")
    strs_push(l, "overwrite of an owned one, no parameter dropped or moved, and at every `return` and `unwind`")
    strs_push(l, "nothing managed is still owned (no leak) and every task list has been joined. It never mutates")
    strs_push(l, "MIR, and running it twice gives the same answer.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Generics.** MIR is post-instantiation. The planner is the one `nazm-lir` used since N11, moved,")
    strs_push(l, "with its bounds (`N0357`, `N0358`); an instance is identified by its definition and its type")
    strs_push(l, "arguments' canonical keys, which is also what its backend symbol is derived from. There is no")
    strs_push(l, "second generic system.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The provenance boundary.** None. Provenance stopped above Core IR (§7.40, §7.41); MIR carries")
    strs_push(l, "no origin set and no summary. **Effects and capabilities:** each function records its published")
    strs_push(l, "effect set as metadata; a capability is an ordinary typed parameter; nothing below MIR is a")
    strs_push(l, "permission check.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Printed form and digest.** `nazm mir FILE` prints `nazm.mir/1`: deterministic JSON, internal and")
    strs_push(l, "unstable, debug-only and not read back. Each function has an *executable digest*: BLAKE3 over its")
    strs_push(l, "signature types, locals' types, blocks and constants, naming definitions and types by durable")
    strs_push(l, "key, with no span, display name or effect metadata. A source-only or effect-only change leaves it")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged; a capability-parameter change moves it (the parameter's type is part of the")
    strs_push(l, "signature); a provenance-only change cannot reach it. It is not yet a cache key: objects are still")
    strs_push(l, "keyed on the emitted unit's bytes, which are a function of MIR (§7.9).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The interpreter decision.** It stays on Core IR. It is a tree walker whose semantics are")
    strs_push(l, "Core IR's structured regions, it runs generic code parametrically, and it needs none of what MIR")
    strs_push(l, "adds — instantiation, explicit reference counting, failure edges. Moving it would be symmetry,")
    strs_push(l, "not a responsibility taken away from anywhere.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Backend boundary.** After N40 the native backend reads MIR and a source-position table for")
    strs_push(l, "failure messages, and nothing of the checker. Remaining exceptions: `nazm-lir` still takes")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-sema`'s *type and key definitions* (`Type`, `Intrinsic`, `DefKey`) as the vocabulary MIR is")
    strs_push(l, "written in — never a `Resolution`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.43 The backend boundary and the Cranelift backend — N41, 2026-10-01")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. `crates/nazm-lir/src/backend.rs` is the interface; `crates/nazm-codegen-clif`")
    strs_push(l, "is the second implementation of it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "MIR (validated) ─ nazm-lir::lower: layout, symbols, linkage, units ─ Native")
    strs_push(l, "                                                                       │")
    strs_push(l, "                     ┌─────────────────── Backend ─────────────────────┤")
    strs_push(l, "                     ▼                                                 ▼")
    strs_push(l, "          LLVM text (nazm-lir::emit)                      Cranelift (nazm-codegen-clif)")
    strs_push(l, "          → clang -c → object                             → object bytes (cranelift-object)")
    strs_push(l, "                     └──────────── clang links, with the runtime ─────┘")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Backend input.** A `Native`: validated MIR, and what `nazm-lir::lower` settled from it for every")
    strs_push(l, "backend alike — the units (one per module, one per generic instance), each function's symbol and")
    strs_push(l, "linkage, and the refusals of the native subset. A backend reads MIR and nothing of the checker,")
    strs_push(l, "and decides nothing about the language.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The interface.** `Backend` names itself (`id`, a version string that enters every cache key),")
    strs_push(l, "states its target, and turns a `Native` into artefacts: LLVM text for clang to compile, or object")
    strs_push(l, "bytes. Nothing from Cranelift appears in its signature, or in any crate above `nazm-codegen-clif`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Codegen unit.** The unit is `nazm-lir`'s: one per module and one per instance, so object reuse is")
    strs_push(l, "per unit for both backends. The runtime and the platform entry are LLVM text in every build — they")
    strs_push(l, "are the runtime, not code generated from a program's MIR, and N43 owns them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Runtime symbol boundary.** Every runtime entry point a backend calls is in one typed registry")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-runtime/src/lib.rs`; in `nazm-lir` from N43 to N52): its symbol, its parameters and result in machine words and")
    strs_push(l, "pointers only, and what it does with ownership. A revision number names the registry; it enters")
    strs_push(l, "every object's cache key. Cranelift code calls the runtime only through it. Where the runtime took")
    strs_push(l, "or returned a first-class aggregate, the registry has a pointer-taking entry (`nz.str_join_to`,")
    strs_push(l, "`nz.read_file_to`, `nz.scope_join_to`) and a scalar accessor for thread-local state")
    strs_push(l, "(`nz.failed_now`), so no aggregate crosses between code two compilers generated.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Internal calling convention (Cranelift).** The target's default convention. `Int` and a")
    strs_push(l, "capability are an `i64`, `Bool` an `i8`, a handle (`Ints`, `Strs`, `Chan`, `Vec`) a pointer; a `Str`,")
    strs_push(l, "record or enum is passed as a pointer to the caller's memory, which the callee borrows and never")
    strs_push(l, "writes, and returned through a pointer the caller supplies as the first argument. This is the")
    strs_push(l, "Cranelift backend's own convention and says nothing about C (N42).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Layout (Cranelift).** Every type has a size and an alignment: 8 for a word, 1 for a `Bool`, 24")
    strs_push(l, "for a `Str` (pointer, length, owner); a record is its fields in the canonical order with natural")
    strs_push(l, "alignment; an enum is an 8-byte discriminant followed by the largest payload, each payload laid")
    strs_push(l, "out as a record. Both backends take field positions and discriminants from `nazm-lir`'s canonical")
    strs_push(l, "tables; the byte layouts differ and never meet, because no value crosses between the two in one")
    strs_push(l, "program.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Object emission and linking.** A Cranelift unit is one object module, written by")
    strs_push(l, "`cranelift-object`. `nazm build` owns nothing past that: clang compiles the LLVM-text artefacts and")
    strs_push(l, "links every object with the runtime, with arguments built as a vector, never through a shell.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Targets.** The v1 matrix is the host: `aarch64-apple-darwin` (verified on this machine) and")
    strs_push(l, "`aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu` (the contained, authoritative evidence); `x86_64` hosts are accepted by")
    strs_push(l, "the ISA but carry no evidence. A requested target that is not the host is refused: an object for a")
    strs_push(l, "foreign target needs a foreign linker and runtime, and building one here would be a claim with")
    strs_push(l, "nothing behind it. ISA flags are Cranelift's baseline for the triple; no host feature is detected.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Settings.** `opt_level` none for `--opt-level 0`, speed otherwise; the Cranelift verifier on for")
    strs_push(l, "every function; position-independent code. All of them are in the backend's version string, so a")
    strs_push(l, "change to any of them is a new cache key.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Choice and fallback.** `nazm build --backend llvm` (the default) or `--backend cranelift`. The")
    strs_push(l, "LLVM backend stays as the default and as the differential reference. A program Cranelift cannot")
    strs_push(l, "compile is refused by name with `N0101` and nothing is written; nothing falls back to the other")
    strs_push(l, "backend without being asked.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Determinism.** The same MIR, target and settings produce the same object bytes; functions, data")
    strs_push(l, "and relocations are defined in MIR order.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Failures.** An unsupported target or operation is a diagnostic (`N0101`); a Cranelift verifier")
    strs_push(l, "rejection of generated code is a compiler defect (`N0900`); a link failure is the toolchain's and")
    strs_push(l, "reported as one — none is a program error.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.44 The ABI and the foreign-function interface — N42, 2026-10-01")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Two ABIs, never one.** The *internal* ABI is how code this compiler generated calls code this")
    strs_push(l, "compiler generated, and it is each backend's own: the LLVM backend passes and returns LLVM")
    strs_push(l, "first-class values (an `Int` an `i64`, a `Bool` an `i1`, a `Str` the `{ ptr, i64, ptr }` it is, a")
    strs_push(l, "record or enum its named struct), and the Cranelift backend follows §7.43 (in-memory values by")
    strs_push(l, "pointer, an in-memory result through a pointer passed first). Neither is C's and neither is")
    strs_push(l, "promised to anything outside one build: the backend's identity and settings are in every object's")
    strs_push(l, "cache key, the runtime's calling contract is `RUNTIME_ABI_REVISION` (`nazm-runtime/src/lib.rs`),")
    strs_push(l, "and no program mixes the two backends' objects. The *external*")
    strs_push(l, "ABI is the C calling convention of the host target, and it is the only one a foreign function is")
    strs_push(l, "called with.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**v1 scope: import only, C only, scalars only.** A Nazm program may call a C function; C may not")
    strs_push(l, "call Nazm (no export, no callbacks, no runtime entry from a foreign thread). Only two types cross:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm | C | LLVM | Cranelift |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Int` | `int64_t` | `i64` | `i64` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Bool` | `bool` (`_Bool`, one byte, 0 or 1) | `zeroext i1` | `i8`, zero-extended |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Everything else is refused by name (`N0381`): a `Str` is not a C string and has no NUL; a sequence,")
    strs_push(l, "channel, record or enum has a layout no C declaration states; a capability is authority and must")
    strs_push(l, "never become a forgeable word; generics have no single C signature. No pointer or opaque handle")
    strs_push(l, "exists in v1, so no ownership crosses the boundary and there is nothing to borrow, transfer or free.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Declaration.** `[pub] extern \"C\" fn name(p: T, …) -> R = \"symbol\";` at the top level. `extern` is")
    strs_push(l, "contextual: it is an identifier everywhere except at the start of an item, so no program that")
    strs_push(l, "names something `extern` changes meaning. The ABI string is exactly `\"C\"` (`N0380` otherwise); the")
    strs_push(l, "symbol is written, never derived, and must be a C identifier — ASCII letters, digits and `_`, not")
    strs_push(l, "starting with a digit, at most 255 bytes — which cannot collide with a Nazm symbol (those contain")
    strs_push(l, "`.`) or the runtime's (`nz.`); anything else is `N0382`, so no malformed name reaches a linker")
    strs_push(l, "command. A foreign declaration has no body, no type parameters and no written effect set (`N0384`).")
    strs_push(l, "Two declarations of one symbol with different signatures are refused (`N0383`); the same signature")
    strs_push(l, "twice is one import.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Authority and effects.** A foreign function can do anything a C function can, so calling one is")
    strs_push(l, "the effect `foreign` and needs the capability `ForeignCap`, held at the call — in every function,")
    strs_push(l, "with or without a declared effect set: N37's compatibility bridge does not extend to it, because")
    strs_push(l, "there is no older program to stay compatible with. `main` may take a `ForeignCap`, minted by the")
    strs_push(l, "runtime at start-up like `IoCap`; nothing else creates one. A wrapper that takes a `ForeignCap` and")
    strs_push(l, "calls the foreign function is the safe pattern; its callers then see `foreign` in its effects and")
    strs_push(l, "must pass it the capability. Importing a module that declares a foreign function grants nothing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Interpreter.** `nazm run` cannot call C. A program that calls a foreign function is refused before")
    strs_push(l, "it runs (`N0385`), not stopped part way; `nazm check` accepts it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Linking.** `nazm build --link FILE` adds an object or archive to the link, each as its own")
    strs_push(l, "argument, never through a shell; the path must exist. A symbol no linked file defines is the")
    strs_push(l, "linker's failure, reported with its output as a toolchain failure, never as a program error. No")
    strs_push(l, "search path, no dynamic loading and no library name resolution exist in v1.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Guarantees kept and lost.** Nazm's checks stop at the boundary. The compiler guarantees the")
    strs_push(l, "declared types and that authority was held; it cannot know what the C function does, and a call")
    strs_push(l, "into C may corrupt memory, block, never return, or longjmp — none of which Nazm's cleanup or failure")
    strs_push(l, "model survives. A foreign call cannot fail the Nazm way, so no failure edge is taken after one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Amended during implementation.** Three rules the first draft did not state. *Reserved symbols*:")
    strs_push(l, "a foreign declaration may not name a C symbol the runtime or the platform entry declares itself")
    strs_push(l, "(`main`, `malloc`, `write`, the `pthread_*` family; `nazm_core::check::RESERVED_C_SYMBOLS`, kept")
    strs_push(l, "equal to the runtime's text by a test), because two declarations of one symbol in one link could")
    strs_push(l, "disagree — `N0383`, like any other conflict, which is also checked across modules when the program")
    strs_push(l, "is built, where every unit's declarations are visible at once. *Provenance*: what C returns carries")
    strs_push(l, "the origin `unknown` and every argument's origins, so a restricted `write_file` path computed from")
    strs_push(l, "it is `N0372`; what C does with an argument is not a Nazm sink. *Threads*: a task may call C — it")
    strs_push(l, "is handed the `ForeignCap` like any value — and C then runs on that task's OS thread, so a C")
    strs_push(l, "function called from two tasks must itself be thread-safe; Nazm adds no lock around it. A failed")
    strs_push(l, "link names the program's foreign symbols and `--link`, never \"a bug in `nazm build`\".")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Interface and versions.** A `pub extern` function is exported with its symbol, so another module")
    strs_push(l, "calls it without seeing the declaration's source: `nazm.interface/7`. The language gained syntax, an")
    strs_push(l, "effect and a capability kind, so the semantic epoch moves from 10 to 11.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.45 The runtime constitution — N43, 2026-10-01")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. The native runtime is compiler-owned LLVM text linked into every")
    strs_push(l, "executable (`crates/nazm-runtime/src/`); this section is the contract it keeps with the code")
    strs_push(l, "both backends generate, with the operating system, and with the language.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the runtime is responsible for, and what it is not.** At run time: the process's entry and")
    strs_push(l, "end; the thread's failure state and the one place a failure is reported; string backings,")
    strs_push(l, "sequences and channels — their allocation, sharing and reclamation; files and the process's")
    strs_push(l, "arguments; starting and joining tasks; the memory accounting. At compile time only, and never in")
    strs_push(l, "the runtime: every check the language makes (types, effects, capabilities, provenance, ownership")
    strs_push(l, "— MIR decides every retain and release, §7.42), layout, and which runtime parts a program links.")
    strs_push(l, "The runtime makes no decision the language specifies: it carries out MIR's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**One inventory.** Every symbol the runtime defines is listed once in")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm_lir::runtime::INVENTORY` — its exact LLVM signature, the runtime part that defines it, its")
    strs_push(l, "responsibility, what it does with ownership, its failure behaviour, its thread safety, and who")
    strs_push(l, "calls it (generated code of either backend, the entry, or the runtime itself) — and every global")
    strs_push(l, "in `GLOBALS`, with who writes it and how it is synchronised. The declarations every unit sees are")
    strs_push(l, "generated from the inventory, not written beside it; the word-level view Cranelift calls through")
    strs_push(l, "(`IMPORTS`, §7.43) must agree with it entry by entry; and tests hold the runtime text to both, so")
    strs_push(l, "a symbol defined and not inventoried, inventoried and not defined, or declared with a signature")
    strs_push(l, "it is not defined with, fails the build.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Runtime ABI revision.** `RUNTIME_ABI_REVISION` names this contract: the inventory's signatures,")
    strs_push(l, "the sequence header (`len` at 0, `cap` at 8, `data` at 16, the reference count at 24), a string's")
    strs_push(l, "`(pointer, length, owner)` and a string backing's count at 0. It enters every object key of both")
    strs_push(l, "backends — Cranelift's directly, and clang's through the code generation configuration — so an")
    strs_push(l, "object built against another revision is never reused. N43 moves it to 2 because the inventory is")
    strs_push(l, "now the contract: the numbering says a revision-1 object was built against a contract nobody wrote")
    strs_push(l, "down.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Startup.** The platform's `main(argc, argv)` is the entry unit's and nothing else is an entry.")
    strs_push(l, "In order: if the program reads its arguments, `nz.argc` (one fewer than `argc`: `argv[0]` is not")
    strs_push(l, "visible) and `nz.argv` are stored — before any task exists, never written again; each root")
    strs_push(l, "capability `main` takes is minted as the word `0` (authority was checked when the program was);")
    strs_push(l, "the program's `main` is called. There is no other initialisation and no lazy one: every other")
    strs_push(l, "global is statically initialised, and every helper set is stateless until called.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Shutdown.** Three ways to end, distinguished. *Normal return*: every scope `main` opened has")
    strs_push(l, "been joined, the memory report is written to stderr if `NAZM_MEMORY_REPORT` is set, and the")
    strs_push(l, "process exits with `main`'s result as its status — one outside `0..=255` writes `N0416`'s message")
    strs_push(l, "and exits 2 — or, when `NAZM_RESULT_REPORT` is set, prints that result to stdout in decimal with")
    strs_push(l, "a newline and exits 0, as every program did before R1 (5b.3). *Failure*: the")
    strs_push(l, "memory report as above (the counts are final: nothing is still running), then `nz.report` writes")
    strs_push(l, "the thread's first failure message to stderr and exits 2. *Explicit exit*: `exit_with(code)` ends")
    strs_push(l, "the process at once with that status — no scope is joined, nothing is reclaimed, no report is")
    strs_push(l, "written — as the spec says. Nothing is freed at exit that the program had not already released:")
    strs_push(l, "the operating system reclaims the process.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Memory.** `malloc`, `realloc` and `free` are the allocator; the runtime owns every block it")
    strs_push(l, "allocates and frees it on the last release. A string backing is a 16-byte header (the reference")
    strs_push(l, "count at 0) and its bytes; a literal and `arg`'s strings are immortal (their owner is null, and")
    strs_push(l, "retaining or releasing null is a no-op). A sequence is a 32-byte header and a data block that grows")
    strs_push(l, "by `realloc`; `nz.vec_release` releases each element with the element type's release function at")
    strs_push(l, "the element's stride, then the sequence — its decrement inlined into the unit, the rest")
    strs_push(l, "(`nz.vec_free`) called only after the last reference (runtime ABI 51). A `Box` is such a sequence")
    strs_push(l, "whose data block is made with it at exactly one element and written once, never grown (binary-trees,")
    strs_push(l, "2026-10-19: a vector's first growth takes four). A channel is a 64-byte block (capacity, length, head,")
    strs_push(l, "closed flag, ring, lock, condition, reference count) and three allocations beside it — the ring,")
    strs_push(l, "the lock and the condition — taken in order and released together, with a failure part-way")
    strs_push(l, "through freeing exactly what was taken. Allocation failure is never undefined behaviour: every allocating entry")
    strs_push(l, "returns null or a status, and the call site records `N0406`. Each release decrements and frees on")
    strs_push(l, "zero; a count never underflows because MIR's validator proves every owned value is released")
    strs_push(l, "exactly once (§7.42).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The counted heap renames by name** (R1d, `nazm build --heap-limit`; `crates/nazm-runtime/src/heap.rs`).")
    strs_push(l, "Every unit but the stack unit has its `malloc`, `realloc` and `free` made `nz.heap_malloc`,")
    strs_push(l, "`nz.heap_realloc` and `nz.heap_free`, each block behind a 16-byte header. That holds only while")
    strs_push(l, "every buffer the runtime frees is one the runtime allocated, so **the runtime never asks the C")
    strs_push(l, "library to allocate for it**: no `strdup`, `getline`, `scandir` or the like (`heap::C_ALLOCATING`),")
    strs_push(l, "and `realpath`, `getcwd` and their Windows forms always get a buffer of the runtime's")
    strs_push(l, "(`heap::C_ALLOCATING_ON_NULL`) — `nz_os_realpath` passes a 4096-byte buffer on its frame. What C")
    strs_push(l, "allocates and releases itself (`getaddrinfo` and `freeaddrinfo`, `opendir` and `closedir`) stays C's")
    strs_push(l, "on both sides. Before 2026-10-15 `nz_os_realpath` let `realpath` allocate and freed the answer, so a")
    strs_push(l, "program built with a limit that called `file_canonical` handed `nz.heap_free` a block with no header")
    strs_push(l, "and ended with SIGTRAP (status 133); `heap.rs`'s")
    strs_push(l, "`the_runtime_never_frees_what_the_c_library_allocated` holds every target's text to the rule.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Thread safety, before N44.** String backings' and channels' counts are atomic (`monotonic` up,")
    strs_push(l, "`release` down with an `acquire` fence before freeing), because both may be shared between")
    strs_push(l, "tasks. Sequence counts are not atomic and need not be: a sequence may not cross into a task")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0321`), so one is only ever touched by one thread. The failure state is thread-local; the")
    strs_push(l, "accounting counters are atomic; `nz.argc`/`nz.argv` are written once before any task starts.")
    strs_push(l, "A channel's operations take its mutex. Nothing else is shared.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Tasks and channels: the primitive boundary.** The runtime provides `nz.spawn` (start an OS")
    strs_push(l, "thread for a task and record it in its scope's list, record-first), `nz.scope_join` (join every")
    strs_push(l, "task in the list and hand back the first failure), and the channel operations (bounded buffer,")
    strs_push(l, "blocking send and receive, close). *Which* thread runs a task, when, and in what order is not a")
    strs_push(l, "runtime contract before N44: v1 starts one OS thread per task.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The failure model.** Four classes, never confused:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Class | Codes | What happens |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| A language failure the spec defines | `N0400` overflow, `N0401` division by zero, `N0405` index or capacity | recorded (the thread's first), unwound by MIR's failure edges, joined at the scope, reported by the entry, exit 2 |")
    strs_push(l, "| The host refused a resource | `N0406` allocation, `N0404` a thread (in a native build `N0404` means the operating system would not start one; in `nazm run`, that the interpreter could not) | recorded and reported the same way: the program cannot continue, and says why |")
    strs_push(l, "| An I/O failure | `N0407` | the same, for `read_file` and `write_file`; `file_exists` answers instead of failing |")
    strs_push(l, "| Explicit exit | — | `exit_with`: the process ends with the program's status |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A `Result` is data and never any of these: nothing in the runtime turns an `Err` into a failure or")
    strs_push(l, "a failure into an `Err`. A runtime invariant the compiler guarantees (a count underflow, a join of")
    strs_push(l, "a list that was never opened) has no code, because MIR's validator makes it unreachable; a")
    strs_push(l, "foreign function that crashes is outside every class (§7.44).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Capability roots.** Only the entry mints capabilities, and only for `main`'s parameters. No")
    strs_push(l, "runtime symbol returns one, no built-in constructs one (`N0370`), and none crosses to C (`N0381`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Foreign code.** A foreign call is made on the calling task's thread with no runtime state")
    strs_push(l, "touched. C cannot call into the runtime: its symbols are `hidden` and none is a C entry point.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The operating system.** The runtime reaches it only through the C library and POSIX-threads")
    strs_push(l, "entry points the adapter (`runtime/os.rs`) declares — the same list on every v1 target — and a")
    strs_push(l, "test holds the runtime text to that list. A target outside the v1 matrix is refused before")
    strs_push(l, "generation (§7.43); there is no per-OS code path in the runtime, so there is no per-OS behaviour.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** A scheduler, work stealing, task priorities (N44); runtime provenance tags (N38")
    strs_push(l, "provenance is static and erased); a runtime for `nazm run` (the interpreter is its own).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.46 Structured concurrency and the scheduler — N44, 2026-10-01")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. `docs/user/spec.md` *Concurrency* is the language rule; this is what both")
    strs_push(l, "implementations — the interpreter and the native runtime (§7.45) — owe it, and what the scheduler")
    strs_push(l, "is and is not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Task and scope.** A *task* is a call started by `spawn f(args)` inside a `scope { … }` block. A")
    strs_push(l, "scope owns every task started in it, and **no task outlives its scope**: every exit from the")
    strs_push(l, "block — its closing brace, a `return`, a `break` or `continue` leaving it, a `?`, and a failure")
    strs_push(l, "unwinding through it — joins every task it started, innermost scope first (§7.42's cleanup law).")
    strs_push(l, "There are no detached tasks, no task handles a program can hold, and no way to name a task.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Task states.** *recorded* (in its scope's list, before its thread exists) → *running* (its")
    strs_push(l, "thread started) → *finished* (its body returned; a failure, if any, published into its block) →")
    strs_push(l, "*joined* (its thread joined by the scope, its block freed). The order is fixed by the runtime:")
    strs_push(l, "`nz.spawn` records first and undoes the record if the thread cannot be started, so no task is")
    strs_push(l, "running and unrecorded; `nz.scope_join` joins in the order tasks were started and frees each block")
    strs_push(l, "after its thread is joined. A task that cannot be started is `N0404` at the `spawn`, and the")
    strs_push(l, "scope still joins every task started before it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Failure.** A failed task stops at its failure and publishes it. Its siblings are **not**")
    strs_push(l, "cancelled: they run to completion. At the scope's join, the first failure *in start order* is")
    strs_push(l, "the scope's, and it continues in the parent as the parent's own failure — at the closing brace or")
    strs_push(l, "the exit that joined. Later failures are dropped. A failure in the parent while tasks run is held")
    strs_push(l, "until they are joined, then unwinds — and it, not any task's, is the one reported, because a")
    strs_push(l, "thread keeps only its first failure and the parent's came first on its own thread. So a scope's result is a function of its tasks' outcomes, not")
    strs_push(l, "of the order they happened to finish in.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Cancellation: none in v1** — amended by N54 (§7.56): cooperative cancellation by closing a channel a task selects on, and a select deadline; no cancellation on a sibling's failure still. In v1 there is no cancel operation, no cancellation on sibling failure,")
    strs_push(l, "and no timeout. A blocked `chan_recv` waits until a value arrives or the channel is closed. This")
    strs_push(l, "is a decision, not an omission to fill quietly: cooperative cancellation needs observation")
    strs_push(l, "points in blocking operations, and both implementations would have to agree on every one of them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The scheduler is the operating system's.** Each task runs on its own OS thread, started at the")
    strs_push(l, "`spawn` and joined by its scope. There is no worker pool, no run queue and no work stealing in")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm, and the compiler emits no scheduling policy — MIR says `spawn` and `join` (§7.42), the")
    strs_push(l, "backends call `nz.spawn` and `nz.scope_join`, and the runtime starts and joins threads. This is")
    strs_push(l, "the simplest architecture that keeps the language's progress guarantee: channel operations block")
    strs_push(l, "the calling thread, so a fixed pool of *N* workers would deadlock any program with more than *N*")
    strs_push(l, "tasks blocked at once — a program that is correct today. A pool becomes possible only with")
    strs_push(l, "suspendable tasks (stack switching or compiled continuations), which is research, not v1.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Fairness and determinism.** Nothing is promised about the order tasks run in, interleave, or")
    strs_push(l, "finish, beyond what the OS scheduler does for threads. Program output that depends on task order")
    strs_push(l, "is the program's nondeterminism. What *is* deterministic: which failure a scope reports (first in")
    strs_push(l, "start order), when a scope ends (after every task), and what is reclaimed (everything).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Blocking.** File I/O, `print` and channel operations block the calling task's thread and no other.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Authority.** `spawn` is the effect `spawn` and needs a `SpawnCap` in scope (N37); holding one is")
    strs_push(l, "not the effect. A child has exactly the authority its arguments carry: a declared child needs its")
    strs_push(l, "capabilities passed to it (`N0369` otherwise), and an undeclared one exercises the spawner's under")
    strs_push(l, "N37's compatibility bridge, which the spawner must therefore hold (`N0369` at the `spawn`). A task")
    strs_push(l, "inherits nothing else.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Provenance.** A task's arguments carry their origins into it: N38's summaries treat a spawn as a")
    strs_push(l, "call, so a value from a file handed to a task that writes to a path derived from it is `N0372`")
    strs_push(l, "exactly as a direct call is.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What may cross into a task.** Scalars, strings (immutable, atomically counted), channels (shared,")
    strs_push(l, "locked), capabilities, and records and enums of those. Not a sequence, nor anything holding one")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0321`): a sequence is shared and mutable, and nothing synchronises it. So **Nazm has no data")
    strs_push(l, "races on its own values**: every value two tasks can reach is immutable or a channel. It does not")
    strs_push(l, "prevent deadlock (two tasks each waiting on a channel the other would fill), livelock or")
    strs_push(l, "starvation, and no diagnostic claims to.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Channels.** `chan_new(n)` is a bounded FIFO of `Int`s with capacity *n*; `chan_send` blocks while")
    strs_push(l, "it is full (backpressure) and returns `false` once the channel is closed; `chan_recv` blocks while")
    strs_push(l, "it is empty, then appends the oldest value to a sequence and returns `true`, or returns `false`")
    strs_push(l, "once the channel is closed **and** drained — a close never discards what was sent. Every state")
    strs_push(l, "change wakes every waiter (a broadcast under the channel's lock), so no wakeup is lost. Only `Int`s")
    strs_push(l, "are queued, so no managed value is owned by a channel; the channel itself is atomically counted")
    strs_push(l, "and freed by its last holder.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Shutdown.** `main` returns only after every scope in it has joined, so no task is running when")
    strs_push(l, "the process ends normally or reports a failure. `exit_with` inside a task ends the whole process at")
    strs_push(l, "once, with its siblings still running: that is what `exit_with` means.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** Cancellation, timeouts, select over several channels, detached tasks, a worker pool,")
    strs_push(l, "task priorities, async I/O.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.47 The standard library — N45, 2026-10-01")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. A foundation, not a catalogue: the smallest set of source-backed modules")
    strs_push(l, "real programs were writing for themselves, with every boundary stated.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Three layers.** *Built-ins* are the compiler's: the operations the language cannot express in")
    strs_push(l, "itself — string bytes and slices, the sequences, channels, the process and file primitives,")
    strs_push(l, "`print` — each an `Intrinsic` with a fixed signature, effect and authority (§7.38–7.40). *The")
    strs_push(l, "prelude* (`@core/prelude`, §7.13) is two enums every module sees without importing them, and stays")
    strs_push(l, "two: `Result` and `Option`. *The standard library* is new: toolchain-owned Nazm modules a program")
    strs_push(l, "imports by name — `use \"@std/text\";` — and that no module sees unless it writes the `use`. A")
    strs_push(l, "standard module is ordinary source (`library/std/*.nz`), checked by the same checker, compiled by")
    strs_push(l, "the same backends, cached by the same keys; nothing in the compiler knows what any of its")
    strs_push(l, "functions does. So the standard library adds no compiler magic, and the list of true primitives")
    strs_push(l, "is the built-in list, unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Naming and resolution.** An import path beginning with `@std/` belongs to the toolchain and is")
    strs_push(l, "never looked for on disk. `@std/NAME` is the standard module `NAME`, keyed `@std/NAME` — a key no")
    strs_push(l, "project path can produce, as `@core` is not (`ModuleKey::relative` refuses both prefixes) — and any")
    strs_push(l, "other `@std/` path is `N0205`, naming the modules there are. *Narrowed during implementation:* the")
    strs_push(l, "first draft reserved every path beginning with `@`, which broke an existing contract — a project")
    strs_push(l, "may keep and import its own files under a directory named `@core` (`prelude.rs`) — so only")
    strs_push(l, "`@std/` is reserved, and every other path resolves on disk as it always has. A standard module may import only standard")
    strs_push(l, "modules. The compiler carries each file's bytes, so a compilation needs no installation directory;")
    strs_push(l, "what is checked is those bytes, parsed as source.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The v1 modules.** `@std/text` (prefix and suffix tests, find, contains, repeat, split, trim,")
    strs_push(l, "`parse_int`), `@std/option` and `@std/result` (the tests and fallbacks every use of them wrote")
    strs_push(l, "again), `@std/seq` (search, sum, maximum and minimum over `Ints`, `Strs` and `Vec[T]`),")
    strs_push(l, "`@std/io` (`println`, `eprintln`, `read` as a `Result`), `@std/process` (the arguments as one")
    strs_push(l, "sequence), `@std/chan` (one value as an `Option`). Function names carry their module's name —")
    strs_push(l, "`text_split`, `option_unwrap_or` — because Nazm has no qualified names and a module's exports")
    strs_push(l, "enter the importer's namespace: a prefix is the only thing that keeps two modules' names apart.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Contracts.** Every standard function declares its effect set: `! {}` for everything pure,")
    strs_push(l, "`! { io }` for `@std/io` and `@std/process`, each of which takes the `IoCap` it needs — so a")
    strs_push(l, "wrapper never has authority its signature does not show, and calling one is as visible as calling")
    strs_push(l, "the built-in. Provenance flows through them because they are ordinary calls N38 follows: what")
    strs_push(l, "`io_read` returns is `file`, exactly as `read_file`'s is.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Errors.** Ordinary failure is a value. `text_parse_int` returns `Err` for no digits, a")
    strs_push(l, "non-digit or a value outside `Int` — never an overflow; `text_find` and `ints_max` return `None`")
    strs_push(l, "rather than a sentinel; `io_read` returns `Err` for a missing file. A standard function traps only")
    strs_push(l, "where the built-in it calls would, and says so: `ints_sum` overflows as `+` does; `io_read`'s read")
    strs_push(l, "of a file that exists and still cannot be read is `N0407`, because the check and the read are two")
    strs_push(l, "steps and the language has no way to make them one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is not here, deliberately.** No `map` or `filter` (Nazm has no function values), no")
    strs_push(l, "formatting framework, no HTTP, JSON, crypto or time. `exit_with`, `print`, `str_concat` and the")
    strs_push(l, "rest are not wrapped: a second name for one thing is a second way to say it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Stability.** Pre-1.0: a standard module may change between milestones, and its interface hash")
    strs_push(l, "says when. Its identity is its key and its bytes; no semantic epoch moves for a library change,")
    strs_push(l, "because the checker's rules did not change.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The compiler written in Nazm** does not resolve `@std` imports: it is a second implementation of")
    strs_push(l, "the front end for the programs in this tree, none of which imports a standard module, and it")
    strs_push(l, "resolves every import against the importing file's directory, so it reports `@std/text` as a")
    strs_push(l, "module it cannot find.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.48 Packages, locking and reproducible builds — N46, 2026-10-01")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. `crates/nazm-package` holds the model; the loader and the command line")
    strs_push(l, "consume it. No registry, no network, no build scripts.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A package** is a directory holding `nazm.toml`, its manifest, `nazm.package/1`:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```toml")
    strs_push(l, "schema = \"nazm.package/1\"")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "[package]")
    strs_push(l, "name = \"geometry\"        # [a-z][a-z0-9-]*, at most 64 bytes")
    strs_push(l, "version = \"1.2.0\"        # MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH, decimal, no pre-release in v1")
    strs_push(l, "root = \"src\"             # the source root, relative to the manifest; default \"src\"")
    strs_push(l, "main = \"main.nz\"         # the entry module, relative to the root; only a binary has one")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "[dependencies]")
    strs_push(l, "shapes = { path = \"../shapes\", version = \"0.3.1\" }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nothing else is accepted: an unknown key is refused by name, so a manifest cannot carry")
    strs_push(l, "configuration the compiler silently ignores. Descriptive metadata (authors, licence) is out of v1.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Identity.** A package is its name, its exact version and its source — in v1 always a path,")
    strs_push(l, "relative to the manifest that names it. Two packages of one name in one build are a conflict and")
    strs_push(l, "refused, whatever their versions: a module's durable key is `NAME@VERSION/path`, and a program")
    strs_push(l, "with two `shapes` would have two answers to which one a `use` means. A dependency's declared")
    strs_push(l, "version must equal the version its own manifest states — exactly; there are no ranges in v1, so")
    strs_push(l, "nothing is ever chosen for a program.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Imports.** `use \"shapes:polygon.nz\";` imports the module `polygon.nz` of the package the")
    strs_push(l, "importing package declares as `shapes`, resolved against that package's source root. Only a")
    strs_push(l, "package's own dependencies are visible to it: its dependency's dependencies are not. A path with")
    strs_push(l, "no `NAME:` stays relative to the importing file and may not leave its package's source root.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Resolution** starts at the root package and visits dependencies in name order, depth first,")
    strs_push(l, "reading each manifest once by its canonical directory; a package reached twice by one identity is")
    strs_push(l, "one package (a diamond), by two is a conflict, and a package reached from itself is a cycle,")
    strs_push(l, "reported with its path. The result is a list sorted by name and a graph whose edges are sorted:")
    strs_push(l, "no hash-map iteration, directory listing order or filesystem timestamp enters it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Digest.** A package's digest is BLAKE3 over its manifest's bytes and every `.nz` file under its")
    strs_push(l, "source root — each as its path relative to the root with `/` separators, its length and its bytes,")
    strs_push(l, "in path order — under a domain-separation tag. No timestamp, permission, absolute path or")
    strs_push(l, "directory order is an input.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The lockfile**, `nazm.lock` beside the root manifest, is `nazm.lock/1`: one entry per package in")
    strs_push(l, "name order — name, version, source (a path relative to the root package, `/`-separated) and")
    strs_push(l, "digest — and each package's dependency names. `nazm lock DIR` writes it, and writes it only when")
    strs_push(l, "its bytes would change: resolving the same packages twice gives the same bytes. Nothing else")
    strs_push(l, "writes it. `--locked` makes it authoritative: the build resolves as usual and refuses — before")
    strs_push(l, "compiling anything — if the lockfile is missing, if any package's identity, source or")
    strs_push(l, "dependencies differ from it, or if any package's bytes no longer match its digest (tampering).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Offline, always.** Every v1 source is a path, so resolution never reaches a network; a missing")
    strs_push(l, "dependency directory is refused by name. There is no download step to disable.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Builds and caches.** `nazm check|build|run DIR` builds the package in `DIR` from its `main`.")
    strs_push(l, "Module keys of dependency modules carry `NAME@VERSION`, and every cache key already covers a")
    strs_push(l, "module's source bytes and its dependencies' interfaces (§7.6), so a changed dependency invalidates")
    strs_push(l, "its dependents and nothing else, and an unchanged one is reused. The build's configuration — the")
    strs_push(l, "backend, its version and settings, the optimisation level, the target and the runtime ABI — is in")
    strs_push(l, "every object key (§7.43, §7.45): that is the profile, and there is no second profile mechanism.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Environment.** A build reads no environment variable that changes its output, except the ones")
    strs_push(l, "the C toolchain is handed by name (`nazm-cli/src/backend.rs`, `PASSED`), which the toolchain's own")
    strs_push(l, "identity then covers. There are no build scripts.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Reproducibility, stated exactly.** The same package sources, lockfile, toolchain, target,")
    strs_push(l, "backend and configuration give byte-identical executables — tested on one host by building two")
    strs_push(l, "copies of a package in two directories from empty caches. Nothing is claimed across operating")
    strs_push(l, "systems or toolchain versions.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Amended during implementation.** Three facts the first draft did not know. *The linker*: the")
    strs_push(l, "Apple linker gives every link a new UUID unless `ZERO_AR_DATE=1` is in its environment, and")
    strs_push(l, "derives the UUID and the ad-hoc signature from the output's file name — so the link is made with")
    strs_push(l, "that variable set, under the final file name, inside the build's working directory, and renamed")
    strs_push(l, "into place (`two_copies_built_from_empty_caches_are_byte_identical` failed until both were done).")
    strs_push(l, "*Stored keys*: `ModuleKey::parse` read back only the prelude's key and project paths, so neither a")
    strs_push(l, "dependency's module (`NAME@VERSION/…`) nor a standard one (`@std/…`, N45's — a gap N45's tests did")
    strs_push(l, "not cover) was ever reused from the cache; both now read back as themselves. *The first")
    strs_push(l, "component*: only a key's first component may not hold `@`, because `lib/@core/x.nz` was already a")
    strs_push(l, "project's own key. The source-root decision (`nazm-service/src/root.rs`) learned a fourth answer,")
    strs_push(l, "`package`, reported by `--cache-report` and `--build-report` as a new value of `root`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.49 Restriction profiles — N47, 2026-10-01")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. One language, and profiles that refuse some of its programs.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a profile is.** A named set of rules, each with a stable identity, each reading a fact the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler already settled and passing or failing with witnesses. A profile may reject a program;")
    strs_push(l, "it never changes what an accepted program means, compiles to or does. Every program a profile")
    strs_push(l, "accepts, `general` accepts, and runs identically. There is no profile-specific syntax, built-in or")
    strs_push(l, "code path, and nothing in a profile reads a name: an effect is an `Effect`, a contract is a")
    strs_push(l, "function's `declared_effects`, a build's lock is `nazm-package`'s verification.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The rules.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Rule | Fact | Refuses |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `declared-effects` | each function's declared contract | any function of the program's own modules (not the prelude's or a standard module's, all of which declare theirs) with no `! { … }` — the ambient bridge of N37 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `no-io` | the effect set `main` requires | `io` anywhere in the program, through any call |")
    strs_push(l, "| `no-spawn` | the same | `spawn`: tasks, and so the scheduler |")
    strs_push(l, "| `no-foreign` | the same | `foreign`: any call into C |")
    strs_push(l, "| `locked-build` | the build | a build that is not a package build whose lockfile verifies |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`main`'s required effect set is transitive by construction (N36): through every call of every")
    strs_push(l, "module, standard wrappers included — `io_println` carries `io` because it calls `print` — and an")
    strs_push(l, "undeclared function of another module is assumed to have every bridged effect, so an effect rule")
    strs_push(l, "over-refuses rather than misses.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The profiles.** `general`: no rules. `embedded`: `no-io`, `no-spawn` — no operating-system")
    strs_push(l, "services and no scheduler; C (hardware access) is allowed. `critical`: `declared-effects`,")
    strs_push(l, "`no-spawn`, `no-foreign`, `locked-build`. `cyber`: `declared-effects`, `no-foreign`,")
    strs_push(l, "`locked-build`; because every function then declares its effects, N38's restricted flow (`N0372`)")
    strs_push(l, "applies to every function of the program. None is a certification, a sandbox or a proof of")
    strs_push(l, "anything beyond its rules.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is not a rule, and why.** No allocation rule: allocation is not tracked. No determinism")
    strs_push(l, "claim: forbidding `spawn` removes one source of nondeterminism, not every one. No provenance rule")
    strs_push(l, "beyond N38's, which `declared-effects` extends to the whole program.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Selection and propagation.** `--profile NAME` on `check`, `build` and `run`, and `profile =")
    strs_push(l, "\"NAME\"` in any package manifest of the build. The profiles in force are all of them; their rules")
    strs_push(l, "are the union, evaluated over the whole program — so a dependency that requires `embedded` holds")
    strs_push(l, "every program it is part of to it. An unknown name is `N0511`. No environment variable selects one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**When, and caching.** After a full check, before the command does its own work: `nazm build`")
    strs_push(l, "under a profile that refuses writes nothing. The rules read the facts of an uncached check, and")
    strs_push(l, "their verdicts are never cached, so a check cached under one profile can never carry its")
    strs_push(l, "acceptance into another — the cost is one check more whenever a profile other than `general` is in")
    strs_push(l, "force. What is compiled does not depend on the profile, so no object key needs it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Diagnostics and the report.** Each failed rule is one `N0510` naming the profiles in force and")
    strs_push(l, "the rule, pointing at its first witness — for an effect, the chain of calls from `main` to the")
    strs_push(l, "built-in, `spawn` or contract where it enters — with the rest as secondary labels. `nazm check")
    strs_push(l, "--profile-report` prints `nazm.profile-report/1`: the profiles, the outcome, and every rule's")
    strs_push(l, "verdict and witnesses in rule order, byte-identical for the same program and build, and marked as")
    strs_push(l, "compiler evidence rather than certification.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.50 Inspection, debugging and profiling — N48, 2026-10-01")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Three surfaces over facts the compiler already has, none of which")
    strs_push(l, "changes what a program does.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The inspector.** `nazm inspect FILE|DIR [--def NAME]` prints `nazm.inspect/1`, one line of JSON")
    strs_push(l, "with sorted keys: the toolchain's identities (compiler version, semantic epoch, interface schema,")
    strs_push(l, "runtime ABI revision, Cranelift version, host target), the package and the state of its lock")
    strs_push(l, "(`verified`, `absent`, `mismatch`) and the profiles its manifests require, whether MIR validated,")
    strs_push(l, "and for each definition in identity order — its durable identity, parameter and result types,")
    strs_push(l, "whether it is generic, declared and required effects, the capabilities it takes, its provenance")
    strs_push(l, "summary (the origins its result carries, the parameters it passes on and those reaching a sink),")
    strs_push(l, "its foreign symbol, its Core IR semantic and body digests, and for each concrete function MIR has")
    strs_push(l, "for it (an instance per type for a generic one) the executable digest and its block, statement")
    strs_push(l, "and local counts. Excluded by construction: absolute paths, times, addresses, process ids,")
    strs_push(l, "iteration order. The same program, toolchain and build give the same bytes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Debug information.** `nazm build --debug` emits DWARF through the LLVM backend: a compile unit")
    strs_push(l, "per object, a subprogram per function — the Nazm name, the native symbol as its linkage name, its")
    strs_push(l, "file and the line of its declaration — and a source position on every instruction, taken from the")
    strs_push(l, "span MIR recorded for the statement or terminator it was emitted for. Compiler-made code carries")
    strs_push(l, "the position of the statement it belongs to, or its function's line; nothing is given a position")
    strs_push(l, "the source does not have, and runtime and entry objects carry none. On macOS the executable's")
    strs_push(l, "debug information is gathered into `OUTPUT.dSYM` with `dsymutil` before the objects are removed.")
    strs_push(l, "What is claimed: a debugger resolves a breakpoint by Nazm function name or by file and line, and")
    strs_push(l, "the line table has a row per statement, which is what stepping by statement reads. *Narrowed during")
    strs_push(l, "implementation:* the first draft also claimed frames and stepping in a live session; launching a")
    strs_push(l, "process under lldb waited on macOS's debugger authorisation in the non-interactive environment N48")
    strs_push(l, "ran in, so the live half was not exercised and is not claimed. What is not: local variables (no")
    strs_push(l, "`DILocalVariable`), types, the Cranelift backend (`--debug` with it is refused, never silently")
    strs_push(l, "ignored), and stepping into the runtime. Without `--debug` nothing changes: the emitter writes the")
    strs_push(l, "same text it always did.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Timings.** `nazm build --timings` writes `nazm.timings/1` to stderr: the wall time of each phase")
    strs_push(l, "in the order it ran — load, front end (parse, check, effects, capabilities, provenance, Core IR),")
    strs_push(l, "MIR, LIR, code generation, native compilation, link — and the total. The front end is one phase")
    strs_push(l, "here because the CLI runs it as one step; the per-pass split of the front end is the benchmark")
    strs_push(l, "`what_each_phase_costs` in-process. The runtime's own counters stay `NAZM_MEMORY_REPORT`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The v1 release audit.** N48 also audits what exists against what is claimed: every capability")
    strs_push(l, "area's status, the security and safety wording across the documents, a centralised list of known")
    strs_push(l, "limitations, release-candidate notes and a human release procedure — and freezes the v1")
    strs_push(l, "performance baseline. Nothing is pushed, tagged or published by it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.51 Usability and native completeness — N49, 2026-10-01")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Four small mechanisms, each closing a line of `limitations.md`, and an")
    strs_push(l, "audit of every construct the interpreter runs and a native backend does not. None is a new")
    strs_push(l, "semantic layer: each is owned by a layer that already owns its neighbours.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**String escapes — the lexer's.** A string literal may contain `\\n` (10), `\\t` (9), `\\r` (13),")
    strs_push(l, "`\\0` (0), `\\\\` (92), `\\\"` (34) and `\\xHH` for `HH` in `00`–`7F` — two hexadecimal digits, either")
    strs_push(l, "case. Each escape **is one byte**; nothing else in a literal changes, so a non-ASCII character")
    strs_push(l, "written in UTF-8 source is its UTF-8 bytes as before. Any other backslash sequence, a `\\x` with")
    strs_push(l, "fewer than two hex digits, or a `\\x` above `7F` is refused (`N0004`) at the escape's own bytes,")
    strs_push(l, "and the literal is still one token so recovery is unchanged. `\\x80`–`\\xFF` are refused rather than")
    strs_push(l, "defined because the reference representation of a literal is UTF-8 text in every layer from the")
    strs_push(l, "token to MIR, and widening it to arbitrary bytes is a representation change with no user it would")
    strs_push(l, "serve that `str_from_byte` does not; no `\\u{…}`, because `Str` is bytes and a Unicode escape is an")
    strs_push(l, "encoding decision. Decoding happens once, in the lexer; the token carries the decoded value and")
    strs_push(l, "the span of the source bytes, so every diagnostic about a literal still points at what was")
    strs_push(l, "written. The formatter prints a literal's source bytes, never its value, so escapes are kept")
    strs_push(l, "exactly as written: the canonical form is the written form. **Semantic epoch moves (11 → 12):**")
    strs_push(l, "a literal containing a backslash meant its bytes literally before N49 and means an escape after")
    strs_push(l, "it, so a cached check of such a source is not a check of the new language. The compiler written")
    strs_push(l, "in Nazm does not decode escapes and **refuses** a literal containing a backslash rather than")
    strs_push(l, "reading it the old way.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Logical operators — the parser's and the checker's, lowered away in Core IR.** `!e` (prefix,")
    strs_push(l, "beside unary `-`), `a && b` and `a || b`; `||` binds loosest, then `&&`, then the comparisons —")
    strs_push(l, "`a == b && c < d || e` is `((a == b) && (c < d)) || e`. Every operand is `Bool` and so is the")
    strs_push(l, "result (`N0304` otherwise, as for any operator). `&&` and `||` are left-associative and")
    strs_push(l, "**short-circuit**: the right operand is evaluated only when the left does not decide the result,")
    strs_push(l, "so its effects, its failures and its non-termination happen only then. Core IR lowers them away")
    strs_push(l, "— `a && b` to `if a { b } else { false }`, `a || b` to `if a { true } else { b }`, `!e` to")
    strs_push(l, "`if e { false } else { true }` — so MIR, both backends and the interpreter run them with no new")
    strs_push(l, "case, and short-circuiting is a fact about control flow they already share rather than three")
    strs_push(l, "implementations of it. The effect, capability and provenance analyses see the operands as the")
    strs_push(l, "`if` they become: the right operand's effects are the expression's, conditionally, as any")
    strs_push(l, "branch's are. No new code; the epoch already moves for escapes. The compiler written in Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "refuses the three operators by name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Native recursion — MIR's stack checks and the runtime's guard.** Recursion, direct and mutual,")
    strs_push(l, "across modules and packages, compiles under both backends. The contract: **a native call that")
    strs_push(l, "would exhaust its thread's stack fails with `N0408` at the function it entered, after which the")
    strs_push(l, "failure unwinds like any other** (cleanup runs, a scope joins its tasks, `main`'s failure is")
    strs_push(l, "reported and the process exits 2). The mechanism: MIR lowering places a `StackCheck` statement")
    strs_push(l, "with a failure edge first in every function that is in a call cycle — the cycles of the call")
    strs_push(l, "graph without `spawn`, which starts a task on its own stack — and each backend emits it as a call")
    strs_push(l, "to the runtime's `nz.stack_check` and a branch to the failure edge. `nz.stack_check` compares the")
    strs_push(l, "frame address with the thread's limit, which it computes once per thread on first use: the")
    strs_push(l, "current frame minus a budget of three quarters of the smaller of the process's `RLIMIT_STACK` and")
    strs_push(l, "8 MiB. Task threads are created with an 8 MiB stack (`pthread_attr_setstacksize`; Linux's default")
    strs_push(l, "already, and raised from macOS's 512 KiB), so every thread's budget is within its stack. **What")
    strs_push(l, "is guaranteed, and what is not:** the check is made on entry to every function in a cycle, so")
    strs_push(l, "unbounded recursion meets it; a chain of non-recursive calls between two checks is bounded by the")
    strs_push(l, "call graph but its stack is not measured, so the guarantee holds when no such chain plus the frames")
    strs_push(l, "it builds exceeds the quarter left as headroom (2 MiB at 8 MiB). A program whose non-recursive")
    strs_push(l, "frames are that large can still exhaust the stack and be killed by the operating system; no")
    strs_push(l, "measured program comes close. There is no tail-call optimisation and none is promised; the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter's limit stays its own (`--max-depth`, `N0403`), so the two implementations agree on")
    strs_push(l, "what a terminating program produces and each reports its own limit. **Runtime ABI revision moves")
    strs_push(l, "(2 → 3):** generated code calls a runtime entry it did not before. The compiler written in Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "still refuses recursion by name: its emitter has no stack check, and the reason it refused is the")
    strs_push(l, "reason it still does.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Qualified names — the loader's, the checker's and the service's.** `use \"PATH\" as NAME;` imports")
    strs_push(l, "a module **under a name**: its exports are not brought into scope unqualified, so they collide with")
    strs_push(l, "nothing, and each is written `NAME::item` wherever a definition is named — a call `t::split(s)`, a")
    strs_push(l, "construction `g::Point(x: 1)`, a variant `g::Shape.Circle(r: 2)`, a type `g::Point`. `as` is")
    strs_push(l, "recognised only after a `use` path, so no identifier is taken from programs. The alias is the")
    strs_push(l, "module's within the importing module only; two aliases may name one module; an alias that is")
    strs_push(l, "also a definition's name, or a second alias of the same name, is refused (`N0209`), and a")
    strs_push(l, "qualified name naming an alias that does not exist or an item the module does not export is")
    strs_push(l, "refused (`N0210`) with the module's exports as candidates. **One resolver:** the checker resolves")
    strs_push(l, "`NAME::item` against exactly the interface entry the unqualified import would have used, so a")
    strs_push(l, "qualified call has the same `FnId`, durable identity, effects, capabilities and provenance as an")
    strs_push(l, "unqualified one, and everything downstream — Core IR, MIR, both backends, the interpreter, the")
    strs_push(l, "cache — sees no difference; the service's references, rename, semantic tokens and completion key on")
    strs_push(l, "the item's name span, which is the same span. A plain `use \"PATH\";` is unchanged. The compiler")
    strs_push(l, "written in Nazm refuses `as` and `::` by name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The construct audit.** `nazm capabilities --json` is read row by row against both backends; every")
    strs_push(l, "construct the interpreter runs and a backend refuses is classified as deliberate, a limitation, or")
    strs_push(l, "a bug, and only the gaps above are closed here (`limitations.md` says which remain).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.52 Function values and closures — N50, 2026-10-01")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. One callable model: a **function value** is a value of a **function type**,")
    strs_push(l, "made from a named function or from a closure expression, and called the way a function is. Traits")
    strs_push(l, "and methods are not part of it, for the reason under *What is not here*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The type.** `fn(T1, …, Tn) -> R`, optionally `! { e… }`, is a type wherever a type is written:")
    strs_push(l, "parameters, results, bindings, fields, payloads, `Vec[…]` and type arguments. It is")
    strs_push(l, "**structural** — two function types are one type exactly when their parameter types, result type")
    strs_push(l, "and effect set are equal — and **invariant**: no subtyping, so a pure function is not a")
    strs_push(l, "`fn(Int) -> Int ! {io}` (effect polymorphism and subsumption are N51's). Unwritten effects mean")
    strs_push(l, "the empty set. A function type has **no equality**, as a capability has none: equality of code is")
    strs_push(l, "not decidable, and identity of objects is not a meaning the language has chosen.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The values.** A non-generic, non-foreign function written as a value (`let f = double;`) is a")
    strs_push(l, "function value of its signature's type. A **closure** is `fn(x: Int) -> Int ! {e} { body }` in")
    strs_push(l, "expression position: parameters and result written in full, as a declaration's are (no inference")
    strs_push(l, "across a function boundary), its effects declared or empty. Its body may name bindings of the")
    strs_push(l, "functions and closures that enclose it; each one it names is **captured by value** when the")
    strs_push(l, "closure is created — a copy, so a handle (`Ints`, `Vec`, `Chan`) is shared and a value is not.")
    strs_push(l, "A `let mut` binding may not be captured (`N0386`): a copy of it would silently stop tracking the")
    strs_push(l, "binding, and sharing state is what handles and channels are for. A capability may not be captured")
    strs_push(l, "either (`N0386`): authority is passed as a parameter, so a closure has no authority its type does")
    strs_push(l, "not show. A generic function, a built-in and a foreign function are not values (`N0387`); a")
    strs_push(l, "closure over them is.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Calls.** `f(args)` where `f` is a parameter or binding of function type is an **indirect call**:")
    strs_push(l, "arguments are checked against the type's parameters, the result is its result, and the call")
    strs_push(l, "exercises the type's effects exactly as a call to a declared function exercises its declaration's.")
    strs_push(l, "A local of function type hides a function of the same name for calls in its scope, as any binding")
    strs_push(l, "hides an outer one. A function value stored in a field or a payload is called by binding it first")
    strs_push(l, "(`let g = r.f; g(1)`): `r.f(1)` is the shape of a variant construction and keeps that meaning.")
    strs_push(l, "Function values may not be passed to a task (`N0321`): their type does not say whether what they")
    strs_push(l, "captured may cross into one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Effects, authority, provenance.** A closure's body is checked against its own declared effects,")
    strs_push(l, "and creating a closure performs none of them; calling a function value performs its type's. A closure's authority is its capability parameters and nothing else. Provenance: the result of an")
    strs_push(l, "indirect call is of unknown origin, joined with what its arguments and the function value carry —")
    strs_push(l, "which function runs is not known where the call is. A closure's body is walked as a function of")
    strs_push(l, "its own: its parameters are of unknown origin (its callers cannot be named), and a capture carries")
    strs_push(l, "the origins of the binding it copies, or unknown when that binding depended on its maker's")
    strs_push(l, "parameters or calls. A restricted sink reached from either is refused, conservatively.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**One lowering.** The checker registers each closure as a definition of its own — a private")
    strs_push(l, "function of the enclosing function's module, identified by the enclosing definition and its")
    strs_push(l, "position among that body's closures — with its captures recorded in order of first mention. Core IR")
    strs_push(l, "lifts it: a closure expression is `Closure { func, captures }`, a named function used as a value is")
    strs_push(l, "`FnValue(func)`, an indirect call is `CallIndirect { callee, args }`, and the closure's body is a Core")
    strs_push(l, "IR function marked as one, whose local 0 is the closure itself, a parameter, followed by its declared")
    strs_push(l, "parameters; its captures are locals its body region owns, listed in order. MIR keeps the same three, adds the **environment**:")
    strs_push(l, "every function a function value can reach — a closure's body, and a **thunk** MIR makes for each")
    strs_push(l, "named function used as a value — takes the environment as its first parameter and reads its")
    strs_push(l, "captures from it at entry (`Rvalue::Capture`). Both backends and the interpreter consume exactly")
    strs_push(l, "that; none rediscovers a closure.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The calling convention.** A function value is one pointer to a **closure object**: a reference")
    strs_push(l, "count, the code pointer, a release function, then the captures in order, each at its type's slot")
    strs_push(l, "size. Each backend lays the captures out itself, and an object never crosses from one backend's code to")
    strs_push(l, "the other's. Calling it passes the object as the first argument and the arguments after. Copying a")
    strs_push(l, "function value retains the object and dropping one releases it; the last release calls the release")
    strs_push(l, "function, which releases every managed capture, and frees the object. A named function's value is")
    strs_push(l, "an object like any other, made where the value is written: its code is the thunk, it carries")
    strs_push(l, "nothing, and its release function is null. *(Amended with the code: the constitution first had a")
    strs_push(l, "static immortal object here, which would have given the two kinds of value two ownership laws; one")
    strs_push(l, "law, at the cost of an allocation per use, is the simpler truth.)* Making an object can fail for")
    strs_push(l, "want of memory (`N0406`), so MIR gives `Closure` a failure edge. The runtime owns allocation and the")
    strs_push(l, "reference count (`nz.closure_new`, `nz.closure_retain`, `nz.closure_release`), atomically as a")
    strs_push(l, "string's, and counts objects for the memory report, whose line gains a fourth class, `closures`;")
    strs_push(l, "the runtime ABI revision moves (3 → 4). A function that makes an indirect call checks its stack")
    strs_push(l, "first, as a function in a call cycle does (N49): which function the call reaches is not known, so")
    strs_push(l, "any cycle through one contains such a function.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Durable interfaces.** A function type in an exported signature, field or payload is persisted as")
    strs_push(l, "`{\"fn\":[…],\"ret\":…,\"effects\":[…]}`. *(Amended with the code: the schema does not move.)* A `/7` reader")
    strs_push(l, "that meets that shape cannot read it as any of the four it knows, refuses the file and treats it")
    strs_push(l, "as no entry — never wrong, only unable — so the major is kept, by the rule that a schema moves only")
    strs_push(l, "when an old reader would otherwise be wrong. A closure is never exported. Captured bindings are one")
    strs_push(l, "binding to a reader: `Resolution::binding_of` maps a closure's copy back to what it copies, so")
    strs_push(l, "references and rename see every use.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The higher-order library.** `@std/seq` gains `vec_map`, `vec_filter` and `vec_fold`, written in")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm over `Vec[T]` and function values, with no compiler knowledge of them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The compiler written in Nazm** has neither: its parser stops at a closure or a function type with")
    strs_push(l, "its ordinary syntax error. That is the recorded parity gap; nothing in it needs a function value.")
    strs_push(l, "Its emitted programs print the memory report's `closures` class, always zero, so the two compilers'")
    strs_push(l, "reports still compare line for line.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is not here, and why.** *Traits and methods.* N50's prompt makes them conditional on a need")
    strs_push(l, "generics and higher-order APIs demonstrate. With function values, the needs in hand — mapping,")
    strs_push(l, "filtering, folding, ordering or rendering by a supplied function — are met by passing the function;")
    strs_push(l, "none requires a constraint the caller cannot supply as an argument. A trait would add a second")
    strs_push(l, "abstraction (dictionaries or instances, coherence, orphan rules, method lookup) for no program the")
    strs_push(l, "language cannot already express, so they are **designed and deferred**: the design questions —")
    strs_push(l, "trait identity as a durable definition, coherence as one impl per trait and type in the trait's or")
    strs_push(l, "the type's module, method syntax as resolution sugar over the same functions, monomorphisation")
    strs_push(l, "before dictionaries — are recorded here and settled when a program needs them. *Function values")
    strs_push(l, "across tasks*, *generic function values*, *closures that call themselves*, *calling a field")
    strs_push(l, "directly*, and *a closure or a named function value inside a generic function* (`N0387`: each")
    strs_push(l, "would need an instance or a thunk per type argument) are refused rather than half-supported.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.53 Effects and capabilities v2 — N51, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. N50 made function values, and with them the gap N36 recorded: a function")
    strs_push(l, "type's effects are fixed, so `vec_map` could take only a pure function, and a closure could not")
    strs_push(l, "hold a capability, so even an effectful one had no authority to use. This section closes that gap")
    strs_push(l, "with the smallest mechanism that does, bounds the N37 bridge at the one edge N50 opened, and")
    strs_push(l, "settles the capability questions N51 asks — implementing what a program in hand needs and")
    strs_push(l, "deferring, with the cost stated, what none does.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Effect parameters.** A function may declare **one** effect parameter, in its type parameter")
    strs_push(l, "list after its type parameters: `fn vec_map[T, U, effects E](xs: Vec[T], f: fn(T) -> U ! { E })")
    strs_push(l, "-> Vec[U] ! { E }`. `effects` is a word only there. The parameter's name may be written in any")
    strs_push(l, "effect set of the function's own signature — its parameters' and result's function types and its")
    strs_push(l, "declared set — and in the effect sets of closures in its body; nowhere else. It stands for a set of")
    strs_push(l, "effects the caller chooses. In the body it is opaque: calling a parameter whose type has `E`")
    strs_push(l, "performs `E`, which the declared set must therefore include, and `E` needs no capability — the")
    strs_push(l, "function value that performs it carries its own authority (below). One parameter per function is")
    strs_push(l, "a decision, not an omission: every higher-order function in hand (map, filter, fold, apply,")
    strs_push(l, "compose over one effect) needs one, and a second would bring row unification with no program to")
    strs_push(l, "test it. Effect parameters do not make a function generic for code generation: effects are")
    strs_push(l, "metadata from Core IR down, so no instance is made per binding. `main` may not declare one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Binding at a call.** At a call to a function with an effect parameter, the parameter is bound by")
    strs_push(l, "matching each argument's type against its parameter's, structurally, as type parameters are")
    strs_push(l, "(N50's unification extended to effect sets): where the parameter's function type writes `! { k…, E }`")
    strs_push(l, "and the argument's is `! { a… }`, `E` binds to `a… − k…`, and `k…` must be within `a…`. Bound twice")
    strs_push(l, "to different sets is `N0389`; bound nowhere, it is the empty set. The call then performs the")
    strs_push(l, "callee's declared set with `E` replaced by its binding, and its argument types are checked against")
    strs_push(l, "the parameter types with `E` replaced, so a mismatch is the ordinary `N0300`. Inside a function")
    strs_push(l, "with its own effect parameter `F`, an argument's type may carry `F` (it is a parameter of the")
    strs_push(l, "caller), and a binding of `E` may contain `F` — which the caller's own declared set then needs, by")
    strs_push(l, "the same rule. So `vec_map(xs, f)` inside `run[effects F](f: fn(Int) -> Int ! { F })` performs `F`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Capabilities a closure captures.** A closure may now capture a capability (`N0386` is narrowed to")
    strs_push(l, "`let mut`): the capability is copied into the closure, as any value is, and the authority the")
    strs_push(l, "closure's body holds is its own capability parameters **and** its captured capabilities.")
    strs_push(l, "*(Amended with the code: \"captured\" is lexical — a closure holds the capabilities visible where")
    strs_push(l, "it is written, as a block does, whether or not its body names them. A capability has no run-time")
    strs_push(l, "representation to copy, so the two readings differ only in which programs a reader must study,")
    strs_push(l, "and the lexical one is the rule every other body already follows.)* The")
    strs_push(l, "closure's type still shows what it does — its declared effects — so a function value's type is")
    strs_push(l, "an honest statement of what calling it may do, and the value carries the authority for it.")
    strs_push(l, "Copying a capability confers nothing new: it is a token that already exists. **Delegation** is")
    strs_push(l, "passing one as an argument or capturing it; **duplication** is copying it; **storage** is as any")
    strs_push(l, "value's (a field may hold one, as before); **task transfer** is unchanged — a capability may be")
    strs_push(l, "passed to a task where its kind allows, and a function value may not be passed to one (`N0321`).")
    strs_push(l, "**Narrowing** has no form: there are no attenuated kinds (below).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The bridge, bounded.** N37's compatibility bridge stays as it is for code that declares nothing:")
    strs_push(l, "an undeclared function exercises its caller's authority, and a declared caller must hold what the")
    strs_push(l, "callee's effects need (`N0369`). N50 opened one more edge: a *value* of an undeclared function.")
    strs_push(l, "Its type assumes the empty set if it is this module's (and the function is held to that, `N0366`)")
    strs_push(l, "or the bridged `{ io, spawn }` if it is another module's — so calling the value performs those")
    strs_push(l, "effects, and since a call through a value needs no authority, declared code could reach the")
    strs_push(l, "ambient bridge through it. N51 closes the edge where the value is **made**: making a value of an")
    strs_push(l, "undeclared function requires, at that point, the capabilities its type's effects need, exactly as")
    strs_push(l, "calling it would (`N0369`). Strict code therefore cannot acquire authority through an undeclared")
    strs_push(l, "import or callback. The policy is stated rather than migrated: no accepted program changes")
    strs_push(l, "meaning; a program that made such a value without holding the authority was unsound and is now")
    strs_push(l, "refused, which the semantic epoch records.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Attenuated capabilities: deferred.** No program in the tree — the compiler written in Nazm, the")
    strs_push(l, "examples, the standard library — needs authority narrower than a kind. The first candidate, an")
    strs_push(l, "`IoCap` scoped to a path prefix, needs a semantics for path containment and the provenance of the")
    strs_push(l, "path (N52); building it without a program would be inventing the use case.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Revocation: deferred, with its cost.** A capability is a value with no identity: two copies are")
    strs_push(l, "indistinguishable, and nothing records that one was handed out. Revocation needs identity — an")
    strs_push(l, "allocated cell per granted capability, a check at every use, and an operation that flips it —")
    strs_push(l, "which is runtime state and a runtime cost at every authorised call. A static flag would be a")
    strs_push(l, "claim the representation cannot back, so there is none.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The trust root** is unchanged: `main`'s parameters are the only source of a capability (`N0370`")
    strs_push(l, "refuses building one; `N0371` a `main` parameter that is not one), an interface carries capability")
    strs_push(l, "*types* and never values, and a closure's capture copies a capability that already exists.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Representation.** `Effect::Param` is a fourth effect: *the effect parameter*. In a function's")
    strs_push(l, "declared set it is that function's; in a function type it is the parameter of the function type's")
    strs_push(l, "`row` owner (`FnSignature::row`, a `ParamOwner`), so a type that mentions one function's parameter")
    strs_push(l, "is never confused with another's. It is never a built-in's effect, needs no capability, is not in")
    strs_push(l, "the bridged or the assumed set, and is not a name a set may write except as the declared")
    strs_push(l, "parameter's. Substitution replaces it as a type parameter is replaced; the interface writes it as")
    strs_push(l, "`\"*\"` in an effect list, a value a `/7` reader refuses as an unknown effect rather than misreads, so")
    strs_push(l, "the schema does not move. Effects analysis treats it as one more effect in the fixed point — what a")
    strs_push(l, "body requires may include it — and a call's contribution is the callee's set with it bound.")
    strs_push(l, "Below the checker effects mean nothing and a binding makes no instance, so Core IR's and MIR's")
    strs_push(l, "verifiers compare the types crossing a call **up to effects** (`same_shape`): the callee's")
    strs_push(l, "parameter `fn(…) ! { E }` takes the caller's `fn(…) ! { io }`. A call's result type is the bound")
    strs_push(l, "one, recorded on the call. That is also why the parameter may not be named inside a type's")
    strs_push(l, "arguments (`N0388`): `Vec[fn() ! { E }]` and `Vec[fn() ! { io }]` would be two `Vec` types, with")
    strs_push(l, "two element tables, for one value.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The standard library** takes the parameter: `vec_map`, `vec_filter` and `vec_fold` are")
    strs_push(l, "`effects E` over their function argument, so a printing closure is accepted and its caller is held")
    strs_push(l, "to `io`, through the wrapper, not around it. **Profiles** read the effect set `main` requires,")
    strs_push(l, "which now includes what a bound parameter contributes, so `embedded`'s `no-io` refuses a program")
    strs_push(l, "whose only `io` is a closure handed to `vec_map`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.54 Resource facts and information flow v2 — N52, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Two gaps, one each side of the language. The capability matrix lists")
    strs_push(l, "allocation as untracked: a reader, an agent or a profile cannot ask where a function allocates,")
    strs_push(l, "retains, blocks or starts a task. And provenance has one source rule and one sink — a path")
    strs_push(l, "`write_file` writes to — so a program that echoes a file's contents to standard output is")
    strs_push(l, "invisible to every policy, and a program that has checked a value has no way to say so.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Resource facts are read off MIR**, where every operation that allocates, retains, blocks, talks")
    strs_push(l, "to a channel, calls C or starts a task is already an explicit statement — no layer below has to")
    strs_push(l, "rediscover them and none above can see them. The classes, each from its MIR form:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| class | MIR |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `allocation` | a built-in that makes storage (`ints_new`, `strs_new`, `vec_new`, `chan_new`, `str_concat`, `int_to_str`, `str_from_byte`, `str_join`, `read_file`, `arg`), a closure object (`Rvalue::Closure`), and a push that may grow its sequence |")
    strs_push(l, "| `retain` | a copy of a managed value (`Rvalue::Copy`, a field or payload read, a capture) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `block` | `chan_send` and `chan_recv` on a bounded channel, and a `scope`'s join |")
    strs_push(l, "| `channel` | every channel operation |")
    strs_push(l, "| `foreign` | a call to a foreign function |")
    strs_push(l, "| `task` | a `spawn` |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Each site carries a **count per call of its function**: `at-most-once` when its block is in no")
    strs_push(l, "cycle of the function's control-flow graph, and `unknown` when it is — inside a loop the count")
    strs_push(l, "depends on values the compiler does not know. `unknown` is a value of its own and is never")
    strs_push(l, "written as a number; there is no \"zero\" in the vocabulary, because a site that exists may run. A")
    strs_push(l, "count is per call: what a caller's loop makes of it is the caller's site. Nothing here is a")
    strs_push(l, "measurement, and nothing claims an upper bound on bytes. `nazm explain-cost` prints the sites,")
    strs_push(l, "by function, for a reader and as `nazm.cost/1` for a tool.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A profile reads them.** `embedded` gains `bounded-allocation`: no allocation site whose count is")
    strs_push(l, "`unknown`, so an accepted embedded program allocates a number of times bounded by its call")
    strs_push(l, "structure (recursion is already a cycle the rule sees through its calls' sites; an indirect call")
    strs_push(l, "is reported as such).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Provenance v2: a registry of sinks.** A sink is an argument of a built-in that takes data out of")
    strs_push(l, "the program, by class: `path` (the path `write_file` writes to, N38's), `output` (what `print`")
    strs_push(l, "and `eprint` write) and `file-data` (what `write_file` writes). The sources are N38's four origins.")
    strs_push(l, "Every sink is reduced to flows and solved through summaries exactly as the path sink is — through")
    strs_push(l, "helpers, higher-order calls (N50's conservative indirect-call rule) and modules — and every solved")
    strs_push(l, "sink is recorded with its origins. The language's own restriction is unchanged: `N0372` for a")
    strs_push(l, "restricted origin at a `path` sink in a declared function. What other classes may receive is")
    strs_push(l, "**profile policy**: `cyber` gains `contents-stay-in-files`, refusing a file's contents (or an unknown")
    strs_push(l, "origin) at an `output` sink. **Containers** stay conservative, and say so: a value read out of a")
    strs_push(l, "sequence or a channel is `unknown`, the whole container standing for every element, because a")
    strs_push(l, "local analysis cannot see every alias that wrote to it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Declassification is authority, not a name.** `str_vouch(s: Str) -> Str` returns its argument with")
    strs_push(l, "no origin. It needs a `VouchCap` held where it is written — in every function, declared or not, as a")
    strs_push(l, "foreign call does — and `VouchCap` is a new capability kind, minted only for `main`'s parameters like")
    strs_push(l, "every other. Nothing is inferred from a function's name, and nothing else clears an origin. Each")
    strs_push(l, "vouch is recorded with the origins it cleared, which `nazm explain-flow` (`nazm.flow/1`) prints")
    strs_push(l, "beside every sink, so the evidence is machine-readable; `critical` gains `no-declassification`,")
    strs_push(l, "refusing any vouch at all.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Bounded and deterministic.** The provenance fixed point is over finite lattices (origins ×")
    strs_push(l, "parameters) and its worklists re-queue callers only on growth; a stress test holds a 2,000-function")
    strs_push(l, "call chain to a deadline and to identical output on two runs. Resource facts are one pass over each")
    strs_push(l, "MIR function's blocks.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** The semantic epoch moves: `str_vouch` and `VouchCap` are new names a program may use,")
    strs_push(l, "and a program that declared a type or function of either name moves from accepted to refused. The")
    strs_push(l, "check artefact's sink facts gain a class; an entry from an older checker is unreachable by the epoch.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.cost/1` and `nazm.flow/1` are new schemas.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.55 The runtime component and generic channels — N53, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Two things the runtime could not do: be a component of its own, and carry")
    strs_push(l, "anything through a channel but an `Int`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The boundary.** The runtime — every function and global generated code calls, its typed")
    strs_push(l, "inventory, its OS adapter, the platform entry and its identity — moves out of the LLVM backend's")
    strs_push(l, "crate into **`nazm-runtime`**, which both backends depend on and neither owns. What stays")
    strs_push(l, "compiler-generated is what depends on a program: per-type retain, release and equality helpers,")
    strs_push(l, "closure release functions, task trampolines. The runtime is still LLVM IR text compiled by clang,")
    strs_push(l, "for both backends: rewriting it as Rust compiled to an object would need a `no_std` runtime with")
    strs_push(l, "no unwinding, built per target at `nazm build` time or shipped prebuilt per target, and a linker")
    strs_push(l, "step neither backend has today — a research item (`docs/internal/research-register.md`), not this")
    strs_push(l, "milestone's. The Cranelift backend therefore still needs clang for the runtime object, and both")
    strs_push(l, "need the system C library and linker; that is stated, not hidden.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Identity.** The runtime ABI revision stays a number a reader can talk about, and beside it the")
    strs_push(l, "runtime gains a **digest** — of every part's text, the entry, the inventory and the globals — that")
    strs_push(l, "enters every object's cache key. A change to the runtime that forgot to bump the revision still")
    strs_push(l, "changes every key, so an object built against another runtime is never reused. Revision 5 is this")
    strs_push(l, "milestone's: generic channels.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**`Chan[T]`.** A channel of any type that may cross into a task (`Int`, `Bool`, `Str`, `Chan`,")
    strs_push(l, "`Chan[U]`, and records and enums of those) — the same rule `spawn` applies to an argument, now")
    strs_push(l, "also the rule for being a channel's element (`N0390` otherwise). `Chan` alone is unchanged: the")
    strs_push(l, "`Int` channel, its four built-ins and its runtime. `Chan[T]` has its own: `chan_new_of[T](capacity)`,")
    strs_push(l, "`chan_send_of(c, v)`, `chan_recv_of(c, out: Vec[T])` and `chan_close_of(c)`, with exactly `Chan`'s")
    strs_push(l, "blocking, closing and draining semantics. **Ownership:** a send copies its value into the channel")
    strs_push(l, "(the sender's binding is untouched, as every argument is); a value refused by a closed channel is")
    strs_push(l, "released at once; a receive moves the value out of the channel into the vector; a channel destroyed")
    strs_push(l, "with values still queued releases each of them, by a release function generated for `T` — the")
    strs_push(l, "helper a `Vec[T]` already has. Equality, ordering and a task's use are as `Chan`'s. The memory")
    strs_push(l, "report counts generic channels with the others.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Runtime representation.** A generic channel is a ring of fixed-size slots, the slot size and the")
    strs_push(l, "element release function given at creation; send and receive copy one slot under the channel's")
    strs_push(l, "lock. The `Int` channel keeps its own ring, so nothing about existing programs changes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.56 Select, deadlines, cancellation and the scheduler's counters — N54, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. §7.46 left five things out: a worker pool, cancellation, timeouts, select")
    strs_push(l, "and any count of what the scheduler did. This section settles what N54 adds, and — as carefully —")
    strs_push(l, "what it decides not to build yet and why.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The model stays one OS thread per task.** An M:N scheduler needs tasks that can be suspended off")
    strs_push(l, "an OS thread: either a stack per task that a worker switches to (stackful), or compiled")
    strs_push(l, "continuations (stackless: every function that may block becomes a state machine). Stackless is")
    strs_push(l, "ruled out for Nazm: it colours every function that can reach a channel operation, doubles every")
    strs_push(l, "backend's lowering, and breaks the debugger's frame model (§7.50). Stackful is the model a pool")
    strs_push(l, "would use — a guarded `mmap`'d stack per task and a small per-target switch routine — and it is not")
    strs_push(l, "built here, because three things the runtime already promises are thread-local and would silently")
    strs_push(l, "break when a task migrated between workers: the first-failure slot (`nz.failed`, §7.45), the stack")
    strs_push(l, "limit `nz.stack_check` budgets from (N49), and the C library's own per-thread state any foreign call")
    strs_push(l, "(N42) may rely on. Each needs a task-local home first, and a foreign call that blocks needs a")
    strs_push(l, "hand-off so it cannot pin a worker. Until then a fixed pool would deadlock correct programs (§7.46),")
    strs_push(l, "so **bounded workers are DESIGNED, not implemented**: the stack model is chosen (stackful, guarded,")
    strs_push(l, "per-target switch), its prerequisites are named, and nothing in the language below depends on it —")
    strs_push(l, "every rule here holds unchanged under a pool.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Suspension points.** The operations that may wait are exactly: `chan_send`/`chan_send_of` on a full")
    strs_push(l, "channel, `chan_recv`/`chan_recv_of` on an empty one, `chan_select_of`/`chan_select_until` with no")
    strs_push(l, "channel ready, and a `scope`'s join. Nothing else waits. These are also the only places a future pool")
    strs_push(l, "would park a task, and the only places cancellation is observed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Select.** `chan_select_of(cs: Vec[Chan[T]], out: Vec[T]) -> Int` waits until some channel in `cs`")
    strs_push(l, "is *ready* — it holds a value, or it is closed and drained — and returns the **lowest index** among")
    strs_push(l, "the channels ready when it looks. A ready channel holding a value gives its oldest value, moved onto")
    strs_push(l, "`out` as `chan_recv_of` moves it; a closed and drained one gives nothing, and `out` is unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "`-1` means `cs` is empty. Tie-breaking is deterministic — lowest index — but *which* channels are")
    strs_push(l, "ready when select looks depends on how tasks were scheduled, so a select's result is classified")
    strs_push(l, "**schedule-dependent**, as any receive from a channel two tasks send into already is. A closed channel")
    strs_push(l, "is always ready: closing is a broadcast, which is what makes it a cancellation signal.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deadlines.** `chan_select_until(cs, out, ms: Int) -> Int` is `chan_select_of` that gives")
    strs_push(l, "up after `ms` milliseconds and returns `-2`; `ms <= 0` looks once and does not wait. Reading the clock")
    strs_push(l, "is reading the host, so it needs authority: a new capability, **`TimeCap`**, held where it is written,")
    strs_push(l, "in every function (as `VouchCap` is, N52). Like a vouch it performs no effect — reading a clock changes")
    strs_push(l, "nothing outside the program, and N51 already says *pure* means *no effect*, not *referentially")
    strs_push(l, "transparent* — so the authority is the one thing that gates it, and the thing a profile refuses.")
    strs_push(l, "`time_now_ms() -> Int` reads a monotonic clock in milliseconds, a fresh `Int` with no origin. So a function that may time")
    strs_push(l, "out says so in its signature, and a profile can refuse time outright: `critical` gains")
    strs_push(l, "**`no-ambient-time`**, refusing any use of `TimeCap`, because a program whose behaviour depends on a")
    strs_push(l, "clock is not reproducible. The interpreter and both native backends read the same host clock; a")
    strs_push(l, "timeout is a lower bound — at least `ms` elapse before `-2` — never a promise of promptness.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Cancellation is cooperative and explicit.** A canceller closes a channel; every task selecting on it")
    strs_push(l, "sees it ready and decides what to do. Cancellation is observed only at the suspension points above, and")
    strs_push(l, "only by a task that looks — a task in a loop that never selects runs to completion. There is still no")
    strs_push(l, "cancellation on a sibling's failure: N44's rule that a scope reports its first failure in start order")
    strs_push(l, "and joins every task is kept unchanged, because cancelling siblings on failure would make which failure")
    strs_push(l, "is reported depend on timing. Cleanup is unchanged too: a cancelled task returns like any other, its")
    strs_push(l, "scope joins it, and everything it held is released on that path (§7.42).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Ownership.** Select moves at most one value, from one channel, onto `out`; nothing else changes hands.")
    strs_push(l, "A value queued in a channel select did not choose stays queued. A timed-out select moves nothing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Counters.** With `NAZM_SCHED_REPORT=1` a program writes one line to standard error at exit,")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-sched: spawned=… joined=… selects=… timeouts=…`: tasks started, tasks joined, select calls")
    strs_push(l, "completed, and selects that timed out. They are counts of what happened, not samples; the interpreter")
    strs_push(l, "and both native backends count the same events, and for a program whose selects cannot race they agree.")
    strs_push(l, "`queued`, `running`, `suspended`, wake-ups and steals are counts only a pool has, and are not invented")
    strs_push(l, "for a scheduler that has none.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Implementation.** Select over typed channels only (N53's `nz.chanv_*`), so the `Int` channel's runtime")
    strs_push(l, "under the self-hosted compiler's parity gate is untouched. A select cannot wait on several condition")
    strs_push(l, "variables, so every typed channel's state change also advances one runtime-wide *event count* and")
    strs_push(l, "broadcasts its condition variable; a selector reads the count, scans the channels in index order under")
    strs_push(l, "each one's lock, and waits only if the count has not moved since it read it — the classic event-count")
    strs_push(l, "protocol, which cannot lose a wake-up. The cost is one extra lock per typed send, receive or close,")
    strs_push(l, "measured below (`docs/internal/performance-log.md`, N54). The counters live in the runtime (`nz.sched_*`), called by")
    strs_push(l, "generated code after a task starts and before a scope joins.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** A worker pool, task migration, work stealing, cancellation on failure, `select` over send")
    strs_push(l, "operations or over the `Int` channel, timers other than a select's deadline, async I/O, deadlock")
    strs_push(l, "detection.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.57 FFI v2: C strings in, exported functions out — N55, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. §7.44 let a program call C with `Int` and `Bool`. N55 widens the boundary")
    strs_push(l, "in the two directions programs most need, and settles — without building — the shapes that need a")
    strs_push(l, "memory model Nazm does not have yet.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A `Str` argument is a borrowed C string.** A foreign parameter may be `Str`. At the call the")
    strs_push(l, "caller makes a NUL-terminated copy of the string's bytes, passes C a `const char *` to it, and frees")
    strs_push(l, "the copy when the call returns: C borrows it for the call and must not keep it. A string containing")
    strs_push(l, "a NUL byte cannot be a C string, so such a call fails before C runs (`N0405`, at the call) — the")
    strs_push(l, "copy is never truncated silently. The cost is one allocation and one copy per string argument,")
    strs_push(l, "stated rather than hidden; zero-copy would need every Nazm string NUL-terminated, which a slice")
    strs_push(l, "cannot be. A `Str` **result** stays refused (`N0381`): who frees a `char *` C returns is a fact no")
    strs_push(l, "declaration states.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**An exported function is a Nazm function C may call.** `pub extern \"C\" fn name(p: Int, …) -> R ! {}")
    strs_push(l, "= \"symbol\" { body }` — an `extern` declaration *with* a body — defines `symbol` with the C calling")
    strs_push(l, "convention, its parameters and result the v1 scalars (`Int` as `int64_t`, `Bool` as `bool`). Its")
    strs_push(l, "body is ordinary Nazm, with three rules, all checked (`N0391`):")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **It is public and declares `! {}`.** C cannot hand Nazm a capability, so an export takes none and")
    strs_push(l, "  performs no effect: it computes, calling pure functions.")
    strs_push(l, "- **It is not generic and takes no `Str`.** A C caller has one signature and owns its own memory; a")
    strs_push(l, "  borrowed string *into* Nazm needs the lifetime rule a callback would, and is not here.")
    strs_push(l, "- **No failure unwinds into C.** A Nazm failure inside an export — an overflow, an out-of-bounds")
    strs_push(l, "  index, out of memory — cannot propagate through C frames, which have no cleanup Nazm knows of. The")
    strs_push(l, "  export's C entry reports it on standard error exactly as `main`'s entry does, and ends the process")
    strs_push(l, "  with status 2. An export either returns its declared value or the process ends with a Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "  diagnostic; it never returns a stand-in.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Libraries.** `nazm build --lib FILE -o OUT.a` builds the program's modules without requiring a `main`,")
    strs_push(l, "writes a static archive of every unit's object and the runtime's, and `OUT.h`, a C header declaring")
    strs_push(l, "each export with `<stdint.h>` and `<stdbool.h>` types, in a fixed order. The archive's other symbols")
    strs_push(l, "stay hidden; only the exports are visible to a C link. One Nazm library per C program: two would")
    strs_push(l, "both carry the runtime. Either backend builds a library, and the header is the same text for both.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The archive is written by nazm (2026-10-17).** Both static archives — a library's and the runtime")
    strs_push(l, "artifact's (§7.83) — are written by `crates/nazm-cli/src/archive.rs`, not the system's `ar`. The")
    strs_push(l, "cause: Apple's Command Line Tools 27.0 write the symbol index of `ar rcs` and `libtool -static`")
    strs_push(l, "(`__.SYMDEF SORTED`) in an order that varies from run to run, so the same objects archived to")
    strs_push(l, "different bytes (4 variants in 6 builds) and the runtime artifact was no longer reproducible; `ar rcS`,")
    strs_push(l, "with no index, is stable, but `ld64` then refuses the members. The archive is now a function of its")
    strs_push(l, "members' names and bytes alone: for Mach-O members, the BSD format `ld64` reads — `#1/N` names")
    strs_push(l, "padded so every member's bytes are 8-byte aligned, zero dates, owners and groups, mode 644, and an")
    strs_push(l, "index sorted by symbol name, ties by member offset; for ELF, COFF and WebAssembly members, the")
    strs_push(l, "GNU/System V format with a `/` index in member order and a `//` table of long names, which GNU,")
    strs_push(l, "MinGW and LLVM linkers read. Each index holds the member's defined global symbols, read from its own")
    strs_push(l, "symbol table (Mach-O `nlist`, ELF `.symtab`, COFF's table, WebAssembly's `linking` section). Apple's")
    strs_push(l, "`ar` had written an empty index for every non-Mach-O member, so a board's, WebAssembly's and")
    strs_push(l, "Windows' archive now index what they define; `nazm doctor` no longer looks for `ar`. Linking a")
    strs_push(l, "Windows program against its runtime artifact with MinGW then showed the artifact lacked the")
    strs_push(l, "Windows `init` unit (`nz_os_args`, which the entry calls) that a generated runtime carries; the")
    strs_push(l, "artifact now carries it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Identity.** An export's symbol enters its function's Core IR and MIR digests and so its unit's")
    strs_push(l, "object key. It is not persisted in the interface: to another Nazm module an export is an ordinary")
    strs_push(l, "function, called by the internal ABI, and its C entry lives in the unit that defines it. Two exports")
    strs_push(l, "of one symbol, or one also imported from C, are refused when the program is built (`N0383`). Accepting syntax that was refused, and a")
    strs_push(l, "`Str` where `N0381` was, moves the semantic epoch (17 → 18).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here, and why.** *Opaque handles* need a nominal type whose values Nazm never dereferences or")
    strs_push(l, "frees — designed (`extern \"C\" type T;`, a word at run time, no equality, not crossing into a task,")
    strs_push(l, "freed only by a C function the program calls) and not built. *C structs* need a layout guarantee")
    strs_push(l, "distinct from Nazm's records, which §7.43 deliberately leaves free. *Callbacks* — C calling a Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "function value — need a trampoline that finds its closure from a C `void *` and a rule for a")
    strs_push(l, "callback called after its environment is gone. *`errno`* is a per-thread location whose symbol")
    strs_push(l, "differs by platform (`__error` on macOS, `__errno_location` on Linux) and belongs with N57's target")
    strs_push(l, "model. Dynamic libraries and exporting to anything but C are also not here.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.58 Packages v2: a local registry and version requirements — N56, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. §7.48 made every dependency an exact path. N56 adds the second source a")
    strs_push(l, "package ecosystem needs — a registry — and the version requirements that make it useful, while")
    strs_push(l, "keeping every N46 guarantee: no network, deterministic resolution, digests, a lockfile that is")
    strs_push(l, "authoritative under `--locked`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A registry is a directory**, named by the root manifest's `[registry] path = \"…\"` (relative to")
    strs_push(l, "it; a dependency's own `[registry]` is ignored, so one build has one registry):")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```text")
    strs_push(l, "REGISTRY/index/NAME.toml              nazm.registry-index/1: name, and every version with its digest")
    strs_push(l, "REGISTRY/packages/NAME/VERSION/…      the published copy: its manifest and its sources, nothing else")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "There is no remote registry and no download: a registry somewhere else is a directory someone")
    strs_push(l, "copied here, and the copy is checked, not trusted. A correctness test never needs a public service.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Coordinates and requirements.** A package is still its name and exact version. A registry")
    strs_push(l, "dependency names a requirement instead of a path: `shapes = { version = \"^1.2.0\" }`. Four forms:")
    strs_push(l, "`1.2.3` and `=1.2.3` (exactly), `^1.2.3` (the same left-most non-zero component: `>=1.2.3,<2.0.0`;")
    strs_push(l, "`^0.2.3` is `<0.3.0`; `^0.0.3` is exact), `~1.2.3` (`>=1.2.3,<1.3.0`). No pre-releases, no")
    strs_push(l, "arbitrary comparators, no features. A path dependency is unchanged: a path and an exact version.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Resolution** visits the path graph as N46 does, then solves the registry requirements in rounds:")
    strs_push(l, "each round collects every requirement on every registry name — from the path packages and from the")
    strs_push(l, "registry packages chosen so far — and chooses, per name, the version the lockfile records if it")
    strs_push(l, "still satisfies them all, else the **highest non-yanked** published version that does. It stops")
    strs_push(l, "when a round changes nothing. **One version per name** stays the rule (§7.48), and there is **no")
    strs_push(l, "backtracking**: if no version satisfies every requirement, resolution is refused naming each")
    strs_push(l, "requirement and who made it (`N0513`). This can refuse a graph a backtracking solver would find;")
    strs_push(l, "it never chooses a surprising version, and its answer is a function of the manifests, the index and")
    strs_push(l, "the lockfile alone — not of their order on disk.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The store refuses what a store must.** A published version is immutable: publishing it again is")
    strs_push(l, "refused (`N0512`). Every package is fetched through its index entry and checked before use: its")
    strs_push(l, "manifest names that package and version, it holds only regular files and directories (a symbolic")
    strs_push(l, "link is `N0514`: it could point anywhere), and its bytes match the digest the index records")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0507`: tampered after publishing). An index that is not `nazm.registry-index/1`, names another")
    strs_push(l, "package, records a version twice or a malformed digest is `N0512`; a version is parsed, so it can")
    strs_push(l, "never be a path. A published package depends only on the registry: a path means nothing in another")
    strs_push(l, "checkout. A registry package and a path package of one name in one build conflict (`N0503`); a")
    strs_push(l, "cycle through registry edges is `N0504`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Identity.** A registry package's source in the lockfile is `registry+NAME@VERSION`, and its")
    strs_push(l, "modules' durable keys are `NAME@VERSION/…` as every dependency's: where the registry is on disk")
    strs_push(l, "enters neither. The digest is N46's, over the published copy.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Lock, frozen, yank.** `nazm lock` records the chosen versions; a later resolution prefers them")
    strs_push(l, "while they still satisfy the manifests, so publishing a newer version changes nothing until the")
    strs_push(l, "lockfile is rewritten. `--locked` refuses any difference, a stale lockfile included. `nazm yank")
    strs_push(l, "NAME@VERSION --registry DIR` withdraws a version: never chosen anew, still used where a lockfile")
    strs_push(l, "names it, and `--undo` restores it. `nazm publish DIR --registry REG` copies a package's manifest")
    strs_push(l, "and sources into the registry and records its digest; it writes the index by rename, so a reader")
    strs_push(l, "never sees half of one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The self-hosted compiler** reads no manifest: its resolver knows relative imports only. Teaching")
    strs_push(l, "it packages needs a TOML reader and a package graph written in Nazm — designed (the graph is")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.lock/1`, which a later milestone can hand it already resolved) and not built here.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** A network registry, signatures (a digest is integrity, not authorship), features,")
    strs_push(l, "pre-releases, version ranges beyond the four forms, multiple versions of one package, workspaces")
    strs_push(l, "with several roots, build scripts.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.59 Targets and cross-compilation — N57, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Since N41 a build named its target and refused every one but the host.")
    strs_push(l, "N57 makes a target a real input: four triples, each built by both backends from any host in the")
    strs_push(l, "matrix, linked where a linker for it is present and handed back as objects where none is.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The target is a value, not the host.** `--target TRIPLE` is one of `aarch64-apple-darwin`,")
    strs_push(l, "`x86_64-apple-darwin`, `aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu`, `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`: an architecture")
    strs_push(l, "(64-bit ARM or x86, little-endian, 64-bit pointers), an operating system (macOS or Linux) and an")
    strs_push(l, "ABI (Darwin's, or glibc's System V). No CPU feature beyond the triple's baseline is used by either")
    strs_push(l, "backend, so an object does not depend on the machine that built it. Anything else is refused by")
    strs_push(l, "name before anything is compiled.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What changes per target, and what does not.** The runtime text is the same for all four: it")
    strs_push(l, "names only what both C libraries share under the same values (`RLIMIT_STACK` 3,")
    strs_push(l, "`CLOCK_REALTIME` 0, `CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW` 4, `struct timespec` two 64-bit words, an attribute")
    strs_push(l, "object of at most 128 bytes) — a fact §7.45 already relied on, now stated as the portability rule")
    strs_push(l, "the runtime keeps. What changes is the code generator's: clang is told the triple (`-target`), and")
    strs_push(l, "Cranelift is built for it (its `x86` and `arm64` backends both compiled in). The object format —")
    strs_push(l, "Mach-O or ELF — follows.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Host tools and target artefacts are separate.** A build runs the compiler, clang and the linker")
    strs_push(l, "— host tools — and never runs what it produced: there is no build script, and nothing in a build")
    strs_push(l, "executes a target binary. Whether a produced program can run on the host is the test harness's")
    strs_push(l, "question, answered separately: an x86_64 macOS program on an ARM Mac runs under Rosetta when it is")
    strs_push(l, "installed; a Linux program runs in a Linux container. The two are reported apart, as")
    strs_push(l, "**run-verified** and **compile-only**.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Linking.** A target linked by the host's own toolchain — the host's triple, or the other macOS")
    strs_push(l, "architecture, whose SDK the Apple toolchain carries — produces an executable. A target the host has")
    strs_push(l, "no linker for (Linux from macOS, macOS from Linux) produces **objects**: `nazm build --objects DIR`")
    strs_push(l, "writes every unit's object, the runtime's and the entry's, and `DIR/link.txt` listing them in link")
    strs_push(l, "order with the system libraries the target needs (`-lpthread`), for the target's own toolchain to")
    strs_push(l, "link. Asking for an executable for such a target is refused by name, not attempted with a host")
    strs_push(l, "linker that would produce the wrong thing. No linker is found on `PATH` by accident: the one used")
    strs_push(l, "is the driver's own, and the driver's resolved command line for the target is in every key.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Identity.** The target triple is in every object's key under both backends — LLVM's through the")
    strs_push(l, "driver's resolved configuration, Cranelift's directly — so an object built for one target is never")
    strs_push(l, "reused for another. `nazm inspect` and the build report name the target. A package's lockfile is")
    strs_push(l, "target-independent: a package's sources do not depend on the target in v1, and none may yet.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Reproducibility across hosts.** Same-target builds from different hosts are a separate claim from")
    strs_push(l, "same-host reproducibility. N57 records what it measured — for which targets two hosts' objects")
    strs_push(l, "agree — and claims nothing it did not measure.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** Windows, 32-bit or big-endian targets, a target-specific runtime part, CPU feature")
    strs_push(l, "selection, a bundled linker or sysroot, target-conditional source, and emulation inside the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.60 Debugger and profiler v2 — N58, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. §7.50 gave a `--debug` build functions and lines, and left two things")
    strs_push(l, "unclaimed: a live session and variables. N58 claims both, for what it can show, and says where the")
    strs_push(l, "evidence comes from.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Where a live session is verified.** On the development Mac, launching a process under lldb waits")
    strs_push(l, "on the operating system's developer-mode authorisation, which a non-interactive agent cannot give")
    strs_push(l, "and must not change; that remains unexercised there. The live session is verified instead in the")
    strs_push(l, "Linux container — a separate image, `nazm-debug`, that adds gdb to the gate's image without")
    strs_push(l, "changing it — on objects built for `aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu` (§7.59) and linked there: a")
    strs_push(l, "breakpoint by file and line and by function, a backtrace naming Nazm functions with their files")
    strs_push(l, "and lines through several calls, `next` and `step` by statement, and variables read while live.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Variables.** A `--debug` build describes every parameter and every source binding of type `Int`,")
    strs_push(l, "`Bool` or `Str` with a `DILocalVariable` on its stack slot — a parameter with its position — and the")
    strs_push(l, "types as DWARF: `Int` a signed 64-bit integer, `Bool` an 8-bit boolean, `Str` a structure of its")
    strs_push(l, "three words (`data`, a pointer to bytes; `len`; `owner`). Temporaries are not described: they have")
    strs_push(l, "no name a reader wrote. Records, enums, sequences, channels and closures are not described yet.")
    strs_push(l, "**No stale value is shown as live**: a managed local's slot is zeroed when it is dropped and before")
    strs_push(l, "its storage is released, so after its last use a `Str` reads as `{data = 0x0, len = 0}`, never as")
    strs_push(l, "the bytes of freed memory; and a slot is zeroed at entry, so a binding read before its statement")
    strs_push(l, "reads `0`. Both are the slot's real contents, not a claim about the variable's value at that point:")
    strs_push(l, "scope ranges (`DILexicalBlock`) are not emitted, so every described variable is visible for its")
    strs_push(l, "whole function.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Amended during implementation.** Two facts the live session taught. *Names*: with the native")
    strs_push(l, "symbol as the subprogram's `linkageName`, gdb named every frame and resolved every breakpoint by")
    strs_push(l, "the symbol (`nz.m.v_2Enz.greet`) and not by `greet`; the subprogram now carries the Nazm name alone,")
    strs_push(l, "and the symbol stays in the object's symbol table. *The prologue*: LLVM marks the end of a")
    strs_push(l, "function's prologue at the entry block's first instruction with a line, and when none has one it")
    strs_push(l, "uses the function's line at its first instruction — so a breakpoint on a function stopped before")
    strs_push(l, "its parameters were stored, and gdb showed `times=0`. The prologue now carries no line and the")
    strs_push(l, "entry block's branch takes the first statement's position, so the breakpoint lands after every")
    strs_push(l, "slot is written.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Optimised builds.** At `-O2` LLVM may delete or move a slot; a variable it removed reads as")
    strs_push(l, "\"optimized out\" in the debugger, which is the debugger's word for it and the honest answer. Nothing")
    strs_push(l, "is claimed about values at `-O2`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Cranelift.** `--debug` with Cranelift stays refused by name: Cranelift 0.136 exposes no DWARF")
    strs_push(l, "emission for an object module through the API this backend uses, so there is no line table to")
    strs_push(l, "write. A blocker with its reason, not a silent difference.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Scheduler and runtime counters in the profiler.** `nazm profile FILE` builds the program,")
    strs_push(l, "runs it once with `NAZM_MEMORY_REPORT` and `NAZM_SCHED_REPORT` set, and prints `nazm.profile/1`: the")
    strs_push(l, "exit status, the wall time, and the memory and scheduler counts parsed from those lines — counts of")
    strs_push(l, "events, not samples. The compiler's phase timings stay `nazm.timings/1`; the two are separate")
    strs_push(l, "documents and are never added together.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** Sampling profilers, timelines, an event trace, closure environments and generic")
    strs_push(l, "instances by name in the debugger, foreign frames' variables, DWARF from Cranelift, and the Mac's")
    strs_push(l, "live session.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.61 Backend performance and what the native build still needs — N59, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. N40 measured the cost of lowering through MIR: at `-O0` the LLVM emitter")
    strs_push(l, "gives every MIR local a stack slot, and clang at `-O0` promotes none of them, so the compiler")
    strs_push(l, "written in Nazm emitted 13,836 `alloca`s where N39's tree walk emitted 3,275, and clang's compile")
    strs_push(l, "grew 17 %. N59 removes the part of that cost that needs no new analysis, and states what the native")
    strs_push(l, "build still depends on.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Scalar temporaries become SSA values.** MIR keeps its slot-per-local model — it is the authority")
    strs_push(l, "for ownership and control flow, and nothing here changes it. The LLVM emitter, deciding how to")
    strs_push(l, "represent a local, gives no slot to a local that MIR lowering made (`Temp`), of type `Int` or")
    strs_push(l, "`Bool`, assigned exactly once, and read only later in the block that assigns it: such a value is")
    strs_push(l, "already in a register, the store and load around it are pure overhead, and SSA's dominance rule is")
    strs_push(l, "satisfied by construction — a use in the same block after the definition. Everything else keeps its")
    strs_push(l, "slot: parameters, source bindings (a debugger reads them, §7.60), managed values (a failure edge's")
    strs_push(l, "cleanup reads and zeroes them), records and enums, and any local read in another block, including a")
    strs_push(l, "cleanup block. The rule is decided per function from MIR alone, so the emitted text is a")
    strs_push(l, "deterministic function of MIR, and its digest of what was emitted (the object key) is unchanged in")
    strs_push(l, "kind.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Measured, not assumed.** The gain is counted — slots and instructions in the compiler's own")
    strs_push(l, "text — and timed as an interleaved A/B on one host, with the variance stated; it is claimed for the")
    strs_push(l, "workloads measured and nothing else. Cranelift needed no counterpart: it already keeps every scalar")
    strs_push(l, "local in an SSA variable (§7.43) and optimises at `-O1` and above; its remaining gap on sequence")
    strs_push(l, "loops is its register allocator and lack of loop-invariant motion over memory, which N59 measures")
    strs_push(l, "and does not claim to close.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the native build still needs.** The runtime is LLVM text (§7.55), so both backends still run")
    strs_push(l, "clang to compile it, and both run the system C compiler driver to link. N59 does not remove either:")
    strs_push(l, "a runtime precompiled per target, or a linker driven directly, is the next step, and the build")
    strs_push(l, "reports both dependencies by name (`nazm inspect`'s toolchain) rather than hiding them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** Promoting locals across blocks (phi construction), promoting managed values, an")
    strs_push(l, "optimisation pipeline of Nazm's own, a precompiled runtime, a built-in linker.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.62 Restriction profiles v2: stack, determinism, unknowns — N60, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. §7.49's profiles refuse effects, the ambient bridge and unlocked builds;")
    strs_push(l, "N52 and N54 added allocation, flow, declassification and time. N60 adds the rules those facts")
    strs_push(l, "make possible next, and gives a verdict a third value.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A verdict is `pass`, `fail` or `unknown`.** A rule whose facts were not established — MIR did not")
    strs_push(l, "lower, or a call target cannot be known — is `unknown`, and a profile treats `unknown` as a refusal")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0510`, with the reason): a restriction that cannot be checked is not met. The report carries the")
    strs_push(l, "three values, so a reader sees which refusals are proofs of a violation and which are absences of a")
    strs_push(l, "proof. `general` has no rules and is unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Stack: `no-recursion` (embedded).** A program whose call graph has a cycle has no stack bound the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler can state. The facts are MIR's: a function in a call cycle is exactly one MIR gives a")
    strs_push(l, "`StackCheck` (N49), and the witness names it. A call through a function value (`CallIndirect`) has a")
    strs_push(l, "target the compiler does not know, so where one exists the rule is `unknown` rather than `pass`. A")
    strs_push(l, "frame-size estimate per function is not computed here: the bound on depth is the claim, not bytes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Determinism: `no-select` (critical).** `critical` already refuses spawning a task, reading a clock and")
    strs_push(l, "declassifying; a select's result depends on which channels are ready when it looks (§7.56), so it is")
    strs_push(l, "refused too, by its call site. What is left inside `critical` — no tasks, no clock, no select — is a")
    strs_push(l, "program whose observable behaviour is a function of its inputs, its files and its arguments; those")
    strs_push(l, "stay allowed under `io`, and refusing them is `embedded`'s `no-io`. Random numbers and the network")
    strs_push(l, "do not exist in the language.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Composition.** A profile only adds rules, and every package's required profile is in force for any")
    strs_push(l, "program it is part of (§7.49): a dependency cannot weaken what the root requires, because nothing a")
    strs_push(l, "dependency declares removes a rule. This was true since N47 and is now tested from the root's side.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here, and why.** *Constant-time* rules — no branch or index depending on a secret — need a")
    strs_push(l, "secret-origin lattice that N52's origins (file, argument, unknown) do not express; a research item,")
    strs_push(l, "not a partial claim. *Bounded loops, queues and tasks* need a declared, checked bound (§7.63's")
    strs_push(l, "subject, N63). *Byte bounds* on allocation stay N52's `at-most-once`/`unknown` counts. Nothing here is")
    strs_push(l, "a certification.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.63 A formal core and bounded model checking — N61, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Nazm's meaning is its specification and its two implementations' agreement;")
    strs_push(l, "nothing about it was machine-checked against a definition independent of both. N61 states a small")
    strs_push(l, "core formally — `docs/internal/formal-core.md`: syntax, typing rules, big-step evaluation rules with traps —")
    strs_push(l, "and checks five properties of it, mechanically, over every program of the core up to a size.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Why bounded model checking and not a proof assistant.** No proof assistant is part of the")
    strs_push(l, "toolchain, and adding one is a dependency decision the project has not made. A checker that")
    strs_push(l, "enumerates every program of the core up to `BOUND` nodes and checks each property on each is")
    strs_push(l, "mechanical, deterministic, runs in the ordinary test suite, and says exactly what it covers: every")
    strs_push(l, "program up to the bound, and nothing beyond it. That is weaker than a proof and stronger than a")
    strs_push(l, "sample, and it is stated as such.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Correspondence.** The semantics is transcribed into `crates/nazm-formal`, one arm per rule, with no")
    strs_push(l, "dependency on the compiler: the compiler cannot be its own oracle. Each core program is printed as a")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm program, and the properties hold the real checker and the real interpreter to the formal")
    strs_push(l, "definition: the checker accepts exactly what the typing rules type, and the interpreter's outcome")
    strs_push(l, "— value or trap code — is the evaluation rules'. A change to either side that the other does not")
    strs_push(l, "share is found by the enumeration.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the critical profile may cite.** A property of the core is evidence about the core's")
    strs_push(l, "constructs — integer and boolean arithmetic with traps, comparison, short-circuit `&&`, `if`,")
    strs_push(l, "`let` — and only those. The profile report names no proof; the matrix records the core's scope.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** Functions, recursion, loops, mutation, strings, sequences, records, enums, effects,")
    strs_push(l, "tasks, closures, memory, and the native backends' code generation; a proof of any property beyond")
    strs_push(l, "the bound.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.64 A freestanding target: no OS, no libc, no heap — N62, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Every target so far runs on an operating system through its C library.")
    strs_push(l, "N62 adds one that runs on neither: `aarch64-unknown-none`, a 64-bit ARM machine with no OS, verified")
    strs_push(l, "on QEMU's `virt` board.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a freestanding program is.** A Nazm program that needs nothing of the hosted runtime: no")
    strs_push(l, "allocation (so no strings built at run time, sequences, channels or closures), no tasks, no files,")
    strs_push(l, "arguments or standard streams, no C, and no call cycle — a stack bound is what a machine without")
    strs_push(l, "an OS needs, and the hosted stack check reads a limit from an OS that is not there. The build reads")
    strs_push(l, "which runtime parts a program reaches (the same `Needs` every build computes) and refuses any beyond")
    strs_push(l, "the freestanding set by name, before anything is linked (`N0101`). `embedded` (§7.49, §7.62) is the")
    strs_push(l, "profile that states the same restrictions as rules; a freestanding build applies them as facts of")
    strs_push(l, "what can be built.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The freestanding runtime.** A failure is recorded in plain globals — there is one thread, and no")
    strs_push(l, "thread-local storage without an OS — and reported by writing its message to the board's UART and")
    strs_push(l, "stopping the machine with status 2. The platform entry is `_start`: it sets the stack pointer to the")
    strs_push(l, "top of a stack the linker reserves, calls `main`, writes its result to the UART in decimal and a")
    strs_push(l, "newline, and stops the machine with status 0. Stopping is ARM semihosting's `SYS_EXIT_EXTENDED`,")
    strs_push(l, "which QEMU honours with `-semihosting`; on a board without a debugger attached it would trap, which")
    strs_push(l, "is stated as the target's contract, not hidden. There are no hidden constructors: every global is a")
    strs_push(l, "constant the linker places, and the entry runs nothing before `main` but setting the stack.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**MMIO.** `mmio_read32(addr: Int) -> Int` and `mmio_write32(addr: Int, value: Int) -> Int` read and")
    strs_push(l, "write a 32-bit device register — a volatile access, never merged, removed or reordered with another")
    strs_push(l, "volatile access — and need an `MmioCap` held where they are written (as `TimeCap` and `VouchCap` are):")
    strs_push(l, "reaching a device is authority, and it performs no effect a Nazm function's contract names, so an")
    strs_push(l, "`embedded` program can use it. They are refused where there is no device: by `nazm run` and by any")
    strs_push(l, "hosted build (`N0392`). Ordinary loads and stores never become volatile; only these two are.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Linking.** The build writes objects (§7.59) and, beside `link.txt`, the linker script `link.ld`: the")
    strs_push(l, "image at `0x40080000` (where QEMU's `virt` loads a kernel), `_start` first, and a 64 KiB stack above")
    strs_push(l, "the image. The host has no ELF linker, so the image is linked by `ld.lld` in the QEMU image and run")
    strs_push(l, "there; the build itself never runs it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deferred, and why.** *Atomics*: one thread and no interrupts make them unobservable; their memory")
    strs_push(l, "orders need the model §7.46 does not yet state for shared memory. *Interrupt handlers*: an ABI, a")
    strs_push(l, "reentrancy rule and a stack requirement are designed here in outline — a handler is a function of no")
    strs_push(l, "parameters and no result, `! {}`, holding at most an `MmioCap`, run on its own stack — and not built.")
    strs_push(l, "*A heap*: a startup-only arena is the next policy; none is built, so a freestanding program allocates")
    strs_push(l, "nothing. *A standard library subset*: every `@std` module allocates, so none is available.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As built (N62), where it differs from the above.** *Recursion builds*: the board runtime carries")
    strs_push(l, "its own `nz.stack_check`, against the linker script's `__stack_bottom` with a quarter of the stack")
    strs_push(l, "in reserve, so a call cycle is checked rather than refused and exhaustion is `N0408` on the UART.")
    strs_push(l, "*The refusal reads symbols, not `Needs`*: `Needs` is coarse — `print` of a static string sets no")
    strs_push(l, "flag yet calls the C library's `write` — so the build refuses what the generated units name and")
    strs_push(l, "nothing defines, by runtime part, with exit status 4 (1 since Q1-C1) rather than `N0101`. *`_start` enables")
    strs_push(l, "floating point and SIMD* (`CPACR_EL1`), trapped at reset, since code generation may use them.")
    strs_push(l, "*Cranelift is refused for the board by name*: its object writer has no format for it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.65 Real-time bounds: what is bounded, what is measured, what is unknown — N63, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. \"Fast\" is not \"real-time\": a real-time claim is an upper bound that holds")
    strs_push(l, "on every run, and Nazm states one only where the compiler or the code generator establishes it. N63")
    strs_push(l, "targets an **analysable subset** — a program on the board (§7.64) whose loops, calls, allocation,")
    strs_push(l, "tasks, queues and blocking the compiler can bound — not hard-real-time certification of anything.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Three kinds of number, never mixed.** A *static bound* is established from the program or its")
    strs_push(l, "generated code and holds on every run of that build. A *measurement* is what one run observed; it is")
    strs_push(l, "evidence that a bound is not violated there, never a bound. An *unknown* is a quantity the compiler")
    strs_push(l, "does not establish, reported as `null` with the reason. Every report below names which each number is.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The `realtime` profile.** `embedded`'s rules (no `io`, no `spawn`, bounded allocation, no")
    strs_push(l, "recursion) and three more, each an existing fact or a new one read the same way:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- `no-blocking`: no channel send, receive or select — the operations whose latency depends on")
    strs_push(l, "  another task or the host scheduler (§7.56). Without tasks they either complete at once or wait")
    strs_push(l, "  forever; either way their latency is not the program's.")
    strs_push(l, "- `no-ambient-time`: as `critical` (§7.56) — a deadline makes behaviour depend on when it runs.")
    strs_push(l, "- `bounded-loops`: every `while` has a trip bound the compiler establishes, or the rule is")
    strs_push(l, "  `unknown` and refused. The bounded form, read off Core IR: a counter `i`, set by `let mut i = A`")
    strs_push(l, "  or `i = A` (`A` an `Int` literal) as the last write to `i` before the loop in its block; the")
    strs_push(l, "  condition `i < B`, `i <= B`, `i > B` or `i >= B` (`B` an `Int` literal, or an immutable local bound")
    strs_push(l, "  to one); and the body's one write to `i`, a top-level `i = i + C` (or `- C` for `>`, `>=`), `C` a")
    strs_push(l, "  positive literal, with no `continue` to the loop. The bound per entry to the loop is the exact")
    strs_push(l, "  trip count of that arithmetic, computed in 128 bits; a `break` or `return` only ends it sooner, and")
    strs_push(l, "  an overflow on the last step traps, which is failure, not another turn. Anything else — a")
    strs_push(l, "  condition on data, a counter written twice — is `unknown`, by loop, with its span.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The bounds report.** `nazm check --profile-report` gains `bounds` whenever a rule needing MIR or")
    strs_push(l, "Core IR facts is in force: each loop's bound or `null`; the longest chain of direct calls from")
    strs_push(l, "`main` (or `null` with a cycle or an indirect call); the allocation, task and queue *sites*, counted")
    strs_push(l, "statically (a count of sites, not of bytes or of executions); and `wcet: null` — no execution-time")
    strs_push(l, "bound is computed, and none is implied.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The stack bound (board only).** A board build (§7.64) writes `bounds.json` (`nazm.bounds/1`) beside")
    strs_push(l, "`link.ld`: the code generator's frame size for every function of the image — clang's own")
    strs_push(l, "prologue/epilogue figures (the remark pass `prologepilog` to LLVM 22, `prolog-epilog` from LLVM 23;")
    strs_push(l, "both are asked for), read at compile time, so the board build does not reuse cached objects — and")
    strs_push(l, "the deepest path through the image's call graph, read from the generated code from `nz_board_main`.")
    strs_push(l, "The sum along that path is a static upper bound on stack bytes for that build, stated with its path,")
    strs_push(l, "beside the 64 KiB the linker script reserves. A call cycle, a call through a value, or a function")
    strs_push(l, "without a reported frame makes it `null` with the reason. Interrupts do not exist (§7.64), so no")
    strs_push(l, "nesting is added.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Measured beside it.** `--stack-watermark` (board only) paints the stack in `_start` and, after")
    strs_push(l, "`main`, writes `nazm-stack: used=N` to the UART: the deepest byte the run touched. A test holds")
    strs_push(l, "measured ≤ bound on QEMU; that is evidence about the bound, and the bound is the claim.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Exhaustion is deterministic.** On the board a stack past the reserve fails with `N0408` and status")
    strs_push(l, "2 (§7.64); no allocation exists to exhaust. That is behaviour, not a bound.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here, and why.** *WCET*: no cycle model of any core is built, and an emulator's timing is not")
    strs_push(l, "one; `null`, always. *Scheduler latency and jitter*: the hosted scheduler's wake-up is measured in")
    strs_push(l, "`performance.md` as a distribution, never a bound, and `realtime` refuses tasks. *Byte bounds on the")
    strs_push(l, "heap*: the board has no heap; a hosted bound is N52's site counts. *Resource annotations*: none are")
    strs_push(l, "needed for the subset; none are added. Nothing here is a certification.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As built (N63), where it differs from the above.** *A function the generated text defines but the")
    strs_push(l, "code generator reports no frame for* was inlined into every caller and removed — at `-O2` most are —")
    strs_push(l, "so it adds nothing and the search continues through what it called, now called from its callers'")
    strs_push(l, "frames; only a callee outside the image makes the bound `null`. *Negated literals* count as")
    strs_push(l, "literals. *`embedded` reports `bounds` too*, since it computes the same MIR facts.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.66 WebAssembly: one more freestanding target, and authority as imports — N64, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. N64 adds `wasm32-unknown-unknown`: a WebAssembly module, compiled by the")
    strs_push(l, "LLVM backend from the same MIR and LIR as every other target. Nothing in the language changes for")
    strs_push(l, "it — no browser semantics, no source construct of its own.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The baseline.** WebAssembly 1.0 (MVP) with the features clang 21's `wasm32` default enables")
    strs_push(l, "(mutable globals, sign extension, multivalue off); `i64` is a WebAssembly `i64`, a pointer is 32")
    strs_push(l, "bits, memory is one linear memory the module defines and exports. The verified toolchain: the host's")
    strs_push(l, "clang for the objects, `wasm-ld` (LLD 19) to link, Node (V8) as the engine — all recorded in")
    strs_push(l, "`docker/wasm.Dockerfile`; another engine is unverified, not unsupported.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Semantics carried, not reinterpreted.** A WebAssembly module has no operating system, so it is a")
    strs_push(l, "freestanding target in §7.64's sense and shares its law: what the program reaches beyond the")
    strs_push(l, "module's runtime is refused by part, before anything is linked. Arithmetic is checked exactly as")
    strs_push(l, "on every target (overflow is LLVM's intrinsic and a branch, not WebAssembly's wrapping `i64.add`),")
    strs_push(l, "and a failure is recorded in plain globals — the module has one thread. Recursion builds under a")
    strs_push(l, "stack check against the linker's `__stack_low`, so exhaustion is `N0408`, not the engine's own")
    strs_push(l, "trap. Static strings are bytes in the module's data. Allocation, sequences, strings built at run")
    strs_push(l, "time, channels, tasks and closures are refused, as on the board: a heap is designed (a bump")
    strs_push(l, "allocator over `memory.grow`, freeing nothing until §7.41's release is ported) and not built.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Authority is an import.** A module imports from one module, `nazm_host`, and only what it uses:")
    strs_push(l, "`write(fd: i32, ptr: i32, len: i32)` exactly where the program writes to standard output or error")
    strs_push(l, "(which needs an `IoCap`, as everywhere), and `report(ptr: i32, len: i32)`, always — the entry")
    strs_push(l, "checks for a failure after `main`, so every module can report one. A program that holds no `IoCap` therefore has no `write` import at all — absent authority")
    strs_push(l, "is an absent import, which a test reads from the module itself. Files, arguments, the clock, the")
    strs_push(l, "network and randomness have no import: the built-ins that need them are refused for this target by")
    strs_push(l, "part, so the host is never asked. Every import is named in the module's import section, in a fixed")
    strs_push(l, "order, so the module's bytes say what it can ask of its host.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The host interface.** The module exports `memory` and `nazm_main() -> i64`: `main`'s result, or —")
    strs_push(l, "after calling `report` with the failure's text — `0`, with the host told by `report` that it")
    strs_push(l, "failed. A string crosses as a pointer into `memory` and a byte length; the host copies, never keeps.")
    strs_push(l, "`--objects DIR` writes the objects, `link.txt` (the `wasm-ld` line) and `host.mjs`, a reference host")
    strs_push(l, "for Node that provides exactly the imports the module declares and refuses to instantiate a module")
    strs_push(l, "asking for any other. It prints `main`'s result and a newline, and exits with status 0, or 2 after a")
    strs_push(l, "failure's text on standard error — the board's contract, carried.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**WebAssembly is not the boundary here.** The engine isolates memory and control; what the module")
    strs_push(l, "can do outside is what its host's imports do. The reference host's `write` writes to its own")
    strs_push(l, "process's streams; nothing else is provided. A different host is a different trust boundary, and the")
    strs_push(l, "module's import section is the contract it is checked against.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Identity and source mapping.** The module is a function of its objects and the link line, which")
    strs_push(l, "are a function of the source and the toolchain; two builds give the same bytes. `--debug` carries")
    strs_push(l, "DWARF in the objects' custom sections, which `wasm-ld` keeps, so a WebAssembly debugger maps code to")
    strs_push(l, "source as a native one does.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here, and why.** *WASI*: its interfaces are a host this milestone does not choose; the")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm_host` imports are the contract. *A heap*: designed above. *Exported Nazm functions*")
    strs_push(l, "(`pub extern \"C\"`, N55) over the module boundary: the same ABI applies to `i64`/`i32`, and they are")
    strs_push(l, "not yet exported — `nazm_main` alone is. *The browser*: no DOM, no event loop. *Cranelift*: its")
    strs_push(l, "WebAssembly support is as a source, not a target.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As built (N64), where it differs from the above.** *`__multi3`*: LLVM's checked `i64` multiply on")
    strs_push(l, "wasm32 calls compiler-rt's 128-bit multiply, and there is no compiler-rt; the runtime defines it from")
    strs_push(l, "64-bit pieces. *The stack bound* of §7.65 is stated for a module too, rooted at `nazm_main`; a host")
    strs_push(l, "import uses the host's stack, not the module's, and adds nothing. *The freestanding refusal names")
    strs_push(l, "each part's symbols*, on the board as here.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.67 The interactive tier: a REPL, comptime and reload checks — and a JIT, blocked — N65, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code is committed. Native AOT stays the foundation (Goals G02): nothing here")
    strs_push(l, "changes what `nazm build` produces or what a program means. The interactive tier is the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter and the checker — the settled Core IR every build starts from, never a second meaning.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The JIT is BLOCKED, by a law of this repository.** An in-process JIT writes machine code to memory")
    strs_push(l, "and calls it: that is `unsafe` Rust, and the workspace forbids `unsafe` code (`unsafe_code =")
    strs_push(l, "\"forbid\"`, `Cargo.toml`). Lifting the law for one audited crate is a decision about the project's")
    strs_push(l, "safety rules, not a milestone's implementation detail, and it is not made here. Designed for when it")
    strs_push(l, "is: Cranelift (already the second backend) compiles MIR to code in memory through `cranelift-jit`;")
    strs_push(l, "the runtime's LLVM text is compiled once by clang into a shared library keyed by the runtime's")
    strs_push(l, "digest and loaded beside it; the entry's call to `main` goes through a pointer the JIT sets; the")
    strs_push(l, "JIT's cache key is the object key Cranelift already uses (MIR, settings, triple, runtime digest), so")
    strs_push(l, "no code survives a semantic, runtime or version change. Until then the fast interactive tier is the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter, whose agreement with native code the existing differential suites hold.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The REPL.** `nazm repl` reads definitions and expressions a line at a time. The session is one")
    strs_push(l, "program — its definitions in the order first given — checked whole on every edit, so a definition's")
    strs_push(l, "identity is its name in the session's module (§7.10) and a redefinition is checked against every")
    strs_push(l, "definition that uses it. One that breaks another is refused by the other's name and leaves the")
    strs_push(l, "session as it was: no definition is ever checked against a predecessor that has gone. An expression")
    strs_push(l, "is the body of a `main` holding an `IoCap`, evaluated by the interpreter as an `Int`, a `Bool` or a")
    strs_push(l, "`Str`; `main` itself is the REPL's. Nothing is cached between lines, so nothing can be stale.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Comptime.** `nazm comptime FILE FUNCTION` evaluates a function of no parameters that is pure —")
    strs_push(l, "declared `! {}` or inferred so — under the interpreter's iteration and depth budgets. That is the")
    strs_push(l, "whole of its isolation — not an operating-system sandbox — and it is the language's own: authority is a value (§7.39), so a function of no")
    strs_push(l, "parameters holds none, and a pure one cannot exercise its caller's through the ambient bridge, so")
    strs_push(l, "files, the clock, the network, tasks and C are unreachable without any check of their own. Anything")
    strs_push(l, "else is refused, by name, with `N0393`; a runaway evaluation stops at its budget with `N0402`.")
    strs_push(l, "In-language comptime (a constant evaluated during checking) is designed on this rule and not built.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Reload checks.** `nazm reload-check OLD NEW` compares two versions of a program's root module, per")
    strs_push(l, "definition: a function whose body changed and whose signature — parameter and result types, and")
    strs_push(l, "effects — did not is `reloadable`, as is anything added; a changed signature, a removed function, or")
    strs_push(l, "a record or enum whose layout changed (its fields by name and type; order is not layout, §7.9) needs")
    strs_push(l, "a `restart`, named with what changed. One `nazm.reload-check/1` line, with the runtime ABI revision;")
    strs_push(l, "a non-zero exit when anything needs a restart. Nothing is reloaded: the check is the rule a hot")
    strs_push(l, "reloader would be held to, stated and tested before any reloader exists.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.68 Vectorisation under checked arithmetic — N66, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Nazm's `Int` arithmetic is checked: every `+` is LLVM's overflow")
    strs_push(l, "intrinsic and a branch (§7.43), so a loop over a sequence carries a failure edge per element, and no")
    strs_push(l, "code generator vectorises it. N66 makes one idiom vectorise without changing what any program means,")
    strs_push(l, "and says for every other loop why it did not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**No vector types in the language.** A source-level vector would be a new kind of value with its own")
    strs_push(l, "overflow, bounds and layout rules, and nothing needs one yet. The semantic addition is one built-in,")
    strs_push(l, "`ints_sum_from(start: Int, v: Ints) -> Int`: `start` plus every element of `v`, left to right, failing")
    strs_push(l, "with `N0400` exactly when one of those running sums would overflow — what the loop computing it")
    strs_push(l, "means, as a function. It is also the manual escape: a program may call it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Legality, exactly.** A vectorised sum reorders additions, and a reordered checked sum can succeed")
    strs_push(l, "where the ordered one fails (`[MAX, 1, -1]`). The runtime keeps the ordered meaning by bounding, not")
    strs_push(l, "reordering, the checks: a block of 64 elements whose magnitudes are all at most 2^56, added to a")
    strs_push(l, "running sum whose magnitude is below 2^62, has every partial sum inside `Int` — 64 · 2^56 = 2^62 —")
    strs_push(l, "so the block's total is exactly what the 64 checked additions give, and it is added without checks,")
    strs_push(l, "in a loop the code generator vectorises. Any other block is added one checked element at a time,")
    strs_push(l, "and the first overflow is the failure. A tail shorter than a block is checked. Bounds need no check:")
    strs_push(l, "the sum reads `0..len`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Automatic, for one idiom, in native builds.** The counted loop `while i < ints_len(v) { s = s +")
    strs_push(l, "ints_get(v, i); i = i + 1; }`, with `i` started at `0` in the loop's block and nothing else in the")
    strs_push(l, "body, is replaced in Core IR before MIR by `s = ints_sum_from(s, v); i = ints_len(v);`, the call at the")
    strs_push(l, "addition's span — so an overflow is the same diagnostic at the same place, and the loop's bounds")
    strs_push(l, "checks could never fail. The interpreter keeps the loop, so its iteration budget still counts each")
    strs_push(l, "turn. Every other loop is left alone, and `nazm explain-cost` names the reason for each.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Targets and identity.** The vectorised code is what clang produces for each target's baseline —")
    strs_push(l, "NEON on `aarch64`, SSE2 on `x86_64` — at `--opt-level 2` or above; nothing asks for a host's own CPU")
    strs_push(l, "features, so no object depends on the machine that built it, and the object key's triple and")
    strs_push(l, "optimisation level already separate what differs. At `-O0` the same code runs unvectorised, with")
    strs_push(l, "the same results. Choosing wider features (AVX2, SVE) per build is designed — a target feature list")
    strs_push(l, "in the object key and in `link.txt` — and not built.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here, and why.** Element-wise maps (`out[i] = a[i] + b[i]`) need the store's failure to stop the")
    strs_push(l, "stores after it, which the same block bound gives, but the idiom's recogniser is not written. Floating")
    strs_push(l, "point does not exist. GPU offload is N67.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.69 Accelerators: kernels, transfers and one GPU — N67, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. No ordinary Nazm function becomes GPU code by itself. A **kernel** is a")
    strs_push(l, "function that meets a stated eligibility, run over a sequence by an explicit command, with every")
    strs_push(l, "movement of data and every synchronisation named in its report.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Eligibility, statically.** A kernel is pure, maps one `Int` to an `Int`, and reaches only")
    strs_push(l, "functions that are themselves pure functions of `Int`s and `Bool`s, without recursion (a work item")
    strs_push(l, "has no stack to recurse on), built-ins (none has a device form), records, enums, closures, tasks or")
    strs_push(l, "C. Anything else is refused before a device is touched, by name and with the span that makes it")
    strs_push(l, "ineligible (`N0394`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Meaning, carried.** Arithmetic is checked on the device exactly as on the host: addition and")
    strs_push(l, "subtraction by the sign rule on wrapping two's-complement results, multiplication by comparing the")
    strs_push(l, "high word with the low word's sign, division and remainder by zero and `i64::MIN / -1`, and")
    strs_push(l, "`i64::MIN % -1` is 0 (the spec's, where C's is undefined). A map is a function of each element alone,")
    strs_push(l, "so its sequential meaning — results in order, or the first element's failure — is recovered from a")
    strs_push(l, "parallel run by recording each failure as `index · 256 + site` with `atomic_min`: the lowest index")
    strs_push(l, "wins, and its site names the operation. Sites and indices are bounded by that one 32-bit word,")
    strs_push(l, "which caps a launch at 8,000,000 elements.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Memory and transfers.** The input is copied host to device once, the results device to host")
    strs_push(l, "once, and a failure word each way; the device never sees host memory, and nothing persists between")
    strs_push(l, "runs. One synchronisation — every work item finished — precedes every read. The report states the")
    strs_push(l, "bytes and the time of each transfer, the kernel's build, and the run.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The first backend: OpenCL on Apple's GPU.** The tooling that exists here is macOS's OpenCL 1.2")
    strs_push(l, "on the M1 Pro's GPU; the kernel is OpenCL C, generated from Core IR. OpenCL is deprecated on macOS")
    strs_push(l, "and absent elsewhere, so this backend is a first, scoped one: SPIR-V (Vulkan) and Metal are its")
    strs_push(l, "portable and native successors, designed, not built. The host side is a C program compiled against")
    strs_push(l, "the system framework and run as a process: the compiler links no GPU API and keeps its `unsafe_code")
    strs_push(l, "= \"forbid\"` law.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Identity.** A kernel's identity is its OpenCL C source, the device's name and driver version, and")
    strs_push(l, "the host program — hashed together (`nazm.kernel/1`); the driver compiles the source on every run,")
    strs_push(l, "and the identity is what a cache of its binaries would be keyed on.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The reference, and no silent fallback.** The command holds the device's results to the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter's, element by element, or the same failure at the same index, and says which. A host")
    strs_push(l, "without the device refuses; nothing runs elsewhere instead.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here, and why.** *Layout specialisation* (coalescing, structure-of-arrays) needs a value")
    strs_push(l, "richer than `Int`; *kernels in the language* (a `kernel` modifier, launched from Nazm) need a device")
    strs_push(l, "handle as a capability, designed on `MmioCap`'s pattern and not built; *occupancy* is not reported by")
    strs_push(l, "the API version here.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.70 Layout: a `Vec` of records, one array per field — N68, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code is committed (the code was prototyped first, for N66's lesson that a")
    strs_push(l, "measurement must precede a claim; this text, and the register's prior art, precede the commit).")
    strs_push(l, "A layout choice is sound only where no program can observe it. In Nazm a `Vec` element has no")
    strs_push(l, "address, cannot cross the FFI (`Int` and `Bool` only, N55), is never serialised, and a record's")
    strs_push(l, "layout is already by field name (§7.9) — so for an element that owns nothing, the layout of a")
    strs_push(l, "`Vec`'s storage is unobservable by construction.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Eligibility.** A `Vec[R]` where `R` is a record with at least one field and every field an `Int`")
    strs_push(l, "or a `Bool`. An element that owns storage (a `Str`, a sequence, a `Vec`, a closure) is excluded,")
    strs_push(l, "not because it is observable but because its release walks elements, and splitting that walk is")
    strs_push(l, "not done here; an enum or a non-record element is excluded likewise. Each excluded type says why.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The layout.** `--layout soa` stores an eligible `Vec[R]` as one 8-byte array per field in one")
    strs_push(l, "allocation, field `k` of element `i` at `data + (k · cap + i) · 8`; `nz.soa_grow` relays the arrays")
    strs_push(l, "out when the vector grows. Get gathers, set scatters, push and pop do both; bounds and failures are")
    strs_push(l, "exactly the element-by-element layout's, checked before any field is touched. The header — `len`,")
    strs_push(l, "`cap`, `data`, the count — is unchanged, so every sequence operation that does not touch elements")
    strs_push(l, "(length, release, sharing) is the same code.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Choice and identity.** Opt-in, by name, LLVM backend only (Cranelift refuses it), and applied to")
    strs_push(l, "every eligible type: the access pattern decides whether it wins, and the compiler has no cost model")
    strs_push(l, "for that yet, so it does not choose. The layout changes the emitted text of every unit that touches")
    strs_push(l, "such a `Vec`, and an object is keyed by its text, so the layout is in every affected object's")
    strs_push(l, "identity and in the emitter's; it is not in the semantic identity, because no program's meaning")
    strs_push(l, "changes. `nazm explain-cost` reports, per `Vec` type, whether `--layout soa` lays it out field by")
    strs_push(l, "field or why not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here, and why.** Automatic selection (a cost model over access patterns); elements that own")
    strs_push(l, "storage; enums; hybrid (AoSoA) blocking; layouts for a single record value, which LLVM already")
    strs_push(l, "scalarises.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.71 Contracts: a chain-neutral model over ordinary Nazm — N69, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. A smart contract is an ordinary Nazm module held to a profile and run by a")
    strs_push(l, "simulator that owns its persistent state. No Web3 dialect: the same pure function means the same")
    strs_push(l, "under every profile, and nothing below is syntax.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The `web3` profile.** `declared-effects`, `no-io`, `no-spawn`, `no-foreign`, `no-ambient-time`,")
    strs_push(l, "`no-blocking` and `no-recursion` (§7.49, §7.62, §7.65): no ambient authority, no clock, no tasks or")
    strs_push(l, "channels, no C, every contract declared, and a call graph whose depth the compiler can state.")
    strs_push(l, "Arithmetic is already deterministic and checked everywhere; nothing changes for it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A contract.** A module with a record `State` whose fields are `Int`s and `Bool`s, a `fn init() ->")
    strs_push(l, "State`, and entrypoints: every `pub fn` of the form `fn name(s: State, caller: Int, a: Int, …) ->")
    strs_push(l, "Result[State, Int]`, pure (`! {}`). Persistent state is therefore not a global: it is the first")
    strs_push(l, "argument and the `Ok` result, and an entrypoint's authority over it is exactly what its body does with")
    strs_push(l, "`s`. `caller` is the signer, handed by the host. `Err(code)` reverts with `code`; a runtime failure")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0400`, `N0401`, `N0405`) reverts with its diagnostic code; a revert leaves the state as it was. An")
    strs_push(l, "optional `fn conserved(s: State) -> Int` names the quantity every successful transaction must leave")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged — the contract's asset.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Machine-readable facts.** `nazm contract FILE --interface` writes `nazm.contract/1`: the state's")
    strs_push(l, "fields, each entrypoint's arguments, and its **read and write sets** — a field it projects from `s`")
    strs_push(l, "is read; a field of an `Ok(State(…))` it builds other than as `s.field` itself is written; anything it")
    strs_push(l, "cannot see through (a helper given `s`, a state built elsewhere) makes the whole state \"may read\" and")
    strs_push(l, "\"may write\", never omitted. External calls do not exist in this model: an entrypoint calls only Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "functions, so there is no reentrancy to analyse, and that is stated rather than claimed as safety.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The simulator.** `nazm contract FILE --txs FILE` runs transactions in order — `CALLER ENTRY ARGS…`")
    strs_push(l, "per line — on the interpreter, threading the state, each from the state the last successful one left.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.contract-run/1` reports, per transaction: the outcome (`ok`, `revert` with the code, or `fail`")
    strs_push(l, "with the diagnostic code), the **dynamic meter** (the interpreter's steps, a count, not gas), the")
    strs_push(l, "fields it changed, and — where `conserved` exists — whether the conserved quantity held. The run is a")
    strs_push(l, "pure function of the module and the transactions: two runs give the same bytes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Assets, designed and checked dynamically.** A linear asset kind — a value that cannot be copied,")
    strs_push(l, "only moved, and cannot be dropped except by an explicit destruction — is a type-system change this")
    strs_push(l, "milestone does not make. In the implemented scope an asset is the declared conserved quantity, and the")
    strs_push(l, "simulator refuses every transaction that changes it (`N0395`); duplication or silent loss of an asset")
    strs_push(l, "is a conservation failure, found at the first transaction that commits it. Static linearity is")
    strs_push(l, "designed: a built-in `Asset[T]` with move-only semantics, its own drop rule, and the checker's existing")
    strs_push(l, "ownership facts (§7.41) — RESEARCH until a backend needs it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here, and why.** Chain host calls (storage, events, crypto) belong to each backend's adapter")
    strs_push(l, "(N70–N72); metering in gas is the EVM's (N70); signer and account constraints beyond `caller` are")
    strs_push(l, "N72's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.72 The EVM backend: the contract model as bytecode — N70, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. The contract model (§7.71) compiled to EVM bytecode, run in a local EVM,")
    strs_push(l, "and held to the simulator. Nothing of the EVM reaches the language: words, selectors, storage slots")
    strs_push(l, "and gas are the backend's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Route: direct, from Core IR.** No Yul and no `solc`: neither is in this toolchain, and a contract's")
    strs_push(l, "body is the small, already-checked Core IR of §7.71 — `Int`/`Bool` arithmetic, `if`, `let`,")
    strs_push(l, "`while`, calls to pure helpers (which `web3` makes acyclic, so the backend inlines them), and the")
    strs_push(l, "entrypoint's `Result[State, Int]`. The backend emits opcodes with labels and resolves them. What it")
    strs_push(l, "does not support — the state used other than through `s.field` and as the returned `Ok(value: s)`")
    strs_push(l, "or `Ok(value: State(…))`, a record or enum other than those, any built-in — is refused before")
    strs_push(l, "emission, by name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Integers.** An `Int` is a 256-bit word holding a sign-extended `i64`. Every arithmetic result is")
    strs_push(l, "held to `i64` exactly as the language holds it: addition, subtraction, multiplication and negation")
    strs_push(l, "are exact in 256 bits for `i64` operands, then checked with `SIGNEXTEND(7, r) == r`; division and")
    strs_push(l, "remainder are `SDIV`/`SMOD` — truncating, the remainder taking the dividend's sign, as `docs/user/spec.md`")
    strs_push(l, "says — after the zero and `i64::MIN / -1` checks. A failure reverts with the five bytes of its")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostic code (`N0400`); an `Err(code)` reverts with the 32-byte word `code`; the two are told apart")
    strs_push(l, "by length. Every revert discards the transaction's writes: the EVM's own rule, and the simulator's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The ABI.** Each entrypoint is a function `name(int64,…)` — its arguments after `caller`, which is the")
    strs_push(l, "EVM's `CALLER`, not an argument anyone can choose. The selector is the first four bytes of")
    strs_push(l, "`keccak256` of that signature, computed by the compiler (its own keccak, tested on known vectors). An")
    strs_push(l, "argument whose 32-byte word is not a sign-extended `i64` reverts before the body runs.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Storage.** Field `f` of `State` lives at slot `keccak256(\"nazm.state.\" + f)`: by name, so reordering")
    strs_push(l, "fields moves nothing (§7.9's rule, kept), and adding one never moves another. `storage.json`")
    strs_push(l, "(`nazm.evm-storage/1`) records each field's name, type and slot; `nazm contract --upgrade-check OLD NEW`")
    strs_push(l, "refuses a change that would misread live storage — a field removed, or its type changed — and allows")
    strs_push(l, "one that adds a field. `init()`'s state is written by the deployment's constructor.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gas.** For an entrypoint without a loop, the backend states a static upper bound on its execution")
    strs_push(l, "gas — the costliest path's opcodes, a cold `SLOAD` per field read, the worst `SSTORE` per field written,")
    strs_push(l, "and its memory — beside the intrinsic cost; a loop makes it `null`. The EVM's measured gas is reported")
    strs_push(l, "beside it, and a test holds measured ≤ bound.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Held to the simulator.** A test harness (`docker/evm.Dockerfile`, py-evm) deploys the bytecode, runs the")
    strs_push(l, "same transactions from the same senders, and the test compares each outcome, revert code and the final")
    strs_push(l, "storage with `nazm contract --txs`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** Events, value transfer and external calls do not exist in the model (§7.71); an")
    strs_push(l, "optimiser; Yul output for audit.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.73 Contracts on WebAssembly: the ordinary backend and a host adapter — N71, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. A contract (§7.71) compiled by the ordinary WebAssembly backend (§7.66), with")
    strs_push(l, "nothing chain-specific in the compiler but one generated adapter: the contract's own unit, its code")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged, gains exported entry functions that move the state across typed host imports.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The adapter.** For each entrypoint `name`, an export `nazm_call_name(caller: i64, a: i64, …) -> i64`")
    strs_push(l, "that reads every state field with `nazm_host.state_get(index) -> i64`, builds the `State`, calls the")
    strs_push(l, "entrypoint, and on `Ok` — after comparing `conserved` before and after, where declared — writes every")
    strs_push(l, "field back with `nazm_host.state_set(index, value)` and returns `0`; on `Err(code)` it calls")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm_host.revert(code)` and returns `1`; a conservation change returns `2` with nothing written; a")
    strs_push(l, "runtime failure is the module's ordinary `report` (§7.66) and returns `3`. `nazm_init()` writes")
    strs_push(l, "`init()`'s state. A field's `index` is its declaration index, and its value an `i64` (`Bool` as 0 or 1):")
    strs_push(l, "the serialisation is the state's declared shape, deterministic and versioned in the metadata.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The host.** The module imports exactly `nazm_host.state_get`, `state_set`, `revert` and `report` —")
    strs_push(l, "read from its import section, and nothing else is granted. The reference host (`contract_host.mjs`)")
    strs_push(l, "keeps the state, instantiates the module afresh for each transaction (a failure leaves nothing behind),")
    strs_push(l, "and applies the result only on `0`. Its run is compared with the simulator's: the same outcomes, codes")
    strs_push(l, "and final state.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Shared, not forked.** The adapter is text appended to a unit the ordinary backend emits; the backend")
    strs_push(l, "itself is unchanged, and the same contract built for the ordinary `wasm32-unknown-unknown` target without")
    strs_push(l, "the adapter is the same unit without it — which a test holds.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** A chain's own host interface (storage keys, events, crypto) is a binding of these four")
    strs_push(l, "imports to it; none is bound.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.74 Account-oriented contracts: signer constraints and metadata; execution blocked — N72, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code is committed. An account-oriented chain hands a program its accounts —")
    strs_push(l, "state it may read, state it may write, keys that signed — and refuses a transaction whose accounts do")
    strs_push(l, "not meet the program's declared constraints. The chain-neutral model (§7.71) already knows most of")
    strs_push(l, "what those constraints must be; this milestone states them and checks the one the model can decide.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Signed writes, statically.** The `accounts` profile is `web3` with one more rule, `signed-writes`:")
    strs_push(l, "an entrypoint whose write set is not empty must decide on its `caller` — `caller` must appear in a")
    strs_push(l, "condition of its own body — or it is refused (`N0510`), naming the entrypoint. A helper handed")
    strs_push(l, "`caller` is not looked into, so a check made only there does not count: the rule refuses rather than")
    strs_push(l, "trusts what it cannot see. A read-only entrypoint needs no signer. This is a missing-signer check in the")
    strs_push(l, "target-neutral model; it is not proof that the decision is the right one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Account metadata.** `nazm contract FILE --accounts DIR` writes `accounts.json`")
    strs_push(l, "(`nazm.sbpf-accounts/1`): the state account, owned by the program, its data laid out as a version byte")
    strs_push(l, "and then each field's 8 bytes by declaration index; and for each instruction its discriminator (the first")
    strs_push(l, "8 bytes of `keccak256(\"nazm.instruction.\" + name)`), its arguments' offsets, and its accounts — the state,")
    strs_push(l, "writable exactly when its write set is not empty, and the caller, a signer exactly when the")
    strs_push(l, "entrypoint decides on it. Cross-program calls do not exist in the model and are reported as none.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Execution is BLOCKED.** There is no sBPF toolchain, validator or emulator on this host. Upstream LLVM's")
    strs_push(l, "`bpfel` target exists, but Solana's sBPF differs from it in its program ABI, syscalls and verifier, so an")
    strs_push(l, "upstream eBPF object would not be evidence of an sBPF program. The backend — the account input")
    strs_push(l, "deserialised into the `State`, the entrypoint called, the data written back, the verifier's constraints —")
    strs_push(l, "is designed by this metadata and not built.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.75 Trust evidence: fuzzing, provenance and reproducibility — N73, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Evidence that a build is what it says, and that the compiler survives")
    strs_push(l, "inputs nobody wrote by hand — never a proof, and labelled as what it is.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Two fuzzers, deterministic.** *Front-end robustness*: every source in the repository's corpora,")
    strs_push(l, "mutated by a seeded generator (bytes deleted, duplicated, swapped, replaced with tokens of the")
    strs_push(l, "language), is parsed and checked in process; the property is that nothing panics — a diagnostic is")
    strs_push(l, "the right answer to any input. *Semantic differential*: a generator of well-typed programs (`Int` and")
    strs_push(l, "`Bool` arithmetic and comparison, `let`, `if`, bounded `while`, calls between generated functions,")
    strs_push(l, "records) — every one terminating by construction — run under the interpreter, the LLVM backend at")
    strs_push(l, "`-O0` and `-O2` and Cranelift; the property is one answer (value, or failure code and place). Both are")
    strs_push(l, "seeded: a seed names a run, and the same seed is the same inputs on every host. A failing input is")
    strs_push(l, "shrunk — statements and subexpressions removed while it still fails — and the shrunk input is printed to")
    strs_push(l, "be added to the regression corpus, which every run replays first. Resource bounds are the test")
    strs_push(l, "harness's and, contained, the gate's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Shown to find a fault.** A backend fault injected on purpose — a signed comparison emitted unsigned —")
    strs_push(l, "is found by the differential fuzzer without any test written for it; it is catalogued as a mutant whose")
    strs_push(l, "only killer is the fuzzer.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Provenance.** `nazm build --provenance FILE` writes `nazm.provenance/1`: every source module with its")
    strs_push(l, "digest, every package with its version and digest, the target, the compiler's version, the C")
    strs_push(l, "compiler's identity, the runtime's ABI revision and digest, the backend and its options, the profiles in")
    strs_push(l, "force, and the output's digest. `--attest-with CMD` runs CMD with the provenance file's path and records")
    strs_push(l, "its standard output as the attestation — a hook for any local signer; nothing online is needed or used.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Reproducibility, scoped.** Two builds of one program in two clean directories with one toolchain are")
    strs_push(l, "the same bytes (N46). Across toolchains — Apple clang 21 on macOS and clang 19 in the Linux image, for")
    strs_push(l, "the same target triple — objects are expected to differ, and are measured and classified rather than")
    strs_push(l, "assumed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**An evidence bundle and the compiler's own bill of materials** (amended before their code, the same")
    strs_push(l, "day). `cargo xtask evidence DIR` adds two files to a directory of evidence — provenance records, gate")
    strs_push(l, "logs, mutation journals, measurements, artefacts. `sbom.json` (`nazm.sbom/1`): every crate the compiler")
    strs_push(l, "is built from, read from `Cargo.lock` — name, version, source and checksum — and the toolchain pin;")
    strs_push(l, "offline, so a crate the lockfile does not name is not in it. `index.json` (`nazm.evidence/1`): every")
    strs_push(l, "other file of DIR by relative path, with its size, BLAKE3 digest and a kind read from its name")
    strs_push(l, "(`provenance`, `sbom`, `tests`, `mutation`, `measurement`, `artefact`), sorted, with no time in it.")
    strs_push(l, "`cargo xtask evidence --verify DIR` recomputes each and refuses a changed, missing or unlisted file by")
    strs_push(l, "name. Who vouches for a bundle is an attestation over `index.json` (the `--attest-with` hook's")
    strs_push(l, "convention), never a field a bundle writes about itself.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here, and why.** Sanitizers over generated code, Miri and Loom: the compiler has no `unsafe`")
    strs_push(l, "code (`unsafe_code = \"forbid\"`), so Miri's subject is absent; sanitizing the C-compiled runtime is a")
    strs_push(l, "separate experiment, not run. Coverage-guided fuzzing (`cargo fuzz`) needs a nightly toolchain and a")
    strs_push(l, "new dependency; the seeded generators stand in for it, and are said to.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.76 Ecosystem tooling: init, API docs, C headers, an editor client — N74, 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Tooling over what the compiler already knows; no language rule moves, so the")
    strs_push(l, "semantic epoch, the interface schema and the runtime ABI stay.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**`nazm init DIR --template T`** writes a project a fresh user can run at once: `nazm.toml`, `src/`")
    strs_push(l, "and a `tests/` corpus `nazm test` replays. Six templates, each built only from what the toolchain")
    strs_push(l, "supports and each checked by the template's own commands in the tests: `cli` (a program with")
    strs_push(l, "`IoCap`), `library` (a package with no `main`, `pub` functions), `server` (a worker pool over")
    strs_push(l, "channels serving the requests in a file named on its command line — Nazm has neither sockets nor a")
    strs_push(l, "way to read standard input, and the template says so),")
    strs_push(l, "`embedded` (`aarch64-unknown-none`, `MmioCap`, built to objects), `wasm`")
    strs_push(l, "(`wasm32-unknown-unknown`, built to objects) and `contract` (the `web3` profile, run by")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm contract --txs`). An existing non-empty directory is refused; nothing is overwritten.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**`nazm doc FILE|DIR [-o OUT]`** documents a program's public API from its semantic definitions,")
    strs_push(l, "not from its text: each module's exported functions, records and enums, with the checker's declared")
    strs_push(l, "and required effects, the capabilities a function takes, its foreign symbol or C export, the")
    strs_push(l, "package's profiles, and a link back to the source — the path relative to the package and the line.")
    strs_push(l, "The only text read is the signature as written and the comment lines directly above a definition,")
    strs_push(l, "shown as its description (a convention of the tool; the language has no doc comments). One")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.api-doc/1` JSON document, and with `-o` that and `api.md`, whose anchors are the definitions'")
    strs_push(l, "identities, so a link survives a rebuild and moves only when the definition does.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**`nazm bindgen HEADER`** turns the supported subset of a C header into `extern \"C\"` declarations: a")
    strs_push(l, "prototype whose parameters are `int64_t` or `bool` (or `const char *`, as N55's borrowed `Str`) and")
    strs_push(l, "whose result is `int64_t` or `bool`. Anything else — `int`, `long`, `void`, a pointer to anything")
    strs_push(l, "else, a struct, a variadic, a function pointer, a macro — is refused by name with the reason, never")
    strs_push(l, "widened or guessed; the output names every prototype as translated or refused")
    strs_push(l, "(`nazm.bindgen/1`), and the declarations it writes are checked by the checker before they are")
    strs_push(l, "printed. Wrappers, not emulation: nothing of C's semantics is reproduced in Nazm.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**`nazm publish --dry-run`** resolves, checks and digests exactly as a publish would, and writes")
    strs_push(l, "nothing to the registry.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A library is checked as modules** (amended before its code: the `library` template found that a")
    strs_push(l, "package with no `main` could be tested and locked but not checked). `nazm check DIR` on such a package")
    strs_push(l, "checks every module of its source root as a module — the root need not have `main`, everything it")
    strs_push(l, "imports is checked with it — and reports each diagnostic once. `run` and `build` still refuse it")
    strs_push(l, "with `N0509`: there is nothing to run.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**An editor client, standard protocols only.** `editors/vscode` is a client for `nazm lsp` (the")
    strs_push(l, "Language Server Protocol) and a launch configuration for N58's debugger through an existing LLDB")
    strs_push(l, "debug adapter; all language logic stays in the compiler's service. The language service is already")
    strs_push(l, "package-aware — definition, references, hover and workspace symbols reach a dependency's sources, and")
    strs_push(l, "renaming a dependency's public function is refused (`Exported`: its other importers are programs no")
    strs_push(l, "open document loads) — and is tested so.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here, and why.** A registry over the network, `nazm update` (versions are exact and the lock")
    strs_push(l, "is rewritten by `nazm lock`), translating C semantics or another language into Nazm, rename across a")
    strs_push(l, "package boundary, and the agent benchmark: no claim of improved agent efficiency is made, so it is")
    strs_push(l, "not re-run.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.77 Syntax completion: incremental reparse, finer recovery, `\\u{…}` — N76, 2026-10-03")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Area 1 stayed PARTIAL for four named gaps: whole-file parsing only, recovery")
    strs_push(l, "coarser than a statement outside blocks, no editor path that edits a parse, and an undecided Unicode")
    strs_push(l, "escape. This section settles each one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**One owner.** `nazm-syntax` owns lexing and parsing, and stays the only place either happens.")
    strs_push(l, "Incremental reparse is not a second parser. It is the same lexer and the same parser, restarted at a")
    strs_push(l, "boundary where their state is provably the same as it was in the previous revision. Everything the")
    strs_push(l, "reparse does not touch is copied from the previous revision and moved by the edit's length delta.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The revision model.** A `Revision` is the result of parsing one file's text. It holds the text,")
    strs_push(l, "the lossless lexemes, the abstract items, the concrete tree, the diagnostics, and a *chunk table*:")
    strs_push(l, "one row per top-level item, recording the bytes and tokens the item owns, how far its parse looked")
    strs_push(l, "ahead, the parser's cascade state on entering it, and the diagnostics it raised. `Revision::edit`")
    strs_push(l, "takes a `TextEdit` (a byte range of the old text and its replacement) and returns the next")
    strs_push(l, "revision. The contract, which is the falsifier: **for every text and every edit, `edit` returns a")
    strs_push(l, "revision equal to `Revision::new` of the edited text.** That means the same lexemes, the same")
    strs_push(l, "concrete tree (kinds, bytes and spans of every node and leaf), the same abstract tree (spans")
    strs_push(l, "included), and the same diagnostics in the same order. Nothing is \"close enough\". A sequence of")
    strs_push(l, "edits converges because each step does.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Where the parse may restart.** The lexer is context-free from any lexeme boundary, and it reads at")
    strs_push(l, "most one byte past a lexeme's end. So relexing begins at the first lexeme of the first affected")
    strs_push(l, "chunk. It ends at the first boundary at or past the edit's end that is also a boundary of the old")
    strs_push(l, "scan, shifted. From that point the old lexemes are exactly what a fresh scan would produce. The")
    strs_push(l, "parser's only state across top-level items is the cascade mute (§7.17), and an item keyword resets")
    strs_push(l, "it. Its only forward reach past an item is the delimiter-balance scan (§7.17), which is recorded per")
    strs_push(l, "chunk as the furthest token the chunk examined. So a chunk is reused if and only if:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- every token it examined lies wholly before the first changed token, or wholly after the relexed")
    strs_push(l, "  region;")
    strs_push(l, "- and it starts at the same token, shifted, with the same entry mute state.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Every other chunk is reparsed. The reparse stops at the first old chunk boundary past the edit")
    strs_push(l, "that it lands on exactly. If the edit unbalances a delimiter so that no later boundary matches, the")
    strs_push(l, "reparse runs to the end of the file. That is correct, and only slower.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Green-node reuse.** A reused chunk's root-level green children are the previous tree's, by")
    strs_push(l, "reference. The new root is assembled from them and from the reparsed region's children. The token")
    strs_push(l, "text resolver becomes an append-only table that the next revision clones and extends, so an old")
    strs_push(l, "leaf's key still resolves.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a reuse may not do.** Reuse a chunk whose lookahead crossed the edit. Reuse after a lexing")
    strs_push(l, "boundary mismatch. Carry a span unshifted. Reuse a completion-probe parse: a hole parse (§7.28) is")
    strs_push(l, "always full. Fall back silently: every revision reports `ParseStats` (lexemes relexed, tokens")
    strs_push(l, "reparsed, chunks reused and reparsed, and whether the revision was full), so a test can see which")
    strs_push(l, "path ran.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Recovery, finer.** Inside a declaration, a malformed member no longer costs the item:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- a record field or enum variant (or payload field) recovers at its `,` or at the list's closing")
    strs_push(l, "  delimiter;")
    strs_push(l, "- a parameter recovers at its `,` or at `)`;")
    strs_push(l, "- a call's argument, a construction's field initialiser or a `match` arm recovers at its `,` or at")
    strs_push(l, "  its closing delimiter.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The malformed member is an `Error` node in the concrete tree. Its siblings stay typed nodes, and a")
    strs_push(l, "later independent mistake in the same item is its own diagnostic. A broken `use` recovers at its")
    strs_push(l, "`;`. Item recovery now also stops at `use`, so one bad import no longer swallows the next.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The abstract tree's contract is unchanged, deliberately.** An item whose header or member list")
    strs_push(l, "needed recovery is absent from the abstract tree. A function whose body needed recovery keeps its")
    strs_push(l, "signature and has no body. The checker never sees a declaration with a hole in it, so recovery adds")
    strs_push(l, "syntax diagnostics and never semantic cascades. The usable abstract tree around a malformed region")
    strs_push(l, "is every other item, and the signature of the item it is in. A hole-tolerant checker is not")
    strs_push(l, "attempted here.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Unicode escapes, decided.** `Str` is bytes, and a literal's bytes are the UTF-8 encoding of its")
    strs_push(l, "source text: that decision was made when `\"é\"` was specified as two bytes. `\\u{H…}` (one to six")
    strs_push(l, "hexadecimal digits, a Unicode scalar value) is therefore those same bytes, spelled in ASCII. It")
    strs_push(l, "denotes nothing a literal could not already contain. It exists so that an invisible or")
    strs_push(l, "bidirectional character can be written visibly. A surrogate (`D800`–`DFFF`), a value above")
    strs_push(l, "`10FFFF`, no digits, more than six digits, a non-hex digit or a missing brace is refused (`N0004`)")
    strs_push(l, "at the escape. `\\xHH` still stops at `7F`. Above that, a lone byte is what `str_from_byte` makes,")
    strs_push(l, "and a `\\x80` meaning one byte would contradict `\\u{80}` meaning two.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Unsaved buffers.** `nazm lsp` moves from full to incremental document sync. The service keeps one")
    strs_push(l, "`Revision` per open document and applies each ranged change to it. Analysis takes the root file's")
    strs_push(l, "parse from that revision instead of parsing the text again (`nazm_core::analyse_parsed`). Because")
    strs_push(l, "of the contract above, the two are interchangeable, and a test holds them equal after every change.")
    strs_push(l, "Imported files are still parsed in full on every analysis.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** Semantic epoch `20 → 21`: `\\u{…}` moved from refused to accepted. Interface schema,")
    strs_push(l, "runtime ABI, Core/MIR/LIR print schemas and package, lock and registry schemas: unchanged. No")
    strs_push(l, "semantic fact, lowering or layout moves; only which source texts parse. Machine schemas: unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "The new diagnostics are existing codes at new positions. Check cache: an unparsable module is never")
    strs_push(l, "written (§7.4), so recovery cannot reach a cache. The epoch bump invalidates every check cached under")
    strs_push(l, "20. Selfhost: unchanged. The compiler written in Nazm still refuses every escape, still has no")
    strs_push(l, "concrete tree, and still does not recover. Parity is N98's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** `fn f() -> Int { 1 }` + edit inserting `{` after the body opens a delimiter")
    strs_push(l, "that no later boundary closes. The reparse runs to the end of the file, and the result equals a")
    strs_push(l, "fresh parse. **Boundary example.** An edit at the exact first byte of an item touches the token")
    strs_push(l, "that ends at that byte, so the previous chunk is reparsed too (`\"ab\"` + `\"c\"` at the boundary of an")
    strs_push(l, "identifier makes one token, not two).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** Any edit sequence over any text for which `edit` differs from")
    strs_push(l, "`Revision::new`, checked over every `.nz` file in the repository with seeded random edit sequences.")
    strs_push(l, "Also: a common one-item edit on the compiler's own sources that reparses most of the file.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** A hole-tolerant checker, incremental semantic analysis of an unsaved buffer (area 2a")
    strs_push(l, "covers saved modules), incremental parsing of imported files, a concrete tree or recovery in the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler written in Nazm, and `\\x` above `7F`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As built (amended after the code).** Relexing starts at the first lexeme whose end reaches the")
    strs_push(l, "edit, not at the affected chunk's first lexeme. The lexer is context-free from every boundary, so")
    strs_push(l, "that is exact, and a one-word edit relexes two lexemes instead of its whole item. The reparse still")
    strs_push(l, "starts at the chunk. The one cross-item read the convergence tests found is not the balance scan")
    strs_push(l, "but recovery: `fn ,` skips to the next `fn NAME`, reading the next item's name. The recorded")
    strs_push(l, "lookahead covers both, and each has a test that fails if lookahead goes unrecorded. Reuse of green")
    strs_push(l, "nodes is by construction (`Revision::edit` clones the old children). cstree exposes no node")
    strs_push(l, "identity without `unsafe`, so the tests observe reuse as chunk counts and equality, not as")
    strs_push(l, "pointers. A declaration dropped from the abstract tree keeps its own concrete node (`RecordItem`,")
    strs_push(l, "`FnItem`) with the malformed member inside it as an `Error`, rather than becoming one `Error` node.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.78 Resolution, persisted: one resolved unit per module, one resolver — N77, 2026-10-03")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Area 2 is PARTIAL, and area 2a names the gap: no written form of name")
    strs_push(l, "resolution exists, so nothing a check decides about a body outlives the process that checked it.")
    strs_push(l, "The answers are the checker's (`Resolution`), addressed by session ids no other process can read.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**One resolver, restated.** `nazm_core::check` decides what every name means. `load.rs` decides which")
    strs_push(l, "module every `use` names: a relative path, `@std/NAME`, `NAME:path` into a declared package, or the")
    strs_push(l, "core prelude. Nothing else decides either. `compiler/module.nz` is the bootstrap subset's own loader,")
    strs_push(l, "and it is not a second answer: it resolves relative paths only. From now on it **refuses `@std/` and")
    strs_push(l, "`NAME:` imports by name**, where until now it looked for a file of that name and reported it missing.")
    strs_push(l, "It still keys modules by a textually normalised path, not a canonical one (`bootstrap.md`). No")
    strs_push(l, "semantic rule is copied into the resolved unit: it is written from the checker's answers and read")
    strs_push(l, "back as data.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The product, `nazm.resolved/1`.** One per module that checked cleanly, holding only durable")
    strs_push(l, "facts:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- the module's durable key (which carries its package, `ModuleKey::in_package`);")
    strs_push(l, "- its source fingerprint, and the checker identity (semantic epoch included);")
    strs_push(l, "- its imports in source order: the path as written, the alias if any, the target's durable key, and")
    strs_push(l, "  the target's interface hash;")
    strs_push(l, "- its definitions, each a `DefKey` with the byte range of its declaration and its name;")
    strs_push(l, "- every resolved occurrence of a declared entity in its text: the byte range, and the target as a")
    strs_push(l, "  durable identity. A function, record or enum is its `DefKey`. A variant, field or payload field is")
    strs_push(l, "  its owner's `DefKey` and its member's name. A built-in is its name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Locals are absent: their identity is a slot in one body, and they are not durable. Session ids,")
    strs_push(l, "absolute paths, timestamps and load order are absent. Occurrences sort by range, then target.")
    strs_push(l, "Ranges are byte offsets into the fingerprinted source, so they mean something exactly as long as")
    strs_push(l, "the fingerprint does.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Where it lives, and why its invalidation is already sound.** The resolved unit is a function of")
    strs_push(l, "exactly what a `CheckKey` covers: the source, the checker, and each direct dependency's interface.")
    strs_push(l, "A body change in a dependency leaves the `DefKey`s it offers, and so every importer's targets,")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged. So the unit is stored in the check entry, under the same key. The check entry becomes")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.check/3`: a `/2` entry has no unit and is a miss. The unit is validated against the entry's")
    strs_push(l, "own fingerprint and module on read. By change:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Change | Invalidated |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| a private body | its own module |")
    strs_push(l, "| an exported signature | its module and every direct importer |")
    strs_push(l, "| an alias or a `use` line | the importing module, through its source |")
    strs_push(l, "| a package's version or name | every module of it, through `ModuleKey` |")
    strs_push(l, "| a semantic epoch | every entry |")
    strs_push(l, "| a profile, a target, an optimisation level | nothing: no checking rule reads them (`key.rs`), and profiles run after checking and are never cached |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Consumers.** `nazm check` writes the unit and reads it back for every module it reuses. `nazm")
    strs_push(l, "references DEF [FILE]` is new. It lists every occurrence of the entity `DEF` (a durable key,")
    strs_push(l, "`module::kind name`) in the compilation as `nazm.references/1`, built from the modules' resolved")
    strs_push(l, "units. A module whose check entry is reused contributes its stored unit, and its body is **not")
    strs_push(l, "checked again**: the output reports how many modules were checked and how many reused. `nazm")
    strs_push(l, "resolve FILE --json` prints the compilation's units as they would be stored.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What does not consume it, deliberately.** `nazm build` needs the typed Core IR of every body it")
    strs_push(l, "lowers, and a resolved unit carries no types or slots, so a build still checks every module")
    strs_push(l, "(area 2a's limitation, unchanged). The language service never persists or reads a cache: an unsaved")
    strs_push(l, "buffer is not state a cache may record (§7.18).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** Semantic epoch: unchanged, because no program moves between accepted and refused. The")
    strs_push(l, "check entry goes `nazm.check/2 → /3`. New machine schemas: `nazm.resolved/1`,")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.references/1`. Interface schema, runtime ABI and Core/MIR/LIR schemas: unchanged, because")
    strs_push(l, "nothing they describe moved. Object and build identity: unchanged, because the build does not read")
    strs_push(l, "the unit.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** A `/2` entry from before N77 is a miss and the module is checked again. A")
    strs_push(l, "unit whose fingerprint differs from the entry's is a miss. **Boundary example.** A dependency whose")
    strs_push(l, "private body changes is checked again, and its importer's unit is reused byte for byte: its")
    strs_push(l, "occurrences of the dependency's functions name the same `DefKey`s.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** Two processes, or two checkouts, writing different bytes for")
    strs_push(l, "one module. A reused unit that names a target a fresh check would not. `nazm references` disagreeing")
    strs_push(l, "with the language service's references over the same saved compilation, which is the independent")
    strs_push(l, "oracle: the service's index is computed in-process from a fresh check.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** Re-exporting a name and exporting it under another name, both language decisions with")
    strs_push(l, "no settled design. A build that skips bodies. A persisted resolution for locals. Making the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler written in Nazm resolve `@std` or packages (N98).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.79 Traits and methods: named capabilities of a type, resolved before Core IR — N78, 2026-10-03")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. §7.52 designed traits and deferred them until a program needed one. The")
    strs_push(l, "need is now named. With `[T: Equality]` the only requirement a type parameter can carry, generic")
    strs_push(l, "code cannot ask anything else of `T`: it cannot render, order, hash or measure one. A program that")
    strs_push(l, "wants to print every element of a `Vec[T]` must take a rendering function as an argument at every")
    strs_push(l, "call, through every layer of generic code in between. That is the problem a nominal capability")
    strs_push(l, "solves, and no larger one is attempted. Coherence, orphan rules and method lookup are therefore")
    strs_push(l, "the smallest that make one answer per call.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Syntax.** Three new forms, and `trait` and `impl` become keywords:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- `[pub] trait Name { fn m(self: Self, p: T) -> R [! {e}]; … }` declares a trait. Each method is a")
    strs_push(l, "  signature ending in `;`, and its first parameter is `self: Self`.")
    strs_push(l, "- `impl Name for Type { fn m(self: Type, p: T) -> R { … } … }` implements one.")
    strs_push(l, "- `recv.m(a, …)` calls a method on a value. `Name.m(recv, a, …)` calls a trait's method by its")
    strs_push(l, "  trait (UFCS).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A bound names a trait the way it names `Equality`: `fn f[T: Show](x: T)`, at most one requirement")
    strs_push(l, "per parameter, as before.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Identity.** A trait is a durable definition, `module::trait Name`, a new `DefKind`. A trait")
    strs_push(l, "method is its trait's key and its name. An impl is identified by its trait and its type. Each")
    strs_push(l, "method an impl defines is an ordinary function of the impl's module, keyed")
    strs_push(l, "`module::fn Trait/Type/m`: `/` is in no identifier, so the key can never be an ordinary function's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What an impl is for.** An impl's type is a non-generic record or enum, a numeric type, `Bool` or `Str`.")
    strs_push(l, "A generic type, a `Vec`, a channel, a function type, a capability or a type parameter is refused")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0604`). That keeps overlap decidable by equality: there are no impls over a pattern of types.")
    strs_push(l, "An impl defines every method of its trait exactly once, with the trait's signature with `Self`")
    strs_push(l, "replaced by its type, effects included (`N0602` missing, `N0603` extra or mismatched).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Coherence.** At most one impl of a trait for a type in a compilation (`N0600`, with the other")
    strs_push(l, "impl as a secondary label). The orphan rule: an impl must be in the module that declares the trait")
    strs_push(l, "or the module that declares the type, and for `Int`, `Bool` and `Str` only the trait's module")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0601`). Both rules are checked over the whole compilation, so a module's impls are part of its")
    strs_push(l, "interface.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Method lookup.** `recv.m(args)`: let `R` be `recv`'s type. Candidates are the traits **in")
    strs_push(l, "scope** — declared in this module or imported — that declare `m` and have an impl for `R`. When")
    strs_push(l, "`R` is a type parameter, the candidates are the traits its bound names. Exactly one candidate is")
    strs_push(l, "the call. None is `N0605`, naming the traits that would have one if imported. More than one is")
    strs_push(l, "`N0606`, and UFCS chooses. `Name.m(recv, args)` takes the trait from the written name and the type")
    strs_push(l, "from `recv`. An enum's variant still wins where `Name` is an enum (`E.A()`), so no program that")
    strs_push(l, "checked before changes meaning: `Name.m(…)` with `Name` a value, or with unlabelled arguments, was")
    strs_push(l, "refused before this milestone. A field of function type is not a method: `r.f(1)` with no method")
    strs_push(l, "`f` is refused as before, with the existing help to bind it first.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here, deliberately.** A trait is not a type (`N0607`): no trait objects, no dynamic dispatch,")
    strs_push(l, "no `dyn`. Default method bodies, associated types and constants, generic traits, generic methods,")
    strs_push(l, "supertraits, impls with bounds, inherent impls without a trait, and methods as values (`x.m`")
    strs_push(l, "without a call, `N0608`) are all out. Each is a language decision this milestone does not need, and")
    strs_push(l, "each is refused by name rather than half-supported. Generic function values and closures inside")
    strs_push(l, "generic functions (`N0387`) stay **outside the supported model**. Each would need a thunk per")
    strs_push(l, "instance, and a bound now covers the programs that wanted them (pass `T: Show` instead of a")
    strs_push(l, "rendering closure). `N0387` is retained with that reason, not retired.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Lowering, one representation per layer.** The checker resolves every method call before Core IR.")
    strs_push(l, "A call on a concrete type becomes an ordinary call of the impl's function, with the receiver first:")
    strs_push(l, "Core IR, MIR, both backends and the interpreter see a call they already understand, and `calls`")
    strs_push(l, "records the impl function at the method's span, so definition, hover and references work unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "A call on a type parameter becomes the one new Core IR form, `CallTrait { trait, method, self_ty,")
    strs_push(l, "args }`. MIR resolves it per instance: `self_ty` substituted, the impl looked up, a direct call")
    strs_push(l, "emitted. MIR never contains it. The interpreter resolves it per frame, from the frame's type")
    strs_push(l, "arguments, in the same table. Dictionaries are not used: monomorphisation already exists, and it")
    strs_push(l, "makes every trait call a direct call in native code. The impl table (trait, type) → functions is")
    strs_push(l, "the checker's, in `Resolution`, and nothing downstream builds another.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Effects, authority, provenance.** A method's effects are its declaration's, and a call exercises")
    strs_push(l, "them as any call does. An impl must declare exactly the trait's effects, so a call through a bound")
    strs_push(l, "cannot exercise more than the bound says. Authority is passed as parameters, as everywhere. For")
    strs_push(l, "provenance, a call on a concrete type is a call of a known function. A call through a bound is of")
    strs_push(l, "unknown origin joined with its arguments, conservatively, as an indirect call's is.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Persisted.** An exported trait, and every impl a module declares, are in its interface, because")
    strs_push(l, "an importer's method lookup and coherence check need them: `nazm.interface/7 → /8`. The resolved")
    strs_push(l, "unit (§7.78) gains the kinds `trait` and `trait method`; its schema stays `/1` because the kinds")
    strs_push(l, "are values of an existing field, and a reader that does not know them is incomplete, not wrong.")
    strs_push(l, "Core IR's printed form gains `CallTrait`: `nazm.core-ir/1 → /2`, since an old reader would misread")
    strs_push(l, "a call it does not know. MIR's printed form is unchanged, because it never contains one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** Semantic epoch `21 → 22`: `trait` and `impl` declarations, method calls and trait")
    strs_push(l, "bounds moved from refused to accepted, and a program using `trait` as a name moved from accepted to")
    strs_push(l, "refused. Interface `/7 → /8`. Core IR print `/1 → /2`. Runtime ABI unchanged, since no runtime")
    strs_push(l, "entry point moves. MIR, LIR, objects and package schemas unchanged. An object's key covers its LLVM")
    strs_push(l, "input, which changes exactly when the code does.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Libraries.** `@std/show` gains `pub trait Show { fn show(self: Self) -> Str; }`, impls for `Int`,")
    strs_push(l, "`Bool` and `Str`, and `show_all[T: Show](v: Vec[T], sep: Str) -> Str`, all written in Nazm. It is")
    strs_push(l, "the higher-order library use this milestone is held to.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Tooling.** A trait's name, its methods' declarations, and a method call through a bound are")
    strs_push(l, "indexed: `ReferenceTarget::Trait`, `ReferenceTarget::TraitMethod`. A concrete call refers to its")
    strs_push(l, "impl's function. The language service's definition, hover and references, and MCP's context")
    strs_push(l, "packets, read those as they read every other target.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The compiler written in Nazm** refuses `trait` and `impl` by its ordinary syntax error. That is")
    strs_push(l, "the recorded parity gap (N98).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative examples.** Two impls of `Show` for `Point` (`N0600`). An impl of `Show` for `Int` in a")
    strs_push(l, "third module (`N0601`). `x.show()` where no trait in scope has an impl for `x`'s type (`N0605`).")
    strs_push(l, "`fn f(s: Show)` (`N0607`). **Boundary examples.** `Show.show(1)` with `Show` imported under an")
    strs_push(l, "alias, `s::Show.show(1)`. An impl in the type's module of a trait from `@std`. A generic call")
    strs_push(l, "`show_all[Point]` that reaches `CallTrait` through two levels of generic functions.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** A program whose method call resolves differently in the")
    strs_push(l, "checker, the interpreter and a native build. A coherence violation accepted because its impls are")
    strs_push(l, "in different modules. A generic body that checks under its bound but cannot be instantiated for a")
    strs_push(l, "type that satisfies it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As built (amended after the code).** An impl is *usable* only from its own module and from modules")
    strs_push(l, "that import it directly. The constitution's lookup said \"an impl for `R`\". That alone would have let a")
    strs_push(l, "module's method resolution depend on an impl in a module outside its check key, so a cached check")
    strs_push(l, "could silently go stale. Coherence is still checked over the whole compilation. A trait's method list")
    strs_push(l, "does not recover member by member: a malformed method gives up the trait, as a record's field list")
    strs_push(l, "did before N76. A persisted interface carries traits, impls and bounds for identity and invalidation,")
    strs_push(l, "but `rehydrate` does not rebuild them, so a module checked against a persisted interface cannot use")
    strs_push(l, "its traits. Each impl method is hidden-linked, not internal, because a generic instance in an object")
    strs_push(l, "of its own may call it through a bound. The interpreter keeps no type arguments per frame, so it")
    strs_push(l, "dispatches a `CallTrait` on the receiver value's runtime type. That type is the one the bound was")
    strs_push(l, "instantiated at, because impls exist only for types whose values carry their type.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.80 Effects and capabilities v3: the bridge made a contract, attenuation, subsumption — N79, 2026-10-03")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Areas 5 and 6 are PARTIAL for four named reasons. First, **the ambient")
    strs_push(l, "bridge**: a function that declares no effect set exercises its caller's authority, and nothing says")
    strs_push(l, "so. Second, **no attenuation**: the only authority is a whole kind. Third, **no effect")
    strs_push(l, "subsumption**: a pure function value is refused where an effectful one is allowed. Fourth, **no")
    strs_push(l, "revocation**. This section settles each, and states plainly what stays.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The bridge, made a representable contract.** Deleting inheritance outright would refuse every")
    strs_push(l, "undeclared function in the repository that prints (more than a thousand checks, the compiler written")
    strs_push(l, "in Nazm among them, whose checker reads no capabilities). That is a migration of the language's")
    strs_push(l, "whole corpus and of the second compiler, which this milestone does not attempt. What it does")
    strs_push(l, "instead:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- Every function's contract now has three parts. Its effects, declared or inferred. Its capability")
    strs_push(l, "  parameters. And its **inherited authority**: the capability kinds its body exercises without")
    strs_push(l, "  holding them lexically, computed by the same rule a declared function's authority is checked by.")
    strs_push(l, "  A declared function's inherited authority is always empty, because missing authority is")
    strs_push(l, "  `N0369`.")
    strs_push(l, "- The inherited authority is recorded in the resolution. It is published in the interface (each")
    strs_push(l, "  export's `inherits`, `nazm.interface/8 → /9`, since a `/8` reader would take an inheriting")
    strs_push(l, "  function for one that inherits nothing). `nazm inspect` reports it. So the bridge is no longer")
    strs_push(l, "  ambient: it is a named part of a callable's type-level contract, and tools and reviewers see")
    strs_push(l, "  exactly which functions use it.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Strict authority is available and enforceable.** The restriction-profile rule")
    strs_push(l, "  `explicit-authority` refuses any function in its package whose inherited authority is not")
    strs_push(l, "  empty. Under it, authority is only what a function's scope holds. Undeclared inheritance is gone")
    strs_push(l, "  for that code, and `main`'s parameters are the only root.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The default does not change.** A program not under the profile still inherits as before, so")
    strs_push(l, "  area 6 stays PARTIAL. Migrating the corpus, and teaching the compiler written in Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "  capabilities, are named as the remaining work.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Attenuation.** One narrower kind, `OutCap`, authorises the standard streams only: `print` and")
    strs_push(l, "`eprint`. It is derived, never constructed: `cap_out(io: IoCap) -> OutCap` is the only way to make")
    strs_push(l, "one (`N0370` still refuses construction), and `main` may take one as a root. Authority is a")
    strs_push(l, "preorder, monotone by construction. Holding an `IoCap` is holding the authority an `OutCap` gives,")
    strs_push(l, "because `print` asks for `OutCap` and an `IoCap` implies it. Nothing implies `IoCap`, and there is")
    strs_push(l, "no built-in from `OutCap` to `IoCap`. A function given only an `OutCap` cannot read a file, write")
    strs_push(l, "one, read the arguments or exit, and each of those is `N0369`. The effect stays `io`: attenuation")
    strs_push(l, "narrows authority, not the effect vocabulary. Its scope is lexical, like every capability's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Effect subsumption.** Where a value of function type is passed or returned, a function type whose")
    strs_push(l, "effect set is a subset of the expected one is accepted: `fn() -> Int ! {}` where `fn() -> Int !")
    strs_push(l, "{io}` is expected. Parameters and results stay invariant, and so does an effect parameter in either")
    strs_push(l, "type, because a row is matched by binding and not by inclusion. Below the checker, effects are")
    strs_push(l, "metadata and every verifier compares types up to effects (§7.53), so nothing downstream moves.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Callable polymorphism and traits.** One effect parameter per function, as N51 settled. A trait")
    strs_push(l, "method's declared effects are its contract, and an impl's must equal them (N78). Capabilities cross")
    strs_push(l, "traits, closures and methods as ordinary parameters and captures, and the profile rule applies to")
    strs_push(l, "an impl's methods like any function.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Revocation: outside the model, deliberately.** A capability has no identity: copies are")
    strs_push(l, "indistinguishable, and nothing records a grant. Revocation would need an allocated cell per grant, a")
    strs_push(l, "check at every authorised call, and runtime state. Nazm's capabilities are static, and the language")
    strs_push(l, "does not offer revocation. A program that needs a revocable grant passes a channel or a value it can")
    strs_push(l, "invalidate. That is ordinary data, not authority.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** Semantic epoch `22 → 23`: `cap_out` and `OutCap` became built-in names (a program")
    strs_push(l, "defining either moved from accepted to refused), and a subsumed function value moved from refused to")
    strs_push(l, "accepted. Interface `/8 → /9` for `inherits`. Runtime ABI unchanged: a capability erases to a word,")
    strs_push(l, "and `cap_out` returns one. Core IR, MIR and LIR schemas unchanged: `cap_out` is a built-in, and")
    strs_push(l, "built-ins are named, not schematised. Profile rule ids gain `explicit-authority`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** `fn log(o: OutCap) -> Int ! {io} { write_file(…) }` is `N0369`: `OutCap`")
    strs_push(l, "does not authorise a file. **Boundary example.** Under `explicit-authority`, `fn helper() -> Int {")
    strs_push(l, "print(\"x\"); 0 }` called from `main(io: IoCap)` is refused, with `helper`'s inherited authority named.")
    strs_push(l, "Outside the profile it is accepted exactly as before.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** A function that exercises authority it does not hold")
    strs_push(l, "lexically, with an empty recorded `inherits`. Any path from `OutCap` to `IoCap`'s authority. A")
    strs_push(l, "subsumed value whose call performs an effect its expected type does not allow.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As built (N79, 2026-10-03).** Four amendments, each narrower or simpler than the text above:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **No `cap_out`.** Attenuation is by passing: the checker's one relation `assignable` accepts an")
    strs_push(l, "  `IoCap` where an `OutCap` is expected (`CapabilitySet::implied`), at every argument, `spawn`")
    strs_push(l, "  argument and result. A built-in would have been a second spelling of the same fact. `OutCap`")
    strs_push(l, "  is still never constructed (`N0370`), and `main` may take one as a root.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The interface stays `/8`.** Inherited authority depends on a body, and an interface publishes")
    strs_push(l, "  declarations. A declared export inherits nothing by construction, and an undeclared import is")
    strs_push(l, "  already every effect to its importer (§7.38), so a `/8` reader loses nothing it relied on. The")
    strs_push(l, "  record is the resolution, and `nazm inspect` reports it as each definition's `inherits`.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The profile is `authority`.** `explicit-authority` is enforced by a profile of that name with")
    strs_push(l, "  that one rule. It is not added to `critical` or `cyber`, whose `declared-effects` already")
    strs_push(l, "  implies it for the program's own modules. It applies to the program's own modules, not the")
    strs_push(l, "  prelude and the standard library, which declare every effect.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Core IR's verifier compares results up to effects**, as it already compared arguments")
    strs_push(l, "  (§7.53). The checker's acceptance of a subsumed result reached a verifier that compared results")
    strs_push(l, "  exactly, and lowering refused it (`N0900`). Nothing else below the checker moved.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The epoch is 23 for `OutCap` becoming a built-in type name and for the two new acceptances.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.81 Provenance v3: container cells, indirect targets, local shapes, one policy engine — N80, 2026-10-03")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Area 7 is PARTIAL for named reasons, and this section settles the ones")
    strs_push(l, "that are precision rather than kind. **Containers**: every read of a sequence, `Vec` or channel is")
    strs_push(l, "`unknown`, so a path built from a `Strs` the program filled with its own arguments is refused.")
    strs_push(l, "**Indirect calls**: a call through a function value or a trait bound returns `unknown`, and a")
    strs_push(l, "closure's parameters are `unknown`. **Records and variants** are tracked whole. **The one")
    strs_push(l, "restriction** is code, not policy: `N0372`'s rule and `cyber`'s `contents-stay-in-files` are two")
    strs_push(l, "implementations of one idea. **No traces**: `nazm explain-flow` names the origins at a sink, never")
    strs_push(l, "how they got there. What stays out is stated at the end.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The domain.** Unchanged: four compiler-owned origins (`argument`, `file`, `authority`,")
    strs_push(l, "`unknown`), explicit data flow only, conditions contributing nothing, joins as set unions, and")
    strs_push(l, "summaries as the least fixed point over the whole program. No origin is added, so no label a")
    strs_push(l, "program writes exists.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Container cells (type-keyed, alias-free).** Every container has a **cell**, named by its type:")
    strs_push(l, "`Ints`, `Strs`, `Vec[T]`, `Chan` and `Chan[T]`, with `T` written as the checker shows it. A cell's")
    strs_push(l, "origins are the join of every value written into **any** container of that type, anywhere in the")
    strs_push(l, "program: `ints_push`, `ints_set`, `strs_push`, `strs_set`, `vec_push`, `vec_set`, `chan_send`,")
    strs_push(l, "`chan_send_of`, and the value `chan_select_of` and `chan_select_until` move from `Chan[T]` onto")
    strs_push(l, "`Vec[T]` (a write of the `Chan[T]` cell into the `Vec[T]` cell). Every read of one — `ints_get`,")
    strs_push(l, "`ints_pop`, `ints_len`, `ints_sum`, the `strs_` and `vec_` reads, `str_join`, `chan_recv`,")
    strs_push(l, "`chan_recv_of` — carries its cell's origins, and its other arguments'. This is sound without alias")
    strs_push(l, "analysis, because a handle of type `T` can only ever hold what was written into some handle of")
    strs_push(l, "type `T`, and every write is one of these built-ins: no foreign function takes a handle (§7.44), and")
    strs_push(l, "the runtime fills none. It is imprecise exactly where two containers share a type, and that is")
    strs_push(l, "stated, not hidden. A container whose type mentions a type parameter, in a generic body, is the")
    strs_push(l, "**wild** cell: a write to it reaches every cell, and a read of it reads every cell. Same-named")
    strs_push(l, "records from two modules share a cell: an over-approximation, never a miss. A select's index is")
    strs_push(l, "control, not data, and carries nothing: implicit flow, outside the model as a condition is.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Indirect targets (type-based).** A call through a function value may reach any function value")
    strs_push(l, "the program makes of a matching type: each named function written as a value, and each closure.")
    strs_push(l, "Types match **up to effects** (N79's subsumption lets a pure value stand where an effectful one is")
    strs_push(l, "expected) and exactly otherwise; a function type that mentions a type parameter matches every")
    strs_push(l, "function value. The call's result is the join of every candidate's summary applied to its")
    strs_push(l, "arguments; each candidate's parameters receive its arguments; a candidate whose parameter reaches")
    strs_push(l, "a restricted sink carries the rule back to the argument. A call through a trait bound (N78) reaches")
    strs_push(l, "every impl's method of that trait method. With no candidate, the call can never run and carries")
    strs_push(l, "nothing. A **closure's parameters** are therefore ordinary parameters, received from the indirect")
    strs_push(l, "calls that can reach it, and its **captures** are parameters received from its maker, at the point")
    strs_push(l, "it is made — so a captured path that comes from the maker's file read is still refused, and one from")
    strs_push(l, "its arguments is not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Local shapes (field and variant sensitive within a body).** Inside a body, a binding assigned")
    strs_push(l, "only constructions — a record, a variant, or another binding with a shape — keeps each field's")
    strs_push(l, "flow apart, keyed by variant and field **name**. A field read, a pattern's binding and `?` on a")
    strs_push(l, "`Result.Ok` read that field's flow; a variant never assigned to the binding contributes nothing. At")
    strs_push(l, "a **call boundary** — an argument, a result, a store into a container — a value is whole again: the")
    strs_push(l, "join of its fields. Flow-insensitive like everything else: a binding assigned anything without a")
    strs_push(l, "shape is whole from then on.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**One policy engine.** A **policy** is a list of rules `(sink class, forbidden origins, scope)`,")
    strs_push(l, "where the scope is *declared functions* or *every function*. The language's policy is one rule,")
    strs_push(l, "`(path, {file, unknown}, declared)`, and it is `N0372`, unchanged in meaning and message. A profile")
    strs_push(l, "adds rules: `cyber`'s `contents-stay-in-files` is `(output, {file, unknown}, every)`, and a new")
    strs_push(l, "rule, `checked-paths`, is the language's rule over every function — the provenance half of N37's")
    strs_push(l, "bridge, closed by profile — added to `cyber`. One function decides a violation for both, and")
    strs_push(l, "gives the same witness.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Traces.** Every sink, as solved, carries for each origin that reaches it one deterministic")
    strs_push(l, "chain: where the origin entered, every call, return, container cell, capture and caller it")
    strs_push(l, "crossed, in order. `nazm explain-flow --json` prints them as `nazm.flow/2`; `/1` had no `traces`.")
    strs_push(l, "`N0372` and `N0510` show the same chain as secondary labels.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What tooling and the programmer observe.** A program accepted before stays accepted except where")
    strs_push(l, "`cyber` gains `checked-paths`. A program refused before for a container read, an indirect call or a")
    strs_push(l, "closure parameter that the cells and targets now prove carries no file contents is accepted. Nothing")
    strs_push(l, "runs differently: provenance is erased before Core IR.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** Semantic epoch `23 → 24`: `N0372` moved from refused to accepted for such programs.")
    strs_push(l, "Check entry `nazm.check/3 → /4`: a module's persisted facts gain cell writes and reads, indirect call")
    strs_push(l, "sites and closure creations; a `/3` entry is a miss. Interface `/8` unchanged: no fact is in it.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.flow/1 → /2` for traces. Core IR, MIR, LIR, runtime ABI and every object key unchanged:")
    strs_push(l, "provenance is erased before Core IR. Profile ids gain `checked-paths`. `nazm.context`,")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.snapshot` and `nazm.delta` unchanged in shape: a summary's fields are the same three.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** `let xs = strs_new(); strs_push(xs, read_file(\"cfg\")); write_file(strs_get(xs,")
    strs_push(l, "0), \"x\")` in a declared function is `N0372`, with a trace through the `Strs` cell to the")
    strs_push(l, "`read_file`. **Boundary example.** The same with `strs_push(xs, arg(1))` is accepted — unless any")
    strs_push(l, "other `strs_push` in the program writes a file's contents into any `Strs`, which the trace names.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not solved, deliberately.** Implicit flow and non-interference; timing and side channels; per-handle")
    strs_push(l, "or per-index precision (two containers of one type share a cell); shapes across calls; user labels,")
    strs_push(l, "sanitisers and a policy language a program writes; runtime tracking; foreign code, whose results")
    strs_push(l, "stay `unknown` and whose arguments are not sinks (the `ForeignCap` authorised them).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** A program where a value written into a container reaches a")
    strs_push(l, "read of another container of the same type with that origin missing from the read. An indirect call")
    strs_push(l, "that runs a function value outside its candidate set. A field read whose flow omits an origin that")
    strs_push(l, "was written to that field. A policy verdict for `N0372` that differs from the language rule it")
    strs_push(l, "replaced, on any program in the repository.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As built (N80, 2026-10-03).** The design held; five additions and one measurement:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **What C hands an export is `unknown`.** An exported function (N55) is called by C, so each of")
    strs_push(l, "  its parameters receives `unknown`. It is pure and has no sink of its own, but it can write a")
    strs_push(l, "  container, and through the cell that reaches the program. The constitution did not say so; the")
    strs_push(l, "  model needed it to be sound.")
    strs_push(l, "- **A device register is a source of `unknown`.** `mmio_read32` was a read of a shared handle; with")
    strs_push(l, "  containers followed it is the one built-in whose result is `unknown`.")
    strs_push(l, "- **A missing module's facts make everything indirect `unknown`.** When a reused module's facts do")
    strs_push(l, "  not rehydrate, its writes, values and callers cannot be seen, so every cell, every indirect call's")
    strs_push(l, "  result and every closure's parameters also carry `unknown`, and its functions reach every sink.")
    strs_push(l, "- **`?` yields every part but `Err` and `None`.** That is the payload of the prelude's `Result`, the")
    strs_push(l, "  only type `?` applies to.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Reach is per sink class.** Which parameters reach a sink is solved for every class, so a rule")
    strs_push(l, "  of the policy over any class and scope uses one solver. The published summary's `reaches` stays")
    strs_push(l, "  the path's, as `nazm.context/3` documents it.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The falsifier was run.** N79 (`8daf107`) and N80 checked all 237 `.nz` files in the repository")
    strs_push(l, "  with identical codes on every one. A cold check of `compiler/emit.nz` costs 1.125×, measured in")
    strs_push(l, "  `performance.md`; later rounds re-solve only the functions that read a grown cell.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.82 The backend contract v2, stage one: bytes, ownership and a printed LIR — N81, 2026-10-03")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Area 10 is PARTIAL because LIR is not a level of its own. `nazm-lir` settles")
    strs_push(l, "units, symbols, linkage and canonical field order from validated MIR, and then **each backend")
    strs_push(l, "translates MIR's operations itself**: `emit.rs` for LLVM, `func.rs`, `prims.rs` and `helpers.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "for Cranelift. Three responsibilities are duplicated or orphaned:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Bytes.** Cranelift decides every record's and enum's byte layout in its own `layout.rs` (an")
    strs_push(l, "  enum a tagged union at a fixed payload offset), with an 8-byte pointer assumed. LLVM never")
    strs_push(l, "  decides bytes: it writes named aggregates and lets LLVM lay them out, an enum as the product of")
    strs_push(l, "  every variant's payload. No value ever crosses between the two, so neither is wrong, but no one")
    strs_push(l, "  owns \"what are the bytes of this type on this target\", and `wasm32`'s 4-byte pointer is known")
    strs_push(l, "  only to LLVM.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Ownership.** Whether a value of a type owns anything a drop must give back is computed twice,")
    strs_push(l, "  as a fixed point in each backend.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Visibility.** Nothing prints what LIR decided, and nothing validates it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What N81 settles (stage one).** `nazm-lir` becomes the one owner of the target's **data layout**")
    strs_push(l, "(pointer width, word, `Bool`, the three-word `Str`), of every record's and enum's **byte layout**")
    strs_push(l, "on that target (offsets, size, alignment; an enum a tag word then a payload area aligned for its")
    strs_push(l, "widest variant), and of the **ownership table**. Both backends read them: Cranelift's `layout.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "keeps only how a byte layout becomes Cranelift values, and both backends' ownership fixed points")
    strs_push(l, "are deleted. A **validator** checks every layout on every native build — fields ascending, inside")
    strs_push(l, "their structure, aligned, sizes multiples of alignment, every variant inside its enum's payload")
    strs_push(l, "area, ownership closed under containment — and a broken table is a compiler bug (`N0900`), never a")
    strs_push(l, "miscompilation. `nazm lir FILE [--target T]` prints `nazm.lir/1`: the target's data layout, every")
    strs_push(l, "unit with its symbols and linkage, every layout and the ownership table, deterministic, with a")
    strs_push(l, "schema checked against real output. The differential fuzzer (N73) gains records with `Bool` and")
    strs_push(l, "`Str` fields and an enum with payloads, so layouts are exercised on the interpreter, LLVM at")
    strs_push(l, "`-O0` and `-O2`, and Cranelift against each other.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What N81 does not settle, stated before the code.** The prompt's acceptance is one MIR→LIR")
    strs_push(l, "lowering into an instruction level that both backends consume, with no semantic path from MIR into")
    strs_push(l, "either backend, an LIR oracle interpreter, and LIR-backed mutations. That is a rewrite of both code")
    strs_push(l, "generators (about 7,400 lines) and of everything they carry — DWARF positions, the struct-of-arrays")
    strs_push(l, "layout, the vectoriser's patterns, exports, the freestanding and WebAssembly targets — and this")
    strs_push(l, "stage does not attempt it: risking the reference compiler's correctness is not a trade this")
    strs_push(l, "programme makes for a dashboard. **N81 is therefore not accepted under its own criteria.** Area 10")
    strs_push(l, "stays PARTIAL, named: operations are still translated per backend, guarded by differential testing")
    strs_push(l, "rather than by construction; LLVM's enum is still the product of its variants. The instruction")
    strs_push(l, "level is recorded as the remaining work.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Observable and versioned.** Nothing a program does changes. `nazm lir` and `nazm.lir/1` are new")
    strs_push(l, "(there was no `/1` before: the prompt's `/2` assumed one). Semantic epoch, interface, Core IR, MIR")
    strs_push(l, "and runtime ABI unchanged: no language rule, interface shape, IR or runtime moved. Cranelift's")
    strs_push(l, "objects are byte-identical, because the layouts are the same numbers computed in one place; the")
    strs_push(l, "object cache keys on bytes, so no key moves. LLVM text is byte-identical.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** A record whose field offset the validator finds outside its size is refused")
    strs_push(l, "as `N0900` before any code is generated. **Boundary example.** On `wasm32-unknown-unknown` a `Str`")
    strs_push(l, "is `{ptr: 0, len: 8, owner: 16}` in 24 bytes, its pointers four bytes each and the length still")
    strs_push(l, "eight; on every 64-bit target the same three words are 0, 8, 16 of 24.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** Any Cranelift object byte that differs from before, on any")
    strs_push(l, "program in the repository; any program both backends compile correctly that the validator refuses;")
    strs_push(l, "any layout whose printed offsets disagree with the bytes Cranelift writes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As built (N81, 2026-10-03).** As constituted, with three notes. The printed form is `nazm.lir/1`,")
    strs_push(l, "there having been no earlier one. The validator also checks ownership against containment, which")
    strs_push(l, "the constitution listed and the code needed a table for: ownership is computed once by")
    strs_push(l, "`abi::owns`, which the LLVM backend's helper now calls. And the falsifier ran: every `.nz` program in")
    strs_push(l, "the repository built by N79 and N81 with each backend gave byte-identical objects, and the extended")
    strs_push(l, "fuzzer agreed on every tier.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.83 Runtime v2: the runtime as a built, versioned, verified artifact — N82, 2026-10-03")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Area 13 is PARTIAL for one named reason this milestone does not touch: one")
    strs_push(l, "OS thread per task (N83's). What N82 settles is the runtime's **form**. Today it is LLVM text the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler generates into every build, specialised to the services the program reaches, and compiled by")
    strs_push(l, "clang on every build whose project store does not already hold that exact text. Nothing can build a")
    strs_push(l, "runtime once, ship it, check that it is the one a compiler expects, and link it from another build.")
    strs_push(l, "Both native backends already link the same runtime implementation — Cranelift's units call the same")
    strs_push(l, "text, through the typed registry — so that half of the prompt's acceptance holds before the code, and")
    strs_push(l, "this section keeps it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is settled.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **A runtime artifact.** `nazm runtime build [--target T] [--profile hosted|board|wasm] [-O N] -o")
    strs_push(l, "  DIR` compiles the whole runtime for one target and profile — every service — once, into")
    strs_push(l, "  `DIR/libnazmrt.a`, beside a manifest `DIR/nazm-runtime.json`, `nazm.runtime/1`: the runtime ABI")
    strs_push(l, "  revision, the runtime digest that already enters every object key, the target, the profile, the")
    strs_push(l, "  services, the optimisation level, the toolchain that compiled it, and BLAKE3 digests of the text and")
    strs_push(l, "  of the archive. The profile is the target's: `hosted` on the four operating-system targets, `board`")
    strs_push(l, "  on `aarch64-unknown-none`, `wasm` on `wasm32-unknown-unknown`; another is refused.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Linking it.** `nazm build --runtime DIR` links that archive and generates no runtime. The")
    strs_push(l, "  platform entry is still the program's own. Before anything is linked, the build refuses — exit 4 (3 or 1 since Q1-C1),")
    strs_push(l, "  the reason named, nothing produced, never a silent fallback to generating the runtime — a missing or")
    strs_push(l, "  unreadable manifest; another schema; another ABI revision or runtime digest (a compiler whose")
    strs_push(l, "  runtime differs); another target or profile; a service the program reaches that the archive does")
    strs_push(l, "  not provide; and an archive whose bytes are not the ones the manifest describes. Both backends take")
    strs_push(l, "  `--runtime`, and link the same archive.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Checking it.** `nazm runtime verify DIR` performs the same checks without a program, and says")
    strs_push(l, "  whether the artifact fits this compiler.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Nothing a program does changes.** The archive holds the same runtime text with every service, so a")
    strs_push(l, "  program linked against it prints the same, ends the same, and reports the same memory counters as")
    strs_push(l, "  one whose runtime was generated. Tested over programs reaching every service, on both backends.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is not settled, stated before the code.** A runtime written in Rust: only the host's Rust")
    strs_push(l, "target is installed and builds stay offline, so it could exist only for one target beside the text")
    strs_push(l, "for every other — two implementations where there is one. An allocator of its own and a scheduler")
    strs_push(l, "beyond one thread per task (N83). Every build without `--runtime` still generates its runtime, as")
    strs_push(l, "before, and is what the tests and the default keep using; the artifact is the path for building a")
    strs_push(l, "runtime once and checking what is linked, not yet the default.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** Runtime ABI revision unchanged: no runtime symbol, signature or global moved.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.runtime/1` is new. `nazm.provenance/1` gains an optional `runtime_archive`, the archive's digest,")
    strs_push(l, "present only when one was linked: additive, as its schema allows. Object keys unchanged: an archive")
    strs_push(l, "is a link input, and nothing about linking is keyed (area 10b). Semantic epoch and interface")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** An archive built by a compiler whose runtime digest differs is refused, naming")
    strs_push(l, "both digests. **Boundary example.** An archive built with `--profile board` for `aarch64-unknown-none`")
    strs_push(l, "links into a freestanding image, and a hosted build given it is refused for the profile.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** A program whose output, ending or memory report differs between")
    strs_push(l, "a generated runtime and the artifact; a mismatched or altered artifact that links.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As built (N82, 2026-10-03).** As constituted. Three details the code settled: a board's and")
    strs_push(l, "WebAssembly's manifests list only `stack`, since what those runtimes lack is refused by the")
    strs_push(l, "freestanding build itself (N62), and the service check applies to the hosted profile; the archive is")
    strs_push(l, "written with `ZERO_AR_DATE`, so the same runtime archives to the same bytes (since 2026-10-17 nazm")
    strs_push(l, "writes the archive itself, §7.57); an unknown target is")
    strs_push(l, "exit 4, as a missing toolchain is (5 since Q1-C1, a usage error). The falsifier ran: every program in the repository built with a")
    strs_push(l, "generated runtime and with the artifact, on both backends — 228 builds — printed, ended and reported")
    strs_push(l, "memory identically.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.84 The task pool: M:N tasks on bounded workers — N83, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Area 15 is RESEARCH: §7.56 chose the model — stackful tasks on guarded")
    strs_push(l, "`mmap`'d stacks with a small per-target switch — and named what must have a task-local home before a")
    strs_push(l, "pool exists. This section settles the pool, as an **opt-in mode of the native runtime**, beside the")
    strs_push(l, "default of one OS thread per task, which does not change.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Selecting it.** A native program whose environment has `NAZM_SCHEDULER=pool` runs its tasks on a")
    strs_push(l, "pool of `NAZM_WORKERS` OS threads (default: the online processors, at most 64), started at the first")
    strs_push(l, "`spawn`. Anything else, or no variable, is today's model. The choice is the runtime's, made once per")
    strs_push(l, "process; the compiler, both backends and the interpreter are unaffected, and so is every program's")
    strs_push(l, "meaning.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Tasks.** A task is a record and a guarded stack: `NAZM_TASK_STACK` bytes (default 256 KiB, rounded")
    strs_push(l, "to pages) above one inaccessible page, `mmap`'d at `spawn` and released when the task ends. A task is")
    strs_push(l, "**pinned to one worker** — the one `spawn` assigned it, round robin — for its whole life. Pinning is")
    strs_push(l, "what makes the runtime's thread-local state sound without rewriting how compiled code reads it: a")
    strs_push(l, "compiler may keep a thread-local's address across a call, so a task must never resume on another")
    strs_push(l, "thread. The four thread-local words the runtime promises — the first-failure flag, message and")
    strs_push(l, "length, and the stack limit — are saved into the task when it leaves its worker and restored when it")
    strs_push(l, "returns, so each task has its own. A task's stack limit is set from its own stack, so `nz.stack_check`")
    strs_push(l, "reports recursion that would reach the guard page as it does on a thread (`N0408`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**States and suspension.** A task is runnable, running, parking, parked or done. The operations that")
    strs_push(l, "wait are exactly §7.56's suspension points: a full channel's send, an empty channel's receive, a select")
    strs_push(l, "with no channel ready, and a scope's join. In a task, each **parks the task and frees its worker**")
    strs_push(l, "instead of blocking it: the task records itself as a waiter on what it waits for, under that thing's")
    strs_push(l, "own lock, then switches to its worker. Whoever changes that state wakes every task waiting on it, as")
    strs_push(l, "the condition variable is broadcast today. A wake that arrives while the task is still switching out is")
    strs_push(l, "not lost: the worker finishes the park and sees it. A select with a deadline parks with that deadline,")
    strs_push(l, "and its worker wakes it when it passes. A select that does not wait — `ms <= 0` — yields its worker")
    strs_push(l, "before returning, so a task polling for another on the same worker cannot starve it. The program's")
    strs_push(l, "`main` is not a task: its waits block its own thread, as now.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Scheduling.** Each worker runs its own tasks in first-in, first-out order until each parks, yields")
    strs_push(l, "or ends. There is no preemption and no work stealing: a task that computes without waiting holds its")
    strs_push(l, "worker until it does, and only its own worker's tasks wait for it. That is the fairness this pool")
    strs_push(l, "promises — first in, first out among a worker's runnable tasks — and no more.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Failure, cancellation and shutdown.** Unchanged in meaning: a failure is the task's own, its scope")
    strs_push(l, "joins every task and reports the first by start order; cancellation is a closed channel. Workers never")
    strs_push(l, "exit; the process ends as it does today, when `main` returns.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is refused or not covered.** A foreign (C) call that blocks holds its worker: there is no")
    strs_push(l, "hand-off, and it is stated, not hidden. A task's stack is fixed: recursion past it is `N0408`, and a")
    strs_push(l, "program that recursed deeply in a task under the thread model may need a larger `NAZM_TASK_STACK`.")
    strs_push(l, "The interpreter keeps a thread per task. Only aarch64 and x86-64 are covered; the switch is verified on")
    strs_push(l, "`aarch64-apple-darwin`, and on `x86_64-apple-darwin` under Rosetta, and compiled but not run for the")
    strs_push(l, "two Linux targets. **Deadlock freedom is not claimed**: a program that deadlocks on threads deadlocks")
    strs_push(l, "on the pool.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** Runtime ABI revision `10 → 11`: the waits and wakes go through three new runtime")
    strs_push(l, "functions, a task record exists, and the per-target switch is a new artefact `switch` that every")
    strs_push(l, "native build reaching tasks links (and every runtime artifact carries). Semantic epoch, interface,")
    strs_push(l, "Core IR, MIR and LIR unchanged: no language rule moved. `nazm.runtime/1` gains nothing: the archive")
    strs_push(l, "holds the switch for its target. `NAZM_SCHED_REPORT` gains `workers=` and `peak=`, the most tasks alive")
    strs_push(l, "at once.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** Ten thousand tasks each waiting on a channel `main` fills: under the thread model")
    strs_push(l, "that is ten thousand OS threads; under the pool, `NAZM_WORKERS` threads, every waiting task parked.")
    strs_push(l, "**Boundary example.** A task in `while true { chan_select_until(cs, out, 0) }` waiting for a sibling on")
    strs_push(l, "the same worker still sees the sibling run, because a non-waiting select yields.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** (§7.56's, kept): many more logical tasks than OS threads with no supported waiting")
    strs_push(l, "operation holding a worker, and spawn latency, switch cost and task memory measured as resident set")
    strs_push(l, "size, with the page size, against the thread model.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** A program whose output, ending or memory report differs between")
    strs_push(l, "the two models; a waiting task that holds its worker; a lost wake-up; a task observing another's")
    strs_push(l, "failure or stack limit.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As built (N83, 2026-10-04).** Three amendments. **The default worker count is 4**, not the online")
    strs_push(l, "processors: the call that reports them takes a constant that differs between macOS and Linux, and")
    strs_push(l, "the runtime text is target-independent. **The pool is joined to the thread model's texts as they are")
    strs_push(l, "emitted**, not written into them: `compiler/emit.nz` carries the task and channel texts line by line")
    strs_push(l, "(`runtime parity`), so those constants are unchanged and the Rust runtime rewrites their waits, wakes,")
    strs_push(l, "join and spawn when it emits them; the compiler written in Nazm keeps one thread per task. **The")
    strs_push(l, "switch is its own artefact**, `switch`, linked wherever the runtime has tasks or channels — always")
    strs_push(l, "under Cranelift, whose runtime is its whole baseline — and carried by a hosted runtime artifact")
    strs_push(l, "(N82) as a second archive member. A test program that waits inside a scope for a task that fails")
    strs_push(l, "first deadlocks on both models, as §7.56 says it must; the pool's tests receive after the scope.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Amended (performance leadership 6.2, 2026-10-16): copied stacks.** A task no longer has a stack of")
    strs_push(l, "its own. Each worker has one guarded **run stack** of the task-stack size (`NAZM_TASK_STACK`,")
    strs_push(l, "`--stack-size`, 256 KiB by default) for the life of the process, and its tasks run on it at the same")
    strs_push(l, "addresses. When a task other than the one whose frames are on the run stack is to run, the worker")
    strs_push(l, "copies those frames — from that task's saved stack pointer to the top — into a buffer the task owns")
    strs_push(l, "(`nz.task_place`), and puts the new task's saved frames back where they were, or lays out its first")
    strs_push(l, "frame on its first run. Same addresses, so nothing moves: frame pointers, unwinding, stack probes")
    strs_push(l, "and the saved registers are untouched, and the stack check and its limit (`N0408`) are as before,")
    strs_push(l, "the limit now the run stack's. Sound because a task is pinned (above) and nothing outside a task")
    strs_push(l, "reads its stack while it is parked: its arguments are a heap block, a waiter is registered by its")
    strs_push(l, "record, and a condition variable's address is only a key. What changes for a program: nothing it")
    strs_push(l, "can observe but memory and speed — `spawn` makes no system call, and a parked task holds its record")
    strs_push(l, "and the bytes of its frames instead of a page. A program whose own C reaches the pool would be the")
    strs_push(l, "one exception (a C library keeping a pointer into a caller's stack across a wait); a program that")
    strs_push(l, "calls C runs a thread per task (N106, §7.107). If the frames cannot be saved for want of memory,")
    strs_push(l, "the process ends with a message. Runtime ABI 39 → 40 (design: `openspec/changes/")
    strs_push(l, "performance-leadership/design.md`, *Concurrency engineering*).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Amended (performance leadership 6.3, 2026-10-16): stealing, spinning, and a join without a lock.**")
    strs_push(l, "*Scheduling* above changes in three ways and keeps its promise — a worker's runnable tasks run first")
    strs_push(l, "in, first out. A worker keeps the tasks that have never run apart from those it resumes (their")
    strs_push(l, "frames are on its run stack, so they stay); both are taken in the order they were queued. A task")
    strs_push(l, "started by a task goes to that task's worker; one `main` starts goes round robin as before. A worker")
    strs_push(l, "with nothing to run takes half (at most 64) of another worker's unstarted tasks, never holding two")
    strs_push(l, "workers' locks; still with nothing, it looks for work for up to 50 µs before it sleeps, and a task")
    strs_push(l, "queued for it signals it only when it sleeps. With one worker there is no stealing and no spin, so")
    strs_push(l, "`NAZM_WORKERS=1` stays deterministic. A scope's join reads a task that is done without a lock; one")
    strs_push(l, "not done counts itself as a joiner first, and a task that ends wakes joiners only when one is")
    strs_push(l, "counted. Runtime ABI 40 → 41.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Amended (performance leadership 6.3, 2026-10-16): preemption at loop back edges.** *Scheduling*'s")
    strs_push(l, "\"no preemption\" no longer holds with more than one worker. Every loop's back edge — an edge to a")
    strs_push(l, "block on the depth-first path from the entry, found when MIR is lowered to LIR, so exactly the")
    strs_push(l, "loops — polls: LLVM's lowering inlines the poll as one load of the process's flag")
    strs_push(l, "`nz.preempt_req` and a branch past a call of `nz.preempt`; Cranelift's and Nazm's own code")
    strs_push(l, "generator call it. A monitor thread looks at the workers every 10 ms; a worker that has run one")
    strs_push(l, "task since the last look (its switch count unmoved) while others wait in its queues is asked to")
    strs_push(l, "yield (its flag, then the process's), and the task, at its next back edge, yields its worker as a")
    strs_push(l, "select that does not wait does: to the back of its worker's queue. A request a task never polls for")
    strs_push(l, "is dropped when the worker next switches. With one worker there is no monitor, so")
    strs_push(l, "`NAZM_WORKERS=1` keeps its order exactly. Unwinding, stack copying and `N0408` are unaffected: a")
    strs_push(l, "yield at a back edge is a call like any other, inside the frame's own stack, and no back edge is")
    strs_push(l, "taken during an unwind's search. A loop in a function no task runs pays the load and the branch;")
    strs_push(l, "`main` and threads under the thread model are never asked. Runtime ABI 42 → 43.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Amended again (performance leadership 6.3, 2026-10-17): preemption by interrupt.** The poll cost")
    strs_push(l, "8-10% on hot loops (`docs/internal/performance-log.md`), so no loop carries one now: the code generator adds no")
    strs_push(l, "instruction to a loop. The monitor, finding a worker asked, interrupts its thread")
    strs_push(l, "(`nz.os_preempt`): on macOS a signal, `SIGURG`, whose handler reads the interrupted address from")
    strs_push(l, "the signal's context; on Windows the thread suspended, its context read, and its return redirected")
    strs_push(l, "through a stub that saves every register a call may clobber. The task yields — as at a back edge")
    strs_push(l, "before — only where that address is in generated code, which the LLVM backend places in a section")
    strs_push(l, "of its own on these targets (`__TEXT,__nz_text`; `.text$nM` between markers), and only while no")
    strs_push(l, "failure unwinds (the exception in flight is the thread's). Generated code holds no lock and")
    strs_push(l, "touches no thread's allocator lists, and every runtime function that does — a pthread mutex, a")
    strs_push(l, "spin lock, the small-block heap, the pool — is `noinline` in a program that has tasks, so")
    strs_push(l, "whole-program optimisation never puts one inside generated code; a program of one thread is never")
    strs_push(l, "preempted and inlines them as before. On macOS the yield runs inside the signal's handler, on the")
    strs_push(l, "task's own stack, so the signal frame is part of the frames 6.2 copies out and back, and the")
    strs_push(l, "handler returns when the task resumes. Linux and Android preempt nothing yet (after 1.0), nor do")
    strs_push(l, "Cranelift's and Nazm's own code generator's builds, whose code is not in the section: a task there")
    strs_push(l, "that computes without waiting holds its worker, as before 6.3. Runtime ABI 43 → 44. **Then (runtime ABI 44 → 47):** Cranelift's and Nazm's own code generator's code goes in the same")
    strs_push(l, "section — Cranelift's object has its code section renamed in its header after it is written, and")
    strs_push(l, "`nzcg` writes the name itself — so their tasks are preempted too; and Windows's names are eight")
    strs_push(l, "bytes, `.text$nM` between `.text$nA` and `.text$nZ`, which every writer keeps in the section header.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Amended (performance leadership 6.4, 2026-10-16): the waiter table's locks.** The table of parked")
    strs_push(l, "waiters keeps its 256 buckets, now under 64 locks (bucket `b` under lock `b mod 64`) in place of one")
    strs_push(l, "for the whole process, so waits and wakes on different channels no longer contend. A wake whose")
    strs_push(l, "bucket is empty takes no lock: a waiter registers while its caller holds the lock under which it")
    strs_push(l, "looked at its condition, and a waker changes that condition under the same lock before it wakes, so")
    strs_push(l, "any registration the wake must see is already visible. A task resumed when it is on no list (a")
    strs_push(l, "waker took it off) takes no lock to leave. Channel texts are unchanged (`runtime parity`); a direct")
    strs_push(l, "hand-off to a parked receiver changes them and their mirror in `compiler/emit.nz`, and is not part")
    strs_push(l, "of this. Runtime ABI 41 → 42.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Amended (performance leadership 6.4, 2026-10-17): a direct hand-off on the `Int` channel.** A")
    strs_push(l, "sender or receiver that must block no longer waits on the channel's one condition variable, which")
    strs_push(l, "every change broadcast to every waiter. It parks on a wait record of its own, at the tail of the")
    strs_push(l, "channel's list of receivers or of senders, and sleeps on the record's condition variable. A receiver")
    strs_push(l, "parks only on an empty ring and a sender only on a full one, so a sender that finds a receiver")
    strs_push(l, "parked writes its value into the record of the one parked longest, marks it done and wakes it alone")
    strs_push(l, "— the ring is never touched — and a receiver that frees a slot while a sender is parked moves the")
    strs_push(l, "value of the one parked longest into the ring's tail and wakes it alone, so values leave in the")
    strs_push(l, "order they were offered. A close marks every record closed and wakes each: a parked receiver then")
    strs_push(l, "finds the channel drained, a parked sender refused, as before. A record lives on the heap, never on")
    strs_push(l, "the waiter's stack, because a parked pool task's frames are copied out and their addresses reused")
    strs_push(l, "(6.2); records go back to the channel's spares and the last reference frees them, so a channel")
    strs_push(l, "allocates no more records than it ever had waiters at once. Without memory for one a waiter waits")
    strs_push(l, "the old way, on the channel's condition variable, counted so that every change broadcasts it while")
    strs_push(l, "anyone does. The text is still the thread model's, joined to the pool by the same hooks, and")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/emit.nz` mirrors it line for line (`runtime parity`). The generic channel (`Chan[T]`) is")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged except that its close is its own. Every function of the channel that takes its lock,")
    strs_push(l, "parks or wakes is `noinline`, as 6.3's preemption by interrupt requires. Runtime ABI 44 → 45.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Amended (performance leadership 6.4, 2026-10-17): a select over channels of different types.**")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/spec.md`, *Select over channels of different types*: built-ins, no syntax. A `Select` is a")
    strs_push(l, "runtime record, `{ count, cases, capacity, case array }`, its count plain because it never crosses")
    strs_push(l, "into a task; a case is `{ channel, kind, slot, vector }` — a receive onto a vector, a send of the")
    strs_push(l, "value in a slot the select owns, a send done. Each case holds a reference to its channel and a")
    strs_push(l, "receive case to its vector; the last release gives them back and releases an unsent value by the")
    strs_push(l, "channel's own element release. A wait is `nz.chanv_select`'s, case by case: it counts itself among")
    strs_push(l, "the selectors, reads the event count, tries every case in index order — a receive by")
    strs_push(l, "`nz.chanv_try` straight into room made on its vector first (so a value taken always has somewhere")
    strs_push(l, "to go), a send by `nz.chanv_offer` — and sleeps only while the count has not moved. The value moves")
    strs_push(l, "in the runtime, not in generated code: the code at a wait does not know its cases' types, while the")
    strs_push(l, "runtime knows each element's size and release from its channel. A send case needs the event count")
    strs_push(l, "to move when room is made, so a generic channel's receive advances it too; `nz.sel_signal` now")
    strs_push(l, "reads the selector count first and touches nothing else while nobody selects — sound because a")
    strs_push(l, "selector counts itself before it reads the count and looks, so a change made before a signaller saw")
    strs_push(l, "no selector is one that selector's look finds. Every select function that allocates, takes a lock")
    strs_push(l, "or waits is `noinline` (6.3). Semantic epoch 90 → 91; runtime ABI 45 → 46.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Amended (performance leadership 6.4, 2026-10-17): the direct hand-off on the generic channel.**")
    strs_push(l, "`Chan[T]` parks and hands off as the `Int` channel does: a 128-byte header with lists of parked")
    strs_push(l, "receivers (80) and senders (96), spare wait records (112) and a count of old-way waiters (120); a")
    strs_push(l, "wait record carries the value at 160, so a record is 160 bytes and a slot. Under the channel's")
    strs_push(l, "mutex, `nz.chanv_put` gives a value to the receiver parked longest — the ring is empty while one is")
    strs_push(l, "— or queues it, and `nz.chanv_get` takes the ring's oldest value and lets the sender parked longest")
    strs_push(l, "fill the slot it frees; a send, a receive, a select's offer (`nz.chanv_offer`) and its look")
    strs_push(l, "(`nz.chanv_try`) all go through the two, so a select and a blocked task see one channel. A close")
    strs_push(l, "ends parked receivers and refuses parked senders, whose values stay theirs to release. Runtime ABI")
    strs_push(l, "46 → 48 (47 is the preemption fix's).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Amended (performance leadership 6.4, 2026-10-17): channels without a lock while nobody waits.**")
    strs_push(l, "Both channel kinds are one implementation (`nz.chq_*` in the `Int` channel's text, mirrored in")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/emit.nz`; `nz.chan_*` and `nz.chanv_*` call it), with one 128-byte header: `{ cap,")
    strs_push(l, "dequeue, enqueue, waiting, ring, mutex, cond, rc, stride, release, receivers, receivers_tail,")
    strs_push(l, "senders, senders_tail, spares, old }`. The ring is `cap` slots of `{ sequence, value }`: a sender")
    strs_push(l, "claims enqueue position `p` by compare-and-swap when the slot's sequence is `2p` and publishes the")
    strs_push(l, "value as `2p + 1`; a receiver claims dequeue position `p` when it reads `2p + 1` and frees the slot")
    strs_push(l, "as `2(p + cap)` — doubled so that one slot is enough. The close is bit 62 of the enqueue position,")
    strs_push(l, "so a send either claimed its position before the close or is refused, and a receiver reports the")
    strs_push(l, "channel drained only when nothing is queued or claimed (one claimed but not yet written is waited")
    strs_push(l, "for). A send or receive takes this path only while `waiting` is zero and reads it again after;")
    strs_push(l, "a task that must block takes the mutex, counts itself in `waiting` and looks once more before it")
    strs_push(l, "parks — sequentially consistent on both sides, so either its look finds the value or room, or")
    strs_push(l, "the lock-free operation sees the count and comes under the mutex to wake it (a receiver told to")
    strs_push(l, "look again; a sender's value moved into the ring). While anyone waits, operations take the mutex:")
    strs_push(l, "a send hands its value to the receiver parked longest when the ring is empty, a receive refills")
    strs_push(l, "from the sender parked longest, so the order values were offered in is the order they leave, and")
    strs_push(l, "a select's look and offer (`nz.chq_try`, `nz.chq_offer`) go the same ways. Every function that")
    strs_push(l, "locks, parks, wakes or spins is `noinline` (6.3). Runtime ABI 48 → 49.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Amended (2026-10-19): a waiter is counted out by whoever takes it off a list.** A parked waiter")
    strs_push(l, "used to leave `waiting` itself, when it ran again; a woken task can wait long for its worker (a")
    strs_push(l, "sleeping worker's signal, or another task's time slice), and while it was counted every send and")
    strs_push(l, "receive on the channel took the mutex. In fan-in (eight producers, one receiver, a ring of 1,024)")
    strs_push(l, "nearly everything did: 0.85–0.997 of the million operations on each side, almost all with nobody")
    strs_push(l, "on either list, and sender parks 14,000–138,000 with up to 54,000 signals to sleeping workers —")
    strs_push(l, "the 445 → 845 ms regression, bimodal by where the producers landed. `nz.chq_take` now takes the")
    strs_push(l, "channel and counts the record out as it takes it, under the mutex, and the woken waiter does not.")
    strs_push(l, "The count still covers every record on a list and every waiter between counting itself and")
    strs_push(l, "enlisting (both under the mutex), so the argument above is unchanged; a waiter told to look again")
    strs_push(l, "counts itself in again if it parks again. Counted the same way afterwards: ≥ 0.995 of each side")
    strs_push(l, "without the lock, parks 800–3,100, signals 660–2,500, in ten runs. Runtime ABI 49 → 50.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.85 The standard library 1.0 — N84, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Area 16 is PARTIAL: N45's foundation is 34 functions in eight modules, enough")
    strs_push(l, "to show how the library works, not enough to write a real program against. A program that counts")
    strs_push(l, "words, reads a table, serves requests over channels or edits a package manifest today reimplements")
    strs_push(l, "sorting, a map, number formatting, path handling and data encoding itself. This milestone fixes the")
    strs_push(l, "**1.0 surface**: what a program may rely on, what is deliberately absent, and how the surface may")
    strs_push(l, "change.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What 1.0 contains.** Ordinary Nazm in `library/std/`, each module imported by name, each function")
    strs_push(l, "documented, total where it can be, and explicit about its effects and authority:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- `@std/text` grows: case (ASCII), trimming either end, replacing, padding, lines, comparison, and")
    strs_push(l, "  byte classes. `@std/seq` grows: a **stable sort by a caller's ordering**, polymorphic in that")
    strs_push(l, "  function's effects; reversal; slices; concatenation; `any` and `all`; and the same for `Ints` and")
    strs_push(l, "  `Strs` where they need their own.")
    strs_push(l, "- New: `@std/fmt` (integers padded to a width, hexadecimal, lists with separators and brackets),")
    strs_push(l, "  `@std/num` (absolute value, sign, clamp, checked power, greatest common divisor), `@std/map` (a map")
    strs_push(l, "  from `Str` keys, ordered by key, found by binary search: `map_new`, `map_get`, `map_set`,")
    strs_push(l, "  `map_remove`, `map_keys`, `map_len`), `@std/path` (join, base name, directory, extension, stem,")
    strs_push(l, "  normalising `.` and `..` lexically), `@std/fs` (reading, writing and testing a file under an")
    strs_push(l, "  `IoCap`, each failure a `Result` value), `@std/time` (a clock reading and elapsed time under a")
    strs_push(l, "  `TimeCap`), `@std/json` (parsing and encoding JSON into an **arena document** — nodes in one")
    strs_push(l, "  `Vec`, children as indices, because a type that owns itself through a `Vec` is refused (`N0359`) —")
    strs_push(l, "  with accessors by key and index), and `@std/test` (expectations that return a `Result` naming what")
    strs_push(l, "  differed).")
    strs_push(l, "- **Concurrency utilities stay channel helpers.** A function value may not cross into a task")
    strs_push(l, "  (`N0321`), so a library cannot spawn a caller's function; what it can do — collect, drain and send")
    strs_push(l, "  many — it does, in `@std/chan`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What 1.0 does not contain.** Networking: there is no network authority or runtime, and none is")
    strs_push(l, "designed here. Cryptography: only an audited external implementation would do, and there is none to")
    strs_push(l, "bind. Floating point: the language has none. Selective adoption by the compiler written in Nazm: it")
    strs_push(l, "refuses every `@std` import by name (N77), and stays so.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Stability.** `library/std/API-1.0` lists every public function of 1.0 with its signature, one per")
    strs_push(l, "line, sorted; a test regenerates it from the modules and requires equality, so the surface changes")
    strs_push(l, "only by editing that file in the same commit. The policy, written into `spec.md`: within 1.x a function")
    strs_push(l, "may be added, never removed or changed in its signature, effects or documented behaviour; a removal or")
    strs_push(l, "change is 2.0. An edition, if the language ever needs one, would be how 2.0 is opted into.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence that it is enough.** Four representative programs under `examples/std/` — a word counter (a")
    strs_push(l, "CLI over a file: split, count in a map, sort, format), a table summer (data: lines, fields, parse,")
    strs_push(l, "fold), a channel service (concurrency: workers over channels, results collected), and a package tool")
    strs_push(l, "(paths and a JSON manifest read, changed and written) — each written only against the library for its")
    strs_push(l, "plumbing, run on the interpreter and both native backends with the same output. The library's own")
    strs_push(l, "tests check every function at its edges on every tier, and the core operations are measured.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** Semantic epoch `24 → 25`: names a program could not import before, it now can, and a")
    strs_push(l, "standard module's bytes are part of every importer's check. Interface, IR, runtime ABI unchanged:")
    strs_push(l, "the library is source.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** `json_parse(\"[1, 2\")` is an `Err` naming the offset where the input ended, never")
    strs_push(l, "a trap. **Boundary example.** `vec_sort_by` on a vector of records with equal keys keeps their order:")
    strs_push(l, "stable, as the documentation says.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** A representative program that still needs a helper the library")
    strs_push(l, "should have provided; a 1.x change to a listed signature that the manifest test does not stop.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As built (N84, 2026-10-04).** Four amendments. **Sorting is `@std/sort`**, not part of `@std/seq`: a")
    strs_push(l, "restriction profile checks every function of every module a program imports, and a sort allocates in")
    strs_push(l, "a loop and calls through a function value, so in `@std/seq` it made a program that only sums a")
    strs_push(l, "sequence fail `embedded`. Seventeen modules, then; the surface is the same 126 items. **No epoch moves**: `spec.md` already says a")
    strs_push(l, "standard module's changes are carried by its interface hash, as N45 settled, and that holds; the")
    strs_push(l, "constitution's epoch 25 was not needed. **Channel helpers are written for `Int` and `Str`**: a")
    strs_push(l, "channel cannot carry a type parameter (`N0390`), so `chan_send_all`, `chan_collect` and `chan_drain`")
    strs_push(l, "are each two functions. **`num_pow` returns `None` for `Int`'s minimum**: its overflow check is on")
    strs_push(l, "magnitudes, and the documentation says so rather than the check growing a special case. A standard")
    strs_push(l, "module may import another (`@std/fs` imports `@std/text`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.86 FFI v3: handles, C-layout records, C-string results, errno, callbacks and shared libraries — N85, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Area 17 is PARTIAL: C is called with `Int`, `Bool` and borrowed `Str`")
    strs_push(l, "arguments, Nazm is exported to C with scalars, and a static library is built. A real C API —")
    strs_push(l, "`sqlite3 *`, a `struct timespec`, `strerror`, `qsort`'s comparator, `errno` — cannot be bound. §7.57")
    strs_push(l, "designed four of the shapes; this milestone settles them, builds a practical subset of the C ABI,")
    strs_push(l, "and names everything outside it as refused.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The sole owner.** The checker (`nazm-core/src/check/foreign.rs`) owns *which* types may cross and in which")
    strs_push(l, "position, by one table: the FFI position rule. Core IR lowering (`nazm-core/src/lower.rs`) owns")
    strs_push(l, "*how* a crossing value changes representation, and writes it as ordinary Core IR — a field read, a")
    strs_push(l, "record or variant built, a test against zero — so MIR, LIR and both backends see a foreign function")
    strs_push(l, "whose parameters and result are `Int`, `Bool`, `Str` (borrowed, as N55) or a C-layout record. The")
    strs_push(l, "backends own only two things they always owned: the C calling convention, and the borrowed copy of an")
    strs_push(l, "argument for the duration of the call (N55's C string, now also a C-layout record). Nothing else")
    strs_push(l, "learns about C.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Opaque handles.** `extern \"C\" struct Db;` — C's own spelling of an incomplete struct — declares a nominal type whose values are C pointers Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "never reads, writes, compares or frees. A handle comes into existence only as a foreign function's")
    strs_push(l, "result; it is passed back to C as an argument, stored in a local, a record field or a `Vec`, and")
    strs_push(l, "returned from Nazm functions — ordinary values otherwise. Refused at the operation:")
    strs_push(l, "constructing one and reading a field of one (`N0611`: it has no fields to name); `==` or `!=` on one")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0304`, as for any type without equality: a pointer's identity is C's to define); and a handle")
    strs_push(l, "crossing into a task, by capture (`N0321`) or by channel (`N0390`), exactly as a sequence is refused —")
    strs_push(l, "C objects are rarely thread-safe, and nothing in a declaration says which are. Each is the existing")
    strs_push(l, "derived rule (§7.13, *Task safety is derived*) answering for a new type, not a new rule. Freeing is C's: the program calls the")
    strs_push(l, "C function that frees it, and using a handle after that is C's undefined behaviour, outside every Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "guarantee — the same trust boundary as everything else C does.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Pointer width (v1, Q1-A1-05).** Below the checker a crossing pointer — a handle, a C string")
    strs_push(l, "result, a callback — is an `Int`, so it crosses as 64 bits. That is C's pointer on every 64-bit")
    strs_push(l, "target and on no 32-bit one: there a C function takes and returns 32-bit pointers and lays a")
    strs_push(l, "pointer field out in four bytes. A build for a 32-bit target (`wasm32-*`, `thumbv7m-none-eabi`)")
    strs_push(l, "refuses each such crossing by name, `N0381` at the foreign declaration (`build/lower.rs`,")
    strs_push(l, "`narrow_pointer_refusal`), rather than importing a signature C does not have; crossing pointers at")
    strs_push(l, "the target's width is not built.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Nullability is in the type.** A result `-> Db` promises a non-null pointer: the call checks it, and")
    strs_push(l, "a null result fails the call with `N0409` *after* C returns — never a handle that is null. A result")
    strs_push(l, "`-> Option[Db]` maps null to `None` and anything else to `Some`. An argument is always a handle: no")
    strs_push(l, "null pointer can be written in Nazm, and a C function that accepts null is called with a handle or")
    strs_push(l, "not at all. `Option[Db]` as an argument is refused (`N0381`): it would be the one place a Nazm value")
    strs_push(l, "means \"no pointer\", and nothing needs it yet.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**C strings returned.** A result `-> Str` is a `const char *` that C still owns: Nazm copies its bytes")
    strs_push(l, "up to the NUL into a Nazm string immediately after the call and never frees C's. A null result fails")
    strs_push(l, "with `N0409`; `-> Option[Str]` makes it `None`. A C function returning a string the *caller* must free")
    strs_push(l, "is bound as a handle and its free function — the ownership is then written in the program, not")
    strs_push(l, "guessed. The copy is one allocation and one `strlen` per call, stated.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**C-layout records.** `extern \"C\" struct Point { x: Int, y: Int }` declares a record whose fields are")
    strs_push(l, "laid out **in declaration order** with C's alignment rules — `int64_t` for `Int`, `bool` for `Bool`, a")
    strs_push(l, "pointer for a handle, the nested struct for a nested C-layout record — so declaration order *is*")
    strs_push(l, "meaning for this record, unlike any other (§7.43). Its fields may be only those. A C-layout record")
    strs_push(l, "crosses as an argument by **borrowed pointer**: C receives a `const struct Point *` to a copy the")
    strs_push(l, "caller made for the call and frees after it, as a borrowed C string is. Passing a struct *by value*,")
    strs_push(l, "a struct result, a union, a bit-field, an array field and a field of any other type are refused")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0381`): each has per-target register rules the compiler does not implement. Otherwise a C-layout")
    strs_push(l, "record is an ordinary record.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**`errno`.** `c_errno()` returns the `errno` value the most recent foreign call on this thread left,")
    strs_push(l, "captured by generated code immediately after the call returns and before anything else runs. It")
    strs_push(l, "performs the effect `foreign`, as calling C does. It is defined on the hosted targets only (`__error`")
    strs_push(l, "on macOS, `__errno_location` on Linux); a freestanding or WebAssembly build that calls it is refused")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0613`). Under the task pool (§7.84) a task is pinned to its worker, so the value is the task's")
    strs_push(l, "unless the task blocked between the call and the read — written down rather than prevented.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Callbacks.** A foreign parameter may have a function type whose parameters and result are `Int` and")
    strs_push(l, "`Bool`: a C function pointer. Its argument must be the name of an **export** (`pub extern \"C\" fn`,")
    strs_push(l, "§7.57) — never a closure or any other function value (`N0612`) — so the pointer C receives is the")
    strs_push(l, "export's C entry, which needs no environment, cannot be freed, and is valid for the life of the")
    strs_push(l, "process. Reentrancy is the export rules' consequence: an export performs no effect, holds no Nazm lock")
    strs_push(l, "and takes no capability, so C may call it from inside the foreign call, again after it, and from any")
    strs_push(l, "thread. **Thread attach**: an export uses no per-thread runtime state except its failure flag, which is")
    strs_push(l, "per-thread; a C thread the runtime never started may call one. **Unwinding**: as N55, a Nazm failure in")
    strs_push(l, "an export ends the process with status 2; it never unwinds through C frames, and a C `longjmp` across")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm frames is outside every guarantee.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Shared libraries.** `nazm build --lib --shared -o libx.dylib` (or `.so`) links the library's objects")
    strs_push(l, "and the runtime into one shared object whose only exported symbols are the program's exports, with the")
    strs_push(l, "same header `--lib` writes. Two Nazm shared libraries in one process each carry a runtime; neither")
    strs_push(l, "sees the other's state. Linking *against* a shared library is `--link libfoo.dylib`, as any link")
    strs_push(l, "input. **Dynamic-library lifecycle**: Nazm never `dlopen`s or `dlclose`s — a library is mapped by")
    strs_push(l, "the loader before `main` and unmapped at process exit, so no handle or callback outlives its code.")
    strs_push(l, "Loading at run time is refused by absence: there is no construct for it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Bindings.** `nazm bindgen` widens with the language: an incomplete `struct S *` becomes `extern \"C\"")
    strs_push(l, "struct S;`, a complete struct of `int64_t`/`bool` fields passed as `const struct S *` becomes `extern")
    strs_push(l, "\"C\" struct S { … }`, and a `const char *` result becomes `Option[Str]` (a header never says non-null).")
    strs_push(l, "Everything else is a line naming its reason: by-value structs, unions, arrays, variadics, floating")
    strs_push(l, "point, non-`int64_t` integers, function pointers whose argument a header cannot name an export for.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the programmer observes, and when.** Compile time: every refusal above, by code and span. Run")
    strs_push(l, "time: `N0409` after a call that broke its declaration's null promise; nothing else is checked after")
    strs_push(l, "C returns. Target time: `N0613`. The interpreter refuses any program calling C or `c_errno` before")
    strs_push(l, "running it (`N0385`, unchanged). **Deterministic**: every compile-time decision, every layout, the")
    strs_push(l, "header. **Target-dependent**: `errno`'s location; a C-layout record's layout follows the target's C")
    strs_push(l, "ABI, which on every target of the matrix is natural alignment for these field types.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Authority and provenance.** Unchanged in kind: every foreign call and `c_errno()` needs a")
    strs_push(l, "`ForeignCap`; what C returns — a handle, a copied string, an `errno` — carries the `unknown` origin")
    strs_push(l, "(N42), and a handle's origin flows through records and `Vec`s as any value's (N80).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** Semantic epoch `24 → 25` (new declarations, new accepted types). Interface schema")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.interface/8 → 9`: a record's C-layout and opaque flags are part of what an importer may do with")
    strs_push(l, "it. Runtime ABI `11 → 12`: `nz.cstr_len`, `nz.errno_save`, `nz.errno_last`. Core IR, MIR and LIR")
    strs_push(l, "schemas unchanged: the crossing is written in existing nodes, plus two internal built-ins")
    strs_push(l, "(`foreign_nonnull`, `cstr_copy`) no program can name. The check cache follows the interface.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** `extern \"C\" struct Db; fn same(a: Db, b: Db) -> Bool ! {} { a == b }` is `N0304`")
    strs_push(l, "at the `==`, and `Db {}` anywhere is `N0611`. **Boundary example.** `extern \"C\" fn find(k: Int) -> Option[Db] = \"find\";` called when C")
    strs_push(l, "returns null is `None`, and the same declaration written `-> Db` fails that call with `N0409` and")
    strs_push(l, "status 2, not a crash in the caller's next use.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** By-value structs and struct results; unions, bit-fields, arrays; floating point;")
    strs_push(l, "integer types other than `int64_t` and `bool`; variadic functions; closures as callbacks (a C")
    strs_push(l, "`void *` environment rule); `dlopen`; ABIs other than C; exports taking `Str` or records; out-buffers")
    strs_push(l, "C writes into. Each is a refusal with a code, not a silent fallback.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** A C-layout record whose bytes as C reads them differ from its")
    strs_push(l, "fields in declaration order on any target of the matrix; a null handle reaching Nazm code; an `errno`")
    strs_push(l, "read that sees a value set by the runtime rather than by the foreign call; an export called from a C")
    strs_push(l, "thread that crashes for want of runtime state.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As built (N85, 2026-10-04).** Five amendments. **The syntax is `extern \"C\" struct`**, for a handle")
    strs_push(l, "and a C struct alike — C's own spelling of an incomplete struct, and no new keyword: `extern` stays")
    strs_push(l, "contextual, read before a string and `struct`. **A handle is a record of one hidden field**")
    strs_push(l, "(`#pointer`, a name no program can write), so it is an ordinary value to every layer below the")
    strs_push(l, "checker; `==` on one, and one reaching a task, are refused by the existing derived rules (`N0304`,")
    strs_push(l, "`N0321`, `N0390`) answering for a new type rather than by a new code. **A callback's address is")
    strs_push(l, "written by Core IR lowering** as an internal built-in on the export's symbol, because a named")
    strs_push(l, "function value is a thunk by MIR, which no longer knows the export it wraps. **`errno`'s location is")
    strs_push(l, "a per-target unit** (`nz_errno_location`, beside the task switch), so the runtime text stays the same")
    strs_push(l, "on every target; the capture is the runtime's `foreign` part, and a freestanding runtime defines a")
    strs_push(l, "capture that does nothing. **Cranelift links the `errno` unit always**, its runtime being its whole")
    strs_push(l, "baseline. Versions as stated: epoch 25, `nazm.interface/9`, runtime ABI 12; Core IR, MIR and LIR")
    strs_push(l, "print schemas unchanged — the crossing is existing nodes and three internal built-ins.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.87 Embedded v2: boards as data, a second architecture, device registers by width — N86, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Area 18 is PARTIAL because everything it shows is one board: N62 built a")
    strs_push(l, "freestanding image for QEMU's AArch64 `virt` machine, N63 bounded its stack, and the board's facts —")
    strs_push(l, "where the image loads, where the UART is, how the machine stops — are constants in one runtime file.")
    strs_push(l, "A second board would be a second copy of that file. This milestone makes a **board a description**")
    strs_push(l, "and adds a second architecture family through it, so that what is specific to a board is data and")
    strs_push(l, "what is the language's is not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The sole owner.** `nazm_runtime::board` owns the board table: for each freestanding target, its")
    strs_push(l, "architecture, load address, stack size, UART (address and access width), how the machine is stopped")
    strs_push(l, "(ARM semihosting, or SiFive's test device), the startup's per-architecture instructions, and the")
    strs_push(l, "emulator command a person runs it with. The linker script, the freestanding runtime and the entry are")
    strs_push(l, "generated from a description and from nothing else; `nazm inspect` prints the table. The language")
    strs_push(l, "gains no board knowledge: a program names device addresses as integers under an `MmioCap`, as in")
    strs_push(l, "N62, and a board's description never changes what a program means.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The second architecture.** `riscv64gc-unknown-none-elf` on QEMU's RISC-V `virt` machine: RV64GC,")
    strs_push(l, "machine mode, no firmware (`-bios none`), the image loaded at `0x8000_0000`, the NS16550A UART at")
    strs_push(l, "`0x1000_0000`, the SiFive test device at `0x10_0000` stopping the machine with a status. Its startup")
    strs_push(l, "sets the stack, enables the floating-point unit (code generation may use it) and calls `main` as")
    strs_push(l, "AArch64's does; its stack check, stack painting and stack bound are N49's and N63's, unchanged. Only")
    strs_push(l, "the LLVM backend builds it, as only it builds AArch64's board; Cranelift is refused by name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Device registers by width.** `mmio_read8`, `mmio_write8`, `mmio_read16` and `mmio_write16` join the")
    strs_push(l, "32-bit pair: one volatile access of exactly that width, zero-extended on read and truncated on write,")
    strs_push(l, "under an `MmioCap`, freestanding only (`N0392` on a hosted build, unchanged). A 16550's registers are")
    strs_push(l, "bytes; a 32-bit store to one writes its three neighbours, so a byte-wide device needs the byte access,")
    strs_push(l, "and the width is the program's to state. No access is reordered against another (volatile), and none")
    strs_push(l, "is merged or split.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Settled and not built.** *Atomics*: an ordering model needs a memory model the language has not")
    strs_push(l, "written (N61's formal core has one thread), and a litmus test on one emulated core shows nothing about")
    strs_push(l, "orderings; refused by absence — there is no atomic built-in — and recorded as DESIGNED. *Interrupts*:")
    strs_push(l, "a handler is code the hardware calls between any two instructions; it needs the effect and capability")
    strs_push(l, "story for preemption and a vector table per board; DESIGNED. *A heap*: the boards have none, and a")
    strs_push(l, "program that allocates is refused as N62 refuses it (what only a hosted runtime has). *Static")
    strs_push(l, "initialisation* is the linker's: `.data` is loaded with the image and `.bss` is zero in QEMU's loaded")
    strs_push(l, "memory; on hardware a loader that does not zero `.bss` is outside this guarantee, written down.")
    strs_push(l, "*Panic path*: unchanged — a failure is reported on the UART and the machine stopped with status 2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence, and what is claimed.** Emulator runs only: each board boots its image under QEMU, in a")
    strs_push(l, "container, and a program's output, failures and measured stack are compared with independent expected")
    strs_push(l, "values. No hardware is claimed; a board on the table is \"emulated\", and the published support matrix")
    strs_push(l, "says which of build, link, boot and measured stack each target has.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** Semantic epoch `25 → 26` (four names a program could not call before). Runtime ABI")
    strs_push(l, "`12 → 13` (four MMIO entries; the board table enters the runtime digest). Interface, Core IR, MIR and")
    strs_push(l, "LIR schemas unchanged. A board image's objects are keyed by target as N57 keyed them, so a RISC-V")
    strs_push(l, "object is never an AArch64 one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** `mmio_write8(268435456, 72)` in a program built for the host is `N0392`; a")
    strs_push(l, "program allocating a `Vec` built for either board is refused before linking, naming the sequences")
    strs_push(l, "runtime. **Boundary example.** On RISC-V, `mmio_write8` of `0x1_48` writes the byte `0x48` (`H`) and")
    strs_push(l, "nothing else — the truncation is the width's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** A board fact needing a change outside its description; a")
    strs_push(l, "program whose output differs between the two boards for anything but its device addresses; a stack")
    strs_push(l, "measured above its stated bound on either.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As built (N86, 2026-10-04).** Three amendments. **RISC-V is built where `clang` can build it**:")
    strs_push(l, "Apple's `clang` has no RISC-V code generator, so the host refuses the target by name before")
    strs_push(l, "compiling (`-print-targets` asked), and the evidence is built and run in `nazm-qemu:n86`, whose")
    strs_push(l, "Debian `clang` has one. **The linker script names more than it did**: RISC-V's small-data sections,")
    strs_push(l, "and `/DISCARD/` for unwind tables — at `-O2` an orphaned `.eh_frame` was placed at the load address")
    strs_push(l, "ahead of `_start`; AArch64's images were unaffected and its script gains the same lines. **The")
    strs_push(l, "hosted refusal (`N0392`) names both boards** in its help. Epoch 26 and runtime ABI 13 as stated;")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm inspect` gains `toolchain.boards`, additive.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.88 Assurance profiles v3: contracts, obligations and what each one's status is — N87, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Areas 19 and 20 are PARTIAL: `critical` and `cyber` are restriction rules")
    strs_push(l, "over effects, spawning, foreign calls, recursion, allocation and locked builds, and a profile report")
    strs_push(l, "names the rule a program broke. Neither can say what a function *promises*, and neither can say, of")
    strs_push(l, "the places a program may fail, which are proved not to, which are checked as the program runs, and")
    strs_push(l, "which nobody knows. This milestone adds **contracts** to the language and an **obligation report** to")
    strs_push(l, "the tooling, and states, for each obligation, which of the three it is. It is profile enforcement and")
    strs_push(l, "evidence for a reviewer; it is not certification, and §7.49's disclaimer stands in full.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Contracts.** A function may state preconditions and postconditions after its effect set:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn isqrt(n: Int) -> Int ! {}")
    strs_push(l, "    requires n >= 0")
    strs_push(l, "    ensures result >= 0 && result * result <= n")
    strs_push(l, "{ … }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`requires E` and `ensures E` may each be written any number of times, in that order; each `E` is a")
    strs_push(l, "`Bool` expression over the parameters (and, in `ensures`, `result`, the value being returned),")
    strs_push(l, "literals, arithmetic, comparison, `&&`, `||`, `!`, and calls of functions that declare `! {}`. Nothing")
    strs_push(l, "else: no effect, no capability, no allocation (a contract that could fail for want of memory would")
    strs_push(l, "be a contract about memory) — each refused at the clause (`N0614`). `result` outside an `ensures` is an")
    strs_push(l, "ordinary name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a contract means.** Every `requires` is evaluated, in order, when the function is entered,")
    strs_push(l, "after its arguments; every `ensures` when it returns, on every path, with `result` the returned")
    strs_push(l, "value. A clause that is false fails the call — `N0410` for a precondition, `N0411` for a")
    strs_push(l, "postcondition — at the clause, through the failure path every other failure takes: status 2 natively,")
    strs_push(l, "the same diagnostic from `nazm run`. A clause that itself fails (an overflow inside it) fails the call")
    strs_push(l, "with that failure. Contracts are never compiled out: a program with contracts means the same under")
    strs_push(l, "every backend, optimisation level and profile.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the compiler proves.** One thing, exactly: a call whose arguments are all integer or boolean")
    strs_push(l, "literals is checked against the callee's `requires` at compile time by evaluating each clause. False")
    strs_push(l, "is `N0615` at the call — it would fail every time it ran; true makes that call's obligation **proved**.")
    strs_push(l, "No other call is reasoned about.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Obligations, and their three statuses.** `nazm check --obligations` prints `nazm.obligations/1`: for")
    strs_push(l, "each function, each obligation with its kind, its span and its status —")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **proved**: discharged at compile time, with the witness (a literal call's evaluated clause; an")
    strs_push(l, "  operation on two literals whose result the checker computed);")
    strs_push(l, "- **checked**: not proved, and checked when the program runs — every contract clause, every")
    strs_push(l, "  arithmetic operation that can overflow or divide by zero, every index and every allocation, since")
    strs_push(l, "  Nazm checks all of them;")
    strs_push(l, "- **unknown**: nothing about it is decided here — a call through a function value, whose callee and")
    strs_push(l, "  so whose contract are not known (N50), and every foreign call (C's behaviour, N42).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The kinds: `precondition`, `postcondition`, `call-precondition` (one per call of a function with a")
    strs_push(l, "`requires`), `overflow`, `division`, `index`, `allocation`, `indirect-call`, `foreign-call`. The report")
    strs_push(l, "is deterministic and states, as its first field, that it is compiler evidence and not certification.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Profiles.** `critical` gains `contracts-hold`: no `call-precondition` may be refuted (already")
    strs_push(l, "`N0615`), and every `unknown` obligation is a witness the profile refuses (`N0510`), so a `critical`")
    strs_push(l, "program's obligations are each proved or checked. `cyber` gains `no-unknown-calls` — the same refusal")
    strs_push(l, "of indirect and foreign calls — and keeps N47's locked build; constant-time checking stays RESEARCH:")
    strs_push(l, "the one subset precise enough to state (no branch, index or division whose operand is derived from a")
    strs_push(l, "named secret) needs secrets in the type system, which N80's provenance tracks only to sinks.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Who owns what.** The parser owns the clauses' syntax; the checker owns their typing and the literal")
    strs_push(l, "proof; Core IR lowering owns their meaning, as ordinary Core IR — a clause is a `Bool` expression and a")
    strs_push(l, "call of an internal `contract_failed` built-in on its negation — so the interpreter, MIR and both")
    strs_push(l, "backends run them with no new node; `nazm-core` owns the obligation census, read off Core IR.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** Semantic epoch `26 → 27` (two clause forms, three codes). Interface schema")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.interface/9 → 10`: an export's contracts are part of what a caller's literal proof and")
    strs_push(l, "obligation report read. Runtime ABI unchanged: a contract failure is the existing failure path. Core")
    strs_push(l, "IR and MIR print schemas unchanged (an internal built-in). `nazm.obligations/1` new, with its schema.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** `isqrt(-4)` is `N0615` at compile time; `isqrt(x)` with `x` negative at run time")
    strs_push(l, "is `N0410` at the `requires`. **Boundary example.** `isqrt(0)` is proved and returns `0`, its `ensures`")
    strs_push(l, "holding as `0 * 0 <= 0`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** Loop invariants and ranges as declarations, initialisation (every Nazm binding is")
    strs_push(l, "initialised by construction), a solver or any proof beyond literal evaluation, separation logic,")
    strs_push(l, "constant time, and any claim of absence of runtime error beyond the census's own `proved` entries.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** A contract a backend or the interpreter does not run; a")
    strs_push(l, "`proved` obligation that fails at run time; an obligation the census omits — a trap site not in it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As built (N87, 2026-10-04).** Four amendments. **The census is its own command**, `nazm")
    strs_push(l, "obligations FILE [--json]`, beside `nazm core-ir`, rather than a flag of `nazm check`: it reads Core")
    strs_push(l, "IR, which only a program that checks has. **The interface carries a count**, `requires`, not the")
    strs_push(l, "clauses: the literal proof stays within a module, and an importer needs only to know a call is an")
    strs_push(l, "obligation. **A contract call is `pure` by its signature** — a declared `! {}`, not foreign — so a")
    strs_push(l, "callee whose interface came from the cache answers as the same callee checked from source. **The")
    strs_push(l, "formatter prints the clauses as the header's**, one level in, the body's `{` back at the function's")
    strs_push(l, "level. The census's kinds and statuses are as stated; a `proved` overflow or division is one on")
    strs_push(l, "literals the census computed, the only proof it makes beyond the checker's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.89 Accelerators v2: maps of one or two sequences, reductions, and a numeric oracle — N88, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Area 21 is PARTIAL: N67's `nazm accel` runs one idiom — a pure")
    strs_push(l, "`(Int) -> Int` map over one sequence — on one GPU through one deprecated API. A user who needs two")
    strs_push(l, "sequences combined, or a total of what was mapped, cannot say it. This milestone widens what a user")
    strs_push(l, "can express to a small compute subset with one meaning everywhere, and holds the device to an")
    strs_push(l, "oracle on generated inputs rather than on chosen ones.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a kernel is.** As N67, plus one shape: a kernel is a pure function of **one or two** `Int`s")
    strs_push(l, "returning an `Int` — `(Int) -> Int`, a *map*, or `(Int, Int) -> Int`, a *zip* — reaching only")
    strs_push(l, "functions of the same kind. A zip takes two input sequences of the same length (`--input A --input")
    strs_push(l, "B`); different lengths are refused before any device (`N0394`). Eligibility, the checked arithmetic,")
    strs_push(l, "the lowest-failing-index rule, the 8,000,000-element cap and the explicit transfers are N67's,")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged; a zip's report names both inputs' transfers.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Reductions.** `--reduce add|min|max` folds the kernel's results, in index order, into one `Int`:")
    strs_push(l, "`add` is `ints_sum`'s fold — checked, failing with `N0400` where a running sum would overflow, even")
    strs_push(l, "if the total would fit — and `min` and `max` cannot fail (an empty sequence reduces to `None`,")
    strs_push(l, "printed as `null`). The fold runs on the host, after the one device-to-host transfer, and the report")
    strs_push(l, "says so and times it: its meaning is a sequential fold's, which a device's tree of partial sums would")
    strs_push(l, "change for `add`; for `min` and `max` it is a choice of where, stated.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**One meaning, three ways.** Every run is held, unless `--no-check`, to the interpreter applying the")
    strs_push(l, "same function to the same elements and folding the same way; a disagreement is a failure of the run,")
    strs_push(l, "never a result. **The oracle on generated inputs:** a fuzzer generates pure kernels over `+ - * / %`,")
    strs_push(l, "comparisons, `if` and literals at the edges of `Int`, and elements across the range, and compares")
    strs_push(l, "the device's results and failure (index and code) with the interpreter's and with an independent")
    strs_push(l, "computation in Rust's 128-bit arithmetic.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Providers.** OpenCL on the Apple M1 Pro's GPU, as N67. A second provider was sought and is not")
    strs_push(l, "available on this host — no Metal compiler (`xcrun metal` absent without Xcode), no Vulkan loader —")
    strs_push(l, "so Metal and SPIR-V stay designed, and the row says BLOCKED for want of the toolchain, not of a")
    strs_push(l, "design. **Vector operations in LIR** — a vector type and operations the backends lower — stay")
    strs_push(l, "DESIGNED: the one vectorised loop (N66) is a pattern, and is reported as one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** No language change: semantic epoch, interface, runtime ABI and IR schemas unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.accel/1 → /2`: `inputs` (one or two, each with its bytes and time), `reduce` (the operation,")
    strs_push(l, "where and how long, its value). `nazm.kernel/1` keeps its form; a zip's kernel has two parameters.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** A zip over inputs of 3 and 4 elements is refused before a device is touched.")
    strs_push(l, "**Boundary example.** `--reduce add` over `[i64::MAX, 1, -1]` fails with `N0400` at the second")
    strs_push(l, "element, as `ints_sum` does, though the total fits.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** A generated kernel whose device result or failure differs from")
    strs_push(l, "the interpreter's; a reduction whose value differs from the interpreter's fold.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As built (N88, 2026-10-04).** As stated, with two notes. The host program now takes `kernel.cl")
    strs_push(l, "output.bin input.bin [input2.bin]`, one buffer per input, and its JSON's `to_device_bytes` counts")
    strs_push(l, "both. The numeric oracle is an ignored test of 40 generated kernels of 200 elements each, seeded and")
    strs_push(l, "deterministic, run on the M1 Pro: every one agreed with the interpreter and with 128-bit arithmetic,")
    strs_push(l, "values and failures alike. No schema file existed for `nazm.accel/1`; `/2` is documented in")
    strs_push(l, "`spec.md` and the matrix, not given one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.90 Workspace editing: renaming what a project exports, and applying a plan stale-safely — N89, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Area 25 is PARTIAL: rename covers locals and private definitions, and an")
    strs_push(l, "exported entity is refused because \"a module no open program loads may use it\" (§7.20) — so the")
    strs_push(l, "one rename a maintainer most needs, of a function a project's other modules call, is the one the")
    strs_push(l, "tools cannot do. And a `nazm.patch/1` plan is a proposal nothing applies. This milestone makes a")
    strs_push(l, "**workspace** the unit of completeness, renames exported entities within one, and applies a plan")
    strs_push(l, "only to the exact bytes it was computed from.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a workspace is.** A source root that is *declared* — a `nazm.root` marker, or `--source-root`")
    strs_push(l, "— and every `.nz` file under it, found by walking the directory (hidden directories and `target/`")
    strs_push(l, "excepted, as the CLI's other walks except them). Every one of those files is analysed as a root, as")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm check` would analyse it, over the editor's unsaved buffers where it has them. A file outside")
    strs_push(l, "the root, and a package's dependency, are not in it. Without a declared root there is no workspace,")
    strs_push(l, "and an exported rename is refused as before.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Which exported renames are complete.** Within a workspace, every module that can name an exported")
    strs_push(l, "entity is a file under the root that imports its module — and every such file is analysed. So an")
    strs_push(l, "exported function, record, enum, field, variant or payload field may be renamed when: its declaring")
    strs_push(l, "file is under the root; every compilation of the workspace that contains it is clean; and the root is")
    strs_push(l, "not a **library package** — a `nazm.toml` with no `main` — whose exported API is what *other*")
    strs_push(l, "packages import, which no walk of this root finds. That last case is refused by name")
    strs_push(l, "(`Refusal::PackageApi`): a library's API changes by its author's decision, never by a rename.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The plan.** The entity is found in each compilation by its declaration's place (file and bytes) —")
    strs_push(l, "its session-local id means nothing outside one compilation — and its occurrences, across every file")
    strs_push(l, "of every compilation that contains it, are the edits: the declaration and every use, each spelled as")
    strs_push(l, "the old name, merged across compilations, one `FileEdit` per file, each bound to that file's exact")
    strs_push(l, "text and its editor version (or, for a file not open, its disk bytes). The candidate workspace —")
    strs_push(l, "every edited file replaced in memory, nothing written — is re-analysed in full: every compilation")
    strs_push(l, "that contains an edited file must be clean and partition its occurrences into entities exactly as")
    strs_push(l, "before, the edits accounted for. Any difference refuses the whole plan.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applying.** `nazm patch apply PLAN.json` applies a `nazm.patch/1` plan to disk, all or nothing: every")
    strs_push(l, "file's bytes must hash to the plan's `digest` and hold each edit's `expected` bytes at its place; if")
    strs_push(l, "any file differs the command refuses, naming it, and writes nothing. The edits are written through a")
    strs_push(l, "temporary file and a rename per file. The language server applies nothing: an editor applies a")
    strs_push(l, "rename's edits, and the protocol's edit is offered only when every file it touches is open at the")
    strs_push(l, "version the plan was computed from — a closed file's edit goes through `nazm patch`, whose plan binds")
    strs_push(l, "its bytes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What does not change.** The language, the compiler, every schema but one addition: `nazm.patch/1`")
    strs_push(l, "already carries several files; `apply` reads it. No semantic epoch, interface, runtime or IR change.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** In a library package, renaming its `pub fn parse` is refused — other packages'")
    strs_push(l, "uses cannot be found. **Boundary example.** Renaming a `pub fn` used by three modules of a workspace")
    strs_push(l, "edits all four files; a fifth file edited after planning makes `apply` refuse and write nothing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** A workspace file that uses the entity and is not edited; a plan")
    strs_push(l, "`apply` writes to a file whose bytes differ from the plan's; a rename that changes what any")
    strs_push(l, "compilation of the workspace means.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As built (N89, 2026-10-04).** Two amendments. **A plan names a file outside the requesting")
    strs_push(l, "root's compilation by its path from the workspace root** — `nazm.patch/1`'s `path` was always")
    strs_push(l, "root-relative, and a workspace rename's other files are under the same root. **`apply` takes")
    strs_push(l, "`--base`**, the directory the plan's paths are relative to, the current directory by default, and")
    strs_push(l, "refuses any path that leaves it. `nazm.patch/1` gains the reason `package_api`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.91 Packages v3: a backtracking resolver that explains itself, and `nazm update` — N90, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Area 26 is PARTIAL. N56's registry chooses each package's highest version")
    strs_push(l, "satisfying the requirements it has seen, round by round, and refuses (`N0513`) the first time a")
    strs_push(l, "choice leaves some package with no version — even when an older version of the package that made the")
    strs_push(l, "demand would have satisfied everyone. \"No backtracking\" was its stated limit. And a lockfile can only")
    strs_push(l, "be written afresh (`nazm lock`); nothing updates one deliberately.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Resolution, settled.** The registry's packages are chosen by a **backtracking search**: packages in")
    strs_push(l, "name order; for each, its published, non-yanked versions highest first — a version the lockfile")
    strs_push(l, "records first, while it satisfies — and each candidate kept only if it satisfies every requirement")
    strs_push(l, "the current choice places on it; a candidate's own requirements then join the set, and the search")
    strs_push(l, "goes on. A dead end undoes the last choice and tries the next candidate. The answer is the first")
    strs_push(l, "complete assignment in that order: deterministic, the same for the same registry and manifests, and")
    strs_push(l, "the newest a lockfile allows. One version per package name, as before: the language has one module")
    strs_push(l, "per path, and two versions of one package would be two modules a program cannot tell apart.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**When there is none.** The search is bounded — at most 10,000 candidates tried — and a failure is")
    strs_push(l, "`N0513` with an **explanation**: the package that could not be chosen, every requirement on it at the")
    strs_push(l, "deepest point the search reached, and which package (at which version) placed each. A search that")
    strs_push(l, "runs out of its bound says so, rather than claiming the registry unsatisfiable.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**`nazm update [NAME…]`.** Re-resolves with the lockfile's preferences dropped — for every registry")
    strs_push(l, "package, or only for those named — writes the lockfile, and prints each change, `name old → new`.")
    strs_push(l, "Without names it is `nazm lock` with no preference; `nazm build --locked` is unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** Signatures and trust roots (no signing implementation is available offline here, and a")
    strs_push(l, "digest is not a signature), a remote registry, pre-release versions and features, multi-root")
    strs_push(l, "workspaces, build scripts (prohibited by absence: there is no construct for one). Each is a named")
    strs_push(l, "limit, not a silent gap.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** No language change. `nazm.lock/1` unchanged: what it records is the same, only how its")
    strs_push(l, "versions were found changes. The registry layout is unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** `a` requires `b ^1` and `c ^1`; every `b 1.x` but `1.0.0` requires `c ^2`: N56")
    strs_push(l, "refused; N90 chooses `b 1.0.0`. **Boundary example.** `a` requires `b =2.0.0` and `c` requires")
    strs_push(l, "`b ^1`: refused, the explanation naming both requirements and who placed them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** Two runs over the same inputs choosing differently; a refusal")
    strs_push(l, "where an assignment exists within the bound; an `update` that changes a package not named.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As built (N90, 2026-10-04).** Three precisions. **A requirement placed on a package already chosen")
    strs_push(l, "is checked again** at every step, since a later choice can constrain an earlier one; such a dead")
    strs_push(l, "end, like a package with no fitting version, is a candidate for the explanation. **`update NAME`")
    strs_push(l, "keeps every other package's lockfile preference**: another package changes only when the named one's")
    strs_push(l, "new version requires it — the exception the last paragraph's \"not named\" admits. **An unknown name")
    strs_push(l, "is `N0501`**, the code for a package that is not there. A path package's requirements are placed")
    strs_push(l, "by `` `name` ``, a registry package's by `` `name` version ``.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.92 Debugger and profiler v3: lexical scopes, Cranelift's DWARF, and sampling — N91, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the records. Area 27 is PARTIAL: an LLVM `--debug` build has line tables and")
    strs_push(l, "`Int`/`Bool`/`Str` variables, but every variable is visible for its whole function; a Cranelift")
    strs_push(l, "build refuses `--debug` (BLOCKED in N48 on \"no DWARF through the API this backend uses\"); and")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm profile` counts events, never samples. This milestone gives bindings their blocks, gives")
    strs_push(l, "Cranelift line tables, and samples a run — each claim exercised by a real debugger or sampler.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Lexical scopes (LLVM).** MIR records, for each `let`, the source block it is in")
    strs_push(l, "(`LocalDecl.scope`; `None` for a parameter or a binding of the function's own body). The emitter's")
    strs_push(l, "variable marker carries that block's first and last positions; `crate::debug` makes one")
    strs_push(l, "`DILexicalBlock` per distinct block, nested by containment, gives each variable its block, and gives")
    strs_push(l, "each instruction the innermost block containing its position. A debugger shows a branch's binding")
    strs_push(l, "inside the branch and not before it. MIR's digest and printed form do not include the scope — it is")
    strs_push(l, "display, like a local's name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Cranelift's DWARF.** No Cranelift API writes DWARF, but Cranelift carries a source location on")
    strs_push(l, "each instruction it is given one for and reports the code ranges each covers. The backend now sets")
    strs_push(l, "one per MIR statement and terminator (the LLVM emitter's positions), and writes DWARF 4 with `gimli`")
    strs_push(l, "— the version Cranelift itself depends on — into the object: a compile unit, a subprogram per MIR")
    strs_push(l, "function, and a line program whose prologue carries the declaration's line and ends")
    strs_push(l, "(`prologue_end`) where the first statement's code begins, a gap at line 0. Addresses are")
    strs_push(l, "relocations: against the function's symbol in ELF; in Mach-O against its section, with the object")
    strs_push(l, "address in place, as `dsymutil` maps addresses through the debug map. **Variables are not")
    strs_push(l, "described** under Cranelift: where a value lives is reported only through value labels this backend")
    strs_push(l, "does not track. A Cranelift debug object is never taken from the cache: its lines are a function of")
    strs_push(l, "the source's text, which no MIR digest is.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Sampling.** `nazm profile --sample [--interval-ms N] FILE` builds with `--debug`, runs the program")
    strs_push(l, "under the host's sampler, and attributes each sample to its innermost frame: a Nazm function and")
    strs_push(l, "`.nz` line (line 0 for code no statement made); the runtime (`nz.*` code without a line); foreign")
    strs_push(l, "code linked into the program; or the system — each system frame named, and those in a fixed list of")
    strs_push(l, "waits (locks, condition variables, sleeps, `kevent`, Mach messages, reads) counted as **blocked**.")
    strs_push(l, "The sampler is macOS's `sample`, the one available here; a host without it is refused before anything")
    strs_push(l, "is built — never a profile without the samples asked for. `nazm.profile/1 → /2`: the same fields,")
    strs_push(l, "and `samples`, `null` unless sampled. Allocations and scheduler events stay the runtime's own counts.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Owners.** MIR lowering owns where a binding is visible; `nazm-lir::debug` owns LLVM's metadata;")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-codegen-clif::dwarf` owns Cranelift's; the CLI owns running the sampler and attributing its")
    strs_push(l, "report. No language, runtime, ABI or schema change but the profile's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** Semantic epoch, interface, runtime ABI, Core IR/MIR/LIR print schemas unchanged (the")
    strs_push(l, "scope is display only). `nazm.profile/2`. The Cranelift backend's version string gains ` debug` for")
    strs_push(l, "a debug build, and a debug build has no object key.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** Under Cranelift, `info locals` says `No locals.` — not a wrong value. **Boundary")
    strs_push(l, "example.** At a function's first statement, a binding of a later branch is not in scope; at the")
    strs_push(l, "branch's statement, it is, with its value.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** Cranelift variables; records, enums, sequences and closures described; DAP; a sampler")
    strs_push(l, "on Linux (no `perf` in the images); timelines and event traces. Area 27 stays PARTIAL.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** A breakpoint by line landing on another line; a variable shown")
    strs_push(l, "outside its block; a sample attributed to a function that was not on the stack.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.93 Performance evidence v2: a register of every claim, and a benchmark that says what it measured — N92, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Area 28 is PARTIAL. `docs/internal/performance-log.md` holds some seventy measured")
    strs_push(l, "sections; a few are regenerated by a command (`cargo xtask bench`, an ignored measurement test), most")
    strs_push(l, "were measured once by a method described in prose, and nothing says which is which. A claim nobody")
    strs_push(l, "can regenerate is an anecdote with a date. `nazm.bench/1` records a median and a minimum, the host's")
    strs_push(l, "name and its CPU count (empty on Linux), and one C and one Python reference.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The register.** `bench/claims.toml` holds one entry per measured section of `performance.md`, by")
    strs_push(l, "its exact heading, with a status:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **reproducible** — `how` names the command that regenerates the numbers: a `cargo xtask` command")
    strs_push(l, "  or a test the tree contains (`cargo test … -- --ignored NAME`), and `metric` what it prints;")
    strs_push(l, "- **dated** — a measurement of the implementation as it was on that date, its method in the prose,")
    strs_push(l, "  superseded or kept as history: not a current claim about the tree, and said so;")
    strs_push(l, "- **unreproduced** — a current claim whose method no command reproduces.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A gate in `cargo xtask check` (**performance claims**) refuses a measured heading with no entry, an")
    strs_push(l, "entry whose heading is gone, an unknown status, and a reproducible entry whose test or command does")
    strs_push(l, "not exist. The gate checks that a command *exists*, not that its numbers still hold: running every")
    strs_push(l, "measurement is the benchmark's job, contained, not a check's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The benchmark, v2.** `nazm.bench/2` adds, to every field of `/1`: a machine fingerprint (CPU model,")
    strs_push(l, "logical CPUs — read on Linux as on macOS — memory, kernel); for each measurement every run, and p90,")
    strs_push(l, "maximum and the median absolute deviation beside the minimum and median; each native executable's")
    strs_push(l, "size in bytes; the noise floor — the `floor` program's native median — named as the floor under")
    strs_push(l, "which no difference is claimed; and the references that were not measured, each with its reason. A")
    strs_push(l, "reference must be the Nazm program statement for statement and say whether its arithmetic is checked:")
    strs_push(l, "`sieve.c` (no), `sieve.py` (unbounded), and new — `sieve.rs`, built with `-O` and")
    strs_push(l, "`-C overflow-checks=on`, growable and bounds-checked like `Ints` (checked: yes); `sieve.go`, bounds-")
    strs_push(l, "checked, wrapping (checked: no), measured where Go is installed. Zig is not installed here and is")
    strs_push(l, "recorded as absent.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Owners.** `xtask` owns the register's gate and the benchmark; `docs/internal/performance-log.md` owns the")
    strs_push(l, "claims' prose; nothing in the compiler changes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** `nazm.bench/1 → /2` (additive). No language, IR, runtime or schema change elsewhere.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** A new `### … — N93, measured …` section without a register entry fails `cargo")
    strs_push(l, "xtask check`. **Boundary example.** A dated entry stays valid when the code it measured is gone: it")
    strs_push(l, "says it is history.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** Running every measurement on every change; energy (no counter is readable here without")
    strs_push(l, "privileges); a cross-host comparison, which `--check` still refuses. Area 28 is VERIFIED only if every")
    strs_push(l, "current claim — every entry not dated — is reproducible.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** A reproducible entry whose command no longer prints its metric;")
    strs_push(l, "a current claim filed as dated to escape the gate.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.94 Coverage-guided fuzzing: a fuzzer that keeps what reaches new code, contained, replayed by the suite — N93, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Area 30's fuzzing half is PARTIAL: N73's two fuzzers are seeded and blind —")
    strs_push(l, "a mutated input is run and thrown away whether or not it reached anything new — and \"not")
    strs_push(l, "coverage-guided\" is the named limit, `cargo fuzz` needing `libfuzzer-sys`, which is not in this")
    strs_push(l, "machine's offline crate cache.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The fuzzer.** `fuzz/` is a crate of its own workspace, as cargo-fuzz's are. Its code under test —")
    strs_push(l, "the compiler's crates — is built with LLVM's SanitizerCoverage in `trace-pc-guard` mode, a stable")
    strs_push(l, "`rustc` option (`-C passes=sancov-module` with its `llvm-args`); the callbacks that count edges are")
    strs_push(l, "C (`fuzz/cov.c`), compiled without instrumentation. An input is **kept** when it reaches an edge no")
    strs_push(l, "earlier input reached, and inputs are mutated from what is kept: byte edits, tokens of the language")
    strs_push(l, "inserted whole, lines duplicated, deleted, swapped or spliced in from another kept input, and names")
    strs_push(l, "renamed everywhere — structure a byte flip rarely makes. Its one `unsafe` is reading the C counters,")
    strs_push(l, "outside the workspace whose lint forbids it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Targets.** The compiler's entry points, in process: `front` (parse and check: a diagnostic is the")
    strs_push(l, "answer to any input, a panic a defect); `lower` (Core IR and MIR for every program the checker")
    strs_push(l, "accepts, and **MIR's validator must accept what lowering produced** — validator fuzzing); `run` (the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter under its step and depth budgets); `manifest` (a package manifest and every version")
    strs_push(l, "requirement in it). A panic is shrunk by lines and recorded; the campaign fails.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Budgets and replay.** `cargo xtask contained fuzz [SECONDS] [TARGET…]` runs each target for")
    strs_push(l, "SECONDS (300 by default) in the contained runner, seeded from its persistent corpus and the")
    strs_push(l, "repository's programs, and exports each target's **minimised** corpus — the smallest set of kept")
    strs_push(l, "inputs, chosen greedily, that reaches every edge reached — and a report, one `nazm.fuzz/1` line per")
    strs_push(l, "target. The minimised inputs are committed to `fuzz/corpus/TARGET/`, and the ordinary suite replays")
    strs_push(l, "every one through the same entry point (`crates/nazm-cli/tests/fuzz_replay.rs`): the evidence a")
    strs_push(l, "release carries is that replay, and the campaign that grew it is rerun by one command.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Who owns what.** `fuzz/` owns the engine and the coverage; `xtask` owns the contained campaign;")
    strs_push(l, "the suite owns the replay. The compiler is unchanged; a defect found is fixed where it lives, with")
    strs_push(l, "a regression input in the corpus and a mutant.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** None change: no language, IR, runtime or schema. `nazm.fuzz/1` is a report line.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** An input that panics the checker fails the campaign and is written, shrunk, to")
    strs_push(l, "the report. **Boundary example.** An input the checker refuses is a kept input when its diagnostic")
    strs_push(l, "path is new — refusals are coverage too.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** Sanitizers (no `unsafe` in the compiler to run them on; ASan on a nightly is not this")
    strs_push(l, "toolchain), Miri over the whole suite, Loom (not in the offline cache), backend and FFI differential")
    strs_push(l, "fuzzing beyond N73's generator, registry archives, and a contract VM. Area 30's fuzzing half is")
    strs_push(l, "VERIFIED for the four targets at the stated budget, not for those.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** A corpus input the replay passes and the campaign's target")
    strs_push(l, "panics on; a \"minimised\" corpus that reaches fewer edges than the kept set.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.95 Reproducibility and provenance v2: a stated model, signed in-toto statements, and an SBOM — N94, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Area 32 is PARTIAL: N73 writes `nazm.provenance/1` and runs a local command")
    strs_push(l, "as an \"attestation\" whose output Nazm neither signs nor checks; reproducibility was measured, not")
    strs_push(l, "stated as a model; there is no SBOM.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The reproducibility model.** Five claims, each with its own evidence, none implied by another:")
    strs_push(l, "1. *Identical input* — the same source, toolchain, target, options and environment give the same")
    strs_push(l, "   executable, object, provenance and SBOM bytes, under either backend.")
    strs_push(l, "2. *Across directories* — the same, built from two checkouts in different places: no absolute path,")
    strs_push(l, "   time or host name enters an artefact Nazm writes.")
    strs_push(l, "3. *Archive* — a release archive (N75) is the same bytes for the same revision.")
    strs_push(l, "4. *Offline* — a locked package build needs nothing but the local registry and the toolchain.")
    strs_push(l, "5. *Across toolchains* — **not** byte identity. Two C compilers are compared and every difference")
    strs_push(l, "   classified (N73's measurement: the program's objects equal, the runtime's differing by a symbol")
    strs_push(l, "   type at `-O0` and by layout at `-O2`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Signed statements.** `nazm attest sign --key KEY PROVENANCE ARTIFACT…` wraps a provenance record in")
    strs_push(l, "an **in-toto Statement v1** — `_type` `https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1`, one `subject` per artefact")
    strs_push(l, "with its `blake3` digest, `predicateType` `urn:nazm:provenance:1`, the record as `predicate` — after")
    strs_push(l, "checking every artefact's digest is one the record names; then signs it with OpenSSH's `ssh-keygen -Y")
    strs_push(l, "sign` (the SSHSIG format git signs commits with), namespace `nazm-attestation`. `nazm attest verify")
    strs_push(l, "--allowed-signers FILE --identity ID STATEMENT ARTIFACT…` succeeds only when the signature verifies")
    strs_push(l, "for that identity, the statement is well formed, and every artefact's digest is a subject's. Keys")
    strs_push(l, "and trust are the user's: Nazm holds none, publishes nothing, and logs nothing to a transparency log —")
    strs_push(l, "this is Sigstore's statement shape signed offline, not Sigstore.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**SBOM.** `nazm build --sbom FILE` writes a **CycloneDX 1.5** JSON document, deterministic: the")
    strs_push(l, "output as the metadata component with its BLAKE3 hash; one component per package (with its version,")
    strs_push(l, "`pkg:generic/NAME@VERSION` and BLAKE3 digest), per source module (a `file` component with its hash),")
    strs_push(l, "and for the runtime and its ABI revision; the tools — `nazm`, its Cranelift, the C compiler as it")
    strs_push(l, "reports itself. Every package of the build is in it, and nothing else.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Owners.** `nazm-cli`'s `provenance` owns the record and the SBOM; a new `attest` module owns")
    strs_push(l, "statements and their verification, through `ssh-keygen`. No compiler semantics change.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** No language, IR, runtime or interface change. New output formats: in-toto Statement v1")
    strs_push(l, "with predicate `urn:nazm:provenance:1`; CycloneDX 1.5. `nazm.provenance/1` unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** Verifying with the artefact edited after signing fails, naming the digest; a")
    strs_push(l, "statement signed by a key the allowed-signers file does not list for the identity fails.")
    strs_push(l, "**Boundary example.** Signing refuses an artefact the provenance does not name, before any key is used.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** A transparency log, keyless signing, SLSA levels claimed, rebuilds on several")
    strs_push(l, "independent machines (one host and one Linux image are what exist here), and dependency-origin")
    strs_push(l, "verification beyond N56's registry digests.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** An artefact that verifies after a byte of it changed; two")
    strs_push(l, "builds of identical input with different bytes; an SBOM that omits a package the build linked.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.96 The platform matrix v2: every cell one of three answers — N95, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Area 33 is PARTIAL: seven targets are accepted, their evidence spread over")
    strs_push(l, "N57, N62, N64 and N86 in prose, and nothing holds the documented matrix to the compiler or says what")
    strs_push(l, "CPU an object is for.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The matrix.** One table in `nazm-lir` (`backend::SUPPORT`) gives, for every accepted triple and")
    strs_push(l, "each backend, exactly one of **run-verified** (programs built for it ran here — host, Rosetta, the")
    strs_push(l, "Linux image, QEMU, Node — and agreed with the interpreter; the evidence named: a test, or a contained")
    strs_push(l, "command), **compile-only** (objects built and read from their headers; nothing ran) or")
    strs_push(l, "**unsupported** (refused by name, with why). It records each target's CPU identity — the C compiler")
    strs_push(l, "driver's default CPU for the triple under LLVM, the baseline ISA under Cranelift, which detects")
    strs_push(l, "nothing of the building host — and what a debugger has been shown to do. `nazm inspect` prints it;")
    strs_push(l, "the capability matrix's table is held to it cell for cell by a test, which also requires every")
    strs_push(l, "accepted target to have a row, every non-refusal to name evidence the tree holds, and each LLVM CPU")
    strs_push(l, "to be what the driver resolves. No cell may say \"supported\".")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Non-goals, decided.** Windows (no linker, SDK or machine here; no runtime port), 32-bit hosted")
    strs_push(l, "targets (`Int` is 64-bit; hosted layouts assume 64-bit pointers — wasm32 is the one 32-bit target,")
    strs_push(l, "freestanding) and big-endian targets (nothing here runs one; layouts and the DWARF writer assume")
    strs_push(l, "little-endian), each with its reason in the same table.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** None: no language, IR, ABI or object change; the CPU is recorded and checked, not pinned")
    strs_push(l, "by a new flag, so no object's bytes move. `nazm.inspect/1` gains `toolchain.support` and")
    strs_push(l, "`toolchain.non_goals`, additive.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** A row claiming x86_64 Linux run-verified fails the test — no x86_64 Linux")
    strs_push(l, "machine has run anything. **Boundary example.** A clang whose default CPU for a triple changes fails")
    strs_push(l, "the CPU test: the identity is then stale, and the table must change with it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** An x86_64 Linux runner, Windows, CPU-feature selection, sysroots, a bundled linker.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** A run-verified cell whose named test does not run a program for")
    strs_push(l, "that target; a target the compiler accepts with no row.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.97 Smart contracts v2: generated sequences on the reference VMs, and what stays blocked — N96, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Area 34 is PARTIAL: the EVM (N70) and WebAssembly (N71) backends were each held")
    strs_push(l, "to the simulator on one written sequence; sBPF execution is BLOCKED (N72); the model has no events,")
    strs_push(l, "external calls, assets as types, or gas beyond a bound.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What this adds.** Generated evidence, not new semantics. Transaction sequences are generated from")
    strs_push(l, "the contract's own facts (`nazm.contract/1`: each entrypoint and its arguments) — seeded, the same on")
    strs_push(l, "every host — with callers among the owner and two others and arguments from the edges of `Int`. Each")
    strs_push(l, "sequence is run by the simulator and by both reference VMs: py-evm (Shanghai, `nazm-evm:n70`) and the")
    strs_push(l, "reference WebAssembly host under Node (`nazm-wasm:n64`). Every transaction's outcome and revert code")
    strs_push(l, "and the final state must agree; every committed state must keep the conserved quantity; every EVM")
    strs_push(l, "transaction must use no more gas than its entrypoint's stated bound.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What stays as it is, and why.** sBPF: no sBPF toolchain, validator or emulator exists on this")
    strs_push(l, "machine — this clang has no BPF target at all, and no Solana tool or crate is installed — so no object")
    strs_push(l, "or run is claimed, and the blocker is external and named. Events, external calls, reentrancy, assets")
    strs_push(l, "as linear types, metering beyond N70's bound, a chain's own WebAssembly host and storage migrations")
    strs_push(l, "beyond `--upgrade-check` are not in the model: adding them is a language change this milestone does")
    strs_push(l, "not make. Area 34 stays PARTIAL, and N100 says so.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** None change.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** A backend whose division truncated differently from the simulator's would")
    strs_push(l, "disagree on a generated `arith` with negative operands. **Boundary example.** `i64::MIN / -1` fails")
    strs_push(l, "with `N0400` in all three.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** A generated sequence on which a VM and the simulator disagree")
    strs_push(l, "while the written sequences agree — which is the point of generating them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.98 Formal semantics v2: statements, loops and recursion, bounded and machine-checked — N97, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. N61's formal core is expressions over `Int` and `Bool`; functions, loops and")
    strs_push(l, "mutation are \"not in the core\", and nothing is proved.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The proof assistant, chosen deliberately: none.** None is installed here — no Coq, Lean, Agda,")
    strs_push(l, "Isabelle, Dafny or SMT solver — and nothing can be installed offline. Proofs of progress and")
    strs_push(l, "preservation, effect soundness and explicit-flow properties are therefore **BLOCKED**, and nothing")
    strs_push(l, "here is called a proof. What extends is the executable model and its bounded, machine-checked")
    strs_push(l, "properties.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Phase A, as a model.** `nazm.formal-core/2` (`docs/internal/formal-core.md` §2, `nazm_formal::statements`):")
    strs_push(l, "`let mut`, assignment, `while`, `if` as a statement, `return`, and one recursive function `f(n: Int)`,")
    strs_push(l, "over the core's arithmetic and traps. Big-step with **fuel** — each loop turn and call spends one, 400")
    strs_push(l, "in all — and running out is no outcome: the semantics declines, since Nazm bounds neither iteration")
    strs_push(l, "nor recursion. Properties over **every** program of a stated bound of three families (loops of two")
    strs_push(l, "mutable bindings, branches with an early return, recursion built on `f(n − 1)`): S1 soundness —")
    strs_push(l, "never stuck; S2 determinism; S3 correspondence — Nazm's interpreter gives the same value or trap for")
    strs_push(l, "every program the semantics finishes; S4 the checker accepts every program of the bound.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not here.** Records, enums, strings and sequences in the model; Phase B (ownership and")
    strs_push(l, "reclamation, effects and capabilities, explicit flows) and Phase C (structured concurrency, Core/MIR")
    strs_push(l, "refinement); any property beyond the bound. The whole language is not formally verified, and nothing")
    strs_push(l, "says so.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** `nazm.formal-core/2` is new and contains `/1`, unchanged. Nothing in the compiler changes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** A loop that never ends within the fuel — `while 0 < x { x = x + 1; }` from 1 —")
    strs_push(l, "is out of fuel, and the interpreter is not asked. **Boundary example.** The same loop from `i64::MAX`")
    strs_push(l, "traps `N0400` on its first turn, in the model and the interpreter alike.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** A program of the bound the model and the interpreter answer")
    strs_push(l, "differently — which, as N61's first run did, may be an error in either.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.99 The compiler written in Nazm: parity measured, not reached — N98, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. The bootstrap is VERIFIED (C2 = C3, area 31), but the compiler written in")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm (`compiler/*.nz`) compiles a subset of the language, and \"the bootstrap subset\" has been a")
    strs_push(l, "standing limitation stated in prose, with no measure of which features it builds.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The parity record.** `compiler/parity/` holds one probe per feature, named by its dimension —")
    strs_push(l, "`syntax`, `types`, `failure`, `modules`, `closures`, `traits`, `effects`, `concurrency`, `contracts`,")
    strs_push(l, "`ffi` — each a program the reference compiler builds. A contained test builds every probe with the")
    strs_push(l, "reference (`nazm build`, run natively) and with `compiler/emit.nz` (built by the reference, its LLVM")
    strs_push(l, "IR linked by clang, run natively), and writes one verdict per probe: **equal** (the same exit status,")
    strs_push(l, "output and failure code), **refused** (the compiler written in Nazm does not build it: a gap, with the")
    strs_push(l, "code it gives), or **differs** (it builds something that behaves otherwise: a defect, which fails the")
    strs_push(l, "test whatever the record says). `compiler/parity.json` (`nazm.parity/1`) is that record, and the test")
    strs_push(l, "fails when it is not what the compilers do — so the record cannot go stale.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What this milestone does not do.** Port the missing features. Closures, traits, effects and")
    strs_push(l, "capabilities, concurrency, contracts, foreign declarations and `@std` are each a body of work in a")
    strs_push(l, "12,800-line compiler, and the acceptance criterion — the selfhost subset equal to the reference's")
    strs_push(l, "native subset — is **not met**. N98 makes the gap measured and gated, which is what an honest N100")
    strs_push(l, "needs to read.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** None. `nazm.parity/1` is a record.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** A probe the emitter refuses is a refusal, never counted as equal. **Boundary")
    strs_push(l, "example.** A failing probe — overflow, division by zero — is equal only when both exit with status 2")
    strs_push(l, "and name the same code.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** A probe recorded equal whose two executables behave differently")
    strs_push(l, "on another input: probes are single programs, and equality is of those programs only.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.100 The interactive tier v2: the JIT question answered, and the tiers held to one answer — N99, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. N65 verified the REPL, `nazm comptime` (isolated by the authority model and")
    strs_push(l, "the interpreter's budgets — no ambient files, network or clock — not an operating-system sandbox) and the reload rule, and left the JIT BLOCKED on the workspace's")
    strs_push(l, "`unsafe_code = \"forbid\"`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Whether safe abstractions suffice: they do not.** Running generated machine code in process needs")
    strs_push(l, "memory that is writable, then executable (`mmap`/`mprotect`, or `MAP_JIT` with")
    strs_push(l, "`pthread_jit_write_protect_np` on this host), and a jump to an address as a function — a raw-pointer")
    strs_push(l, "cast to a function pointer. The standard library offers none of this safely, and no crate that wraps")
    strs_push(l, "it is in this machine's offline cache (`cranelift-jit`, `region`, `memmap2`: absent). A subprocess is")
    strs_push(l, "not a JIT. So the JIT stays **BLOCKED**, by two causes: the forbid lint, and the absent crate.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would lift it, designed and not built.** One crate, `nazm-jit-mem`, the only member allowed")
    strs_push(l, "`unsafe` (`xtask/src/rules.rs`'s allowlist, the workspace lint relaxed to `deny` in the same change,")
    strs_push(l, "§2's rule): it maps a buffer read-write, copies relocated code in, flips it to read-execute (W^X —")
    strs_push(l, "never both), and returns a handle whose call goes through one audited `unsafe` cast. Threat model:")
    strs_push(l, "the code is the compiler's own output from validated LIR, never input bytes; the handle owns the")
    strs_push(l, "mapping and unmaps on drop, so no call outlives its code; a stale-code test after recompilation and")
    strs_push(l, "a W^X test are its acceptance. Lifting the lint is the project's decision, not a milestone's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What this milestone adds.** The tiers that exist held to one answer: a REPL session's every value")
    strs_push(l, "and failure code equal to `nazm run`'s and to native builds' by LLVM and by Cranelift, on the same")
    strs_push(l, "definitions — recursion, loops, both trap codes, `i64::MIN / -1` and `% -1`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** None.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** An overflow inside a function the REPL defined fails with `N0400` in all four")
    strs_push(l, "tiers. **Boundary example.** `i64::MIN % -1` is 0 in all four.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this unsuitable.** A REPL answer no other tier gives.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.101 The grand audit: every area against its evidence, and one candidate through every gate — N100, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the gate runs. N76–N99 each moved or narrowed one area. This milestone adds no")
    strs_push(l, "feature. It audits every row of the capability matrix — `area | status | remaining limitation |")
    strs_push(l, "owner milestone | executed evidence | proposed final status` (`docs/internal/audits/audit-n100.md`) — and runs one")
    strs_push(l, "candidate, the head of N99's records, through the gate the programme deferred to its end: the full")
    strs_push(l, "workspace suite, the selfhost suite and the bootstrap, contained; the mutation campaign over every")
    strs_push(l, "mutant N76–N99 added or repointed (215, every verdict class reported); and the container-backed runs")
    strs_push(l, "— the live debugger sessions, both boards under QEMU, WebAssembly, the EVM and the contract")
    strs_push(l, "properties.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The objective, and its answer stated in advance.** The ideal is no row PARTIAL, RESEARCH, BLOCKED")
    strs_push(l, "or MISSING. It is not met, and the audit will not force it: fifteen rows are PARTIAL with named,")
    strs_push(l, "executed limits — among them sBPF and the JIT BLOCKED by what this machine lacks, proofs BLOCKED by")
    strs_push(l, "the absence of a proof assistant, the selfhost compiler at 13 of 21 parity probes, eight performance")
    strs_push(l, "claims unreproduced. N100 therefore **fails the zero-partial objective** and says so; the candidate is")
    strs_push(l, "a release candidate for what the matrix states, with a human procedure, and nothing is tagged,")
    strs_push(l, "pushed or published.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove the audit wrong.** A row whose stated evidence a reader cannot find or rerun; a")
    strs_push(l, "gate step reported passed that did not run.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.102 Evidence closure: the N100 survivor, the four without a verdict, and a catalogue with no silent tier — N101, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. N100 ended with one mutant SURVIVED (`n79-a-held-io-cap-is-read-alone`,")
    strs_push(l, "called \"possibly equivalent\") and four with no verdict (`every-definition-is-exported`,")
    strs_push(l, "`a-record-drop-does-not-recurse`, `task-safety-stops-at-the-first-level`,")
    strs_push(l, "`lowered-propagation-falls-through-on-error`): suite-tier entries, no declared killer, each needing a")
    strs_push(l, "whole workspace suite per run. Owner: the mutation catalogue (`xtask/mutations/mutations.toml`) and")
    strs_push(l, "its validation (`xtask/src/plan.rs`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The survivor is reachable.** The mutant reads a held `IoCap` without what it implies, so a")
    strs_push(l, "declared function holding only an `IoCap` that calls `print` is refused (`N0369`, no `OutCap`). N100's")
    strs_push(l, "probe of exactly that program reported success because it ran in a directory holding a warm check")
    strs_push(l, "cache: the cache's key is the checker identity — semantic epoch, package version, schemas, the")
    strs_push(l, "built-in table — and a mutant changes the checker without changing any of these, so a warm entry")
    strs_push(l, "answered for the unmutated checker. That key is right for a released build, whose rules change only")
    strs_push(l, "with the epoch, a counter bumped by hand (§7.4); it is not evidence about a mutated build. Mutation probes and killers run in")
    strs_push(l, "fresh directories. The focused killer is `authority::a_held_io_cap_authorises_its_own_print`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The four get focused killers**, each a test whose failure under the mutant was observed:")
    strs_push(l, "`build::the_same_name_defined_privately_in_two_files_is_not_a_conflict`,")
    strs_push(l, "`memory::a_nested_record_releases_through_both_levels`,")
    strs_push(l, "`scheduler::nothing_mutable_crosses_into_a_task`,")
    strs_push(l, "`propagation::locals_are_released_once_when_an_error_propagates`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**No silent tier.** The other 175 catalogue entries without a declared killer are the same problem")
    strs_push(l, "waiting for N108, whose full-catalogue campaign would spend a whole suite on each (about 50 hours).")
    strs_push(l, "Each gets a killer found by applying it and running its crate's tests, then `nazm-cli`'s, in a")
    strs_push(l, "dedicated worktree, and a declared killer is verified by the contained runner. An entry no test")
    strs_push(l, "catches is recorded with a `no_killer` reason and its classification — a known survivor, or not")
    strs_push(l, "injectable — never left unclassified. The catalogue's validation then refuses an entry with neither")
    strs_push(l, "killers nor a `no_killer` reason.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** None: no semantic epoch, schema, ABI or cache key changes; the catalogue gains killer")
    strs_push(l, "metadata only.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** An entry with no `killers` and no `no_killer` fails `cargo xtask check`.")
    strs_push(l, "**Boundary example.** An entry whose `find` text no longer occurs is NOT INJECTED: its definition is")
    strs_push(l, "repaired to the code that now owns the rule, never dropped.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this wrong.** A declared killer that passes with its mutant applied, in a fresh")
    strs_push(l, "directory, under the contained runner.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.103 The compiler written in Nazm at parity: 21 of 21, and what each dimension means — N102, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written with the port rather than before it: the constitution below states what the work")
    strs_push(l, "established, and it was settled probe by probe as each refusal was replaced. N98 measured the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler written in Nazm (`compiler/*.nz`) against the reference on 21 probes: 13 equal, 8 refused.")
    strs_push(l, "Owner: the compiler written in Nazm, held by `crates/nazm-cli/tests/selfhost.rs` and")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/parity.json`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What was ported, each as the reference has it and none for a probe.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Feature | Lexer / parser | Checker | Emitter |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Effect sets `! { … }` | `!`, the set on the function's text | `N0366`–`N0368`, inferred in rounds as `effects.rs` does; the bridge's assumption for another module's undeclared function | nothing |")
    strs_push(l, "| Capabilities | the seven type names | types; `IoCap` accepted where `OutCap` is expected; `N0371` for a parameter of `main` that is none; no equality | an `i64` nothing reads; `main` given one per parameter |")
    strs_push(l, "| Recursion | — | — | `nz.stack_check` on entry to every function in a call cycle or calling through a value, failing `N0408` at the function's name — the reference runtime's, derived and gated (`check-runtime`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Contracts | `requires`/`ensures` as children of the function: parameters, `requires`, body, `ensures` | a `Bool` (`N0300`); `N0614` for what a clause may not contain; `result` in a slot of the function's own | `N0410` on entry; every exit stores into `result`'s slot and leaves through one block, `nz.ens`, where `N0411` is checked before the frame goes |")
    strs_push(l, "| Foreign declarations | `extern \"C\" fn … = \"symbol\";` | no body; contract `foreign` | the C symbol declared, and a function under the definition's own symbol calling it; `Int` only |")
    strs_push(l, "| Standard modules | `@std/NAME` keyed as itself, read from the library beside the core prelude | — | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| Traits | `trait`, `impl`, `recv.m(…)`, `Trait.m(x)`; a method named `#Trait.Type.m`, in no namespace a call by name searches | `N0600`–`N0607`, `N0609`, `N0364` for a bound; a concrete call resolved to the impl's definition | a call through a bound resolved per instance |")
    strs_push(l, "| Closures and function values | `fn(T) -> R ! {…}` types; closure literals | captures through every enclosing closure; `N0386`, `N0387`; effects checked per closure; effect subsumption where a value is passed | the reference's objects (`nz.closure_new`, counted), captures retained into them, code taking the object first, thunks for named functions, the closure runtime derived and gated |")
    strs_push(l, "| `&&`, `\\|\\|`, `!` | the reference's binding powers | `N0304` | short-circuit branches and a `phi` |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Parity, dimension by dimension.** Parse: the selfhost parser's tree is compared with the reference's on")
    strs_push(l, "every source in the tree, as before. Resolution: unchanged rules, plus trait and method resolution")
    strs_push(l, "compared in `the_nazm_checker_agrees_with_the_reference_on_the_n102_features` (39 sources, every code")
    strs_push(l, "and span). Checking: the same test, plus every earlier one; **authority is not checked** by the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler written in Nazm — no `N0369` — so it accepts a program whose function exercises authority")
    strs_push(l, "it does not hold, which the reference refuses (N104 removes the bridge that makes that rule")
    strs_push(l, "complicated; the port is its natural successor). Effects: as the reference, including the bridge's")
    strs_push(l, "assumption. Code generation and runtime ABI: the same failure codes, the same memory report, closure")
    strs_push(l, "counters included, on every probe and on")
    strs_push(l, "`the_nazm_written_compiler_compiles_the_n102_features_with_the_same_memory_semantics` (16 programs and")
    strs_push(l, "4 failures, on stated answers). Packages: refused by name (`NAME:path`). Profiles: none, as before.")
    strs_push(l, "Diagnostics: codes and primary spans compared; message text is not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What still differs, outside the parity record's subset, each refused by name or recorded:**")
    strs_push(l, "string escapes, `::`, `as`, effect parameters, a function type inside another type, foreign types")
    strs_push(l, "other than `Int` and foreign exports, `Chan[T]`, `select`, the clock, device registers, `N0615`")
    strs_push(l, "(a literal call proved against a precondition at compile time — checked at run time instead),")
    strs_push(l, "reserved words, and authority. The release-native subset the parity record defines is its 21 probes'")
    strs_push(l, "features.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Bootstrap.** C2 = C3 (`8cc750c6…`) at 16,030 source lines, 34 conformance cases (14 multi-module)")
    strs_push(l, "and 29 refusals agreeing across C2, C3 and the reference — the new features among them. Self-reproduction,")
    strs_push(l, "not correctness.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Cost.** The source grew 27% (12,767 → 16,200 lines across `compiler/*.nz`); `nazm check` of it cold")
    strs_push(l, "1.05 → 1.36 s and 50 → 75 MB; `nazm build` 2.39 → 2.66 s and 82 → 106 MB.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** Semantic epoch, interface schema, runtime ABI, Core/MIR/LIR and machine schemas:")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged — no rule of the language changed; the compiler written in Nazm caught up with it. `nazm.parity/1`")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged; its record moved to 21 equal.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** A trait method whose impl declares `! { io }` where the trait declares `! {}` is")
    strs_push(l, "`N0603` in both checkers. **Boundary example.** `false && boom()` never calls `boom` in either")
    strs_push(l, "compiler's program.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this wrong.** A program both compilers accept whose two executables differ in")
    strs_push(l, "status, output, failure code or memory report.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.104 Re-exports: one definition under another module's names — N103, 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written with the code. Area 2's standing limitation was that a module could neither re-export")
    strs_push(l, "a name nor export one under another name. Owner: `nazm-syntax` (the grammar), `nazm-sema` (the")
    strs_push(l, "graph's edge and the interface), `nazm-core` (applying re-exports), `nazm-iface` (persisting")
    strs_push(l, "them), `nazm-service` (rename) and the compiler written in Nazm.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The syntax.** `pub use \"PATH\";` re-exports every name the module at `PATH` offers;")
    strs_push(l, "`pub use \"PATH\" { a, b as c };` the names chosen, `c` the name `b` is offered under. A")
    strs_push(l, "`pub use` is also an ordinary `use`: the module sees what it re-exports. `pub use \"PATH\" as m;`")
    strs_push(l, "is refused — a re-export is not imported under a name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The semantics: one definition, several names.** A re-export adds no definition. The export it")
    strs_push(l, "adds carries the defining module's id, so a call, a type, a trait bound, a reference, a rename and")
    strs_push(l, "a persisted interface all answer with the definition — `shapes.nz::fn double`, whichever module's")
    strs_push(l, "name was written. What a module offers is its own `pub` definitions and what it re-exports;")
    strs_push(l, "what an import brings is what its module offers, unchanged in every other respect: not")
    strs_push(l, "transitive beyond what is re-exported, collisions refused as before (`N0207`, `N0208`). A trait")
    strs_push(l, "is re-exported under its own name only; its name is how bounds and calls find it. An impl in a")
    strs_push(l, "module re-exported from is usable wherever the re-exporting module is imported, and is carried in")
    strs_push(l, "its interface.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Refusals.** A chosen name the module does not offer: `N0211`, at the name. A name the module")
    strs_push(l, "already offers — its own, or another re-export's: `N0212`. Modules re-exporting from each other")
    strs_push(l, "in a cycle: `N0213`, at each `pub` — a cycle of re-exports offers nothing in particular, and")
    strs_push(l, "applying re-exports in dependency order is what keeps the answer deterministic.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Durability.** `nazm.interface/11`: a re-export's export carries `reexport` and the defining")
    strs_push(l, "module's `DefKey`; a type offered under another name, or by another module, is listed in")
    strs_push(l, "`reexported_types`. An importer's check key covers the re-exporting module's interface, and so")
    strs_push(l, "every signature it re-exports: a re-exported signature's change re-checks the importer; a")
    strs_push(l, "private body's change does not. Resolved units name the definition. `nazm.api-doc/2` documents")
    strs_push(l, "each re-export with the identity it offers.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**One resolution model.** `nazm_core::declared_interfaces` is the stages a compilation runs before")
    strs_push(l, "any body, re-exports included; `nazm interface` publishes from it rather than from a shorter")
    strs_push(l, "second path, which until N103 it did.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The compiler written in Nazm.** Its parser accepts `pub use`; its checker reads the re-exports")
    strs_push(l, "from the tokens and the module graph, computes what each module offers — functions, types,")
    strs_push(l, "traits — in the same order, and reports `N0211`–`N0213` at the reference's positions; impls")
    strs_push(l, "follow re-exports as the reference's do.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** Semantic epoch 27 → 28 (programs that did not parse are accepted).")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.interface/10` → `/11`; `nazm.api-doc/1` → `/2`. Runtime ABI, Core/MIR/LIR: unchanged — a")
    strs_push(l, "re-export is resolved before any of them exists. Check and object keys: through the interface")
    strs_push(l, "schema and the epoch, both moved; no other key input.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** `pub use \"shapes.nz\" { hidden };` where `hidden` is private: `N0211`.")
    strs_push(l, "**Boundary example.** A rename of `double` re-exported as `twice`: the list's `double` and")
    strs_push(l, "every use written `double` are renamed; every use written `twice` is not, and still means it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this wrong.** Two identities for one definition in any output: a reference,")
    strs_push(l, "a resolved unit, a persisted interface or a symbol.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.105 Authority is a parameter: no inheritance — N104, 2026-10-05")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. N37's compatibility bridge let a function with no declared effect set")
    strs_push(l, "exercise its **caller's** authority; N79 recorded what each such function inherits (its")
    strs_push(l, "`inherits`), published it, and offered a profile rule, `explicit-authority`, that refused it — but")
    strs_push(l, "the default stayed: `fn main() -> Int { print(\"x\"); 0 }` was accepted, and so was a helper that")
    strs_push(l, "prints without holding anything. Area 6 is PARTIAL for that reason. Owner: the authority check")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-core/src/effects.rs`), with every program in the repository and the compiler")
    strs_push(l, "written in Nazm as its migration.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The rule.** A capability is a value, and authority is what a function's scope holds lexically:")
    strs_push(l, "its capability parameters, a binding of capability type, a capture of one. Every call that needs")
    strs_push(l, "authority — a built-in whose identity needs a kind, a `spawn`, a foreign call — needs it held")
    strs_push(l, "**there**, in every function, declared or not. A call to a function needs nothing at the call:")
    strs_push(l, "whatever its body exercises it holds itself, so its authority is in its parameter list and type")
    strs_push(l, "checking has already made the caller supply it. Missing authority is `N0369`, as it was for a")
    strs_push(l, "declared function, with the function and the kind named. `main`'s parameters are the root: the")
    strs_push(l, "runtime hands `main` one capability per parameter, and nothing else is a source.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What goes.** The bridge's authority half, entirely: `Needs::Ambient`, the inherited-authority")
    strs_push(l, "record in the resolution, and its report in `nazm inspect`. A")
    strs_push(l, "function value of an undeclared function no longer needs its maker to hold anything: the")
    strs_push(l, "function holds what it needs. The profile rule `explicit-authority` is now the language's rule;")
    strs_push(l, "it stays named, so a manifest that lists it still parses, and can no longer fire.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What stays.** The bridge's **effect** half: a function in another module that declares no")
    strs_push(l, "effect set is assumed to have the bridged effects (`io`, `spawn`), because its interface publishes")
    strs_push(l, "no set. That is an effect contract, conservative and representable, and it grants nothing:")
    strs_push(l, "authority is now always a parameter. Attenuation (`OutCap`), subsumption and the capability kinds")
    strs_push(l, "are unchanged; no kind is added.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Migration.** Every program in the repository — examples, the standard library, the corpora,")
    strs_push(l, "every program inside a test, the compiler written in Nazm — gains the capability parameters its")
    strs_push(l, "functions exercise, threaded from `main`, by a migrator that reads the pre-N104 checker's")
    strs_push(l, "`inherits` (the exact set each function exercised without holding) and adds `io: IoCap`,")
    strs_push(l, "`out: OutCap` or `tasks: SpawnCap` where needed, and the caller's own at each call. The")
    strs_push(l, "compiler written in Nazm also gains the check itself: `N0369` at the reference's spans, for a")
    strs_push(l, "built-in or a `spawn` with no capability of the kind in scope.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** Semantic epoch 28 → 29: programs accepted before are refused. `nazm.interface/11`:")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged — an interface never carried inherited authority (an importer assumed the bridged")
    strs_push(l, "effects of an undeclared export, and still does), and a function's authority is its parameters'")
    strs_push(l, "types, which it already publishes. `nazm.inspect/1 → /2`: a definition no longer reports")
    strs_push(l, "`inherits`. Runtime ABI,")
    strs_push(l, "Core/MIR/LIR: unchanged — authority is a check, and a capability's representation is untouched.")
    strs_push(l, "Check and object keys: through the epoch and the interface schema.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Negative example.** `fn shout() -> Int { print(\"!\"); 0 } fn main(io: IoCap) -> Int { shout() }`:")
    strs_push(l, "`N0369` in `shout`, which holds no `OutCap`; `main`'s `io` is not reachable from it.")
    strs_push(l, "**Boundary example.** `fn shout(out: OutCap) -> Int { print(\"!\"); 0 } fn main(io: IoCap) -> Int")
    strs_push(l, "{ shout(io) }` is accepted: an `IoCap` is given where an `OutCap` is expected.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this wrong.** A program in which a function exercises a capability kind that")
    strs_push(l, "no binding in its scope holds, accepted by either compiler.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 8. Toolchain, and one real incompatibility")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Availability is not compatibility. Declared MSRVs checked 2026-09-19:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Crate | Version | MSRV | vs local Rust 1.93.1 |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `cranelift` | 0.135.2 | **1.95.0** | **fails** |")
    strs_push(l, "| `cranelift` | 0.132.3 | 1.93.0 | ok |")
    strs_push(l, "| `redb` | 4.3.0 | 1.90 | ok |")
    strs_push(l, "| `salsa` | 0.28.4 | 1.88 | ok |")
    strs_push(l, "| `cstree` | 0.14.0 | 1.85 | ok — added in N15 against 1.98.1, resolved and built (§7.17) |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The machine's `stable` was **1.93.1 (2026-02-11)** while current stable was **1.98.1")
    strs_push(l, "(2026-09-01)** — seven months behind. Resolved by pinning 1.98.1 rather than holding")
    strs_push(l, "Cranelift at 0.132. **This establishes declared MSRVs, not that the set resolves and builds")
    strs_push(l, "together**; that check happens when each dependency is actually added.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Choices for the compiler, with the corrections an external review forced:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Need | Pick | Reasoning |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Lexer | Handwritten | Incremental relexing, trivia attachment, interpolation, recovery |")
    strs_push(l, "| Parser | Handwritten recursive descent + Pratt | Justified by *Nazm's* requirements — incremental reparse of a changed subtree, per-construct diagnostics, control of trivia — **not** by disparaging alternatives. An earlier draft dismissed `chumsky` for \"poor recovery\"; that was wrong, `chumsky` supports recovery and partial ASTs via `recover_with`. rust-analyzer, Roslyn, Swift, and TypeScript chose handwritten RD for the incremental-IDE reasons above |")
    strs_push(l, "| CST | `cstree` over `rowan` | An earlier draft claimed `rowan` blocks parallelism. Also wrong: `rowan`'s `GreenNode` **is** `Send + Sync`; only the red `SyntaxNode` wrapper is not, and that is architectable around. The real reasons are interned strings in the green tree and a thread-safe red layer out of the box. A preference, not a blocker |")
    strs_push(l, "| Incremental | `salsa` in memory + own content-addressed store on disk | rust-analyzer is the existence proof; salsa's persistence is weak and its API churns |")
    strs_push(l, "| Dev backend / JIT / comptime | `cranelift` | One component, four jobs |")
    strs_push(l, "| Release backend | LLVM IR as text → `clang`/`opt` | No build-time LLVM dependency |")
    strs_push(l, "| Hashing / serialisation / store | `blake3` · `postcard` (disk) + `serde_json` (agent/LSP) · `redb` | Keeps the bootstrap chain free of C dependencies |")
    strs_push(l, "| Diagnostics | `ariadne` to render; **own structured schema** | The renderer is cosmetic. Stable codes, JSON, machine-applicable fixits are the artifact |")
    strs_push(l, "| LSP / MCP | `lsp-server` (not `tower-lsp` — cancellation control) · `rmcp` | |")
    strs_push(l, "| Testing | `insta` · `tests/ui/` golden tests · `proptest` + `arbitrary` + `libfuzzer-sys` | Golden UI tests are the highest-value compiler test investment |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.106 One LIR both backends consume — N105, 2026-10-05")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Area 10 is PARTIAL because LIR owns bytes and nothing else: since N40 each")
    strs_push(l, "native backend translates MIR itself. An inventory at N105's start found three decisions made once")
    strs_push(l, "— byte layouts and the ownership predicate (`abi.rs`), symbols and linkage (`symbol.rs`), the")
    strs_push(l, "runtime's functions — and everything else made twice, in `nazm-lir/src/emit.rs` (LLVM text) and in")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-codegen-clif` (Cranelift): every guard, its order, failure code and message; 33 of the 57")
    strs_push(l, "built-ins' semantics; which runtime function retains or releases each type; the record, enum,")
    strs_push(l, "closure and task-block layouts the code actually uses (LLVM's enum was one slot per variant, the")
    strs_push(l, "tables' a tagged union); the internal calling convention; literals. The two agreed because tests")
    strs_push(l, "compared them, not because they were one. Owner: `nazm-lir`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The level.** LIR is an instruction set below MIR and above either backend, target-shaped but")
    strs_push(l, "backend-neutral, in `nazm-lir/src/op/`:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- *Values* are typed by a machine class — `I8`, `I32`, `I64`, `Ptr` — and are defined once and used")
    strs_push(l, "  only in the block that defines them; a value that crosses blocks lives in a *variable* (a mutable")
    strs_push(l, "  scalar) or a *slot* (stack memory of a stated size and alignment).")
    strs_push(l, "- *Instructions*: constants and symbol addresses; slot addresses; loads and stores at a byte offset;")
    strs_push(l, "  wrapping and overflow-checked arithmetic; comparisons; selects; extensions and truncations;")
    strs_push(l, "  pointer offsets; variable reads and writes; direct, indirect and runtime calls; memory copy and")
    strs_push(l, "  zero of a constant size; a source position for debug information.")
    strs_push(l, "- *Terminators*: jump, branch, switch on an integer, return, and `unreachable`.")
    strs_push(l, "- A *module* is one unit: its functions (MIR's, and every helper, trampoline, closure release and C")
    strs_push(l, "  entry they need), the data they reference (literals, failure texts), what they import, and which")
    strs_push(l, "  parts of the runtime they reach.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the lowering from MIR decides, once.** Every failure: code, message and its")
    strs_push(l, "`file:line:col` text. Every guard and its order (division by zero before overflow; `MIN % -1` is 0).")
    strs_push(l, "Comparisons, string equality and the equality helpers. Which runtime entry each operation calls —")
    strs_push(l, "only the runtime's word-level view, the same symbol for both backends. Every retain and release, and")
    strs_push(l, "the helpers that do them. Every offset — records, the enum's tag word and one payload area, closure")
    strs_push(l, "objects, task blocks, `--layout soa` — from `abi.rs`, which gains the closure and task layouts. The")
    strs_push(l, "calling convention: a value held in memory by pointer, an in-memory result through a pointer passed")
    strs_push(l, "first; a foreign function's C classes and extensions.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a backend decides.** Instruction selection, registers, the object or text format, and how a")
    strs_push(l, "position becomes debug information. Nothing it decides is observable to a program. The LLVM backend")
    strs_push(l, "becomes a printer of LIR as LLVM text; the Cranelift backend a translator of LIR into Cranelift IR.")
    strs_push(l, "Neither reads MIR: a layering rule refuses the dependency.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Validation and an oracle.** A validator holds every module to the rules above — classes agree,")
    strs_push(l, "a value is defined before it is used in its block, every symbol and slot and block exists, every")
    strs_push(l, "call matches its callee's signature — before either backend sees it, and a broken module is")
    strs_push(l, "`N0900`. An interpreter of LIR executes it against a model of the runtime's services, for the")
    strs_push(l, "sequential subset: tasks, channels, foreign calls, the clock and device registers are refused by")
    strs_push(l, "name. It is the oracle that the three executions are held to — LLVM `-O0` and `-O2` and Cranelift")
    strs_push(l, "against the LIR interpreter — over the N73 generator's programs and a new fuzz target.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Keys.** A Cranelift object is a function of its unit's LIR (which carries every failure text, and")
    strs_push(l, "so every position), the translator's revision, Cranelift's version and settings, the target and the")
    strs_push(l, "runtime; until N105 it omitted positions and reused an object reporting a moved failure at its old")
    strs_push(l, "line. An LLVM object stays keyed by its text and clang.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** Semantic epoch and interface schema: unchanged — the language does not move. Runtime")
    strs_push(l, "ABI: unchanged unless a word-level entry is added, and then a revision. `nazm.lir/1 → /2`: the")
    strs_push(l, "document gains each unit's instructions. Every object key moves, since the code does.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Non-goals.** No optimisation in LIR: clang's and Cranelift's. The GPU kernels (N88) and contract")
    strs_push(l, "bytecode (N70) are other targets with their own generators, not native backends.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove this wrong.** A failure code or message, a guard, an offset, a runtime entry or a")
    strs_push(l, "retain/release decision found in a backend rather than in LIR; or a program whose observable")
    strs_push(l, "behaviour differs between the LIR interpreter, LLVM and Cranelift.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As built (N105, 2026-10-05).** The level is as written above, with three differences, each now the")
    strs_push(l, "record:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- *Values cross blocks under dominance.* A value is used where its definition dominates the use, not")
    strs_push(l, "  only in its own block: a checked operation's result is used in the block after the guard that")
    strs_push(l, "  tests its overflow bit (`v3, v4 = mul.ovf v1, v2; branch v4, b3, b4` and `b4: return v3`), and")
    strs_push(l, "  a promoted temporary (N59) is read past the guards its expression made. The validator checks")
    strs_push(l, "  dominance (Cooper, Harvey and Kennedy's immediate dominators over reverse postorder). Its first")
    strs_push(l, "  form was the cubic bit-vector iteration, which made the debug build of `compiler/emit.nz` spend")
    strs_push(l, "  21 s of its 21 s validating; the contained selfhost suite went from 84 s (N104) to 236 s, and to 83 s")
    strs_push(l, "  once replaced. A release build of `compiler/emit.nz` takes the same time as N104's (1.47 s and")
    strs_push(l, "  1.50 s); the executable it makes runs the same (20.7 s and 21.0 s compiling the compiler, the")
    strs_push(l, "  same bytes out) and is 17% smaller.")
    strs_push(l, "- *`nazm.lir/2` carries text.* Each unit's `lir` is the module as `nazm lir --ops` prints it and its")
    strs_push(l, "  BLAKE3 digest, not a structured form: the text is the stable, reviewable statement of the")
    strs_push(l, "  instructions, and the digest is what keys a Cranelift object.")
    strs_push(l, "- *`--layout soa` is both backends'.* N68's layout was LLVM's and refused on Cranelift; it is LIR's")
    strs_push(l, "  now (`op/soa.rs`), so Cranelift takes it, and its object for one layout is never reused for the")
    strs_push(l, "  other because the LIR differs.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What the inventory deleted: `nazm-lir/src/emit.rs` (4,405 lines) and Cranelift's `func.rs`,")
    strs_push(l, "`prims.rs`, `helpers.rs`, `unit.rs` and `layout.rs` (2,963; their deletion was committed by mistake")
    strs_push(l, "in the N104 gate fix `388d11b`, which does not build on its own). What replaced them: `op/` (5,982")
    strs_push(l, "lines, the interpreter's 960 and the validator's tests included) and `translate.rs` (645). Of the")
    strs_push(l, "mutation catalogue's 93 entries on the deleted files, 76 were repointed at the LIR line that now")
    strs_push(l, "carries their rule, 16 retired as one of an LLVM/Cranelift pair that is now one rule, one")
    strs_push(l, "(`n91-a-debug-object-is-reused`) retired as equivalent, and N68's `n68-cranelift-takes-the-layout-silently` retired with the refusal it attacked: a debug build's LIR carries every position,")
    strs_push(l, "so the key moves when a line does. Eleven of the 76 survived their old killers, which compared the")
    strs_push(l, "two backends — and two backends translating one LIR agree on its defects. Each has a killer with an")
    strs_push(l, "independent expectation now. Eight new mutants attack what N105 added (`n105-*`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions, decided.** Semantic epoch 29 and `nazm.interface/11`: unchanged, the language did not")
    strs_push(l, "move. Runtime ABI: unchanged — no runtime entry was added or changed; generated code reaches only the")
    strs_push(l, "word-level registry it reached before. `nazm.lir/1 → /2`. Core IR and MIR: unchanged. Cranelift")
    strs_push(l, "object key: the unit's LIR digest, `TRANSLATOR_REVISION` 1, Cranelift's version and settings, the")
    strs_push(l, "target and the runtime digest (was MIR without positions). LLVM object key: unchanged in form (its")
    strs_push(l, "text and clang), every key moved because the text did. Package, lock and registry: unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The failure bit (R1, 5b.8, 2026-10-14; since 4.2 not on the hosted targets under LLVM, which")
    strs_push(l, "unwind: §7.115).** A caller used to learn that a Nazm callee failed by")
    strs_push(l, "reading the thread's failure flag after every call — a load, on the path of every recursive call.")
    strs_push(l, "Now a Nazm function (`Conv::Nazm`: MIR's functions, and a large frame's entry) returns one more")
    strs_push(l, "thing than its signature says, a bit beside its result: false on every `return`, true on its")
    strs_push(l, "failure exit, the new terminator `fail` (MIR's `Unwind`). A call of one takes the bit")
    strs_push(l, "(`v1, failed v2 = call @f(…)`) and branches on it to the statement's failure edge; a call through")
    strs_push(l, "a function value does the same, since every function value's code is a Nazm function. The flag is")
    strs_push(l, "untouched: `nz.fail` sets it and the message as before, it stays the runtime's record of the")
    strs_push(l, "failure, and everything that is not a Nazm caller reads it — a runtime entry's caller")
    strs_push(l, "(`nz.chan_recv`), a task's trampoline, an export's C entry, the platform entry. The runtime's")
    strs_push(l, "entries and the generated helpers take the new `Conv::Plain`: the internal convention without the")
    strs_push(l, "bit. A function the platform calls by its symbol — `main`, an interrupt handler, a board's task or")
    strs_push(l, "failure hook (`Sig::entered`) — keeps that symbol as a plain entry with its old signature, which")
    strs_push(l, "calls the function under `<symbol>.body` and leaves the bit; every Nazm caller, in any unit, calls")
    strs_push(l, "the `.body`. The LLVM backend returns `{ T, i1 }` (`i1` alone for no result), which arm64 and x86_64")
    strs_push(l, "return in two registers; Cranelift a second result (`enable_multi_ret_implicit_sret` for a pair that")
    strs_push(l, "needs more registers than a target returns in); the oracle a pair. The WebAssembly contract adapter,")
    strs_push(l, "which calls a contract's functions by symbol, takes the pair and reads the flag. Both backends also")
    strs_push(l, "lay out the blocks only a failure reaches as cold (`Function::cold_blocks`: LLVM branch weights,")
    strs_push(l, "Cranelift cold blocks) — a layout hint, nothing a program observes. Measured on `fib(35)` (Apple M1")
    strs_push(l, "Pro, hyperfine median of 20): LLVM `-O2` 66.8 → 55.4 ms, Cranelift 106.3 → 83.8 ms. The bit alone")
    strs_push(l, "was slower under LLVM (82 ms): clang merges the two returns, so the path that did not fail set the")
    strs_push(l, "bit and jumped to the shared return; the weights put that return in line, and with them the bit")
    strs_push(l, "measured 56.2 ms against the flag's 57.6 on this program (hand-built from the two IR texts) — most")
    strs_push(l, "of the gain is the layout, not the register. Versions: semantic epoch, interface and")
    strs_push(l, "runtime ABI unchanged — no runtime entry or signature changed; `TRANSLATOR_REVISION` 4; every")
    strs_push(l, "object key moves because the LIR text does.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.107 The pool by default, and two regressions attributed — N106, 2026-10-05")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code. Area 13 is PARTIAL with *one OS thread per task by default*: N83 built an")
    strs_push(l, "M:N pool — stackful tasks on guarded stacks, pinned to bounded workers, parked at the four")
    strs_push(l, "suspension points (`nz.cwait`, `nz.ctimedwait`, `nz.cwake`, `nz.join_one`) — and verified it, but")
    strs_push(l, "only behind `NAZM_SCHEDULER=pool`. Area 28 names two regressions since N75 without causes inside")
    strs_push(l, "the milestones that caused them. Owner: `nazm-runtime` (the scheduler's decision), `nazm-cli` (the")
    strs_push(l, "build's policy and its report).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The default.** On every hosted target the pool has a switch for — AArch64 and x86-64, macOS and")
    strs_push(l, "Linux — a native program's tasks run on the pool unless the environment says")
    strs_push(l, "`NAZM_SCHEDULER=threads`. `NAZM_SCHEDULER=pool` asks for it explicitly, as before. Any other value")
    strs_push(l, "is refused rather than read as one or the other: no task starts, and the first `spawn` fails as a")
    strs_push(l, "pool that could not start does (`N0404`, *this task could not be started*). A pool that cannot start")
    strs_push(l, "— its tables or workers not allocated — is the same refusal, never a quiet return to threads.")
    strs_push(l, "Freestanding and WebAssembly targets have no tasks and are unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The one policy exception: C.** A program that declares a foreign function runs a thread per task")
    strs_push(l, "unless `NAZM_SCHEDULER=pool` asks otherwise. A task blocked in C holds its worker and every task")
    strs_push(l, "pinned to it, and there is no hand-off of a blocking foreign call (§7.84's non-goal); a program")
    strs_push(l, "whose tasks wait on each other through C would deadlock on the pool and does not on threads. The")
    strs_push(l, "build decides it from the program, the entry records it, and `nazm explain-cost` says which")
    strs_push(l, "scheduler a program gets and why (`nazm.cost/1 → /2`, a `scheduler` object).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is kept.** Scopes, joins, cancellation, failure adoption, channels, `select`, deadlines and")
    strs_push(l, "cleanup are the pool's as N83 verified them, now on the default path; the thread model stays, by")
    strs_push(l, "name. **A deterministic test mode:** `NAZM_WORKERS=1` runs every task on one worker, first in, first")
    strs_push(l, "out, each until it suspends — the same interleaving on every run of a program that reads no clock.")
    strs_push(l, "**The stack:** a pool task's stack is `NAZM_TASK_STACK` (default 256 KiB, at least four pages, a")
    strs_push(l, "guard page below), where a task thread's is 8 MiB; the N49 stack check budgets each from its own")
    strs_push(l, "stack, so a deep recursion in a task meets `N0408` sooner on the pool and is reported the same way.")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/spec.md`'s N49 table says so. The interpreter keeps a thread per task (it is Rust); the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler written in Nazm emits the thread model's runtime text (the `runtime parity` gate holds it")
    strs_push(l, "to the Rust text), so its programs keep threads — recorded as a gap, not a semantic difference.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The regressions.** Attributed before anything is optimised, by builds of the milestones' own")
    strs_push(l, "commits on one host and by sampling, then confirmed contained. Only a cause that is measured may be")
    strs_push(l, "changed, and each change is measured against the same baseline; a cost that is the price of a")
    strs_push(l, "feature is stated and accepted, not hidden. A benchmark claim is added for each cause found")
    strs_push(l, "(`bench/claims.toml`), so it is held from now on.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Measured, and published in `performance.md`:** logical tasks against OS threads (the pool's")
    strs_push(l, "`peak` against its workers), resident bytes per task with the page size, spawn and join, a channel")
    strs_push(l, "round trip, and a blocked receive woken — on the pool and on threads, from the same programs.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** Semantic epoch 29: unchanged — no program means anything else. Runtime ABI revision")
    strs_push(l, "5 → 6: the default and the policy global the entry defines. `nazm.cost/1 → /2`. Interface, MIR and")
    strs_push(l, "LIR schemas unchanged. Every object key moves with the runtime's revision and digest.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Non-goals.** Work stealing, preemption, growable stacks, an event reactor, the blocking-C hand-off,")
    strs_push(l, "the pool in the compiler written in Nazm. **What would prove this wrong:** a program that is correct")
    strs_push(l, "on threads and deadlocks, fails or answers differently on the default; the suite not passing on the")
    strs_push(l, "default; a `NAZM_SCHEDULER` value accepted as something it does not say.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As built (N106, 2026-10-05).** As written, with three corrections, each now the record:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- *The revision was 13, not 5:* the constitution read an old count; the runtime ABI moves 13 → 14.")
    strs_push(l, "- *The policy is a runtime global, not a weak one.* The first form declared `nz.pool_policy`")
    strs_push(l, "  `extern_weak` for the entry to define; on macOS a weak reference resolves only against a dylib,")
    strs_push(l, "  so a library and the C harness that links the runtime alone failed to link. The runtime defines it")
    strs_push(l, "  (2, the pool) and the entry of a program that calls C stores 1 before `main` runs; a library, which")
    strs_push(l, "  has no entry, keeps the pool.")
    strs_push(l, "- *\"Calls C\" is the program's declaration, not the linked runtime.* Cranelift links every part of the")
    strs_push(l, "  runtime, C's included, so a policy read from the runtime's parts ran every Cranelift program on")
    strs_push(l, "  threads; the build asks whether any unit declares a foreign function.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The regressions, as measured (`performance.md`, N106): the `channels` build's is N83's pool text,")
    strs_push(l, "accepted; the check's is N76's lossless tree and N80's provenance, a third and a fifth of the")
    strs_push(l, "analysis, with a comparison sort and SipHash inside them removed — a counting pass orders node")
    strs_push(l, "openings, and `nazm_span::fast` (multiply-rotate, FxHash's) keys the interner and the resolver's")
    strs_push(l, "span tables. Contained, `compiler/check` 213.7 → 180.2 ms. The bench baseline is re-saved at this")
    strs_push(l, "tree. Mutants: seven new (`n106-*`), two repointed (`n15-nodes-at-one-place-nest-inside-out`,")
    strs_push(l, "`n53-the-runtime-abi-stays`), and N83's nine re-verified against the tests that now ask for threads")
    strs_push(l, "by name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Amended (performance leadership, multicore, 2026-10-15).** §7.84 wrote the default worker count as")
    strs_push(l, "the online processors; the code started four on every machine, and the capability matrix recorded")
    strs_push(l, "four. A parallel program on a ten-processor host therefore used at most four of them, and fewer")
    strs_push(l, "when its tasks' work was uneven, since a task stays on the worker `spawn` gave it. The default is")
    strs_push(l, "now §7.84's: `nz.os_cpus`, a sixth function of the per-target `stack` unit (`sysconf`'s")
    strs_push(l, "`_SC_NPROCESSORS_ONLN` — 58 on Darwin, 84 in glibc and musl, 0x61 in Bionic — and")
    strs_push(l, "`GetSystemInfo`'s `dwNumberOfProcessors` on Windows), at most 64, and four where the system will not")
    strs_push(l, "say; `NAZM_WORKERS` still overrides it, and `NAZM_WORKERS=1` is still the deterministic mode. The")
    strs_push(l, "name has a dot, so it is no C identifier a foreign declaration could name: no reserved symbol and")
    strs_push(l, "no semantic epoch. Runtime ABI 34 → 35. Unchanged: round-robin placement, pinning, no stealing, no")
    strs_push(l, "preemption — the same output, ending and memory report. Measured in `performance.md`, *Multicore:")
    strs_push(l, "the parallel workload and the pool's default, measured (2026-10-15)*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.108 The core's scope, audited — N107, 2026-10-05")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the audit's results. Five language-core rows are PARTIAL — 2 (resolution and modules),")
    strs_push(l, "3 (types), 5 (effects), 6 (capabilities), 7 (provenance) — each for a list of features another")
    strs_push(l, "language has. A row that is PARTIAL until it has every mechanism anyone has built is a checklist,")
    strs_push(l, "and a checklist inflates a kernel law 12 says stays small. Owner: `docs/internal/capability-matrix.md`, with")
    strs_push(l, "this section as its reason.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The method, for every candidate gap.** The root problem the row exists for; what Nazm already")
    strs_push(l, "does about it, with its evidence; whether the candidate is *required* — a program the repository or")
    strs_push(l, "a stated goal needs and cannot write, or an unsound answer — or merely another language's")
    strs_push(l, "mechanism; whether it conflicts with the small kernel; and whether a real Nazm use case asks for it.")
    strs_push(l, "Required gaps stay, as named blockers or future work. Gaps that are not required leave the row, and")
    strs_push(l, "the row's name and limitation say exactly what VERIFIED promises, with every absent construct still")
    strs_push(l, "refused by name. **What may not happen:** a defect scoped away, a refusal turned into a silent")
    strs_push(l, "absence, or a row renamed because the work is hard. Each candidate is first checked for being a")
    strs_push(l, "defect — a wrong answer on a path a program takes — and a defect stays a defect.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not in scope:** the ecosystem and domain rows (21 AI/HPC, 25 the language service, 26 packages,")
    strs_push(l, "27 the debugger, 28 performance, 30's fuzzing half, 32 reproducibility, 33 platforms, 34 contracts),")
    strs_push(l, "which N108 classifies; no code changes, so no epoch, schema, ABI or key moves.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What would prove the audit wrong:** a program in the repository, or one a stated goal describes,")
    strs_push(l, "that the narrowed promise says Nazm handles and it does not; or a dropped candidate that turns out")
    strs_push(l, "to be an unsound answer rather than a missing feature.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.109 The core release gate — N108, 2026-10-05")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the gate runs. N108 adds nothing: it decides whether the core N101–N107 closed is")
    strs_push(l, "a release candidate, on one tree, by evidence gathered on that tree. Owner: the release record")
    strs_push(l, "(`docs/internal/releases/`), with this section as its method.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Classification.** *A — core*, required for the language, compiler, runtime, backends and the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler written in Nazm to be mature: areas 1, 2, 2a, 3–9, 10, 10a, 10b, 11–15, 22–24, 29, 30's")
    strs_push(l, "mutation half, 31, and the selfhost parity record. *B — ecosystem and domain*, a release limitation")
    strs_push(l, "and never core debt: 16 (stdlib breadth), 17 (FFI breadth), 18–20 (profiles and boards), 21")
    strs_push(l, "(AI/HPC), 25 (LSP/MCP), 26 (packages, registry scale, build check reuse), 27 (debugger), 28")
    strs_push(l, "(performance claims), 30's fuzzing half, 32 (transparency log), 33 (platform breadth), 34")
    strs_push(l, "(contracts). *C — external blockers*, stated with their cause: the in-process JIT (area 12:")
    strs_push(l, "`unsafe` forbidden, no executable-memory crate offline), proofs of the formal core (no proof")
    strs_push(l, "assistant or solver in the image), sBPF execution (area 34: no toolchain offline), a second GPU")
    strs_push(l, "provider (area 21).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The gate, contained, serial, from a clean worktree of one candidate.** The entire mutation")
    strs_push(l, "catalogue, targeted with every killer verified, resumed until every entry has a verdict, each entry")
    strs_push(l, "accounted for (CAUGHT, SURVIVED, UNUSABLE, NOT INJECTED, MUTANT CRASH, TIMED OUT, RUNNER ERROR or")
    strs_push(l, "UNEXECUTED, never converted); the workspace suite; the full lifecycle suite; the selfhost suite;")
    strs_push(l, "the bootstrap; fuzzing of every target from its corpus; the LIR oracle and backend differential (in")
    strs_push(l, "the suite, and the N73 generator at a larger budget); scheduler and channel stress (the pool's ten")
    strs_push(l, "thousand tasks, in the suite); supported platforms and emulators that run offline here; the FFI,")
    strs_push(l, "embedded, WebAssembly and contract smoke tests the suite and its images hold; the performance")
    strs_push(l, "baseline checked; `cargo xtask contained release` — assembly, provenance, evidence bundle — and")
    strs_push(l, "the manifest redigested independently of the tool that wrote it. Anything that cannot run here is")
    strs_push(l, "recorded as not run, with why.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted only if** no class-A row is PARTIAL (N107), N102's parity holds, the authority bridge is")
    strs_push(l, "gone (N104), the single-LIR contract holds (N105), the default runtime is the pool (N106), every")
    strs_push(l, "catalogue entry is accounted for with no unresolved SURVIVED, and the artifact and its evidence")
    strs_push(l, "verify independently. A survivor is fixed — a killer or the code — and re-run, or the gate is NOT")
    strs_push(l, "ACCEPTED and says so. Nothing is tagged, pushed or published; the release procedure stays manual.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions frozen:** whatever the candidate carries — semantic epoch 29, `nazm.interface/11`,")
    strs_push(l, "runtime ABI 14, `nazm.lir/2`, `nazm.cost/2` — recorded, not moved.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**As run (N108, 2026-10-05/06).** The gate ran in the order written, and found four things, each fixed")
    strs_push(l, "in a commit of its own and gated again where it reached (`releases/920a2a5.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- *Thirty-four catalogue entries no contained run could decide.* A targeted session defers a mutant")
    strs_push(l, "  every declared killer passed on, and retries it in every later session, so these consumed most of")
    strs_push(l, "  each session and would have looped. Sixteen killers saw their defect on macOS only — glibc keeps a")
    strs_push(l, "  freed block's bytes; AArch64 does not fault on `MIN % -1`; one oracle sum let two wrong remainders")
    strs_push(l, "  cancel — and the killers that see it on Linux were found by running each mutant in a container of")
    strs_push(l, "  its own. Nine survived on macOS too: N90's resolver had left `Index::choose` without a caller (deleted,")
    strs_push(l, "  its mutants repointed); N105 decided a foreign function's exclusion twice, each copy masking the other")
    strs_push(l, "  (decided once); N104 left a capability table read only by its consistency test; a restriction's")
    strs_push(l, "  `Unknown` origin, a requirement filter and a statement's debug line had no test that saw them (three")
    strs_push(l, "  added). One was equivalent and is retired. Eight are observable only with macOS tools or Apple's clang")
    strs_push(l, "  and are verified on the host. **What this says about the catalogue:** a killer verified on one")
    strs_push(l, "  platform is evidence on that platform; `architecture.md` keeps N101's no-silent-tier law, and N108")
    strs_push(l, "  adds that the release gate's platform is where its killers are verified.")
    strs_push(l, "- *A timing-dependent killer:* the polling-select test, fixed to fix who waits first and to run five")
    strs_push(l, "  times.")
    strs_push(l, "- *A debugger regression from N105,* found by the live gdb test the suite ignores (it needs an image):")
    strs_push(l, "  the prologue's `llvm.memset` carried a line and a guard's continuation took the text's last line.")
    strs_push(l, "  Fixed in the lowering and the debug pass, held by two debugger-free tests.")
    strs_push(l, "- *The release assembly no longer fits one CPU in the runner's 2,400 s;* it ran with four.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Versions frozen as written. Classes: no class-A row PARTIAL; class B's eight PARTIAL rows and class C's")
    strs_push(l, "four blockers are the release's limitations. **ACCEPTED** as a candidate; tagging and publishing stay")
    strs_push(l, "a person's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.110 A function written as a value is a reference to it — R1-C1, 2026-10-07")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Found by R1's precheck, when the tour's `examples/tour/closures.nz` entered the corpus the")
    strs_push(l, "reference audits read: `apply_twice(double, 5)` checked, ran and compiled, and `double` there was")
    strs_push(l, "in no entity's set. A corrective step before v0.3.0, not a language change. Owner: the reference")
    strs_push(l, "index (`crates/nazm-sema/src/references.rs`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The contract, stated first.** Every occurrence the checker resolved to an entity the reference")
    strs_push(l, "index models is a use of that entity, whatever the occurrence's syntactic role: a function's name")
    strs_push(l, "is a use whether it is called, spawned or written as a value. It is therefore in the index, in")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm references` and `nazm resolve`, in the LSP's references, in a snapshot's `references` and")
    strs_push(l, "`dependencies`, and in every plan read from the index (rename, patch). There is one way a use is")
    strs_push(l, "found — the checker's recorded answer — and no second one: nothing reads the source again.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What was wrong.** N50 records each named function written as a value")
    strs_push(l, "(`Resolution::record_fn_value`, keyed by the name's span, with the `FnId` the checker resolved).")
    strs_push(l, "Lowering, MIR and effects read it; `Resolution::each_use`, the one list the index is built from,")
    strs_push(l, "did not, so the index — and everything over it — held the call `double(1)` and not the value")
    strs_push(l, "`double`. N50 had taught the index that a capture is the binding it copies (`binding_of`) and left")
    strs_push(l, "this out. Rename was never unsafe: its plan missed the value, the re-check found `double` undefined")
    strs_push(l, "in the candidate, and it refused (`Rejected`, `N0200`); the comment that justified")
    strs_push(l, "`Coverage::Complete` for a function (\"there are no function values\") predated N50.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The fix.** `each_use` reports every recorded function value as a use of the function it names,")
    strs_push(l, "at the name's span, between calls and variables — the kinds are recorded in disjoint positions, so")
    strs_push(l, "no occurrence has two answers and none is listed twice. Every form the language accepts is one")
    strs_push(l, "path in the checker and so is covered by it: passed as an argument, bound by `let`, returned,")
    strs_push(l, "stored in a field, passed to a generic parameter, imported, and imported under a re-export's alias")
    strs_push(l, "(where rename keeps the alias's spelling, as for a call). A qualified name (`m::f`) and a method")
    strs_push(l, "(`x.m`) are refused as values (`N0100`, `N0608`), so neither has a use to record. A closure is not a")
    strs_push(l, "named function and refers to none.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What did not move.** No checking rule, diagnostic, interface, lowering or runtime behaviour:")
    strs_push(l, "semantic epoch 29, `nazm.interface/11`, `nazm.diagnostic/1`, runtime ABI 14. `nazm.resolved/1` and")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.snapshot/3` keep their shapes and now carry the occurrences they always promised — a")
    strs_push(l, "correctness fix within the schema, so no major moves; a snapshot of a program with a function")
    strs_push(l, "value has different `references` and `dependencies` digests than before, which is the fix. A check")
    strs_push(l, "cache entry stores its module's resolved unit under the checker's identity; the crate version in")
    strs_push(l, "that identity moved to 0.3.0 in R1A, so only unreleased builds since then could have stored a unit")
    strs_push(l, "without these uses, and the repository's own `.nazm` caches were deleted.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Two audits, stale since N50 and N78, fixed with it.** The corpus audit that asks the resolution")
    strs_push(l, "one accessor at a time took a closure's capture slot for a declaration of its own (a capture is")
    strs_push(l, "`binding_of`'s binding, N50) and knew no call through a bound (N78). The structure audit took every")
    strs_push(l, "name after `x.` in a variant's shape for a variant; `x.m()` with no arguments has that shape and is")
    strs_push(l, "a method call when the checker read `x` as a value (N78, *Unchanged meanings*). Structure has no")
    strs_push(l, "member to offer at a method's name, which is now stated by a test rather than assumed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence.** `crates/nazm-service/tests/references.rs` (every accepted position, exact spans, no")
    strs_push(l, "duplicate, imported and aliased); `crates/nazm-cli/tests/resolved_units.rs` (`nazm references`,")
    strs_push(l, "cold and from a reused unit); `crates/nazm-cli/tests/lsp.rs` (the real process, UTF-16, local and")
    strs_push(l, "imported); `crates/nazm-service/tests/snapshot.rs` (a value use changes the function's")
    strs_push(l, "`references` and no call edge); `crates/nazm-service/tests/rename.rs` (a complete plan, from every")
    strs_push(l, "occurrence); `crates/nazm-service/tests/closures.rs` (no capture slot is a source definition);")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-service/tests/structure.rs` (a field and a method of one name told apart); two")
    strs_push(l, "catalogue entries, `r1c1-a-function-value-is-no-use` and `r1c1-a-function-value-is-a-use-of-its-maker`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.111 A closure's environment is a node of the ownership graph — Gate 1-C1, 2026-10-07")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What Gate 1 found.** N11 refused every ownership cycle a *definition* could describe (`N0359`),")
    strs_push(l, "and the argument that counting reclaims everything rested on the graph of definitions being the")
    strs_push(l, "whole graph. N50 added a node the graph of definitions does not show: a closure's environment,")
    strs_push(l, "which owns what it captured, behind a function type that says nothing of it. A closure capturing")
    strs_push(l, "a `Vec[fn() -> Int]` and stored into that vector owned itself; the checker accepted it and the")
    strs_push(l, "memory report ended with it live.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The decision: refuse, by type, at the capture.** Three facts carry it (`spec.md`, *Cycles*): an")
    strs_push(l, "environment is made once and never changes, so its edges point at older values; an edge into an")
    strs_push(l, "existing value is made only by storing into a counted handle; and a counted handle that cannot")
    strs_push(l, "hold a function value holds nothing that leads back to an environment. So the only way to close a")
    strs_push(l, "cycle through an environment is for it to capture a container that can hold one, and that is")
    strs_push(l, "what `N0616` refuses. `nazm_sema::UserTypes::function_holder` answers the question over a captured")
    strs_push(l, "binding's type — a `Vec` or channel element that is, or reaches through record and enum fields or")
    strs_push(l, "further handles, a function type — and `check.rs`'s capture lookup asks it once per capture, where")
    strs_push(l, "it already refuses a captured `let mut` (`N0386`). It reads the same instance fields every derived")
    strs_push(l, "property reads (`task_safety`, `equality`), so it is not a second type walker, and a future owning")
    strs_push(l, "container is covered by being asked the same way.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What was considered and not done.** A rule at the store — `vec_push(fs, f)` refused when `f`")
    strs_push(l, "might reach `fs` — needs to know what an opaque function value captured, which its type does not")
    strs_push(l, "say, and alias analysis of handles; either a new capture-carrying component of function types or")
    strs_push(l, "refusing every store of an unknown function value, including inside every generic container")
    strs_push(l, "function. Refusing at the capture needs neither: every function value, wherever it came from,")
    strs_push(l, "was held to the rule where it was written, so storing one is always safe and generic code is")
    strs_push(l, "untouched. A cycle collector was the constitution's third option; it would be a second")
    strs_push(l, "reclamation mechanism with its own timing, pauses, task-safety and profile questions, beside a")
    strs_push(l, "counting scheme that is otherwise complete. Not introduced.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it costs.** Some closures that would never close a cycle are refused — one that only")
    strs_push(l, "reads a vector of handlers. The remedy is to pass the vector as an argument. The rule is stated")
    strs_push(l, "by type so that a reader can apply it without running the program.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The compiler written in Nazm** refuses the same capture with the same code and span")
    strs_push(l, "(`compiler/analyse.nz`, `holds_functions`). Its type arguments are never function types, so in")
    strs_push(l, "its subset the container is a `Vec` of records with a function field; that form is in")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/conformance/refused/` and `crates/nazm-cli/tests/refusals/`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Identity.** The semantic epoch moved 29 → 30: programs accepted before are refused. `Type::ALL`,")
    strs_push(l, "hashed into the checker's identity, gained the five capability types it lacked since before they")
    strs_push(l, "existed (so completion offers all seven); it moved in the same epoch. The interface schema and the")
    strs_push(l, "runtime ABI are unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence.** `crates/nazm-cli/tests/closures.rs`: every shape refused once, with nothing else")
    strs_push(l, "(direct, alias, mutual, nested closure, a record, a `Vec` of records, an enum, an `Option`, a `Vec`")
    strs_push(l, "of `Vec`s, a closure made in a helper); an acyclic program — named functions, closures capturing")
    strs_push(l, "`Int`, `Str`, `Vec[Int]` and another closure, a record with a function field, a closure through a")
    strs_push(l, "generic function and one stored by a function that cannot know what it captured — agreeing under")
    strs_push(l, "the interpreter, LLVM at `-O0` and `-O2` and Cranelift with every count `live=0`; and a closure made")
    strs_push(l, "in another module. `tests/compat/v1/`: five refusals and one run case. Catalogue entries `g1c1-*`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.112 The general-purpose foundation — Gate 2, 2026-10-07")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Gate 2's decisions are recorded in [`general-purpose.md`](general-purpose.md), written before its")
    strs_push(l, "code: one section per mechanism, each with the problem, the mechanism Nazm already had, why it was")
    strs_push(l, "not enough, the semantic cost, its placement and its evidence plan. The constraints it states are")
    strs_push(l, "architectural and are restated here so that they are found where the laws are:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **No second mechanism where one exists.** Floats and fixed-width integers are built-in types with")
    strs_push(l, "  the existing operator and call rules; wrapping is a function, not an operator. A view is a counted")
    strs_push(l, "  reference, as `Str`'s slices already were — no lifetime syntax. A socket wait parks through the")
    strs_push(l, "  pool's existing hooked wait, woken by a reactor, not through a second suspension mechanism or an")
    strs_push(l, "  `async` syntax. Maps are library code over one new derived requirement, `Hash`, the twin of")
    strs_push(l, "  `Equality`.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Authority stays a capability.** `NetCap`, `RandomCap` and `ProcessCap` join the seven kinds;")
    strs_push(l, "  the set widens to sixteen bits and no id changes.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Every new value kind joins the ownership graph.** `Bytes` and `OsHandle` hold no values and")
    strs_push(l, "  close no cycle; arrays are inline and own what their elements own.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Conditions are the build's, never the environment's.** `@cfg` is decided from target, features")
    strs_push(l, "  and profiles, which are part of every key that could reuse a result.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.113 The user cache: the runtime and the standard library compiled once per user — R1.5 D12, 2026-10-15")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code (`openspec/changes/r1-5-performance-and-dx/design.md`, D12). Until now every")
    strs_push(l, "project compiled its own runtime and its own copy of every `@std` module it imports, once per")
    strs_push(l, "`.nazm/`: a new project, a second checkout or a scratch directory paid for clang on the runtime")
    strs_push(l, "before it paid for anything of its own. The objects of those units do not depend on the project, so")
    strs_push(l, "they are kept where every project finds them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is settled.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Where.** The user cache is `NAZM_USER_CACHE_DIR` when that is set (empty turns the user cache")
    strs_push(l, "  off, and its units return to the project store); otherwise `NAZM_CACHE_DIR` when that is set, so")
    strs_push(l, "  one variable still moves everything; otherwise `~/Library/Caches/nazm` on macOS and")
    strs_push(l, "  `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/nazm` (an absolute `XDG_CACHE_HOME`), or `~/.cache/nazm`, elsewhere. With no home")
    strs_push(l, "  directory there is no user cache. Its objects are a `native/` store of `nazm.object/1` entries,")
    strs_push(l, "  exactly the project store's format.")
    strs_push(l, "- **What.** The runtime's units — the runtime, the context switch, the platform's initialisation,")
    strs_push(l, "  its stacks, `errno`, its files and the counted heap — and each `@std` or prelude module's own")
    strs_push(l, "  unit. A generic instance is the program's (its type arguments are), and so are the entry and every")
    strs_push(l, "  module of the project's own: those stay in `.nazm/native/`.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The key.** The project store's, unchanged: a digest of the exact bytes handed to the object")
    strs_push(l, "  compiler, the compiler's identity and the configuration it resolves (`-###`), for LLVM text; for a")
    strs_push(l, "  Cranelift object, its backend's key over the unit's LIR, settings, target and runtime ABI. So")
    strs_push(l, "  everything that changes an object's bytes is in its key by construction — the target and its")
    strs_push(l, "  CPU, the optimisation level, the counted heap and its limit (the runtime's text is rewritten, and")
    strs_push(l, "  the heap unit holds the limit), debug information, the services the program reached (the")
    strs_push(l, "  runtime's text is specialised to them, N82), the runtime ABI and the toolchain — and nothing")
    strs_push(l, "  enumerates them. One runtime object per distinct runtime text, target and profile, not one")
    strs_push(l, "  archive: `nazm runtime build`'s archive holds every service, with thread-local failure state, and")
    strs_push(l, "  a build linked to it is a different executable from a build without the cache.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Publication.** As the project store: a uniquely named temporary file, then a rename, so two")
    strs_push(l, "  builds at once both write and one rename lands second with identical bytes. An entry is checked")
    strs_push(l, "  as every entry is before it is a hit; a damaged one is a miss.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Linking.** Copied out of the entry into the build's own working directory, as a project hit")
    strs_push(l, "  is, and linked from there: an entry is a header and then an object, never an object file.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Off.** `--no-cache` uses neither store. A board build (N63) uses neither, as before. Deleting the")
    strs_push(l, "  user cache changes no program: it is derived data, and the next build compiles what it lacks.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence.** `crates/nazm-cli/tests/user_cache.rs`: a second project reuses the first one's runtime")
    strs_push(l, "and `@std` objects and compiles only its own, its `.nazm/` holds no runtime object, and its")
    strs_push(l, "executable is byte-identical to a `--no-cache` build's; another optimisation level, heap limit or")
    strs_push(l, "target reuses nothing of the other's; deleting the user cache changes nothing; `NAZM_CACHE_DIR`")
    strs_push(l, "alone still moves everything. Every test names a temporary user cache, and `.cargo/config.toml`")
    strs_push(l, "turns the user cache off for every other test, so no test writes to a real one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not settled.** Eviction: like the project store, the user cache grows until it is deleted.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.114 Dead-stripping: what nothing calls is not linked — R1.5 D14, 2026-10-15")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code (`openspec/changes/r1-5-performance-and-dx/design.md`, D14). An executable")
    strs_push(l, "carried every function of every unit it linked: each `@std` module's whole unit, and under")
    strs_push(l, "Cranelift every part of the runtime, whether the program called it or not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is settled.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Mach-O** (macOS, iOS): the link passes `-dead_strip`. `ld64` strips by symbol, since clang's")
    strs_push(l, "  objects (and Cranelift's) are divided at each symbol already; no compile argument changes, so no")
    strs_push(l, "  Mach-O object key changes.")
    strs_push(l, "- **ELF** (Linux, Android): each object is compiled with `-ffunction-sections -fdata-sections` and")
    strs_push(l, "  the link passes `--gc-sections`. The compile arguments are in every object's resolved")
    strs_push(l, "  configuration (`-###`), so every ELF key changes once, by construction.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Executables only.** A static or shared library keeps every function, for its C callers, and")
    strs_push(l, "  Windows, WebAssembly and the boards link as before. `crates/nazm-cli/src/backend.rs` decides, from")
    strs_push(l, "  the target, in one function the link and the probe share.")
    strs_push(l, "- **What a program does is unchanged.** The linker leaves out only what nothing reachable from the")
    strs_push(l, "  entry refers to; a function a task, an export, an interrupt table or a pointer reaches is")
    strs_push(l, "  referred to, and kept.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence.** `crates/nazm-cli/tests/dead_strip.rs`: a program calling one `@std/text` function")
    strs_push(l, "carries none of its others under either backend at `-O0` and `-O2` and prints what it did before; the")
    strs_push(l, "same objects linked whole from `--objects` are larger and hold the unused function. Measured in")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/internal/performance-log.md`, *R1.5 D14*. Two mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.115 Failures by unwinding: how a failure crosses a call, by target — Performance leadership 4.2, 2026-10-15")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written from `openspec/changes/performance-leadership/design.md`, *4.2 in detail* and *Coordinator's")
    strs_push(l, "answers on 4.2*. The failure bit (§7.106, *The failure bit*) costs a recursive call a second result")
    strs_push(l, "and a branch after it; on `fib` that bit and a stack check whose fast path was a taken branch were")
    strs_push(l, "the whole of Nazm's gap to C with the same checks.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a program sees is unchanged.** MIR gives every statement that can fail its failure edge,")
    strs_push(l, "which releases what the frame owns, joins every open `scope` and ends in `Unwind` (LIR's `fail`).")
    strs_push(l, "`nz.fail` still records the first failure, its diagnostic and position, in the thread's flag;")
    strs_push(l, "`defer` blocks still do not run on a failure (`docs/user/spec.md`, `defer`); the process still exits 2")
    strs_push(l, "from the plain entry, and a task's failure still fails its `scope`. Only how a failure crosses a")
    strs_push(l, "*call* is the target's, and a program cannot tell the two conventions apart. No semantic epoch")
    strs_push(l, "moves.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The conventions.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **The bit** — WebAssembly, WASI, the boards, Windows, Cranelift and the LIR oracle: as §7.106")
    strs_push(l, "  says. (R9's code generator kept it too until its 7.5; it now unwinds as LLVM does on the macOS")
    strs_push(l, "  targets it builds, §7.116.) These have no unwinder this compiler uses, and a board's image must")
    strs_push(l, "  not grow one. Windows (MinGW, SEH, `__gcc_personality_seh0`) unwinds only once verified under Wine.")
    strs_push(l, "  Cranelift keeps the bit until it writes `.eh_frame` with a personality and a `gcc_except_table`")
    strs_push(l, "  per function (`try_call` exists; `cranelift-object` writes no personality or LSDA, and none for")
    strs_push(l, "  Mach-O); its objects and LLVM's are never linked into one program, so the convention is per")
    strs_push(l, "  backend.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Unwinding** — the hosted targets under LLVM (macOS, Linux, Android, iOS; `Target::failures`,")
    strs_push(l, "  `op::llvm::Failures`). A Nazm function returns its result alone. A failure exit calls `nz.raise`,")
    strs_push(l, "  which starts a **forced unwind** (`_Unwind_ForcedUnwind`: phase 2 only, no search, no catch")
    strs_push(l, "  clause, no type information, no C++ runtime) with a per-thread exception object `nz.exc` and a stop")
    strs_push(l, "  function `nz.unwind_stop` that aborts only at the end of the stack — never reached, below. The")
    strs_push(l, "  personality is C's, `__gcc_personality_v0` (libSystem's compiler-rt on Apple, `libgcc_s` or")
    strs_push(l, "  `libunwind` elsewhere); every landing pad is a `cleanup`. `nz.raise`, its stop function and")
    strs_push(l, "  `nz.exc` are defined `linkonce_odr hidden` by each unit that has a failure exit, so an image has")
    strs_push(l, "  one of each and needs no runtime part for them; `nz.exc` is an ordinary global in a program of one")
    strs_push(l, "  thread (`SINGLE_THREAD_STATE`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Calls, where failures unwind.** A Nazm call whose failure edge is a bare `fail` — a block that")
    strs_push(l, "releases nothing — is a plain `call`: the unwind passes through the frame at no cost, and the edge is")
    strs_push(l, "never taken in the caller (`fib` has no landing pad at all). A Nazm call whose edge has work (a")
    strs_push(l, "release, a `scope` join) is an `invoke`; its landing pad joins the normal path with the edge taken,")
    strs_push(l, "so LIR's own branch goes where the failure goes, does the work and reaches `fail`, which raises")
    strs_push(l, "again: each frame that owns something lands once, and an unwind is linear in the depth. A function")
    strs_push(l, "with a landing pad names the personality; one without names none.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Boundaries.** Every call of a Nazm function with no failure edge — a plain entry's call of its")
    strs_push(l, "body: `main`, a C export (and so a callback C calls), a task's body, an interrupt handler or a board's")
    strs_push(l, "hooks where those unwind — is an `invoke` whose landing pad continues as if the call had returned,")
    strs_push(l, "its result a zero. The plain entry's caller then reads the flag, as it always has. So C is never")
    strs_push(l, "unwound into, and a task's failure stops at its entry, where its `scope` learns of it as before.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**LIR.** Unchanged in text and schema: `v1, failed v2 = call …` is now read as *the call's failure")
    strs_push(l, "edge*, an abstract value. The validator has one more rule (`validate::failure_edges`): a `failed`")
    strs_push(l, "value is only the condition of the branch that ends the call's block, the call that block's last")
    strs_push(l, "instruction — so every backend can make it an unwind edge, or keep it in a register where the bit")
    strs_push(l, "is kept. `nazm.lir/2` is unchanged (every module the lowering makes already obeyed the rule).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**`N0408`.** The stack check is unchanged (§7.106; 4.1). The unwinder runs in the quarter of the")
    strs_push(l, "stack the limit leaves as headroom — at least 2 MiB on every hosted thread. The check's slow branch")
    strs_push(l, "is now weighted cold, on every target: alone it gained nothing; with the bit gone it is half of what")
    strs_push(l, "a recursive call gains.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Debug information.** A definition the unit carries for the runtime (`linkonce_odr`) gets no")
    strs_push(l, "subprogram; an `invoke` is a call, so it carries a location even in a prologue; and a function with")
    strs_push(l, "no statement of its own (a plain entry) ends its prologue at its entry block's branch, so its landing")
    strs_push(l, "pad and join are at the function's line.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Versions.** Runtime ABI revision `33 → 34`: a Nazm function's machine result on the hosted")
    strs_push(l, "targets, `nz.raise` and the personality, and the system's unwinder an image links. The LLVM")
    strs_push(l, "backend's object keys follow it. Cranelift's `TRANSLATOR_REVISION` does not move. No semantic epoch")
    strs_push(l, "or schema moves.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Measured** (release `nazm`, `--opt-level 2`, `hyperfine -N --warmup 3 --runs 15`, same host and")
    strs_push(l, "session): `fib(35)` 55.7 ± 0.3 → **44.3 ± 0.3 ms** (−20%), C's time with the same overflow and stack checks;")
    strs_push(l, "word frequency 132.4 ± 1.0 → 129.4 ± 0.8 ms (−2%). The failure path is slower where frames own")
    strs_push(l, "something: the unwind lands once in each, and each landing starts a new forced unwind, whose cost")
    strs_push(l, "on macOS is the system unwinder's lookup of every frame's unwind information. A stack exhausted")
    strs_push(l, "196,098 frames deep at `-O2`, each frame owning a string and a `defer`, fails in 2.26 s against")
    strs_push(l, "8.9 ms with the bit (`docs/user/limitations.md`). A failure ends its program or its task, and is not")
    strs_push(l, "what speed is measured on (the coordinator's answer 4).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence.** `crates/nazm-cli/tests/failure_convention.rs` (once `failure_bit.rs`): a failure deep")
    strs_push(l, "in a recursion, through a function value, a trait method, a task and a C export; ten thousand frames")
    strs_push(l, "deep through `defer`s; with the stack exhausted; through a callback C calls — the same output,")
    strs_push(l, "status and memory counts on the interpreter where it reaches, LLVM `-O0` and `-O2` and Cranelift;")
    strs_push(l, "the hosted IR's shape, and that only a hosted target's object names the unwinder and the")
    strs_push(l, "personality. `op::llvm::tests` prints one module both ways; `op::validate::tests` holds the new rule.")
    strs_push(l, "Seven mutants, and the bit's LLVM exit mutant repointed to the printer's test.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The compiler written in Nazm** (R3's port, `toolchain/pipeline`) prints LIR, whose text is")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged, and no LLVM: it regenerates `rtext.nz` for runtime ABI 34 and takes the validator's rule")
    strs_push(l, "(`openspec/changes/performance-leadership/design.md`, *4.2 in the reference*).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.116 Nazm's own code generator as a backend: `nazm build --backend nazm` — R9 D15, 2026-10-15")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written from `openspec/changes/r9-code-generator/design.md`, D14 and D15. Nazm's own code")
    strs_push(l, "generator, `nzcg` (`toolchain/codegen/`, written in Nazm), turns a unit's printed LIR into a")
    strs_push(l, "relocatable object; it is to replace Cranelift as the fast build before 1.0. Since D15 it is a third")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm_lir::backend::Backend`, beside LLVM's and Cranelift's: `--backend nazm`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The crate.** `nazm-codegen-nazm` has no code generation of its own, and the same boundary as")
    strs_push(l, "Cranelift's backend (`xtask` *rules*: span, diagnostics, LIR). `plan` is Cranelift's — modules,")
    strs_push(l, "then instances, in link order. `generate` lowers and validates the unit's LIR as Cranelift does")
    strs_push(l, "(the counted heap and the field-by-field layout included), prints it as `nazm lir --ops` does —")
    strs_push(l, "with `--debug`, its positions and one `; file INDEX NAME` line per file they name, the one printer")
    strs_push(l, "both use (`nazm_codegen_nazm::text`) — writes it into a scratch directory of its own (created")
    strs_push(l, "exclusively, mode 0700) and runs `nzcg --target TRIPLE [--one-thread] UNIT.lir OUTDIR`, reading back")
    strs_push(l, "the one object it wrote. `--one-thread` is `Native::single_thread`, the fact that makes the runtime")
    strs_push(l, "define the stack limit as a plain global, which the generator then reads inline (its 7.3). One")
    strs_push(l, "process per unit keeps the per-unit object cache.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Where it is.** `NAZM_NZCG` names it; otherwise it is installed beside `nazm` as")
    strs_push(l, "`../libexec/nazm/nzcg`, built from `toolchain/codegen/` by the build that ships `nazm` (until R8")
    strs_push(l, "cuts over, with the LLVM backend). It is read once, when first needed; a build with another backend")
    strs_push(l, "never reads it. Both places a toolchain is assembled install it on the macOS targets, built by the")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm` being packaged, without a cache, outside the checkout: `scripts/host-archive.sh` (the")
    strs_push(l, "archive's `INSTALL.txt` says so) and `scripts/release-candidate.sh` (its `MANIFEST.txt` and")
    strs_push(l, "`PROVENANCE.txt` give its SHA-256). `scripts/clean-install-test.sh` builds with `--backend nazm`")
    strs_push(l, "when the archive carries it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Cache identity.** The backend's version is `nzcg-` and the generator's BLAKE3 digest, the")
    strs_push(l, "runtime ABI revision and `debug`: a changed generator is a new key, as Cranelift's")
    strs_push(l, "`TRANSLATOR_REVISION` and settings are. A unit's key also covers the target, the runtime's digest,")
    strs_push(l, "whether the program has one thread, and the LIR's digest. A debug object is never reused. The same")
    strs_push(l, "digest is in a program's provenance record when the generator built it (`backend.nzcg`, the")
    strs_push(l, "optional field `nazm.provenance/1` gained for it, and a tool of the SBOM's); `nazm profile")
    strs_push(l, "--backend nazm` profiles the program as it builds it, its samples attributed by its line tables.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Refusals, and no fallback.** Before anything is compiled: a target the generator does not carry")
    strs_push(l, "before 1.0 — anything but `aarch64-apple-darwin`, `x86_64-apple-darwin` (its D13) and")
    strs_push(l, "`x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` (its D16, section 8, 2026-10-16: PE/COFF and Windows x64's convention,")
    strs_push(l, "run-verified on a Windows host by `BACKEND=nazm scripts/windows-host.sh`) — is refused (exit 5), and so is a generator that is not there (exit 4, naming the path looked at). After: the")
    strs_push(l, "generator's exit status 3, one `nzcg: refused: …` line per construct, is one `N0101` per line,")
    strs_push(l, "naming the construct, with nothing written; any other failure is `N0900`, a compiler defect, with")
    strs_push(l, "the generator's own words. Neither falls back to another backend.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The failure convention.** The generator unwinds on a failure as LLVM does on these targets (§7.115;")
    strs_push(l, "its D14, task 7.5): `fail` calls a forced unwind under the C personality, a call whose failure edge")
    strs_push(l, "has work has a landing pad — the edge's own block — and every plain entry lands the unwind. Its")
    strs_push(l, "`nz.raise` and stop function are local to each unit, and its exception object lives in `nz.raise`'s")
    strs_push(l, "frame, so it needs no thread-local storage; objects of the two backends link into one program. On")
    strs_push(l, "`x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` it keeps the failure bit, as LLVM does there (no unwinder this compiler")
    strs_push(l, "uses), with a `.pdata`/`.xdata` entry per function for the platform's own unwinder.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence.** `crates/nazm-cli/tests/nazm_backend.rs`: every input of the generator's differential")
    strs_push(l, "suite (`toolchain/codegen/tests/run.sh`'s 117) built with `--backend nazm` behaves as the LLVM build —")
    strs_push(l, "output, diagnostics, status and the memory report; the generator is told the target and whether")
    strs_push(l, "the program has one thread, and handed the positions with `--debug`; a refusal is `N0101` per")
    strs_push(l, "construct with nothing written, any other failure `N0900`; a missing generator and a target it")
    strs_push(l, "does not carry are refused before compiling. The backend-differential harness")
    strs_push(l, "(`tests/differential`) and `failure_convention.rs` gain a `nazm` column on macOS: the same output,")
    strs_push(l, "status and memory counts as the interpreter, LLVM and Cranelift, failures through recursion,")
    strs_push(l, "function values, trait methods, tasks, C exports and callbacks, ten thousand frames of `defer`s and")
    strs_push(l, "an exhausted stack included. The tests build the generator from `toolchain/codegen/` with the")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm` under test, once per test process. Mutants in `xtask/mutations/mutations.toml` (`r9-…`).")
    strs_push(l, "In process, without a subprocess, comes at R8, when the compiler driving it is itself Nazm.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.117 Release builds: a hardened macOS executable — R1.5 D15, 2026-10-15")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written before the code (`openspec/changes/r1-5-performance-and-dx/design.md`, D15).")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm build --release` makes the same program as `nazm build`, harder to attack. The default build")
    strs_push(l, "is unchanged: nothing below happens without the flag.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What each step does.** (`crates/nazm-cli/src/build/release.rs`)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Stack protection.** Every function the generated LLVM text defines — the program's units, the")
    strs_push(l, "  runtime's and the entry's — carries `sspstrong`: one with a local array or a local whose address")
    strs_push(l, "  is taken stores a canary from `__stack_chk_guard` in its frame and checks it before returning,")
    strs_push(l, "  calling `__stack_chk_fail` (the process ends) when an overrun has written over it. It is written")
    strs_push(l, "  into the text because `-fstack-protector-strong` is a C front end's option and does nothing to")
    strs_push(l, "  LLVM IR handed to clang (measured 2026-10-15). The text is what every object key covers, so a")
    strs_push(l, "  protected object never answers for an unprotected one in either cache.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Position independence.** The link passes `-pie`: the executable loads at a randomised")
    strs_push(l, "  address. `ld64` already links macOS executables so; the flag states it rather than relying on it.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Stripped.** `strip` removes the symbol table but for what the dynamic loader needs, and the")
    strs_push(l, "  debug map with it: no function name of the program or the runtime is left.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Signed ad hoc with the hardened runtime.** `codesign --force --sign - --options runtime`: the")
    strs_push(l, "  kernel refuses the process code injection, unsigned executable memory and `DYLD_*` variables.")
    strs_push(l, "  Ad hoc — no identity is needed and none is claimed. Stripping invalidates the linker's own ad hoc")
    strs_push(l, "  signature, so signing is last. Both tools run with the driver's controlled environment, and two")
    strs_push(l, "  release builds of one program are the same bytes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Where it is refused** (`USAGE`, by name, before anything is compiled): another backend (Cranelift")
    strs_push(l, "and Nazm's generator write no canary), another target than this host's macOS, and — by the command")
    strs_push(l, "line — with `--debug`, `--lib`, `--objects` or `--runtime` (a prebuilt runtime was compiled")
    strs_push(l, "without the canary). A provenance record names a release build (`backend.release`), and only one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence.** `crates/nazm-cli/tests/release_build.rs`, a test per property read with the system's")
    strs_push(l, "tools: `nm -U` and `nm -a` (no symbol, no debug map), `otool -hv` (`PIE`), `nm -u`")
    strs_push(l, "(`___stack_chk_fail`, `___stack_chk_guard`, which the default build does not import), `codesign -dv`")
    strs_push(l, "and `--verify --strict` (`adhoc,runtime`); the same bytes twice; the refusals; the provenance")
    strs_push(l, "record. Four mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.118 The `tls` runtime part: an engine over buffers, a library found on the host — v1 C1, 2026-10-16")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written with the code; the design is `openspec/changes/v1-every-domain/design.md`, *C.3*, and its")
    strs_push(l, "*Decisions during C1*. TLS is the runtime's thirteenth part, `Part::Tls` and `Needs::tls`, reached by")
    strs_push(l, "the eleven `os_tls_*` built-ins and nothing else.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Two texts.** The target-independent part (`crates/nazm-runtime/src/tls.rs`, `TLS_RUNTIME`) is")
    strs_push(l, "  the session table — 65 535 slots of { object, generation, kind, hold word }, made on first use —")
    strs_push(l, "  and the `nz.os_tls_*` entries, each holding one slot for one engine call. The per-target **engine")
    strs_push(l, "  unit** (`tls::emit_tls`, an artefact named `tls` beside `os` and `stack`) defines `nz_tls_*` over")
    strs_push(l, "  the platform's library: OpenSSL 3 over two memory BIOs per session on macOS and Linux, with a")
    strs_push(l, "  macOS client's chain and name judged by `SecTrustEvaluateWithError` through OpenSSL's")
    strs_push(l, "  certificate-verify callback, and Linux's by OpenSSL with `SSL_set1_host`. A target without a unit")
    strs_push(l, "  (Windows, whose SChannel unit `tls::emit_schannel` is compiled and linked but has not run on a")
    strs_push(l, "  Windows host; Android) is refused by `nazm build`, `N0830`; a freestanding target names")
    strs_push(l, "  the part among what it cannot give, as for networking.")
    strs_push(l, "- **No wait inside.** No entry reads or writes a socket. `@std/tls` moves ciphertext through the")
    strs_push(l, "  parking `os_read` and `os_write` (§ *Networking*'s waits), so a task waiting for its peer parks.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Linking what is used.** The engine unit is compiled whenever the part is reached, which is")
    strs_push(l, "  whenever `@std/http` is imported, every module being lowered whole. The platform's library is not:")
    strs_push(l, "  `build::link::linked` links an executable without it, dead-stripped (§7.114), and links again with")
    strs_push(l, "  it (`build::tls::link_args`) only when that fails — when a call that survived stripping needs the")
    strs_push(l, "  engine. A shared library is not stripped and so always takes the second link; a static archive's")
    strs_push(l, "  host links the library itself. The hosted runtime artifact (§7.83) carries the engine unit as a")
    strs_push(l, "  member where the target has one.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The interpreter** calls no C (`unsafe_code` is forbidden): its `eval::tls` answers `-ENOSYS` for")
    strs_push(l, "  a configuration and `Closed` for every id, and `docs/user/spec.md`, *TLS*, says so.")
    strs_push(l, "- **What the self-hosted pipeline must follow** (R3): `toolchain/pipeline/rtext.nz` regenerated by")
    strs_push(l, "  `runtime_text.py` from the new module, the `Tls` part, the engine artefact, the eleven lowerings")
    strs_push(l, "  `crates/nazm-lir/src/op/files.rs` gained, and the retried link.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.119 The small-block heap: small blocks reused per thread — R1.5 3.1, 2026-10-16")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written with the code (`openspec/changes/r1-5-performance-and-dx/design.md`, D13). A compiled")
    strs_push(l, "program allocated every string backing, list header and growth through C's `malloc` and `free`; a")
    strs_push(l, "loop that builds and drops a few small values spent almost all its time there (`docs/internal/performance-log.md`,")
    strs_push(l, "*R1.5 3.1*).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is settled.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **The unit.** `nazm_runtime::heap::emit_small` is a unit of its own, `small`, defining")
    strs_push(l, "  `nz.small_malloc`, `nz.small_free` and `nz.small_realloc`. Every block has a 16-byte header")
    strs_push(l, "  holding its size class: 1 to 32 for up to 512 bytes, the capacity sixteen times the class; 0 for")
    strs_push(l, "  a larger block, which is C's. A thread keeps up to 64 freed blocks of each class on a list of its")
    strs_push(l, "  own (`SMALL_KEPT`) and allocates from it without calling C; a block freed past that, and every")
    strs_push(l, "  large one, goes back to C, so a block one thread allocates and another frees — a producer and a")
    strs_push(l, "  consumer — costs at most the bound, never a list that grows with the program's lifetime. In a")
    strs_push(l, "  program of one thread (`Native::single_thread`) the lists are plain globals; elsewhere they are")
    strs_push(l, "  `thread_local`, whose access on macOS is a call, so the gain there is smaller (measured). A")
    strs_push(l, "  program of one thread has no other thread to free what it allocates, so its lists have no bound")
    strs_push(l, "  (`SMALL_KEPT_ONE_THREAD`, binary-trees, 2026-10-19): every block it frees it will ask for again,")
    strs_push(l, "  and at 64 a program that freed a tree of a million boxes and built another gave all but 64 back")
    strs_push(l, "  to C and asked C for each again — 23.1 million calls of C's `malloc` at depth 16, 524,317 after.")
    strs_push(l, "- **How a program reaches it.** As the counted heap (R1d, D5) is reached: by renaming. Every unit")
    strs_push(l, "  (`nazm_runtime::heap::small_heap` on LLVM text, `nazm_lir::op::small_heap` on Cranelift's and")
    strs_push(l, "  `nzcg`'s LIR, so their object keys change with it), the runtime, the entry and every runtime")
    strs_push(l, "  unit but `stack` (task stacks are not heap) and the TLS engine (`tls`, which allocates with")
    strs_push(l, "  `calloc` and frees only what it allocated) call it in place of C's allocator.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Where.** A hosted executable (a target with a `switch` unit: macOS, iOS, Linux, Android,")
    strs_push(l, "  Windows) built with no heap limit, no prebuilt runtime (`--runtime`), no")
    strs_push(l, "  `--link`, not a library, whose program declares no foreign function")
    strs_push(l, "  (`nazm_lir::backend::small_heap`). Anywhere C may free what the program allocated, or hand it")
    strs_push(l, "  memory to free, C's allocator stays. The runtime already never frees what C allocated")
    strs_push(l, "  (`heap::tests::the_runtime_never_frees_what_the_c_library_allocated`).")
    strs_push(l, "- **What a program does is unchanged**: the same output and memory report on every backend.")
    strs_push(l, "- **What the self-hosted pipeline follows** (R3): `toolchain/pipeline/rtgen.nz`'s")
    strs_push(l, "  `runtime_units` adds `small` and renames the same units for a hosted program with no heap limit")
    strs_push(l, "  that calls no C; `objcache.nz`'s digest covers the unit; `units.py` compares it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence.** `crates/nazm-cli/tests/small_heap.rs`: a program of strings, a list grown past 512")
    strs_push(l, "bytes and emptied, and a map agrees with the interpreter on every backend with nothing live, and")
    strs_push(l, "only `small` and `stack` call C's allocator; a program of tasks has thread-local lists and one of one")
    strs_push(l, "thread plain ones; a program calling C, and one with a heap limit, have no `small` unit; 200,000")
    strs_push(l, "strings a task allocates and `main` frees peak at about 2 MiB, not the 50 MiB an unbounded list")
    strs_push(l, "holds. Four mutants. Runtime ABI 39.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7.120 Whole-program optimisation: the runtime and the program optimised together — R1.5 3.4, 2026-10-16")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Written with the code (`openspec/changes/r1-5-performance-and-dx/design.md`, D13). Each unit — a")
    strs_push(l, "module, a generic instance, the runtime, the small-block heap, the entry — was optimised alone, so")
    strs_push(l, "a call into another unit was never inlined: word frequency's hash, its map's probe and the")
    strs_push(l, "runtime's allocator were each a call per word.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is settled.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **ThinLTO at the link.** An executable the LLVM backend builds at `-O2` or above for macOS")
    strs_push(l, "  (aarch64 or x86_64, `crate::backend::whole_program`) compiles every unit with `-flto=thin` to")
    strs_push(l, "  bitcode and links with `-flto=thin`; `ld64` optimises them as one program through the")
    strs_push(l, "  toolchain's `libLTO`, so the runtime's and `@std`'s functions inline into the program.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Keys.** The probe resolves the same arguments, so a bitcode object's configuration — and every")
    strs_push(l, "  object key, in the project store and the user cache — differs from a machine object's; neither")
    strs_push(l, "  is ever reused for the other.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The link's cache.** Where the build has a store, the link keeps ThinLTO's cache in the")
    strs_push(l, "  project's `.nazm/lto` (`-Wl,-cache_path_lto`), keyed by content, so a rebuild whose inputs are")
    strs_push(l, "  unchanged does not optimise again; `--no-cache` uses none. It changes no executable.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Where not.** `-O0` and `-O1`; Cranelift and `nzcg` (their units are machine code); a library")
    strs_push(l, "  and `--objects` (their objects are for another linker); `--debug` (its `.dSYM` reads the")
    strs_push(l, "  objects); every target but macOS — Windows links with MinGW-w64's `ld`, which reads no bitcode,")
    strs_push(l, "  and Linux is after 1.0. What a program does is unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence.** `crates/nazm-cli/tests/whole_program.rs`: a program over strings, a map and `@std`'s")
    strs_push(l, "hash prints the same at `-O0`, `-O2`, `-O2` with Cranelift and `-O2 --debug`, built fresh and from")
    strs_push(l, "the store; at `-O2` on macOS every object filed is bitcode, and none at the others.")
    strs_push(l, "`backend::tests::only_an_optimised_macos_build_is_optimised_whole` holds the targets and levels,")
    strs_push(l, "and the probe test the keys. Measured in `docs/internal/performance-log.md`, *R1.5 3.4*. Four mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Amended (2026-10-19): the link generates for the target's CPU.** The code of a whole-program build")
    strs_push(l, "is generated at the link by `libLTO`, which knows no CPU but its own default; the bitcode names none.")
    strs_push(l, "On arm64 that was the first ARMv8.0, without the large-system extensions, so every atomic — a")
    strs_push(l, "string's count, the memory report's counters, the lock-free channel's compare-and-swap — was a")
    strs_push(l, "load-/store-exclusive loop where a separately optimised object has one instruction (`ldadd`,")
    strs_push(l, "`casal`): the four-task allocation loop was 13% slower after 3.4, and the channel's contended")
    strs_push(l, "compare-and-swap retried. The link now passes `-Wl,-mcpu,CPU` with the CPU clang compiles a")
    strs_push(l, "separate object for by default on that triple — `apple-m1` for arm64, `penryn` for x86_64")
    strs_push(l, "(`backend::whole_program_cpu`) — the target's baseline, never the host's, so N66 (§7.68) holds.")
    strs_push(l, "`backend::tests::a_whole_program_link_generates_for_the_cpu_a_separate_object_is_compiled_for`")
    strs_push(l, "holds it to what `clang -###` resolves; an `-O2` executable of the four-task loop had 28")
    strs_push(l, "exclusive-loop atomics and no LSE instruction before, none and 31 after. One mutant.")
    str_join(l, str_from_byte(10)) + str_from_byte(10)
}

fn dd_doc2() -> Str {
    let l = strs_new()
    strs_push(l, "# The bootstrap: how it was designed, what it does, and what it establishes")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**One document for the whole subject.** It absorbed `bootstrap-design.md` on 2026-09-21 —")
    strs_push(l, "the pre-implementation design record — because a reader asking \"why is the self-hosted")
    strs_push(l, "compiler shaped like this?\" and one asking \"what does the fixpoint prove?\" were being sent")
    strs_push(l, "to two files that each answered half.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 1. The design, and why it came first — *historical, 2026-09*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*This section is the design record as written **before** the language was extended, kept")
    strs_push(l, "because the reasoning is the point. It describes intent at the time, not current status;")
    strs_push(l, "`capability-matrix.md` is the authority on what exists.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler was designed first, on purpose: **the language features added next were")
    strs_push(l, "derived from a compiler that had been designed**, not chosen from a wish list and justified")
    strs_push(l, "afterwards. `nazmc` reads `.nz` files and writes LLVM IR text, then hands it to `clang` —")
    strs_push(l, "the same pipeline `nazm build` already ran, so the target was known exactly rather than")
    strs_push(l, "imagined.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The whole compiler is expressible with `Int`, `Bool`, `Str`, and growable arrays of `Int`")
    strs_push(l, "and `Str`.** No generics, traits, closures, user-defined types, pattern matching, or a")
    strs_push(l, "shared-pointer graph. The technique is the one bootstrap compilers have always used:")
    strs_push(l, "*structures of parallel arrays, addressed by index*, with every traversal iterative and")
    strs_push(l, "every work stack an explicit `Ints`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "That analysis produced the feature list, and nothing beyond it:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Needed for | Feature | Milestone |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| reading source, names, literals, building output | `Str` with length, byte access, slicing, concatenation, comparison, `Int` conversion | B1 |")
    strs_push(l, "| every table above | growable `Ints` and `Strs` with `push`, indexed get/set, `len` | B2 |")
    strs_push(l, "| reading input, writing the `.ll`, reporting, exit status | file read/write, arguments, stderr, exit codes | B3 |")
    strs_push(l, "| a compiler in more than one file | modules with deterministic multi-file resolution | B4 |")
    strs_push(l, "| every traversal | nothing — iterative algorithms use the `Ints` stack from B2 | B5 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Deliberately not added, and still absent:** generics, traits, closures, user-defined")
    strs_push(l, "records or tagged unions, pattern matching, a hash map, reference types, a borrow checker,")
    strs_push(l, "destructors, exceptions, iterators, operator overloading, a package registry. Each may be a")
    strs_push(l, "good idea later; none was a prerequisite for the first compiler. This list is the source")
    strs_push(l, "for the *deferred rather than delivered* distinction in `capability-matrix.md`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The memory model was stated as a limitation, not discovered as a bug.** Strings and")
    strs_push(l, "arrays are immutable in identity and allocated from a process-lifetime region that is never")
    strs_push(l, "freed: a compiler process reads input, produces output and exits, so reclaiming memory")
    strs_push(l, "inside that lifetime buys nothing and costs an ownership system the bootstrap does not")
    strs_push(l, "otherwise need. The consequence was named at design time and required testing rather than")
    strs_push(l, "assuming — *peak memory grows with input size and with the number of intermediate strings,")
    strs_push(l, "so string building uses an array plus one join rather than repeated concatenation.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "That sentence is the one this project paid for. Three stage drivers were written with")
    strs_push(l, "`str_concat` in a loop anyway, and on 2026-09-21 the quadratic retention that follows from")
    strs_push(l, "never freeing took the machine down three times. `runbook.md` carries the incident and the")
    strs_push(l, "containment rules it produced.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **Partly superseded by N7, 2026-09-22.** Sequence storage is reclaimed now, under")
    strs_push(l, "> `docs/user/spec.md`'s *memory constitution*, and a workload whose live set is constant no")
    strs_push(l, "> longer grows. **The sentence above still stands for this document's subject**, twice")
    strs_push(l, "> over: `Str` storage is still not reclaimed, so the quadratic `str_concat` shape is")
    strs_push(l, "> exactly as dangerous as it was; and the compiler written in Nazm emits no reclamation at")
    strs_push(l, "> all, so a program *it* compiles behaves as this paragraph describes in every respect. The")
    strs_push(l, "> containment rules are unchanged and are not a milestone's to relax.")
    strs_push(l, ">")
    strs_push(l, "> **Both halves retired by N8, 2026-09-22.** `Str` storage is reclaimed — a `Str` carries")
    strs_push(l, "> the allocation that owns its bytes, `architecture.md` §7.8 — and `compiler/emit.nz` emits")
    strs_push(l, "> the same model, held to the Rust emitter's runtime by the `runtime parity` gate and to")
    strs_push(l, "> its *decisions* by a differential test that compares what each compiler's programs")
    strs_push(l, "> reclaimed. Measured on the shape this document is about: the accumulator loop at 8,000")
    strs_push(l, "> iterations fell from **70.66 MiB to 2.23 MiB**.")
    strs_push(l, ">")
    strs_push(l, "> **The advice above is still the advice.** `str_concat` in a loop is quadratic in *time*")
    strs_push(l, "> whatever happens to the memory, and `str_join` is still one pass and one allocation. What")
    strs_push(l, "> changed is that getting it wrong now costs time rather than the machine.")
    strs_push(l, ">")
    strs_push(l, "> **The containment rules do not change, and the reason is not that they might still be")
    strs_push(l, "> needed.** A leak that has been fixed is not evidence that the incident of 2026-09-21")
    strs_push(l, "> cannot recur: an unbounded loop, a runaway recursion in a future language version, or a")
    strs_push(l, "> defect in this very reclamation reaches the machine exactly as the original did.")
    strs_push(l, "> Containment is operational law — `runbook.md` owns it — not a workaround with an expiry.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What the design did not settle")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- The public ABI and value layout stay unfrozen. `Str` and arrays are compiler-internal")
    strs_push(l, "  representations, and no program can observe their layout.")
    strs_push(l, "- Whether the self-hosted compiler eventually uses records and pattern matching is a")
    strs_push(l, "  question for after it exists. Writing it with arrays first was a claim about the shortest")
    strs_push(l, "  sound path, not about the language's eventual shape.")
    strs_push(l, "- Concurrency was designed separately and was expected to share none of this. It is now")
    strs_push(l, "  **compiled by this compiler** — `compiler/emit.nz` carries the task and channel runtime.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 2. What the chain does")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/bootstrap.sh` runs, from one compiler source **S**:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "1. the retained Rust implementation compiles S into **C1**;")
    strs_push(l, "2. C1 compiles S into **C2**;")
    strs_push(l, "3. C2 compiles S into **C3**;")
    strs_push(l, "4. C2 and C3 are compared, and both compile the conformance corpus.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Each stage writes to its own directory, so no stage can read another's artefacts and a")
    strs_push(l, "stale binary cannot stand in for one that was never built. Every stage is checked and")
    strs_push(l, "failure propagates — a script that prints success after a failed stage is worse than no")
    strs_push(l, "script.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The source is imported, not concatenated.** Every stage compiles `compiler/emit.nz` and")
    strs_push(l, "resolves its `use` lines itself, with the resolver written in Nazm (`compiler/module.nz`),")
    strs_push(l, "so what is bootstrapped is the compiler as it is actually written. The script used to strip")
    strs_push(l, "the `use` lines and paste the files together, which worked but meant the chain never")
    strs_push(l, "exercised the thing it was meant to prove.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 3. The result, on the verified configuration")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Host | **Linux aarch64**, inside `nazm-contained:1.98.1` — the configuration of record since containment became mandatory. Darwin arm64 remains *a* verified configuration, historically |")
    strs_push(l, "| Toolchain | rustc 1.98.1 (pinned); Debian clang 19.1.7 in the container, Apple clang 21.0.0 on Darwin |")
    strs_push(l, "| S | `compiler/{lex,parse,analyse,module,emit}.nz`, **16,573 lines** (5,041 at the first result, 2026-09) |")
    strs_push(l, "| **C2 vs C3, emitted IR** | **byte-identical** |")
    strs_push(l, "| **C2 vs C3, executables** | **byte-identical**, including the runnable form |")
    strs_push(l, "| Conformance | 34 cases and 30 refusals, each agreeing across C2, C3 **and the reference** — 14 of the cases multi-module (10 cases, 5 multi-module, at the first result) |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The IR being identical is the fixpoint: compiling S with a compiler built by Rust and with")
    strs_push(l, "a compiler built by itself produces the same output. That is what self-hosting means, and")
    strs_push(l, "it is checked rather than asserted.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The reference compiler, and a correction — 2026-09-22")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "This script does not build `$nazm`; it requires it to exist. Inside the contained runner")
    strs_push(l, "`CARGO_TARGET_DIR` is `/work/target`, and `docker/contained.Dockerfile` warms that")
    strs_push(l, "directory with a build of the whole workspace when the **image** is built. So every")
    strs_push(l, "contained bootstrap from the image's build date until this one used that binary — for the")
    strs_push(l, "reference check at the top, and for stage 1 — regardless of what was in the tree mounted at")
    strs_push(l, "`/src`, and said nothing about the substitution. `cargo xtask contained bootstrap` now runs")
    strs_push(l, "`cargo build -p nazm-cli` first.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What this does and does not change: the fixpoint is C1 → C2 → C3, and C2 vs C3 is a")
    strs_push(l, "statement about the compiler written in Nazm, which the substitution does not touch. What")
    strs_push(l, "was wrong is narrower and still worth correcting — *which* front end produced C1, and")
    strs_push(l, "whether the reference check at the top of the script was checking the language the tree")
    strs_push(l, "currently defines. It was not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Visibility, since N2 — 2026-09-22")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler source states its own module boundaries. **84 of its 224 top-level functions")
    strs_push(l, "are `pub`; 140 are private**, and the split is computed from which names are actually")
    strs_push(l, "called across a file boundary rather than applied to everything: `lex.nz` exports 40,")
    strs_push(l, "`parse.nz` 23, `analyse.nz` 18, `module.nz` 3, and `emit.nz` — the largest at 58 functions")
    strs_push(l, "— exports nothing at all, because nothing imports it. `emit.nz`, `check.nz` and `parser.nz`")
    strs_push(l, "gained `use` lines for modules they were using and naming nowhere; `emit.nz` was calling")
    strs_push(l, "into `lex.nz` and `parse.nz` through `analyse.nz`'s imports, which stopped working when")
    strs_push(l, "imports stopped being transitive.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "That the compiler can express those boundaries cleanly, and that fewer than half its")
    strs_push(l, "functions are part of any interface, is the useful evidence: a visibility model the real")
    strs_push(l, "multi-file workload cannot express is a model that would have been worked around.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Semantic parity, and why it is a separate claim — N2.1, 2026-09-22")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**C2 = C3 is a fixpoint.** It says the compiler written in Nazm reproduces itself, and a")
    strs_push(l, "compiler that consistently accepts a program the specification forbids reaches a fixpoint")
    strs_push(l, "too. It is not evidence that the two implementations agree about the language.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "For one day they did not. N2 taught the Nazm-written compiler to *parse* `pub` and nothing")
    strs_push(l, "else: it still resolved every name across the whole program, so it accepted eight kinds of")
    strs_push(l, "program the reference refuses and **miscompiled** a ninth — two modules each defining a")
    strs_push(l, "private `helper` both emitted `@nz.f0`, and clang rejected the module as an invalid")
    strs_push(l, "redefinition. The fixpoint was undisturbed throughout, which is the point.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The evidence that replaced it has three parts, kept apart on purpose:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Claim | What runs | What it establishes |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **C2 = C3** | `compiler/bootstrap.sh` stages 2 and 3 | a fixpoint: the Nazm compiler reproduces itself, byte for byte |")
    strs_push(l, "| **reference = C2 = C3** | the conformance corpus, `compiler/conformance/` including `modules/` | the three agree on what a program **means** |")
    strs_push(l, "| **accept = accept, refuse = refuse** | `the_two_compilers_agree_on_every_module_and_visibility_rule` | the two agree on which programs are in the language at all, comparing the diagnostic code where both produce one |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The third is the one that would have caught the divergence, and it is fifteen cases: every")
    strs_push(l, "rule `spec.md` settles about modules, run through both compilers and required to give the")
    strs_push(l, "same answer. The multi-module conformance cases are the second; they are directories rather")
    strs_push(l, "than files because each compiler resolves `use` for itself, and a single-file corpus cannot")
    strs_push(l, "exercise a module boundary.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**How the Nazm compiler knows.** `compiler/module.nz` returns the merged text **and** the")
    strs_push(l, "module graph: where each file's text begins, and which module each `use` names. That the")
    strs_push(l, "text is concatenated is a representation detail of this compiler; the boundaries travel")
    strs_push(l, "beside it, and every question about ownership is answered from those rather than from the")
    strs_push(l, "text. `compiler/analyse.nz` reads a definition's owner from where its declaration sits and")
    strs_push(l, "its `pub` bit from the function node, collects every module's interface before any body is")
    strs_push(l, "checked — which is why an import cycle has no ordering to violate here either — and records")
    strs_push(l, "what each call resolved to. Emission reads that and never looks a name up again. The last")
    strs_push(l, "part is not tidiness: it is why two modules' private `helper` now get two symbols.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The remaining difference from the reference is not about visibility.** `load.rs` keys a")
    strs_push(l, "file by its canonical path and this keys by a textually normalised one, so a file reached")
    strs_push(l, "through a symbolic link is one module to the reference and two here. Recorded above, and")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged by N2.1.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What is normalised, and why it is narrow")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The macOS linker stamps an `LC_UUID` and embeds the output *filename* in the ad-hoc code")
    strs_push(l, "signature. Neither is anything the compiler produced. The script therefore assembles each")
    strs_push(l, "stage **twice**: once runnable, and once with `-Wl,-no_uuid` purely to compare — a binary")
    strs_push(l, "without an `LC_UUID` is one macOS refuses to load, so the normalised copy is never")
    strs_push(l, "executed. Each stage links to the same filename in its own directory, which removes the")
    strs_push(l, "second difference.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nothing about code or data is touched. On this configuration the runnable binaries turn out")
    strs_push(l, "to be byte-identical too (`runnable-bytes-differing: 0`), because the UUID clang computes")
    strs_push(l, "is a function of the content — so the normalisation removes a difference that did not")
    strs_push(l, "arise. It is kept because it *can* arise, and finding out by having the check fail would be")
    strs_push(l, "worse.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The cache is not part of this chain — N4, 2026-09-22")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N4 gave `nazm check` a store of semantic results. **The bootstrap neither reads nor writes")
    strs_push(l, "one**, and that is a decision rather than an omission.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/bootstrap.sh` runs `nazm check` on the compiler source as its reference leg, and")
    strs_push(l, "the stages it builds are `nazm build` invocations, which reuse nothing. Each stage works in")
    strs_push(l, "its own directory, so no `.nazm` store from one run is visible to another, and the fixpoint")
    strs_push(l, "is a comparison of emitted IR — a thing no cache is involved in producing. **A cache hit is")
    strs_push(l, "therefore not a prerequisite for self-host success, and could not become one.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nor is the cache ported into the compiler written in Nazm. It is toolchain architecture,")
    strs_push(l, "not language semantics: no Nazm program can observe a `CheckKey`, and a second store")
    strs_push(l, "written in a language with no `realpath` would be a second thing to keep correct in")
    strs_push(l, "exchange for symmetry nobody needs. What the two implementations must agree on is the")
    strs_push(l, "language, which is what §3 measures. `nazm.root` changes nothing for either — the")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm-written compiler computes no durable identity at all, so there is nothing for a")
    strs_push(l, "declared root to change.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 4. What this does **not** establish")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **It is not evidence that the compiler is correct.** A compiler that miscompiles S in a")
    strs_push(l, "  way that reproduces the same miscompilation is a fixpoint too. Reproducibility and")
    strs_push(l, "  correctness are different claims; the conformance corpus and the differential tests in")
    strs_push(l, "  `crates/nazm-cli/tests/selfhost.rs` are what speak to the second, and they compare")
    strs_push(l, "  against the Rust implementation and against explicit expectations rather than against the")
    strs_push(l, "  Nazm compiler itself.")
    strs_push(l, "- **It is one target per run.** Nothing here says what an unverified target would do.")
    strs_push(l, "- **It says nothing about archive reproducibility.** That is a separate claim with a")
    strs_push(l, "  separate answer; see the release report.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The Rust implementation is still required**, to build C1 and to run `nazm check` inside")
    strs_push(l, "  the script. It is the bootstrap toolchain and the semantic oracle, and deleting it after")
    strs_push(l, "  the first successful build is exactly what must not happen.")
    strs_push(l, "- **External dependencies remain**: `clang` assembles the IR and links, and libc supplies")
    strs_push(l, "  `malloc`, `realloc`, `memcmp`, `memcpy`, `snprintf`, `write`, `exit` and the `stdio` file")
    strs_push(l, "  functions. Emitting LLVM and invoking an external assembler is permitted and documented;")
    strs_push(l, "  it is not hidden.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 5. Current limitations")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Module resolution keys files by a textually normalised path, not a canonical one.**")
    strs_push(l, "  `./x.nz`, `x.nz` and `a/../x.nz` are one file; two names reaching one file through a")
    strs_push(l, "  symbolic link are two, and it would be read twice. The Rust driver keys by the canonical")
    strs_push(l, "  path instead, because it can — the emitted runtime has no `realpath`.")
    strs_push(l, "- **No package imports.** The reference resolves `@std/NAME` and a package's `NAME:path`")
    strs_push(l, "  (`load.rs`); this loader resolves `@std/NAME` since N102, from the library beside the core prelude,")
    strs_push(l, "  and refuses a package import **by name**. Until N102 it refused both, since N77 (\"the compiler written in Nazm does not")
    strs_push(l, "  resolve `@std/text`: it names a standard library module\", exit 2), where until then it looked for")
    strs_push(l, "  a file of that name and reported it missing. Aliases (`as`) and qualified names (`::`) are refused")
    strs_push(l, "  by its parser.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Nothing is freed** — *until N8, which closed it*. See §1; the design stated it, and")
    strs_push(l, "  `capability-matrix.md` area 4 carries the current status and the acceptance condition.")
    strs_push(l, "- **A record's or an enum's native type name is its index**, `%nz.t<n>`, exactly as a")
    strs_push(l, "  function's symbol is `@nz.f<n>`. Sound because this compiler emits one LLVM module for a")
    strs_push(l, "  whole program, and the same limitation N5 removed for the reference compiler and")
    strs_push(l, "  deliberately not for this one. It is one limitation, not three: whatever fixes the symbols")
    strs_push(l, "  fixes the type names.")
    strs_push(l, "- **A bare block is not an expression here**, so a `match` arm's body may not be one. See")
    strs_push(l, "  §5's N10 note; the limitation is N2's and predates enums — *closed by N12.1, below*.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The chain cannot run uncontained**, by design. See §6.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Records, and what the chain now carries — N9, 2026-09-23")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler written in Nazm understands records: `struct` and `.` in the lexer,")
    strs_push(l, "declarations and named construction and projection-path assignment in the parser, a record")
    strs_push(l, "table with three declaration stages in the analyser, and named LLVM aggregates with")
    strs_push(l, "generated retain and release helpers in the emitter. **There is no divergence to record** —")
    strs_push(l, "it accepts and rejects the same record language the reference does, which is the standard")
    strs_push(l, "N2.1 set and which this document exists partly to keep.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "It also **uses** one. `Place { line, column }` replaced `line_of` and `column_of` in")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/emit.nz`, which were two functions because a function returns one value. So S —")
    strs_push(l, "the source this chain compiles with itself — now contains a record, and C1, C2 and C3 each")
    strs_push(l, "compile one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The corpus grew with it: `compiler/conformance/records.nz` covers construction, copy,")
    strs_push(l, "replacement, nesting, both return edges, a projection out of a temporary and two hundred")
    strs_push(l, "short-lived records with heap fields; `modules/exported-record` sends a record with an")
    strs_push(l, "owning field across a module boundary and back. Both are compiled by C2 and C3 and run")
    strs_push(l, "against the reference.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The digest moved, twice, and that is expected.** `spec.md` and the milestone directive")
    strs_push(l, "both say so: a compiler that gained a language feature emits different bytes. The fixpoint")
    strs_push(l, "is what matters, and it held at every step —")
    strs_push(l, "`1ce9aafb…` (N8) → `3ecf0921…` (records) → `3491dfed…` (a record in the compiler's own")
    strs_push(l, "source). Preserving an old digest by declining the change would have been preserving the")
    strs_push(l, "number rather than the property it stands for.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Enums, and the one divergence this document has to record — N10, 2026-09-23")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler written in Nazm understands enums and `match`: `enum`, `match` and `=>` in the")
    strs_push(l, "lexer; declarations, variant construction and arms in the parser; a data model in the")
    strs_push(l, "analyser that is **one flag** on the table N9 already had — an enum is a record whose fields")
    strs_push(l, "are its variants, and a variant is a record whose fields are its payload — and, in the")
    strs_push(l, "emitter, tagged aggregates with generated helpers that switch on the discriminant and then")
    strs_push(l, "call the variant's own.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Parity is compared on **codes rather than spans**, and that is a limitation of the")
    strs_push(l, "comparison rather than of either compiler: the self-hosted parser records one span per arm,")
    strs_push(l, "so a diagnostic about a payload field inside a pattern points at the arm where the reference")
    strs_push(l, "points at the field. Forty cases compare what each compiler *decides*, which is what N2.1 is")
    strs_push(l, "about.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**There is one divergence, and it is N2's.** A bare block used as an expression is still")
    strs_push(l, "refused by name in the self-hosted parser, so an arm body there may be `n + 1` but not")
    strs_push(l, "`{ let n = str_len(s); n }`. The reference accepts both. N10 did not introduce the")
    strs_push(l, "limitation and did not remove it; it made it reachable in one more position, and")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/*.nz` and the corpus are written without it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The corpus grew again: `compiler/conformance/enums.nz` covers every variant shape, both")
    strs_push(l, "directions of composition with records, nesting, a payload returned from an arm,")
    strs_push(l, "replacement across variants and within one, two hundred short-lived values with heap")
    strs_push(l, "payloads and an inactive owning variant that must cost nothing — and it declares its")
    strs_push(l, "variants in **none** of the orders that matter, so a compiler that took the parser's order")
    strs_push(l, "for the canonical one would build one value and read another. `modules/exported-enum` sends")
    strs_push(l, "an enum with an owning payload across a module boundary, inside a record, and back.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**It also uses one.** `enum Owning { Nothing, Sequence, Strings, Backing, Channel,")
    strs_push(l, "Record(at: Int), Enum(at: Int) }` replaced the small integer `owns` returned in")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/emit.nz`, so S — the source this chain compiles with itself — now contains an enum")
    strs_push(l, "as well as a record, and C1, C2 and C3 each compile one. `architecture.md` §7.11 says why")
    strs_push(l, "that structure and not another: it is the case where the value is returned and never stored,")
    strs_push(l, "which is the only case a container is not needed for.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**And making that dispatch exhaustive found an N9 defect in this compiler.** A record passed")
    strs_push(l, "to a task produced a wrong answer and leaked its fields: the argument block's offsets were")
    strs_push(l, "arithmetic that predated records, and the trampoline released four kinds of value and not a")
    strs_push(l, "record's. The block is a named LLVM type now, as the reference emitter's always was. The")
    strs_push(l, "divergence was real, it was a year of milestones old in compiler time, and **no N9 test")
    strs_push(l, "passed a record to a task through this compiler** — the gap was in the corpus.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**And a second one, found the same way.** A surviving mutation asked why zeroing a")
    strs_push(l, "variant's assembly slot mattered, and the answer was that a `break`, a `continue` or a")
    strs_push(l, "`return` out of a half-evaluated expression gave back nothing it was holding — the")
    strs_push(l, "arguments already produced, and the value a `match` was holding while an arm ran. That was")
    strs_push(l, "N8's, in this compiler and in the reference both, and `architecture.md` §7.11 writes it up.")
    strs_push(l, "The fix here is `leave_loop`, and the differential memory case that carries it abandons a")
    strs_push(l, "record, an enum and an arm in one program.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The digest moved a third and a fourth time**, for the same reason and with the same")
    strs_push(l, "property intact: `1ce9aafb…` (N8) → `3ecf0921…` → `3491dfed…` (N9) → `8030ecbb…` (enums and")
    strs_push(l, "`match`, an enum in the compiler's own source, and the task-block fix) → `ba8615e4…` (what")
    strs_push(l, "a `break` and a `continue` give back). `ir: identical`, executables byte-identical once the")
    strs_push(l, "linker UUID is removed, and C2 = C3 over 14 conformance cases, 7 of them multi-module, at")
    strs_push(l, "8,724 source lines. Preserving the old number by declining the change would have been")
    strs_push(l, "preserving the number rather than the property it stands for.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### A transfer in a value position, the divergence N10 left open — N10.1, 2026-09-23")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N10's evidence exposed one divergence older than N10, and it is recorded here rather than")
    strs_push(l, "written out of the history above:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "let v = pick(int_to_str(i), if i == 1 { continue; } else { i });")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The reference checked, interpreted and compiled this to `7` with every string reclaimed.")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler written in Nazm — interpreted, as C1, as C2 and as C3, identically, because")
    strs_push(l, "they are one program — emitted `call i64 @nz.f0({ ptr, i64, ptr } %19, void %24)`, which")
    strs_push(l, "clang refuses. Its neighbours were worse: with the other branch leaving, or both, it failed")
    strs_push(l, "**inside itself** with `N0405 this sequence is empty` at `compiler/emit.nz:2887`, exit 2. A")
    strs_push(l, "`let`, a `return`, a comparison and an assignment of the same shape each produced a")
    strs_push(l, "different `void` operand, and a `match` over one reported \"`s` is not defined\". One string")
    strs_push(l, "comparison compiled, ran, answered correctly, and leaked three strings.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The exit status 133 recorded against an intermediate state of this work did not reproduce")
    strs_push(l, "at `2f0cba9`** in any of those forms, under the selfhost suite's 512 MiB address-space ceiling")
    strs_push(l, "or without it. 133 is 128 + `SIGTRAP` on the contained runner's aarch64 Linux — the signal")
    strs_push(l, "`llvm.trap` raises there, measured — and neither emitter's runtime contains `llvm.trap`.")
    strs_push(l, "Reaching an `unreachable` at `-O0` was measured too, and it does *not* trap: control falls")
    strs_push(l, "into whatever follows. So the most that can be said of the unreproduced 133 is that it")
    strs_push(l, "belongs to no committed tree, and that the class of defect it would have been — emitted code")
    strs_push(l, "running on past a point that was never meant to be reached — is the class this correction")
    strs_push(l, "removes: every accepted case now emits valid IR, and the reachable paths through it are the")
    strs_push(l, "ones the reference has.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The cause was one representation missing twice.** The checker folded \"this never")
    strs_push(l, "completes\" into `unknown`, which also meant a statement and an error, and typed an `if` by")
    strs_push(l, "its then-branch; the emitter opened every join whether any branch reached it. Records")
    strs_push(l, "survived by accident — their field types came from the declaration — which is why N9's and")
    strs_push(l, "N10's corpora, full of record and variant transfers, never saw it. `architecture.md` §7.11")
    strs_push(l, "has the repair.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**And the audit found three more, all of them rules the reference already kept.** A")
    strs_push(l, "`break`, a `continue` or a `return` out of a `scope` did not join it, so a task that failed")
    strs_push(l, "there was never waited for and the program printed `1` where the reference stopped with")
    strs_push(l, "`N0401`. A statement after one that leaves was compiled rather than refused as `N0313`. And")
    strs_push(l, "a value that never arrives was `unknown` where the reference makes it `Int`, so")
    strs_push(l, "`match (if c { break; } else { continue; }) { … }` was accepted. A fifth finding was not")
    strs_push(l, "this compiler's alone: `==` on two strings leaked its operands in **both** native backends.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is still not the same, stated.** The self-hosted checker has no `Unit` rule — the")
    strs_push(l, "reference's `N0300`, *this produces no value* — and does not compare the types of an `if`'s")
    strs_push(l, "two branches (`N0302`). Each concerns only programs the reference refuses, so neither is a")
    strs_push(l, "divergence in the accepted language; but for those programs this compiler emits IR clang")
    strs_push(l, "refuses, or fails with `N0405`, rather than refusing by name. That, and N2's bare block,")
    strs_push(l, "are the known differences, and the second of them is still the only one a program the")
    strs_push(l, "reference accepts can reach. *The first two were closed by N10.2, below.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The corpus carries all of it: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/transfers/` holds 32 programs, the")
    strs_push(l, "original among them byte for byte, run five ways; and six of them are conformance cases")
    strs_push(l, "here, so C2 and C3 compile them too.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The digest moved a fifth time**, and the property held: `ba8615e4…` (N10) → `ce458be3…`.")
    strs_push(l, "`ir: identical`, executables byte-identical once the linker UUID is removed, and C2 = C3")
    strs_push(l, "with the reference over 20 conformance cases, 7 of them multi-module, at 8,959 source")
    strs_push(l, "lines.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### No value, as a third completion — N10.2, 2026-09-23")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The two refused-program differences recorded above are closed. The Nazm checker now has the")
    strs_push(l, "reference's three completions — a value, no value, never finishing — in one array beside")
    strs_push(l, "the type, and `unknown` means only \"already reported\". A value position given nothing is")
    strs_push(l, "`N0300`; an `if` whose branches disagree, or one with a value and one without, is `N0302`;")
    strs_push(l, "a body and a `return` are held to the signature, which this checker had never done at all.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/refusals/` holds forty programs, and each is checked by the reference")
    strs_push(l, "and by the Nazm checker compiled and interpreted, on code **and** span. All agree, and the")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm compiler refuses every refused one before it emits anything. One pair crosses a module")
    strs_push(l, "boundary: two records laid out alike from two modules are two types, `N0302` at the same")
    strs_push(l, "line and column in the reference and in the Nazm compiler, compiled and interpreted.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted programs did not move.** The Nazm compiler's IR for all 58 accepted programs in")
    strs_push(l, "the transfer corpus, the conformance corpus and `examples/` is byte-identical to N10.1's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is still not the same.** When an expression has *already* failed, the two checkers")
    strs_push(l, "recover differently: the reference gives it the expected type, or `Int`, and may then report")
    strs_push(l, "a consequence; this checker gives it `unknown`, which agrees with everything, and reports")
    strs_push(l, "none. Every comparison above is of programs whose first error is the one being tested, and")
    strs_push(l, "that is the scope of the claim. The bare block of N2 is unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The digest moved a sixth time**, with the property intact: `ce458be3…` (N10.1) →")
    strs_push(l, "`37785cef…`. `ir: identical`, executables byte-identical once the linker UUID is removed,")
    strs_push(l, "C2 = C3 with the reference over 20 conformance cases, 7 of them multi-module, at 9,194")
    strs_push(l, "source lines.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Generics, and a refusal corpus — N11, 2026-09-23")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler written in Nazm implements N11: type parameters and applications in its parser,")
    strs_push(l, "parametric checking and inference in its checker, and an instance planner and `Vec[T]` in its")
    strs_push(l, "emitter (`architecture.md` §7.12, *The compiler written in Nazm*). It remains a program with")
    strs_push(l, "no recursion — substitution is a post-order walk with an explicit stack, and interning only")
    strs_push(l, "enqueues, because `apply → settle → complete → substitute → apply` is a call cycle the")
    strs_push(l, "native backend refuses and did refuse, the first time.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the chain now carries.** Two generic programs (`compiler/conformance/generics.nz` and")
    strs_push(l, "`vectors.nz`) and two generic module cases — a library exporting a generic record, enum and")
    strs_push(l, "function that only the importer instantiates, and one instance requested from two modules —")
    strs_push(l, "join the corpus. And the chain gained a half it never had: **refusals**.")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/conformance/refused/` holds programs every compiler must refuse, each naming its")
    strs_push(l, "code on its first line — an ownership cycle through a `Vec` (`N0359`), an impossible inline")
    strs_push(l, "layout through a generic record (`N0336`), conflicting inference (`N0355`) and an instance")
    strs_push(l, "family that never ends (`N0357`) — and C2, C3 and the reference must each refuse each one with")
    strs_push(l, "that code. Agreement about what is accepted says nothing about agreement about what is not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The compiler uses what it compiles.** Its diagnostics were four parallel arrays and are a")
    strs_push(l, "`Vec[Diag]` now, so the chain compiles a `Vec` of records at every stage — C1 built by the")
    strs_push(l, "reference, C2 and C3 by the compiler itself.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The digest moved a seventh time**, twice within the milestone: `37785cef…` (N10.2) →")
    strs_push(l, "`4e473d4a…` with generics → `c58b91dd…` with the dogfood migration. `ir: identical`,")
    strs_push(l, "executables byte-identical once the linker UUID is removed, 24 conformance cases (9 of them")
    strs_push(l, "multi-module) and 4 refusals agreeing across C2, C3 and the reference, at 11,877 source")
    strs_push(l, "lines. Fixpoint is not semantic proof; the parity tests in `crates/nazm-cli/tests/selfhost.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "are what compare the two compilers on meaning, and they are recorded in")
    strs_push(l, "`capability-matrix.md`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is still not the same.** The Nazm compiler emits one LLVM module and numbers its")
    strs_push(l, "instances `@nz.g<n>` by the planner's worklist; the reference emits one object per instance")
    strs_push(l, "named from the canonical key. That is a difference in decomposition, not in meaning. Spans of")
    strs_push(l, "declaration-level diagnostics that are not compared — a record declared twice, a built-in")
    strs_push(l, "type name redeclared — still point at the whole declaration in this checker and at the name")
    strs_push(l, "in the reference.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Typed errors, and a prelude every stage loads — N12, 2026-09-24")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler written in Nazm implements N12: `?` in its lexer and parser, the core `Result`")
    strs_push(l, "recognised by definition in its checker, and propagation in its emitter as the `match` it")
    strs_push(l, "means, leaving by `return`'s exact sequence (`architecture.md` §7.13, *The compiler written")
    strs_push(l, "in Nazm*).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The prelude is part of the chain.** `library/core/prelude.nz` is the toolchain's source,")
    strs_push(l, "not the compiler's, so it is not one of S's files: every stage is **given** it —")
    strs_push(l, "`nazmc FILE CORE` — and loads it as the last module of every compilation, the compiler's own")
    strs_push(l, "included. C1 is built by the reference, which carries the same file's bytes; C2 and C3 read")
    strs_push(l, "the file. There is no stage-local definition of `Result` anywhere, and no warm cache is")
    strs_push(l, "involved. The record gains a `core-prelude:` line with the file's digest and length, beside")
    strs_push(l, "each source's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the chain now carries.** A propagation program (`compiler/conformance/results.nz` —")
    strs_push(l, "`?` out of a loop, an argument, an initialiser, a scrutinee, a generic function and two")
    strs_push(l, "layers of `Result`), a module exporting a `Result` API that its importer propagates")
    strs_push(l, "through, and five more refusals: `?` on an `Option` and on a lookalike enum (`N0360`), `?`")
    strs_push(l, "in `main` (`N0361`), two error types with identical fields (`N0362`), and a project")
    strs_push(l, "`Result` (`N0363`). C2, C3 and the reference must each accept the first two with the same")
    strs_push(l, "output and refuse each refusal with its code.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The compiler uses what it compiles.** The front end is one stage returning")
    strs_push(l, "`Result[Checked, Vec[Diag]]`, and the emitter's driver begins with `check_program(…)?` — so")
    strs_push(l, "every stage of the chain compiles, and runs, a `?` over a record of twenty handles with a")
    strs_push(l, "`Vec[Diag]` error.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The digest moved an eighth time**: `c58b91dd…` (N11) → `08895900…`. `ir: identical`,")
    strs_push(l, "executables byte-identical once the linker UUID is removed — and on this run the runnable")
    strs_push(l, "forms too, with no byte differing — 26 conformance")
    strs_push(l, "cases (10 of them multi-module) and 9 refusals agreeing across C2, C3")
    strs_push(l, "and the reference, at 12,046 source lines.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is still not the same.** This compiler's modules are session indices, so the prelude")
    strs_push(l, "is identified as *the last module* rather than by a durable key; the reference finds it by")
    strs_push(l, "`@core/prelude`. Both are exact within a compilation and neither can be confused with a")
    strs_push(l, "project module — *N12.1 closed this, below*. The earlier differences — one LLVM module and `@nz.g<n>` instance names, and")
    strs_push(l, "whole-declaration spans for the declaration diagnostics that are not compared — stand.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### One block, and the prelude by its key — N12.1, 2026-09-24")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Both differences N12 recorded as this compiler's own are closed.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*A block used as a value.* The parser takes `{` where an operand is expected — suspending")
    strs_push(l, "the expression exactly as an `if` does — and wraps the block in a `blockexpr` node, the")
    strs_push(l, "reference AST's `Expr::Block` and the encoding `selfhost.rs` had already written down for")
    strs_push(l, "it. The checker gives it its block's completion and type; the emitter treats it as")
    strs_push(l, "structure, like `block`. So a `match` arm, a `let` initialiser, an argument, a field and an")
    strs_push(l, "operand may each be a block, a statement may be a bare block, and a statement `match` may")
    strs_push(l, "have arms that produce nothing. The same programs compile in `nazm build`, which refused")
    strs_push(l, "all of them until N12.1 as well.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*The prelude's identity.* A module's `mpath` entry is its key, and `attach_core` keys the")
    strs_push(l, "prelude `@core/prelude`. `core_module` finds that key — once, in `check_program` — and both")
    strs_push(l, "consumers, the reserved-name rule and `?`'s `Result`, read the one answer. A project path in")
    strs_push(l, "the `@core` namespace is re-keyed out of it, so no project file can hold the key; such a")
    strs_push(l, "file still compiles, as it does in the reference. A harness drives `check_program` with the")
    strs_push(l, "prelude where the loader puts it, between two project modules, and absent, and the answers")
    strs_push(l, "are the same wherever it is.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The compiler uses what it compiles.** `record_owned` returns `Option[Int]`: its four")
    strs_push(l, "consumers `match` on it, and four `>= 0` guards are gone — the guards whose job was to keep a")
    strs_push(l, "`-1` meaning *no declaration* from equalling the `-1` `definition_of` answers for a type that")
    strs_push(l, "is not a record. `performance.md` has the before and after.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the chain now carries.** `compiler/conformance/blocks.nz` — arm blocks over `Option`")
    strs_push(l, "and a generic `T`, a three-arm `match` where one arm returns, one produces a value and one")
    strs_push(l, "propagates with `?`, a block argument and a block field initialiser that leave half-way,")
    strs_push(l, "an all-leaving `match`, `break` and `continue` out of arm blocks, `Unit` arms in a statement")
    strs_push(l, "`match`, and a block producing a `Result` for `?` — a module case whose importer takes")
    strs_push(l, "another module's enum and an `Option` apart with arm blocks, and three refusals: arm blocks")
    strs_push(l, "of two types (`N0302`), a `Unit` arm used as a value and a `Unit` block used as an argument")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0300`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The digest moved a ninth time**: `08895900…` (N12) → `a9ead258…`. `ir: identical`,")
    strs_push(l, "executables byte-identical once the linker UUID is removed and the runnable forms too, 28")
    strs_push(l, "conformance cases (11 of them multi-module) and 12 refusals agreeing across C2, C3 and the")
    strs_push(l, "reference, at 12,164 source lines.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is still not the same.** One LLVM module and `@nz.g<n>` instance names;")
    strs_push(l, "whole-declaration spans for the declaration diagnostics that are not compared; modules")
    strs_push(l, "keyed by normalised rather than canonical path. The prelude is the only module whose key")
    strs_push(l, "is not a path.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Derived equality, and the first enum comparison in the compiler — N13, 2026-09-25")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*The checker.* `equality_blocker` in `analyse.nz` is the reference's `UserTypes::equality`")
    strs_push(l, "over the same table — an enum's fields are its variants and a variant's are its payload, so")
    strs_push(l, "one walk answers both kinds — and `check_binary` refuses `==` exactly when the reference")
    strs_push(l, "does, at the same span with the same code. `the_nazm_checker_agrees_with_the_reference_on_equality`")
    strs_push(l, "compares the two on 30 programs, 20 of them refusals.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*The emitter.* A comparison of two records or two enums calls `@nz.eq<entry>`, generated")
    strs_push(l, "after every function for each entry a comparison reached. A record's helper compares fields")
    strs_push(l, "in layout order and leaves at the first difference; an enum's compares tags, then `switch`es")
    strs_push(l, "to the variant's slot and hands it to the variant's own helper. Both operands are released")
    strs_push(l, "after the answer, as a `Str` comparison's already were.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*The compiler uses what it compiles.* A node's completion was `0`, `1` or `2` in an `Ints`,")
    strs_push(l, "with `-1` for \"no arm yet\" in a `match`'s fold. It is an `enum Completion` in a")
    strs_push(l, "`Vec[Completion]`, the fold is an `Option[Completion]`, and every test of one is an enum")
    strs_push(l, "`==` — so every stage of the chain compiles enum equality in the compiler itself.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the chain now carries.** `compiler/conformance/equality.nz` — records with a heap")
    strs_push(l, "field built separately, different and equal variants, `Option[Int]`, `Result[Int, Str]` and")
    strs_push(l, "`Box[Shape]` — a module case comparing an imported record, enum and `Option[Point]`, and")
    strs_push(l, "seven refusals, all `N0304`: a `Vec`, an `Ints`, a `Chan`, a record holding a `Vec`, an enum")
    strs_push(l, "with one variant holding one, a generic body over `Box[T]`, and two records of one shape.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The digest moved a tenth time**: `a9ead258…` (N12.1) → `76598c43…`. `ir: identical`,")
    strs_push(l, "executables byte-identical once the linker UUID is removed and the runnable forms too, 30")
    strs_push(l, "conformance cases (12 of them multi-module) and 19 refusals agreeing across C2, C3 and the")
    strs_push(l, "reference, at 12,412 source lines.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### A type parameter that requires equality — N14, 2026-09-25")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*The parser.* `T: Equality` is written into the parameter list's text after the parameter's")
    strs_push(l, "position — `[T@5=Equality@8]` — where every existing reader of that text stops, and the")
    strs_push(l, "reference parse-tree dump carries it the same way, so parser parity covers it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*The checker.* The table's new `req` column marks a parameter whose declaration requires")
    strs_push(l, "equality; `has_no_equality` reads it for a parameter, which is the reference's single")
    strs_push(l, "assumption point; `check_generic_call` checks every argument by `equality_blocker` and reports")
    strs_push(l, "`N0364` at the reference's spans; an unknown capability is `N0365` and a requirement on a")
    strs_push(l, "record's or enum's parameter `N0101`. The emitter needed no change: instances are concrete.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Dogfood:* none. The compiler has no generic helper that needs a capability — its searches are")
    strs_push(l, "over `Ints` and `Strs` — and none was invented.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the chain now carries.** `compiler/conformance/requirements.nz` — bounded bodies at")
    strs_push(l, "`Int`, `Str`, a record, an enum, `Box[T]`, `Option[T]`, `Result[T, E]`, and a forwarded call —")
    strs_push(l, "a module case that calls and forwards to an imported bounded function, including a")
    strs_push(l, "`count_same[T: Equality]` over a `Vec[T]`, and six refusals: an unconstrained `T` compared")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0304`), a `Vec`, a `Chan` and an `Option[Vec[Int]]` holding `None` given to a bounded")
    strs_push(l, "parameter, an unconstrained wrapper forwarding (`N0364`), and two bounded parameters compared")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0304`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The digest moved an eleventh time**: `76598c43…` (N13) → `0e1a40e6…`. `ir: identical`,")
    strs_push(l, "executables byte-identical once the linker UUID is removed and the runnable forms too, 32")
    strs_push(l, "conformance cases (13 of them multi-module) and 25 refusals agreeing across C2, C3 and the")
    strs_push(l, "reference, at 12,543 source lines.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Parity on every probe — N102, 2026-10-05")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.103. The compiler gained what N98's eight refused probes needed — effects and")
    strs_push(l, "capabilities, recursion with the reference's stack check, contracts, foreign declarations, `@std`,")
    strs_push(l, "traits, closures and function values — and `&&`, `||` and `!`, without using any of them in its own")
    strs_push(l, "source: it still has no recursion and no `&&` of its own, and lexes, parses and compiles itself as")
    strs_push(l, "before.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the chain now carries.** `compiler/conformance/features.nz` (every N102 feature in one")
    strs_push(l, "program, expected 243) and `modules/features/` (a trait and its impl in another module, a closure")
    strs_push(l, "passed to a function of that module, and a standard module, expected 19), and four refusals: an impl missing a method (`N0602`), a closure")
    strs_push(l, "capturing a `let mut` binding (`N0386`), an undeclared effect (`N0366`) and an impure contract")
    strs_push(l, "clause (`N0614`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The digest moved**: since N14's `0e1a40e6…`, by each milestone that changed the compiler, to")
    strs_push(l, "`8cc750c6…`. `ir: identical`, executables byte-identical once the linker UUID is removed, 34")
    strs_push(l, "conformance cases (14 of them multi-module) and 29 refusals agreeing across C2, C3 and the")
    strs_push(l, "reference, at 16,030 source lines.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Authority as a parameter — N104, 2026-10-05")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler's own source no longer relies on inherited authority: 30 of its functions take an")
    strs_push(l, "`IoCap` (those that read, print or stop with a diagnostic), threaded from each stage's `main`;")
    strs_push(l, "none takes a `SpawnCap`. Its checker reports `N0369` — a built-in or a `spawn` with no capability")
    strs_push(l, "of its kind in scope — at the reference's spans. **The digest moved**: `8cc750c6…` → `18481f2a…`.")
    strs_push(l, "`ir: identical`, executables byte-identical once the linker UUID is removed, 34 conformance cases")
    strs_push(l, "(14 of them multi-module) and 29 refusals agreeing across C2, C3 and the reference, at 16,573")
    strs_push(l, "source lines.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### A closure's environment in the ownership graph — Gate 1-C1, 2026-10-07")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler written in Nazm refuses a closure that captures a value able to hold a function value")
    strs_push(l, "behind a `Vec`'s handle (`N0616`), at the reference's span. Its type arguments are never function")
    strs_push(l, "types, so in its subset that container is a `Vec` of records with a function field — the form of")
    strs_push(l, "the new refusal case, `refused/closure-capture-cycle.nz`. 34 conformance cases and 30 refusals.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 6. Reproducing it")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```sh")
    strs_push(l, "cargo xtask contained bootstrap      # builds the image if needed, writes the record")
    strs_push(l, "cat target/bootstrap/record.txt")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`./compiler/bootstrap.sh` on its own **refuses to run**: the script requires an external")
    strs_push(l, "memory ceiling, because a stage written in Nazm allocates without bound and reaches the")
    strs_push(l, "machine rather than the process. Setting `NAZM_CONTAINED=1` on the host to satisfy it would")
    strs_push(l, "be exactly the mistake the refusal exists to prevent. `runbook.md` owns that rule.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The record names the date, host, toolchain versions, commit, whether the tree was clean,")
    strs_push(l, "each source with its own digest and line count, both compiler digests, and the conformance")
    strs_push(l, "count.")
    str_join(l, str_from_byte(10)) + str_from_byte(10)
}

fn dd_doc3() -> Str {
    let l = strs_new()
    strs_push(l, "# Capability matrix")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Status: this file is the current status authority for the tree it is committed in.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Two things are kept apart here. **Frozen candidates** are commits a release candidate was tested")
    strs_push(l, "at, each with an immutable record in `releases/` that nothing later updates: the latest is")
    strs_push(l, "**`996984f7063a5b9590443c81fb027a7de75c11c4`** ([`releases/996984f.md`](releases/996984f.md), the")
    strs_push(l, "v0.3.0 candidate, R1), before it `920a2a5` ([`releases/920a2a5.md`](releases/920a2a5.md), the core")
    strs_push(l, "closure, N101–N108) and `84d3c80` ([`releases/84d3c80.md`](releases/84d3c80.md), the v1 foundation,")
    strs_push(l, "N40–N48), and the first was `4fb15542dfbf9af0bf34c42fe52783637b3daed4`")
    strs_push(l, "([`releases/4fb1554.md`](releases/4fb1554.md)). **The claims below are current-tree claims**: they")
    strs_push(l, "include behaviour added after any candidate, each milestone having changed the compiler and run its")
    strs_push(l, "own evidence, and a row is checked against its own evidence, not against a candidate commit.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Each row carries the evidence for the milestone that changed it — the tests, the contained")
    strs_push(l, "runs and the dates — so a claim is checked against its row, not against a single commit. A")
    strs_push(l, "row that rests on nothing newer than the candidate says so or cites only what the candidate")
    strs_push(l, "already had.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "This is one table serving two purposes. The directive asked for a capability matrix and a")
    strs_push(l, "gap map; they are the same information at the same granularity, so the five fields of a")
    strs_push(l, "gap map are the columns of the matrix and there is one document instead of two.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Vocabulary:** VERIFIED · PARTIAL · DESIGNED · RESEARCH · BLOCKED · MISSING, defined in")
    strs_push(l, "[`master-architecture.md`](master-architecture.md) §1. A VERIFIED row cites a path; a")
    strs_push(l, "`cargo xtask check` rule fails if it does not, or if a cited path stops existing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What this document does not cover.** Construct-level support — whether `while` or")
    strs_push(l, "`spawn` or a given built-in runs interpreted, compiles natively, or is refused — is")
    strs_push(l, "answered by the compiler itself:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```sh")
    strs_push(l, "cargo run -p nazm-cli --bin nazm -- capabilities --json")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "That output is read from the compiler's own dispatch tables (`crates/nazm-cli/src/capabilities.rs`),")
    strs_push(l, "so it cannot drift from the implementation the way a written table can. Ask it, not this")
    strs_push(l, "file. The schema is `schema/nazm.capabilities-1.json`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Summary")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Current suite: 2,570 passed, 0 failed, 69 ignored** across 205 test binaries, run contained at")
    strs_push(l, "`c8dc395` (Q1-C1, 2026-10-08: the v1 exit contract frozen — 0–5, `docs/user/stability.md`; the four new")
    strs_push(l, "ignored tests are the macOS-only host-refusal tests; `target/gates/q1c1/contained-tests.log`),")
    strs_push(l, "selfhost 43 of 43 with the bootstrap fixpoint. *Before Q1-C1:* 2,560 passed, 0 failed, 65 ignored")
    strs_push(l, "across 203 test binaries, run contained at")
    strs_push(l, "`fd90b06` (Q1 of the v4 programme, 2026-10-08; toolchain 1.0.0, semantic epoch 34, runtime ABI 15,")
    strs_push(l, "check entries `nazm.check/5`, not yet a release candidate; `target/gates/q1/contained-tests.log`),")
    strs_push(l, "selfhost 43 of 43 with the bootstrap chain's fixpoint test passing. Over M1: Q1's fixes and their")
    strs_push(l, "tests (`docs/internal/security-qualification.md`); the seven more ignored tests are platform-bound ones Q1")
    strs_push(l, "stopped counting as passes off their platform (Q1-D-02). The catalogue holds 1,345 entries. Q1's")
    strs_push(l, "campaign — the 21 `q1-*` entries, Gate 2's 38 and the 15 entries Gate 2 and Q1 repointed, 74 in all,")
    strs_push(l, "every killer verified — caught 73 at tier 1 (campaigns `a7eac5bb685e1822`, `3e9515c5f7f07b9e`,")
    strs_push(l, "`1290489029d48800`); `g2-a-view-does-not-keep-its-buffer` was not caught, and a contained probe of")
    strs_push(l, "it showed no observable difference in output or memory counts — Gate 2's contained gate owes its")
    strs_push(l, "verdict (`target/gates/q1/probe-mutants-2.log`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Historical, not current:* 2,538 passed, 0 failed, 58 ignored across 203 test binaries, run contained at")
    strs_push(l, "`8190cca` (M1, 2026-10-08), selfhost 43 of 43 with the fixpoint; M1's two new mutants caught at tier 1.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Historical, not current:* 2,509 passed, 0 failed, 47 ignored across 180 test binaries, run contained and")
    strs_push(l, "offline at `6ab6319` (Gate 1-C1 of the v1 programme, 2026-10-07; toolchain 1.0.0, semantic epoch")
    strs_push(l, "30, not yet a release candidate), with selfhost 43 of 43 and the bootstrap's fixpoint, C2 = C3 =")
    strs_push(l, "`178a799c…`, 34 conformance cases and 30 refusals agreeing. The catalogue holds 1,285 entries:")
    strs_push(l, "Gate 1-C1's six and the fifty responsibility-mapped entries beside them (closures, the ownership")
    strs_push(l, "graph, `Vec` retain and release, the cycle refusal, the epoch, Gate 1's two) were caught in")
    strs_push(l, "campaign `ee2ea936f8cb26ad`, 55 of 56 at tier 1 with every killer verified (pristine passes, mutant")
    strs_push(l, "fails, restored passes); the 56th, made equivalent by Gate 1-C1's shared type list, was retargeted")
    strs_push(l, "and caught in `9f505c6cde2715d7`. Area 4 is VERIFIED again since Gate 1-C1.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Historical, not current:* 2,505 passed, 0 failed, 47 ignored at `709960c` (Gate 1), selfhost 43")
    strs_push(l, "of 43, C2 = C3 = `18481f2a…`, 29 refusals; the catalogue held 1,279 entries and Gate 1's six were")
    strs_push(l, "caught in `b05c9651bed81041`. Area 4 was PARTIAL — a recorded cycle defect, open for decision.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Historical, not current:* 2,492 passed, 0 failed, 47 ignored, run contained and offline at the v0.3.0")
    strs_push(l, "candidate `996984f` inside both release assemblies (2026-10-07), with selfhost 43 of 43, the")
    strs_push(l, "bootstrap's fixpoint and the lifecycle tests 19 of 19 (`releases/996984f.md`). The mutation")
    strs_push(l, "catalogue holds 1,273 entries: the 1,268 present at N108's gate were all caught there")
    strs_push(l, "(`releases/920a2a5.md`), and R1-C1's two and R1's three were caught in their own")
    strs_push(l, "responsibility-mapped campaigns. Each release record under `releases/` is the frozen account of its")
    strs_push(l, "own candidate, and the latest one supersedes this line.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Historical, not current:* the N48 release gate (2026-10-01, at `a8a7b3f`) ended at 2,021 passed,")
    strs_push(l, "0 failed, 29 ignored, across 136 suites, with the catalogue 808 of 808 caught. The durable record of")
    strs_push(l, "that gate, and of N40–N48 as a whole, is [`releases/84d3c80.md`](releases/84d3c80.md): frozen")
    strs_push(l, "release-candidate notes for the tested candidate `84d3c80`, not updated by later commits — the")
    strs_push(l, "documentation commits after it do not change what it says. It is the canonical N40–N48 evidence")
    strs_push(l, "location; the long per-milestone working report used to produce it is kept outside the repository.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Historical, not current:* N39 ended at 1,903 passed, 0 failed, 25 ignored, across 121 suites, run contained and")
    strs_push(l, "offline (2026-09-30), scheduled at P4W2T4; nineteen of the ignored are the xtask lifecycle")
    strs_push(l, "tests, run on their own (19 of 19 passed, contained), and six are N33's, N34's, N36's, N38's (the")
    strs_push(l, "3,000-request MCP confirmation) and N39's release-build measurements, run by hand or in the")
    strs_push(l, "release-benchmark stage (`performance.md`). N38")
    strs_push(l, "ended at 1,869 across 117 with 23 ignored; N37 ended at 1,846 across 115 with 23")
    strs_push(l, "ignored; N36 ended at 1,825 across 111 with 23")
    strs_push(l, "ignored; N35 ended at 1,795 across 108 with 22")
    strs_push(l, "ignored; N34 ended at 1,773 across 104 with 22 ignored; N33 ended at 1,757 across 99 with 21 ignored; N32-H3 ended at 1,728 across 95 with 19 ignored; N32-H2 ended at 1,718 across 95; N32 ended at 1,706 across 95; N31 ended at 1,669 across 91, 1,663 before its closure correction, N30 ended at 1,647 across 89, N29 ended at 1,629 across 88, N28 ended at 1,609 across 87, N27 ended at 1,582 across 86 (1,580 before its closure correction), N26 ended at 1,555 across 83, N25 ended at 1,532 across 81, N24 ended at 1,514 across 80, N23 ended at 1,491 across 79, N22 ended at 1,476 across 78, N21 ended at 1,461 across 77, N20 ended at 1,448 across 76, N19 at 1,435 across 75, N18 at 1,417 across 74, N17 at 1,395 across 73, N16 at 1,376 across 72, N15 at 1,348 across 68, N14 at 1,317 across 67, N13 at 1,291 across 65, N12.2 at 1,255 across 63, N12.1 at 1,211 across")
    strs_push(l, "63, N12 at 1,186 across 62, N11 at 1,125 across 58. The frozen count at the tested release commit is in")
    strs_push(l, "[`releases/4fb1554.md`](releases/4fb1554.md) and does not move.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| # | Area | Status |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1 | Syntax, parser, CST | VERIFIED — the reference parser: incremental reparse and recovery (N76); attributes and conditional compilation (Gate 2); the compiler written in Nazm's syntax is N98's |")
    strs_push(l, "| 2 | Name resolution and modules | VERIFIED — durable identities, interfaces and resolved units, a declared root, packages, re-exports with one identity (N103, N107); check reuse for builds is area 26's |")
    strs_push(l, "| 2a | Incremental semantic checking | VERIFIED |")
    strs_push(l, "| 3 | Type system | VERIFIED as scoped (N107, Gate 2) — records, closed enums, generics with bounds, closures, traits with static dispatch (N78); fixed-width integers, `Float32`/`Float64`, bit operators and conversions, fixed arrays of plain data and module constants, `Bytes` buffers and views, and `Text` (Gate 2); trait objects, generic traits and default methods refused by name |")
    strs_push(l, "| 4 | Memory model and reclamation | VERIFIED for the current type universe — closure environments are ownership-graph nodes; the capture that could close a cycle is refused (`N0616`, Gate 1-C1) |")
    strs_push(l, "| 5 | Effects | VERIFIED as scoped (N107) — inferred, checked compiler-owned effects with subsumption (N79); no handlers or user effects; pure is not total |")
    strs_push(l, "| 6 | Capabilities (language) | VERIFIED as scoped (N107) — static, coarse, shareable: no inherited authority (N104), `OutCap` attenuation (N79); `NetCap`, `RandomCap`, `ProcessCap`, and an open handle as its own authority (Gate 2) |")
    strs_push(l, "| 7 | Provenance and information flow (language) | VERIFIED as scoped (N107) — explicit data flow by cell, target and field (N80); implicit flow RESEARCH (R6), not claimed |")
    strs_push(l, "| 8 | Core IR | VERIFIED (v1) |")
    strs_push(l, "| 9 | MIR | VERIFIED (v1) |")
    strs_push(l, "| 10 | LIR and the backend contract | VERIFIED (v2) — one instruction-level LIR, lowered once, that LLVM prints and Cranelift translates; validated; LIR's interpreter the oracle for the sequential subset; `nazm.lir/2` (N105) |")
    strs_push(l, "| 10a | Per-module code generation and linking | VERIFIED |")
    strs_push(l, "| 10b | Native object reuse | VERIFIED |")
    strs_push(l, "| 11 | LLVM backend | VERIFIED |")
    strs_push(l, "| 12 | Cranelift backend | VERIFIED (v1, native subset, host) |")
    strs_push(l, "| 12a | Nazm's own code generator (`--backend nazm`, R9) | EXPERIMENTAL — macOS aarch64 and x86_64 (under Rosetta) before 1.0; every input of its differential suite agrees with LLVM, failures unwinding as LLVM's (`architecture.md` §7.116). `x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` (R9 section 8: PE/COFF, Windows x64's convention, `.pdata`/`.xdata`, the failure bit as LLVM keeps it there) is run-verified on a Windows host: `BACKEND=nazm scripts/windows-host.sh`, 68 agree, 0 differ, 8 skipped on a Windows 10 laptop (2026-10-16); `toolchain/codegen/tests/coff.sh`, 120 of 120 inputs structurally sound against LLVM's objects and linked by MinGW-w64 |")
    strs_push(l, "| 13 | Runtime | VERIFIED (v1 contract; a built, versioned, verified artifact, N82; M:N tasks on bounded workers by default, N106) — no allocator of its own, runtime still text |")
    strs_push(l, "| 14 | Structured concurrency | VERIFIED |")
    strs_push(l, "| 15 | Advanced scheduler | VERIFIED as scoped (N83; the default since N106): an M:N pool, run on macOS aarch64 and x86-64 and on Linux aarch64; no stealing or preemption |")
    strs_push(l, "| 16 | Standard library | VERIFIED as scoped — 1.0 (N84): seventeen modules, a checked API manifest, four representative programs; Gate 2's collections, files and handles, I/O errors, networking, environment, processes, errors, binary encoding, randomness and logging (twenty-nine modules); no cryptography; numbers are the language's since Gate 2 (area 3) |")
    strs_push(l, "| 17 | FFI and ABI | VERIFIED as scoped — a practical C ABI subset (N85): opaque handles, C structs by borrowed pointer, strings both ways, `errno`, exports as callbacks, static and shared libraries, header bindings; every number across in both directions (Gate 2); no by-value structs, variadics or `dlopen`; on the 32-bit targets a C pointer crossing is refused by name (`N0381`, Q1-A1-05) |")
    strs_push(l, "| 18 | Embedded support | VERIFIED as scoped — three emulated boards in three architecture families (N86, Gate 3E): atomics, statics, `@section`, board manifests, AArch64 and Cortex-M interrupts, a heap arena on 64-bit boards, `@on_failure`, a fixed-priority `@task` scheduler and a watchdog (Gate 3D–3G), each emulator-verified under QEMU; RISC-V has no interrupts, Cortex-M no heap; no hardware |")
    strs_push(l, "| 19 | Critical profile | VERIFIED as scoped — profile enforcement and obligation evidence (N87): contracts, an obligation census with three statuses, no obligation of unknown status; not certification |")
    strs_push(l, "| 20 | Cybersecurity profile | VERIFIED as scoped — profile enforcement (N87): declared authority, no C, a locked build, contents kept in files, checked paths, no unknown calls; constant time RESEARCH; not certification |")
    strs_push(l, "| 21 | AI/HPC | PARTIAL — maps, zips and reductions of `Int`, `Float32` and `Float64` kernels behind a provider boundary: OpenCL on Apple's GPU and a CPU provider that is its second oracle, `Float64` refused on the GPU (N67, N88, Gate 3H); vectorised sums (N66); SIMD measured, no speed-up claimed; Metal, CUDA, ROCm and SPIR-V providers not built |")
    strs_push(l, "| 22 | Diagnostics | VERIFIED |")
    strs_push(l, "| 23 | Formatter | VERIFIED |")
    strs_push(l, "| 24 | Machine-applicable fixes | VERIFIED |")
    strs_push(l, "| 25 | LSP and MCP | PARTIAL / PARTIAL — across package boundaries tested; an editor client (N74) |")
    strs_push(l, "| 26 | Package and build tooling | PARTIAL — templates, a library check, API docs and a publish dry run (N74); a backtracking resolver that explains a refusal, and `nazm update` (N90); `@test` functions, fuzz targets and `nazm bench`, package features (Gate 2) |")
    strs_push(l, "| 27 | Debugger and profiler | PARTIAL — lexical scopes, Cranelift line tables and a sampling profiler on macOS (N91); no Cranelift variables, no DAP |")
    strs_push(l, "| 28 | Performance measurement | PARTIAL — every measured claim filed in a gated register (N92): 10 reproducible, 53 dated, 8 current claims unreproduced |")
    strs_push(l, "| 29 | Differential testing | VERIFIED |")
    strs_push(l, "| 30 | Mutation testing and fuzzing | VERIFIED / PARTIAL — coverage-guided fuzzing of five targets with a replayed corpus (N93; `lir`, N105), re-run in Q1: 3.4 million executions, no crash; no sanitizers, Miri, Loom or backend/FFI/registry fuzzing |")
    strs_push(l, "| 31 | Bootstrap | VERIFIED as scoped — the declared subset the Nazm-written compiler carries; not Gate 2 (Q1-D-25) |")
    strs_push(l, "| 32 | Reproducibility and provenance | PARTIAL — a stated five-part model, signed in-toto statements and a CycloneDX SBOM (N94); one host and one image, no transparency log |")
    strs_push(l, "| 33 | Platform and target matrix | PARTIAL — every cell in the support matrix's words (N95, Gate 3): twelve targets — five run-verified, three emulator-verified, Windows run-verified on a Windows host (a Windows 10 laptop, `scripts/windows-host.sh`, 2026-10-15) and under Wine, Android run-verified on a Linux kernel only, x86_64 Linux and iOS compile-only; x86_64 Linux deferred to the final v1 qualification |")
    strs_push(l, "| 34 | Smart contracts (chain-neutral model and backends) | PARTIAL — model and simulator (N69); EVM backend, run in py-evm (N70); WebAssembly adapter (N71); signed writes and account metadata, sBPF execution BLOCKED (N72); both VMs held to the simulator on generated sequences (N96) |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "After N107, 2026-10-05: twenty-nine VERIFIED (areas 2, 3, 5, 6 and 7 moved, the last four as scoped:")
    strs_push(l, "`audit-n107.md`), eight PARTIAL — every one an ecosystem or domain row — none RESEARCH or MISSING.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Historical.* After N106, 2026-10-05: twenty-four VERIFIED (area 13 moved: the M:N pool by default, its policy")
    strs_push(l, "stated), thirteen PARTIAL, none RESEARCH or MISSING.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Historical.* After N105, 2026-10-05: twenty-three VERIFIED (area 10 moved: one LIR both backends translate, with its")
    strs_push(l, "oracle), fourteen PARTIAL, none RESEARCH or MISSING. N101–N104 moved no row.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Historical.* After N100, 2026-10-04 (`docs/internal/audits/audit-n100.md`): twenty-two VERIFIED (several as scoped, area 30 for")
    strs_push(l, "mutation testing), fifteen PARTIAL, none RESEARCH or MISSING; BLOCKED parts named inside areas 12")
    strs_push(l, "(JIT), 34 (sBPF) and the formal evidence (proofs). Nothing moved between N88 and N100: N89–N99")
    strs_push(l, "widened PARTIAL rows and measured them. The zero-partial objective is not met.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Historical.* After N88, 2026-10-04: unchanged — area 21 widened and still PARTIAL.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Historical.* After N87, 2026-10-04: twenty-two VERIFIED (areas 19 and 20 moved, as scoped: profile enforcement")
    strs_push(l, "and obligation evidence, not certification), fifteen PARTIAL, none RESEARCH.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Historical.* After N86, 2026-10-04: twenty VERIFIED (area 18 moved, as scoped: two emulated")
    strs_push(l, "boards), seventeen PARTIAL, none RESEARCH.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Historical.* After N85, 2026-10-04: nineteen VERIFIED (area 17 moved, as scoped: a practical C ABI")
    strs_push(l, "subset), eighteen PARTIAL, none RESEARCH.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Historical.* After N84, 2026-10-04: eighteen VERIFIED (area 16 moved, as scoped: the standard")
    strs_push(l, "library 1.0), nineteen PARTIAL, none RESEARCH.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Historical.* After N83, 2026-10-04: seventeen VERIFIED (area 15 moved, as scoped: an opt-in pool,")
    strs_push(l, "macOS), twenty PARTIAL, none RESEARCH; nothing else moved between N77 and N82.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Historical.* After N76, 2026-10-03: sixteen VERIFIED (area 1 moved, for the reference parser),")
    strs_push(l, "twenty PARTIAL, one RESEARCH.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Historical, not current.* After N75's audit, 2026-10-02, across the 37 rows above (34 areas, with 2a, 10a and 10b): fifteen")
    strs_push(l, "VERIFIED (areas 4, 8, 9, 12 and 30 with a stated qualification — area 30 for mutation testing, its")
    strs_push(l, "fuzzing PARTIAL), twenty-one PARTIAL, one RESEARCH (15, the advanced scheduler), none MISSING. No")
    strs_push(l, "row says DESIGNED or BLOCKED as its whole status; the blocked parts are named inside areas 12 (no JIT:")
    strs_push(l, "`unsafe_code = \"forbid\"`, N65) and 34 (no sBPF toolchain, N72).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Historical, not current.* After N48 the count read fifteen VERIFIED, sixteen PARTIAL, two RESEARCH,")
    strs_push(l, "one MISSING, written as \"across the 34 rows\" though the table then had the same 37.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Historical, not current — kept as it was written.* After N39 the count read thirteen VERIFIED,")
    strs_push(l, "thirteen PARTIAL, three DESIGNED, two RESEARCH, five MISSING; before that, nine, sixteen, three,")
    strs_push(l, "two, five, not kept up since the first era. The first era's summary follows: the shape is")
    strs_push(l, "worth reading directly: **everything verified is either a front-end capability, a tooling")
    strs_push(l, "interface, or an evidence mechanism.** Nothing in the semantic core — ownership, effects,")
    strs_push(l, "capabilities, provenance — exists at all, and that is the accurate summary of where the")
    strs_push(l, "project stood after the first era. That stopped being true at N36–N38, and the rows below are the")
    strs_push(l, "current account.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Front end")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 1. Syntax, parser, CST — VERIFIED (the reference parser, N76)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1d (2026-10-14)** · *A bounded heap: `--heap-limit`* (`spec.md`, *A bounded heap*;")
    strs_push(l, "`openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, D5). `nazm build --heap-limit N` (bytes or")
    strs_push(l, "`K`/`M`/`G`, 64 KiB to 1024 GiB), or `heap-limit = \"N\"` in the root package's manifest, which the")
    strs_push(l, "flag overrides, builds a program whose every allocation — its units', the runtime's and the")
    strs_push(l, "platform unit's — goes through the counted heap: `nz.heap_malloc`, `nz.heap_realloc` and")
    strs_push(l, "`nz.heap_free`, a new runtime unit holding the limit, which keep the bytes asked for in a 16-byte")
    strs_push(l, "header and one atomic live count. An allocation that would pass the limit writes `nazm: error[N0406]:")
    strs_push(l, "out of memory: the heap limit of N bytes is reached` and exits 2 at once, from any task; the stack")
    strs_push(l, "unit's task stacks are not heap and keep C's allocator. LLVM units are renamed in their text, a")
    strs_push(l, "Cranelift unit's LIR imports before its object is keyed; refused for a board, WebAssembly, a library")
    strs_push(l, "and a runtime artifact. Without a limit the program's text is what it was. Build provenance records")
    strs_push(l, "the limit. EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since). Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/heap_limit.rs` — 3,000 live")
    strs_push(l, "strings print what the interpreter and the LIR oracle print, with the same memory report and nothing")
    strs_push(l, "live, under a 4 MiB limit at LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift, and end with the fixed line, status 2")
    strs_push(l, "and what was printed before under 64 KiB; four pool tasks five times over allocate millions of bytes")
    strs_push(l, "through 64 KiB; the manifest's limit and the flag over it; the refusals; and without a limit no unit")
    strs_push(l, "names the counted heap, while with one no unit but the heap's and the stack's reaches C's allocator.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1d (2026-10-14)** · *Streaming standard input* (`spec.md`, *Files and handles*, **Lines of")
    strs_push(l, "standard input**, and *The standard library*; `openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, P3).")
    strs_push(l, "`os_read_line(h, buf) -> Int`: standard input to and including its next newline, at most the buffer,")
    strs_push(l, "never past the line; `os_read` of standard input now reads the same 16 KiB buffer first, so lines")
    strs_push(l, "and frames mix — LSP's headers then the body they announce, MCP's lines. Any other handle is a")
    strs_push(l, "status (`InvalidInput`, a directory `IsADirectory`). `@std/io` gains `io_stdin_read`,")
    strs_push(l, "`io_stdin_read_exact` and `io_stdin_read_line`. EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since). Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/stdin_lines.rs` — two `\\r\\n` header lines, a five-byte frame, a line read")
    strs_push(l, "three bytes at a time, a byte, whole lines, a last line without a newline, the end and an")
    strs_push(l, "`UnexpectedEof`, alike in the interpreter, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift, fed whole and a byte at a")
    strs_push(l, "time, with the same memory report and nothing live; another handle's statuses alike everywhere;")
    strs_push(l, "`os_read`'s authority, effect and provenance. The LIR oracle runs no `os_` built-in, so it has no")
    strs_push(l, "answer here.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1e (2026-10-13)** · *`@std/regex`* (`spec.md`, *The standard library*; `openspec/changes/r1-language-")
    strs_push(l, "for-the-rewrite`, S5). Regular expressions in Nazm, matched in time linear in the text: a pattern is")
    strs_push(l, "parsed into a tree, compiled into a Thompson NFA, and every search runs it as a Pike VM — all states")
    strs_push(l, "advancing together a scalar value at a time, each held by at most one thread, preferred threads first —")
    strs_push(l, "so a search is O(m·n) and nothing backtracks. Leftmost-first, as Rust's `regex` and Perl; capture groups;")
    strs_push(l, "`find_all` with Rust's empty-match rule. Rust's syntax less what an automaton cannot do (backreferences,")
    strs_push(l, "lookbehind, lookahead past one scalar value — each refused by name); a one-scalar lookahead `(?!C)` is")
    strs_push(l, "kept, which the GPT-2 and `cl100k_base` pre-tokenisers' `\\s+(?!\\S)` needs. UTF-8 aware: `.` and a class")
    strs_push(l, "match one scalar value. Unicode 16.0's general categories `L`, `M`, `N`, their subcategories and `Pc`")
    strs_push(l, "are carried as compact range tables; `\\d`, `\\s`, `\\w` are Unicode's (`\\w` but for a few")
    strs_push(l, "`Other_Alphabetic` scalar values); `(?i)` folds ASCII letters only. Errors are `what at byte N`.")
    strs_push(l, "EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since). Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/regex.rs` — 77 patterns on their texts,")
    strs_push(l, "the first part's expectations checked against Python's `re` searched as Rust's `find_iter` searches,")
    strs_push(l, "the Unicode classes and both pre-tokenisers' patterns by hand; nine captures; 26 malformed patterns")
    strs_push(l, "refused at their offset; five patterns exponential under backtracking (`(a*)*b`, `(a|aa)*c`, …) failing")
    strs_push(l, "at once on 40 `a`s interpreted and on 200,000 compiled; a `cl100k_base` pre-split, captures, a search")
    strs_push(l, "from an offset and an error alike under the interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and")
    strs_push(l, "Cranelift with nothing live.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1b (2026-10-13)** · *Linear-time string building* (`spec.md`, *Strings*, **Building**, and")
    strs_push(l, "*What this costs*; `openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, D2). Core IR lowering writes `s =")
    strs_push(l, "str_concat(s, t)` on a `let mut` binding — not one a closure shares — as the internal `str_append`.")
    strs_push(l, "LIR appends `t` in place when `s`'s storage has one reference (the binding's), was made by an")
    strs_push(l, "append — its capacity carries a mark no other allocation's can — and has room after `s`'s bytes,")
    strs_push(l, "taking a reference for the new value that the old value's release gives back; otherwise it copies")
    strs_push(l, "into storage of twice the length (at least 16), marked. A literal has no storage of its own and is")
    strs_push(l, "copied. The interpreter applies the same rule to a backing an append made, taking the binding's")
    strs_push(l, "string out before it appends, so the two allocate the same strings. No checker rule moved, so no")
    strs_push(l, "epoch.")
    strs_push(l, "EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since). Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/string_append.rs` — two names for")
    strs_push(l, "one string each appended to, a slice kept across an append, a string appended to itself and a")
    strs_push(l, "literal, under the interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with nothing live;")
    strs_push(l, "100,000 appends allocating fewer than 64 strings under LLVM and Cranelift (200,000 allocated one")
    strs_push(l, "each before); `memory.rs`, sixteen appends filling one allocation exactly and a padded string's")
    strs_push(l, "spare byte left alone, counted the same by both implementations. The memory tests whose loops were")
    strs_push(l, "allocator churn or a count of concatenations now prepend, which still allocates each time.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1b (2026-10-13)** · *Warnings* (`spec.md`, *Patterns*; `diagnostics.md`;")
    strs_push(l, "`openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, L15). A warning severity: `nazm.diagnostic/1`'s")
    strs_push(l, "`severity` takes `\"warning\"`, and the first warning is `N0632` — a `_` or a name in a written")
    strs_push(l, "`match` of an enum that covers variants no arm names, listing them (the voice L3 kept when it")
    strs_push(l, "admitted `_`). The checker records warnings on the resolution, apart from the errors a stage stops")
    strs_push(l, "on; `nazm check` and `nazm build` report them and succeed, `--deny-warnings` refuses, and the")
    strs_push(l, "language service publishes them at the warning severity. A module that warns is not kept as")
    strs_push(l, "checked, so the warning is not cached away. Semantic epoch 66; EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since).")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm run` and `nazm test` do not report warnings, and a `@deprecated` use draws none yet (`N0620`")
    strs_push(l, "reserved). Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/warnings.rs` — both forms of the warning with exact")
    strs_push(l, "lists, none for a match naming every variant or an `if let`, again from the cache, as JSON;")
    strs_push(l, "`--deny-warnings` refusing a check and a build; a build that warns and runs.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1b (2026-10-13)** · *The stack asked for: `--stack-size`* (`spec.md`, *Native recursion, and")
    strs_push(l, "the stack it runs on*; `openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, L14). `nazm build")
    strs_push(l, "--stack-size N` (bytes or `K`/`M`/`G`, 64 KiB to 4 GiB; refused for a board or WebAssembly) runs")
    strs_push(l, "`main` on a thread of `N` bytes — the platform entry starts it and joins it, and runs `main` in place")
    strs_push(l, "if it cannot start — and stores `N` in the runtime's `nz.stack_bytes`, which a task's thread, the")
    strs_push(l, "pool's task stacks (under `NAZM_TASK_STACK`) and `nz.stack_check`'s limit read in place of 8 MiB,")
    strs_push(l, "256 KiB and 8 MiB. Runtime ABI 31; build provenance records the size. The interpreter's threads")
    strs_push(l, "follow `--max-depth`, as before. EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since). Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/stack_size.rs` — a 250,000-deep recursion in `main` and in a task that")
    strs_push(l, "meets `N0408` by default and finishes with `--stack-size 64M`, and meets it again with `4M`, under")
    strs_push(l, "LLVM and Cranelift, on the pool and a thread per task; the refusals. **Corrected (2026-10-13):**")
    strs_push(l, "`main`'s thread ended with its failure state, which is thread-local, so a sized program whose")
    strs_push(l, "`main` failed exited 0 with its stand-in value; the thread now hands the state back for the entry's")
    strs_push(l, "report. Found by CI, where a million-deep test's 512 MiB stacks passed Linux's address-space")
    strs_push(l, "ceiling.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R9 D15 (2026-10-15)** · *`nazm build --backend nazm`* (`docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.116;")
    strs_push(l, "`openspec/changes/r9-code-generator`, D14, D15). A third backend: each unit's LIR, printed, compiled")
    strs_push(l, "by Nazm's own code generator `nzcg` (`toolchain/codegen/`, written in Nazm), found by `NAZM_NZCG` or")
    strs_push(l, "installed as `libexec/nazm/nzcg`; its digest in every object's key; `--one-thread` from the")
    strs_push(l, "program's one-thread fact. A construct it refuses is `N0101` per construct with no fallback, any")
    strs_push(l, "other failure `N0900`; a missing generator or a target it does not carry (anything but the two")
    strs_push(l, "macOS targets before 1.0) is refused before compiling. Failures unwind as LLVM's do (its 7.5), so")
    strs_push(l, "the two backends' objects link together. EXPERIMENTAL. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/nazm_backend.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "(117 inputs agree with LLVM, output, diagnostics, status and memory report), a `nazm` column in the")
    strs_push(l, "backend-differential harness and `failure_convention.rs` on macOS; mutants `r9-…`. Packaged (its")
    strs_push(l, "7.8): `scripts/host-archive.sh` and `scripts/release-candidate.sh` build `nzcg` with the `nazm` they")
    strs_push(l, "package and install it as `libexec/nazm/nzcg` on the macOS targets (the candidate's `MANIFEST.txt`")
    strs_push(l, "and `PROVENANCE.txt` name its digest), and `scripts/clean-install-test.sh` builds with")
    strs_push(l, "`--backend nazm` where the archive carries it; the unpacked toolchain finds it with `NAZM_NZCG`")
    strs_push(l, "unset (`the_packaged_toolchain_finds_its_generator_beside_nazm_without_the_variable`). Its 7.9:")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm profile --backend nazm`, sampled too (`debugger.rs`, `debugger_v3.rs`), and the provenance")
    strs_push(l, "record naming the generator by its digest (`backend.nzcg`, checked against the schema; the SBOM")
    strs_push(l, "lists it as a tool; `a_program_nazms_own_generator_built_names_it_by_its_digest`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Performance leadership (2026-10-15)** · *Failures by unwinding* (`docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.115;")
    strs_push(l, "`openspec/changes/performance-leadership`, 4.2). On the hosted targets under LLVM a Nazm function")
    strs_push(l, "returns its result alone and a failure is a forced unwind (`nz.raise`, `_Unwind_ForcedUnwind`, the C")
    strs_push(l, "personality `__gcc_personality_v0`): a call whose failure edge releases something is an `invoke`")
    strs_push(l, "whose landing pad continues on that edge, one into a bare failure exit a plain call, and every plain")
    strs_push(l, "entry lands the unwind and reads the flag, so C is never unwound into. WebAssembly, WASI, the boards,")
    strs_push(l, "Windows, Cranelift and the LIR oracle keep the failure bit; LIR's text and schema are unchanged, its")
    strs_push(l, "validator holds a call's `failed` value to the branch ending its block. Runtime ABI 34; no semantic")
    strs_push(l, "epoch. `fib(35)` at `-O2` 55.7 → 44.3 ms; `words` 132.4 → 129.4 ms; a failure through frames that")
    strs_push(l, "own something is slower (`limitations.md`). EXPERIMENTAL until the performance-leadership change")
    strs_push(l, "closes; Linux and the mobile targets are built and checked by object here, not run. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/failure_convention.rs` — failures through recursion, function values, trait")
    strs_push(l, "methods, a task, a C export, a callback C calls, ten thousand frames of `defer`s and an exhausted")
    strs_push(l, "stack, the same on every implementation; the hosted IR's shape and which targets' objects name the")
    strs_push(l, "unwinder; `op::llvm::tests`, `op::validate::tests`; seven mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1.5 (2026-10-15)** · *A `for` over a split builds no list* (R1.5 task 3.3). `for w in")
    strs_push(l, "s.split(sep)` is lowered in Core IR through `@std/text`'s `text_split_end` and `text_split_next`,")
    strs_push(l, "which find each piece as `text_split` does; the pieces, the empty ones, `break` and `continue` are")
    strs_push(l, "the list's. Word frequency 189 → 143 ms on the host (with the one-byte separator's own loop).")
    strs_push(l, "Evidence: `shorter_forms.rs` (`a_for_over_a_split_reads_its_pieces_without_a_list_everywhere`)")
    strs_push(l, "under the interpreter and both backends, and Core IR's calls; three mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1.5 (2026-10-15)** · *The prelude's standard modules; `top` and `sort_by`* (`spec.md`, *Shorter")
    strs_push(l, "forms*; R1.5 design D9, D10). A program's own module is given `@std/hash`, `@std/hashmap`,")
    strs_push(l, "`@std/ordmap`, `@std/sort` and `@std/text` where it names one of their items; a name the module")
    strs_push(l, "declares or a written import brings in hides the prelude's; a package's and a standard module's")
    strs_push(l, "imports stay written; a module naming none is unchanged, so restriction profiles see what they")
    strs_push(l, "saw. `m.top(n)` and `m.sort_by(less)`. Semantic epoch 85; EXPERIMENTAL until R1.5 closes.")
    strs_push(l, "Evidence: `shorter_forms.rs` — four tests (everywhere, hiding, profiles, packages) and the D5 test")
    strs_push(l, "restated; five mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1.5 (2026-10-15)** · *`@std/option` and `@std/result` in the prelude* (`spec.md`, *Shorter forms*;")
    strs_push(l, "R1.5 task 4.5). The two join D9's prelude modules, so `r.unwrap_or(1)`, `o.is_some()` and `r.ok()`")
    strs_push(l, "need no `use` in a program's own module; `unwrap_or`, which both answer, attaches both and the")
    strs_push(l, "receiver's type picks the function. A method called only in an interpolation's hole now names its")
    strs_push(l, "module too (D9 had missed it). Hiding, packages and profiles as D9. Semantic epoch 86;")
    strs_push(l, "EXPERIMENTAL until R1.5 closes. Evidence: `shorter_forms.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "(`option_and_result_methods_need_no_use_everywhere` under the interpreter and both backends;")
    strs_push(l, "`a_module_s_own_option_function_hides_the_prelude_s_and_a_profile_sees_what_is_named`); three mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1.5 (2026-10-15)** · *A line break separates `match` arms* (`spec.md`, *Shorter forms*; R1.5 task")
    strs_push(l, "4.6). An arm ending at a line break needs no `,` before the next, as a statement needs no `;`")
    strs_push(l, "(5b.19); `,` is still read and the two mix; two arms on one line still need it (`N0100`); `nazm fmt`")
    strs_push(l, "keeps whichever was written. The grammar's `match_arms` says so in prose (a line break is not a")
    strs_push(l, "token). Semantic epoch 87; EXPERIMENTAL until R1.5 closes. Evidence: `shorter_forms.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "(`match_arms_on_their_own_lines_need_no_comma_everywhere` under the interpreter and both backends;")
    strs_push(l, "`two_arms_on_one_line_still_need_their_comma_and_fmt_keeps_what_was_written`); two mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1.5 (2026-10-15)** · *`nazm build --release`* (`docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.117; R1.5 design D15). A")
    strs_push(l, "hardened macOS executable from the LLVM backend: every function stack-protected (`sspstrong`, so")
    strs_push(l, "one with a local array or an address-taken local checks a canary), linked `-pie`, stripped of its")
    strs_push(l, "symbols and debug map, and signed ad hoc with the hardened runtime. Refused, by name, for another")
    strs_push(l, "backend or target and with `--debug`, `--lib`, `--objects` or `--runtime`; the default build is")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged. Linux, Windows and the other targets are not hardened yet. EXPERIMENTAL until R1.5")
    strs_push(l, "closes. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/release_build.rs` (macOS host) — a test per property with")
    strs_push(l, "`nm`, `otool` and `codesign`, reproducibility, refusals, provenance; four mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1.5 (2026-10-15)** · *Printing in your own program* (`spec.md`, *Shorter forms*; R1.5 design")
    strs_push(l, "D8). In a module of the program itself — a key with no `@`, so not `@std`, the prelude or a package —")
    strs_push(l, "the authority check (`effects::authority`) counts the output authority `main` holds as held, so a")
    strs_push(l, "function prints with no `out` passed; a package's function still needs it, and every other")
    strs_push(l, "authority is passed as before. Semantic epoch 82; EXPERIMENTAL until R1.5 closes. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/shorter_forms.rs` — a helper calling a helper that prints, under every")
    strs_push(l, "implementation; a dependency's printing function refused with `N0369`; a file still needing an")
    strs_push(l, "`IoCap`; two mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1.5 (2026-10-15)** · *A standard module by its dotted path* (`spec.md`, *Shorter forms*; R1.5")
    strs_push(l, "design D7). `use std.json` is `use \"@std/json\"`, with `as name` as before; a quoted path is still a")
    strs_push(l, "file. Semantic epoch 81; EXPERIMENTAL until R1.5 closes. Evidence: `shorter_forms.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "(`a_standard_module_by_its_dotted_path_is_the_quoted_import_everywhere`) under every")
    strs_push(l, "implementation; one mutant.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1.5 (2026-10-15)** · *`List[T]` is the list; `Chain[T]`* (`spec.md`, *Shorter forms* and")
    strs_push(l, "*Immutable indirection*; R1.5 design D7). `List[T]` in a type position is `Vec[T]` — one type with")
    strs_push(l, "`Vec[T]`, `Ints` and `Strs`, shown as before — a prelude name a module's own `List` hides. R1a's")
    strs_push(l, "immutable sequence, which held the name, is `Chain[T]` with built-ins `chain_from_vec`,")
    strs_push(l, "`chain_empty`, `chain_len` and `chain_get`, in every layer's spelling of it (Core IR, MIR keys,")
    strs_push(l, "symbols, messages, the Nazm-written pipeline's type spellings), `@derive(json)`/`(toml)`'s")
    strs_push(l, "generated code and `@std/toml`'s `Toml`; a call of a `list_` built-in a module does not define is")
    strs_push(l, "refused, `N0637`, naming the `chain_` one. A breaking change of a 0.10.0-stable surface, listed for")
    strs_push(l, "the next release; the compatibility corpus held no case using it. The checker's Rust identifiers")
    strs_push(l, "(`Type::List`, `Intrinsic::List*`) keep their names. Semantic epoch 83; EXPERIMENTAL until R1.5")
    strs_push(l, "closes. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/shorter_forms.rs` — `List[T]` as a `Vec[T]` and `Chain[T]`")
    strs_push(l, "as R1a's list under every implementation, the refusal by name; `box_list.rs`, `order_hash.rs`,")
    strs_push(l, "`derive_json.rs`, `toml.rs` and `build.rs`' coverage of every built-in, renamed; two mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1.5 (2026-10-15)** · *`[…]` is a list* (`spec.md`, *Shorter forms* and *Arrays*; R1.5 design D6).")
    strs_push(l, "`[1, 2, 3]` where no fixed array `[T; n]` is expected is a `Vec[Int]`, its element type the first")
    strs_push(l, "element's; a fixed array is written where its type says so, and `[v; n]` is always one. A changed")
    strs_push(l, "meaning, listed as a breaking change for the next release: an unannotated `let a = [1, 2, 3]` was")
    strs_push(l, "an array, copied on assignment, and is now a list every name shares. An empty `[]` with no type to")
    strs_push(l, "take is refused (`N0618`). The tests, the compatibility corpus's three array cases (re-pinned) and")
    strs_push(l, "the Nazm-written code generator's two array uses write `[T; n]` where they mean arrays. Semantic")
    strs_push(l, "epoch 84; EXPERIMENTAL until R1.5 closes; `nazm fix`'s annotation (D6) is not yet written.")
    strs_push(l, "Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/shorter_forms.rs` — a shared list and a copied typed array under")
    strs_push(l, "every implementation, the empty list's refusal; `arrays.rs`, `const_tables.rs`, `compat_v1.rs`;")
    strs_push(l, "two mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1.5 (2026-10-15)** · *Map literals and `Map[K, V]`* (`spec.md`, *Shorter forms*; R1.5 design D5).")
    strs_push(l, "`{\"a\": 1, \"b\": 2}` is read by the parser as the block that builds it — `hashmap_single` for the")
    strs_push(l, "first entry, which settles the types, then `hashmap_set` — and `Map[K, V]` is `HashMap[K, V]` where")
    strs_push(l, "the hash map is in scope — since D9, in a program's module with no `use`. The empty `{}` is still")
    strs_push(l, "an empty block; an empty map is `hashmap_new()`. Semantic epoch 80; EXPERIMENTAL")
    strs_push(l, "until R1.5 closes. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/shorter_forms.rs` under every implementation;")
    strs_push(l, "three mutants, one holding D4's conversions (`UInt64(x)` stays a call, found when D5's first test")
    strs_push(l, "ran).")
    strs_push(l, "**R1.5 (2026-10-16)** · *The empty map `{}`* (`spec.md`, *Shorter forms*; D5). `{}` where a")
    strs_push(l, "`Map[K, V]` is expected — a typed `let`, an argument, a field, a result, a `match` arm — is the")
    strs_push(l, "empty map, `hashmap_new()` checked at the braces; anywhere else it is the empty block, and a")
    strs_push(l, "value wanted of it is refused (`N0300`) with help that writes the type. The front end written")
    strs_push(l, "in Nazm follows (`compiler/sema.nz`, `compiler/core.nz`). Semantic epoch 90; EXPERIMENTAL until")
    strs_push(l, "R1.5 closes. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/shorter_forms.rs` under every implementation; two")
    strs_push(l, "mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1.5 (2026-10-15)** · *Fields by position, variants without their enum* (`spec.md`, *Shorter")
    strs_push(l, "forms*; R1.5 design D4). `Point(1, 2)`, `Shape.Rect(3, 4)`, `Circle(2)`, `Dot`, and in a pattern")
    strs_push(l, "`Rect(w, h)` and `Circle(r)`: the checker names positional fields in declaration order and finds a")
    strs_push(l, "variant written alone among the enums in scope (`N0636` where two share it; in a pattern, the")
    strs_push(l, "value's own enum); Core IR lowers such a construction or name as the variant it was read as, and")
    strs_push(l, "provenance takes a positional payload whole, which is sound. Semantic epoch 79; EXPERIMENTAL until")
    strs_push(l, "R1.5 closes. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/shorter_forms.rs` — every form under every")
    strs_push(l, "implementation, the refusals by name, a secret bound by position still refused at a write; three")
    strs_push(l, "mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1.5 (2026-10-15)** · *Short closures* (`spec.md`, *Shorter forms*; R1.5 design D3).")
    strs_push(l, "`|a, b| a < b`, `|n: Int| n + 1`, `|| e`: the closure node a function expression makes, its")
    strs_push(l, "unwritten types taken from the function type expected where it is written, or — with none")
    strs_push(l, "expected — the result type its body's (settled after the body is checked) and each parameter's")
    strs_push(l, "written (`N0635`). Semantic epoch 78; EXPERIMENTAL until R1.5 closes. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/shorter_forms.rs` — arguments, a typed `let`, captures and `||` under every")
    strs_push(l, "implementation; the refusal; two mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1.5 (2026-10-15)** · *Expression bodies* (`spec.md`, *Shorter forms*; R1.5 design D2).")
    strs_push(l, "`fn double(n: Int): Int = n * 2`; a private function may leave its result type to the expression,")
    strs_push(l, "`fn add(a: Int, b: Int) = a + b`. Those bodies are checked first, each after the inferred functions")
    strs_push(l, "it calls (`crates/nazm-core/src/check/infer.rs`), and the type settled in the resolution and the")
    strs_push(l, "module's names before any caller is checked; a `pub` function, a method, a body that reaches itself")
    strs_push(l, "or one with no value is `N0634`. Semantic epoch 77; EXPERIMENTAL until R1.5 closes. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/shorter_forms.rs` — `main` written first and a caller before its callees,")
    strs_push(l, "the interpreter and both backends agreeing; the refusals by name; four mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1.5 (2026-10-15)** · *`nazm run` compiles* (`spec.md`, *`nazm run` compiles*; R1.5 design D11).")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm run` builds the program with Cranelift in process into a private temporary directory, runs it")
    strs_push(l, "with the caller's standard streams and environment, and ends with its status (`128 +` a signal's);")
    strs_push(l, "nothing about the build is printed. `nazm run --interpret` is the interpreter, still the oracle;")
    strs_push(l, "`--max-iterations` and `--max-depth` require it. A refusal only a native build makes (`N0101`,")
    strs_push(l, "`N0357`, `N0358`) is `nazm run`'s, with help naming `--interpret`: neither falls back. Every test that")
    strs_push(l, "meant the interpreter says `--interpret`. `fib(35)`: 5.24 s → 0.17 s warm (`performance.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "EXPERIMENTAL until R1.5 closes. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/run_compiled.rs` — the two agree on")
    strs_push(l, "stdout, stderr, the memory report and the status; both refusals, the limits, the temporary")
    strs_push(l, "directory removed; mutants in `xtask/mutations/mutations.toml`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1.5 (2026-10-15)** · *Dead-stripping* (`docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.114; R1.5 design D14). A hosted")
    strs_push(l, "executable is linked with `-dead_strip` (macOS, iOS) or with `--gc-sections` over objects compiled")
    strs_push(l, "with `-ffunction-sections -fdata-sections`, and Cranelift's with a section per function and datum")
    strs_push(l, "(translator revision 6) (Linux, Android), so a standard function or runtime part")
    strs_push(l, "nothing calls is left out; libraries, Windows, WebAssembly and the boards link as before. `words`")
    strs_push(l, "at `-O2` 105,728 → 61,184 bytes under LLVM, 197,216 → 74,816 under Cranelift (`performance.md`,")
    strs_push(l, "*R1.5 D14*). EXPERIMENTAL until R1.5 closes; Linux's sizes are unmeasured on the host, but")
    strs_push(l, "`dead_strip.rs` passes on Linux x86_64 (CI) and aarch64 (contained) since `0c8bad53`. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/dead_strip.rs` — an unused `@std/text` function absent under both backends")
    strs_push(l, "at `-O0` and `-O2`, the program's output unchanged, the same objects linked whole larger;")
    strs_push(l, "`backend::tests` for each target's arguments; two mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1.5 (2026-10-15)** · *The user cache* (`docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.113; R1.5 design D12). The")
    strs_push(l, "runtime's units and each `@std` or prelude module's own unit are filed in a user cache —")
    strs_push(l, "`~/Library/Caches/nazm` on macOS, `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/nazm` or `~/.cache/nazm` elsewhere,")
    strs_push(l, "`NAZM_CACHE_DIR` when that is set, `NAZM_USER_CACHE_DIR` above both (empty: off) — under the project")
    strs_push(l, "store's `nazm.object/1` keys, so a new project compiles only its own units; the project's own")
    strs_push(l, "objects stay in its `.nazm/`. No new key: everything that changes an object's bytes was already in")
    strs_push(l, "it. `--no-cache` and board builds use neither store; cargo-started tests turn it off")
    strs_push(l, "(`.cargo/config.toml`). EXPERIMENTAL until R1.5 closes. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/user_cache.rs` — a second project reuses the runtime and `@std/text` under")
    strs_push(l, "both backends and files only its own two units; its executable is byte-identical to a `--no-cache`")
    strs_push(l, "build's; `-O2`, a heap limit and another target reuse nothing, and a 64K limit is never taken from a")
    strs_push(l, "1G build's objects or the reverse; deleting the user cache changes nothing; the platform default,")
    strs_push(l, "`NAZM_CACHE_DIR` alone and the empty variable; three mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1.5 (2026-10-15)** · *A result type after `:`* (`spec.md`, *Shorter forms*; R1.5 design D1).")
    strs_push(l, "`fn fib(n: Int): Int`, `fn(Int): Int`, a trait method's and a function expression's: the parser")
    strs_push(l, "takes `:` or `->` before a result type, so every implementation reads them alike; `nazm fmt` keeps")
    strs_push(l, "the form written until R2. Semantic epoch 76; EXPERIMENTAL until R1.5 closes. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/shorter_forms.rs` — the interpreter and both backends agree, `->` beside `:`;")
    strs_push(l, "two mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1 (2026-10-14)** · *Speed: the failure bit, and the failure paths laid out cold*")
    strs_push(l, "(`openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, 5b.8; `docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.106, *The failure")
    strs_push(l, "bit*). A Nazm function returns whether it failed beside its result — `{ T, i1 }` under LLVM, a")
    strs_push(l, "second result under Cranelift, a pair in the LIR oracle — false on every `return`, true on the new")
    strs_push(l, "`fail` exit; a direct or indirect call of one branches on that bit rather than loading the")
    strs_push(l, "thread's failure flag. `nz.fail` still sets the flag and the message, and what calls a Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "function from outside still reads it: a task's trampoline, an export's C entry, the platform entry,")
    strs_push(l, "which calls `main` (an interrupt handler, a board's task or failure hook) through a plain entry")
    strs_push(l, "under its symbol with its old signature, the function itself being `<symbol>.body`. The runtime is")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged (ABI as before); `TRANSLATOR_REVISION` 4. Blocks only a failure reaches are laid out cold")
    strs_push(l, "in both backends (LLVM branch weights, Cranelift cold blocks), without which the bit was slower")
    strs_push(l, "under clang. `fib(35)`, Apple M1 Pro, hyperfine median of 20: LLVM `-O2` 66.8 → 55.4 ms, Cranelift")
    strs_push(l, "106.3 → 83.8 ms. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/failure_convention.rs` — a failure 400 frames deep in a")
    strs_push(l, "direct recursion, through a function value, through a trait method's generic instance, and in a")
    strs_push(l, "task, each ending with status 2 and `N0401` at its line with nothing live on the interpreter, LLVM")
    strs_push(l, "`-O0` and `-O2` and Cranelift (and the LIR oracle outside tasks); one inside a C export under both")
    strs_push(l, "backends at both levels; the LIR naming the bit and the plain entry; the validator refusing a bit")
    strs_push(l, "or a `fail` where the convention has none. Seven mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1 (2026-10-14)** · *Conveniences for the first program* (`spec.md`, *Conveniences for the")
    strs_push(l, "first program*; 5b.16 and 5b.17, in part). `let x: T = e` checks `e` against `T`; a generic call's")
    strs_push(l, "type parameter its arguments leave open is unified with the type its result is wanted as")
    strs_push(l, "(`check_generic_call`'s `expected`); `/* … */` nests, `N0007` when unclosed, and the formatter keeps")
    strs_push(l, "what follows one on its line; the parser reads `loop` as `while true`, `while let` as a `match` with")
    strs_push(l, "a `break` arm, and an impl without a trait as functions named `<type>_<method>`. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/conveniences.rs` — all of them in one program, alike everywhere, nothing")
    strs_push(l, "live; the refusals that stand. Seven mutants. Left of 5b.16–5b.17: `[1, 2, 3]` as a `Vec`, match")
    strs_push(l, "guards, `?` on `Option`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1 (2026-10-14)** · *Methods and indexes by name* (`spec.md`, *Methods and indexes by name*;")
    strs_push(l, "5b.15). Where no trait gives the receiver's type the method, `x.m(args)` is checked as the call")
    strs_push(l, "`<prefix>_m(x, args)` keyed by the method's name, its prefix the type's name in lower case (and")
    strs_push(l, "`text` after `str` for a `Str`), and Core IR lowering reads the call the checker recorded")
    strs_push(l, "(`Resolution::named_method`); `xs[i]` and a binding's `xs[i] = v` on a `Vec`, `Ints`, `Strs` or")
    strs_push(l, "`Bytes` are its `_get` and `_set` the same way. A compound assignment's read of an element is keyed")
    strs_push(l, "apart from its write. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/named_methods.rs` — methods on a `Vec`, a")
    strs_push(l, "`Str`, an `Int` and a `HashMap`, indexes read, written and compounded, a trait's method winning,")
    strs_push(l, "alike everywhere with nothing live; what has no function of the name refused. Six mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1 (2026-10-14)** · *R1 promoted to stable* (8.1; `spec.md`, *Stability classification for 1.0*).")
    strs_push(l, "Nineteen R1 sections and every inline \"EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since)\" became STABLE 1.0, as a 1.x")
    strs_push(l, "addition stable since R1 closed (0.10.0); `stability.md` and `limitations.md` follow. Seven cases")
    strs_push(l, "joined the 1.0 compatibility corpus, pinned (`tests/compat/v1/run/r1-*`): syntax, methods and")
    strs_push(l, "maps, patterns and tuples, strings, cells, `defer` and `for`, derived ordering and JSON, and R1e's")
    strs_push(l, "libraries — each run interpreted and by both backends. Writing them found three defects, fixed")
    strs_push(l, "under epoch 75: a `defer`'s last value was refused (it is discarded, as a loop body's is), a")
    strs_push(l, "pattern `let` needed its `;`, and a line beginning with `(` or `[` was read as a call or index of")
    strs_push(l, "the line before (`let (a, b) = p` then `(b, a)`); a call's `(` and an index's `[` are now on the")
    strs_push(l, "line of what they apply to. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/compat_v1.rs`, `defer.rs`,")
    strs_push(l, "`line_breaks.rs`. Three mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1 (2026-10-14)** · *The interpreter's stack bounds its depth* (4.9). Each evaluation thread —")
    strs_push(l, "the main one and every task's — records where its stack ends (`eval::mark_stack`), and a call")
    strs_push(l, "made past that, less the margin the shape-recursive passes need, is `N0403` (\"recursed deeper than")
    strs_push(l, "the interpreter's stack holds\"), so a call nested in an expression, several evaluator frames on a")
    strs_push(l, "debug build, reports instead of crashing below `--max-depth`. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/stack_floor.rs` — a million-deep nested recursion at the default and at")
    strs_push(l, "`--max-depth 15000`, `N0403` and never a signal. One mutant.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1 (2026-10-14)** · *Word frequency at 195.5 ms* (5b.9; `docs/internal/performance-log.md`). The idiomatic")
    strs_push(l, "5b.10 program went from 531 to 195.5 ms (Apple M1 Pro, hyperfine median of 20): `@std/text`'s")
    strs_push(l, "`text_split` compares a slice only where the first byte matches and `text_lines` is one pass;")
    strs_push(l, "`@std/hashmap` remembers the entry `m[k]` found so `m[k] += n` writes without a second probe, and")
    strs_push(l, "reads its vectors once a probe; MIR borrows a field of a local read only to be an operand")
    strs_push(l, "(`Rvalue::FieldBorrow`: no reference taken or given back, left out of the unwind block's drops, and")
    strs_push(l, "the validator refusing a drop or move of one); the LLVM backend declares the runtime's state")
    strs_push(l, "`hidden`, so it is addressed without the global offset table. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/borrowed_fields.rs` — a borrowed field live across a failure, every")
    strs_push(l, "implementation reclaiming everything; `named_methods.rs` — a remembered entry never another key's,")
    strs_push(l, "nor surviving a removal; lines and splits at their edges. Seven mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1 (2026-10-14)** · *One list type* (`spec.md`, *Sequences are shared, mutable, and never freed*;")
    strs_push(l, "5b.18). `Ints` and `Strs` resolve to `Vec[Int]` and `Vec[Str]` — interned before any type is")
    strs_push(l, "resolved, in the built-ins' signatures and when an interface is read — and are shown by those")
    strs_push(l, "shorter names; the interpreter's `ints_*` and `strs_*` are its `vec_*` on one value, the separate")
    strs_push(l, "`Value::Ints` and `Value::Strs` gone; native code already shared one layout. A `Strs` and a")
    strs_push(l, "`Vec[Str]` share one provenance cell. Epoch 74. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/lists.rs` — the")
    strs_push(l, "two names passed for each other through every family of built-ins and through `@std/text`, alike")
    strs_push(l, "everywhere with nothing live; `for_loops.rs` for the shared cell. Three mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1 (2026-10-14)** · *The program's authority reported* (`spec.md`, *What `main` holds, and how it")
    strs_push(l, "ends*; 5b.1). `nazm build` writes `authority: …` on standard error after a build of a program with a")
    strs_push(l, "`main` — each capability `main` holds, given by option C or written, and what it reaches — and")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm inspect` gives the same as `authority` (`crates/nazm-cli/src/authority.rs`, read from `main`'s")
    strs_push(l, "signature as parsed). 5b.5, effects inferred for a function that is not `pub`, was found to be the")
    strs_push(l, "rule since N36 and is pinned. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/main_ends.rs` — a given `OutCap` and a")
    strs_push(l, "written `IoCap` and `NetCap`, from `build` and `inspect`; a private function with no effect set")
    strs_push(l, "called by a pure one, and another module's undeclared one refused (`N0366`). Two mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1 (2026-10-14)** · *Match guards* (`spec.md`, *Patterns*, Guards; 5b.17). `P if G => E`: the")
    strs_push(l, "parser reads the guard into `MatchArm::guard`; the checker types it as a `Bool` (`N0301`) with the")
    strs_push(l, "pattern's names bound and leaves a guarded arm out of exhaustiveness and reachability; Core IR")
    strs_push(l, "lowering sends any `match` with a guard to the general lowering, whose arm test becomes `if <pattern")
    strs_push(l, "matches> { <names bound>; G } else { false }`, the names bound in a region of their own before the")
    strs_push(l, "arm's body binds them again. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/match_guards.rs` — guards on")
    strs_push(l, "integers, on variants with an `Int` and a `Str` payload, on `Option`, and in a loop, alike")
    strs_push(l, "everywhere with nothing live; a guard that is not a `Bool`, a guarded arm relied on for coverage, a")
    strs_push(l, "guarded arm below a catch-all, and a name a guard cannot see, refused. Five mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1 (2026-10-14)** · *Map entries by index* (`spec.md`, *Methods and indexes by name*; 5b.7). On any")
    strs_push(l, "type but a sequence, `m[k]` is `<prefix>_at(m, k)` and a binding's `m[k] = v` its `_set`, the prefix")
    strs_push(l, "as a method's; a compound update's read is `<prefix>_at_or(m, k, zero)` with the value type's zero")
    strs_push(l, "(`check::zero_of`; `Resolution::map_fallback`, which Core IR lowering reads to pass the same zero).")
    strs_push(l, "`@std/hashmap` and `@std/ordmap` gained `_at` and `_at_or`. A compound update's key may be a string.")
    strs_push(l, "Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/named_methods.rs` — counting words, a `Str` and a `Float64` entry")
    strs_push(l, "built by `+=` and `*=`, written and read, alike everywhere with nothing live; an absent entry read by")
    strs_push(l, "index failing `N0405` in every implementation. Five mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1 (2026-10-14)** · *Short variants and inferred enum arguments* (`spec.md`, *Short variants*;")
    strs_push(l, "`openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, 5b.14). An enum's construction written without type")
    strs_push(l, "arguments takes them from the type it is wanted as, or from payload fields declared as its")
    strs_push(l, "parameters (`check/construct.rs`, `inferred_enum`), each payload value checked once; where neither")
    strs_push(l, "decides, `N0352` as before. The parser reads `Some(x)`, `Ok(x)`, `Err(e)` and `None` as the")
    strs_push(l, "prelude's variants in expressions and patterns, `Enum.Variant` without `()` in a pattern, and a")
    strs_push(l, "capitalised `Name.Member` without `()` in an expression as a variant. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/short_variants.rs` — a program of them alike under the interpreter and each")
    strs_push(l, "backend, nothing live; what nothing decides still `N0352`. Seven mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1 (2026-10-14)** · *`print` of any value, and `println`* (`spec.md`, *Output*; 5b.4 and 5b.13).")
    strs_push(l, "The parser reads `print(x)` and `eprint(x)` of anything but a string literal as `print(f\"{x}\")`,")
    strs_push(l, "and `println(x)`/`eprintln(x)` as `print(f\"{x}\\n\")` — the hole keyed by the argument list's span,")
    strs_push(l, "so a `Show` resolves as an interpolation's does; `println` and `eprintln` are built-in names.")
    strs_push(l, "Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/printing.rs` — every kind of value on both streams alike")
    strs_push(l, "everywhere, nothing live; what has no text, a function named `println`, and printing without")
    strs_push(l, "`OutCap` refused. Three mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1 (2026-10-13)** · *Compound assignment* (`spec.md`, *Mutation is opt-in and visible at the")
    strs_push(l, "binding*; `openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, 5b.12). `+=`, `-=`, `*=`, `/=`, `%=`,")
    strs_push(l, "`&=`, `|=`, `^=`, `<<=` and `>>=`, each one token, parse as `place = place op e`, so nothing below")
    strs_push(l, "the parser changed; an index in the place is a name, a field of one or a number, and one with a")
    strs_push(l, "call is refused by name rather than computed twice. Epoch 72. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/compound_assign.rs` — every operator on a binding, a field and an element,")
    strs_push(l, "alike under the interpreter and each backend; overflow failing as the operator does; what it cannot")
    strs_push(l, "mean refused; the formatter keeping each token. Six mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1 (2026-10-13)** · *`else if`, a line break for `;`, and a value nobody wants*")
    strs_push(l, "(`spec.md`, *`else if`, and a line break for `;`* and *One block*;")
    strs_push(l, "`openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, 5b.11 and 5b.19). `else if` (and `else if let`)")
    strs_push(l, "parses as `else { if … }`, so nothing below the parser changed; `docs/user/grammar.ebnf` and the guide")
    strs_push(l, "had written it since 2026-09-21 while the parser refused it, which no example caught — two")
    strs_push(l, "examples now do. A missing statement `;` is taken as written where a line break or the block's")
    strs_push(l, "`}` follows; an expression still continues over a line wherever the parser can continue it; a")
    strs_push(l, "member's name must be on its `.`'s line. `nazm fmt` reads the same rule, so a program without")
    strs_push(l, "semicolons is laid out as one with them is. A loop body's last value is discarded, and an `if` as")
    strs_push(l, "a statement — or the last line of a loop body, or of such an `if`'s branch — may end its branches")
    strs_push(l, "differently and produces nothing; where a value is wanted, `N0302` stands. Epoch 71. Eight test")
    strs_push(l, "fixtures that relied on a line break not ending a statement were put on one line, and an")
    strs_push(l, "`incomplete.rs` expectation that existed only because its fixture lacked a `;` now offers the")
    strs_push(l, "variants. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/line_breaks.rs` — `else if` and `else if let` chains as")
    strs_push(l, "values and as statements, a program without semicolons and the discarded values reclaimed, alike")
    strs_push(l, "under the interpreter and each backend; what still needs a `;` refused by name; the formatter's")
    strs_push(l, "layout of such a program, kept. Eight mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1 (2026-10-13)** · *Speed: integer text, the map's table, one string per interpolated")
    strs_push(l, "integer, inlined reference counting* (`openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, 5b.9). An")
    strs_push(l, "integer's text is the runtime's own digit loop (`nz.format_int`, `nz.format_u64`), not `snprintf`.")
    strs_push(l, "`@std/hashmap`'s table holds positions into dense arrays of hashes, keys and values, a power of two")
    strs_push(l, "long: a probe compares hashes, a replaced value allocates nothing, a removal moves the last entry")
    strs_push(l, "into the freed place; the slots, and so the iteration order, are as before. An interpolation's hole")
    strs_push(l, "of an integer type of at most 64 bits after other text lowers to the internal `str_concat_num`: one")
    strs_push(l, "string, the digits written after the text. A hosted unit carries `available_externally` copies of")
    strs_push(l, "`nz.arr_retain`, `nz.arr_release`, `nz.seq_release`, `nz.str_retain` and `nz.str_release`, inlined")
    strs_push(l, "where it is optimised; a board's runtime defines its own and is left alone. Word frequency over")
    strs_push(l, "2,000,000 words under LLVM `-O2`: 392 → 222 ms; `fib(35)` unchanged at 68 ms. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/speed_text.rs` — every integer type's extremes, alone and after text, alike")
    strs_push(l, "under the interpreter and each backend; a thousand `f\"w{i}\"` allocating one string each,")
    strs_push(l, "everywhere; the map against a model of itself over 3,000 operations; a hosted unit's copies. Seven")
    strs_push(l, "mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1 (2026-10-13)** · *Speed: a program of one thread, and the inlined stack check*")
    strs_push(l, "(`openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, 5b.8). The stack check (N49) is three instructions")
    strs_push(l, "in the function — this frame against the thread's limit — calling the runtime only on a thread's")
    strs_push(l, "first check or past the limit (LLVM; Cranelift still calls it). A program whose `main` holds no")
    strs_push(l, "`SpawnCap`, `NetCap` or `ForeignCap` and is not a library has one thread, and its failure state and")
    strs_push(l, "stack limit are plain globals rather than thread-local ones, in every unit, the entry and the")
    strs_push(l, "runtime (`Native::single_thread`, `Needs::single`); a program linked to a prebuilt runtime keeps")
    strs_push(l, "them thread-local. `fib(35)` under LLVM `-O2`: 141.6 ms before, 68.3 ms after (C 36.8, Go 41.0, the")
    strs_push(l, "same machine); word frequency 453 → 392 ms. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/single_thread.rs` —")
    strs_push(l, "the state plain for a `main` of output alone, thread-local for one with `SpawnCap`, `NetCap` or")
    strs_push(l, "`ForeignCap` and for a library, the check inlined; a stack overflow and an overflow still reported")
    strs_push(l, "by a program of one thread under LLVM and Cranelift. Five mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Performance leadership (2026-10-15)** · *Plain reference counts in a program of one thread*")
    strs_push(l, "(`openspec/changes/performance-leadership`, design.md). In the same program of one thread")
    strs_push(l, "(`Needs::single`) a string's, a closure's and a channel's reference count is an ordinary load, add")
    strs_push(l, "or subtract and store, with the old count still deciding the free, and no acquire fence: in the")
    strs_push(l, "runtime unit (both backends link it) and in the copies a hosted LLVM unit inlines. Every other")
    strs_push(l, "program, and one linked to a prebuilt runtime, keeps the atomic counts. Word frequency −7 to −8%")
    strs_push(l, "(three rounds, `-O2`), `fib` unchanged. Evidence: the runtime's")
    strs_push(l, "`a_program_of_one_thread_counts_without_atomics_and_any_other_with_them` (plain counts, nothing")
    strs_push(l, "else changed, atomic otherwise, the inlined copies alike); `single_thread.rs`'s")
    strs_push(l, "`a_program_of_one_thread_counts_its_strings_without_atomics` (built IR, one thread against")
    strs_push(l, "`SpawnCap`); the memory suite through the plain counts. Six mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1e (2026-10-13)** · *`@std/sha256`, `@std/blake3` and `file_walk`* (`spec.md`, *The standard")
    strs_push(l, "library*; `openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, D4 and S1). Two digests in Nazm, over")
    strs_push(l, "32-bit wrapping arithmetic and rotations: SHA-256 (FIPS 180-4) and BLAKE3's unkeyed 32-byte output")
    strs_push(l, "(the reference algorithm: 1024-byte chunks, seven-round compression, a stack of subtree chaining")
    strs_push(l, "values, `ROOT` on the last compression). Each is a one-shot function, a hex form and an incremental")
    strs_push(l, "hasher — a handle whose finish leaves it unchanged. Digests for identity and integrity, not the")
    strs_push(l, "cryptography 1.0 leaves out: no constant-time claim, no audit. `@std/file` gained `file_walk(io,")
    strs_push(l, "dir)`: every regular file and directory under `dir`, sorted by bytes. With no `lstat` built-in yet")
    strs_push(l, "(P2), a symbolic link is walked as what it names; a dangling one is left out, and one reaching its")
    strs_push(l, "own ancestor ends in the system's `Err`. EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since). Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/hash_vectors.rs` — FIPS 180-4's examples and messages on each side of the")
    strs_push(l, "padding's boundaries, and the BLAKE3 team's `test_vectors.json` lengths up to 3,073 bytes, each")
    strs_push(l, "whole and in uneven pieces, alike under the interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and")
    strs_push(l, "Cranelift with nothing live; a million `a`s and every official BLAKE3 length to 102,400 bytes under")
    strs_push(l, "LLVM `-O2` and Cranelift; the embedded BLAKE3 vectors checked against the `blake3` crate.")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/file_walk.rs` — a tree sorted as bytes, not as a depth-first listing, under")
    strs_push(l, "the interpreter and LLVM; on Unix, links to a file, to a directory, dangling and looping. Seven")
    strs_push(l, "mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "**R1e (2026-10-13)** · *`@std/args`* (`spec.md`, *The standard library*; `openspec/changes/r1-language-")
    strs_push(l, "for-the-rewrite`, S4). A command-line parser in Nazm, for writing the toolchain's own command line:")
    strs_push(l, "a specification built by functions (`args_program`, `args_command` for sub-commands nested to any")
    strs_push(l, "depth, `args_flag`, `args_option` and its default and required forms, `args_positional`,")
    strs_push(l, "`args_rest`, `args_conflict`) into one arena, and `args_parse` over any `Strs` — `process_args(io)`")
    strs_push(l, "for the process's own — answering an `Args` read by name, or an `Err` naming the command and the")
    strs_push(l, "argument at fault. The POSIX and GNU forms: `--name value`, `--name=value`, `-n value`, `-nvalue`,")
    strs_push(l, "bundled `-abc`, `--`, `-`; repeated options and counted flags; `--help`, and the help and usage text")
    strs_push(l, "generated from the specification. No new built-in and no checker change: the arguments come from the")
    strs_push(l, "existing `arg`/`args_count` through `@std/process`. EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since). Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/args.rs` — twenty-six command lines (every form, and every mistake with its")
    strs_push(l, "message) and the help of three commands, alike under the interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM")
    strs_push(l, "`-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with nothing live; and executables built by LLVM and Cranelift parsing the")
    strs_push(l, "arguments they were started with (spaces and non-ASCII in values, `--`, help on standard output,")
    strs_push(l, "an error on standard error with status 2).")
    strs_push(l, "**R1e (2026-10-13)** · *`@std/bytebuf`, `@std/ordmap`, `@std/bitset` and the in-place sorts*")
    strs_push(l, "(`spec.md`, *The standard library*; `openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, S2 and S3). In")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm, each a handle like the other collections. `ByteBuf`: one buffer doubling as it fills, numbers")
    strs_push(l, "in either byte order, ULEB128 and SLEB128, padding to an alignment, patching a field written")
    strs_push(l, "earlier, and indexed reads and writes that answer `None` or `false` outside the bytes written.")
    strs_push(l, "`@std/ordmap`: the `Ord` trait, implemented for every integer type, `Bool` and `Str`, and")
    strs_push(l, "`OrdMap[K: Ord, V]`, an AVL tree in parallel vectors — insertion, lookup and removal in `O(log n)`")
    strs_push(l, "comparisons, a removed node's slot taken by the last so nothing removed stays alive — with its ends,")
    strs_push(l, "floor and ceiling, a half-open range, and keys, values and entries in ascending order.")
    strs_push(l, "`@std/bitset`: a growable set of non-negative `Int`s in 64-bit words, with a walk by `bitset_next`")
    strs_push(l, "and union, intersection and difference. `@std/sort` gained `vec_sort_in_place_by` (stable,")
    strs_push(l, "effect-polymorphic: insertion runs of sixteen, merged bottom-up through one scratch vector),")
    strs_push(l, "`ints_sort_in_place` and `strs_sort_in_place`. API-1.0 gains 57 lines. EXPERIMENTAL until R1")
    strs_push(l, "closes. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/collections_r1e.rs` — one program, the same output under")
    strs_push(l, "the interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with nothing live: LEB128 at its")
    strs_push(l, "edges and at both ends of `Int` and `UInt64`, and six hundred fixed-seed values written alike by a")
    strs_push(l, "`ByteBuf` and `@std/binary`'s `Writer`; an `OrdMap` over `Str`, a program's own `Ord` key and `Int`,")
    strs_push(l, "the last under three thousand fixed-seed insertions, removals and lookups checked against a sorted")
    strs_push(l, "vector, its keys, values, ends, neighbours and ranges compared as it goes, then ascending and")
    strs_push(l, "descending runs; a `BitSet` against a vector of flags; the in-place sorts against the copying ones,")
    strs_push(l, "stability checked by original positions, at lengths around the insertion runs. Three hundred")
    strs_push(l, "thousand ascending keys, half removed, finish natively within twenty seconds; a key type with no")
    strs_push(l, "`Ord` is refused. Not measured: speed against the Rust containers the rewrite replaces.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1c (2026-10-13)** · *`@derive(toml)`* (`spec.md`, *Derived serialisation*, **TOML**;")
    strs_push(l, "`openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, L2c). The same shape over `@std/toml`'s `Toml` tree,")
    strs_push(l, "alone or beside `json`: `t_toml_value` and `t_toml_read` for a record or an enum, and for a record —")
    strs_push(l, "a document is a table — `t_to_toml` and `t_from_toml`. `@codec` shapes it as it shapes JSON. TOML")
    strs_push(l, "has no `null`: a `None` is left out and a missing key read as `None`, so an `Option` inside another")
    strs_push(l, "type is refused (`N0619`). The generator is per format (`crates/nazm-core/src/derive.rs`), the text")
    strs_push(l, "importing each format it used; `@std/toml` gained `toml_is_table`. Semantic epoch 70. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/derive_toml.rs` — a deployment of nested records, an array of tables and")
    strs_push(l, "both enum encodings, written, read back to the same text, read from hand-written TOML and refused")
    strs_push(l, "at its path, under the interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with nothing")
    strs_push(l, "live; the repository's own package manifest read through a derived record; what TOML cannot")
    strs_push(l, "carry. Five mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1c (2026-10-13)** · *`@codec(…)`* (`spec.md`, *Derived serialisation*, **Shaping it**;")
    strs_push(l, "`openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, L2b). The closed attribute set: on a derived type")
    strs_push(l, "`rename_all` (five cases), `deny_unknown`, and for an enum `tag` (internally tagged) or `untagged`")
    strs_push(l, "(the first variant that decodes, so its schema is `anyOf`); on a field `rename`, `default` (a")
    strs_push(l, "number's zero, `false`, `\"\"`, `None`, an empty `Vec` or `List`), `omit_none`; on a variant")
    strs_push(l, "`rename`. An attribute may now stand before a field or a variant — the parser, the incremental")
    strs_push(l, "tree, and the formatter (its own line in a list one to a line, inline in one kept on one line) —")
    strs_push(l, "and only `@codec` is one there. Every misuse is `N0619`, and nothing is generated for a type it")
    strs_push(l, "refuses. Semantic epoch 69. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/derive_json.rs` — every argument")
    strs_push(l, "under the interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with nothing live; thirteen")
    strs_push(l, "misuses refused alone; the formatting, and its stability. The three schemas passed an independent")
    strs_push(l, "2020-12 validator, valid documents accepted and each malformed one refused. Seven mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1c (2026-10-13)** · *`@derive(json)`* (`spec.md`, *Derived serialisation*;")
    strs_push(l, "`openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, L2a). Before a `struct` or `enum` that is not")
    strs_push(l, "generic, it gives the type `t_to_json`, `t_from_json`, `t_json_schema` and the helpers a derived")
    strs_push(l, "type of another module calls — ordinary Nazm the loader appends to the file")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-core/src/derive.rs`), with the `use` of `@std/json` it needs, so every implementation")
    strs_push(l, "runs the same functions and nothing below the front end is new. Decoding never traps: an `Err`")
    strs_push(l, "names the path. The schema is JSON Schema 2020-12 with `$defs`, so a recursive type's is finite. A")
    strs_push(l, "generic type, an unknown format, a field of a type the format cannot carry, or of a type the program")
    strs_push(l, "declares without the derive, is `N0619` at the attribute or the field. Semantic epoch 68;")
    strs_push(l, "EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since); the attribute set (L2b) and `@derive(toml)` (L2c) remain. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/derive_json.rs` — every carried field kind, out-of-range and mistyped")
    strs_push(l, "members refused at their path, under the interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and")
    strs_push(l, "Cranelift with nothing live; a derived type of another module, plain and qualified; each refusal")
    strs_push(l, "alone. The schema also passed an independent 2020-12 validator when written. Six mutants.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1c (2026-10-13)** · *`@std/toml`* (`spec.md`, *The standard library*; `openspec/changes/r1-language-")
    strs_push(l, "for-the-rewrite`, S1). TOML 1.0, in Nazm: `pub enum Toml`, recursive through `List`, and")
    strs_push(l, "`toml_parse`, `toml_encode`, `toml_get`. A document is built in an arena of mutable nodes — where a")
    strs_push(l, "later header or dotted key can still extend a table, and where each table records how it was made")
    strs_push(l, "(explicitly, as a header's prefix, by a dotted key, inline) so that every redefinition TOML forbids is")
    strs_push(l, "refused — then turned into the immutable tree. Errors are `line:column: what`; nothing traps. The")
    strs_push(l, "LIR oracle gained `nz.float_parse` and `nz.float_parses`, which it had refused by name. The first")
    strs_push(l, "repository source to use interpolation and an `if let` with no `else` found two faults the sweeps")
    strs_push(l, "over every file now hold: the incremental lexer moved an interpolated string after an edit but not")
    strs_push(l, "its holes' positions (fixed), and the syntax test's own walk counted the empty `else` such an `if")
    strs_push(l, "let` is given as a written block (fixed in the test). EXPERIMENTAL")
    strs_push(l, "until R1 closes. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/toml.rs` — a document of every form decoded alike")
    strs_push(l, "under the interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with nothing live, its encoding")
    strs_push(l, "a fixed point; eighteen invalid shapes refused at their line and column; every `nazm.toml` in the")
    strs_push(l, "repository and a `nazm.lock` from `nazm lock`, parsed and round-tripped. Beyond the repository: the")
    strs_push(l, "553 TOML 1.0 cases of the `toml-test` suite (v2.2.0), all decoded as expected — and every valid one")
    strs_push(l, "re-encoded, re-parsed to the same values and found a fixed point — under LLVM and under Cranelift; the")
    strs_push(l, "suite is a third party's and is not vendored.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1b (2026-10-13)** · *128-bit integers and the widening multiply* (`spec.md`, *Numbers*;")
    strs_push(l, "`openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, L13b). `Int128` and `UInt128` under every rule of")
    strs_push(l, "*Numbers* at their width; literals up to `UInt128`'s maximum, and a negated one past `Int`'s")
    strs_push(l, "magnitude judged whole where an `Int128` is expected; `widening_mul(a: UInt64, b: UInt64) ->")
    strs_push(l, "UInt128`, exact. A value's exact integer is `nazm_sema::numeric::Wide` (`[-2^127, 2^128 - 1]`) and")
    strs_push(l, "its bits 128 wide; LIR has a class `i128`, laid out in 16 bytes aligned to 8 (stated on every LLVM")
    strs_push(l, "load and store); LLVM and Cranelift make instructions of the rest, and division, remainder, the")
    strs_push(l, "signed checked product, float conversions and text are the runtime's wide part, taking values by")
    strs_push(l, "address (runtime ABI 32), which a board or WebAssembly build that reaches it refuses by name. A")
    strs_push(l, "derived hash is `hash_combine` of the two words' `hash_u64`, as `@std/hash`'s new impls are. No C")
    strs_push(l, "export of one (`N0391`). Semantic epoch 67; EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since). Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/wide.rs` — every operation at each bound, the conversions by every mode, a")
    strs_push(l, "`Vec` and an `Option` of one, `Bytes` at sixteen, literals, under the interpreter, the LIR oracle,")
    strs_push(l, "LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with nothing live; each failure with its code everywhere; a hash map")
    strs_push(l, "keyed by one and derived hashes; a constant across modules and the cache; the refusals. Eleven")
    strs_push(l, "mutants; six earlier ones repointed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1b (2026-10-13)** · *Checked arithmetic* (`spec.md`, *Numbers*, **Functions**;")
    strs_push(l, "`openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, L13a). `checked_add`, `checked_sub` and")
    strs_push(l, "`checked_mul`, over every integer type, return `Option[T]` — `Some` of the exact result, `None`")
    strs_push(l, "where it does not fit — as prelude names; a built-in signature may now name the prelude's `Option`")
    strs_push(l, "(`Shape::OptionT`). Core IR lowering writes each from operations every implementation has: a sum or")
    strs_push(l, "difference overflows exactly when its wrapping and saturating results differ; a product, `a` being")
    strs_push(l, "neither `0` nor `-1`, exactly when the wrapped product divided by `a` is not `b`, and `-1` times a")
    strs_push(l, "signed minimum is tested by name. Nothing below Core IR is new. Semantic epoch 65; EXPERIMENTAL")
    strs_push(l, "until R1 closes. `Int128`, `UInt128` and the widening multiply (L13b) remain. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/checked.rs` — each bound, `-1` times the minimum and zero at `Int`, `Int8`")
    strs_push(l, "and `UInt8` under the interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with nothing")
    strs_push(l, "live; a float refused; the prelude name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1b (2026-10-13)** · *Scope-exit cleanup: `defer`* (`spec.md`; `openspec/changes/")
    strs_push(l, "r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, L12). `defer { … }` runs a block whenever its block is left — at its")
    strs_push(l, "end, or by `return`, `?`, `break` or `continue` — the last registered first, after a returned value")
    strs_push(l, "or a block's final value is computed. `defer` is a word only at a statement's start before `{`. The")
    strs_push(l, "checker refuses a body that would leave (`N0631`: `return`, `?`, or a `break`/`continue` out of it)")
    strs_push(l, "and a body with a value; a loop inside one may leave itself, a closure inside one may return.")
    strs_push(l, "Lowering only: Core IR registers each body with its loop depth and emits it — lowered afresh —")
    strs_push(l, "where its block falls through, in `leave` before every `return` (and so every `?` and `ensures`),")
    strs_push(l, "and before a `break`/`continue` for the bodies registered inside the loop it leaves; nothing below")
    strs_push(l, "Core IR is new. Provenance walks a body where it is written and again where its block ends.")
    strs_push(l, "Semantic epoch 64; EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since). Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/defer.rs` —")
    strs_push(l, "order, nesting, an early return, a loop's `break` and `continue`, `?` on success and failure,")
    strs_push(l, "under the interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with nothing live; the")
    strs_push(l, "refusals and what stays accepted; provenance reaching a body from after it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1b (2026-10-13)** · *Impls of generic types* (`spec.md`, *Traits and methods*, **Impls of generic")
    strs_push(l, "types**; `openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, L11b). `impl[A: Show, B] Show for Pair[A,")
    strs_push(l, "B]` implements a trait for every instance whose arguments meet the impl's requirements. The parser")
    strs_push(l, "writes the impl's parameters first into each method, so each is a generic function; the checker")
    strs_push(l, "files the impl under the generic definition (`generic_impl_type`; `N0604` unless the header is the")
    strs_push(l, "definition applied to exactly the parameters), gives each method `Self` as the definition applied")
    strs_push(l, "to its own parameters, and records each parameter's requirement on the impl. A lookup for an")
    strs_push(l, "instance falls back to its definition's impl with the instance's arguments")
    strs_push(l, "(`Traits::applying`, `Resolution::method_target`), and is usable only where those arguments meet")
    strs_push(l, "the requirements, recursively (`Checker::satisfies`); a direct call records the arguments, MIR's")
    strs_push(l, "bound dispatch passes them, the instance planner follows each call through a bound inside an")
    strs_push(l, "instance to the impl or default it reaches, and Core IR carries each instance's definition for the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter's impl table. Coherence and the orphan rule are the definition's. Semantic epoch 63;")
    strs_push(l, "EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since). Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/generic_impls.rs` — a pair and an")
    strs_push(l, "option of nested instances shown directly, by UFCS, through a bound and by a default, under the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with nothing live; across modules by")
    strs_push(l, "both backends; the header's form, unmet requirements by a call and by a bound, coherence, the")
    strs_push(l, "orphan rule.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1b (2026-10-13)** · *Default trait methods* (`spec.md`, *Traits and methods*, **Default bodies**;")
    strs_push(l, "`openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, L11a). A trait method may end in a body, which an")
    strs_push(l, "impl that writes none gets; an impl may still write its own. The parser writes each body as a")
    strs_push(l, "function `Trait/default/m` generic over `Self: Trait`, so the checker checks it once, through the")
    strs_push(l, "bound, against the signature's declared effects (none written is none); `N0602` spares a method")
    strs_push(l, "with a body. A call on a type whose impl leaves the method to it — direct, UFCS, or through a bound")
    strs_push(l, "— resolves to the default at that type (`Resolution::method_target`): the checker records the")
    strs_push(l, "receiver's type as the call's type argument, MIR's bound dispatch passes the instance's type, the")
    strs_push(l, "instance planner plans the default at every type whose impl relies on it, and Core IR's impl")
    strs_push(l, "table, which the interpreter dispatches through, fills the slot with the default. A default called")
    strs_push(l, "from another module is held to its trait method's effects, as an impl's method is (M1). Semantic")
    strs_push(l, "epoch 62; EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since). Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/default_methods.rs` —")
    strs_push(l, "defaults called directly, by UFCS and through a bound, one overridden, one performing `io`, under")
    strs_push(l, "the interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with nothing live; a trait and its")
    strs_push(l, "impl in different modules built by both backends; a body checked once, generic over `Self`, held")
    strs_push(l, "to its effects; a method with no body still required.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1b (2026-10-13)** · *Closures in generic functions; a shared `let mut`* (`spec.md`, *Function")
    strs_push(l, "values and closures*; `openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, L10). A closure, and a named")
    strs_push(l, "function's value, may be written in a generic function, the closure's types naming the function's")
    strs_push(l, "type parameters (`N0387` narrowed): `nazm run` is parametric, and the instance planner instantiates")
    strs_push(l, "each closure with the generic function it is written in — through every closure between —")
    strs_push(l, "substituting under that function's parameters (`Resolution::type_owner`); a thunk a generic body")
    strs_push(l, "makes a value of is bindable across objects, as what a generic body calls is. A captured `let mut`")
    strs_push(l, "binding is shared, not copied (`N0386` narrowed to one that can hold a function value): the")
    strs_push(l, "checker records it and every closure's copy as shared, and Core IR lowering keeps it in a `Cell` —")
    strs_push(l, "`let mut x = e` makes the cell, a read is `vec_get(x, 0)`, `x = v` is `vec_set(x, 0, v)` and")
    strs_push(l, "`x.f = v` copies out, changes and sets back — so nothing below Core IR is new. Provenance reads and")
    strs_push(l, "writes a shared binding through its cell, so a closure's write reaches its function's read.")
    strs_push(l, "Semantic epoch 61; EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since). Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/")
    strs_push(l, "generic_closures.rs` — generic closures (nested, over `Int` and `Str`, with a named function's")
    strs_push(l, "value) and shared bindings (a closure's writes, a field through a closure, a write after the closure")
    strs_push(l, "is made, nested closures, a generic function's) by hand-worked output under the interpreter, the LIR")
    strs_push(l, "oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with nothing live; a generic closure and a thunk built")
    strs_push(l, "across modules by both backends; provenance through a shared binding. The compat case")
    strs_push(l, "`refuse/capture-let-mut.nz` is SUPERSEDED.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1b (2026-10-12)** · *A mutable cell: `Cell[T]`* (`spec.md`; `openspec/changes/")
    strs_push(l, "r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, L7). One value that can be replaced, reached through a handle, so a")
    strs_push(l, "callee's `cell_set` is its caller's: `cell_new`, `cell_get` and `cell_set` as prelude names. The")
    strs_push(l, "kind `Vec` is — a mutable handle — so an ownership edge through it is counted (`N0359`), it has no")
    strs_push(l, "equality (`N0304`), it does not cross into a task (`N0321`), and a closure may not capture one that")
    strs_push(l, "can hold a function value (`N0616`). A `Vec[T]` of one element underneath and a distinct type to the")
    strs_push(l, "checker only: Core IR lowering writes the three as `vec_new` with `vec_push`, `vec_get(c, 0)` and")
    strs_push(l, "`vec_set(c, 0, v)`, so the interpreter, MIR, LIR and both backends need nothing new, and no runtime")
    strs_push(l, "ABI moved. Provenance follows what a cell holds, from `cell_new` and from every `cell_set`.")
    strs_push(l, "Semantic epoch 60; EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since). Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/cell.rs` — a")
    strs_push(l, "context record updated by callees, sharing, replacement releasing what it replaced (a string, a")
    strs_push(l, "record, a vector) and a cell inside a box, by hand-worked output under the interpreter, the LIR")
    strs_push(l, "oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with nothing live; the ownership rule; the refusals; the")
    strs_push(l, "prelude names; provenance; a `Cell` type crossing a module's interface.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1a (2026-10-12)** · *String interpolation* (`spec.md`; `openspec/changes/")
    strs_push(l, "r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, L4). `f\"…\"` and `f\"\"\"…\"\"\"`: holes `{expr}` and `{expr:spec}`")
    strs_push(l, "(`[<|>][width][.precision]`), `{{`/`}}` for braces; a hole holds a `Str`, a number, a `Bool` or a")
    strs_push(l, "value with `Show` in scope (its `show()` resolved as the method call at the hole's braces, through a")
    strs_push(l, "bound too). The lexer reads an `FSTRING` token whose holes the parser parses on their own and")
    strs_push(l, "places; lowering joins the pieces with `str_concat`. New prelude built-ins `float_to_str_fixed`")
    strs_push(l, "(runtime `nz.format_fixed`, C's `%.*f`; runtime ABI 30) and `str_pad_start`/`str_pad_end` (a")
    strs_push(l, "loop in LIR). `N0006`; semantic epoch 59; EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since). Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/interpolation.rs` — every kind of hole by hand-worked output on the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with nothing live; ties to even and")
    strs_push(l, "`-0.0`; refusals by code.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1a (2026-10-12)** · *Multi-line and raw strings* (`spec.md`; `openspec/changes/")
    strs_push(l, "r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, L9). `\"\"\"` strings whose closing delimiter's indentation comes off")
    strs_push(l, "every line (`N0005` for a line short of it, or text after the opening delimiter), escapes as an")
    strs_push(l, "ordinary literal's and a backslash ending a line joining it; raw `r\"…\"`/`r#\"…\"#` with any number of")
    strs_push(l, "`#`s, no escape, line breaks as written; CR LF read as LF in both. The lexer decides each from the")
    strs_push(l, "literal's own bytes, so incremental relexing is unchanged; an ordinary literal stays one line.")
    strs_push(l, "Semantic epoch 58; EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since). Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/")
    strs_push(l, "string_literals.rs` — the bytes by hand on the interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and")
    strs_push(l, "Cranelift; the formatter keeping each as written; refusals by code.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1a (2026-10-12)** · *Constant tables and exported constants* (`spec.md`;")
    strs_push(l, "`openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, L8). An array may hold `Str`, `Text` and records,")
    strs_push(l, "enums and arrays of them (`N0621` names a handle): MIR counts an array managed by its element,")
    strs_push(l, "writing an element moves the value in and releases the old one, and LIR retains on every copy in")
    strs_push(l, "and out and releases element by element (`each_owned`'s array loop). A constant may be a record,")
    strs_push(l, "enum value, tuple or array of constant parts, computed by a second phase once types are known,")
    strs_push(l, "and lowered at each use to its construction; `pub const` publishes the value in the interface")
    strs_push(l, "(`nazm.interface/12`, each value keyed by field and variant names) and an importer reads it as")
    strs_push(l, "`NAME` or `m::NAME`; a stage 1b computes constants in dependency order so one may be computed")
    strs_push(l, "from an import's. Semantic epoch 57; EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since). Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/const_tables.rs` — string arrays and constant tables by hand-worked output")
    strs_push(l, "in the interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with nothing live; constants")
    strs_push(l, "across modules, plain and under a name, under `run` and two `build`s (the second from the cache);")
    strs_push(l, "the published interface; refusals by code.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1a (2026-10-12)** · *Ordering and hashing are derived* (`spec.md`; `openspec/changes/")
    strs_push(l, "r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, L6). `< <= > >=` on `Bool`, `Str` (bytes) and records, enums and")
    strs_push(l, "tuples of ordered components, by the **names** of fields and variants (the canonical order the")
    strs_push(l, "layout already used, so reordering a declaration changes no comparison), a tuple by position (at")
    strs_push(l, "most eight elements, so its field names sort as its positions); `==` on `Box` and `List` by what")
    strs_push(l, "they hold; `@std/hash`'s `Hash` satisfied without an impl by a concrete record, enum or tuple of")
    strs_push(l, "integers, `Bool`s and `Str`s, `hash` folding `hash_combine` from `hash_u64(0)` (or the variant's")
    strs_push(l, "name) in the canonical order and `same` being `==`. The interpreter computes both from Core IR's")
    strs_push(l, "new canonical-order table; MIR lowers a derived trait call to `Rvalue::Hash` or a comparison; LIR")
    strs_push(l, "generates `ord.*` and `hash.*` helpers (FNV-1a and SplitMix64 as instructions, constants folded at")
    strs_push(l, "build time). Semantic epoch 56; EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since). Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/order_hash.rs` — orders and hashes by hand-worked output, and against the")
    strs_push(l, "library's own functions, in the interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with")
    strs_push(l, "nothing live; reordering a declaration changes no order and no hash; refusals by code, naming the")
    strs_push(l, "component; a written impl keeps its meaning.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1a (2026-10-12)** · *Tuples* (`spec.md`; `openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, L5).")
    strs_push(l, "`(A, B, …)` types, `(a, b, …)` values, `t.0` (and `t.0.1`, which the lexer reads as a float and the")
    strs_push(l, "parser splits), `t.0 = e` on a `let mut`, tuple patterns, `let P = e;` (a `let` whose pattern must")
    strs_push(l, "match every value, `N0343` otherwise) and `for (a, b) in e`. A tuple is an anonymous generic record")
    strs_push(l, "the checker interns by arity (fields `0`, `1`, …), so layout, release, equality, task crossing and")
    strs_push(l, "every backend take it as a record with no new code; an interface writes it as its elements")
    strs_push(l, "(`{\"tuple\":[…]}`). `(x,)` is refused (`N0101`). Semantic epoch 55; EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since).")
    strs_push(l, "Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/tuples.rs` — a program of every form by hand-worked output in the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with nothing live; refusals by code with")
    strs_push(l, "one error each; a tuple across a module's interface under `run` and `build`; the formatter's")
    strs_push(l, "spelling.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1a (2026-10-12)** · *Patterns* (`spec.md`; `openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, L3).")
    strs_push(l, "`_`, a name, a literal (an integer, perhaps negated, a string, `true`, `false`), a variant pattern")
    strs_push(l, "whose fields are patterns, and `|` alternatives — in a `match` of any type a pattern fits, in")
    strs_push(l, "`if let`, and in `let … else`, which the parser writes as the `match` each means (a")
    strs_push(l, "`MatchSource`). Exhaustiveness and reachability are the standard usefulness algorithm")
    strs_push(l, "(`check/usefulness.rs`), naming a value no arm matches; a `match` written variant by variant is")
    strs_push(l, "refused with the words it was before R1a. A `match` of plain variant patterns lowers to one Core")
    strs_push(l, "IR `match` as before; any other is `{ scrutinee; which arm; that arm }`, each pattern's test a")
    strs_push(l, "`Bool` of plain matches and comparisons and each arm's body written once, its bindings read out of")
    strs_push(l, "the scrutinee (a branch exhaustiveness rules out is an `exit_with`, which Core IR now counts as a")
    strs_push(l, "transfer). `N0629`, `N0630`; semantic epoch 54; EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since); no warning for a `_`")
    strs_push(l, "over variants until L15. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/patterns.rs` — every kind of pattern by")
    strs_push(l, "hand-worked output in the interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with nothing")
    strs_push(l, "live; exhaustiveness witnesses; ten refusals by code; one error, not a cascade, for a wrong")
    strs_push(l, "pattern; the syntax, core and service suites unchanged but for three tests whose examples the")
    strs_push(l, "language now accepts.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1a (2026-10-11)** · *`for` loops* (`spec.md`; `openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`,")
    strs_push(l, "D3). `for x in e` over an `Ints`, `Strs`, `Vec[T]` or `Bytes`, and `for x in a..b`; `..` a token, `in`")
    strs_push(l, "a word only after a `for` loop's name, and a `for` of any other shape still refused by name")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0101`); a non-sequence is `N0628`. Checked once and lowered to Core IR as the `while` loop the")
    strs_push(l, "specification gives, so the interpreter, the LIR oracle and both backends run what the `while`")
    strs_push(l, "runs. Semantic epoch 52; EXPERIMENTAL in `spec.md`'s classification until R1 closes, so not yet in")
    strs_push(l, "the compatibility corpus. The compiler written in Nazm does not carry it (area 31, R2). Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/for_loops.rs` — every rule of the section by hand-worked output in the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0` and `-O2` and Cranelift, nothing left live in any memory")
    strs_push(l, "report; the same program written with the specification's `while` loops printing and reclaiming")
    strs_push(l, "identically; ten refusals by code; `in` as a function, parameter and binding name; the formatter")
    strs_push(l, "gluing `a..b`; `docs/user/grammar.ebnf`'s example.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 2 (2026-10-09)** · *Attributes* and *Conditional compilation* (`general-purpose.md` §16–§17;")
    strs_push(l, "`spec.md`). `@name` and `@name(args)` before a top-level declaration, a closed vocabulary refused")
    strs_push(l, "by name otherwise (`N0619`); a malformed one is one syntax error. A declaration whose `@cfg` does")
    strs_push(l, "not hold is removed before name resolution, an `impl` with its methods, decided by the build's")
    strs_push(l, "target (`nazm build --target`), or the host's, and the profiles held; a module that writes `@cfg`")
    strs_push(l, "is checked under its configuration and never reused under another. The formatter puts each")
    strs_push(l, "attribute on its own line. Semantic epoch 42. *G2-C1:* `@deprecated` is metadata-only deprecation —")
    strs_push(l, "on a `pub` function, `struct` or `enum` only (`N0619` elsewhere), published by `nazm doc` as the")
    strs_push(l, "item's `deprecated` in `nazm.api-doc/2` and in the Markdown, reported by no diagnostic — epoch 43")
    strs_push(l, "(`deprecation_is_metadata_the_api_documentation_publishes`, `schemas.rs`). Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/attributes.rs` —")
    strs_push(l, "the kept declaration in the interpreter and both backends, a cross build that reaches code the")
    strs_push(l, "host's check never saw, a check under `--profile` not reusing one without it, fourteen refusals,")
    strs_push(l, "one error for a malformed attribute, and the formatter's layout; `docs/user/grammar.ebnf`'s examples.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N76 (2026-10-03)** · *Incremental reparse, finer recovery, `\\u{…}`* (`architecture.md` §7.77).")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm_syntax::Revision` is one file's parse kept per top-level item; `Revision::edit` relexes from")
    strs_push(l, "the first lexeme the lexer read past and reparses from the first item that read a changed token,")
    strs_push(l, "until both land on old boundaries, keeping the rest (green nodes by reference, items and diagnostics")
    strs_push(l, "moved by the edit's length). Its contract is **equality with a fresh parse** — lexemes, every node")
    strs_push(l, "and leaf of the concrete tree with kind, span and bytes, the abstract tree with every span, and the")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostics in order — held by `crates/nazm-syntax/tests/incremental.rs`: seeded edit sequences over")
    strs_push(l, "every `.nz` file in the repository (220 files, 2,604 edits, each compared field by field with")
    strs_push(l, "`Revision::new` and `parse_both` of the same text), sixteen edits at the hard places (an item's first")
    strs_push(l, "byte, merged tokens, an unclosed delimiter, inside a string and a comment, the whole file), and the")
    strs_push(l, "one cross-item read, recovery skipping to the next `fn NAME`, with a test that fails if an item's")
    strs_push(l, "lookahead is not recorded. A one-word edit in the middle of `compiler/emit.nz` reparses one of 126")
    strs_push(l, "items and 618 of 40,284 tokens, relexes 2 lexemes, and takes 1.2 ms against 8.2 ms for a full parse")
    strs_push(l, "in a release build (`performance.md`, *Incremental reparse*).")
    strs_push(l, "Recovery reaches inside lists: a malformed record field, enum variant or payload field, parameter,")
    strs_push(l, "call argument, field initialiser or `match` arm is an `Error` node of its own beside typed siblings,")
    strs_push(l, "and a later independent mistake in the same list is its own diagnostic; a broken `use` ends at its")
    strs_push(l, "`;` and recovery stops at `use` (`crates/nazm-syntax/tests/recovery.rs`). The abstract tree's")
    strs_push(l, "contract is unchanged on purpose: a declaration that needed recovery is absent, a body that needed")
    strs_push(l, "it is. `\\u{H…}` is the UTF-8 encoding of a scalar value, refused (`N0004`) for surrogates, values")
    strs_push(l, "above `10FFFF` and malformed forms, the same bytes in the interpreter and three native builds")
    strs_push(l, "(`usability.rs`); semantic epoch 21. `nazm lsp` synchronises incrementally: the service keeps a")
    strs_push(l, "revision per open document, applies each ranged change to it, and analyses the root file from it,")
    strs_push(l, "equal to a whole-document change in every published diagnostic and every answer")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-service/tests/unsaved.rs`, `crates/nazm-cli/tests/lsp.rs`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N49 (2026-10-01)** · string escapes (`\\n \\t \\r \\0 \\\\ \\\" \\xHH` up to `7F`, one byte each, decoded")
    strs_push(l, "once by the lexer, `N0004` otherwise, kept as written by the formatter), the logical operators")
    strs_push(l, "`&&`, `||` and prefix `!` (lowered to `if` in Core IR), and `use \"PATH\" as NAME;` with `NAME::item`")
    strs_push(l, "(the `::` token). `crates/nazm-cli/tests/usability.rs` holds each across the interpreter and three")
    strs_push(l, "native builds; `crates/nazm-syntax/src/lexer.rs` its unit tests; the grammar and the guide carry")
    strs_push(l, "the rules (`docs/user/spec.md`, *String escapes*, *Logical operators*, *Qualified names*).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · Hand-written lexer and recursive-descent/Pratt parser,")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-syntax/src/lexer.rs` and `crates/nazm-syntax/src/parser.rs`. The grammar is a")
    strs_push(l, "tested artefact, not prose: `crates/nazm-syntax/tests/grammar.rs` requires every lexer")
    strs_push(l, "token to appear in `docs/user/grammar.ebnf`, every nonterminal to be reachable from `program`,")
    strs_push(l, "and every `(* @example *)` in it to parse with zero diagnostics. `docs/user/guide.md`'s syntax")
    strs_push(l, "section is generated from the same file by `xtask/src/guide.rs`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Since N1, each file is parsed on its own text through `nazm_syntax::parse_map`, so the")
    strs_push(l, "parser no longer requires a concatenated buffer. Since N2 the grammar has one visibility")
    strs_push(l, "bit — `function = [ visibility ] , \"fn\" , ...` — and the AST records `pub_span`, which is")
    strs_push(l, "where the word was written and nothing about what it means.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Since N11, `[` and `]` are tokens and mean one thing: type parameters after a declared name")
    strs_push(l, "(`type_parameters`) and type arguments after a type or an expression's name")
    strs_push(l, "(`type_arguments`). A `TypeName` is recursive, carries its name's span and its whole span,")
    strs_push(l, "and counts against the parse budget; `[]` parses and is the checker's to refuse. The")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm-written parser produces the same tree for every generic shape in")
    strs_push(l, "`the_nazm_parser_produces_the_same_tree_as_the_reference`, spans included.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Since N12, `?` is a token and one postfix operator, parsed beside projection in any order —")
    strs_push(l, "`primary = atom , { \".\" , IDENT | \"?\" }` — so `-r?` is `-(r?)` and `r??` is two layers. The")
    strs_push(l, "formatter glues it to its operand; the Nazm-written parser produces the same trees.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Since N15 there is a lossless concrete syntax tree — **the lossless CST is VERIFIED; the")
    strs_push(l, "area stays PARTIAL** for the limitations below.* One lossless scan")
    strs_push(l, "(`lexer::lex_lossless_in`) gives every byte of a file to exactly one lexeme; the one parser")
    strs_push(l, "builds the abstract tree and a `cstree` 0.14 green tree (`crates/nazm-syntax/src/cst.rs`)")
    strs_push(l, "from the same decisions, and `parse_cst` returns it. Its leaves, concatenated, are the input")
    strs_push(l, "byte for byte — whitespace, comments, punctuation, refused characters, trailing trivia —")
    strs_push(l, "and every leaf is the bytes it was scanned from, never a spelling rebuilt from its kind.")
    strs_push(l, "Comments are leaves of the tree; the formatter's comment list is derived from the same scan.")
    strs_push(l, "Inside a block, a malformed statement becomes an `Error` node and parsing resumes at the next")
    strs_push(l, "statement boundary, so what follows it is still structured syntax and a later independent")
    strs_push(l, "mistake is its own diagnostic. Evidence in `crates/nazm-syntax/tests/cst.rs`:")
    strs_push(l, "`a_lossless_tree_preserves_every_byte_and_recovers_inside_a_function`; every `.nz` file in")
    strs_push(l, "the repository and every grammar example round-trips with its byte-ownership invariants;")
    strs_push(l, "13 malformed fixtures each keep the construct after the error; seeded random input (3,000")
    strs_push(l, "cases) and seeded token deletions of the compiler written in Nazm always round-trip and")
    strs_push(l, "terminate; the abstract and concrete trees agree on the span of every construct the checker")
    strs_push(l, "sees, over the whole clean corpus. Against the pre-N15 parser, all 196 files give an")
    strs_push(l, "identical abstract tree and identical diagnostics, and 4,240 single-token corruptions of")
    strs_push(l, "real programs give the same first diagnostic and abstract tree in every case and one more")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostic in one (`architecture.md` §7.17). Sixteen N15 mutations were caught with verified")
    strs_push(l, "killers; the campaign is in area 30.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · *Narrowed in N76:* until then, full-file parsing only, and recovery at")
    strs_push(l, "statements alone. Incremental reparse is per top-level item, so an edit inside one item reparses")
    strs_push(l, "that whole item; an edit that leaves a delimiter open reparses to the end of the file; the scan is")
    strs_push(l, "copied and its suffix moved on every edit, which is linear in the file's lexemes (`performance.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "Imported files in an editor's compilation are parsed in full on every analysis, and every command")
    strs_push(l, "outside the language service parses in full. Recovery inside an expression is at list members:")
    strs_push(l, "a mistake in an operand that is not a list member (`1 + * 2`) still costs its statement. After an")
    strs_push(l, "item's first recovery, if its delimiters do not balance, its further syntax diagnostics are withheld")
    strs_push(l, "as cascades. **Deliberate, not debt:** the abstract tree has no body for a function whose body")
    strs_push(l, "needed recovery, and no declaration whose header or member list did — the checker is never shown a")
    strs_push(l, "declaration with a hole, so recovery adds syntax diagnostics and never semantic cascades; a")
    strs_push(l, "hole-tolerant checker is not attempted. The concrete tree is built on every parse and costs about 2×")
    strs_push(l, "the parse time and 1.8× the peak parse heap (`performance.md`). The compiler written in Nazm has no")
    strs_push(l, "concrete tree, does not recover, and refuses every escape (N98). Parse nesting is bounded at 512 with")
    strs_push(l, "a 24 MiB parse stack. `\\x` above `7F` stays refused (`spec.md`, *String escapes*).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · None inside this area's scope. The compiler written in Nazm reached parity on its probes in N102 (area 31).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Met, 2026-10-03 (N76), for the reference parser: an edit sequence converges")
    strs_push(l, "exactly to a fresh parse in lexemes, both trees and diagnostics, so no stale node or span survives;")
    strs_push(l, "the round trip stays lossless and the formatter's tests are unchanged and green; an edit inside one")
    strs_push(l, "item reparses that item; recovery reaches every delimited list; the escape policy is decided. Met")
    strs_push(l, "before that, 2026-09-25 (N15): a round trip through the tree preserves every byte including trivia,")
    strs_push(l, "and the parser produces a usable tree for a file with an error in the middle of a function.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 2. Name resolution and modules — VERIFIED (N107)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N107, 2026-10-05: the scope audited (`audit-n107.md`, `architecture.md` §7.108).* Every answer a name has is the same whether a build re-checks a module or reuses it, so the one remaining gap — `nazm build` and `nazm run` re-checking every module — is a cost, and is area 26's limitation now. What VERIFIED means here: one durable identity per definition across modules, packages and re-exports, persisted and read back, in both compilers.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N103, 2026-10-05: re-exports, one identity.* `architecture.md` §7.104 first. `pub use \"PATH\";`")
    strs_push(l, "offers everything the module at `PATH` offers; `pub use \"PATH\" { a, b as c };` the names chosen,")
    strs_push(l, "`c` the name `b` is offered under. A re-export adds no definition: its export carries the")
    strs_push(l, "defining module's identity, so a call, a type, a trait bound, a reference, a rename, a persisted")
    strs_push(l, "interface (`nazm.interface/11`) and the API document (`nazm.api-doc/2`) all answer with the")
    strs_push(l, "definition. Refused: a name not offered `N0211`, a name offered twice `N0212`, a cycle of")
    strs_push(l, "re-exports `N0213`; `pub use … as m`. An impl in a module re-exported from is usable where the")
    strs_push(l, "re-exporting module is imported. Across a package boundary too. `nazm interface` publishes from")
    strs_push(l, "the stages a compilation runs (`declared_interfaces`), no longer a shorter path of its own. The")
    strs_push(l, "compiler written in Nazm reads re-exports and reports `N0211`–`N0213` at the reference's positions.")
    strs_push(l, "Held by `crates/nazm-cli/tests/reexports.rs` (nine tests: both backends, refusals, references, the")
    strs_push(l, "persisted interface alone, check reuse — a re-exported signature's change re-checks the importer, a")
    strs_push(l, "private body's does not — a workspace rename that keeps an alias, the API document, a warm build,")
    strs_push(l, "a package) and the selfhost suite. Nine new mutants, all caught. **Stays PARTIAL:** `nazm build`")
    strs_push(l, "and `nazm run` still check every module; a warm build reuses objects, not checks.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N77 (2026-10-03)** · *Resolution, persisted* (`architecture.md` §7.78). A module that checks")
    strs_push(l, "cleanly leaves a **resolved unit**, `nazm.resolved/1`: its imports (as written, alias, target")
    strs_push(l, "key, target interface hash), its definitions and every resolved occurrence of a declared entity,")
    strs_push(l, "each by durable identity (`DefKey`, with a member name for a variant, field or payload field), no")
    strs_push(l, "session id, no path, no local. It is written from the checker's own `Resolution` and reference")
    strs_push(l, "index (`crates/nazm-iface/src/resolved.rs`) and stored in the module's check entry, now")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.check/3`, under the same key. Its invalidation is therefore the check's, and the table in")
    strs_push(l, "§7.78 is held by `crates/nazm-cli/tests/resolved_units.rs`. The same bytes come out of two")
    strs_push(l, "processes and two checkouts. A private body change re-checks its module and leaves the importer's")
    strs_push(l, "unit byte-identical. An exported change re-checks every direct importer. An alias is part of the")
    strs_push(l, "importer's unit. A unit forged to claim other text is never read. `nazm references DEF FILE` reads")
    strs_push(l, "reused modules' units instead of checking their bodies: warm, `checked` is 0, and the answer")
    strs_push(l, "equals the language service's references from a fresh in-process check, the independent oracle.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm resolve FILE` prints the units. Both schemas are validated against real output")
    strs_push(l, "(`schemas.rs`); a missing, foreign or mis-versioned unit is a miss (`crates/nazm-cache/tests/store.rs`).")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler written in Nazm's loader, `compiler/module.nz`, refuses `@std/` and `NAME:` imports by")
    strs_push(l, "name (`selfhost.rs`), where it used to report a missing file; it resolves relative paths only.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · Lexical scoping with shadowing rules and a separate function namespace,")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-core/src/check/`. `use \"relative/path.nz\";` resolved by the driver,")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-service/src/load.rs` — canonical-path keyed, read-once, depth-first, cycles")
    strs_push(l, "terminate rather than erroring. A second resolver written in Nazm, `compiler/module.nz`,")
    strs_push(l, "serves the bootstrap stages. Codes `N0200`–`N0210` in `crates/nazm-diag/src/lib.rs`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N49 (2026-10-01)** · qualified names: an import under a name keeps its module's exports out of")
    strs_push(l, "the unqualified namespace and holds them as `alias::name` in the same environments, so `NAME::item`")
    strs_push(l, "resolves to exactly the definition an unqualified import would, at the item's own span — one")
    strs_push(l, "resolver. The graph's edge records whether a plain `use` named the module and each alias.")
    strs_push(l, "`N0209` (an alias that already means something), `N0210` (a qualified name that names nothing).")
    strs_push(l, "Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/usability.rs` (two modules exporting one name used side by side,")
    strs_push(l, "which was `N0207`; a module imported both ways; `@std`; types, constructions, variants and match")
    strs_push(l, "arms), `crates/nazm-service/tests/qualified.rs` (definition and references at the item's bytes).")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler written in Nazm refuses `::` and `as` by name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Resolution is singular as of N1 (2026-09-21).** `nazm_core::check` produces a")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm_sema::Resolution` — function definitions, call targets, and the slot every name")
    strs_push(l, "mention refers to — and both the evaluator and `crates/nazm-lir/src/lower.rs` read it.")
    strs_push(l, "Since N2 that is true of the **evaluator** as well: its `HashMap<String, usize>` over every")
    strs_push(l, "function, and its own copy of the built-in-first rule, are gone. The backend's last two")
    strs_push(l, "name lookups went with them — `crates/nazm-lir/src/lower.rs` pairs definitions with")
    strs_push(l, "declarations through `FnDef::decl` and finds the entry point through `Resolution::entry`,")
    strs_push(l, "so neither consumer knows the spelling `main`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Source identity is real as of N1.** `nazm_span::Span` is `{ file, start, end }` with")
    strs_push(l, "file-local offsets, and `crates/nazm-service/src/load.rs` produces a `SourceMap` whose files")
    strs_push(l, "are parsed separately. The merged buffer, and the binary search that recovered a file from")
    strs_push(l, "an offset, are gone.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**There is a compilation unit as of N2 (2026-09-22).** One module is one file.")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-sema/src/module.rs` holds `ModuleId` and the `ModuleGraph` the driver builds")
    strs_push(l, "while loading; `crates/nazm-sema/src/interface.rs` holds the `UnitInterface` a module")
    strs_push(l, "offers. Checking is two stages, `declare_unit` then `check_unit`")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-core/src/check/`), and the second takes its dependencies as **interfaces**.")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-core/tests/unit_checking.rs` checks a module against an interface for a module")
    strs_push(l, "whose source does not exist, and refuses the same module when that interface is empty.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Visibility exists as of N2.** Top-level definitions are private to their module; `pub`")
    strs_push(l, "exports; imports are not transitive; every collision is a diagnostic naming both sides")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0206`–`N0208`). Twenty cases in `crates/nazm-cli/tests/visibility.rs`, most of them run")
    strs_push(l, "interpreted and compiled and required to agree. The self-hosted compiler was migrated")
    strs_push(l, "rather than exempted: 84 of its 224 functions are `pub`, 140 are private, and since N2.1 it enforces the rule as well as expressing it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A toolchain-owned module exists as of N12 (2026-09-24).** The core prelude,")
    strs_push(l, "`library/core/prelude.nz`, is loaded into every compilation after its project modules and")
    strs_push(l, "imported by every one of them with no `use` (`ModuleGraph::attach_prelude`). Its key,")
    strs_push(l, "`@core/prelude`, is fixed by the toolchain and disjoint from every project key; its two type")
    strs_push(l, "names are reserved (`N0363`). It is a dependency like any import, so it is in every module's")
    strs_push(l, "check key. It is **not** a package system.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Durable identity and persisted interfaces exist as of N3 (2026-09-22).** A module's")
    strs_push(l, "`ModuleKey` is its normalised path relative to the compilation's source root, and a")
    strs_push(l, "definition's `DefKey` is that key plus its kind and name")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-sema/src/key.rs`). `nazm interface FILE` writes a module's interface as")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.interface/3` — durable keys, canonical type names, exported **record and enum")
    strs_push(l, "definitions** closed over their field and payload types, no spans, no session ids, no")
    strs_push(l, "discriminants (`crates/nazm-iface/`) — and `--hash` fingerprints it with BLAKE3. It was")
    strs_push(l, "`/1` until N9 and `/2` until N10; a `/1` file describes a language with no records and a")
    strs_push(l, "`/2` one a language with no enums, so reading either as a `/3` would be believing a module")
    strs_push(l, "offers less than it does, and every direction is refused rather than reinterpreted. The session ids are")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged and were not renamed; both layers coexist.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/durable_identity.rs` establishes it across real boundaries: the same")
    strs_push(l, "project gives identical bytes in two processes and in two different directories, a module")
    strs_push(l, "whose private body changed gives the same fingerprint, and **a dependent checks against a")
    strs_push(l, "deserialised interface with the dependency's source deleted.** A module outside the source")
    strs_push(l, "root, or one a symbolic link gave two names, is refused a durable key rather than given a")
    strs_push(l, "guess.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A project can declare where it begins, as of N4 (2026-09-22).** An empty `nazm.root`")
    strs_push(l, "marker, or `--source-root DIR`, fixes the root a module's key is relative to, so")
    strs_push(l, "`lib/common.nz` is the same module whichever entry file named it")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-service/src/root.rs`, ten cases in `crates/nazm-cli/tests/source_root.rs`). With")
    strs_push(l, "neither, the root is derived from the named file exactly as before. The marker must be")
    strs_push(l, "empty and is refused otherwise: it says where a project begins and owns nothing else.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · A module is named by a relative path, `@std/NAME` or a package's `NAME:path`; the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler written in Nazm resolves the first two (N102) and refuses the third by name. A resolved unit carries no types and no slots, so `nazm build` and")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm run` still check every module (area 2a); locals have no persisted resolution; the language")
    strs_push(l, "service never reads or writes a unit (an unsaved buffer is not cache state). *The sentence that")
    strs_push(l, "stood here — that nothing is separately compiled — was true until N5 and is now area 10a.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · Check reuse for `nazm build` and `nazm run`: a persisted unit that carries")
    strs_push(l, "types and slots, so a warm build lowers a module it did not re-check.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Met for identity, interfaces and a declared root.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 2a. Incremental semantic checking — VERIFIED")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · `nazm check` reuses the result of checking a module whose semantic inputs")
    strs_push(l, "are unchanged, as of N4 (2026-09-22). `crates/nazm-cache/` computes what those inputs are —")
    strs_push(l, "`SourceFingerprint` over the exact source bytes, `CheckerIdentity` over the checker's own")
    strs_push(l, "tables plus an explicit `SEMANTIC_EPOCH`, and `CheckKey` over both plus each direct")
    strs_push(l, "import's `(ModuleKey, InterfaceHash)` — and stores a `nazm.check/1` entry per module in")
    strs_push(l, "`.nazm/check/`, published by `rename` and validated on read.")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-core/src/check/` gained one hook, `Reuse`; `check_unit` is still the only")
    strs_push(l, "thing that decides what a body means.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Twenty-nine tests in `crates/nazm-cli/tests/incremental.rs`, each running the binary")
    strs_push(l, "repeatedly, establish the model: a private body change re-checks its own module and leaves")
    strs_push(l, "its importer alone; an exported signature change re-checks the importer and finds the error")
    strs_push(l, "it now has; in `A → B → C`, a change to C that leaves B's interface unchanged stops at B.")
    strs_push(l, "Sixteen more in `crates/nazm-cache/tests/store.rs` break one thing about a stored entry —")
    strs_push(l, "truncation, a future schema, an edited fingerprint, an edited interface, a valid entry")
    strs_push(l, "under the wrong name — and every one is a miss.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is reused, exactly** · The second stage of checking a module: its bodies. Every")
    strs_push(l, "module is still read, parsed and declared from source on every run, which is why a skipped")
    strs_push(l, "module is invisible — the interface other modules' keys depend on, and whether the")
    strs_push(l, "compilation has a `main`, are recomputed rather than recalled.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · **This is not incremental native compilation, and no such claim is made.**")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm run` and `nazm build` reuse *this* cache not at all: both need the typed resolution that")
    strs_push(l, "only checking a body produces. Since N77 a module's *names* persist, as its resolved unit")
    strs_push(l, "(area 2), but its types and slots do not, and lowering needs them. (`nazm build` reuses objects as")
    strs_push(l, "of N6 — a different cache, a different key, area 10b — and a build that reused every object")
    strs_push(l, "still checked every module.) There is no IR or LIR cache, no query database, no scheduler and no")
    strs_push(l, "eviction policy. A module with no durable identity is checked every time.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**And the measured gain is about a millisecond.** On the compiler's own five modules,")
    strs_push(l, "`performance.md` records 40.5 ms with the cache disabled against 38.9 ms warm — 18% of the")
    strs_push(l, "work above a 31.7 ms process floor, and 3.9% of the wall clock. The first run is **24 ms")
    strs_push(l, "slower**, because publishing five entries costs an `fsync` each. The decisions are right;")
    strs_push(l, "the saving is small because parsing and declaring happen every run and are most of the")
    strs_push(l, "cost. Recorded rather than averaged away: a reader deciding whether to depend on this")
    strs_push(l, "should know it buys correctness of invalidation, not speed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · *Met in part by N77:* name resolution now has a written form, the resolved")
    strs_push(l, "unit, and `nazm references` reads it instead of checking a reused module's bodies. A build that")
    strs_push(l, "skips bodies needs typed Core IR to be persisted too, which a resolved unit deliberately is not. Not a `CodegenKey`: N6 found that native reuse")
    strs_push(l, "needed no semantic key at all (area 10b), so the dependency this row once named is gone")
    strs_push(l, "rather than met.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Met for semantic checking. Native reuse is a separate row that does not")
    strs_push(l, "exist.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 3. Type system — VERIFIED as scoped (N107, Gate 2)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 2 (2026-10-08)** · *Bytes* and *Text* (`spec.md`; `general-purpose.md` §5, §6). `Bytes`,")
    strs_push(l, "a counted view of a fixed-length buffer: `bytes_new`, `bytes_from_str`, `bytes_get`/`_set`,")
    strs_push(l, "`bytes_slice` sharing the buffer, `bytes_copy` (overlap-safe), and reads and writes of every")
    strs_push(l, "numeric type in either byte order. `Text`, UTF-8 by construction: literals where a `Text` is")
    strs_push(l, "expected, `Text(s)`, `try_convert[Text](s)`, `utf8_valid`, slicing at boundaries, scalar")
    strs_push(l, "iteration, `scalar_text`. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/bytes_text.rs` — eight tests, each program run")
    strs_push(l, "under the interpreter, LLVM `-O0` and `-O2` and Cranelift: views sharing writes, every width and")
    strs_push(l, "byte order, RFC 3629's validation table (27 sequences) agreeing with the host, scalar iteration")
    strs_push(l, "and boundaries, every trap (`N0405`, `N0413`) with its sentence, every refusal (`N0003`, `N0203`,")
    strs_push(l, "`N0300`, `N0304`, `N0321`, `N0331`, `N0621`), reclamation counted equal (16 of 16) in all three,")
    strs_push(l, "and both types across a public signature, cold and cached. Not crossing the C boundary yet, and")
    strs_push(l, "refused by name by the EVM and accelerator-kernel targets, as every built-in is.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 2 (2026-10-08)** · *Arrays* and *Constants* (`spec.md`; `general-purpose.md` §4, §15).")
    strs_push(l, "`[T; N]` of plain data — numbers, `Bool`, and records, enums and arrays of them — at most 64 KiB;")
    strs_push(l, "`[a, b]`, `[value; count]`, a checked `xs[i]` and `xs[i] = v` through any path of fields and")
    strs_push(l, "indexes; copied as a value, compared element by element, held inline in records, vectors and")
    strs_push(l, "tasks; and `const NAME: T = value;`, computed by the checker with the same numeric semantics,")
    strs_push(l, "module-private. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/arrays.rs` — seven tests, each program run under the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter, LLVM `-O0` and `-O2` and Cranelift: building, copying and writing in place, arrays in")
    strs_push(l, "records and records in arrays, a copy crossing into a task, every index (read, write, negative,")
    strs_push(l, "nested) stopping with `N0405`, constants, every refusal (`N0003`, `N0101`, `N0300`, `N0618`,")
    strs_push(l, "`N0621`–`N0624`) with the 64 KiB bound exact, and an array in a public signature across modules,")
    strs_push(l, "cold and from the cached interface. Compatibility corpus: one run case, one trap case, six")
    strs_push(l, "refusals. Ten mutants (`g2-…array…`, `g2-…constant…`). Not crossing the C boundary, not in the EVM")
    strs_push(l, "or accelerator-kernel targets (refused by name), and no slices or views — that is §5's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 2 (2026-10-07)** · *Numbers* (`spec.md`, *Numbers*; `general-purpose.md` §1–§3). `Int8`,")
    strs_push(l, "`Int16`, `Int32`, `UInt8`, `UInt16`, `UInt32`, `UInt64`, `Float32` and `Float64` beside `Int`;")
    strs_push(l, "float, hexadecimal, octal and binary literals typed by the type expected; `&`, `|`, `^`, `~`, `<<`,")
    strs_push(l, "`>>`; `T(x)`, `try_convert`, `wrap_convert`, `saturate_convert`; 43 numeric built-ins, generic over")
    strs_push(l, "a class of types. One semantics, `nazm_sema::numeric`, is what the interpreter and the LIR oracle")
    strs_push(l, "run; both native backends are held to it by `crates/nazm-cli/tests/numbers.rs` — eleven tests,")
    strs_push(l, "each run under the interpreter, LLVM `-O0` and `-O2` and Cranelift: shortest-digit float text,")
    strs_push(l, "IEEE comparison with NaN, every width's range and signedness, wrapping and saturation, shifts,")
    strs_push(l, "rotations and counts, every conversion mode, numbers in records, vectors and tasks, every trap")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0400`, `N0401`, `N0412`) with its code, every refusal (`N0003`, `N0300`, `N0304`, `N0354`,")
    strs_push(l, "`N0617`), and the C library's functions to six places. Compatibility corpus: one run case, two")
    strs_push(l, "trap cases, three refusals, and the superseded `1.5` refusal now held to checking. Not crossing")
    strs_push(l, "the C boundary yet, and not in the EVM or accelerator-kernel targets, which refuse them by name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N107, 2026-10-05: the scope audited (`audit-n107.md`, `architecture.md` §7.108).* The scope is the type system the spec states — records, closed enums, exhaustive variant match, first-order generics with `Vec[T]`, typed `Result` and `?`, structural equality and equality bounds, function values and closures, traits with impls, methods and bounds, dispatched statically. Trait objects, generic traits, associated types, default methods and supertraits are not required by any program or stated goal (dynamic dispatch exists through function values and enums, and the goals ask that it be exposed and restricted, not added); each stays refused by name (`N0602`–`N0608`). Checking against a persisted interface alone, without source, cannot use traits: a tooling boundary (area 26), not a wrong answer — the cached check path handles traits.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N78 (2026-10-03)** · *Traits and methods* (`architecture.md` §7.79, `spec.md`, *Traits and")
    strs_push(l, "methods*). `trait Name { fn m(self: Self, …) -> R; }`, `impl Name for Type { … }`, `recv.m(…)` and")
    strs_push(l, "`Trait.m(recv, …)`, and a type parameter's bound naming a trait (`[T: Show]`). Coherence holds over")
    strs_push(l, "the whole compilation: at most one impl of a trait for a type (`N0600`), in the trait's module or")
    strs_push(l, "the type's (`N0601`). An impl defines exactly its trait's methods with its signatures and effects")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0602`, `N0603`), for a non-generic record or enum, a numeric type, `Bool` or `Str` (`N0604`). Method")
    strs_push(l, "lookup is over the traits in scope and the impls of this module and its direct imports, which keeps")
    strs_push(l, "a cached check sound (`N0605`, `N0606`). There are no trait objects (`N0607`), and methods are not")
    strs_push(l, "values (`N0608`). A concrete call is resolved before Core IR to the impl's ordinary function; a call")
    strs_push(l, "through a bound is Core IR's one new form, `CallTrait`, which MIR resolves per instance and the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter per value. The same program prints the same in the interpreter, LLVM at -O0 and -O2,")
    strs_push(l, "and Cranelift, with every allocation reclaimed (`crates/nazm-cli/tests/traits.rs`, 17 tests: impls")
    strs_push(l, "on a record, an enum and a built-in, calls through two levels of generic code, cross-module and")
    strs_push(l, "aliased traits, `@std/show`'s `show_all` over a `Vec` of a program's records, and each refusal by")
    strs_push(l, "code). `@std/show` is the first standard trait. Traits, trait methods and calls through bounds are")
    strs_push(l, "reference targets (`nazm resolve`, `nazm references`, the language service; semantic tokens")
    strs_push(l, "`interface` and `method`). The persisted interface carries exported traits, every impl and every")
    strs_push(l, "bound (`nazm.interface/8`), and adding an impl moves its fingerprint. Semantic epoch 22; Core IR")
    strs_push(l, "print `nazm.core-ir/2`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N50 (2026-10-02)** · function values and closures, `architecture.md` §7.52 and `docs/user/spec.md`,")
    strs_push(l, "*Function values and closures*. `Type::Fn`, interned by parameters, result and effects")
    strs_push(l, "(structural, invariant, no equality, never into a task); a named, monomorphic Nazm function as a")
    strs_push(l, "value; `fn(x: T) -> R ! {e} { … }` closures capturing by copy; calls through a binding of function")
    strs_push(l, "type. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/closures.rs` holds each across the interpreter, LLVM −O0/−O2 and")
    strs_push(l, "Cranelift with the memory report compared line for line, and every refusal (`N0386`, `N0387`, and")
    strs_push(l, "the existing `N0300`, `N0303`, `N0304`, `N0310`, `N0321`, `N0366`, `N0369`, `N0372` with their")
    strs_push(l, "meanings unchanged). Traits and methods: **DESIGNED**, deferred — §7.52 records why and the")
    strs_push(l, "questions they would settle. Closures and function values inside generic functions: refused.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · Six built-in types, `crates/nazm-sema/src/types.rs`: `Int`, `Bool`, `Str`,")
    strs_push(l, "`Ints`, `Strs`, `Chan` — **and, since N9, user-defined records; since N10, user-defined")
    strs_push(l, "enums**. Local inference for `let`; parameters and returns always written. Completion")
    strs_push(l, "analysis decides whether a block produces a value, which is what lets one `if` serve both")
    strs_push(l, "statement and value position. Codes `N0300`–`N0314` and `N0330`–`N0345`. 114 behavioural")
    strs_push(l, "tests in `crates/nazm-core/tests/language.rs`, 33 in `crates/nazm-core/tests/records.rs`,")
    strs_push(l, "47 in `crates/nazm-core/tests/enums.rs`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N9, 2026-09-23.* `struct Point { x: Int, y: Int, }` — nominal value records with named")
    strs_push(l, "fields, named construction, projection, field replacement through a projection path,")
    strs_push(l, "nesting, and separate type and function namespaces. The type enum stopped being closed:")
    strs_push(l, "`Type::Record(RecordId)` names a definition rather than a shape, because two records with")
    strs_push(l, "identical fields are different types. Every property a record has — cleanup, task safety,")
    strs_push(l, "copy, destroy — is **derived from its fields**, recursively, and that composition rather")
    strs_push(l, "than the syntax is what the milestone was for. `docs/user/spec.md`, *Records*, is the law;")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.10 is the implementation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N10, 2026-09-23.* `enum State { Ready, Done(code: Int), }` with `match` — closed nominal")
    strs_push(l, "sum types with named payload fields, qualified construction, exhaustive variant matching")
    strs_push(l, "with named payload bindings, and composition with records in both directions. The")
    strs_push(l, "milestone's question was not whether enums compile but whether the ownership model holds")
    strs_push(l, "when **which fields exist is a runtime fact**: copy and release act on the active variant")
    strs_push(l, "alone, derived and dispatched in the emitted program, while task safety stays a property of")
    strs_push(l, "the **type** and quantifies over every variant. `docs/user/spec.md`, *Enums*, is the law;")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.11 is the implementation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N11, 2026-09-23.* First-order parametric generics — `struct Pair[A, B]`, `enum Maybe[T]`,")
    strs_push(l, "`fn identity[T]` — checked **once, parametrically**, with call-site type arguments written")
    strs_push(l, "or inferred from the arguments and never from the expected result, and one generic")
    strs_push(l, "container, `Vec[T]`. An applied type is an interned table entry with substituted fields, so")
    strs_push(l, "every derivation above holds after substitution unchanged; parameters are positions, so")
    strs_push(l, "renaming one changes no interface byte. Codes `N0350`–`N0359`. 40 tests in")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-core/tests/generics.rs` with code and span, 7 native ones in")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/generics.rs`, and `the_nazm_checker_agrees_with_the_reference_on_generics`")
    strs_push(l, "comparing both checkers on 42 programs by code **and** span. `docs/user/spec.md`, *Generics*, is")
    strs_push(l, "the law; `architecture.md` §7.12 is the implementation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N12, 2026-09-24.* **Typed error values.** `Result[T, E]` and `Option[T]` are ordinary")
    strs_push(l, "generic enums declared by the core prelude, and `?` propagates the core `Result` — recognised")
    strs_push(l, "by definition, never by name or shape — with the exact rule `expr: Result[T, E]` in a function")
    strs_push(l, "returning `Result[U, E]` gives `expr?: T`, the identical `E` required. No exceptions, no")
    strs_push(l, "unwinding, no conversion between error types, no `?` on `Option`. Codes `N0360`–`N0363`. 33")
    strs_push(l, "tests in `crates/nazm-core/tests/results.rs` with code and span, 12 native memory cases in")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/propagation.rs`, 10 module, interface and cache cases in")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/prelude.rs`, and")
    strs_push(l, "`the_nazm_checker_agrees_with_the_reference_on_propagation` comparing both checkers on 22")
    strs_push(l, "programs by code **and** span. `docs/user/spec.md`, *Typed error values*, is the law;")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.13 is the implementation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N12.1, 2026-09-24, changed no rule here.* A block used as a value — a `match` arm, a `let`")
    strs_push(l, "initialiser, an argument, a field, an operand — was always part of the checked language; it")
    strs_push(l, "now also compiles natively in both compilers, which is area 9's and area 10's row rather")
    strs_push(l, "than this one's. What this row gains is the first `Option` doing real work inside the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler: `record_owned` returns `Option[Int]` instead of a `-1`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N13, 2026-09-25.* **Derived structural equality.** `==` and `!=` apply to two operands of")
    strs_push(l, "one type when that type has equality, and for a user type it is derived, never declared:")
    strs_push(l, "a record has it exactly when every field does, an enum exactly when every payload field of")
    strs_push(l, "**every** variant does, and a concrete generic instance after substitution — so")
    strs_push(l, "`Option[Int]` and `Result[Int, Str]` have it as ordinary enums, with no rule naming them.")
    strs_push(l, "One derivation, `UserTypes::equality` in `crates/nazm-sema/src/udt.rs`, beside cleanup and")
    strs_push(l, "task safety and independent of both; the checker asks it and nothing else, and its refusal")
    strs_push(l, "names the blocking component (`Outer`'s `inner.values`). No code was added — the rule moved")
    strs_push(l, "under `N0304` — so `SEMANTIC_EPOCH` went 5 → 6; the interface schema is unchanged at")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.interface/4`. 20 tests in `crates/nazm-core/tests/equality.rs` with code and span, 11")
    strs_push(l, "native ones in `crates/nazm-cli/tests/equality.rs` at `-O0` and `-O2` with every memory")
    strs_push(l, "counter, `the_nazm_checker_agrees_with_the_reference_on_equality` comparing both checkers on")
    strs_push(l, "30 programs by code **and** span, and the interface-only case with the dependency deleted.")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/spec.md`, *Equality is derived*, is the law; `architecture.md` §7.15 is the")
    strs_push(l, "implementation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | equality |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Int`, `Bool`, `Str` (primitive) | VERIFIED, unchanged — `Str` by its bytes |")
    strs_push(l, "| record, derived | VERIFIED |")
    strs_push(l, "| enum, derived over every variant | VERIFIED |")
    strs_push(l, "| concrete generic instance, after substitution | VERIFIED |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Option[T]` / `Result[T, E]`, inherited as ordinary enums | VERIFIED |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Vec[T]`, `Ints`, `Strs` — sequence equality | absent, deliberately |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Chan` | absent, deliberately |")
    strs_push(l, "| equality over a constrained type parameter | absent at N13 — there was no constraint mechanism; N14 added one (below) |")
    strs_push(l, "| custom (user-defined) equality | absent |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N14, 2026-09-25.* **A type parameter may require equality.** `fn same[T: Equality](a: T,")
    strs_push(l, "b: T) -> Bool { a == b }` is accepted, the same without `: Equality` is still refused, and")
    strs_push(l, "every argument — written or inferred, concrete or a caller's own parameter — is checked")
    strs_push(l, "against the requirement by N13's one derivation, which now reads a required parameter as")
    strs_push(l, "having equality. So `Box[T]`, `Option[T]` and `Result[T, E]` with both required compare")
    strs_push(l, "inside a bounded body, `Vec[Int]` and `Option[Vec[Int]]` never satisfy it, and an")
    strs_push(l, "unconstrained wrapper cannot forward to a bounded callee. One compiler-owned capability,")
    strs_push(l, "`Equality`, on function parameters only; nothing is emitted at run time. Codes `N0364`,")
    strs_push(l, "`N0365`; `SEMANTIC_EPOCH` 6 → 7 and the interface schema `/4` → `/5`, which persists each")
    strs_push(l, "export's required positions. 14 tests in `crates/nazm-core/tests/constraints.rs` with code")
    strs_push(l, "and span, 3 native ones in `crates/nazm-cli/tests/constraints.rs`, interface-only and cache")
    strs_push(l, "cases in `durable_identity.rs` and `incremental.rs`, and")
    strs_push(l, "`the_nazm_checker_agrees_with_the_reference_on_requirements` comparing both checkers on 23")
    strs_push(l, "programs by code **and** span. `docs/user/spec.md`, *A type parameter may require equality*, is")
    strs_push(l, "the law; `architecture.md` §7.16 is the implementation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | status |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| first-order generics | VERIFIED |")
    strs_push(l, "| a generic parameter that requires the built-in equality capability | VERIFIED |")
    strs_push(l, "| a requirement on a record's or an enum's parameter | refused (`N0101`), deferred |")
    strs_push(l, "| any other capability, user-defined traits, `impl`, methods | absent (traits and methods DESIGNED, §7.52) |")
    strs_push(l, "| function types, named functions as values, closures, indirect calls (N50) | VERIFIED (`crates/nazm-cli/tests/closures.rs`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| custom equality, sequence or channel equality, ordering, hashing | absent |")
    strs_push(l, "| higher kinds, const generics, specialisation | absent |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Seven constructs are verified rather than partial: **records**, **closed enums**,")
    strs_push(l, "**exhaustive variant match**, **first-order generics with `Vec[T]`**, **typed `Result`")
    strs_push(l, "propagation**, **derived structural equality** and **equality-requiring type parameters**.")
    strs_push(l, "What surrounds them is not verified, and none of it is a trait system. Typed errors are **not** effects: a `Result` in a")
    strs_push(l, "signature is a return type, and area 5 is unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · Generics remain narrowly constrained: N14 adds exactly one compiler-owned")
    strs_push(l, "requirement, `Equality`, on a function's type parameters, and that is not a trait system.")
    strs_push(l, "*Narrowed in N78:* until then there were no user-defined traits, no `impl` and no methods. What")
    strs_push(l, "remains is deliberate, and each is refused by name: no trait objects or dynamic dispatch, no")
    strs_push(l, "default methods, no associated types or constants, no generic traits or methods, no supertraits,")
    strs_push(l, "no impls with bounds or for generic types, no inherent impls without a trait, no methods as values,")
    strs_push(l, "one requirement per type parameter. Calling a field of function type as `r.f(1)` stays refused.")
    strs_push(l, "Generic function values (`N0387`) are outside the supported model: each would need a thunk per")
    strs_push(l, "instance, and a bound covers the programs that wanted one. A closure, and a named function's value,")
    strs_push(l, "inside a generic function are accepted since R1b (L10). No")
    strs_push(l, "higher kinds, const generics, defaults, variance or specialisation. A persisted interface's traits")
    strs_push(l, "are not rehydrated, so a module checked against one (rather than its source) cannot use them. The")
    strs_push(l, "compiler written in Nazm has traits, closures and function values since N102. A requirement cannot be written on a record's or an enum's parameter (`N0101`).")
    strs_push(l, "`Option` has no `?`, `Result` no")
    strs_push(l, "methods and no conversion between error types, and `main` cannot return one; no")
    strs_push(l, "indexing syntax on a `Vec`; no `spawn` of a generic function. Function values and closures")
    strs_push(l, "exist (N50), inside a generic function too since R1b (L10); no unit type, no `Never`.")
    strs_push(l, "Since N78 a generic definition can require a trait of `T`, and a program can declare traits of its")
    strs_push(l, "own; nothing can say \"`T` can be passed to a task\". No ordering, hashing or custom equality on any user type, and no")
    strs_push(l, "equality at all on a sequence, a `Vec` or a `Chan`. No field-level or per-variant visibility, no")
    strs_push(l, "default field values, no record update syntax. The pattern language is variant selection")
    strs_push(l, "with named payload bindings and `_` — no top-level wildcard arm, no guards, no or-patterns,")
    strs_push(l, "no literal, record, tuple or range patterns, and no `let` destructuring. Four words — `for`,")
    strs_push(l, "`label`, `loop` and `mod` — remain reserved and refused by name rather than silently absent")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-syntax/src/parser.rs`); `struct` left that list in N9, `enum` and `match`")
    strs_push(l, "in N10 and `impl` in N78, for the same reason `print` did in B3 — a reserved word earns its place by naming")
    strs_push(l, "something absent. *Until N11 this said neither a record nor an enum could be put in a")
    strs_push(l, "sequence; `Vec[T]` holds either.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · None forced by a program yet. N14's requirement covered the need N13")
    strs_push(l, "exposed with one built-in capability, and its dogfood found no compiler code that wanted")
    strs_push(l, "another (`research-register.md`, N14). *Until N14 this named constrained generics, which N14")
    strs_push(l, "added for equality; until N13 equality on user types; until N12 typed errors; until N12.1")
    strs_push(l, "blocks as values in the native backends.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Chosen by the milestone that needs it, not by completeness.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Semantic core")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 4. Memory model and reclamation — VERIFIED for the current type universe, closure environments included (Gate 1-C1)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1a (2026-10-12)** · *Immutable indirection: `Box[T]` and `List[T]`* (`spec.md`;")
    strs_push(l, "`openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, D1/L1). A definition may reach itself through a")
    strs_push(l, "`Box` or `List`: the ownership graph labels those edges immutable and refuses only a cycle with a")
    strs_push(l, "counted edge on it (`N0359`), with the reclamation argument in the specification. Both are a")
    strs_push(l, "`Vec[T]` underneath, nothing writes after they are made, and they are distinct types to the")
    strs_push(l, "checker only: Core IR lowering writes `box_new` and `list_from_vec` with three internal built-ins")
    strs_push(l, "no program can name, and the interpreter, the LIR oracle and LIR carry each operation out as the")
    strs_push(l, "`Vec` one it means. Release is a worklist, not recursion, in all three: the interpreter's")
    strs_push(l, "sequence storage hands its elements to a per-thread queue, and the runtime's `nz.vec_release`")
    strs_push(l, "takes the queue of the release in progress — runtime ABI 29. Prelude names: a module's own `Box`,")
    strs_push(l, "`List` or `box_new` keeps its meaning. Semantic epoch 53; EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since). Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/box_list.rs` — trees of boxes and lists by hand-worked output under the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter, the LIR oracle, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with nothing live; a million-deep `Box`")
    strs_push(l, "chain built and released by the interpreter, LLVM and Cranelift with every sequence reclaimed")
    strs_push(l, "(before the queue the interpreter overflowed its stack and a compiled program died releasing it);")
    strs_push(l, "the ownership rule's acceptances and refusals; no equality, no task, no bare `Box`; a closure")
    strs_push(l, "capturing a `List` of function values accepted and a `Vec` of them refused (`N0616`); the prelude")
    strs_push(l, "names; provenance through both; a recursive type crossing a module's interface.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**v1 (2026-10-11, Q1-M-01, Q1-M-02)** · The type universe this row's VERIFIED covers is now written")
    strs_push(l, "down whole: `spec.md`'s four kinds list Gate 2's numbers and arrays (immediates), `Text` (a shared")
    strs_push(l, "immutable value), `Vec[T]` and `Bytes` (owned mutable handles; a buffer lives while any view does)")
    strs_push(l, "and `Chan[T]`, and *What is not promised* names them. `Bytes` and `Text` reclamation is held by two")
    strs_push(l, "programs: `every_buffer_is_reclaimed_by_its_last_view_everywhere` (views outliving their buffer's")
    strs_push(l, "first holder, under scribbled freed memory) and")
    strs_push(l, "`a_buffer_and_a_text_are_reclaimed_in_every_shape_on_every_path` — a buffer and a text in a record")
    strs_push(l, "field, a `Vec`, a closure's environment and a `Result` passed on by `?`, on the normal end and on a")
    strs_push(l, "trap, every count balanced, under the interpreter and both backends.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 1-C1 (2026-10-07)** · *Status restored from PARTIAL to VERIFIED by a rule and its evidence,")
    strs_push(l, "not by a narrower claim.* A closure's environment is a node of the ownership graph")
    strs_push(l, "(`docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.111, `docs/user/spec.md` *Cycles*): a closure may not capture a value whose")
    strs_push(l, "type can hold a function value behind a counted handle (`N0616`), decided from the type alone, so")
    strs_push(l, "an alias, a record field, a `Vec` of records, an enum or `Option` payload, nested vectors and a")
    strs_push(l, "container made in another function are covered without alias analysis. An environment is")
    strs_push(l, "immutable and points only at older values, the only edges into an existing value are stores into")
    strs_push(l, "counted handles, and a handle that cannot hold a function value holds no environment — so storing")
    strs_push(l, "a function value anywhere, through any parameter, is never refused, and no accepted program forms")
    strs_push(l, "a cycle. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`a_closure_capturing_a_container_of_function_values_is_refused_in_every_shape` (direct, alias,")
    strs_push(l, "mutual, nested, record, records in a vector, enum, `Option`, `Vec[Vec[fn]]`, made in a helper —")
    strs_push(l, "each `N0616`, and `nazm run` refuses);")
    strs_push(l, "`acyclic_closures_in_containers_are_accepted_and_reclaimed_everywhere` (named functions and")
    strs_push(l, "closures capturing values, vectors and other closures, stored in vectors, records and through an")
    strs_push(l, "opaque parameter and a generic function: the same output and `live=0` for sequences, strings,")
    strs_push(l, "channels and closures in the interpreter, LLVM `-O0` and `-O2` and Cranelift);")
    strs_push(l, "`the_rule_holds_where_a_closure_is_written_in_any_module`; five refusal cases and one run case in")
    strs_push(l, "the compatibility corpus; the compiler written in Nazm refuses the same programs at the same span")
    strs_push(l, "(bootstrap: 30 refusal cases). Semantic epoch 30; `nazm.interface/11` and runtime ABI 14 unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "There is no collector, and none is needed for a program the checker accepts. The rule is")
    strs_push(l, "conservative: a closure that only reads a vector of handlers is refused too, and is written by")
    strs_push(l, "passing the vector as an argument. The Gate 1 entry below is the historical record of the defect.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Gate 1 → Gate 1-C1, historical:* the heading read \"PARTIAL: verified for the current type")
    strs_push(l, "universe, one recorded cycle defect (Gate 1)\".")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 1 (2026-10-07), historical — closed by Gate 1-C1 above** · *Status moved from VERIFIED to PARTIAL by a defect, not by a goal.* A")
    strs_push(l, "closure that captures a `Vec` able to hold function values and is then stored into that `Vec` is")
    strs_push(l, "a value that owns itself. The checker accepts it, and counting does not reclaim it: built natively,")
    strs_push(l, "`let fs = vec_new[fn() -> Int](); let f = fn() -> Int { vec_len(fs) }; vec_push(fs, f);` ends")
    strs_push(l, "with `nazm-memory: sequences allocated=1 reclaimed=0 live=1 … closures allocated=1 reclaimed=0")
    strs_push(l, "live=1`, where the same program with the closure capturing another vector reclaims everything.")
    strs_push(l, "N50 added the value kind *Cycles* said must arrive with a policy, and supplied none; the *Next")
    strs_push(l, "dependency* below already named \"a closure capturing its own handle\" as the case to settle, and it")
    strs_push(l, "was not settled. `docs/user/spec.md` *Cycles* carries the correction; the reclamation claim holds for")
    strs_push(l, "programs that form no such cycle. **Accepted when** the cycle is refused by the type system (as")
    strs_push(l, "`N0359` refuses ownership cycles in definitions) or reclaimed by a stated policy, with a test")
    strs_push(l, "either way — a decision for review, not taken in Gate 1.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N52 (2026-10-02)** · resource sites are facts: `nazm explain-cost` (`nazm.cost/1`) lists each")
    strs_push(l, "function's allocation, retain, block, channel, foreign and task sites from MIR with a count per")
    strs_push(l, "call — `at-most-once`, or `unknown` inside a loop, never a number the compiler does not know")
    strs_push(l, "(`explain_cost_reports_each_site_with_a_count_per_call`). Not a byte count and not a measurement.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N50 (2026-10-02)** · a function value is a counted closure object; what it captured is released")
    strs_push(l, "when its last reference goes, on a normal exit, a `return`, a loop's next iteration and a failure")
    strs_push(l, "inside the closure's own code (`a_failure_inside_a_closure_reclaims_its_captures_and_its_callers`,")
    strs_push(l, "`an_early_return_and_a_loop_release_the_closures_they_made`). The memory report counts closure")
    strs_push(l, "objects as a fourth class, in the interpreter and in both backends' runtime alike.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*This row was \"Ownership and resource semantics — MISSING\" until N7 (2026-09-22), and")
    strs_push(l, "PARTIAL between N7 and N8 (the same day). The paragraph it used to carry is kept below,")
    strs_push(l, "because what it said was true and the numbers in it are what the work was measured against.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Read the status carefully.** VERIFIED here means: **every heap-backed type the language")
    strs_push(l, "currently has is reclaimed, in both compiler implementations and in the reference")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter, and that is tested rather than asserted.** It does **not** mean whole-language")
    strs_push(l, "leak freedom, and it says nothing about types that do not exist.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N9, 2026-09-23, extended the type universe and the claim with it.* Records are covered:")
    strs_push(l, "a record owns exactly what its fields own, recursively, and copy, destroy, cleanup and")
    strs_push(l, "task safety are all **derived** rather than declared. The cycle argument survives because")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/spec.md`'s *Cycles* was satisfied the first way it offered — the type system refuses")
    strs_push(l, "containment cycles (`N0336`), because a record holds its fields by value and a cycle has")
    strs_push(l, "no finite layout.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N10, 2026-09-23, extended it to variants.* An enum owns exactly what its **active**")
    strs_push(l, "variant's payload owns: copy, destroy and cleanup dispatch on the discriminant in the")
    strs_push(l, "emitted program, and an inactive variant is ownership-inert. A payload is held inline like")
    strs_push(l, "a field, so the same refusal (`N0336`) covers a containment cycle through a variant, across")
    strs_push(l, "modules too.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N11, 2026-09-23, extended it to generics and `Vec[T]`.* An applied record or enum owns")
    strs_push(l, "exactly what its substituted fields own; a `Vec[T]` is a reference-counted handle whose")
    strs_push(l, "elements are copied in by `vec_push` and `vec_set`, copied out by `vec_get`, transferred")
    strs_push(l, "out by `vec_pop`, and released by `T`'s law when the last reference dies. A `Vec` is the")
    strs_push(l, "first way a definition can reach itself with a finite layout, so the argument needed its")
    strs_push(l, "second satisfaction, and got it the first way again: every definition whose values could")
    strs_push(l, "own themselves through a counted handle is refused (`N0359`), over an ownership graph that")
    strs_push(l, "keeps acyclic nesting and phantom parameters legal.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N12, 2026-09-24, needed no extension.* `Result` and `Option` are ordinary enums, so they")
    strs_push(l, "reclaim by the enum law, and `?` is a `match` with a `return`: its success payload takes its")
    strs_push(l, "own reference before the temporary `Result` is released, and its error payload is owned by")
    strs_push(l, "the returned `Result` before anything it came out of is. Every shape — `Ok` and `Err` of")
    strs_push(l, "`Int`, `Str`, a record, an enum, a `Vec` and a `Chan`; `None` and `Some` of four kinds — and")
    strs_push(l, "every way out — a half-evaluated call, a half-built record or variant, a scope with a running")
    strs_push(l, "task, three functions deep — reports `live=0` in both implementations, under allocator churn,")
    strs_push(l, "in `crates/nazm-cli/tests/propagation.rs`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · `docs/user/spec.md`'s *memory constitution* settles assignment, parameters,")
    strs_push(l, "returns, aliasing, mutation, reclamation, cross-task transfer, cycles and cost visibility")
    strs_push(l, "as four kinds of value and five rules. `docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.7 carries the audit it was")
    strs_push(l, "derived from, §7.8 the string and channel model, §7.9 the one classification cleanup")
    strs_push(l, "dispatches on. No program that was legal before changed its meaning.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Type | Storage | Status |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Int`, `Bool` | none | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Str` | a backing allocation, named by the value's third field; null for a literal or an `arg` | **VERIFIED** |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Ints`, `Strs` | a reference-counted header; a `Strs` releases every element's backing first | **VERIFIED** |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Chan` | a reference-counted header, with its ring, mutex and condition variable | **VERIFIED** |")
    strs_push(l, "| a **record** | none of its own — an inline aggregate whose fields own what they own | **VERIFIED**, composed: one generated retain and release helper per record that owns anything, and none at all for one that does not |")
    strs_push(l, "| an **enum** | none of its own — an inline discriminant and payload slots; only the active variant's payload owns anything | **VERIFIED** since N10: one generated helper pair per enum that owns anything, dispatching on the discriminant |")
    strs_push(l, "| an applied **record** or **enum** | as its definition's, with the substituted field types | **VERIFIED** since N11: its own helpers, generated from the substituted fields |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Vec[T]` | the sequence header an `Ints` has, holding elements of `T`'s layout | **VERIFIED** since N11: one release helper per owning element type, releasing each element before the storage; a `Vec` of non-owning elements is released as an `Ints` is |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N68, 2026-10-02: layout specialisation — VERIFIED for one layout, opt-in.* `architecture.md`")
    strs_push(l, "§7.70 and research register R4 (with its prior art) first. `--layout soa` stores a `Vec[R]` of a")
    strs_push(l, "record of `Int`s and `Bool`s one array per field (`nz.soa_grow`; runtime ABI 10). Evidence,")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/layout.rs` (6): the same answers and the same `N0405` failures as the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter and the element-by-element layout at `-O0` and `-O2`, through growth past 1,000")
    strs_push(l, "elements, set, pop, get; reordered fields giving identical code; the differing unit recompiled")
    strs_push(l, "for the other layout and every unit reused for the same; an owning element staying whole with")
    strs_push(l, "its reason; refusals. Measured (`performance.md`, N68): a one-field scan of 1,000,000 eight-field")
    strs_push(l, "records 2.8× faster than element by element and equal to hand-written per-field `Ints`; reading")
    strs_push(l, "all eight fields 2× slower. **Limitation**: opt-in, every eligible type at once; no cost model,")
    strs_push(l, "no owning elements, no enums, no hybrid blocking; LLVM only.")
    strs_push(l, "| a `spawn`'s argument block, a file path's terminated copy | runtime-internal | **VERIFIED** — freed since N8; each was one `malloc` per operation before |")
    strs_push(l, "| a literal's constant, the process's `argv` | not this program's | **not reclaimed, correctly.** Nothing allocated them and nothing may free them |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**How.** Reference counting, which `docs/user/spec.md` deliberately does **not** make the law —")
    strs_push(l, "the rule is that storage stays valid while a reference exists, and an arena, an interning")
    strs_push(l, "pass or an escape analysis would satisfy it. The count is non-atomic on a sequence because")
    strs_push(l, "`N0321` refuses to let one cross into a task, and atomic on a string backing and a channel")
    strs_push(l, "because both do cross. Cleanup is on the three exit edges of a generated function — the")
    strs_push(l, "tail, each `return`, and the shared unwind block a failure takes — with parameter slots")
    strs_push(l, "excluded, which *is* rule 2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Tested.** 68 cases in `crates/nazm-cli/tests/memory.rs`, each run twice and each requiring")
    strs_push(l, "the interpreter and the compiled program to agree on the value **and** on what they")
    strs_push(l, "allocated and reclaimed, by class: slices outliving their buffers, slices of slices, empty")
    strs_push(l, "strings, borrowed strings returned on both edges, strings stored in and read out of")
    strs_push(l, "sequences, a string read out of a **temporary** sequence, self-assignment of an element,")
    strs_push(l, "embedded NUL bytes, a process argument, the failure path, channel scaling, a returned")
    strs_push(l, "channel, blocked senders and receivers woken by a close, a task that fails while holding a")
    strs_push(l, "channel, and a string and a channel crossing into two tasks at once.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*The 27 record cases added by N9* cover: a scalar record allocating nothing, a heap-string")
    strs_push(l, "field, a sliced-string field, `Ints` and `Strs` and `Chan` fields, a nested owning record,")
    strs_push(l, "a copy taking one reference per owning field, whole-record replacement including")
    strs_push(l, "self-assignment, field replacement including one backed by the same allocation, tail and")
    strs_push(l, "explicit return, a projection out of a temporary, a failed constructor at one and two")
    strs_push(l, "levels, a failing replacement expression, a task-safe record crossing into two siblings, a")
    strs_push(l, "record built in one branch of an `if`, four hundred short-lived records against a constant")
    strs_push(l, "live set, and three cases where a failure leaves while a temporary is still in hand.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*The 14 enum cases added by N10* cover: an inactive owning variant owning nothing, a")
    strs_push(l, "zero-payload variant beside owning ones, a copy retaining the active payload once, a")
    strs_push(l, "payload returned out of an arm (and still valid after the allocator reused the block), a")
    strs_push(l, "discarded payload, replacement across variants, a failed payload initialiser, a failure")
    strs_push(l, "inside an arm, a matched sequence handle, a constant live set of short-lived enums, an enum")
    strs_push(l, "inside a record and a record inside an enum, a nested enum, and an enum crossing into two")
    strs_push(l, "tasks. The Nazm-written compiler is held to the same counts by four enum programs in")
    strs_push(l, "`the_nazm_written_compiler_emits_the_same_memory_semantics`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*The 12 generic cases added by N11* cover: `Vec[Int]` under the `Ints` law, `Vec[Str]`")
    strs_push(l, "owning each string, a record read out of a `Vec` surviving its slot being overwritten, a")
    strs_push(l, "`Vec` of enums releasing only each element's active payload, a nested `Vec` releasing each")
    strs_push(l, "inner vector and what it holds, a `Vec[Chan]` holding a reference to each channel, a `Vec`")
    strs_push(l, "returned by tail and by `return`, a generic function returning each kind of value by its own")
    strs_push(l, "law, a generic record releasing each field by its substituted type, an element replaced by a")
    strs_push(l, "copy of itself surviving the allocator, a failed `Vec` operation giving back what the frame")
    strs_push(l, "held, and many short-lived vectors keeping a constant live set. The Nazm-written compiler is")
    strs_push(l, "held to the same counts by five generic programs in the same test.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Two of those were written because a mutation survived**, and the pair is the lesson.")
    strs_push(l, "Removing `strs_get`'s own reference broke nothing the suite could see, because a binding")
    strs_push(l, "retains what it stores whether or not the built-in already did — the shape that finds it is")
    strs_push(l, "a sequence with **no** binding. And releasing a replaced field before taking the new value")
    strs_push(l, "broke nothing the *counters* could see, because both orders end with the same two numbers —")
    strs_push(l, "the shape that finds it is `h.name = h.name` followed by enough small allocations that the")
    strs_push(l, "block the wrong order freed is handed back out, after which the program stops with a")
    strs_push(l, "signal. A compensating mechanism makes a defect invisible without making it absent, and")
    strs_push(l, "the compensation is sometimes the allocator.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Measured, N11** (contained, Linux aarch64). 5,000 / 20,000 / 80,000 short-lived `Vec[Str]`,")
    strs_push(l, "`Vec[Row]`, `Vec[Tok]` and `Vec[Vec[Str]]` against a constant live set all peak at **1.17 MiB**,")
    strs_push(l, "the empty program's floor, with nothing live at exit. `Vec[Int]` and `Vec[Str]` cost what")
    strs_push(l, "`Ints` and `Strs` cost. `performance.md` has the rows, and the enum-in-a-`Vec` pressure: 48")
    strs_push(l, "bytes a token against 40 for parallel arrays, +18% peak.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Measured, N9.** 80,000 short-lived two-string records against a constant live set:")
    strs_push(l, "**1.72 MiB**, against 1.73 MiB for the same two strings without a record, and 1.69 MiB for")
    strs_push(l, "an empty program. The N8 controls are unmoved — 80,000 temporary strings 1.77 MiB, 80,000")
    strs_push(l, "short-lived sequences 1.78 MiB, 2,000 short-lived channels 1.75 MiB. In time, at `-O2`, a")
    strs_push(l, "record is **not measurable**: three million two-field constructions and reads take 34 ms")
    strs_push(l, "against 34 ms for the same two integers through bindings, and a million record copies with")
    strs_push(l, "an owning field take 54 ms against 55 ms for copying that field directly. `performance.md`")
    strs_push(l, "carries the `-O0` figures, where the helpers are real calls, and the executable-size delta")
    strs_push(l, "(**+96 bytes** for a record that owns something, zero for one that does not).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Measured, N8.** 5,000 / 20,000 / 80,000 temporary heap strings against a constant live set:")
    strs_push(l, "1.88 / 2.33 / 4.17 MiB → **1.73 / 1.77 / 1.77 MiB**. The accumulator shape from the")
    strs_push(l, "2026-09-21 incident, at 8,000 iterations: 70.66 MiB → **2.23 MiB**. 2,000 short-lived")
    strs_push(l, "channels: 2.38 MiB → **1.80 MiB**. Sequences, a genuinely live 2,000,000-element sequence")
    strs_push(l, "and a sieve are unchanged, which is the control. `performance.md` has the runtime cost:")
    strs_push(l, "about 13–16 ns per string operation, and nothing measurable anywhere else.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Self-hosted parity — VERIFIED**, records included. `compiler/emit.nz` emits the same model. Its runtime")
    strs_push(l, "text is **derived** from `crates/nazm-runtime/src/core.rs` rather than transcribed, and")
    strs_push(l, "`cargo xtask check`'s `runtime parity` gate re-derives it and refuses a difference; its")
    strs_push(l, "*decisions* are held by `the_nazm_written_compiler_emits_the_same_memory_semantics`, which")
    strs_push(l, "builds eight programs with both compilers and requires the same reclamation report from")
    strs_push(l, "each. Between N7 and N8 the two disagreed for a whole milestone and every behavioural test")
    strs_push(l, "passed throughout, which is what the gate exists to prevent.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Completion is part of it since N10.1.** A `break`, `continue` or `return` inside a value")
    strs_push(l, "position — an argument, an operand, an initialiser, a condition, a scrutinee, an arm, the")
    strs_push(l, "operand of `return` — produces no value on that path in either compiler, and")
    strs_push(l, "`a_transfer_in_a_value_position_is_never_a_value` holds it: 32 programs in")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/transfers/`, each run by the interpreter, the reference backend, and")
    strs_push(l, "the Nazm-written compiler compiled **and** interpreted, whose IR must be byte-identical,")
    strs_push(l, "against a value written by hand and a reclamation report that must match and be zero live.")
    strs_push(l, "Before it the compiler written in Nazm passed `void` operands for the shape")
    strs_push(l, "`pick(int_to_str(i), if i == 1 { continue; } else { i })` and failed inside itself for a")
    strs_push(l, "construct whose branches all left. `architecture.md` §7.11 has the mechanism.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**And one leak the reference shared.** `==` on two strings never gave its operands back, in")
    strs_push(l, "both native backends, with no transfer involved — `int_to_str(i) == \"5\"` allocated a string")
    strs_push(l, "per evaluation and reclaimed none. The interpreter was right. Fixed in both, held by")
    strs_push(l, "`a_string_comparison_gives_back_its_operands`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**And for refused programs, since N10.2.** The Nazm checker's completion is the")
    strs_push(l, "reference's three states — a value, no value, never finishing — so a value position given")
    strs_push(l, "nothing is `N0300`, an `if` whose branches disagree is `N0302`, and a body or a `return` is")
    strs_push(l, "held to its signature. `the_nazm_checker_agrees_with_the_reference_on_what_produces_a_value`")
    strs_push(l, "compares **code and span** with the reference over 40 programs in")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/refusals/`, with the Nazm checker both compiled and interpreted, and")
    strs_push(l, "requires the Nazm compiler to refuse each one before emission; one more pair crosses a")
    strs_push(l, "module boundary with two records laid out alike. What is claimed is diagnostic *codes and")
    strs_push(l, "primary spans*, not message text, and not the diagnostics that follow an earlier error in")
    strs_push(l, "the same expression, where the two checkers recover differently (`bootstrap.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not claimed.** Whole-language leak freedom as a permanent property; anything about a")
    strs_push(l, "kind of value the language does not have — a weak reference, a closure, a trait object;")
    strs_push(l, "deadlock freedom; user-visible destruction, RAII or any ordering a program can")
    strs_push(l, "observe; a clean sanitizer run. `exit_with` reclaims nothing and reports nothing, which is")
    strs_push(l, "correct and is tested so nobody later treats it as a bug.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation, in the words this row carried before N7** · *\"Compiled programs allocate and")
    strs_push(l, "never release: `@free` appears zero times in [the Rust emitter, `emit.rs`, retired by N105] and zero times")
    strs_push(l, "in `compiler/emit.nz`, against 11 `@malloc` and 2 `@realloc` sites in each.\"* Both halves")
    strs_push(l, "are false now, and the second was still true between N7 and N8. **Whole-language leak")
    strs_push(l, "freedom is still NOT VERIFIED and is still not claimed** — the sentence above about types")
    strs_push(l, "that do not exist is the reason, and it is not a formality.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · None for the current type universe. *Until N11 this named a generic")
    strs_push(l, "container, which would make a cycle expressible again; N11 added one and refused the cycles")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0359`).* The next value kind that could form a cycle — a closure capturing its own")
    strs_push(l, "handle, a weak or shared reference — has to satisfy `docs/user/spec.md`'s *Cycles* a third time.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · A compiled program's peak RSS is bounded by live data rather than by")
    strs_push(l, "total allocation, demonstrated on the self-hosting compiler compiling itself. **Met since")
    strs_push(l, "N8**, and unmoved by N9: contained on Linux aarch64, the compiler written in Nazm compiling")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/emit.nz` peaks at 32.75 MiB against a 3,756-line input, and 80,000 short-lived")
    strs_push(l, "records with heap fields peak at the empty-program floor.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 5. Effects — VERIFIED as scoped (N107)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N107, 2026-10-05: the scope audited (`audit-n107.md`, `architecture.md` §7.108).* The scope is the compiler-owned effects (three; `spec.md` *Effects*), inferred and checked, with declared sets as contracts and purity assertable. Handlers and user-defined effects are algebraic effects, a control mechanism; who may act is capabilities' (area 6), so neither is required. **Pure is not total:** a pure function may diverge; whether divergence is an effect stays an open question (`research-register.md`), and nothing relies on the answer.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N36, 2026-09-30: Typed Effects v1 — VERIFIED; Effect propagation v1 — VERIFIED; Effect-bearing")
    strs_push(l, "interfaces v1 — VERIFIED; Purity checking v1 — VERIFIED. The row is PARTIAL: handlers, effect")
    strs_push(l, "polymorphism, user-defined effects and divergence are not here.* Two compiler-owned effects,")
    strs_push(l, "`io` (the eight outside-world built-ins) and `spawn` (a `spawn` statement), each with a stable id")
    strs_push(l, "and classified by the built-in's identity in an exhaustive `match` (`crates/nazm-sema/src/")
    strs_push(l, "effect.rs`); sets are a bit per id, canonical by construction. A function may declare `! { … }`;")
    strs_push(l, "every function's effects are inferred from its resolved calls to the least fixed point over the")
    strs_push(l, "module, cycles included, with a shortest witness (`crates/nazm-core/src/effects.rs`); a declared")
    strs_push(l, "set is a contract (`N0366`), and unknown or repeated names are `N0367` and `N0368`. Across modules")
    strs_push(l, "only the declared set travels, in `nazm.interface/6`; an undeclared import is every effect to its")
    strs_push(l, "importer. `SEMANTIC_EPOCH` 8. Tools: signatures, hover, `nazm.context/2`, `nazm.snapshot/2`,")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.delta/2` (`architecture.md` §7.38, `spec.md` *Effects*). Evidence: `crates/nazm-core/tests/")
    strs_push(l, "effects.rs` — ordinary computation (records, enums, generics, equality, sequences, channels,")
    strs_push(l, "loops, `Result` and `?`) pure and assertable; each of the eight built-ins refused in a pure")
    strs_push(l, "function; a `spawn` and its task's effects; order and repetition changing nothing, a wider")
    strs_push(l, "contract allowed and read by callers; a purity assertion failing through four calls with the")
    strs_push(l, "shortest witness; direct, mutual and generic recursion at the least fixed point, in any order;")
    strs_push(l, "unknown and repeated names refused once with no cascade and an exact fix; the effect namespace;")
    strs_push(l, "a broken body adding nothing; determinism and the recorded witness; a 2,000-long chain, a")
    strs_push(l, "300-wide fan-out and a 500-long cycle settled in one test; nothing changing what runs.")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-iface/tests/persistence.rs` — a declared set published by name in id order, absent")
    strs_push(l, "for none, read back exactly, malformed ones refused, `/5` refused. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/")
    strs_push(l, "incremental.rs` — an effect-only change rechecking the importer and finding what it breaks, a")
    strs_push(l, "body change within its contract reaching nobody, an undeclared import every effect to a pure")
    strs_push(l, "caller, the cached interface carrying the declared set. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/effects.rs` — the")
    strs_push(l, "same IR with and without declarations, and every `examples/effects/` program agreeing interpreted")
    strs_push(l, "and compiled. `crates/nazm-service/tests/context.rs`, `snapshot.rs` and `effects.rs` — packet")
    strs_push(l, "effects with reasons, an effect-only change as its own snapshot section, and every program of the")
    strs_push(l, "tree still checking. Seventeen N36 mutations (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · Three effects only (`io`, `spawn`, `foreign`), and a function that declares nothing is, to another module,")
    strs_push(l, "every effect — so in the multi-module compiler sources 152 of 1,044 function checks come out")
    strs_push(l, "`{ io, spawn }`, most because they call an undeclared import, not because they print or spawn.")
    strs_push(l, "Pure means *no effect*, not *referentially transparent*: a function may write into a sequence it")
    strs_push(l, "was handed. Effect polymorphism is one effect parameter per function (N51), which the")
    strs_push(l, "higher-order library uses; no handlers and no user-defined effects; allocation, channels, traps")
    strs_push(l, "and divergence are not effects. The compiler written in Nazm reads effect sets and checks a")
    strs_push(l, "function value's against the expected type's (N102). Effects are not authority: since N37 that is area 6, checked apart. Typed diagnostic facts (`nazm.diagnostic-detail/1`)")
    strs_push(l, "stay unavailable; the effect facts are in the packet.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · Handlers; more than one effect parameter, and effect subtyping, when a")
    strs_push(l, "program needs them. Authority is area 6.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N51, 2026-10-02: Effect polymorphism v1 — VERIFIED.* One effect parameter per function")
    strs_push(l, "(`effects E`), opaque in the body, bound at each call from the function-typed arguments, the")
    strs_push(l, "callee's declared set performed with it replaced; through a wrapper (`@std/seq`), a module and its")
    strs_push(l, "cached interface, and visible to profiles. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/effect_params.rs`, interpreter")
    strs_push(l, "and both backends; `N0388`, `N0389`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N79, 2026-10-03: Effect subsumption v1 — VERIFIED.* Where a function value is passed, spawned")
    strs_push(l, "with or returned, one whose effects are a subset of the expected type's is accepted; parameters and")
    strs_push(l, "results stay invariant, an effect parameter matches only by binding, and nothing converts inside")
    strs_push(l, "another type (`architecture.md` §7.80, `spec.md` *Function values*). The checker's one relation is")
    strs_push(l, "`assignable` (`crates/nazm-core/src/check/call.rs`); below it, Core IR's verifier compares results up to")
    strs_push(l, "effects as it already compared arguments, so the interpreter and both native backends run a")
    strs_push(l, "subsumed value unchanged. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/authority.rs` —")
    strs_push(l, "`a_function_value_with_fewer_effects_is_accepted_passed_or_returned` (interpreter and Cranelift),")
    strs_push(l, "`a_function_value_with_more_effects_is_refused` (passed and returned, `N0300`). The row stays")
    strs_push(l, "PARTIAL for handlers, user-defined effects and divergence.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N50, 2026-10-02.* A function type carries an effect set; a call through a function value performs")
    strs_push(l, "it, a closure's body is checked against its own set (`! {}` unwritten), and an undeclared function")
    strs_push(l, "used as a value is held to the none its value's type assumed (`N0366`). A closure's authority is")
    strs_push(l, "its own capability parameters (`N0369`). `a_function_value_carries_its_effects_and_takes_its_authority_as_parameters`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Before N36 this row was MISSING. N12 did not change it.* A function's error type is visible because it is inside its")
    strs_push(l, "return type, `Result[T, E]`; a caller may store, pass or ignore that value, and nothing about")
    strs_push(l, "it is tracked as an effect.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence of absence** · No effect row, annotation, inference or purity analysis. The")
    strs_push(l, "only occurrences of the word in the language crates are the English phrase \"evaluated for")
    strs_push(l, "its effects\" and `crates/nazm-lir/src/lib.rs`'s statement that there are *\"no effects to")
    strs_push(l, "track\"* — given as a reason there is one IR level rather than eight.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · The blocking question is open and named: **is divergence an effect?**")
    strs_push(l, "Without an answer, \"drop an unused pure call\" is unsound, so the optimiser cannot be given")
    strs_push(l, "that transformation at all. `docs/user/spec.md` *Open* carries it, along with whether allocation")
    strs_push(l, "failure and panic are effects.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · An answer to whether divergence is an effect. *Until R1 this named a typed core IR to carry a row on a function type: Core IR (N39) and effect-carrying function types (N50) met it.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · A function's row is inferred, checked, and a compile-fail test shows an")
    strs_push(l, "effectful call refused where a pure one is accepted.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 6. Capabilities, as a language feature — VERIFIED as scoped (N107: static, coarse, shareable)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N107, 2026-10-05: the scope audited (`audit-n107.md`, `architecture.md` §7.108).* The promise is the static one the checker keeps: no authority without being handed it, `main` the only root, `OutCap` narrower than `IoCap`. Runtime enforcement, revocation, finer kinds and linear capabilities are not required — finer authority is a library built from today's kinds — and the row's name now says the scope.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N104, 2026-10-05: no inherited authority — VERIFIED.* `architecture.md` §7.105 first. The")
    strs_push(l, "bridge's authority half is removed: every body, declared or not, holds what it exercises")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0369` otherwise), a call needs nothing of its caller, and `main`'s parameters are the only")
    strs_push(l, "root. `Resolution::inherits` and `nazm inspect`'s `inherits` are gone (`nazm.inspect/2`); the")
    strs_push(l, "`explicit-authority` rule can no longer fire. Every program in the repository was migrated — eleven")
    strs_push(l, "`.nz` programs and examples, the compiler written in Nazm (30 of its functions take an `IoCap`,")
    strs_push(l, "none a `SpawnCap`), and the programs inside the tests — by threading from `main` the capabilities")
    strs_push(l, "each function's own body uses. The migration found two N79 defects in attenuation, both fixed and")
    strs_push(l, "held by `authority::an_io_cap_given_for_an_out_cap_compiles_on_both_backends`: an `IoCap` handed")
    strs_push(l, "for an `OutCap` failed MIR validation (`N0900`), because MIR's copy of the shape relation had no")
    strs_push(l, "capability rule; and a generic function could not be handed one (`N0300`), because a generic")
    strs_push(l, "call compared its concrete parameters exactly. The compiler written in Nazm also checks it: `N0369` at the")
    strs_push(l, "reference's spans (six new agreement cases). Semantic epoch 29. Nine catalogue entries that")
    strs_push(l, "attacked the bridge are retired, three repointed, six added. **Stays PARTIAL** for the reasons")
    strs_push(l, "below: static only, coarse, shareable.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N79, 2026-10-03: Inherited authority as a recorded contract v1 — VERIFIED; Strict authority by")
    strs_push(l, "profile v1 — VERIFIED; Attenuation by a narrower kind v1 — VERIFIED; Revocation — declared outside")
    strs_push(l, "the model.* The checker computes each function's **inherited authority** — the kinds its body")
    strs_push(l, "exercises without holding them — by the rule that checks a declared function, and records it in")
    strs_push(l, "the resolution (`Resolution::inherits`, `crates/nazm-core/src/effects.rs`); `nazm inspect` shows it")
    strs_push(l, "as each definition's `inherits`. The `authority` profile's `explicit-authority` rule refuses every")
    strs_push(l, "function of the program's own modules that inherits, by name and kind (`N0510`). `OutCap` (id 6)")
    strs_push(l, "authorises `print` and `eprint` only; an `IoCap` implies it and is accepted where one is expected,")
    strs_push(l, "never the reverse, and `main` may take one as a root (`crates/nazm-sema/src/capability.rs`,")
    strs_push(l, "`CapabilitySet::implied`). Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/authority.rs` — an `OutCap` printing and")
    strs_push(l, "refused a file read, a write and an existence check (`N0369`); `IoCap` for `OutCap` accepted and the")
    strs_push(l, "reverse refused, as argument and result; `main(o: OutCap)` interpreted and native; `OutCap` not")
    strs_push(l, "redefinable (`N0331`); the recorded `inherits` of undeclared, pure and declared functions; the")
    strs_push(l, "profile refusing inheritance and accepting held authority and pure undeclared code; the profile")
    strs_push(l, "report naming the rule. **Still PARTIAL**, for one reason: by default an undeclared function still")
    strs_push(l, "inherits its caller's authority — the corpus and the compiler written in Nazm rely on it, and")
    strs_push(l, "migrating both is named work. The interface stays `nazm.interface/8`: inherited authority depends")
    strs_push(l, "on bodies, and an interface publishes declarations; a declared export inherits nothing, and an")
    strs_push(l, "undeclared import is already every effect to its importer (§7.80, as built).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N51 (2026-10-02)** · a closure holds the capabilities visible where it is written, as captured,")
    strs_push(l, "and its type states what it does with them (`a_closure_holds_the_capabilities_it_captures`);")
    strs_push(l, "making a value of an undeclared function needs the authority its type's effects need, so declared")
    strs_push(l, "code cannot reach the N37 bridge through a value")
    strs_push(l, "(`a_value_of_an_undeclared_import_needs_the_authority_a_call_would`). Attenuated capabilities and")
    strs_push(l, "revocation: **DESIGNED**, deferred (`architecture.md` §7.53 states the missing use case and the")
    strs_push(l, "runtime cost). The trust root is unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N37, 2026-09-30: Compiler-owned capability kinds v1 — VERIFIED; Explicit authority passing v1 —")
    strs_push(l, "VERIFIED; Effect-capability checking v1 — VERIFIED; Cross-module authority contracts v1 —")
    strs_push(l, "VERIFIED; Capability unforgeability v1 — VERIFIED. Attenuation, resource-specific authority,")
    strs_push(l, "revocation, linearity and runtime enforcement are not here.* Two compiler-owned kinds with stable")
    strs_push(l, "ids, `IoCap` and `SpawnCap` — three since N42 added `ForeignCap`, whose call-site check has no")
    strs_push(l, "compatibility bridge (area 17) — as built-in types (`crates/nazm-sema/src/capability.rs`); each")
    strs_push(l, "built-in's required authority is an exhaustive table on its identity. A function that declares an")
    strs_push(l, "effect set holds exactly the capability values its scope reaches — lexically, recorded per call")
    strs_push(l, "site by the checker — and every built-in, `spawn` and call of an undeclared function needs the")
    strs_push(l, "authority for what it does, or it is `N0369`, reported apart from and before an effect's `N0366`")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-core/src/effects.rs`). Nothing constructs a capability (`N0370`); `main` is the root")
    strs_push(l, "and takes only capabilities (`N0371`), which the interpreter and the native entry hand it. Authority")
    strs_push(l, "crosses a module as ordinary parameter types in `nazm.interface/6` (`architecture.md` §7.39,")
    strs_push(l, "`spec.md` *Capabilities*). Evidence: `crates/nazm-core/tests/capabilities.rs` — passing through")
    strs_push(l, "helpers, recursion and mutual recursion, storage in a record, a `Vec` and a variant, a pure function")
    strs_push(l, "carrying one; every outside-world built-in refused without authority and accepted with it; effect")
    strs_push(l, "versus authority errors apart and in order; spawn needing a `SpawnCap`, and a task's authority only")
    strs_push(l, "what it is handed; the witness through undeclared functions; shadowing, records, type parameters,")
    strs_push(l, "block scope, the wrong kind and a missing argument; construction and redefinition refused, no")
    strs_push(l, "equality; `main`'s roots. `crates/nazm-core/tests/effects.rs` — N36's laws unchanged with")
    strs_push(l, "capabilities held. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/incremental.rs` — a capability-only change, including a")
    strs_push(l, "kind swap under one name, rechecking the importer; an undeclared import needing every authority;")
    strs_push(l, "the cached interface carrying `IoCap`. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/capabilities.rs` — a capability")
    strs_push(l, "parameter lowering to exactly an `Int` one's IR, the entry passing one word per root, a non-capability")
    strs_push(l, "`main` refused before building, and `examples/capabilities/` agreeing interpreted and compiled.")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-service/tests/capabilities.rs` and `snapshot.rs` — hover, completion (a type, never a")
    strs_push(l, "constructor), semantic tokens, and a capability-only change as a `shape` change under the same")
    strs_push(l, "identity. Twenty N37 mutations (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · **Static only**: a capability erases to a word nothing reads, and nothing at runtime")
    strs_push(l, "enforces authority — there is no sandbox, broker or operating-system boundary, and a Nazm program can")
    strs_push(l, "affect its machine as much as the process running it. **Coarse**: one `IoCap` authorises every file,")
    strs_push(l, "both standard streams, the arguments and exit; nothing is least-privilege, and there is no")
    strs_push(l, "attenuation beyond `OutCap` (N79) because there is no other narrower kind to derive. **Shareable**: capabilities copy freely,")
    strs_push(l, "with no linearity and no revocation. **No bridge since N104.** Possession is lexical, not use: the built-ins")
    strs_push(l, "do not take the capability as an argument.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Do not confuse this with `nazm capabilities`.** `schema/nazm.capabilities-1.json` is a")
    strs_push(l, "*toolchain descriptor* — what one build of the compiler supports. It is unrelated to")
    strs_push(l, "object capabilities or capability-safety, and it is VERIFIED under area 22.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · For finer attenuation, a")
    strs_push(l, "resource-parametrised kind; for linearity, move semantics;")
    strs_push(l, "for enforcement beyond the checker, a runtime or operating-system boundary; for foreign code, FFI.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Before N37 this row was MISSING.* **Evidence of absence, then** · Authority was **ambient and")
    strs_push(l, "labelled as such**: `crates/nazm-sema/src/intrinsic.rs` said *\"These are callable from anywhere, and")
    strs_push(l, "nothing in the language restricts which functions may reach the file system or the process")
    strs_push(l, "arguments. That is a real limitation, not a design.\"* `fn main(io: IO)` had been written down as the")
    strs_push(l, "plan of record and then not adopted. N37 adopted a capability parameter on `main`, for the reason")
    strs_push(l, "`spec.md` now states: it is the only place a value can come from that no expression produced.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · A function without the authority cannot reach the filesystem, and the refusal is")
    strs_push(l, "a compile error with a span — met for every function that declares its effects, and not for an")
    strs_push(l, "ambient one, which is the bridge above.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 7. Provenance and information flow, as a language feature — VERIFIED as scoped (N107: explicit data flow)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N107, 2026-10-05: the scope audited (`audit-n107.md`, `architecture.md` §7.108).* The promise is explicit data flow: a `Secret` that reaches an output through data is refused, by cell, target and field, through calls, values, bounds and channels. Implicit flow — non-interference — was never claimed and is RESEARCH (`research-register.md` R6); labels a program writes and per-handle precision would only refine it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N80, 2026-10-03: Container cells v1 — VERIFIED; Indirect targets v1 — VERIFIED; Local field and")
    strs_push(l, "variant shapes v1 — VERIFIED; Flow policy engine v1 — VERIFIED; Origin-to-sink traces v1 —")
    strs_push(l, "VERIFIED.* `architecture.md` §7.81 is the constitution, `spec.md` *Containers* and *Calls through")
    strs_push(l, "values and bounds* the law. Every container is read and written through a **cell** named by its")
    strs_push(l, "type, so a read carries what any container of that type was given — exhaustively, by the built-in's")
    strs_push(l, "identity (`Origin::container`, `crates/nazm-sema/src/provenance.rs`) — and generic code is every")
    strs_push(l, "cell; a receive and a select move a channel's cell, and a select's index carries nothing. A call")
    strs_push(l, "through a function value reaches every function value of its type up to effects, a call through a")
    strs_push(l, "bound every impl of its method; a closure's parameters and captures are received like any")
    strs_push(l, "parameter. Within a body a record or variant keeps its fields apart. `N0372` and the profile flow")
    strs_push(l, "rules are one engine (`FlowRule`), and `cyber` gains `checked-paths`, the language's rule in every")
    strs_push(l, "function. Each sink carries one chain per origin, printed by `nazm explain-flow` as `nazm.flow/2`.")
    strs_push(l, "Facts persist in `nazm.check/4`; epoch 24. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/flow_v3.rs` — eleven")
    strs_push(l, "end-to-end tests, each in both directions, covering every container form, receive and select,")
    strs_push(l, "generic code, named values and closures and a pure value standing for an effectful one,")
    strs_push(l, "parameters and captures, fields, variants, a field write and `?`, bounds, an export to C,")
    strs_push(l, "`checked-paths`, the trace and its determinism, and an affected program run interpreted and natively;")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-core/tests/provenance.rs` (containers by type, fields, the trace through a cell);")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/incremental.rs` — a cell and a function value from a module the cache reused;")
    strs_push(l, "`closures.rs`, `cost_and_flow.rs`, `profiles.rs`. **Falsifier, run:** `nazm check` of N79 and N80")
    strs_push(l, "over all 237 `.nz` files in the repository gave identical codes on every one — no new refusal and no")
    strs_push(l, "other change (`architecture.md` §7.81, as built). **Still PARTIAL**, for named reasons: implicit")
    strs_push(l, "flow is not tracked, so this is not non-interference; precision is by type, not by handle, index")
    strs_push(l, "or across a call; there are no labels a program writes. Cost: `nazm check` of `compiler/emit.nz`")
    strs_push(l, "1.125× (`performance.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N52 (2026-10-02)** · a sink registry (`SinkClass`: `path`, `output`, `file-data`, and `vouch`")
    strs_push(l, "for the evidence of a declassification), each solved through helpers' parameters, closures and")
    strs_push(l, "modules with the origins that reach it (`every_sink_class_is_solved_through_helpers_closures_and_containers`);")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm explain-flow` prints them as `nazm.flow/1`. Declassification is `str_vouch` under a")
    strs_push(l, "`VouchCap` held anywhere, recorded with the origins it cleared")
    strs_push(l, "(`a_vouch_needs_its_authority_everywhere_and_is_recorded`). Profiles: `cyber`'s")
    strs_push(l, "`contents-stay-in-files`, `critical`'s `no-declassification`. Containers remain whole-container")
    strs_push(l, "conservative, stated. A 2,000-function chain solves deterministically within a deadline")
    strs_push(l, "(`a_long_call_chain_is_solved_deterministically_and_in_bounded_time`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N50 (2026-10-02)** · a closure's body is reduced to flows as a function of its own; its")
    strs_push(l, "parameters are of unknown origin, its captures carry what the captured binding carried (unknown")
    strs_push(l, "when that depended on its maker's parameters or calls), and the result of an indirect call is of")
    strs_push(l, "unknown origin — conservative, so a restricted sink reached through a function value is refused")
    strs_push(l, "(`a_path_through_a_function_value_is_of_unknown_origin`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N38, 2026-09-30: Provenance identity v1 — VERIFIED; Explicit data-flow propagation v1 — VERIFIED;")
    strs_push(l, "Function summary propagation v1 — VERIFIED; Cross-module provenance summaries v1 — VERIFIED;")
    strs_push(l, "Restricted-flow checking v1 — VERIFIED. Implicit flow, field and element precision, user labels,")
    strs_push(l, "declassification and runtime tracking are not here.* Four compiler-owned origins with stable ids —")
    strs_push(l, "`argument`, `file`, `authority`, `unknown` — entered only by the built-ins that bring data in (an")
    strs_push(l, "exhaustive table on their identity) and by `main`'s capabilities (`crates/nazm-sema/src/provenance.rs`).")
    strs_push(l, "Each module's checked bodies are reduced to flows over parameters and calls, and the whole program's")
    strs_push(l, "summaries — origins a result carries, parameters passed on, parameters reaching a sink, and what each")
    strs_push(l, "parameter is handed — are solved by worklist to the least fixed point on every run")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-core/src/provenance.rs`). Facts cross modules in the check entry (`nazm.check/2`), by")
    strs_push(l, "durable name, so a reused module still contributes them and no conclusion is cached. One restricted")
    strs_push(l, "flow: in a function with a declared effect set, `write_file`'s path may not derive from a file's")
    strs_push(l, "contents or from shared storage the checker does not follow, directly or through any function whose")
    strs_push(l, "parameter reaches it (`N0372`, one witness chain). Tools: `nazm.context/3`, `nazm.snapshot/3`,")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.delta/3` (`architecture.md` §7.40, `spec.md` *Provenance*). Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-core/tests/provenance.rs` — the sources and that output is not input; joins through")
    strs_push(l, "operators, built-ins, records, variants, `Result`, `?` and loops, in any order; pass-through, derived")
    strs_push(l, "and constant-returning summaries (a constant is never tainted); conditions contributing nothing;")
    strs_push(l, "recursion, mutual recursion and reversed source order; shared storage and channels `unknown`;")
    strs_push(l, "authority handed through passing, records and a `spawn`; provenance adding no effect and granting no")
    strs_push(l, "authority; the restricted path refused with its witness, through declared, undeclared, nested and")
    strs_push(l, "spawned helpers, and allowed from the command line or the program; the codes' order; a 2,000-long")
    strs_push(l, "chain and a 500-long cycle settling. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/incremental.rs` — a callee's body change")
    strs_push(l, "reaching a caller the cache reused, both ways, and every module reused; a helper in another module")
    strs_push(l, "carrying the rule; an entry keeping the facts. `crates/nazm-service/tests/snapshot.rs` and")
    strs_push(l, "`context.rs` — a provenance-only change as its own section where no byte of the function moved, and")
    strs_push(l, "the packet's summary. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/provenance.rs` — `examples/provenance/` agreeing")
    strs_push(l, "interpreted and compiled, and a refused flow never built. Twenty-five N38 mutations (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · **Explicit data flow only**: a value is not tainted by the condition that chose it,")
    strs_push(l, "so this is not non-interference, and timing and every side channel are outside it. **Coarse**: records,")
    strs_push(l, "variants and `Result` are tracked whole, and every read of a sequence, `Vec` or channel is `unknown`,")
    strs_push(l, "because aliasing hides their writers — conservative, and over-restrictive for a path built in one. One")
    strs_push(l, "sink, `write_file`'s path; no user labels, sanitisers, declassification or policy. **The bridge**: a")
    strs_push(l, "function with no declared effect set is not checked itself, though explicit code cannot launder")
    strs_push(l, "through it. Authority has no restriction of its own, since types already keep it out of every output.")
    strs_push(l, "Static only: nothing is tracked at runtime. Checking `compiler/emit.nz` costs about 10 % more.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · For implicit flow, a control-dependence model; for precision, a MIR that tracks")
    strs_push(l, "places; for more sinks and declassification, a policy design; for foreign code, FFI summaries.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Before N38 this row was MISSING.* **Evidence of absence, then** · No labels, lattice, sanitizers or")
    strs_push(l, "declassification anywhere in the language crates. `architecture.md` §5 designs a lattice-valued")
    strs_push(l, "qualifier (`Untrusted`, `Secret`, `PII`) and records that an earlier draft calling provenance")
    strs_push(l, "*\"nearly free once effects exist\"* was overclaiming; N38 is not that qualifier.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · A `Secret` reaching an output is refused, with a stated and documented")
    strs_push(l, "approximation of what the analysis misses — met in kind for one origin and one sink (a file's contents")
    strs_push(l, "at `write_file`'s path), with the approximation above; `Secret`, as a label a program writes, does not")
    strs_push(l, "exist.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## IR and backend")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 8. Core IR — VERIFIED (v1)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · N39 (2026-09-30). `crates/nazm-cir` is the representation, its invariants")
    strs_push(l, "(`verify.rs`), its printed form `nazm.core-ir/3` since R3, `/2` since N78, `/1` before (`print.rs`, `nazm core-ir`) and each")
    strs_push(l, "function's digests (`digest.rs`); `crates/nazm-core/src/lower.rs` is **the one lowering** from a")
    strs_push(l, "checked program, private to `nazm-core` and reached only after checking succeeded;")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-core/src/eval/` runs Core IR and nothing else; `crates/nazm-lir/src/lower.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "lowers Core IR, and `nazm-lir` no longer depends on `nazm-syntax`. `architecture.md` §7.41 is the")
    strs_push(l, "constitution, written before the code.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Claim | Status | Evidence |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Core IR exists, and is the one checked-to-IR lowering | VERIFIED v1 | both backends consume it; `xtask/src/rules.rs` places `nazm-cir` and forbids `nazm-lir` the syntax tree; `crates/nazm-core/tests/core_ir.rs` (a rejected program never reaches a consumer) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Typed Core IR | VERIFIED | every value carries the checker's type or *never*; `cir::verify` runs on every lowering; `every_value_is_typed_by_what_the_checker_established` |")
    strs_push(l, "| Canonical semantic lowering | VERIFIED | all 205 `.nz` sources: `nazm check`, `nazm run` (value, output, memory report, status) and every one of 383 emitted LLVM IR files byte-identical before and after (`performance.md`, N39) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Control-flow normalisation | VERIFIED | explicit `LoopId` targets, explicit completion, value and statement `if` apart, `?` a `match` whose error arm returns; `every_break_and_continue_names_the_loop_it_leaves`, `a_question_mark_is_a_match_whose_error_arm_returns` |")
    strs_push(l, "| Backend-neutral semantic operations | VERIFIED | `Intrinsic` by identity, `Law` on every comparison, records, variants and fields by identity, no layout, symbol or runtime call; the `core ir boundary` gate (`cargo xtask check`, and `nothing_below_core_ir_asks_what_a_source_position_meant` in the suite) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Deterministic, durable printed form | VERIFIED | `the_printed_core_ir_is_the_same_bytes_in_every_process` (`crates/nazm-cli/tests/core_ir.rs`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Per-function digests, semantic and body | VERIFIED | the digest-law tests in `crates/nazm-core/tests/core_ir.rs`: a body change moves both, an effect change only the semantic one, a capability parameter both, provenance neither; a span, a local's name, a declaration's order, an arm's order and an unrelated definition none |")
    strs_push(l, "| Digests used as a cache key | MISSING | nothing keys on them yet; the object cache keys on emitted IR (area 10b) |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · Level 3 by responsibility, not by `architecture.md` §2's shape: a tree of")
    strs_push(l, "structured regions, not ANF. Core IR is built from each run's")
    strs_push(l, "full check and never persisted, so no reuse happens at this level. Generic bodies stay generic;")
    strs_push(l, "instantiation is the native backend's. Ownership operations are not in it — regions state what")
    strs_push(l, "they own, and a MIR would lower from that.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Introducing the level **removed** code: the evaluator's name-keyed frames and")
    strs_push(l, "per-step resolution lookups, and the native lowering's span lookups and its own `?` lowering, are")
    strs_push(l, "gone, and a mechanical gate keeps them gone.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 9. MIR — VERIFIED (v1)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · N40 (2026-10-01). `crates/nazm-mir` is the representation (`ir.rs`), **the one")
    strs_push(l, "lowering** from Core IR (`lower.rs`) with the instance planner moved into it (`instance.rs`), the")
    strs_push(l, "validator (`verify.rs`), the printed form `nazm.mir/1` (`print.rs`, `nazm mir`) and each function's")
    strs_push(l, "executable digest (`digest.rs`). `nazm build` lowers Core IR to MIR, validates it — a rejection")
    strs_push(l, "after a clean check is `N0900` — and hands the native backend MIR and nothing of the checker.")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.42 is the constitution, written before the code.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Claim | Status | Evidence |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| MIR exists, and is the one Core IR → native lowering | VERIFIED v1 | `nazm build` goes through `crates/nazm-cli/src/mir.rs::lower`; `nazm-lir` depends on `nazm-mir` and not on `nazm-cir` (`xtask/src/rules.rs`), and the core ir boundary gate refuses `Resolution` or Core IR in it |")
    strs_push(l, "| Explicit, deterministic CFG | VERIFIED | basic blocks, one terminator each; blocks, locals and temporaries numbered by a deterministic walk; `lowering_twice_gives_the_same_mir`, `the_printed_mir_is_the_same_bytes_in_every_process` |")
    strs_push(l, "| Typed MIR | VERIFIED | concrete types on every local; the validator checks every operation's operand and result types, call and primitive signatures, field and payload identities; `the_validator_refuses_a_local_of_the_wrong_type`, `…_a_call_with_the_wrong_arguments`, `…_a_primitive_with_a_bad_signature` |")
    strs_push(l, "| Cleanup obligations explicit and mechanically validated | VERIFIED | `copy`, `move`, `drop`, scope joins and failure edges are statements; an ownership dataflow refuses a use of an empty local, an overwrite of an owned one and anything still owned at `return` or `unwind`; `the_validator_refuses_a_leak_at_return`, `…_a_use_after_move`, `…_a_scope_left_without_its_join`, `…_dropping_a_parameter` |")
    strs_push(l, "| Completion, `?`, records, enums and `match` without backend re-analysis | VERIFIED | `?` is a `switch` whose error arm returns; a `switch` names each variant once, and a payload read is valid only in its arm (`the_validator_refuses_a_payload_read_outside_its_arm`, `…_a_switch_that_misses_a_variant`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Finite, typed runtime primitives | VERIFIED | `Intrinsic` by identity with its element type; scope open, spawn, join and the failure check as MIR statements |")
    strs_push(l, "| Behaviour preserved | VERIFIED | all 205 `.nz` sources before and after N40: `nazm check` and `nazm run` identical, every build diagnostic identical, and all 104 built executables' stdout, stderr, status and memory report identical (`performance.md`, N40) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Executable digest | VERIFIED | formatting, comments, local names, effect contracts and unrelated definitions leave it; an executable change and a capability parameter move it (`crates/nazm-cli/tests/mir.rs`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Digests used as a cache key | MISSING | objects are keyed on the emitted unit's bytes (area 10b), a function of MIR |")
    strs_push(l, "| The interpreter on MIR | not wanted | it stays on Core IR, by decision (§7.42): nothing it needs is below Core IR |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · Level 6 by responsibility, not by `architecture.md` §2's shape: no borrow")
    strs_push(l, "checking and no optimisation run on it, locals are mutable slots, and there are no phi nodes.")
    strs_push(l, "Every local becomes a stack slot in the emitted code, so an unoptimised build carries more")
    strs_push(l, "loads and stores than N39's (`performance.md`, N40). MIR is built per run and never persisted.")
    strs_push(l, "The ownership dataflow costs a word per 64 tracked locals per block, so a very large function")
    strs_push(l, "costs more than linearly to validate (measured, N40).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Introducing the level **removed** code: the native lowering's temporaries,")
    strs_push(l, "partial-construction slots and `?` completion rules, and the emitter's cleanup bookkeeping — its")
    strs_push(l, "`owned`, `outstanding`, `building` and `frame` sets and every per-exit release decision — are")
    strs_push(l, "gone; a validator and a mechanical gate keep the boundary.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 10. LIR and the backend contract — VERIFIED (v2, N105: one instruction-level LIR both backends translate)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N105, 2026-10-05: one LIR both backends consume — VERIFIED; LIR validator v2 — VERIFIED; LIR")
    strs_push(l, "oracle interpreter — VERIFIED for the sequential subset (tasks, channels, C and the clock refused by")
    strs_push(l, "name); `nazm.lir/2` — VERIFIED.* *v1 (Q1-B-07): the oracle formats floats and `UInt64`s")
    strs_push(l, "(`nz.format_float`, `nz.format_u64`) by the interpreter's own `nazm_sema::numeric::to_str`, so a")
    strs_push(l, "program printing a number has its oracle tier — until then it refused them by name")
    strs_push(l, "(`floats_and_unsigned_words_print_alike_on_the_oracle`, the `numbers` compatibility case).* `architecture.md` §7.106 is the constitution, written before the")
    strs_push(l, "code. `crates/nazm-lir/src/op/` is an instruction set below MIR: values of a machine class (`bit`,")
    strs_push(l, "`i8`, `i32`, `i64`, `ptr`) defined once and used where they dominate, variables, stack slots, loads")
    strs_push(l, "and stores at byte offsets, wrapping and overflow-checked arithmetic, comparisons, selects, calls")
    strs_push(l, "direct, indirect and to the runtime, copies, and source positions. `op/lower.rs`, `func.rs`,")
    strs_push(l, "`prims.rs`, `helpers.rs` and `soa.rs` lower each unit's MIR to it once, and that lowering is the")
    strs_push(l, "only place a failure's code, message and position, a guard and its order, an offset, a runtime")
    strs_push(l, "entry, or a retain or release is decided. The LLVM backend is a printer of it (`op/llvm.rs`); the")
    strs_push(l, "Cranelift backend a translator of it (`nazm-codegen-clif/src/translate.rs`), and since N105 may not")
    strs_push(l, "depend on `nazm-mir` at all (`xtask/src/rules.rs`,")
    strs_push(l, "`the_cranelift_backend_reads_lir_and_nothing_above_it`). The old per-backend lowerings are deleted:")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-lir/src/emit.rs` (4,405 lines) and Cranelift's `func.rs`, `prims.rs`, `helpers.rs`, `unit.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "and `layout.rs` (2,963). `op/validate.rs` checks every module before either backend sees it —")
    strs_push(l, "definition before use under dominance, classes, every symbol, slot, variable and block, every call")
    strs_push(l, "against its callee's signature, every return against its function's — and a broken module is")
    strs_push(l, "`N0900`; `validate::tests` breaks each rule by hand and requires it named. `op/interp.rs` executes")
    strs_push(l, "LIR against a model of the runtime's services and is `nazm lir --run`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Independent evidence** · `crates/nazm-cli/tests/lir_oracle.rs`: programs with answers worked out")
    strs_push(l, "by hand — arithmetic and both failure codes, `Int::MIN % -1`, control flow and recursion, strings and")
    strs_push(l, "sequences, records, enums and equality, closures in vectors, the program's arguments — each run on")
    strs_push(l, "the oracle, LLVM `-O0` and `-O2` and Cranelift, all four required to equal the hand-written answer")
    strs_push(l, "(and a program with tasks refused by the oracle, not answered). `crates/nazm-cli/tests/fuzz_diff.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "gains the oracle as a fifth tier beside the tree-walking interpreter (independent of LIR): the default")
    strs_push(l, "run and 300 further generated programs (seed 105105) agree on all five. The coverage fuzzer gains an")
    strs_push(l, "`lir` target (`fuzz/src/main.rs`): a checked program's LIR must validate and run without the oracle")
    strs_push(l, "finding a defect. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/layout.rs`: `--layout soa`, refused on Cranelift until N105,")
    strs_push(l, "is LIR's now and agrees on both backends. **Falsifier, run:** the host suite (2,424 tests in 196 binaries, the selfhost")
    strs_push(l, "suite refusing to run uncontained), and contained: the workspace (2,464 passed, 0 failed, 46 ignored),")
    strs_push(l, "selfhost (43 of 43), bootstrap (C2 = C3, 34 conformance cases and 29 refusals agreeing) and the `lir`")
    strs_push(l, "fuzz target (319,609 executions in 300 s, no crash); the 76")
    strs_push(l, "historical mutants on the deleted code repointed at the LIR and each caught by a named killer.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What N105 found** · Two-backend agreement is no evidence for a decision both now share. Eleven of")
    strs_push(l, "the 76 repointed mutants survived their old killers, which compared LLVM with Cranelift; each now")
    strs_push(l, "has a killer with an independent expectation (the memory suite's counts, a unit test, or a")
    strs_push(l, "hand-written answer), and three new tests exist for that reason")
    strs_push(l, "(`a_reassigned_sequence_is_released_once_when_a_failure_follows`,")
    strs_push(l, "`a_c_bool_is_zero_extended_and_an_internal_one_is_not`,")
    strs_push(l, "`a_state_field_is_found_at_its_canonical_offset_not_its_declared_one`). The Cranelift object key was")
    strs_push(l, "MIR without positions until N105 and reused an object reporting a moved failure at its old line; it")
    strs_push(l, "is now the unit's LIR digest, which carries every position, with the translator's revision.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · The oracle runs the sequential subset only: a program with tasks, channels, a")
    strs_push(l, "foreign call or the clock is refused (status 1 since Q1-C1; 4 before), and those are held by backend agreement and the")
    strs_push(l, "memory and concurrency suites as before. The runtime itself is LLVM text both backends link (area 13),")
    strs_push(l, "not LIR. No optimisation happens in LIR; clang's and Cranelift's do.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N81, 2026-10-03: Target data layout v1 — VERIFIED; Byte layouts owned by LIR v1 — VERIFIED;")
    strs_push(l, "Ownership table v1 — VERIFIED; Layout validator v1 — VERIFIED; `nazm.lir/1` — VERIFIED. One")
    strs_push(l, "instruction-level LIR both backends consume — MISSING; LIR oracle interpreter — MISSING.*")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.82 is the constitution, written before the code and stating that N81 is not")
    strs_push(l, "accepted under its own criteria. `crates/nazm-lir/src/abi.rs` owns a target's data layout (a pointer")
    strs_push(l, "8 bytes, or 4 on `wasm32`), every record's and enum's byte layout on it, and whether a type owns")
    strs_push(l, "anything; the Cranelift backend reads them (its `layout.rs` decides nothing now) and the LLVM backend")
    strs_push(l, "reads ownership, and both validate the tables before generating any code (`N0900` if broken). `nazm")
    strs_push(l, "lir` prints `nazm.lir/1` (`schema/nazm.lir-1.json`; since N105 `nazm.lir/2`, `schema/nazm.lir-2.json`, the only one in the tree). Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/lir.rs` —")
    strs_push(l, "determinism, canonical order at natural alignment, an enum's tag and payload, wasm32's narrower")
    strs_push(l, "handles with nothing else moving, ownership through containment, refusals, and a program using")
    strs_push(l, "every shape agreeing on the interpreter, LLVM and Cranelift; `abi::tests` — the validator naming")
    strs_push(l, "each broken invariant; `schemas.rs`; the N73 fuzzer generating a three-width record inside an")
    strs_push(l, "enum's payload on every tier. **Falsifier, run:** every program in the repository built with both")
    strs_push(l, "backends by N79 and by N81 produced byte-identical objects. *N81 left the row PARTIAL because each")
    strs_push(l, "backend still translated MIR's operations itself, so their agreement was tested, not constructed, and")
    strs_push(l, "LLVM's enum was the product of its variants, not the tagged union these tables describe; N105 closed")
    strs_push(l, "both — one lowering, and both backends lay every value out by these tables.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · Since N40 `crates/nazm-lir` reads **validated MIR** (area 9) and nothing of the")
    strs_push(l, "checker: `lower.rs` settles layout (canonical by name, from the order MIR carries), symbols from")
    strs_push(l, "MIR's durable identities, linkage, units and externals, and refuses what the native subset does")
    strs_push(l, "not cover — recursion over MIR's call graph, a `main` taking anything but capabilities or not")
    strs_push(l, "returning `Int`, a sequence handed to a task — with the same diagnostics as before;")
    strs_push(l, "`op/lower.rs` (since N105; `emit.rs` before it) writes each MIR block as a label, each local as a slot, each statement and terminator")
    strs_push(l, "as the instructions it means. The distinguishing information it adds is how each operation")
    strs_push(l, "fails at the machine level; every fallible statement carries a span and a MIR failure edge.")
    strs_push(l, "Layering is gated: `xtask/src/rules.rs` forbids `nazm-lir` depending on `nazm-core` or")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-cir`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · Since N105 LIR is an instruction-level IR of its own, lowered from MIR, validated,")
    strs_push(l, "interpreted as an oracle and translated by both backends; between N40 and N105 only layout, symbols")
    strs_push(l, "and LLVM text emission over MIR were left of it. No optimisation, inlining or constant folding")
    strs_push(l, "happens here; the backends' own do.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*The duplicate built-in table and the second resolver this row used to name were removed by")
    strs_push(l, "N1; the forbidden dependency on `nazm-core` still holds, and is satisfied by both crates")
    strs_push(l, "depending on `nazm-sema`, which owns the shared vocabulary since N2.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N12 added no node.* `?` is lowered to the LIR `match` it means, with a `Stmt::Return` in its")
    strs_push(l, "error arm, so its cleanup is `return`'s and the emitter did not change. *Since N39 that `match`")
    strs_push(l, "is Core IR's* — the lowering in `nazm-core` makes it once for both backends, and `lower_propagate`")
    strs_push(l, "is gone; the LIR it produces is byte-identical.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N12.1 added two, and removed a refusal.* A block used as a value compiles natively: every")
    strs_push(l, "value block goes through one `lower_block`, a `match` arm written as a block is its bindings")
    strs_push(l, "followed by that block, `Expr::Block` carries a block in any other value position, and")
    strs_push(l, "`Stmt::Match` is the statement `match` whose arms may produce nothing — the pairing")
    strs_push(l, "`Stmt::If` already had. Until then *a block used as an expression* was refused as `N0101`;")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm capabilities` now reports it compiled. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/value_blocks.rs`,")
    strs_push(l, "19 cases each interpreted and native and required to agree on value and on every memory")
    strs_push(l, "counter. `architecture.md` §7.14.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*The paragraph that stood here until N5 said the backend was whole-program: one LLVM")
    strs_push(l, "module, functions numbered `@nz.fN`, modules existing in the front end and nowhere below")
    strs_push(l, "it. That was accurate, and it is no longer true — see area 10a.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · Only what a real optimisation pass demands. The second backend (Cranelift, N41) consumes the same LIR since N105.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · A second consumer exists that the contract serves unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 10a. Per-module code generation and linking — VERIFIED")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · As of N5 (2026-09-22) each Nazm module is lowered, emitted and assembled on")
    strs_push(l, "its own, and the objects are linked. `crates/nazm-lir/src/lower.rs` splits into a global")
    strs_push(l, "`plan` — signature admissibility and, until N49, the recursion refusal, both of which span modules —")
    strs_push(l, "and `lower_module`, which reads one module's bodies and every function's *signature*;")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-lir/src/op/lower.rs` has `lower_unit` (N105; `emit_unit` wraps it), and `crates/nazm-runtime/src/` `emit_runtime` and `emit_entry` (moved by N43, its own crate since N53);")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/src/build/objects.rs` runs `clang -c` per artefact and `build/link.rs` links.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A symbol is a spelling of the definition's `DefKey` (`crates/nazm-lir/src/symbol.rs`), not")
    strs_push(l, "a position: `@nz.m.lib_2Futil_2Enz.parse`. The encoding escapes every byte outside")
    strs_push(l, "`[A-Za-z0-9]` including `_`, so it is injective and collisions are impossible **by")
    strs_push(l, "construction** rather than improbable.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Sixteen cases in `crates/nazm-cli/tests/native_units.rs`, each running the compiler and the")
    strs_push(l, "program: a cross-module call resolved by the linker, three modules with the same private")
    strs_push(l, "`helper`, a diamond generated once, a legal import cycle, a cross-module call cycle still")
    strs_push(l, "refused, an imported `main` that is not the process entry, per-unit constants that do not")
    strs_push(l, "collide, a runtime defined exactly once, identical symbols across two checkouts and from")
    strs_push(l, "two entry points, and `pub` changing linkage without changing spelling. A `native identity`")
    strs_push(l, "gate covers what a test cannot: that no session id, no `pub` and no positional number")
    strs_push(l, "reaches a symbol, and no LLVM spelling reaches `nazm-sema`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What an object depends on, measured** · A's artefact names B in one `declare` and one")
    strs_push(l, "`call`. Changing B's body, adding a private definition to B, or adding an export A does not")
    strs_push(l, "call each leave A's artefact **byte-identical** — so an object depends on its dependencies'")
    strs_push(l, "symbol identity and ABI signature, and not on their implementations.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Since N11* a generic function instance is a unit and an object of its own — artefacts")
    strs_push(l, "`g0`, `g1`, … — named from its definition's `DefKey` and its type arguments' canonical")
    strs_push(l, "keys, never folded into a caller's unit: `one_instance_requested_by_two_modules_is_one_unit_and_one_object`,")
    strs_push(l, "`a_callers_unit_never_carries_a_generic_body`, and a caller that declares an instance")
    strs_push(l, "carries every type the declaration names (`a_call_carries_the_types_its_callee_is_declared_with`,")
    strs_push(l, "found by the conformance corpus).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · The clean build is roughly **twice as slow** for a small program, almost")
    strs_push(l, "entirely because there are now several `clang` processes where there was one — measured in")
    strs_push(l, "`performance.md` together with a 10% smaller optimised executable, which is cross-module")
    strs_push(l, "inlining no longer happening. No LTO. `nazm build` still compiles a narrower subset than")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm run`. The call-cycle analysis is still whole-program: since N49 it places the stack check")
    strs_push(l, "MIR emits first in every function in a cycle, across modules (area 11).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Until N6 this row also read \"nothing is reused, and no native cache exists\". That was")
    strs_push(l, "accurate and is no longer true — see area 10b.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · None for this row.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Met for separate generation and linking. Native reuse is area 10b.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 10b. Native object reuse — VERIFIED")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · As of N6 (2026-09-22) an emitted LLVM unit whose object was compiled before")
    strs_push(l, "is not compiled again. `crates/nazm-cache/src/object.rs` defines `ObjectKey` over three")
    strs_push(l, "things and nothing else — a digest of the exact bytes handed to the object compiler, the")
    strs_push(l, "identity of that compiler, and the configuration it resolves for the run — and")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cache/src/objects.rs` is the store. `crates/nazm-cli/src/backend.rs` is the")
    strs_push(l, "single place the object compiler is invoked: one `clang -###` per build reads the resolved")
    strs_push(l, "command line, so the triple, the CPU features, the relocation model and the ABI are in the")
    strs_push(l, "key without anyone having enumerated them, and the invocation runs with an environment")
    strs_push(l, "built from nothing plus ten named variables, because `CCC_OVERRIDE_OPTIONS`, `SDKROOT` and")
    strs_push(l, "`MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET` were each measured to change the object.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Thirty-three cases in `crates/nazm-cli/tests/native_cache.rs` and eighteen in")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cache/tests/objects.rs`. The precision ones: a dependency's body change and an")
    strs_push(l, "export the caller never calls each recompile one unit of seven; a comment that moves no")
    strs_push(l, "emitted position recompiles nothing, and one above a fallible operation recompiles the unit")
    strs_push(l, "it moved. The safety ones: two optimisation levels share nothing, a backend that reports a")
    strs_push(l, "different version shares nothing, a truncated, edited, mis-filed or wrongly-headed entry is")
    strs_push(l, "a miss rather than a link failure, eight concurrent writers of one key leave one valid")
    strs_push(l, "entry, deleting the whole store changes only the time, and cold, warm and `--no-cache`")
    strs_push(l, "builds produce the same program. An `object cache` gate covers what a test cannot: that the")
    strs_push(l, "key still has all three fields, that a lookup still recomputes the key and the object's")
    strs_push(l, "digest, that nothing semantic is imported into the key, that an entry carries no field")
    strs_push(l, "nothing validates, and that the arguments hashed and the arguments executed come from one")
    strs_push(l, "function.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Since N11, for generic instances* (`crates/nazm-cli/tests/native_cache.rs`, seven cases):")
    strs_push(l, "a new instantiation compiles the caller, the new instance and any runtime it newly reaches;")
    strs_push(l, "a generic **body** edit recompiles exactly its instances and no caller — not even its own")
    strs_push(l, "module's unit, which never carries the body; renaming a type parameter recompiles nothing;")
    strs_push(l, "a warm build compiles nothing. The key needed no change: an instance's key is its bytes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Measured** · On the five-module compiler, `-O0`: 665.4 ms with `--no-cache`, 730.7 ms")
    strs_push(l, "cold, **157.6 ms** warm; `-O2`: 1693.0 ms, 1755.4 ms, **157.6 ms**. A one-module edit costs")
    strs_push(l, "198–218 ms whether the edit is a private body, a called export's body, or an export nobody")
    strs_push(l, "calls — the three are indistinguishable, which is the point of the key. A warm build runs")
    strs_push(l, "**two** external processes where a cache-disabled one runs eight.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · This is object reuse, not incremental native compilation. Reading,")
    strs_push(l, "parsing, checking, backend admissibility, lowering, emission and fingerprinting run on every")
    strs_push(l, "build, and so does the final link. No executable cache, no `LinkKey`, no incremental linker,")
    strs_push(l, "no persistent LIR or LLVM, no remote cache, no LTO. Cold builds pay about 65 ms more than a")
    strs_push(l, "cache-disabled build for hashing, `fsync` and publication. Nothing is evicted: the store")
    strs_push(l, "grows until it is deleted, 852 KiB for this workload's seven units at `-O0`. A backend that")
    strs_push(l, "reports one version and behaves differently is indistinguishable, which is a stated limit")
    strs_push(l, "rather than a missing check.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · A `LinkKey` if executable reuse is ever justified, and a decision")
    strs_push(l, "about whether the per-build `clang -###` probe — 60 ms of a 158 ms warm build — is worth")
    strs_push(l, "memoising, which is a cache of a toolchain fact with an invalidation question of its own.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Met for per-unit object reuse. Executable and link-result reuse are not")
    strs_push(l, "claimed anywhere.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 11. LLVM backend — VERIFIED")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · `crates/nazm-lir/src/op/llvm.rs` prints the LIR as LLVM IR text (N105); `crates/nazm-cli/src/build/`")
    strs_push(l, "hands it to `clang`. No LLVM is linked, so there is no build-time LLVM dependency. 127")
    strs_push(l, "end-to-end tests in `crates/nazm-cli/tests/build.rs`, each at `-O0` **and** `-O2`, against")
    strs_push(l, "a written expectation and against the interpreter.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N49 (2026-10-01)** · recursion, direct and mutual, across modules and through generic")
    strs_push(l, "instances, compiles: MIR places a `StackCheck` first in every function in a call cycle and both")
    strs_push(l, "backends emit it as a call to the runtime's `nz.stack_check` and a branch to the failure edge, so")
    strs_push(l, "unbounded recursion fails with `N0408` and unwinds instead of dying of a signal (`docs/user/spec.md`,")
    strs_push(l, "*Native recursion*). Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/usability.rs` (agreement in four builds, a")
    strs_push(l, "depth of 50,000 natively, `N0408` under both backends at `-O0` and `-O2` and inside a task),")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/mir.rs` (placement, and none where no cycle is), `native_cache.rs` (an edit")
    strs_push(l, "that puts an unchanged module into a cycle recompiles it). The guarantee is conditional on the")
    strs_push(l, "non-recursive frames between two checks fitting the quarter of the stack kept as headroom.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N59 (2026-10-02)** · `architecture.md` §7.61 first. A scalar temporary MIR assigns once and reads")
    strs_push(l, "only later in its block has no slot: the compiler written in Nazm's text at `-O0` went from 13,867")
    strs_push(l, "`alloca`s to 6,328 and from 177.5k instructions to 157.3k; `nazm build -O0` of it, interleaved A/B,")
    strs_push(l, "five runs each, debug compiler: medians 2,087 → 1,983 ms; a loop program built at `-O0` ran")
    strs_push(l, "133–144 → 103–105 ms with the same output (`docs/internal/performance-log.md`, N59). Bindings, parameters,")
    strs_push(l, "managed values and anything read across blocks keep their slots")
    strs_push(l, "(`a_scalar_temporary_has_no_slot_and_every_other_local_keeps_one`). Both backends still need clang")
    strs_push(l, "for the runtime's text and the C driver for the link; `nazm inspect` names both.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · The arithmetic contract is the load-bearing part and is deliberately")
    strs_push(l, "conservative: `nsw` is not used, because it would promise overflow cannot happen and")
    strs_push(l, "license an optimiser to delete the trap. Debug information is emitted only under `nazm build")
    strs_push(l, "--debug` (N48, N58, N91; area 27); an ordinary build carries none.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · None for correctness.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Already met for the current subset.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 12. Cranelift backend — VERIFIED (v1, for the native subset, on the host)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N99, 2026-10-04: the interactive tier v2 — the tiers VERIFIED to agree; the JIT still BLOCKED.*")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.100 first. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/tiers.rs`: one REPL session's thirteen answers,")
    strs_push(l, "four of them failures (`N0400` twice, `N0401`, and `i64::MIN / -1`), equal to `nazm run`'s and to the")
    strs_push(l, "native builds' of the same definitions by LLVM and by Cranelift. The JIT stays BLOCKED by two causes,")
    strs_push(l, "stated: the workspace forbids `unsafe`, which executable memory needs, and no crate that provides it")
    strs_push(l, "(`cranelift-jit`, `region`, `memmap2`) is in the offline cache; the isolated crate that would lift it,")
    strs_push(l, "with its W^X and stale-code acceptance tests, is designed in §7.100 and not built.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N65, 2026-10-02: the interactive tier — VERIFIED for the REPL, comptime and reload checks; the JIT")
    strs_push(l, "BLOCKED.* `architecture.md` §7.67 first. `nazm repl` checks the session as one program on every")
    strs_push(l, "edit and refuses a redefinition that breaks a caller by the caller's name; `nazm comptime`")
    strs_push(l, "evaluates parameterless pure functions under budgets and refuses anything else (`N0393`), a runaway")
    strs_push(l, "stopping with `N0402`; `nazm reload-check` names each change `reloadable` or `restart`")
    strs_push(l, "(`nazm.reload-check/1`). Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/live.rs` (5), `live.rs`'s unit tests (5).")
    strs_push(l, "**BLOCKED**: an in-process JIT needs `unsafe` code, which the workspace forbids")
    strs_push(l, "(`unsafe_code = \"forbid\"`); lifting that is the project's decision. Designed in §7.67; no JIT")
    strs_push(l, "differential exists, and none is claimed. Nothing is hot-reloaded: the reload check is the rule.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · N41 (2026-10-01). `crates/nazm-codegen-clif` implements `nazm-lir`'s `Backend`")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-lir/src/backend.rs`) with Cranelift 0.136.1, pinned exactly: every MIR function body")
    strs_push(l, "of a unit becomes Cranelift IR, verified by Cranelift's verifier, and one object per unit is written")
    strs_push(l, "by `cranelift-object`; the per-type retain, release and equality helpers and the task trampolines")
    strs_push(l, "are generated with it. `nazm build --backend cranelift` selects it; `llvm` stays the default and")
    strs_push(l, "the differential reference. `architecture.md` §7.43 is the constitution, written first.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Claim | Status | Evidence |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| A Cranelift-independent backend boundary | VERIFIED | `Backend` names no Cranelift type; `nazm-lir` and `nazm-cli` do not depend on a code generator (`cargo xtask check`, codegen reach) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Cranelift consumes LIR, and nothing above it | VERIFIED | `nazm-codegen-clif` depends on `nazm-lir` (and `nazm-span`, `nazm-diag`) only, since N105 — not `nazm-mir` (`the_cranelift_backend_reads_lir_and_nothing_above_it`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| The whole native subset compiles with Cranelift | VERIFIED | all 104 programs of the 205-source corpus that build: stdout, stderr, exit status and memory report identical to the LLVM backend's (`performance.md`, N41); `crates/nazm-cli/tests/cranelift.rs` against the interpreter too |")
    strs_push(l, "| Traps and arithmetic edges | VERIFIED | `every_trap_is_the_same_trap` (overflow, `/` and `%` by zero, `MIN / -1`, bounds, capacities), `signed_arithmetic_and_its_edges_agree` (`MIN % -1` is 0) |")
    strs_push(l, "| No silent fallback | VERIFIED | `choosing_cranelift_writes_no_llvm_text_for_any_unit`; a refusal writes nothing (`crates/nazm-cli/tests/cranelift.rs`); recursion compiles under both since N49 (`recursion_compiles_under_both_backends_and_agrees`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Typed, centralised runtime imports | VERIFIED | every call into the runtime is built from `crates/nazm-runtime/src/lib.rs`; `a_runtime_entry_the_registry_names_is_one_the_runtime_defines` |")
    strs_push(l, "| Object-cache identity and reuse | VERIFIED | a key over each unit's LIR digests (MIR's until N105), layouts, callee signatures, target, backend version and settings and the runtime ABI revision, known before generation; `an_unchanged_unit_is_reused_by_its_key_and_a_changed_one_is_regenerated`, `a_cache_key_moves_with_every_setting_that_changes_the_code_and_only_those` |")
    strs_push(l, "| Deterministic objects | VERIFIED | `the_same_mir_gives_the_same_object_bytes` (the compiler's own source) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Debug information | VERIFIED as scoped | DWARF line tables, scopes and variables under `--debug` (N58, N91; area 27); MISSING until then, function symbols only (N48) |")
    strs_push(l, "| A target other than the host | VERIFIED as scoped | `--target` and object output for another toolchain (N57); each target's evidence in the support matrix (area 33); refused by name until then |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · Every local that is not a scalar lives in a stack slot and is copied by")
    strs_push(l, "`memcpy`-sized loads and stores; no optimisation pass runs beyond Cranelift's own. The runtime")
    strs_push(l, "and the platform entry are still the runtime's LLVM text compiled by clang, and clang links, so a")
    strs_push(l, "Cranelift build still needs clang. A Cranelift build links the whole runtime (a reused object is")
    strs_push(l, "not generated, so it cannot say which parts it reaches). The backend has its own internal calling")
    strs_push(l, "convention and layout; nothing passes a value between code the two backends generated.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Already met for the declared set: the native subset, on the host.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Runtime and concurrency")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 13. Runtime — VERIFIED (the v1 contract; the M:N pool by default since N106; no allocator, and text, not a Rust crate)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N106, 2026-10-05: the pool by default — VERIFIED; the C policy — VERIFIED; a refused scheduler name")
    strs_push(l, "— VERIFIED; a deterministic single-worker mode — VERIFIED.* `architecture.md` §7.107, written first.")
    strs_push(l, "With `NAZM_SCHEDULER` unset a native program's tasks run on N83's pool — `NAZM_WORKERS` workers (default: one per processor online since 2026-10-15, four before),")
    strs_push(l, "each task a guarded `NAZM_TASK_STACK` (256 KiB) stack — on every hosted target with a switch;")
    strs_push(l, "`threads` asks for a thread per task, `pool` for the pool, and any other value starts no task")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0404`). A program that calls C runs a thread per task unless the pool is asked for — a task")
    strs_push(l, "blocked in C would hold its worker — and `nazm explain-cost` says which scheduler and why")
    strs_push(l, "(`nazm.cost/2`). Runtime ABI revision 14 (`nz.pool_policy`, stored by the entry before `main`).")
    strs_push(l, "Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/scheduler_default.rs` — the default on both backends with the same")
    strs_push(l, "output, ending and reports as on threads; ten thousand tasks on four workers")
    strs_push(l, "(`workers=4 peak=10000`); four names refused; the C policy on both backends and in the cost report;")
    strs_push(l, "one worker giving the same order five times — and the whole suite, host (macOS aarch64) and")
    strs_push(l, "contained (Linux aarch64), running every native program on the default. x86-64 macOS under Rosetta:")
    strs_push(l, "a channel program runs on the pool by default. `docs/internal/performance-log.md` (N106): spawn and join 6.7 µs")
    strs_push(l, "against 26.1 on threads, a parked receive woken 7.8 against 24.6, 17.8 KB per live task. **Scope:**")
    strs_push(l, "the interpreter and the compiler written in Nazm keep a thread per task; no work stealing,")
    strs_push(l, "preemption or hand-off of a blocking C call.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · N43 (2026-10-01): `architecture.md` §7.45 is the runtime constitution, written")
    strs_push(l, "first. The runtime is LLVM text generated into each program, emitted only for the parts reached,")
    strs_push(l, "from `crates/nazm-runtime/src/` (in `nazm-lir` from N43 to N52): `core.rs` (the portable text — state, failure and report,")
    strs_push(l, "sequences, strings, I/O, join, tasks, channels, the second-backend shims), `os.rs` (the operating-")
    strs_push(l, "system adapter: the only C-library and POSIX-threads entry points anything calls), `entry.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "(the platform entry) and `lib.rs` (the contract). *N53:* those four files are the")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-runtime` crate, which depends on nothing of the compiler (`cargo xtask check`, layering);")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-lir` and `nazm-codegen-clif` consume it. Runtime ABI revision 5, and `digest()` — blake3 of")
    strs_push(l, "the whole runtime text, the platform entry and the inventory — enters every object key beside the")
    strs_push(l, "revision under both backends (`the_runtime_s_digest_is_part_of_every_configuration`,")
    strs_push(l, "`the_runtime_is_revision_five_and_its_digest_covers_generic_channels`, renamed with each revision since — `…_revision_twenty_eight_…` at v1). *N49:* runtime ABI revision 3 — `nz.stack_check`")
    strs_push(l, "and its thread-local limit, emitted only where a function in a call cycle calls it, and task")
    strs_push(l, "threads started with an 8 MiB stack (`a_task_thread_has_the_stack_the_check_budgets_for_on_every_host`). `compiler/emit.nz`'s copy is **derived** from")
    strs_push(l, "`core.rs` line by line, re-derived by `cargo xtask check`'s `runtime parity` gate since N8.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Claim | Status | Evidence |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| One typed, versioned inventory of every runtime symbol | VERIFIED | `INVENTORY` (32 functions: signature, part, responsibility, ownership, effect, failure, thread safety) and `GLOBALS` (11); units' declarations generated from it; `every_runtime_definition_is_inventoried_with_its_exact_signature`, `every_runtime_global_is_inventoried`, `the_word_view_agrees_with_the_inventory` |")
    strs_push(l, "| Runtime ABI revision in every object key | VERIFIED | `RUNTIME_ABI_REVISION` (2 when this row was written; 28 at v1); Cranelift keys (N41) and clang's configuration (`the_runtime_abi_revision_is_part_of_every_configuration`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Startup and shutdown defined | VERIFIED | arguments stored once without the program's name, roots minted by the entry alone, three distinguished endings (`the_three_ways_a_program_ends_are_distinguished`, `the_arguments_are_stored_once_at_startup_without_the_program_name`, `root_capabilities_come_from_the_entry_alone`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Memory contract | VERIFIED | strings, sequences, sequences of strings and of records, channels, shared backings across four threads, allocation-failure paths, all counted exactly (`the_runtime_s_services_keep_their_contract_when_called_directly`, a C harness linked against the runtime alone) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Failure classes | VERIFIED | language, host-refused, I/O and explicit exit distinguished; a `Result` never becomes one (`an_err_is_data_and_never_a_failure`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Portable core, one OS adapter | VERIFIED | `a_runtime_calls_the_operating_system_only_through_the_adapter`; the same POSIX surface on every v1 target |")
    strs_push(l, "| A built, versioned, verified runtime artifact (N82) | VERIFIED | `nazm runtime build` writes `libnazmrt.a` and a `nazm.runtime/1` manifest per target and profile (hosted, board, wasm); `nazm build --runtime DIR` links it on both backends and refuses every artifact that does not fit, by name, before writing anything; `nazm runtime verify`. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/runtime_artifact.rs` (build and determinism, a program reaching every service identical with the artifact on both backends, nine refusals, profiles and a board's archive, provenance), `schemas.rs`; every program in the repository built both ways, 228 builds, identical output, ending and memory report |")
    strs_push(l, "| A scheduler beyond one thread per task, by default | VERIFIED | N106: the pool, with its policy stated (`scheduler_default.rs`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| A runtime crate, an allocator | MISSING | the runtime is still LLVM text, one implementation for every target; `malloc` is the C library's |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · Still no `nazm-rt` crate: the runtime is text, so its tests link it with a C")
    strs_push(l, "harness rather than call it from Rust. Thread safety is by construction (atomic string and channel")
    strs_push(l, "counts, sequences confined by `N0321`), not by a sanitizer run. *One OS thread per task* stood here")
    strs_push(l, "until N106.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · None for the v1 contract. The scheduler arrived as the pool (N83, the default")
    strs_push(l, "since N106, area 15); a runtime written as a Rust crate would need the `unsafe` allowance the")
    strs_push(l, "workspace forbids, and no program has needed an allocator of its own.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · For v1: met. For the area (met by N106): a scheduler beyond one thread per task, with its")
    strs_push(l, "policy stated.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 14. Structured concurrency — VERIFIED")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · Specified in `docs/user/spec.md` before implementation, then interpreted")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-core/src/eval/`, 18 tests in `crates/nazm-core/tests/concurrency.rs`), then")
    strs_push(l, "compiled (17 tests in `crates/nazm-cli/tests/concurrent.rs` at `-O0` and `-O2`, each")
    strs_push(l, "against a written expectation *and* the interpreter), **then compiled by the compiler")
    strs_push(l, "written in Nazm** — `compiler/emit.nz` carries the task and channel runtime. Every test")
    strs_push(l, "carries a deadline, so a hang fails by name. Static rules are real: `N0320` for `spawn`")
    strs_push(l, "outside a `scope`, `N0321` for a sequence crossing into a task.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Narrowed in N10.1:* the compiler written in Nazm joined a scope when control fell off its")
    strs_push(l, "end or failed, and not when a `break`, `continue` or `return` left it — so a task that failed")
    strs_push(l, "inside a scope a `break` left was never waited for and its failure never taken on. The")
    strs_push(l, "reference and the interpreter were right. Held by the `scope_*_joins` cases in")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/transfers/`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N44 (2026-10-01):* `architecture.md` §7.46 is the scheduler contract — task states, scope")
    strs_push(l, "ownership, which failure a scope reports (the first in start order, the body's before any")
    strs_push(l, "task's), no cancellation, the OS as scheduler and why a pool would break the progress guarantee,")
    strs_push(l, "fairness and determinism, authority and provenance across a spawn, what may cross, channels,")
    strs_push(l, "shutdown. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/scheduler.rs` holds it under the interpreter, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2`")
    strs_push(l, "and Cranelift with every native run fully reclaimed: 5,000 short tasks, thirty nested scopes")
    strs_push(l, "joined innermost first, the reported failure in start order not time order, a failure deep in")
    strs_push(l, "nested scopes, records and enums handed to tasks, a waiting receiver woken, authority passed,")
    strs_push(l, "withheld and bridged, provenance through a spawn (`N0372`), nothing mutable crossing (`N0321`,")
    strs_push(l, "transitively), `exit_with` from a task. Peak RSS stays at 3.8 MB from 5,000 to 500,000 tasks.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · A native program's tasks run on the M:N pool by default (N106, area 15) — bounded")
    strs_push(l, "workers, a task pinned to one, no work stealing, no preemption and no fairness guarantee; the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter, the compiler written in Nazm and a program that calls C keep a thread per task.")
    strs_push(l, "Deadlines exist on selects (N54), and there is **no cancellation beyond closing a channel**.")
    strs_push(l, "`Chan` alone carries `Int`; `Chan[T]` (N53) carries any `T` that may cross into a task, no")
    strs_push(l, "sequence or closure (`N0390`); since N54 a select over `Chan[T]` receives, a deadline needs a")
    strs_push(l, "`TimeCap`, and closing a channel is how a task is cancelled — cooperatively, where it waits. Ownership prevents data races; **that is not deadlock freedom**")
    strs_push(l, "and is not claimed as such (`architecture.md` §5).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N53, 2026-10-02: Generic channels — VERIFIED.* `Chan[T]` with `chan_new_of[T]`, `chan_send_of`,")
    strs_push(l, "`chan_recv_of(c, out)` and `chan_close_of`: strings, records and enums with payloads cross tasks")
    strs_push(l, "through typed channels identically under the interpreter, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift, every")
    strs_push(l, "run fully reclaimed — a value still queued when the last reference goes released exactly once, a")
    strs_push(l, "send after close refused and its value released by the sender. The type persists in interfaces")
    strs_push(l, "(`{\"chan\":T}`, which a `/7` reader refuses as an unknown shape), and a typed channel's operations")
    strs_push(l, "are `explain-cost` sites. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/generic_channels.rs`, 8 tests; fourteen N53")
    strs_push(l, "mutations.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N54, 2026-10-02: Select, deadlines, cooperative cancellation, counters — VERIFIED for one OS thread")
    strs_push(l, "per task.* `chan_select_of` (lowest ready index; a closed channel is ready) and `chan_select_until`")
    strs_push(l, "(`-2` after at least `ms`) over `Vec[Chan[T]]`; `time_now_ms`; both clock built-ins need a `TimeCap`")
    strs_push(l, "held (`N0369`), and `critical`'s `no-ambient-time` refuses them. A task waiting in a select is")
    strs_push(l, "woken by another task's send and cancelled by a close; N44's failure rule is unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "`NAZM_SCHED_REPORT` counts tasks spawned and joined, selects and timeouts, and the interpreter, LLVM")
    strs_push(l, "and Cranelift agree on it. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/select.rs`, 9 tests; sixteen N54 mutations.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Performance leadership 6.4, 2026-10-17: a select over channels of different types — VERIFIED.*")
    strs_push(l, "`Select` with `sel_new`, `sel_recv[T](s, c, out)`, `sel_send[T](s, c, v)`, `sel_wait` and")
    strs_push(l, "`sel_wait_until` (`docs/user/spec.md`, *Select over channels of different types*): the lowest ready case")
    strs_push(l, "performed, a send case spent once sent, `-3 - i` for a closed channel, `-1` with no case left, `-2`")
    strs_push(l, "after the deadline; a `Select` refused to a task (`N0321`), its name the language's (`N0331`), the")
    strs_push(l, "deadline needing a `TimeCap` (`N0369`). The interpreter, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2`, Cranelift and Nazm's own")
    strs_push(l, "code generator print the same, count the same selects and reclaim everything, an unsent value")
    strs_push(l, "included. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/select.rs`, 5 tests more; `toolchain/interp` and the pipeline's")
    strs_push(l, "`ops.nz` carry it; mutations `ps-*`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · None for the current model; area 15 for anything beyond it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Met for the model as specified.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 15. Advanced scheduler — VERIFIED as scoped (N83)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N106, 2026-10-05: the pool is the default (area 13); the whole suite runs on it, on macOS aarch64 and,")
    strs_push(l, "contained, Linux aarch64 — the Linux run N83 did not have.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N83, 2026-10-04: M:N tasks on bounded workers v1 — VERIFIED (opt-in); suspension instead of a")
    strs_push(l, "blocked worker — VERIFIED; per-task failure state and stack limit — VERIFIED; deadlines on parked")
    strs_push(l, "tasks — VERIFIED; work stealing, preemption, blocking-FFI hand-off, a model checker — not here.*")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.84 is the constitution, written first. With `NAZM_SCHEDULER=pool` a native")
    strs_push(l, "program's tasks run on `NAZM_WORKERS` threads (default: the processors online, at most 64; 4 before 2026-10-15), each task a guarded stack")
    strs_push(l, "(`NAZM_TASK_STACK`, default 256 KiB) pinned to one worker, switched by a per-target routine")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-runtime/src/switch.rs`); the four suspension points park the task and free the worker")
    strs_push(l, "(`nz.cwait`, `nz.ctimedwait`, `nz.cwake`, `nz.join_one`), its failure state and stack limit saved and")
    strs_push(l, "restored at every switch. The thread model's runtime texts are unchanged and the pool is joined to")
    strs_push(l, "them as they are emitted, so `compiler/emit.nz`'s copy still matches (`runtime parity`). Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/scheduler_pool.rs` — four concurrency shapes (fan-in, a three-stage pipeline")
    strs_push(l, "of `Chan[Str]`, a select, nested scopes) giving the same output, ending and memory report on the pool")
    strs_push(l, "as on threads, on both backends; ten thousand tasks all alive at once on two workers")
    strs_push(l, "(`nazm-pool: workers=2 peak=10000`); a failing task and a sibling on one worker, and recursion past a")
    strs_push(l, "task's stack reported as `N0408` rather than a crash; a polling select letting a sibling on its worker")
    strs_push(l, "run; a parked task's deadline firing; every run under a deadline, so a lost wake-up fails rather than")
    strs_push(l, "hangs. The whole `nazm-cli` suite also passed with `NAZM_SCHEDULER=pool` exported, every native")
    strs_push(l, "program it builds running on the pool. Measured (`performance.md`): spawn and join 7.4 µs against")
    strs_push(l, "25.4 µs on threads, a round trip 5.0 µs against 6.7 µs, about 17.8 KB resident per task against 18.4")
    strs_push(l, "KB, page 16 KiB; 50,000 tasks on four workers in 891 MB, where threads did not finish 6,000 within")
    strs_push(l, "40 s. **Scope**: opt-in, the default unchanged; verified on `aarch64-apple-darwin` and on")
    strs_push(l, "`x86_64-apple-darwin` under Rosetta, compiled and not run for Linux; the interpreter and the compiler")
    strs_push(l, "written in Nazm keep a thread per task.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · `architecture.md` §5 and `roadmap.md`'s C-4/C-5 rows: M:N tasks, work")
    strs_push(l, "stealing, growable stacks, an event reactor, blocking-FFI handoff. N44 measured the baseline any")
    strs_push(l, "of it must beat (`docs/internal/performance-log.md`, N44): a task started and joined in 13 µs, a channel round")
    strs_push(l, "trip between two tasks 4.6 µs, a streamed value 60 ns, and linear scaling to four tasks; and")
    strs_push(l, "decided against a fixed worker pool, which with blocking channels and no suspendable tasks would")
    strs_push(l, "deadlock programs that are correct today (§7.46).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N54, 2026-10-02 — DESIGNED.* §7.56 chose the model a pool would use — stackful tasks on guarded")
    strs_push(l, "stacks with a per-target switch, stackless continuations ruled out for colouring every function")
    strs_push(l, "that can block — and named what has to move first: the thread-local first-failure slot, the stack")
    strs_push(l, "limit, and a hand-off for blocking foreign calls. Select, deadlines and cancellation were built so")
    strs_push(l, "that nothing in them depends on the thread model.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · No work stealing, no preemption, no hand-off of a blocking foreign call and no")
    strs_push(l, "model checker (N83): a task that computes without waiting holds its worker, and a program that")
    strs_push(l, "calls C runs a thread per task unless `NAZM_SCHEDULER=pool`. Measured on macOS (N83) and run,")
    strs_push(l, "contained, on Linux aarch64 (N106). `architecture.md` records that the \"1M live tasks under 2GB\"")
    strs_push(l, "target was **withdrawn** as arithmetically unsupported — the right precedent for anything proposed")
    strs_push(l, "here. *Until R1 this said \"none of it exists\", true before N83.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · Work stealing and a blocking-FFI hand-off, each with its own measurement; neither")
    strs_push(l, "is scheduled. *Until R1 this named `nazm-rt` and the `unsafe` allowance; the pool was built without")
    strs_push(l, "either.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Spawn-to-first-instruction latency, context-switch cost and task memory")
    strs_push(l, "as **RSS, not virtual reservation, with page size recorded**, measured against a named")
    strs_push(l, "implementation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Libraries and interop")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 16. Standard library — VERIFIED as scoped (1.0, N84)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**R1d (2026-10-14)** · *The platform, further: processes and the file system* (`spec.md`, *The")
    strs_push(l, "platform, further*; `openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`, D4's built-ins, P1 and P2).")
    strs_push(l, "Seventeen prelude built-ins over Gate 2's handle table and statuses. Standard output and errors as")
    strs_push(l, "handles (`os_stdout`, `os_stderr`), written in order with `print`, a close leaving the stream open.")
    strs_push(l, "A child in a directory with exactly a given environment, handed over ordered by name so every")
    strs_push(l, "implementation gives the same one (`os_spawn_in`), leading a new process group or reading a null")
    strs_push(l, "standard input (`os_spawn_with`); its id (`os_child_pid`) and this process's (`os_pid`); bounded")
    strs_push(l, "waits (`os_try_wait` → `WouldBlock`, `os_wait_until` → `TimedOut`, the child left running); a signal")
    strs_push(l, "to a group (`os_kill_group`, `ProcessCap`); a waited child's peak resident memory (`os_child_rusage`,")
    strs_push(l, "`wait4`'s `ru_maxrss`). A path's own facts with a symbolic-link kind, device and inode (`os_lstat`),")
    strs_push(l, "permissions (`os_chmod`), a canonical path (`os_realpath`), a new private directory whose path is a")
    strs_push(l, "`Str` as clean as its parent, so a program may write under it (`os_mkdtemp`), and advisory whole-file")
    strs_push(l, "locks held by the open file (`os_lock`, `os_try_lock`, `os_unlock`: `flock`, `LockFileEx`).")
    strs_push(l, "`@std/file` (`file_stdout`, `file_stderr`, `EntryKind`, `LinkMetadata`, `file_symlink_metadata`,")
    strs_push(l, "`file_set_permissions`, `file_canonical`, `dir_create_temp`, `file_lock`, `file_try_lock`,")
    strs_push(l, "`file_unlock`), `@std/process` (`process_id`, `process_spawn_in`, `process_spawn_with`,")
    strs_push(l, "`process_child_id`, `process_try_wait`, `process_wait_until`, `process_kill_group`,")
    strs_push(l, "`process_peak_memory`) and `@std/fs` (`fs_temp_dir`): API-1.0 gains 20 lines. `file_walk` lists a")
    strs_push(l, "symbolic link and never follows it, as D4 approved. EXPERIMENTAL until R1 closed (2026-10-15; `stability.md` gives its status since). Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/platform_files.rs` and `process_control.rs` — each program in a fresh")
    strs_push(l, "directory under the interpreter, LLVM `-O0`/`-O2` and Cranelift with the same memory report and")
    strs_push(l, "nothing live: raw bytes among `print`'s and a closed stream handle; a file, a directory, a link, a")
    strs_push(l, "dangling link and a hard link by `os_lstat` (the same file by device and inode), `chmod` through a")
    strs_push(l, "link, a canonical path, two temporary directories written under and removed; locks held by the open")
    strs_push(l, "file, converted, tried, let go by a close, refused on a directory and standard input; a child's")
    strs_push(l, "environment exactly given and ordered, a relative program beside its directory, seven refusals")
    strs_push(l, "before anything starts, a null standard input; bounded waits on a child that ends and on one that")
    strs_push(l, "does not, a group of two ended by `SIGTERM` and checked gone (by the program and again by the test),")
    strs_push(l, "id, peak memory (positive natively), and the library over all of it; the authority (`N0369`) and")
    strs_push(l, "sink (`N0372`) refusals; a program's own `os_lstat` kept; a WASI build of the file-system ones and")
    strs_push(l, "the refusal by name of a process one; the Windows units built by both backends. `file_walk.rs`:")
    strs_push(l, "links listed, not followed. **Unexecuted**: Windows (written against Win32 — `CreateProcessW` with an")
    strs_push(l, "environment block and directory, `GetFileInformationByHandle`, `GetFinalPathNameByHandleW`,")
    strs_push(l, "`LockFileEx`, `K32GetProcessMemoryInfo` — compiled, not run under Wine), Linux and Android (compiled;")
    strs_push(l, "the contained run has not executed them), WASI (built, not run under Node). **Scope**: the interpreter")
    strs_push(l, "cannot ask a child's peak memory without C and answers `ENOSYS`; it signals a group through the")
    strs_push(l, "system's `kill`; no tree removal (listed names are `file`-origin); no signal handling")
    strs_push(l, "(`limitations.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 2 (2026-10-09)** · *Reference applications* (`general-purpose.md` §24). Five programs in")
    strs_push(l, "`examples/apps/` — `nwc`, `jsonpipe`, `nbody`, `kvstore`, `kvd` — use the standard library for real")
    strs_push(l, "work: files and standard input, JSON and maps, floats, a synced log with atomic compaction, and a")
    strs_push(l, "TCP server with a task per connection and an owner task behind channels. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/apps.rs`, every app in the interpreter and three native builds, held to its")
    strs_push(l, "recorded output and status; time and memory recorded in `examples/apps/README.md`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N84, 2026-10-04: The standard library 1.0 — VERIFIED as scoped.* `architecture.md` §7.85 first.")
    strs_push(l, "Seventeen modules, 126 public items (`library/std/API-1.0`): text grown (case, trimming either end,")
    strs_push(l, "replace, count, padding, lines, comparison, byte classes), seq grown (reverse, slice, concat, any,")
    strs_push(l, "all), a new `sort` (a stable sort by a caller's ordering, polymorphic in its effects; `Int` and `Str`")
    strs_push(l, "sorts — its own module so that `@std/seq` stays importable under `embedded`), and")
    strs_push(l, "`fmt`, `num`, `map` (ordered by key), `path` (lexical), `fs` (`IoCap`, failures as values), `time`")
    strs_push(l, "(`TimeCap`), `json` (an arena document, integers only, every malformed input an `Err` naming its byte")
    strs_push(l, "offset) and `test`; channel helpers for `Int` and `Str`. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/stdlib_1_0.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "— every new function at its edges on the interpreter, LLVM `-O0` and `-O2` and Cranelift with")
    strs_push(l, "everything reclaimed; a JSON round trip and nine malformed inputs; four representative programs under")
    strs_push(l, "`examples/std/` — a word counter, a table summer, a channel service and a package-manifest tool —")
    strs_push(l, "written against the library for all their plumbing and giving the same output on every tier; and the")
    strs_push(l, "manifest regenerated and compared, so a 1.x change to a listed item fails. `stdlib.rs` keeps every")
    strs_push(l, "module checking cleanly, documented and listed. Measured (`performance.md`): sorting 100,000 integers")
    strs_push(l, "19.6 ms; 10,000 map insertions 391 ms (an insertion moves the entries after it); parsing and")
    strs_push(l, "re-encoding 128 KB of JSON about 14 ms. **Scope**: no networking, cryptography or floating point, by")
    strs_push(l, "decision; the map's insertion is linear; the compiler written in Nazm cannot import any of it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 2 (2026-10-09)** · *Logging* (`general-purpose.md` §20). `@std/log`: levelled records with")
    strs_push(l, "fields, one JSON object a line on standard error under an `OutCap`, and timed spans. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`log_records_are_one_json_object_a_line_alike_everywhere`. **Scope**: no `task_id()` or")
    strs_push(l, "`runtime_stats()` (`limitations.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 2 (2026-10-09)** · *Randomness* (`general-purpose.md` §21; `spec.md`, *Randomness*).")
    strs_push(l, "`RandomCap` (id 8) and `os_random_bytes` from the system's entropy; `@std/random`'s seeded")
    strs_push(l, "xoshiro256** generator, pure. Runtime ABI 20; semantic epoch 40. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`a_seeded_generator_repeats_everywhere_and_entropy_does_not` (the sequence an independent Python")
    strs_push(l, "implementation gives, every implementation), `entropy_needs_a_random_cap_and_a_seeded_generator_needs_none`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 2 (2026-10-09)** · *Serialization* (`general-purpose.md` §14). `@std/json` reads and writes")
    strs_push(l, "floats beside its frozen integer parser, and pretty-prints; `@std/binary` encodes fixed-width")
    strs_push(l, "integers and floats in either order, varints, zig-zag and length-prefixed data. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`json_reads_and_writes_floats_beside_its_frozen_integers_everywhere`,")
    strs_push(l, "`binary_encodes_byte_for_byte_and_reads_back_everywhere` (the bytes Python's `struct` and an")
    strs_push(l, "independent LEB128 give) — every implementation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 2 (2026-10-09)** · *Errors* (`general-purpose.md` §13). `@std/error`'s `Error`, its")
    strs_push(l, "context gathered innermost first and shown outermost first, `error_from_io`, `error_io_result` for")
    strs_push(l, "`?`, and `@std/ioerror`'s `io_error_from_errno`. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`an_error_gathers_context_and_reads_outermost_first_everywhere` (every implementation).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 2 (2026-10-09)** · *Process and environment* (`general-purpose.md` §12; `spec.md`,")
    strs_push(l, "*Process and environment*). The environment (`os_env_*`, `@std/env`), standard input's helpers")
    strs_push(l, "(`@std/io`), and `ProcessCap` (id 9) for `os_spawn`: a program run with three pipes that are handles")
    strs_push(l, "waiting as sockets do, its exit code or signal, and `SIGKILL`; `@std/process`'s `process_run`")
    strs_push(l, "collects output and errors without a pipe filling unread. Runtime ABI 19; semantic epoch 39.")
    strs_push(l, "Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/process.rs` — a program run with input whose output, errors and")
    strs_push(l, "status come back, 300 KB and 200 KB on its two streams, a signal's ending as 265, a missing program")
    strs_push(l, "as `NotFound` (interpreter, LLVM −O0/−O2, Cranelift); the environment and standard input alike;")
    strs_push(l, "`a_task_reading_a_childs_pipe_does_not_hold_its_worker` (one worker, both backends); the")
    strs_push(l, "`ProcessCap`, sink and `IoCap` refusals. **Scope**: no signal handling; a child's exit is waited for")
    strs_push(l, "on the worker (`limitations.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 2 (2026-10-09)** · *Time* (`general-purpose.md` §11; `spec.md`, *Time*). `time_now_ns`")
    strs_push(l, "(the monotonic clock `time_now_ms` reads), `time_wall_ns` and `time_sleep_ms`, which parks on the")
    strs_push(l, "pool; `@std/time` gains `Duration`, `Instant` and `WallTime`. Runtime ABI 18; semantic epoch 38.")
    strs_push(l, "Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/time.rs` — the clocks, a sleep, deadlines and the library alike in")
    strs_push(l, "every implementation; `a_sleeping_task_does_not_hold_its_worker` (one worker, a computing task")
    strs_push(l, "finishing before a sleeping one started first, both backends); the `TimeCap` and `critical`")
    strs_push(l, "refusals.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 2 (2026-10-09)** · *Networking* (`general-purpose.md` §9–§10; `spec.md`, *Networking*).")
    strs_push(l, "`NetCap` (id 7) and the network `os_` built-ins over the same handle table: TCP listen, accept,")
    strs_push(l, "connect with a deadline, read, write, shutdown; UDP bind, send, receive with the sender; local")
    strs_push(l, "and peer addresses; name resolution; a deadline per handle. Every wait parks: one reactor thread")
    strs_push(l, "(`kqueue` on macOS, `epoll` on Linux) wakes a waiting task through the pool's existing wait, and a")
    strs_push(l, "close wakes it with `Closed`. `@std/net` gives `Result` APIs. Runtime ABI 17; semantic epoch 37.")
    strs_push(l, "Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/net.rs` — an echo server answering clients, a datagram's round")
    strs_push(l, "trip with its sender, eight failure kinds (`AddressInUse`, `TimedOut` on accept and receive,")
    strs_push(l, "`ConnectionRefused`, `Closed`, four `InvalidInput` addresses) and resolution, a close waking a")
    strs_push(l, "waiting task, a peer that has gone being an error and never a signal — interpreter, LLVM −O0/−O2,")
    strs_push(l, "Cranelift — and `a_task_waiting_on_a_socket_does_not_hold_its_worker` (eight tasks parked on")
    strs_push(l, "**one** pool worker while a ninth computes, both backends); the authority, handle and sink")
    strs_push(l, "refusals; `every_targets_os_unit_is_llvm_its_toolchain_compiles`. **Scope**: no TLS or")
    strs_push(l, "Unix-domain sockets; resolution holds the worker (`limitations.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 2 (2026-10-09)** · *Files and handles* (`general-purpose.md` §8; `spec.md`, *Files and")
    strs_push(l, "handles*). The `os_` built-ins over an `OsHandle` — a descriptor and its generation in a handle")
    strs_push(l, "table the interpreter and the runtime each keep — and `@std/ioerror` and `@std/file` over them:")
    strs_push(l, "open, create, append, create-new, read, write every byte, seek, sync, close, metadata, list,")
    strs_push(l, "make, remove, rename and replace atomically, every failure an `IoError` whose kind each platform")
    strs_push(l, "family's table in `@std/ioerror` decides. Runtime ABI 16: the `nz.os_*` entries and a per-target")
    strs_push(l, "`os` unit (`open` flags, `struct stat` and `struct dirent` layouts, the 64-bit-inode symbols,")
    strs_push(l, "`strerror_r`). Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/files.rs` —")
    strs_push(l, "`the_library_opens_writes_seeks_lists_renames_and_replaces_alike_everywhere` (forty lines through")
    strs_push(l, "every operation and seven failure kinds, interpreter, LLVM −O0/−O2 and Cranelift, everything")
    strs_push(l, "reclaimed), `a_closed_handle_answers_closed_and_never_reaches_a_reused_descriptor`,")
    strs_push(l, "`standard_input_is_read_alike_everywhere`, `a_buffer_too_short_for_a_stat_stops_the_program_everywhere`,")
    strs_push(l, "`the_platform_family_is_the_hosts`, and the authority (`N0369`), equality (`N0304`) and sink")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0372`) refusals. **Scope**: a handle is closed by `os_close` or at exit, not at its last")
    strs_push(l, "reference; reading a file holds the worker; no locking, mapping or link creation")
    strs_push(l, "(`limitations.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 2 (2026-10-09)** · *Collections* (`general-purpose.md` §7; `spec.md`, *Standard library*).")
    strs_push(l, "`@std/hash` (a `Hash` trait for every integer type, `Bool` and `Str`; FNV-1a then SplitMix64's")
    strs_push(l, "finaliser), `@std/hashmap` (open addressing, linear probing, tombstones, doubling before")
    strs_push(l, "three-quarters full; a seed), `@std/hashset` and `@std/deque` (a ring buffer): twenty-one modules,")
    strs_push(l, "158 public items. An impl may be for any numeric type (epoch 35). Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`hash_maps_sets_and_deques_behave_alike_everywhere` (a thousand inserts through growth, removal")
    strs_push(l, "past tombstones, a set of a program's records, the hash vectors computed independently, a deque")
    strs_push(l, "wrapping both ways — interpreter, LLVM −O0/−O2, Cranelift, everything reclaimed),")
    strs_push(l, "`a_seed_changes_a_maps_order_and_nothing_else`,")
    strs_push(l, "`a_number_of_any_width_has_impls_and_its_methods_run_everywhere`. **Scope**: `HashMap` is written in")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm over `Vec`, so its constant factor is the interpreter's and the backends' `Vec` access, not a")
    strs_push(l, "tuned table; no ordered map other than `StrMap`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · N45 (2026-10-01), `architecture.md` §7.47 first. Seven toolchain-owned Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "modules in `library/std/`, imported by name — `use \"@std/text\";` — resolved by the loader")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-service/src/load.rs`) to the compiler's copy of their bytes")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-sema/src/stdlib.rs`) and keyed `@std/NAME`, which no project path can take. They are")
    strs_push(l, "ordinary source: no compiler support beyond resolution, and the built-in table is unchanged. The")
    strs_push(l, "prelude (`library/core/prelude.nz`, `Result` and `Option`) is still the only module imported")
    strs_push(l, "without a `use`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Claim | Status | Evidence |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Found by name and only by name; `@std/` never read from disk | VERIFIED | `every_standard_module_is_found_by_name_and_checks_cleanly`, `no_project_path_is_keyed_as_a_standard_module` |")
    strs_push(l, "| Text, option, result, sequence, I/O, process and channel helpers behave as documented at their edges | VERIFIED | `text_behaves_as_documented_at_its_edges`, `option_result_and_seq_helpers_work_for_every_type`, `chan_take_receives_one_value_at_a_time_across_tasks` — interpreter, LLVM −O0/−O2 and Cranelift, everything reclaimed |")
    strs_push(l, "| Authority visible in every signature | VERIFIED | `io_and_process_need_the_authority_they_show` |")
    strs_push(l, "| Origins preserved through wrappers | VERIFIED | `what_a_standard_function_reads_keeps_its_origin` |")
    strs_push(l, "| Ordinary failure is a value | VERIFIED | `text_parse_int` `Err` for no digits, a non-digit and both ends of the range; `None` for an absent search or an empty maximum |")
    strs_push(l, "| Documented where the spec lists it | VERIFIED | `every_public_standard_function_is_documented_and_listed`; `nazm docs --section spec:std`; the spec's example runs (`the_spec_s_example_runs_everywhere`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Higher-order helpers | PARTIAL | `vec_map`, `vec_filter`, `vec_fold` in `@std/seq` (N50), plain Nazm over function values, on records and enums (`map_filter_and_fold_work_over_records_and_enums`); pure functions only until effects can be abstracted over |")
    strs_push(l, "| Formatting, domains (HTTP, JSON, time, crypto) | PARTIAL | JSON (`@std/json`, N84) and time (`@std/time`, Gate 2) exist; HTTP/1.1 (`@std/http`, v1 C2) and TLS (`@std/tls`, v1 C1), below; HTTP/2 and cryptography MISSING |")
    strs_push(l, "| HTTP/1.1 server, client and router (`@std/http`, v1 track C, C2; `spec.md`, *HTTP*) | PARTIAL — EXPERIMENTAL | Run-verified on the interpreter, LLVM −O0/−O2, Cranelift and the Nazm backend, macOS: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/http.rs` — a 56-request corpus parsed or refused with RFC 9112's status (smuggling framings, bare CR/LF, obs-fold, limits 413/414/431, 505), 1500 seeded damaged requests all values and none a trap, responses read as a client reads them, the writers' framing, URLs, the router (parameters, wildcard, 404, 405 with `allow`), a server and client over loopback (keep-alive, chunked, HEAD, a refused `https` connection reported as `Io`, drain), malformed requests answered on the wire with 400/417/408/505 and pipelining in order, 100-continue, and four concurrent clients served by a task per connection; mutants in `xtask/mutations/mutations.toml` (`c2-*`). Over TLS (C1): `crates/nazm-cli/tests/tls.rs`, `http_is_served_and_fetched_over_tls`, on the compiled tiers — `http_listen_tls` and `http_serve`, `http_connect_tls` with keep-alive and a 40 KB body, the platform's store refusing the test CA (`Tls(Untrusted)`), plain HTTP to a TLS server answered by no response. Not yet: HTTP/2, streamed bodies, the C gate's load, soak and conformance legs; handlers run on one task under `http_serve` because a function value may not cross into a task (`N0321`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| TLS (`@std/tls`, the runtime's `tls` part; v1 track C, C1; `spec.md`, *TLS*) | PARTIAL — EXPERIMENTAL | Run-verified on macOS (aarch64) under LLVM −O0/−O2, Cranelift and the Nazm backend: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/tls.rs`, with a test CA, server certificates, an expired one, a self-signed one and a foreign CA's made at test time by OpenSSL 3's command line — a server and a client over loopback agreeing TLS 1.3 and the server's ALPN preference (and none when they share none), 48 KiB echoed intact across many records, TLS's close seen as the end; the client refusing an expired certificate (`Expired`), another name (`WrongHost`), a self-signed one and an untrusted root (`Untrusted`) and the test CA against the platform's store, the server seeing each as a failed handshake; configurations refused for a key not the certificate's, bytes not PEM and an ALPN name too long; closed, made-up and wrong-generation ids answering `Closed`; the interpreter refusing TLS as a value (`-ENOSYS`), and Windows (`N0830`) and WASI (by name) refusing the build. The engine is OpenSSL 3 over memory BIOs, with the Security framework's `SecTrust` deciding a macOS client's trust; Linux's unit (OpenSSL's own verification and `SSL_set1_host`) was exercised on macOS against Homebrew's OpenSSL through the runtime's entries directly, not on Linux. Mutants `c1-*`, each killed by hand. Windows (C1b): the SChannel unit (`tls::emit_schannel`) compiles for `x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` and links, with the runtime's TLS part and a driver calling every entry, against MinGW-w64's `libsecur32`, `libcrypt32` and `libncrypt` alone — `the_windows_engine_compiles_and_links_with_mingw`, mutants `c1b-*` — **compile- and link-verified only**: the Windows host was unreachable, so it has never run, and a Windows build reaching TLS is still refused (`N0830`); `the_windows_engine_runs_on_a_windows_host` (ignored) is the run that would lift it. Not yet: Windows run-verified, Linux run-verified, the C gate's `testssl.sh`, load and soak legs |")
    strs_push(l, "| A service's operations: calendar time, metrics, configuration, log fields, a drain with a deadline (v1 track C, C4; `spec.md`, *Calendar time*, *Metrics*, *Configuration*, *HTTP*'s drain) | PARTIAL — EXPERIMENTAL | Run-verified on the interpreter, LLVM −O0/−O2, Cranelift and the Nazm backend, macOS: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/service_ops.rs` — known days both ways and every 997th day for ±2000 years there and back, RFC 3339 and HTTP dates written and every refusal read, durations as text to `Duration`'s limits; counters, a gauge and a histogram counted from three tasks and written as Prometheus text with every registration refused that should be; settings from a TOML file and the environment into a derived record, each kind of bad value named; a log record's request, trace and time fields; a drain closing an idle connection at once, a request in flight answered with `connection: close` and one past the deadline closed unanswered, the drain returning at its deadline. Mutants `c4-*`. Not yet: termination signals (`@std/signal`, runtime ABI 38), the C gate's shutdown-under-load leg |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · Functions carry their module's name (`text_split`): `use \"@std/text\" as t;` and")
    strs_push(l, "`t::text_split` qualify them since N49, and a plain import still needs the prefix. The compiler")
    strs_push(l, "written in Nazm resolves `@std` since N102. No networking, cryptography or floating point, by")
    strs_push(l, "decision; a listed item does not change within 1.x (`library/std/API-1.0`). *Until R1 this said")
    strs_push(l, "there were no qualified names and that the compiler written in Nazm reported an `@std` import as a")
    strs_push(l, "missing module — true before N49 and N102.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · None forced by a program: effect polymorphism (N51) lets the higher-order")
    strs_push(l, "helpers take effectful functions, and `@std/sort` sorts by a caller's ordering (N84).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · For v1: met. For the area: a library a real program can be written against")
    strs_push(l, "without reimplementing collections or text handling, with a stability policy past 1.0.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 17. FFI and ABI — VERIFIED as scoped (a practical C ABI subset, N85; native builds on the host)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 2 (2026-10-09)** · *The C foundation* (`general-purpose.md` §23). An export takes and returns")
    strs_push(l, "every fixed-width integer and both floats as their C types, which the header names; with what")
    strs_push(l, "foreign calls already carried, the scalar C ABI every binding generator reads is complete.")
    strs_push(l, "Semantic epoch 41. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/c_foundation.rs` — the header's declarations,")
    strs_push(l, "and the same answers at the edges of every width and both floats from a C program linking the")
    strs_push(l, "static archive and the shared library and from Python's `ctypes`, under both backends.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · N42 (2026-10-01). `extern \"C\" fn name(p: T, …) -> R = \"symbol\";` declares a C")
    strs_push(l, "function by its signature and its C symbol (`crates/nazm-syntax/src/parser.rs`; `extern` is")
    strs_push(l, "contextual, not a keyword); `architecture.md` §7.44 is the constitution, written first, and")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/spec.md` *Foreign functions* the language rule. `nazm build --link FILE` hands objects and")
    strs_push(l, "libraries to the linker. Both backends declare the symbol with the target's C convention and call")
    strs_push(l, "it with no failure check after it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Claim | Status | Evidence |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| A C function is declared and called, with both backends agreeing | VERIFIED | `a_program_calls_c_with_ints_and_bools_and_both_backends_agree` (registers and the stack, `INT64_MAX`, nested calls, C state), clang-compiled fixtures |")
    strs_push(l, "| Only FFI-safe types cross | VERIFIED | `Int` as `int64_t`, `Bool` as zero-extended `bool`; `Str`, sequences, records, enums, capabilities refused, `N0381` (`every_declaration_outside_the_subset_is_refused_by_its_own_code`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| The declaration's shape is checked | VERIFIED | ABI `N0380`, symbol `N0382`, generic or effect-annotated `N0384`, conflicting or runtime-reserved symbol `N0383` in one module and across modules (`two_modules_that_disagree_about_a_symbol_are_refused_before_linking`, `a_reserved_c_symbol_is_every_one_the_runtime_calls`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Calling C is an effect and needs authority | VERIFIED | effect `foreign`; a `ForeignCap` held at every call, declared set or not (`a_foreign_call_needs_a_foreign_cap_everywhere`, `an_imported_foreign_function_needs_a_foreign_cap_too`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| The provenance question | VERIFIED | what C returns carries `unknown` and its arguments' origins; `N0372` for a restricted `write_file` path computed from it (`what_c_returns_carries_the_unknown_origin`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Ownership across the call | VERIFIED | nothing managed crosses; values live across calls are reclaimed on every path, a failure after a foreign call included (`a_foreign_call_inside_managed_code_leaks_nothing`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| The interpreter | VERIFIED (refusal) | `nazm run` refuses a program calling C before running any of it, `N0385` (`nazm_run_refuses_a_foreign_call_before_running_anything`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Link inputs | VERIFIED | `--link` is passed in order; a missing file is refused before compiling; an unresolved symbol is reported as a missing `--link`, not a compiler bug (`the_linker_is_handed_exactly_what_link_names`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Interface and cache | VERIFIED | `nazm.interface/7` carries a foreign export's symbol; semantic epoch 11; the C symbol enters the object key (`the_c_symbol_enters_the_object_key`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Str` arguments (N55) | VERIFIED | a borrowed NUL-terminated copy for the call, freed after it, under both backends with a balanced memory report; a NUL byte refused before C runs, `N0405`; a sequence result still `N0381` (`a_str_crosses_into_c_as_a_borrowed_c_string_under_both_backends`, `a_str_holding_a_nul_is_refused_before_c_runs`, `a_str_result_from_c_is_a_copy_since_n85_and_a_sequence_result_is_still_refused`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Exporting Nazm functions to C (N55) | VERIFIED | `pub extern \"C\" fn … ! {} = \"sym\" { … }`, `Int`/`Bool` only, `N0391` otherwise; one symbol per program (`N0383`); a failure ends the process with status 2 instead of unwinding into C (`an_export_is_public_effect_free_scalar_and_not_generic`, `an_export_symbol_is_defined_once_in_a_program`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Static libraries (N55) | VERIFIED | `nazm build --lib -o OUT.a` with no `main`, and `OUT.h` in a fixed order; a C program links and calls it under both backends; two builds are the same bytes (`a_library_and_its_header_link_into_a_c_program_under_both_backends`, `a_library_is_the_same_bytes_on_every_build_and_needs_no_main`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Opaque handles (N85) | VERIFIED | `extern \"C\" struct Db;`: made only by a foreign result, held in a binding, a record field and a `Vec`, passed back to C, under both backends; built or taken apart `N0611`, `==` `N0304`, into a task `N0321`, through a channel `N0390` (`a_handle_a_c_struct_a_c_string_errno_and_a_callback_cross_under_both_backends`, `every_misuse_of_a_handle_a_c_struct_or_a_callback_is_refused_by_its_code`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nullability (N85) | VERIFIED | `-> Db` and `-> Str` fail the call with `N0409` on null, before Nazm sees it, status 2 under both backends; `-> Option[…]` makes null `None`; `Option[Db]` as an argument `N0381` (`a_null_where_the_declaration_promised_a_value_fails_the_call_with_n0409`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| C-layout structs (N85) | VERIFIED | `extern \"C\" struct P { … }` of `Int`, `Bool`, handles and nested C structs, laid out in declaration order — C reads `flag` at 8 and `y` at 16 whatever order a construction names them in — passed as a `const struct *` to a copy freed after the call (10 000 calls leave the allocator's block count where it was, macOS); any other field, a struct result, a by-value struct `N0381` (`a_struct_passed_to_c_is_a_copy_freed_after_every_call`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Str` results (N85) | VERIFIED | a `const char *` C keeps, copied into an owned `Str` at the call; balanced memory report (`a_handle_a_c_struct_a_c_string_errno_and_a_callback_cross_under_both_backends`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `errno` (N85) | VERIFIED | `c_errno()` is what the latest foreign call on this thread left, captured as the call returns under both backends; needs a `ForeignCap`; refused by `nazm run` (`N0385`) and on freestanding and WebAssembly targets (`N0613`) (`a_program_reading_errno_runs_only_natively_and_only_where_there_is_one`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Callbacks (N85) | VERIFIED | an export's name passed for a `fn(Int) -> Int` parameter is its C entry: C calls it inside the call and from a thread C starts, under both backends; a closure or a non-export `N0612` |")
    strs_push(l, "| Modules and cache (N85) | VERIFIED | a handle and a C struct imported from another module keep what they are through `nazm.interface/9` and the check cache; moving a C struct's fields changes its interface, an ordinary record's does not (`a_handle_and_a_c_struct_keep_what_they_are_across_a_module_boundary_and_in_the_cache`, `a_c_struct_s_field_order_is_its_interface_and_an_ordinary_record_s_is_not`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Shared libraries (N85) | VERIFIED (macOS) | `nazm build --lib --shared`: only the exports are visible (`nm`), named `@rpath/NAME`, linked and run by a C program under both backends; a failure in an export exits 2 (`a_shared_library_links_into_a_c_program_and_shows_only_its_exports`). Linux's `-shared` link is the same command, not run here |")
    strs_push(l, "| Bindings (N85) | VERIFIED | `nazm bindgen` reads incomplete structs and `typedef struct S S;` as handles, complete structs of crossing fields as C structs, `const char *` results as `Option[Str]`; arrays, unions, by-value structs, function pointers and buffers refused by name (`bindgen_reads_handles_structs_and_returned_strings_and_names_what_it_refuses`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Outside the subset | Refused by name | floating point, integers other than `int64_t`, variadics, by-value structs and struct results, unions, arrays, bit-fields, closures as callbacks, out-buffers, `dlopen`, ABIs other than `\"C\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| Other ABIs and cross-target | MISSING | `\"C\"` only; a foreign call builds for every target of the matrix, and runs on the host only (area 33) |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · The subset above, and only it. C is trusted entirely once called: an abort, a loop,")
    strs_push(l, "a use of a freed handle or memory corruption inside it is outside every Nazm guarantee, and nothing")
    strs_push(l, "but a promised non-null is checked after the call. `errno` is per thread: a pool task that blocks")
    strs_push(l, "between a call and `c_errno()` may read another task's. `nazm run` cannot call C, so a program that")
    strs_push(l, "does has one implementation, not two. Shared libraries are linked and run on macOS here; the")
    strs_push(l, "self-hosted compiler reads none of N85's declarations (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · By-value structs and struct results need each target's register rules for")
    strs_push(l, "aggregates; floating point needs the language to have it; closures as callbacks need a `void *`")
    strs_push(l, "environment rule a C API states; `dlopen` would need a handle whose lifetime bounds every function")
    strs_push(l, "taken from it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Met, as scoped (N85): a record and a string cross with their layout and")
    strs_push(l, "ownership stated, in both directions for strings, under both backends, with every shape outside the")
    strs_push(l, "subset refused by name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Domain profiles")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`NAZM_LANGUAGE_GOALS.md` §10 owns what each profile is *for*. `master-architecture.md`")
    strs_push(l, "§4 owns the invariant that makes them profiles rather than dialects, and the ladder a")
    strs_push(l, "profile has to climb to become real. **This section owns what exists**, which is: one")
    strs_push(l, "profile, unnamed, and five ambitions.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**General — PARTIAL.** What `nazm run` and `nazm build` accept today: ambient authority,")
    strs_push(l, "checked arithmetic that traps, structured concurrency over OS threads, and automatic")
    strs_push(l, "reclamation of every heap-backed value with no annotation to write. *That last clause read")
    strs_push(l, "\"no reclamation\" until N8.* It")
    strs_push(l, "is the widest profile and every other is a restriction of it. PARTIAL rather than VERIFIED")
    strs_push(l, "for one reason: **the interpreter's subset and the native subset are not the same** —")
    strs_push(l, "recursion ran under `nazm run` and was refused by both compilers until N49; since, the reference")
    strs_push(l, "compiler builds it and the compiler written in Nazm still refuses it, and the interpreter's")
    strs_push(l, "iteration budget remains its own. A profile whose implementations accept different programs is")
    strs_push(l, "not yet a profile. *Accepted when* the two")
    strs_push(l, "subsets coincide, or the difference is itself declared as a profile boundary rather than")
    strs_push(l, "left as a gap.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Systems — MISSING.** Would need explicit control over allocation and layout, no hidden")
    strs_push(l, "allocation where none is declared, and a stated ABI; would grant raw memory access and")
    strs_push(l, "foreign calls inside a named, narrow boundary. Nothing profile-specific exists. Blocked on")
    strs_push(l, "area 17 (FFI and ABI, PARTIAL: scalars only) and on area 4, which is now VERIFIED for the current type")
    strs_push(l, "universe but says nothing about *explicit* control over allocation and layout — a profile")
    strs_push(l, "that must declare where memory comes from needs more than automatic reclamation. The architectural")
    strs_push(l, "commitment that keeps it reachable — field access stays symbolic until the lowest level, so")
    strs_push(l, "layout selection remains possible — is already honoured and must be preserved rather than")
    strs_push(l, "undone when this profile arrives.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 18. Embedded support — VERIFIED as scoped (two emulated boards, N86)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N86: boards as data, a second architecture — VERIFIED, emulated.** `architecture.md` §7.87 first.")
    strs_push(l, "A board is a description (`nazm_runtime::board::BOARDS`, printed by `nazm inspect` as")
    strs_push(l, "`toolchain.boards`), and its linker script, runtime and entry are generated from it alone")
    strs_push(l, "(`every_board_s_texts_are_generated_from_its_description_and_differ_where_it_does`). The second")
    strs_push(l, "architecture family, `riscv64gc-unknown-none-elf`, boots on QEMU's RISC-V `virt` machine; device")
    strs_push(l, "registers have 8-, 16- and 32-bit accesses. The published support matrix:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Board | Build | Link | Boot (QEMU) | Failure path | Stack: measured ≤ bound | Hardware |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `aarch64-unknown-none`, QEMU `virt` Cortex-A53 | host or container | `ld.lld` | `-O0`, `-O2` | `N0400`, `N0408`, status 2 | 176 ≤ 176, 32 ≤ 48 bytes | no |")
    strs_push(l, "| `riscv64gc-unknown-none-elf`, QEMU `virt` RV64GC, M-mode | container only (needs a RISC-V `clang`; refused by name elsewhere) | `ld.lld` | `-O0`, `-O2` | `N0400`, `N0408`, status 2 | 152 ≤ 160, 32 ≤ 48 bytes | no |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Evidence: the four tests of `crates/nazm-cli/tests/boards.rs` on the host, and its ignored")
    strs_push(l, "`both_boards_boot_and_agree_under_qemu`, run in `nazm-qemu:n86` — `nazm` built from the tree in the")
    strs_push(l, "container, then each board's programs at `-O0` and `-O2`: identical UART output (`HI` and `100`, the")
    strs_push(l, "byte write truncating `0x149` to `I`), the overflow and the exhausted stack each reported with")
    strs_push(l, "status 2; with the stack painted, every measured use within the stated bound")
    strs_push(l, "(`docs/internal/performance-log.md`, N86). **Not claimed**: hardware; atomics and memory orderings, interrupts")
    strs_push(l, "and vectors, a heap or arena (each DESIGNED in §7.87, with the reason it is not built); `.bss`")
    strs_push(l, "zeroing by a loader other than QEMU's; RISC-V on a macOS host's Apple `clang`, which has no RISC-V")
    strs_push(l, "code generator.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N62: a freestanding target — VERIFIED on QEMU's `virt` board, one board.** `aarch64-unknown-none`")
    strs_push(l, "builds to objects and `link.ld`, links with `ld.lld` and boots under `qemu-system-aarch64`: no OS, no")
    strs_push(l, "C library, no heap; device registers through `mmio_read32`/`mmio_write32` under an `MmioCap`. The")
    strs_push(l, "evidence and its limits are in area 33's N62 paragraph. Atomics, interrupts, a heap and `@std` are")
    strs_push(l, "DESIGNED only (§7.64); no hardware was run.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N63: real-time bounds — PARTIAL, an analysable subset.** `architecture.md` §7.65 first. The")
    strs_push(l, "`realtime` profile adds `no-blocking` and `bounded-loops` to `embedded`'s rules and `no-ambient-time`;")
    strs_push(l, "the profile report states each loop's exact trip bound for the counted form, the call depth and the")
    strs_push(l, "site counts, with `wcet` `null`. A board build states a static stack bound from clang's own frame")
    strs_push(l, "sizes along the image's deepest call path (`bounds.json`). Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/realtime.rs` (9 + 1 ignored) — bounds against hand-computed trip counts,")
    strs_push(l, "including the widest `Int` span; every unbounded shape refused as `unknown` with its reason; the")
    strs_push(l, "board's bound equal to its path's frames and the same twice; recursion `null`; the search's own")
    strs_push(l, "four unit tests (`crates/nazm-cli/src/stack.rs`). **Run-checked**, the ignored test in")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-qemu:n62`: three programs at `-O0` and `-O2`, the stack painted, the measured use below the")
    strs_push(l, "stated bound in every run (176/192, 304/320, 264/288 bytes at `-O0`; 24/48 at `-O2`). **Not")
    strs_push(l, "claimed**: WCET, latency or jitter bounds, interrupt nesting, certification; the loop form is one")
    strs_push(l, "form.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it would restrict** · No allocation after startup, or none at all; a stack bound")
    strs_push(l, "that is computed;**What it would restrict** · No allocation after startup, or none at all; a stack bound")
    strs_push(l, "that is computed; no I/O except through declared capabilities; a freestanding target with")
    strs_push(l, "no libc.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence of absence** · No cross-compilation, no target triple handling, no freestanding")
    strs_push(l, "target, no `no_std` equivalent, no control over allocation. `crates/nazm-cli/src/build/`")
    strs_push(l, "emits a module with no triple and lets `clang` supply the host's. The emitted runtime")
    strs_push(l, "declares 18 libc and pthread symbols and cannot currently be built without them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N47: the `embedded` profile — PARTIAL.** *N47, 2026-10-01: restriction profiles v1 (`architecture.md` §7.49).* `--profile NAME` on `check`,")
    strs_push(l, "`build` and `run`, or `profile = \"NAME\"` in any package manifest of the build; rules read semantic")
    strs_push(l, "facts only — `main`'s required effect set, each function's declared contract, the build's lock —")
    strs_push(l, "and refuse with `N0510` and witnesses; `nazm check --profile-report` prints the deterministic")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.profile-report/1`, marked compiler evidence and not certification. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/profiles.rs` — every profile's verdicts on one program, the chain of calls")
    strs_push(l, "in a refusal, the ambient bridge refused, foreign calls refused, `io` seen through a standard")
    strs_push(l, "wrapper, a locked package build satisfying the build rule and a tampered one not, a dependency's")
    strs_push(l, "required profile holding the whole program, a profile never changing what runs nor its verdict")
    strs_push(l, "being cached, and the report's bytes and outcome. `embedded` refuses `io` and `spawn` —")
    strs_push(l, "no operating-system services, no scheduler — and allows `foreign`, the way hardware is reached.")
    strs_push(l, "It does **not** bound the stack, and there is still no freestanding target, so a program it")
    strs_push(l, "accepts still links the host's C library. *N52, 2026-10-02:* allocation is no longer untracked —")
    strs_push(l, "`embedded` gains `bounded-allocation`, refusing an allocation site whose count per call is")
    strs_push(l, "`unknown` (inside a loop), read off MIR by `nazm_mir::cost`; a per-byte bound is not claimed")
    strs_push(l, "(`profiles_read_resource_and_flow_facts`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · Cross-compilation (area 33), then a freestanding runtime — which")
    strs_push(l, "means area 13. *This clause added \"and therefore area 4\" with the sentence \"A language that")
    strs_push(l, "never frees cannot run on a device with kilobytes.\" The first half of that is closed since")
    strs_push(l, "N8; the second is not, because the profile's real requirement is \"no allocation after")
    strs_push(l, "startup, or none at all\", and reclaiming what you allocate is not the same as not")
    strs_push(l, "allocating.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · A program runs on a target with no libc, within a stack bound that was")
    strs_push(l, "computed rather than hoped for. Native frame counts do not bound stack bytes, and that")
    strs_push(l, "obligation is inherited here.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 19. Critical profile — VERIFIED as scoped (enforcement and evidence, N87; not certification)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N87: contracts and the obligation census — VERIFIED, as enforcement and evidence.**")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.88 first. `requires` and `ensures` clauses, checked as a function is entered and")
    strs_push(l, "on every return path (its tail, `return`, `?`) identically by `nazm run` and both backends (`N0410`,")
    strs_push(l, "`N0411`), never compiled out; a call of literals proved or refused at compile time (`N0615`); a clause")
    strs_push(l, "only of what cannot fail for want of authority or memory (`N0614`). `nazm obligations` prints")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.obligations/1`: every contract clause, call of a function with a precondition, overflow,")
    strs_push(l, "division, index, allocation, call through a function value and call into C, each `proved` (with its")
    strs_push(l, "witness), `checked` as the program runs, or `unknown`. `critical` adds `no-unknown-calls`, so with")
    strs_push(l, "`no-foreign` every obligation of an accepted program is proved or checked. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/contracts.rs` (11) — the three tiers agreeing on holds and failures, a `?`")
    strs_push(l, "leaving through a postcondition, a `Str` result reclaimed, a failing clause failing the call, the")
    strs_push(l, "literal proof and refusal, the clause shape, the census's exact rows and bytes, the profile rule, a")
    strs_push(l, "callee's preconditions reaching an importer through `nazm.interface/10` and the cache, the formatter;")
    strs_push(l, "`examples/contracts/` (an integer square root and a ledger). **Not claimed**: loop invariants or")
    strs_push(l, "ranges as declarations, any proof beyond evaluating a literal call, absence of runtime error beyond")
    strs_push(l, "the census's own `proved` entries, and certification against any standard — the next paragraph stands.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Read this before the rest.** This profile is an architectural intention. It is **not** a")
    strs_push(l, "claim that Nazm is suitable for any safety-related, airborne, medical, automotive or")
    strs_push(l, "otherwise regulated use; it is not a certification path; and no artefact in this repository")
    strs_push(l, "has been produced under a safety standard or assessed against one. **The architecture")
    strs_push(l, "anticipating a Critical profile is not evidence for one.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it would restrict** · No dynamic allocation, no recursion, bounded loops with an")
    strs_push(l, "established bound, total functions, and every failure mode enumerated rather than trapped;")
    strs_push(l, "contracts and invariants checked rather than asserted.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N97, 2026-10-04: formal semantics v2 — PARTIAL (bounded, machine-checked; proofs BLOCKED).*")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.98 first. `nazm.formal-core/2` (`docs/internal/formal-core.md` §2,")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-formal/src/statements.rs`): `let mut`, assignment, `while`, `if` statements, `return` and")
    strs_push(l, "one recursive function over `Int`, big-step with fuel. Over all 12,900 programs of a stated bound")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-formal/tests/statements.rs`): never stuck, deterministic, accepted by the checker, and")
    strs_push(l, "for the 11,137 the model finishes — 3,194 of them traps — the interpreter's value or trap is the")
    strs_push(l, "model's; 1,763 run out of fuel and are not compared. **Proofs BLOCKED**: no proof assistant or solver")
    strs_push(l, "is installed and none can be installed offline, so progress, preservation, effect soundness and flow")
    strs_push(l, "properties are not proved. Phase B (ownership, effects, flows) and Phase C (concurrency, refinement)")
    strs_push(l, "are not modelled. Two mutants of the model's own rules, each caught by the correspondence.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N61, 2026-10-02: a formal core — PARTIAL (bounded, machine-checked; no proof).* `docs/internal/formal-core.md`")
    strs_push(l, "states integers and booleans with traps, comparison, short-circuit `&&`, `if` and `let` by typing and")
    strs_push(l, "big-step rules; `crates/nazm-formal` transcribes them with no dependency on the compiler, and")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-formal/tests/exhaustive.rs` checks five properties over **every** program of the core")
    strs_push(l, "up to five nodes — 94,352 programs, 28,238 well-typed (27,680 before R1a made `<` on `Bool` well typed): soundness (never stuck, the right type),")
    strs_push(l, "determinism, checked arithmetic against 128-bit integers, the interpreter's outcome equal to the")
    strs_push(l, "rules' for every typed program, and the checker accepting exactly what the rules type. The check's")
    strs_push(l, "first run found an error in the formal transcription, not the compiler — `i64::MIN % -1` is 0 by")
    strs_push(l, "the spec, and the transcription trapped — which is the correspondence working in both directions.")
    strs_push(l, "No proof assistant, nothing beyond the bound, no function, loop, string, effect or backend in the core.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N60, 2026-10-02: restriction profiles v2 — VERIFIED for the rules named.* `architecture.md` §7.62")
    strs_push(l, "first. A verdict is `pass`, `fail` or `unknown`, `unknown` refused and reported as such.")
    strs_push(l, "`embedded` adds `no-recursion` — a cycle of MIR's direct call and spawn edges, each function in it")
    strs_push(l, "named; `unknown` where a call goes through a function value — and `critical` adds `no-select`, by")
    strs_push(l, "call site, so with `no-spawn` and `no-ambient-time` a `critical` program's behaviour is a function of")
    strs_push(l, "its inputs. Composition: a dependency declaring `general` does not weaken a root requiring")
    strs_push(l, "`embedded`. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/profiles_v2.rs` (4), the profile tables in")
    strs_push(l, "`profiles.rs`; overhead on `compiler/emit.nz`: `general` 652, `critical` 653, `embedded` 739 ms")
    strs_push(l, "(medians of five). Constant-time rules are RESEARCH; bounded loops, queues and tasks are N63's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What `--profile critical` enforces now** · *N47, 2026-10-01: restriction profiles v1 (`architecture.md` §7.49).* `--profile NAME` on `check`,")
    strs_push(l, "`build` and `run`, or `profile = \"NAME\"` in any package manifest of the build; rules read semantic")
    strs_push(l, "facts only — `main`'s required effect set, each function's declared contract, the build's lock —")
    strs_push(l, "and refuse with `N0510` and witnesses; `nazm check --profile-report` prints the deterministic")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.profile-report/1`, marked compiler evidence and not certification. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/profiles.rs` — every profile's verdicts on one program, the chain of calls")
    strs_push(l, "in a refusal, the ambient bridge refused, foreign calls refused, `io` seen through a standard")
    strs_push(l, "wrapper, a locked package build satisfying the build rule and a tampered one not, a dependency's")
    strs_push(l, "required profile holding the whole program, a profile never changing what runs nor its verdict")
    strs_push(l, "being cached, and the report's bytes and outcome. `critical` requires every function of the")
    strs_push(l, "program to declare its effect set (no ambient bridge), forbids `spawn` and `foreign`, and requires a")
    strs_push(l, "package build held to its lockfile. Nothing about allocation, loop bounds, totality or contracts:")
    strs_push(l, "those stay DESIGNED, and the disclaimer above stands in full.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What exists that is genuinely relevant** · Three things, and they are real. Arithmetic is")
    strs_push(l, "**specified rather than inherited from the hardware** — overflow traps, and")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-lir/src/op/llvm.rs` refuses `nsw` so no optimiser may delete the check. Recursion was")
    strs_push(l, "refused by both compilers until N49; it now compiles with a stack guard (`N0408`), so a profile")
    strs_push(l, "that wants it refused would need a rule of its own (none exists yet). Everything outside a backend's coverage is **refused by")
    strs_push(l, "name with a span**, never silently approximated or partially compiled.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Missing prerequisites** · A memory model; effects; contracts; a bounded-stack story; and")
    strs_push(l, "a qualified toolchain, which the bootstrap explicitly does **not** provide — `docs/internal/bootstrap.md`")
    strs_push(l, "§4 puts compiler trustworthiness on the list of things a fixpoint does not establish.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · A proof obligation is discharged on a real Nazm program and assessed")
    strs_push(l, "against a named standard by someone qualified to make that assessment. Not a test count.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 20. Cybersecurity profile — VERIFIED as scoped (enforcement, N87; not certification)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N87: `cyber` v3.** `cyber` adds `no-unknown-calls` to declared effects, no C, a locked build,")
    strs_push(l, "contents kept in files (N52) and checked paths (N80): no call reaches a callee, or a contract, the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler does not know. Every obligation of an accepted program is proved or checked")
    strs_push(l, "(`critical_and_cyber_refuse_an_obligation_of_unknown_status`). **Constant time stays RESEARCH**: the")
    strs_push(l, "one subset precise enough to state needs secrets in the type system, which provenance tracks only to")
    strs_push(l, "its sinks (§7.88). Dynamic loading has no construct to refuse (§7.86). Not a sandbox, and not")
    strs_push(l, "certification.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it would restrict** · Untrusted input tracked to its uses; declassification")
    strs_push(l, "explicit and audited; no ambient authority; constant-time obligations honoured where they")
    strs_push(l, "are declared.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · The one real ingredient present is refuse-by-name-with-a-span rather than")
    strs_push(l, "silent degradation, and failures that are diagnostics rather than undefined behaviour.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N47: `--profile cyber`** · *N47, 2026-10-01: restriction profiles v1 (`architecture.md` §7.49).* `--profile NAME` on `check`,")
    strs_push(l, "`build` and `run`, or `profile = \"NAME\"` in any package manifest of the build; rules read semantic")
    strs_push(l, "facts only — `main`'s required effect set, each function's declared contract, the build's lock —")
    strs_push(l, "and refuse with `N0510` and witnesses; `nazm check --profile-report` prints the deterministic")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.profile-report/1`, marked compiler evidence and not certification. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/profiles.rs` — every profile's verdicts on one program, the chain of calls")
    strs_push(l, "in a refusal, the ambient bridge refused, foreign calls refused, `io` seen through a standard")
    strs_push(l, "wrapper, a locked package build satisfying the build rule and a tampered one not, a dependency's")
    strs_push(l, "required profile holding the whole program, a profile never changing what runs nor its verdict")
    strs_push(l, "being cached, and the report's bytes and outcome. `cyber` requires declared effect sets everywhere — so no")
    strs_push(l, "ambient authority, and N38's restricted flow (`N0372`) applies to every function — forbids")
    strs_push(l, "`foreign`, and requires a locked, integrity-checked package build. Capabilities (area 6, N37) and")
    strs_push(l, "information flow (area 7, N38) are what it rests on. It is not a sandbox, it does not make a")
    strs_push(l, "program secure, and it claims nothing about side channels, constant time or declassification.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · Untrusted input is tracked only to `write_file` paths (N38); there is no")
    strs_push(l, "declassification and no constant-time rule.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · More sinks and an explicit declassification, in N38's framework.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Untrusted input is tracked to its uses and declassification is explicit")
    strs_push(l, "and audited, with the approximation's blind spots stated.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 21. AI/HPC — PARTIAL")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N88, 2026-10-04: maps of one or two sequences, reductions, a numeric oracle — VERIFIED on one GPU;")
    strs_push(l, "the area stays PARTIAL.* `architecture.md` §7.89 first. A kernel is `(Int) -> Int` (a map) or")
    strs_push(l, "`(Int, Int) -> Int` (a zip over two inputs of one length); `--reduce add|min|max` folds the results")
    strs_push(l, "in index order on the host, `add` checked as `ints_sum` is. Every run held to the interpreter —")
    strs_push(l, "results and fold. Evidence, `crates/nazm-cli/tests/accel.rs`: on any host, the zip's two-buffer")
    strs_push(l, "kernel and its refusals before a device (arity, unequal lengths); on the M1 Pro (ignored, run by")
    strs_push(l, "hand), a zip and each reduction agreeing with the interpreter and with an independent computation,")
    strs_push(l, "`add` failing at the running sum's overflow, and **40 generated kernels** over `+ - * / %`, `if`")
    strs_push(l, "and literals at `Int`'s edges, 200 elements each, agreeing with the interpreter and with the spec's")
    strs_push(l, "arithmetic in 128 bits — values, or the lowest failing index and its code. **Why still PARTIAL**: one")
    strs_push(l, "provider, OpenCL on macOS, deprecated by its vendor — a second (Metal, SPIR-V) is BLOCKED here for")
    strs_push(l, "want of a toolchain (no Metal compiler, no Vulkan loader), not of a design; vector operations in LIR")
    strs_push(l, "are DESIGNED, the one vectorised loop (N66) still a pattern; and the measured workload (N88,")
    strs_push(l, "`performance.md`) is one a native CPU loop serves faster than the device and its transfers, so the")
    strs_push(l, "row's acceptance — a workload a CPU cannot serve — is unmet.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N67, 2026-10-02: accelerator kernels — VERIFIED on one GPU, OpenCL on an Apple M1 Pro.*")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.69 first. `nazm accel FILE KERNEL --input FILE` runs a pure `(Int) -> Int`")
    strs_push(l, "function — and the functions it calls — as an OpenCL C kernel generated from Core IR, over up to")
    strs_push(l, "8,000,000 `Int`s; checked arithmetic is carried, and a failure is the lowest failing index's at its")
    strs_push(l, "site, as a sequential map's. Ineligible functions are refused by name before any device (`N0394`).")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.accel/1` names the device, both transfers with their bytes and time, the one")
    strs_push(l, "synchronisation, the build and run times, the kernel's identity (`nazm.kernel/1`), and whether the")
    strs_push(l, "results agree with the interpreter's, which they are always held to unless `--no-check`. Evidence,")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/accel.rs` (3 on any host — the kernel's checked operations and failure rule,")
    strs_push(l, "six refusals, bad input; 2 ignored, run on the M1 Pro — 20,000 Collatz kernels agreeing with the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter and with an independent Rust computation, transfer bytes, identity stable and distinct;")
    strs_push(l, "the lowest failing index for overflow and division by zero, `i64::MIN` edges). Measured")
    strs_push(l, "(`performance.md`, N67): 1,000,000 elements in 23–30 ms on the GPU plus 3–6 ms of transfers, against")
    strs_push(l, "190 ms on one CPU core. **Limitation**: one API on one vendor's GPU, deprecated by that vendor; maps")
    strs_push(l, "of `Int` only; no kernels in the language; no layout specialisation or occupancy; Linux and CI cannot")
    strs_push(l, "run it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence of absence (before N66)** · No tensors, no GPU path, no vectorisation work, no measurement.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · A reason. `architecture.md` §1 says MLIR should be revisited *only")
    strs_push(l, "if* Nazm pivots toward tensor/accelerator codegen, and nothing proposes that pivot.")
    strs_push(l, "Treating this as a profile rather than a declined direction is itself the open question,")
    strs_push(l, "tracked as R7 in `research-register.md`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · A workload the project actually has, that a CPU backend cannot serve.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Tooling")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 22. Diagnostics — VERIFIED")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · `crates/nazm-diag/src/lib.rs` — the stable codes (33 when this row was written, at N31; far more since — `docs/user/diagnostics.md` lists them), byte-offset spans, a")
    strs_push(l, "versioned JSON schema `schema/nazm.diagnostic-1.json` emitted per object. Conformance is")
    strs_push(l, "tested against real binary output in `crates/nazm-cli/tests/schemas.rs`, and")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/codes.rs` requires every declared code to be provoked by a test or")
    strs_push(l, "listed as unprovokable with a written reason. The capability inventory")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-cli/src/capabilities.rs`) is read from the compiler's own tables, and")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/diagnostics.md` states the compatibility contract.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N30, 2026-09-28: Compact Diagnostic Index v1, `nazm.diagnostic-index/1` — VERIFIED; Diagnostic")
    strs_push(l, "Detail v1, `nazm.diagnostic-detail/1` — VERIFIED; G74, G75, G77 — PARTIAL.* An index")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-service/src/diagnostics.rs`, `architecture.md` §7.32) is every current diagnostic")
    strs_push(l, "of a root compilation as compiler-owned facts — `code@file:start-end#n` id, code, severity, file")
    strs_push(l, "and UTF-8 byte range, owning durable definition, fix counts by applicability — with no prose,")
    strs_push(l, "bound to a digest of the loaded sources and, where N28 has one, the snapshot; detail is one")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostic exactly as `nazm.diagnostic/1` publishes it, its places in their files, and for each")
    strs_push(l, "fix the N29 selector where a semantic patch is plannable. Compact diagnostics never infer")
    strs_push(l, "structured semantics from diagnostic prose; a compiler fix and an N29 semantic patch are distinct")
    strs_push(l, "capabilities. The goals are partial because no diagnostic carries typed expected/actual/entity")
    strs_push(l, "facts (`facts: \"unavailable\"`), only the compact and detail levels exist, and there is no")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostic history. Evidence: `crates/nazm-service/tests/diagnostics.rs` — an index with no")
    strs_push(l, "sentence the compiler wrote in it, ordered by place, owned by `main`; each detail the canonical")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostic with the index's code, place and owner; lexer and parser errors, a missing `;`, an")
    strs_push(l, "unterminated string and a mutable parameter indexed with no snapshot and no owner, their compiler")
    strs_push(l, "fixes no semantic patches; an automatic and a needs-review fix counted by applicability, each")
    strs_push(l, "detail's selector planning exactly that patch through N29; one code twice in one file and across")
    strs_push(l, "files as distinct ids, `lib.nz`'s places its own and its published offsets the concatenation's; a")
    strs_push(l, "`+` after `é😀` at its byte offset, not its character index; a fake id refused, and after a move, a")
    strs_push(l, "repair or another state every old id `stale_state`; byte-identical indexes from another directory,")
    strs_push(l, "an edit in an imported file a new state, a broken file nothing imports absent, and two roots over")
    strs_push(l, "one file each their own; unknown name, type mismatch, arity, visibility, a refused duplicate")
    strs_push(l, "(no owner), a generic mismatch, an unsatisfied requirement and a task capture each indexed with")
    strs_push(l, "its owner and detail; and 500 index and detail pairs leaving retained state unchanged. The unit")
    strs_push(l, "tests tell two structurally identical diagnostics apart by ordinal alone and show rewording a")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostic changes no index byte. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/schemas.rs` the real command's indexes")
    strs_push(l, "and details valid against their schemas, every detail's diagnostic equal to a line of `nazm check")
    strs_push(l, "--json` and valid as `nazm.diagnostic/1`. `crates/nazm-mcp/tests/protocol.rs` the real server:")
    strs_push(l, "six read-only tools, index and detail equal to the service's, the index carried once, no root or")
    strs_push(l, "file argument accepted, a stale id after an edit, syntax errors indexed, and 1,000 calls through")
    strs_push(l, "edits and repairs with flat resident memory. Eighteen N30 mutations (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · *At N31:* two codes were unprovokable by construction, and spans were offsets")
    strs_push(l, "into a merged buffer, so file identity was recovered rather than carried. *Since:* one code is")
    strs_push(l, "unprovokable, and a span carries its file (`FileId`, area 2) — published spans are offsets into the")
    strs_push(l, "files' concatenation; the N30 index and")
    strs_push(l, "detail recover it, by the same source map. No diagnostic carries typed facts, and the index is a")
    strs_push(l, "module's analysis — a missing `main` (`N0204`) is `nazm check`'s, not the index's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · None.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Met.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 23. Formatter — VERIFIED")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · `crates/nazm-syntax/src/format.rs`, token-driven so comments survive, with")
    strs_push(l, "no options by design. `crates/nazm-syntax/tests/format.rs` asserts on every input that")
    strs_push(l, "tokens are unchanged, that `format(format(x)) == format(x)`, that comments are identical,")
    strs_push(l, "and that output ends in exactly one newline — applied to every `.nz` in the tree and to 15")
    strs_push(l, "hand-written ugly inputs.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · No reflow, no reordering, no insertion. Per file, not per merged program.")
    strs_push(l, "Canonical in the sense of \"one output\". Since N15 a lossless tree exists (area 1), and the")
    strs_push(l, "formatter reads its comments from the same scan the tree is built from, but it still lays")
    strs_push(l, "out from tokens rather than from the tree.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · None for formatting; edits are a separate item.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Met for formatting.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 24. Machine-applicable fixes — VERIFIED")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · `crates/nazm-cli/src/fix.rs`, schema `schema/nazm.fix-1.json`. Only")
    strs_push(l, "`Automatic` fixes apply; nothing is written without `--apply`; edits apply right-to-left;")
    strs_push(l, "overlaps are skipped; and a result that no longer parses is rolled back wholesale. Ten")
    strs_push(l, "workflow tests in `crates/nazm-cli/tests/workflow.rs`. *N24, 2026-09-26:* the code has")
    strs_push(l, "**seven** skip reasons, not the four this entry used to count, and each is now reached by its")
    strs_push(l, "own unit test in `fix.rs` — `write_back` reads and writes through injected functions, so an")
    strs_push(l, "unreadable and an unwritable file are arranged rather than hoped for: a fix that needs review")
    strs_push(l, "(`it needs review`), an unreadable file, two overlapping edits (the later applied, the earlier")
    strs_push(l, "skipped, and exactly the one written), a span past the end and one inside a character (`the")
    strs_push(l, "span does not name a range of this file`), bytes that are no longer the ones checked (nothing")
    strs_push(l, "written), a result that does not parse (nothing written), and a failed write (not reported")
    strs_push(l, "applied). Each asserts the exact `skipped` text. `docs/user/diagnostics.md` lists the seven. The")
    strs_push(l, "same fixes reach an editor as quick fixes (area 25), a distinct consumer of one fix contract.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · Stale-edit protection is by expected-bytes comparison, not a file hash or")
    strs_push(l, "document version — which is what a command that reads and writes a file in one run needs.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · None.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Each skip reason has a test that reaches it: met, 2026-09-26 (N24), for")
    strs_push(l, "the seven the code has.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 25. LSP — PARTIAL · MCP — PARTIAL")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · *N16, 2026-09-25.* `nazm lsp` serves the Language Server Protocol over stdio")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-cli/src/lsp.rs`) as an adapter over a protocol-independent language service")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-service/src/service.rs`, `architecture.md` §7.18) that answers from the loader,")
    strs_push(l, "parser, checker and resolution every command uses — nothing is re-implemented, and the")
    strs_push(l, "layering and `one resolver` gates keep it so. Open buffers are the source: they override the")
    strs_push(l, "disk for every compilation, an unsaved dependency is what its importer sees, closing a buffer")
    strs_push(l, "gives the file back to the disk, and an unsaved `use` changes the graph. Diagnostics keep")
    strs_push(l, "their Nazm codes and are published per version, an empty set included. Definition follows the")
    strs_push(l, "resolution's identities — calls, locals (by slot), record constructions, variants, fields and")
    strs_push(l, "payload fields — across files; hover shows a function's declared signature or a local's type,")
    strs_push(l, "from the same resolution. Positions are converted between byte offsets and UTF-16 at the")
    strs_push(l, "adapter boundary only. Evidence: `crates/nazm-service/tests/service.rs` (overlays, close,")
    strs_push(l, "import edits, versions, a broken buffer never answering from the clean one, every definition")
    strs_push(l, "category, a spelling with three meanings, the prelude, the cursor rule, the service's")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostics equal to the command line's over every example and multi-module conformance")
    strs_push(l, "program, a thousand edits with constant retained state); `crates/nazm-cli/tests/lsp.rs` (the")
    strs_push(l, "real process over real framing — handshake, exact capability set, diagnostics and definition")
    strs_push(l, "in UTF-16 after `é→😀`, an unsaved dependency and its close, unimplemented methods refused,")
    strs_push(l, "malformed source and a malformed frame without a panic, stdout nothing but frames); the")
    strs_push(l, "position unit tests in `lsp.rs`. Fourteen N16 mutations were caught with verified killers")
    strs_push(l, "(area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N17, 2026-09-25: references — VERIFIED as a sub-capability.* `textDocument/references` and")
    strs_push(l, "`LanguageService::references` answer from one reference index per analysis")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-sema/src/references.rs`, `architecture.md` §7.19): the resolution read backwards,")
    strs_push(l, "with no name resolved again. Functions, locals (parameters, `let`s, pattern bindings, by slot")
    strs_push(l, "of a function), records (their constructions), variants, fields (projections, assignments and")
    strs_push(l, "construction labels) and payload fields; across files and across every open compilation that")
    strs_push(l, "loads the declaring file; from unsaved buffers; declaration apart from uses, combined only for")
    strs_push(l, "`includeDeclaration`; ordered by file and position, each occurrence once. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-service/tests/references.rs` — one spelling given to a function, a parameter, two")
    strs_push(l, "shadowing `let`s, fields of two records, variants of two enums and private functions of two")
    strs_push(l, "modules, each its own set asked from every one of its occurrences; definition and references")
    strs_push(l, "agreeing at every byte of every file; shadowing; a generic record's field through two")
    strs_push(l, "instances; the unsaved program (a use added, removed, moved to another same-named entity, and")
    strs_push(l, "the disk back on close); a broken buffer; only analysed programs searched; unsupported")
    strs_push(l, "positions; the prelude; a thousand edits with constant retained state; and, over 40")
    strs_push(l, "compilations of the repository's own source (the compiler, the conformance programs, the")
    strs_push(l, "examples), every resolved name token in exactly one entity's set and the service's answer equal")
    strs_push(l, "to the command line's resolution read backwards. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/lsp.rs` adds the real")
    strs_push(l, "process: the capability, UTF-16 after `é→😀` on both the query and the answers, an unsaved")
    strs_push(l, "edit, and the same answer with a warm semantic cache beside the sources and without one.")
    strs_push(l, "Sixteen N17 mutations, all caught at tier 1 (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N18, 2026-09-25: rename — VERIFIED for locals and private definitions only.*")
    strs_push(l, "`textDocument/prepareRename` and `textDocument/rename` over `LanguageService::rename`'s")
    strs_push(l, "validated plan (`crates/nazm-service/src/rename.rs`, `architecture.md` §7.20). Renameable:")
    strs_push(l, "parameters, `let`s and pattern bindings; and private functions, records, enums, and the fields,")
    strs_push(l, "variants and payload fields of private records and enums. The proof of completeness is the")
    strs_push(l, "language's own: a local is written only in its body, and a private entity only in its module")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0337` keeps private types out of public signatures), in a clean analysis whose every written")
    strs_push(l, "type name, qualifier, label and use the checker now records — type names and enum qualifiers")
    strs_push(l, "since N18. Every plan's candidate program is re-checked in memory in every open compilation")
    strs_push(l, "containing the edited file and must partition its occurrences into entities exactly as before.")
    strs_push(l, "Refused: exported entities (their importers cannot be known), core-prelude entities, built-ins")
    strs_push(l, "and type parameters, programs with errors, a name the lexer does not read as one identifier,")
    strs_push(l, "and every collision or capture the checker or the partition finds. The protocol edit is")
    strs_push(l, "versioned `documentChanges` only, only for a client that accepts them, and only when every file")
    strs_push(l, "the plan edits is open. Evidence: `crates/nazm-service/tests/rename.rs` — a type rename through")
    strs_push(l, "declaration, parameter, return, field, payload, nested generic argument, construction and")
    strs_push(l, "qualifiers, stated as the exact edited text; one rename from any occurrence; definition on a")
    strs_push(l, "type annotation and on a qualifier; same-spelled locals, fields, variants and a record and a")
    strs_push(l, "function of one name renamed apart; an enum, its variant, its payload field and the pattern")
    strs_push(l, "local bound to it, apart; capture and collision refused and legal shadowing accepted; built-in")
    strs_push(l, "names; invalid names; non-entities and the prelude; a program with errors; private accepted and")
    strs_push(l, "exported refused across modules, and a private rename validated in the importer's compilation;")
    strs_push(l, "stale plans by generation, version and text; a thousand plans with constant retained state.")
    strs_push(l, "`references.rs` adds the corpus gate — every name token of every clean compilation of the")
    strs_push(l, "repository indexed or explicitly a non-entity. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/lsp.rs` adds the real")
    strs_push(l, "process: the capability, prepare-rename's range and placeholder, refusals as `null`, a versioned")
    strs_push(l, "edit with every range in UTF-16 after `é→😀`, an unsaved edit's new version, refusals with")
    strs_push(l, "reasons, and a client without versioned edits refused. Fourteen N18 mutations, all caught at")
    strs_push(l, "tier 1 (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N19, 2026-09-25: completion — VERIFIED for identifier completion in value, call-head and type")
    strs_push(l, "contexts only.* `LanguageService::scope_at` answers what may be written at any position, and")
    strs_push(l, "`completion` and `textDocument/completion` complete the identifier under the cursor, from a")
    strs_push(l, "`ScopeTrace` the checker writes as it pushes scopes, defines bindings and builds environments")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-sema/src/scope.rs`, `architecture.md` §7.21) — with no lookup of its own. Values")
    strs_push(l, "are locals (parameters, `let`s, pattern bindings), visible from where the checker introduced")
    strs_push(l, "them and hidden where it recorded a nearer binding hiding them; calls are the module's")
    strs_push(l, "functions, its direct imports' exports and the built-ins (`Intrinsic::ALL`); types are type")
    strs_push(l, "parameters in their own definition, the module's and its direct imports' records and enums,")
    strs_push(l, "and the built-in types (`Type::ALL`, `Vec`). A name the checker refused (an ambiguous import, a")
    strs_push(l, "collision, a same-scope duplicate) is offered as nothing. A position whose function needed")
    strs_push(l, "syntax recovery has no locals, and a compilation with any recovery has no function or type")
    strs_push(l, "completion. Invoked only (no trigger characters), `resolveProvider` false, `isIncomplete`")
    strs_push(l, "false. Evidence: `crates/nazm-service/tests/completion.rs` — one spelling as a record, a")
    strs_push(l, "function, a parameter and a shadowing `let`, each offered only in its own context and scope;")
    strs_push(l, "later locals absent, a `let` absent from its own initializer, loop, branch, `scope` and arm")
    strs_push(l, "bindings not leaking, sibling arms apart; a later top-level function callable; type parameters")
    strs_push(l, "in their own definition only; built-ins from the compiler's inventories and none spelled in the")
    strs_push(l, "service; direct imports' exports only — no private, no transitive; an ambiguous import offering")
    strs_push(l, "neither; another open program never mixed in; unsaved locals, imports and dependencies, and the")
    strs_push(l, "disk back on close; recovery refused, type errors not; non-sites refused; a thousand edits with")
    strs_push(l, "constant retained state; and over the repository's own clean compilations every one of 23,821")
    strs_push(l, "resolved names offered, once, as exactly what it resolved to. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/lsp.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "adds the real process: the capability, the whole identifier replaced in UTF-16 after `é😀`, a")
    strs_push(l, "built-in call head by prefix, a string refused, an unsaved local. Fourteen N19 mutations (area")
    strs_push(l, "30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N20, 2026-09-26: signature help — VERIFIED for calls of user functions (the module's own and")
    strs_push(l, "imported ones), generic instantiations (written and inferred) and built-ins, and for `spawn`.*")
    strs_push(l, "`LanguageService::call_at` and `signature_help`, and `textDocument/signatureHelp`, report the")
    strs_push(l, "call whose argument list holds the position from a `CheckedCall` the checker records wherever")
    strs_push(l, "it checks a call against a resolved callee (`Resolution::checked_call`, `architecture.md`")
    strs_push(l, "§7.22): the callee, the argument spans, the parameter and return types the environment gave —")
    strs_push(l, "an import's from its interface — and what a generic call settled. The tree decides only which")
    strs_push(l, "argument list holds the position (innermost by nesting) and which argument (that list's own")
    strs_push(l, "commas). Too few or too many arguments and wrong argument types still answer; an unresolved")
    strs_push(l, "callee, a record or variant construction, a position outside any argument list and a")
    strs_push(l, "compilation with any syntax recovery do not. One `Signature` and one renderer serve hover,")
    strs_push(l, "completion and signature help. Triggered by `(` and `,`, no retrigger characters, one")
    strs_push(l, "signature, parameters as UTF-16 label offsets; `null` past the last parameter; no active")
    strs_push(l, "parameter for a callee with none. Evidence: `crates/nazm-service/tests/signature.rs` — a record,")
    strs_push(l, "a function, a local and another module's private function sharing a spelling, each call shown")
    strs_push(l, "as the function it resolved to (by declaration, through the reference index); a generic call")
    strs_push(l, "inferred and written, with its settled arguments; a built-in; `[T: Equality]`; a zero-parameter")
    strs_push(l, "call; a construction refused; twenty-two positions across nested calls, strings, comments,")
    strs_push(l, "parenthesised arguments, constructions and nested type arguments, each with its exact active")
    strs_push(l, "parameter; too few, too many, wrong types, an unresolved callee, a `spawn`; a stale version, a")
    strs_push(l, "broken and a repaired source, a recovery elsewhere in the file, an unsaved and then closed")
    strs_push(l, "dependency signature, another open program; a thousand edits with constant retained state and")
    strs_push(l, "checked-call count; hover and signature help rendering one signature; a structural test that")
    strs_push(l, "the module looks nothing up and substitutes nothing; and over the repository's own clean")
    strs_push(l, "compilations 9,030 calls (71 generic) whose record is the resolution's callee with the")
    strs_push(l, "declaring signature and the backend's type arguments, 4,814 of them asked of the service.")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/durable_identity.rs` adds a call checked against a deserialised interface")
    strs_push(l, "with the dependency deleted, recorded with the interface's signature. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/lsp.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "adds the real process: the capability, label offsets, a comma inside a string after `😀`, a")
    strs_push(l, "nested built-in, no active parameter, `null` past the end and outside the call, an unsaved edit.")
    strs_push(l, "Fourteen N20 mutations (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N21, 2026-09-26: structure completion and constructor signature help — VERIFIED for member")
    strs_push(l, "fields after `.` (variables, temporaries, chains, generic records), enum variants after `E.`")
    strs_push(l, "(in a construction, a pattern, or before its `(` for a non-generic enum), record construction")
    strs_push(l, "labels, variant construction payload labels, pattern payload labels, and record and variant")
    strs_push(l, "constructor signature help.* `LanguageService::structure_at`, the structure contexts of")
    strs_push(l, "`completion`, and `help_at` answer from what the checker recorded — a field's `FieldRef`, a")
    strs_push(l, "variant's `VariantRef`, a construction's record, a payload's `PayloadRef` — and from one narrow")
    strs_push(l, "checker fact, `Resolution::looked_up_on`, the record or enum an unresolved member name was")
    strs_push(l, "looked for on, written only where a lookup failed (`architecture.md` §7.23). The service and")
    strs_push(l, "the LSP adapter perform no name lookup and no semantic re-resolution; normal structure sites")
    strs_push(l, "consume checker-recorded identities. The only spelling-based lookup N21 introduced is the")
    strs_push(l, "canonical checker's incomplete-source anchor for `E.name` written before its `(`: after `E`")
    strs_push(l, "fails as a value, the checker consults its existing module type environment and records a")
    strs_push(l, "non-generic enum (§7.23). No diagnostic and no language semantics changed. Candidates are that record's fields, that enum's variants or that variant's payload")
    strs_push(l, "fields, in canonical order, with substituted types; labels given elsewhere are excluded by")
    strs_push(l, "identity and the label being edited is kept. Constructor signature help is its own")
    strs_push(l, "`Constructor`, never a call; its active field is its label's identity at its canonical")
    strs_push(l, "position. Answered around a recovery only when it is inside another function's body.")
    strs_push(l, "Evidence: `crates/nazm-service/tests/structure.rs` — two records sharing `value`, two enums")
    strs_push(l, "sharing `Ready`, two variants sharing a payload `value`, a record and a function sharing `Box`,")
    strs_push(l, "a temporary receiver, a chain through `Holder[A]`, `Pair[Int, Str]` and `Opt[Int]` substituted,")
    strs_push(l, "each candidate identified by its declaration; a pattern binding refused as a label; labels given")
    strs_push(l, "elsewhere excluded, the edited label kept, an unknown label offered what is not given; an")
    strs_push(l, "unknown field, an unknown variant and `EA.Rea` with no `(` offered their anchor's members, and")
    strs_push(l, "unknown receivers, constructors and enums refused; constructor help out of canonical order,")
    strs_push(l, "between initialisers, on an unknown label, around a nested call, nested constructions, generics,")
    strs_push(l, "variants, a construction inside a call; reordered fields, payloads and variants changing no")
    strs_push(l, "answer; recoveries in another function answered and in the same function, the top level and")
    strs_push(l, "another file refused; an unsaved and closed dependency, a private dependency record refused,")
    strs_push(l, "another open program; a thousand edits with constant retained state; and over the repository's")
    strs_push(l, "own source 518 resolved sites — 278 members, 126 variants, 73 construction labels, 31 pattern")
    strs_push(l, "labels — each offered, once, as exactly the identity the checker gave it.")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/durable_identity.rs` adds the construction, fields, unknown member and")
    strs_push(l, "variant payload read from a deserialised interface with the dependency deleted;")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/lsp.rs` the real process with `é😀` before every site. Fifteen N21")
    strs_push(l, "mutations (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N22, 2026-09-26: document symbols — VERIFIED; workspace symbols over the current analysed")
    strs_push(l, "LanguageService universe — VERIFIED.* `LanguageService::document_symbols` is one open")
    strs_push(l, "document's functions, records, enums, variants, fields and payload fields, nested — a record's")
    strs_push(l, "fields under it, an enum's variants under it, a variant's payload fields under the variant — in")
    strs_push(l, "source order, each with its whole declaration as its range and its declared name as its")
    strs_push(l, "selection. `LanguageService::workspace_symbols` is every such declaration of every file the")
    strs_push(l, "open documents' compilations load, each once however many compilations load it, identified by")
    strs_push(l, "file, kind and name span and never by spelling, filtered by a case-sensitive substring of the")
    strs_push(l, "name and ordered by name, file, position and kind. Both are derived on demand from the")
    strs_push(l, "checker's definition tables and the parsed items their `decl` indices name")
    strs_push(l, "(`architecture.md` §7.24); nothing is kept. Over the protocol: `textDocument/documentSymbol`")
    strs_push(l, "(nested, or flat with container names for a client without hierarchical support) and")
    strs_push(l, "`workspace/symbol` (`resolveProvider: false`). Evidence: `crates/nazm-service/tests/symbols.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "— two records' `value`, two enums' `Ready`, a record and a function both `Box`, two modules'")
    strs_push(l, "`helper`, each separate; an import absent from its importer's outline; a broken body kept, an")
    strs_push(l, "unreadable item and refused duplicates absent, a type error kept; two roots sharing a module")
    strs_push(l, "listing it once, then after one closes, then none; an unimported `orphan.nz` beside them never")
    strs_push(l, "listed; the prelude and a missing module never located; unsaved edits seen at once and close")
    strs_push(l, "restoring the disk; a stale version refused; the query rule pinned on `Point`, `Pointer`,")
    strs_push(l, "`Checkpoint`; one order over ten runs; 1,000 edits with retained state constant; every symbol")
    strs_push(l, "the entity the reference index records at its name and where definition goes from every use;")
    strs_push(l, "over the repository's own source, every one of 817 declarations in 70 clean documents one")
    strs_push(l, "symbol with the same kind, name, range and parent as its concrete tree, and the compiler opened")
    strs_push(l, "as four overlapping programs listing each of its 500 declarations in its 8 files exactly once.")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/lsp.rs` the real process, with `é😀` before every checked position.")
    strs_push(l, "Thirteen N22 mutations (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N23, 2026-09-26: semantic identifiers and `textDocument/semanticTokens/full` — VERIFIED for")
    strs_push(l, "functions, intrinsics, parameters, locals and pattern bindings, records, enums, variants,")
    strs_push(l, "record fields, payload fields, type parameters and built-in types, each as a declaration or a")
    strs_push(l, "reference.* `LanguageService::semantic_identifiers` classifies each identifier of an open")
    strs_push(l, "document by what the checker recorded at exactly its span — an entity in the reference index,")
    strs_push(l, "a built-in call, or a written built-in or type-parameter name (`Resolution::written_type`, the")
    strs_push(l, "one checker record N23 added; `architecture.md` §7.25) — keeping the compiler's identity for")
    strs_push(l, "what it names; an identifier the checker resolved to nothing is not classified. Over the")
    strs_push(l, "protocol: `semanticTokens/full` only — no range, no delta, no `resultId`, no token cache —")
    strs_push(l, "under a fixed legend of nine types and two modifiers (`declaration`, and `defaultLibrary` on")
    strs_push(l, "intrinsics and built-in types only), relatively encoded in UTF-16. Semantic identifiers only:")
    strs_push(l, "no keywords, comments, strings, numbers or operators. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-service/tests/semantic.rs` — every identifier of a fixture pinned with its class")
    strs_push(l, "and role, nothing from a comment or string; a record and a function both `Box`, two records'")
    strs_push(l, "`value`, two enums' `Ready`, shadowed locals, a parameter named like a field, and `State.Done(code:")
    strs_push(l, "code) => code` each keeping its identity, each declaration and its uses one identity; unknown")
    strs_push(l, "call heads, members, types and qualifiers unclassified; a recovered body losing only what it")
    strs_push(l, "left unresolved and a renamed declaration's old use disappearing, not remembered; a refused")
    strs_push(l, "signature lending its type parameters to no one; an imported function, an unsaved edit,")
    strs_push(l, "another open program and close; 1,000 edits with retained state constant; over the")
    strs_push(l, "repository's own source, 24,870 entity occurrences in 70 clean documents each one identifier of")
    strs_push(l, "the same entity and role, 817 declarations matching their N22 symbols, 2,371 built-in type")
    strs_push(l, "names, 94 type-parameter names and 5,875 intrinsic calls, nothing unaccounted, and 2,679 type")
    strs_push(l, "names found from the concrete tree alone all classified. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/lsp.rs` the real")
    strs_push(l, "process with `é😀` before tokens across blank lines, the exact integer array computed")
    strs_push(l, "independently, and range and delta requests refused. Fourteen N23 mutations (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N24, 2026-09-26: `textDocument/codeAction` for current compiler diagnostic fixes — VERIFIED;")
    strs_push(l, "quick fixes only, open versioned documents only, no resolve, no fix-all; both `automatic` and")
    strs_push(l, "`needs_review` fixes are surfaced.* `LanguageService::fix_plans` turns each fix the current")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostics touched by the requested range carry into a `FixPlan` — the diagnostic, the fix's")
    strs_push(l, "applicability, description and precondition, the generation, and one versioned edit with the")
    strs_push(l, "bytes it replaces — and `fix_plan_is_current` holds it to all of them with the freshness law")
    strs_push(l, "renames use (`architecture.md` §7.26). Nothing is invented from a code or a message; the")
    strs_push(l, "client's diagnostics are not consulted. An automatic fix is preferred when it is its")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostic's only fix; a needs-review fix is titled with its precondition and never preferred.")
    strs_push(l, "Evidence: `crates/nazm-service/tests/fixes.rs` — all five fixes the compiler attaches (`mut`")
    strs_push(l, "on a `let`, `mut` off a parameter, `;` after a loop's value, `;` after an expression, a closing")
    strs_push(l, "quote), each planned exactly from its diagnostic, applied in memory to text that parses, with")
    strs_push(l, "its diagnostic gone and, when automatic, nothing outside its span changed; the edit on the")
    strs_push(l, "fix's span while relevance is the diagnostic's; the range rule at a cursor inside, at either")
    strs_push(l, "end, across two diagnostics and adjacent; a plan refused for other bytes, another version, no")
    strs_push(l, "version, another generation, a change outside its edit and one inside it; unsaved buffers, an")
    strs_push(l, "unsaved dependency and its close; no fix from an earlier analysis; 1,000 edits with retained")
    strs_push(l, "state constant; and, at the plan layer, two overlapping alternatives kept apart and a fix in a")
    strs_push(l, "file not open never planned. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/lsp.rs` the real process: a quick fix after")
    strs_push(l, "`é😀` with its versioned edit's UTF-16 range computed independently, unchanged until the client")
    strs_push(l, "sends `didChange`, then gone with its diagnostic; a stale and a fabricated client diagnostic")
    strs_push(l, "producing nothing; a needs-review fix with its precondition; `only` honoured; a client without")
    strs_push(l, "versioned edits offered none. Seventeen N24 mutations (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N25, 2026-09-26: `textDocument/prepareCallHierarchy`, `callHierarchy/incomingCalls` and")
    strs_push(l, "`callHierarchy/outgoingCalls` — VERIFIED; source-backed functions only, the bound current")
    strs_push(l, "compilation snapshot only, direct checked calls only, no filesystem or project-wide caller")
    strs_push(l, "discovery, and no item for an intrinsic or a function without source.* An item is a function")
    strs_push(l, "the checker declared from source, prepared from its declaration or a call through the reference")
    strs_push(l, "index, with its outline symbol's ranges; an edge is a `CheckedCall` to such a function,")
    strs_push(l, "attributed to the body whose call sites the checker recorded it in, grouped by the function at")
    strs_push(l, "the other end and located at each callee name (`architecture.md` §7.27). No per-call state was")
    strs_push(l, "added and nothing is kept between requests. An item's opaque locator binds it to the")
    strs_push(l, "compilation it was prepared in and the generation it was prepared at; any change, or closing")
    strs_push(l, "that root, leaves it unanswered. **This is complete only for the bound current compilation")
    strs_push(l, "snapshot: it is not evidence that every importer or caller in a project is loaded**, and it")
    strs_push(l, "does not lift the exported-rename refusal. Evidence: `crates/nazm-service/tests/hierarchy.rs` —")
    strs_push(l, "preparation from a declaration, a call and the position just after a name, and none from a")
    strs_push(l, "same-spelled record, a construction, a field, an enum, a variant, a payload label, a local, a")
    strs_push(l, "parameter, an intrinsic or a type; items at their N22 symbol's ranges; two callers and two")
    strs_push(l, "callees each grouped with every call in order, two calls on one line; calls nested in")
    strs_push(l, "arguments, `if`, `while` and `match` owned by their function; recursion and mutual recursion;")
    strs_push(l, "three instantiations of one generic function as one item, each range the callee name alone;")
    strs_push(l, "constructions, variants and intrinsics not edges, a `spawn` an edge and a refused generic")
    strs_push(l, "`spawn` — a reference with no checked call — none; four files through an import cycle, a")
    strs_push(l, "private function, and two `helper`s kept apart as callees and as callers; a call with a type")
    strs_push(l, "error kept, a misspelt call dropped beside a kept one, an unparsable body losing its calls with")
    strs_push(l, "nothing brought back; unsaved callers, an unsaved dependency and its close; a refused duplicate")
    strs_push(l, "declaration no item, its calls the checker's; two roots over one shared file each seeing only")
    strs_push(l, "its own callers, and a closed root's item unanswered, never rebound; an item unanswered at")
    strs_push(l, "another version, after an unrelated edit and after an identical one; 1,000 edits through six")
    strs_push(l, "shapes with every old item unanswered and retained state constant; and, over the repository's")
    strs_push(l, "own source, every checked call of 70 clean documents to a function with source exactly one edge")
    strs_push(l, "occurrence from the body that holds it — found independently by containment — to the function")
    strs_push(l, "the checker resolved, seen alike from both ends, at the entity the reference index records,")
    strs_push(l, "at items matching their N22 symbols, and classified by N23 as a function declared or")
    strs_push(l, "referenced. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/lsp.rs` the real process: prepare, incoming and outgoing")
    strs_push(l, "after `é😀` with every range computed independently in UTF-16, a cross-file callee, a stale item")
    strs_push(l, "and forged data answered `null`, and two roots over one file. Fourteen N25 mutations (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N26, 2026-09-27: completion at a structured hole — a bare member after `.`, a bare enum variant")
    strs_push(l, "after `E.` or `E[T].`, a bare construction or pattern label after `(` — and `.` as the")
    strs_push(l, "completion trigger character — VERIFIED; anchored only where the canonical compiler establishes")
    strs_push(l, "one record, enum or variant.* A request with no name at the cursor, right after a `.` or `(`")
    strs_push(l, "token, runs a completion probe: the compilation's current sources parsed by the same parser told")
    strs_push(l, "the cursor's offset — which reads a zero-width empty name there and nothing else differently — and")
    strs_push(l, "checked by the same checker, which anchors the hole where it already decides: the type an unknown")
    strs_push(l, "member was looked for on, the enum an `E.` names when no value does, the variant a construction")
    strs_push(l, "or pattern names, and — only where the module calls no function by that name — the record a bare")
    strs_push(l, "`Name(` would construct (`architecture.md` §7.28). Its candidates are N21's, from one function:")
    strs_push(l, "identities, canonical order, substituted details; the range is empty at the cursor. Nothing is")
    strs_push(l, "recorded by an ordinary analysis, the probe's diagnostics are never published, and nothing is")
    strs_push(l, "kept. Evidence: `crates/nazm-service/tests/incomplete.rs` — a parameter, a local, a temporary, a")
    strs_push(l, "projection chain and a call argument each giving exactly the receiver's fields; an applied generic")
    strs_push(l, "record substituted; a non-generic and an applied generic enum's variants, and a generic enum with")
    strs_push(l, "no arguments refused; a record type, an unknown name, an enum value, an `Int` and `p..` refused; a")
    strs_push(l, "local named like an enum reading as the local; two records' `value`, two enums' `Ready` and two")
    strs_push(l, "variants' `value` kept apart; a record's labels after `Point(`, `Point()` and `Point();`, a generic")
    strs_push(l, "record's substituted, none for a generic record with no arguments, a function, an unknown name, a")
    strs_push(l, "record and a function of one spelling, or a generic record and function of one spelling; payload")
    strs_push(l, "labels in a construction, an applied generic's, and a pattern alone, before another arm and after")
    strs_push(l, "one; the same candidates as `p.|x`, differing only in the range, and `p.x` unchanged; declaration")
    strs_push(l, "order irrelevant; the hole alone answered, another error before or after it in its function, at the")
    strs_push(l, "top level or in a dependency refused, another function's allowed; strings, comments, whitespace")
    strs_push(l, "and a second dot no hole; a private dependency record and an ambiguous import never anchors;")
    strs_push(l, "unsaved receivers, an unsaved dependency and its close, no earlier answer, a stale version refused,")
    strs_push(l, "another open program lending nothing; the published diagnostics, the text and retained state")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged by asking; 1,000 edits through ten shapes; and, over the repository's own source, cut")
    strs_push(l, "member and variant sites each completing to a list holding exactly the member the checker had")
    strs_push(l, "resolved there. `crates/nazm-syntax/tests/holes.rs` — over every corpus file, broken test programs")
    strs_push(l, "included, a probe parse at an offset with no hole the ordinary parse exactly; the hole read only at")
    strs_push(l, "the exact byte and changing only its statement; a later missing `;`, two dots and a written label")
    strs_push(l, "still what they were. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/lsp.rs` the real process: `.` advertised alone,")
    strs_push(l, "invoked and triggered completion identical after `é😀`, each edit empty at the UTF-16 cursor, and a")
    strs_push(l, "trigger in a string, a comment or whitespace answered `null`. Eight N26 mutations (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N27, 2026-09-27: Semantic Context Packet v1, `nazm.context/1` — VERIFIED for source-backed")
    strs_push(l, "functions, records and enums, in the current root compilation, with direct semantic links and")
    strs_push(l, "target-local diagnostics; and MCP — PARTIAL: one read-only stdio tool, `nazm.semantic_context`,")
    strs_push(l, "reading the disk at each call.* A packet (`crates/nazm-service/src/context.rs`, `architecture.md`")
    strs_push(l, "§7.29) is the target found through the reference index at a byte offset, its durable identity, its")
    strs_push(l, "signature or shape by the existing renderers, its exact source by N22's range, and compact links —")
    strs_push(l, "identity, kind, name, place — for its dependencies (every entity used inside it, grouped by")
    strs_push(l, "identity), related types (N18's written names of program records and enums, directly), references (uses only), callers and")
    strs_push(l, "callees (N25; `not_applicable` for a type) and diagnostics inside it; effects, capabilities, tests,")
    strs_push(l, "semantic changes and deltas are `unsupported`, never empty. Paths are source-root-relative and")
    strs_push(l, "nothing session-local is serialised. `nazm context --json` prints it; `nazm-mcp`")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-mcp/src/main.rs`), on the official Rust SDK, serves it with")
    strs_push(l, "`schema/nazm.context-3.json` (`-2` before N38) as its output schema. This establishes semantic context retrieval for")
    strs_push(l, "those three kinds and a compact-by-design contract for the fields it promises; it does not make a")
    strs_push(l, "packet sufficient for every task, and G68–G70 remain broader. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-service/tests/context.rs` — a function, record and enum each the same packet from its")
    strs_push(l, "declaration and from a use, a record and a function of one name and two modules' `helper` apart;")
    strs_push(l, "locals, parameters, fields, variants, labels, intrinsics, built-in types, whitespace, keywords and")
    strs_push(l, "comments refused, a file beside the root and `/etc/passwd` not in the compilation; the exact source")
    strs_push(l, "slice; dependencies grouped by identity with every occurrence, same-named fields of two records")
    strs_push(l, "apart, locals, intrinsics and the target itself excluded; related types direct; the core prelude's")
    strs_push(l, "`Option` and `Result` and a built-in type never linked, since v1 links only entities with a")
    strs_push(l, "declaration in a file of the compilation, and every link's place checked to be one; a private definition of an imported module still linked; references every use and not the")
    strs_push(l, "declaration; callers and callees equal to call")
    strs_push(l, "hierarchy's, a type's not applicable; diagnostics only the target's; availability unsupported; a")
    strs_push(l, "syntax error or a missing module refusing; two roots over one file each seeing its own; a hundred")
    strs_push(l, "serialisations and a copy in another directory byte-identical with no absolute path; each packet of")
    strs_push(l, "the disk as it is then; and, over the repository's own source, 649 packets of 70 clean documents")
    strs_push(l, "matching N22's ranges and signatures and N23's classification, every dependency occurrence the")
    strs_push(l, "reference index's use of the linked entity, and callers and callees N25's. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/schemas.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "the real command's packets and refusals valid against the schema. `crates/nazm-mcp/tests/protocol.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "the real server through the SDK's client: only tools advertised, one read-only tool with the")
    strs_push(l, "published output schema, packets equal to the service's and carried once — structured content, an")
    strs_push(l, "empty `content`, the packet's schema string exactly once on the wire — protocol errors for an unknown tool and bad")
    strs_push(l, "arguments, refusals for files outside the compilation, the disk re-read between calls with a broken")
    strs_push(l, "edit refused and a repair answered, two servers with two roots isolated, 1,000 calls with flat")
    strs_push(l, "resident memory, and nothing but JSON-RPC on standard output. Sixteen N27 mutations (area 30). Context")
    strs_push(l, "packet v1 exposes source-linked program dependencies only: compiler-owned, built-in, interface-only")
    strs_push(l, "or toolchain definitions with no navigable declaration may affect checking but are not linked.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N28, 2026-09-27: Semantic snapshot v1, `nazm.snapshot/1` — VERIFIED; Semantic delta v1,")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.delta/1` — VERIFIED; for durable source-backed functions, records and enums of the current")
    strs_push(l, "root compilation, and the sections the compiler records of them. G71 — PARTIAL; MCP — PARTIAL,")
    strs_push(l, "three read-only tools.* A snapshot (`crates/nazm-service/src/snapshot.rs`, `architecture.md` §7.30)")
    strs_push(l, "is every such definition by `DefKey`, with one BLAKE3 digest each for its exact source, shape")
    strs_push(l, "(kind, visibility, signature or fields or variants), source-linked dependencies, related types,")
    strs_push(l, "references, callers and callees (a function's; null for a type) and diagnostics — relationships")
    strs_push(l, "digested by identity and count, never offset — plus the root's module key and compiler, a count of")
    strs_push(l, "definitions with no durable key, and `unsupported` naming effects, capabilities, tests, semantic")
    strs_push(l, "history and behavioural equivalence. A delta (`crates/nazm-service/src/delta.rs`) validates a")
    strs_push(l, "baseline as data and reports added, removed and changed definitions by key, with a record of which")
    strs_push(l, "sections changed. N28 reports changes in the semantic surfaces Nazm currently records; it is not a")
    strs_push(l, "proof of behavioural equivalence: `{ 1 }` to `{ 2 }` is `source` alone, and effects, capabilities")
    strs_push(l, "and tests are unsupported, not unchanged. G71 is partial for that reason — a delta names what the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler records, and no behavioural, effect or test delta. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-service/tests/snapshot.rs` — every durable definition by identity, ordered, with two")
    strs_push(l, "modules' `helper` apart and no source text or packet inside; byte-identical from fresh services, at")
    strs_push(l, "any service generation, and from a copy in another directory with no host path and no git")
    strs_push(l, "repository; a file nothing imports absent and another root's compilation its own; a module outside")
    strs_push(l, "the source root counted untracked, never matched; recovery and a missing module refusing; no edit")
    strs_push(l, "and a moved definition no change; a comment and a changed literal `source` alone; a function added,")
    strs_push(l, "an enum and a function and a record removed, a rename removed plus added and never inferred; a")
    strs_push(l, "signature, a field, a variant and visibility `shape`; a new call changing the callee's references")
    strs_push(l, "and callers and the caller's dependencies and callees, and a second call counting; a use elsewhere")
    strs_push(l, "changing only a record's references; a new diagnostic changing only its definition; a broken edit")
    strs_push(l, "refusing and the repair answering; every malformed baseline refused with its reason — another")
    strs_push(l, "schema, an unavailable snapshot, an unknown or missing field, a record's callers, a non-canonical,")
    strs_push(l, "wrong-kind, absolute or prelude identity, a duplicate, a bad digest, another root, another")
    strs_push(l, "compiler; and 500 snapshot and delta pairs leaving the service's retained state unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/schemas.rs` the real commands' snapshots, deltas and refusals valid against")
    strs_push(l, "both schemas. `crates/nazm-mcp/tests/protocol.rs` the real server: three read-only tools with the")
    strs_push(l, "published output schemas, a snapshot equal to the service's and a delta needing only it, each")
    strs_push(l, "carried once on the wire, an edit seen between calls, a broken edit refused for both tools and the")
    strs_push(l, "repair answered, a path or path-shaped object refused as a baseline without being read, protocol")
    strs_push(l, "errors for missing or extra arguments, and 1,000 snapshot and delta calls with flat resident")
    strs_push(l, "memory. Twenty N28 mutations (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N29, 2026-09-27: Semantic Patch Plan v1, `nazm.patch/1` — VERIFIED, for two operations,")
    strs_push(l, "`rename` and `diagnostic_fix`; patch application — MISSING; MCP write or edit tools — MISSING;")
    strs_push(l, "G72 — PARTIAL.* A patch (`crates/nazm-service/src/patch.rs`, `architecture.md` §7.31) is N18's")
    strs_push(l, "validated rename or the fix a current diagnostic carries (N24), as minimal exact-byte edits, bound")
    strs_push(l, "to BLAKE3 of the root's `nazm.snapshot/1`, each edited file's BLAKE3 digest and each edit's")
    strs_push(l, "expected bytes; a fix's applicability and precondition are structured fields. N29 plans edits but")
    strs_push(l, "never applies them. Exported rename remains refused, because one root compilation is not a")
    strs_push(l, "complete importer universe; N29 does not alter LSP closed-file safety. G72 is partial because")
    strs_push(l, "minimal structured edit planning exists for these two operations, and generic semantic edits,")
    strs_push(l, "application and write automation do not. Evidence: `crates/nazm-service/tests/patch.rs` — a")
    strs_push(l, "private function renamed at exactly its declaration and call, with its durable key, the file's")
    strs_push(l, "digest, the snapshot's digest, each edit's bytes and no other text; every N18 category — local,")
    strs_push(l, "record, field, enum, variant, payload field — at exactly its occurrences, each applied to a copy")
    strs_push(l, "and checking clean; a local named by its place and its function, never a key; a private function")
    strs_push(l, "of an imported file no editor has open planned from disk while the service's own rename there is")
    strs_push(l, "still refused; exported, invalid, unchanged, colliding, unentitied, out-of-range, unloaded,")
    strs_push(l, "unclean and unparsable requests refused; an automatic and a needs-review fix with the compiler's")
    strs_push(l, "applicability and precondition, each applied and its diagnostic gone; no fix at a position with no")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostic, at an index past the fixes, after the repair, or for a syntax diagnostic; each")
    strs_push(l, "freshness layer going stale when what it protects moves, and the same request re-planned fresh;")
    strs_push(l, "byte-identical plans from another directory; the N28 delta after a rename (the old key removed,")
    strs_push(l, "the new added, the caller's source, dependencies and callees, and the record it took's references)")
    strs_push(l, "and after a fix (the definition's source and diagnostics); and 500 rename and fix plans each")
    strs_push(l, "leaving retained state unchanged. The unit tests order edits and refuse duplicates, overlaps and")
    strs_push(l, "two insertions at one point. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/schemas.rs` the real commands' patches and")
    strs_push(l, "refusals valid against the schema (with `oneOf` added to its validator for the tagged operation).")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-mcp/tests/protocol.rs` the real server: four read-only tools, `nazm.semantic_patch`'s")
    strs_push(l, "input the SDK's derivation of its typed request, patches equal to the service's and carried once,")
    strs_push(l, "the files untouched, exported refused, unloaded files and `/etc/passwd` refused, a root, an unknown")
    strs_push(l, "operation or argument and a client-written replacement protocol errors, a disk edit re-planned, a")
    strs_push(l, "broken edit and a vanished target refused, and 1,000 plans with flat resident memory.")
    strs_push(l, "Sixteen N29 mutations (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N32, 2026-09-28: Machine-addressable documentation index v1, `nazm.docs-index/1` — VERIFIED;")
    strs_push(l, "Selective documentation retrieval v1, `nazm.docs-section/1` — VERIFIED; G78 — PARTIAL; G79 —")
    strs_push(l, "PARTIAL.* `nazm docs` and `nazm-mcp`'s `nazm.docs_index` and `nazm.docs_section`")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-docs/`, `architecture.md` §7.34) section Nazm's own fourteen canonical documents,")
    strs_push(l, "each with the authority `master-architecture.md` §5 gives it, and return one section's own text")
    strs_push(l, "byte for byte by exact id, bound to a corpus state. The index is not a second source of")
    strs_push(l, "documentation truth; retrieval never paraphrases; a goal is never evidence and a plan never a")
    strs_push(l, "rule. G78 is partial: no semantic search, no documentation history, no rule ids below sections,")
    strs_push(l, "no documentation outside a source checkout. G79 is partial: one mechanical audit — no id, and so")
    strs_push(l, "no anchored rule, defined twice — and no whole-spec deduplication, rule graph or contradiction")
    strs_push(l, "detection. Evidence: `crates/nazm-docs/tests/corpus.rs` — ids from anchors, labels and heading")
    strs_push(l, "paths in that order, with two `Child` sections under two parents distinct; a parent's body its own")
    strs_push(l, "text and its children listed, a document equal to its sections concatenated; an anchored section")
    strs_push(l, "keeping its id reworded and moved, an unanchored one's old id not found; a removed section not")
    strs_push(l, "found and an added one moving no other id; a `#` line in a fence not a section and a Unicode")
    strs_push(l, "heading's id deterministic, stable under an ASCII anchor; every structural defect — a duplicate id,")
    strs_push(l, "anchor or label, a malformed or misplaced anchor, a setext or HTML heading, an unclosed fence, no")
    strs_push(l, "title, an empty identity, a broken link, a missing document — refused as unavailable; links")
    strs_push(l, "resolved to section ids, outside and external links kept as written, and a link to a reworded")
    strs_push(l, "heading refused; a grammar sectioned by production with exact text, examples and references, and")
    strs_push(l, "a broken one refused; the corpus state moving with one byte and with the manifest, only the edited")
    strs_push(l, "section's digest moving, a stale state refused, unknown ids and paths not found; the same state")
    strs_push(l, "and bytes from two directories, naming neither; and on the real corpus, every Markdown document")
    strs_push(l, "equal to its sections, `spec:generics` direct, the one fragment link resolved, each document's")
    strs_push(l, "authority, and every generated guide rule `generated_from` its production.")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-docs/src/markdown.rs` and `grammar.rs` — fences, anchors, setext and HTML refusal,")
    strs_push(l, "links outside code, locale-free slugs; production blocks. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/documentation.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "— one object on stdout and nothing on stderr for every answer and refusal, exit 0 and 1; a section")
    strs_push(l, "for a person exactly its body; one document's index equal to its part of the whole; two copies of")
    strs_push(l, "the repository giving the default's bytes; a rewording stale by state and still found by anchor; a")
    strs_push(l, "broken link and an empty root unavailable; every ambiguous flag set refused. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/schemas.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "— every status valid against both schemas. `crates/nazm-mcp/tests/protocol.rs` — nine tools, the")
    strs_push(l, "documentation tools taking ids and a state and never a path, file or root; answers equal to the")
    strs_push(l, "library's and carried once; `../README.md` and `/etc/passwd` not found, a path, a root, a query")
    strs_push(l, "and a missing state refused; a disk edit stale by state and read at the next call; a broken corpus")
    strs_push(l, "unavailable; and 1,001 calls through edits and repairs with flat resident memory. Seventeen N32")
    strs_push(l, "mutations (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N89, 2026-10-04: workspace editing — VERIFIED for exported renames within a declared workspace and")
    strs_push(l, "stale-safe application; the area stays PARTIAL.* `architecture.md` §7.90 first. A **workspace** is a")
    strs_push(l, "declared source root — a `nazm.root` marker, `--source-root`, or an application package — and every")
    strs_push(l, "`.nz` under it, each analysed as a root over the editor's buffers. An exported function, record,")
    strs_push(l, "enum, field, variant or payload field is renamed in every module of it that uses it — those the")
    strs_push(l, "requesting root's compilation does not load included — the entity found in each compilation by its")
    strs_push(l, "declaration's place, every compilation that contains an edited file re-analysed whole, clean and")
    strs_push(l, "partitioned as before; a library package's API (`package_api`) and a root nobody declared")
    strs_push(l, "(`exported`) are refused. `nazm patch apply PLAN` writes a `nazm.patch/1` plan all or nothing, only")
    strs_push(l, "to files whose bytes hash to the plan's digests. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/workspace_edit.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "(5) — a function renamed in three modules and nowhere else, applied and run; an edit after planning")
    strs_push(l, "refused with nothing written, and a path leaving the base refused; no declared root, a library")
    strs_push(l, "package, an application package; a capture in an importer refused; an exported record field renamed")
    strs_push(l, "through construction labels and projections. **Why still PARTIAL**: MCP has no planning tool for")
    strs_push(l, "the workspace rename and no apply; there is no DAP integration in the language server; and no")
    strs_push(l, "editor was driven — protocol tests do not show an editor's behaviour.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N33, 2026-09-29: Repository Context Map v1, `nazm.repository-map/1` — VERIFIED; Minimum Task")
    strs_push(l, "Context Planner v1, `nazm.task-context/1` — VERIFIED; G80 — PARTIAL; G69 — PARTIAL; G68 — PARTIAL,")
    strs_push(l, "strengthened; G70 — PARTIAL, unchanged; G83, G84, G85 — RESEARCH, with a byte-level foundation")
    strs_push(l, "only.* `nazm repo` and `nazm-mcp`'s `nazm.repository_map` and `nazm.task_context`")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-repo/`, `architecture.md` §7.35) map this repository's entities that have durable")
    strs_push(l, "identity — Cargo packages and targets, three Nazm source roots and their thirty compilation roots,")
    strs_push(l, "modules, 477 durable definitions, fourteen documents, sixteen schemas, twelve mutation profiles —")
    strs_push(l, "each with its authority and only structural, authority-named relationships, validated before")
    strs_push(l, "publication; and plan, for seed ids and an intent, the smallest context the repository can")
    strs_push(l, "justify, one step from each seed, every item with its reason, class, authority and retrieval,")
    strs_push(l, "under a structural budget whose cut is always `partial`. It composes N27, N28, N30 and N32 and adds")
    strs_push(l, "one service accessor; no grammar, semantics, `SEMANTIC_EPOCH` (7), `nazm.interface/5` or existing")
    strs_push(l, "schema changed. G80 and G69 are partial: one repository, the manifest's compilations only, no Rust")
    strs_push(l, "semantics, no transitive or project-wide closure, and sufficiency shown for seven representative")
    strs_push(l, "tasks by mechanical checks, not for every task. G83–G85 have measurements a later agent benchmark")
    strs_push(l, "can use — context bytes, entity counts, latency, check success — and no model, token or cost")
    strs_push(l, "result. Evidence: `crates/nazm-repo/tests/repository.rs` — ids from each authority, a directory")
    strs_push(l, "without `main.rs` not a target, a recovered compilation's modules mapped and its definitions not;")
    strs_push(l, "the same bytes twice and from two directories; the state moving with every input class and a stale")
    strs_push(l, "one refused; understand, edit and test closures, callers from two compilations, a type's users, a")
    strs_push(l, "test related only where its mutation lands; a section's own text and never its document's; a goal")
    strs_push(l, "and a plan ranked below the specification and the evidence, and cut first; a budget at, below and")
    strs_push(l, "above an exact fit, the seeds refused rather than cut; a cycle visited once and a fan-out of twenty")
    strs_push(l, "cut at sixteen and counted; paths, `..`, absolute and glob seeds refused and never read, unknown ids")
    strs_push(l, "not found; a definition only a recovered compilation loads `incomplete_compilation`; a broken link,")
    strs_push(l, "killer, manifest or root and a compilation reading outside its root unavailable; the validator")
    strs_push(l, "refusing duplicate, dangling, unknown and unordered maps; and the workspace equal to `cargo")
    strs_push(l, "metadata`'s. `crates/nazm-repo/tests/benchmark.rs` — seven real tasks, each checked against N27,")
    strs_push(l, "N32 and the catalogue parsed independently (`performance.md`). `crates/nazm-cli/tests/repository.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "and `tests/schemas.rs` — one object and an empty stderr for every answer, exit 0 and 1, the")
    strs_push(l, "library's bytes, ambiguous flags refused, every status valid against both schemas.")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-mcp/tests/protocol.rs` — eleven tools, the repository tools taking ids and a state and")
    strs_push(l, "never a path, answers equal to the library's and carried once, a disk edit stale by state, and")
    strs_push(l, "1,000 task contexts with flat resident memory. Nineteen N33 mutations (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*R1-C1, 2026-10-07: a function written as a value is a reference — corrected.* Until this step the")
    strs_push(l, "reference index held a function's calls and not its uses as a value (`apply_twice(double, 5)`,")
    strs_push(l, "N50), so references, `nazm references`, the LSP and a snapshot's `references` left them out, and")
    strs_push(l, "rename refused such a function (its re-check found the name undefined). Undocumented until R1's")
    strs_push(l, "precheck found it; fixed before v0.3.0 by reading the checker's recorded function values into the")
    strs_push(l, "index (`architecture.md` §7.110), with no change to the language. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-service/tests/references.rs`, `rename.rs`, `snapshot.rs`, `closures.rs` and")
    strs_push(l, "`structure.rs`; `crates/nazm-cli/tests/lsp.rs` and `resolved_units.rs`; two catalogue entries")
    strs_push(l, "(area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · Diagnostics, definition, hover, references, rename, completion, signature")
    strs_push(l, "help, symbols, full-document semantic tokens, quick fixes and call hierarchy only: no")
    strs_push(l, "formatting, refactors, source actions or inlay hints, no cancellation and no watched files.")
    strs_push(l, "Call hierarchy is one level of direct checked calls per request within the compilation an item")
    strs_push(l, "was prepared in: no transitive or persistent call graph, no callers from files that compilation")
    strs_push(l, "does not load, and no item for an intrinsic or a function without source. Quick fixes")
    strs_push(l, "are the fixes the compiler attaches, for open documents at their current version; a fix whose")
    strs_push(l, "file is not open is not offered, and there is no post-apply rollback — the server never writes. Semantic tokens are")
    strs_push(l, "`semanticTokens/full` only — no range, no delta, no token cache — and cover identifiers the")
    strs_push(l, "checker resolved: no keywords, comments, strings, numbers or operators, which an editor")
    strs_push(l, "grammar colours, and nothing for a name the checker did not resolve. Workspace symbols cover the files the open")
    strs_push(l, "documents' compilations load: there is no manifest-defined complete project index, no")
    strs_push(l, "filesystem scan, and no persistent workspace symbol database, so an unloaded orphan file is")
    strs_push(l, "not searched, and a declaration known only from a persisted interface, with no source location,")
    strs_push(l, "is not a symbol. That is not a project boundary, and it does not lift the exported-rename")
    strs_push(l, "refusal below. Every change re-analyses every open document in full; no")
    strs_push(l, "incremental reparse or graph maintenance, and no persistent cache in the editor. A built-in, a")
    strs_push(l, "type parameter and anything in a body that did not parse have no definition and no references;")
    strs_push(l, "the core prelude has no file, so a definition in it has")
    strs_push(l, "no location and a references answer for one of its entities has no declaration. References")
    strs_push(l, "cover the programs being analysed — each open document's compilation — and not files on disk")
    strs_push(l, "that no open document loads. Rename covers locals and private definitions, and — within a declared workspace, since N89 — exported")
    strs_push(l, "ones across every module under the root; without a declared root, and for a library package's API,")
    strs_push(l, "an exported entity is refused, because a module no walk finds may use it. The editor protocol's")
    strs_push(l, "edit is offered only when every file it touches is open, because the protocol cannot make a closed")
    strs_push(l, "file's content a precondition; such a plan goes through `nazm patch`, whose `apply` binds every")
    strs_push(l, "file's bytes. Completion is of an")
    strs_push(l, "identifier in a value, call-head or type position only — no field, variant, label, pattern or")
    strs_push(l, "import-path completion, no auto-import, no ranking — and there is none where the source needed")
    strs_push(l, "syntax recovery. Signature help is for calls and `spawn`s whose callee")
    strs_push(l, "the checker resolved — not record or variant constructions, and none while any file of the")
    strs_push(l, "compilation needs syntax recovery (an unclosed argument list included); a built-in's parameters")
    strs_push(l, "are shown by type, having no names; no documentation. Structure completion offers no methods")
    strs_push(l, "(a method's name after `.` has no member answer; methods are N78's), no import paths, no auto-import and no ranking. At a hole — right after")
    strs_push(l, "a `.` or `(` with nothing written (N26) — it needs the probe's anchor: nothing at a `(` the")
    strs_push(l, "module calls as a function (a record of the same name included), after a generic enum or record")
    strs_push(l, "with no type arguments, after a record type, an unknown name, an enum value or a second `.`; no")
    strs_push(l, "completion after a comma or at an empty label slot later in a list; nothing in a function with")
    strs_push(l, "another syntax error, and nothing when any other file, or the document's top level, recovered.")
    strs_push(l, "`.` is the only trigger character; `(` is not one. A hole's completion costs a second parse and")
    strs_push(l, "check of the compilation per request (`performance.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "`N0204` (no `main`) is not reported, because an open file is analysed as a module. Diagnostics")
    strs_push(l, "are published for open documents only. **MCP is eleven read-only tools** (N27–N33): the semantic")
    strs_push(l, "context packet, the semantic snapshot, the delta against a client-kept snapshot, a planned rename")
    strs_push(l, "or fix, the current diagnostics compactly or one in full, a compact summary of the root's")
    strs_push(l, "check — no build and no test run, which write files, over stdio, from disk, for one fixed root —")
    strs_push(l, "and Nazm's own documentation and the repository's context map and task contexts, by id, over one")
    strs_push(l, "fixed repository — no resources, prompts,")
    strs_push(l, "completions, sampling or edits, no tool that applies a patch, no HTTP, no server-side history, and")
    strs_push(l, "no view of an editor's unsaved buffers. A patch covers rename and compiler-owned fixes only — no")
    strs_push(l, "exported rename, no multi-file edit, and no fix of a syntax diagnostic, whose compilation has no")
    strs_push(l, "snapshot to bind it to. A packet has no effects,")
    strs_push(l, "capabilities, test mapping or semantic history (each `unsupported`); a snapshot's digests are of the")
    strs_push(l, "sections the compiler records, so equal digests are not equal behaviour, and a delta has no rename")
    strs_push(l, "inference and no effect, capability or test delta. All three cover only the root's compilation — no")
    strs_push(l, "project-wide completeness — and are refused for a compilation that needed syntax recovery.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · None for what exists. Each further request needs its own semantic")
    strs_push(l, "contract; incremental reparse needs latency evidence, which N16's measurements do not give.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Met for the LSP, 2026-09-25 (N16): an adapter shares the compiler's")
    strs_push(l, "semantic engine rather than re-implementing it. MCP: partial since N27 (2026-09-27) — read-only")
    strs_push(l, "tools over the same service, three since N28, four since N29, six since N30, seven since N31, nine since N32, eleven since N33; not accepted, since they answer a")
    strs_push(l, "few of the questions the service can, and none edits.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 26. Package and build tooling — PARTIAL")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 2 (2026-10-09)** · *Package features* (`general-purpose.md` §22; `spec.md`). `[features]`")
    strs_push(l, "in `nazm.toml`, a dependency's `features`, `--features`; additive, settled to a fixed point per")
    strs_push(l, "package; each module's `@cfg(feature = …)` reads its own package's set; `nazm.lock/2` records the")
    strs_push(l, "enabled sets, `/1` kept without them. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/features.rs` — defaults, a")
    strs_push(l, "dependent's request, a feature enabling a dependency's, isolation between packages, interpreter")
    strs_push(l, "and native build agreeing, three refusals, and the lockfile's schema, contents and staleness.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 2 (2026-10-09)** · *Tests and benchmarks* (`general-purpose.md` §18–§19; `spec.md`). `nazm")
    strs_push(l, "test` runs every `@test` and `@fuzz` function by name under the interpreter and as an executable,")
    strs_push(l, "each in its own process through a generated entry that blanks the file's `main` (R1: rather than")
    strs_push(l, "renaming it) without moving an offset; `--filter`, `--fuzz N`; `@test(fails)`; `nazm.test/1` gained `kind`. `nazm bench`")
    strs_push(l, "measures `@bench` functions natively at `-O2` (`nazm.bench/1`, EXPERIMENTAL). `@std/test` gained")
    strs_push(l, "five assertions and `property`. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/user_tests.rs` — pass, `Err` with")
    strs_push(l, "its message from both legs, a trap under `@test(fails)`, a wrongly expected failure, a test holding")
    strs_push(l, "authority, a property over 50 cases, a `@cfg`-excluded test not run, the filter, a fuzz target's")
    strs_push(l, "first failing case identical across legs and runs, six shape refusals, a diagnostic at its line,")
    strs_push(l, "and a benchmark's row; `schemas.rs` validates both outputs.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · Multi-file builds work through path-relative `use`, two independent")
    strs_push(l, "implementations: `crates/nazm-service/src/load.rs` and `compiler/module.nz`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N46, 2026-10-01: packages v1 — VERIFIED for path dependencies, one host.* `architecture.md`")
    strs_push(l, "§7.48 first. `crates/nazm-package`: the `nazm.package/1` manifest (unknown keys refused), exact")
    strs_push(l, "versions, deterministic name-order resolution with conflicts, mismatches and cycles refused by")
    strs_push(l, "code (`N0500`–`N0504`), BLAKE3 package digests, and the `nazm.lock/1` lockfile `nazm lock` writes;")
    strs_push(l, "`--locked` refuses a missing, mismatched or tampered lock (`N0505`–`N0507`). `use \"NAME:path\"`")
    strs_push(l, "reaches a declared dependency and nothing else (`N0508`); dependency modules are keyed")
    strs_push(l, "`NAME@VERSION/path`. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/packages.rs` — a diamond built from its")
    strs_push(l, "directory by the interpreter and both backends; every refusal by code; visibility; the lockfile's")
    strs_push(l, "bytes independent of the directory and not rewritten when unchanged; tampering refused before")
    strs_push(l, "anything is built; dependency keys; an unchanged dependency reused and a changed one rechecked")
    strs_push(l, "alone; two copies byte-identical from empty caches; 200 packages resolved and locked in name order.")
    strs_push(l, "No registry, no remote sources, no version ranges, no build scripts, no workspaces of several")
    strs_push(l, "roots.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N90, 2026-10-04: packages v3 — VERIFIED for backtracking resolution and `nazm update`, one host;")
    strs_push(l, "the area stays PARTIAL.* `architecture.md` §7.91 first. `crates/nazm-package/src/lib.rs` `Search`:")
    strs_push(l, "registry packages in name order, each one's non-yanked versions newest first with the lockfile's")
    strs_push(l, "first while it satisfies; a candidate is kept only if every requirement the current choice places")
    strs_push(l, "on it holds, a later requirement on a package already chosen is checked again, and a dead end undoes")
    strs_push(l, "the last choice. The first complete assignment is the answer — deterministic, the newest a lockfile")
    strs_push(l, "allows. At most 10,000 candidates: past that the refusal says the search stopped, not that no answer")
    strs_push(l, "exists. A refusal (`N0513`) names the package no version fitted where the search got deepest and")
    strs_push(l, "every requirement on it with who placed it, a registry package at its version. `nazm update DIR")
    strs_push(l, "[NAME…]` re-resolves with the lockfile's preference dropped for the named packages (every one")
    strs_push(l, "without names), prints `name old → new` per change, and writes the lockfile; a name that is no")
    strs_push(l, "registry package is `N0501`. Evidence: `crates/nazm-package/tests/registry.rs` (+4): an older version")
    strs_push(l, "chosen where N56 refused, an explained conflict naming both requirements, the bound reached on")
    strs_push(l, "100,000 dead-ending assignments, and `update` holding the packages not named;")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/registry.rs` (+1): `nazm update` prints the change, rewrites the lockfile, and")
    strs_push(l, "the build runs the new version. Five mutants. Still not here: signatures and trust roots, a remote")
    strs_push(l, "registry, features and pre-releases, multi-root workspaces — the area stays PARTIAL.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N56, 2026-10-02: packages v2 — VERIFIED for a local registry, one host.* `architecture.md` §7.58")
    strs_push(l, "first. `crates/nazm-package/src/registry.rs`: `nazm.registry-index/1` indexes and an immutable copy")
    strs_push(l, "per version; `^`, `~`, `=` and exact requirements; per name, the lockfile's version while it still")
    strs_push(l, "satisfies, else the highest non-yanked, one version per name and no backtracking — backtracking since")
    strs_push(l, "N90 — (`N0513` naming every requirement); `nazm publish` and `nazm yank`. Refused by code: a version published twice and")
    strs_push(l, "a malformed or equivocating index (`N0512`), a copy changed after publishing (`N0507`), a link in a")
    strs_push(l, "package (`N0514`), a path package and a registry dependency of one name (`N0503`), a cycle through")
    strs_push(l, "registry edges (`N0504`), a path dependency in a published package. A registry source is")
    strs_push(l, "`registry+NAME@VERSION`, so where the registry is enters no lockfile. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-package/tests/registry.rs` (14) — choice by operator, transitive narrowing and a named")
    strs_push(l, "conflict, reordered index entries, two registry locations, lockfile preference after a newer")
    strs_push(l, "publish, a stale lockfile under `--locked`, yanking with and without a lockfile, immutability,")
    strs_push(l, "tampering by edit and by addition, a symbolic link, five malformed indexes and equivocation, a name")
    strs_push(l, "that is a path, a cycle, a name conflict — and `crates/nazm-cli/tests/registry.rs` (3): publish,")
    strs_push(l, "resolve, lock, `--locked` run and build, yank; tampering refused before anything is written; the")
    strs_push(l, "commands' refusals. The compiler written in Nazm reads no manifest (DESIGNED: hand it `nazm.lock/1`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N31, 2026-09-28: Compact Command Summary v1, `nazm.command-summary/1` — VERIFIED; Compact Test")
    strs_push(l, "Summary v1, `nazm.test-summary/1` — VERIFIED; G76 — PARTIAL.* `--summary-json` on `nazm check`")
    strs_push(l, "and `nazm build` (`crates/nazm-service/src/summary.rs`, `architecture.md` §7.33) prints the")
    strs_push(l, "command's own status — `success`, `rejected`, `unreadable`, `refused`, `toolchain_failed`, one per")
    strs_push(l, "exit path — its unchanged exit status, counts, and a reference to every diagnostic it reported:")
    strs_push(l, "N30's id where N30 indexes it, an explicit `command` reference where it does not (`N0204`, a")
    strs_push(l, "backend's `N0101`), code, place and fix counts, no prose. On `nazm test` it prints counts from each")
    strs_push(l, "case's own verdict and every case that did not pass, with how each leg ended, from what the runner")
    strs_push(l, "did. Summary is an additive view, not a replacement for existing detailed machine output; absence")
    strs_push(l, "of diagnostics does not imply command success. G76 is partial: no test impact, test-detail query,")
    strs_push(l, "remote logs or agent task cost. Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/summary.rs` — a clean check, type")
    strs_push(l, "errors, a syntax error and a missing `main` each summarized with the check's exit status, exactly")
    strs_push(l, "the diagnostics `--json` gives by code, and none of their prose; `N0204` kept as a command reference")
    strs_push(l, "with no id, the type error with N30's id, its place and state answered by `nazm diagnostics")
    strs_push(l, "--detail`, and the references in N30's canonical order; an unreadable root and a missing module")
    strs_push(l, "`unreadable` with their diagnostics; a build that writes its executable and names it as the build")
    strs_push(l, "does, builds rejected by the checker, for no `main` and by the backend with nothing written, and a")
    strs_push(l, "build refused with no diagnostic at all and not a success; every ambiguous flag pair refused, and")
    strs_push(l, "`--json` and the human rendering as they were; a summary the same from another directory; a test")
    strs_push(l, "run counting each verdict, listing only the four cases that failed — output mismatched, a runtime")
    strs_push(l, "error, a type error, a build the compiler refused — with each leg, and `not_run` when interpreted")
    strs_push(l, "only; no cases and an unreadable path refused as the command refuses them; 201 cases summarized by")
    strs_push(l, "counts and one failure, no passed name; and the MCP server's check summary equal to `nazm check")
    strs_push(l, "--summary-json` with and without its cache. *N31 closure:* every public N31 outcome variant has at")
    strs_push(l, "least one regression test that executes its production branch — a test driver that cannot be")
    strs_push(l, "started (`could_not_run`, and `could_not_build` beside it), a build that cannot be started after the")
    strs_push(l, "program ran (`could_not_build`, not `build_failed`), a build that reports success and writes no")
    strs_push(l, "program (`could_not_run`, not `mismatched`), a test run with nowhere to build (`toolchain_failed`),")
    strs_push(l, "and `nazm build` with a `clang` that refuses to compile, one that compiles and will not link, no")
    strs_push(l, "`clang` on PATH, and nowhere to write (`toolchain_failed`, no diagnostic, exit 4, not a success);")
    strs_push(l, "each beside the same run without `--summary-json`, with the same exit status. The runner's driver")
    strs_push(l, "is chosen through `NAZM_TEST_DRIVER`, a test seam; `clang` through the process's own PATH. Not")
    strs_push(l, "every way a process can fail to start is tested — one per branch. `crates/nazm-service/tests/summary.rs` — a reference")
    strs_push(l, "linked only while the file is exactly what the command read. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/schemas.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "every status valid against both schemas. `crates/nazm-mcp/tests/protocol.rs` — seven tools, the")
    strs_push(l, "summary tool accepting only `check` (not `build`, `test`, a root, arguments or a command), nothing")
    strs_push(l, "written, and 1,000 calls through edits, breaks and repairs with flat resident memory.")
    strs_push(l, "Fifteen N31 mutations, and seven in its closure (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Since N107 (moved from area 2)** · `nazm build` and `nazm run` check every module on every run; a warm build reuses objects, not checks. Every answer is the same either way — it is a cost. A check against a persisted interface alone, without source, cannot use that module's traits.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · A package is built from its `nazm.toml` and `nazm.lock` (N46), resolved by a")
    strs_push(l, "backtracking resolver that explains a refusal (N90) against a **local** registry (N56): no remote")
    strs_push(l, "registry or network source, and no signature on a registry entry. A declared root — a `nazm.root`")
    strs_push(l, "marker, `--source-root` or a package directory — fixes where a module's durable identity is")
    strs_push(l, "relative to; without one, the source root is derived from the file named (N3). The compiler")
    strs_push(l, "written in Nazm reads no manifest and refuses a package import by name. *Until R1 this said there")
    strs_push(l, "was no manifest, resolution, lockfile, registry or declared root — true before N46 and N56.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The two resolvers still differ deliberately — the Nazm one normalises paths textually")
    strs_push(l, "because the emitted runtime has no `realpath`, so a symlinked file is read twice there and")
    strs_push(l, "once here. N3 settled what that means for identity rather than closing it: a module reached")
    strs_push(l, "under two names gets **no** durable key, in either implementation, so the two cannot")
    strs_push(l, "disagree about one (`spec.md`, *Durable identity*).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · A remote registry source and signed entries (a post-release track); the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler written in Nazm reading manifests.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · A project builds from a manifest and the two resolvers agree on")
    strs_push(l, "identity.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 27. Debugger and profiler — PARTIAL")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · N48 (2026-10-01), `architecture.md` §7.50 first. `nazm build --debug` emits DWARF")
    strs_push(l, "through the LLVM backend (`crates/nazm-lir/src/debug.rs`): a subprogram per function and a source")
    strs_push(l, "position on every instruction from MIR's spans, gathered into `OUTPUT.dSYM` on macOS. `nazm")
    strs_push(l, "inspect` prints `nazm.inspect/1` (`crates/nazm-cli/src/inspect.rs`); `nazm build --timings` prints")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.timings/1`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N91, 2026-10-04: debugger and profiler v3 — VERIFIED for the host matrix below; the area stays")
    strs_push(l, "PARTIAL.* `architecture.md` §7.92 first. MIR records each binding's block (`LocalDecl.scope`) and an")
    strs_push(l, "LLVM debug build nests a `DILexicalBlock` per block. Cranelift writes DWARF 4 through `gimli`")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-codegen-clif/src/dwarf.rs`): a compile unit, a subprogram per function and a line table")
    strs_push(l, "from the source location set on every statement, relocated per object format; a debug object is never")
    strs_push(l, "reused from the cache. `nazm profile --sample` runs the debug build under macOS's `sample` and")
    strs_push(l, "attributes each sample's innermost frame to a Nazm function and line, the runtime, foreign code or")
    strs_push(l, "the system, counting the system's waits as blocked; `nazm.profile/2`. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/debugger_v3.rs` (5, and 1 run with `--ignored` in the `nazm-debug` image) and")
    strs_push(l, "the sampler's attribution unit test; eight mutants, one repointed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Feature | LLVM, aarch64-apple-darwin | LLVM, aarch64-linux (gdb, container) | Cranelift, aarch64-apple-darwin | Cranelift, aarch64-linux (gdb, container) |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Breakpoint by function and by `.nz` line | lldb, static | live | lldb, static | live |")
    strs_push(l, "| Backtrace naming `.nz` lines; step by statement | — (developer mode) | live | — (developer mode) | live |")
    strs_push(l, "| Parameters and bindings (`Int`, `Bool`, `Str`) | described | live | not described | `No locals.` |")
    strs_push(l, "| A binding visible only in its block | described (IR) | live | — | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| Sampled run attributed to `.nz` lines | `sample` | no sampler in the image | `sample` | no sampler in the image |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Claim | Status | Evidence |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Line tables: a breakpoint by Nazm function or by `.nz` file and line resolves to that line | VERIFIED (static, lldb on aarch64-apple-darwin) | `a_debugger_finds_nazm_functions_and_lines` |")
    strs_push(l, "| A debug build behaves as an ordinary one; an ordinary build carries no debug metadata | VERIFIED | `a_debug_build_runs_as_an_ordinary_one_and_an_ordinary_one_carries_no_debug_information` |")
    strs_push(l, "| A live session — run to a breakpoint, backtrace, step (N58) | VERIFIED (gdb, aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, in the `nazm-debug` image) | a breakpoint by Nazm function name stops on its first statement with the parameters stored; the backtrace names Nazm functions with files and lines through two calls; `next` and `step` by statement (`a_live_session_shows_nazm_frames_lines_and_variables`, run with `--ignored` where Docker is). On macOS, launching under lldb still waits on developer-mode authorisation and is not exercised |")
    strs_push(l, "| Local variables, types (N58) | VERIFIED for `Int`, `Bool`, `Str` | parameters (with their positions) and source bindings, never temporaries; `Str` as `{data, len, owner}`; a dropped or not-yet-bound slot reads as its zeroed contents, never freed storage (`parameters_and_bindings_are_described_and_temporaries_are_not`, and the live test). Records, enums, sequences, channels and closures not described; no lexical scopes, so a variable is visible for its whole function |")
    strs_push(l, "| Cranelift debug information (N91) | VERIFIED for functions and lines; variables not described | DWARF written with `gimli` from Cranelift's per-instruction source locations: breakpoints by function and line resolved by lldb (`a_debugger_finds_a_cranelift_build_s_functions_and_lines`) and a live gdb session (`a_live_session_on_either_backend_shows_nazm_frames_and_lines`); a line added above the code moves the next build's lines (no debug object is reused). Variables: Cranelift reports where a value lives only through value labels, not tracked — `No locals.` |")
    strs_push(l, "| Lexical scopes (N91) | VERIFIED (LLVM) | a branch's binding in a `DILexicalBlock` of its own (`a_binding_is_scoped_to_its_own_block`); live, a binding of a later branch not in scope at the function's first statement and in scope, with its value, in its branch |")
    strs_push(l, "| Deterministic inspection of a program's facts | VERIFIED | `inspect_is_one_deterministic_document_of_the_program_s_facts` |")
    strs_push(l, "| Compiler phase timings | VERIFIED | `timings_account_for_every_phase` |")
    strs_push(l, "| Runtime profiling (N58) | VERIFIED as counts | `nazm profile FILE` prints one run's exit, wall time, output size, memory counts and scheduler counts (tasks spawned and joined, selects, timeouts), under either backend (`a_profile_reports_what_one_run_did_under_both_backends`); `nazm.profile/2` since N91 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Sampling profiler (N91) | VERIFIED on aarch64-apple-darwin; BLOCKED on Linux here | `nazm profile --sample [--interval-ms N]`: every sample attributed once, by its innermost frame, to a Nazm function and `.nz` line, the runtime, foreign code or the system, a system wait counted as blocked (`a_sampled_run_is_attributed_to_nazm_functions_and_lines`, both backends; `each_sample_is_attributed_once_by_its_innermost_frame`). macOS's `sample` only: no `perf` in the images, and a host without a sampler is refused. No timeline or event trace |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · The runtime and entry objects carry no debug information. Records, enums,")
    strs_push(l, "sequences, channels and closures are not described; Cranelift describes no variables. No DAP: a")
    strs_push(l, "debugger is driven by its own commands. Sampling is macOS's `sample`; no Linux sampler here.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · Cranelift value labels; the remaining types; a debug adapter; a Linux")
    strs_push(l, "sampler.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · A native backtrace taken in a live session names a `.nz` line — the static half")
    strs_push(l, "is met.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Evidence and infrastructure")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N66, 2026-10-02: vectorisation — VERIFIED for one idiom, `Ints` sums, on `aarch64-apple-darwin`.*")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.68 first. `ints_sum_from(start, v)` keeps the ordered checked sum's meaning exactly")
    strs_push(l, "— a 64-element block is added unchecked only when every partial sum is provably inside `Int` — and a")
    strs_push(l, "native build replaces the counted summation loop with it; `nazm explain-cost` names every other")
    strs_push(l, "loop's reason. Evidence, `crates/nazm-cli/tests/simd.rs` (5): every length 0–200 at three magnitudes")
    strs_push(l, "about the fast path's bound, equal to a scalar loop under the interpreter and both backends at `-O0`")
    strs_push(l, "and `-O2`; overflows at eight positions about the block boundaries, a block that would wrap, a start")
    strs_push(l, "too close to `MAX`, and a prefix overflow whose total fits — all failing where the loop fails; the")
    strs_push(l, "rewrite's IR and failure location; the interpreter's loop kept; the explain facts. A C harness of")
    strs_push(l, "200,000 random cases against a checked scalar sum found no difference. Measured (`performance.md`,")
    strs_push(l, "N66): 1.9× at 1,000 and 100,000 elements, 1.75× at 10,000,000, at `-O2`; the fallback for elements")
    strs_push(l, "past 2^56 is 1.33× *slower* than the scalar loop. **Limitation**: one idiom; no element-wise maps;")
    strs_push(l, "baseline target features only (NEON, SSE2), no per-build feature selection; x86_64 not measured.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 28. Performance measurement — PARTIAL")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N106, 2026-10-05: the two regressions since N75 attributed, one partly recovered, both accepted.*")
    strs_push(l, "`performance.md` (N106). `channels` builds: N83's pool — the runtime unit grew from 38 to 62.5 KB of")
    strs_push(l, "LLVM text and a `switch` unit joined it; the pool is the default runtime's now, paid once per cold")
    strs_push(l, "build. Checking the compiler: N76's lossless tree (about a third of the analysis) and N80's")
    strs_push(l, "provenance (about a fifth); a comparison sort and SipHash inside them removed — contained,")
    strs_push(l, "the contained bench's compiler check 213.7 → 180.2 ms; the fixed-input chain back at N75's parse time. The baseline is")
    strs_push(l, "re-saved at N106's tree, so the bench gate holds both. Eight claims are still unreproduced, so the")
    strs_push(l, "area stays PARTIAL.")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · `xtask/src/bench.rs` times five stages per program plus the compiler's own")
    strs_push(l, "source, with a correctness gate that refuses to time anything not producing its `.expected`")
    strs_push(l, "output first. One discarded warm-up, then N runs, median compared. Peak RSS captured where")
    strs_push(l, "readable. A regression must clear **both** 25% and 5 ms. External references are built and")
    strs_push(l, "timed from `bench/reference/sieve.c` and `bench/reference/sieve.py`, and a reference whose")
    strs_push(l, "answer differs from the Nazm program's is not timed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N92, 2026-10-04: performance evidence v2 — the register VERIFIED; the area stays PARTIAL.*")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.93 first. `bench/claims.toml` files each of `performance.md`'s 71 measured")
    strs_push(l, "sections — 10 **reproducible** by a named command (`cargo xtask contained bench`, or a measurement")
    strs_push(l, "test run with `--ignored`), 53 **dated** (records of the tree before the post-v1 baseline), 8")
    strs_push(l, "**unreproduced**: the current claims of N80, N82, N83, N84, N85, N86, N87 and N88, measured once by")
    strs_push(l, "the scripts their prose describes. `cargo xtask check` (**performance claims**, `xtask/src/claims.rs`)")
    strs_push(l, "refuses a measured section with no entry, an entry for no section, a status it does not know, a dated")
    strs_push(l, "or unreproduced entry with no reason, and a reproducible entry whose test or command is not in the")
    strs_push(l, "tree. `nazm.bench/2` (`xtask/src/bench.rs`) records the CPU model, logical CPUs, memory and kernel;")
    strs_push(l, "every run with p90, maximum and median absolute deviation; each executable's size; the noise floor;")
    strs_push(l, "how each reference's arithmetic compares; and each reference not measured, with why. New references:")
    strs_push(l, "`bench/reference/sieve.rs` (overflow- and bounds-checked, the closest to Nazm's meaning) and")
    strs_push(l, "`sieve.go` (bounds-checked, wrapping). Evidence: the gate's fixture test, the statistics and baseline")
    strs_push(l, "tests, a contained run's `bench/baseline-linux-aarch64.json` (replacing one older than N75 that made")
    strs_push(l, "`--check` report its configuration as regressions); five mutants. The run measured two regressions")
    strs_push(l, "since N75 and `performance.md` states them: checking the compiler written in Nazm is 54 % slower,")
    strs_push(l, "stepping up at N76 and N80, and `channels` builds 13–31 % slower, not located. **The area is VERIFIED")
    strs_push(l, "when the eight are reproducible**; the N91 section was made so by `what_debugging_and_sampling_cost`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · `bench/baseline.json` (Darwin) is **stale** and not a valid comparison;")
    strs_push(l, "re-recording it means running generated programs on the host, which the resource contract")
    strs_push(l, "forbids. `bench/baseline-linux-aarch64.json` is current. Cross-host comparison is refused")
    strs_push(l, "rather than attempted. Every measurement under ~15 ms is below the method's noise floor.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N34, 2026-09-29: Tokenizer-Independent Context Measurement v1, `nazm.token-cost/1` — VERIFIED;")
    strs_push(l, "Multi-Tokenizer Benchmark v1 — VERIFIED; G81 Tokenizer Independence — VERIFIED for context")
    strs_push(l, "measurement and selection; G82 Multi-Tokenizer Benchmarking — VERIFIED; G80 — PARTIAL,")
    strs_push(l, "strengthened; G83, G84, G85 — RESEARCH.* `nazm-tokens` (`crates/nazm-tokens/`, `architecture.md`")
    strs_push(l, "§7.36), a tool beside the compiler that nothing depends on (the `tokenizer reach` gate), counts")
    strs_push(l, "exact text under four pinned tokenizers of three families — OpenAI byte-level BPE (`cl100k_base`,")
    strs_push(l, "`o200k_base`, one family), SentencePiece BPE (Mistral-7B-v0.1) and SentencePiece Unigram")
    strs_push(l, "(T5-small) — offline, each identity carrying its library version, source revision, licence,")
    strs_push(l, "normalisation, special-token policy and a BLAKE3 digest checked at load. Content only: template")
    strs_push(l, "framing and unknown pieces are reported beside the count, and nothing is normalised first. The")
    strs_push(l, "seven N33 tasks, with N33's baselines unchanged, keep a 72.7–97.5 % token reduction under every")
    strs_push(l, "tokenizer, a median cross-tokenizer spread of 1.15 points and at most 6.25; the one-function")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostic is 14–20× its program under all four and is reported as the stress case it is. G81 is")
    strs_push(l, "verified at that scope — the planner selects by entities and bytes before any tokenizer counts, and")
    strs_push(l, "no tokenizer reaches the compiler, the service, the planner or a server — not as an audit of the")
    strs_push(l, "language's syntax decisions against tokenizers. G82 is verified: three families, pinned and")
    strs_push(l, "reproducible offline. G83–G85 remain research: no model was run and no cost measured. Evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-tokens/tests/tokens.rs` — every tokenizer's ids equal to independent Python")
    strs_push(l, "implementations' (`tiktoken` 0.12.0, `tokenizers` 0.22.2 with onig) on thirteen fixtures of ASCII,")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm, JSON, Markdown, Bangla, Arabic, emoji, combining marks, punctuation, a long identifier and")
    strs_push(l, "special-token strings; the families and the two SentencePiece algorithms distinct; the same counts")
    strs_push(l, "from every call and every registry; framing and unknown pieces reported, special-token text")
    strs_push(l, "ordinary; composed and decomposed text two inputs; unknown ids unsupported and never another")
    strs_push(l, "tokenizer; a missing, altered or non-JSON asset refused by name; large and unusual texts counted;")
    strs_push(l, "the tool reading only standard input; every answer valid against `schema/nazm.token-cost-1.json`.")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-tokens/tests/benchmark.rs` — the seven tasks under every tokenizer with every N33")
    strs_push(l, "mechanical check in the same pass, the report byte-identical twice, every non-stress reduction at")
    strs_push(l, "least 50 % under every tokenizer, worst ≤ median ≤ best; the fixed overhead attributed; source,")
    strs_push(l, "JSON, Markdown and three scripts compared; one selection's range in tokens (`performance.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "Eleven N34 mutations (area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N35, 2026-09-29: Agent Task Token Benchmark v1 — VERIFIED; Agent Cost Accounting v1 — VERIFIED;")
    strs_push(l, "Token-to-Correctness Benchmark v1 — VERIFIED; G83, G84, G85 — VERIFIED within the benchmark's")
    strs_push(l, "scope, one model configuration; G80 — PARTIAL, materially strengthened; G68 and G69 — PARTIAL,")
    strs_push(l, "strengthened.* `nazm-agent-bench` (`crates/nazm-agent-bench/`, `architecture.md` §7.37),")
    strs_push(l, "evaluation tooling nothing depends on (the `network reach` and `tokenizer reach` gates), puts eight")
    strs_push(l, "tasks over the seven N33 scenarios — understand, edit, diagnose, documentation, test selection,")
    strs_push(l, "Scenario C among them — to a real model with the naive baseline and with `nazm repo --task`'s")
    strs_push(l, "context, byte for byte, digest-addressed, one system text, wording, contract and parameter set for")
    strs_push(l, "both. Every answer is scored fact by fact, offline, against truths read from the authorities;")
    strs_push(l, "hallucinations are counted apart from misreadings; usage is recorded raw and normalised; dated")
    strs_push(l, "prices are applied in integer pico-USD, never in an identity, with input, cache reads, cache writes")
    strs_push(l, "and output priced separately. **Scope:** `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` through the Claude Code client")
    strs_push(l, "2.1.283 in print mode — no tools, no thinking, the model's default temperature, which the client")
    strs_push(l, "does not set — two trials, suite `b7db4ccc…`, prompt `nazm.agent-bench-prompt/1`, at the prices of")
    strs_push(l, "2026-09-29. The N33 context solved 12 of 16 requests to the baseline's 6, 112 of 116 facts to 95,")
    strs_push(l, "with no hallucination in either arm, 94.36 % fewer input tokens, 94.05 % fewer total tokens, and")
    strs_push(l, "95.39 % less cost as billed or 92.86 % with every input token uncached; 4,141 tokens and $0.0064 per")
    strs_push(l, "solved task against 139,311 and $0.2781. Correctness was preserved on 7 of 8 tasks: on T2 the N33")
    strs_push(l, "arm had every fact and added 32 false claims (builtins listed as definitions) while the baseline")
    strs_push(l, "gave no valid answer, which the pre-declared rule scores as baseline better. On the 123-byte")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostic both arms solved it and raw source was the cheaper input, 744 tokens to 1,367; every")
    strs_push(l, "other task's N33 context was cheaper, so for this model the crossover lies between 744 and 6,720")
    strs_push(l, "input tokens. G83–G85 are verified for that configuration only: the direct OpenAI and Anthropic")
    strs_push(l, "adapters are tested against recorded responses and were not run, because no key was supplied. G80")
    strs_push(l, "stays partial — one repository, one model, eight tasks. Evidence: `crates/nazm-agent-bench/tests/")
    strs_push(l, "agent.rs` — the suite's categories, Scenario C, the arms' distinct digests and the N33 arm equal to")
    strs_push(l, "the planner's own bytes; one prompt for both arms, as the provider receives it; a perfect answer")
    strs_push(l, "solving every task under either arm; missing, wrong and hallucinated claims counted apart; a bare")
    strs_push(l, "name only when unambiguous; extra and invented citations; invalid output and refusal; exact cost")
    strs_push(l, "arithmetic per category; zero denominators absent; identities and resume; the plan and its")
    strs_push(l, "alternation; the cap before and during a run; bounded retries never counted incorrect; model drift;")
    strs_push(l, "each adapter's normalisation and redaction; the report deterministic in any order; every record and")
    strs_push(l, "report valid against `schema/nazm.agent-benchmark-1.json`; the dry run with no credential and no")
    strs_push(l, "network. The results: `tools/agent-bench/results/`, `performance.md`. Sixteen N35 mutations")
    strs_push(l, "(area 30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · A Darwin machine on which running generated programs is contained.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Both baselines are current and recorded under containment.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 29. Differential testing — VERIFIED")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Scope (v1, Q1-D-20)** · The comparisons with the compiler written in Nazm cover what it carries —")
    strs_push(l, "its declared subset, which does not include Gate 2's numbers, arrays, `Bytes`, `Text` or the Gate 2")
    strs_push(l, "and Gate 3 built-ins it lists as not carried (`selfhost.rs`, `NOT_CARRIED`). Every other mechanism")
    strs_push(l, "here compares the interpreter, the LIR oracle and both backends over the whole language.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · Five independent mechanisms. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/build.rs` — two oracles")
    strs_push(l, "per case, both opt levels. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/concurrent.rs` — the same for")
    strs_push(l, "concurrency. `crates/nazm-cli/src/test.rs` — `nazm test` runs every case interpreted and")
    strs_push(l, "native and requires agreement. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/selfhost.rs` — the Nazm-written")
    strs_push(l, "lexer, parser and checker against the Rust ones, token-for-token and span-for-span, over")
    strs_push(l, "every `.nz` in the tree including their own sources, and eleven programs built by **both**")
    strs_push(l, "compilers and required to report the same reclamation — plus, since N10.1, the 32-case")
    strs_push(l, "transfer corpus run five ways. `compiler/bootstrap.sh` — at N10.1, thirteen conformance cases (twenty at v1), six of")
    strs_push(l, "them the N10.1 transfer shapes and one the original reproducer byte for byte, and seven")
    strs_push(l, "multi-module ones, under C2, C3 and the interpreter. *Since N12, propagation: 22 programs")
    strs_push(l, "through both checkers by code and span, four `?` programs built by both compilers with equal")
    strs_push(l, "reclamation reports, and a `results.nz` and a `Result`-library module case in the corpus.*")
    strs_push(l, "*Since N12.1, value blocks: 26 programs through both checkers by code and span, 10 parser")
    strs_push(l, "trees, six block programs built by both compilers with equal reclamation reports, the core")
    strs_push(l, "prelude found by key with the prelude last, between two project modules and absent, and a")
    strs_push(l, "`blocks.nz`, a value-block module case and three refusals in the corpus.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · The interpreter is the oracle, so a shared specification error is")
    strs_push(l, "invisible to all five. `docs/user/spec.md` names what must be settled before")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm test --backend=all` would mean anything.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · None.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Met.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 30. Mutation testing — VERIFIED · Fuzzing — PARTIAL (N73; MISSING until then)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Q1, 2026-10-08: the fuzz campaign re-run contained over all five targets, 300 s each* —")
    strs_push(l, "`front` 271,640 executions, `lower` 280,060, `run` 190,551, `lir` 272,626, `manifest` 2,388,876:")
    strs_push(l, "no crash; 36 `run` inputs blocked past two seconds and were counted, not kept (Q1-F-01,")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/limitations.md`). Log: `target/gates/q1/fuzz-contained.log`. Q1's mutation campaign is")
    strs_push(l, "recorded below its fixes (`docs/internal/security-qualification.md`, *Mutation*).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N108, 2026-10-06: the whole catalogue at the release gate — 1,268 of 1,268 caught.* Contained,")
    strs_push(l, "targeted with every killer verified (`releases/920a2a5.md`). Thirty-four entries were first undecidable")
    strs_push(l, "on Linux — killers verified on macOS only, and nine whose code N90, N104 and N105 had moved — and were")
    strs_push(l, "repaired; eight are observable only with macOS tools and are verified there. Every fuzz target ran 300 s")
    strs_push(l, "at the gate, 0 crashes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N105, 2026-10-05: a fifth fuzz target and an oracle tier.* `lir` (`fuzz/src/main.rs`): a checked")
    strs_push(l, "program's instruction-level LIR must validate and run on LIR's interpreter without a defect; run")
    strs_push(l, "contained for 300 s — 319,609 executions, 19,245 edges, no crash, no hang — and its minimised corpus")
    strs_push(l, "(532 inputs) is `fuzz/corpus/lir/`. The N73 differential gains LIR's interpreter as a fifth tier. The")
    strs_push(l, "mutation catalogue: 76 entries on code N105 deleted repointed, 18 retired with their reasons, 8 new")
    strs_push(l, "(`n105-*`), each new or repointed one caught by its named killer on the host.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N101, 2026-10-05: no silent tier.* `architecture.md` §7.102. N100's one survivor,")
    strs_push(l, "`n79-a-held-io-cap-is-read-alone`, is reachable and caught by")
    strs_push(l, "`authority::a_held_io_cap_authorises_its_own_print`; N100 had probed it in a directory with a warm")
    strs_push(l, "check cache, whose key does not change under a mutant (runbook: a probe runs in a fresh directory).")
    strs_push(l, "N100's four without a verdict have focused killers. The 175 other entries without a declared killer")
    strs_push(l, "were applied one at a time and each was caught: 132 in a dedicated host worktree, 43 selfhost and")
    strs_push(l, "bootstrap entries under the contained runner. Of **1,255** entries, **1,254** declare a killer;")
    strs_push(l, "`n13-native-operands-are-released-before-they-are-compared` is a known survivor, its reason in")
    strs_push(l, "`no_killer`. `xtask/src/plan.rs` refuses an entry with neither (`an_entry_without_a_killer_must_say_why`).")
    strs_push(l, "Not claimed: that a declared killer is a minimal one, or that zero survivors would mean no defect.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N93, 2026-10-04: coverage-guided fuzzing — VERIFIED for four targets at the stated budget; fuzzing")
    strs_push(l, "stays PARTIAL.* `architecture.md` §7.94 first. `fuzz/` (its own workspace): the compiler's crates")
    strs_push(l, "built with SanitizerCoverage (`trace-pc-guard`, a stable `rustc` option), the edge callbacks in")
    strs_push(l, "uninstrumented C (`fuzz/cov.c`), and an engine that keeps an input when it reaches a new edge and")
    strs_push(l, "mutates kept inputs by bytes, whole tokens of the language, whole lines and spliced lines, and names")
    strs_push(l, "renamed. Targets: `front` (parse and check), `lower` (Core IR, MIR, and MIR's validator over every")
    strs_push(l, "checked program), `run` (the interpreter, each execution bounded to 2 s — a program may block")
    strs_push(l, "forever, which the language allows), `manifest`. `cargo xtask contained fuzz [SECONDS] [TARGET…]`;")
    strs_push(l, "the minimised corpora are committed as `fuzz/corpus/TARGET/` and replayed by the ordinary suite")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-cli/tests/fuzz_replay.rs`, 1,826 inputs, about 2 s). **Campaign** (contained, four")
    strs_push(l, "CPUs, 300 s per target): `front` 318,377 executions, 13,293 of 109,890 edges, 487 minimised inputs;")
    strs_push(l, "`lower` 338,902, 17,467 edges, 531; `run` 221,834, 14,522 edges, 503, 35 inputs that block; `manifest`")
    strs_push(l, "2,995,846, 2,347 edges, 298 — **no crash**. A minimised set reaches 99.3 % or more of the edges its")
    strs_push(l, "campaign reached, not always all: the remainder are edges whose reaching varies between runs (threads, hash order).")
    strs_push(l, "No defect was found, so none gained a regression or a mutant; the engine is outside the workspace the")
    strs_push(l, "mutation catalogue covers. Not here: sanitizers (no `unsafe` in the compiler), Miri, Loom, backend and")
    strs_push(l, "FFI differential fuzzing beyond N73's generator, registry archives, a contract VM.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · `xtask/mutations/mutations.toml` holds **686** catalogued defects (158 when")
    strs_push(l, "this sentence was first written, 233 at N12.2, 266 at N13, 288 at N14, 304 at N15, 318 at N16, 334 at N17, 348 at N18, 362 at N19, 376 at N20, 391 at N21, 404 at N22, 418 at N23, 435 at N24, 449 at N25, 457 at N26, 473 at N27 with its closure correction, 493 at N28, 509 at N29, 527 at N30, 542 at N31 before its closure correction, 549 after it, 568 at N32, 575 at N32-H2, 582 at N32-H3, 601 at N33, 612 at N34, 628 at N35, 643 at N36, 662 at N37), **498** of them with a verified killer and all")
    strs_push(l, "of them owned by one of fourteen focused profiles;")
    strs_push(l, "`xtask/src/mutate.rs` injects each under a kernel advisory lock with a write-ahead backup,")
    strs_push(l, "requires the pattern to match exactly once, rebuilds, runs the suite and restores. It")
    strs_push(l, "distinguishes seven verdicts and refuses to fold a non-result into \"survived\" — a")
    strs_push(l, "distinction added after an incident that produced 19 false survivors. Lifecycle behaviour")
    strs_push(l, "is tested in `xtask/tests/lifecycle.rs`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N4 added six on 2026-09-22 and ran all six contained: four remove one input each from a")
    strs_push(l, "check key — the module's own source, its dependencies' interfaces, the checker's identity,")
    strs_push(l, "and which module it is — one stops an entry's recorded inputs being checked against the key")
    strs_push(l, "it is filed under, and one publishes an entry for a module that did not check cleanly. Each")
    strs_push(l, "is a wrong answer rather than a slow build, which is why they were worth the run.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N2 added two and ran four contained on 2026-09-22 — `every-definition-is-exported` and")
    strs_push(l, "`imports-become-transitive`, plus the two existing entries in the files N2 rewrote most, to")
    strs_push(l, "confirm their patches still apply. All four were caught, by 8 to 18 tests each. N2.1 added")
    strs_push(l, "four more against the **self-hosted** path — the `pub` bit ignored, resolution across every")
    strs_push(l, "module, the first ambiguous import winning, and any `main` accepted as the entry point —")
    strs_push(l, "and all four were caught by the parity suite. Both are targeted runs, not catalogue runs;")
    strs_push(l, "the row below still stands.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N9 added fifteen on 2026-09-23 and ran all fifteen contained and serial, in four")
    strs_push(l, "batches.* Each attacks the composition rather than the syntax: a copy that forgets a field,")
    strs_push(l, "a drop that omits one, a drop that does not recurse, a replacement that releases before it")
    strs_push(l, "takes, a projection out of a temporary that does not preserve ownership, a construction")
    strs_push(l, "that fails and leaks what it built, a task-safety derivation that stops at the first level,")
    strs_push(l, "an interface that omits its records, a published field that loses its type, a published")
    strs_push(l, "record named by its spelling, a layout that follows the declaration, a field read from the")
    strs_push(l, "wrong position, a recursive record accepted, a private type leaked through a public")
    strs_push(l, "signature, and the **self-hosted** emitter forgetting a record field. All fifteen are")
    strs_push(l, "caught; two runs were needed, because one survived and one did not compile.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The survivor is the interesting one and it is written up in `architecture.md` §7.10: a")
    strs_push(l, "replacement that releases before it takes is invisible to the reclamation counters, because")
    strs_push(l, "both orders end with the same two numbers. The one that did not compile is a different")
    strs_push(l, "verdict and was reported as one rather than folded into a pass — which is what the")
    strs_push(l, "seven-verdict distinction exists for.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N10 added twenty-two on 2026-09-23 and ran all twenty-two contained and serial, in five")
    strs_push(l, "batches, with nothing else running.* Eighteen attack the composition becoming dynamic: an")
    strs_push(l, "enum's properties taken from one variant, a discriminant from the parser rather than from")
    strs_push(l, "the names, a payload laid out as written, a published enum in source order, an exported")
    strs_push(l, "enum missing from the interface, a helper branching on the wrong tag, a copy that takes no")
    strs_push(l, "reference, a `match` that does not take over what it matches and one that never lets go, a")
    strs_push(l, "partly built variant left uncleaned, a task that does not give back what it borrowed, the")
    strs_push(l, "five checker rules — coverage, a repeated arm, another enum's variant, a missing payload")
    strs_push(l, "field, a private payload type — and the **self-hosted** checker skipping exhaustiveness and")
    strs_push(l, "the self-hosted emitter not taking over a payload.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Four more came out of the one that survived, and they are the interesting ones.")
    strs_push(l, "`a-variant-slot-keeps-what-the-last-round-left-in-it` was injected, compiled, and the suite")
    strs_push(l, "still passed. Asking why found that a `break`, a `continue` or a `return` out of a")
    strs_push(l, "half-evaluated expression gave back nothing it was holding — a defect of **N8's**, in both")
    strs_push(l, "backends and in the compiler written in Nazm — and then that the mutation itself no longer")
    strs_push(l, "described a defect, because the slot it zeroes is zero on every path that reaches it.")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.11 writes it up. It was retired and replaced by four that do describe")
    strs_push(l, "one: a transfer that keeps the temporaries, one that keeps the values being built, one that")
    strs_push(l, "releases the temporaries of the loop *around* it — a premature free rather than a leak —")
    strs_push(l, "and the same omission in the self-hosted emitter.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N10.1 added thirteen on 2026-09-23, repointed two whose text the correction moved, and")
    strs_push(l, "ran all fifteen contained and serial in five batches of three, with nothing else running:")
    strs_push(l, "**fifteen caught, none survived**, none unapplied, none that did not build, no timeout.* Each")
    strs_push(l, "puts back one half of the missing representation or one thing the audit found: an `if`")
    strs_push(l, "typed by the branch that left — the root cause — a join opened that no branch reached, for")
    strs_push(l, "an `if` and for a `match`; a node emitted though control never reaches it, and the same for")
    strs_push(l, "assignment alone; a `phi` read from a fixed two incomings; an unreachable node's operands")
    strs_push(l, "left on the stack; a `break` and a `return` that leave a `scope` without joining it; the")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm checker silent after a transfer; a value that never arrives given no type; and `==`")
    strs_push(l, "on strings keeping its operands, in each backend. The two repointed —")
    strs_push(l, "`the-self-hosted-emitter-skips-one-release-path` and")
    strs_push(l, "`the-self-hosted-compiler-keeps-what-a-continue-abandons` — were caught as before. Targeted")
    strs_push(l, "batches, not a catalogue run.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N10.2 added fifteen on 2026-09-23, repointed one, and retired one it superseded, and ran")
    strs_push(l, "the sixteen contained and serial in six batches with nothing else running: **sixteen")
    strs_push(l, "caught, none survived**, none unapplied, none that did not build, no timeout.* They are the")
    strs_push(l, "ways the three completions can collapse into two — no value read as a value, a value that")
    strs_push(l, "never arrives refused as none, an `if` with no `else` taken to leave, a `continue` taken to")
    strs_push(l, "complete — each half of the `if` join taking the wrong branch's type, two types accepted, a")
    strs_push(l, "value with nothing accepted, a `Unit` arm leaving its `match` a value, a body and a")
    strs_push(l, "`return` not held to the signature, the arms of a refused `match` still checked, and the")
    strs_push(l, "emitter's discarded arm value kept, or discarded without being given back. The repointed one")
    strs_push(l, "is N10.1's `N0313` entry, whose line the block's rewrite moved;")
    strs_push(l, "`an-if-is-typed-by-the-branch-that-left` is retired because its rule is now one line of the")
    strs_push(l, "three-state join, which `a-then-branch-that-leaves-still-gives-the-type` mutates exactly.")
    strs_push(l, "Targeted batches, not a catalogue run.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N11 added twenty-six on 2026-09-23 and repointed four the diagnostics migration moved, and")
    strs_push(l, "ran them contained and serial in five batches with nothing else running.* By category —")
    strs_push(l, "**type system** (six: parameter order forgotten, wrong arity accepted, inference keeping the")
    strs_push(l, "first conflicting type, `==` on a parameter, two definitions of one shape unified, parameter")
    strs_push(l, "names persisted in the interface), **native instances** (four: a symbol built from the first")
    strs_push(l, "argument alone, an instance planned twice, an instance's own calls never planned, polymorphic")
    strs_push(l, "recursion not counted as expanding), **`Vec` ownership** (five: push without a reference of")
    strs_push(l, "its own, get handing out the vector's, set releasing before taking, pop copying instead of")
    strs_push(l, "transferring, destruction without the elements), **cycles** (two: a `Vec` hiding what it")
    strs_push(l, "owns, every parameter counted as used) and **the compiler written in Nazm** (nine, across")
    strs_push(l, "all four). First run: **twenty caught, six survived**, none unapplied, none that did not")
    strs_push(l, "build, no timeout. The six were two holes and one equivalence:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "* `two-generic-definitions-of-one-shape-unify` and `an-instance-symbol-keeps-only-its-first-argument`")
    strs_push(l, "  had no test that could see them — no call passed one generic record where another of the")
    strs_push(l, "  same arity was declared, and no two instances differed only after their first argument.")
    strs_push(l, "  Now `inference_does_not_unify_two_generic_definitions_of_one_shape` and")
    strs_push(l, "  `two_instances_that_differ_only_in_a_later_argument_are_two_functions`;")
    strs_push(l, "* `vec-get-returns-a-borrowed-element`, in both compilers, is the N8 lesson a third time:")
    strs_push(l, "  every shape bound what it read, and a binding takes a reference of its own. Now")
    strs_push(l, "  `an_unbound_vec_read_outlives_the_element_being_replaced`, in both, reads an element into")
    strs_push(l, "  an argument and replaces it in the next argument, and churns the allocator in the callee;")
    strs_push(l, "* `vec-set-releases-before-it-takes`, in both, survived a second run and is **equivalent**:")
    strs_push(l, "  the order is observable only when the new value's one reference is the slot it replaces,")
    strs_push(l, "  and `vec_get` always gives out a reference of its own, so no program can build that. Both")
    strs_push(l, "  are retired, with the reason in the catalogue.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Rerun: **all four remaining caught**. Final: **24 of 24 live mutations caught**, 2 retired as")
    strs_push(l, "equivalent. Targeted batches, not a catalogue run; the catalogue is 182 entries.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N12 added twenty-six on 2026-09-24 and ran all twenty-six contained and serial, in six")
    strs_push(l, "batches, with nothing else running.* Result identity — `?` recognising `Result` by name, by")
    strs_push(l, "an `Ok`/`Err` shape, or as the first enum of that name; a project path taking the `@core`")
    strs_push(l, "key; the prelude left out of every check key; rehydration giving each interface its own")
    strs_push(l, "types. The rule — `?` outside a `Result` function, the error type ignored, the success type")
    strs_push(l, "demanded equal, a project type taking a prelude name. Control flow — the lowered `match`")
    strs_push(l, "testing the error tag, returning the operand's `Result`, falling through on error, and the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter carrying on with the error. And in the compiler written in Nazm, the same checks")
    strs_push(l, "plus ownership and the scope join: the error or the success value not retained, the operand")
    strs_push(l, "leaked on success, the join skipped, earlier temporaries or the frame left unreleased, the")
    strs_push(l, "error path falling into the success path, the prelude never imported. **All twenty-six")
    strs_push(l, "caught on the first run** — none survived, none unusable, none unapplied, none without a")
    strs_push(l, "verdict, and none retired. Targeted batches, not a catalogue run; the catalogue is 208")
    strs_push(l, "entries.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N12.1 added twenty-five on 2026-09-24 and re-pointed two of N12's,* whose patterns the")
    strs_push(l, "`Option` dogfood had moved; their defects were unchanged, so they were rerun rather than")
    strs_push(l, "retired. Run contained and serial, with nothing else running. Prelude identity in the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler written in Nazm: the last module taken as the prelude, any module called `prelude`,")
    strs_push(l, "a project path keeping the `@core` key, the prelude losing its key, the root module's")
    strs_push(l, "`Result`, the reserved-name rule following position — and in the reference graph, the last")
    strs_push(l, "module named the prelude. The reference backend: an arm block dropping its statements, a bare")
    strs_push(l, "block emitted as its tail alone, a block's value released as it leaves, a statement block")
    strs_push(l, "skipped, a statement `match` claiming every arm leaves, an arm that never rejoins, a")
    strs_push(l, "scrutinee never let go, a tail emitted after a transfer. The compiler written in Nazm: a block")
    strs_push(l, "operand refused or given an empty span, a statement block needing a `;`, every block")
    strs_push(l, "expression a value, a diverging one `Unit`, a block expression emitted as something. The")
    strs_push(l, "dogfood: `None` confused with `Some`, the `-1` brought back for a compilation with no")
    strs_push(l, "prelude, a check's arms reversed, a found declaration discarded. **All twenty-seven caught.**")
    strs_push(l, "None survived, none unusable, none unapplied, none retired.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "One needed three runs, and the reason is the suite's rather than the compiler's. *A")
    strs_push(l, "statement `match` claiming every arm leaves* drops a loop's increment, so the compiled")
    strs_push(l, "programs it produces never finish — and three places ran compiled programs with no deadline")
    strs_push(l, "(`value_blocks.rs`, the corpus run in `schemas.rs` and `workflow.rs`), while `run_bounded`")
    strs_push(l, "killed a stage but not what the stage had started. The first run ended at the batch's 3000 s")
    strs_push(l, "deadline with no verdict, and the second was stopped when it hung in the next such place; a")
    strs_push(l, "timeout was not counted as a catch. Each now fails its case under a deadline and kills its")
    strs_push(l, "process group, and the third run caught the mutant with 25 failing tests. The catalogue is")
    strs_push(l, "233 entries.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N12.2 (2026-09-24/25) replaced the runner's evidence shape without changing what a verdict")
    strs_push(l, "means, and then ran the whole catalogue for the first time.* The harness is")
    strs_push(l, "`xtask/src/campaign.rs`, `xtask/src/plan.rs` and `xtask/src/procs.rs`, operated as")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/internal/runbook.md` \"Mutation campaigns\" describes: per mutant, a verified **killer** (tier 1),")
    strs_push(l, "then a **focused profile** (tier 2), then the **workspace suite** (tier 3), stopping at the")
    strs_push(l, "first failure. A tier-1 or tier-2 catch is the same evidence as a tier-3 one — the test is a")
    strs_push(l, "member of the suite, passed in the baseline and failed under the mutant — and only tier 3 can")
    strs_push(l, "report SURVIVED. A timeout is its own no-verdict. `--strategy full` keeps the legacy shape")
    strs_push(l, "as the oracle. Lifecycle is in `xtask/tests/lifecycle.rs`: every tier transition, a deadline")
    strs_push(l, "at each tier, stale killer metadata, build reuse across four mutants, interruption and")
    strs_push(l, "resume, resume refused for another tree or catalogue, and the watchdog under SIGKILL and")
    strs_push(l, "SIGINT.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Measured, contained, serial, nothing else running:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| run | mutants | wall | per mutant, median |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| N12.1's catalogue batches, legacy, productive time | 27 | 10,782 s (13,870 s with the no-verdict reruns) | ≈ 240 s |")
    strs_push(l, "| the same 27, v2, profiles only | 27 | 1,807 s | 52 s |")
    strs_push(l, "| the same 27, v2, verified killers | 27 | **523 s** | **1.4 s** |")
    strs_push(l, "| differential sample, `--strategy full` | 10 | 3,058 s | 246 s |")
    strs_push(l, "| the same 10, `--strategy targeted`, profiles only | 10 | 945 s | 23 s |")
    strs_push(l, "| **whole catalogue, targeted** | **233** | **10,686 s**, five resumable sessions | 22 s |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The differential sample spans the checker, native symbols, memory, the interface, the cache")
    strs_push(l, "key, the compiler written in Nazm, the agent harness and the parser: **identical verdicts**")
    strs_push(l, "(ten caught under both) and identical original, mutated and restored digests. Two mutants")
    strs_push(l, "that crash a binary gave MUTANT CRASH under both strategies too.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The whole catalogue, on `f444d0d`:** 233 selected, 233 finalized. **228 caught** — 38 at")
    strs_push(l, "tier 1, 185 at tier 2, 5 at tier 3. Six workspace-suite runs in all; 227 avoided. And five")
    strs_push(l, "problems, each accounted for rather than folded into a pass:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "* **2 UNUSABLE** — `a-sequence-does-not-retain-the-string-it-stores` and")
    strs_push(l, "  `a-published-field-loses-its-type`: their *replacements* had drifted from the code (a")
    strs_push(l, "  renamed field; a field type that is no longer a string), so the mutants did not compile.")
    strs_push(l, "  Repaired, rerun, **caught**.")
    strs_push(l, "* **1 SURVIVED** — `a-record-that-contains-itself-is-accepted` disabled")
    strs_push(l, "  `UserTypes::layout_cycle`, which has had no caller since N11 moved the checker to")
    strs_push(l, "  `ownership_cycles`. An equivalent mutation of dead code; **retired**, and")
    strs_push(l, "  `an-inline-containment-cycle-is-not-refused` attacks the rule where it lives: **caught**.")
    strs_push(l, "* **2 MUTANT CRASH** — `nesting-unbounded` and `stack-not-sized-from-the-budget` overflow the")
    strs_push(l, "  stack inside the `nazm-syntax` and `nazm-core` test binaries. The legacy strategy gives the")
    strs_push(l, "  same verdict. The effect is observed; no test *asserts* it. Open — the cases must move")
    strs_push(l, "  out of process, which is a change to those crates' tests and not N12.2's to make.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N13 (2026-09-25) added thirty-three and repointed thirteen,* each new one written with the")
    strs_push(l, "semantic test that observes it and its killer confirmed by `--verify-killer` before it was")
    strs_push(l, "committed. They break the capability derivation (a `Vec`, a sequence, a `Chan` given")
    strs_push(l, "equality; only the first component, only the first variant, no nested type walked), the")
    strs_push(l, "checker (two types of one shape compared, a refusal that names nothing), the interpreter")
    strs_push(l, "(first field only, variants not compared, `!=` not the negation, `Str` by length), the")
    strs_push(l, "native helpers (first field only, tags not compared, a zero-payload variant unequal to")
    strs_push(l, "itself, arms in the wrong order, `!=` not negated, each temporary leaked, helper names")
    strs_push(l, "without their type arguments, operands released before they are read), the Nazm-written")
    strs_push(l, "checker and emitter (the same families), and the dogfooded completion fold. Nine of the")
    strs_push(l, "thirteen repointed entries compared a completion with `99`; the enum made that")
    strs_push(l, "inexpressible, so they became typed (`x != x`) — the invalid state they simulated no longer")
    strs_push(l, "exists. **Campaign `418a5e5921b866cc`, targeted, one session, 1,997 s:** the 33 new, the 13")
    strs_push(l, "repointed and 12 existing entries whose target code N13's diff touched or sits beside — 58")
    strs_push(l, "selected, 58 finalized. **57 caught**, 45 at tier 1 and 12 at tier 2, none at tier 3; no")
    strs_push(l, "timeout, no runner error, nothing unapplied or unusable, no crash; the workspace suite ran")
    strs_push(l, "once. **1 SURVIVED**: `n13-native-operands-are-released-before-they-are-compared`, a real")
    strs_push(l, "use-after-free — the helper reads operands whose storage was just released. It is **not")
    strs_push(l, "equivalent** and is **not counted as caught**. It survives because nothing allocates between")
    strs_push(l, "the release and the read, so the freed bytes are unchanged and every answer and counter is")
    strs_push(l, "right; glibc 2.41 in the image ignores `MALLOC_PERTURB_` and `glibc.malloc.perturb`")
    strs_push(l, "(measured), so **no deterministic direct killer exists under the supported allocator and")
    strs_push(l, "harness**. It stays **live** in the catalogue, with the `native` profile and a `no_killer`")
    strs_push(l, "reason, as a known surviving mutation: a mutation-sensitivity limitation of this suite, not")
    strs_push(l, "a verdict about the defect. Three")
    strs_push(l, "candidate killers were refuted by verification and not used. The whole catalogue was not")
    strs_push(l, "re-run: N13 did not change the harness, and the two open MUTANT CRASH entries were not")
    strs_push(l, "reached by it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N14 (2026-09-25) added twenty-two and repointed six,* each with its test and a killer")
    strs_push(l, "verified by `--verify-killer` (27 of 27 verified). They break the body rule (a requirement")
    strs_push(l, "ignored, never recorded, keyed by position across owners), what may be written (any name a")
    strs_push(l, "capability, a record's parameter allowed), the call (arguments never checked, only the first,")
    strs_push(l, "written or inferred ones skipped, a caller's parameter always satisfying), the interface (a")
    strs_push(l, "requirement not published, not read back, not validated, the schema or the epoch left")
    strs_push(l, "behind), the parser, and the Nazm-written parser and checker. **Campaign")
    strs_push(l, "`05f7bfb4d7869a2d`, targeted, one session, 1,025 s:** the 22 new, the 6 repointed, and 12")
    strs_push(l, "existing entries on the code N14 changed or beside it — among them N13's four capability-walk")
    strs_push(l, "and nominality mutants, because N14 changed that walk's leaf rule. **40 of 40 caught**, 36 at")
    strs_push(l, "tier 1 and 4 at tier 2; no survivor, nothing unusable or unapplied, no crash, no timeout; the")
    strs_push(l, "workspace suite never ran. N14 did not touch the native equality code, so N13's known")
    strs_push(l, "use-after-free survivor was not re-run and stays as it was: live, SURVIVED, no killer.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N15 (2026-09-25) added sixteen and repointed three.* Of those nineteen entries, **seventeen")
    strs_push(l, "list a killer** — the sixteen new ones and the repointed `a-failed-body-drops-the-function` —")
    strs_push(l, "and each was verified by `--verify-killer` (17 of 17: pristine passes, mutant fails, restored")
    strs_push(l, "passes), first in a session a host build overlapped and then again uncontended, contained at")
    strs_push(l, "P1, with the same result. The other two repointed entries, `a-block-does-not-count-its-contents`")
    strs_push(l, "and `parentheses-count-as-a-node`, list no killer, as before N15; their tier-2 profile decides")
    strs_push(l, "them, and the campaign below caught both there. The seventeen killers are fourteen distinct")
    strs_push(l, "tests: `a_lossless_tree_preserves_every_byte_and_recovers_inside_a_function` kills three")
    strs_push(l, "entries and `the_abstract_tree_keeps_its_contract_for_a_body_that_recovered` two. They break the tree's promises — whitespace, comments, a refused character or the")
    strs_push(l, "trailing trivia missing from it, a leaf normalised or spelled from its kind, trivia inside")
    strs_push(l, "the construct before it, nodes at one position nested inside out, a token given the wrong")
    strs_push(l, "kind — and recovery's: abandoning the block as before N15, consuming nothing, swallowing")
    strs_push(l, "the next statement, leaving no error node, handing a recovered body to the checker,")
    strs_push(l, "reporting a cascade, forgetting the braces the failed statement opened. **Campaign")
    strs_push(l, "`f1f15052a1be61f0`, targeted, P1, one session, 1,015 s:** every entry on")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-syntax` — the 16 new and the 10 existing parser entries, the three repointed")
