    strs_push(l, "linking section sent whole, callers from one compilation, a compilation outside its root")
    strs_push(l, "answered, a Cargo target found twice, a definition asked for at its declaration, and the MCP task")
    strs_push(l, "taking any argument. **One warm session, campaign `82a3ad10e55b2183`, targeted, P1, 1,057 s wall")
    strs_push(l, "from empty caches:** those nineteen and the fifteen MCP entries N33's server change touches —")
    strs_push(l, "**34 of 34 caught at tier 1**, no survivor, crash, timeout, unusable or uninjected entry — and")
    strs_push(l, "**every declared killer verified, 36 of 36**.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N34 (2026-09-29) added eleven mutations and a thirteenth profile, `tokens`,* on the frozen final")
    strs_push(l, "source: one tokenizer counting for all, an unknown tokenizer ignored, bytes reported as tokens,")
    strs_push(l, "framing counted as content, an altered asset loaded, the vocabulary digest ignoring the")
    strs_push(l, "vocabulary, text normalised before counting, unknown pieces not reported, the stress case dropped")
    strs_push(l, "from the report, a reduction's sign inverted, and a tokenizer's worst result reported as its best.")
    strs_push(l, "**One warm session, campaign `17c8f2bebd2c1dd4`, targeted, P1, offline, 818 s wall from empty")
    strs_push(l, "caches: 11 of 11 caught at tier 1** — no survivor, crash, timeout, unusable or uninjected entry —")
    strs_push(l, "and **every declared killer verified, 12 of 12**. Three of the eleven are in the benchmark's own")
    strs_push(l, "code (`tests/benchmark.rs`), where the numbers it reports are computed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N35 (2026-09-29) added sixteen mutations and a fourteenth profile, `agent`,* on the frozen final")
    strs_push(l, "source: both arms carrying one context, every answer scored by another task's oracle, a name the")
    strs_push(l, "truths lack taken as a truth, a hallucination counted as a misreading, output recorded as input,")
    strs_push(l, "cache reads priced as uncached input, output left out of a total, a zero denominator divided by,")
    strs_push(l, "an identity without its prompt, a runner error counted as an answer, the stress case left out of")
    strs_push(l, "the plan, one arm given another system text, a third retry, the cap checked without the attempt")
    strs_push(l, "about to be made, a credential kept in error text, and the Claude Code client run with its tools.")
    strs_push(l, "**One warm session, campaign `e8c0c93340e2158c`, targeted, P1, offline, 1,504 s wall: 16 of 16")
    strs_push(l, "caught at tier 1** — no survivor, crash, timeout, unusable or uninjected entry — and **every")
    strs_push(l, "declared killer verified, 16 of 16**. A first campaign on the fifteen before the Claude Code")
    strs_push(l, "provider existed, `7b5dc0b2ba230b56`, caught all fifteen too.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N36 (2026-09-30) added seventeen mutations and retired two,* on the frozen final source: a union")
    strs_push(l, "dropping an effect, a set iterated against id order, `print` classified as pure, a free `spawn`,")
    strs_push(l, "a callee's effects kept from its caller, one round taken as the fixed point, a contract not held,")
    strs_push(l, "an unknown effect read as `io`, a repeated effect accepted, an undeclared import taken as pure, the")
    strs_push(l, "witness pointing at the function rather than the call, the interface omitting and the reader")
    strs_push(l, "dropping a declared set, an effect change invisible to a snapshot, a packet without effects, the")
    strs_push(l, "interface schema staying `/5` and the epoch staying 7. N14's two pins on `/5` and epoch 7 are")
    strs_push(l, "retired in favour of the last two; N27's and N28's entries on effects being unsupported now guard")
    strs_push(l, "capabilities, the section that still is. **Campaign `39b5858f7f2e7ab7`, targeted, P1, offline:")
    strs_push(l, "all 85 selected caught** — the seventeen, the two repointed, the sixteen MCP-shared entries and")
    strs_push(l, "every existing entry in the interface writer, the packet, the snapshot, the delta and the")
    strs_push(l, "signature renderer — **78 at tier 1 with every killer verified in the session that caught it, and")
    strs_push(l, "7 of the interface writer's killerless entries at tier 2**; no survivor, crash, timeout, unusable")
    strs_push(l, "or uninjected entry. It took two sessions (5,862 s of the gate, three further resumes finding")
    strs_push(l, "nothing left), and the harness's one-session coverage check reads *incomplete* because the 78")
    strs_push(l, "verifications are split across them, not because any is missing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N37 (2026-09-30) added twenty mutations and retired one,* and was the first milestone selected")
    strs_push(l, "by the **responsibility law**: new mutations, and existing ones only where N37 changed the code")
    strs_push(l, "they guard or the tests that kill them, never because a layer was touched. The twenty attack the")
    strs_push(l, "authority laws — the outside-world built-ins or `print` needing nothing, a `SpawnCap` authorising")
    strs_push(l, "`io`, a free `spawn`, an undeclared callee or import bringing its own authority, a task inheriting")
    strs_push(l, "its spawner's, an effect set granting authority, a `! {}` contract skipping the check, holding")
    strs_push(l, "treated as an effect, the witness stopping at the callee, authority by spelling, a shadowed")
    strs_push(l, "capability held, a capability built, a `main` taking anything, a capability with equality, the")
    strs_push(l, "interface dropping authority or forgetting its kind, `main` handed no roots, and the epoch staying")
    strs_push(l, "8. `n36-the-epoch-stays` is retired for the last. Thirteen N36 entries were selected with a link")
    strs_push(l, "each: ten whose code (`effects.rs`, where the authority check now sits) or whose killer tests N37")
    strs_push(l, "edited to hand functions their capabilities, and three on the interface's effect field and schema")
    strs_push(l, "version, which N37 reads as the authority mode and kept at `/6`. N13's equality leaves, N17's")
    strs_push(l, "reference index and the lowering entries in the files N37 touched were considered and left out: N37")
    strs_push(l, "changes nothing they guard. **Campaign `60c5ee822617e3c9`, targeted, P1, offline: 33 of 33 caught,")
    strs_push(l, "32 at tier 1 with killers verified, 1 at tier 2**, no survivor; two sessions (4,395 s of the gate).")
    strs_push(l, "The tier-2 one, `n37-holding-authority-is-an-effect`, exposed a declared killer whose pure function")
    strs_push(l, "made no call; the test was strengthened after the gate and the mutant verified alone at tier 1")
    strs_push(l, "(164 s). The one-session coverage check reads *incomplete* for the split, as N36's did.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N38 (2026-09-30) added twenty-five mutations and retired one,* selected by the responsibility")
    strs_push(l, "law. The twenty-five attack the provenance laws — a file read or the command line misclassified,")
    strs_push(l, "output taken for input, shared storage followed or a channel dropping an origin, file contents or")
    strs_push(l, "`unknown` let through to `write_file`'s path, a join order-dependent or dropping a side, a binding")
    strs_push(l, "keeping only its first value, a condition flowing, a constant inheriting its input, the worklist")
    strs_push(l, "stopping after one pass, `main`'s authority misclassified, a `spawn` resetting provenance, a helper —")
    strs_push(l, "declared or not — laundering a path, the witness stopping at the callee, a reused module or its entry")
    strs_push(l, "losing its facts, the entry, snapshot and epoch pins, and a snapshot or packet without provenance.")
    strs_push(l, "`n37-the-epoch-stays` is retired for `n38-the-epoch-stays`. Nine existing entries were selected, each")
    strs_push(l, "guarding a contract N38 edited directly: the entry validation and the planner's hit path, which now")
    strs_push(l, "carry facts (`a-cache-entry-is-trusted-because-it-parsed`, `the-prelude-is-left-out-of-every-check-key`);")
    strs_push(l, "the delta's baseline validation and its sections, which gained `provenance`")
    strs_push(l, "(`n28-another-schema-is-accepted-as-a-baseline`, `n28-an-unknown-baseline-field-is-accepted`,")
    strs_push(l, "`n28-caller-changes-are-omitted`, `n28-callee-changes-are-omitted`, `n28-a-source-only-change-is-unchanged`);")
    strs_push(l, "and the snapshot digest and packet structures N38 extended (`n36-an-effect-change-is-invisible-to-a-snapshot`,")
    strs_push(l, "`n36-a-packet-has-no-effects`). Every N38 killer was first verified by hand on the host, which found four")
    strs_push(l, "weak ones before the gate, each strengthened. **Campaign, targeted, P1, offline: 34 of 34 caught — 32 at")
    strs_push(l, "tier 1 with killers verified, and the two selected killerless entries at tier 2 and tier 3** (the store")
    strs_push(l, "suite, and the workspace suite for the prelude key entry); no survivor, over two sessions and three")
    strs_push(l, "resumes that found nothing left (5,848 s of the gate).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N39 (2026-09-30) added nineteen mutations, repointed twelve and retired one.* The nineteen attack")
    strs_push(l, "the Core IR laws: a call resolved by its spelling, a read with no type, a value `if`'s branches")
    strs_push(l, "swapped, a loop's back edge, a `return` falling through, a `break` in a condition naming its own")
    strs_push(l, "loop, a `continue` naming the outermost, an initialiser filling the field at its position, a variant")
    strs_push(l, "losing its identity, the effect contract and a function's authority dropped, a digest naming a callee")
    strs_push(l, "by session number, ignoring the body, collapsing effects into the body digest or keeping arm order,")
    strs_push(l, "the verifier accepting a stray `break`, a generic call keeping its declared result, the interpreter")
    strs_push(l, "running a `match`'s first arm, and the backend asking the resolution again — which only the boundary")
    strs_push(l, "gate the suite now runs can see. Twelve historical entries were **repointed**, because the rule each")
    strs_push(l, "pins moved: into the one lowering (the three `lowered-propagation-*`, now reaching both backends),")
    strs_push(l, "into the Core IR evaluator (`call-depth-never-released`, `return-does-not-leave-its-block`,")
    strs_push(l, "`remainder-inherits-the-hardware-fault`, `n13-interpreted-inequality-is-not-the-negation`,")
    strs_push(l, "`a-returned-value-is-discarded`, `a-flow-in-value-position-is-an-error`) and into native lowering")
    strs_push(l, "from Core IR (`return-does-not-end-the-block-it-is-in`, `lowered-arm-block-drops-its-statements`,")
    strs_push(l, "`a-statement-block-is-skipped`); the last two of the evaluator's were found *unusable* by the")
    strs_push(l, "campaign — their text still matched and their replacements named the tree walker's variables — and")
    strs_push(l, "were repointed after it. `interpreted-propagation-carries-on-with-the-error` is **retired**: the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter has no `?` of its own. Six more were selected for a rule N39 rewrote the code of: the")
    strs_push(l, "call-depth guard and the stack's sizing (`call-depth-unbounded`, `stack-not-sized-from-the-budget`),")
    strs_push(l, "and native lowering's construction cleanup, field positions and statement-`match` completion")
    strs_push(l, "(`a-partly-built-record-is-not-cleaned`, `a-partly-built-variant-is-not-cleaned`,")
    strs_push(l, "`a-field-is-read-from-the-wrong-position`, `a-statement-match-claims-every-arm-leaves`). Layout,")
    strs_push(l, "symbol, linkage and cycle-check entries were not selected: their code did not change and every")
    strs_push(l, "emitted IR file is byte-identical. Every N39 killer was verified by hand on the host first, which")
    strs_push(l, "found the boundary gate blind to a lookup written across lines; it reads code whitespace-free now.")
    strs_push(l, "**Campaign, targeted, P1, offline: 37 of 37 caught — 23 at tier 1 with killers verified, 13 at tier")
    strs_push(l, "2, 1 at tier 3 — and no survivor.** `stack-not-sized-from-the-budget`, a MUTANT CRASH in every")
    strs_push(l, "campaign that had run it, is caught for the first time: the in-process test that aborted its binary")
    strs_push(l, "(`a_raised_budget_still_runs_what_fits_inside_it`) recursed deeper than its own comment's bound, and")
    strs_push(l, "recurses 200 levels now, leaving the out-of-process check to fail. It took six sessions and")
    strs_push(l, "13,876 s; the first session's journal was not read by the next, whose campaign key differed, so its")
    strs_push(l, "23 verdicts were established twice. 34 verdicts are at `ab0a761`; the three repaired entries' are at")
    strs_push(l, "`eb80464`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · **VERIFIED here means the harness runs every catalogued mutant and accounts for")
    strs_push(l, "every verdict — not that every meaningful mutation is killed.** A killer verified on one platform")
    strs_push(l, "is evidence on that platform (N108); eight entries are observable only with macOS tools or Apple's")
    strs_push(l, "clang and are verified on the host. A whole-catalogue campaign takes several contained sessions,")
    strs_push(l, "resumed from its journal; a supervisor killed mid-session loses that session's verdicts, which then")
    strs_push(l, "simply run again. Fuzzing covers five targets — the front end, lowering with MIR's validator, the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter, package manifests and LIR — at 300 s each per campaign, with no sanitizer, Miri or Loom")
    strs_push(l, "run and no backend or FFI target (`limitations.md`). *Until R1 this named a crashing entry and a")
    strs_push(l, "known survivor (neither remains: N108 caught all 1,268 entries) and said fuzzing did not exist (N73 began it).*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · For fuzzing, a sanitizer run and backend and FFI targets. For mutation, none")
    strs_push(l, "for the catalogue as it stands.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · A full catalogue run completes with every verdict accounted for. **Met on")
    strs_push(l, "2026-09-25**: 233 of 233, as above. Fuzzing's status is separate and unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 31. Bootstrap — VERIFIED as scoped")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Scope (v1, Q1-D-20)** · The bootstrap is of the declared subset the compiler written in Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "carries; it does not carry Gate 2 or Gate 3 (`selfhost.rs`, `NOT_CARRIED`; `limitations.md`,")
    strs_push(l, "*Self-hosted compiler*), so a program using them is the reference compiler's alone.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N102, 2026-10-05: parity on every probe — 21 of 21.* `architecture.md` §7.103 first. The eight")
    strs_push(l, "refusals N98 measured are gone: effects and capabilities, recursion (the reference's stack check,")
    strs_push(l, "derived and gated by `check-runtime`), contracts, foreign declarations (`Int` only), `@std`, traits,")
    strs_push(l, "closures and function values, and with them tasks and channels; `&&`, `||` and `!` too.")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/parity.json`: **21 equal, 0 refused, none differs**. The checker's answers are compared")
    strs_push(l, "with the reference's — codes and spans — on 39 sources of the N102 features and four new refusals")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0602`, `N0386`, `N0366`, `N0614`); `compiler/conformance/features.nz` and a two-module case run")
    strs_push(l, "through C2, C3 and the reference with the same memory counters, closures included. Contained:")
    strs_push(l, "selfhost 43 of 43, bootstrap C2 = C3 (`8cc750c6…`, 16,030 lines, 34 cases of which 14")
    strs_push(l, "multi-module, 29 refusals). **Mutation**, contained: all 100 catalogue entries on `compiler/`,")
    strs_push(l, "nine of them new, applied one at a time — 100 caught; one only after the memory test gained a case")
    strs_push(l, "(a capture not retained into a closure, invisible until a later string reuses the freed storage),")
    strs_push(l, "and one, `selfhost-a-success-value-is-not-retained`, crashing the whole suite and caught cleanly by")
    strs_push(l, "its declared killer. Parity on the probes is not parity on the language: what remains is in")
    strs_push(l, "`limitations.md` (packages, generic channels, `select`, the clock, devices, `c_errno`, provenance,")
    strs_push(l, "profiles, escapes, `::`, `as`). A fixpoint is self-reproduction, not correctness.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N98, 2026-10-04: parity of the compiler written in Nazm — measured and gated; not reached.*")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.99 first. `compiler/parity/` holds 21 probes, one per feature; the contained")
    strs_push(l, "test `the_parity_record_is_what_both_compilers_do_with_each_feature` (`crates/nazm-cli/tests/selfhost.rs`)")
    strs_push(l, "builds each with the reference and with `compiler/emit.nz`, runs both natively, and holds")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/parity.json` to the verdicts: **13 equal** — arithmetic, loops, both failure traps, modules")
    strs_push(l, "of files, records, enums, generics, `Result` with `?`, sequences, `Vec`, strings, equality — **8")
    strs_push(l, "refused** — closures, traits, effects with `IoCap`, tasks and channels, contracts, `@std`, foreign")
    strs_push(l, "declarations, and a recursive function with `if` as its value (`N0101`) — and **none differs**. The")
    strs_push(l, "bootstrap stays VERIFIED; parity with the reference's native subset is not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · `compiler/bootstrap.sh` runs C1 → C2 → C3 from one source and compares two")
    strs_push(l, "things: the emitted IR byte for byte, and the linker-normalised executables byte for byte.")
    strs_push(l, "Five conformance cases under `compiler/conformance/` must agree across C2, C3 and the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter. The script refuses to run without an external memory ceiling. `docs/internal/bootstrap.md`")
    strs_push(l, "states what this does and does not establish, and the answer is narrower than it sounds.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · A fixpoint establishes self-consistency, not correctness — a compiler with")
    strs_push(l, "a bug that reproduces itself reaches a fixpoint too.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The reference compiler was stale until 2026-09-22.** `compiler/bootstrap.sh` requires")
    strs_push(l, "`$nazm` to exist and does not build it, and inside the contained runner `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`")
    strs_push(l, "is `/work/target` — which `docker/contained.Dockerfile` warms with a binary at *image build")
    strs_push(l, "time*. Every contained bootstrap between the image's build and this date therefore used")
    strs_push(l, "that binary for the reference check and for stage 1, whatever the tree said, and reported")
    strs_push(l, "nothing about the discrepancy. The workload now runs `cargo build -p nazm-cli` first. The")
    strs_push(l, "fixpoint claim itself is unaffected — C1 → C2 → C3 is about the compiler written in Nazm,")
    strs_push(l, "and the reference check is explicitly not part of the chain — but *which front end built")
    strs_push(l, "C1* was not what the record said it was.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Since N2** the compiler source states its own module boundaries: 84 of its 224 functions")
    strs_push(l, "are `pub`, 140 are private, and `emit.nz`, `check.nz` and `parser.nz` gained the `use` lines")
    strs_push(l, "for modules they were reaching through someone else's import.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Since N2.1 the two implementations accept the same language.** For one day they did not:")
    strs_push(l, "the Nazm-written compiler parsed `pub` and resolved every name across the whole program, so")
    strs_push(l, "it accepted eight kinds of program the reference refuses and emitted an invalid module for a")
    strs_push(l, "ninth. It now carries a module graph, a per-definition owner and visibility, per-module")
    strs_push(l, "interfaces collected before any body, and a recorded resolution that emission consumes.")
    strs_push(l, "Fifteen rules are compared through both compilers")
    strs_push(l, "(`the_two_compilers_agree_on_every_module_and_visibility_rule`), and five multi-module")
    strs_push(l, "conformance cases agree across the reference, C2 and C3 — which is a **different** claim")
    strs_push(l, "from C2 = C3 and is recorded separately in `bootstrap.md`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Since N11** the compiler written in Nazm implements generics and `Vec[T]` and uses one — its")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostics are a `Vec[Diag]` — so every stage compiles a `Vec` of records. The corpus has 24")
    strs_push(l, "cases, 9 of them multi-module, including a generic library instantiated only by its importer")
    strs_push(l, "and one instance requested from two modules, and a **refusal corpus** of 4 programs that C2,")
    strs_push(l, "C3 and the reference must each refuse with the named code. The fixpoint moved to")
    strs_push(l, "`c58b91dd…` at 11,877 source lines. `bootstrap.md` has the record.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Since N12** every stage loads the same core prelude — named on its command line, its digest")
    strs_push(l, "in the record — and the compiler uses `?` itself: its front end returns")
    strs_push(l, "`Result[Checked, Vec[Diag]]`. The corpus has 26 cases, 10 of them multi-module, and 9")
    strs_push(l, "refusals. The fixpoint moved to `08895900…` at 12,046 source lines, with the runnable")
    strs_push(l, "executables byte-identical as well.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Since N12.1** the compiler written in Nazm compiles a block used as a value and finds the")
    strs_push(l, "prelude by the key `@core/prelude` rather than as the last module, and its checker takes an")
    strs_push(l, "`Option[Int]` apart where it used to test for `-1`. The corpus has 28 cases, 11 of them")
    strs_push(l, "multi-module, and 12 refusals. The fixpoint moved to `a9ead258…` at 12,164 source lines,")
    strs_push(l, "runnable executables byte-identical too.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Since N13** the compiler written in Nazm derives equality and emits it — a helper per")
    strs_push(l, "compared record and enum, a tag comparison and then the active slot alone — and uses it on")
    strs_push(l, "itself: a node's completion is an `enum Completion` in a `Vec[Completion]` rather than `0`,")
    strs_push(l, "`1` or `2` in an `Ints`, compared with `==`. The corpus has 30 cases, 12 of them")
    strs_push(l, "multi-module (one compares an imported record, enum and `Option[Point]`), and 19 refusals,")
    strs_push(l, "seven of them equality's. The fixpoint moved to `76598c43…` at 12,412 source lines,")
    strs_push(l, "runnable executables byte-identical too.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Since N14** the compiler written in Nazm parses `T: Equality`, records it on the parameter's")
    strs_push(l, "entry, reads it in the one place equality is derived, and checks every call's type arguments")
    strs_push(l, "against it at the reference's spans. The corpus has 32 cases, 13 of them multi-module (one")
    strs_push(l, "calls and forwards to an imported bounded function, including a `count_same[T: Equality]`")
    strs_push(l, "over a `Vec[T]`), and 25 refusals, six of them requirements'. No compiler code uses a")
    strs_push(l, "requirement: the audit found none that needs one. The fixpoint moved to `0e1a40e6…` at 12,543")
    strs_push(l, "source lines, runnable executables byte-identical too.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · None.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Met.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 32. Reproducibility and provenance — PARTIAL")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N94, 2026-10-04: reproducibility and provenance v2 — VERIFIED under the model of §7.95, on one host;")
    strs_push(l, "the area stays PARTIAL.* `architecture.md` §7.95 first. The model's claims, apart: identical input")
    strs_push(l, "and another directory give the same executable, provenance and SBOM bytes under either backend")
    strs_push(l, "(`identical_input_gives_identical_artefacts_here_and_in_another_directory`); the release archive (N75)")
    strs_push(l, "and offline locked builds (N56) as before; across toolchains, differences classified, never equal")
    strs_push(l, "(N73). `nazm build --sbom FILE` writes CycloneDX 1.5 read off the provenance record — the output,")
    strs_push(l, "every package with `pkg:generic/NAME@VERSION`, every source module, the runtime, BLAKE3 hashes, the")
    strs_push(l, "tools (`the_sbom_lists_every_package_source_and_the_runtime_with_their_digests`). `nazm attest sign`")
    strs_push(l, "wraps the record in an in-toto Statement v1 (`urn:nazm:provenance:1`) over artefacts it names, and")
    strs_push(l, "signs it with `ssh-keygen -Y sign` in the namespace `nazm-attestation`; `nazm attest verify` checks the")
    strs_push(l, "signature for an identity in an allowed-signers file and every artefact's digest among the subjects")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-cli/src/attest.rs`; `a_signed_statement_verifies_for_its_signer_and_its_artefacts_only`:")
    strs_push(l, "a stray artefact refused before a key is used, another identity, an edited artefact, an edited")
    strs_push(l, "statement and an unlisted key each refused). Four mutants, one repointed. Not here: a transparency")
    strs_push(l, "log, keyless signing, SLSA levels, rebuilds on independent machines, dependency origins beyond N56's")
    strs_push(l, "digests.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · `scripts/release-candidate.sh` runs every gate, writes `PROVENANCE.txt` and")
    strs_push(l, "`MANIFEST.txt`, and validates the package against its own manifest with counts compared")
    strs_push(l, "both ways so a file copied in but not listed fails.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N46, 2026-10-01: reproducible executables — VERIFIED on one host.* Two copies of one package,")
    strs_push(l, "built from empty caches in two directories, give byte-identical executables under both backends")
    strs_push(l, "(`two_copies_built_from_empty_caches_are_byte_identical`): the link runs with `ZERO_AR_DATE=1` and")
    strs_push(l, "under the final file name, because the Apple linker otherwise mixes a time and a temporary name")
    strs_push(l, "into the executable's UUID and signature. The package lockfile records BLAKE3 digests of every")
    strs_push(l, "package's sources and refuses a changed one. Not claimed across hosts, operating systems or")
    strs_push(l, "toolchain versions.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · Three claims, kept apart. Archive **entry metadata is normalised** — tar")
    strs_push(l, "sorted with zeroed owner and mtime, gzip with no timestamp — and since R1 the dates the provenance")
    strs_push(l, "and bootstrap records carry are the commit's (`SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH`), not the run's. Whether two")
    strs_push(l, "assemblies of one commit are byte-identical is recorded in that candidate's release record")
    strs_push(l, "(`releases/`), on one host and one image — never across hosts, operating systems or toolchains.")
    strs_push(l, "**C2 and C3 are byte-identical within one run** after the build-id is stripped. The source digest")
    strs_push(l, "covers a **declared file set**; since R1 a `build-input-digest` beside it covers every file git")
    strs_push(l, "tracks or would (`scripts/source-digest.sh`) — Cargo manifests, `Cargo.lock`,")
    strs_push(l, "`rust-toolchain.toml`, the Dockerfile, the catalogue and every fixture included. *Until R1 the")
    strs_push(l, "records embedded their own run date, which made bit-reproducibility impossible, and only the")
    strs_push(l, "declared set was digested.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*R1, 2026-10-07: two assemblies, one archive — on one host and one image.* `cargo xtask contained")
    strs_push(l, "--profile p4t4 release`, run twice at `996984f` in `nazm-contained:1.98.1` on one macOS host, gave")
    strs_push(l, "byte-identical archives (`a5e2ee97…`) with identical `MANIFEST.txt` and `PROVENANCE.txt`, every date")
    strs_push(l, "inside the commit's; the manifest was redigested independently, 220 of 220")
    strs_push(l, "(`releases/996984f.md`). The archive was signed by nobody, and nothing is claimed across hosts.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · A comparison across two independent hosts, which needs a second machine.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · Two runs at one commit produce identical archives, or the claim is")
    strs_push(l, "permanently retired. *Met on one host and one image, R1 (2026-10-07); the row stays PARTIAL for what")
    strs_push(l, "N94 lists as not here — a transparency log, keyless signing, SLSA levels and rebuilds on independent")
    strs_push(l, "machines.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 33. Platform and target matrix — PARTIAL")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Ignored tests, run and kept (v1, 2026-10-11, Q1-D-04)** · Every cell and sub-claim here and in")
    strs_push(l, "areas 18, 19, 21, 27 and 34 that rests on an `#[ignore]`d test — one that starts a container,")
    strs_push(l, "QEMU, a WebAssembly engine, Wine, py-evm, gdb or the GPU — was run at `6b3b85c`, one at a time:")
    strs_push(l, "**38 run, 38 passed**, `target/gates/v1/ignored.log` (08:47–08:58 UTC). They are: both boards and")
    strs_push(l, "the Cortex-M board booting, their interrupts, sections, manifests, the heap arena and the kernel")
    strs_push(l, "workload; the six domain workloads and the traffic light; the realtime scheduler and stack bound;")
    strs_push(l, "the WebAssembly corpus, its absent authority and its stack check, and WASI's two; the EVM and")
    strs_push(l, "WebAssembly contracts against the simulator, generated sequences included (N96); the GPU's four")
    strs_push(l, "and the CPU provider's; the Bionic and Cocoa runs; Windows under Wine, both; and gdb live under both")
    strs_push(l, "backends. The cost measurements (`what_…_cost…`) were not re-run: they record numbers, not claims.")
    strs_push(l, "A VERIFIED sub-claim resting on an ignored test cites this log, and the release gate re-runs it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 3 (2026-10-10)** · *Prebuilt toolchains* (`systems-domains.md` Part A; `support.md`). Host")
    strs_push(l, "archives by `scripts/host-archive.sh` — the release binary with the standard library and runtime")
    strs_push(l, "inside it — and `scripts/clean-install-test.sh`, which installs one where no Rust is reachable and")
    strs_push(l, "checks, runs, builds and runs a program: passed for `aarch64-apple-darwin` (native),")
    strs_push(l, "`x86_64-apple-darwin` (cross-built, **under Rosetta**) and `aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu` (built by the")
    strs_push(l, "new `cargo xtask contained archive`, installed in a clean Debian container with only clang,")
    strs_push(l, "`docker/clean-install.Dockerfile`). The contained runner gained `--platform amd64` for the")
    strs_push(l, "`linux/amd64` image. Found on the way: `nazm build` blamed the generated IR for a toolchain failure")
    strs_push(l, "in the link step; it now says the toolchain or its environment failed")
    strs_push(l, "(`a_toolchain_environment_failure_is_not_blamed_on_the_ir`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 3C (2026-10-10)** · *Windows x86_64* (`spec.md` *Windows x86_64*; `systems-domains.md` Part")
    strs_push(l, "A-W). `x86_64-pc-windows-gnu`, built to objects and `link.txt` for MinGW-w64's `gcc` (`-static`,")
    strs_push(l, "`-lws2_32`, `-lbcrypt`), by both backends. The runtime reaches the system only through its platform")
    strs_push(l, "layer — the `os`, `stack` and (Windows) `init` units, runtime ABI 21 — so the Windows port is a")
    strs_push(l, "third binding of each function, never a branch in the runtime: the Win64 context switch (the TIB's")
    strs_push(l, "stack bounds, `xmm6`–`xmm15`), task stacks by `VirtualAlloc` with a `VirtualProtect` guard, UTF-16")
    strs_push(l, "files and directories, Winsock with a `WSAPoll` reactor of epoll's one-shot meaning and pipes")
    strs_push(l, "checked by `PeekNamedPipe`, children by `CreateProcessW` with quoted command lines, the clocks by")
    strs_push(l, "`QueryPerformanceCounter` and `GetSystemTimePreciseAsFileTime`, entropy by `BCryptGenRandom`, the")
    strs_push(l, "arguments as UTF-8 through `__wgetmainargs`; Windows' errors are translated to Linux's numbers at")
    strs_push(l, "the boundary, so the library's one mapping serves every target. A DLL is refused by name.")
    strs_push(l, "**Run-verified under Wine** (Wine 8 in a Debian x86_64 container, `docker/wine.Dockerfile`; never a")
    strs_push(l, "Windows host): `windows.rs`'s ignored tests — the 20 conformance programs, and files, TCP and UDP,")
    strs_push(l, "the reactor waking a closed socket's waiter, a peer gone as an error, processes and pipes, the")
    strs_push(l, "clocks, a waiting task releasing the only worker (socket, sleep and pipe), UTF-8 arguments, a trap")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0400`) and an exhausted stack on a thread and in a task (`N0408`), each agreeing with the native")
    strs_push(l, "run, by both backends. Two differences, stated in the spec: `os_family()` is 2, and `os_kill` ends a")
    strs_push(l, "child with exit code 1. Found on the way: an IR string carried a literal NUL byte (now `\\00`).")
    strs_push(l, "**Not done**: a DLL, the MSVC environment, Windows ARM64, a prebuilt toolchain for a Windows host.")
    strs_push(l, "*Execution on a real Windows host, 2026-10-15* (macOS and Windows x86_64 both targets, by the")
    strs_push(l, "copyright holder's decision): `scripts/windows-host.sh` on a Windows 10 laptop (1903,")
    strs_push(l, "10.0.18362.113) — the differential set built for Windows by each backend, linked by MinGW-w64's")
    strs_push(l, "`gcc`, run over `ssh` and compared with the native build: 68 agree, 0 differ, 7 skipped (C,")
    strs_push(l, "arguments, input or files), under LLVM and Cranelift. The first run found two target bugs, fixed in")
    strs_push(l, "`e974b437` with a test and a mutant each: LLVM's `\"probe-stack\"=\"inline-asm\"` became a call to a")
    strs_push(l, "function `inline-asm` on Windows, so a frame of a page or more did not link (now the platform's")
    strs_push(l, "`___chkstk_ms`); and Windows' 1 MiB main stack met `N0408` where macOS and Linux's 8 MiB does not")
    strs_push(l, "(now `-Wl,--stack,8388608`). Files, sockets, processes and arguments remain shown under Wine.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence** · *At N95:* two verified targets: `aarch64-apple-darwin` and `aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu`")
    strs_push(l, "(the latter inside `docker/contained.Dockerfile`). The emitter states its own scope, and")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/docs.rs` asserts the documented target and the emitter agree.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N57, 2026-10-02: cross-compilation — VERIFIED for four targets, with run evidence for three.*")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.59 first. `--target` builds any of the four triples with both backends from")
    strs_push(l, "this host: clang is told the triple, Cranelift is built with its `x86` and `arm64` backends, and")
    strs_push(l, "the runtime text is one for all four under a stated portability rule. An executable where the")
    strs_push(l, "host's toolchain links the target (the host and the other macOS architecture); otherwise")
    strs_push(l, "`--objects DIR` writes every object and `link.txt`, and an executable is refused by name. The")
    strs_push(l, "triple is in every object key under both backends; `nazm inspect` lists each target and what this")
    strs_push(l, "host makes of it. Evidence, `crates/nazm-cli/tests/cross.rs`: all four triples by both backends,")
    strs_push(l, "each object's format and architecture read from its header; the refusal; two targets never one")
    strs_push(l, "cache entry; triples outside the matrix refused. **Run-verified**: `aarch64-apple-darwin` (host),")
    strs_push(l, "`x86_64-apple-darwin` under Rosetta (both backends, `a_program_for_the_other_macos_architecture_runs_where_rosetta_does`),")
    strs_push(l, "`aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu` from macOS-built objects linked and run in the Linux container")
    strs_push(l, "(both backends, by hand: `performance.md`, N57). **Compile-only**: `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N62, 2026-10-02: a freestanding target — VERIFIED on QEMU, one board.* `architecture.md` §7.64")
    strs_push(l, "first. `aarch64-unknown-none`: objects, `link.txt` and `link.ld` (image at `0x40080000`, `_start`")
    strs_push(l, "first, a 64 KiB stack); a board runtime with no thread-local storage and nothing of a C library —")
    strs_push(l, "failure state in plain globals, reported on the PL011 UART, the machine stopped by semihosting —")
    strs_push(l, "and a stack check against the linker's `__stack_bottom`. `mmio_read32`/`mmio_write32` are volatile,")
    strs_push(l, "need an `MmioCap` held, and are refused by `nazm run` and hosted builds (`N0392`). What a board")
    strs_push(l, "program reaches beyond that is read from the generated units' unresolved symbols and refused by")
    strs_push(l, "part. Evidence, `crates/nazm-cli/tests/freestanding.rs` (10, plus one ignored): the objects' ELF")
    strs_push(l, "headers, the linker script, no `STT_TLS` symbol in a board unit or runtime against a hosted one that")
    strs_push(l, "has them, each refusal; **run-verified** by the ignored test in `nazm-qemu:n62` — `ld.lld` links")
    strs_push(l, "the image and `qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a53 -semihosting` boots it: `Hi` written by")
    strs_push(l, "`mmio_write32`, then `100`, status 0; an overflow's `N0400` and a deep recursion's `N0408` on the")
    strs_push(l, "UART, status 2. **Limitation**: one board; no atomics, interrupts, heap or `@std` (§7.64,")
    strs_push(l, "DESIGNED); semihosting stops the machine only under a debugger or QEMU; Cranelift builds no board.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N64, 2026-10-02: WebAssembly — VERIFIED for the freestanding subset, one engine.*")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.66 first. `wasm32-unknown-unknown` from the LLVM backend with the board's")
    strs_push(l, "freestanding law; a runtime that reaches its host only through `nazm_host.write` and")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm_host.report`, a `__multi3` of its own for checked multiplication; `host.mjs`, a reference host")
    strs_push(l, "granting exactly those. Evidence, `crates/nazm-cli/tests/wasm.rs` (5, plus two ignored run in")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-wasm:n64` — `wasm-ld` 19, Node 20): the objects, link line and host; a bound rooted at")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm_main`; the same bytes twice; DWARF in the objects under `--debug`; each refusal. **Run**: the")
    strs_push(l, "linked module's import section read from its bytes — `write` and `report` with `print`, `report`")
    strs_push(l, "alone without an `IoCap`; 64 corpus programs (`transfers`, `compiler/conformance`,")
    strs_push(l, "`bench/programs`, `examples`): 14 run with the interpreter's exact standard output and status,")
    strs_push(l, "50 refused by part, none disagree. **Limitation**: no heap, so most programs are refused; no WASI;")
    strs_push(l, "exports beyond `nazm_main`; no other engine run; a debugger's source mapping not exercised, only")
    strs_push(l, "the sections' presence.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N95, 2026-10-04: the support matrix — VERIFIED as stated; the area stays PARTIAL.*")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.96 first. One table, `nazm_lir::backend::SUPPORT`, printed by `nazm inspect`")
    strs_push(l, "(`toolchain.support`, `toolchain.non_goals`), and this one held to it cell for cell by")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/platform_matrix.rs`, which also requires every target the compiler accepts to")
    strs_push(l, "have a row, every run-verified or compile-only cell to name evidence the tree holds, and each LLVM CPU")
    strs_push(l, "to be the one the C compiler driver resolves for the triple.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Target | LLVM | Cranelift | CPU (LLVM / Cranelift) | Debugger |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `aarch64-apple-darwin` | run-verified | run-verified | apple-m1 / aarch64 baseline | lldb, breakpoints resolved statically, both backends |")
    strs_push(l, "| `x86_64-apple-darwin` | run-verified | run-verified | penryn / x86-64 baseline (SSE2) | not exercised |")
    strs_push(l, "| `aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu` | run-verified | run-verified | generic / aarch64 baseline | gdb, live, both backends |")
    strs_push(l, "| `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu` | compile-only | compile-only | x86-64 / x86-64 baseline (SSE2) | not exercised |")
    strs_push(l, "| `x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` | run-verified on a Windows host | run-verified on a Windows host | x86-64 / x86-64 baseline (SSE2) | not exercised |")
    strs_push(l, "| `aarch64-unknown-none` | run-verified | unsupported | generic / none | not exercised |")
    strs_push(l, "| `riscv64gc-unknown-none-elf` | run-verified | unsupported | generic-rv64 / none | not exercised |")
    strs_push(l, "| `thumbv7m-none-eabi` | run-verified | unsupported | cortex-m3 / none | not exercised |")
    strs_push(l, "| `thumbv8m.main-none-eabihf` | run-verified | unsupported | generic / none | not exercised |")
    strs_push(l, "| `riscv32imc-unknown-none-elf` | run-verified | unsupported | generic-rv32 / none | not exercised |")
    strs_push(l, "| `wasm32-unknown-unknown` | run-verified | unsupported | generic / none | DWARF present, not exercised |")
    strs_push(l, "| `wasm32-wasip1` | run-verified | unsupported | generic / none | DWARF present, not exercised |")
    strs_push(l, "| `aarch64-linux-android` | run-verified on a Linux kernel | unsupported | generic / none | not exercised |")
    strs_push(l, "| `aarch64-apple-ios` | compile-only | unsupported | apple-a7 / none | not exercised |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Run-verified means programs built for the target ran and agreed with the interpreter: on the host,")
    strs_push(l, "under Rosetta, in the Linux image, under QEMU — the three boards, which `support.md` writes")
    strs_push(l, "**emulator-verified**, the kind of run-verified no hardware stands behind (Q1-D-24) — under Node — each cell's test is named in the table in")
    strs_push(l, "code. `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu` is compile-only: no x86_64 Linux machine or image is here. (The Nazm-written pipeline's acceptance of the Linux triples is internal to the container self-build, with no user-facing support claim: `support.md`, 2026-10-20.) A")
    strs_push(l, "freestanding target is unsupported by Cranelift, whose object writer has no format for it, and")
    strs_push(l, "WebAssembly by this Cranelift build. `x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` is run-verified **on a Windows host**: a Windows 10")
    strs_push(l, "laptop, by `scripts/windows-host.sh` (2026-10-15), beside Gate 3C's runs under Wine in a Linux")
    strs_push(l, "container. **Non-goals, by")
    strs_push(l, "decision**: Windows with Microsoft's toolchain and Windows ARM64 (no Microsoft SDK or C runtime is")
    strs_push(l, "accepted here, and no ARM64 Windows machine is here), 32-bit hosted targets (`Int` is 64-bit and hosted layouts assume 64-bit")
    strs_push(l, "pointers), big-endian targets (nothing here runs one; layouts and the DWARF writer assume")
    strs_push(l, "little-endian). The CPU of an LLVM object is the driver's default for its triple, recorded and")
    strs_push(l, "checked, not pinned by a flag — and the driver's own: the recorded CPUs are Apple clang 21's, and the")
    strs_push(l, "Linux image's clang 19 resolves `core2` for `x86_64-apple-darwin` (found by N100's gate), so the check")
    strs_push(l, "runs against Apple clang only. Cranelift detects nothing of the building host.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation** · One Windows host (Windows 10 1903) has run the differential set, files, sockets")
    strs_push(l, "and processes only under Wine; no MSVC or Windows ARM64; no 32-bit,")
    strs_push(l, "big-endian or CPU-feature targets; no bundled linker or")
    strs_push(l, "sysroot, so a Linux target from macOS is objects only; cross-host byte reproducibility not")
    strs_push(l, "measured.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**BLOCKED, and it is a real finding** · `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs")
    strs_push(l, "`cargo test --workspace` and sets neither `NAZM_CONTAINED` nor `NAZM_ALLOW_UNCONTAINED`,")
    strs_push(l, "while `crates/nazm-cli/tests/common/mod.rs` turns that into a panic for the four selfhost")
    strs_push(l, "stage builders. The workflow was last changed before the containment gate existed, so by")
    strs_push(l, "reading, those tests cannot pass in CI. CI also runs on `ubuntu-latest` x86_64, which is")
    strs_push(l, "**neither** verified target. Two candidate fixes — run the selfhost stages through")
    strs_push(l, "`cargo xtask contained`, or exclude them from the CI test step and say so — and choosing")
    strs_push(l, "between them is outside this task.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*R1, 2026-10-07: decided, not yet evidenced.* CI is the **host-safe subset**, and not the release")
    strs_push(l, "gate. `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs `cargo xtask workspace-tests --host-safe`, which builds every")
    strs_push(l, "test binary and runs each except those whose source calls the containment guard — today")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-cli test:selfhost` — naming each one it leaves out; the guard itself is unchanged. The")
    strs_push(l, "mutation catalogue left CI for the contained gate, where the runbook already required it. The")
    strs_push(l, "selfhost stages, bootstrap, fuzzing and mutation run only in `cargo xtask contained` and the release")
    strs_push(l, "gate. The runner is x86_64 Linux, and that changes no target cell: a compile-only target becomes")
    strs_push(l, "run-verified by a recorded run of Nazm-built programs there, not by CI compiling the project.")
    strs_push(l, "Nothing has been pushed, so the workflow has not run on GitHub; its first run is the evidence this")
    strs_push(l, "section is still waiting for.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Next dependency** · A first green run of the host-safe workflow on GitHub, recorded.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Accepted when** · CI runs green on a stated target and the stated target is one the")
    strs_push(l, "project verifies.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### 34. Smart contracts — PARTIAL")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N96, 2026-10-04: generated sequences on the reference VMs — VERIFIED; the area stays PARTIAL, sBPF")
    strs_push(l, "BLOCKED.* `architecture.md` §7.97 first. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/contract_property.rs`: three seeded")
    strs_push(l, "sequences of 250 transactions, generated from `nazm.contract/1`'s entrypoints with callers among the")
    strs_push(l, "owner and two others and arguments at `Int`'s edges, over a contract with transfers, an owner's")
    strs_push(l, "switch, a conservation breach, a loop, overflow and division. On any host the simulator is")
    strs_push(l, "deterministic and every committed state keeps the conserved quantity; with `--ignored`, py-evm")
    strs_push(l, "(`nazm-evm:n70`) and the WebAssembly reference host (`nazm-wasm:n64`) agree with it on all 750")
    strs_push(l, "outcomes, codes and final states, and every EVM transaction stays inside its stated gas bound. sBPF")
    strs_push(l, "remains BLOCKED: this machine has no BPF target in its C compiler and no Solana toolchain, validator or")
    strs_push(l, "emulator. Not in the model, and not added: events, external calls and reentrancy, assets as types,")
    strs_push(l, "metering beyond the bound, a chain's own WebAssembly host, migrations beyond `--upgrade-check`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N69, 2026-10-02: the chain-neutral model — VERIFIED for the model and its simulator.*")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.71 first. A contract is an ordinary module — a `State` record of `Int`s and")
    strs_push(l, "`Bool`s, `init`, and pure entrypoints returning `Result[State, Int]` — held to the `web3` profile")
    strs_push(l, "(declared effects; no `io`, tasks, channels, clock, C or recursion). `nazm contract` writes")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.contract/1`: the state, each entrypoint's arguments, and its read and write sets, exact for a")
    strs_push(l, "state built in the result and conservative (\"all\") where the analysis does not follow it; external")
    strs_push(l, "calls do not exist in the model, so no reentrancy is claimed or analysed. `nazm contract --txs` runs")
    strs_push(l, "transactions deterministically on the interpreter: `Ok` commits, `Err` and runtime failures revert")
    strs_push(l, "with their codes, a declared `conserved` quantity must hold or the transaction is rejected (`N0396`),")
    strs_push(l, "and a meter counts calls and loop turns. Evidence, `crates/nazm-cli/tests/contract.rs` (7): the")
    strs_push(l, "facts for six entrypoints; thirteen transactions — commits, reverts by code, the owner's authority,")
    strs_push(l, "a conservation breach rejected with the state unchanged, malformed lines — and the same bytes twice;")
    strs_push(l, "a runtime failure reverting with `N0400`; five profile refusals; four not-a-contract refusals; a pure")
    strs_push(l, "function the same under `web3`. **Limitation**: no chain backend yet; assets are a conserved")
    strs_push(l, "quantity checked per transaction, not a linear type; no events, external calls or gas.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N70, 2026-10-02: the EVM backend — VERIFIED against py-evm for the contract model's subset.*")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.72 first. `nazm contract --evm DIR` compiles a contract directly from Core IR")
    strs_push(l, "to deployment and runtime bytecode (no Yul or `solc`): `i64` held exactly in 256-bit words, helpers")
    strs_push(l, "inlined, the state read and written at name-derived slots, `conserved` enforced on-chain, failures")
    strs_push(l, "and `Err` reverting distinguishably. `abi.json` gives each `name(int64,…)` and its selector from the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler's keccak-256 (agreeing with `eth_hash`); `storage.json` the slots; `--upgrade-check` refuses a")
    strs_push(l, "removed or retyped field and allows an added one. Evidence, `crates/nazm-cli/tests/evm.rs` (3 on any")
    strs_push(l, "host — selectors and a slot pinned, a bound for every loop-free entrypoint and none for a loop, the")
    strs_push(l, "deployment copying its runtime from the right offset, the same bytes twice, a refusal before")
    strs_push(l, "emission, the upgrade check; 1 ignored, run in `nazm-evm:n70` — 19 transactions with the")
    strs_push(l, "simulator's outcomes, codes and final storage, the language's truncating division, remainder sign,")
    strs_push(l, "zero divisor and `i64::MIN / -1` on the EVM, and measured gas inside every stated bound, e.g.")
    strs_push(l, "`transfer` 21,598 of 63,806). **Limitation**: one reference EVM (py-evm, Shanghai); no events, value")
    strs_push(l, "or external calls (none in the model); the gas bound is loose (worst-case `SSTORE`s) and open for")
    strs_push(l, "loops; the EVM's execution semantics are held by the ignored test only.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N71, 2026-10-02: contracts on WebAssembly — VERIFIED with the reference host, one engine.*")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.73 first. `nazm contract --wasm DIR` builds the contract with the ordinary")
    strs_push(l, "WebAssembly backend (§7.66) and appends one generated adapter to its own unit: `nazm_init` and a")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm_call_<entry>` per entrypoint, moving the state across `nazm_host.state_get`/`state_set` by")
    strs_push(l, "declaration index, reverting through `nazm_host.revert`, checking `conserved` in the module, and")
    strs_push(l, "reporting failures through `report`. `contract.json` (`nazm.wasm-contract/1`) records fields,")
    strs_push(l, "exports, imports and status codes; `contract_host.mjs` keeps the state and runs each transaction in")
    strs_push(l, "a fresh instance. Evidence, `crates/nazm-cli/tests/wasm_contract.rs` (2 anywhere — the metadata, the")
    strs_push(l, "unit's host imports, the same bytes twice, the ordinary build without the adapter; 1 ignored, run in")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-wasm:n64` — 14 transactions with the simulator's outcomes, codes and final state, a run-time")
    strs_push(l, "overflow reverting with `N0400`, and the linked module importing exactly the four host functions).")
    strs_push(l, "**Limitation**: no chain's own host interface is bound to the four imports; one engine (Node).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N72, 2026-10-02: account-oriented contracts — VERIFIED for signed writes and metadata; sBPF execution")
    strs_push(l, "BLOCKED.* `architecture.md` §7.74 first. The `accounts` profile adds `signed-writes`: an entrypoint that")
    strs_push(l, "writes the state must decide on its `caller` in its own body, or is refused by name; a check made only")
    strs_push(l, "in a helper is not trusted. `nazm contract --accounts DIR` writes `accounts.json`")
    strs_push(l, "(`nazm.sbpf-accounts/1`): the state account's layout, each instruction's discriminator and argument")
    strs_push(l, "offsets, and its accounts' writable and signer constraints derived from the read and write sets.")
    strs_push(l, "Evidence, `crates/nazm-cli/tests/accounts.rs` (3): an unguarded write refused while three others pass,")
    strs_push(l, "`web3` alone not asking for signers; a helper's check not trusted; the metadata's layout, discriminator,")
    strs_push(l, "offsets and constraints. **BLOCKED**: no sBPF toolchain, validator or emulator here; upstream `bpfel`")
    strs_push(l, "is not sBPF, so no object or run is claimed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N73, 2026-10-02: trust evidence — fuzzing PARTIAL (area 30), build provenance VERIFIED (area 32),")
    strs_push(l, "cross-toolchain reproducibility measured.* `architecture.md` §7.75 first. Two seeded fuzzers, the same")
    strs_push(l, "inputs on every host. `crates/nazm-core/tests/fuzz_front.rs` mutates every source of six corpora")
    strs_push(l, "(deletions, duplications, swaps, replaced characters, inserted tokens) and checks each in process: no")
    strs_push(l, "panic, shrunk if one is found; 1,500 cases per run, 60,000 run clean once. `crates/nazm-cli/tests/fuzz_diff.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "generates well-typed, terminating programs (every `Int` operator from edge literals, comparisons,")
    strs_push(l, "`&&`/`||`, `let`, `if`, bounded `while`, calls, a record) and requires one answer from the interpreter,")
    strs_push(l, "LLVM at `-O0` and `-O2` and Cranelift — the value, or the failure code and place; a disagreement is")
    strs_push(l, "shrunk by lines, and `tests/fuzz-corpus/` is replayed first. 24 cases per run; 150 on another seed agree.")
    strs_push(l, "**Shown to find faults**: an unsigned `<` injected into either backend is caught by the differential")
    strs_push(l, "fuzzer (Cranelift's by N41's named test as well), and a lexer panic on one character by the robustness")
    strs_push(l, "fuzzer and by no `nazm-syntax` or `nazm-core` test — three mutants whose named killer is a fuzzer. `nazm build --provenance FILE` writes `nazm.provenance/1` — sources and packages with BLAKE3")
    strs_push(l, "digests, target, compiler, C compiler, runtime ABI and digest, backend and options, profiles, output")
    strs_push(l, "digests — and `--attest-with CMD` keeps a local command's output as `FILE.sig`. `cargo xtask evidence")
    strs_push(l, "DIR` writes an evidence bundle's `index.json` (`nazm.evidence/1`: every file's path, size, BLAKE3 and")
    strs_push(l, "kind) and the compiler's `sbom.json` (`nazm.sbom/1`: the 261 crates `Cargo.lock` pins, and the")
    strs_push(l, "toolchain), offline; `--verify` refuses a changed, missing or unindexed file by name")
    strs_push(l, "(`xtask/tests/evidence.rs`, 3). Evidence, `crates/nazm-cli/tests/build_provenance.rs` (5): digests recomputed from the files, two clean")
    strs_push(l, "directories giving one record, a change seen in its own digest and the output's, the backend recorded,")
    strs_push(l, "a failing signer leaving no signature, a failed build leaving no record. *Across toolchains*: one")
    strs_push(l, "program built for `aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu` by Apple clang 21 (host) and clang 19 (Linux image) —")
    strs_push(l, "the program's and the entry's objects byte-identical at `-O0` and `-O2`; the runtime's object differs,")
    strs_push(l, "at `-O0` by one symbol-table byte (a mapping symbol's type) and at `-O2` by code layout (clang 21's")
    strs_push(l, "cold-path splitting). **Limitation**: not coverage-guided (`cargo fuzz` needs nightly and a new")
    strs_push(l, "dependency); the differential generator covers `Int`/`Bool` programs only; no sanitizer, Miri or Loom")
    strs_push(l, "run (no `unsafe` code to run them on); an attestation is whatever the local command printed — Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "neither signs nor verifies.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N74, 2026-10-02: ecosystem tooling — VERIFIED as scoped (areas 17, 25, 26).* `architecture.md` §7.76")
    strs_push(l, "first, amended twice before code. `nazm init` writes six templates — `cli`, `library`, `server`,")
    strs_push(l, "`embedded`, `wasm`, `contract` — each a package whose own commands check, test, lock and document it,")
    strs_push(l, "and build or run it where the target allows; a library package is checked as its modules. `nazm doc`")
    strs_push(l, "documents exactly the public definitions, from the checker's facts, anchored by identity and linked")
    strs_push(l, "to source lines; `nazm bindgen` translates the `int64_t`/`bool`/`const char *` subset of a C header")
    strs_push(l, "and refuses the rest by name; `nazm publish --dry-run` writes nothing and names the digest the publish")
    strs_push(l, "then records; `nazm capabilities` lists every authority type, target and command. The language")
    strs_push(l, "service is tested across a package boundary — definition, references, hover and workspace symbols reach")
    strs_push(l, "the dependency, its errors are published against it, and renaming its public function is refused —")
    strs_push(l, "and `editors/vscode` is a client for `nazm lsp` with a launch configuration for an LLDB adapter.")
    strs_push(l, "Evidence: `crates/nazm-cli/tests/ecosystem.rs` (10: every template end to end, init's refusals, every")
    strs_push(l, "template file written, the library check reporting a shared error once, the API document's members,")
    strs_push(l, "facts, sources, anchors, determinism and size, bindgen's translations and nine refusals, its output")
    strs_push(l, "linked against real C and run, the dry run, the inventory, the editor client), `nazm-service`'s")
    strs_push(l, "`tests/across_packages.rs` (3), and four new schemas validated against real output in")
    strs_push(l, "`tests/schemas.rs`. **Limitation**: the editor client is not exercised inside an editor here and is")
    strs_push(l, "not published; no Nazm debug adapter; rename across packages is refused, not performed; `bindgen`")
    strs_push(l, "reads declarations, not the C preprocessor; no network registry; the agent benchmark was not re-run,")
    strs_push(l, "and no efficiency claim is made.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 3D (2026-10-10)** · *The systems foundation* (`spec.md` *Atomics*, *Statics*, *Boards*;")
    strs_push(l, "`systems-domains.md` Part B). **Atomics:** `Atomic`, one `Int` cell, sequentially consistent, that")
    strs_push(l, "crosses into a task — the interpreter, both backends (four runtime entries; `atomic_add` a checked")
    strs_push(l, "compare-and-swap loop) and the LIR oracle (`atomics.rs`). **Statics:** a number, a `Bool` or an")
    strs_push(l, "atomic, read-only unless an atomic (`N0625`), defined in its module's own unit under a durable")
    strs_push(l, "`nz.s.` symbol and imported by every other — generic instances too (`statics.rs`). **Boards:** a")
    strs_push(l, "manifest (`--board`, `N0626`) that the built-in boards print as; `@section`, kept by the generated")
    strs_push(l, "`link.ld` (`sections.rs`); 64-bit device registers; AArch64 interrupts — a vector table, a GICv2,")
    strs_push(l, "the virtual timer, named lines, handlers held to their shape (`N0627`, `interrupts.rs`); a bump")
    strs_push(l, "arena for a manifest's `[heap]` that admits strings, sequences and closures, and `no-heap` in the")
    strs_push(l, "new `kernel` profile (`heap.rs`); `@on_failure` (`kernel.rs`). **Emulator-verified**, every")
    strs_push(l, "mechanism and the reference kernel-style workload booted under QEMU at `-O0` and `-O2` in the")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-qemu:n86` image (each file's ignored test, run by hand); RISC-V has no interrupts, and nothing")
    strs_push(l, "has run on hardware. Semantic epoch 49, runtime ABI 24. Found on the way: Cranelift's x86-64")
    strs_push(l, "backend converts a float only to a 32- or 64-bit integer (3B-2, fixed); a placed function was")
    strs_push(l, "inlined away at `-O2` (now hidden linkage); a failure hook's first call looked like a failure while")
    strs_push(l, "the program's flag was set (cleared before the hook).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 3E (2026-10-11)** · *Embedded* (`spec.md` *A freestanding target*, *Boards*; `systems-domains.md`")
    strs_push(l, "Part C). **The Cortex-M board:** `thumbv7m-none-eabi` on QEMU's `mps2-an385`, the ninth target — 32-bit")
    strs_push(l, "pointers and a 64-bit `Int`; a vector table at 0; the CMSDK UART; AArch32 semihosting; the 64-bit")
    strs_push(l, "atomics (interrupts masked), division and the EABI's memory functions the board's runtime defines;")
    strs_push(l, "floating point, 64-bit device registers and a heap refused by name (`cortex_m.rs`). **Interrupts on a")
    strs_push(l, "Cortex-M:** an NVIC and SysTick from a manifest's `controller = \"nvic\"` and `clock_hz`. **`@std/hal`:**")
    strs_push(l, "`Uart`, `Pin`, `Timer` and the emulated boards' impls. **The reference workload:** one traffic light,")
    strs_push(l, "generic over the HAL, run unchanged on both AArch64 `virt` and the Cortex-M3 (`embedded.rs`).")
    strs_push(l, "**Emulator-verified** at `-O0` and `-O2` in the `nazm-qemu:n86` image; nothing on hardware. Runtime ABI")
    strs_push(l, "25. Found on the way: an atomic passed by value reached the string runtime's reference counting on a")
    strs_push(l, "heapless board (now a no-op there, every owner being null), and a Cortex-M3 has no CMSDK GPIO in QEMU,")
    strs_push(l, "so its pins are the FPGA LED register.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 3F (2026-10-11)** · *Realtime* (`spec.md` *Restriction profiles*, *Boards*; `systems-domains.md`")
    strs_push(l, "Part D). `realtime` gains `bounded-stack` (no call cycle, no call through a function value) and")
    strs_push(l, "`no-heap`. A board's **fixed-priority scheduler**: `@task(priority = \"N\", period = \"P\")` in board-timer")
    strs_push(l, "ticks; `main` runs first as the initialisation, then the highest-priority released task runs to")
    strs_push(l, "completion, one at a time, the core waiting for an interrupt when none is; a task released again before")
    strs_push(l, "it has run fails the image (`N0414`, new); a task's non-zero answer ends the run; the scheduler owns the")
    strs_push(l, "timer. **Emulator-verified** on both boards at `-O0` and `-O2` (`realtime_tasks.rs`): the higher priority")
    strs_push(l, "ten times by the lower's fourth run (`1004`), an overrun reported. No WCET, no preemption, never \"hard")
    strs_push(l, "real-time\". Semantic epoch 50. Found on the way: `-O2` deletes a busy loop that does nothing visible, so")
    strs_push(l, "an overrun test must do observable work.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 3G-1 (2026-10-11)** · *Domain profiles* (`spec.md` *Restriction profiles*, *Domain profiles*,")
    strs_push(l, "*Boards*; `systems-domains.md` Parts E–J). The constitution for the six domain profiles and their")
    strs_push(l, "three domain rules (`watchdog`, `audit`, `no-float-nondeterminism`), the runtime watchdog and")
    strs_push(l, "`N0415`. Four are enforced now, each a composition held to its definition (`domain_profiles.rs`):")
    strs_push(l, "`robotics` (`realtime` + `explicit-authority`), `automotive` (`realtime` + `critical`), `aerospace`")
    strs_push(l, "(`embedded` + `realtime` + `critical` + `no-float-nondeterminism`, refusing the nine transcendental")
    strs_push(l, "built-ins by site) and `assurance` (`critical` + `no-recursion`, `bounded-loops`, `bounded-stack`,")
    strs_push(l, "`no-heap`). A board's periodic program, as a locked package, passes and builds under all four. The")
    strs_push(l, "`spec.md` rows for `critical` and `cyber` now name `no-unknown-calls` and `checked-paths`, which they")
    strs_push(l, "had held since N80 and N87. No certification, qualification or approval is claimed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 3G-2 (2026-10-11)** · *Domain workloads* (`systems-domains.md` Parts E–J; `domains.rs`).")
    strs_push(l, "`@std/linalg`: `Vec3`, `Mat3` and their sums, products, norm and length bound over `Float64`, nothing")
    strs_push(l, "allocated, every operation correctly rounded. Four reference workloads, each held to its profile as a")
    strs_push(l, "locked package and booted under QEMU at `-O0` and `-O2`: **robotics** (sense, control through")
    strs_push(l, "`@std/linalg`, a bounded command, convergence, a missed deadline stopping safely), **aerospace**")
    strs_push(l, "(simulated sensors, a complementary filter, telemetry, a sensor fault and its transition,")
    strs_push(l, "byte-identical across levels), **automotive** (an ECU state machine and checksummed frames,")
    strs_push(l, "byte-identical on AArch64 and Cortex-M3) and **assurance** (a heater controller whose every obligation")
    strs_push(l, "is `proved` or `checked`, holding and tripping on both boards). Found and fixed on the way: a heapless")
    strs_push(l, "64-bit board had no `memcpy` or `memset`, which code generation calls for a large value's copy — now")
    strs_push(l, "every AArch64 and RISC-V board has the C library's memory functions; and AArch64 board code may now")
    strs_push(l, "make no unaligned access (`-mstrict-align`), since with the MMU off every access is to Device memory")
    strs_push(l, "and a 16-byte SIMD copy at an 8-byte boundary faulted. Found, not fixed: `float_round`, `float_min`")
    strs_push(l, "and `float_max` call the C library and are refused on a board (`limitations.md`). Emulator-verified;")
    strs_push(l, "sensors simulated; no certification.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 3G-3 (2026-10-11)** · *Industrial and the watchdog* (`spec.md` *Boards*, *Domain profiles*;")
    strs_push(l, "`domains.rs`). A board's manifest may have `[watchdog] ticks = N`, counted on the scheduler's ticks:")
    strs_push(l, "`watchdog_feed()` — a device's authority, as `mmio_*` — re-arms it, and `N` ticks without a feed fail")
    strs_push(l, "the image with `N0415` (new), the failure hook first. Refused by name: a feed for a board without one,")
    strs_push(l, "a watchdog with no `@task`, a watchdog without the timer (`N0626`), a hosted feed (`N0392`). The")
    strs_push(l, "`industrial` profile is `realtime` + `critical` + `watchdog`, the rule that a `@task` feeds it. The")
    strs_push(l, "batch controller runs three batches on both boards at both levels, fails safe on overfill, and a loop")
    strs_push(l, "`bounded-loops` admits — 10^12 turns — is caught by the watchdog: a stated bound is not an execution")
    strs_push(l, "time. Semantic epoch 51, runtime ABI 26. The watchdog is the runtime's, not a hardware one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 3G-4 (2026-10-11)** · *Medical-device style* (`spec.md` *Domain profiles*; `domains.rs`).")
    strs_push(l, "`@std/audit`'s `audit_transition` writes a transition's record, a JSON object on its own line, to a")
    strs_push(l, "board's UART, allocating nothing. The `medical` profile is `realtime` + `critical` + `audit`: every")
    strs_push(l, "function of the program that calls `atomic_store`, `atomic_swap` or `atomic_compare_swap` must call")
    strs_push(l, "`audit_transition` itself, each unrecorded change refused by its site; `atomic_add` counts and is not")
    strs_push(l, "a transition. The infusion pump runs on both boards at both levels, its six records in order, a pause")
    strs_push(l, "and resume, and an occlusion's fault state. No regulatory approval is claimed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 3G-5 (2026-10-11)** · *Cybersecurity* (`systems-domains.md` Part K; `secure_service.rs`). The")
    strs_push(l, "reference secure service: a TCP service whose protocol answers five capital letters reversed and")
    strs_push(l, "anything else `DENY!`, never echoed, its authority handed down from `main`. Held to `cyber` as a")
    strs_push(l, "locked package and served to three real clients on the loopback. Each of `cyber`'s refusals is shown")
    strs_push(l, "on a variant of it: a source changed after locking, a client's bytes on standard output (and, without")
    strs_push(l, "an `OutCap`, the language's own `N0369` first), a function with no declared contract, a call into C,")
    strs_push(l, "a call through a function value. Built twice in two directories, its executable, provenance record")
    strs_push(l, "and SBOM are byte-identical; its record, signed with `ssh-keygen`, verifies and is refused once the")
    strs_push(l, "executable changes. Run-verified on macOS AArch64; signing is the host's `ssh-keygen`. No sandboxing,")
    strs_push(l, "non-interference or certification claim.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 3H (2026-10-11)** · *AI / HPC* (`spec.md` *Accelerator kernels*, *Providers*, *SIMD*;")
    strs_push(l, "`systems-domains.md` Part L; `accel_providers.rs`). A **provider boundary**: a kernel is one source")
    strs_push(l, "text — the OpenCL C a device builds, with an element function `nz_item` beside the `__kernel` — and a")
    strs_push(l, "provider runs it. The OpenCL provider builds it for Apple's GPU; the new **CPU provider** compiles")
    strs_push(l, "the same text as C behind a prelude for OpenCL's words and runs `nz_item` over a pool of threads.")
    strs_push(l, "`--provider auto|opencl|cpu`: `auto` runs on the GPU where it can and otherwise on the CPU, saying")
    strs_push(l, "why in the report and on stderr; where the GPU ran it, the CPU provider runs it too as a second")
    strs_push(l, "oracle (`cross_check`). **Float kernels**, `Float32` and `Float64`, one type throughout, `float_sqrt`")
    strs_push(l, "and `float_abs` the built-ins they may call, held to the interpreter bit for bit (every NaN alike):")
    strs_push(l, "no fused multiply-add on either provider, division and square root correctly rounded on the device.")
    strs_push(l, "Verified here: `Int` and `Float32` on the GPU and the CPU, agreeing with each other and the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter; `Float64` refused by name on Apple's GPU (no `cl_khr_fp64`) and run on the CPU. `--scalar`")
    strs_push(l, "builds the CPU loop without LLVM's vectoriser; the comparison is filed in `performance.md`.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.accel/3`. Metal, CUDA, ROCm and SPIR-V remain named future providers.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 3I (2026-10-11)** · *Storage and the distributed foundation* (`systems-domains.md` Parts M,")
    strs_push(l, "N; `storage.rs`, `distributed.rs`). `examples/apps/pagestore`: fixed checksummed pages written in")
    strs_push(l, "place behind a redo log of whole page images, a fresh store made atomically, one owner task serving")
    strs_push(l, "readers and a writer through channels, a lock for one process. A run is crashed at **every** write")
    strs_push(l, "boundary — half that write written — and each recovery checked against a model of the acknowledged")
    strs_push(l, "writes: all there, nothing else but the one in flight, torn pages repaired from the log. The test")
    strs_push(l, "found two defects in the engine as first written (a log handle kept across the checkpoint that")
    strs_push(l, "replaced its file; a reopen that reset the crash counter), both fixed before this was committed.")
    strs_push(l, "`@std/dist`: `NodeId`, framed `Msg`, the `Transport` trait with `Tcp` and `Local`, `retry` with")
    strs_push(l, "backoff and an idempotency key. `examples/apps/ledger`: a server stopped after logging a credit and")
    strs_push(l, "before answering, restarted on its address, the client's retry carrying it through, every credit")
    strs_push(l, "applied exactly once; in one process, a lost answer timing out through `select`, interpreted and")
    strs_push(l, "native alike. No database-maturity, consensus or partition-tolerance claim.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 3J (2026-10-11)** · *WASI* (`spec.md` *WASI*; `systems-domains.md` Part O; `wasi.rs`).")
    strs_push(l, "`wasm32-wasip1`, the tenth target: a heap — a bump arena grown by")
    strs_push(l, "`memory.grow` — under the parts a board with a heap takes, so strings, sequences, `Bytes` and")
    strs_push(l, "closures run; standard streams, arguments, the clocks and `time_sleep`; files and handles beneath")
    strs_push(l, "the first preopened directory, a path outside it refused by the host; a failure reported with")
    strs_push(l, "status 2. Tasks, channels and the network are refused by name: preview 1 has no threads or")
    strs_push(l, "sockets. Run-verified at `-O0` and `-O2` under Node's `node:wasi` in `nazm-wasm:n64`, every import")
    strs_push(l, "`wasi_snapshot_preview1`'s. Narrowed: no directory listing, environment or freeing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 3K (2026-10-11)** · *Mobile and desktop* (`spec.md` *Mobile targets*; `systems-domains.md`")
    strs_push(l, "Parts P, Q; `mobile.rs`). Two more targets. `aarch64-linux-android`: Linux's kernel with Bionic, a")
    strs_push(l, "switch target of its own; a C host and a Nazm library, and a whole program with its task pool,")
    strs_push(l, "channels, files and clock, built as static executables by the NDK r27c and **run on an aarch64 Linux")
    strs_push(l, "kernel** — a new support status, `run-verified on a Linux kernel`, because no Android device or")
    strs_push(l, "emulator ran them. `aarch64-apple-ios`: Darwin's unit; an archive and a program **linked** against")
    strs_push(l, "Xcode 27's iOS SDK and never run (`compile-only`), no simulator runtime being installed. `--backend")
    strs_push(l, "cranelift` is refused for both. The desktop example, `examples/desktop/counter`: a Cocoa window whose")
    strs_push(l, "button callbacks call a Nazm shared library's state machine through the C ABI, driven by synthetic")
    strs_push(l, "clicks, every label checked — run-verified on this host.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 3L (2026-10-11)** · *Web3 qualification and traceability* (`systems-domains.md` Parts R, S;")
    strs_push(l, "`spec.md` *Requirements traceability*). The web3 qualification: every claim of the contract model,")
    strs_push(l, "its profiles, the EVM and WebAssembly backends' agreement with the simulator and the upgrade check,")
    strs_push(l, "each against the test that holds it. Tightened: an EVM entrypoint's gas bound now runs through a")
    strs_push(l, "loop in the counted form — its turns times its condition and body — where it had been `null`; the")
    strs_push(l, "EVM stays inside it (`evm.rs`, py-evm). sBPF BLOCKED. `nazm trace FILE --requirements FILE`,")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.trace/1`: each requirement to its definitions by durable identity and Core IR digest, their")
    strs_push(l, "obligations keyed by definition, and its `@test`s run; a renamed definition, a missing or failing test")
    strs_push(l, "reported by name and failing the trace (`trace.rs`, `examples/requirements`). No certification.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    str_join(l, str_from_byte(10)) + str_from_byte(10)
}

fn dd_doc4() -> Str {
    let l = strs_new()
    strs_push(l, "# Master architecture")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Status: the durable constitution. Every other document is dated; this one states what")
    strs_push(l, "must stay true across all of them.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "This document does not describe the compiler. [`architecture.md`](architecture.md) does")
    strs_push(l, "that, and does it well — the IR levels (§2), the layout-selection boundary (§4), mutable")
    strs_push(l, "value semantics with a region hedge and the three-way split of effects, capabilities and")
    strs_push(l, "provenance (§5). None of that is restated here. What did not exist anywhere until now is")
    strs_push(l, "the layer above: the invariants that outrank any particular design, the vocabulary claims")
    strs_push(l, "must be made in, and the model under which one language serves several domains.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "It is also not a plan and not an ambition. [`roadmap.md`](../user/roadmap.md) is the ordering")
    strs_push(l, "authority. [`NAZM_LANGUAGE_GOALS.md`](NAZM_LANGUAGE_GOALS.md) is where Nazm is ultimately")
    strs_push(l, "going and why — **this file is what must stay true while it gets there.** The two are")
    strs_push(l, "separate on purpose: the Goals document is deliberately broad and changes rarely; this one")
    strs_push(l, "has to stay cheap enough to load on every task.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Where this document and a dated one disagree about *what is true today*, the evidence in")
    strs_push(l, "[`capability-matrix.md`](capability-matrix.md) decides — not this file. And nothing in the")
    strs_push(l, "Goals document is evidence for anything: **a goal appearing there never moves a capability")
    strs_push(l, "row.** That file says so itself, in its §0.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 1. How a claim is allowed to be stated")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The repository has separated evidence classes since the 2026-09-20 decision record, which")
    strs_push(l, "named four kinds of statement and where each lives. **That record was retired on 2026-09-21")
    strs_push(l, "and its vocabulary lives here**, at the granularity a matrix row needs:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Word | Means | The original four kinds |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **VERIFIED** | Executed evidence against the current tree, and a named artefact that fails if it stops being true | Implemented behaviour |")
    strs_push(l, "| **PARTIAL** | Real and running, but narrower than the name suggests. The row says exactly how much narrower | Implemented behaviour, scoped |")
    strs_push(l, "| **DESIGNED** | Decided and written down; no implementation. Changing it is a re-founding decision | Accepted design |")
    strs_push(l, "| **RESEARCH** | A hypothesis with a falsifier. Not entitled to be called a plan | Research proposal |")
    strs_push(l, "| **BLOCKED** | Wanted, specified enough to start, and stopped by a named dependency | Open question, with the blocker named |")
    strs_push(l, "| **MISSING** | Absent, and nothing here commits to adding it | — |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Three rules govern their use, and the first is the one this project has actually broken:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "1. **A document, a stub, a crate name or a passing test does not move a row up this")
    strs_push(l, "   table.** The 2026-09-20 record said this before any of it was built. It was still violated:")
    strs_push(l, "   `crates/nazm-lir` exists and matches the *name* of `architecture.md` §2's level 7, and")
    strs_push(l, "   four documents concluded from the name that the level existed. See §3.")
    strs_push(l, "2. **VERIFIED cites a path.** A row without one is PARTIAL at best. `cargo xtask check`")
    strs_push(l, "   now enforces this — see `xtask/src/main.rs`, `check_doc_claims`.")
    strs_push(l, "3. **Absence of a refutation is not evidence.** A quiet period is observation. A test that")
    strs_push(l, "   self-skips has established nothing; `crates/nazm-bench/tests/docker_boundary.rs` is ignored")
    strs_push(l, "   by default (M1) and refuses without `NAZM_REQUIRE_DOCKER=1`, rather than counting itself as")
    strs_push(l, "   coverage (`docs/internal/integration-testing.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "4. **A count is not a proof.** Source inspection, a successful compile, runtime behaviour,")
    strs_push(l, "   mutation discrimination, performance and platform support are **different evidence")
    strs_push(l, "   classes**, and one never substitutes for another. Test counts are not capability proofs.")
    strs_push(l, "   LLVM validation catches malformed IR, not semantic miscompilation — which is why every")
    strs_push(l, "   native case is checked against an explicit expected outcome rather than against exit")
    strs_push(l, "   status. **passed**, **skipped**, **refused**, **failed** and **unexecuted** are five")
    strs_push(l, "   outcomes and are never reported as one another.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 2. The twelve laws")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Each law is followed by where the repository actually stands against it. That second line")
    strs_push(l, "is the point: a law nobody has checked against the tree is decoration. *Every status below was")
    strs_push(l, "checked against the tree again for the v0.3.0 release (R1, 2026-10-07); a status that had")
    strs_push(l, "fallen behind was rewritten, with what it used to say kept where the argument needs it. Gate 1")
    strs_push(l, "of the v1 programme (2026-10-07) froze the 1.x contract (`stability.md`) without moving a law,")
    strs_push(l, "and found one status that had overclaimed: law 3's reclamation claim had an exception, a closure")
    strs_push(l, "stored into a `Vec` it captured (`spec.md`, *Cycles*). Gate 1-C1 closed it by refusing the")
    strs_push(l, "capture (`N0616`), so the law stands as it was written.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**1 — Plain UTF-8 `.nz` files in git are the authoritative source.**")
    strs_push(l, "*Honoured.* No derived-source store exists. `architecture.md` §3 gives the reasoning and")
    strs_push(l, "the counter-example (Unison) it is drawn from. Content addressing, if it ever arrives,")
    strs_push(l, "applies to derived artefacts only.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**2 — Native execution is the primary execution model.**")
    strs_push(l, "*Honoured.* `nazm build` produces a native executable with no runtime process, through LLVM")
    strs_push(l, "or Cranelift, and the two paths cover the same language: `nazm capabilities` lists every")
    strs_push(l, "construct for both, and the only differences are deliberate — a call into C is compiled and not")
    strs_push(l, "interpreted, and the iteration budget is the interpreter's. *Until N49 this read \"partial, and the")
    strs_push(l, "gap is the wrong way round\": recursion ran under `nazm run` and both compilers refused it with")
    strs_push(l, "`N0101`. Native recursion has a stack check on entry to every function in a call cycle (`N0408`).*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**3 — Safety must not require a mandatory garbage collector.**")
    strs_push(l, "*Honoured, and partly earned as of N7 (2026-09-22).* There is no GC and no tracing of any")
    strs_push(l, "kind. Sequence storage is reclaimed by counting references to the handle, deterministically")
    strs_push(l, "and on every exit edge including the one a failure takes; `docs/user/spec.md`'s *memory")
    strs_push(l, "constitution* is the law and `architecture.md` §7.7 the implementation. A short-lived")
    strs_push(l, "sequence workload that grew linearly with work done — 43.52 MiB for a live set of 400 bytes")
    strs_push(l, "— is now flat at 1.86.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Earned for the current type universe as of N8 (2026-09-22).* `Str` and `Chan` storage is")
    strs_push(l, "reclaimed too, in both compilers and in the reference interpreter — a `Str` carries the")
    strs_push(l, "allocation that owns its bytes (`architecture.md` §7.8), a channel's ring, mutex and")
    strs_push(l, "condition variable go with its last reference, and the self-hosted backend emits the same")
    strs_push(l, "model. The string accumulator that took the machine down on 2026-09-21 fell from 70.66 MiB")
    strs_push(l, "to 2.23 MiB at 8,000 iterations.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Whole-language leak freedom is still not claimed, and the reason is not modesty.** The")
    strs_push(l, "claim covers six built-in types and rests on the fact that none of them can refer to a value")
    strs_push(l, "that refers back. The first recursive user-defined type ends that argument, and")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/spec.md`'s *Cycles* states in advance what admitting one requires.")
    strs_push(l, "`capability-matrix.md` area 4 states the scope per type.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Gate 1, 2026-10-07: an exception was found.* Function values (N50) are a value kind that can")
    strs_push(l, "refer back: a closure holds the handles it captured, so a closure stored into a `Vec` it captures")
    strs_push(l, "owned itself, and counting did not reclaim it. **Gate 1-C1 (2026-10-07) refused it** the way N11")
    strs_push(l, "refused cycles of definitions: a closure's environment is a node of the ownership graph, and a")
    strs_push(l, "closure may not capture a value that can hold a function value behind a counted handle (`N0616`).")
    strs_push(l, "No collector was added — counting is still the whole reclamation story — and the claim again covers")
    strs_push(l, "every value a program can write, environments included (`architecture.md` §7.111).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Until N7 this paragraph read: \"There is also no reclamation of any kind … 'No GC' is")
    strs_push(l, "currently achieved by never freeing, which is not a memory strategy.\" That was accurate,")
    strs_push(l, "and it is the sentence the milestone was written to retire. Between N7 and N8 it read")
    strs_push(l, "\"`Str` and `Chan` storage is still not reclaimed, and the self-hosted backend emits no")
    strs_push(l, "reclamation at all\"; both halves were true and both are now closed.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**4 — Runtime cost is zero where possible and observable where it is not.**")
    strs_push(l, "*Partial.* The costs that exist are observable and specified: checked arithmetic traps")
    strs_push(l, "rather than wrapping, and the LLVM translation (`crates/nazm-lir/src/op/llvm.rs`) emits the")
    strs_push(l, "`llvm.s*.with.overflow` intrinsics and never `nsw`, precisely because `nsw` would license an")
    strs_push(l, "optimiser to delete the check (`crates/nazm-cli/tests/build.rs` holds it). There is no opt-out, so")
    strs_push(l, "\"zero-cost where possible\" has not been tested against a case where it conflicts with")
    strs_push(l, "safety.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**5 — Concurrency is part of the language, not a library.**")
    strs_push(l, "*Honoured.* `scope`, `spawn` and `Chan` are grammar (`docs/user/grammar.ebnf`), are checked")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0320` outside a scope, `N0321` for a sequence crossing into a task), lower natively,")
    strs_push(l, "and are compiled by the compiler written in Nazm — `Chan` of `Int`; `Chan[T]` of another")
    strs_push(l, "element type and selection are outside its subset (*corrected Gate 1, 2026-10-07*). There is no library alternative and no")
    strs_push(l, "way to express a task without them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**6 — AI-native means machine-consumable compiler interfaces, never AI-themed syntax.**")
    strs_push(l, "*Honoured.* Twenty-nine versioned schemas under `schema/`, a diagnostic stream with byte-exact")
    strs_push(l, "spans, a capability inventory read from the compiler's own tables. No keyword anywhere")
    strs_push(l, "exists to support the label, and `roadmap.md` forbids adding one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**7 — A successful compilation is not correctness evidence.**")
    strs_push(l, "*Honoured, and structurally.* `crates/nazm-cli/tests/build.rs:6-25` states the two-oracle")
    strs_push(l, "rule — every native case is checked against a written expectation *and* against the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter, at `-O0` and `-O2`. The mutation catalogue exists to test the tests.")
    strs_push(l, "The sharp version, stated in §1 rule 4: LLVM validation catches malformed")
    strs_push(l, "IR, not semantic miscompilation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**8 — Unsafe code stays narrowly isolated and explicitly justified.**")
    strs_push(l, "*Honoured, more strictly than the law requires.* `Cargo.toml:97` is")
    strs_push(l, "`unsafe_code = \"forbid\"` workspace-wide — not `deny`, not per-crate. This already shapes")
    strs_push(l, "design rather than merely constraining it: the test harness bounds a child's address space")
    strs_push(l, "through a shell wrapper (`crates/nazm-cli/tests/common/mod.rs`) because `pre_exec` is")
    strs_push(l, "unavailable. When `nazm-rt` eventually needs it, the allowance narrows to that crate and")
    strs_push(l, "`xtask check` enforces the narrowness (`architecture.md:317-319`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**9 — Reproducibility and provenance are first-class.**")
    strs_push(l, "*Partial, and honestly scoped.* A bootstrap record, `PROVENANCE.txt` and `MANIFEST.txt`")
    strs_push(l, "are produced and self-validated; an SBOM and signed in-toto statements are available (N94).")
    strs_push(l, "Since R1 the records' dates are the commit's rather than the run's (`SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH`), and a")
    strs_push(l, "`build-input-digest` covers every file git tracks or would, beside the older source digest over a")
    strs_push(l, "declared file set. Whether two assemblies of one commit are byte-identical is a per-release fact,")
    strs_push(l, "recorded in that release's record under `docs/internal/releases/`; nothing is claimed across hosts.")
    strs_push(l, "`capability-matrix.md` area 32 keeps the claims apart. *Until R1 this said the archive could not be")
    strs_push(l, "bit-reproducible while the provenance embedded its own run date, and that the source digest omitted")
    strs_push(l, "every Cargo manifest, `Cargo.lock`, `rust-toolchain.toml` and the Dockerfile — both true then.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**10 — One semantic language, exposed through capability and restriction profiles — never")
    strs_push(l, "incompatible dialects.**")
    strs_push(l, "*Honoured as built.* Restriction profiles exist — `general`, `embedded`, `critical`, `cyber`,")
    strs_push(l, "`realtime`, `authority` and `web3`, chosen with `--profile NAME` or by a package's manifest")
    strs_push(l, "(`spec.md` *Restriction profiles*) — and each refuses more and reinterprets nothing; there is")
    strs_push(l, "exactly one dialect. §4 states the invariant; `capability-matrix.md` *Domain profiles* states how")
    strs_push(l, "far each is verified, and none is a certification. *Until N47 this read \"designed only\".*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**11 — Claims follow evidence.**")
    strs_push(l, "*Honoured in intent, and it failed in practice.* The discipline was cultural, and culture")
    strs_push(l, "does not survive a milestone: on 2026-09-21 the front page said the project was \"an")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter, not a compiler\" forty lines after showing it bootstrap itself, and the ledger")
    strs_push(l, "called the formatter \"planned | nothing exists\" thirty lines after marking that milestone")
    strs_push(l, "complete. The response is not more prose — it is")
    strs_push(l, "[`capability-matrix.md`](capability-matrix.md) with a gate under it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**12 — The semantic kernel stays small.**")
    strs_push(l, "*Honoured, and grown on purpose.* The kernel is the compiler's own answer: `nazm")
    strs_push(l, "capabilities` lists 8 built-in types (two of them capabilities), 7 kinds of authority and 53")
    strs_push(l, "built-ins, with one module mechanism; four words — `for`, `label`, `loop` and `mod` — are")
    strs_push(l, "reserved and refused **by name** rather than silently unavailable")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-syntax/src/parser.rs`, `RESERVED`). `struct`, `enum`, `match` and `impl` left that")
    strs_push(l, "list as each became the construct it reserved. Refusing by name is what makes a small kernel")
    strs_push(l, "legible instead of merely incomplete. *It once listed six types, 31 built-ins and eight")
    strs_push(l, "reserved words.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Two invariants that are easy to lose in a refactor")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Absorbed 2026-09-21 from the Era-1 execution contract's §5, which had no other home.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A refusal is never disguised as a result.** No dummy value, silent fallback type,")
    strs_push(l, "poison-producing arithmetic shortcut, or unreachable terminator may stand in for something")
    strs_push(l, "the backend does not support or lowers incorrectly. Everything outside a subset is refused")
    strs_push(l, "**by name, with a span**, before anything is written — a refusal that arrives after the")
    strs_push(l, "output is on stdout is a refusal nobody can act on. This is law 7 read from the")
    strs_push(l, "implementation side: a program that compiles because the compiler invented a value has not")
    strs_push(l, "been compiled.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Recursive work over the tree stays on a stack whose size is known.** Parsing, checking,")
    strs_push(l, "lowering and *dropping* an AST all recurse with the shape of the input, so they run on the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter's own sized stack rather than the caller's — including teardown, because a")
    strs_push(l, "deeply nested tree can overflow while being freed. Returning a recursive owned structure to")
    strs_push(l, "an inadequately sized caller stack reintroduces the bound it was written to remove. Note")
    strs_push(l, "what does **not** follow from this: an AST nesting limit bounds nesting, not call-graph")
    strs_push(l, "depth, module depth or runtime call depth; and **native frame counts do not bound stack")
    strs_push(l, "bytes.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 3. What the IR diagram means, and what exists")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §2 gives eight levels, source through machine code. Exactly **one**")
    strs_push(l, "crate below the AST exists, and the relationship between the two needs stating plainly,")
    strs_push(l, "because four documents got it wrong by reading the crate list as a progress bar.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-lir` is named for level 7 and `crates/nazm-lir/src/lib.rs:1-27` says it is")
    strs_push(l, "\"level 7 and nothing else\". Its *content* is not level 7 as §2 defines it. §2 describes")
    strs_push(l, "level 7 as SSA with concrete layouts over a CFG of places; what `crates/nazm-lir/src/ir.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "defines is a **structured, typed tree over numbered slots** — `While`, `If` and `Scope`")
    strs_push(l, "nest, `Local`s are indices, and nothing is in SSA form. It is a real IR that owns a real")
    strs_push(l, "responsibility: it records *which operations can fail and where the source said so*, which")
    strs_push(l, "the AST does not carry and the backend cannot recover.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "So the honest statement is: **the diagram is a target, the crate shares its name, and no")
    strs_push(l, "level between the AST and this one exists.** Neither HIR, nor a typed core, nor MIR, nor")
    strs_push(l, "monomorphisation — and the last of those is not a gap, because nothing is polymorphic.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Two consequences worth naming, because both are dependencies rather than complaints:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Name resolution happens twice**, independently — once in `crates/nazm-core/src/check/`")
    strs_push(l, "  and again in `crates/nazm-lir/src/lower.rs`, against two separately transcribed built-in")
    strs_push(l, "  tables of 31 entries each (`crates/nazm-core/src/intrinsic.rs`,")
    strs_push(l, "  `crates/nazm-lir/src/ir.rs`) kept in agreement by a test rather than by construction.")
    strs_push(l, "  That is one semantic responsibility with two implementations.")
    strs_push(l, "- **A span has no file identity.** `architecture.md:307` credits `nazm-span` with a")
    strs_push(l, "  `FileId`; no such type exists. `crates/nazm-cli/src/load.rs` concatenates every reachable")
    strs_push(l, "  file into a single buffer and recovers the filename from the offset. That is a sound")
    strs_push(l, "  design for a whole-program compiler and a hard stop for separate compilation, incremental")
    strs_push(l, "  compilation, content-addressed definitions and any language server.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **Both bullets were closed between 2026-09-21 and 2026-09-22, and are kept above because")
    strs_push(l, "> the argument they make is the reason the work happened.**")
    strs_push(l, ">")
    strs_push(l, "> N1 ended the double resolution: `crates/nazm-core/src/check/` produces one")
    strs_push(l, "> `nazm_sema::Resolution` and both the evaluator and `crates/nazm-lir/src/lower.rs` read")
    strs_push(l, "> it, with a `cargo xtask check` rule failing if the backend declares a name-keyed table.")
    strs_push(l, "> N1 also gave `nazm_span::Span` a `FileId` and replaced the merged buffer with a")
    strs_push(l, "> `SourceMap`. N2 added a compilation unit and per-unit checking, N3 durable identity and a")
    strs_push(l, "> persisted interface, **N4 incremental semantic checking**, **N5 separate code generation")
    strs_push(l, "> and linking**, and **N6 native object reuse** — so of the four things the second bullet")
    strs_push(l, "> called blocked, three now exist and the fourth, a language server, is blocked on a")
    strs_push(l, "> lossless CST rather than on identity. *N15 supplied the lossless CST; the language server")
    strs_push(l, "> itself has not been started.*")
    strs_push(l, ">")
    strs_push(l, "> \"Incremental compilation\" in that list is worth reading narrowly: a module's semantic")
    strs_push(l, "> check may be skipped, and a unit's `clang -c` may be skipped. Lowering, emission and the")
    strs_push(l, "> link run on every build. `capability-matrix.md` areas 2a and 10b state exactly what each")
    strs_push(l, "> covers.")
    strs_push(l, ">")
    strs_push(l, "> The paragraph below still holds, and the level it pointed at was built: the")
    strs_push(l, "> responsibility it named was owned twice, and now is not.")
    strs_push(l, ">")
    strs_push(l, "> **2026-09-30 (N39).** \"No level between the AST and this one exists\" is no longer true,")
    strs_push(l, "> and is kept above for the reason the bullets are. Core IR, `crates/nazm-cir`, sits between")
    strs_push(l, "> checking and both backends (`architecture.md` §7.41), and it met this section's test: what")
    strs_push(l, "> each position of the tree *means* — which slot, which callee, which field, what `?`")
    strs_push(l, "> becomes, which loop a `break` leaves — was decided twice, by the evaluator as it ran and")
    strs_push(l, "> by `crates/nazm-lir/src/lower.rs` as it lowered, and is now decided once. It is level 3 by")
    strs_push(l, "> responsibility, not by §2's shape: a tree of regions, not ANF. HIR, MIR and")
    strs_push(l, "> monomorphisation remain absent.")
    strs_push(l, ">")
    strs_push(l, "> **2026-10-07 (R1).** Two more levels exist since, each owning a responsibility: MIR (N40,")
    strs_push(l, "> `capability-matrix.md` area 9), where every copy, move and drop is explicit and validated, and")
    strs_push(l, "> an instruction-level LIR both native backends translate (N105, area 10). Generic bodies are")
    strs_push(l, "> monomorphised by the native path. HIR is still absent, and the language server has existed since")
    strs_push(l, "> N16.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**An IR level earns its existence by owning a semantic responsibility no existing level")
    strs_push(l, "owns.** Matching the diagram is not such a reason. By that test, the next level is the one")
    strs_push(l, "that would end the double resolution — and that is an argument from the tree, not from §2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 4. One language, many profiles")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A domain is served by **restricting** the one semantic language and by **granting or")
    strs_push(l, "withholding capabilities** — never by forking the semantics. That is law 10, and this is")
    strs_push(l, "what it means precisely:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **A program valid under a narrower profile is valid under a wider one and means exactly")
    strs_push(l, "> the same thing.** A profile refuses more. It never reinterprets.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A profile may withhold a construct, withhold an authority, or impose an additional")
    strs_push(l, "obligation. It may **not** change what a construct means, add a keyword, or alter an")
    strs_push(l, "arithmetic, evaluation-order or failure rule. The moment a profile needs one of those it is")
    strs_push(l, "a dialect, and the answer is no.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "This is adopted before anything implements it, because that is the cheap moment to adopt")
    strs_push(l, "it. **A profile becomes real in this order**, and the first step is the one usually skipped:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "1. **Name what it refuses** — constructs and authorities — in `spec.md`.")
    strs_push(l, "2. **Show the refusals are expressible as restrictions.** If one requires changing a")
    strs_push(l, "   meaning, it is a dialect and it is refused.")
    strs_push(l, "3. **Implement the restriction** where refusals already live, using the existing")
    strs_push(l, "   refuse-by-name machinery and a distinct diagnostic code.")
    strs_push(l, "4. **State the obligation** the profile takes on and the evidence class that discharges it.")
    strs_push(l, "   Source inspection, successful compilation, runtime behaviour, mutation discrimination,")
    strs_push(l, "   performance and platform support are different evidence classes and one does not")
    strs_push(l, "   substitute for another.")
    strs_push(l, "5. **Only then** describe it as existing, in `capability-matrix.md`, with a path.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What each profile is *for* is `NAZM_LANGUAGE_GOALS.md` §10. What exists today is")
    strs_push(l, "`capability-matrix.md` under *Domain profiles*. Today that is seven named profiles (`spec.md` *Restriction")
    strs_push(l, "profiles*), each VERIFIED or PARTIAL as scoped there — and the Critical one in particular is")
    strs_push(l, "enforcement and evidence that says nothing about certification or fitness for safety-related use.")
    strs_push(l, "*Until N47 this read \"one profile, unnamed, and five ambitions\".*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 5. Documentation authority")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Every normative statement has exactly one owner.** Another document may summarise it in a")
    strs_push(l, "sentence and link; no document may restate it at length. When two files disagree, the owner")
    strs_push(l, "wins — and the other one is the bug.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Authority | Owns | Changes |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| [`NAZM_LANGUAGE_GOALS.md`](NAZM_LANGUAGE_GOALS.md) | Why Nazm exists · historical barriers · ultimate objectives · domain ambitions · the token-efficiency constitution · non-goals | **rarely** |")
    strs_push(l, "| **this file** | Durable engineering law · the evidence vocabulary · the one-language/many-profiles invariant · context routing | rarely |")
    strs_push(l, "| [`architecture.md`](architecture.md) | Compiler architecture · IR responsibilities · backend strategy · the layout boundary · effects/capabilities/provenance separation | as design evolves |")
    strs_push(l, "| [`spec.md`](../user/spec.md) | **What a Nazm program means.** Settled strata, versioned; *Open* is the register of what is not | per language change |")
    strs_push(l, "| [`capability-matrix.md`](capability-matrix.md) | **What exists today**, with evidence — the only status authority | per implementation change |")
    strs_push(l, "| [`roadmap.md`](../user/roadmap.md) | What comes next, and why in that order | per milestone |")
    strs_push(l, "| [`research-register.md`](research-register.md) | Hypotheses, each with a falsifier. Deliberately not commitments | per hypothesis |")
    strs_push(l, "| [`bootstrap.md`](bootstrap.md) | Self-hosting: its design, its result, and what it does **not** establish | rarely |")
    strs_push(l, "| [`diagnostics.md`](../user/diagnostics.md) | The machine interface: schemas, spans, fixes, exit statuses, the compatibility contract | per schema version |")
    strs_push(l, "| [`performance.md`](performance-log.md) | Runtime and compiler performance claims, and the measurements under them | per measurement |")
    strs_push(l, "| [`runbook.md`](runbook.md) | **Containment, resource safety, recovery.** Read before anything heavy | per incident |")
    strs_push(l, "| [`guide.md`](../user/guide.md) + [`grammar.ebnf`](../user/grammar.ebnf) | The human guide, and the machine-checked canonical grammar it is generated from | per syntax change |")
    strs_push(l, "| `releases/` | Frozen evidence for one tested commit each. Never updated after the fact | per release |")
    strs_push(l, "| `research/` | The comparative agent-cost protocol, with frozen thresholds | rarely |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Three separations are deliberate and must not be collapsed. **Goals answer where we are")
    strs_push(l, "ultimately going; this file answers what must stay true while we get there.** **`spec.md`")
    strs_push(l, "says what a program means; `architecture.md` says how the compiler is built** — semantics")
    strs_push(l, "and implementation are different authorities. **`performance.md` measures the language;")
    strs_push(l, "`research/evaluation.md` measures agent development efficiency** — two experiments, never")
    strs_push(l, "one score.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Documents retired on 2026-09-21, their obligations rehomed and their text kept by Git:")
    strs_push(l, "`direction.md` (the 2026-09-20 decision record), `NAZM_AUTONOMOUS_GOAL.md` (the completed")
    strs_push(l, "Era-1 execution contract), `goal-status.md` (its ledger), `domain-profiles.md` and")
    strs_push(l, "`bootstrap-design.md`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 6. Context routing")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Load the minimum sufficient authoritative context, not the whole docs directory.** This")
    strs_push(l, "is `NAZM_LANGUAGE_GOALS.md`'s token-efficiency constitution applied to this repository: a")
    strs_push(l, "reader who has to ingest everything to change anything is paying for the documentation's")
    strs_push(l, "disorganisation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Task | Read |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Foundational language decision** — a principle changes | `NAZM_LANGUAGE_GOALS.md` · this file · the relevant `architecture.md` section · the relevant `spec.md` section · `capability-matrix.md` · the relevant research item |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Ordinary semantic change** | the relevant `spec.md` section · `capability-matrix.md` · `roadmap.md` · the relevant `architecture.md` section. **Not** the whole Goals document |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Compiler implementation change** | this file · the relevant `architecture.md` section · the relevant `spec.md` section · `capability-matrix.md` · `roadmap.md` |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Bootstrap or self-hosting** | `bootstrap.md` · the relevant `spec.md` section · `runbook.md` · the capability row |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Performance** | `performance.md` · `runbook.md` · the capability row |")
    strs_push(l, "| **AI tooling or diagnostics** | `diagnostics.md` · the Goals token-efficiency sections (§6) · the capability row. `research/evaluation.md` **only** when running a comparative agent evaluation |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Anything heavy — generated stages, selfhost, bootstrap, mutation, benchmarks** | **`runbook.md`, always, first** |")
    strs_push(l, "| **\"Is X implemented?\"** | `capability-matrix.md`. For a construct or built-in, ask `nazm capabilities --json` instead — it is read from the compiler's own tables and cannot drift |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Two rules that save more context than any routing table. **Ask the compiler before asking a")
    strs_push(l, "document**: `nazm capabilities --json` answers construct-level questions from the")
    strs_push(l, "implementation. **A document's own status line is not evidence**; `capability-matrix.md`")
    strs_push(l, "cites paths, and `cargo xtask check` fails when one of them stops existing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The same rule, applied to source — the structural half, since N2")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Routing documents is the half this repository can do by writing things down. The half that")
    strs_push(l, "needs the language is routing **source**, and N2 built its prerequisite rather than its")
    strs_push(l, "mechanism: a module is now private by default, exports an explicit interface, and does not")
    strs_push(l, "pass its dependencies on to its importers. So \"what does a reader of module A need\" has an")
    strs_push(l, "answer that is not \"everything reachable\" — A's source, and the *interfaces* of what A")
    strs_push(l, "directly imports.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm_core::check_unit` takes exactly that and no more, which is the property being relied")
    strs_push(l, "on rather than a description of an intention. What does **not** exist is anything that")
    strs_push(l, "hands an agent that subset: no context packet, no semantic delta, no language server, and")
    strs_push(l, "no interface that can be written to a file. `capability-matrix.md` area 2 says so. The")
    strs_push(l, "structure is a precondition for those; it is not a smaller version of them. *All four exist")
    strs_push(l, "since — `nazm interface` (N3), `nazm lsp` (N16), `nazm context` (N27) and `nazm delta` (N28) —")
    strs_push(l, "and the paragraph is kept for the order of the argument.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## 7. What this document deliberately does not decide")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The surface memory model (mutable value semantics against a full region calculus in the")
    strs_push(l, "IR), whether divergence is an effect, and the eligibility predicate for layout selection.")
    strs_push(l, "*The authority model that replaces ambient I/O and whether the scheduler becomes M:N stood here")
    strs_push(l, "too; both are settled now, by evidence — authority as a parameter (N37, N104; area 6) and the M:N")
    strs_push(l, "pool by default (N83, N106; area 15).* Each has a home — `spec.md` *Open*, `architecture.md` §§4-5, `research-register.md` — and each is")
    strs_push(l, "open on purpose. A constitution that settled them would be a design document with")
    strs_push(l, "delusions of permanence.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it does decide** is that none of them may be described as implemented before the")
    strs_push(l, "source proves it, and that the proof lives in a row with a path in it.")
    str_join(l, str_from_byte(10)) + str_from_byte(10)
}

fn dd_doc5() -> Str {
    let l = strs_new()
    strs_push(l, "# Performance claims, and how each is measured")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Status (2026-10-15).** The measurements below cover this implementation against itself and,")
    strs_push(l, "since R1 (5b.10, below), against fifteen languages on three programs — `hello`, recursive `fib`")
    strs_push(l, "and word frequency — re-run for 0.10.0. The standing target, set by the copyright holder on")
    strs_push(l, "2026-10-15, is to lead every compared language on every measured parameter")
    strs_push(l, "(`openspec/changes/performance-leadership`); it is a research target, and **no section here claims")
    strs_push(l, "it**: on 2026-10-15 Nazm's word frequency took 132 ms against C's 74, Rust's 66 and Zig's 48, and `fib` 55 ms")
    strs_push(l, "against C's 35. The paragraph below is the history of how the first comparison arrived.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Before R1 (kept as written):* the first measurements covered this implementation against")
    strs_push(l, "itself — interpreter against native, and one optimisation pass against its own baseline — and,")
    strs_push(l, "**on one program only**, against `clang` and `python3`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Corrected 2026-09-21.** This paragraph said the measurements *\"say nothing about C, Rust,")
    strs_push(l, "Zig, Go or Python: no cross-language comparison has been run\"*. That stopped being true")
    strs_push(l, "when `bench/reference/sieve.c` and `bench/reference/sieve.py` were added and `xtask bench`")
    strs_push(l, "began timing them — refusing to time a reference whose answer differs from the Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "program's. What is accurate now: **one program, one host, one C compiler**, recorded in")
    strs_push(l, "`bench/baseline-linux-aarch64.json` as the `reference-c` stage. Nothing has been measured")
    strs_push(l, "against Rust, Zig or Go, and one sieve is not a language comparison. The claims in the")
    strs_push(l, "second half of this file remain targets.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "This file exists so that claims are written down *before* benchmarks are chosen, which")
    strs_push(l, "is the only order in which a benchmark can falsify anything.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Every measured section is filed (N92).** `bench/claims.toml` names each section below whose heading")
    strs_push(l, "says *measured* or *frozen* as **reproducible** — and the command that regenerates it — **dated**, a")
    strs_push(l, "record of the tree on its date and not a claim about this one, or **unreproduced**, a current claim")
    strs_push(l, "no command regenerates yet. `cargo xtask check` refuses a section the register does not file.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## The measurements")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`cargo xtask bench` times six programs in `bench/programs/` plus the compiler's own")
    strs_push(l, "source, through five stages each — six where an external reference exists (`reference-c`,")
    strs_push(l, "`reference-python`), and a seventh program, `floor.nz`, exists to measure the process floor")
    strs_push(l, "rather than the language. Seven runs after one discarded warm-up; the median is")
    strs_push(l, "reported, and one baseline file per host holds the full record.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Machine | Darwin arm64, 10 CPUs |")
    strs_push(l, "| Toolchain | rustc 1.98.1, Apple clang 21.0.0 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Baseline commit | `8ec8729`, clean tree |")
    strs_push(l, "| Not controlled | thermal state, other processes, CPU frequency scaling, address-space layout |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> **`bench/baseline.json` (Darwin) is stale and has not been re-recorded.** Two things")
    strs_push(l, "> changed under it: a failure now leaves a compiled function through an explicit exit, so")
    strs_push(l, "> the emitter writes a check after every call; and the compiler benchmark's input changed")
    strs_push(l, "> from a four-file concatenation to the real five-file source with its imports resolved.")
    strs_push(l, "> Re-recording it means running generated programs on the host, which the resource")
    strs_push(l, "> contract forbids, so it stays as it is and is **not** a valid comparison until someone")
    strs_push(l, "> re-records it on a Darwin machine. `bench/baseline-linux-aarch64.json` *has* been")
    strs_push(l, "> re-recorded, inside the contained runner, and is current.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What the emitter revision cost")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Measured rather than estimated, because the number is large enough to matter:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | before | after |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `strings/build-O0` (unchanged program) | 38.8 ms | 39.1 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `strings/build-O2` (unchanged program) | 49.1 ms | 49.7 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `compiler/check` (no emission) | 12.4 ms | 12.5 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `compiler/build-O0` | 200.1 ms | 468.7 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An unchanged program costs **under 1%**. The compiler's own build is 2.4×, and the two")
    strs_push(l, "causes — a different emitter and a different input — are separated by measuring all four")
    strs_push(l, "combinations rather than by assuming the split follows the line count. The *before* row is")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-lir/src/emit.rs` and `ir.rs` restored to `cea9158^`, with the rest of the tree")
    strs_push(l, "left alone; every cell was measured in one session, on one machine, inside the runner,")
    strs_push(l, "three runs each:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| median of 3 | baseline-era input, 3,561 lines | current input, 4,501 lines |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| emitter before this change | **190 ms** | **247 ms** |")
    strs_push(l, "| emitter after it | **380 ms** | **475 ms** |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The emitter revision costs **2.00× on the old input and 1.92× on the new one**; the input")
    strs_push(l, "change costs **1.30× with the old emitter and 1.25× with the new one**. The two are")
    strs_push(l, "consistent across both rows and both columns, which is what makes *this* decomposition a")
    strs_push(l, "measurement rather than an apportionment. The 190 ms cell also corroborates the recorded")
    strs_push(l, "baseline's 200.1 ms for the same combination.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it does not decompose.** Three commits touched those two files between the rows —")
    strs_push(l, "`cea9158` (the failure protocol), `eefac34` (`chan_recv`'s allocation failure) and")
    strs_push(l, "`ada3ae2` (branching a failed call straight to the function exit) — 241 insertions against")
    strs_push(l, "15 deletions. So the 2.00× is the **emitter revision's overall effect**, not the isolated")
    strs_push(l, "cost of the failure check. Splitting it further would need a build with only `cea9158`")
    strs_push(l, "reverted, and that has not been measured; claiming the whole figure for the failure")
    strs_push(l, "protocol would repeat, one level down, the error corrected below.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An earlier draft of this section attributed 1.22× to the input because the line count had")
    strs_push(l, "risen 22%. That was a guess dressed as an attribution — line count is not compile time,")
    strs_push(l, "and the measured figure is 1.25–1.30×. It is recorded here because the number happening to")
    strs_push(l, "land near the guess is exactly what would have kept the guess from being noticed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The failure protocol is the largest part of that revision and the part with a cost model:")
    strs_push(l, "the check is written once per call site, so the cost tracks how call-dense a program is")
    strs_push(l, "rather than how long it is. The compiler has about sixteen hundred call sites; the")
    strs_push(l, "benchmark programs have a handful each, which is why they moved under 1%. That explains")
    strs_push(l, "why the revision should be expensive here and cheap there — it is not a measurement of the")
    strs_push(l, "check on its own.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Of the 503 ms measured before the block reduction below, **457 ms was clang** and about")
    strs_push(l, "46 ms was Nazm's own emission — so this is IR volume reaching the assembler, not the")
    strs_push(l, "emitter being slow. Branching a failed call straight to the function's exit, rather than")
    strs_push(l, "through a block that only forwards to it, removed 1,564 basic blocks of 9,310 and about")
    strs_push(l, "28 ms. The remainder is the price of reporting a failure only once every task in scope has")
    strs_push(l, "been joined, and it was paid deliberately.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The comparison unit is two runs on one machine minutes apart.** `cargo xtask bench")
    strs_push(l, "--check` refuses to compare across hosts rather than producing a percentage that means")
    strs_push(l, "nothing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The regression threshold, and the noise floor under it")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A change counts as a regression when the median is **both more than 25% and more than")
    strs_push(l, "5 ms slower** than the baseline. The absolute bar is not a way of being lenient; it is")
    strs_push(l, "there because a ratio is the wrong test near zero, and the first `--check` run proved")
    strs_push(l, "it by reporting `arith/check` at 3.3 → 5.8 ms as a regression on a code path nothing")
    strs_push(l, "had touched. Timing the same command fifteen times in one burst gives a spread of 1.13×")
    strs_push(l, "to 1.34× on anything in the three-to-eight millisecond range; across bursts minutes")
    strs_push(l, "apart it is wider, because process start-up and filesystem cache state are most of what")
    strs_push(l, "is being timed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The consequence, stated rather than left to be discovered: **every measurement under")
    strs_push(l, "about fifteen milliseconds is below this method's noise floor**. Those numbers are")
    strs_push(l, "recorded and not gated. Measuring them properly needs a harness that does not pay")
    strs_push(l, "process start-up per sample, and this one does.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Verifying that the work is real")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Two things can make a benchmark number meaningless, and both were checked rather than")
    strs_push(l, "assumed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The compiled form might have been folded away.** None of these programs reads external")
    strs_push(l, "input, so an optimiser is entitled to compute the answer at compile time and leave a")
    strs_push(l, "loop that does nothing. Checked by scaling the input and seeing whether the time")
    strs_push(l, "scales — `calls` at 1M, 4M and 16M iterations, at `-O2`, with the process floor")
    strs_push(l, "subtracted:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| iterations | wall | minus the floor |")
    strs_push(l, "| ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1 000 000 | 3.80 ms | 0.92 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| 4 000 000 | 6.03 ms | 3.15 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| 16 000 000 | 13.41 ms | 10.53 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Four times the work takes about 3.4× and 3.3× the time. That is linear within the")
    strs_push(l, "noise, so the loop runs.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The two implementations might not be doing the same thing.** Every program states its")
    strs_push(l, "answer in a `.expected` file beside it, and `cargo xtask bench` runs both forms and")
    strs_push(l, "compares before it times anything. A program whose implementations disagree, or which")
    strs_push(l, "has no recorded answer, is refused rather than measured.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Everything below includes process start-up.** `floor.nz` is an empty program and")
    strs_push(l, "measures that cost alone: about **2.9 ms**. It is not subtracted from the table — the")
    strs_push(l, "numbers are wall time of a whole process, which is the thing a person waits for — but")
    strs_push(l, "it is measured every run so it can be.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Interpreter against native")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Median milliseconds, after the optimisation pass below.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Program | `nazm run` | native `-O2` | ratio |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `arith` — 3M iterations of checked arithmetic | 423.3 | 8.2 | 52× |")
    strs_push(l, "| `calls` — 1M iterations through two small functions | 647.3 | 4.8 | 135× |")
    strs_push(l, "| `sieve` — primes below 400 000 | 294.2 | 6.0 | 49× |")
    strs_push(l, "| `sequences` — 400 000 pushes, then a read/write pass | 228.0 | 4.9 | 47× |")
    strs_push(l, "| `strings` — 60 000 parts through one `str_join` | 17.5 | 6.8 | 2.6× |")
    strs_push(l, "| `channels` — 50 000 hand-offs over a capacity-1 channel | 254.0 | 223.3 | 1.1× |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Three of these are worth saying out loud because they are the ones that could be")
    strs_push(l, "misread:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **`strings` is 2.6×, not 50×.** Both implementations spend their time in the")
    strs_push(l, "  allocator, so compiling the surrounding loop buys little. A speed claim drawn from")
    strs_push(l, "  `arith` and applied to string-building work would be wrong by a factor of twenty.")
    strs_push(l, "- **`channels` is 1.1×.** 223 ms for 50 000 hand-offs is about **4.5 µs per message**,")
    strs_push(l, "  and both implementations are dominated by the cost of waking a thread rather than by")
    strs_push(l, "  anything the compiler emits. The structured-concurrency model is usable for")
    strs_push(l, "  coarse-grained work and is **not** suitable for fine-grained message passing; nothing")
    strs_push(l, "  here claims otherwise, and no scheduler work has been done.")
    strs_push(l, "- **`calls` is 135×, and that ratio is the least useful number here.** The interpreter")
    strs_push(l, "  builds an environment frame per call and the native code does not, so the gap is")
    strs_push(l, "  real — but 4.8 ms of native wall time is about 1.9 ms of work on a 2.9 ms floor, so")
    strs_push(l, "  the ratio is as much a statement about process start-up as about the compiler. Every")
    strs_push(l, "  native figure in the table has the same shape; `arith`, with roughly 4.8 ms of work,")
    strs_push(l, "  is the one where the measurement is mostly the program.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Compile time")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | check | build `-O0` | build `-O2` |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| Any one benchmark program | 2.8 – 4.4 ms | 59 – 62 ms | 65 – 78 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| The compiler's own source (3 500 lines then; **4,647** now, so this row is not comparable to a current run) | 8.2 ms | 198.6 ms | — |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Nazm's own front end is not what a `nazm build` waits for.** Checking the whole")
    strs_push(l, "self-hosting compiler takes 8 ms; building a four-line program takes 60. The difference")
    strs_push(l, "is `clang` assembling and linking, which is a fixed cost this compiler pays per")
    strs_push(l, "invocation and has done nothing about. That is the honest answer to \"is it fast to")
    strs_push(l, "compile\": the part written here is fast, and it is a small part of the wall clock.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Incremental semantic checking — measured 2026-09-22, and smaller than it sounds")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N4 lets `nazm check` skip checking the bodies of a module whose semantic inputs are")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged. Measured on the largest module graph this repository has — the compiler written")
    strs_push(l, "in Nazm, five modules and 5,041 lines — with the release binary, medians of seven runs,")
    strs_push(l, "Darwin arm64. **These are within-host comparisons taken minutes apart, which is the only")
    strs_push(l, "kind this method supports**; they are not comparable to `bench/baseline-linux-aarch64.json`")
    strs_push(l, "and no cross-host claim is made.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | wall clock | modules checked | reused | entries written |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `--no-cache` | 40.5 ms | 5 | 0 | 0 |")
    strs_push(l, "| cold, store empty | **64.8 ms** | 5 | 0 | 5 |")
    strs_push(l, "| warm, nothing changed | 38.9 ms | 0 | 5 | 0 |")
    strs_push(l, "| a private definition added to `lex.nz` | 39.0 ms | 1 | 4 | 1 |")
    strs_push(l, "| an exported definition added to `lex.nz` | 39.3 ms | 4 | 1 | 4 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The reuse decisions are exactly right and the time saved is about a millisecond.** That")
    strs_push(l, "is the finding, and it is stated first because the opposite is what a reader expects from a")
    strs_push(l, "cache.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The reason is arithmetic rather than a defect. A `nazm check` of a one-line program takes")
    strs_push(l, "**31.7 ms** on this machine — process start, dynamic linking, and the interpreter-owned")
    strs_push(l, "thread `spec.md` requires. So the whole of this graph's *work* is about 8.8 ms, and what")
    strs_push(l, "N4 reuses is the body-checking stage of it:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| process floor | 31.7 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| work, `--no-cache` | 8.8 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| work, warm | 7.2 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| **saved** | **1.6 ms — 18% of the work, 3.9% of the wall clock** |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Fifteen runs each, twice, put the minima at 39.8/39.9 ms disabled and 38.8/38.8 ms warm,")
    strs_push(l, "so the ordering is stable; the magnitude is near this method's noise floor and is reported")
    strs_push(l, "as an order of magnitude, not a figure.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The first run is slower, by 24 ms.** Publishing five entries costs an `fsync` each.")
    strs_push(l, "That is the price of a `rename` that cannot expose a half-written file, and it is paid once")
    strs_push(l, "per changed module rather than per run — but a build that checks once and never again is")
    strs_push(l, "worse off, and saying so is more useful than averaging it away.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What this says about the next lever.** Parsing and declaring every module happens on")
    strs_push(l, "every run and is *most* of the 8.8 ms; body checking is the minority. Making reuse pay")
    strs_push(l, "would mean reusing the front of the pipeline too, which needs either an incremental parse")
    strs_push(l, "over a lossless CST or a second cache keyed on source alone. Both are real milestones, and")
    strs_push(l, "neither is what N4 built. `capability-matrix.md` area 2a states the bound rather than the")
    strs_push(l, "hope.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What a consumer of an interface does not have to read")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Not a token measurement: bytes, and no tokenizer has been run. For the same five modules,")
    strs_push(l, "what each one's implementation weighs against what its published interface weighs — the")
    strs_push(l, "schema was `nazm.interface/1` when this was measured, `/2` since N9 and `/3` since N10, each")
    strs_push(l, "of which added definitions — records, then enums — that move these numbers for a module")
    strs_push(l, "exporting one:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | source | interface |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `lex.nz` | 9,921 B | 3,344 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| `parse.nz` | 40,538 B | 2,090 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| `analyse.nz` | 45,536 B | 2,474 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| `module.nz` | 11,034 B | 468 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| `emit.nz` | 129,467 B | 124 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| **total** | **236,496 B** | **8,500 B** |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A consumer that needs only what these modules *offer* reads **3.6%** of what a consumer")
    strs_push(l, "that reads their implementations does. The ratio tracks how much of a module is exported")
    strs_push(l, "rather than how large it is — `emit.nz` is the biggest file in the tree and exports")
    strs_push(l, "nothing, so its interface is 124 bytes. Call this **context reduction**; converting it to")
    strs_push(l, "a token claim would need a tokenizer and a stated model, and neither has been run.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Separate code generation — measured 2026-09-22, and it costs")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N5 gives each Nazm module its own LLVM module and object, and links them. Nothing is")
    strs_push(l, "reused, so every artefact is regenerated on every build: this is an architecture change,")
    strs_push(l, "and the numbers are what it cost. Medians of five, Darwin arm64, against a worktree at the")
    strs_push(l, "commit immediately before N5 (`0bf58be`). Within-host, minutes apart, and not comparable to")
    strs_push(l, "`bench/baseline-linux-aarch64.json`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | before | after | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `sieve.nz` (1 module) build `-O0` | 121.7 ms | **249.6 ms** | +105% |")
    strs_push(l, "| `sieve.nz` build `-O2` | 138.1 ms | 267.3 ms | +94% |")
    strs_push(l, "| compiler (5 modules) build `-O0` | 335.7 ms | **658.2 ms** | +96% |")
    strs_push(l, "| compiler build `-O2` | 1670.8 ms | 1705.8 ms | **+2%** |")
    strs_push(l, "| `sieve` executable `-O2` | 50,440 B | 50,552 B | +112 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| compiler executable `-O2` | 615,080 B | **554,648 B** | **−10%** |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The cost is `clang` processes, not code generation.** Timing each step of the five-module")
    strs_push(l, "build at `-O0` separately:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| artefact | IR | `clang -c` |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `m0` (`emit.nz`) | 1,556,038 B | 191.3 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `m1` (`analyse.nz`) | 390,149 B | 114.0 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `m2` (`parse.nz`) | 298,514 B | 106.1 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `m3` (`module.nz`) | 65,446 B | 85.4 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `m4` (`lex.nz`) | 75,867 B | 86.3 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| runtime | 8,100 B | 80.5 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| entry | 2,474 B | **79.4 ms** |")
    strs_push(l, "| link | | 91.3 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The entry artefact is 2.4 kilobytes of IR and takes 79 ms, so **about 79 ms of each of the")
    strs_push(l, "eight invocations is process startup** — roughly 630 ms of the 658 ms build. The marginal")
    strs_push(l, "cost of actually generating code is 5–112 ms per artefact. At `-O2` on a real program that")
    strs_push(l, "overhead is 2% of the total, because optimisation dominates.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "That is also the cost a cache removes: an unchanged module's `clang -c` does not run at")
    strs_push(l, "all. N5 does not build one, and `capability-matrix.md` does not claim one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The executable got 10% smaller at `-O2`, and that is the same fact from the other side.**")
    strs_push(l, "Per-module objects mean LLVM cannot inline across a module boundary, so less code is")
    strs_push(l, "duplicated into callers — and less is specialised. Measured against a possible runtime")
    strs_push(l, "regression: eleven runs each, twice, put `sieve` at 35.9/35.5 ms minimum before and")
    strs_push(l, "36.9/36.6 ms after, with overlapping medians. **About a millisecond on thirty-six, at the")
    strs_push(l, "edge of what this method resolves** — reported rather than dismissed, and not called a")
    strs_push(l, "regression on this evidence. Recovering cross-module inlining is what LTO is for; N5")
    strs_push(l, "establishes the boundary and adds none, because adding it to recover a number would hide")
    strs_push(l, "whether the boundary was affordable.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Native object reuse — measured 2026-09-22, and it pays for the section above")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N6 keys each emitted LLVM unit's object on the bytes handed to the object compiler, that")
    strs_push(l, "compiler's identity and the configuration it resolves, and links the recorded object instead")
    strs_push(l, "of compiling again. The workload is the same five-module compiler, on the same host, with")
    strs_push(l, "the same method: medians of five runs, and **the cache state each row names is")
    strs_push(l, "re-established before every one of those runs** — a row that cleared the store once and then")
    strs_push(l, "timed four warm builds would be reporting a number nobody experiences.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | wall | units / compiled / reused |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `--no-cache` clean, `-O0` | 665.4 ms | 7 / 7 / 0 |")
    strs_push(l, "| cold store, `-O0` | 730.7 ms | 7 / 7 / 0 |")
    strs_push(l, "| **warm unchanged, `-O0`** | **157.6 ms** | 7 / 0 / 7 |")
    strs_push(l, "| private body edit, `-O0` | 198.5 ms | 7 / 1 / 6 |")
    strs_push(l, "| called export's body edit, `-O0` | 211.2 ms | 7 / 1 / 6 |")
    strs_push(l, "| an export nobody calls, `-O0` | 217.7 ms | 7 / 1 / 6 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `--no-cache` clean, `-O2` | 1693.0 ms | 7 / 7 / 0 |")
    strs_push(l, "| cold store, `-O2` | 1755.4 ms | 7 / 7 / 0 |")
    strs_push(l, "| **warm unchanged, `-O2`** | **157.6 ms** | 7 / 0 / 7 |")
    strs_push(l, "| private body edit, `-O2` | 255.7 ms | 7 / 1 / 6 |")
    strs_push(l, "| called export's body edit, `-O2` | 259.1 ms | 7 / 1 / 6 |")
    strs_push(l, "| an export nobody calls, `-O2` | 257.3 ms | 7 / 1 / 6 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The three edits are indistinguishable, and that is the result.** A private body, the body")
    strs_push(l, "of an export every other module calls, and an export nobody calls all cost one unit of")
    strs_push(l, "seven. Nothing in the compiler says so; it follows from keying on the emitted bytes, which")
    strs_push(l, "N5 measured to contain a dependency only as a `declare` and a `call`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Warm builds are the same at both optimisation levels** — 157.6 ms — because no code is")
    strs_push(l, "generated in either. The `-O2` speedup is larger only because the work avoided was.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The cold build pays about 65 ms**, at both levels: fingerprinting seven units, writing")
    strs_push(l, "seven entries and `fsync`ing each. That is 9.8% at `-O0` and 3.7% at `-O2`, and it is")
    strs_push(l, "reported rather than optimised away, because the durability is what makes a half-written")
    strs_push(l, "entry impossible.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is left in a warm build.** Two external processes, against eight with the cache off:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm`'s own process, measured on a one-line program | ~36 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `clang -###`, the probe that reads the resolved configuration | 60.0 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| the link, 7 objects | 89.1 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| everything else — parse, check, admit, lower, emit, hash, look up | the remainder |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Those three do not sum to 157.6 ms; measured standalone from a shell each pays a spawn the")
    strs_push(l, "build does not, so they are an ordering rather than an addition. What they do establish is")
    strs_push(l, "that **the front end is not the cost** — `nazm check --no-cache` on all five modules is")
    strs_push(l, "45.0 ms, of which 36 ms is the process starting.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Why the backend is identified by its version report and not by its bytes.** Hashing the")
    strs_push(l, "driver would be stronger and was measured: `/usr/bin/clang` on this host is a 200 KB shim in")
    strs_push(l, "front of a 124 MB executable, so it identifies the wrong file; reading the right one costs")
    strs_push(l, "146 ms and digesting it 61 ms. Two hundred milliseconds to protect a 158 ms build is not a")
    strs_push(l, "trade, and the limit that leaves — a toolchain replaced in place without changing what it")
    strs_push(l, "calls itself — is written down in `architecture.md` §7.6 rather than papered over.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Store size.** 852 KiB in seven entries at `-O0`, 596 KiB at `-O2`; the largest entry is")
    strs_push(l, "562 KB, which is `emit.nz`, and the smallest is 1.6 KB, which is the entry wrapper. Nothing")
    strs_push(l, "is evicted. For a project that builds at several optimisation levels and edits often the")
    strs_push(l, "store grows without bound until someone deletes it, which is an operational limitation and")
    strs_push(l, "not a plan.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Reclamation — measured 2026-09-22, and the instrument matters")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N7 made `Ints` and `Strs` storage reclaimable. Two instruments, because they answer")
    strs_push(l, "different questions and each is misleading about the other's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Peak resident memory** answers *does this workload still grow*. Medians are not used")
    strs_push(l, "here: peak is a maximum, and a maximum over repeated runs of a deterministic program does")
    strs_push(l, "not move. Darwin arm64, `-O2`, against the commit before N7.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Workload | Live set | Before | After |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| 5,000 short-lived sequences | ~400 B | 4.38 MiB | **1.78 MiB** |")
    strs_push(l, "| 20,000 | ~400 B | 12.28 MiB | **1.88 MiB** |")
    strs_push(l, "| 80,000 | ~400 B | 43.52 MiB | **1.86 MiB** |")
    strs_push(l, "| one 2,000,000-element sequence | 16 MiB | 19.08 MiB | 19.08 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| string-heavy loop, no sequences | grows | 23.77 MiB | 23.78 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| the self-hosted compiler on `emit.nz` | — | 46.81 MiB | 42.59 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The first three rows are the result. Before, memory tracked **work done** — 1 : 3.9 : 15.6")
    strs_push(l, "against iteration ratios of 1 : 4 : 16. After, it is flat, and the floor is an empty")
    strs_push(l, "program's 1.69 MiB. The next two rows are the control: a sequence that is genuinely live")
    strs_push(l, "is unchanged, and a workload whose allocation is `Str` is unchanged, which is what")
    strs_push(l, "reclaiming exactly one kind of value should look like.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler's 9% is the honest one. Its memory is mostly `Str` bytes — it builds 2.15 MB")
    strs_push(l, "of output by concatenation — and `Str` is outside this slice by the argument in")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.7. A number that had moved further would have meant something else was")
    strs_push(l, "going on.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Allocation and reclamation counts** answer *was this value reclaimed*, which peak")
    strs_push(l, "resident memory cannot: `free` returns storage to the allocator, not to the operating")
    strs_push(l, "system, so a program can reclaim everything and show no change at all. That is not a")
    strs_push(l, "hypothetical — it is why the first measurement of this work appeared to show nothing until")
    strs_push(l, "the counters existed. Both implementations report the same three numbers under")
    strs_push(l, "`NAZM_MEMORY_REPORT`, and `crates/nazm-cli/tests/memory.rs` compares them case by case.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Runtime cost.** The traffic is at bindings, not at calls: passing a sequence to a")
    strs_push(l, "function emits no instruction, which is rule 2 of the constitution turned into a number.")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/*.nz` creates 176 sequences and aliases **zero** of them with a `let`, so the")
    strs_push(l, "self-hosted compiler pays for one retain per sequence returned — it returns one — and one")
    strs_push(l, "release per binding at each of three exit edges. The bootstrap is unchanged at")
    strs_push(l, "`e5779c70…`, and the contained suite is 823 tests against 806.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What is not claimed.** Peak memory bounded by live data for a whole program. `Str` and")
    strs_push(l, "`Chan` storage is still not reclaimed, so the string-heavy row above still grows without")
    strs_push(l, "bound, and `capability-matrix.md` area 4 states the scope per type rather than as one word.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*The last paragraph was true until N8, below, which is the same day. The rest of this")
    strs_push(l, "section is unchanged and its numbers are what N8 was measured against.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Strings and channels — measured 2026-09-22, and the incident's shape is gone")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N8 made `Str` and `Chan` storage reclaimable, which completes the current type universe.")
    strs_push(l, "Same two instruments, same reason: peak resident memory answers *does this workload still")
    strs_push(l, "grow*, and the runtime counters answer *was this value reclaimed*, which peak memory cannot.")
    strs_push(l, "Darwin arm64, `-O2`, against the commit before N8. Peak is a maximum over a deterministic")
    strs_push(l, "program, so no median is taken.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Workload | Live set | Before | After |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| 5,000 temporary heap strings | one string | 1.88 MiB | **1.73 MiB** |")
    strs_push(l, "| 20,000 | one string | 2.33 MiB | **1.77 MiB** |")
    strs_push(l, "| 80,000 | one string | 4.17 MiB | **1.77 MiB** |")
    strs_push(l, "| accumulator loop, 2,000 `str_concat` | 4 KB | 6.28 MiB | **2.02 MiB** |")
    strs_push(l, "| accumulator loop, 8,000 `str_concat` | 16 KB | **70.66 MiB** | **2.23 MiB** |")
    strs_push(l, "| 200 short-lived channels | one | 1.83 MiB | **1.80 MiB** |")
    strs_push(l, "| 2,000 short-lived channels | one | 2.38 MiB | **1.80 MiB** |")
    strs_push(l, "| 64 channels of capacity 256 | one | 1.88 MiB | **1.75 MiB** |")
    strs_push(l, "| 5,000 / 20,000 / 80,000 short-lived **sequences** | ~400 B | 1.72 / 1.77 / 1.77 MiB | 1.73 / 1.75 / 1.77 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| one 2,000,000-element sequence, genuinely live | 16 MiB | 19.06 MiB | 19.06 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| 20,000 values through one channel | one | 1.97 MiB | 1.95 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| empty program | — | 1.70 MiB | 1.69 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The fifth row is the one this work was for. That shape — `str_concat` in a loop, small live")
    strs_push(l, "result — is what took the machine down on 2026-09-21 and what `bootstrap.md` §1 is about;")
    strs_push(l, "at 8,000 iterations it is **31× smaller**, and what remains is the live string plus the")
    strs_push(l, "floor. The three sequence rows are the N7 regression check: unchanged, which is what")
    strs_push(l, "reclaiming two more kinds of value should do to the first. The genuinely live sequence, the")
    strs_push(l, "channel handoff and the empty program are the controls — memory that is *in use* does not")
    strs_push(l, "move, and neither does the floor.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**`str_concat` in a loop is still quadratic in time.** Nothing here changes that, and")
    strs_push(l, "`str_join` is still one pass and one allocation. What changed is that getting it wrong now")
    strs_push(l, "costs time rather than the machine.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Records — measured 2026-09-23, and the cost is the fields'")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N9 added user-defined records. A record allocates nothing of its own, so the question is")
    strs_push(l, "whether the *composition* costs anything: whether reading a field is slower than reading a")
    strs_push(l, "binding, and whether copying a record is slower than copying what it holds.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Median of five, `-O2`, Darwin arm64. Each loop runs three million times except the two")
    strs_push(l, "marked, which run one million.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Workload | Without a record | With one | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| two `Int`s built and read | 34 ms | **34 ms** | not measurable |")
    strs_push(l, "| a record inside a record, three fields read | — | **36 ms** | +2 ms over the flat case |")
    strs_push(l, "| three million field replacements | — | **32 ms** | |")
    strs_push(l, "| copying a `Str` twice, one million times | 55 ms | **54 ms** | not measurable |")
    strs_push(l, "| a cross-module call returning two values | 43 ms | **40 ms** | one call instead of two |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The last row is the shape `compiler/emit.nz` actually adopted: `line_of` and `column_of`")
    strs_push(l, "were two functions because a function returns one value, and `Place { line, column }` is")
    strs_push(l, "one. The measured win is small and the reason it exists is not — the second scan ran")
    strs_push(l, "*backwards* over the same bytes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "At `-O0`, where the generated retain and release helpers are real calls rather than")
    strs_push(l, "inlined, the cost appears and is still small:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Workload | Without | With | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| two `Int`s built and read | 39 ms | 41 ms | +2 ms over three million |")
    strs_push(l, "| a record inside a record | — | 49 ms | +10 ms; two aggregates per iteration |")
    strs_push(l, "| copying a `Str` twice | 55 ms | 56 ms | +1 ms over one million |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Peak resident memory**, same platform, `-O2`:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Workload | Live set | Peak |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| 80,000 short-lived records of two heap strings | one record | **1.72 MiB** |")
    strs_push(l, "| the same two strings, no record | one string | 1.73 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| 80,000 temporary strings — the N8 control | one string | 1.77 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| 80,000 short-lived sequences — the N7 control | ~400 B | 1.78 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| 2,000 short-lived channels — the N8 control | one | 1.75 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| empty program | — | 1.69 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The first two rows are the claim: a record holding heap strings costs what the strings")
    strs_push(l, "cost. The next three are the controls, and they are unmoved — adding a composite type did")
    strs_push(l, "not disturb the reclamation of the types it composes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Executable size.** A program using a record whose fields own nothing is **byte-identical**")
    strs_push(l, "in size to the same program written without one (50,696 bytes), because no helper is")
    strs_push(l, "generated. One whose fields own something costs **+96 bytes** — the retain and release")
    strs_push(l, "helpers, once each, however many times the record is copied.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The compiler itself**, Darwin arm64 host: `nazm check compiler/emit.nz` 42 ms,")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm build … --opt-level 0` 143 ms, peak 44.75 MiB.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Contained, Linux aarch64, on `compiler/emit.nz` — now 3,756 lines:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Peak | Wall |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| the reference compiler | 112.94 MiB | 1.01 s |")
    strs_push(l, "| the compiler written in Nazm | **32.75 MiB** | 4.01 s |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N8 recorded 107.61 MiB and 24.86 MiB for the same pair, **on a 3,221-line file**, so these")
    strs_push(l, "are not a controlled comparison and are not presented as one. The reference compiler's")
    strs_push(l, "figure moved about as much as the input did; the self-hosted one moved more, and the reason")
    strs_push(l, "is visible rather than mysterious — its node arena gained two columns and it now carries a")
    strs_push(l, "record table of its own. What is being claimed here is only that neither grew unexpectedly,")
    strs_push(l, "and that both still fit the 4,096 MiB the runbook allows them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Enums — measured 2026-09-23, and the cost is a branch and some space")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N10 added closed sum types. An enum allocates nothing of its own either, so there are two")
    strs_push(l, "questions: what a value **costs in space**, because the representation is not a union; and")
    strs_push(l, "what selecting on one **costs in time**, because copy and release now branch.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Median of five, extremes dropped, `-O2`, Darwin arm64. The process floor on this machine is")
    strs_push(l, "**6.5 ms**, and a row at or under it is not a measurement.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Space, computed by LLVM's own layout** for the types the compiler emits. The right-hand")
    strs_push(l, "column is what an ideal tagged union would be — the tag plus the largest payload — and the")
    strs_push(l, "gap is the cost of one slot per variant:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Enum | Ours | Ideal union | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `{ A, B, C(n: Int) }` | 16 | 16 | zero-payload variants are size 0 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `{ Empty, Text(value: Str) }` | 32 | 32 | one owning variant costs nothing extra |")
    strs_push(l, "| `{ A(v: Str), B(v: Str), C(v: Str) }` | **80** | 32 | 2.5× |")
    strs_push(l, "| `{ Nothing, Rec(r: Big), Small(n: Int), Wide(a: Str, b: Str) }` | **120** | 64 | 1.9× |")
    strs_push(l, "| the record `Big { a: Str, b: Str, c: Int }`, for scale | 56 | 56 | |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**So the waste is exactly proportional to how many variants carry a payload**, and it is")
    strs_push(l, "nothing at all when one does. `architecture.md` §7.11 says why this form was chosen over a")
    strs_push(l, "sized payload area — an arithmetic mistake in the second is a buffer overflow rather than a")
    strs_push(l, "compile error — and `spec.md` promises nothing about an enum's size, so it can change.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Time**, `-O2`:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Workload | Without an enum | With one | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| 30M selections on a tag | 26.3 ms (an `Int` and an `if`) | **26.2 ms** | not measurable |")
    strs_push(l, "| 3M of the same | 5.4 ms | 5.2 ms | both under the floor |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1M × build, copy twice, read a `Str` | 71.5 ms | **81.4 ms** | +10 ns per round |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1M of the same over a record payload | 71.5 ms | **81.5 ms** | +10 ns per round |")
    strs_push(l, "| 3M cross-module calls | 15.6 ms (two `Int` calls) | **11.9 ms** | one call instead of two |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A scalar enum costs nothing a hand-rolled integer tag does not. An enum that **owns**")
    strs_push(l, "something costs about ten nanoseconds a round more than the payload alone: a branch on the")
    strs_push(l, "discriminant, and a larger aggregate to move. The last row is the same shape records")
    strs_push(l, "produced and for the same reason — returning one value instead of making two calls.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "At `-O0`, where the generated helpers are real calls rather than inlined, the cost appears")
    strs_push(l, "and is the branch:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Workload | Without | With | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| 3M selections on a tag | 19.7 ms | 23.3 ms | +1.2 ns per round |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1M × copy a `Str` twice | 78.6 ms | 104.6 ms | +26 ns per round |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1M of the same over a record payload | 83.2 ms | 117.9 ms | +35 ns per round |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Peak resident memory**, `-O2`:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Workload | Live set | Peak |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| 80,000 short-lived enums of two heap strings | one value | **1.73 MiB** |")
    strs_push(l, "| 80,000 short-lived records of the same two strings | one record | 1.72 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| empty program | — | 1.67 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "That is the scaling claim: a value holding heap strings costs what the strings cost, and an")
    strs_push(l, "enum costs what the same record does. The count of live backings does not grow with the")
    strs_push(l, "number of values ever built.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Executable size**, `-O0`, where the helpers survive. An enum whose payloads own nothing is")
    strs_push(l, "**byte-identical** to the same program written with an integer tag and an `if` (51,480")
    strs_push(l, "bytes both). One that owns something costs **+144 bytes** over the same program without it,")
    strs_push(l, "against a record's +120 — the difference is the `switch` the enum's two helpers carry.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The compiler itself**, Darwin arm64 host, release binary, on a `compiler/emit.nz` that")
    strs_push(l, "grew from 3,756 lines to 4,276 (and to 4,359 with what a `break` gives back): `nazm check --no-cache` 10 ms, peak 12.6 MiB; `nazm build")
    strs_push(l, "--no-cache --opt-level 0` 720 ms, peak 57.7 MiB, and 120 ms with a warm object cache. These")
    strs_push(l, "are not comparable with N8's or N9's figures for the same command — different binary and")
    strs_push(l, "different cache state — and are recorded as a baseline rather than as a delta.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Generics and `Vec[T]` — measured 2026-09-23, and the cost is the instances")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N11 added parametric generics, monomorphised by `nazm build`, and one generic container.")
    strs_push(l, "Measured **contained, Linux aarch64** (`nazm-contained:1.98.1`, one CPU), release compiler,")
    strs_push(l, "median of five by a nanosecond clock; these are not comparable with the Darwin rows above,")
    strs_push(l, "and the process floor here is about **1.3 ms**. The programs are `target/n11/perf/gen.py`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**`Vec[Int]` against `Ints`, `Vec[Str]` against `Strs`** — 3M push, get-and-set and pop of")
    strs_push(l, "`Int`s; 1M of the same over heap strings, each set taking another element's string:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Workload | `Ints` / `Strs` | `Vec[T]` | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| 3M `Int`s, `-O2` | 19.5 ms, 24.0 MiB | **19.4 ms**, 24.7 MiB | the same code |")
    strs_push(l, "| 3M `Int`s, `-O0` | 60.5 ms | 59.1 ms | |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1M strings, `-O2` | 156.2 ms, 69.7 MiB | **151.3 ms**, 70.4 MiB | within noise |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1M strings, `-O0` | 159.6 ms | 162.6 ms | |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A `Vec[T]` is the sequence runtime with the element's layout, and it costs what the")
    strs_push(l, "sequence it generalises costs. The stride is asked of LLVM, and at `-O2` it folds.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Peak resident memory, short-lived containers against a constant live set**, `-O2`:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Workload, per iteration | 5,000 | 20,000 | 80,000 |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| a `Vec[Str]` of two heap strings | 1.17 MiB | 1.17 MiB | 1.17 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| a `Vec[Row]`, `Row { name: Str, n: Int, tags: Ints }` | 1.17 MiB | 1.17 MiB | 1.17 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| a `Vec[Tok]` of a string, an `Int` and a zero-payload variant | 1.17 MiB | 1.17 MiB | 1.17 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| a `Vec[Vec[Str]]` holding one inner vector | 1.17 MiB | 1.17 MiB | 1.17 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| empty program | 1.16 MiB | | |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Every row reports `live=0` for sequences and strings. What a program ever built does not")
    strs_push(l, "reach its peak; what it holds does.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Enum pressure** — the first workload where an enum's size is multiplied. 200,001 tokens")
    strs_push(l, "of `enum Tok { Word(text: Str), Num(v: Int), Punct(c: Int), End }` in a `Vec[Tok]`, against")
    strs_push(l, "the same tokens as three parallel arrays (`Ints` kind, `Ints` number, `Strs` text), built")
    strs_push(l, "and then read by a `match`:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | parallel arrays | `Vec[Tok]` | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| bytes per token | 40 (8 + 8 + 24) | **48** (tag 8, `Num` 8, `Punct` 8, `Word` 24, `End` 0) | +20% |")
    strs_push(l, "| peak RSS, `-O2` | 11.8 MiB | **14.0 MiB** | +18% |")
    strs_push(l, "| time, `-O2` | 12.3 ms | 12.5 ms | not measurable |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The slot-per-variant layout N10 chose costs 8 bytes a token here, a fifth; an ideal union")
    strs_push(l, "would be 32. `spec.md` promises nothing about the size, so a compact representation stays")
    strs_push(l, "possible — and is a separate milestone, not an N11 optimisation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Monomorphisation's growth** — one generic function, `twice[T]`, instantiated for 1, 10 and")
    strs_push(l, "100 distinct records:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Instances | `nazm check` | cold build | warm build | instance units compiled cold / warm | IR | cache | executable |")
    strs_push(l, "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1 | 2.2 ms | 0.11 s | 0.04 s | 1 / **0** | 19 KB, 4 units | 12 KB | 72,496 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| 10 | 1.9 ms | 0.27 s | 0.04 s | 10 / **0** | 75 KB, 13 units | 41 KB | 74,360 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| 100 | 2.7 ms | 1.79 s | 0.05 s | 100 / **0** | 637 KB, 103 units | 324 KB | 93,008 B |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Checking does not grow**: a generic body is checked once, however many instances there")
    strs_push(l, "are. **Code generation grows linearly**: about 6.2 KB of IR, 3.2 KB of cached object, 206")
    strs_push(l, "bytes of executable and 17 ms of cold build per instance, almost all of it one `clang -c`")
    strs_push(l, "each. A warm build compiles **no** instance, and the build report says so")
    strs_push(l, "(`native.instances.compiled = 0`). An instance symbol names its definition and its")
    strs_push(l, "arguments' canonical keys, which makes it long — 60 bytes for `twice[R7]` in a module named")
    strs_push(l, "`inst_10.nz` — and injective. No cross-instance deduplication, polymorphisation or LTO was")
    strs_push(l, "added; this is the measurement a later milestone would start from.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The compiler itself**, same host: `nazm check --no-cache compiler/emit.nz` 45.5 ms, peak")
    strs_push(l, "20.5 MiB; `nazm build` cold 1.68 s, peak 119 MiB, warm **0.15 s**.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The dogfood** — the Nazm-written compiler's diagnostics moved from four parallel arrays to")
    strs_push(l, "one `Vec[Diag]`. C1 compiling `compiler/emit.nz`, three runs each:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | four arrays | `Vec[Diag]` |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| source lines, `compiler/*.nz` | 11,885 | 11,877 |")
    strs_push(l, "| wall | 10.31–10.36 s | 10.22–10.27 s |")
    strs_push(l, "| peak RSS | 54.1–56.3 MiB | 51.7–52.3 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| emitted IR | 6,000,902 B | 5,974,992 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| C2 executable | 1,724,704 B | 1,724,800 B |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The same output, a little less IR and memory, and no claim about speed: 1% of wall time is")
    strs_push(l, "inside the noise of one run to the next. What the migration bought is the invariant — a code")
    strs_push(l, "cannot be pushed without its message — not a number.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Typed errors — measured 2026-09-24, and `?` costs what the `match` it means costs")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N12 added `Result`, `Option` and `?`. Measured **contained, Linux aarch64**")
    strs_push(l, "(`nazm-contained:1.98.1`, one CPU), release compiler, median of five by a nanosecond clock,")
    strs_push(l, "as for N11. The programs are `target/n12/perf/gen.py`; the raw output is")
    strs_push(l, "`target/n12/perf/results.txt`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Layout** — read off the emitted IR. An enum is one slot per variant (N10's choice), so a")
    strs_push(l, "`Result` carries both payloads:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Type | bytes | an ideal tagged union | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Result[Int, Int]` | 24 | 16 | tag 8, `Err` 8, `Ok` 8 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Result[Str, Str]` | 56 | 32 | two 24-byte strings |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Result[Large, Small]`, a 72-byte record and an 8-byte one | 88 | 80 | the small variant's size is the overhead |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Result[Int, Vec[Diag]]` | 24 | 16 | a `Vec` is one pointer |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Option[Int]` | 16 | 16 | `None` is empty |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Option[Str]` | 32 | 32 | |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Option[Rec]`, a 32-byte record | 40 | 40 | |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`Option` costs nothing over a tagged union, because `None` has no payload; `Result` costs the")
    strs_push(l, "smaller variant. No niche is used anywhere — `Option[Str]` is not a null pointer — and none is")
    strs_push(l, "promised; a compact representation is a later milestone that can start from this table.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Explicit `match` against `?`** — the same function spelled both ways, 20,000,000 calls,")
    strs_push(l, "each taking apart a `Result[Int, Oops]` from a leaf and returning its own:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | `match` | `?` |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| success, `-O2` | 21.3 ms | 21.3 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| error, `-O2` | 19.4 ms | 19.2 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| success, `-O0` | 284.2 ms | 288.7 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| error, `-O0` | 353.0 ms | 350.0 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**No difference**, which is the expected result: `?` lowers to the `match` (`architecture.md`")
    strs_push(l, "§7.13), and every gap above is inside run-to-run noise. At `-O0` a propagation is about 14 ns")
    strs_push(l, "of the loop; at `-O2` the leaf and the `match` fold.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Propagation depth** — a static chain `f100 → f99 → … → f0`, each level `f(k-1)(…)? + 1`,")
    strs_push(l, "the top called 1,000,000 times:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Depth | `nazm check` | `nazm build` | IR | executable | success, `-O0` | error, `-O0` |")
    strs_push(l, "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1 | 1.5 ms | 72 ms | 23 KB | 71,648 B | 15.0 ms | 18.4 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| 10 | 1.7 ms | 81 ms | 69 KB | 72,128 B | 80.5 ms | 92.5 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| 100 | 3.2 ms | 135 ms | 537 KB | 77,088 B | 1,070 ms | 1,197 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Linear throughout: about 5.1 KB of IR, 55 bytes of executable and 0.6 ms of build per level,")
    strs_push(l, "and 10–12 ns per level per call unoptimised. The chain is static, so the stack is the depth of")
    strs_push(l, "ordinary calls and nothing more; an error at depth 100 travels a hundred returns and costs a")
    strs_push(l, "little more than a success because each return releases the `Result` it took apart.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Code per generic instance** — `pass[T, E](r: Result[T, E]) -> Result[T, E]` instantiated for")
    strs_push(l, "1, 10 and 50 records, once returning `r` and once written `let v = r?; Result[T, E].Ok(value: v)`:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Instances | IR, plain | IR, with `?` | executable, plain | executable, with `?` |")
    strs_push(l, "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1 | 29 KB | 39 KB | 73,056 B | 73,072 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| 10 | 185 KB | 282 KB | 78,224 B | 78,456 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| 50 | 886 KB | 1,379 KB | 166,880 B | 233,608 B |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "From 10 to 50 instances a plain instance costs 17.5 KB of IR and 2.2 KB of executable, one with")
    strs_push(l, "`?` 27.4 KB and 3.9 KB: the propagation's two blocks, its tag test and the error path's")
    strs_push(l, "release of the frame are duplicated in **every** instance, as monomorphisation duplicates")
    strs_push(l, "everything. No cross-instance deduplication was added. A warm rebuild of the 50-instance")
    strs_push(l, "program compiles **0** units and **0** instances (`native.instances.compiled = 0`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The dogfood** — the Nazm-written compiler's front end as one stage returning")
    strs_push(l, "`Result[Checked, Vec[Diag]]`, with `emit_program` beginning `check_program(…)?`. C1 (built by")
    strs_push(l, "the reference) compiling `compiler/emit.nz`, three runs each, against the same compiler with")
    strs_push(l, "the migration mechanically undone (`target/n12/dogfood/`):")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | before | after |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| source lines, `compiler/*.nz` | 12,227 | 12,216 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `check.nz` / `emit.nz` / `analyse.nz` | 171 / 5,236 / 4,409 | **64** / 5,174 / 4,567 |")
    strs_push(l, "| front-end pipelines written out | 2 | **1** |")
    strs_push(l, "| drivers testing `vec_len(diags) > 0` to decide whether to continue | 2 | 1 (`check.nz`'s output) |")
    strs_push(l, "| driver lines threading the diagnostic sink, `check.nz` + `emit.nz`'s `main` | 12 + 12 | 4 + 0 (the four print it) |")
    strs_push(l, "| tables declared by `check.nz` | 57 | 7 |")
    strs_push(l, "| wall | 10.93–10.97 s | 11.04–11.09 s |")
    strs_push(l, "| peak RSS | 55.4–56.8 MiB | 54.6–55.4 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| emitted IR | 6,332,226 B | 6,360,949 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| C2 executable | 1,987,168 B | 1,987,712 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| C2 compiling itself | 10.97 s | 11.03 s |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What moved is the structure: the front end exists once, and `check.nz` lost two-thirds of its")
    strs_push(l, "lines. The cost is 0.45% more IR and about 1% more time — consistent across the runs, and too")
    strs_push(l, "small to attribute with one session's measurements; no speed claim is made in either")
    strs_push(l, "direction. The C2 and C3 of the migrated compiler emit identical IR.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Value blocks and the first `Option` in the compiler — measured 2026-09-24")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N12.1 made a block used as a value compile natively and moved one compiler table from a `-1`")
    strs_push(l, "sentinel to an `Option[Int]`. Measured **contained, Linux aarch64** (`nazm-contained:1.98.1`,")
    strs_push(l, "one CPU), release compiler, median of five, as for N12. Programs: `target/n121/perf/gen.py`;")
    strs_push(l, "raw output: `target/n121/perf/results.txt` and `target/n121/dogfood/results.txt`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**One `match` arm written four ways**, 20,000,000 calls of a function that builds a")
    strs_push(l, "two-variant enum (an `Int` payload or a `Str` one) and takes it apart:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| arm | `-O2` | `-O0` | IR | `pick` in IR |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `=> n + 1` — a direct expression | 510.0 ms | 743.3 ms | 23,377 B | 129 lines |")
    strs_push(l, "| `=> { n + 1 }` — the same, as a block | 514.8 ms | 738.9 ms | 23,287 B | 129 lines |")
    strs_push(l, "| `=> { let m = n + 1; m }` — one local | 506.5 ms | 773.4 ms | 23,487 B | 135 lines |")
    strs_push(l, "| `=> { let t = s0; n + str_len(t) }` — an owning local | 847.1 ms | 1,053.4 ms | 24,804 B | 161 lines |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A block costs nothing over the expression it contains**: the first two rows lower to the")
    strs_push(l, "same instructions, and every gap between them is noise. A local costs a store and a load at")
    strs_push(l, "`-O0` — about 1.5 ns a call — and nothing at `-O2`, where the slot is promoted. The owning")
    strs_push(l, "row does more work, not the same work more slowly: binding a `Str` local takes a reference")
    strs_push(l, "and the frame gives it back, and the arm calls `str_len`, so the extra ~17 ns a call is that")
    strs_push(l, "pair and that call. No claim is made that blocks are free in general: that is measured for")
    strs_push(l, "these shapes, and a block whose locals own something pays for what it owns.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Arms per `match`** — an enum of N one-field variants and one `match` over it, each arm a")
    strs_push(l, "direct expression or a block with one local:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| N | IR, direct | IR, blocks | executable, direct / blocks | `nazm build` | `nazm check` |")
    strs_push(l, "| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1 | 11,672 B | 11,744 B | 71,600 B / 71,600 B | 68 / 71 ms | 1.6 / 1.5 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| 10 | 19,443 B | 20,391 B | 71,608 B / 71,600 B | 73 / 71 ms | 1.6 / 1.6 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| 100 | 100,756 B | 110,935 B | 71,632 B / 71,632 B | 94 / 102 ms | 2.2 / 2.6 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Linear: a block arm with a local costs about 100 bytes of IR more than the direct arm — the")
    strs_push(l, "local's store and load — and nothing in the executable at these sizes. No pathological")
    strs_push(l, "growth.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The `Option` dogfood** — `record_owned` returning `Option[Int]` instead of `-1`. C1 (built")
    strs_push(l, "by the reference) compiling `compiler/emit.nz`, three runs each, the N12 script unchanged;")
    strs_push(l, "*before* is N12.1's compiler with the migration undone:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | before | after |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| guards testing a `record_owned` result for `>= 0` | 4 | **0** |")
    strs_push(l, "| sites taking a `record_owned` result apart | 4 `if`s | 4 `match`es and `applies_core_result` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `analyse.nz` lines / non-comment lines | 4,580 / 3,613 | 4,598 / 3,622 |")
    strs_push(l, "| wall | 11.03–11.11 s | 10.91–10.95 s |")
    strs_push(l, "| peak RSS | 53.4–55.5 MiB | 53.2–55.3 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| emitted IR | 6,366,359 B | 6,361,900 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| C2 executable | 1,987,872 B | 1,922,368 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| C2 compiling itself | 10.98 s | 10.94 s |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What moved is the meaning: \"none\" is a variant, so no comparison of a declaration with a")
    strs_push(l, "definition can see it. The code is 0.07% smaller in IR; the time and memory differences are")
    strs_push(l, "within one session's run-to-run spread, and no speed claim is made. The executable size")
    strs_push(l, "moves by one 64 KiB page between runs of unrelated compilers here — N12's own compiler,")
    strs_push(l, "measured in the same session, gave 1,922,176 B — so it is not attributed to the migration.")
    strs_push(l, "C2 and C3 of the migrated compiler emit identical IR.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Derived equality — measured 2026-09-25, and at `-O2` it is the fields' comparisons")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N13 made records, enums and their generic instances comparable, each through a helper the")
    strs_push(l, "emitter generates per compared type. Two questions: what a comparison costs against the")
    strs_push(l, "scalar comparisons it stands for, and what the helpers cost in code.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Time.** Contained (Linux aarch64, 1 CPU), median of five, one comparison per iteration with")
    strs_push(l, "operands built from the loop counter so nothing is loop-invariant; 10M iterations at `-O0`,")
    strs_push(l, "30M at `-O2`. The rows are the programs in `target/n13/bench/` at the N13 commit.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Workload | `-O0`, 10M | `-O2`, 30M |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Int` baseline — `(i % 8) == ((i / 2) % 8)` | 56 ms | 14 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Str` baseline — two literals chosen by parity | 157 ms | 176 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| record `{ x, y: Int }`, equal a quarter of the time | 71 ms | 15 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| record, unequal in the first field in layout order | 31 ms | 0 ms — folded |")
    strs_push(l, "| record, unequal in the last field | 60 ms | 14 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| nested record (two records and an `Int`) | 94 ms | 14 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| enum, different variants | 57 ms | 0 ms — folded |")
    strs_push(l, "| enum, same variant, payload compared | 78 ms | 15 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| enum, same variant, payload always unequal | 38 ms | 0 ms — folded |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Option[Int]`, both `Some` | 78 ms | 14 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Result[Int, Str]`, both `Ok` | 88 ms | 15 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "At `-O2` the helpers are inlined and a composite comparison costs what its field comparisons")
    strs_push(l, "cost: every row that compares is within a millisecond of the `Int` baseline over 30M, and")
    strs_push(l, "the rows LLVM can decide from the construction — different variants, a first field that")
    strs_push(l, "always differs — are folded away with the loop. **At `-O0`** the helper is a real call: about")
    strs_push(l, "**1.5 ns** per comparison over the baseline for a two-field record, 3.8 ns for the nested")
    strs_push(l, "one, 2.2 ns for an enum's tag and payload, and 3.2 ns for a `Result` — and less than the")
    strs_push(l, "baseline where the first comparison decides (the unequal-early record and different-variant")
    strs_push(l, "enum stop there). The `Str` rows are the existing `memcmp` path and are not changed by N13.")
    strs_push(l, "No zero-cost claim is made for `-O0`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Code.** One helper per compared record or enum per unit, generated only when a comparison")
    strs_push(l, "reaches it — a type nobody compares carries none — and one per instance: `Box[Int]` and")
    strs_push(l, "`Box[Str]` are two. A nested type's helper calls its fields' helpers (the nested row above")
    strs_push(l, "has two). Against the `Int` baseline program, the two-field record's helper adds 1,011 bytes")
    strs_push(l, "of unoptimised IR and 56 bytes of executable at `-O0`; the enum's adds 2,293 bytes of IR; a")
    strs_push(l, "`Result[Int, Str]`'s, which compares a `Str` arm too, 2,828. At `-O2` every executable is")
    strs_push(l, "within 24 bytes of the baseline's 72,928. **Across units** a helper is `internal` and")
    strs_push(l, "duplicated: a record compared in two modules is emitted once in each (measured: one helper")
    strs_push(l, "in each of the two units, none in the entry or runtime units). Nothing is exported, so no")
    strs_push(l, "symbol is promised.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The dogfood** — the compiler's completion states as an enum, compared with `==` —")
    strs_push(l, "measured by the bootstrap of record before and after, contained:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | before | after |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `analyse.nz` lines | 4,662 | 4,678 |")
    strs_push(l, "| C2 IR | 6,486,154 B | 6,488,724 B (+2,570, +0.04%) |")
    strs_push(l, "| C2 executable | 1,922,560 B | 1,922,496 B (−64) |")
    strs_push(l, "| C2 compiling `emit.nz`, median of 3 | 11.64 s, 54.2 MB peak | 11.65 s, 54.0 MB peak |")
    strs_push(l, "| C2 compiling `check.nz`, median of 3 | 3.30 s, 25.8 MB peak | 3.29 s, 25.8 MB peak |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Every difference is within noise; none is claimed. What changed is what a completion can be:")
    strs_push(l, "three variants rather than any `Int`, and \"no arm yet\" an `Option` rather than `-1`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Equality requirements — measured 2026-09-25, and the requirement itself costs nothing")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N14 lets a generic function require equality of `T`. A requirement is a fact for the checker,")
    strs_push(l, "so the questions are what it costs to check and publish, and whether anything of it reaches")
    strs_push(l, "the program. Contained (Linux aarch64, 1 CPU), median of five; programs in")
    strs_push(l, "`target/n14/bench/` at the N14 commit.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Checking**, release `nazm check --no-cache` on 200 generic functions each called once:")
    strs_push(l, "bounded and compared, 4 ms; the same 200 as concrete `Int` functions, 4 ms; unbounded, 4 ms;")
    strs_push(l, "200 refused calls, 5 ms. All at the process floor — no cost is measurable, and none is")
    strs_push(l, "claimed either way.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The interface.** `pub fn same[T](…)` publishes 226 bytes; `pub fn same[T: Equality](…)`")
    strs_push(l, "250 — the 24 bytes of `\"requires_equality\":[0],`. Renaming `T` to `Value` gives identical bytes")
    strs_push(l, "and an identical `InterfaceHash`; adding the requirement moves it. A function that requires")
    strs_push(l, "nothing is written exactly as before the field existed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The program.** One comparison per iteration, operands built from the loop counter:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Workload | `-O0`, 10M | `-O2`, 30M | exe `-O2` |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| hand-written `same_int(a: Int, b: Int)` | 70 ms | **15 ms** | 72,936 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| unbounded generic call at `Int` (`keep[T]`) | 88 ms | 50 ms | 73,072 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| bounded `same[T: Equality]` at `Int` | 72 ms | 50 ms | 73,048 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| … at a two-field record | 82 ms | 50 ms | 73,096 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| … at an enum, same variant | 91 ms | 54 ms | 73,088 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| … at `Box[Int]` | 83 ms | 50 ms | 73,096 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| … at `Str` (the `memcmp` path) | 180 ms | 342 ms | 73,120 B |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The requirement adds nothing**: a bounded instance runs as fast as an unbounded generic")
    strs_push(l, "call, and its IR body is the concrete function's instruction for instruction")
    strs_push(l, "(`a_requirement_leaves_no_trace_in_the_program`) — no dictionary, descriptor or test exists.")
    strs_push(l, "**What does cost is genericity, and it predates N14**: an instance is defined in a unit of its")
    strs_push(l, "own and is external to every caller (`architecture.md` §7.5), so at `-O2` the call is not")
    strs_push(l, "inlined and `same[Int]` costs 50 ms where an inlined `same_int` costs 15. That is recorded as")
    strs_push(l, "the cross-unit-inlining item in `roadmap.md`, not as a cost of requirements. The `Str` row is")
    strs_push(l, "slower at `-O2` than at `-O0` over three times the iterations for the same reason — the call")
    strs_push(l, "survives — and is not a regression of N14.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Dogfood**: none. No compiler code uses a requirement, so the bootstrap's size and speed")
    strs_push(l, "moved only by the checker's own new code (`bootstrap.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The lossless syntax tree — measured 2026-09-25, and it doubles the parse")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N15 builds a concrete tree on every parse, so parsing now keeps what it used to discard:")
    strs_push(l, "every byte of trivia, every punctuation token, and a node per construct. Measured in")
    strs_push(l, "process, because a parse is below process-launch noise: the committed pre-N15 parser")
    strs_push(l, "(`git show a129cae`'s `nazm-syntax`, abstract tree only) against the N15 parser on the same")
    strs_push(l, "text, release build, median of 30 parses after 3 warm-ups, heap from a counting allocator.")
    strs_push(l, "Contained, P1, nothing else running (`target/n15/bench`, not committed).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Input | Bytes | Leaves / nodes | pre-N15 | N15 `parse_file` | N15 `parse_cst` | Peak heap, pre-N15 → N15 |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `compiler/*.nz`, concatenated | 606,088 | 136,056 / 56,847 | 14.3 ms | 28.9 ms (**2.0×**) | 29.0 ms | 15.8 MB → 29.2 MB (1.8×) |")
    strs_push(l, "| the same, every 40th token removed | 599,185 | 133,089 / 9,912 | 5.1 ms | 15.7 ms (3.1×) | 14.8 ms | 9.6 MB → 19.1 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "| `examples/sum.nz` | 550 | 197 / 70 | 13.5 µs | 36.2 µs | 34.4 µs | 15 KB → 38 KB |")
    strs_push(l, "| `library/core/prelude.nz` | 901 | 83 / 23 | 2.8 µs | 14.2 µs | 12.8 µs | 6 KB → 20 KB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the numbers say.** On real code the tree costs about as much as the parse did before")
    strs_push(l, "it: 2.0× the time and 1.8× the peak heap, for a tree that holds 2.7 MB of a 606 KB source.")
    strs_push(l, "The malformed input is 3.1× because the pre-N15 parser did less work there, not because")
    strs_push(l, "recovery is slow: it abandoned every broken body, and N15 parses the rest of each. The two")
    strs_push(l, "small files show a fixed cost of about 10 µs — the builder and its interner — which is")
    strs_push(l, "invisible in any command but is most of their ratio. `parse_file`, which the compiler uses,")
    strs_push(l, "builds the tree and drops it; a parse that built only one tree would be a second path")
    strs_push(l, "through the grammar, which N15 does not have.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Where it does not show.** Parsing is a small part of any command: the contained selfhost")
    strs_push(l, "suite, which parses the compiler written in Nazm many times over, took 42.8 s of test time")
    strs_push(l, "against 37.2 s at N14.1's final run (contained, P4T4, one run each): +15%, which is the tree's")
    strs_push(l, "cost where parsing is a large share of the work. The workspace suite took 150 s against")
    strs_push(l, "118 s, with 27 more tests in it. The release `nazm` binary grew from 2,312,000 to 2,397,984 bytes")
    strs_push(l, "(+3.7%), and the workspace gained ten locked crates, nine of them `cstree`'s: `lock_api`,")
    strs_push(l, "`parking_lot`, `parking_lot_core`, `rustc-hash`, `scopeguard`, `stable_deref_trait`,")
    strs_push(l, "`text-size`, `triomphe`, and `redox_syscall`, which is only resolved for that target.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "One cost was removed after it was measured: the first version copied every token — each")
    strs_push(l, "identifier's and string's text — out of the lossless scan for the parser to read. Borrowing")
    strs_push(l, "them took the compiler's parse from 33.6 ms and 34.6 MB to the figures above.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The language service — measured 2026-09-25, and it is fast enough without incremental reparse")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm lsp` re-analyses every open document in full on every change (`architecture.md`")
    strs_push(l, "§7.18). Whether that is acceptable is a latency question, measured rather than assumed: in")
    strs_push(l, "process against `nazm-service` for everything but startup, and against the real release")
    strs_push(l, "binary for startup. Release build, contained, P1 — one CPU — nothing else running; medians")
    strs_push(l, "(`target/n16/bench`, not committed).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| What | Small file (`examples/sum.nz`, 550 B) | The compiler written in Nazm (`compiler/emit.nz` and its imports, 12,543 lines) |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| cold start: spawn to `initialize` response | 0.8 ms (10 runs) | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| cold open → diagnostics, new service | 0.3 ms | 76.8 ms (7) |")
    strs_push(l, "| warm edit → diagnostics, same process | 0.2 ms | 79.2 ms (7) |")
    strs_push(l, "| definition query | 7.5 µs | 1.86 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "And on the compiler: a syntax error in the middle of `emit.nz`, cold open → diagnostics,")
    strs_push(l, "77.4 ms, two diagnostics; a signature edit in `lex.nz` with both `lex.nz` and `emit.nz` open,")
    strs_push(l, "82.5 ms to both documents' diagnostics. Resident memory: 1.9 MB at start, 44.2 MB with the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler open, 46.3 MB after 10 edits and 46.3 MB after 100 — flat, with one analysis and")
    strs_push(l, "0.89 MB of source text retained whatever the edit count.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the numbers say.** A warm edit costs what a cold open does: nothing is reused")
    strs_push(l, "between versions except the process, and the process was never the cost — startup is under")
    strs_push(l, "a millisecond. On the largest program there is, an edit is answered in about 80 ms on one")
    strs_push(l, "CPU; on anything a person edits by hand it is below a millisecond, which is below the noise")
    strs_push(l, "of any editor's round trip and is reported as measured rather than as a percentage. The")
    strs_push(l, "definition query walks the document's leaves to find the token, which is the 1.9 ms on the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler. None of this makes a case for incremental reparse yet; a file much larger than")
    strs_push(l, "the compiler, or a workspace with many large documents open, would be the evidence.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it added to the binary.** The release `nazm` grew from 2,397,984 to 2,768,592 bytes")
    strs_push(l, "(+370,608, +15.5%), almost all of it the protocol's message types; the workspace gained six")
    strs_push(l, "locked crates — `lsp-server`, `lsp-types`, `crossbeam-channel`, `crossbeam-utils`,")
    strs_push(l, "`fluent-uri`, `serde_repr` — all pure Rust. That was the measurement the choice between")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm lsp` and a separate `nazm-lsp` binary waited for, and a third of a megabyte did not")
    strs_push(l, "earn a second executable every editor configuration would have to find: the server is")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm lsp`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The reference index — measured 2026-09-25, and it does not change the incremental-reparse answer")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N17 builds one reference index per analysis (`architecture.md` §7.19) and rebuilds it with the")
    strs_push(l, "analysis on every change. Measured as N16 was: in process against `nazm-service`, release,")
    strs_push(l, "contained, P1 — one CPU — nothing else running; medians (`target/n17/bench`, not committed).")
    strs_push(l, "Index construction is timed apart from analysis, and a query apart from both.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| What | Small file (`examples/sum.nz`) | The compiler (`compiler/emit.nz` and its imports) |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| parse and check (`nazm_core::analyse`) | 0.08 ms | 32.3 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| **index construction** (`ReferenceIndex::of`) | 0.006 ms | **3.85 ms** |")
    strs_push(l, "| cold open → diagnostics | 0.2 ms (N16: 0.3) | 80.3 ms (N16: 76.8) |")
    strs_push(l, "| warm edit → diagnostics and a new index | 0.2 ms (N16: 0.2) | 81.4 ms (N16: 79.2) |")
    strs_push(l, "| definition query | 7.1 µs (N16: 7.5) | 1.72 ms (N16: 1.86) |")
    strs_push(l, "| references query | 8.0 µs | 1.76 ms (a function, 62 uses); 1.76 ms (a local of the emitter) |")
    strs_push(l, "| cross-file references, three compilations open | — | 2.27 ms (`t_int`, 62 uses) |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The compiler's index: 21,884 occurrences, 3,752 entities, 18,132 uses. Resident memory: 1.9 MB")
    strs_push(l, "at start, 48.1 MB with the compiler open (N16: 44.2), 50.2 MB after 10 edits and 50.2 MB after")
    strs_push(l, "100 (N16: 46.3 both) — flat, with one analysis and one index retained whatever the edit count.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the numbers say.** The index costs about 12% of a check and under 5% of an edit on the")
    strs_push(l, "largest program there is — 3.9 ms of an 81 ms warm edit, which is inside the run-to-run spread")
    strs_push(l, "of the N16 figures it is compared with. A query costs what finding the token does: the 1.7 ms")
    strs_push(l, "is the leaf walk definition already paid, and the reverse lookup itself is a hash probe and a")
    strs_push(l, "copy of the uses. About 4 MB more is resident with the compiler open, the index's spans.")
    strs_push(l, "Nothing here makes a case for incremental reparse or for incremental index maintenance: a")
    strs_push(l, "complete rebuild with the analysis is cheap, and correct by construction.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it added to the binary.** The release `nazm` grew from 2,768,592 to 2,823,040 bytes")
    strs_push(l, "(+54,448, +2.0%); no dependency was added.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Rename — measured 2026-09-25")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N18 adds type-name occurrences to every index and a rename that re-analyses its candidate")
    strs_push(l, "program. Measured as N17 was: in process, release, contained, P1, nothing else running;")
    strs_push(l, "medians (`target/n18/bench`, not committed). Planning and validation are one call, so the")
    strs_push(l, "validation's share is stated from its parts: a rename re-runs one full analysis per open")
    strs_push(l, "compilation that contains the edited file.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| What | Small (`sum_to` in `examples/sum.nz`) | The compiler (private `nl` in `emit.nz`) | Cross-file (private `is_digit` in `lex.nz`, `lex.nz` and `emit.nz` open) |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| prepareRename | 12.2 µs | 2.25 ms | 175 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| rename: plan, candidate re-analysis, partition comparison | 0.3 ms (2 edits) | **93.3 ms** (17 edits, 1 compilation) | 97.8 ms (4 edits, 2 compilations) |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "And against N17's figures, on the compiler: index construction 3.91 ms (N17: 3.85), now 22,088")
    strs_push(l, "occurrences (N17: 21,884 — the difference is the written type names); warm edit 83.3 ms (N17:")
    strs_push(l, "81.4); references 1.78 ms (N17: 1.76); cross-file references 2.17 ms (N17: 2.27); definition")
    strs_push(l, "1.81 ms. Resident memory: 48.1 MB with the compiler open (N17: 48.1), 48.6 MB after 10 edits")
    strs_push(l, "and 50.5 MB after 100 (N17: 50.2 at both) — one sample each, with retained documents, analyses,")
    strs_push(l, "text and index sizes constant (`retained()`, `indexed()` and the thousand-plan test); a")
    strs_push(l, "1.9 MB difference between two RSS samples is not evidence of growth, and is not claimed as its")
    strs_push(l, "absence either.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the numbers say.** Recording type names costs nothing measurable: every difference from")
    strs_push(l, "N17 is inside the run-to-run spread. A rename costs what it proves: the plan itself is a")
    strs_push(l, "references query, and the rest is one full check of the candidate program per compilation that")
    strs_push(l, "contains the file — about 80 ms for the whole compiler, so a rename there is answered in under")
    strs_push(l, "a tenth of a second, and a rename in a file anyone edits by hand in well under a millisecond. A")
    strs_push(l, "rename request is expected to cost more than a cursor query, and this one does not make a case")
    strs_push(l, "for incremental reparse. Serialising the edit is not measured separately: it is a handful of")
    strs_push(l, "ranges.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it added to the binary.** The release `nazm` grew from 2,823,040 to 2,888,576 bytes")
    strs_push(l, "(+65,536, +2.3%); no dependency was added.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Scope at a position and completion — measured 2026-09-25")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N19 records the checker's scopes as it checks. Measured as N18 was: in process, release,")
    strs_push(l, "contained, P1, nothing else running; medians (`target/n19/bench`, not committed). The trace is")
    strs_push(l, "written inside the check, so its cost is inside `analyse` and is stated as the difference from")
    strs_push(l, "N18's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| What | Small (`examples/sum.nz`) | The compiler (`emit.nz` and imports) | Multi-module (`diamond/main.nz`) | 200 nested scopes |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| scope trace recorded (frames, bindings) | 8, 7 | 2,725, 3,250 | 8, 0 | 202, 200 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `scope_at` | 6.6 µs | 0.72 ms | 5.8 µs | 59 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| `completion` | 14.3 µs (1 item) | 2.12 ms (a call head, 16 items) | 15.2 µs (40 items) | 208 µs (111 items) |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "On the compiler, against N18: `analyse` 32.9–33.5 ms over two runs (N18: 33.6) — the trace's")
    strs_push(l, "cost is not separable from the run-to-run spread; warm edit 80.7–81.6 ms (N18: 83.3); index")
    strs_push(l, "construction 3.85–3.88 ms (N18: 3.91). Resident memory: 49.5–49.9 MB with the compiler open")
    strs_push(l, "(N18: 48.1), 51.7–51.8 MB after 10 edits and the same after 100 (N18: 48.6 and 50.5) — about")
    strs_push(l, "1.5 MB more, the trace's frames and bindings, and flat across edits, with retained documents,")
    strs_push(l, "analyses, text, index and trace sizes held constant by the thousand-edit test.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the numbers say.** Recording what the checker already decides costs nothing measurable.")
    strs_push(l, "A scope query on the whole compiler is under a millisecond — it scans the trace's frames and")
    strs_push(l, "checks the function around the position for recovery — and a completion there is about 2 ms,")
    strs_push(l, "most of it finding the token, as definition's is. The protocol's conversion is not measured")
    strs_push(l, "apart: it is one range and a list of names. None of this makes a case for incremental reparse.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it added to the binary.** The release `nazm` grew from 2,888,576 to 2,954,112 bytes")
    strs_push(l, "(+65,536, +2.3%); no dependency was added.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The call at a position and signature help — measured 2026-09-26")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N20 records every checked call as the checker checks it. Measured as N19 was: in process,")
    strs_push(l, "release, contained, P1, nothing else running; medians over two runs (`target/n20/bench`, not")
    strs_push(l, "committed). The record is written inside the check, so its cost is inside `analyse` and a warm")
    strs_push(l, "edit, stated against N19's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| What | Small (`examples/sum.nz`) | The compiler (`emit.nz` and imports) | 200 nested calls | Multi-module (an imported generic) |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| checked calls recorded | 2 | 8,873 | 200 | 2 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `call_at` | 2.0 µs | 5.9 µs | 61 µs (innermost) | 2.0 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| `signature_help` (structured, rendered) | 2.3 µs | 6.3 µs | 62 µs | 2.6 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "On the compiler, against N19: `analyse` 34.9–38.3 ms (N19: 32.9–33.5); warm edit 84.7–86.4 ms")
    strs_push(l, "(N19: 80.7–81.6); index construction 3.93–3.99 ms (N19: 3.85–3.88); `scope_at` 0.70–0.73 ms")
    strs_push(l, "and completion 2.09–2.13 ms, unchanged. Resident memory: 58.7–58.8 MB with the compiler open,")
    strs_push(l, "and the same after 10 and after 100 edits (N19: 49.5–49.9 open, 51.7–51.8 after edits) — about")
    strs_push(l, "9 MB more, and flat, with retained documents, analyses, text and checked-call count held")
    strs_push(l, "constant by the thousand-edit test. The protocol's conversion is not measured apart: it is one")
    strs_push(l, "label and its parameters' offsets.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the numbers say.** A query is a walk down one path of the tree and one lookup, so it is")
    strs_push(l, "microseconds even on the whole compiler — faster than hover, which scans the tokens. The cost")
    strs_push(l, "is the record: about 8,900 calls, each with its argument spans and parameter types, add 2–5 ms")
    strs_push(l, "to checking the compiler, 3–5 ms (4–7%) to a warm edit, and about 9 MB of resident memory. The")
    strs_push(l, "memory was not attributed further than that; the record is what changed. It is paid by every")
    strs_push(l, "compilation, since the checker writes it whether or not a tool reads it. None of this makes a")
    strs_push(l, "case for incremental reparse; whether the record should become cheaper, or optional outside the")
    strs_push(l, "language service, is left to review.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it added to the binary.** The release `nazm` grew from 2,954,112 to 3,019,648 bytes")
    strs_push(l, "(+65,536, +2.2%); no dependency was added.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Structure at a position — measured 2026-09-26")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N21 answers from facts the checker already recorded, plus `Resolution::looked_up_on`, which is")
    strs_push(l, "written only where a field or variant lookup fails. **No persistent table was introduced.** The")
    strs_push(l, "new fact holds **0 entries** in every clean fixture measured — the compiler included — and one")
    strs_push(l, "per unresolved member name in a program being edited.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The host was contended throughout (other processes drove its load average between 3 and 70),")
    strs_push(l, "and two sequential runs of the usual benchmark disagreed by up to 5× on code N21 did not touch.")
    strs_push(l, "So the cost to checking and editing was measured **interleaved**: the N20 tree (`b7bb35d`) and")
    strs_push(l, "the N21 tree built side by side in one container and run alternately, four times each,")
    strs_push(l, "contained, P1 (`target/n21/ab`, not committed).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| On the compiler | N20 | N21 |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `analyse` | 38.5–48.9 ms | 37.7–41.6 ms (and one 117 ms run during a load spike) |")
    strs_push(l, "| warm edit | 95.0–106.6 ms | 94.2–105.3 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| resident, compiler open | 34.40 MB | 34.40 MB (+4 kB) |")
    strs_push(l, "| resident, after 15 edits | 35.5–36.2 MB | 35.5–36.8 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The queries, from the quieter of the two sequential runs (`target/n21/bench`), medians:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| What | Small | The compiler (`emit.nz`) | Generic record and enum | Construction inside 200 nested calls | Imported record and enum |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `structure_at` | 14–15 µs | 3.5–5.5 ms | 9–10 µs | 127–148 µs | 7–8 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| member / variant / label completion | 16 µs | 3.6–5.5 ms | 10–11 µs | 138–161 µs | 8–9 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| constructor signature help (`help_at`) | 5 µs | 14–17 µs | 5 µs | 147–167 µs | 5 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the numbers say.** Under the contended host, the interleaved N20/N21 comparison detected")
    strs_push(l, "no N21-specific analyse, warm-edit or RSS delta. Because host load was high, this is not precise")
    strs_push(l, "evidence that the true delta is zero; it establishes that no delta was detectable in this")
    strs_push(l, "measurement. N21 adds no persistent clean-program structure table: `looked_up_on` has zero")
    strs_push(l, "entries in clean code. A structure query on the whole")
    strs_push(l, "compiler is a few milliseconds, and almost all of it is finding the token under the position —")
    strs_push(l, "the same scan N19's completion and N16's definition make; constructor signature help, which")
    strs_push(l, "walks down the tree from the root instead, is microseconds. The benchmark's usual whole-program")
    strs_push(l, "figures for this run are not reported against N20's, because the host, not N21, moved them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it added to the binary.** Nothing measurable: the release `nazm` is 3,019,648 bytes, as it")
    strs_push(l, "was at N20; no dependency was added.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Document and workspace symbols — measured 2026-09-26")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N22 adds no work to analysis and keeps nothing: both queries are derived on demand from the")
    strs_push(l, "checker's definition tables and the parsed items, when asked. **No persistent symbol table was")
    strs_push(l, "introduced**; the compiler open as four programs holds exactly the documents, analyses and")
    strs_push(l, "text it held before (`retained` = 4 documents, 4 analyses, 1,316,013 bytes of text), and the")
    strs_push(l, "number of symbol entries kept between queries is zero by construction.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The host was quiet this time (load average about 2.4–3.6), but the comparison was made the same")
    strs_push(l, "way as N21's, **interleaved**: the N21 tree (`ce0c4ae`) and the N22 tree built side by side in")
    strs_push(l, "one container and run alternately, four times each, contained, P1 (`target/n22/ab`, not")
    strs_push(l, "committed).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| On the compiler (`emit.nz`) | N21 | N22 |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `analyse` | 35.5–36.1 ms | 35.4–36.6 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| warm edit | 85.8–87.5 ms | 86.2–88.2 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| resident, compiler open | 34.39–34.61 MB | 34.33–34.54 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "| resident, after 15 edits | 35.5–36.6 MB | 35.4–36.5 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The queries, two runs in the same container (`target/n22/bench`), medians:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| What | Result |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `document_symbols`, small (`examples/sum.nz`, 3 symbols) | 2.4–2.5 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| `document_symbols`, generic record and enum (9 symbols) | 3.5–3.7 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| `document_symbols`, the compiler's `emit.nz` (135 symbols) | 133 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| `document_symbols`, one of 40 modules declaring the same names (29 symbols) | 11.5–11.6 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| `workspace_symbols(\"\")`, small | 3.2 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| `workspace_symbols(\"\")`, the compiler, 1 root (5 files, 497 symbols) | 1.48–1.49 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `workspace_symbols(\"\")`, the compiler, 4 roots sharing `lex.nz` (8 files, 500 symbols) | 2.18–2.19 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `workspace_symbols(\"emit\")`, same (14 symbols) | 1.88–1.89 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `workspace_symbols(\"Zzz\")`, same (none) | 1.89 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `workspace_symbols(\"\")`, 40 roots declaring the same names (1,160 symbols) | 4.19–4.20 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `workspace_symbols(\"Point\")`, same (40 symbols) | 3.12–3.19 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `workspace_symbols(\"f1\")`, same (440 symbols) | 3.45–3.54 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the numbers say.** The interleaved N21/N22 comparison detected no N22-specific analyse,")
    strs_push(l, "warm-edit or RSS delta, and none is expected: N22 changes no code that analysis runs. This is")
    strs_push(l, "still a measurement, not a proof — the ranges overlap, which is all it can show. A document's")
    strs_push(l, "outline is microseconds, the whole compiler's file 0.13 ms. A workspace query derives every")
    strs_push(l, "analysed file's symbols from every current compilation and deduplicates them, so it costs")
    strs_push(l, "about the same whatever the query: the filter is applied to a universe built each time, and")
    strs_push(l, "most of the cost is building it (four compilations of the compiler, 2.2 ms; forty small")
    strs_push(l, "programs, 4.2 ms). That is well inside an interactive request, so no index was kept to make it")
    strs_push(l, "cheaper and no result is truncated; if an open universe grows until it is not, an index is the")
    strs_push(l, "measured next step, not an assumption. The protocol conversion was not timed separately: it is")
    strs_push(l, "one line-table pass per file over results of this size.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it added to the binary.** The release `nazm`, built from both trees in the same container,")
    strs_push(l, "is 3,019,648 bytes at N21 (the accepted baseline, reproduced) and 3,085,184 bytes at N22:")
    strs_push(l, "**+65,536 bytes, +2.2%**, one 64 KiB step of the file's layout, for the symbol module and the two")
    strs_push(l, "protocol handlers and their `lsp-types` structures. No dependency was added.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Semantic identifiers and semantic tokens — measured 2026-09-26")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N23 derives its view on demand and keeps no token array, no previous result and no cache. It")
    strs_push(l, "adds one checker record, `Resolution::written_type`: every written built-in type name and type")
    strs_push(l, "parameter name the checker resolved, and every type parameter's declaration. That record is")
    strs_push(l, "kept with each analysis like the other resolution maps, and it is the only new retained state:")
    strs_push(l, "**1,989 entries** for `emit.nz`'s compilation (the compiler's emitter and its four imports),")
    strs_push(l, "1,151 for `analyse.nz`'s, 12 for `examples/sum.nz`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Compared interleaved, as at N21 and N22: the N22 tree (`19be58e`) and the N23 tree built side")
    strs_push(l, "by side in one container and run alternately, four times each, contained, P1, on a quiet host")
    strs_push(l, "(`target/n23/ab`, not committed).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| On the compiler (`emit.nz`) | N22 | N23 |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `analyse` | 34.70–34.85 ms | 34.77–35.58 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| warm edit | 84.45–84.91 ms | 84.03–87.12 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| resident, compiler open | 34.33–34.35 MB | 34.52–34.53 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "| resident, after 15 edits | 35.4–36.5 MB | 35.6–36.7 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The queries, two runs in the same container (`target/n23/bench`), medians:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Document | Identifiers | `semantic_identifiers` | `semanticTokens/full`, real server over stdio |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `examples/sum.nz` | 34 | 9.9–10.0 µs | 88–91 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| `compiler/emit.nz` (286 KB) | 13,550 | 3.24 ms | 9.27 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `compiler/analyse.nz` (210 KB) | 10,891 | 2.89–2.94 ms | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| 200 functions of shadowing, generics and a record and a function both `Box` | 6,820 | 1.62 ms | 4.95 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the numbers say.** The resident delta is real and detected in every round: about")
    strs_push(l, "**+180 kB (+0.5%)** with the compiler open, which is what 1,989 recorded spans cost in a hash")
    strs_push(l, "map. `analyse` was at or above N22 in each paired round, by 0.0–0.9 ms; the ranges overlap and")
    strs_push(l, "this measurement cannot say whether recording the names costs anything measurable — it is not")
    strs_push(l, "evidence of zero. The warm edit showed no detectable delta. Deriving a whole compiler file's")
    strs_push(l, "identifiers is a few milliseconds, one hash lookup or three per identifier token; the full")
    strs_push(l, "request over the protocol, which adds line and UTF-16 conversion, the relative encoding, JSON")
    strs_push(l, "of 67,750 integers and the pipe, is about 9 ms for the largest file in the repository, so the")
    strs_push(l, "adapter's share is about 6 ms there. Nothing justifies a range request, deltas or a cache yet.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it added to the binary.** Nothing measurable: the release `nazm`, built from both trees in")
    strs_push(l, "the same container, is 3,085,184 bytes at N22 and at N23 — the new code fits the layout step N22")
    strs_push(l, "reached. No dependency was added.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Quick fixes — measured 2026-09-26")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N24 keeps nothing: a fix plan is made per request from the current analysis's diagnostics and")
    strs_push(l, "dropped with the response — no action cache, no resolve state, no stored edit. **Persistent")
    strs_push(l, "code-action state: zero entries**, and no checker record was added.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Compared interleaved with N23 (`21f626e`), four rounds each in one container, contained, P1")
    strs_push(l, "(`target/n24/ab`, not committed):")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| On the compiler (`emit.nz`) | N23 | N24 |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `analyse` | 35.33–36.16 ms | 35.29–36.18 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| warm edit | 85.72–87.41 ms | 85.21–87.79 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| resident, compiler open | 34.50–34.52 MB | 34.50–34.53 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The requests, two runs in the same container (`target/n24/bench`), medians:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Document | Fix-bearing diagnostics | `fix_plans` at a cursor | `fix_plans`, whole file | `fix_plan_is_current`, every plan | `codeAction` over stdio, cursor / whole file |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| one automatic fix | 1 | 1.9–2.0 µs | 1.9 µs | 1.3 µs | 98 / 97 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| one fix needing review | 1 | 1.9–2.0 µs | 1.9 µs | 1.3 µs | 96–100 / 96–99 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| one fix after `é😀` | 1 | 1.9–2.0 µs | 1.9 µs | 1.3 µs | 98 / 97 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| 100 assignments to immutable bindings | 100 | 10–11 µs | 83–84 µs | 131 µs | 139–140 µs / 1.54–1.55 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the numbers say.** The interleaved comparison detected no analyse, warm-edit or resident")
    strs_push(l, "delta, and none is expected: N24 changes no code that analysis runs, and keeps nothing. Planning")
    strs_push(l, "a document's fixes is microseconds; the currency check compares the document's whole text once")
    strs_push(l, "per plan, which is what makes 100 plans 131 µs. A request is dominated by the protocol round")
    strs_push(l, "trip for a few actions (about 0.1 ms) and by building, converting and serialising the edits for")
    strs_push(l, "many — 100 actions in 1.5 ms, of which the adapter's share, conversion to UTF-16 and JSON and")
    strs_push(l, "the pipe, is about 1.3 ms.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it added to the binary.** The release `nazm`, built from both trees in the same")
    strs_push(l, "container, is 3,085,184 bytes at N23 and 3,150,720 bytes at N24: **+65,536 bytes, +2.1%**, one")
    strs_push(l, "64 KiB step of the file's layout, for the fix-plan module, the quick-fix handler and their")
    strs_push(l, "`lsp-types` structures. No dependency was added.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Call hierarchy — measured 2026-09-26")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N25 adds no per-call state: the caller of each checked call is the body whose `call_sites` the")
    strs_push(l, "checker already records at the same point. **Persistent call-hierarchy state: zero entries** —")
    strs_push(l, "no item table, no graph, no field on `CheckedCall`. Incoming calls scan every call site of the")
    strs_push(l, "item's compilation once (O(calls), a hash lookup each, into a request-local map from caller to")
    strs_push(l, "spans that is dropped with the answer); outgoing calls read the item's own call sites")
    strs_push(l, "(O(its calls)). On the compiler's largest compilation (`emit.nz`, 286,160 bytes): 120 functions")
    strs_push(l, "in the file, 8,873 checked calls in its compilation, 603 outgoing edges carrying 1,702")
    strs_push(l, "navigable call occurrences from the file's functions, to 191 distinct callees.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Compared interleaved with N24 (`7406b3e`), four rounds each in one container, contained, P1")
    strs_push(l, "(`target/n25/ab`, not committed):")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| On the compiler (`emit.nz`) | N24 | N25 |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `analyse` | 34.63–35.28 ms | 34.68–35.76 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| warm edit | 84.58–85.69 ms | 84.98–85.16 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| resident, compiler open | 34.51–34.53 MB | 34.51–34.72 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The requests, two runs in the same container (`target/n25/bench`), medians:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Fixture | prepare | incoming | outgoing | over stdio: prepare / incoming / outgoing |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| two functions, two calls | 4.8 µs | 2.7 µs | 1.4 µs | 83–96 / 91–104 / 79–91 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| four modules, an import cycle | 4.3 µs | 3.8 µs | 3.7 µs | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| two roots over one file, each root | 4.1–4.2 µs | 2.5–2.7 µs | 1.5 µs | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| one target, 200 callers | 285 µs | 239 µs | 1.7 µs | 587–593 µs / 2.98–2.99 ms / 102–103 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| one caller, 200 callees | 288 µs | 10 µs | 235 µs | 639–680 µs / 110–111 µs / 2.94–2.98 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `emit.nz`, its busiest caller (30 callees, 260 calls) | 1.84 ms | 369 µs | 124 µs | 2.04–2.15 / 0.78–0.79 / 1.32 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `emit.nz`, its most-called function (48 callers, 372 calls) | 1.81 ms | 567 µs | 2.1 µs | 2.45–2.46 / 2.04–2.06 ms / 101 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the numbers say.** The interleaved comparison detected no analyse, warm-edit or resident")
    strs_push(l, "delta beyond the rounds' own spread — one N25 round's resident figure is 0.2 MB higher, within")
    strs_push(l, "what the edits leave behind — and none is expected: N25 changes no code analysis runs and keeps")
    strs_push(l, "nothing. Preparing costs what finding the name under the cursor costs: `definition` at the same")
    strs_push(l, "name in `emit.nz` is 1.84 ms, the same as prepare, because both walk the document's concrete")
    strs_push(l, "tree to find the token (N16's rule, shared). Incoming calls over the whole compiler's")
    strs_push(l, "compilation are about half a millisecond; outgoing, a tenth. Over stdio, a request with many")
    strs_push(l, "edges is dominated by building and serialising the items — 200 items with their data in about")
    strs_push(l, "3 ms. Before any evidence run the adapter built a line index of the whole file for every item")
    strs_push(l, "and range list, which made incoming calls of `emit.nz`'s most-called function 21 ms over stdio")
    strs_push(l, "on the host; it now builds one per file per response (and a mutation guards that).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it added to the binary.** The release `nazm`, built from both trees in the same")
    strs_push(l, "container, is 3,150,720 bytes at N24 and 3,216,256 bytes at N25: **+65,536 bytes, +2.1%**, one")
    strs_push(l, "64 KiB step of the file's layout, for the hierarchy module, the three handlers and their")
    strs_push(l, "`lsp-types` structures. No dependency was added.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Completion at a hole — measured 2026-09-27")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N26 keeps nothing and records nothing in an ordinary analysis: **clean-program N26 state is zero")
    strs_push(l, "entries**, and an incomplete program's ordinary analysis is unchanged — `nazm check` from the N25")
    strs_push(l, "and N26 release binaries gives byte-identical output and status on all 200 `.nz` files of the")
    strs_push(l, "repository (the CLI's deliberately broken test programs among them) and thirteen unfinished")
    strs_push(l, "fixtures (`target/n26/incomplete`). What a hole costs is its **probe**: one more parse and check")
    strs_push(l, "of the compilation, made for the request and dropped with the response, whose resolution holds the")
    strs_push(l, "hole's anchor — one unresolved-member or construction entry — and whose diagnostics are never")
    strs_push(l, "published. No completion, probe or anchor is cached.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Compared interleaved with N25 (`e0982a5`), four rounds each in one container, contained, P1")
    strs_push(l, "(`target/n26/ab`, not committed), on the final source:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| On the compiler (`emit.nz`) | N25 | N26 |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| parse | 25.51–26.24 ms | 25.48–25.90 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `analyse` | 35.02–35.75 ms | 35.20–35.40 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| warm edit | 84.64–85.50 ms | 85.47–86.74 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| resident, compiler open | 34.51–34.54 MB | 34.53–34.54 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**An ordinary-path regression, found and removed.** The first comparison, on the source frozen")
    strs_push(l, "before this one, showed the ordinary parse 1.7 ms slower (25.3–25.9 against 27.2–28.2 ms, in")
    strs_push(l, "either order across six more rounds, and not on the host) though that path runs no hole code: the")
    strs_push(l, "hole blocks inlined into the parser's hottest recursive functions had changed their shape. Moved")
    strs_push(l, "into cold, never-inlined helpers, parse and `analyse` overlap N25 again. The warm-edit ranges of")
    strs_push(l, "the final run touch rather than overlap (N26's median about 1 ms, 1 %, higher); an earlier")
    strs_push(l, "interleaved run of the same code gave 84.99–86.31 against 85.06–85.78 ms. No delta is detected")
    strs_push(l, "beyond that, and none is claimed to be zero.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The requests, two runs in the same container (`target/n26/bench`), medians:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Hole | `completion` in process | `.`-triggered over stdio |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `p.` on a record, small | 92.5–93.2 µs | 195–196 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| `b.` on `Box[Int]`, small | 94.8–94.9 µs | 194–196 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| `State.`, small | 91.8 µs | 191–192 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Maybe[Int].`, small | 94.5–95.1 µs | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Point(`, small | 91.1–92.6 µs | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| `State.Done(`, small | 92.3–92.4 µs | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| a pattern's `State.Done(`, small | 93.7–94.5 µs | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| a member hole in `emit.nz` (286,156 bytes, 19 candidates) | 41.0–41.8 ms | 41.7–42.3 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The probe apart, on the compiler's compilation: **parse 25.4–25.9 ms, parse and check together")
    strs_push(l, "33.8–34.8 ms** — the same as an ordinary `analyse` (34.7–34.8 ms), which it is, less the")
    strs_push(l, "reference index and concrete tree the service builds beside it. The rest of a compiler-scale")
    strs_push(l, "request is finding the hole and building the candidates. Resident memory rises by the probe's")
    strs_push(l, "peak while it is alive — 35.0 MB to 51.1–51.8 MB here, the high-water mark of one more analysis of")
    strs_push(l, "the compiler — and nothing it allocated is kept. So a hole costs a compilation's analysis: about")
    strs_push(l, "0.1 ms on a small file, about 42 ms on the compiler, which is the price of reading a buffer the")
    strs_push(l, "ordinary analysis cannot. A name already written is answered from the current analysis as before,")
    strs_push(l, "without a probe.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it added to the binary.** The release `nazm`, built from both trees in the same")
    strs_push(l, "container, is 3,216,256 bytes at N25 and at N26: **no change**, the additions inside the file's")
    strs_push(l, "existing 64 KiB layout step. No dependency was added.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Semantic context packets and `nazm-mcp` — measured 2026-09-27")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N27 keeps nothing between requests: a packet is derived from one analysis of its root, serialised")
    strs_push(l, "and dropped with it — no packet, dependency graph or analysis cache. **Persistent N27 state: zero")
    strs_push(l, "entries.** The ordinary compiler path does no packet work.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Compared interleaved with N26 (`2798b98`), four rounds each in one container, contained, P1")
    strs_push(l, "(`target/n27/ab`, not committed):")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| On the compiler (`emit.nz`) | N26 | N27 |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| parse | 25.06–25.46 ms | 24.92–25.67 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `analyse` | 34.33–36.42 ms | 34.20–34.52 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| warm edit | 83.34–84.17 ms | 82.88–83.86 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| resident, compiler open | 34.54–34.56 MB | 34.53–34.54 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "No delta is detected; the ranges overlap.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A packet, in process, two runs in the same container (`target/n27/bench`), medians — opening the")
    strs_push(l, "root from disk and analysing it, deriving the packet, and serialising it, which is what")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm context` does once per run:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Target | open + analyse | derive | serialise | packet | target source | compilation source |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| small function | 0.13 ms | 0.049 ms | 0.004 ms | 1,627 B | 35 B | 1,021 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| small record | 0.12 ms | 0.036 ms | 0.003 ms | 714 B | 24 B | 1,021 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| small enum | 0.12 ms | 0.036 ms | 0.003 ms | 732 B | 32 B | 1,021 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| a function with 500 callers, 1,000 references | 6.09 ms | 5.43–5.48 ms | 0.37 ms | 159,709 B | 24 B | 21,316 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| `emit.nz`, a typical function (`hex_digit`) | 80.4–80.6 ms | 21.2–21.3 ms | 0.013 ms | 1,225 B | 234 B | 601,518 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| `emit.nz`, its largest function (`emit_module`) | 80.4–80.5 ms | 21.6–21.7 ms | 0.14 ms | 103,431 B | 59,243 B | 601,518 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| `emit.nz`, a record | 80.6 ms | 20.9 ms | 0.011 ms | 835 B | 48 B | 601,518 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| `emit.nz`, an enum | 80.3–80.4 ms | 20.4–20.7 ms | 0.016 ms | 3,284 B | 375 B | 601,518 B |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Over `stdio`, the real `nazm-mcp` process, medians of the full `tools/call` round trip:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Target | `tools/call` | response frame | server resident: before, after, peak |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| small function | 0.48 ms | 1,715 B (was 3,643) | 3.2 → 4.3 MB, peak 4.3 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "| 500 callers | 16.2 ms | 159,796 B (was 347,632) | 3.2 → 11.4 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "| `emit.nz`, typical function | 108.1 ms | 1,312 B (was 2,752) | 3.2 → 37.3 MB, peak 37.3 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "| `emit.nz`, largest function | 108.4 ms | 103,518 B (was 214,808) | 3.2 → 38.5 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the numbers say.** A packet costs one analysis of its root: about 80 ms of the compiler's")
    strs_push(l, "105 ms tool call is loading and analysing the compilation from disk, which every call does so")
    strs_push(l, "that it answers the disk as it is; the protocol adds a few milliseconds. Deriving a packet at")
    strs_push(l, "compiler scale is about 21 ms whatever the target, because it walks the compilation's reference")
    strs_push(l, "index once and re-parses the target's file for the token at the offset; serialising is")
    strs_push(l, "negligible. Resident memory rises by one analysis during a call and stays at that high-water")
    strs_push(l, "mark afterwards (the allocator keeps its pages): 1,000 calls in `crates/nazm-mcp/tests/protocol.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "leave it within a megabyte of where it settled, which the test asserts (48 kB in the host run). No cache was added to reduce the 80 ms: that would need a")
    strs_push(l, "freshness contract this milestone does not have.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a packet weighs.** A typical function's packet is 0.2 % of the bytes its compilation's")
    strs_push(l, "sources hold, a record's 0.1 %, an enum's 0.5 %. It is not always smaller than source: a target")
    strs_push(l, "with many references carries one link per use — 500 callers and 1,000 references make 160 kB, 7.5")
    strs_push(l, "times the fixture's source, because nothing is truncated — and a large function carries its own")
    strs_push(l, "source, 59 kB of `emit_module`'s 103 kB packet. These are byte ratios, not token counts: no")
    strs_push(l, "tokenizer was measured, and no token saving is claimed. Over MCP the frame carries the packet")
    strs_push(l, "**once**, as structured content, with an empty `content`: each frame is the packet plus an 87-byte")
    strs_push(l, "JSON-RPC envelope. The first measurement (the \"was\" column) sent it twice — the SDK's constructor")
    strs_push(l, "also copies structured content into a text block, which the specification only suggests for older")
    strs_push(l, "clients — and the closure correction removed the copy: **52–54 % fewer bytes per response**, in")
    strs_push(l, "bytes, not tokens.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it added to the binaries.** Built from both trees in the same container: `nazm` is")
    strs_push(l, "3,216,256 bytes at N26 and 3,347,328 at N27, **+131,072 bytes (+4.1 %)**, two 64 KiB steps, for the")
    strs_push(l, "packet module, its serialisation and the `context` command — no MCP crate reaches it (`cargo tree")
    strs_push(l, "-p nazm-cli` has no `rmcp`, `tokio` or `schemars`). `nazm-mcp` is a separate binary of **2,627,296")
    strs_push(l, "bytes**, carrying the SDK: 54 crates new to `Cargo.lock` (`rmcp` 3.4.1 and its tree — `tokio`,")
    strs_push(l, "`futures`, `schemars`, `chrono`, `pastey` and others), all in that crate alone, and a one-time")
    strs_push(l, "rebuild of the contained image so they are fetched ahead of offline runs.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Semantic snapshots, deltas and their MCP tools — measured 2026-09-27")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N28 keeps nothing between requests: a snapshot or delta is derived from one analysis of its root,")
    strs_push(l, "serialised and dropped with it — no snapshot cache, dependency graph, call graph or history.")
    strs_push(l, "**Persistent N28 state: zero entries.** The ordinary compiler path does no snapshot work; the only")
    strs_push(l, "change on it is two helpers N27 and N25 code now calls (`context::incomplete`,")
    strs_push(l, "`hierarchy::callee`) with the bodies they had inline.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "In process, contained, P1 (`target/n28/bench`, not committed), medians — opening the root from disk")
    strs_push(l, "and analysing it, deriving the snapshot, serialising it:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Root | definitions | open + analyse | derive | serialise | snapshot | loaded source | all N27 packets |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| small (a record, an enum, two functions) | 4 | 0.13 ms | 0.046 ms | 0.003 ms | 2,958 B | 1,021 B | 4,028 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| 500 callers, 1,000 references | 501 | 6.24 ms | 6.29 ms | 0.27 ms | 376,319 B | 21,316 B | 721,000 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| 2,000 definitions (250 records, 250 enums, 1,500 functions) | 2,000 | 32.0 ms | 29.7 ms | 1.40 ms | 1,441,797 B | 82,794 B | 3,376,156 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| the compiler (`emit.nz` and its imports) | 438 | 80.7 ms | 13.4 ms | 0.33 ms | 332,252 B | 601,518 B | 2,227,799 B |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A delta, in process, against a baseline of the same root — parsing the baseline, validating it (a")
    strs_push(l, "baseline refused at its last digest, so every entry is checked), deriving the current snapshot, the")
    strs_push(l, "whole delta, and serialising it:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Root and edit | parse | validate | current snapshot | whole delta | delta |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| small, no edit | 0.007 ms | 0.007 ms | 0.045 ms | 0.053 ms | 329 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| 500 callers, no edit | 0.86 ms | 1.08 ms | 6.40 ms | 7.59 ms | 334 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| 2,000 definitions, no edit | 3.12 ms | 5.52 ms | 30.3 ms | 36.6 ms | 337 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| compiler, no edit | 0.82 ms | 1.19 ms | 13.2 ms | 14.4 ms | 334 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| compiler, a comment in one body | 0.80 ms | 1.19 ms | 13.4 ms | 14.5 ms | 600 B — one definition, `source` alone |")
    strs_push(l, "| compiler, one new call (`add_line` → `max_instances`) | 0.84 ms | 1.24 ms | 13.6 ms | 15.7 ms | 871 B — the caller's source, dependencies and callees; the callee's references and callers |")
    strs_push(l, "| compiler, one added function | 0.81 ms | 1.20 ms | 13.1 ms | 14.6 ms | 449 B — one added |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Comparing is under a millisecond everywhere; a delta costs a snapshot plus reading the baseline.")
    strs_push(l, "Over `stdio`, the real `nazm-mcp` process, medians of the full `tools/call` round trip:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Root | snapshot call | snapshot frame | delta call (baseline sent) | delta frame | server resident: before, after |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | ---: | --- | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| small | 0.48 ms | 3,045 B | 0.64 ms | 416 B | 3.3 → 4.5 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "| 500 callers | 16.8 ms | 376,405 B | 36.0 ms | 420 B | 3.2 → 13.2 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "| 2,000 definitions | 76.2 ms | 1,441,883 B | 190 ms | 423 B | 3.2 → 45.7 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "| compiler | 99.9 ms | 332,338 B | 125 ms | 420 B | 3.2 → 40.4 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Each frame is the result plus an 86–87-byte JSON-RPC envelope: the result travels once. A delta")
    strs_push(l, "call costs more than a snapshot call because the client sends the whole baseline, which the server")
    strs_push(l, "parses from the request and validates before deriving the current snapshot. Resident memory rises")
    strs_push(l, "by one analysis and stays at that high-water mark (the allocator keeps its pages); 1,000 snapshot")
    strs_push(l, "and delta calls in `crates/nazm-mcp/tests/protocol.rs` stay within a megabyte of where they settled,")
    strs_push(l, "which the test asserts.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a snapshot weighs.** About 720–760 bytes per definition — an identity, a place and eight")
    strs_push(l, "64-digit digests — whatever the definition's size. So a snapshot is **smaller than its sources")
    strs_push(l, "where definitions are real** — the compiler's is 55 % of its 601 kB of source, and 15 % of the")
    strs_push(l, "2.2 MB its 438 N27 packets would be — and **larger** where they are tiny: the generated fixtures of")
    strs_push(l, "one-line functions are 17–18 times their source, and the four-definition file is three times its.")
    strs_push(l, "A delta is proportional to what changed, not to the compilation: 329–337 bytes for no change,")
    strs_push(l, "about 270 more per changed definition. These are byte counts, not token counts: no tokenizer was")
    strs_push(l, "measured, and no token saving is claimed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it added to the binaries.** Built in the same container: `nazm` is 3,347,328 bytes at N27")
    strs_push(l, "and **3,478,400** at N28, **+131,072 bytes (+3.9 %)**, two 64 KiB steps, for the snapshot and delta")
    strs_push(l, "modules, the baseline parser and two commands; `nazm-mcp` is 2,627,296 and **2,823,904**, +196,608")
    strs_push(l, "bytes. No crate was added to `Cargo.lock` — one dependency edge: `nazm-service` now uses the")
    strs_push(l, "workspace's existing `blake3`, the one hash the cache and interface already use.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Semantic patch plans and `nazm.semantic_patch` — measured 2026-09-28")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N29 keeps nothing between requests: a patch is planned from one analysis of its root, serialised")
    strs_push(l, "and dropped. **Persistent N29 state: zero entries** — no patch cache, patch history or")
    strs_push(l, "application history, and nothing is applied. The ordinary compiler path does no patch work; the")
    strs_push(l, "only change on it is `rename::Edit` gaining a serialisation and one of N18's functions becoming")
    strs_push(l, "visible to the patch module.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "In process, contained, P1 (`target/n29/bench`, not committed), medians — opening the root from disk")
    strs_push(l, "and analysing it; binding the snapshot (deriving `nazm.snapshot/1`, serialising it, BLAKE3); the")
    strs_push(l, "whole patch; the underlying N18 rename or N24 fix plan alone; and serialising:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Case | open + analyse | snapshot binding | whole patch | N18 / N24 plan | serialise | edits | patch | replacement | affected source |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| small, local rename | 0.19 ms | 0.083 ms | 0.31 ms | 0.19 ms | 0.001 ms | 2 | 667 B | 6 B | 312 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| small, private function rename | 0.19 ms | 0.083 ms | 0.31 ms | 0.19 ms | 0.002 ms | 2 | 708 B | 12 B | 312 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| small, field rename | 0.19 ms | 0.083 ms | 0.32 ms | 0.20 ms | 0.002 ms | 3 | 738 B | 6 B | 312 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| small, variant rename | 0.19 ms | 0.083 ms | 0.32 ms | 0.20 ms | 0.002 ms | 3 | 756 B | 12 B | 312 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| small, automatic fix | 0.09 ms | 0.017 ms | 0.029 ms | 0.002 ms | 0.001 ms | 1 | 733 B | 5 B | 53 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| small, needs-review fix | 0.10 ms | 0.017 ms | 0.029 ms | 0.002 ms | 0.001 ms | 1 | 745 B | 1 B | 99 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| compiler, private function `v` (373 occurrences) | 82.7 ms | 14.0 ms | 117 ms | 97.4 ms | 0.036 ms | 373 | 25,096 B | 1,865 B | 286,160 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| compiler, automatic fix | 82.1 ms | 14.2 ms | 14.0 ms | 0.012 ms | 0.003 ms | 1 | 749 B | 5 B | 286,216 B |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A rename costs N18's validation — the candidate program re-parsed and re-checked, about 97 ms on")
    strs_push(l, "the compiler — plus the snapshot binding, about 14 ms there (N28's derivation and a hash). A fix")
    strs_push(l, "costs the binding and almost nothing else: the compiler already attached it. No multi-file case")
    strs_push(l, "exists: N18's scope rule keeps a private entity's occurrences in its declaring file.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Over `stdio`, the real `nazm-mcp` process, medians of the full `tools/call` round trip:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Case | `tools/call` | frame | server resident: before, after |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| small, local rename | 0.82 ms | 754 B | 3.3 → 4.5 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "| small, automatic fix | 0.41 ms | 820 B | 3.3 → 4.3 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "| compiler, private function rename | 203 ms | 25,182 B | 3.4 → 64.2 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "| compiler, automatic fix | 101 ms | 835 B | 3.4 → 36.1 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Each frame is the patch plus an 86–87-byte JSON-RPC envelope: the patch travels once. Resident")
    strs_push(l, "memory rises to one analysis's high-water mark — a rename's, which analyses the candidate too, is")
    strs_push(l, "higher — and stays there; 1,000 planning calls in `crates/nazm-mcp/tests/protocol.rs` stay within a")
    strs_push(l, "megabyte of where they settled, which the test asserts.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a patch weighs.** About 650–750 bytes of fixed structure — the operation, the target or")
    strs_push(l, "the fix's facts and precondition, three 64-digit digests, the root — plus about 65 bytes per edit.")
    strs_push(l, "So **a patch is larger than the source for tiny fixtures**: 2.1–2.4 times the 312-byte file for a")
    strs_push(l, "small rename, and 7.5–14 times a one-function file for a fix. At compiler scale it is small beside")
    strs_push(l, "what it edits: a 373-occurrence rename is 8.8 % of its 286 kB file, and a fix 0.26 %. The bytes a")
    strs_push(l, "patch changes are only its replacements — 1,865 bytes for the 373-edit rename. These are byte")
    strs_push(l, "counts, not token counts: no tokenizer was measured, and no token saving is claimed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it added to the binaries.** Built in the same container: `nazm` is 3,478,400 bytes at N28")
    strs_push(l, "and **3,609,504** at N29, **+131,104 bytes (+3.8 %)**, for the patch module and the `patch`")
    strs_push(l, "command; `nazm-mcp` is 2,823,904 and **3,020,512**, +196,608 bytes, for the tool and its typed")
    strs_push(l, "request. No crate was added to `Cargo.lock` — one dependency edge: `nazm-mcp` names `serde`")
    strs_push(l, "directly for the request, and uses the `schemars` derivation `rmcp` already carries.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Compact diagnostics and diagnostic detail — measured 2026-09-28")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N30 keeps nothing between requests: an index or a detail is derived from one analysis of its")
    strs_push(l, "root and dropped. **Persistent N30 state: zero entries** — no index or detail cache, no history.")
    strs_push(l, "The ordinary compiler path, `nazm check --json` and the language server's diagnostics do no N30")
    strs_push(l, "work.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "In process, contained, P1 (`target/n30/bench`, not committed), medians. `nazm.diagnostic/1` stream")
    strs_push(l, "is every diagnostic as `nazm check --json` prints it, one line each:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Fixture | diagnostics | open + analyse | index | serialise | detail | index | one detail | `nazm.diagnostic/1` stream |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| unterminated string (a syntax error) | 2 | 0.080 ms | 0.008 ms | 0.001 ms | 0.008 ms | 682 B | 881 B | 909 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| one type error, two secondary labels | 1 | 0.082 ms | 0.023 ms | 0.001 ms | 0.026 ms | 611 B | 948 B | 356 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| one error with help and a fix | 1 | 0.093 ms | 0.023 ms | 0.001 ms | 0.027 ms | 623 B | 1,280 B | 571 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| 20 functions, each with help, a fix and labels | 40 | 0.53 ms | 0.31 ms | 0.016 ms | 0.30 ms | 10,156 B | 1,276 B | 18,798 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| 500 type errors | 500 | 6.26 ms | 7.25 ms | 0.28 ms | 7.01 ms | 123,238 B | 950 B | 184,864 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| the compiler, with 20 such functions added | 40 | 83.0 ms | 16.0 ms | 0.024 ms | 16.2 ms | 10,862 B | 1,334 B | 19,500 B |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A detail costs what an index does: it derives the current diagnostics to find its id and check")
    strs_push(l, "its state, then projects one. At compiler scale both are about 16 ms after the 83 ms analysis —")
    strs_push(l, "the snapshot binding and the outline behind owners.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the bytes say.** An index is about 330 bytes of fixed structure — root, two 64-digit state")
    strs_push(l, "digests, counts — plus about 245 bytes per diagnostic (180 for a syntax error with no owner),")
    strs_push(l, "whatever its prose. So **for one or two")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostics the index is not smaller**: 611 bytes against a 356-byte diagnostic, 1.7 times, and")
    strs_push(l, "75 % of a two-diagnostic stream. From about twenty it is **54–67 % of the stream** — 10,156 against")
    strs_push(l, "18,798 bytes for forty diagnostics with help, fixes and labels, 123,238 against 184,864 for five")
    strs_push(l, "hundred terse ones — the saving larger where the prose is longer. Progressive disclosure: an")
    strs_push(l, "agent that reads the index of forty diagnostics and then one in full receives 11,432 bytes, 61 %")
    strs_push(l, "of the stream (12,196, 63 %, at compiler scale). These are byte counts, not token counts: no")
    strs_push(l, "tokenizer was measured, and no token saving is claimed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Over `stdio`, the real `nazm-mcp` process, medians of the full `tools/call` round trip:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Fixture | `nazm.diagnostics` | frame | `nazm.diagnostic_detail` | frame | server resident: before, after |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | ---: | --- | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| unterminated string | 0.34 ms | 769 B | 0.37 ms | 968 B | 3.4 → 4.7 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "| 40 diagnostics | 1.30 ms | 10,243 B | 1.14 ms | 1,363 B | 3.4 → 5.0 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "| the compiler, 40 diagnostics | 98.4 ms | 10,948 B | 99.0 ms | 1,420 B | 3.3 → 36.7 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Each frame is the result plus an 87-byte envelope: it travels once. 1,000 index, detail, edit and")
    strs_push(l, "repair calls in `crates/nazm-mcp/tests/protocol.rs` stay within a megabyte of resident memory,")
    strs_push(l, "which the test asserts.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it added to the binaries.** Built in the same container: `nazm` is 3,609,504 bytes at N29")
    strs_push(l, "and **3,675,040** at N30, **+65,536 bytes (+1.8 %)**, one 64 KiB step, for the diagnostics module")
    strs_push(l, "and the `diagnostics` command; `nazm-mcp` is 3,020,512 and **3,151,584**, +131,072 bytes, for the")
    strs_push(l, "two tools. No crate and no dependency edge was added: `Cargo.lock` is unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Command and test summaries — measured 2026-09-28")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N31 keeps nothing: a summary is derived from the command's own outcome, printed and dropped.")
    strs_push(l, "**Persistent N31 state: zero entries**; no timing is recorded, so none is reported. Without")
    strs_push(l, "`--summary-json`, `nazm check`, `nazm build` and `nazm test` do no N31 work.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Contained, P1 (`target/n31/bench`, not committed), medians of the real `nazm` process. `--json` is")
    strs_push(l, "what the same command prints with it (stdout and stderr); a summary is its one stdout line:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Command | diagnostics | `--json` | summary | summary + one detail | time: `--json` → summary |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| check, clean | 0 | 3 B | 305 B | — | 1.0 → 1.2 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| check, a syntax error | 1 | 250 B | 494 B | 1,137 B | 1.0 → 1.2 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| check, no `main` | 1 | 311 B | 439 B | — (a command reference has no detail) | 1.0 → 1.2 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| check, 40 diagnostics | 40 | 18,814 B | 7,723 B | 8,986 B | 1.4 → 2.5 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| check, the compiler plus 40 | 40 | 19,516 B | 8,110 B | 9,438 B | 72 → 175 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| build, success | 0 | 6 B | 317 B | — | 36.8 → 37.5 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| build, 40 diagnostics | 40 | 18,814 B | 7,723 B | 8,986 B | 1.4 → 2.5 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A summary costs one more analysis of the root: linking references to N30's ids analyses it as N30")
    strs_push(l, "does, in process 1.0 ms after a 0.3 ms check at 40 diagnostics and **98 ms after a 38 ms check on")
    strs_push(l, "the compiler** — the summary's dominant cost at scale, paid only when it is asked for. Serialising")
    strs_push(l, "is under 0.03 ms.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the bytes say.** A summary is about 300 bytes of fixed structure — command, status, exit")
    strs_push(l, "status, root, state digest, counts — plus about 185 bytes per diagnostic reference. So **for a clean")
    strs_push(l, "or single-diagnostic run it is larger than what the command prints**: 305 bytes against a")
    strs_push(l, "three-byte `ok`, 494 against a 250-byte syntax error. With forty diagnostics it is **41–42 % of the")
    strs_push(l, "`--json` stream**, and reading the summary and then one diagnostic in full is 48 %. These are")
    strs_push(l, "bytes, not tokens: no tokenizer was measured, and no token saving is claimed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Tests, `--interpret-only`, the same run three ways:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Run | `nazm.test/1` stream | summary | share | run time |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1 case, passing | 158 B | 161 B | 102 % | 1.8 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| 10 cases, all passing | 1,590 B | 163 B | 10 % | 9.8 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| 100 cases, 10 failing | 16,301 B | 1,134 B | 7.0 % | 91 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1,000 cases, 5 failing | 164,790 B | 650 B | 0.39 % | 919 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A test summary lists no passed case, so its size is about 150 bytes plus about 100 per failure,")
    strs_push(l, "whatever the run's size: **a one-case run is not smaller** (161 against 158 bytes), and a thousand")
    strs_push(l, "cases with five failures is 0.39 % of the stream. The run time is the tests', unchanged by asking")
    strs_push(l, "for a summary.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Over `stdio`, the real `nazm-mcp` process, medians of `nazm.command_summary`: 1.88 ms and a 7,808-byte")
    strs_push(l, "frame at 40 diagnostics; 167.5 ms and 8,195 bytes on the compiler, where resident memory rises from")
    strs_push(l, "3.3 to 37.4 MB (peak 54.8 MB: the check's analysis and N30's, one after the other). 1,000 calls through")
    strs_push(l, "edits, breaks and repairs in `crates/nazm-mcp/tests/protocol.rs` stay within a megabyte, which the")
    strs_push(l, "test asserts.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it added to the binaries.** Built in the same container: `nazm` is **3,675,040 bytes at N30")
    strs_push(l, "and at N31 — no change**, the additions inside the file's existing 64 KiB layout step; `nazm-mcp`")
    strs_push(l, "is 3,151,584 and **3,217,120**, +65,536 bytes, for the summary tool. No crate and no dependency edge")
    strs_push(l, "was added: `Cargo.lock` is unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Documentation index and sections — measured 2026-09-29")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm docs` and `nazm-mcp`'s two documentation tools (N32, `architecture.md` §7.34), contained at")
    strs_push(l, "P1 on the M1 Pro, release builds, over the corpus as it stood when the gate ran: **14 documents,")
    strs_push(l, "1,042 sections, 48 of them grammar productions, 1,157,667 bytes**. Bytes, lines and Unicode scalars")
    strs_push(l, "only — no tokenizer was run, and no token claim is made.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Retrieval | Whole document | Section body | `nazm.docs-section/1` | Document index + section |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| A generic-semantics rule, `spec:generics/generic-definitions-are-checked-once-parametrically` | 142,128 B | 1,005 B (0.71%) | 1,577 B (1.11%) | 28,174 B (19.8%) |")
    strs_push(l, "| The diagnostic compatibility law, `diagnostics:what-compatibility-means` | 12,326 B | 1,363 B (11.1%) | 1,903 B (15.4%) | 3,923 B (31.8%) |")
    strs_push(l, "| An architecture invariant, `architecture:3/cache-key-correctness` | 259,005 B | 603 B (0.23%) | 1,135 B (0.44%) | 40,311 B (15.6%) |")
    strs_push(l, "| G78, `goals:G78` | 130,787 B | 409 B (0.31%) | 924 B (0.71%) | 75,055 B (57.4%) |")
    strs_push(l, "| One production, `grammar:function` | 16,667 B | 429 B (2.57%) | 1,732 B (10.4%) | 10,643 B (63.9%) |")
    strs_push(l, "| One capability row, `capabilities:25` | 192,375 B | 47,474 B (24.7%) | 48,528 B (25.2%) | 58,450 B (30.4%) |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Three things the table does not hide. **The whole-corpus index is 225,915 bytes**, 19.5% of the")
    strs_push(l, "corpus — larger than every document but `architecture.md` — because it lists 1,042 sections with a")
    strs_push(l, "64-hex digest each; asking for one document's index (`--document`) is what makes index-then-section")
    strs_push(l, "smaller than reading the document, and for the goals, whose 394 sections are short, it is still 57%.")
    strs_push(l, "**A tiny section is larger as JSON than as text**: the smallest, `capabilities:tooling`, is 12 bytes")
    strs_push(l, "of body and 610 of detail. And a long section is long: capability row 25 is a quarter of its")
    strs_push(l, "document. What selective retrieval avoids is the unrelated text, not the metadata.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Cost | Median |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| read the 14 files | 1.89 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| load: read, section, resolve links, digest | 19.65 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| build the index / serialise it | 0.110 ms / 0.179 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| look up and extract one section / serialise it | 0.0013 ms / 0.0017 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm docs --index --json`, `--section ID --json`, `--section ID` (process) | 22.3 / 22.0 / 21.9 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.docs_index` / `nazm.docs_section` over MCP | 23.7 ms (226,001-byte frame) / 21.2 ms (1,010-byte frame) |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Parsing dominates, and it is paid at every request because nothing is kept. The MCP server's")
    strs_push(l, "resident memory was 3.5 MB at start, 10.9 MB after 60 calls and 13.6 MB after 1,000 more over")
    strs_push(l, "the full corpus, peak equal to the last — the growth of an allocator's arenas under a 226 KB frame,")
    strs_push(l, "not a cache, of which there is none; over a small corpus `crates/nazm-mcp/tests/protocol.rs` holds")
    strs_push(l, "1,001 calls through edits within a megabyte. `nazm` grew from 3,675,040 to 3,806,112 bytes")
    strs_push(l, "(+131,072) and `nazm-mcp` from 3,217,120 to 3,413,728 (+196,608); one new crate, no new external")
    strs_push(l, "dependency.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Repository map and task contexts — measured 2026-09-29")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm repo` and `nazm-mcp`'s two repository tools (N33, `architecture.md` §7.35), contained at P1")
    strs_push(l, "on the M1 Pro, release builds, over this repository at `16b5b27`. **Bytes, never tokens**: no")
    strs_push(l, "tokenizer was run, and no model.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The map is 111,263 bytes — 4.1 % of what it indexes**: 1,192,961 bytes of the fourteen canonical")
    strs_push(l, "documents, 1,024,292 of Nazm source in the three source roots, and 472,905 of Cargo manifests, the")
    strs_push(l, "mutation catalogue and the published schemas (2,690,158 in all). It lists 15 packages, 84 targets,")
    strs_push(l, "3 source roots, 30 compilation roots (7 incomplete — they needed syntax recovery), 34 modules, 477")
    strs_push(l, "durable definitions, 14 documents, 16 schemas and 12 profiles, and delegates 1,038 sections, 601")
    strs_push(l, "mutations, 256 catalogue tests and 16 diagnostics to the answers that enumerate them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Seven representative tasks** (`crates/nazm-repo/tests/benchmark.rs`). The naive baseline is what")
    strs_push(l, "an agent without the planner reads: the whole files the facts are in, the whole documents the")
    strs_push(l, "sections are in, and — for tests — the catalogue entries a search for the file's path returns. Every")
    strs_push(l, "row's mechanical checks pass against the authorities themselves (N27's packet, N32's section, the")
    strs_push(l, "catalogue parsed independently): the exact signature and source, each direct dependency and")
    strs_push(l, "signature type, each direct caller in both compilations, each killer of a mutation inside the seed,")
    strs_push(l, "the diagnostic's code, message and owner's source, each linked or generating section's exact text.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Task | Naive bytes | Context bytes (JSON) | Reduction | Source + text included | Items | Checks |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| A understand `analyse.nz::fn check_program` | 356,043 | 20,059 | 94.4 % | 6,642 | 20 | 22 |")
    strs_push(l, "| B edit `module.nz::fn attach_core` | 348,233 | 7,844 | 97.7 % | 3,242 | 10 | 7 |")
    strs_push(l, "| C diagnose `N0300` in `return_type_mismatch.nz` | 123 | 1,925 | **−1,465 %** | 84 | 2 | 3 |")
    strs_push(l, "| D understand `spec:returns` | 142,128 | 3,769 | 97.3 % | 2,540 | 2 | 3 |")
    strs_push(l, "| D understand `guide:the-syntax/record` | 53,386 | 2,768 | 94.8 % | 1,561 | 2 | 3 |")
    strs_push(l, "| E tests of `package:nazm-docs` | 26,649 | 5,577 | 79.1 % | 0 | 19 | 19 |")
    strs_push(l, "| E tests of `module.nz::fn core_module` | 18,223 | 1,911 | 89.5 % | 186 | 4 | 2 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Row C is recorded as measured: the whole program is 123 bytes, and a structured context with its")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostic, owner, retrieval and state is larger than the program. The reduction appears at the")
    strs_push(l, "scale of a real module, not of a one-function example.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Latency**, in-process, three runs each after the first: a map **433 ms the first time in the")
    strs_push(l, "process, then 372–380 ms**, serialising 0.16 ms. A task whose seed needs no compilation — a section,")
    strs_push(l, "a package's tests, a diagnostic of a small example — **50–54 ms**, almost all of it reading and")
    strs_push(l, "digesting the repository's inputs for the state; `lex.nz::fn is_alnum` 170 ms, `attach_core`")
    strs_push(l, "(edit: four compilations) 240–244 ms, `check_program` (twenty packets from the largest")
    strs_push(l, "compilation) 479–605 ms. Serialising a context: 0.01–0.08 ms. The command line, one process each:")
    strs_push(l, "the map 352 ms; tasks 46 ms (`package:nazm-docs`), 50 ms (`spec:returns`), 237 ms")
    strs_push(l, "(`attach_core`), 579 ms (`check_program`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Memory.** `nazm-mcp` over this repository, five mixed seeds in rotation: **1,000 task contexts at")
    strs_push(l, "100.5 ms each on average, resident memory 73,224 kB settled and 73,224 kB after them.** Flat")
    strs_push(l, "across those calls — which is what was measured, not a claim that nothing can ever leak. The")
    strs_push(l, "protocol suite also runs 1,000 task contexts over a small repository on every workspace run, and")
    strs_push(l, "asserts they stay within 1 MB.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it added to the binaries.** `nazm` is **4,527,008 bytes, from 3,806,112 at N32-H3:")
    strs_push(l, "+720,896 (+19 %)**, for `nazm-repo` and the TOML reader it brings into the binary (`toml` was")
    strs_push(l, "already in the lockfile, for `xtask`). The compiler's own speed is unchanged: `cargo xtask contained")
    strs_push(l, "bench`, back to back at `75a2859` and at `16b5b27`, has a median ratio of **1.02** over 38")
    strs_push(l, "measurements, the largest 1.26 on a 1.9 → 2.4 ms check, under the 5 ms reporting floor. Both are")
    strs_push(l, "about twice the 2026-09-21 baseline for the `nazm` process's own stages — compiled programs and")
    strs_push(l, "the C reference are unchanged — a drift that predates N33 and is not attributed to it here.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The MILESTONE gate** (`gate-plan`: full lifecycle, the MCP entries, every benchmark family —")
    strs_push(l, "the root manifest and `xtask/` changed), every cache empty after a disk-full Docker failure was")
    strs_push(l, "cleaned up: mutation 1,076 s, workspace 319 s (1,757 passed across 99 suites; the container's")
    strs_push(l, "memory peak read 4 GiB, its limit, with no OOM kill — a cold build's page cache counts toward")
    strs_push(l, "it), lifecycle 188 s, selfhost 57 s, bootstrap 37 s, release benchmarks 535 s (re-run: the first")
    strs_push(l, "attempt's script used a shell form the container's `sh` refused, and failed in 10 s before")
    strs_push(l, "measuring anything), compiler benchmark 200 s, checks 16 s — **2,428 s, 40.5 minutes**. The")
    strs_push(l, "benchmark stage's release builds and the mutation stage's pristine build started from nothing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The post-v1 baseline — N75, frozen 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The release gate's benchmark stage at the candidate `054efc1`: `cargo xtask contained bench`, one")
    strs_push(l, "CPU, 4 GiB, offline, with the host otherwise idle. Milliseconds, minimum / median, five runs; the")
    strs_push(l, "record is kept with the gate's evidence (`bench/record.json` of that run). It replaces N48's as the")
    strs_push(l, "reference; no single score is derived from it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| program | check | build `-O0` | build `-O2` | interpret | native `-O2` |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| arith | 2.8 / 2.9 | 88.2 / 95.3 | 98.9 / 99.7 | 2,749.5 / 2,765.2 | 4.5 / 4.5 |")
    strs_push(l, "| calls | 3.1 / 3.3 | 91.4 / 93.7 | 98.1 / 100.1 | 1,531.2 / 1,534.7 | 0.9 / 1.0 |")
    strs_push(l, "| channels | 2.9 / 3.1 | 99.3 / 103.0 | 149.8 / 150.5 | 1,036.9 / 1,335.9 | 1,259.8 / 1,331.5 |")
    strs_push(l, "| floor | 2.8 / 3.0 | 88.7 / 90.4 | 95.3 / 99.2 | 2.4 / 2.5 | 0.3 / 0.3 |")
    strs_push(l, "| sequences | 3.0 / 3.1 | 91.8 / 93.5 | 112.7 / 115.6 | 764.5 / 771.1 | 2.3 / 2.7 |")
    strs_push(l, "| sieve | 3.0 / 3.1 | 91.3 / 95.1 | 116.7 / 117.5 | 1,003.9 / 1,013.2 | 2.9 / 2.9 |")
    strs_push(l, "| strings | 2.9 / 3.2 | 91.4 / 94.3 | 121.7 / 129.0 | 48.7 / 48.9 | 7.1 / 7.4 |")
    strs_push(l, "| compiler | 107.2 / 107.4 | 1,924.7 / 1,939.6 | | | |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`sieve/reference-c` 1.8 / 2.6; `reference-python` not measured (no Python in the image). Peak")
    strs_push(l, "memory, bytes: interpreted 5.7 M (`arith`) to 13.0 M (`strings`); native 1.2 M to 5.8 M.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Against N48**, medians: the compiler's own `-O0` build is 9 % faster (2,131 → 1,940 ms), the")
    strs_push(l, "direction N59's SSA temporaries predicted; checking is slower — `compiler/check` 97.1 → 107.4 ms")
    strs_push(l, "(+11 %), the small programs 0.2–0.5 ms each — over the twenty-six milestones' checker work, not")
    strs_push(l, "attributed to one; `-O2` builds of `channels`, `strings`, `sieve` and `sequences` are 11–15 % slower,")
    strs_push(l, "and `channels` runs 9 % slower natively (1,225 → 1,332 ms) and interpreted, with a wide spread")
    strs_push(l, "(1,037 / 1,336) that one run cannot settle. Nothing here is a claim against another language.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Beside it, on the host** (Apple M1 Pro, release builds, while the contained mutation campaign used")
    strs_push(l, "four of ten cores — indicative, not a baseline): 10,000 tasks started and joined in scopes of 50 in")
    strs_push(l, "143.5 ms (LLVM) / 159.6 ms (Cranelift); a channel round trip 4.66 / 4.82 µs; a streamed value 58 /")
    strs_push(l, "60 ns; 400 M iterations over 1, 2 and 4 tasks 1,655, 828 and 417 ms (LLVM; Cranelift the same within")
    strs_push(l, "1 ms). A three-package build: lock 4.4 ms, check 6.1 ms cold and 7.4 ms warm, build 211.6 ms with no")
    strs_push(l, "cache and 82.0 ms warm. The figures of N62–N68 above — a board image's bytes and stack, a vectorised")
    strs_push(l, "sum, a GPU map, field-by-field vectors — were measured at their milestones and not again here; their")
    strs_push(l, "run-verified tests passed at the candidate. A contract's static gas bound for the `contract`")
    strs_push(l, "template: `transfer` 59,420, `pause` 30,824, 831 bytes of runtime code; the EVM run stays inside it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The v1 baseline — N48, frozen 2026-10-01")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The numbers a later milestone compares against**, in place of `bench/baseline-linux-aarch64.json`,")
    strs_push(l, "which was recorded at `ada3ae2` — before N1 — and against which every row now reads 2–6× slower for")
    strs_push(l, "reasons forty milestones old (the per-milestone gate runs have been compared with each other, not")
    strs_push(l, "with it, since N33). That file is left as it is; these are the v1 figures.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Contained compiler benchmark (`cargo xtask contained bench`), Linux aarch64, 1 CPU, offline, at")
    strs_push(l, "`74727bb` (`a8a7b3f` and `84d3c80` differ from it in tests and the mutation catalogue only), min /")
    strs_push(l, "median ms:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| program | check | build `-O0` | build `-O2` | interpret | native `-O2` |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| arith | 2.5 / 2.6 | 88.6 / 89.0 | 95.9 / 96.0 | 2,753.8 / 2,760.9 | 4.5 / 4.5 |")
    strs_push(l, "| calls | 2.6 / 2.7 | 91.4 / 94.4 | 96.6 / 104.6 | 1,466.8 / 1,471.1 | 1.0 / 1.0 |")
    strs_push(l, "| channels | 2.8 / 2.9 | 96.3 / 99.0 | 122.5 / 130.8 | 951.6 / 1,012.0 | 1,203.5 / 1,225.2 |")
    strs_push(l, "| floor | 2.5 / 2.8 | 88.2 / 90.2 | 92.9 / 97.9 | 2.0 / 2.0 | 0.3 / 0.3 |")
    strs_push(l, "| sequences | 2.6 / 2.6 | 90.6 / 94.9 | 102.3 / 104.4 | 764.4 / 771.8 | 2.3 / 2.4 |")
    strs_push(l, "| sieve | 2.7 / 2.7 | 91.0 / 92.6 | 104.4 / 104.8 | 998.7 / 1,025.2 | 2.9 / 3.0 |")
    strs_push(l, "| strings | 2.5 / 2.9 | 101.4 / 102.7 | 111.6 / 115.1 | 49.1 / 51.6 | 7.4 / 7.6 |")
    strs_push(l, "| compiler | 92.3 / 97.1 | 2,045.7 / 2,131.0 | | | |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`sieve/reference-c` 1.7 / 1.8 ms. The run was not on an idle machine (host builds ran beside it),")
    strs_push(l, "so a later comparison should be made on one, or as an interleaved A/B like the one below.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Against N39's own gate run** the interpreted rows hold within 0.3–6 % (`calls` 1,467 → 1,471,")
    strs_push(l, "`sequences` 770 → 772, `arith` 2,748 → 2,761, `sieve` 999 → 1,025, `strings` 48.7 → 51.6) and")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/check` 93.0 → 97.1; `compiler/build-O0` moved 1,847 → 2,159 at N40 (2,131 now). An")
    strs_push(l, "interleaved A/B on the host, release, N39's `ab0a761` against HEAD on the same input (N39's")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/emit.nz`) attributes it: `nazm check` 59.6 / 60.1 ms (1.01), `arith` interpreted")
    strs_push(l, "617.6 / 611.3 ms (0.99), **`nazm build -O0` 1,025 / 1,201 ms (1.17)**. The build's extra time is")
    strs_push(l, "clang's: the MIR emitter (N40) hands it 8.44 MB of LLVM text against 6.77 MB, 177,239")
    strs_push(l, "instructions against 138,522, and 13,836 `alloca`s against 3,275 — a stack slot per MIR local,")
    strs_push(l, "which `-O0` does not promote — and clang's compile is 1,091 ms of the build's 1,256. No program's")
    strs_push(l, "behaviour changed. Promoting locals to SSA in the emitter is the evidence-backed fix, and it is a")
    strs_push(l, "backend change for after v1, not a release-audit one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Restriction profiles — N47, measured 2026-10-01")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Host, release, `nazm check --no-cache`, median of 9. The rules themselves cost nothing measurable:")
    strs_push(l, "they read facts the check already settled. What a profile costs is the check it runs to get those")
    strs_push(l, "facts, before the command's own: a 2,000-function pure program takes 31.4 ms under `general`, 56.2 ms")
    strs_push(l, "under `embedded` (accepted: two checks) and 31.8 ms under `cyber` (refused before the command")
    strs_push(l, "checks); `--profile-report` alone costs the same second check, 56.0 ms. On the compiler's own")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/emit.nz`, refused under `embedded` and `critical`, 59.4 ms against 59.5 ms. Reusing the")
    strs_push(l, "command's check for the profile would remove the second one; v1 does not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Packages — N46, measured 2026-10-01")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Host, best of 5 (`what_packages_cost`, `crates/nazm-cli/tests/packages.rs`, `--ignored`), the")
    strs_push(l, "three-package diamond of the tests: `nazm lock` 5.2 ms (resolution, three manifests, three")
    strs_push(l, "digests, the lockfile's bytes compared and left alone); `nazm check` 8.5 ms with `--no-cache` and")
    strs_push(l, "10.0 ms from a warm cache (for three one-function packages the cache's reads cost more than the")
    strs_push(l, "checking they save); `nazm build --no-cache` 210.9 ms and a warm build 86.9 ms (clang is most of")
    strs_push(l, "both). Two hundred packages, each depending on up to three earlier ones: resolving, locking,")
    strs_push(l, "checking and locking again takes 2.6 s in all, dominated by checking 200 modules. Every existing")
    strs_push(l, "program is unaffected: nothing that is not a package takes the new paths, and the only change to")
    strs_push(l, "the link — `ZERO_AR_DATE=1`, and linking under the final file name — makes executables")
    strs_push(l, "reproducible without changing what they contain.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The standard library — N45, measured 2026-10-01")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The standard library is Nazm source, so what it costs is what the code generators make of it.")
    strs_push(l, "Host, `-O2`, best of 5 (`what_the_standard_library_costs`, `crates/nazm-cli/tests/stdlib.rs`,")
    strs_push(l, "`--ignored`):")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | LLVM | Cranelift |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `text_split` of a 120 KB string into 20,000 pieces, 50 times (1 M pieces) | 111.9 ms | 84.6 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `text_find` over 100,001 bytes, 20 times (2 M positions) | 27.2 ms | 27.3 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `text_parse_int` of `int_to_str(i)` for 1 M values | 83.0 ms | 102.8 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `ints_sum` and `ints_max` over 1 M elements, 20 times | 17.4 ms | 72.6 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "About 110 ns a piece to split (each piece a borrowed slice pushed into a `Strs`), 14 ns a")
    strs_push(l, "position to search (a slice and a byte comparison), 80–100 ns to format and parse an integer. The")
    strs_push(l, "sequence loop is where the backends differ most: LLVM keeps the loop in registers; Cranelift, which")
    strs_push(l, "holds every local in a stack slot (§7.43), reloads it each iteration. No program's code changed:")
    strs_push(l, "nothing in the tree imports a standard module.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The formal core's check — N61, measured 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`cargo test -p nazm-formal`, debug, M1 Pro: 94,352 programs enumerated, 28,238 well-typed (27,680 before R1a, L6), each")
    strs_push(l, "typed program checked and run in-process by the interpreter and each program checked by the")
    strs_push(l, "checker — 54 s for the five properties. The bound is five nodes; six would be roughly twenty times")
    strs_push(l, "as many programs.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Scalar temporaries — N59, measured 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The LLVM emitter now gives no slot to a scalar temporary assigned once and read only in its block")
    strs_push(l, "(§7.61). M1 Pro, Apple clang 21.0.0, the debug `nazm` before (`0acdf20`) and after, interleaved,")
    strs_push(l, "on a host also running a contained mutation session — so the spread is wide:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | before | after |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `compiler/emit.nz` at `-O0`: `alloca`s | 13,867 | 6,328 |")
    strs_push(l, "| its LLVM text | 8.47 MB, 177,531 instructions | 7.69 MB, 157,328 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm build -O0` of it, five runs | 1,992 / 2,067 / 2,087 / 2,091 / 2,101 ms | 1,937 / 1,982 / 1,983 / 2,011 / 2,993 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| a 20 M-iteration loop and `fib(27)`, built `-O0`, three runs | 133 / 144 / 759 ms | 103 / 105 / 443 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The build's median moved 5 %: clang's `-O0` time is not mostly slots. The `-O0` program is about a")
    strs_push(l, "quarter faster, because a promoted temporary is a register and not a store and a load. `-O2` is")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged in kind — LLVM promoted these already. Cranelift was not touched: its scalar locals were")
    strs_push(l, "already SSA variables.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Targets — N57, measured 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "One program (a recursive `fib(20)` and a task sending a string through a `Chan[Str]`), built on an")
    strs_push(l, "M1 Pro (macOS, Apple clang 21.0.0) by both backends for each target:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| target | how | result |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `aarch64-apple-darwin` | built and run on the host | `from task 6765`, all reclaimed |")
    strs_push(l, "| `x86_64-apple-darwin` | built and linked on the host, run under Rosetta | the same, both backends |")
    strs_push(l, "| `aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu` | `--objects` on the host; `cc 00-m0.o 01-runtime.o 02-entry.o -lpthread` and run in `nazm-contained:1.98.1` (`docker run --network none`) | the same, both backends |")
    strs_push(l, "| `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu` | `--objects` on the host; ELF x86-64 objects | compile-only: no amd64 image or emulator here |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Cross-host reproducibility — the same target's objects from two hosts — was not measured.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Field-by-field vectors — N68, measured 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "1,000,000 records of eight `Int` fields in a `Vec`, `--opt-level 2`, Apple M1 Pro; seconds, the")
    strs_push(l, "median of the last four of five runs (fill included, ~0.13 s of each):")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| loop | element by element (`aos`) | field by field (`soa`) | hand-written, eight `Ints` |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| sum of one field, 500 passes | 0.58 | 0.21 | 0.21 |")
    strs_push(l, "| sum of all eight fields, 50 passes | 0.10 | 0.20 | — |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The layout wins where a loop reads few fields of wide records and loses where it reads them all;")
    strs_push(l, "nothing here chooses between them for a program.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### A GPU map — N67, measured 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`collatz` (steps to 1, plus a helper call) over 1..=1,000,000 on the M1 Pro's GPU through macOS's")
    strs_push(l, "OpenCL 1.2 (`nazm accel --no-check`, three runs), against the same sum by a native `-O2` build on one")
    strs_push(l, "CPU core:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | GPU | CPU, one core |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| kernel build | 1.6–3.3 ms (the driver's cache warm; 300 ms cold) | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| host to device, 8,000,004 B | 2.3–4.4 ms | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| run, to the synchronisation | 22.6–29.6 ms | 190 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| device to host, 8,000,004 B | 1.0–1.8 ms | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| checksum | 144434412 | 144434412 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "End to end about 6× one core; not compared against all cores, and not a claim about any other")
    strs_push(l, "kernel: a map whose elements do little work loses to its transfers.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Vectorised sums — N66, measured 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`total(v)`, the counted summation loop, against the same loop with its operands swapped")
    strs_push(l, "(`s = ints_get(v, i) + s` — the same work and checks, not the idiom), each summing `v` until 2·10⁹")
    strs_push(l, "elements are added, `--opt-level 2`, Apple M1 Pro, Apple clang 21. Seconds, steady state (the median")
    strs_push(l, "of the last four of five runs; the first run of each is ~0.35 s slower, warming):")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| elements | scalar | vectorised | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1,000 | 0.77 | 0.40 | 1.9× |")
    strs_push(l, "| 100,000 | 0.75 | 0.39 | 1.9× |")
    strs_push(l, "| 10,000,000 | 0.79 | 0.45 | 1.75× (memory-bound) |")
    strs_push(l, "| 100,000 of ±2^60 (every block on the checked path) | 0.75 | 1.00 | 0.75× — the fallback's scan |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The executables differ by 24 bytes: `nz.ints_sum` is in every runtime that has sequences, used or not.")
    strs_push(l, "x86_64 was not measured. At `-O0` the runtime is not vectorised and the speed-up is not claimed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Stack: the stated bound and a painted run — N63, measured 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/realtime.rs`'s ignored test: each program built for `aarch64-unknown-none`")
    strs_push(l, "with `--stack-watermark`, `bounds.json` read, the image booted on QEMU `virt` (`nazm-qemu:n62`),")
    strs_push(l, "and the deepest painted word the run overwrote reported on the UART. Bytes, measured / bound:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| program | `-O0` | `-O2` |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| three counted loops and a call (`BOUNDED`) | 176 / 192 | 24 / 48 |")
    strs_push(l, "| a four-deep call chain in a 1,000-turn loop | 304 / 320 | 24 / 48 |")
    strs_push(l, "| a nine-argument call in a loop | 264 / 288 | 24 / 48 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The bound is the claim; each measurement is one run on an emulator and says only that this run")
    strs_push(l, "stayed inside it. The gap is the deepest path's frames that this run's path did not take (at `-O2`,")
    strs_push(l, "the failure path through `nz.fail`). No timing is reported: an emulator's is not a machine's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### A freestanding image — N62, measured 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-cli/tests/freestanding.rs`'s program (`Hi` through `mmio_write32`, a loop and a")
    strs_push(l, "recursive `fib(10)`), built on the host with `--target aarch64-unknown-none --objects`, linked with")
    strs_push(l, "`ld.lld -T link.ld` and booted with `qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a53 -nographic -nic none")
    strs_push(l, "-semihosting` in `nazm-qemu:n62` (`docker/qemu.Dockerfile`, `docker run --network none`):")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| image | `.text` 1,424 B, `.rodata` 583 B, `.bss` 24 B — 2,421 B, plus the 64 KiB stack the script reserves |")
    strs_push(l, "| output | `Hi`, `100`; status 0 |")
    strs_push(l, "| QEMU start to exit, three runs | 50, 27, 29 ms — QEMU's own start-up, not the program |")
    strs_push(l, "| an overflow, a deep recursion | `N0400`, `N0408` on the UART; status 2 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "One board, emulated: no hardware was run, and the timing says nothing about one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Select and the event count — N54, measured 2026-10-02")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N54 added a process-wide event count that every typed send and close advances (§7.56), so what is")
    strs_push(l, "measured is what that costs a channel and what a select costs over a receive. Host (Apple M1 Pro,")
    strs_push(l, "Apple clang 21.0.0), LLVM `-O2`, three runs of one program at `4ce95f3`+N54, with a contained")
    strs_push(l, "mutation session running beside it, so the spread is wide and the figures are an order of")
    strs_push(l, "magnitude, not a benchmark:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | three runs |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| 100,000 typed send-then-receive pairs on one task, a 1-slot `Chan[Int]` | 20–30 ns a pair |")
    strs_push(l, "| 100,000 round trips between two tasks through two `Chan[Int]`, received with `chan_recv_of` | 6.7–7.4 µs each |")
    strs_push(l, "| the same, the worker waiting in `chan_select_of` over one channel | 6.4–7.1 µs each |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **The event count costs a send one atomic increment and one load** when nobody selects —")
    strs_push(l, "  a single-task pair stays in tens of nanoseconds.")
    strs_push(l, "- **A select costs no more than a receive** at one channel: both wait on a condition variable and")
    strs_push(l, "  are woken by a broadcast; the wake-up dominates.")
    strs_push(l, "- The round trip is slower than N44's `Int`-channel 4.6 µs (best of 5, quiet host); this run did")
    strs_push(l, "  not repeat N44's conditions, so no regression is claimed or excluded. What a pool would change —")
    strs_push(l, "  the thread wake-up behind every figure here — is §7.56's designed and unbuilt part.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Tasks and channels — N44, measured 2026-10-01")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N44 kept the scheduler — one OS thread per task, joined by its scope — and wrote its contract")
    strs_push(l, "down, so what is measured is the baseline anything more elaborate would have to beat. Host, `-O2`,")
    strs_push(l, "best of 5 (`what_tasks_and_channels_cost`, `crates/nazm-cli/tests/scheduler.rs`, `--ignored`),")
    strs_push(l, "with a one-core mutation container running beside it:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | LLVM | Cranelift |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| 10,000 tasks started and joined, in scopes of 50 | 131.7 ms (13.2 µs each) | 128.8 ms (12.9 µs) |")
    strs_push(l, "| 100,000 channel round trips between two tasks | 462.7 ms (4.63 µs each) | 468.2 ms (4.68 µs) |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1,000,000 values streamed through a 1,024-slot channel | 59.7 ms (60 ns each) | 60.3 ms (60 ns) |")
    strs_push(l, "| 400 M loop iterations over 1 / 2 / 4 tasks | 1,653 / 829 / 419 ms | 1,655 / 829 / 416 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Scaling** is linear to four tasks (3.95× at 4), because independent tasks share nothing but")
    strs_push(l, "  the atomic accounting counters.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Memory plateau.** A program running rounds of 100 tasks that each allocate a string and")
    strs_push(l, "  report on a channel: peak RSS 3.75 MB after 5,000 tasks, 3.83 MB after 50,000, 3.80 MB after")
    strs_push(l, "  500,000 (`/usr/bin/time -l`, 16 KiB pages). No per-task growth: every thread is joined and every")
    strs_push(l, "  block freed by its scope.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The runtime contract — N43, measured 2026-10-01")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N43 moved the runtime into `crates/nazm-lir/src/runtime/` (its own crate, `crates/nazm-runtime/`, since N53) and wrote its contract down; it changed")
    strs_push(l, "no instruction, so what is measured is what the runtime costs, now that there is a harness that")
    strs_push(l, "calls it directly.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Nothing a program runs changed.** All 205 sources, N42 (`9b35099`) against N43 release builds,")
    strs_push(l, "  `nazm build --no-cache --emit-ir`: the same status and diagnostics for all 205, and every LLVM")
    strs_push(l, "  file of the 104 that build — runtime and entry units included — byte-identical.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Cold start.** An executable whose `main` returns `0`, host, 200 runs: median 3.65 ms (LLVM),")
    strs_push(l, "  3.73 ms (Cranelift); p10–p90 3.25–4.22 and 3.37–4.30 ms. Nothing is initialised lazily and the")
    strs_push(l, "  entry does four stores before calling `main`, so this is the process's own cost.")
    strs_push(l, "- **What a runtime call costs**, host, clang `-O2`, 10 million iterations, best of four: a string")
    strs_push(l, "  backing allocated and released 15.3 ns; a retain and a release of a shared backing (two atomic")
    strs_push(l, "  operations) 11.6 ns; a sequence push through `nz.arr_grow`, amortised over doubling, 1.7 ns.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Memory.** The same harness peaks at 84.1 MB, which is the 10-million-element sequence")
    strs_push(l, "  (80 MB of data after doubling) and nothing else; the direct-test harness runs at under 10 MB.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Size.** The smallest executable is 50,680 B (LLVM) and 52,832 B (Cranelift, which links the")
    strs_push(l, "  whole runtime); unchanged by N43.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Foreign calls — N42, measured 2026-10-01")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A foreign call is a direct call with the C convention and no failure check after it, so what is")
    strs_push(l, "measured is what one costs against a Nazm call, and what the feature costs a build.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **A call into C costs what a Nazm call costs.** Host, `-O2`, best of 3, a checked loop of 10")
    strs_push(l, "  million iterations whose body is one call (`t = add(t, i)`) and an overflow-checked `+`: calling")
    strs_push(l, "  a clang `-O1` C `c_add` 56.6 ms with the LLVM backend and 53.8 ms with Cranelift; the same loop")
    strs_push(l, "  calling a Nazm `add` 48.0 ms (LLVM, which can inline it) and 62.3 ms (Cranelift, which cannot,")
    strs_push(l, "  and checks for a failure after each call). About 5–6 ns an iteration either way; nothing is")
    strs_push(l, "  marshalled, because only `Int` and `Bool` cross.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Nothing else moved.** A build of the loop takes 0.14 s with or without the foreign")
    strs_push(l, "  declaration and `--link`. A program with no foreign declaration is untouched: all 205 sources in")
    strs_push(l, "  the tree, N41 (`eceeccc`) against N42 release builds, `nazm build --no-cache --emit-ir` — the same")
    strs_push(l, "  status and diagnostics for all 205, and every LLVM file of the 104 that build byte-identical.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The Cranelift backend — N41, measured 2026-10-01")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Every buildable program behaves identically under both backends**: the 104 programs of the")
    strs_push(l, "  205-source corpus that build, stdout, stderr, exit status and the memory report.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Build time.** `nazm build --no-cache compiler/emit.nz` at `-O0`, host: Cranelift 0.74 s, LLVM")
    strs_push(l, "  (clang) 1.21 s. The Cranelift figure still includes clang compiling the runtime's LLVM text and")
    strs_push(l, "  linking.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Code size.** The resulting executable: 1.89 MB (Cranelift) and 1.87 MB (LLVM `-O0`).")
    strs_push(l, "- **Reuse.** An unchanged unit's Cranelift object is found by a key computed from MIR before any")
    strs_push(l, "  code is generated, so a warm rebuild generates nothing for it")
    strs_push(l, "  (`an_unchanged_unit_is_reused_by_its_key_and_a_changed_one_is_regenerated`).")
    strs_push(l, "### MIR — N40, measured 2026-10-01")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Nothing changed in any program.** All 205 sources, N39 against N40: `check`, `run` and `build`")
    strs_push(l, "  diagnostics identical, and the 104 buildable programs' stdout, stderr, exit status and memory")
    strs_push(l, "  report identical.")
    strs_push(l, "- **What each phase costs**, container, release, median of 15 (`what_each_phase_costs_on_the_compiler`):")
    strs_push(l, "  `compiler/emit.nz` parse 29.3 ms, checking +19.3, Core IR +11.6 (verifying 0.4), **MIR +8.1")
    strs_push(l, "  (verifying 2.3)**, layout +1.2, LLVM text +40.1 — 111.9 ms; a 3,001-function chain 96.8 ms, of")
    strs_push(l, "  which MIR 8.3. On the host during development: MIR 5.6 ms (verifying 2.0) in an 85.7 ms pipeline.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Its size.** `compiler/emit.nz` is 432 MIR functions, 4,633 blocks, 20,077 statements and 13,835")
    strs_push(l, "  locals; the largest function, `check_all`, 427 blocks and 1,238 locals.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Scale.** Linear: 1.5 ms for a function of 250 bindings, 6.9 ms for 1,000 (release, host).")
    strs_push(l, "- **Size.** Contained release: `nazm` 4,920,224 B (+65,536 against N39's 4,854,688), `nazm-mcp`")
    strs_push(l, "  4,265,696 B, unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Core IR — N39, measured 2026-09-30")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Core IR is a lowering every checked program now passes through (`architecture.md` §7.41), so what")
    strs_push(l, "is measured is what it costs a build and a run, what it changed in what programs do, and what")
    strs_push(l, "the interpreter gained by running it instead of the tree.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Nothing changed in any program.** All 205 `.nz` sources in the tree, under the N38 release")
    strs_push(l, "  build (`git archive 5e7e487`) and the N39 one, host: `nazm check --no-cache` output and status")
    strs_push(l, "  identical for 205; `nazm run` stdout, stderr, `NAZM_MEMORY_REPORT` line and status identical for")
    strs_push(l, "  205 (95 exit 0, the rest their documented diagnostics); `nazm build --no-cache --emit-ir`")
    strs_push(l, "  identical output for all 205, and **every one of the 383 LLVM IR files the 104 buildable ones")
    strs_push(l, "  emit byte-identical**. The native backend now lowers Core IR and produces the same text,")
    strs_push(l, "  hidden slots and all.")
    strs_push(l, "- **What each phase costs**, release, host, median of 15")
    strs_push(l, "  (`what_each_phase_costs_on_the_compiler`, `crates/nazm-cli/tests/core_ir.rs`), cumulative:")
    strs_push(l, "  `compiler/emit.nz` parse 16.7 ms, checking +15.9, **to Core IR +5.6** (verifying it 0.4 of that),")
    strs_push(l, "  to LIR +4.1, to LLVM text +29.9 — 72.1 ms; `compiler/check.nz` parse 9.3, checking +8.6, to")
    strs_push(l, "  Core IR +2.6; a 3,001-function chain parse 14.0, checking +12.2, to Core IR +3.4, to LIR +4.0,")
    strs_push(l, "  to LLVM text +20.4.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Whole commands, N38 against N39**, release, host: `nazm check --no-cache compiler/emit.nz`")
    strs_push(l, "  57.3 and 57.5 ms, `compiler/check.nz` 34.6 and 34.5 (median of 25) — checking builds no Core")
    strs_push(l, "  IR; `nazm build --no-cache compiler/emit.nz` 947 and 958 ms (+1.1 %, median of 7, clang")
    strs_push(l, "  dominating); `examples/primes.nz` 137.6 and 136.3 ms.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The interpreter got faster**, because it no longer searches frames for a name or asks the")
    strs_push(l, "  resolution at every call and field (median of 7): `bench/programs/calls.nz` 897.6 → 430.9 ms")
    strs_push(l, "  (−52 %), `sieve.nz` 424.4 → 245.0 (−42 %), `sequences.nz` 330.9 → 199.1 (−40 %), `strings.nz`")
    strs_push(l, "  25.8 → 19.7 (−24 %), `arith.nz` 733.6 → 615.0 (−16 %), `channels.nz` 271.8 → 256.7 (−6 %),")
    strs_push(l, "  `floor.nz` 4.5 → 4.4.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Memory.** Peak RSS, host, median of 5, N38 and N39: `nazm check compiler/emit.nz` 29.3 and")
    strs_push(l, "  29.2 MB; `nazm build compiler/emit.nz` 64.0 and 63.5; `nazm run` of the 3,001-function chain")
    strs_push(l, "  51.2 and 50.5; `nazm build` of it 68.2 and 68.2; `nazm run` of a 2,000-binding function 37.1 and")
    strs_push(l, "  38.6. The tree is dropped as soon as Core IR exists, in both `nazm run` and `nazm build`, and the")
    strs_push(l, "  interpreter no longer clones the tree and the resolution into itself; what a run keeps is Core")
    strs_push(l, "  IR alone.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Scale.** Lowering is linear in functions and in one function's size")
    strs_push(l, "  (`crates/nazm-core/tests/core_ir.rs`, a 3,000-function program and a 1,000-binding function")
    strs_push(l, "  against a quarter of each). Checking is not linear in the number of bindings one function has:")
    strs_push(l, "  `nazm check` of a function with 1,000, 2,000 and 4,000 bindings takes 0.05, 0.19 and 0.69 s under")
    strs_push(l, "  N38 and N39 alike — a cost of the checker's own, found by N39's stress test and not addressed by")
    strs_push(l, "  it.")
    strs_push(l, "- **In the container the interpreter's gain does not hold everywhere.** The compiler benchmark's")
    strs_push(l, "  interpreted rows, against N38's own gate run, Linux, 1 CPU: `calls` 1,672 → 1,467 ms (−12 %),")
    strs_push(l, "  `strings` 48.6 → 48.7, `sieve` 948 → 999 (+5 %), `sequences` 723 → 770 (+6.5 %), `arith` 2,495")
    strs_push(l, "  → 2,748 (+10 %). Those rows had held within about 2 % from N33 to N38, so the slowdown is real on")
    strs_push(l, "  that platform while the same programs run 16–52 % faster on the host. Why is not established: the")
    strs_push(l, "  interpreter's work per step fell on paper (a slot index for a name search, no frame per region),")
    strs_push(l, "  and a profile on Linux is what would say. No optimisation was attempted — N39 adds no optimiser.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The compiler benchmark otherwise** moved within a few per cent of N38's run: `compiler/check`")
    strs_push(l, "  98.2 → 93.0 ms, `compiler/build-O0` 1,779 → 1,847 (+3.9 %), every program's `-O0` and `-O2`")
    strs_push(l, "  build within −4 % to +3.5 %. The 21 drifts it reports are the same pre-N33 baseline ones.")
    strs_push(l, "- **In the container**, the phase benchmark (`what_each_phase_costs_on_the_compiler`, release,")
    strs_push(l, "  median of 15): `compiler/emit.nz` parse 29.0 ms, checking +20.5, to Core IR +9.3 (verifying 0.4),")
    strs_push(l, "  to LIR +7.5, to LLVM text +36.6 — 102.8 ms; the 3,001-function chain 84.1 ms, of which Core IR 7.4.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Size.** Linux release, contained: `nazm` 4,723,616 → 4,854,688 B (+131,072, +2.8 %); `nazm-mcp`")
    strs_push(l, "  4,265,696 B, unchanged, since the server does not reach the lowering.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The planner and servers**, contained: `repo --map` 391–411 ms, the four task contexts 52–635 ms,")
    strs_push(l, "  1,000 MCP task contexts 115.5 ms each, the docs index 26.1 ms — within N38's. The MCP memory law")
    strs_push(l, "  saw one allocator step during warm-up and a flat measured window (112,012–112,168 kB), `Flat`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The gate**, offline, at `ab0a761`: mutation 13,876 s over six sessions (37 of 37 caught — 23 at")
    strs_push(l, "tier 1 with killers verified, 13 at tier 2, 1 at tier 3; 34 at `ab0a761` and the three entries")
    strs_push(l, "repaired after it at `eb80464`; `capability-matrix.md` area 30), workspace 478 s (1,903 passed, 0")
    strs_push(l, "failed, 25 ignored, 121 suites; `memory.peak` again read its 4 GiB limit with no OOM kill), lifecycle")
    strs_push(l, "186 s (19 of 19 — selected in full, since the harness's rules and catalogue changed), selfhost 61 s")
    strs_push(l, "(38 of 38), bootstrap 39 s (C2 = C3, IR identical, executables identical once the linker UUID is")
    strs_push(l, "removed), release benchmarks 960 s, compiler benchmark 212 s, checks 8 s (19 of 19, the new *core")
    strs_push(l, "ir boundary* among them) — every stage passed, with no network (`NETWORK-ABSENT`). After the gate,")
    strs_push(l, "`eb80464` changed one test's recursion depth, from 1,000 to 200 (area 30); that binary passes 116 of")
    strs_push(l, "116 on the host.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Provenance — N38, measured 2026-09-30")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Provenance is a checker fact and a whole-program solve over kept facts (`architecture.md` §7.40),")
    strs_push(l, "so what is measured is what it costs the compiler, what it leaves in programs, and what it did to")
    strs_push(l, "the servers that analyse the repository.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Nothing in the program.** `nazm build --emit-ir -O0` under the N37 and N38 release builds gives")
    strs_push(l, "  byte-identical IR for `examples/capabilities/workers.nz` and `ledger.nz`, `examples/effects/tasks.nz`,")
    strs_push(l, "  `examples/provenance/tally.nz`, `examples/primes.nz`, `examples/pipeline.nz` and `compiler/emit.nz`")
    strs_push(l, "  (host, built and not run). `nazm-lir` reads no provenance.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Compatibility.** All 203 `.nz` sources at N37's HEAD (`git archive 6577c14`) give byte-identical")
    strs_push(l, "  `nazm check --no-cache` output and exit status under the N37 and N38 release builds: none is newly")
    strs_push(l, "  refused, since no existing function with a declared effect set writes to a file-derived path.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Checking time.** Release, host, median of 25: `compiler/emit.nz` 51.3 ms under N37 and 56.6 ms")
    strs_push(l, "  under N38 (+10 %); `compiler/check.nz` 31.7 and 34.7 ms. Of the added time on `emit.nz`, reducing")
    strs_push(l, "  bodies to facts is about 5 ms and the solve about 1.5 ms. Two optimisations came before the gate: a")
    strs_push(l, "  join that reports whether it grew, rather than a clone compared after, and re-walking a body only")
    strs_push(l, "  when a binding grew after it was read — 261 of `emit.nz`'s 432 functions had needed a second,")
    strs_push(l, "  confirming walk. In the container the compiler benchmark's `compiler/check` is 98.2 ms, against")
    strs_push(l, "  N37's 80.6 (+22 %).")
    strs_push(l, "- **Memory.** Peak RSS of `nazm check compiler/emit.nz`, host, median of 7: 29.0 MB under N37, 29.6 MB")
    strs_push(l, "  under N38.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Size.** Linux release, contained: `nazm` 4,592,544 → 4,723,616 B (+131,072, +2.85 %); `nazm-mcp`")
    strs_push(l, "  4,134,624 → 4,265,696 B (+131,072). Host (macOS) `nazm`: 4,782,752 B.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The large graph.** A 2,000-function chain passing the command line through, and a 500-function")
    strs_push(l, "  cycle one of whose members reads a file, check in one debug test well under its 60 s bound — the")
    strs_push(l, "  whole provenance suite is 1.3 s in debug. Before the worklist the same test took 29 s: rounds that")
    strs_push(l, "  moved a summary one call each were quadratic along a chain.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Precision.** A function returning a constant is handed a file's contents and its result is local;")
    strs_push(l, "  a function returning its second parameter carries only that one; a choice made on `file_exists`")
    strs_push(l, "  is local (`crates/nazm-core/tests/provenance.rs`).")
    strs_push(l, "- **The planner and servers**, contained: `repo --map` 407–419 ms (N37 352–363), the four task")
    strs_push(l, "  contexts 59–634 ms (49–567), 1,000 MCP task contexts 113.6 ms each (104.2), the docs index 28.4 ms")
    strs_push(l, "  (25.6) — about 10–15 % slower, since every analysis they request now includes the solve.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The MCP task-context memory check, and why its law changed.** In the gate it failed: RSS read")
    strs_push(l, "  53,240 kB after warm-up and 93,576 kB after 1,000 calls, over its +4 MB allowance. Diagnosis:")
    strs_push(l, "  sampled every 250 calls over 3,000, RSS was flat at 53,252 kB for 750 calls, stepped once to")
    strs_push(l, "  93,416 kB, and stayed flat to the end; with `MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=1` — a diagnostic only, never the")
    strs_push(l, "  benchmark's environment — the same run was flat at 61,308–61,320 kB throughout. The step is glibc")
    strs_push(l, "  giving a worker thread its own arena the first time threads contend, at a moment set by")
    strs_push(l, "  scheduling rather than by how many requests came before: a sequential warm-up of 1,000 requests,")
    strs_push(l, "  flat throughout, was followed by the step inside the measured window. Concurrent warm-up")
    strs_push(l, "  absorbed it, but reached 174–321 MB of retained memory a leak could hide in, and was not used.")
    strs_push(l, "  **The law now** (`crates/nazm-mcp/tests/protocol.rs`, `growth`): after a sequential warm-up,")
    strs_push(l, "  bounded at 3,000 requests and ended once five consecutive samples 250 requests apart lie within")
    strs_push(l, "  4 MB, the 1,000-request window is sampled every 250 requests. It passes if every sample is within")
    strs_push(l, "  +4 MB of the baseline, or if there is exactly one adjacent increase over +4 MB with every sample")
    strs_push(l, "  before it within +4 MB of the baseline and at least one after it, all within +4 MB of the first")
    strs_push(l, "  post-step sample. Two steps, growth past the bound before or after one, and a step at the last")
    strs_push(l, "  sample, with no plateau seen, fail — synthetic sequences in its unit test cover each.")
    strs_push(l, "  Confirmation, 3,000 sequential requests, normal allocator: 72,904 kB at every one of 13 samples")
    strs_push(l, "  (the step came before the first), peak 74,872 kB. The release-benchmark stage, run again alone:")
    strs_push(l, "  warm-up 1,000 requests at 53,128 kB, measured window 53,128 kB at all five samples, `Flat`, peak")
    strs_push(l, "  72,760 kB — **passed**.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The gate**, offline, at `2861d31`: mutation 5,848 s (34 of 34 caught: 32 at tier 1 with killers")
    strs_push(l, "verified, one killerless entry at tier 2 and one at tier 3, over two sessions and three resumes that")
    strs_push(l, "found nothing left), workspace 416 s (1,869 passed, 0 failed, 23 ignored, 117 suites; the container's")
    strs_push(l, "`memory.peak` again read its 4 GiB limit with no OOM kill), lifecycle 185 s (19 of 19), selfhost 57 s")
    strs_push(l, "(38 of 38), bootstrap 37 s (C2 = C3, IR identical, executables identical once the linker UUID is")
    strs_push(l, "removed), release benchmarks 460 s (failed at the MCP memory check above; after its law changed, run")
    strs_push(l, "again alone at `e6e9454` and passed in 327 s), compiler benchmark 197")
    strs_push(l, "s (the same 21 pre-N33 drifts), checks 17 s (18 of 18) — 7,217 s of wall time, one run, no network")
    strs_push(l, "(`NETWORK-ABSENT`). The compiler benchmark's harness counted one `nazm-` container at its end; none")
    strs_push(l, "remained afterwards, and which it was is not established.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Capabilities — N37, measured 2026-09-30")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Authority is checked statically and a capability erases (`architecture.md` §7.39), so what is")
    strs_push(l, "measured is what the check costs the compiler and what a capability leaves in the program.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Next to nothing in the program.** A function taking an `IoCap` lowers to exactly the IR of the")
    strs_push(l, "  same function taking an `Int` (`crates/nazm-cli/tests/capabilities.rs`); `main` receives one")
    strs_push(l, "  `i64 0` per root from the entry wrapper. `examples/capabilities/workers.nz` and its twin with")
    strs_push(l, "  `Int` in place of every capability build to executables of the same size at `-O2` (52,104 B,")
    strs_push(l, "  host); the `-O2` IR differs by 254 B, `main`'s two parameters and the entry's call.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Compatibility.** The 200 `.nz` sources at N36's HEAD (`git archive 9deed77`) were checked with")
    strs_push(l, "  the N36 and N37 release builds (host, `--no-cache`): 197 give byte-identical output and exit")
    strs_push(l, "  status; the three that differ are `examples/effects/pure.nz`, `report.nz` and `tasks.nz`, which")
    strs_push(l, "  declared effects and exercised them with no capability, and were migrated. The N36 build used is")
    strs_push(l, "  the one built from its sources before its last commits, none of which touched `crates/*/src`.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Census** over the tree's roots: 1,054 function checks, 20 declaring a set, 11 holding a")
    strs_push(l, "  capability; the inferred sets are N36's plus the new examples (870 `{}`, 27 `{ io }`, 3")
    strs_push(l, "  `{ spawn }`, 154 `{ io, spawn }`).")
    strs_push(l, "- **Checking time.** `nazm check --no-cache`, release, host, median of 25: `compiler/emit.nz`")
    strs_push(l, "  52.4–52.9 ms under N36 and 52.9–53.0 ms under N37; `compiler/check.nz` 33.0–33.5 and 33.0–33.4")
    strs_push(l, "  ms — the same within noise, since no function there declares a set and the check runs only for")
    strs_push(l, "  those that do. A synthetic 3,001-function chain in which every function declares `! { io }` and")
    strs_push(l, "  threads an `IoCap` checks in 73.3–73.8 ms, against 66.6–67.8 ms for its twin with no sets and an")
    strs_push(l, "  `Int` in place of the capability: about 6.5 ms for 3,001 contracts checked for effects and")
    strs_push(l, "  authority. The compiler benchmark's `compiler/check` is 80.6 ms (N36: 83.0).")
    strs_push(l, "- **Memory.** Peak RSS of `nazm check compiler/emit.nz`, host: 27.9 MB under N36, 27.8 MB under N37.")
    strs_push(l, "  One capability set per call site is recorded.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Size.** Linux release, contained: `nazm` 4,592,544 B and `nazm-mcp` 4,134,624 B, both the same as")
    strs_push(l, "  N36 at the 64 KiB granularity these sizes move in. Host (macOS) `nazm`: 4,631,328 → 4,647,984 B.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The planner and servers**, contained: `repo --map` 352–363 ms, the four task contexts 49–567 ms,")
    strs_push(l, "  1,000 MCP task contexts 104.2 ms each, RSS settled 72,268 kB; the docs index 25.6 ms (frame")
    strs_push(l, "  237,983 B). Within N36's range.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The gate**, offline, at `0c94d74`: mutation 4,395 s (33 of 33 caught, 32 at tier 1 with killers")
    strs_push(l, "verified and 1 at tier 2, over two sessions and three resumes that found nothing left), workspace")
    strs_push(l, "392 s (1,846 passed, 0 failed, 23 ignored, 115 suites), lifecycle 185 s (19 of 19), selfhost 53 s")
    strs_push(l, "(38 of 38), bootstrap 37 s (C2 = C3, IR identical, executables identical once the linker UUID is")
    strs_push(l, "removed), release benchmarks 463 s, compiler benchmark 195 s (the same 21 pre-N33 drifts), checks")
    strs_push(l, "17 s (18 of 18) — 5,737 s of wall time, one run. The container had no network (`NETWORK-ABSENT`).")
    strs_push(l, "The workspace container's `memory.peak` read 4,294,967,296 B — its limit — with no OOM kill; that")
    strs_push(l, "counter includes page cache, and N36's read 1.96 GB. Why it was higher this time was not")
    strs_push(l, "established. After the gate, the tier-2 mutant's declared killer was strengthened and the mutant")
    strs_push(l, "verified alone at tier 1 (164 s, one test file changed).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Typed effects — N36, measured 2026-09-30")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Effects are a checker fact (`architecture.md` §7.38), so what is measured is what they cost the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler and what they leave in the program.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Nothing in the program.** A program with every function's effects declared and the same")
    strs_push(l, "  program without them emit byte-identical IR at `-O0`, one module and two")
    strs_push(l, "  (`crates/nazm-cli/tests/effects.rs`), with each body at the same line and column in both — a")
    strs_push(l, "  runtime error message carries its position, and an annotation on a body's own line moves it.")
    strs_push(l, "  The interpreter never reads a set.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Compatibility.** Every one of the 116 `.nz` sources the tree had before N36 — the compiler,")
    strs_push(l, "  the conformance corpus, `examples/` including `examples/bad/`, `corpus/`, `bench/programs/` —")
    strs_push(l, "  gives byte-identical `nazm check` output and exit status under the N35 and the N36 release")
    strs_push(l, "  builds (host, `--no-cache`). None needed a change; none declares a set.")
    strs_push(l, "- **What the checker infers** over the tree's 34 compilation roots (1,044 function checks, 11")
    strs_push(l, "  declared, all in `examples/effects/`): 867 `{}`, 22 `{ io }`, 3 `{ spawn }`, 152 `{ io, spawn }`")
    strs_push(l, "  — the last almost all in the multi-module compiler sources, whose calls to undeclared imports")
    strs_push(l, "  must assume every effect (`crates/nazm-service/tests/effects.rs`, the ignored census).")
    strs_push(l, "- **Checking time.** `nazm check --no-cache`, release, host, median of eight after a warm-up:")
    strs_push(l, "  `compiler/emit.nz` 52.9 ms under N35 and 51.9 ms under N36; `compiler/check.nz` 33.9 and 31.5 ms")
    strs_push(l, "  — the same within noise. In the container, `analyse` of `compiler/emit.nz` (432 functions)")
    strs_push(l, "  takes 40.6 ms in all, effects included. The compiler benchmark's `compiler/check` is 83.0 ms")
    strs_push(l, "  against N35's 81.1, inside the drift every measurement shows (below). The synthetic graph — a")
    strs_push(l, "  2,000-long chain, a 300-wide fan-out and a 500-long cycle in one module — settles in one test")
    strs_push(l, "  in debug, well under its 60 s bound.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Memory.** Peak RSS of `nazm check compiler/emit.nz`, host: 27.4 MB under N35, 28.7 MB under")
    strs_push(l, "  N36 (+4.5 %): one reason per effect per function, and the declared and inferred sets, are kept;")
    strs_push(l, "  no provenance graph is.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Size.** `nazm` 4,527,008 B at N35, 4,592,544 B at N36 (+65,536, +1.45 %); `nazm-mcp`")
    strs_push(l, "  4,134,624 B, unchanged. Linux release, contained.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The planner and servers** over this repository, contained, against N33's run of the same")
    strs_push(l, "  harness: `repo --map` 360–367 ms (350–356), the four task contexts 50–594 ms (46–579), 1,000 MCP")
    strs_push(l, "  task contexts 107.0 ms each (100.5), RSS settled 73,256 kB (73,224); the docs index 24.7 ms")
    strs_push(l, "  (23.1). A few per cent slower over a corpus that has grown since (the docs index frame is")
    strs_push(l, "  234,410 B, was 228,934), and nothing on those paths reads an effect beyond the one set a packet")
    strs_push(l, "  carries.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The gate**, offline, at `973ae9f`: mutation 5,862 s (85 of 85 caught: 78 at tier 1 with killers")
    strs_push(l, "verified, 7 at tier 2), workspace 360 s (1,825 passed, 0 failed, 23 ignored, 111 suites, peak")
    strs_push(l, "1.96 GB), lifecycle 185 s (19 of 19), selfhost 47 s (38 of 38), bootstrap 38 s (C2 = C3, IR")
    strs_push(l, "identical, executables identical once the linker UUID is removed), release benchmarks 537 s (run")
    strs_push(l, "again on its own: the gate script's form of the stage used a `bash`-only `time ( … )` that the")
    strs_push(l, "container's `sh` refused before anything ran), compiler benchmark 200 s (the same 21 pre-N33 drifts")
    strs_push(l, "as N34's and N35's, each within about 2 % of them), checks 12 s (18 of 18) — 7,242 s of wall time.")
    strs_push(l, "Two earlier runs of the gate were not evidence: the first stopped at its disk guard before the")
    strs_push(l, "lifecycle with four failures of new tests in the workspace, the second with two; each was fixed and")
    strs_push(l, "the gate run again whole. The container had no network (`NETWORK-ABSENT`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Agent task tokens, cost and correctness — N35, measured 2026-09-29")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-agent-bench` (N35, `architecture.md` §7.37). **One model configuration, recorded here and")
    strs_push(l, "nowhere generalised:** Anthropic's `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001`, reached through the Claude Code")
    strs_push(l, "client in print mode (`claude --print`, client 2.1.283) on this session's own sign-in — one turn,")
    strs_push(l, "no tools, no MCP server, no setting source, no thinking (`MAX_THINKING_TOKENS=0`), at most 1,024")
    strs_push(l, "output tokens, the benchmark's system text in place of the client's. **The client sets no")
    strs_push(l, "temperature, so the model's default applies**; this is the benchmark's largest limitation. The")
    strs_push(l, "direct OpenAI and Anthropic adapters exist, are tested against recorded responses, and were not")
    strs_push(l, "run: no API key was supplied, and a developer who wants them brings their own")
    strs_push(l, "(`runbook.md`, *The agent task benchmark*).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Frozen before the run, at `c130f72`: suite `b7db4ccc…` (`nazm.agent-bench-suite/1`, eight tasks,")
    strs_push(l, "116 required facts over two trials), prompt `nazm.agent-bench-prompt/1` (template `de954887…`),")
    strs_push(l, "benchmark `ce659979f4f695b8`, two trials per task and arm, the arms alternating in order by")
    strs_push(l, "trial, every request independent. The price list is `tools/agent-bench/pricing.toml`, read")
    strs_push(l, "2026-09-29 from the provider's pricing page: $1 per million input tokens, $0.10 cache reads, $2")
    strs_push(l, "one-hour cache writes, $5 output. The client's own list-price cost of every one of the 34 paid")
    strs_push(l, "requests (the pilot's and the run's) equals the benchmark's to the micro-dollar.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Per task** (medians over two trials; *solved* is every fact correct and no false claim;")
    strs_push(l, "*lenient* reads an answer that was prose around a JSON block by that block, and is never the")
    strs_push(l, "verdict; cost is the sum of both trials):")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Task | Solved, base / N33 | Lenient | Facts, base / N33 | False claims, base / N33 | Input tokens, base → N33 | Output, base / N33 | Cost billed, base → N33 | Cost uncached, base → N33 | Verdict |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| T1 understand `check_program` | 1/2 / 2/2 | 1/2 / 2/2 | 35/36 / 36/36 | 1 / 0 | 111,398 → 7,791 | 329 / 328 | $0.4489 → $0.0344 | $0.2261 → $0.0189 | N33 better |")
    strs_push(l, "| T2 `attach_core`'s dependencies and callers | 0/2 / 0/2 | 0/2 / 0/2 | 0/8 / 8/8 | 0 / 32 | 111,471 → 3,360 | 676 / 293 | $0.4526 → $0.0097 | $0.2297 → $0.0097 | baseline better |")
    strs_push(l, "| T3 edit plan for `attach_core` | 0/2 / 2/2 | 0/2 / 2/2 | 10/12 / 12/12 | 3 / 0 | 111,568 → 3,454 | 158 / 152 | $0.4478 → $0.0084 | $0.2247 → $0.0084 | N33 better |")
    strs_push(l, "| T4 diagnose N0300 (stress case) | 2/2 / 2/2 | 2/2 / 2/2 | 6/6 / 6/6 | 0 / 0 | 744 → 1,367 | 72 / 72 | $0.0022 → $0.0035 | $0.0022 → $0.0035 | baseline better |")
    strs_push(l, "| T5 specification: `return` | 1/2 / 2/2 | 1/2 / 2/2 | 11/12 / 12/12 | 0 / 0 | 37,914 → 1,916 | 122 / 102 | $0.1529 → $0.0049 | $0.0771 → $0.0049 | N33 better |")
    strs_push(l, "| T6 grammar: `record` | 2/2 / 2/2 | 2/2 / 2/2 | 12/12 / 12/12 | 0 / 0 | 18,987 → 1,699 | 106 / 100 | $0.0770 → $0.0044 | $0.0390 → $0.0044 | N33 better |")
    strs_push(l, "| T7 tests of `nazm-docs` | 0/2 / 0/2 | 0/2 / 0/2 | 21/26 / 22/26 | 0 / 0 | 16,090 → 2,486 | 823 / 324 | $0.0529 → $0.0082 | $0.0404 → $0.0082 | N33 better |")
    strs_push(l, "| T8 tests of `core_module` | 0/2 / 2/2 | 2/2 / 2/2 | 2/2 / 2/2 | 0 / 0 | 6,720 → 1,310 | 752 / 90 | $0.0344 → $0.0035 | $0.0210 → $0.0035 | N33 better |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**By category and in all** (input and cost over both trials):")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Group | Correctness preserved | Solved, base / N33 | Facts, base / N33 | Input reduction | Total-token reduction | Cost reduction, billed | Cost reduction, uncached | Context-only reduction (o200k) |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| understand (T1, T2) | 1/2 | 1/4 / 2/4 | 35/44 / 44/44 | 95.00 % | 94.74 % | 95.11 % | 93.74 % | 95.40 % |")
    strs_push(l, "| edit (T3) | 1/1 | 0/2 / 2/2 | 10/12 / 12/12 | 96.90 % | 96.77 % | 98.12 % | 96.25 % | 97.46 % |")
    strs_push(l, "| diagnose (T4) | 1/1 | 2/2 / 2/2 | 6/6 / 6/6 | −83.68 % | −76.30 % | −56.41 % | −56.41 % | −960.38 % |")
    strs_push(l, "| docs (T5, T6) | 2/2 | 3/4 / 4/4 | 23/24 / 24/24 | 93.65 % | 93.32 % | 95.98 % | 92.03 % | 96.18 % |")
    strs_push(l, "| tests (T7, T8) | 2/2 | 0/4 / 2/4 | 21/30 / 26/30 | 83.35 % | 82.73 % | 86.56 % | 80.88 % | 83.20 % |")
    strs_push(l, "| **all eight** | **7/8** | **6/16 / 12/16** | **95/116 / 112/116** | **94.36 %** | **94.05 %** | **95.39 %** | **92.86 %** | **95.43 %** |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Correctness first.** The N33 context solved 12 of 16 requests and the baseline 6; N33 got")
    strs_push(l, "  112 of 116 facts, the baseline 95. Neither arm hallucinated a repository fact. The baseline's")
    strs_push(l, "  four false claims were misreadings (`parse.nz::build_children`, `emit.nz::emit_program`, and a")
    strs_push(l, "  package given as a test target); four of its answers broke the JSON-only contract by reasoning")
    strs_push(l, "  in prose first — two of them (T8) correct when read leniently.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The one correctness regression is T2, by the pre-declared rule.** The N33 arm named all")
    strs_push(l, "  eight facts in both trials, and also listed sixteen of the language's builtins")
    strs_push(l, "  (`ints_push`, `str_concat`, …) as `module.nz` definitions that `attach_core` depends on: 32")
    strs_push(l, "  false claims, each a name the context does show being called. The baseline produced no valid")
    strs_push(l, "  answer in either trial. The rule (solved, then facts minus false claims) scores that as")
    strs_push(l, "  baseline better; it is reported as the rule says, not special-cased.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Tokens and cost.** Across all sixteen pairs the N33 arm used 46,772 input tokens to the")
    strs_push(l, "  baseline's 829,789 (−94.36 %), 49,694 total to 835,867 (−94.05 %), and cost $0.0770 to $1.6687")
    strs_push(l, "  as billed (−95.39 %) or $0.0614 to $0.8602 with every input token at the uncached rate")
    strs_push(l, "  (−92.86 %). The client wrote a one-hour cache for every prompt of 4,096 tokens or more and")
    strs_push(l, "  read one back once in 32 requests, so its bill charges large prompts about twice the uncached")
    strs_push(l, "  rate; the uncached figure is the comparison no caching choice can tilt. Output was 2,922 tokens")
    strs_push(l, "  to 6,078: the smaller context did not buy its saving with longer answers.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Efficiency.** Tokens per solved task: 139,311 baseline, 4,141 N33. Cost per solved task:")
    strs_push(l, "  $0.2781 and $0.0064. Correct facts per thousand input tokens: 0.11 and 2.39; per dollar billed,")
    strs_push(l, "  56.93 and 1,455.32.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Scenario C and the crossover.** On the 123-byte program both arms solved both trials; the")
    strs_push(l, "  structured context cost 1,367 input tokens to the raw source's 744 (+84 %, $0.0035 to $0.0022).")
    strs_push(l, "  The client's own framing is about 430 tokens of every request, and the benchmark's fixed prompt")
    strs_push(l, "  233–346 more (o200k); both are the same in both arms. The N33 context was the cheaper input")
    strs_push(l, "  on every other task, the smallest of which had a 6,720-token baseline: for this model and suite")
    strs_push(l, "  the crossover lies between 744 and 6,720 input tokens. That is an observation, not a routing")
    strs_push(l, "  rule; nothing routes on it.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Local counts.** Haiku's input was 1.08–1.26× the local `o200k_base` count of the same text")
    strs_push(l, "  once the client's ~430 framing tokens are set aside (1.01× on the 53-token program): no N34")
    strs_push(l, "  tokenizer is Anthropic's, and none is claimed to be.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Latency** (a reply's own; no request was retried): baseline median 5,879 ms, 3,240–14,038;")
    strs_push(l, "  N33 median 3,857 ms, 3,153–5,553. One baseline answer (T7, trial 2) reached the output limit")
    strs_push(l, "  and the client continued it in a second call, which the record keeps.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Spend: the authoritative run $1.745696, the two pilots $0.016399 and $0.021533 — $1.783628 of the")
    strs_push(l, "$2 cap, which every attempt was checked against before it was sent. The pilots are not evidence:")
    strs_push(l, "the first found that the worst case priced input as uncached though a cache write costs more, and")
    strs_push(l, "that the client's own spend limit, set from that worst case, withheld one answer, which had been")
    strs_push(l, "scored as the model's; both were fixed and the pilot re-run before the suite was frozen. The")
    strs_push(l, "structured report is `tools/agent-bench/results/n35-v1-claude-code-haiku-4-5.json`; the journal")
    strs_push(l, "and raw replies stay in the local, ignored evidence directory.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The gate**, offline after the paid run, at `0419b25`, contained on the M1 Pro: mutation 1,508 s")
    strs_push(l, "(16 of 16 caught, 16 killers verified), workspace 393 s (1,795 passed, 0 failed, 22 ignored, 108")
    strs_push(l, "suites, peak 3.6 GB), lifecycle 185 s (19 of 19), selfhost 57 s (38 of 38), bootstrap 38 s (C2 = C3,")
    strs_push(l, "IR identical), release benchmarks 596 s, compiler benchmark 198 s (the same 21 pre-N33 drifts as")
    strs_push(l, "N34's, each within 1 % of it), checks 2 s (18 of 18) — 2,977 s of wall time. The container had no")
    strs_push(l, "network (`NETWORK-ABSENT`); the agent benchmark's 21 tests passed there on the fake provider and")
    strs_push(l, "recorded responses. `nazm` is 4,527,008 bytes and `nazm-mcp` 4,134,624, both the same as at N34;")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-agent-bench` is 11,343,120 and ships in neither.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What this does not show.** One model, one client, two trials, the model's default")
    strs_push(l, "temperature; the ranges above are what two samples show, not confidence intervals, and no")
    strs_push(l, "significance is claimed. Eight tasks over one repository. At the recorded prices.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Context under four tokenizers — N34, measured 2026-09-29")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-tokens` (N34, `architecture.md` §7.36), contained at P1 on the M1 Pro with **no network in")
    strs_push(l, "the container**, release builds, at `ab499fa`. Four pinned tokenizers of three families:")
    strs_push(l, "`openai-bpe/cl100k_base` and `openai-bpe/o200k_base` (one family), `sentencepiece-bpe/mistral-7b-v0.1`")
    strs_push(l, "and `sentencepiece-unigram/t5-small`. Content tokens only — no template framing, no chat protocol.")
    strs_push(l, "Every count is the library's own encoding of the exact bytes; the golden fixtures hold every")
    strs_push(l, "tokenizer to an independent implementation's ids.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The seven N33 tasks, baselines unchanged** (one definition, `crates/nazm-repo/tests/scenarios/`,")
    strs_push(l, "used by both benchmarks), naive → N33 tokens and reduction; every N33 mechanical check passes in the")
    strs_push(l, "same run:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Task | Naive → N33 bytes | cl100k_base | o200k_base | Mistral 7B v0.1 | T5-small | Spread |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| A understand `check_program` | 356,043 → 20,059 (94.37 %) | 89,446 → 6,031 (93.26 %) | 89,260 → 5,936 (93.35 %) | 112,475 → 7,248 (93.56 %) | 121,458 → 9,872 (91.87 %) | 1.69 pts |")
    strs_push(l, "| B edit `attach_core` | 348,233 → 7,844 (97.75 %) | 88,399 → 2,232 (97.48 %) | 88,337 → 2,245 (97.46 %) | 111,444 → 2,836 (97.46 %) | 124,660 → 3,660 (97.06 %) | 0.42 pts |")
    strs_push(l, "| D understand `spec:returns` | 142,128 → 3,769 (97.35 %) | 34,334 → 1,054 (96.93 %) | 34,338 → 1,060 (96.91 %) | 38,782 → 1,256 (96.76 %) | 41,388 → 1,523 (96.32 %) | 0.61 pts |")
    strs_push(l, "| D understand guide `record` | 53,386 → 2,768 (94.82 %) | 15,812 → 846 (94.65 %) | 15,857 → 854 (94.61 %) | 18,488 → 1,060 (94.27 %) | 22,383 → 1,329 (94.06 %) | 0.59 pts |")
    strs_push(l, "| E tests of `nazm-docs` | 26,649 → 5,577 (79.07 %) | 7,327 → 1,541 (78.97 %) | 7,306 → 1,577 (78.42 %) | 9,605 → 2,081 (78.33 %) | 10,530 → 2,873 (72.72 %) | 6.25 pts |")
    strs_push(l, "| E tests of `core_module` | 18,223 → 1,911 (89.51 %) | 4,824 → 535 (88.91 %) | 4,788 → 545 (88.62 %) | 6,023 → 721 (88.03 %) | 6,449 → 983 (84.76 %) | 4.15 pts |")
    strs_push(l, "| **C diagnose `N0300` — the fixed-overhead stress case** | 123 → 1,925 (−1,465 %) | 40 → 563 (−1,308 %) | 40 → 565 (−1,313 %) | 50 → 782 (−1,464 %) | 51 → 1,007 (−1,875 %) | 567 pts |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Excluding only the stress case: median reduction **93.95 %** (cl100k), **93.98 %** (o200k),")
    strs_push(l, "**93.91 %** (Mistral), **92.96 %** (T5); every tokenizer's worst task is the `nazm-docs` tests")
    strs_push(l, "(72.72–78.97 %) and its best the `attach_core` edit (97.06–97.48 %); **median spread 1.15 points,")
    strs_push(l, "largest 6.25**. The benefit is not one tokenizer's: the smallest reduction under any tokenizer is")
    strs_push(l, "72.72 %, and the ranking of tasks is the same under all four. T5 is consistently the lowest, because")
    strs_push(l, "its vocabulary has no piece for `{`, `}` and several other characters JSON is made of — its")
    strs_push(l, "repository-map count carries 2,188 unknown pieces — which is a property of the tokenizer, not of the")
    strs_push(l, "context. A task context's exact token count also moves with its `state` digest, which is in the")
    strs_push(l, "text: two builds of the same tree at different commits differ by a few tokens.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Where the stress case's tokens go** (cl100k / o200k / Mistral / T5): the whole context 563 / 565")
    strs_push(l, "/ 782 / 1,007; without the three retrieval references 437 / 442 / 599 / 788; without the envelope")
    strs_push(l, "(schema, state, budget, used, empty lists) 437 / 441 / 600 / 794; without reason, class, authority,")
    strs_push(l, "via and compilation 478 / 484 / 663 / 845; the content strings alone (source, message, help) 53 /")
    strs_push(l, "53 / 58 / 65; the naive program 40 / 40 / 50 / 51. The overhead is structural and fixed, about 400–700")
    strs_push(l, "tokens, spread across retrieval, envelope and explanation roughly equally — and every tokenizer")
    strs_push(l, "agrees on that ordering. No compact transport was adopted: each part is what the planner's law")
    strs_push(l, "requires (a way to retrieve the item, the state it is of, and why it is there), and it is constant,")
    strs_push(l, "not proportional to the task.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Source, JSON, Markdown and scripts** (tokens, bytes per token): `compiler/lex.nz` (11,558 B) 3,251")
    strs_push(l, "(3.56) / 3,231 (3.58) / 3,957 (2.92) / 4,564 (2.53, 355 unknown); the repository map (112,735 B)")
    strs_push(l, "29,241 (3.86) / 29,067 (3.88) / 36,608 (3.08) / 59,933 (1.88, 2,188 unknown); `spec:generics` 270 /")
    strs_push(l, "270 / 330 / 345; `architecture:7.35` 2,264 / 2,267 / 2,608 / 2,836. Bangla prose (290 B): **133 /")
    strs_push(l, "37 / 123 / 35** (T5 with 17 unknown); Arabic (149 B): 63 / 30 / 76 / 27 (13 unknown); mixed English,")
    strs_push(l, "Bangla and code (164 B): 64 / 34 / 57 / 42. The families differ most on scripts — `cl100k_base`")
    strs_push(l, "spends 3.6× the tokens of `o200k_base` on the same Bangla — and least on JSON and code, where the")
    strs_push(l, "two OpenAI vocabularies agree within 1 %.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**One byte budget, one selection** (`check_program`, understand, `max_entities` 3, 8, 20): 3, 8 and")
    strs_push(l, "20 items — the planner's, the same whichever tokenizer then counts them — at 10,591, 13,266 and")
    strs_push(l, "20,057 bytes; in tokens 3,114–4,995, 3,950–6,454 and 5,936–9,870, **1.63–1.66× between the")
    strs_push(l, "cheapest and the dearest tokenizer**. A token budget would select differently for each tokenizer;")
    strs_push(l, "the byte and entity budgets select once.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What measuring costs.** Loading the four tokenizers: 256 ms (the OpenAI vocabularies are digested")
    strs_push(l, "rank by rank at load). The stress context (1,925 bytes): 0.37–0.80 ms per tokenizer. Task A's naive")
    strs_push(l, "baseline (356,043 bytes): 17.7 ms (o200k), 26.9 ms (cl100k), 100.2 ms (Mistral), 117.4 ms (T5).")
    strs_push(l, "**1,000 measurements of an N33 context under all four: 4.24 ms each on average, resident memory")
    strs_push(l, "209,392 kB settled and 209,392 kB after** — flat across those calls, in a process that had already")
    strs_push(l, "loaded the tokenizers for earlier tests. `nazm-tokens` is 9,180,488 bytes. **`nazm` is 4,527,008")
    strs_push(l, "bytes, exactly as at N33**; neither it nor `nazm-mcp` (4,134,624) has a tokenizer in its graph.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The MILESTONE gate** (`gate-plan`: full lifecycle — `xtask/`, the root manifest and")
    strs_push(l, "`tools/` changed — the eleven N34 mutations and every benchmark family; no MCP entries, the server")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged), every workload with no network, every cache empty — the lockfile changed, and the")
    strs_push(l, "N33-key caches were cleared first for disk: mutation 835 s, workspace 318 s (1,773 passed across")
    strs_push(l, "104 suites; the first run, 344 s, failed one test — the interface table did not list")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.token-cost/1` — and was re-run after the row was added), lifecycle 185 s, selfhost 58 s,")
    strs_push(l, "bootstrap 39 s, release benchmarks 459 s, compiler benchmark 193 s, checks 3 s: **2,090 s of stages,")
    strs_push(l, "2,436 s (40.6 minutes) of wall time** including the failed run. The compiler benchmark shows the")
    strs_push(l, "same ~2× drift against the 2026-09-21 baseline as at N33, which N33's back-to-back comparison placed")
    strs_push(l, "before N33; `nazm` is unchanged byte for byte. The image was rebuilt once before the gate, with the")
    strs_push(l, "network, to carry the new crates; that was bootstrap, not evidence.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What the counting costs")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Workloads sized so process start is noise. Median of five, `-O2`, Darwin arm64.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Workload | Before | After | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1,000,000 short strings | 31.7 ms | 48.2 ms | **+16.5 ms**, ≈16 ns per string |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1,000,000 slices of one string | 31.9 ms | 45.2 ms | **+13.3 ms**, ≈13 ns per slice |")
    strs_push(l, "| 200,000 strings through a `Strs` | 45.9 ms | 50.3 ms | +4.4 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1,000,000 sequences | 63.5 ms | 64.3 ms | noise |")
    strs_push(l, "| 4,000,000 pushes into one sequence | 46.0 ms | 46.0 ms | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| 50,000 channels | 38.5 ms | 36.9 ms | noise |")
    strs_push(l, "| 200,000 values through one channel | 49.8 ms | 48.6 ms | noise |")
    strs_push(l, "| sieve to 2,000,000 | 47.0 ms | 48.1 ms | noise |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The cost is where the ownership is and nowhere else. A string operation pays an atomic")
    strs_push(l, "adjustment and, for a heap string, a `free`; a sequence pays nothing new; arithmetic and")
    strs_push(l, "indexing pay nothing at all. **13 ns for a slice is the honest price of N8's central")
    strs_push(l, "decision** — a slice retains the buffer it points into, and that is what lets a slice")
    strs_push(l, "outlive the binding of the buffer it was cut from.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Executable size: **+512 bytes** for a program that touches a string, +352 more for one that")
    strs_push(l, "touches a channel, against ~50 KB.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The compiler process, and the programs it emits")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Two different questions, so two measurements. Both inside `nazm-contained:1.98.1`, Linux")
    strs_push(l, "aarch64, so the two columns are comparable with each other and not with the table above.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Before | After |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| the **self-hosted** compiler compiling `emit.nz` — the compiler *process* | 52.61 MiB | **24.86 MiB** |")
    strs_push(l, "| a program that compiler emitted: 80,000 temporary strings | 6.04 MiB | **1.17 MiB** |")
    strs_push(l, "| the **reference** compiler compiling `emit.nz` | 98.82 MiB | 107.61 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The first row is the milestone's own dogfood: the Nazm-written compiler is a string-heavy")
    strs_push(l, "program, so reclaiming strings halves its peak. The second is the question §34 of the")
    strs_push(l, "directive keeps separate from it — what the emitted program costs, which is not the same")
    strs_push(l, "question and does not have the same answer.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The third row went **up 8.9%**, and that is a real cost rather than noise. The reference")
    strs_push(l, "compiler holds the whole LLVM text it is building, the emitted IR now carries retain and")
    strs_push(l, "release calls and the string runtime, and a bigger text is a bigger buffer. It is the price")
    strs_push(l, "of the emitted program's 5× and it is recorded rather than left for a reader to find.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Incremental reparse — N76, measured 2026-10-03")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Hypothesis:** an edit inside one item reparses that item, not the file. **Changed path:**")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm_syntax::Revision::edit` against `Revision::new` and `parse_both` of the same text.")
    strs_push(l, "**Workload:** the three largest compiler sources, one `x` inserted after the first `let ` past the")
    strs_push(l, "middle of the file. **Method:** `cargo test --release -p nazm-syntax --test incremental -- --ignored")
    strs_push(l, "--nocapture measure_full_parse_against_one_edit`, 5 warm-ups discarded, the median of 31; every")
    strs_push(l, "result is checked for being a full or an incremental parse as labelled, and its correctness is")
    strs_push(l, "the convergence suite's, not this run's. Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2, rustc 1.98.1, release profile,")
    strs_push(l, "one thread, same host and process for all three columns.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| File | Bytes | `parse_both` | `Revision::new` | One edit | Relexed | Reparsed tokens | Items kept |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `compiler/emit.nz` | 286,952 | 8.23 ms | 8.11 ms | 1.22 ms | 2 of 58,947 | 618 of 40,284 | 125 of 126 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `compiler/analyse.nz` | 210,347 | 6.66 ms | 6.55 ms | 1.01 ms | 2 of 50,327 | 518 of 32,060 | 158 of 159 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `compiler/parse.nz` | 77,480 | 2.50 ms | 2.45 ms | 0.38 ms | 2 of 19,030 | 290 of 12,152 | 92 of 93 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "About 6.6–6.8× faster than a full parse. The rest is not parsing: 1.5% of the tokens are reparsed,")
    strs_push(l, "and an edit still copies the scan and moves its suffix, which is linear in the file's lexemes. That")
    strs_push(l, "copy is the next cost, and it is not attacked here. No variance beyond the median is recorded, and")
    strs_push(l, "peak memory was not measured. A revision holds the scan, the chunk table and the tree, which is more")
    strs_push(l, "than a parse that drops its scan.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The compiler written in Nazm at parity — N102, measured 2026-10-05")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What changed:** `compiler/*.nz` grew from 12,767 to 16,200 lines (`cat compiler/*.nz | wc -l`).")
    strs_push(l, "**Method:** the debug `nazm` binary on the host (Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2), the tree before N102 (a")
    strs_push(l, "pristine export of `875f459`) against the tree after, `nazm check compiler/emit.nz` with every")
    strs_push(l, "`.nazm` cache removed before each of three runs, and `nazm build --no-cache compiler/emit.nz`;")
    strs_push(l, "`/usr/bin/time -l`, wall time and maximum resident set.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Before | After |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| cold check, wall | 1.05 s | 1.36 s |")
    strs_push(l, "| cold check, peak resident | 50 MB | 75 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "| build, wall | 2.39 s | 2.66 s |")
    strs_push(l, "| build, peak resident | 82 MB | 106 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "About a quarter more source, about 30 % more check time and half again the check's memory: the")
    strs_push(l, "checker's work is the compiler's size, and the new trait and effect tables. A debug binary")
    strs_push(l, "measures the compiler's own cost on a large input, not a release user's; no release or contained")
    strs_push(l, "run was made for this row.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Performance evidence v2 — N92, measured 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Method:** `cargo xtask contained bench --save` at N92's tree: one CPU, 4 GiB, offline, the host")
    strs_push(l, "otherwise idle, five runs after a discarded warm-up; `nazm.bench/2` in `bench/record.json` and")
    strs_push(l, "`bench/baseline-linux-aarch64.json`, which it replaces — the file held a baseline older than N75's,")
    strs_push(l, "from another configuration, and `--check` against it reported twenty-one \"regressions\" that were the")
    strs_push(l, "configuration's. Medians in ms, with N75's from the section below.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| program | check | build `-O0` | build `-O2` | interpret | native `-O2` | executable |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| arith | 2.8 | 90.5 (95.3) | 98.9 (99.7) | 2,718.7 (2,765.2) | 4.6 (4.5) | 71,984 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| calls | 3.0 | 91.3 (93.7) | 99.1 (100.1) | 1,492.2 (1,534.7) | 1.0 (1.0) | 71,984 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| channels | 3.1 | 116.3 (103.0) | 197.8 (150.5) | 1,270.2 (1,335.9) | 1,239.4 (1,331.5) | 77,040 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| floor | 2.9 | 89.3 (90.4) | 94.3 (99.2) | 2.3 (2.5) | 0.3 (0.3) | 71,936 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| sequences | 3.0 | 91.2 (93.5) | 115.2 (115.6) | 765.0 (771.1) | 2.3 (2.7) | 72,896 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| sieve | 3.1 | 90.8 (95.1) | 119.0 (117.5) | 1,009.9 (1,013.2) | 3.4 (2.9) | 72,888 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| strings | 3.1 | 93.3 (94.3) | 124.6 (129.0) | 49.5 (48.9) | 7.1 (7.4) | 73,376 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| compiler | **165.6 (107.4)** | 2,030.2 (1,939.6) | | | | |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The noise floor (the empty program, natively) is 0.3 ms; the median absolute deviation is under 1.5")
    strs_push(l, "ms everywhere but the two `channels` runs (51 and 32 ms), whose spread N75 also recorded. The sieve's")
    strs_push(l, "references: C (`-O2`, unchecked) 2.5 ms, **Rust (`-O`, overflow- and bounds-checked) 2.6 ms**, Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "3.4 ms; Python and Go are not in the image, and the record says so.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Two regressions since N75, stated and not hidden.** `nazm check compiler/emit.nz` is 54 % slower")
    strs_push(l, "(107.4 → 165.6 ms), and `channels` builds 13 % (`-O0`) and 31 % (`-O2`) slower. Located for the")
    strs_push(l, "first by release builds of each milestone's records commit on the host (Apple M1 Pro, eleven runs,")
    strs_push(l, "median, the same `compiler/` for all): N75 54.0 ms, N76 63.9, N77 67.3, N78 68.8, N79 67.5, N80")
    strs_push(l, "75.2, N92 76.0 — the steps are N76 (the lossless tree beneath every parse) and N80 (provenance v3),")
    strs_push(l, "each of which `performance.md` measured on its own files at the time; nothing since moved it. Which")
    strs_push(l, "work inside those milestones costs it is not measured. The `channels` build regression is not")
    strs_push(l, "located. Interpretation and native code are unchanged within noise.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Debugging and sampling — N91, measured 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Hypothesis:** sampling observes a run without changing what it measures much, and Cranelift's")
    strs_push(l, "debug information costs a debug build little. **Method:** Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2, debug `nazm`;")
    strs_push(l, "seven runs each, median (min–max). **Sampling:** one LLVM `--debug` executable of a 120,000,000-step")
    strs_push(l, "checked loop (`work` in `crates/nazm-cli/tests/debugger_v3.rs`'s `SPIN`, at that count), run alone")
    strs_push(l, "and under `/usr/bin/sample` at two intervals, wall time from launch to exit.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | wall, ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| alone | 775 (774–802) |")
    strs_push(l, "| sampled every 1 ms | 821 (811–822) |")
    strs_push(l, "| sampled every 10 ms | 783 (782–784) |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "About 6% at the default interval, 1% at 10 ms: the sampler suspends the process for each sample, so")
    strs_push(l, "the cost is per sample, not per instruction. **A Cranelift debug build:** `bench/programs/strings.nz`,")
    strs_push(l, "`--no-cache`, five builds each — 198 ms ordinary, 222 ms with `--debug` (`dsymutil` included). Not")
    strs_push(l, "measured: the cost on a large program, and memory.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A launch is not the program's time.** A fresh executable spends about 300 ms before its first")
    strs_push(l, "instruction on this host, and a sample taken then names `_dyld_start` in `dyld`: `nazm profile`")
    strs_push(l, "builds a new executable every time, so its `wall_ms` includes that launch, and its samples show it")
    strs_push(l, "as system time — never as the program's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Accelerators v2 — N88, measured 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Hypothesis:** a zip and a fold are expressible and agree, and what they cost is stated whole —")
    strs_push(l, "transfers and the host fold included. **Workload:** `zipped(x, y) = x * y + x` over 1,000,000 pairs")
    strs_push(l, "(`x` = 1…1,000,000, `y` = `x % 7`) folded with `add`; the same as a native loop computing `y`")
    strs_push(l, "itself. **Method:** debug `nazm`, OpenCL on the Apple M1 Pro's GPU, three runs (the first builds the")
    strs_push(l, "kernel); the native loop at `--opt-level 2`, best of five including the 32 ms process floor.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| kernel build (first run / cached by the driver) | 129.6 / 1.5 |")
    strs_push(l, "| host to device, two inputs (16 MB) | 2.9–3.2 |")
    strs_push(l, "| run | 0.77–0.85 |")
    strs_push(l, "| device to host (8 MB) | 0.94–0.99 |")
    strs_push(l, "| fold on the host, in index order (a debug build of `nazm`) | 13.8–14.2 |")
    strs_push(l, "| the whole job as a native loop, less the process floor | about 3 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The device is not the cost; the transfers and the fold are, and the CPU computes this workload faster")
    strs_push(l, "than it can be shipped. This is the honest answer for a light kernel: the row's acceptance — a")
    strs_push(l, "workload a CPU cannot serve — is unmet, and N88 does not claim it. The fold's time would shrink in a")
    strs_push(l, "release build of `nazm`; a device-side `min`/`max` would remove it, and is not built.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Contracts — N87, measured 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Hypothesis:** a contract costs its clauses' evaluation and nothing more. **Workload:** 20,000,000")
    strs_push(l, "calls of a two-line function `step(n, k)` with `requires n >= 0 && k > 0` and `ensures result >= n`,")
    strs_push(l, "against the same program with the two clauses removed; the result printed and equal. **Method:**")
    strs_push(l, "debug `nazm`, `--opt-level 2`, best of five wall-clock runs including process start. Apple M1 Pro,")
    strs_push(l, "macOS 27.2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| 20,000,000 calls | LLVM | Cranelift |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| with the contract | 116.3 ms | 114.6 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| without | 117.1 ms | 108.0 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Under LLVM the difference is inside the run-to-run noise: the checks are compares and a branch to")
    strs_push(l, "the failure path, which `-O2` schedules among the call's own work. Under Cranelift about 6 %, the")
    strs_push(l, "compares and branches as written. Not measured: checking time (the clauses are typed with the body),")
    strs_push(l, "and a clause that calls a function, which costs that call.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Two boards under QEMU — N86, measured 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Hypothesis:** a program means the same on both boards, and each board's measured stack stays within")
    strs_push(l, "its stated bound. **Method:** `nazm-qemu:n86` (Debian, clang 19 with RISC-V, `ld.lld`, QEMU 10.0),")
    strs_push(l, "no network, 8 GiB memory and swap, 4 CPUs; `nazm` built from the tree inside it; each program built")
    strs_push(l, "at `-O0` and `-O2`, linked with `ld.lld -T link.ld`, booted with the board's `emulator` line and a")
    strs_push(l, "20 s deadline; the stack painted with `--stack-watermark`. Host: Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Program | AArch64 `virt` | RISC-V `virt` |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| byte writes to the UART, result `100` | `HI` / `100`, status 0 | `HI` / `100`, status 0 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Int` overflow in a loop | `N0400`, status 2 | `N0400`, status 2 |")
    strs_push(l, "| recursion past the stack | `N0408`, status 2 | `N0408`, status 2 |")
    strs_push(l, "| stack used ≤ bound, `-O0` | 176 ≤ 176 bytes | 152 ≤ 160 bytes |")
    strs_push(l, "| stack used ≤ bound, `-O2` | 32 ≤ 48 bytes | 32 ≤ 48 bytes |")
    strs_push(l, "| `fib(20)`, recursive (no bound stated), used `-O0` / `-O2` | 1,696 / 688 bytes | 1,344 / 688 bytes |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Found on the way, and fixed before these numbers: at `-O2` the RISC-V unit carries an `.eh_frame`")
    strs_push(l, "section the linker script did not name, which `ld.lld` placed at the load address ahead of `_start`,")
    strs_push(l, "so the machine started in data; the script now discards unwind tables and names RISC-V's small-data")
    strs_push(l, "sections. The AArch64 bound at `-O0` is met exactly: the bound is clang's frames along the deepest")
    strs_push(l, "path, and the run took that path. No timing is claimed: an emulator's speed says nothing about a")
    strs_push(l, "board's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### FFI v3 — N85, measured 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Hypothesis:** what crosses costs what §7.86 states, and nothing more. A foreign call now also")
    strs_push(l, "captures `errno` (one runtime call and a thread-local store); a C struct crosses as a `malloc`'d copy")
    strs_push(l, "freed after the call; a `Str` result is a `strlen` and a copy. **Workloads:** a loop of 10,000,000")
    strs_push(l, "iterations whose body is one foreign call: `c_add(t, i)` (scalars), `c_psum(P(x: i, flag: true, y:")
    strs_push(l, "1))` (a three-field C struct), `str_len(c_hi(i))` (a five-byte C string copied and dropped).")
    strs_push(l, "**Method:** debug `nazm`, `--opt-level 2`, clang `-O2` C fixture, best of five wall-clock runs")
    strs_push(l, "including process start; an empty program measures 32.3 ms the same way. Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Loop of 10,000,000 | LLVM | Cranelift |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| scalar call, `errno` captured | 73.0 ms | 77.7 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| C struct by borrowed copy | 198.7 ms | 250.2 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Str` result copied | 328.1 ms | 335.3 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Less the floor, a scalar call with its capture is about 4–5 ns an iteration; the struct copy adds")
    strs_push(l, "about 13–17 ns (an allocation and a free), the string copy about 30 ns (an allocation, a `strlen`, a")
    strs_push(l, "copy, a release). Not isolated: the capture's own cost against an N84 build of the same loop — N42's")
    strs_push(l, "56.6 ms for the scalar loop was measured by another method and is not a comparator. A program that")
    strs_push(l, "calls no C is unchanged: it reaches no `errno` part and links no `errno` unit under LLVM.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Build time across Gate 2 — measured 2026-10-09")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Hypothesis:** Gate 2's runtime and language additions cost a program that uses none of them")
    strs_push(l, "little or nothing to build, and nothing to run.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What flagged it.** `cargo xtask contained bench` (one CPU, Linux aarch64) against the baseline")
    strs_push(l, "re-saved at N106: `arith`, `channels` and `sequences` built 25–39 % slower at `-O0` or `-O2`, in two")
    strs_push(l, "runs. **Attributed** by building the tree before Gate 2 (`b5f7506`, Gate 1-C1D) and running the same")
    strs_push(l, "contained bench on it, and on `0f60b4b` (measured as `a9dc706`, its id before G2-C1 rewrote the")
    strs_push(l, "unpushed Gate 2 history; the tree is the same), both in one session, min of the bench's runs:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | before Gate 2 | after (`0f60b4b`) | N106's baseline |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `arith` build `-O0` | 102.7 ms | 109.1 ms | 87.5 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `calls` build `-O0` | 105.2 | 110.8 | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| `floor` build `-O0` | 101.7 | 108.6 | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| `sequences` build `-O0` | 104.8 | 112.0 | 91.2 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `strings` build `-O2` | 143.5 | 160.8 | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| `compiler/check` | 178.6 | 186.5 | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| every `native-O2` run | equal within 0.2 ms | | |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Most of the distance to the baseline — about 17 points of the 25 — was already there before Gate 2:")
    strs_push(l, "the session's machine and image, not a milestone (the tree before Gate 2 is under the threshold")
    strs_push(l, "against the same baseline). Gate 2's own share is a near-constant **6–7 ms per Linux build**: about")
    strs_push(l, "1.4 ms is linking `-lm`, which every Linux link now names for the float built-ins (an empty `main`")
    strs_push(l, "linked 15 times in the same container: 13.2 ms without it, 14.6 with); about 0.8 ms is checking")
    strs_push(l, "(the larger prelude and built-in tables: `arith/check` 2.8 → 3.7 ms); the rest is clang reading the")
    strs_push(l, "larger runtime and entry declarations. `strings` pays more at `-O2` (+12 %): its runtime unit grew by")
    strs_push(l, "a third with the text built-ins it reaches. On the host (Apple M1 Pro, best of seven,")
    strs_push(l, "`--no-cache`) the same two compilers differ by 0.5–1.4 % on five programs and 6.3 % on `strings -O2`.")
    strs_push(l, "Running time is unchanged, and the interpreter is 10–15 % faster on the loops (`arith/interpret`")
    strs_push(l, "2,694 → 2,294 ms). **Accepted** as the cost of numbers, handles and the rest in every build; linking")
    strs_push(l, "`-lm` only when the float built-ins are reached is a possible 1.4 ms, not taken.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Held from now on:** `bench/baseline-linux-aarch64.json` is re-saved at Gate 2's tree, so the")
    strs_push(l, "contained bench flags any build growing again by more than 25 % and 5 ms.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The standard library 1.0 — N84, measured 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Workloads:** `ints_sort` of 100,000 pseudo-random integers; 10,000 `map_set`s of distinct keys in a")
    strs_push(l, "scrambled order; `json_parse` then `json_encode` of a 128 KB array of 2,000 small objects, five times.")
    strs_push(l, "**Method:** release build, LLVM `-O2`, five runs, median. Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Operation | Median |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `ints_sort`, 100,000 | 19.6 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| `map_set` × 10,000 | 390.6 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| JSON parse + encode, 128 KB × 5 | 69.8 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The map is a sorted array: an insertion moves every entry after it, so building one of `n` keys is")
    strs_push(l, "quadratic; at 10,000 keys that is the cost above. A hash map needs hashing in the library, and is not")
    strs_push(l, "in 1.0. Sorting is a merge sort through `vec_sort_by`, its comparison an indirect call.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The default scheduler and the two regressions — N106, measured 2026-10-05")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Hypothesis:** the pool, now the default, keeps N83's advantage over threads; and the two")
    strs_push(l, "regressions N92 recorded have causes inside the milestones that introduced them, which can be named,")
    strs_push(l, "and — where they are not the price of a feature — removed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The scheduler.** `cargo test --release -p nazm-cli --test cli_s_z -- --ignored --nocapture")
    strs_push(l, "scheduler_default::what_the_default_scheduler_costs`: each program built at `-O2`, five runs, median, resident set from")
    strs_push(l, "`/usr/bin/time`; Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2, page size 16 KiB. Per operation, process start included:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Pool (the default, 4 workers) | Threads (`NAZM_SCHEDULER=threads`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| Spawn and join one task (50,000) | 6.66 µs | 26.07 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| Round trip `main` ↔ a task over two `Chan`s (50,000) | 4.51 µs | 4.24 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| A blocked receive woken, scope and channel made each time (20,000) | 7.75 µs | 24.63 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1,000 tasks alive at once | 19.8 MB, 17.8 KB per task, 41 ms | 20.4 MB, 18.4 KB per task, 816 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| 10,000 tasks alive at once | 179.9 MB, 17.8 KB per task, 387 ms; **4 OS threads** | not run: 10,000 OS threads |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Logical tasks against OS threads: the pool's report line says `workers=4 peak=10000` for the last")
    strs_push(l, "row — ten thousand tasks on four threads. A round trip with `main` still crosses threads (`main`")
    strs_push(l, "is not a pool task), so it is no cheaper on the pool; starting a task and waking a parked one are")
    strs_push(l, "about three times cheaper. Memory per task is the stack page it touches and its record, as N83")
    strs_push(l, "found: the pool saves threads and start-up, not bytes. Not measured: Linux, where the suite runs on")
    strs_push(l, "the pool by default but nothing here was timed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The regressions, attributed.** Release builds of each milestone's commit on the host, and")
    strs_push(l, "samples of the phase harness (`core_ir.rs`'s `what_each_phase_costs_on_the_compiler`) with symbols.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*`channels` builds, 13–31 % slower:* N83. The commit before the pool (`eb6bc1a`) builds `channels.nz`")
    strs_push(l, "as N75 does — 149 and 200 ms at `-O0` and `-O2` (`--no-cache`, eleven runs, median), against N75's")
    strs_push(l, "151 and 203 — and the pool's commit (`1bc5b02`) in 181 and 261: the runtime unit grew from 38,322 to")
    strs_push(l, "62,537 bytes of LLVM text (clang `-O2` on it alone: 69 → 102 ms) and a `switch` unit joined it. It is")
    strs_push(l, "the pool's code, which is now the default runtime's: **accepted**, and paid once — the runtime's")
    strs_push(l, "object is reused by every warm build, keyed by its digest.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Checking the compiler written in Nazm, 54 % slower:* N76 and N80, as N92 located, and now inside")
    strs_push(l, "them. Of the time `analyse_parsed` spends on `compiler/emit.nz` and what it imports, the lossless")
    strs_push(l, "tree (N76) is about a third — `cst::Builder::leaf`, interning each leaf's text, `finish_node`, the")
    strs_push(l, "lossless lexer — and provenance (N80) about a fifth (`provenance::solve`). Two parts of that were not")
    strs_push(l, "the features' necessary cost and were removed: a comparison sort ordering node openings (a tenth of")
    strs_push(l, "a parse; a counting pass gives the same order in linear time), and SipHash in the interner and in")
    strs_push(l, "the resolver's span-keyed tables (about a tenth of a check; the multiply-rotate hash rustc's tables")
    strs_push(l, "use, `nazm_span::fast`). The fixed-input program — a 3,001-function chain, the same text at every")
    strs_push(l, "milestone — parsed in 15.1 ms at N75, 19.0 before N106 and 15.5 after; checked in 14.5, 17.0 and")
    strs_push(l, "15.5. **Contained** (`cargo xtask contained bench`, one CPU, Linux aarch64, at N105 and at N106's")
    strs_push(l, "tree): `compiler/check` 213.7 → 180.2 ms, every other measurement within noise. The compiler's own")
    strs_push(l, "source grew by 31 % since N92 (609 → 797 KB), which is the rest of the distance from N92's 165.6 ms:")
    strs_push(l, "per kilobyte of source, 0.177 ms at N75, 0.272 at N92, 0.226 at N106. What remains above N75 is the")
    strs_push(l, "lossless tree and provenance — **accepted** as the cost of the formatter, the language service and")
    strs_push(l, "information-flow checking, and stated.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Held from now on:** `bench/baseline-linux-aarch64.json` is re-saved at N106's tree, so")
    strs_push(l, "`cargo xtask contained bench` flags either cost growing again by more than 25 % and 5 ms.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The task pool — N83, measured 2026-10-04")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Hypothesis:** tasks on a bounded pool start faster than threads, wait as cheaply, and let far more")
    strs_push(l, "of them be alive at once. **Workloads:** `spawns.nz` (start and join one empty task, 50,000 times),")
    strs_push(l, "`pingpong.nz` (50,000 round trips between `main` and a task over two `Chan`s), `many.nz` (N tasks")
    strs_push(l, "each waiting for one job, all alive before the first is sent). **Method:** release build, `-O2`; five")
    strs_push(l, "runs each, median; resident set size from `/usr/bin/time -l`. Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2, page size")
    strs_push(l, "16 KiB.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Model | Spawn + join | Round trip |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| One thread per task | 25.44 µs | 6.74 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| Pool, 1 / 2 / 4 workers | 7.43 / 7.38 / 7.40 µs | 4.98 / 4.99 / 4.97 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Tasks alive at once | Pool (4 workers), resident | Threads, resident |")
    strs_push(l, "| ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1,000 | 19.9 MB | 20.3 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "| 4,000 | — | 75.5 MB |")
    strs_push(l, "| 10,000 | 179.8 MB | did not finish 6,000 within 40 s |")
    strs_push(l, "| 50,000 | 891.1 MB | — |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "About 17.8 KB per pooled task (one 16 KiB page of stack touched, and the record), against about")
    strs_push(l, "18.4 KB per thread: the pool does not save memory per task here, it saves OS threads, starts faster,")
    strs_push(l, "and keeps going where threads stop. The switch is 22 instructions each way; a round trip with `main`")
    strs_push(l, "still crosses threads, so it is not a pure switch cost. Not measured: work stealing (there is none),")
    strs_push(l, "Linux.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The runtime artifact — N82, measured 2026-10-03")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Hypothesis:** a prebuilt runtime saves the runtime's compile on every build that does not already")
    strs_push(l, "hold that exact text. **Workload:** the program in `runtime_artifact.rs` that reaches every runtime")
    strs_push(l, "service, built with `--no-cache` so every unit is compiled. **Method:** release build, the two")
    strs_push(l, "configurations interleaved, 11 runs each, median (minimum–maximum). Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2,")
    strs_push(l, "Apple clang 21.0.0.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Backend | Generated runtime | `--runtime` artifact |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| LLVM | 146 ms (144–151) | 112 ms (111–116) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Cranelift | 119 ms (117–122) | 85 ms (84–88) |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "About 34 ms a build, the runtime's clang compile at `-O2`; a build whose project store already held the")
    strs_push(l, "runtime's object saw none of that cost before. The executable is the same program: its output,")
    strs_push(l, "ending and memory report are identical (tested), though its bytes need not be, since the artifact is")
    strs_push(l, "the runtime with every service.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Provenance v3 — N80, measured 2026-10-03")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Hypothesis:** container cells, indirect targets and local shapes cost the checker a bounded,")
    strs_push(l, "measurable amount, and nothing at runtime. **Changed path:** `nazm check --no-cache`, whose")
    strs_push(l, "provenance walk and solve changed; nothing below the checker did. **Workload:** the two largest")
    strs_push(l, "compiler sources and one small example, checked cold. **Method:** release builds of N79's head")
    strs_push(l, "(`8daf107`, in a worktree) and of N80, the two run interleaved in one Python loop, 21 to 31 runs")
    strs_push(l, "each, the median with its minimum and maximum. Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2, rustc 1.98.1.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| File | N79 | N80 | Ratio |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `compiler/emit.nz` | 71.1 ms (69.7–83.5) | 80.0 ms (78.3–83.1) | 1.125 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `compiler/analyse.nz` | 41.6 ms (40.4–43.0) | 45.2 ms (43.9–46.9) | 1.085 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `examples/pipeline.nz` | 5.5 ms (5.0–7.7) | 5.5 ms (5.1–7.0) | 0.99 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A regression of about 9 ms on the largest file, accepted and recorded. Instrumented, the solve on")
    strs_push(l, "`emit.nz` takes four rounds as cells grow, about 7.7 ms in all. Three changes brought it down from a")
    strs_push(l, "first build at 1.19×: an index of call sites per body (a container call's cell was a linear search),")
    strs_push(l, "receive edges evaluated once per round, and later rounds starting from the previous one's summaries")
    strs_push(l, "and re-solving only functions that read a grown cell. Further work would be incremental values and")
    strs_push(l, "receives inside a round. Peak memory was not measured. The runtime is unchanged: provenance is")
    strs_push(l, "erased before Core IR, and `flow_v3.rs` runs an affected program interpreted and natively.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Mutation harness v2 — what a mutant costs (N12.2, 2026-09-24/25)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Tooling, not language performance, recorded here because this is where measured cost lives.")
    strs_push(l, "Contained, one CPU, one Cargo job, one test thread, nothing else running.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Where the legacy runner's time went, per mutant:** a workspace rebuild of 11–15 s for a Rust")
    strs_push(l, "file and 0.1 s for a `compiler/*.nz` one, then the workspace suite, **228 s**. Per session, a")
    strs_push(l, "cold build of 92 s and the baseline suite. The suite, run for every mutant, was the cost.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | legacy (N12.1 batches) | v2, profiles only | v2, verified killers |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| the 27 N12.1 mutants, wall | 10,782 s productive, 13,870 s with no-verdict reruns | 1,807 s | **523 s** (20.6× less) |")
    strs_push(l, "| per mutant, median / p90 | ≈ 240 s | 52 s / 84 s | **1.4 s / 13.8 s** |")
    strs_push(l, "| workspace suites run | 27, plus baselines | 0 | 0 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The 523 s is 331 s of cold build and baseline, 131 s of workspace builds — kept, because")
    strs_push(l, "UNUSABLE is decided on the whole tree — and 44 s of killers.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The whole catalogue, targeted:** 233 mutants in 10,686 s over five sessions (1,770 s of it")
    strs_push(l, "cold builds and baselines), median 22 s and p90 84 s per mutant; 2,116 s of workspace")
    strs_push(l, "builds, 6,694 s of tests. Six workspace suites were run and 227 avoided. The legacy shape")
    strs_push(l, "would have run 233 suites at about 245 s each — about sixteen hours, never measured, because")
    strs_push(l, "no session could hold it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What remains:** the selfhost profile. The 71 `compiler/*.nz` entries are 45 % of per-mutant")
    strs_push(l, "time, and the 51 without a killer each pay most of the selfhost binary (≈ 80–100 s) at tier 2.")
    strs_push(l, "A killer takes such an entry to a few seconds. Compilation is the second cost (24 %), and it")
    strs_push(l, "is the build UNUSABLE depends on.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## The warm mutation session — N32-H, measured 2026-09-28/29")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N32's killer verification was running at **246–291 s per killer** (18 finished, median 266 s) — 32")
    strs_push(l, "of them would have taken about 2 h 20 min before its campaign had started. One of them,")
    strs_push(l, "profiled phase by phase at P1: container start 1.4 s; copy and `xtask` build about 16 s; **the")
    strs_push(l, "pristine `cargo build --workspace --tests`, cold, 190.3 s — 68%**; killer listing 5.3 s; the")
    strs_push(l, "mutant build 31.8 s; the restored build 31.5 s; the killer itself, three runs, about 2 s. Every")
    strs_push(l, "killer paid a fresh container and a cold target.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A session is now one warm worker (`runbook.md`, *The warm-worker law*): one pristine build on the")
    strs_push(l, "image's warmed dependency cache — 92 s instead of 190 s — one baseline, and killer verification")
    strs_push(l, "inside the campaign's loop, around each mutant's one injection. Still P1: one CPU, one job, one")
    strs_push(l, "thread, one mutant at a time.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| N32 MILESTONE gate, 2026-09-28/29, M1 Pro | Seconds |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| warm session: 31 mutations, 34 killers verified, targeted campaign — setup 806 s once (pristine build, baseline suite, listing), 31 mutants 662 s, median 21.0 s, p95 40.1 s | 1,478 |")
    strs_push(l, "| contained workspace suite, P4T4 | 439 |")
    strs_push(l, "| lifecycle suite, P1 | 171 |")
    strs_push(l, "| selfhost, P4T4 | 57 |")
    strs_push(l, "| bootstrap, P1 | 62 |")
    strs_push(l, "| N32 benchmark and binary sizes, P1 | 196 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `cargo xtask check` and the doc-claim tests | 3 |")
    strs_push(l, "| **the gate, wall clock** | **2,406 — 40.1 min** |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The five-mutant checkpoint before it: setup 793 s, first mutant 13.1 s, then 27.8, 27.1, 32.6 and")
    strs_push(l, "53.2 s. No second worker was built: the gate was under an hour without one. The setup is now")
    strs_push(l, "dominated by the baseline workspace suite at one CPU, which the campaign needs to be green before")
    strs_push(l, "any mutant is judged; it is the next stage to look at, and it was not weakened to get here.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Verification harness V3 — N32-H3, measured 2026-09-29")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "From the gate's own summary (`target/n32h3/v3/summary.json`, harness evidence, not a schema):")
    strs_push(l, "one authoritative harness-changing gate — 45 mutations (N32's seventeen, the twelve MCP entries,")
    strs_push(l, "all sixteen harness entries), 48 killers, the scheduled workspace suite at P4W2T4, the full")
    strs_push(l, "lifecycle suite, selfhost, bootstrap, the docs and MCP benchmark, the gates.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Stage, seconds | V1 | V2 warm | V3 |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| mutation session (V3: setup 93, 45 mutants 738, median 13.4, p95 34.9) | 1,478 | 770 | 840 |")
    strs_push(l, "| — of which the mutants' workspace builds | not recorded | 497 | 529 |")
    strs_push(l, "| workspace suite | 439 | 418 (P4T4) | **257** (P4W2T4) |")
    strs_push(l, "| lifecycle suite, full | 171 | 183 | 189 |")
    strs_push(l, "| selfhost | 57 | 46 | 46 |")
    strs_push(l, "| bootstrap | 62 | 37 | 37 |")
    strs_push(l, "| benchmark | 196 | 199 | 224 (first fill of the bench cache) |")
    strs_push(l, "| gates | 3 | 2 | 2 |")
    strs_push(l, "| **the gate** | **2,406** | **1,655** | **1,595 — 26.6 min** |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "V3 decided 45 mutations where V2 decided 38. **The workspace suite fell 39%** against the P4T4")
    strs_push(l, "run measured the same morning (424 s): 83 binaries over two workers of four threads, 250.7 s of")
    strs_push(l, "running led by `nazm-service test:context` 80.5 s, `test:incomplete` 76.7 s and `nazm-cli")
    strs_push(l, "test:selfhost` 60.5 s — the same 1,728 passed, 19 ignored, 95 result lines, each binary's counts")
    strs_push(l, "identical to the plain run's, at a container peak of 1.63 GB against P4T4's 2.07 GB.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The gate is over the 25-minute closure line, and the largest stage is at a floor.** The mutation")
    strs_push(l, "session's builds are `cargo build --workspace --tests` after each injection, the check that")
    strs_push(l, "separates UNUSABLE from CAUGHT: a `nazm-docs` mutant compiles 40 dependent units in 24–31 s, an")
    strs_push(l, "MCP one 2 in about 5.5 s, a harness one 2 to 4 in about 2 s — the order was already grouped by")
    strs_push(l, "package, so bucketing measured no saving. The remaining 86 s is the restored killers' rebuild,")
    strs_push(l, "which the restoration law requires. Neither is removed. The benchmark's 224 s included its")
    strs_push(l, "cache's first fill.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Two P4W* profiles were not run: `p4w2t2` was stopped before it started, and `p4w4t1`, `p4w3t2` and")
    strs_push(l, "`p4w1t4` were not run — dominated by the model (serialising the slow few-test binaries, more")
    strs_push(l, "oversubscription, `cargo test`'s own order). The scheduler's correctness is its unit tests,")
    strs_push(l, "including a real-concurrency stress test repeated ten times, not repeated suite runs.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## The mutation baseline and the persistent cache — N32-H2, measured 2026-09-29")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "V1's session paid 806 s of setup before its first mutant. V1 did not record its parts; V2's cold")
    strs_push(l, "gate did, for everything V1 also did: the pristine build 125.7 s and the killer listing 58.0 s.")
    strs_push(l, "The remaining ~620 s of V1's setup was the workspace suite run as the baseline at one CPU — work")
    strs_push(l, "no Tier-1 verdict needs, and which the MILESTONE gate's own P4T4 workspace stage repeats anyway.")
    strs_push(l, "V2 runs each unique declared killer once on the pristine tree instead (35 of them, 10.9 s), runs")
    strs_push(l, "the whole suite only when a mutant needs a later tier (none did), reads each mutant's")
    strs_push(l, "verification from the very run its verdict came from, and keeps build state between sessions in")
    strs_push(l, "two harness-owned volumes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Stage, seconds | V1 (N32 gate) | V2 cold (cache cleared) | V2 warm |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| mutation setup | 806 | 195 | **86** |")
    strs_push(l, "| — pristine build / listing / pristine killers / baseline suite | not recorded | 125.7 / 58.0 / 10.9 / — | 62.5 / 12.3 / 10.9 / — |")
    strs_push(l, "| mutants decided (median, p95) | 662 (21.0, 40.1) | 684 (13.6, 36.1) | 679 (13.4, 35.3) |")
    strs_push(l, "| mutation session, contained | 1,478 | 896 | **770** |")
    strs_push(l, "| workspace suite, P4T4 | 439 | 452 | 418 |")
    strs_push(l, "| lifecycle suite, full | 171 | 183 | 183 |")
    strs_push(l, "| selfhost | 57 | 57 | 46 |")
    strs_push(l, "| bootstrap | 62 | 38 | 37 |")
    strs_push(l, "| N32 benchmark | 196 | 206 | 199 |")
    strs_push(l, "| gates | 3 | 8 | 2 |")
    strs_push(l, "| **the gate** | **2,406** | **1,841** | **1,655 — 27.6 min** |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "V2 decided 38 mutations and verified 41 killers where V1 decided 31 and verified 34: the seven")
    strs_push(l, "harness mutations N32-H2 added are in both V2 columns. The warm gate is **31% faster than V1**")
    strs_push(l, "(−751 s) and passes the ≤ 30-minute MILESTONE target; the 25-minute stretch was not reached.")
    strs_push(l, "The cold gate, 30.7 min, missed the target by 41 s, which is why the warm one was run; its")
    strs_push(l, "lifecycle stage also failed, on a test that had assumed macOS's recovery route (below), so it is")
    strs_push(l, "a timing and not an acceptance. What is left is the workspace suite — 418 s, of which about 410 s")
    strs_push(l, "is test execution, led by five binaries of 20–76 s each — the mutants' own builds (497 s of the")
    strs_push(l, "770), and the full lifecycle suite this harness-changing round needs; a milestone that does not")
    strs_push(l, "change the harness runs only the lifecycle suite's invariants (`runbook.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "One CPU, one job and one thread throughout the mutation session: no memory kill in any stage, and")
    strs_push(l, "the benchmark's MCP server settled at 10.9 MB and held 11.1 MB after 1,000 more calls.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Two findings, both kept as tests. **A mutation copy and the checkout must not share a target**:")
    strs_push(l, "the first cold gate's workspace suite ran a `nazm` a mutation session had built, because Cargo")
    strs_push(l, "copies a binary out under its bare name and does not copy a fresh unit again — the two now have")
    strs_push(l, "separate volumes, and a mutation guards it. **A damaged target is recovered, not trusted**: on")
    strs_push(l, "macOS rustc's incremental cache reuses damaged object files whose source is unchanged and the")
    strs_push(l, "build fails, so a harness-owned target is cleaned and rebuilt once; on Linux Cargo rebuilds them")
    strs_push(l, "itself. Neither route ever produced a verdict.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Development and evidence pipeline parallelism — N14.1, measured 2026-09-25")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Tooling, not language performance. The question: how much of the machine may **one**")
    strs_push(l, "contained workload use inside the same ceilings — 4 GiB memory with swap equal, 512 pids,")
    strs_push(l, "8 GiB storage, the same deadlines — without changing a verdict or approaching a limit.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The machine.** Apple M1 Pro, 10 cores (8 performance, 2 efficiency), 32 GiB; Docker")
    strs_push(l, "Desktop VM with 10 CPUs and 7.75 GiB, kernel 7.0.12-linuxkit, aarch64, `nazm-contained:1.98.1`.")
    strs_push(l, "Nothing else heavy ran during any cell; cells alternated profiles so thermal drift could")
    strs_push(l, "not line up with one of them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The gates, frozen before any profile was chosen.** Total cgroup peak (`memory.peak`) at or")
    strs_push(l, "below 85 % of the limit, 3,482 MiB; anonymous memory at or below 70 %, 2,867 MiB; zero")
    strs_push(l, "`memory.events` max, oom and oom_kill; no swap. Total, anonymous and page-cache peaks are")
    strs_push(l, "reported separately because they mean different things (the first round's build cells")
    strs_push(l, "recorded only the total; anonymous and page-cache figures come from the later rounds): anonymous memory is what the")
    strs_push(l, "workload needs, page cache is what the kernel kept of the files it wrote.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Semantics did not move.** Every cell of every profile gave the same answer: the workspace")
    strs_push(l, "suite 1,317 passed / 0 failed / 13 ignored in 67 binaries, selfhost 38 of 38, every mutant")
    strs_push(l, "the same verdict and tier. No cell anywhere had an OOM kill, a limit event or swap.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Workload (median of n) | P1 | P4T4 | P6 (6 CPUs, 6 jobs, 4 threads) |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| cold workspace build | 97.5 s (4) | **26.9 s (3), 3.6×** | 19.2 s (4) |")
    strs_push(l, "| incremental rebuild, one `nazm-core` file | 16.0 s (4) | **4.7 s (3), 3.4×** | 3.3 s (4) |")
    strs_push(l, "| worst total / anonymous peak, build | 3,328 / 375 MiB | 3,311 / 1,050 MiB | **3,658** / 1,302 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| workspace suite | 294.4 s (3) | **97.0 s (3), 3.03×** | 96.9 s (3) |")
    strs_push(l, "| worst total / anonymous peak, suite | 2,704 / 354 MiB | 2,857 / 359 MiB | 2,944 / 362 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| selfhost suite | 131.2 s (2) | **38.1 s (2), 3.44×** | 38.0 s (2) |")
    strs_push(l, "| worst total / anonymous peak, selfhost | 764 / 100 MiB | 1,076 / 303 MiB | 1,102 / 287 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What decided it.** The suites scale with *test threads*, not with the CPU quota: P4 with")
    strs_push(l, "two threads ran the suite in 146.6 s and P6 with two in 146.7 s, P4 with one thread in")
    strs_push(l, "270.2 s. P6's extra quota helps compilation only, and its incremental rebuild crossed the")
    strs_push(l, "total gate in all four measurements (3,506–3,658 MiB) — six concurrent `rustc` processes'")
    strs_push(l, "anonymous memory on top of 2.3 GiB of page cache. P1's own worst build total, 3,328 MiB, is")
    strs_push(l, "above P4T4's: the total is mostly page cache, which is why anonymous memory is reported")
    strs_push(l, "beside it. Where P4T4 and P6 tie, the rule was the lower-resource profile. P2 (1.9×) and the one- and two-thread P4 variants were measured in")
    strs_push(l, "the first round and dropped.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Mutation stays P1.** One fast tier-1 mutant, `n13-a-vec-has-equality`:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | wall | verdict | total / anonymous / page cache |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| P1 | 374.9 s | caught, tier 1 | 2,998 / 373 / 2,630 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| P4T4 | 130.8 s | caught, tier 1 | **3,623** / 868 / 2,642 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| 4 CPUs, 2 jobs, 4 threads | 156.7 s | caught, tier 1 | **3,853** / 619 / 3,292 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Both parallel profiles crossed the total gate. The total is dominated by page cache — a")
    strs_push(l, "campaign holds a tree copy, a target directory and every test binary it built — and it is")
    strs_push(l, "not monotonic in parallelism: halving the jobs lowered anonymous memory by 250 MiB and the")
    strs_push(l, "total *rose* by 230 MiB. The gate was not changed after this evidence appeared, so the")
    strs_push(l, "default did not move and **N14.1 claims no mutation speedup.** Accelerating mutation needs")
    strs_push(l, "its own experiment on how page cache and the container's memory limit interact, not a")
    strs_push(l, "looser gate.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The defaults.** `contained tests` and `contained selfhost` take P4T4; `mutate`,")
    strs_push(l, "`bootstrap`, `release` and `run` stay P1; `bench` is P1 permanently. `--profile p1`")
    strs_push(l, "reproduces any older result. All build-cell and mutation numbers above are direct paired")
    strs_push(l, "measurements on the current tree; the per-workload speedups are measured, not derived.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The final runs, on the frozen tree that was then committed unchanged, each under its")
    strs_push(l, "adopted default:** the workspace suite at P4T4 in 116 s of container time (1,321 passed,")
    strs_push(l, "the four new tests included), selfhost at P4T4 in 45 s, the xtask lifecycle suite 13 of")
    strs_push(l, "13, a frozen seven-mutant P1 sample with every verdict and tier as established (five at")
    strs_push(l, "tier 1, two at tier 2, no timeout, every source restored to its digest), and the bootstrap")
    strs_push(l, "at P1 in 52 s with `0e1a40e6…` unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## The CPU provider's SIMD path, measured (Gate 3H, 2026-10-11)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm accel --provider cpu`, 8,000,000 elements, `--no-check`, the median `run_ms` of seven runs")
    strs_push(l, "— the pool's work alone, not the build or the files — with LLVM's vectoriser (the default) and")
    strs_push(l, "without it (`--scalar`). Apple M1 Pro, 10 cores, 10 threads; Apple clang 21.0.0; the commit that")
    strs_push(l, "filed this section (Gate 3H). The kernels: `square` (`Int`, `x * x`, checked), `axpy` (`Float32`,")
    strs_push(l, "`2.5 * a + b`, a zip) and `poly` (`Float64`, a square root and a division).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| kernel | element | vectorised | scalar | what LLVM did with the loop |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `square` | `Int` | 8.55 ms | 8.96 ms | **not vectorised**: checked arithmetic leaves the element function early on overflow |")
    strs_push(l, "| `axpy` | `Float32` | 5.07 ms | 4.95 ms | vectorised, 4 lanes, interleaved 4 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `poly` | `Float64` | 6.20 ms | 7.13 ms | vectorised, 2 lanes, interleaved 4 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The two builds are within each other's spread (minimum to maximum over the seven runs: 6.4–12.8,")
    strs_push(l, "4.1–6.8, 5.8–11.8 ms). Ten threads over 64 to 128 MB of elements are bound by memory bandwidth,")
    strs_push(l, "not arithmetic, so the lanes LLVM made have nothing to win here. **No SIMD speed-up is claimed**;")
    strs_push(l, "what is shown is that the path exists — the float loops vectorise and agree with the interpreter")
    strs_push(l, "bit for bit either way (`accel_providers.rs`) — and that this workload does not profit from it.")
    strs_push(l, "A compute-bound kernel, or one thread, would be the next measurement.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Gate 4 light: a small cross-language set, measured (2026-10-11)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What Gate 4 light set out to measure, and why so little: three programs already in")
    strs_push(l, "`bench/programs/`, each against references written **statement for statement** in the other languages")
    strs_push(l, "(`bench/reference/`), because a different algorithm would measure the algorithm. `floor` does nothing")
    strs_push(l, "and measures what a process costs to start; `sieve` is the program this file already compared with C")
    strs_push(l, "and Python; `channels` hands 50,000 integers through a channel of capacity one from one task to")
    strs_push(l, "another — the synchronisation the concurrency model rests on, and the one shape a Go service lives on.")
    strs_push(l, "Chosen for the C, Rust, Go and Python rows of `v1-competitor-map.md`; Zig and Julia are **unmeasured**,")
    strs_push(l, "not installed here.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`python3 bench/cross.py NAZM OUT` (in the tree; results in `target/gates/v1/bench/cross.json`). Apple M1")
    strs_push(l, "Pro, 10 cores, macOS (Darwin 27.2); `nazm` 1.0.0 built `--release` from the compiler of `734443e`;")
    strs_push(l, "Apple clang 21.0.0; rustc 1.98.1; go 1.27.1; Python 3.14.8. Every executable printed the program's")
    strs_push(l, "`.expected` answer before it was timed. Three unmeasured warm-up runs, then 21 runs, each the wall")
    strs_push(l, "clock around a whole process; the median, the extremes and the interquartile range. Build time is")
    strs_push(l, "measured apart from run time, five builds each. Not controlled: thermal state, other processes,")
    strs_push(l, "frequency scaling.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| program | variant | arithmetic | run, median | min–max | IQR | peak RSS | build, median |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| floor | Nazm, LLVM `-O2` | checked | 3.86 ms | 3.29–8.81 | 0.98 | 1.7 MiB | 151 ms cold |")
    strs_push(l, "| floor | Nazm, Cranelift | checked | 3.87 ms | 3.65–5.23 | 0.46 | 1.7 MiB | 262 ms cold |")
    strs_push(l, "| sieve | Nazm, LLVM `-O2` | checked, bounds-checked | 5.82 ms | 5.36–7.33 | 0.54 | 6.9 MiB | 178 ms cold, 84 ms warm |")
    strs_push(l, "| sieve | Nazm, Cranelift | checked, bounds-checked | 7.78 ms | 7.20–8.82 | 0.53 | 6.9 MiB | 265 ms cold |")
    strs_push(l, "| sieve | C, `clang -O2` | unchecked | 4.81 ms | 4.34–6.30 | 0.58 | 4.8 MiB | 81 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| sieve | Rust, `rustc -O -C overflow-checks=on` | checked, bounds-checked | 5.65 ms | 5.17–8.04 | 0.41 | 7.0 MiB | 173 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "| sieve | Go, `go build` | wrapping, bounds-checked | 8.48 ms | 7.64–9.72 | 0.73 | 16.9 MiB | 64 ms warm |")
    strs_push(l, "| sieve | Python 3.14 | unbounded | 78.1 ms | 75.2–85.5 | 3.80 | 19.1 MiB | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| sieve | Nazm, interpreter | checked | 274 ms | 268–284 | 8.94 | 11.5 MiB | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| channels | Nazm, LLVM `-O2` | checked | 233 ms | 226–260 | 17.0 | 1.9 MiB | 302 ms cold, 81 ms warm |")
    strs_push(l, "| channels | Nazm, Cranelift | checked | 238 ms | 234–358 | 8.47 | 1.9 MiB | 258 ms cold |")
    strs_push(l, "| channels | Go, `go build` | wrapping | 11.0 ms | 9.82–13.5 | 1.49 | 4.3 MiB | 63 ms warm |")
    strs_push(l, "| channels | Python 3.14, threads | unbounded | 407 ms | 391–519 | 32.4 | 14.5 MiB | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| channels | Nazm, interpreter | checked | 266 ms | 256–285 | 9.95 | 6.5 MiB | — |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it shows.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **The sieve is not a compute comparison.** Every native variant finishes within about 1 to 5 ms")
    strs_push(l, "  of a process that does nothing (Nazm's `floor`, 3.9 ms), so the column is mostly process start-up.")
    strs_push(l, "  It says only that on this program the natively compiled variants land within a few milliseconds of")
    strs_push(l, "  one another and an order of magnitude ahead of CPython. It does **not** say Nazm matches Rust or C,")
    strs_push(l, "  or beats Go: a larger input is the measurement that would.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Nazm's channel hand-off is about 21 times slower than Go's here** — 233 ms against 11 ms for")
    strs_push(l, "  50,000 hand-offs, about 4.6 µs each against 0.2 µs, on this workload. The interpreter is within 15 %")
    strs_push(l, "  of the native builds, which **suggests** the cost is the runtime's hand-off — each send and receive a")
    strs_push(l, "  wait and a wake on the pool — rather than the code generated around it; that is a hypothesis, not")
    strs_push(l, "  profiled. It is a measured weakness of this workload under the 1.0 runtime, stated as one.")
    strs_push(l, "  CPython's threads are slower again, at 407 ms.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Builds.** A cold Nazm build (`--no-cache`, the runtime compiled with the program) took 150 to 300")
    strs_push(l, "  ms; with its object cache warm, 81 to 84 ms — beside `clang`'s 81 ms, `rustc`'s 173 ms, both from")
    strs_push(l, "  source, and Go's 63 ms with its build cache warm. Like with like is the warm rows with Go's.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Memory.** Nazm's native programs held 1.7 to 6.9 MiB at peak, in the range of C's and Rust's and")
    strs_push(l, "  below Go's and CPython's on these programs.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it does not show.** Nothing about a language as a whole, nothing about a larger input or")
    strs_push(l, "another machine, and nothing about server throughput, latency under load, task scalability, numeric")
    strs_push(l, "kernels or memory over time — each its own measurement, none taken. A result inside `cargo xtask")
    strs_push(l, "bench`'s 25 % regression threshold is a statement about Nazm against its own baseline, never about a")
    strs_push(l, "competitor. No aggregate score is derived.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## The optimisation pass, and what it was based on")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "One pass, chosen from a profile rather than from intuition. `sample` on the release")
    strs_push(l, "binary running `bench/programs/arith.nz` — a loop doing nothing but arithmetic on five")
    strs_push(l, "locals — attributed **81 of 277 samples on the evaluation thread (29%)** to looking up")
    strs_push(l, "variable names:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | samples |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `RandomState::hash_one::<String>` | 43 |")
    strs_push(l, "| SipHash `Hasher::write` | 23 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `memcmp` (hash-map key comparison) | 15 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Interpreter::eval` (the dispatch itself) | 122 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Interpreter::block` | 26 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `drop_glue::<Value>` | 20 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Interpreter::binary` | 15 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The environment was `Vec<HashMap<String, Value>>`, so every variable read hashed a")
    strs_push(l, "string. A frame holds a handful of bindings and the checker refuses two of one name in")
    strs_push(l, "one scope, so the map was replaced with a short association list scanned linearly.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Measured against the recorded baseline, same machine, minutes apart:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Program | before | after | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `arith/interpret` | 876.7 ms | 423.3 ms | **2.07×** |")
    strs_push(l, "| `calls/interpret` | 908.8 ms | 647.3 ms | **1.40×** |")
    strs_push(l, "| `sieve/interpret` | 467.0 ms | 294.2 ms | **1.59×** |")
    strs_push(l, "| `sequences/interpret` | 290.0 ms | 228.0 ms | 1.27× |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Larger than the 29% the profile accounted for, because removing the hashing also removes")
    strs_push(l, "the per-lookup setup and touches less memory. Nothing measured got slower.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Re-profiling afterwards: SipHash is absent, and the remaining time is the `eval` dispatch")
    strs_push(l, "itself (65 of 119 non-idle samples), `block` (15), `memcmp` from the linear scan (15),")
    strs_push(l, "`binary` (11) and dropping `Value` (10). **The next pass would have to attack the")
    strs_push(l, "dispatch**, which means resolving names to slot indices at check time — a much larger")
    strs_push(l, "change, and not one to start without a reason beyond \"it is next in the profile\".")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## The claim, stated so a hostile reader can check it")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "> Nazm compiles through LLVM for release builds, so on scalar single-threaded code it")
    strs_push(l, "> targets **parity with C, Rust, and Zig — not a win**.")
    strs_push(l, ">")
    strs_push(l, "> Where Nazm is designed to win:")
    strs_push(l, "> - **Layout-bound workloads**, measured against **both idiomatic Rust and hand-written SoA")
    strs_push(l, ">   Rust**. Beating only idiomatic Rust measures a different representation, not a better")
    strs_push(l, ">   compiler.")
    strs_push(l, "> - **Allocation-heavy workloads vs Go**: throughput and p99.9 latency, no GC.")
    strs_push(l, "> - **Scripts vs Python**.")
    strs_push(l, ">")
    strs_push(l, "> Nazm does not claim to beat C on scalar code.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**All numeric targets are provisional until baselines are measured.** An earlier draft")
    strs_push(l, "asserted \"geomean within 1.05× of Rust and 1.10× of C\" and \"any loss beyond 1.2× is a")
    strs_push(l, "tracked bug\". Those are removed rather than left standing: there is no measured")
    strs_push(l, "distribution to set them against, so they were decoration.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Where the headroom actually is")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Ranked by expected payoff. Only the first is a genuine differentiator.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Lever | Expected payoff | Against | Confidence |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Data-oriented layout selection (auto SoA, field reorder, hot/cold split) | large on layout-bound code | C, Rust, Zig, Go | the one real unlock — and unproven |")
    strs_push(l, "| Escape analysis + region/arena inference, no GC | large on allocation-heavy code; p99.9 latency | Go, Java, Python | high |")
    strs_push(l, "| Comptime + whole-program specialisation | moderate | Go interfaces, C++ vtables | medium-high |")
    strs_push(l, "| No-alias from the ownership model | small | C | medium — Rust has this and has struggled to cash it |")
    strs_push(l, "| Runtime quality (scheduler, allocator, no false sharing) | tail latency, not throughput | Go | medium |")
    strs_push(l, "| PGO / JIT respecialisation | moderate, branchy code | everyone | expensive, stage late |")
    strs_push(l, "| Auto-vectorisation | ~zero as a differentiator | nobody | **do not market this.** LLVM already does it; wins attributed to it are usually the layout lever giving the vectoriser something it can use |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Avoiding LLVM's compile-time cost is a **compile-time** lever. It does not belong in a")
    strs_push(l, "runtime performance claim, and Cranelift output is meaningfully slower than LLVM `-O2`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## What will make Nazm slower than C for a long time")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The standard library. A young `HashMap` loses to `hashbrown`, and library quality compounds")
    strs_push(l, "across a whole program.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An earlier draft said \"real programs are 80% library calls\" and predicted a three-year")
    strs_push(l, "disadvantage. Both are removed — the percentage was unsupported and the duration was a")
    strs_push(l, "guess presented as a forecast.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Measurement rules")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "1. **Layout wins are measured against hand-written SoA Rust**, not only idiomatic Rust.")
    strs_push(l, "2. **Compile time and runtime are reported separately.** They trade against each other.")
    strs_push(l, "3. **Agent development efficiency is reported separately from both**, under")
    strs_push(l, "   [`evaluation.md`](research/evaluation.md). Go is a runtime reference there, not an arm.")
    strs_push(l, "4. **The task-memory benchmark states its terms**: task states distinguished (created /")
    strs_push(l, "   parked / runnable / running), stack allocation strategy, lazy commit, **RSS measured")
    strs_push(l, "   rather than virtual reservation**, page size recorded per platform.")
    strs_push(l, "5. Every published figure carries the machine, toolchain version, and commit hash.")
    strs_push(l, "6. **An external comparator must do equivalent work and produce the same result**, and is")
    strs_push(l, "   not timed at all if its answer differs from the Nazm program's. `xtask/src/bench.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "   enforces this rather than trusting it: a reference program has to reproduce the case's")
    strs_push(l, "   `.expected` output before a single measurement is taken. *(Absorbed 2026-09-21 from the")
    strs_push(l, "   Era-1 contract §12, which is otherwise retired.)*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## R1, 5b.10: the cross-language comparison")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What it measures: three small programs, each written once per language in `bench/compare/<lang>/`,")
    strs_push(l, "idiomatically and as short as is natural there, not statement for statement. `hello` prints one")
    strs_push(l, "line and measures what a process costs to start; `fib` is recursive `fib(35)`, call overhead and")
    strs_push(l, "integer arithmetic; `words` reads a 13 MB file of 2,000,000 words (`bench/compare/gen_words.py`, a")
    strs_push(l, "fixed-seed xorshift generator, so the file is the same on every Python), counts them with the")
    strs_push(l, "language's standard hash map and prints the number of distinct words and the ten most frequent.")
    strs_push(l, "Every program must print the expected output (`bench/compare/words.expected` for `words`) before")
    strs_push(l, "it is timed; one that does not is recorded as not measured, and an absent toolchain as absent.")
    strs_push(l, "Each language is built with its usual release flags, recorded in the output. C has no standard")
    strs_push(l, "hash map, so its `words` carries a short open-addressing table of its own. It is re-run for each")
    strs_push(l, "publication.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`python3 bench/compare/compare.py NAZM OUT_DIR` writes `OUT_DIR/compare.json` and")
    strs_push(l, "`OUT_DIR/compare.md` and nothing outside `OUT_DIR`. Run time is `hyperfine --warmup 2 --runs 10")
    strs_push(l, "--shell=none` (3 runs for a program whose checking run took over 2 s); peak memory is the maximum")
    strs_push(l, "resident set size of one run from `/usr/bin/time -l`; build time is the median of three builds after")
    strs_push(l, "one unmeasured build, so each toolchain's caches of its own standard library are warm — Nazm builds")
    strs_push(l, "with `--no-cache`, every unit and the runtime compiled each time, and Go's build cache may reuse the")
    strs_push(l, "package itself; LOC counts non-blank lines that are not wholly a comment. *Since R1.5 (1.2)* Nazm's")
    strs_push(l, "build is two rows: `nazm build --opt-level 2` with `--no-cache` as above, and `(user cache warm)`,")
    strs_push(l, "whose user cache (D12) the unmeasured build fills and whose project store is emptied before every")
    strs_push(l, "build, so the program's own units are compiled each time and the runtime's and `@std`'s are reused —")
    strs_push(l, "what a new project costs once Nazm has built anything on the machine. Both caches are under")
    strs_push(l, "`OUT_DIR/work`; the tables below predate the second row, which *R1.5 1.2* measures.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Measured 2026-10-15 on an Apple M1 Pro, 10 cores, 32 GiB, macOS 27.2, with `nazm` 0.10.0 — the")
    strs_push(l, "release binary, built `--release` from `403aa68d` — and Apple clang 21.0.0, go 1.27.1, rustc 1.98.1,")
    strs_push(l, "Zig 0.17.0, OpenJDK 27, .NET SDK 10.0.402 (installed by `dotnet-install.sh` in `~/.dotnet`, which")
    strs_push(l, "the script finds), Python 3.14.8, Ruby 4.0.7, Node 24.13.0, Bun 1.3.10, Swift 6.4, Free Pascal")
    strs_push(l, "3.2.2, GNAT 16.1.0, hyperfine 2.0.0. Every program printed the expected output before it was timed.")
    strs_push(l, "The host is not controlled: thermal state and frequency scaling reach every number.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**hello**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| language | variant | LOC | run median (ms) | run min–max (ms) | peak RSS (KiB) | binary (KiB) | build median (ms) |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm | nazm build --opt-level 2 | 1 | 2.3 | 2.1–2.5 | 1744 | 35 | 176 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm | nazm run (interpreter) | 1 | 4.1 | 4.1–4.7 | 6480 | — | — |")
