    strs_push(l, "| Zig | zig build-exe -O ReleaseFast | 24 | 47.6 | 47.5–47.8 | 15280 | 404 | 8435 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Java | javac + java | 18 | 388.3 | 386.5–392.6 | 221808 | — | 361 |")
    strs_push(l, "| C# | dotnet build -c Release | 10 | 272.4 | 270.7–282.6 | 197296 | 122 | 766 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Python | python3 | 6 | 250.2 | 248.6–252.9 | 157328 | — | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| Ruby | ruby | 3 | 349.6 | 348.5–354.4 | 139712 | — | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| JavaScript | node | 8 | 377.0 | 373.8–387.4 | 304464 | — | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| TypeScript | bun | 8 | 292.2 | 289.6–296.9 | 243248 | — | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| Swift | swiftc -O | 11 | 484.3 | 481.9–486.6 | 183040 | 58 | 795 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Pascal | fpc -O3 | 31 | 590.9 | 589.5–592.7 | 38592 | 2558 | 2482 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Ada | gnatmake -O2 | 56 | 248.6 | 246.7–251.2 | 3040 | 696 | 3439 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Toolchains:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- nazm: nazm 0.10.0")
    strs_push(l, "- clang: Apple clang version 21.0.0 (clang-2100.3.34.2)")
    strs_push(l, "- go: go version go1.27.1 darwin/arm64")
    strs_push(l, "- rustc: rustc 1.98.1 (48a229cea 2026-09-01)")
    strs_push(l, "- zig: 0.17.0")
    strs_push(l, "- java: openjdk version \"27\" 2026-09-15")
    strs_push(l, "- dotnet: 10.0.402")
    strs_push(l, "- python3: Python 3.14.8")
    strs_push(l, "- ruby: ruby 4.0.7 (2026-09-15 revision 229531a6cf) +PRISM [arm64-darwin27]")
    strs_push(l, "- node: v24.13.0")
    strs_push(l, "- bun: 1.3.10")
    strs_push(l, "- swiftc: Apple Swift version 6.4 (swiftlang-6.4.0.34.1 clang-2100.3.34.1)")
    strs_push(l, "- fpc: 3.2.2")
    strs_push(l, "- gnat: GNATMAKE 16.1.0")
    strs_push(l, "- hyperfine: hyperfine 2.0.0")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it shows.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **`hello`**: every natively compiled program, Nazm's included, starts and exits in 1.9 to 2.9 ms;")
    strs_push(l, "  the runtimes with a virtual machine or interpreter take 11 to 42 ms. Nazm's native binary is")
    strs_push(l, "  35 KiB, beside C's 33 KiB and Go's 2.3 MiB.")
    strs_push(l, "- **`fib`**: Nazm's `-O2` build took 55.3 ms against 35.2 to 35.9 ms for C, C++, Rust and Zig,")
    strs_push(l, "  39.6 ms for Go, 44.7 ms for Swift, 59.9 ms for Java and 79.9 ms for C# — about 1.6 times C's time")
    strs_push(l, "  on this program (1.9 times before 5b.8: 67.0 ms in the 2026-10-14 run). Nazm's arithmetic is")
    strs_push(l, "  checked and every call checks the stack; C's, C++'s, Zig's (`ReleaseFast`) and Go's arithmetic is")
    strs_push(l, "  not checked. 5b.8 returns a function's failure in a register beside its result and lays the")
    strs_push(l, "  failure paths out cold (`docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.106, *The failure bit*); C's 35 ms also comes")
    strs_push(l, "  from clang turning one of the two recursive calls into a loop, which a checked `+` cannot allow.")
    strs_push(l, "  Ada's 13.3 ms is below C's, most likely because GCC transforms this recursion further (not")
    strs_push(l, "  inspected). The interpreter took 5.2 s, about four times CPython's 1.2 s.")
    strs_push(l, "- **`words`**: Nazm's `-O2` build took 188.0 ms (531 ms before 5b.9's work: `text_split` and")
    strs_push(l, "  `text_lines` without a slice per byte, the map remembering the entry `m[k]` found, its vectors")
    strs_push(l, "  read once a probe, a field read as an operand borrowed): faster than Ada (249 ms), Python")
    strs_push(l, "  (250 ms), C# (272 ms), TypeScript (292 ms), Ruby, JavaScript, Java, Swift and Pascal; about 2.5")
    strs_push(l, "  times C's 74 ms and 2.9 times Rust's 65 ms, slower than Zig (48 ms), Go (89 ms) and C++ (160 ms).")
    strs_push(l, "  It held 19 MiB at peak. The interpreter took 26 s and needs `--max-iterations` raised: under the")
    strs_push(l, "  default limit it stops with `N0402`.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Lines of code**: Nazm's three programs are 1, 6 and 19 lines — the same order as Rust's (3, 6,")
    strs_push(l, "  15) and C++'s (4, 5, 18), longer than Python's and Ruby's (`words` in 6 and 3), shorter than C's")
    strs_push(l, "  41 and Ada's 56 for `words`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it does not show.** Nothing about a language as a whole, another machine or a larger input;")
    strs_push(l, "three programs are not a suite, and no aggregate score is derived. Idiomatic programs differ in")
    strs_push(l, "algorithm and library: the `words` column compares each language's ordinary way of writing the")
    strs_push(l, "task, not one algorithm.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## R1.5, D11: `nazm run` compiles — measured 2026-10-15")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm run` builds with Cranelift (`--opt-level 2`'s `speed`) and runs the executable; `nazm run")
    strs_push(l, "--interpret` is the interpreter that `nazm run` was until this change, unchanged. Measured on")
    strs_push(l, "`bench/compare/nazm/fib.nz` (`fib(35)`) with a release build of the change, on the Apple M1 Pro")
    strs_push(l, "above, `hyperfine 2.0.0 -N`, five runs after one warm-up:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| command | mean | min–max |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm run --interpret fib.nz` (before: what `nazm run` did) | 5.239 s | 5.232–5.243 s |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm run fib.nz`, the project's object store warm | 0.173 s | 0.169–0.184 s |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm run fib.nz`, `.nazm/` removed before each run | 0.741 s | 0.729–0.755 s |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Of the warm 173 ms, the executable itself takes 85 ms and the build — load, check, lower, Cranelift,")
    strs_push(l, "link — about 88 ms; a warm `nazm build --backend cranelift` of the same file takes 85 ms at")
    strs_push(l, "`--opt-level 0` and at `2`, so the faster code costs nothing in the build here. The cold row compiles")
    strs_push(l, "the runtime with `clang` each time; caching that per user (R1.5, D12) is what it waits for. Peak")
    strs_push(l, "memory rises from 6.7 MiB to 38 MiB: the compiler's, not the program's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## R1.5 D14: dead-stripping, measured (2026-10-15)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What changed (`docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.114): a hosted executable is linked with `-dead_strip` on")
    strs_push(l, "macOS and iOS, and with `--gc-sections` over `-ffunction-sections -fdata-sections` objects on Linux")
    strs_push(l, "and Android, so what nothing reachable from the entry calls — an `@std` function the program never")
    strs_push(l, "names, a runtime part only another service uses — is left out.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The executables of `bench/compare/nazm/*.nz`, built `--no-cache` with the release binary before")
    strs_push(l, "(`dd362e77`) and after the change, on an Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2, Apple clang 21.0.0; bytes:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| program | backend | `-O0` before | `-O0` after | `-O2` before | `-O2` after |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| hello | LLVM | 35,472 | 34,432 | 35,648 | 34,400 |")
    strs_push(l, "| hello | Cranelift | 116,304 | 34,768 | 116,304 | 34,768 |")
    strs_push(l, "| fib | LLVM | 36,296 | 34,920 | 36,328 | 34,904 |")
    strs_push(l, "| fib | Cranelift | 116,432 | 35,344 | 116,416 | 35,312 |")
    strs_push(l, "| words | LLVM | 125,056 | 70,720 | 105,728 | 61,184 |")
    strs_push(l, "| words | Cranelift | 197,232 | 75,168 | 197,216 | 74,816 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`words`, which imports four standard modules, lost 42% at `-O2`; a Cranelift build, which links")
    strs_push(l, "every runtime part, lost 62 to 70%; `hello` and `fib` are now within 1 KiB of each other under both")
    strs_push(l, "backends, the rest being the Mach-O headers and page alignment. Every program printed the expected")
    strs_push(l, "output. Linux (`--gc-sections`) was not measured on this host: its arguments are covered by")
    strs_push(l, "`backend::tests`, and its sizes are for the contained gate to record.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## R1.5 1.2: Nazm's build, uncached and from a warm user cache, measured (2026-10-15)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`fib.nz` and `words.nz` from `bench/compare/nazm/`, `--opt-level 2`, with the release binary of")
    strs_push(l, "`efde17f9`, `hyperfine -N --runs 15 --warmup 2`, interleaved per program, the project store emptied")
    strs_push(l, "before every run (`--prepare`). Four builds: `--no-cache` (the comparison's first row); a fresh")
    strs_push(l, "project with the user cache off (`NAZM_USER_CACHE_DIR=`, what every new project paid before D12); a")
    strs_push(l, "fresh project with the user cache warm (the comparison's second row, after D12); and, for")
    strs_push(l, "reference, a rebuild with both stores warm. Medians, in ms:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| program | `--no-cache` | fresh project, before D12 | fresh project, user cache warm | both stores warm |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| fib | 237.5 | 292.3 | 209.3 | 109.3 |")
    strs_push(l, "| words | 1562.6 | 1691.3 | 950.4 | 107.6 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A new project's `words` now builds in 56% of the time it took before D12 (39% less than")
    strs_push(l, "`--no-cache`), since its four `@std` modules and the runtime are no longer compiled; `fib`, whose")
    strs_push(l, "only shared unit is the runtime, saves 83 ms against the fresh build and 28 ms against")
    strs_push(l, "`--no-cache`, the rest of its time being its own unit, the entry, the link and the `clang -###`")
    strs_push(l, "probe a cached build makes. The host was loaded by other work throughout (load average 8 to 20 on")
    strs_push(l, "10 cores), so the absolute numbers are above the 0.10.0 run's 207 and 1097 ms for `--no-cache`; the")
    strs_push(l, "columns were measured interleaved, so their ratios are the result. `python3 bench/compare/compare.py`")
    strs_push(l, "on the same host and hour gave the two Nazm rows as 297 and 219 ms (`fib`) and 1564 and 1289 ms")
    strs_push(l, "(`words`), median of three each; its output was checked for both.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## R1.5 3.3: word frequency without a split list, measured (2026-10-15)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What changed: `for w in s.split(sep)` builds no list — it is lowered through `text_split_end` and")
    strs_push(l, "`text_split_next`, which find each piece as `text_split` does (`8e871bb7`) — and a one-byte")
    strs_push(l, "separator has its own loop, whose only check each step is the bound (`R1.5 3.3`, the commit after")
    strs_push(l, "it). Before that change, a profile over twenty million words put 20% of the time in allocating and")
    strs_push(l, "freeing each line's list (`openspec/changes/performance-leadership/design.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`bench/compare/nazm/words.nz` on the comparison's input (`gen_words.py`), built `--opt-level 2`")
    strs_push(l, "(LLVM) by release binaries of each tree, `hyperfine -N --warmup 3 --runs 15`, interleaved, on an")
    strs_push(l, "Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2, Apple clang 21.0.0, with other work running; every run printed")
    strs_push(l, "`words.expected`:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| tree | mean | ± σ | peak memory |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| before (`c86f2f81`) | 189.0 ms | 1.9 ms | 19.4 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| no list (`8e871bb7`) | 151.0 ms | 3.3 ms | 19.2 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| and the one-byte loop | 143.1 ms | 1.6 ms | 19.2 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "24% less time; memory unchanged, since each word was already a view of its line. Linking every")
    strs_push(l, "unit with LTO (`clang -flto`) was tried and gave 3.4% more, so the remaining cost is in the")
    strs_push(l, "operations — the byte scan, the map's probe and update, the string comparison — not in the calls")
    strs_push(l, "between modules. C (73.9 ms) and Rust (65.0 ms) from the 0.10.0 run are 1.9× and 2.2× ahead.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## R1.5: the comparison re-run, measured (2026-10-15)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`python3 bench/compare/compare.py` with the release binary of `71858468` (R1.5 D1–D12, D14 and 3.3),")
    strs_push(l, "on a quiet host — no other build, test or agent running — with `DOTNET_ROOT` set so C# is measured.")
    strs_push(l, "`bench/compare/nazm/words.nz` is now ten lines: no `use` (D9) and `counts.top(10)` (D10) in place of")
    strs_push(l, "sorting every key, which is also faster (140 → 132 ms). Where Nazm stands: first or tied on")
    strs_push(l, "`hello`'s run time, lines and (with C) size; `fib` behind C, C++, Rust, Zig, Go, Swift and Ada")
    strs_push(l, "(Ada's GCC build takes 13 ms, an outlier worth studying); word frequency behind Zig, Rust, C and")
    strs_push(l, "Go, ahead of C++, C#, Java, Swift, Python, Ruby, JavaScript, TypeScript, Pascal and Ada, and the")
    strs_push(l, "shortest compiled program. The target (`openspec/changes/performance-leadership`) is not met.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Host: Apple M1 Pro, 10 CPUs, 32 GiB, macOS 27.2 (Darwin 27.2.0, arm64); 2026-10-15. Not controlled.")
