    strs_push(l, "## R1.5 3.1: the small-block heap, measured (2026-10-16)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What changed (`docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.119, runtime ABI 39): a hosted executable that calls no C")
    strs_push(l, "allocates through the runtime's small-block heap — per-thread lists of freed blocks of up to 512")
    strs_push(l, "bytes, at most 64 per size class — in place of C's `malloc` and `free`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Three programs, each built `--opt-level 2` (LLVM) by release binaries of `24c09da6` (before) and")
    strs_push(l, "this change (after), `hyperfine -N --warmup 3 --runs 15`, interleaved, on an Apple M1 Pro, macOS")
    strs_push(l, "27.2, Apple clang 21.0.0, load average 4 to 7 from other agents; every pair printed the same")
    strs_push(l, "output, and `words` printed `words.expected`:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| program | before | after | peak memory before → after |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| a loop building a string and a one-element list 5,000,000 times, one thread | 284.7 ± 4.5 ms | 115.4 ± 1.4 ms (2.5× faster) | 1.8 → 1.7 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| the same loop, Cranelift (`--backend cranelift`), ten runs | 393.3 ± 7.4 ms | 306.0 ± 1.6 ms (−22%) | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| four tasks each building 1,000,000 strings (thread-local lists) | 465.6 ± 58.7 ms | 390.1 ± 23.2 ms (−16%, noisy) | 2.1 → 2.0 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| `bench/compare/nazm/words.nz` | 118.7 ± 4.6 ms | 117.3 ± 2.3 ms (no change) | 19.2 → 19.2 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A profile of the first loop before the change put about 95% of its samples in `malloc` and `free`.")
    strs_push(l, "A program of tasks gains less because its lists are `thread_local`, whose every access on macOS is")
    strs_push(l, "a call through the thread-local descriptor (a plain-global prototype of the same loop measured")
    strs_push(l, "118 ms, a thread-local one 208 ms). Word frequency does not allocate in its loop since 3.3 —")
    strs_push(l, "each word is a view of its line — so the allocator cannot speed it; its remaining time is the")
    strs_push(l, "byte scan, the hash and the map's probe (3.2, 3.4). Memory: each small block carries a 16-byte")
    strs_push(l, "header, and a thread keeps at most 64 freed blocks per class (at most about 270 KiB a thread);")
    strs_push(l, "a test holds a producer and a consumer on two threads to about 2 MiB, where an unbounded list")
    strs_push(l, "reached 51 MiB. The x86_64 macOS build (under Rosetta) printed what the arm64 build printed, and the")
    strs_push(l, "Windows build links with MinGW-w64; the Windows host was down, so no Windows run is claimed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## R1.5 3.4: whole-program optimisation, measured (2026-10-16)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What changed (`docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.120): an `-O2` LLVM build for macOS compiles every unit to")
    strs_push(l, "bitcode and links with ThinLTO, so the runtime and the standard library are optimised with the")
    strs_push(l, "program; the link keeps ThinLTO's cache in the project's `.nazm/lto`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`bench/compare/nazm/*.nz` and the allocation loop of *R1.5 3.1*, built `--no-cache --opt-level 2`")
    strs_push(l, "by release binaries of `0deab3ef` (before, with 3.1) and this change (after), `hyperfine -N")
    strs_push(l, "--warmup 3 --runs 15`, interleaved, on an Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2, Apple clang 21.0.0, load")
    strs_push(l, "average about 8 from other agents; every pair printed the same output, `words` printed")
    strs_push(l, "`words.expected`:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| program | before | after | binary before → after |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `hello` | 2.1 ± 0.1 ms | 2.1 ± 0.1 ms | 51,312 → 34,648 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| `fib` | 44.8 ± 0.1 ms | 44.7 ± 0.1 ms | 51,976 → 35,208 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| `words` | 114.1 ± 0.3 ms | 103.6 ± 0.4 ms (−9.2%) | 76,880 → 86,728 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| `primes 1` | 171.7 ± 0.2 ms | 173.0 ± 0.2 ms (+0.7%) | 72,208 → 71,040 B |")
    strs_push(l, "| the allocation loop | 114.2 ± 0.1 ms | 81.0 ± 2.6 ms (−29%) | 51,600 → 34,776 B |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The build, `hyperfine -N --runs 10`: `--no-cache` `fib` 251.8 → 234.7 ms and `words` 960.7 →")
    strs_push(l, "840.2 ms (a bitcode object is cheaper to make than a machine object, and the link does the code")
    strs_push(l, "generation once); a rebuild with the project store warm, `fib` 86.6 → 88.2 ms and `words` 110.3 →")
    strs_push(l, "116.6 ms (+5.7%), the link's ThinLTO cache answering what it optimised before. A first attempt with")
    strs_push(l, "full LTO (`-flto=full`, no cache) measured `words` −5.5% and a warm rebuild 2.4× slower, which is why")
    strs_push(l, "it is ThinLTO with a cache. `fib` and `primes` are one unit's work and do not change; `words` is")
    strs_push(l, "now 1.6× C's 74 ms of the 0.10.0 run, from 1.8×. Not measured: Windows, which keeps per-unit")
    strs_push(l, "optimisation (MinGW's linker reads no bitcode). Two builds of the same program differ in their")
    strs_push(l, "`LC_UUID` and signature, before this change as after it (`ld64` hashes the temporary directory's")
    strs_push(l, "path into the UUID): byte-for-byte reproducibility is 7.2's to settle.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Multicore: the parallel workload and the pool's default, measured (2026-10-15)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The comparison's first parallel program (`bench/compare/{nazm,c,go,rust}/primes.*`, performance")
    strs_push(l, "leadership's multicore focus): the primes below 3,000,000 counted by trial division, printing")
    strs_push(l, "216816, on W workers — Nazm tasks in a `scope` sending their counts on a channel, C pthreads, Go")
    strs_push(l, "goroutines on a buffered channel, Rust `std::thread::scope`. The numbers are dealt in blocks of")
    strs_push(l, "1,000, block b to worker b mod W. The first draft dealt single numbers (n ≡ w mod W); with W even")
    strs_push(l, "that gives every odd number, so every prime but 2, to the odd workers, and half the workers have")
    strs_push(l, "nothing to do in every language — so it measured the workload, not the languages.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What was wrong in Nazm.** A first quick run of that draft showed Nazm at W = 8 using about two")
    strs_push(l, "processors (197% CPU). Two causes, one the draft's and one the runtime's: the draft left four of")
    strs_push(l, "eight tasks idle; and the pool started **four workers on every machine** (`NAZM_WORKERS`'s default")
    strs_push(l, "in `nz.pool_start`), where `architecture.md` §7.84 wrote the processors online. Tasks are placed")
    strs_push(l, "round robin and pinned (§7.84: no stealing, no preemption), so the four busy tasks of W = 8 fell")
    strs_push(l, "on two of the four workers. `spawn` itself never blocks: it queues the task on its worker and")
    strs_push(l, "returns, `main` is not a task, and a channel or join wait parks the task and frees its worker —")
    strs_push(l, "none of these was a cause. The fix (runtime ABI 35): the default is the processors online")
    strs_push(l, "(`nz.os_cpus`, from each target's `stack` unit), at most 64, four only where the system will not")
    strs_push(l, "say; `NAZM_WORKERS` still overrides it. Placement, pinning, and every output, ending and memory")
    strs_push(l, "report are unchanged (the scheduler, select, memory, runtime and FFI tests pass).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Measured.** Apple M1 Pro (8 performance and 2 efficiency cores), 32 GiB, macOS 27.2; Apple clang")
    strs_push(l, "21.0.0 `-O2`, Go 1.27.2, rustc 1.98.1 `-C opt-level=3`, Nazm release from `8870ec9c` and this change,")
    strs_push(l, "`--opt-level 2`. The host was shared with other agents' builds and tests throughout — load averages")
    strs_push(l, "between 17 and 81 on ten processors — so only **relative** scaling is reported, each language")
    strs_push(l, "against its own W = 1, and the languages were run interleaved.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Three interleaved rounds (each W, each language, `hyperfine -N --warmup 3 --runs 15`; the median of")
    strs_push(l, "the three rounds' medians, and in brackets the median CPU use over wall time — at W = 1 the load")
    strs_push(l, "left each process 81–86% of a processor):")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| language | W=1 | W=2 | W=4 | W=8 | W=10 | W=16 |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| C (pthreads) | 1.00× | 1.74× | 3.45× | 4.09× | 5.51× (489%) | 5.35× |")
    strs_push(l, "| Rust (std threads) | 1.00× | 1.63× | 3.24× | 4.38× | 5.04× (493%) | 5.67× |")
    strs_push(l, "| Go (goroutines) | 1.00× | 1.93× | 3.10× | 3.67× | 4.73× (430%) | 4.52× |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm (the pool, default workers) | 1.00× | 1.94× | 3.19× | 4.37× | 4.89× (461%) | 4.91× |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm, `NAZM_WORKERS=4` (the old default) | 1.00× | 1.84× | 2.90× | 3.47× | 3.27× (280%) | 3.68× |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm, n ≡ w mod W and four workers (the first quick run) | 1.00× | 0.92× | 1.89× | 2.15× | 2.09× (167%) | 2.13× |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Then `python3 bench/compare/compare.py NAZM OUT --runs 10 --only primes`, at a lower load (17–23):")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| language | lines | W=1 | W=2 | W=4 | W=8 | W=10 |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm `--opt-level 2` | 43 | 173.1 ms | 1.91× | 3.81× | 5.15× | 4.90× |")
    strs_push(l, "| C `clang -O2` | 33 | 176.7 ms | 1.96× | 3.83× | 4.93× | 5.33× |")
    strs_push(l, "| Go | 46 | 144.6 ms | 1.94× | 3.70× | 4.69× | 4.70× |")
    strs_push(l, "| Rust `-C opt-level=3` | 31 | 194.6 ms | 2.00× | 3.89× | 4.98× | 5.25× |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Read with the load in mind: no language reached the eight performance cores' 8×, since other work")
    strs_push(l, "held the processors; within that, Nazm's tasks now scale with C's, Rust's and Go's threads (all four")
    strs_push(l, "within the rounds' spread of each other at every W), where the old default capped it near 3.5×")
    strs_push(l, "whatever W. Nazm's one-worker time is C's (173 against 177 ms): the checked arithmetic costs little")
    strs_push(l, "in a loop of divisions. Not claimed: any lead — the spread between rounds is larger than the")
    strs_push(l, "differences between languages — nor anything at W above the processors, where a pinned task cannot")
    strs_push(l, "move to an idle worker (no stealing, §7.84's non-goal) and the blocks dealt round robin are what")
    strs_push(l, "keeps the workers even.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Concurrency: the baseline against Go's goroutines, measured (performance leadership 6.1, 2026-10-16)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Where Nazm's tasks stand against Go's goroutines before any scheduler work (6.2–6.5). Measurement")
    strs_push(l, "only: no scheduler, channel or stack code changed. Each workload is written once in Nazm and once in")
    strs_push(l, "Go, idiomatically, under `bench/compare/{nazm,go}/`: `spawn` (1,000,000 tasks in one `scope`, each")
    strs_push(l, "adding 1 to a shared atomic, against goroutines and a `sync.WaitGroup`), `pingpong` (100,000 round")
    strs_push(l, "trips between two tasks over two channels of capacity 1), `fanin` (8 producers each sending 125,000")
    strs_push(l, "integers into one channel of capacity 1,024, one consumer summing), `idle` (100,000 tasks blocked on")
    strs_push(l, "one channel at once; peak resident memory against the same program at 1,000), and `httpd` (an")
    strs_push(l, "HTTP/1.1 server answering every `GET /` with `200 hello` — `@std/http`'s `http_serve_conn` in a task")
    strs_push(l, "per connection, against `net/http`) under one shared load generator, `go/httpload.go` (`wrk` and")
    strs_push(l, "`hey` are not installed: 64 keep-alive connections, one second's warm-up, 10 s counted).")
    strs_push(l, "`bench/compare/concurrency.sh NAZM OUT --wait` builds both, checks they print the same answers")
    strs_push(l, "(`spawn` 1000000, `pingpong` 5000050000, `fanin` 499999500000, `primes` 216816), waits until the")
    strs_push(l, "1-minute load is below 2 with no cargo, nextest or rustc running, then measures.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Host and builds.** Apple M1 Pro (8 performance and 2 efficiency cores), 32 GiB, macOS 27.2; Go")
    strs_push(l, "1.27.2 `go build`; Nazm release from `b98b2f73`, `--opt-level 2` (LLVM), the default scheduler — the")
    strs_push(l, "pool, one worker per processor, 256 KiB guarded task stacks (architecture §7.84, N106).")
    strs_push(l, "`hyperfine -N --warmup 2`, 5 runs for `spawn` and 10 for the rest, Go and Nazm in one invocation.")
    strs_push(l, "Two runs, each begun below load 2 with no other agent's build or suite running (the second at")
    strs_push(l, "1.89, and no cargo, nextest or rustc at its end); the later loads in the table are the benchmark's")
    strs_push(l, "own threads — ten processors busy in `spawn`, the HTTP server and its 64 clients — not other work.")
    strs_push(l, "In the first run another agent's suite started during the second HTTP round, so that run's later")
    strs_push(l, "rounds and its `primes` are not used; the second run supplies them. Where the two runs agree within")
    strs_push(l, "their spread one figure is given; otherwise both, first; second.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| workload | Go | Nazm | Nazm against Go | load before |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| spawn 1,000,000 tasks, wall | 275 ± 28 ms; 265 ± 15 ms | 3,645 ± 15 ms; 3,691 ± 48 ms | 13.2×; 14.0× slower | 1.94; 1.89 |")
    strs_push(l, "| spawn 1,000,000 tasks, peak RSS | 12.5 MiB | 244 MiB | 19.5× more | |")
    strs_push(l, "| ping-pong, per round trip | 0.32 µs | 4.37 µs | 13.9× slower | 2.94; 3.30 |")
    strs_push(l, "| fan-in, 1,000,000 values from 8 producers | 68.1 ± 1.1 ms; 67.6 ± 0.9 ms | 445 ± 7 ms; 455 ± 10 ms | 6.5×; 6.7× slower | 2.87; 3.35 |")
    strs_push(l, "| memory per blocked task (100,000 against 1,000) | 2.7 KiB | 17.4 KiB | 6.5× more | 3.44; 3.41 |")
    strs_push(l, "| HTTP/1.1, 64 connections, 10 s rounds (first run's one; second run's three) | 93,630; 96,529–97,155 requests/s | 80,735; 80,848–81,626 requests/s | 0.86×; 0.84× | 3.4–14.7 |")
    strs_push(l, "| HTTP server RSS under that load | 21.7 MiB | 11.1 MiB | 0.51× | |")
    strs_push(l, "| primes, W = 1 (second run) | 144.3 ± 0.3 ms | 171.6 ± 0.3 ms | 1.19× slower | 15.3 |")
    strs_push(l, "| primes, W = 10 (second run) | 26.4 ± 1.4 ms | 29.5 ± 2.5 ms | 1.12× slower | 14.3 |")
    strs_push(l, "| peak RSS of a small concurrent program (`pingpong`, `fanin`) | 4.3–4.9 MiB | 1.9–2.1 MiB | 0.44× | |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the numbers say.**")
    strs_push(l, "- **Starting a task is the largest gap, 13×,** and the same cause is the memory: each task `mmap`s")
    strs_push(l, "  its 256 KiB stack and guard page at `spawn` and `munmap`s it when it ends (§7.84) — system time")
    strs_push(l, "  dominates a run (on an earlier, loaded trial 10.4 s of system against 3.7 s of user time) — where a")
    strs_push(l, "  goroutine starts on a small stack from Go's own allocator. A blocked task holds 17.4 KiB resident,")
    strs_push(l, "  a goroutine 2.7 KiB. This is 6.2's subject: growable or stackless task frames.")
    strs_push(l, "- **A channel hand-off between tasks costs 4.4 µs, Go's 0.3 µs.** A wait parks the task under the")
    strs_push(l, "  channel's lock and the sender's wake broadcasts to every waiter (§7.84); tasks are pinned round")
    strs_push(l, "  robin with no stealing, so ping-pong's two tasks sit on two workers and every hand-off crosses")
    strs_push(l, "  threads. Fan-in, 6.5×, is the same cost with eight producers on one lock. 6.3 and 6.4's subject:")
    strs_push(l, "  work stealing, and lock-free channels.")
    strs_push(l, "- **HTTP is near Go: 0.84–0.86× its requests per second at half its memory.** Here a request is")
    strs_push(l, "  parsing and writing within one connection's task, not hand-offs between tasks. The load generator")
    strs_push(l, "  shared the ten processors with the server, as `wrk` would.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Parallel CPU work scales like Go's:** one task's arithmetic is 19% slower (the checked")
    strs_push(l, "  overflow of the inner loop), ten tasks 12% (*R1.5 5.1* has the job against C and Rust as well).")
    strs_push(l, "- **A small concurrent program's memory is Nazm's:** 2 MiB against Go's 4–5 MiB.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What each side guarantees — the two sides do not pay for the same thing.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Nazm | Go |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Data races | refused at compile time: nothing shared and mutable unsynchronised reaches a task (`N0321`) | allowed; found at run time only under `-race`, and only when the race happens |")
    strs_push(l, "| A task outliving its parent | refused at compile time: every task is joined by its `scope` (`N0320`) | allowed: a goroutine no one waits for leaks silently |")
    strs_push(l, "| Authority | a task reaches only the capabilities passed to it | any goroutine may open files, sockets and processes |")
    strs_push(l, "| Integer overflow | fails the program | wraps silently |")
    strs_push(l, "| Preemption | none: a task computing without waiting holds its worker (§7.84) | asynchronous since Go 1.14 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Work stealing | none: tasks pinned round robin | yes |")
    strs_push(l, "| `select` | `chan_select_of` over channels of one element type | over any channels |")
    strs_push(l, "| Deadlock | not detected | detected at run time when every goroutine is asleep |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Not claimed: any lead in concurrency. On this baseline Go leads task start-up and every hand-off by")
    strs_push(l, "an order of magnitude; Nazm leads memory for small programs and for an HTTP server, and is within")
    strs_push(l, "16% of Go's HTTP throughput and 12–19% of its parallel CPU time, with two compile-time")
    strs_push(l, "guarantees Go does not give.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## R1.5 5.1: the comparison with safety-equivalent rows and a checks column, measured (2026-10-16)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`python3 bench/compare/compare.py NAZM OUT` (10 runs, hyperfine), now with a second build of each")
    strs_push(l, "compiled language that can carry Nazm's checks — Rust `-C overflow-checks=on`, Zig `ReleaseSafe`,")
    strs_push(l, "C and C++ with `-fsanitize=address,undefined` — and a `checks` column saying what each row checks")
    strs_push(l, "and when (`SAFETY` in `compare.py`). Same host as the concurrency baseline; Nazm release from")
    strs_push(l, "`b98b2f73` (3.5's streaming `file_lines` in `words.nz`); started at load 2.11 with no other")
    strs_push(l, "agent's build or suite running, and none ran during it (sampled every 15 s); the load stayed")
    strs_push(l, "between 2.1 and 4.1, the comparison's own builds and parallel runs. Medians, in milliseconds; the")
    strs_push(l, "full tables are in the run's `compare.md`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| workload | Nazm (always checked) | Rust, overflow checks | Zig ReleaseSafe | C, ASan + UBSan | Swift `-O` | C `-O2`, unchecked | Rust `-O3` | Go |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| hello | 1.9 | 2.1 | 2.4 | 14.4 | 1.9 | 1.8 | 2.2 | 2.9 |")
    strs_push(l, "| fib(35) | 44.1 | 44.6 | 44.7 | 56.9 | 44.9 | 35.2 | 35.6 | 39.5 |")
    strs_push(l, "| words, time | 115.6 | 66.8 | 53.6 | 112.2 | 479.3 | 73.6 | 66.0 | 88.6 |")
    strs_push(l, "| words, peak RSS (MiB) | 8.7 | 14.9 | 14.9 | 32.1 | 178.8 | 15.3 | 14.9 | 61.5 |")
    strs_push(l, "| primes, W = 1 | 171.7 | 166.9 | — | 198.1 | — | 176.1 | 191.2 | 144.3 |")
    strs_push(l, "| primes, W = 8 (speed-up) | 23.8 (7.21×) | 23.3 (7.16×) | — | 38.3 (5.17×) | — | 24.5 (7.20×) | 26.3 (7.28×) | 21.4 (6.73×) |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Read with the checks column.** Against the languages that check what Nazm checks, Nazm is")
    strs_push(l, "first or tied on `hello` and `fib` (44.1 ms against 44.6, 44.7 and 44.9 — within the runs' spread, so")
    strs_push(l, "tied with Rust, Zig and Swift, and 22% ahead of sanitized C), and the unchecked rows' lead on `fib`")
    strs_push(l, "— C 35.2, Rust 35.6 — is the cost of the overflow checks, as the checked Rust and Zig rows show.")
    strs_push(l, "On `words` it is behind checked Rust (1.7×) and Zig (2.2×) and 3% behind sanitized C, while using")
    strs_push(l, "the least memory of any compiled row but C++ and Ada (8.7 MiB; 19.1 MiB before 3.5's streaming")
    strs_push(l, "`file_lines`). On the parallel job, Nazm's one-task time is between checked Rust's and C's, and it")
    strs_push(l, "scales with them (7.2× at eight workers). Not claimed: a lead where the spread overlaps; any lead")
    strs_push(l, "on `words` time.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## The compilers' growth, phase by phase, measured (performance leadership 7.1–7.2, 2026-10-17)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Both compilers, every phase each exposes, on generated programs of n, 2n, 4n and 8n")
    strs_push(l, "(`bench/complexity/gen.py`, timed by `bench/complexity/measure.py`): **lines** (functions of ten")
    strs_push(l, "lines — a loop, a branch, a call — n = 2,000 lines, so 2,104 to 16,104), **nest** (one function of")
    strs_push(l, "`if`s nested 25 to 200 deep; the parser refuses more than 512 levels, `N0102`), **chain** (one")
    strs_push(l, "expression of 60 to 480 terms joined by `+`, ten to a line) and **modules** (10 to 80 modules of")
    strs_push(l, "ten functions, `main` importing each). Phases: the Rust `nazm` — lexing and parsing through")
    strs_push(l, "`toolchain/frontend-tests/refdump` (`tokens`, `tree`), `check --no-cache` and `check` with its")
    strs_push(l, "cache warm, `core-ir`, `mir`, `lir` (each runs the phases before it), and `build --timings` (load,")
    strs_push(l, "front end, MIR, LIR, IR generation, native compile, link) uncached, warm (the object cache) and at")
    strs_push(l, "`--opt-level 2`; the Nazm-written compiler — `compiler/tokens.nz`, `tree.nz` and `diagnose.nz`")
    strs_push(l, "(`--syntax`, the whole check, `--core`) built as `toolchain/frontend-tests/run.sh` builds them,")
    strs_push(l, "`toolchain/pipeline` (`mir`, `lir`, reading `nazm core-ir --json --with-sources`) and")
    strs_push(l, "`toolchain/codegen`'s `nzcg` (reading `nazm lir --ops`), built as their `run.sh` build them.")
    strs_push(l, "Resolution and checking are one pass in both compilers and no option times them apart.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Host and method.** Apple M1 Pro (8 performance and 2 efficiency cores), 32 GiB, macOS 27.2, Apple")
    strs_push(l, "clang 21.0.0; release `nazm` from `e9d9fa40`, the drivers built by it. Each point is the median of 5")
    strs_push(l, "runs after one warm-up (σ under 2% of the median almost everywhere), peak memory the largest")
    strs_push(l, "`maximum resident set size` of `/usr/bin/time -l` over the runs; every measurement waited for a")
    strs_push(l, "1-minute load below 2 with no cargo, rustc or nextest running: 360 measurements, begun at load")
    strs_push(l, "1.12–1.91 (2.46 at most after one). The growth exponent is log2(t(8n)/t(4n)) after subtracting the")
    strs_push(l, "same phase on a program of a few lines; above 1.25 is flagged. A phase whose whole range lies")
    strs_push(l, "within 3 ms is reported as flat (below resolution).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| phase | lines 2,104 → 16,104 | exp. | nest 25 → 200 | exp. | chain 60 → 480 | exp. | modules 10 → 80 | exp. |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | ---: | --- | ---: | --- | ---: | --- | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Rust** `check --no-cache` | 20.0 → 82.8 ms, 15 → 69 MiB | 1.03 | 11.4 → 14.5 ms | 1.17 | flat (11.7 → 12.7 ms) | — | 17.0 → 57.5 ms | 1.06 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Rust `check`, cache warm | 20.2 → 85.6 ms | 1.05 | 11.6 → 14.8 ms | 1.53 | flat | — | 17.3 → 58.2 ms | 1.05 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Rust `core-ir` | 31.1 → 168.0 ms, 21 → 117 MiB | 1.01 | 11.8 → 23.0 ms, 10 → 25 MiB | **1.53** | 12.1 → 19.7 ms, 9 → 19 MiB | 1.21 | 22.5 → 100.0 ms | 1.02 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Rust `mir` | 25.8 → 126.2 ms | 1.02 | 11.6 → 15.5 ms | 1.25 | 12.2 → 46.6 ms, **11 → 97 MiB** | **1.78** | 20.2 → 79.6 ms | 1.01 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Rust `lir` | 44.8 → 253.8 ms | 1.00 | 12.2 → 18.4 ms | 1.18 | 14.4 → 56.5 ms, 12 → 100 MiB | **1.49** | 28.5 → 142.0 ms | 1.02 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Rust `build --no-cache` (LLVM, `-O0`) | 295 → 976 ms, 41 → 162 MiB | 0.97 | 181 → 199 ms | 1.23 | 190 → 265 ms, 38 → 103 MiB | **1.31** | 522 → 2,985 ms | 1.01 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Rust `build`, warm | 127 → 371 ms | 0.99 | 89 → 98 ms | flat | 89 → 136 ms | **1.61** | 114 → 252 ms | 1.01 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Rust `build --opt-level 2 --no-cache` | 942 → 4,908 ms | 1.16 | 199 → 214 ms | 1.34 | 204 → 269 ms | **1.39** | 649 → 3,715 ms | 0.99 |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Nazm** lexer (`tokens.nz`) | 16.4 → 82.8 ms, 10 → 50 MiB | 0.98 | flat | — | flat | — | flat (`main.nz` only) | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm parser (`tree.nz`, with its dump) | 41.9 → 270.5 ms, 26 → 162 MiB | 0.97 | 7.6 → 23.3 ms, 4 → 24 MiB | **1.50** | 9.2 → 18.8 ms, 4 → 18 MiB | 1.13 (memory 1.52) | flat | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm `diagnose --syntax` | 23.3 → 130.0 ms | 0.94 | 6.9 → 11.9 ms | 1.14 | flat | — | flat | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm check (`diagnose`) | 85.3 → 598.8 ms, 15 → 84 MiB | 1.13 | 22.0 → 44.1 ms, 8 → 18 MiB | **1.41** | 22.8 → 32.8 ms | 0.99 | 51.5 → 280.2 ms | 1.06 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm Core IR (`diagnose --core`) | 362 → 2,640 ms, **71 → 471 MiB** | 1.02 | 30.9 → 167.3 ms, 12 → 126 MiB | **1.49** | 31.5 → 143.0 ms, **15 → 123 MiB** | **1.34** | 180 → 1,306 ms, 37 → 241 MiB | 1.03 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm MIR (`pipeline mir`) | 275 → 2,018 ms, 21 → 137 MiB | 1.00 | refused from 100 deep | — | refused at 480 terms | — | 131 → 1,003 ms | 1.02 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm LIR (`pipeline lir`) | **579 → 12,943 ms** | **1.69** | refused from 100 deep | — | refused at 480 terms | — | 180 → 1,405 ms | 1.03 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm code generator (`nzcg`) | 108 → 780 ms, 14 → 79 MiB | 1.18 | **8.9 → 233.9 ms** | **2.67** | 12.8 → 159.1 ms, 4 → 21 MiB | **1.70** | 49 → 337 ms | 1.04 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Where the Rust build's time goes (`--timings`, medians; lines 16,104 / modules 80): load 37.3 / 26.5")
    strs_push(l, "ms, front end 43.4 / 28.9, MIR 11.9 / 6.8, LIR 0.6 / 0.5, IR generation 144.8 / 68.5, native")
    strs_push(l, "compile 646.5 / 2,778.5 uncached and 37.9 / 53.6 warm, link 55.6 / 63.5. On a program of a few")
    strs_push(l, "lines: load 3.3, front end 0.5, native compile 116.8 (uncached; the runtime's units) or 24.6 (warm),")
    strs_push(l, "link 49.5 — **a warm build of a small program is 78 ms, of which 74 ms is the native compile's")
    strs_push(l, "cache and the link.** Many modules cost far more native compile than one large module (2.8 s for")
    strs_push(l, "80 modules of 100 lines against 0.65 s for one of 16,000: a clang process per module), linearly.")
    strs_push(l, "`check` with its cache warm costs what an uncached check costs on these single-package programs.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Flagged: worse than n log n, with the input that shows it.**")
    strs_push(l, "1. **The Nazm pipeline's LIR, quadratic in a module's size** (exponent 1.69, 0.58 → 12.9 s on the")
    strs_push(l, "   lines program, where its MIR is linear, 2.0 s). A sample at 16,104 lines puts 2,374 of about")
    strs_push(l, "   2,900 samples in `toolchain/pipeline/ops.nz`'s `line_col`, which finds a position's line and")
    strs_push(l, "   column by scanning the source from its first byte for every position asked — positions × file")
    strs_push(l, "   size. A table of line starts searched by halving makes it n log n. The Rust LIR on the same")
    strs_push(l, "   input is linear (254 ms).")
    strs_push(l, "2. **The Nazm code generator, quadratic or worse in a function's blocks** (2.67 on `nest`, 1.70 on")
    strs_push(l, "   `chain`): `toolchain/codegen/common.nz`'s `allocate` keeps live-in and live-out as dense bit sets")
    strs_push(l, "   of every name for every block and iterates them to a fixed point — B × N / 32 words a pass, and")
    strs_push(l, "   more passes the deeper the nesting (a sample of a 250-deep function: `allocate` 172 of about")
    strs_push(l, "   200 samples).")
    strs_push(l, "3. **The Rust MIR, quadratic in an expression chain's length** (1.78: 480 terms, 31.9 ms of MIR in a")
    strs_push(l, "   build against 0.6 ms at 60 terms, and peak memory 11 → 97 MiB for a 54-line program); the warm")
    strs_push(l, "   build follows it (1.61), and Rust's `core-ir` grows 1.53 with nesting (25 MiB at 200 deep).")
    strs_push(l, "4. **The Nazm Core IR lowering's memory**: 123 MiB for the 54-line chain and 126 MiB for the")
    strs_push(l, "   200-deep function (exponents 1.3–1.5 in time and memory); on ordinary code it is linear but")
    strs_push(l, "   heavy — 471 MiB, about 29 KiB a line, at 16,104 lines, where the Rust `core-ir` peaks at 117 MiB.")
    strs_push(l, "5. **The Nazm checker and parser grow 1.4–1.5 with nesting** (check 22 → 44 ms, parser memory")
    strs_push(l, "   4 → 24 MiB at 200 deep); small in absolute terms below the parser's 512-level limit.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Not compiler findings: `refdump tree`'s time on `nest` and `chain` grows as n³ (47 ms → 18.6 s at")
    strs_push(l, "200 deep) because its `{:#?}` dump indents every line by the depth (840 KB of output at 50 deep, 3.1")
    strs_push(l, "MB at 100); the Rust parser itself is inside `check`, 14.5 ms there. **Two limits found:** a flat")
    strs_push(l, "chain of `+` counts each operator as a level, so a sum of 512 terms is refused by the Rust parser")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0102`) — ordinary in generated code; and **the Nazm pipeline refuses Core IR nested deeper than")
    strs_push(l, "256 JSON levels** (`pipeline: not JSON: nesting deeper than 256`) — on a 100-deep `if` nest and a")
    strs_push(l, "480-term chain the Rust compiler builds — so the Nazm pipeline refuses programs the Rust compiler")
    strs_push(l, "accepts until the reader's limit follows the parser's (or the interchange stops being JSON).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Constant factors, Nazm-written against Rust (lines, 16,104).** Lexing 4.8 against 2.4 µs a line")
    strs_push(l, "(the Rust figure includes `refdump`'s printing); the whole check 359 against 45 µs a function (8×);")
    strs_push(l, "Core IR 1.6 ms a function and 4× the memory; MIR 1.25 ms a function in the pipeline, most of it")
    strs_push(l, "reading the Core IR's JSON, against 7.4 µs in the Rust build (`--timings`); code generation by")
    strs_push(l, "`nzcg` 480 µs a function, against 90 µs for the Rust compiler's LLVM IR text and 330 µs for clang's")
    strs_push(l, "`-O0` compile of it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Latency budgets proposed (7.2), from these figures** — today's value, and what a test should hold:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| what | today (Rust `nazm`) | budget now | target |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm check` of a program of ≤ 100 lines | 10.5 ms wall (load 3.3 + front end 0.5 ms in process) | ≤ 15 ms wall, ≤ 5 ms in process | ≤ 1 ms in process |")
    strs_push(l, "| warm `nazm build` of a small program | 78 ms (object cache 24.6 + link 49.5) | ≤ 100 ms | ≤ 25 ms (no relink when nothing changed) |")
    strs_push(l, "| front end, per function of ten lines | 27 µs (45 µs as `check`) | ≤ 40 µs | ≤ 10 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| MIR, per function | 7.4 µs | ≤ 10 µs | ≤ 2 µs |")
    strs_push(l, "| LIR, per function | 370 ns | ≤ 1 µs | ≤ 500 ns |")
    strs_push(l, "| IR generation, per function | 90 µs | ≤ 120 µs | the own code generator's |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm-written check, per function | 359 µs | ≤ 450 µs | ≤ 2× the Rust compiler's |")
    strs_push(l, "| growth of every phase on `lines`, `nest`, `chain`, `modules` | five phases above 1.25 | exponent ≤ 1.25 | ≤ 1.1 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Not done here: the budgets are proposed, not yet enforced as tests (7.2's tests, 7.4's growth")
    strs_push(l, "guards), and nothing found is fixed (7.3).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Preemption's cost on hot loops, measured (performance leadership 6.3, 2026-10-17)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**More than the 1–2% the design allows: a hot loop with no call pays 8–9%, word frequency 9–10%.**")
    strs_push(l, "`bench/compare/preempt_cost.sh BASE NEW OUT --wait`: BASE a release `nazm` of `a4ac8e9f` (runtime ABI")
    strs_push(l, "42, before preemption, built in its own target directory), NEW one of `e9d9fa40` (ABI 43, a poll of")
    strs_push(l, "one process-wide flag at every loop back edge); `fib`, `words` and `primes` of `bench/compare/nazm/`")
    strs_push(l, "and the script's tight arithmetic loop, each built `--opt-level 2`; `hyperfine -N --warmup 2 --runs")
    strs_push(l, "15`. Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2, Apple clang 21.0.0. The script's run began at load 1.58; its later")
    strs_push(l, "pairs started at 2.6–2.9, the 1-minute average still carrying its own 1.7-second loops (nothing else")
    strs_push(l, "ran: no cargo, rustc or nextest), so the pairs that moved were run again on their own, each begun")
    strs_push(l, "below load 2 (1.72–1.85), once with NEW first and once with BASE first:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| program | BASE (no poll) | NEW (poll at back edges) | cost | load before |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| tight loop, no call (400,000,000 iterations) | 1.656 ± 0.002 s | 1.803 ± 0.001 s; 1.807 ± 0.002 s | **+8.9%; +9.1%** | 1.58; 1.80 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `words` (the comparison's input) | 105.0 ± 0.4 ms; 105.1 ± 0.4; 105.0 ± 0.6 | 115.2 ± 0.2 ms; 115.6 ± 0.5; 115.7 ± 0.5 | **+9.7%; +10.0%; +10.2%** | 2.92; 1.85; 1.78 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `fib(35)` | 44.3 ± 0.2 ms; 44.7 ± 0.2 | 44.4 ± 0.2 ms; 44.8 ± 0.2 | +0.1%; +0.2% | 2.92; 1.72 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `primes`, one worker | 173.3 ± 0.3 ms | 173.1 ± 0.3 ms | −0.1% | 2.77 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `primes`, ten workers | 28.7 ± 2.9 ms | 29.4 ± 3.5 ms | within the spread | 2.63 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Peak memory is unchanged throughout. `fib` has no loop, and `primes`' inner loop is dominated by a")
    strs_push(l, "division, which hides a load and a branch; the cost shows where a loop's body is a few instructions:")
    strs_push(l, "the tight loop, and `words`' byte scan and hash. With one worker the poll is still compiled in (the")
    strs_push(l, "flag is never set), so a single-threaded program pays it too. **This reopens the design (design.md,")
    strs_push(l, "6.3: \"more than 1-2% reopens the design\").** Candidates, not measured here: poll once per N")
    strs_push(l, "iterations (a counter in a register), leave the poll out of a program that starts no task, hoist")
    strs_push(l, "the flag's address out of the loop, or a signal-based preemption that puts nothing in the loop at")
    strs_push(l, "all, as Go 1.14 does.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Eighteen languages on every parameter the comparison measures, measured (2026-10-17)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`python3 bench/compare/compare.py NAZM OUT --runs 10`, Nazm release from `e9d9fa40`, now with three")
    strs_push(l, "more languages — **Fortran** (`gfortran -O2`, and `-fcheck=all -ftrapv` for Nazm's checks), **COBOL**")
    strs_push(l, "(GnuCOBOL `cobc -x -free -O2`) and **hand-written aarch64 assembly** (`bench/compare/{fortran,cobol,asm}/`)")
    strs_push(l, "— and three more columns: the run time's σ, the program's **characters** (of the counted lines,")
    strs_push(l, "without indentation), and the **cold build** (the run's first, its work directory's caches empty)")
    strs_push(l, "beside the warm median. `primes` gained C++, Java and C# programs (written for the concurrency")
    strs_push(l, "section below). Not written: `words` in COBOL and assembly (neither has a hash map, and a faithful")
    strs_push(l, "one is a program of its own), `primes` in the interpreted languages (the harness times the parallel")
    strs_push(l, "job on compiled builds only) and in Zig, Swift, Pascal, Fortran, COBOL, assembly and Ada; Erlang,")
    strs_push(l, "Elixir, Kotlin, Haskell, OCaml, Nim, Crystal, D and Odin are not installed on this Mac (nothing was")
    strs_push(l, "installed for this). The COBOL `fib` returned its result through `RETURN-CODE`, which became the")
    strs_push(l, "process's exit status (201), so the harness refused it; fixed (`MOVE 0 TO RETURN-CODE`) and timed")
    strs_push(l, "by hand with the harness's method for slow programs (`hyperfine -N --warmup 1 --runs 3`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Host.** Apple M1 Pro (8 performance and 2 efficiency cores), 32 GiB, macOS 27.2; Apple clang 21.0.0,")
    strs_push(l, "Go 1.27.2, rustc 1.98.1, Zig 0.17.0, OpenJDK 27, .NET 10.0.402, Swift 6.4, Python 3.15.0, Ruby")
    strs_push(l, "4.0.7, Node 24.13.0, Bun 1.3.10, Free Pascal 3.2.2, GNAT 16.1.0, GNU Fortran 16.2.0, GnuCOBOL 3.2.0,")
    strs_push(l, "hyperfine 2.0.0. Begun at load 1.96 with no cargo, rustc or nextest running; the loads before")
    strs_push(l, "`hello`, `fib`, `words` and `primes` W = 1 were 1.96, 1.68, 1.42 and 1.81; the parallel rows' later")
    strs_push(l, "loads (2.0–4.2) are their own workers, nothing else.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Nazm's rank on each parameter**, among the languages (each language's best measured row; Nazm's")
    strs_push(l, "figures from its `--no-cache` row, its warm build from its user-cache row; lower is better")
    strs_push(l, "everywhere; the interpreter row left out):")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| workload | run time | peak RSS | binary | build cold | build warm | lines | characters | run time among rows checking overflow and bounds |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| hello (start-up) | 2.0 ms, **#3** of 18 (assembly 1.85, C 1.9) | 1.7 MiB, **#1** of 18 (tied with C, C++, assembly) | 34.6 KB, #5 of 13 (C 33.4) | 194 ms, #7 of 14 (assembly 65) | 164 ms, #8 of 14 (Go 62) | 1, **#1** of 18 | 38, #6 of 18 (Ruby 20) | **#1** of 8 (Swift 1.97, Rust 2.27) |")
    strs_push(l, "| fib(35) | 44.8 ms, #9 of 17 (Fortran 3.8, Ada 13.5, C 35.2) | 1.7 MiB, #4 of 17 | 35.2 KB, #4 of 12 | 231 ms, #7 of 13 | 172 ms, #7 of 13 | 6, #8 of 17 | 99, #7 of 17 | #4 of 8 (Fortran 3.9, Ada 13.5, Rust 44.4) |")
    strs_push(l, "| words | 115.4 ms, #6 of 16 (Zig 47.5, Rust 65.7, C 73.9, Fortran 85.5, Go 88.2) | 8.6 MiB, **#3** of 16 (C++ 2.3, Ada 3.0) | 87.9 KB, #5 of 11 | 1,166 ms, #10 of 12 | 718 ms, #7 of 12 | 11, #6 of 16 | 242, **#3** of 16 (Ruby 131, Python 195) | #4 of 8 (Zig 53.7, Rust 66.5, C sanitized 111.8) |")
    strs_push(l, "| primes, W = 1 | 173.6 ms, **#3** of 7 (Go 145.1, Rust checked 167.9) | 2.0 MiB, #4 of 7 | 71.0 KB, #3 of 6 | 464 ms, #5 of 7 | 276 ms, #4 of 7 | 43, #6 of 7 | 734, #6 of 7 | **#2** of 4 (Rust checked 167.9) |")
    strs_push(l, "| primes, W = 8 | 24.3 ms (7.14×), **#3** of 7 (Go 23.4, Rust checked 24.0) | 2.1 MiB, #4 of 7 | | | | | | **#2** of 4 |")
    strs_push(l, "| primes, W = 10 | 31.8 ms (5.46×), #4 of 7 (Go 27.5) | 2.2 MiB, #4 of 7 | | | | | | #2 of 4 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Every row, medians in milliseconds (σ under 2% of the median except where given), peak RSS in MiB,")
    strs_push(l, "build cold / warm in milliseconds:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| language, build | checks | hello | fib | words | words RSS | primes W=1 | build cold / warm (words) | lines / chars (words) |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Nazm** `--opt-level 2` | overflow, bounds, memory; races refused | 2.0 | 44.8 | 115.4 | 8.6 | 173.6 | 1,166 / 718 (user cache) | 11 / 242 |")
    strs_push(l, "| C `clang -O2` | none | 1.9 | 35.2 | 73.9 | 15.3 | 176.7 | 79 / 79 | 41 / 1,219 |")
    strs_push(l, "| C, ASan + UBSan | overflow, bounds, memory | 14.6 | 56.8 | 111.8 | 32.1 | 198.9 | 91 / 91 | |")
    strs_push(l, "| C++ `clang++ -O2` | none | 2.1 | 35.3 | 158.9 | 2.3 | 177.9 | 814 / 804 | 18 / 589 |")
    strs_push(l, "| C++, ASan + UBSan | overflow, bounds, memory | 15.7 | 57.4 | 484.8 | 18.3 | 199.9 | 1,269 / 1,276 | |")
    strs_push(l, "| Rust `-C opt-level=3` | bounds, memory, races; overflow wraps | 2.4 | 35.9 | 65.7 | 14.9 | 192.0 | 324 / 236 | 15 / 438 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Rust, overflow checks | overflow, bounds, memory, races | 2.3 | 44.4 | 66.5 | 14.9 | 167.9 | 236 / 236 | |")
    strs_push(l, "| Zig `ReleaseFast` | none | 2.6 | 36.8 | 47.5 | 14.9 | — | 8,238 / 8,273 | 24 / 1,105 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Zig `ReleaseSafe` | overflow, bounds | 2.5 | 45.9 | 53.7 | 14.9 | — | 9,271 / 9,223 | |")
    strs_push(l, "| Go | bounds, memory; overflow wraps | 3.3 | 40.1 | 88.2 | 61.2 | 145.1 | 207 / 62 | 26 / 478 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Swift `-O` | overflow, bounds, memory | 2.0 | 45.4 | 482.9 | 178.8 | — | 1,043 / 813 | 11 / 381 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Fortran `gfortran -O2` | none | 3.6 | 3.8 ¹ | 85.5 | 15.9 | — | 163 / 164 | 63 / 1,490 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Fortran, `-fcheck=all -ftrapv` | overflow, bounds | 3.7 | 3.9 ¹ | 150.6 | 15.9 | — | 190 / 191 | |")
    strs_push(l, "| Ada `gnatmake -O2` | overflow, bounds | 2.8 | 13.5 ¹ | 249.9 | 3.0 | — | 3,137 / 3,063 | 56 / 1,476 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Pascal `fpc -O3` | none | 2.1 | 74.9 | 592.9 | 37.7 | — | 994 / 934 | 31 / 842 |")
    strs_push(l, "| COBOL `cobc -O2` | none | 7.5 | 7,684 | — | — | — | — | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| Assembly, by hand | none | 1.85 | 44.3 | — | — | — | 65 / 65 (`fib`) | 39 / 757 (`fib`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Java (OpenJDK 27) | bounds, memory; overflow wraps | 30.7 | 63.4 | 387.2 | 216.7 | 208.3 | 361 / 357 | 18 / 640 |")
    strs_push(l, "| C# (.NET 10) | bounds, memory; overflow wraps | 33.1 | 81.1 | 266.9 | 192.7 | 213.0 | 843 / 711 | 10 / 458 |")
    strs_push(l, "| TypeScript (Bun) | bounds, memory | 11.4 | 67.5 | 294.8 | 237.9 | — | — | 8 / 362 |")
    strs_push(l, "| JavaScript (Node) | bounds, memory | 30.7 | 136.3 | 380.5 | 297.3 | — | — | 8 / 340 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Python 3 | bounds, memory; no overflow | 25.5 | 1,163 | 229.6 | 153.9 | — | — | 6 / 195 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Ruby | bounds, memory; no overflow | 42.8 | 986 | 350.7 | 136.6 | — | — | 3 / 131 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm, interpreter | as Nazm | 7.3 | 5,233 | 25,709 | 21.2 | — | — | 11 / 242 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "¹ GCC's optimiser (Fortran and Ada are both GCC) turns the doubly recursive `fib` into far fewer")
    strs_push(l, "calls; the source is the same algorithm, so the row stands, but it measures GCC's recursion")
    strs_push(l, "transformations rather than a call's cost. The hand-written assembly `fib` (44.3 ms, a plain")
    strs_push(l, "recursive call per call) is the honest floor for a call-per-call `fib` on this core.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What changed since *R1.5 5.1*.** `words` 115.6 → 115.4 ms (no change: 3.4's gain is spent by")
    strs_push(l, "preemption's poll, *Preemption's cost on hot loops*); `fib` 44.1 → 44.8; `primes` W = 8 23.8 → 24.3;")
    strs_push(l, "the Nazm cold build of `words` 1,166 ms against the cached 718 ms. **Where Nazm leads:** start-up")
    strs_push(l, "among checked languages (2.0 ms, first of eight), peak memory (first on `hello`, third of sixteen on")
    strs_push(l, "`words`, with C++ and Ada), the shortest `hello`, the third-shortest `words` by characters, and the")
    strs_push(l, "parallel job among checked rows (second only to checked Rust, within its spread at W = 8). **Where it")
    strs_push(l, "is behind:** `words` time (Zig 2.4×, Rust 1.7×, C 1.6×, Go 1.3× faster), `fib` against unchecked")
    strs_push(l, "C/C++/Rust/Zig (the overflow checks: checked Rust is 44.4), and build time (a cold `words` build is")
    strs_push(l, "15× C's and 5× Rust's; warm, 718 ms against Go's 62 ms and C's 79 ms).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Build speed: `nazm check` and `nazm build`, cold and warm, beside every compiled language, measured (2026-10-17)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`hyperfine -N` (10 runs, 5 for the cold builds) of the release `nazm` from `e9d9fa40` on three")
    strs_push(l, "programs: `hello`, `words` (`bench/compare/nazm/`) and a large one, the Nazm-written front end")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/diagnose.nz` with the `compiler/` modules it imports (`compiler/` holds 50,315 lines).")
    strs_push(l, "Cold is `--no-cache` (every unit and the runtime compiled); warm is the same build again with the")
    strs_push(l, "user cache and the project store filled and nothing changed. Each measurement begun below load 2")
    strs_push(l, "(1.43–1.98) with no cargo, rustc or nextest running; user and project caches in the run's own")
    strs_push(l, "directory. Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| program | `check --no-cache` | `check`, cache warm | build cold `-O0` | build warm `-O0` | build cold `-O2` | build warm `-O2` | binary `-O0` / `-O2` | peak RSS of the build (cold `-O2`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `hello` | 7.4 ± 0.2 ms | 7.5 ± 0.3 ms | 177.5 ± 0.9 ms | 88.5 ± 7.8 ms | 192.4 ± 2.6 ms | 85.5 ± 2.3 ms | 51,336 / 34,648 B | 56 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| `words` | 18.7 ± 0.1 ms | 20.2 ± 0.2 ms | 861.7 ± 4.7 ms | 124.5 ± 1.0 ms | 1,156 ± 5 ms | 131.3 ± 1.3 ms | 106,280 / 87,880 B | 78 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| `compiler/diagnose.nz` | 297.8 ± 3.0 ms | 331.5 ± 1.8 ms | 4.135 ± 0.011 s | 1.024 ± 0.002 s | **26.65 ± 0.14 s** | 1.114 ± 0.003 s | 5.45 / 5.03 MB | **724 MiB** |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Start-up: the `-O2` `hello` runs in 2.0 ± 0.1 ms at 1.7 MiB.")
