    strs_push(l, "| | Nazm | C | C++ | Rust | Go | Zig | Swift | Fortran | Ada | Pascal | COBOL | Java (`javac`) | C# (`dotnet build`) | assembly | Nazm's rank |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `hello`, cold | 194 | 68 | 540 | 109 | 2,233 | 10,085 | 240 | 125 | 1,005 | 101 | 141 | 293 | 852 | 65 | 7 of 14 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `hello`, warm | 164 | 67 | 528 | 110 | 62 | 7,416 | 244 | 125 | 984 | 102 | 140 | 293 | 724 | 65 | 8 of 14 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `words`, cold | 1,166 | 79 | 814 | 324 | 207 | 8,238 | 1,043 | 163 | 3,137 | 994 | — | 361 | 843 | — | 10 of 12 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `words`, warm | 718 | 79 | 804 | 236 | 62 | 8,273 | 813 | 164 | 3,063 | 934 | — | 357 | 711 | — | 7 of 12 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "In milliseconds, medians. **Findings.** (1) `check` with its cache warm is *slower* than")
    strs_push(l, "`--no-cache` — 20.2 against 18.7 ms on `words`, 331.5 against 297.8 ms on the front end (+11%): on")
    strs_push(l, "one package the cache is read and checked and saves nothing. (2) A cold `-O2` build of the front end")
    strs_push(l, "takes 26.6 s and 724 MiB (`-O0`: 4.1 s, 300 MiB); a warm one 1.1 s, which is the link and the")
    strs_push(l, "cache's lookups. (3) Nazm's builds are behind C, Rust, Go and Fortran on both programs; a warm")
    strs_push(l, "rebuild of an unchanged `words` (`nazm build`, 125–131 ms with the project store filled) is the")
    strs_push(l, "fair figure against Go's 62 ms, and 7.2's budget (≤ 100 ms) is not met there. On `words` a cold")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm build is ahead only of Ada and Zig; with the user cache warm it is also ahead of C++, Swift and")
    strs_push(l, "Pascal.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Preemption by interrupt: the cost on hot loops, re-measured (quiet window, 2026-10-19)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**No measurable cost: 0.0% on the tight loop, `fib` and `primes`, and `words` is 0.9% faster, where")
    strs_push(l, "the poll at every back edge had cost 8–10%.** `bench/compare/preempt_cost.sh BASE NEW OUT --wait`:")
    strs_push(l, "BASE a release `nazm` of `a4ac8e9f` (runtime ABI 42, no preemption; its own target directory), NEW one of")
    strs_push(l, "`0a52becf` (preemption by interrupt, ABI 44: nothing in any loop, commit `442c9b2e`, and Cranelift's and")
    strs_push(l, "nzcg's code too, `ef21fcc9`); `fib`, `words` and `primes` of `bench/compare/nazm/` and the script's")
    strs_push(l, "tight arithmetic loop, each built `--opt-level 2`; `hyperfine -N --warmup 2 --runs 15`. Apple M1 Pro,")
    strs_push(l, "10 processors, 32 GiB, macOS 27.2. Nothing else ran: no cargo, rustc or nextest (checked with")
    strs_push(l, "`pgrep -x` before the script and after), no other agent; the 1-minute load is the figure at the start of")
    strs_push(l, "each pair, the later ones still carrying the script's own loops.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| program | BASE (no preemption) | NEW (interrupt) | cost | load before |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| tight loop, no call (400,000,000 iterations) | 1.653 ± 0.001 s | 1.653 ± 0.002 s | 0.0% | 1.96 |")
    strs_push(l, "| tight loop, run again, NEW first, then BASE first | 1.653 ± 0.001 s | 1.653 ± 0.001 s; 1.651 ± 0.002 s | 0.0%; −0.1% | 1.45; 1.45 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `words` (the comparison's input) | 104.9 ± 0.5 ms | 103.9 ± 0.4 ms | −0.9% | 1.47 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `fib(35)` | 44.4 ± 0.3 ms | 44.4 ± 0.3 ms | 0.0% | 1.47 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `primes`, one worker | 173.5 ± 0.3 ms | 173.4 ± 0.4 ms | −0.1% | 1.43 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `primes`, ten workers | 30.8 ± 3.9 ms | 29.3 ± 2.9 ms | within the spread | 1.40 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Peak memory is unchanged throughout (the largest difference, `fib`, 0.9%, is the process's own noise:")
    strs_push(l, "1.7 MiB). Against the poll's measurement (*Preemption's cost on hot loops*, 8.9–9.1% on the tight loop and")
    strs_push(l, "9.7–10.2% on `words`) the interrupt removes the whole cost: the 1–2% the design allows is met, with room.")
    strs_push(l, "Not measured here: the latency of a preemption itself (how long a task computing without waiting holds")
    strs_push(l, "its worker before another runs).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Concurrency against every installed language with a concurrency model, measured (quiet window, 2026-10-19)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm's tasks, after 6.2's growable stacks, 6.3's preemption by interrupt and 6.4's channels, beside")
    strs_push(l, "eight other languages on the same six workloads (the baseline above compared Go alone). The programs")
    strs_push(l, "are `bench/compare/<lang>/{spawn,pingpong,fanin,idle,httpd}` with each language's existing `primes`")
    strs_push(l, "for the parallel job; Go's and Nazm's are the baseline's pair; the rest are new, written in the idiom")
    strs_push(l, "of the language's concurrency model: **Rust** `std::thread` and `sync_channel`; **C** pthreads with a")
    strs_push(l, "mutex-and-condvar channel (`c/chan.h`); **C++** `std::thread` with the same channel (`cpp/chan.h`);")
    strs_push(l, "**Java** virtual threads with `ArrayBlockingQueue` and `com.sun.net.httpserver`; **C#** `Task.Run`,")
    strs_push(l, "`System.Threading.Channels` and `HttpListener`; **Node** async functions on the one event loop with a")
    strs_push(l, "promise channel (`javascript/chan.js`) and `node:http`; **Python** `asyncio` tasks and queues and")
    strs_push(l, "`ThreadingHTTPServer` (threads for `primes`, which the interpreter lock serialises).")
    strs_push(l, "`bench/compare/concurrency_all.sh NAZM OUT --wait` builds them all, checks every pair of answers")
    strs_push(l, "against the others' (`spawn` 1000000, `pingpong` N(N+1)/2, `fanin` 499999500000, `idle` N, `primes`")
    strs_push(l, "216816), waits before each measurement until the 1-minute load is below 2 with no cargo, rustc or")
    strs_push(l, "nextest running, and records that load beside the number.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Host and builds.** Apple M1 Pro (8 performance and 2 efficiency cores), 32 GiB, macOS 27.2; Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "release from `0a52becf`, `--opt-level 2`; Go 1.27.2; rustc 1.98.1 `-O`; Apple clang 21.0.0 `-O2`")
    strs_push(l, "(C++20); OpenJDK 27; .NET 10.0.402 (`dotnet build -c Release`, workstation GC); Node 24.13.0; Python")
    strs_push(l, "3.15.0. `hyperfine -N --warmup 1`, 5 runs for `spawn`, 10 for the rest. **Load:** every number")
    strs_push(l, "began below load 2 (1.28–1.99) except where marked; the 1-minute average carries the previous")
    strs_push(l, "measurement's own threads, and a macOS background daemon (`knowledgeconstructiond`) held about 0.8 of")
    strs_push(l, "a processor throughout. Five rows began above 2 (C, C++, Java and C# `spawn` at 2.55, 2.22, 3.56 and 2.53,")
    strs_push(l, "and C#'s third HTTP round at 2.60) and were run again alone below 2; the table gives the re-runs and")
    strs_push(l, "the third C# round is left out. Two complete runs agree to within their spreads wherever a row")
    strs_push(l, "was measured twice.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Skipped, with the reason:** Erlang, Elixir, Kotlin and Haskell (not installed); Rust's `tokio` (no")
    strs_push(l, "offline crate cache); HTTP for C, C++ and Rust (no HTTP in their standard libraries: a hand-written parser")
    strs_push(l, "would measure the parser).")
    strs_push(l, "Thread-per-task languages cannot hold a million live threads: C, C++ and Rust `spawn` 1,000,000")
    strs_push(l, "threads, 1,000 at a time, each joined (so it measures thread creation), and their `idle` is 4,000")
    strs_push(l, "threads against 1,000, not 100,000.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| workload | Nazm | Go | best | Nazm's rank | against the baseline |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| spawn 1,000,000 tasks, wall | 1,501 ± 31 ms | 271 ± 11 ms | Node 183 ms | **5 of 9** (Node 183, Go 271, C# 493, Java 590, **Nazm 1,501**, Python 4,880, C 13,361, C++ 13,622, Rust 16,640) | 3,645 → 1,501 ms (2.4× faster); 13–14× Go → 5.5× |")
    strs_push(l, "| ping-pong, 100,000 round trips | 60.0 ± 23.0 ms (0.60 µs a trip; fastest run 40.8 ms) | 31.4 ± 0.2 ms | Go | **2 of 9** (Go 31, **Nazm 60**, Node 93, C# 294, Rust 329, C++ 390, C 407, Java 469, Python 3,017) | 437 → 60 ms (7.3× faster); 13.9× Go → 1.9× |")
    strs_push(l, "| fan-in, 1,000,000 values, 8 producers | 845 ± 213 ms (fastest run 639) | 67.3 ± 0.7 ms | Go | **8 of 9** (Go 67, Rust 146, Java 167, Node 277, C 366, C++ 463, Python 825, **Nazm 845**, C# 934) | 445 → 845 ms: **slower**, and bimodal (below) |")
    strs_push(l, "| memory per blocked task | 1,215 B | 2,744 B | C# 331 B | **3 of 9** (C# 331, Node 944, **Nazm 1,215**, Python 1,459, Java 2,012, Go 2,744, C 16,198, C++ 16,515, Rust 19,300) | 17.4 KiB → 1.2 KiB (14×); 6.5× Go → 0.44× |")
    strs_push(l, "| HTTP/1.1 requests/s, 64 connections, 10 s | 81,778; 82,164; 82,407 | 91,523; 91,602; 91,595 | Java 93,799; 93,590; 95,338 | **3 of 6** (Java ~94 k, Go ~91.6 k, **Nazm ~82.1 k**, C# 73.4–76.1 k, Node ~51.5 k, Python ~17.2 k) | 0.84–0.86× Go → 0.90× |")
    strs_push(l, "| HTTP server RSS under that load | 9.6 MiB | 22 MiB | Nazm | **1 of 6** (Nazm 9.6, Go 22, Python 23, Node 79, C# 83, Java 233) | 11.1 → 9.6 MiB |")
    strs_push(l, "| primes, W = 1 | 173.4 ± 0.3 ms | 144.3 ± 0.2 ms | Go | **2 of 8** (Go 144, **Nazm 173**, C 176, C++ 177, Rust 190, Java 208, C# 213, Python 6,488) | 171.6 → 173.4 ms; 1.19× → 1.20× Go |")
    strs_push(l, "| primes, W = 10 | 29.7 ± 3.0 ms | 27.8 ± 1.6 ms | Go | **3 of 8**, tied with Rust (Go 27.8, C 28.0, **Nazm 29.7**, Rust 29.7, C++ 30.2, C# 71, Java 73, Python 6,521) | 29.5 → 29.7 ms; 1.12× → 1.07× Go |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the numbers say.**")
    strs_push(l, "- **Task start-up is 2.4× faster than the baseline and still the largest gap to the lightweight")
    strs_push(l, "  models.** 1.5 µs a task; Go 0.27 µs, Node 0.18 µs, C# 0.49 µs, Java 0.59 µs. The OS-thread")
    strs_push(l, "  languages (C, C++, Rust) pay 13–17 µs a task and Nazm is ten times ahead of them; only Python's")
    strs_push(l, "  asyncio is behind among the task models.")
    strs_push(l, "- **A channel hand-off is 7× faster and within 1.9× of Go's, second of nine.** 0.6 µs a round trip")
    strs_push(l, "  against Go's 0.31 µs; every OS-thread implementation is 5–7× slower than Nazm, Java's virtual")
    strs_push(l, "  threads 8×, Python's asyncio 50×.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Fan-in is the one regression and the one place Nazm is near the bottom.** 845 ms against a")
    strs_push(l, "  baseline 445 ms and Go's 67 ms (12.5×). It is not noise in the host: with the same program built by")
    strs_push(l, "  the baseline's `a4ac8e9f` and by `a6f0fff2` (before this track) and run in the same window below load 2,")
    strs_push(l, "  the older compilers gave 490 ± 138 ms and 482 ± 7 ms, `0a52becf` 660 ± 85 and 750 ± 230 ms")
    strs_push(l, "  (rows run alone, begun at load 1.93–1.99), and the new runs are bimodal — 231 ms in the")
    strs_push(l, "  best, 800 ms and more in the worst. Eight producers on one capacity-1,024 channel after the lock-free")
    strs_push(l, "  hand-off of 6.4 is the first thing to look at.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Memory per blocked task is 1.2 KiB, third of nine** behind only the stackless models (C# async")
    strs_push(l, "  state machines, Node's promises), and under Go's 2.7 KiB; Java's virtual threads 2.0 KiB.")
    strs_push(l, "  The three OS-thread languages hold 16–19 KiB a thread, as Nazm did before 6.2.")
    strs_push(l, "- **HTTP is within 10% of Go's requests per second at 0.44× its memory** (a loopback load")
    strs_push(l, "  generator that shares the ten processors with the server, as before); Java's `httpserver` on virtual")
    strs_push(l, "  threads is ahead of both and 24× Nazm's memory.")
    strs_push(l, "- **The parallel CPU job is unchanged and as close to Go's as before** (the 20% on one worker is the")
    strs_push(l, "  checked overflow of the inner loop); with ten workers Nazm ties Rust and is within 7% of Go.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Not claimed: any lead in concurrency over Go. What the table supports: second of nine on hand-off")
    strs_push(l, "latency, third of nine on memory per task, first on HTTP server memory, ahead of every OS-thread")
    strs_push(l, "language on spawn, hand-off and memory; behind on fan-in, and behind Go, Node, C# and Java on spawn.")
    strs_push(l, "Python's `primes` rows serialise on the interpreter lock (W = 10 costs what W = 1 does).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## R1.5 3.1 (the small-block heap) and 3.4 (ThinLTO) re-measured, on a quiet host (2026-10-19)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The two sections above were measured at load 4–8 from other agents. Four release `nazm` builds on")
    strs_push(l, "the same six programs, each program built `--no-cache --opt-level 2` by each: **v0** `b0c57c59`")
    strs_push(l, "(before 3.1: C's `malloc`; the commit before `0b7f8749`), **v1** `65ddcd60` (3.1's heap, per-unit")
    strs_push(l, "optimisation; `764997dd~2`), **v2** `a6f0fff2` (3.4's ThinLTO) and **v3** `0a52becf`, today's tree. The")
    strs_push(l, "builds of v0–v2 are the release binaries left from the earlier quiet-window runs")
    strs_push(l, "(`~/.cache/nazm-target-quiet-<commit>`); v3 was built for this one. `hyperfine -N --warmup 3 --runs 15`,")
    strs_push(l, "the four builds in one invocation, each invocation begun below load 2 (1.76–1.99) with no cargo, rustc or")
    strs_push(l, "nextest running; Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2, Apple clang 21.0.0. Every build printed the same answers")
    strs_push(l, "(`fib` 9227465, `primes` 216816, `words` byte for byte `words.expected`). The allocation loops")
    strs_push(l, "are new files (`bench/compare/nazm/alloc.nz`, `alloc4.nz`), written from 3.1's prose — the section")
    strs_push(l, "gave no source — so they reproduce its shape, not its exact program; `words` is the source of its")
    strs_push(l, "day (`read_file(..).lines()`, from `b0c57c59`) in the second table, since the current one")
    strs_push(l, "(`file_lines`, 3.5) does not compile on the old builds.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| program | v0 (before 3.1) | v1 (3.1) | v2 (3.4) | v3 (today) | 3.1 | 3.4 | v0 → v3 |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| string and one-element list, 5,000,000 times | 322.7 ± 20.7 ms | 149.7 ± 0.2 ms | 104.8 ± 2.6 ms | 104.7 ± 0.1 ms | 2.2× faster | −30% | 3.1× faster |")
    strs_push(l, "| the same, Cranelift (`--backend cranelift`) | 464.3 ± 4.1 ms | 305.3 ± 3.6 ms | 304.1 ± 3.2 ms | 304.6 ± 2.2 ms | −34% | 0 | −34% |")
    strs_push(l, "| four tasks, 1,000,000 strings each | 256.0 ± 6.8 ms | 202.9 ± 5.4 ms | 228.9 ± 17.1 ms | 228.6 ± 4.7 ms | −21% | +13%, noisy | −11% |")
    strs_push(l, "| `words`, current source (3.5's `file_lines`) | — | — | — | 103.7 ± 0.2 ms | | | |")
    strs_push(l, "| `words`, 3.3's source | 114.1 ± 0.5 ms | 113.6 ± 0.3 ms | 104.0 ± 0.7 ms | 103.4 ± 0.2 ms | −0.4% | −8.4% | −9.4% |")
    strs_push(l, "| `fib(35)` | 44.2 ± 0.1 ms | 44.3 ± 0.2 ms | 44.3 ± 0.2 ms | 44.2 ± 0.2 ms | 0 | 0 | 0 |")
    strs_push(l, "| `primes`, one worker | 172.0 ± 0.2 ms | 172.0 ± 0.2 ms | 173.2 ± 0.3 ms | 173.3 ± 0.3 ms | 0 | +0.7% | +0.8% |")
    strs_push(l, "| `hello` start-up | 1.9 ± 0.0 ms | 1.9 ± 0.0 ms | 1.9 ± 0.0 ms | 1.9 ± 0.0 ms | 0 | 0 | 0 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Binary sizes (bytes), v0 / v1 / v2 / v3: `hello` 51,208 / 51,304 / 34,648 / 34,632; `fib` 51,880 /")
    strs_push(l, "51,976 / 35,208 / 35,096; `words` (3.3's source) 76,728 / 76,872 / 86,728 / 86,872 and v3's current")
    strs_push(l, "`words` 87,880; the allocation loop 51,528 / 51,672 / 34,824 / 34,808. Peak memory: both allocation loops")
    strs_push(l, "1.7–2.1 MiB on every build; 3.3's `words` 19.9 MiB on every build, the current `words` 8.6 MiB (`file_lines`")
    strs_push(l, "reads a chunk at a time, 3.5).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What this confirms.** 3.1's heap: **2.2× on the string-and-list loop** (3.1 recorded 2.5×) and")
    strs_push(l, "−34% on Cranelift's (−22% recorded); four tasks −21% (−16% recorded, noisy there too). 3.4: **`words`")
    strs_push(l, "−8.4%** (−9.2% recorded), `fib` and `primes` unchanged, binaries 16,500 bytes smaller for the tiny")
    strs_push(l, "programs, 10,000 bytes larger for `words`. **What it does not:** 3.4's recorded 81.0 ms on the allocation")
    strs_push(l, "loop (−29%) is 104.8 ms here (−30% of this loop's 149.7 — the ratio holds, the absolute does not,")
    strs_push(l, "because the loop is a reconstruction); four tasks got 13% slower with 3.4 (202.9 → 228.9 ms, σ 17 on v2, 5 on v1")
    strs_push(l, "and v3; v3 agrees with v2, 228.6 against 228.9, so the slowdown has held since 3.4: the")
    strs_push(l, "cause is not profiled here). The heap's cost on")
    strs_push(l, "`words` is none: it allocates nothing in its loop.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Builds with `NAZM_CACHE_DIR` private to each, `hyperfine -N --runs 10`, `-O2`, begun at load")
    strs_push(l, "1.60–1.96 (`bench/compare/nazm/fib.nz`; `words` in 3.3's source so every build compiles it):")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| build | v0 | v1 | v2 | v3 | v2 → v3 |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `fib`, cold (`--no-cache`) | 209.1 ± 0.9 ms | 241.7 ± 0.8 ms | 223.5 ± 1.0 ms | 113.7 ± 0.7 ms | 2.0× faster |")
    strs_push(l, "| `fib`, warm | 81.5 ± 0.5 ms | 82.1 ± 1.0 ms | 83.0 ± 0.9 ms | 30.7 ± 0.2 ms | 2.7× faster |")
    strs_push(l, "| `words`, cold | 884.2 ± 1.3 ms | 918.8 ± 1.5 ms | 796.7 ± 2.5 ms | 241.5 ± 3.0 ms | 3.3× faster |")
    strs_push(l, "| `words`, warm | 103.5 ± 0.6 ms | 106.0 ± 0.7 ms | 110.8 ± 1.1 ms | 47.1 ± 0.4 ms | 2.4× faster |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "3.4's own build numbers reproduce on v1 → v2: `words` cold 918.8 → 796.7 ms (−13%; recorded 960.7 → 840.2),")
    strs_push(l, "warm 106.0 → 110.8 ms (+4.5%; recorded +5.7%). The step from v2 to v3 is the compiler-speed track")
    strs_push(l, "(units generated and compiled side by side, no relink of an unchanged program, two quadratic loops")
    strs_push(l, "removed): a warm `words` build is 47 ms, inside 7.2's 100 ms budget, where the *Build speed*")
    strs_push(l, "section measured 125 ms.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## The compilers' growth, phase by phase, re-measured (quiet window, 2026-10-19)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The 7.1–7.2 audit run again on `0a52becf` (the tree after the compiler-speed track and the quadratic")
    strs_push(l, "loops found by that audit), with the same programs and method: `bench/complexity/gen.py` shapes")
    strs_push(l, "**lines** (n = 2,000, so 2,104 to 16,104 lines), **nest** (25 to 200 `if`s deep), **chain** (60 to 480")
    strs_push(l, "terms) and **modules** (10 to 80), timed by `bench/complexity/measure.py`, the median of 5 runs after one")
    strs_push(l, "warm-up, peak memory the largest `maximum resident set size` of `/usr/bin/time -l`, every measurement")
    strs_push(l, "waiting for a 1-minute load below 2 with no cargo, rustc or nextest running: 360 measurements, begun at load")
    strs_push(l, "1.29–2.16 (three above 2: 2.16, 2.01 and 2.08, none a point a finding rests on). Release `nazm`")
    strs_push(l, "from `0a52becf`, the Nazm-written drivers `tokens`, `tree`, `diagnose`, `pipeline` and `nzcg` built by it")
    strs_push(l, "as `toolchain/*/tests/run.sh` build them, `refdump` release. Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2. Exponent: log2(t(8n)/t(4n)),")
    strs_push(l, "the empty program's time subtracted, **bold** above 1.25; \"flat\" is a range within 3 ms.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| phase | lines 2,104 → 16,104 | exp. | nest 25 → 200 | exp. | chain 60 → 480 | exp. | modules 10 → 80 | exp. |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | ---: | --- | ---: | --- | ---: | --- | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Rust** `check --no-cache` | 12.1 → 42.3 ms, 13 → 54 MiB | 1.01 | flat (8.4 → 9.8 ms) | — | flat (8.3 → 9.1 ms) | — | 12.1 → 38.6 ms | 1.03 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Rust `check`, cache warm | 11.7 → 38.4 ms | 1.01 | flat | — | flat | — | 11.5 → 35.4 ms | 1.06 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Rust `core-ir` | 24.2 → 131.4 ms, 20 → 103 MiB | 1.01 | 8.9 → 18.7 ms | **1.54** | 9.1 → 16.4 ms | **1.61** | 17.6 → 82.3 ms | 0.99 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Rust `mir` | 18.4 → 87.0 ms, 17 → 73 MiB | 1.00 | flat (8.5 → 10.9 ms) | — | flat (8.5 → 11.0 ms) | — | 15.5 → 61.3 ms | 1.04 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Rust `lir` | 37.2 → 212.0 ms, 22 → 105 MiB | 0.97 | 9.3 → 13.7 ms | 1.06 | 10.5 → 21.4 ms | 0.98 | 23.3 → 121.9 ms | 1.02 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Rust `build --no-cache` (LLVM, `-O0`) | 198 → 809 ms, 41 → 141 MiB | 0.97 | 97 → 110 ms | **1.51** | 100 → 132 ms | 1.09 | 154 → 535 ms | 1.04 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Rust `build`, warm | 68 → 263 ms | 0.97 | flat (35.6 → 41.2 ms) | — | 36.4 → 46.5 ms | 0.85 | 50 → 132 ms | 1.07 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Rust `build --opt-level 2 --no-cache` | 748 → 4,363 ms | 1.19 | 111 → 117 ms | 0.65 | 113 → 133 ms | **1.43** | 219 → 791 ms | 1.01 |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Nazm** lexer (`tokens.nz`) | 16.5 → 83.2 ms, 10 → 50 MiB | 0.97 | 6.4 → 9.8 ms | **1.49** | flat (6.5 → 8.1 ms) | — | flat | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm parser (`tree.nz`, with its dump) | 42.0 → 274.3 ms, 26 → 162 MiB | 0.97 | 7.6 → 23.6 ms, 4 → 24 MiB | **1.46** | 7.4 → 19.1 ms, 4 → 18 MiB | **1.40** | flat | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm `diagnose --syntax` | 23.2 → 128.8 ms | 0.95 | 7.0 → 11.7 ms | 1.14 | flat | — | flat | — |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm check (`diagnose`) | 84.3 → 592.7 ms, 15 → 83 MiB | 1.13 | 22.2 → 44.0 ms | **1.46** | 21.7 → 32.1 ms | 0.99 | 50.6 → 275.4 ms | 1.06 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm Core IR (`diagnose --core`) | 341 → 2,516 ms, **55 → 352 MiB** | 1.02 | 29.3 → 103.9 ms, 10 → 46 MiB | 1.24 | 30.1 → 95.6 ms, 13 → 64 MiB | 1.11 | 171 → 1,237 ms, 30 → 179 MiB | 1.03 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm MIR (`pipeline mir`) | 276 → 2,028 ms, 22 → 137 MiB | 1.00 | refused from 100 deep | — | refused at 480 terms | — | 131 → 1,005 ms | 1.02 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm LIR (`pipeline lir`) | 371 → 2,715 ms, 28 → 193 MiB | **1.00** | refused from 100 deep | — | refused at 480 terms | — | 175 → 1,364 ms | 1.03 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Nazm code generator (`nzcg`) | 86.9 → 708.8 ms, 13 → 78 MiB | 1.22 | 8.0 → 16.6 ms | **1.02** | 10.4 → 36.6 ms | **0.99** | 43.6 → 301.6 ms | 1.02 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the 7.1 findings did.**")
    strs_push(l, "1. *The Nazm pipeline's LIR was quadratic in a module's size* (1.69, 579 → 12,943 ms): **fixed**, 1.00, 371 →")
    strs_push(l, "   2,715 ms (4.8× faster at 16,104 lines).")
    strs_push(l, "2. *The Nazm code generator was quadratic in a function's blocks* (2.67 on `nest`, 1.70 on `chain`): **fixed**,")
    strs_push(l, "   1.02 and 0.99: the 200-deep function 233.9 → 16.6 ms, the 480-term chain 159.1 → 36.6 ms.")
    strs_push(l, "3. *The Rust MIR was quadratic in an expression chain's length* (1.78, 12.2 → 46.6 ms and 11 → 97 MiB):")
    strs_push(l, "   **fixed**: 8.5 → 11.0 ms, memory flat; the warm build's 1.61 is 0.85 and the `-O0` build's 1.31 is 1.09.")
    strs_push(l, "4. *The Nazm Core IR lowering's memory* (123 MiB for the 54-line chain, 126 MiB for the 200-deep function,")
    strs_push(l, "   471 MiB at 16,104 lines): **halved, not gone** — 64, 46 and 352 MiB; the time exponents on `chain` and")
    strs_push(l, "   `nest` fall from 1.34 and 1.49 to 1.11 and 1.24.")
    strs_push(l, "5. *The Nazm checker and parser grow 1.4–1.5 with nesting*: **unchanged** (check 1.41 → 1.46, parser 1.50 → 1.46,")
    strs_push(l, "   22 → 44 ms and 4 → 24 MiB at 200 deep); the lexer joins them at 1.49 on `nest` (6.4 → 9.8 ms, a 3.4 ms range).")
    strs_push(l, "   Rust's `core-ir` still grows 1.54 and 1.61 on `nest` and `chain` (9 → 19 ms and 9 → 16 ms: small in")
    strs_push(l, "   absolute terms; its memory 7 → 21 MiB at 200 deep), and the Rust `-O0` build 1.51 on `nest`")
    strs_push(l, "   (97 → 110 ms).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Cells above 1.25: eight, at 7.1 fourteen, among them four quadratic loops. All eight are ranges of 3–25 ms")
    strs_push(l, "on the nesting and chain programs; none is a loop that costs on ordinary code. The two limits found stand: a sum")
    strs_push(l, "of 512 terms is refused by the Rust parser, and the Nazm pipeline refuses Core IR nested deeper than 256 JSON")
    strs_push(l, "levels (a 100-deep `if` nest, a 480-term chain).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Where the Rust build's time goes** (`--timings`, medians; lines 16,104 / modules 80), against 7.1's in")
    strs_push(l, "parentheses: load 16.6 / 19.3 ms (37.3 / 26.5), front end 23.5 / 18.0 (43.4 / 28.9), MIR 11.5 / 6.4 (11.9 / 6.8), LIR")
    strs_push(l, "0.7 / 0.5, IR generation 142.9 / 18.1 (144.8 / 68.5), native compile 530.5 / 388.8 uncached (646.5 / 2,778.5) and 37.6 /")
    strs_push(l, "55.2 warm (37.9 / 53.6), link 57.2 / 64.2 (55.6 / 63.5). **Many modules cost 7× less to compile** (the 80-module")
    strs_push(l, "program's native compile 2.78 s → 0.39 s: the units are compiled side by side now). On a program of a few lines:")
    strs_push(l, "load 0.4 (3.3), front end 0.4 (0.5), native compile 35.2 uncached or 23.7 warm (116.8; 24.6), link 50.4 uncached and")
    strs_push(l, "**0.8 warm** (49.5): **a warm build of a small program is 26.3 ms in `--timings`, from 78 ms** (an unchanged program")
    strs_push(l, "is not linked again).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Constant factors, Nazm-written against Rust (lines, 16,104).** Lexing 5.2 against 2.8 µs a line (4.8 against 2.4 at")
    strs_push(l, "7.1); the whole check 368 against 26 µs a function (14×, from 8×: Rust's check got 1.7× faster, Nazm's did not); Core")
    strs_push(l, "IR 1.56 ms a function; MIR 1.26 ms a function in the pipeline; LIR 1.69 ms in the pipeline (reading the Core IR's")
    strs_push(l, "JSON, as before); code generation by `nzcg` 440 µs a function (480).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**7.2's latency budgets against today** (Rust `nazm`): `nazm check` of a small program 4.2 ms wall, from 10.5 (budget")
    strs_push(l, "≤ 15 ms, met; target ≤ 1 ms in process); a warm `nazm build` of a small program 26.3 ms in `--timings` and 30.5 ms wall")
    strs_push(l, "for `hello` (budget ≤ 100 ms, met; target ≤ 25 ms, nearly); front end per function 26 µs as `check` (≤ 40 µs, met);")
    strs_push(l, "MIR per function 7.1 µs (≤ 10 µs, met); LIR per function 0.4 µs (≤ 1 µs, met); IR generation per function 89 µs (≤ 120,")
    strs_push(l, "met); Nazm-written check per function 368 µs (≤ 450, met; target ≤ 2× the Rust compiler's: 14×, not met); growth: eight")
    strs_push(l, "cells above 1.25 (budget: none).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Build speed re-measured: `nazm check` and `nazm build`, cold and warm (quiet window, 2026-10-19)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`hyperfine -N` (10 runs; 5 for the cold `-O0` builds and for `compiler/diagnose.nz`; 3 for its cold `-O2`) of the")
    strs_push(l, "release `nazm` of `0a52becf`, on the same three programs as *Build speed* above: `hello`, `words`")
    strs_push(l, "(`bench/compare/nazm/`) and `compiler/diagnose.nz` with the `compiler/` modules it imports (`compiler/` now holds")
    strs_push(l, "51,063 lines in 23 files, from 50,315). Cold is `--no-cache`; warm is the same build again with the user cache and")
    strs_push(l, "the project store filled. Each measurement begun below load 2 (1.85–1.99) with no cargo, rustc or nextest running;")
    strs_push(l, "caches in the run's own directory. Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| program | `check --no-cache` | `check`, warm | build cold `-O0` | build warm `-O0` | build cold `-O2` | build warm `-O2` | binary `-O0` / `-O2` | peak RSS, cold `-O0` / `-O2` |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |")
    strs_push(l, "| `hello` | 4.2 ± 0.1 ms (7.4) | 4.2 ± 0.1 ms (7.5) | 92.1 ± 1.4 ms (177.5) | 30.5 ± 0.3 ms (88.5) | 104.3 ± 1.6 ms (192.4) | 30.8 ± 0.2 ms (85.5) | 51,336 / 34,632 B | 37 / 56 MiB (56) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `words` | 11.5 ± 0.1 ms (18.7) | 10.4 ± 0.1 ms (20.2) | 201.3 ± 1.2 ms (861.7) | 57.6 ± 0.5 ms (124.5) | 361.2 ± 4.6 ms (1,156) | 58.0 ± 0.4 ms (131.3) | 106,200 / 87,880 B | 38 / 78 MiB (78) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `compiler/diagnose.nz` | 166.7 ± 1.1 ms (297.8) | 152.9 ± 0.7 ms (331.5) | 1.689 ± 0.002 s (4.135) | 0.593 ± 0.002 s (1.024) | **20.32 ± 0.05 s** (26.65) | 0.597 ± 0.002 s (1.114) | 5.43 / 5.04 MB | 339 / **736 MiB** (724) |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The figure in parentheses is *Build speed*'s, 2026-10-17. Start-up of the `-O2` `hello`: 1.9 ± 0.0 ms.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What changed.** A warm build of an unchanged program is 1.7–2.9× faster (`hello` 88.5 → 30.5 ms, `words` 124.5 →")
    strs_push(l, "57.6 ms, the front end 1.024 → 0.593 s): 7.2's 100 ms budget is met by `words` at 58 ms, and the ≤ 25 ms target is")
    strs_push(l, "within 6 ms for `hello`. Cold builds are 1.8–4.3× faster on the small programs (`words` `-O0` 862 → 201 ms: the")
    strs_push(l, "runtime's units and the program's compile side by side) and 1.3–2.4× on the large one (`-O0` 4.1 → 1.7 s; `-O2`")
    strs_push(l, "26.7 → 20.3 s). `check` is 1.6–1.8× faster, and **with its cache warm is now faster than `--no-cache`** (10.4 against")
    strs_push(l, "11.5 ms on `words`, 152.9 against 166.7 ms on the front end), where it was 8–11% slower. What did not change: a cold")
    strs_push(l, "`-O2` build of the front end takes 20.3 s and 736 MiB (`-O0`: 1.7 s and 339 MiB): the memory is LLVM's, on one unit of")
    strs_push(l, "51,000 lines. The comparison with the other compiled languages' build times is in the run below (*Eighteen")
    strs_push(l, "languages, re-run*).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Eighteen languages on every parameter, re-run and measured (quiet window, 2026-10-19)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`python3 bench/compare/compare.py NAZM OUT --runs 10`, Nazm release from `0a52becf`, against the same")
