    strs_push(l, "¹ GCC's optimiser (Fortran and Ada are both GCC) turns the doubly recursive `fib` into far fewer calls; the")
    strs_push(l, "hand-written assembly `fib` (44.1 ms, a plain recursive call per call) is the honest floor for a call-per-call `fib`")
    strs_push(l, "on this core.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What changed since 2026-10-17.** `words` 115.4 → 103.8 ms (−10%: the preemption poll's cost is gone with")
    strs_push(l, "preemption by interrupt, and `file_lines` and ThinLTO are in); `fib` 44.8 → 44.2; `primes` W = 1 173.6 → 173.3 ms,")
    strs_push(l, "W = 8 24.3 → 23.9, W = 10 31.8 → 27.4 ms. **Builds are the largest move**: a cold `words` build 1,166 → 352 ms (rank #10 → #6 of 12: behind C, Fortran, Go, Rust and Java, whose 348 ms is within 1%, and ahead of C++, Pascal, Swift, C#, Ada and Zig); warm 718 → 370 ms; `hello` cold 194 → 107 ms (#7 → #3 of 14, behind only the assembly and C). **Where Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "leads:** start-up among checked languages (1.93 ms, first of ten rows), peak memory (first on `hello`, third of sixteen on")
    strs_push(l, "`words`), the shortest `hello`, the third-shortest `words` by characters, and the parallel job among checked rows")
    strs_push(l, "(second only to checked Rust, within 1–4%). **Where it is behind:** `words` time (Zig 2.2×, Rust 1.6×, C 1.4×,")
    strs_push(l, "Fortran 1.2×, Go 1.2× faster), `fib` against unchecked C/C++/Rust/Zig (1.26×: the overflow checks; checked Rust is 44.5),")
    strs_push(l, "and build time against C, Rust's cached build, Go and Fortran on `words` (a cold build is 4.6× C's; warm, 370 ms against Go's")
    strs_push(l, "62 ms and C's 78 ms).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Fan-in and the four-task program after their fixes, measured (quiet window, 2026-10-19)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The two regressions of the quiet-window runs above, after `6b5d066e` (a channel waiter is counted out by")
    strs_push(l, "whoever takes it off a list, runtime ABI 50: woken waiters no longer hold every send and receive on the")
    strs_push(l, "locked path) and `26e5e64a` (a whole-program link generates for the target's baseline CPU, so ThinLTO's")
    strs_push(l, "atomics are single LSE instructions on arm64 rather than exclusive-load retry loops). The same sources built")
    strs_push(l, "`--no-cache --opt-level 2` by the release `nazm` of `0a52becf` and of `26e5e64a`, run side by side in one")
    strs_push(l, "`hyperfine -N --warmup 3` call (20 runs fan-in, 15 the four-task `alloc4.nz`), each begun below load 2 (1.82,")
    strs_push(l, "1.56) with no cargo, rustc or nextest running. Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2. Both fan-in builds print 499999500000.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| program | `0a52becf` median (min–max) | `26e5e64a` median (min–max) | change |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| fan-in, 1,000,000 values, 8 producers | 908.1 ms (68.0–1,490.3); CPU 4.89 s | **365.9 ms** (244.7–798.3); CPU 2.37 s | 2.5× faster; below the 445 ms baseline |")
    strs_push(l, "| four tasks (`bench/compare/nazm/alloc4.nz`) | 294.4 ms (261.0–436.8); CPU 1.14 s | **214.2 ms** (199.1–234.5); CPU 0.85 s | −27%; within 5% of v1's 203 ms |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Fan-in is still spread (σ about a third of the mean) and 5.4× Go's 67 ms: the remaining gap is the")
    strs_push(l, "many-producer path of the channel itself, not the regression.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## nbody and binary-trees in every language, measured (quiet window, 2026-10-19)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`python3 bench/compare/compare.py NAZM OUT --runs 10 --only nbody,bintrees` at `7963c0c9`, the release `nazm`")
    strs_push(l, "of `26e5e64a` (`--opt-level 2`), the toolchains of *Eighteen languages, re-run* above. nbody: the Benchmarks")
    strs_push(l, "Game's five bodies, 5,000,000 steps; binary-trees: depth 18. Every row printed the expected output. Nazm's")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter is not timed on these two (minutes a run, never ranked); COBOL and the hand-written assembly have")
    strs_push(l, "no source. nbody began at load 1.91 and binary-trees at 2.33 (`compare.py` does not wait between programs; the")
    strs_push(l, "1-minute average carried nbody's own runs), with no cargo, rustc or nextest running. Apple M1 Pro, macOS 27.2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Nazm's rank** among the languages (each language's best row; lower is better):")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| program | run time | peak RSS | binary | build cold | build warm | lines | characters | among rows checking overflow and bounds |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| nbody | 228.5 ms, **#3** of 16 (Rust 154.1, Zig 160.3; C 287.6, Go 294.7, Fortran 305.2) | 1.70 MiB, **#1** of 16 | 50 KiB, #4 of 12 | 175 ms, **#3** of 12 (C 92, Pascal 165) | 172 ms, #5 of 12 (Go 61) | 79, #8 of 16 | 2,452, #4 of 16 | **#3** of 7 (Rust checked 154.1, Zig safe 160.6) |")
    strs_push(l, "| binary-trees | 3,804 ms, **#14** of 16 (Java 350, Bun 557, Node 676, Go 866, C 1,154, Rust 1,314) | 163 MiB, #15 of 16 (C 17.8 MiB) | 67 KiB, #5 of 12 | 203 ms, #5 of 12 (C 76) | 205 ms, #5 of 12 (Go 60) | 37, #14 of 16 | 973, #12 of 16 | #3 of 7 (Fortran checked 1,175, Ada 1,209; Zig safe 3,695) |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the numbers say.** nbody, floating point in a fixed array, is ahead of C, C++, Go and Fortran (1.26× C's")
    strs_push(l, "speed) and behind only Rust and Zig, with the least memory of all. binary-trees is the largest gap measured so")
    strs_push(l, "far: 3.3× C, 11× Java (a generational collector built for exactly this), and 9× C's memory — allocation and")
    strs_push(l, "release of many small boxed nodes (`enum Tree` with `Box[Tree]`) is the path to work on, and the program is")
    strs_push(l, "long beside the languages with classes. Not claimed: any lead on binary-trees.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## binary-trees after the box and free-list fixes, measured (quiet window, 2026-10-19)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`python3 bench/compare/compare.py NAZM OUT --runs 10 --only bintrees` at `95793836` (runtime ABI 51: a box holds one")
    strs_push(l, "element, a one-thread program keeps every freed small block, a release that is not the last is inlined), begun at")
    strs_push(l, "load 1.82 with no cargo, rustc or nextest running and Apple's `knowledgeconstructiond` stopped. Every row printed the")
    strs_push(l, "expected output; the other languages' rows agree with *nbody and binary-trees* above to within 3%.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | before (`26e5e64a`) | after (`95793836`) | rank among 16 languages |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| run time, median | 3,804 ms | **1,971.7 ms** (1.93× faster) | #14 → **#13** (Java 355, Bun 568, Node 696, Go 898, C# 1,078, Fortran 1,116, C 1,158) |")
    strs_push(l, "| peak RSS | 163 MiB | **98.3 MiB** (−40%) | #15 → **#12** (C 17.8 MiB) |")
    strs_push(l, "| among the 7 rows checking overflow and bounds | | | **#4** (Fortran checked 1,182, Ada 1,222, Rust checked 1,384); the earlier section's \"#3 of 7\" should read #5 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Against C: 1.7× the time and 5.5× the memory, from 3.3× and 9×. What remains is the box's representation (a header")
    strs_push(l, "block plus a data block where C has one node) and the retain/release pairs of a MIR without moves —")
    strs_push(l, "performance-leadership 8.2, for the optimisation stage after R8. Not claimed: any lead on binary-trees.")
    str_join(l, str_from_byte(10)) + str_from_byte(10)
}

fn dd_doc6() -> Str {
    let l = strs_new()
    strs_push(l, "# Research register")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Status: hypotheses, kept apart from commitments. Nothing here is a plan, a roadmap entry")
    strs_push(l, "or a capability, and nothing here may be cited as evidence for one.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`master-architecture.md` §1 separates implemented behaviour, accepted design, open")
    strs_push(l, "questions and research proposals — a distinction inherited from the 2026-09-20 decision")
    strs_push(l, "record, which noted that the last is *\"speculative, and not entitled to be described as a")
    strs_push(l, "plan\"*. That distinction survived the first era in one place — automatic")
    strs_push(l, "layout selection, which `architecture.md` §4 labels a proposed research direction pending a")
    strs_push(l, "literature review that has not been done — and nowhere else. This document gives the rest of")
    strs_push(l, "them the same treatment.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Every item carries a falsifier.** An item without a result that would invalidate it is")
    strs_push(l, "not a hypothesis; it is a preference, and it belongs in `architecture.md` as a design")
    strs_push(l, "decision or nowhere.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The spine of the open-question set is `docs/user/spec.md` *Open* and `docs/internal/performance-log.md`'s")
    strs_push(l, "ranked headroom, both of which state their questions better than a summary would. Those are")
    strs_push(l, "referenced, not restated.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## R1 · Mutable value semantics is ergonomic enough to be the surface model")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Hypothesis** · A surface model of read-only projection, exclusive mutation, and")
    strs_push(l, "consumption/move gives ordinary programs memory safety without a lifetime annotation the")
    strs_push(l, "programmer writes, while a full region and borrow calculus is retained *inside* the IR so")
    strs_push(l, "the architecture is not trapped if the surface proves insufficient. `architecture.md` §5")
    strs_push(l, "states the design and names the hedge.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Required prerequisite** · A typed core IR to carry places and regions; `docs/user/spec.md`")
    strs_push(l, "*Open* lists the four questions that must be answered first, of which copy elision is the")
    strs_push(l, "sharp one — MVS is unusable if what the compiler guarantees, versus what it merely usually")
    strs_push(l, "does, is folklore.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence needed** · The self-hosting compiler rewritten against the surface model without")
    strs_push(l, "an escape hatch, and peak RSS bounded by live data rather than total allocation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Invalidating result** · A common pattern in the existing `compiler/*.nz` sources that")
    strs_push(l, "cannot be expressed without exposing regions in the surface syntax. One would be enough;")
    strs_push(l, "the compiler is the honest test case because it was written before the model existed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N7 answered this, and the answer was no — for a reason worth keeping.** The hypothesis")
    strs_push(l, "was that mutable value semantics should be Nazm's *surface* model. The audit")
    strs_push(l, "(`architecture.md` §7.7) established that Nazm's surface model is already the opposite and")
    strs_push(l, "has been since sequences existed: `let b = a;` on an `Ints` aliases, a push through one is")
    strs_push(l, "visible through the other, and `docs/user/spec.md` has specified that in those words. Adopting")
    strs_push(l, "MVS would not have been choosing a surface model; it would have been **changing** one, and")
    strs_push(l, "the measured programs that depend on the current one include every sequence parameter in")
    strs_push(l, "the self-hosted compiler.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "So the question this item asks — *is MVS ergonomic enough to be the surface model* — turned")
    strs_push(l, "out to be the wrong question to ask second. The right one was asked first: *what do values")
    strs_push(l, "mean now*. The answer made the hypothesis moot for `Ints` and `Strs`, and **already true**")
    strs_push(l, "for `Str`, which has value semantics with no observable copy and needed no machinery at")
    strs_push(l, "all to get them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The prerequisite is also gone rather than met. It said a typed core IR was needed to carry")
    strs_push(l, "places and regions, with copy elision as the sharp question. Reclamation arrived with no")
    strs_push(l, "core IR, no regions, no places and no elision question, because counting references to a")
    strs_push(l, "handle needs none of them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What survives, narrower and sharper.** MVS remains a live hypothesis for a *future* kind")
    strs_push(l, "of value — user-defined records, where there is no existing meaning to break and where the")
    strs_push(l, "choice between value and reference semantics is genuinely open. The invalidating result is")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged and is still the right test: a pattern in `compiler/*.nz` that cannot be")
    strs_push(l, "expressed without exposing regions.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence needed** (revised) · Not a rewrite of the compiler. A user-defined record type,")
    strs_push(l, "and a demonstration that value semantics for it are ergonomic in the compiler's own")
    strs_push(l, "patterns and implementable without regions in the surface syntax.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Status: RESEARCH, and re-scoped.** Not verified: no design was chosen for records, and a")
    strs_push(l, "design chosen is not a hypothesis tested. What changed is that it no longer blocks")
    strs_push(l, "reclamation, and reclamation no longer waits on it — which was the dependency this item was")
    strs_push(l, "carrying without being asked to.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N8 sharpened it once more, without answering it.** Completing reclamation for the current")
    strs_push(l, "type universe removed the last reason to reach for MVS *defensively* — \"peak RSS bounded by")
    strs_push(l, "live data rather than total allocation\", the evidence this item originally asked for, is now")
    strs_push(l, "measured and true for every type the language has, and it was obtained by counting")
    strs_push(l, "references rather than by changing what a value means. So the remaining question for records")
    strs_push(l, "is a question about **ergonomics and expressiveness alone**, which is what it should always")
    strs_push(l, "have been.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "One thing N8 did add to the terms. A record is the first type that can be made recursive,")
    strs_push(l, "and the leak-freedom claim in `capability-matrix.md` area 4 rests on the fact that no")
    strs_push(l, "current value can refer to one that refers back. Whichever way records go, the cycle policy")
    strs_push(l, "is part of the design rather than a follow-up: `docs/user/spec.md`'s *Cycles* says so in advance.")
    strs_push(l, "**This item is not resolved by N8 and must not be read as resolved** — strings and channels")
    strs_push(l, "being reclaimed says nothing about whether value semantics suit a user-defined type.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N9 ran the experiment, 2026-09-23. Status: **SUPPORTED, not VERIFIED.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Records exist, and they are **nominal value types whose fields keep their own semantics**:")
    strs_push(l, "an `Int` field copies, a `Str` field is a value with the same bytes, an `Ints` or `Chan`")
    strs_push(l, "field is another reference to the same storage, and a nested record recurses. No lifetime")
    strs_push(l, "syntax, no region, no borrow annotation, and no escape hatch. `docs/user/spec.md`, *Records*,")
    strs_push(l, "is the model; `architecture.md` §7.10 is what it took to implement.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the evidence is.** The invalidating result this item names — *a pattern in")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/*.nz` that cannot be expressed without exposing regions in the surface syntax* —")
    strs_push(l, "did not appear. Records were implemented in both compilers, used across module boundaries,")
    strs_push(l, "passed into tasks, returned from functions on both edges, nested, and copied in loops, and")
    strs_push(l, "none of it needed a region, a lifetime or an annotation. 27 memory cases and 15 mutations")
    strs_push(l, "hold the ownership half; `spec.md`'s cost table states what a copy costs so that the")
    strs_push(l, "ergonomics are not bought with a hidden price.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**And the compiler uses one.** `Place { line, column }` in `compiler/emit.nz`. That is")
    strs_push(l, "deliberately one record rather than a migration, and the reason is itself the finding:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "* the structures this compiler is built from — the token columns, the node arena, the")
    strs_push(l, "  function table, the record table N9 itself added — are **parallel arrays**, and each")
    strs_push(l, "  wants a `Vec<Record>` before a rewrite would be honest. There is no container that can")
    strs_push(l, "  hold a record, so a migration would have meant packing fields into strings, which is what")
    strs_push(l, "  the arrays already avoid;")
    strs_push(l, "* several of those arrays are passed **because they are shared mutable state** — the value")
    strs_push(l, "  counter, the label counter, the ownership set, the block-liveness flags. A record is a")
    strs_push(l, "  value, so it cannot replace them. That is not a defect in records; it is the value/handle")
    strs_push(l, "  distinction doing exactly what `spec.md` says it does, and it means records and sequences")
    strs_push(l, "  are complements rather than alternatives;")
    strs_push(l, "* what was left is the case where the language genuinely could not say what the code meant:")
    strs_push(l, "  a function returning two values. `line_of` and `column_of` existed as two functions for")
    strs_push(l, "  that reason alone, one scanning forward and one backward. That is a small win, and it is")
    strs_push(l, "  a *real* one, and one real win is worth more than a manufactured migration.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Why SUPPORTED and not VERIFIED.** The hypothesis is about ergonomics, and one record in")
    strs_push(l, "one compiler plus a test suite is evidence, not proof. Three questions the experiment did")
    strs_push(l, "not reach:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "* **no container has been asked the question.** `Vec<Record>` is where value semantics")
    strs_push(l, "  usually start to hurt — element access, in-place mutation, and whether `xs[i].f = v` is")
    strs_push(l, "  expressible without a place calculus the surface hides;")
    strs_push(l, "* **no variant has been asked it.** A payload's ownership is a record's question, but a")
    strs_push(l, "  payload that is *sometimes* there is not;")
    strs_push(l, "* **copy elision is still folklore.** This item's original prerequisite called that the")
    strs_push(l, "  sharp question and it remains unanswered: `let b = a;` on a record with many owning")
    strs_push(l, "  fields costs one reference adjustment per field, `spec.md` says so, and nothing yet")
    strs_push(l, "  promises when the compiler may elide the pair. `performance.md` measures the cost;")
    strs_push(l, "  nobody has specified when it disappears.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence needed next** · A generic container holding a record, and a statement of when")
    strs_push(l, "redundant retain/release pairs may be elided. Either could still invalidate the surface")
    strs_push(l, "model; neither has been tried.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N10 asked the second of those three questions, 2026-09-23. Status: still **SUPPORTED,")
    strs_push(l, "not VERIFIED.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*\"No variant has been asked it\"* was one of the three gaps N9 left. N10 asked it: closed")
    strs_push(l, "nominal enums with named payload fields, eliminated by exhaustive `match`, composing with")
    strs_push(l, "records in both directions. The answer, on the same terms as before, is that the")
    strs_push(l, "invalidating result did not appear — **a payload that is sometimes there needed no region,")
    strs_push(l, "no lifetime and no annotation either.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What the experiment adds to the evidence, and what it does not:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "* **the surface model held where the ownership question became dynamic.** A record's copy")
    strs_push(l, "  is a fixed walk; an enum's is a branch and then a walk, and which walk is a value the")
    strs_push(l, "  program carries. That is the first place the language's memory rules could not be")
    strs_push(l, "  answered statically, and the surface did not have to change to accommodate it: `let b =")
    strs_push(l, "  a` still means what it meant, and a pattern binding is a borrowed view of a payload with")
    strs_push(l, "  nothing written down about how long it lives;")
    strs_push(l, "* **the ergonomics were tested where they are sharpest** — a payload returned out of the")
    strs_push(l, "  arm that matched it, out of a value dying on the same line. `take_name` is four lines and")
    strs_push(l, "  says nothing about lifetimes. That shape is the variant equivalent of N8's return-order")
    strs_push(l, "  tests, and it is the one a surface model without regions most plausibly cannot express;")
    strs_push(l, "* **the exhaustiveness rule is an ergonomic cost, honestly.** No wildcard arm means adding")
    strs_push(l, "  a variant breaks every importer that believed it had handled the whole enum. That is")
    strs_push(l, "  intended while the language is young and it is a real friction, and a later")
    strs_push(l, "  `non_exhaustive` design will have to weigh it;")
    strs_push(l, "* **and the compiler uses one, in the one place a container is not needed.**")
    strs_push(l, "  `enum Owning { Nothing, Sequence, Strings, Backing, Channel, Record(at: Int),")
    strs_push(l, "  Enum(at: Int) }` replaced the small integer `compiler/emit.nz`'s `owns` returned. The")
    strs_push(l, "  node kinds, token kinds and type codes stayed integers, because they live in an `Ints`")
    strs_push(l, "  and there is no container that can hold an enum — which is the same wall N9 hit, reached")
    strs_push(l, "  from the other side. What `Owning` shows is that the ergonomic win is real where the")
    strs_push(l, "  language can express it: the dispatch became exhaustive, and **making it exhaustive found")
    strs_push(l, "  a defect N9 had shipped**, where a record crossing a task boundary produced a wrong answer")
    strs_push(l, "  and leaked its fields in the self-hosted compiler.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Why still SUPPORTED and not VERIFIED.** Two of the three gaps N9 named are open, and one")
    strs_push(l, "of them is the same one:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "* **no container has been asked the question.** Unchanged, and now the sharper of the two:")
    strs_push(l, "  `Vec[Token]` is what the self-hosted compiler would need to use an enum for anything, and")
    strs_push(l, "  it is what would let an element's payload be mutated in place;")
    strs_push(l, "* **copy elision is still folklore.** Unchanged, and an enum makes it slightly worse: a")
    strs_push(l, "  copy now costs a branch as well as the reference adjustments, and nothing says when")
    strs_push(l, "  either may be elided;")
    strs_push(l, "* what N10 *closed* is the variant question, and closing it moved nothing else.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence needed next** · Unchanged, and now with a name: a generic container holding a")
    strs_push(l, "record or an enum, which is `Vec[T]`. It is the prerequisite for the dogfood this item has")
    strs_push(l, "now failed to reach twice, and that repetition is itself the finding.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N11 asked the container question, 2026-09-23. Status: still **SUPPORTED, not VERIFIED**")
    strs_push(l, "— one of the three gaps closed, the sharpest one left.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`Vec[T]` exists, in both compilers, and holds records, enums, strings and other `Vec`s. The")
    strs_push(l, "invalidating result did not appear: **a container of records needed no region, no lifetime,")
    strs_push(l, "no annotation and no place calculus.** What made that true is a decision, not a discovery,")
    strs_push(l, "and it is the one this item has to weigh:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "* **`Vec[T]` is a handle, and its elements are values.** `let b = a` on a `Vec` aliases, as it")
    strs_push(l, "  does on an `Ints`; `vec_get` returns **its own copy** of an element by the element's law,")
    strs_push(l, "  and `vec_set` replaces one. So a record inside a `Vec` keeps value semantics — mutating the")
    strs_push(l, "  copy changes nothing in the vector — and the surface never had to say who may hold a")
    strs_push(l, "  reference into the storage, because nobody can.")
    strs_push(l, "* **The price is the one this item predicted.** There is no `xs[i].f = v`. Updating an")
    strs_push(l, "  element's field is get, change, set — three operations and a copy of every owning field")
    strs_push(l, "  twice. That is not hidden: `spec.md` says why the indexing form is absent, and")
    strs_push(l, "  `performance.md` measures what the copy costs. It is exactly the place where \"value")
    strs_push(l, "  semantics usually start to hurt\", and the answer N11 gives is to make the hurt explicit")
    strs_push(l, "  rather than to remove it.")
    strs_push(l, "* **The cycle argument held a second time, by refusal.** A container that can hold a record")
    strs_push(l, "  is what makes an ownership cycle expressible, and the type system refuses every definition")
    strs_push(l, "  that could form one (`N0359`) while leaving acyclic nesting legal. So counting is still")
    strs_push(l, "  complete for every type a program can write.")
    strs_push(l, "* **And the dogfood this item failed to reach twice happened.** The self-hosted compiler's")
    strs_push(l, "  diagnostics were four parallel arrays and are a `Vec[Diag]` now. No other structure was")
    strs_push(l, "  migrated, deliberately: the node arena and the record table are shared mutable state as")
    strs_push(l, "  much as they are data, which is the handle/value distinction N9 recorded, and the integer")
    strs_push(l, "  tags that N10 wanted as enums are compared in hundreds of places where an enum has no `==`")
    strs_push(l, "  — a cost this item should count against value semantics rather than hide.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Why still SUPPORTED and not VERIFIED.** What remains is the item's original sharp")
    strs_push(l, "question, now larger than ever: **copy elision is still folklore.** A `vec_get` of a record")
    strs_push(l, "copies every owning field and a `vec_set` copies them again, and nothing says when either")
    strs_push(l, "pair may be removed. The surface model is ergonomic where the language has run it; whether")
    strs_push(l, "it stays affordable depends on a specification that does not exist.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence needed next** · A statement of when redundant retain/release pairs may be elided,")
    strs_push(l, "tested against the get-change-set shape, and a second real migration — one where the")
    strs_push(l, "elements are updated in place in a loop — measured before and after.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N12 added typed errors as values, 2026-09-24. Status: still **SUPPORTED, not VERIFIED**.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A failure became a value like any other, and the value model needed nothing new for it:")
    strs_push(l, "`Result` and `Option` are ordinary enums, a propagated `Vec[Diag]` is one handle through")
    strs_push(l, "every return, and the front end's `Result[Checked, Vec[Diag]]` carries twenty handles in a")
    strs_push(l, "record without copying a table. So the evidence this item gains is that **value semantics")
    strs_push(l, "absorbed error handling without a second model** — no exception object, no unwinding, no")
    strs_push(l, "ownership rule special to failures. What N12 adds to the cost side is small and measured")
    strs_push(l, "(`performance.md`): `?` on success is a retain of the payload and a release of the")
    strs_push(l, "`Result`, which is the pair copy elision would remove, and the explicit form of an early")
    strs_push(l, "return from an arm is awkward in the native subset because an arm cannot be a block there.")
    strs_push(l, "Neither changes the status.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N12.1, 2026-09-24, closed the second of those and adds one observation.* A block used as a")
    strs_push(l, "value needed no ownership rule of its own in either native backend: its locals are frame")
    strs_push(l, "storage, its tail is borrowed, and whatever takes the value over takes its own reference —")
    strs_push(l, "the rule every value already follows. And the `Option` dogfood (`record_owned`) removed four")
    strs_push(l, "`>= 0` guards whose only job was to stop a `-1` meaning *none* from comparing equal to a")
    strs_push(l, "`-1` meaning *not a record*: a sentinel is a value that participates in comparisons it was")
    strs_push(l, "never meant for, and an enum is not. Status unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N13 derived equality, 2026-09-25. Status: still **SUPPORTED, not VERIFIED** — and one new finding.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Derived equality composes; abstraction over it does not.** Structural `==` composed")
    strs_push(l, "successfully through every nominal value type whose components already have equality —")
    strs_push(l, "records, enums over every variant, concrete generic instances after substitution, and")
    strs_push(l, "`Option` and `Result` as the ordinary enums they are — with no declaration, no rule naming")
    strs_push(l, "a type, and no new ownership rule: comparing borrows, and a compared temporary is released")
    strs_push(l, "once, which is the rule a `Str` comparison already followed. The value model gained a")
    strs_push(l, "capability and needed nothing for it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What did **not** compose is generic abstraction over that capability. After N13 a concrete")
    strs_push(l, "`Box[Int]` has equality and `fn same_box[T](a: Box[T], b: Box[T]) -> Bool { a == b }` does")
    strs_push(l, "not, nor does `fn same[T](a: T, b: T)`, because nothing can say \"`T` has equality\" — Nazm has")
    strs_push(l, "no constraint or trait mechanism, and checking a generic body once, parametrically, is")
    strs_push(l, "exactly what makes the refusal correct. This is the first capability the language derives")
    strs_push(l, "for concrete types that a generic definition cannot ask for, and it is the evidence that may")
    strs_push(l, "justify a constrained-generics milestone; it does not settle what such a mechanism looks")
    strs_push(l, "like, and N13 did not begin one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The dogfood adds the second observation R1 has been collecting: `analyse.nz`'s completion")
    strs_push(l, "states were three integers in an `Ints`, with a fourth meaning \"no arm yet\", and are an")
    strs_push(l, "`enum Completion` in a `Vec[Completion]` and an `Option[Completion]` now, compared with")
    strs_push(l, "`==`. Nine historical mutations that compared a completion with `99` could no longer be")
    strs_push(l, "written: the invalid state they simulated is not a value of the type. Performance moved")
    strs_push(l, "within noise (`performance.md`). Status unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N14 let a generic definition require equality, 2026-09-25. Status: still **SUPPORTED, not VERIFIED**.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**One built-in capability requirement solved the abstraction N13 could not express.**")
    strs_push(l, "`fn same_box[T: Equality](a: Box[T], b: Box[T])` is valid, and nothing new was needed to make")
    strs_push(l, "it so beyond recording which parameters require equality: N13's single derivation, reading a")
    strs_push(l, "required parameter as having equality, gives `Box[T]`, `Option[T]` and `Result[T, E]` their")
    strs_push(l, "answers under the body's assumptions, and the same derivation checks every argument at the")
    strs_push(l, "call. No solver, no implication graph, no dictionary, no runtime cost — an instance at `Int`")
    strs_push(l, "is the instructions a hand-written `same_int` is.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What it did not expose is a need for user-defined traits.** Nothing in N14's")
    strs_push(l, "implementation reached for one, and its dogfood audit found no generic helper in the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler that needed any capability at all: the compiler's membership searches are over")
    strs_push(l, "`Ints` and `Strs`, not `Vec[T]`, and the `Vec`s it has are never searched. So the evidence")
    strs_push(l, "says the immediate need was a *built-in* capability requirement, and that a full trait system")
    strs_push(l, "is **not yet justified** by any program here — the next one would have to be forced by code")
    strs_push(l, "that needs behaviour the language cannot derive (an ordering it has not chosen, a conversion")
    strs_push(l, "between error types), not by the symmetry of having one bound.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N78 update (2026-10-03).** Traits were built (`architecture.md` §7.79), against a program named")
    strs_push(l, "before the code: rendering every element of a `Vec[T]` from generic code (`@std/show`'s")
    strs_push(l, "`show_all`). Recorded honestly, that program could also be written by passing a rendering")
    strs_push(l, "function, as N50 allowed; what a bound saves is threading that function through every generic")
    strs_push(l, "layer, not a capability the language lacked. So the hypothesis \"user-defined traits pay for")
    strs_push(l, "themselves\" is **still open**. The design is deliberately small — nominal, static, coherent, no")
    strs_push(l, "dictionaries — so that it costs little if the answer is no. *Falsifier:* after N84's standard")
    strs_push(l, "library, count the generic standard functions that take a bound against those that take a")
    strs_push(l, "function argument for the same job. If bounds are not the common shape, the trait system is")
    strs_push(l, "ceremony and should not grow.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N80 (2026-10-03): is type-keyed precision enough?** Containers are followed by a cell per type,")
    strs_push(l, "not per handle, which is sound without alias analysis and coarse where two containers share a type.")
    strs_push(l, "*Measure:* across the corpus, count `N0372` and profile refusals whose trace crosses a cell written")
    strs_push(l, "by a different function than the one read. *Falsifier for staying here:* if real programs are")
    strs_push(l, "refused through a cell another part of the program polluted — a `Strs` of file lines making every")
    strs_push(l, "`Strs` path suspect — the next step is allocation-site cells, which need MIR's places. None was")
    strs_push(l, "found in the repository at N80.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N79 (2026-10-03): is the ambient bridge still load-bearing?** The bridge was kept as the default")
    strs_push(l, "and made visible rather than deleted, because removing it would refuse most of the repository's")
    strs_push(l, "undeclared functions, the compiler written in Nazm among them. The open question is whether that")
    strs_push(l, "cost is a migration or a design signal. *Measure:* with `inherits` recorded per function, count")
    strs_push(l, "across the corpus how many undeclared functions inherit anything, and of which kinds. *Falsifier")
    strs_push(l, "for keeping it:* if, after the compiler written in Nazm learns capabilities (N98), nearly every")
    strs_push(l, "inheriting function inherits only `OutCap` for diagnostics, a strict default with one threaded")
    strs_push(l, "`OutCap` is cheap, and the bridge should go.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## R2 · Content-addressed semantic IR pays for itself")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Hypothesis** · Normalising each top-level definition after type checking — names erased")
    strs_push(l, "to de Bruijn indices, dependencies replaced by their hashes — and keying compilation")
    strs_push(l, "results on the resulting Merkle DAG makes incremental compilation and cross-machine caching")
    strs_push(l, "correct by construction. `architecture.md` §3 carries the design and the cache-key")
    strs_push(l, "correctness conditions.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Required prerequisite** · A compilation unit and an identity that survives a process.")
    strs_push(l, "**Both are met as of N3 (2026-09-22).** A module can be checked from its own source and its")
    strs_push(l, "dependencies' interfaces (`crates/nazm-core/tests/unit_checking.rs`); a module has a")
    strs_push(l, "`ModuleKey` and a definition a `DefKey` that are equal across processes and across")
    strs_push(l, "checkouts; and a module's interface has a deterministic persisted form with a BLAKE3")
    strs_push(l, "fingerprint (`crates/nazm-cli/tests/durable_identity.rs`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A store keyed on semantic inputs exists as of N4 (2026-09-22), and it is not this.**")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-cache` computes `SourceFingerprint`, `CheckerIdentity` and `CheckKey`, and `nazm")
    strs_push(l, "check` reuses the result of checking a module whose inputs are unchanged")
    strs_push(l, "(`crates/nazm-cli/tests/incremental.rs`). That answers the *dependency* question — which")
    strs_push(l, "modules must be re-checked — and it does so from a module's **source bytes** and its")
    strs_push(l, "imports' interfaces.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "R2 is about **content addressing**: normalising each definition after type checking so that")
    strs_push(l, "two definitions which mean the same thing hash the same, and keying compilation *results*")
    strs_push(l, "on the resulting Merkle DAG. None of that exists. There is no normalised form of a")
    strs_push(l, "definition and no hash of one; `SourceFingerprint` is deliberately the opposite of one, and")
    strs_push(l, "its documentation says so — it normalises nothing, so a re-indent moves it. `InterfaceHash`")
    strs_push(l, "is deliberately not a cache key for an artefact, because it excludes bodies. What N4 built")
    strs_push(l, "is the *architecture* R2 would slot into, not the hypothesis.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The one measurement R2 asked for now has a first data point, and it is narrow.** A real")
    strs_push(l, "edit to one module of a real graph re-checks that module and reuses the rest; the saving is")
    strs_push(l, "in `performance.md`. It is a saving on semantic checking, against a key over source bytes —")
    strs_push(l, "not a rebuild saving against a key over normalised definitions, which is what would move")
    strs_push(l, "this hypothesis.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence needed** · A measured rebuild saving on a real edit, against a key over")
    strs_push(l, "normalised definitions rather than source bytes, and covering compiler identity, schema")
    strs_push(l, "version, transitive dependency hashes, target and CPU features, optimisation flags and ABI.")
    strs_push(l, "The three-key separation in `architecture.md` §7.4 says which of those N4 has and which it")
    strs_push(l, "deliberately does not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N5 narrowed one of those inputs, with evidence.** This item and N4's report both assumed")
    strs_push(l, "a dependent's *object* would have to be invalidated by its dependency's implementation.")
    strs_push(l, "Measured on the architecture N5 actually built (`architecture.md` §7.5): it does not. An")
    strs_push(l, "object names its dependencies in a `declare` and a `call`, so it depends on their symbol")
    strs_push(l, "identity and ABI signature, and changing a dependency's body leaves it byte-identical —")
    strs_push(l, "there is no cross-module optimisation for a body to reach through. A later key over")
    strs_push(l, "normalised definitions would therefore need **fewer** transitive inputs than assumed, not")
    strs_push(l, "more. Still nothing implemented: there is no normalised form of a definition, no hash of")
    strs_push(l, "one, and no artefact store.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N6 built an artefact store, and it took the opposite approach on purpose.** There is one")
    strs_push(l, "now — objects, keyed and validated (`architecture.md` §7.6) — and its key is not over")
    strs_push(l, "normalised definitions and not over source. It is a digest of the **exact bytes handed to")
    strs_push(l, "the object compiler**, plus that compiler's identity and the configuration it resolves.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "That is worth stating as a result against this hypothesis rather than as progress towards")
    strs_push(l, "it. R2's argument is that normalising definitions is how a key becomes both complete and")
    strs_push(l, "precise. N6 got completeness and precision at that one stage without normalising anything,")
    strs_push(l, "because the boundary it caches at consumes a byte string, and hashing what is actually")
    strs_push(l, "handed over cannot omit an input by construction. A dependency's body change and an export")
    strs_push(l, "the caller never calls both leave the caller's object reusable — the precision R2 promises —")
    strs_push(l, "with no semantic fact in the key at all.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What that does **not** settle: the same trick is unavailable anywhere the input is not a")
    strs_push(l, "byte string. Reusing a *semantic check*, or a lowering, or a resolution needs a key over")
    strs_push(l, "something structured, and that is still R2's territory. So the hypothesis is narrower than")
    strs_push(l, "it was, and more clearly aimed: content addressing has to earn its place above the backend")
    strs_push(l, "boundary, because below it the bytes are already the address.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Invalidating result** · The key must cover so much that hits are rare in practice, or an")
    strs_push(l, "omission produces a silent miscompile in testing. `architecture.md` already names the")
    strs_push(l, "second as the failure mode: anything omitted from the key is a silent miscompile waiting to")
    strs_push(l, "happen. N4's six mutations and N6's six remove one input each and require the suite to catch")
    strs_push(l, "it; that is the method the eventual content-addressed key would be held to.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Status: RESEARCH.** Unchanged. The prerequisites are met and two neighbouring results")
    strs_push(l, "exist; the hypothesis is untested, and N6 narrowed where it would have to be tested.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N12 found the identity rule a persisted-interface design has to state, 2026-09-24.**")
    strs_push(l, "An interface carries every type its exported shapes mention, including other modules'.")
    strs_push(l, "Rehydrated one at a time, each interface gave those types a fresh identity, so two")
    strs_push(l, "interfaces that both mentioned the core `Result` produced two `Result`s — invisible until a")
    strs_push(l, "consumer compared them, and fatal to `?` checked from interfaces alone. The fix is the rule")
    strs_push(l, "this item's design implies: a definition is identified by its `DefKey` across **every**")
    strs_push(l, "interface one compilation reads, so a type met twice is one type")
    strs_push(l, "(`PersistentUnitInterface::rehydrate_into`). A hash-keyed design would need the same rule")
    strs_push(l, "for the same reason, and would have hidden the defect the same way until something shared a")
    strs_push(l, "type. Status unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## R3 · Definition-hash equality is useful to an agent")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Hypothesis** · When an agent rewrites a function and the normalised Core hash is")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged, the compiler can tell it the edit produced an identical definition — detecting")
    strs_push(l, "one class of no-op edit and shortening a class of agent loop. `architecture.md` §3 states")
    strs_push(l, "both the idea's origin (Unison) and the contribution claimed here, which is the")
    strs_push(l, "agent-facing use rather than the hashing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Required prerequisite** · R2. N3 gives a definition an identity that survives a process,")
    strs_push(l, "which is the part an agent needs to be *told* which definition is meant — `DefKey` names")
    strs_push(l, "one across runs and across checkouts. It is not the part this hypothesis is about:")
    strs_push(l, "`DefKey` says *which* definition, and the claim here is about telling an agent that an edit")
    strs_push(l, "produced **the same** definition, which needs a content identity R2 does not have yet.")
    strs_push(l, "Nothing here is implemented, and `DefKey` existing is not an agent protocol.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence needed** · A measured reduction in wasted agent effort, under the protocol in")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/internal/research/evaluation.md` — whose thresholds are frozen and may not be relaxed — rather than an")
    strs_push(l, "anecdote.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Invalidating result** · No-op edits turn out to be rare, or agents do not act differently")
    strs_push(l, "when told. Note the honest scope already recorded: this detects normalised-Core")
    strs_push(l, "alpha-equivalence, **not** all behaviour-preserving rewrites, so a result showing agents")
    strs_push(l, "need the general case would invalidate the usefulness without touching the mechanism.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Status: RESEARCH.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## R4 · Automatic data-layout selection is sound and worth it")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Hypothesis** · Keeping field access symbolic through the IR — `project(place, field_id)`,")
    strs_push(l, "with offsets appearing only at the lowest level — lets the compiler choose layouts the")
    strs_push(l, "programmer did not, and wins enough to justify the constraint. `architecture.md` §4 is the")
    strs_push(l, "design and §7 records the Phase 1 deliverable.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Required prerequisite** · User-defined types, which do not exist. And the literature")
    strs_push(l, "review, which `architecture.md` §4 has called outstanding since it was written — **this")
    strs_push(l, "project is not entitled to claim the idea is novel until it is done.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence needed** · The eligibility predicate stated, behaviour settled under address")
    strs_push(l, "identity, escaping references, FFI, serialisation, atomics and separate compilation, and a")
    strs_push(l, "measured win on a benchmark that is not chosen to flatter it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Invalidating result** · The eligibility predicate excludes everything interesting, or the")
    strs_push(l, "literature shows the win is already available without the constraint.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Status: RESEARCH.** The architectural commitment that preserves the option — offsets only")
    strs_push(l, "at the lowest level — is already honoured and is the hardest thing here to reverse, so")
    strs_push(l, "keeping it costs nothing today and buys the experiment later.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N68 ran a first experiment, 2026-10-02. Status: **SUPPORTED for one layout, not for automatic selection.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Prior art, recorded before choosing* (from the literature as known to this project; the")
    strs_push(l, "citations were not re-fetched in this session, and no novelty is claimed): structure splitting")
    strs_push(l, "and field reordering for cache behaviour — Chilimbi, Davidson and Larus, *Cache-Conscious")
    strs_push(l, "Structure Definition*, PLDI 1999; Hundt, Mannarswamy and Chakrabarti, *Practical Structure Layout")
    strs_push(l, "Optimization and Advice*, CGO 2006; GCC's `-fipa-struct-reorg` (structure peeling, removed in")
    strs_push(l, "GCC 4.8 for lack of a safe eligibility analysis); Lattner and Adve's data-structure analysis for")
    strs_push(l, "pool allocation. Language-level and library SoA: ISPC's `soa<N>` types, Zig's")
    strs_push(l, "`std.MultiArrayList`, Jai's announced SoA, Halide's separation of an algorithm from its storage")
    strs_push(l, "schedule. None of them needs a constraint Nazm does not already have: the *eligibility* is what")
    strs_push(l, "the literature finds hard in C (addresses, casts, separate compilation), and in Nazm it is nearly")
    strs_push(l, "trivial — a `Vec` element has no address, crosses no FFI, is never serialised, and layout was")
    strs_push(l, "already by field name (§7.9). That is the finding, and it is about the language, not the idea.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*What was built and measured* (§7.70): `--layout soa` lays out every `Vec[R]` whose fields are")
    strs_push(l, "`Int`s and `Bool`s one array per field. Same results and failures everywhere tested; a one-field")
    strs_push(l, "scan over 1,000,000 eight-field records is 2.8× faster and equal to hand-written per-field")
    strs_push(l, "`Ints`; a scan reading all eight fields is 2× **slower**. So the layout is a win only by access")
    strs_push(l, "pattern, which is the cost model the compiler does not yet have — the invalidating half of the")
    strs_push(l, "hypothesis (*automatic* selection wins) is untested, and the option stays opt-in.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## R5 · An M:N scheduler with growable stacks beats one OS thread per task")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Hypothesis** · Green tasks over a work-stealing scheduler with growable stacks and an")
    strs_push(l, "event reactor give task density and latency that one OS thread per task cannot, without")
    strs_push(l, "`async`/`await` colouring the language.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Required prerequisite** · `nazm-rt`, which needs the workspace `unsafe_code = \"forbid\"`")
    strs_push(l, "to narrow to a per-crate allowance, which needs the memory model. Also a settled answer to")
    strs_push(l, "preemption — cooperative at back-edges and calls, or signal-based — which `docs/user/spec.md`")
    strs_push(l, "lists as open.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence needed** · Spawn-to-first-instruction latency, context-switch cost, and task")
    strs_push(l, "memory as **RSS, not virtual reservation, with page size recorded**, against a named")
    strs_push(l, "implementation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Invalidating result** · No measured advantage at the task counts real programs reach.")
    strs_push(l, "The precedent is set and should be followed: `architecture.md` withdrew the \"1M live tasks")
    strs_push(l, "under 2GB\" target as arithmetically unsupported rather than keeping it as aspiration.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Status: RESEARCH.** The shipped model — one POSIX thread per task, a mutex/condvar ring")
    strs_push(l, "per channel — is the semantic baseline and stays so until this is measured. Ownership")
    strs_push(l, "prevents data races; **that is not deadlock freedom** and must never be reported as such.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## R6 · Provenance and information flow can be checked at a usable approximation")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Hypothesis** · A lattice-valued qualifier on types, propagated position-sensitively,")
    strs_push(l, "catches real leaks at a false-positive rate programmers tolerate. `architecture.md` §5")
    strs_push(l, "states the design, keeps it a separate concern from effects and capabilities even where")
    strs_push(l, "machinery is shared, and records that calling it *\"nearly free once effects exist\"* was")
    strs_push(l, "overclaiming.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Required prerequisite** · Effects, and a MIR that tracks places.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence needed** · The chosen approximation stated **with what it misses**, and a")
    strs_push(l, "corpus where it finds real leaks without drowning the user. Full non-interference is")
    strs_push(l, "usually unusable in practice; the claim has to be about the approximation, not the ideal.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Invalidating result** · Implicit flows force either an unusable false-positive rate or an")
    strs_push(l, "approximation that misses the leaks people actually have.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Status: RESEARCH.** Every sub-question — implicit flows, sanitizers, aliasing through a")
    strs_push(l, "projection, declassification, the FFI boundary — is open in `docs/user/spec.md`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## R7 · Heterogeneous CPU/GPU/accelerator execution belongs in Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Hypothesis** · There is a version of accelerator support that fits a small semantic")
    strs_push(l, "kernel rather than bolting a second language onto the first.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Required prerequisite** · A reason to believe it, which does not currently exist.")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §1 says MLIR should be revisited *only if* Nazm pivots toward")
    strs_push(l, "tensor/accelerator codegen, and `roadmap.md` places tensors, GPUs, model providers and")
    strs_push(l, "distributed execution out of scope and not planned.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence needed** · A workload the project actually has, that a CPU backend cannot serve.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Invalidating result** · The honest default. This item exists to be **declined explicitly")
    strs_push(l, "rather than drift in through the phrase \"AI-native\"**, which law 6 defines as")
    strs_push(l, "machine-consumable compiler interfaces and not as an argument for syntax or for hardware.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Status: RESEARCH, and presumed no.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N67 tested the narrowest version, 2026-10-02. Status: **SUPPORTED for one map, still RESEARCH in general.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A kernel as an eligibility over existing functions, not a second language: `nazm accel` runs a")
    strs_push(l, "pure `(Int) -> Int` function as an OpenCL kernel on the M1 Pro's GPU with the language's checked")
    strs_push(l, "arithmetic and the sequential map's failure carried exactly, about 6× one CPU core on a Collatz")
    strs_push(l, "map (§7.69). It fits the small semantic kernel; whether it is worth more than a library call is")
    strs_push(l, "what a workload of the project's own would decide, and none exists yet.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## R8 · Critical-system verification techniques are reachable from this architecture")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Hypothesis** · Specified-rather-than-inherited arithmetic, refuse-by-name, and a")
    strs_push(l, "restriction-profile model are the right foundations for a subset amenable to formal")
    strs_push(l, "argument, and the distance to one is smaller than starting over.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Required prerequisite** · Nearly everything: a memory model, effects, contracts, a")
    strs_push(l, "bounded-stack story, and a toolchain qualification argument that the bootstrap explicitly")
    strs_push(l, "does **not** supply — `docs/internal/bootstrap.md` puts compiler trustworthiness on the list of")
    strs_push(l, "things a reproducible fixpoint does not establish.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Evidence needed** · A proof obligation discharged on a real Nazm program, and an")
    strs_push(l, "assessment against a named standard by someone qualified to make it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Invalidating result** · A semantic decision made for ergonomics that turns out to be")
    strs_push(l, "irreconcilable with the subset — which is the reason this item is worth tracking now rather")
    strs_push(l, "than later, since such a decision is cheap to avoid and expensive to undo.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Status: RESEARCH.** See the warning paragraph in")
    strs_push(l, "[`capability-matrix.md`](capability-matrix.md) under area 19; it applies to every sentence")
    strs_push(l, "here.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Where the rest of the open questions live")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Subject | Where |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Copy semantics, closure capture, copy elision, region assignment | `docs/user/spec.md` *Open* → Memory and values |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Is divergence an effect?** — blocks dropping an unused pure call | `docs/user/spec.md` *Open* → Effects |")
    strs_push(l, "| Allocation failure, panic, evaluation order, handler lowering | `docs/user/spec.md` *Open* → Effects |")
    strs_push(l, "| Cancellation semantics, preemption, captured globals under transfer | `docs/user/spec.md` *Open* → Concurrency |")
    strs_push(l, "| Layout eligibility and its interaction with identity, FFI, atomics | `docs/user/spec.md` *Open* → Layout selection |")
    strs_push(l, "| What must be settled before `nazm test --backend=all` means anything | `docs/user/spec.md` *Open* → Backend semantics |")
    strs_push(l, "| Surface syntax, and novelty as a budget | `docs/user/spec.md` *Open* → Syntax |")
    strs_push(l, "| Where the performance headroom is, ranked with confidence labels | `docs/internal/performance-log.md` |")
    strs_push(l, "| Authority: ambient by default, recorded as inherited authority and refusable by profile since N79; making the default strict is open | `docs/user/spec.md`, `architecture.md` §7.80, and `capability-matrix.md` area 6 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Visibility: private-by-default is a known future break | `docs/user/spec.md` |")
    str_join(l, str_from_byte(10)) + str_from_byte(10)
}

fn dd_doc7() -> Str {
    let l = strs_new()
    strs_push(l, "# Runbook — operating environment and execution safety")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**This document owns every operational rule in the repository.** If a heavy workload is")
    strs_push(l, "about to run, this is the file to read, and it is the only one that has to be read.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Facts measured on the development machine on 2026-09-19 and 2026-09-21, not")
    strs_push(l, "assumptions.** Re-measure before trusting any figure here; every one is machine-specific")
    strs_push(l, "and several are the kind that change without anyone noticing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Mandatory containment")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Absorbed 2026-09-21 from `NAZM_AUTONOMOUS_GOAL.md` §2.1, which was the completed Era-1")
    strs_push(l, "execution contract. These rules did not expire with it.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What must never run uncontained")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Only through the verified contained runner, `cargo xtask contained <workload>`:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- any generated compiler stage built **without a heap limit** — `nzlex`, `nzparse`, `nzcheck`,")
    strs_push(l, "  `nzemit`, `nazmc` — and any program written in Nazm built without one;")
    strs_push(l, "- the selfhost suite and `compiler/bootstrap.sh`;")
    strs_push(l, "- the self-build, `toolchain/selfbuild/selfbuild.sh` (`cargo xtask contained selfbuild`);")
    strs_push(l, "- fuzzing, the mutation catalogue, and heavy benchmarks.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**An environment variable is a declaration, not a ceiling. Never set `NAZM_CONTAINED=1` on")
    strs_push(l, "the host, and never use `NAZM_ALLOW_UNCONTAINED=1`.** The runner sets `NAZM_CONTAINED=1`")
    strs_push(l, "only *inside* an environment where a real ceiling already applies.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What may run on the host: one bounded-heap stage — R6, 2026-10-20")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Decided by the copyright holder on 2026-10-20, on the evidence of")
    strs_push(l, "`openspec/changes/r6-host-qualification/` (decision 3).*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "One program written in Nazm — the front end (`compiler/diagnose.nz`), the pipeline")
    strs_push(l, "(`toolchain/pipeline/main.nz`), the code generator (`toolchain/codegen/main.nz`), a command of")
    strs_push(l, "`toolchain/commands/`, or a harness tool — may run on the **macOS host** when **all** of these hold:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- it was built with a heap limit of **at most 2 GiB** (`nazm build --heap-limit`, or the")
    strs_push(l, "  self-build's runtime with that limit), which its runner checks before starting it: the counted")
    strs_push(l, "  heap is linked (`nz.heap_malloc` is in the executable) and the limit its `N0406` message names")
    strs_push(l, "  is not larger. A program that never allocates links no counted heap and is refused;")
    strs_push(l, "- it is the **only** such process, and no contained workload is running;")
    strs_push(l, "- it runs in the foreground under a wall-clock deadline, its output bounded and drained as the")
    strs_push(l, "  contained runner's is;")
    strs_push(l, "- its peak resident memory is recorded (`/usr/bin/time -l` reports memory; no timing is taken")
    strs_push(l, "  from it).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The one way to start it is `cargo xtask host-run [--deadline-secs N] -- EXECUTABLE [ARGS...]`")
    strs_push(l, "(`xtask/src/host_run.rs`; default deadline 900 s, at most 3600 s). It refuses, by name: `not-macos`,")
    strs_push(l, "`host-environment` (either containment variable set), `usage`, `no-executable`, `no-counted-heap`,")
    strs_push(l, "`no-heap-limit`, `ambiguous-heap-limit`, `heap-limit-too-large`, `withdrawn`,")
    strs_push(l, "`another-stage-running` and `contained-workload-running`. Do not run a Nazm-built program on the")
    strs_push(l, "host any other way.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`host-run` is the program's own as far as a script can see it. Its standard output is the program's")
    strs_push(l, "bytes, unchanged; its standard error is the program's, and the runner's one report line (heap")
    strs_push(l, "limit, peak resident memory, instructions retired where the platform counts them, the exit) goes")
    strs_push(l, "there only when no `--report FILE` is given, and is appended to FILE when it is. Its exit status is")
    strs_push(l, "the program's; the statuses that are not are 1 (refused or a usage error), 70 (the rule withdrawn),")
    strs_push(l, "124 (the deadline), 125 (killed by a signal) and 126 (output past `--max-output-mib`, default 4,")
    strs_push(l, "at most 256: the output is cut there, never compared as a prefix without saying so).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Every script under `toolchain/` that builds and runs a program written in Nazm sources")
    strs_push(l, "`toolchain/lib/stage.sh`: the program is built by the checkout's `nazm` with `--heap-limit` of at")
    strs_push(l, "most 2 GiB (`STAGE_HEAP`), and runs through `toolchain/lib/stage-run.sh`, which is a direct run under")
    strs_push(l, "a deadline inside the contained runner and a `host-run` (one at a time, report to a file) on the")
    strs_push(l, "macOS host. The scripts that run programs in parallel, built without a limit (`nazm test`), or as a")
    strs_push(l, "mutation campaign (`toolchain/commands/tests/run.sh`, `toolchain/harness/tests/{run.sh,mutants.sh}`)")
    strs_push(l, "refuse to start outside the contained runner.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The heap limit is a ceiling the program enforces on itself: every byte its code and runtime ask")
    strs_push(l, "for is counted first, and an allocation past the limit does not happen (`N0406`, status 2;")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/spec.md`, *A bounded heap*). It does not count a task's stack, the image, C's own")
    strs_push(l, "allocations or child processes — hence at most two at once (4 GiB of counted heap at worst, on a")
    strs_push(l, "32 GB host; the copyright holder's decision of 2026-10-22, which replaced one at a time), and the")
    strs_push(l, "deadline.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Still contained only:** the selfhost suite, `compiler/bootstrap.sh`, the self-build, fuzzing, the")
    strs_push(l, "mutation catalogue, heavy benchmarks, any program built without a limit, and two host stages at")
    strs_push(l, "once. `NAZM_CONTAINED=1` and `NAZM_ALLOW_UNCONTAINED=1` stay forbidden on a host.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Withdrawn at once**, back to contained only until investigated, if a host run's peak resident")
    strs_push(l, "memory exceeds its heap limit by more than 256 MiB, if an `N0406` does not stop the program, or")
    strs_push(l, "when the counted heap's runtime changes (`crates/nazm-runtime/src/heap.rs`, the pipeline's")
    strs_push(l, "`count_heap`) until `cargo xtask contained selfbuild` passes again with its heap probe. The runner")
    strs_push(l, "reports the first two itself, as `WITHDRAWAL CONDITION`, and writes a marker")
    strs_push(l, "(`~/.cache/nazm-host-run/withdrawn`) that makes every later `host-run` refuse until a person has")
    strs_push(l, "investigated and removed it. The third is a person's to apply: leave that marker in place.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The reason is specific to this platform: **macOS cannot cap a child's memory.** `RLIMIT_AS`")
    strs_push(l, "is an alias of `RLIMIT_RSS` there, and `setrlimit(2)` documents it as advisory — the system")
    strs_push(l, "*prefers* to reclaim from an offender rather than refusing its allocation. The ceiling must")
    strs_push(l, "come from outside the process.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/bootstrap.sh` and selfhost's four stage builders enforce this themselves: they")
    strs_push(l, "refuse to start rather than run unbounded.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**`nazm build` written in Nazm (R8 slice 4, accepted 2026-10-20).** The Nazm-built `nazm build`, itself")
    strs_push(l, "started through `host-run`, starts the pipeline and the code generator as stages one at a time and checks")
    strs_push(l, "each as `host-run` does (the counted heap linked, a limit of at most 2 GiB, the withdrawal conditions and")
    strs_push(l, "the marker). While a stage runs, the waiting driver (its front end's state freed first) and that one")
    strs_push(l, "stage are both Nazm-built processes; the copyright holder accepted this as one stage at a time. On the")
    strs_push(l, "default LLVM backend (slice 5) the stages are the pipeline alone — it writes each unit as LLVM text and")
    strs_push(l, "`clang` compiles it — and `nzcg` is only `--backend nazm`'s.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Slice 6 adds stages of the same kind, each admitted and run the same way, one at a time: the pipeline asked for")
    strs_push(l, "the `clang -###` probe's identity, for the object stores' lookups and fillings (`llvm-get`, `llvm-put`), for")
    strs_push(l, "the runtime's identity (`runtime-abi`) and, in `nazm runtime build`, for the runtime's texts")
    strs_push(l, "(`runtime-artifact`). `nazm runtime build` and `verify`, `--lib`, `--runtime` and the provenance files add no")
    strs_push(l, "other kind of process: `clang`, `strip`, `codesign`, `dsymutil` and the command `--attest-with` names.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What the runner must enforce")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Memory and swap set equal.** A cap that can be swapped past is not a cap.")
    strs_push(l, "- CPU and pid limits.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Wall-clock deadlines** — and a deadline is not a memory bound. Both are required.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Bounded stdout and stderr, drained concurrently**, so a flood cannot grow the parent.")
    strs_push(l, "- Bounded temporary and artefact storage. A memory limit does not stop a disk fill.")
    strs_push(l, "- Descendant cleanup and reaping. Killing a client is not killing the workload.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Compilation bounded too**, not only the execution of generated programs.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Explicit failure when containment is unavailable.** A silent skip reporting green on no")
    strs_push(l, "  evidence is a defect, not a pass.")
    strs_push(l, "- Effective limits verified by probes that allocate *and touch* memory, whose own maximum")
    strs_push(l, "  stays safe even if enforcement fails. Require a confirmed limit event, not a generic")
    strs_push(l, "  nonzero exit. `cargo xtask contained probe` is that check.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Refusal tests prove the gate works; they do not prove self-hosting works. The real selfhost")
    strs_push(l, "suite and the real bootstrap must run through the runner and produce correct results within")
    strs_push(l, "budget, with verified cleanup.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Serial execution")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "No competing heavy workloads: one contained workload at a time, and one mutant at a time.")
    strs_push(l, "**When a workload exceeds a budget, investigate the cause rather than raising the limit.**")
    strs_push(l, "Do not change machine-wide settings and do not delete unrelated files.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*History.* Until N14.1 this section also said \"one Cargo build job and one test thread where")
    strs_push(l, "applicable\". That rule came from the 2026-09-21 incident, when an unbounded selfhost run")
    strs_push(l, "took the host down, and it was kept because nothing had measured what parallelism *inside*")
    strs_push(l, "a bounded container cost. N14.1 measured it (`performance.md`, *Development and evidence")
    strs_push(l, "pipeline parallelism*) and relaxed exactly one thing: the **internal** parallelism of a")
    strs_push(l, "workload, chosen by a named profile.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Workload | Default profile | Why |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `contained tests` | P4T4 — 4 CPUs, 4 jobs, 4 test threads | 3.03× faster, inside every memory gate |")
    strs_push(l, "| `contained selfhost` | P4T4 | 3.44× faster, inside every memory gate |")
    strs_push(l, "| `contained mutate` | P1 — 1 CPU, 1 job, 1 thread | every parallel profile crossed the total-memory gate |")
    strs_push(l, "| `contained bootstrap`, `release`, `run` | P1 | not calibrated |")
    strs_push(l, "| `contained bench` | P1, permanently | a measurement shares the machine with nothing |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`--profile p8t8` (8 CPUs, 8 jobs, 8 test threads; R1.5 8.2, approved 2026-10-22) is opt-in for any workload but `bench`, under the same memory ceiling: a run it pushes past the ceiling is stopped like any other and the workload keeps its default.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`cargo xtask contained --profile p1 <workload>` reproduces any older result. What did not")
    strs_push(l, "change: containment is mandatory, the memory, swap, pid, storage and deadline ceilings are")
    strs_push(l, "the same numbers, workloads never overlap, mutants never run two at once, and a campaign's")
    strs_push(l, "journal is bound to the profile it ran under — a resume under another profile reuses")
    strs_push(l, "nothing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### CI runs the host-safe subset, and is not the release gate")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*R1, 2026-10-07.* GitHub's runners have no verified contained runner, so")
    strs_push(l, "`.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs only what may run on a host: formatting, `cargo lint`,")
    strs_push(l, "`cargo xtask check`, `cargo xtask workspace-tests --host-safe` (every test binary built; each run")
    strs_push(l, "except those whose source calls the containment guard, which it names as NOT RUN), the lifecycle")
    strs_push(l, "suite and the accounting selftest. The selfhost suite, the bootstrap, fuzzing and the mutation")
    strs_push(l, "catalogue are never run there and never waived: they run in `cargo xtask contained` and in the")
    strs_push(l, "release gate. A green CI run says nothing about them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The lifecycle suite's interruption tests restore SIGINT's default action in the process they")
    strs_push(l, "interrupt (through `perl`, since `unsafe` is forbidden), because a suite started as a `&` job of")
    strs_push(l, "a non-interactive shell hands every child an *ignored* SIGINT — N108's one lifecycle failure.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Autonomy limits")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Do not publish, push, tag, deploy, buy services, use paid model APIs, expose credentials,")
    strs_push(l, "change account permissions, delete unrelated files, reset user work, or prune shared Docker")
    strs_push(l, "resources. Do not disable Gatekeeper, SIP or watchdogs, and do not downgrade or reinstall")
    strs_push(l, "the OS. A missing remote is not a blocker to local development or local checks.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Status vocabulary")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**passed**, **skipped**, **refused**, **failed** and **unexecuted** are five different")
    strs_push(l, "outcomes and are never reported as one another. A timeout is a failure, not a result.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## The incident that produced these rules — 2026-09-21")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Condensed from the Era-1 ledger. The full narrative, the panic reports and the before/after")
    strs_push(l, "measurements are in Git history and at `~/nazm-incident-2026-09-21/`.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Three kernel panics (08:12:30, 08:26:49, 08:44:44), all *\"watchdog timeout: no checkins")
    strs_push(l, "from watchdogd in ~93 seconds\"*, while `xtask → cargo → selfhost` ran nine stage binaries")
    strs_push(l, "plus `nazmc` at once — `cargo test` uses one thread per core and this machine has ten.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Cause, measured.** `lexer.nz`, `parser.nz` and `check.nz` accumulated output with")
    strs_push(l, "`out = str_concat(out, ..)` in a loop. Each concatenation allocates a new buffer and copies")
    strs_push(l, "everything accumulated, and **the generated runtime never frees**, so retained bytes are")
    strs_push(l, "quadratic in output length. `emit.nz` had already been migrated to `strs_push` + `str_join`;")
    strs_push(l, "the other three had not. Doubling the input quadrupled the peak.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Repaired**, with byte-identical output across 24 stage/input combinations. `nzlex` on")
    strs_push(l, "21,490 B went from 2,889 MB to **7.1 MB**; inputs that had OOM'd at 3 GiB now peak near")
    strs_push(l, "11 MB.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Still open, and not to be reported as closed:**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- `nzemit` was reported at ~17 GB in the panic yet **could not be reproduced** — it")
    strs_push(l, "  measures linear and modest. Unexplained.")
    strs_push(l, "- The panic's `residentMemoryBytes` sums to 173.9 GB on a 32 GiB machine, so it is not")
    strs_push(l, "  disjoint physical RAM and its exact meaning is unconfirmed.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Kernel-panic causation is unproven.** A watchdog panic reports starvation, not")
    strs_push(l, "  causation, and this was a beta kernel (macOS 27.2, build 26B5086k). The compiler workload")
    strs_push(l, "  is a strong suspect, not a demonstrated cause.")
    strs_push(l, "- Quiet uptime since is an observation, not proof of stability.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The standing lesson is the one the rules above encode: **a deadline does not bound memory.**")
    strs_push(l, "A wall-clock timeout was already in place when the machine went down.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## A second incident, recorded — Q1, 2026-10-08")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What happened.** To confirm that `compiler/bootstrap.sh` refuses a host, an agent ran it once in")
    strs_push(l, "its own shell with `NAZM_CONTAINED=1` set for that command. The script refused at once — its new")
    strs_push(l, "check found no numeric `memory.max` — and nothing was built or run. No ceiling was bypassed. Setting")
    strs_push(l, "the variable on a host is nonetheless forbidden by this runbook (*What must never run uncontained*,")
    strs_push(l, "and `AGENTS.md`), whatever the command is expected to do: a check that was wrong, or a different")
    strs_push(l, "script, would have run uncontained on the agent's word.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What changed.** Nothing in these rules — they were right, and are not weakened. The refusal is now")
    strs_push(l, "tested the way it may be: `xtask/tests/host_refusal.rs` starts each guarded entry point as a **child")
    strs_push(l, "process** whose environment the test builds, so the variable exists only in that child, never in an")
    strs_push(l, "agent's or a developer's shell. Recorded in `.agent/handoffs/q1.md` and the Q1-C1 report.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The rule, restated.** Exercising a refusal means a test-constructed child environment or an")
    strs_push(l, "injected one (`contained::host_env_refusal`), never `NAZM_CONTAINED=1` or")
    strs_push(l, "`NAZM_ALLOW_UNCONTAINED=1` typed or exported on a host.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Docker address pool — the most imminent failure, and it is not disk")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Docker's built-in default pool is `172.17.0.0/12` carved into /16s, giving fifteen usable")
    strs_push(l, "networks (`172.17`–`172.31`). Measured:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "$ docker network ls -q | wc -l          → 16 networks")
    strs_push(l, "$ …inspect each, collect subnets        → 172.17 … 172.30, contiguous")
    strs_push(l, "$ docker info --format '{{json .DefaultAddressPools}}'  → null (built-in defaults)")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Fourteen of fifteen are already consumed** by unrelated projects on this machine")
    strs_push(l, "(`erp_default`, `news_default`, `rx_default`, several `fintant-*`, and others). One /16")
    strs_push(l, "remains.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Measured, versus predicted — kept apart on purpose")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Measured:** fourteen of fifteen default /16s are consumed; this machine's LAN address is")
    strs_push(l, "`192.168.0.101` with gateway `192.168.0.1`, i.e. `192.168.0.0/24`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Documented behaviour:** when the `172.17.0.0/12` pool is exhausted Docker's next default")
    strs_push(l, "pool is `192.168.0.0/16`, allocated in /20 chunks — the first of which, `192.168.0.0/20`,")
    strs_push(l, "overlaps this machine's LAN.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Not established:** that Docker *would* actually hand out the overlapping subnet. Its IPAM")
    strs_push(l, "performs some host-route conflict avoidance, and whether that is sufficient here has not")
    strs_push(l, "been tested — deliberately, because testing it means provoking the failure on a machine")
    strs_push(l, "someone is using. So this is a **potential conflict**, not a predicted outage.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The distinction matters for how much weight the mitigation carries: the harness allocates")
    strs_push(l, "from an explicitly configured block precisely so that none of this has to be predicted")
    strs_push(l, "correctly. The overlap is a reason not to rely on the default allocator, not a forecast.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Consequence for the harness:** a single leaked network per attempt exhausts the")
    strs_push(l, "remaining /16 quickly, after which behaviour depends on a fallback path nobody here has")
    strs_push(l, "tested.")
    strs_push(l, "Networks are therefore allocated from an explicitly reserved block with a collision check")
    strs_push(l, "at allocation time, ownership tracked, and cleanup verified.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**On the reserved block.** `10.201.x.0/24` was proposed. Measured: no `10.x` routes exist")
    strs_push(l, "on the host (`netstat -rn -f inet`), and the only non-loopback address is the 192.168 LAN")
    strs_push(l, "one. Four `utun*` interfaces exist (VPN/tunnel), currently carrying no `10.x` routes — but")
    strs_push(l, "a VPN that comes up later could. **So the block is a configurable default, not a")
    strs_push(l, "reservation**, and the allocator checks for collision at the moment it allocates rather")
    strs_push(l, "than trusting this measurement to still hold.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The harness never modifies or removes a network it did not create.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Disk")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "$ df -h ~          → 19Gi free of 460Gi (96% full)")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Docker Desktop's `Docker.raw` grows to its high-water mark and does not shrink when space")
    strs_push(l, "is freed inside the VM. Reclaiming inside the VM (`docker builder prune`, `image prune`)")
    strs_push(l, "frees space for containers but does not necessarily return it to macOS.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Reclaiming space is an operator action, never an agent's.** No run prunes anything —")
    strs_push(l, "not `docker container prune`, `volume prune`, `network prune`, `image prune`,")
    strs_push(l, "`builder prune` or `system prune` — and nothing stops, removes, recreates or renames a")
    strs_push(l, "Docker resource it did not create. The harness cleans up only what it owns, through the")
    strs_push(l, "contained runner, and verifies that it did. If the disk is too full to run, stop and say")
    strs_push(l, "so; the operator decides what to reclaim, and whether `Docker.raw` then needs Docker")
    strs_push(l, "Desktop's own purge to return the space to macOS.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "This paragraph used to say *\"Before a long run: prune\"*, and on 2026-09-23 a run did")
    strs_push(l, "exactly that: `docker container prune` removed the exited containers of unrelated projects")
    strs_push(l, "on this machine. Their volumes were reported intact and were left alone. A prune is")
    strs_push(l, "machine-wide by construction — it cannot tell this project's resources from anyone")
    strs_push(l, "else's — which is why it is never the harness's to run.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Toolchain")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "$ rustc --version  → 1.98.1 (pinned in rust-toolchain.toml)")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The local `stable` was 1.93.1 (seven months behind) when this project started; the pin is")
    strs_push(l, "what makes that irrelevant. `cranelift` 0.135 declares MSRV 1.95.0, so the pin is")
    strs_push(l, "load-bearing for Stage 7 even though nothing depends on Cranelift yet.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Mutation campaigns")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*Mutation harness v2, N12.2, 2026-09-24. The mechanism is `xtask/src/campaign.rs`,")
    strs_push(l, "`plan.rs` and `procs.rs`; this section is how to operate it.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The one command")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```sh")
    strs_push(l, "cargo xtask contained mutate [--only NAME]… [--strategy targeted|full] [--resume] [--verify-killers]")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Always contained. One container is one **session** of a campaign: the tree is copied to a")
    strs_push(l, "disposable directory on the container's capped writable layer (`.git`, `target/` and every")
    strs_push(l, "derived `.nazm/` cache excluded), built once, the workspace suite run once as the")
    strs_push(l, "**baseline**, and then every selected mutant is injected, judged, restored, verified and")
    strs_push(l, "journaled in catalogue order. `/src` stays read-only and the checkout is never mutated.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The warm-worker law — N32-H and N32-H2, 2026-09-29")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A session is one warm worker, never one container per mutant.** One copy, one pristine")
    strs_push(l, "build, one killer listing, one mutation baseline; then each mutant in turn — at most one")
    strs_push(l, "injected at a time, restored to its original bytes and digest-checked before the next is")
    strs_push(l, "touched — against the same target directory. Nothing is `cargo clean`ed between mutants:")
    strs_push(l, "Cargo rebuilds from the bytes on disk, and `xtask/tests/lifecycle.rs` holds that to account —")
    strs_push(l, "A, then B, then A again in one target, and a fresh copy against a persistent target, every")
    strs_push(l, "killer run observed against its own bytes. At the end the whole tree must digest to the tree")
    strs_push(l, "the session began with, or the session stops.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Two baselines, two questions.** The *mutation baseline* is that every declared killer a")
    strs_push(l, "pending mutant may be decided by passes on the pristine tree: each unique killer is run once,")
    strs_push(l, "and its result is held for the session, keyed by the tree's digest, the killer's structured")
    strs_push(l, "selector and the parallelism — never across trees, and never a mutant's or a restoration's")
    strs_push(l, "result. A killer that does not pass refuses the session before anything is injected. The")
    strs_push(l, "*workspace baseline* is that the whole suite is green, and it is the MILESTONE gate's own")
    strs_push(l, "`contained tests` stage that establishes it. A session no longer runs the whole suite to")
    strs_push(l, "decide Tier-1 verdicts, and it says nothing about the workspace's health: an unrelated failing")
    strs_push(l, "test does not stop its verdicts, and the gate's workspace stage is what fails on it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Two passes, one law.** Pass 1 decides every targeted mutant with declared killers at Tier 1")
    strs_push(l, "alone — its build, then its killers, judged exactly as the full law judges them there, which a")
    strs_push(l, "unit test holds to verdict-for-verdict. A mutant every killer passed on is restored and")
    strs_push(l, "deferred. Only then, and only if something was deferred, does the session run the workspace")
    strs_push(l, "suite once as the Tier-3 baseline, and pass 2 decides the deferred mutants by the unchanged")
    strs_push(l, "full law — the one case where a mutant is injected twice. `--strategy full` runs the baseline")
    strs_push(l, "first, as it always did.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**One observation, two facts.** With `--verify-killers`, a killer's mutant observation is the")
    strs_push(l, "very run its Tier-1 verdict was read from — not a second run of the same test on the same")
    strs_push(l, "bytes; a killer the verdict did not reach is run once on the same mutant. Its pristine")
    strs_push(l, "observation is the mutation baseline's, and its restored one is taken after the")
    strs_push(l, "digest-checked restoration, every mutation, which `cargo test` rebuilds from. Verified only as")
    strs_push(l, "passes, fails, passes. It changes no verdict and is not journaled, so a resumed session that")
    strs_push(l, "reuses a verdict says those killers were not verified here and ends incomplete.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**P1 means one active mutation worker**, with one CPU, one job and one thread — not one fresh")
    strs_push(l, "container per mutation. No second worker was needed (`performance.md`); every parallel profile")
    strs_push(l, "for this workload crossed the total-memory gate in N14.1.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The persistent verification cache — N32-H2")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`mutate`, `tests`, `selfhost` and `bootstrap` build in a harness-owned Docker volume mounted at")
    strs_push(l, "`/work/target`, which survives the container; `bench`, `release` and `run` never do. There are")
    strs_push(l, "**two namespaces, never one**: `nazm-verify-mutate-<key>` for mutation sessions, whose copy is")
    strs_push(l, "always `/work/mut`, and `nazm-verify-src-<key>` for the workloads that build the read-only")
    strs_push(l, "checkout at `/src`. They must not share a target: Cargo copies each binary out to")
    strs_push(l, "`target/debug/<name>` and does not copy a unit it finds fresh again, so in one shared target the")
    strs_push(l, "workspace suite ran the `nazm` a mutation copy had built — N32-H2's first cold gate found it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The key is BLAKE3 over the image id and environment, `Cargo.lock`, `rust-toolchain.toml`, the")
    strs_push(l, "flags and the profile: any change is a new volume, never a partial reuse. Source is not in the")
    strs_push(l, "key; Cargo's fingerprints handle it, and a mutation copy is extracted with fresh modification")
    strs_push(l, "times (`tar -m`), so no workspace artefact of an earlier session is ever taken for current. A")
    strs_push(l, "new volume is filled from the image's warmed target on first mount. Volumes carry the labels")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.owner=nazm-verification-harness`, `nazm.compat`, `nazm.created`, `nazm.namespace` and")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.cache-version`; at most two generations per namespace are kept, the oldest removed, and a")
    strs_push(l, "volume over 16 GiB is emptied at the start of the next workload that mounts it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```sh")
    strs_push(l, "cargo xtask contained cache          # list the harness's volumes")
    strs_push(l, "cargo xtask contained cache clear    # remove them; the next run is slower, nothing else changes")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Only volumes with the owner label are listed or removed. **The cache is never authority**: it")
    strs_push(l, "is not in any campaign's identity or journal, cold and warm decide identically, a damaged one is")
    strs_push(l, "rebuilt — where rustc's incremental cache would reuse damaged objects and the pristine build")
    strs_push(l, "fails, a session whose target is the harness's own (`--disposable-target`, which the contained")
    strs_push(l, "launcher passes) cleans it and builds once more — and deleting it loses nothing but time.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Stopping a run")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Stop the supervisor — the `cargo xtask contained …` process. Signalling it, or its process")
    strs_push(l, "group, does **not** reliably stop the container: on 2026-09-29 the Docker client took SIGINT")
    strs_push(l, "and the container ran on. The checkout is read-only, so a stranded container holds a disposable")
    strs_push(l, "copy and nothing of the host's, and it stops itself at its own deadline. Every contained run")
    strs_push(l, "labels its container `nazm.owner=nazm-contained-runner` with its supervisor's pid and host, and")
    strs_push(l, "starts by removing, by exact name, a container carrying that label whose name is")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-<workload>-<pid>` with the same pid, whose host is this one, and whose pid `ps` reports as no")
    strs_push(l, "process — and nothing else. A name alone is never ownership: Compose's `nazm-postgres-1` is not")
    strs_push(l, "the runner's (Q1-A2-01). A container from before the label existed is never removed")
    strs_push(l, "automatically; to free one at once, `docker rm -f` that exact name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Verification gates — v2")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Gate | What | Target on the M1 Pro | When |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **DEV** | focused tests, host probes of new or changed mutations, `fmt`, `clippy`, `cargo xtask check` | < 10 min | while iterating |")
    strs_push(l, "| **MILESTONE** | every affected killer verified and one targeted campaign, in one warm session; the contained workspace suite (P4T4); the lifecycle suite `gate-plan` calls for; selfhost; bootstrap; the milestone's benchmark; the gates | ≤ 30 min | to close a milestone |")
    strs_push(l, "| **RELEASE** | the full lifecycle suite, broader and full campaigns, fuzzing, platforms, long benchmarks, reproducibility | as long as it takes | a release, not every milestone |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`cargo xtask gate-plan PATH…` says which lifecycle evidence the changed paths call for: a path")
    strs_push(l, "under `xtask/`, `docker/`, or the manifests and toolchain pin is the harness and calls for the")
    strs_push(l, "whole lifecycle suite; a path under `crates/`, `compiler/`, `library/`, `docs/`, `schema/` or")
    strs_push(l, "`examples/` calls for its three invariant tests; the MCP server brings its shared mutations; an")
    strs_push(l, "unknown path, or no path at all, calls for everything. It narrows nothing else, and reads no")
    strs_push(l, "Git history.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "MILESTONE is not DEV with a new name: its speed comes from not repeating work, never from")
    strs_push(l, "dropping a killer, the campaign, the suite, selfhost or bootstrap. N32's gate measured 40.1 min")
    strs_push(l, "under v1 and N32-H2's 27.6 min under v2, warm (`performance.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Verification harness V3 — N32-H3, 2026-09-29")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Bucketed execution.** A session injects its mutants grouped by the package that owns the")
    strs_push(l, "mutated file — Cargo's metadata says which, not a table kept here — then by the first killer's")
    strs_push(l, "target, then catalogue order: a deterministic sort on structured keys. Only execution order")
    strs_push(l, "changes: every mutant still starts from the digest-checked pristine tree, and selection,")
    strs_push(l, "identity, journal and verdicts are the catalogue's. Each mutant's workspace build now reports,")
    strs_push(l, "from Cargo's JSON messages, which units it compiled. That build — `cargo build --workspace")
    strs_push(l, "--tests` — stays: it is what tells UNUSABLE from CAUGHT, and a `nazm-docs` mutant compiling 40")
    strs_push(l, "dependent units is the price of that, recorded rather than removed.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The scheduled workspace suite**, `xtask workspace-tests`, runs through a calibration profile")
    strs_push(l, "(`contained --profile p4w2t4 tests`, and the other `p4w*` names): Cargo builds every test binary")
    strs_push(l, "once (`cargo test --workspace --no-run`) and names each in its JSON; each runs exactly once, in")
    strs_push(l, "its package's directory with its package's variables, over a bounded number of workers, longest")
    strs_push(l, "first; a failure cancels nothing; the report is in canonical order, not completion order; the")
    strs_push(l, "doc-tests follow. A timing history in the checkout cache (`.nazm-suite-timings.json`, one")
    strs_push(l, "schedule, bounded by the suite, removed by `contained cache clear`) decides the order and nothing")
    strs_push(l, "else — absent or damaged, the order is canonical. **P4W2T4 is this machine's calibrated profile")
    strs_push(l, "(M1 Pro)**; no workload defaults to it, and `contained tests` without a profile is still")
    strs_push(l, "`cargo test --workspace` at P4T4.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Normal and harness-changing gates.** `gate-plan` now names every stage and responsibility a")
    strs_push(l, "change calls for — the core stages, the lifecycle tests, the MCP shared mutations and the")
    strs_push(l, "benchmark families (`compiler`, `docs`, `mcp`, `harness`; an unknown path brings all four) — and")
    strs_push(l, "a test holds that a product or docs change's plan is covered by the plan for the same change")
    strs_push(l, "plus a harness change. A measured harness-changing gate therefore bounds the normal gate over")
    strs_push(l, "the same paths.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The bench cache.** `contained --cache bench run …` keeps a benchmark's release builds in a")
    strs_push(l, "third harness-owned namespace, `nazm-verify-bench-<key>`, apart from `mutate` and `src`. A")
    strs_push(l, "benchmark measures the binary it runs, the same bytes wherever they were compiled.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Evidence tiers — escalate only while a mutant is still alive")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The default strategy, `targeted`, runs for each mutant, stopping at the first failure:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "1. **Direct**: each verified killer the entry names, one exact test each;")
    strs_push(l, "2. **Focused**: each whole target of the entry's profile (`[[profile]]` in the catalogue);")
    strs_push(l, "3. **Full**: the workspace suite, exactly the legacy invocation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A failure at any tier is **CAUGHT at that tier**, and it is the same evidence as a failure")
    strs_push(l, "in the workspace suite: the killer is a member of that suite, it passed in the baseline,")
    strs_push(l, "and it failed with the mutant installed. **Only tier 3 can report SURVIVED.** A killer or")
    strs_push(l, "a profile that passes escalates; it never concludes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`--strategy full` is the legacy shape — build, then the workspace suite, for every mutant —")
    strs_push(l, "and is kept as the oracle the targeted strategy is compared with.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Verdicts, and what is never converted into one")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| word | meaning |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `caught` | a tier's tests failed with the mutant installed |")
    strs_push(l, "| `SURVIVED` | every step passed, the workspace suite last |")
    strs_push(l, "| `UNUSABLE` | the mutated tree does not build, tests included |")
    strs_push(l, "| `NOT INJECTED` | the pattern matched zero or several times, or changed nothing |")
    strs_push(l, "| `MUTANT CRASH` | a test binary died with the mutant installed |")
    strs_push(l, "| `TIMEOUT` | a step passed its deadline — **no verdict** |")
    strs_push(l, "| `RUNNER ERROR` | a step did not run to completion — **no verdict** |")
    strs_push(l, "| `NOT RESTORED` | the source could not be put back — the run stops |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A timeout is never caught and never survived. A no-verdict mutant is not escalated past:")
    strs_push(l, "a later tier passing would not mean the earlier one said nothing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Serial, and alone")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "One mutant at a time, and nothing else heavy on the machine: no bootstrap, no benchmark, no")
    strs_push(l, "second campaign, no full verification. The speed of v2 comes from running fewer tests, which")
    strs_push(l, "holds on a constrained machine; it must never come from running mutants concurrently, which")
    strs_push(l, "makes deadline-bearing verdicts a function of scheduling.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A campaign runs under P1 — one CPU, one Cargo job, one test thread — by default. N14.1 tried")
    strs_push(l, "P4T4 and a two-job variant: verdicts and tiers matched P1, but both crossed the frozen")
    strs_push(l, "total-memory gate (`performance.md`), so the default did not move. `--profile` still sizes")
    strs_push(l, "each step if given, and the profile is part of the campaign identity: a journal recorded")
    strs_push(l, "under one profile is never read by a resume under another.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### A probe runs in a fresh directory, and every entry names its killer")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A warm check cache answers for the unmutated checker.** The cache is keyed by the checker's")
    strs_push(l, "identity — semantic epoch, package version, schemas, the built-in table — and a mutant changes the")
    strs_push(l, "checker without changing any of these. A probe of a mutant in a directory that already holds a")
    strs_push(l, "`.nazm` cache reads the unmutated answer from it. N100 called `n79-a-held-io-cap-is-read-alone`")
    strs_push(l, "\"possibly equivalent\" for that reason; N101 found the program it had probed is refused under the")
    strs_push(l, "mutant in a fresh directory. Probes by hand and killers both run in fresh directories.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**No silent tier (N101).** Every catalogue entry declares `killers`, or says why it has none in")
    strs_push(l, "`no_killer`: a known survivor, an equivalent mutant, or one that cannot be injected, with the")
    strs_push(l, "evidence. `cargo xtask check` refuses an entry with neither. A new entry's killer is the test whose")
    strs_push(l, "failure under the mutant was observed; for a historical entry without one, N101's method was to")
    strs_push(l, "apply the mutant in a dedicated worktree with its own target directory, run the owning crate's")
    strs_push(l, "tests and then `nazm-cli`'s, and take the first failing test that is not a whole-chain test (the")
    strs_push(l, "bootstrap fixpoint, the parity record). Selfhost and bootstrap mutants refuse to run uncontained,")
    strs_push(l, "so theirs were found under the contained runner against a pristine export.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Deadlines and process trees")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Every build and test the campaign starts runs through one subprocess runner")
    strs_push(l, "(`procs.rs`), in **a process group of its own** with a **watchdog** in a separate group:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "* at a deadline, the tree is walked by parent id and stopped, then killed — so a compiled")
    strs_push(l, "  program a test put in *another* group dies too;")
    strs_push(l, "* after an ordinary exit, anything left in the group is swept, so a grandchild holding a")
    strs_push(l, "  pipe cannot hang the reader;")
    strs_push(l, "* if the harness itself dies (SIGINT, SIGKILL, a panic), the watchdog sees its pipe close")
    strs_push(l, "  and kills the group.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Deadlines bound pathology, not speed: build 1800 s, a killer 1200 s, a profile target")
    strs_push(l, "1500 s, the workspace suite 2400 s. Lowering them to make a campaign faster converts slow")
    strs_push(l, "catches into no-verdicts.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**`kill -KILL -<pgid>` does not work in the container.** procps `kill` reads `-123` after a")
    strs_push(l, "signal as an option and signals nothing; `kill -KILL -- -<pgid>` works there and on macOS.")
    strs_push(l, "N12.2 found N12.1's test deadlines using the first spelling and corrected them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A test that runs a compiled program needs its own deadline.** `nazm build` emits no")
    strs_push(l, "iteration budget, so a backend mutant that makes a loop run away makes a bare `.output()`")
    strs_push(l, "wait for ever. `value_blocks.rs`, `schemas.rs`, `workflow.rs` (N12.1) and `memory.rs`")
    strs_push(l, "(N12.2) bound theirs; a new suite that runs programs must too, or its tier times out and")
    strs_push(l, "the mutant gets no verdict.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Sessions, the journal and `--resume`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A session has a 3000 s container deadline and a 2400 s budget: past the budget it starts")
    strs_push(l, "no new mutant, ends **incomplete** (exit 3), and says which mutants were not reached.")
    strs_push(l, "Nothing is established about those. A mutant still in flight at the deadline is killed")
    strs_push(l, "with the container, is never journaled, and runs again; that is also reported as")
    strs_push(l, "incomplete, never as a memory limit. Continue with the same selection:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```sh")
    strs_push(l, "cargo xtask contained mutate [same --only …] --resume")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Each finalized mutant — verdict known, source restored **and read back** — is printed as a")
    strs_push(l, "journal line and collected on the host at `target/mutation-campaigns/<key>/journal.jsonl`.")
    strs_push(l, "`<key>` is a digest of the campaign's **identity**: the tree's contents, the catalogue, the")
    strs_push(l, "harness, the toolchain, the strategy, the selection, the deadlines and the cache-isolation")
    strs_push(l, "rule. A resumed session reuses only verdicts journaled under the identical key; a changed")
    strs_push(l, "file anywhere, a changed catalogue or a different selection is a different campaign and")
    strs_push(l, "reuses nothing. A timeout or runner error is never reused — it is attempted again.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The journal is evidence, not a cache: an old verdict is never inferred from an old binary or")
    strs_push(l, "log. Journal lines reach the host when the container ends; a supervisor killed with the")
    strs_push(l, "container running loses that session's lines, and those mutants are simply run again.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Authoring a mutation (the N13 workflow)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "1. Write the semantic regression test that observes the rule.")
    strs_push(l, "2. Add the `[[mutation]]` entry; `cargo xtask check-mutations` validates it statically.")
    strs_push(l, "3. Verify the killer — pristine passes, mutant fails, restored passes:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "   ```sh")
    strs_push(l, "   cargo xtask contained mutate --verify-killer NAME --killer nazm-cli:test=memory:the_test")
    strs_push(l, "   ```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "   (`PACKAGE:lib:PATH`, `PACKAGE:test=T:PATH` or `PACKAGE:bin=B:PATH`.) It prints the")
    strs_push(l, "   `killers = [...]` line to add.")
    strs_push(l, "4. Add it, then `cargo xtask contained mutate --only NAME`, which now stops at tier 1.")
    strs_push(l, "5. Commit.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`cargo xtask mutate --plan [--only NAME]` prints each mutant's tiers and runs nothing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A killer is authoritative only after step 3 observed it. Never write one from a test's")
    strs_push(l, "name; never name the workspace suite or the bootstrap as a killer — an entry with no narrow")
    strs_push(l, "killer simply has none, and says why in `no_killer` if it names a profile.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Artefacts and disk")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Everything a campaign writes on the host is under `target/mutation-campaigns/<key>/`. The")
    strs_push(l, "Cargo build of a session lives in the container and goes with it (about 2.6 GB of the 8 GB")
    strs_push(l, "writable layer). Nothing here cleans up automatically, and nothing ever runs `cargo clean`,")
    strs_push(l, "`rm -rf target` or a Docker prune; delete a campaign's directory by hand when it is no")
    strs_push(l, "longer evidence.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Recovering an interrupted mutation run")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*This section is about a tree mutated in place, which only an uncontained run does. A")
    strs_push(l, "contained campaign (above) mutates a disposable copy and leaves nothing here to recover.*")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`cargo xtask mutate` mutates the working tree in place and restores each file after")
    strs_push(l, "testing it. If the run is killed in between, the tree is left holding a mutation and a")
    strs_push(l, "write-ahead record at `target/.nazm-mutation-backup` describing how to undo it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Recovery is not automatic, and that is deliberate.** Killing a run releases its lock at")
    strs_push(l, "once — the runner's `cargo` and `rustc` descendants never held it, because Rust opens")
    strs_push(l, "files `O_CLOEXEC` — so those descendants keep running and keep writing to the tree. The")
    strs_push(l, "runner has no way to establish that they have stopped:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "* a **pid** may have been reused, and the one in the record belongs to a process that is")
    strs_push(l, "  already gone;")
    strs_push(l, "* a **content digest** describes the file at the instant it was read, not what will be")
    strs_push(l, "  written to it next;")
    strs_push(l, "* a **delay** proves nothing at any length.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Restoring the source while one of them is still running, and then injecting the next")
    strs_push(l, "mutation on top, would produce verdicts about a file two processes are editing. So a")
    strs_push(l, "stranded record makes the next run **refuse to start**, and repair is an operator action.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### The procedure")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "1. **Establish that nothing is still writing to the tree.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "   These commands help you look. **Neither is proof**, and the difference matters:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "   ```sh")
    strs_push(l, "   pgrep -g <pgid>        # the interrupted run's process group, if you know it")
    strs_push(l, "   pgrep -fl \"$(pwd)\"     # build and test processes mentioning this path")
    strs_push(l, "   ```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "   A process-group search misses anything that called `setsid` or `setpgid`. A")
    strs_push(l, "   path-or-name search misses a process whose command line does not mention the")
    strs_push(l, "   checkout, one that holds an open descriptor to a file whose path has since changed,")
    strs_push(l, "   and anything that has not started yet. Both are **investigative aids**; what")
    strs_push(l, "   establishes quiescence is your knowledge of what you were running, and nothing here")
    strs_push(l, "   can substitute for it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "2. **Repair.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "   > Since the catalogue moved inside `cargo xtask contained mutate`, it runs against a")
    strs_push(l, "   > disposable copy on the container's writable layer, never against the checkout. An")
    strs_push(l, "   > interrupted contained run therefore leaves **nothing here to recover** — the copy")
    strs_push(l, "   > dies with the container, and `git status` on this tree stays clean. What follows")
    strs_push(l, "   > applies to a tree that was mutated directly, which is the uncontained path the")
    strs_push(l, "   > contract now forbids; it is kept because a tree mutated before that rule still needs")
    strs_push(l, "   > repairing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "   ```sh")
    strs_push(l, "   cargo xtask mutate-recover --confirm-no-writers")
    strs_push(l, "   ```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "   The flag is **your attestation that the workspace is quiet** — not a check the tool")
    strs_push(l, "   performs, and not a claim the searches above succeeded. The tool has no way to")
    strs_push(l, "   perform such a check, which is precisely why recovery is not automatic and why no")
    strs_push(l, "   automatic mechanism is being added. Recovery itself is still conservative: it restores the original bytes only")
    strs_push(l, "   if the file still matches what the record describes, reports `already-restored` if the")
    strs_push(l, "   run was killed after restoring but before clearing its record, and refuses outright if")
    strs_push(l, "   the contents match neither. A file you edited by hand since the crash is never")
    strs_push(l, "   overwritten.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "3. **Re-run.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "   ```sh")
    strs_push(l, "   cargo xtask contained mutate")
    strs_push(l, "   ```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### If recovery refuses")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "It will say the file matches neither the mutation it applied nor the original it saved.")
    strs_push(l, "That means something changed the file after the interruption. The original is still in")
    strs_push(l, "`target/.nazm-mutation-backup`, after its fourth line. Compare it with the working copy,")
    strs_push(l, "resolve by hand, then delete the record.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Interoperating with an older runner")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The lock protocol changed: it was a file whose *existence* was the lock, and it is now an")
    strs_push(l, "advisory lock (`flock`) on `target/.nazm-mutation-lock.v2`, which is never unlinked. **The")
    strs_push(l, "two protocols do not coordinate reliably, and the supported boundary is not to run both")
    strs_push(l, "against one tree.** The new runner takes the old marker while it runs so an old runner")
    strs_push(l, "usually stands down, and refuses to start if the old marker names a live process — but a")
    strs_push(l, "first-protocol runner that has already passed its own check and not yet published is not")
    strs_push(l, "covered by anything. Use one version.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## The agent task benchmark")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-agent-bench` (N35, `architecture.md` §7.37) puts the eight N33 tasks to a real model with")
    strs_push(l, "the naive context and with the N33 context, and records usage, cost and a fact-by-fact score. It")
    strs_push(l, "is the one tool here that reaches a network, and it is never part of a gate: every test and")
    strs_push(l, "mutation killer drives it with a fake provider or recorded responses, offline.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Providers.** `openai` and `anthropic` call the APIs directly and **bring their own key**;")
    strs_push(l, "`claude-code` runs the Claude Code client (`claude --print`) on the credentials it is already")
    strs_push(l, "signed in with, and needs no key. A key comes from `OPENAI_API_KEY` or `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, or")
    strs_push(l, "from a file only its owner can read:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```sh")
    strs_push(l, "mkdir -p ~/.config/nazm-agent-bench && chmod 700 ~/.config/nazm-agent-bench")
    strs_push(l, "read -s k && printf %s \"$k\" > ~/.config/nazm-agent-bench/openai.key && unset k")
    strs_push(l, "chmod 600 ~/.config/nazm-agent-bench/openai.key")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Type it in your own terminal. The key is passed to `curl` on its standard input, never on a")
    strs_push(l, "command line; it is never written to a record, and it is removed from any error text kept.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Prices.** `tools/agent-bench/pricing.toml`, dated, with the page each rate came from. A run")
    strs_push(l, "refuses a provider and model with no entry. When a price changes, add an entry; a report prices")
    strs_push(l, "old usage again under the newest one without re-running anything.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The steps**, with `B=target/release/nazm-agent-bench` (`cargo build --release -p nazm-agent-bench`):")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```sh")
    strs_push(l, "$B suite                                               # the tasks, contexts and digests")
    strs_push(l, "$B dry-run --provider P --model M --cap-usd 2          # requests, sizes, worst case — no network")
    strs_push(l, "$B run     --provider P --model M --cap-usd 2 --pilot  # 4 requests; never evidence")
    strs_push(l, "$B run     --provider P --model M --cap-usd 2 --suite-digest D    # D from the dry run: frozen")
    strs_push(l, "$B report [--markdown]                                 # authoritative records only")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **The cap is required** and covers everything the evidence directory's ledger has charged,")
    strs_push(l, "  pilots included. Every attempt's worst case is checked against it before it is sent; a run that")
    strs_push(l, "  would pass it stops there, with what it did in the journal. A run does not start when its")
    strs_push(l, "  dearest single request could not fit.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Freezing.** An authoritative run needs `--suite-digest`, and refuses a checkout whose suite")
    strs_push(l, "  differs. The suite's N33 contexts carry the repository's state, so a benchmark is of one")
    strs_push(l, "  checkout; commit first, run, then write anything up.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Resume.** Run the same command again: every request already recorded is skipped. A runner")
    strs_push(l, "  error — no reply after two retries — is repeated only with `--retry-runner-errors`. A different")
    strs_push(l, "  model, parameter, prompt, trial count or suite is a different benchmark and starts from the")
    strs_push(l, "  beginning.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Where results live.** `target/n35/agent-bench/` (ignored): `spend.jsonl`, the ledger, and per")
    strs_push(l, "  benchmark `benchmark.json`, `journal.jsonl` (`nazm.agent-benchmark/1` records) and `raw/`, the")
    strs_push(l, "  providers' whole responses. It refuses to grow past 256 MiB. Commit the report, not the raw")
    strs_push(l, "  replies.")
    str_join(l, str_from_byte(10)) + str_from_byte(10)
}

fn dd_doc8() -> Str {
    let l = strs_new()
    strs_push(l, "# The machine interface")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Everything `nazm` says to a program, rather than to a person, is JSON under a **named,")
    strs_push(l, "versioned schema**. The schemas live in [`schema/`](../../schema) as JSON Schema documents,")
    strs_push(l, "and `crates/nazm-cli/tests/schemas.rs` validates the real output of the real commands")
    strs_push(l, "against them — so these documents are tested rather than described.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Schema | Command | Where | Shape |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.diagnostic/1` | `nazm check --json`, `nazm run --json`, `nazm build --json` | stderr | one object per line |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.fix/1` | `nazm fix --json` | stdout | one object per line |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.capabilities/1` | `nazm capabilities --json` | stdout | one object |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.test/1` | `nazm test --json` | stdout | one object per case |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.check-report/1` | `nazm check --cache-report` | stdout | one object |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.build-report/1` | `nazm build --build-report` | stdout | one object, before the executable's path |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.context/3` | `nazm context --json`, and the `nazm-mcp` tool `nazm.semantic_context` | stdout; the tool result's structured content | one object |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.snapshot/3` | `nazm snapshot --json`, and the `nazm-mcp` tool `nazm.semantic_snapshot` | stdout; the tool result's structured content | one object |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.delta/3` | `nazm delta --json`, and the `nazm-mcp` tool `nazm.semantic_delta` | stdout; the tool result's structured content | one object |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.patch/1` | `nazm patch rename --json`, `nazm patch fix --json`, and the `nazm-mcp` tool `nazm.semantic_patch` | stdout; the tool result's structured content | one object |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.diagnostic-index/1` | `nazm diagnostics --json`, and the `nazm-mcp` tool `nazm.diagnostics` | stdout; the tool result's structured content | one object |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.diagnostic-detail/1` | `nazm diagnostics --detail ID --state DIGEST --json`, and the `nazm-mcp` tool `nazm.diagnostic_detail` | stdout; the tool result's structured content | one object |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.command-summary/1` | `nazm check --summary-json`, `nazm build --summary-json`, and the `nazm-mcp` tool `nazm.command_summary` (check only) | stdout; the tool result's structured content | one object |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.test-summary/1` | `nazm test --summary-json` | stdout | one object |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.docs-index/1` | `nazm docs --index --json`, and the `nazm-mcp` tool `nazm.docs_index` | stdout; the tool result's structured content | one object |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.docs-section/1` | `nazm docs --section ID --json`, and the `nazm-mcp` tool `nazm.docs_section` | stdout; the tool result's structured content | one object |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.repository-map/1` | `nazm repo --map --json`, and the `nazm-mcp` tool `nazm.repository_map` | stdout; the tool result's structured content | one object |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.task-context/1` | `nazm repo --task --seed ID --json`, and the `nazm-mcp` tool `nazm.task_context` | stdout; the tool result's structured content | one object |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.token-cost/1` | `nazm-tokens measure` (the text on standard input) and `nazm-tokens list`, a separate tool beside the compiler | stdout | one object |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.resolved/1` | `nazm resolve FILE`, and stored in each `nazm.check/4` entry (N77) | stdout | one object per module, per line |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.references/1` | `nazm references DEF FILE` (N77) | stdout | one object |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.agent-benchmark/1` | `nazm-agent-bench suite`, its journal records (`journal.jsonl` in the local evidence directory) and `nazm-agent-bench report`; evaluation tooling beside the compiler | stdout, and one record per journal line | one object, or one record per line |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Every object carries its own `schema` field. Not a header: the output is a stream of")
    strs_push(l, "lines and a consumer may read, log or replay any single one of them, and a version that")
    strs_push(l, "only the first reader sees is not a version.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## What compatibility means")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The number after the `/` is a **major** version and the only one there is. It changes")
    strs_push(l, "when a consumer written against the previous version would now be **wrong** — not merely")
    strs_push(l, "incomplete.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Compatible, and may happen in any release.** A consumer must tolerate all of these,")
    strs_push(l, "which in practice means *ignore what you do not recognise*:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- A new field on an existing object.")
    strs_push(l, "- A new diagnostic code. Codes are stable and never reused, but new ones appear.")
    strs_push(l, "- A new value in an existing enum — a new `applicability`, a new `severity`.")
    strs_push(l, "- A new element in an array: another fix on a diagnostic, another built-in in the")
    strs_push(l, "  inventory, another secondary label.")
    strs_push(l, "- A change to any `message`, `help`, `description` or `precondition`. **These are prose.**")
    strs_push(l, "  Match on `code`, never on text.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Breaking, and requires a new major version.** None of these will happen inside a")
    strs_push(l, "version:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- Removing or renaming a field.")
    strs_push(l, "- Changing a field's type, or the meaning of its value.")
    strs_push(l, "- Changing what an existing diagnostic code means, or reusing a retired one.")
    strs_push(l, "- Changing `span` offsets from bytes to anything else.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N37, capabilities.** No schema moved. Three diagnostic codes appeared —")
    strs_push(l, "`N0369` (missing authority), `N0370` (a capability constructed) and `N0371` (a `main`")
    strs_push(l, "parameter that is not a capability) — which is a new code, compatible. `IoCap` and")
    strs_push(l, "`SpawnCap` are two more built-in types, so `nazm.capabilities/1`'s type list has two more")
    strs_push(l, "elements, compatible. A function's authority is its parameter list, which")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.context/2`, `nazm.snapshot/2` and `nazm.delta/2` already carry, so a capability-only")
    strs_push(l, "change is a `shape` change there and needed no new field; whether a function is ambient is")
    strs_push(l, "whether `effects.declared` is `null`, which already meant *declares none*. The persisted")
    strs_push(l, "module interface, which is not one of these schemas, stays `nazm.interface/6` for the same")
    strs_push(l, "reason: a capability parameter is written as every built-in type already is.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N38, provenance.** Three schemas moved, each because an object valid under the old")
    strs_push(l, "major could not carry what the new one must say: `nazm.context/3` adds a function's")
    strs_push(l, "`provenance` — the origins its result carries, the parameters it passes on and those reaching")
    strs_push(l, "`write_file`'s path, and what each parameter is handed; `nazm.snapshot/3` adds a `provenance`")
    strs_push(l, "digest per function; `nazm.delta/3` reports it. A `/2` reader would not know to compare the new")
    strs_push(l, "section, and a function's provenance can change with no byte of it changing — when a callee's")
    strs_push(l, "body does — so reporting it under `/2` would call such a function unchanged. One code appeared,")
    strs_push(l, "`N0372`: in a function with a declared effect set, `write_file`'s path derives from a file's")
    strs_push(l, "contents or from a sequence or channel the checker does not follow. Its primary span is the")
    strs_push(l, "`write_file`, or the call handing such a value to a function whose parameter reaches one; its")
    strs_push(l, "secondary labels are one chain to the sink and to where the origin entered; it carries no fix.")
    strs_push(l, "The provenance facts themselves are machine-readable only in the packet; the persisted module")
    strs_push(l, "interface stays `nazm.interface/6`, and the cache's own entry format moved to `nazm.check/2`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N39, Core IR.** No schema moved. One code appeared, `N0900`: the compiler")
    strs_push(l, "contradicted itself — a program that checked with no diagnostic could not be lowered to Core IR,")
    strs_push(l, "or its Core IR broke an invariant (`architecture.md` §7.41). It describes the compiler, not the")
    strs_push(l, "program, carries no fix, and nothing is run or built after it. The printed Core IR,")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.core-ir/3`, is a debugging form with its own version and is not one of these schemas.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N40, MIR.** No schema moved and no code appeared. `N0900` gained one more way to be")
    strs_push(l, "raised: a program that checked whose MIR the validator rejects (`architecture.md` §7.42) — `nazm")
    strs_push(l, "build` then emits nothing. The native subset's own refusals (`N0101` for recursion, a `main` it")
    strs_push(l, "cannot call, a sequence handed to a task) are raised from MIR now and read exactly as before:")
    strs_push(l, "across all 205 sources in the tree, every build diagnostic is byte-identical. The printed MIR,")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.mir/1`, is a debugging form with its own version and is not one of these schemas.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N41, the backend boundary.** No schema moved and no code appeared. A program the")
    strs_push(l, "Cranelift backend cannot compile is refused under `N0101`, naming the construct and the")
    strs_push(l, "backend, and never falls back to LLVM; a target triple that is not the host is refused by name")
    strs_push(l, "before anything is compiled. `nazm.build-report/1` is unchanged: a Cranelift object reused by")
    strs_push(l, "its key counts as reused, exactly as a clang one does.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N60, restriction profiles v2.** No code appeared: a rule's refusal is `N0510`, and an")
    strs_push(l, "`unknown` verdict is `N0510` too, with a label saying the rule's facts could not be established.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.profile-report/1` gains two rule identities (`no-recursion`, `no-select`) and one verdict")
    strs_push(l, "value (`unknown`), new values of existing fields.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N58, debugger and profiler v2.** No code appeared. One schema did: `nazm.profile/1`")
    strs_push(l, "(`nazm profile FILE`): `schema`, `backend`, `exit`, `wall_ms`, `stdout_bytes`, `memory` (per class:")
    strs_push(l, "`allocated`, `reclaimed`, `live`) and `scheduler` (`spawned`, `joined`, `selects`, `timeouts`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N56, packages v2.** Three codes appeared, compatible: `N0512` (a registry index that")
    strs_push(l, "is not `nazm.registry-index/1`, names another package, records a version twice or a malformed")
    strs_push(l, "digest; or a publish of a version already there), `N0513` (no published version satisfies every")
    strs_push(l, "requirement on a package, each named with who made it) and `N0514` (a registry package holding a")
    strs_push(l, "link or anything but files and directories). A copy changed after publishing is the existing")
    strs_push(l, "`N0507`; a registry package conflicting with a path package of its name is `N0503`; a cycle through")
    strs_push(l, "the registry is `N0504` — each with its meaning unchanged. Schemas: `nazm.registry-index/1` is new;")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.package/1` gains an optional `[registry]` table and path-less dependencies, which an older")
    strs_push(l, "reader refuses as unknown rather than misreads; `nazm.lock/1` gains a source form,")
    strs_push(l, "`registry+NAME@VERSION`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N74, ecosystem tooling.** No code appeared: `nazm check DIR` on a package with no `main`")
    strs_push(l, "now checks its modules, so `N0509` is raised by `run` and `build` alone; `nazm bindgen` reports the")
    strs_push(l, "checker's own code for a declaration it refuses. `nazm.api-doc/1` (`nazm doc`), `nazm.bindgen/1`")
    strs_push(l, "(`nazm bindgen -o`) and `nazm.publish-plan/1` (`nazm publish --dry-run`) are new, each with a schema")
    strs_push(l, "in `schema/` checked against real output; `nazm.capabilities/1` gains `authority`, `targets` and")
    strs_push(l, "`commands` — new fields, compatible.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N73, trust evidence.** No code appeared. `nazm.provenance/1` (`nazm build --provenance`)")
    strs_push(l, "is new, with a schema checked against real output; `cargo xtask evidence` writes `nazm.evidence/1`")
    strs_push(l, "and `nazm.sbom/1`, tooling of the repository rather than of the compiler, tested by")
    strs_push(l, "`xtask/tests/evidence.rs`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N72, account-oriented contracts.** No code appeared: `signed-writes` refuses with the")
    strs_push(l, "existing `N0510`. `nazm.sbpf-accounts/1` is new; `nazm.profile-report/1` gains a profile and a rule.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N71, contracts on WebAssembly.** No code appeared: a failure is the existing code,")
    strs_push(l, "through the host's `report`. `nazm.wasm-contract/1` and `nazm.wasm-contract-run/1` are new.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N70, the EVM backend.** Three codes appeared, compatible: `N0397` (a sender address")
    strs_push(l, "that is not an `Int`), `N0398` (calldata that is not an entrypoint's selector and `int64`")
    strs_push(l, "arguments), `N0399` (a construct the backend does not emit, or a storage upgrade it refuses). On the")
    strs_push(l, "EVM a failure reverts with its existing code's five bytes. `nazm.evm/1`, `nazm.evm-abi/1`,")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.evm-storage/1`, `nazm.evm-upgrade/1` and `nazm.evm-run/1` are new.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N69, contracts.** Two codes appeared, compatible: `N0395` (a module `nazm contract`")
    strs_push(l, "was given that is not a contract, naming what it lacks) and `N0396` (a transaction changed the")
    strs_push(l, "conserved quantity and was rejected). The `web3` profile refuses with the existing `N0510`.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.contract/1` and `nazm.contract-run/1` are new; `nazm.profile-report/1` gains a profile name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N68, layout specialisation.** No code appeared: a field-by-field `Vec`'s failures are")
    strs_push(l, "the existing `N0405` and `N0406`, unchanged. `nazm.cost/1` gains `layouts` — each `Vec` type and")
    strs_push(l, "whether `--layout soa` lays it out field by field, or why not — a new field, compatible.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N67, accelerator kernels.** One code appeared, compatible: `N0394` (a function `nazm")
    strs_push(l, "accel` will not run as a kernel, naming why). A kernel's failures are the existing `N0400` and")
    strs_push(l, "`N0401`, with \"at element *i*\" added to the message. `nazm.accel/1` and `nazm.kernel/1` are new.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N66, vectorisation.** No code appeared: `ints_sum_from`'s overflow is the existing")
    strs_push(l, "`N0400`, at the addition a replaced loop failed at. `nazm.cost/1` gains `loops` — each loop, whether")
    strs_push(l, "it was vectorised and by which idiom, or why not — a new field, compatible.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N65, the interactive tier.** One code appeared, compatible: `N0393` (a function")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm comptime` will not evaluate: it has parameters, or it is not pure). A runaway comptime")
    strs_push(l, "evaluation is the interpreter's existing `N0402`; a REPL line's errors are the checker's own codes.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.reload-check/1` is new.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N64, WebAssembly.** No code appeared: device registers in a module are the existing")
    strs_push(l, "`N0392`, a stack exhausted is `N0408`, an overflow `N0400`, each reported through the host's")
    strs_push(l, "`report`. What a module cannot have is the freestanding refusal (§7.64), which now names each part's")
    strs_push(l, "symbols. `nazm inspect` lists one more target; `nazm.bounds/1` is written for a module too, rooted at")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm_main`. No schema moved.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N63, real-time bounds.** No code appeared: `no-blocking` and `bounded-loops` refuse with")
    strs_push(l, "the existing `N0510`, an unbounded loop as `unknown` with its reason, the meaning unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.profile-report/1` gains a profile name (`realtime`), two rule identities and an optional")
    strs_push(l, "`bounds` object — new values and a new field, compatible. `nazm.bounds/1` is new, written by a board")
    strs_push(l, "build beside `link.ld`; `nazm-stack:` is a UART line under `--stack-watermark`, not a schema.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N62, a freestanding target.** One code appeared, compatible: `N0392` (`mmio_read32` or")
    strs_push(l, "`mmio_write32` reached by `nazm run` or a hosted build, which have no device registers). A register")
    strs_push(l, "access without an `MmioCap` held is the existing `N0369`; a board program's overflow and stack")
    strs_push(l, "exhaustion are the existing `N0400` and `N0408`, written to the UART. What a board cannot have is a")
    strs_push(l, "build refusal by name, not a code: it is a fact of the target, as a host without a linker is")
    strs_push(l, "(§7.59) — exit 1 since Q1-C1 (the program asks for what the target lacks), 4 before. No schema moved; `nazm inspect` lists one more target, a new value of an")
    strs_push(l, "existing field.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N55, FFI v2.** One code appeared, compatible: `N0391` (an `extern \"C\"` export that is")
    strs_push(l, "not `pub`, does not declare `! {}`, is generic, or takes or returns a type other than `Int` and")
    strs_push(l, "`Bool`). A `Str` holding a NUL byte passed to C is the existing `N0405` at run time; an export's")
    strs_push(l, "symbol defined twice or also imported is the existing `N0383`; its ABI and symbol rules are")
    strs_push(l, "`N0380` and `N0382`, unchanged. No schema moved; `nazm build --lib` writes a C header, which is C,")
    strs_push(l, "not a Nazm schema.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N54, select, deadlines and the scheduler's counters.** No code appeared: a clock read")
    strs_push(l, "without a `TimeCap` held is the existing `N0369`, with its meaning unchanged, and `critical`'s new")
    strs_push(l, "rule, `no-ambient-time`, is the existing `N0510`. `nazm.profile-report/1` gains that rule's identity,")
    strs_push(l, "a new value of an existing field. No schema moved; the counters are a diagnostic line,")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-sched:`, on standard error under `NAZM_SCHED_REPORT`, as the memory report is.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N53, the runtime component and generic channels.** One code appeared, compatible:")
    strs_push(l, "`N0390` (a `Chan[T]` written or made whose element may not cross into a task — a sequence, a")
    strs_push(l, "closure, or a record or enum holding one — with the path to the offending field). Everything")
    strs_push(l, "else a typed channel can get wrong is an existing code with its meaning unchanged: an element of")
    strs_push(l, "the wrong type is `N0303`, `Chan` with two arguments `N0300`. No schema moved: a channel type in")
    strs_push(l, "a persisted interface is a new shape, `{\"chan\":T}`, which a `nazm.interface/7` reader refuses")
    strs_push(l, "rather than misreads. `nazm.cost/1` gains no field; a typed channel's operations are sites of")
    strs_push(l, "the existing kinds.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N52, resource facts and information flow.** No code appeared: a vouch without a")
    strs_push(l, "`VouchCap` is the existing `N0369`, and a profile's new rules are the existing `N0510`. Two")
    strs_push(l, "schemas appeared, `nazm.cost/1` (`nazm explain-cost --json`: per function, each site's `kind`,")
    strs_push(l, "`op`, `at`, `count` — `at-most-once` or `unknown`, never a number — and `on_failure`; and per")
    strs_push(l, "kind, totals by count) and `nazm.flow/1` (`nazm explain-flow --json`: each sink's `class`,")
    strs_push(l, "`function`, `at` and `origins`). `nazm.profile-report/1` gains three rule identities, a new value")
    strs_push(l, "of an existing field. The check artefact's sink facts gain an optional `class`, unread by an older")
    strs_push(l, "checker whose entries the semantic epoch already keeps apart.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to R1b, L15 (warnings).** A severity appeared, compatibly: `\"warning\"` beside")
    strs_push(l, "`\"error\"`, in `nazm.diagnostic/1`'s `severity` — a consumer that knows only `\"error\"` reads a")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostic it does not recognise, as the rule above requires it to tolerate. A warning is a")
    strs_push(l, "program the checker accepts, with something its author should know: `nazm check` and `nazm build`")
    strs_push(l, "report it and succeed, and refuse under `--deny-warnings`; the language service publishes it at")
    strs_push(l, "the warning severity. One code appeared, `N0632`, the first warning. No schema's major moved.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to R1.5, D7 (`List[T]` and `Chain[T]`).** One code appeared, compatibly: `N0637`, a")
    strs_push(l, "call of one of R1a's `list_` built-ins, renamed `chain_` with their type; its help names the new")
    strs_push(l, "built-in. Messages show the renamed sequence as `Chain[T]`; a `List[T]`, being `Vec[T]`, is shown")
    strs_push(l, "as a `Vec[T]` always was. No schema moved.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to R1.5, D4 (positional fields, variants without their enum).** One code appeared,")
    strs_push(l, "compatibly: `N0636`, a variant name two enums in scope share. `N0334` gained two cases — fields")
    strs_push(l, "given both by position and by name, and a positional list that does not give every field. No")
    strs_push(l, "schema moved.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to R1.5, D3 (short closures).** One code appeared, compatibly: `N0635`, a short")
    strs_push(l, "closure's parameter with nothing to take its type from. No schema moved.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to R1.5, D2 (expression bodies).** One code appeared, compatibly: `N0634`, a function")
    strs_push(l, "written `= e` that must still write its result type. No schema moved.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to R1b, L12 (`defer`).** One code appeared, compatibly: `N0631`, a `defer` body that")
    strs_push(l, "would leave it. No schema moved.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to R1b, L11 (default trait methods; impls of generic types).** `N0602` narrowed")
    strs_push(l, "compatibly: an impl may leave out a method its trait gives a default body. `N0604` gained a case —")
    strs_push(l, "an impl with type parameters whose header is not a generic record or enum applied to exactly them —")
    strs_push(l, "with its meaning unchanged: an impl for a type that cannot have one. No code appeared; no schema")
    strs_push(l, "moved.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to R1b, L10 (closures in generic functions, a shared `let mut`).** Two codes narrowed,")
    strs_push(l, "both compatibly — each now refuses less: `N0387` no longer covers a closure or a named function's")
    strs_push(l, "value written inside a generic function, and `N0386` no longer covers a captured `let mut` binding,")
    strs_push(l, "which is shared through a cell, except one whose type can hold a function value. No code appeared")
    strs_push(l, "and none moved; no schema moved.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N51, effect parameters.** Two codes appeared, both compatible: `N0388` (an effect")
    strs_push(l, "parameter where none may be: a second one, on a foreign function, on `main`, on a function with")
    strs_push(l, "no declared effect set, or named inside a type's arguments) and `N0389` (a call binding one effect")
    strs_push(l, "parameter to two different sets). `N0386` narrowed to a `let mut` binding: a captured capability")
    strs_push(l, "is now accepted. `N0369` gained a case — making a value of an undeclared function without the")
    strs_push(l, "authority its type's effects need — with its meaning unchanged. No schema moved: an effect list")
    strs_push(l, "may hold `\"*\"`, the effect parameter, which a `nazm.interface/7` reader refuses as an unknown")
    strs_push(l, "effect rather than misreads.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N50, function values and closures.** Two codes appeared, both compatible: `N0386`")
    strs_push(l, "(a closure captures a `let mut` binding or a capability) and `N0387` (a generic, built-in or")
    strs_push(l, "foreign function used as a value, or a closure or named function value written inside a generic")
    strs_push(l, "function). Everything else a function value can get wrong is an existing code with its meaning")
    strs_push(l, "unchanged: a call through one with the wrong arguments is `N0303` or `N0300`, `==` on one is")
    strs_push(l, "`N0304`, passing one to a task is `N0321`, effects its type or body lacks are `N0366`, and missing")
    strs_push(l, "authority is `N0369`. No schema moved: a function type in a persisted interface is a fifth shape")
    strs_push(l, "of type that a `nazm.interface/7` reader refuses rather than misreads. The memory report line gained")
    strs_push(l, "a fourth class, `closures`, after the other three, so a reader that finds classes by name is")
    strs_push(l, "unaffected.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N42, foreign functions.** Six codes appeared, all compatible: `N0380` (an ABI")
    strs_push(l, "other than `\"C\"`), `N0381` (a parameter or result type that cannot cross the C boundary — only")
    strs_push(l, "`Int` and `Bool` can), `N0382` (a symbol that is not a C identifier), `N0383` (two declarations")
    strs_push(l, "of one C symbol that disagree about its signature — in one module at check time, across modules")
    strs_push(l, "when the program is built — or a symbol the native runtime declares itself), `N0384` (type")
    strs_push(l, "parameters or a written effect set on a foreign declaration) and `N0385` (`nazm run` asked to")
    strs_push(l, "run a program that calls a foreign function, refused before any of it runs). A foreign call")
    strs_push(l, "without a `ForeignCap` held is the existing `N0369`, with or without an effect set; a declared")
    strs_push(l, "set that leaves `foreign` out is the existing `N0366`. One schema moved: the persisted module")
    strs_push(l, "interface is `nazm.interface/7`, because an export may now carry `foreign`, its C symbol, and a")
    strs_push(l, "`/6` reader would take such an export for an ordinary function with no body. `effects` lists")
    strs_push(l, "may contain `\"foreign\"` — a new value of an existing field, which is compatible. A link that")
    strs_push(l, "fails for a program with foreign calls names the foreign symbols and `--link` rather than")
    strs_push(l, "reporting a compiler bug.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N43, the runtime constitution.** No schema moved and no code appeared. The runtime's")
    strs_push(l, "failures keep their codes and now have one written classification (`architecture.md` §7.45):")
    strs_push(l, "`N0400`, `N0401` and `N0405` are the language's; `N0406` and `N0404` are the host refusing memory")
    strs_push(l, "or a thread — `N0404` in a native build means the operating system would not start a task's")
    strs_push(l, "thread, as `nazm run` uses it when the interpreter could not start; `N0407` is I/O. Status 2 is a")
    strs_push(l, "reported failure, `exit_with`'s is the program's, and 0 a normal return.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N45, the standard library.** No schema moved and no code appeared. `N0205` (a module")
    strs_push(l, "that cannot be found) gained a case: an import beginning with `@std/` that names no standard module,")
    strs_push(l, "whose help lists the ones there are. A standard module's definitions are named `@std/NAME::…` in")
    strs_push(l, "every packet that names a definition, exactly as a project module's are named by its path.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N46, packages.** Ten codes appeared, all compatible: `N0500` (an invalid manifest),")
    strs_push(l, "`N0501` (a dependency that is not there), `N0502` (a version mismatch), `N0503` (two packages of")
    strs_push(l, "one name, or a declared name the package does not have), `N0504` (a cycle), `N0505` (`--locked`")
    strs_push(l, "with no lockfile), `N0506` (other packages than the lockfile records), `N0507` (a package whose")
    strs_push(l, "bytes no longer match its digest), `N0508` (an import naming a package the importer does not")
    strs_push(l, "declare) and `N0509` (a package with no `main`). They are about manifests, directories and the")
    strs_push(l, "lockfile rather than positions in a module, so they carry a synthetic span. Two new formats have")
    strs_push(l, "their own versions and are not these schemas: the manifest, `nazm.package/1`, and the lockfile,")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.lock/1`. `nazm.check-report/1` and `nazm.build-report/1` gained `\"package\"` as a value of")
    strs_push(l, "`root`, compatible.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N47, restriction profiles.** Two codes appeared, compatible: `N0510` (a rule of a")
    strs_push(l, "profile in force refused the program — one per rule, at its first witness, with the rest as")
    strs_push(l, "secondary labels) and `N0511` (an unknown profile). One new format has its own version:")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.profile-report/1`, one line of JSON — `schema`, `profiles`, `outcome` (`accepted` or")
    strs_push(l, "`refused`), `rules` (each `id`, `verdict` `pass`/`fail`, `witnesses` of `file`, `start`, `end`,")
    strs_push(l, "`note`), and a `note` that it is not a certification. Rule ids are stable: `declared-effects`,")
    strs_push(l, "`no-io`, `no-spawn`, `no-foreign`, `locked-build`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A consumer that fails on an unrecognised field is not compatible with this contract, and")
    strs_push(l, "the `additionalProperties: false` in the schema documents is a statement about *this*")
    strs_push(l, "version's output, not a promise that the next one adds nothing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N76, syntax.** No schema moved and no code appeared. `N0004` also covers a refused")
    strs_push(l, "`\\u{…}` escape, at the escape's own bytes. Recovery inside lists reports existing codes at new")
    strs_push(l, "positions: a later independent mistake in the same item is now its own diagnostic.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N77, persisted resolution.** Two schemas appeared: `nazm.resolved/1`, a module's")
    strs_push(l, "imports, definitions and resolved occurrences by durable identity, and `nazm.references/1`, one")
    strs_push(l, "entity's occurrences read from those units. The cache's own entry moved to `nazm.check/3`, and a")
    strs_push(l, "`/2` entry is a miss. No code appeared, and the interface stays `nazm.interface/7`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N78, traits and methods.** Eleven codes appeared, all compatible: `N0600` (two impls")
    strs_push(l, "of one trait for one type), `N0601` (an impl in a module declaring neither), `N0602` (an impl")
    strs_push(l, "missing a method), `N0603` (an impl method its trait does not declare, or with another signature")
    strs_push(l, "or effects), `N0604` (an impl for a type that cannot have one), `N0605` (no trait in scope gives the")
    strs_push(l, "receiver the method), `N0606` (more than one does), `N0607` (a trait where a type is expected),")
    strs_push(l, "`N0608` (a method taken as a value), `N0609` (a trait method whose first parameter is not `self:")
    strs_push(l, "Self`) and `N0610` (a bound or an impl naming a type that is not a trait). They are the checker's,")
    strs_push(l, "in a new block because N03xx is full. The persisted interface moved to `nazm.interface/8`, and Core")
    strs_push(l, "IR's printed form to `nazm.core-ir/2`. No other schema moved; `nazm.resolved/1` gained the target")
    strs_push(l, "kinds `trait` and `trait method`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N79, effects and capabilities v3.** No code appeared. An `OutCap` that is asked to")
    strs_push(l, "authorise a file, the arguments or exit is the existing `N0369`, naming the `IoCap` it lacks; an")
    strs_push(l, "`OutCap` given for an `IoCap`, and a function value with more effects than expected, are the")
    strs_push(l, "existing `N0300`; a program defining `OutCap` is the existing `N0331`; the `authority` profile's")
    strs_push(l, "`explicit-authority` refuses with the existing `N0510`, naming the function, the kinds it inherits")
    strs_push(l, "and where it first exercises them. `nazm inspect` gains `inherits` per definition, a new field and")
    strs_push(l, "compatible; `nazm.profile-report/1` gains a profile and a rule. The interface stays")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.interface/8`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N80, provenance v3.** No code appeared. `N0372` keeps its meaning, and is now raised")
    strs_push(l, "also at a call through a value whose candidate writes to a path from its parameter, and at a closure")
    strs_push(l, "that captures what reaches a path, with a message saying which; its secondary labels follow cells,")
    strs_push(l, "captures, callers and exports. `checked-paths` refuses with the existing `N0510`. `nazm.flow/1 →")
    strs_push(l, "/2` adds `traces`; the check entry moved to `nazm.check/4`; `nazm.profile-report/1` gains a rule.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N81, the backend contract v2, stage one.** No code appeared: a layout table that does")
    strs_push(l, "not hold is the existing `N0900`, a compiler defect, raised before any code is generated.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.lir/1` is new (`nazm lir`), with `schema/nazm.lir-1.json` checked against real output.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N82, the runtime as an artifact.** No code appeared: an artifact that does not fit is")
    strs_push(l, "refused with one sentence naming the mismatch, not a code — exit 1 since Q1-C1 (the artifact named")
    strs_push(l, "does not fit the request), 3 when it cannot be read; it was 4, a missing toolchain's status. `nazm.runtime/1` is new, with `schema/nazm.runtime-1.json` checked against real")
    strs_push(l, "manifests of every profile; `nazm.provenance/1` gains an optional `runtime.archive`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N83, the task pool.** No code appeared: a task past its stack is the existing")
    strs_push(l, "`N0408`, a pool that was asked for and could not start makes `spawn` fail as a thread that could not")
    strs_push(l, "be created does (`N0404`), and five C symbols the pool calls join the reserved list (`N0383`).")
    strs_push(l, "`NAZM_SCHED_REPORT` gains a second line, `nazm-pool: workers=… peak=… stack=…`, printed only where")
    strs_push(l, "the pool ran; the first line is unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N85, FFI v3.** Four codes appeared, all compatible. `N0409` is a run-time failure: a")
    strs_push(l, "foreign function returned null where its declaration promised a value — a handle or a `Str` not")
    strs_push(l, "written as an `Option` — raised after C returns and before Nazm sees the pointer, status 2 as every")
    strs_push(l, "failure. `N0611` (an opaque handle built or taken apart) and `N0612` (a callback that is not an")
    strs_push(l, "export's name) are the checker's, continuing N78's block. `N0613` names `c_errno()` in a build for a")
    strs_push(l, "freestanding or WebAssembly target, inside the existing refusal of what only a hosted runtime has.")
    strs_push(l, "Existing codes answer for the new types without changing meaning: `N0381` for what may cross where")
    strs_push(l, "(now: handles, C structs, export function types; and `Str` and handle results), `N0304` for `==` on a")
    strs_push(l, "handle, `N0321` and `N0390` for a handle reaching a task, `N0380`/`N0384` for an `extern \"C\" struct`'s")
    strs_push(l, "ABI and type parameters, `N0385` for `c_errno()` under `nazm run`. The persisted interface moved to")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.interface/9` (a record's `c`); `nazm.runtime/1` gains the service name `foreign`, additive.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N86, embedded v2.** No code appeared. The four device-register widths are refused")
    strs_push(l, "where there is no device exactly as the 32-bit pair is (`N0392`), whose help now names both boards;")
    strs_push(l, "a RISC-V build on a host whose `clang` has no RISC-V code generator is an environment refusal, exit")
    strs_push(l, "4 and one sentence, as a missing toolchain is.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N87, contracts.** Four codes appeared, all compatible. `N0410` and `N0411` are run-time")
    strs_push(l, "failures — a precondition or a postcondition that evaluated `false`, at the clause, the same sentence")
    strs_push(l, "from the interpreter and both backends. `N0614` (a clause that is not pure) and `N0615` (a call of")
    strs_push(l, "literals that breaks its callee's precondition) are the checker's, continuing N78's block. A clause")
    strs_push(l, "that is not a `Bool` is the existing `N0300`. `nazm.obligations/1` is new, with")
    strs_push(l, "`schema/nazm.obligations-1.json` checked against real output; the persisted interface moved to")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.interface/10` (an export's `requires`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N90, packages v3.** No code appeared. `N0513`'s meaning is unchanged — no choice of")
    strs_push(l, "versions satisfies every requirement — and it is now said after a backtracking search, naming the")
    strs_push(l, "package no version fitted where the search got deepest and every requirement on it with who placed")
    strs_push(l, "it; a search that reaches its 10,000-candidate bound is `N0513` saying it stopped. `nazm update`")
    strs_push(l, "naming no registry package is the existing `N0501`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N91, debugger and profiler v3.** No code appeared. One schema moved, compatibly in")
    strs_push(l, "every field it had: `nazm.profile/1 → /2` adds `samples` — `null` unless `--sample`, else the")
    strs_push(l, "sampler, the interval, the total, the samples by Nazm function and line, by runtime, foreign and")
    strs_push(l, "system symbol (each system frame with `blocked`), the blocked count and the unattributed count. The")
    strs_push(l, "removed refusal of `--debug` with Cranelift was a toolchain message, not a code.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N92, performance evidence v2.** No code appeared. `nazm.bench/1 → /2`, additive:")
    strs_push(l, "`cpu_model`, `memory_bytes`, `kernel`, and `cpus` read on Linux too; per measurement `p90_ms`,")
    strs_push(l, "`max_ms`, `mad_ms` and `runs_ms`; `noise_floor_ms`, `binary_bytes`, `references` (how each is built")
    strs_push(l, "and whether its arithmetic is checked) and `not_measured` (each absent reference, with why). A `/1`")
    strs_push(l, "baseline is still read by `--check`. `bench/claims.toml` is new and is a register, not a schema.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N103, re-exports.** Three codes: `N0211`, a `pub use` names something the module it")
    strs_push(l, "re-exports from does not offer (or renames a trait, which is offered under its own name only);")
    strs_push(l, "`N0212`, a module offers one name twice; `N0213`, a cycle of re-exports, at each `pub`. Each at the")
    strs_push(l, "name or keyword it is about. Two schemas moved: `nazm.interface/10` → `nazm.interface/11` (a re-export's export")
    strs_push(l, "carries `reexport` and the defining module's identity; `reexported_types`), and")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.api-doc/1` → `nazm.api-doc/2` (a re-export is an item of kind `reexport` with `of`, the identity it")
    strs_push(l, "offers).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N106, the pool by default.** No new code. `N0404`, *this task could not be started*,")
    strs_push(l, "is now provoked on purpose as well: a `NAZM_SCHEDULER` that names neither `pool` nor `threads` starts")
    strs_push(l, "no task, and the first `spawn` reports it at its span — the unprovokable list lost it. One schema")
    strs_push(l, "moved: `nazm.cost/1` → `nazm.cost/2`, additive — `scheduler`, `null` for a program that starts no")
    strs_push(l, "task, otherwise `default` (`pool` or `threads`), `why`, `workers`, `task_stack_bytes` and the")
    strs_push(l, "`environment` that changes it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to N105, one LIR both backends consume.** No code appeared: a module LIR's validator refuses")
    strs_push(l, "is still `N0900`, a compiler defect, and its message names the function and the broken rule. One")
    strs_push(l, "schema moved: `nazm.lir/1` → `nazm.lir/2`, additive — each unit carries `lir`, its instruction-level")
    strs_push(l, "LIR as text (what `nazm lir --ops` prints) and that text's BLAKE3 `digest`, validated before it is")
    strs_push(l, "shown. `nazm lir --run` (LIR's interpreter) writes the program's own output and status, and exits 1,")
    strs_push(l, "naming what it does not run, for a program outside its subset (4 until Q1-C1); a spent budget is 2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to Gate 1 and Gate 1-C1, Nazm 1.0.** One code appeared, compatible: `N0616`, a closure")
    strs_push(l, "capturing a value that can hold a function value behind a counted handle — the one way a closure's")
    strs_push(l, "environment could come to own itself (`spec.md`, *Cycles*). It names the captured binding and its")
    strs_push(l, "type, and the handle through which it can hold function values where that differs; it carries no")
    strs_push(l, "fix, because the remedy — passing the value as an argument instead — changes a signature. It")
    strs_push(l, "continues N78's block, the N03xx block being full. One refusal changed code: `1.5` is `N0101`")
    strs_push(l, "(floating point, refused by name) where it was `N0100`; `N0100`'s meaning is unchanged, and no")
    strs_push(l, "code's meaning moved. `nazm.capabilities/1`'s `types` gained the five capability types it lacked,")
    strs_push(l, "new array values.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## The code registry")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Every code `nazm` can report, generated from `crates/nazm-diag/src/lib.rs` (`codes`) and held to it")
    strs_push(l, "by `crates/nazm-cli/tests/codes.rs`, which fails if a declared code is missing here, a row names a")
    strs_push(l, "code that is not declared, or two rows share a code (v1, Q1-D-11). A code's meaning is the first")
    strs_push(l, "sentence of its declaration's comment, or its constant's name where it has none; the sections above")
    strs_push(l, "say how each family is used. A **reserved** row names a code that is not declared and will not be")
    strs_push(l, "given a different meaning. Codes are never reused (*What compatibility means*).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "<!-- registry:begin -->")
    strs_push(l, "| Code | Constant | What it reports |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0001` | `UNKNOWN_CHARACTER` | Unknown character |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0002` | `UNTERMINATED_STRING` | Unterminated string |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0003` | `INTEGER_TOO_LARGE` | Integer too large |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0004` | `INVALID_ESCAPE` | A backslash in a string literal that is not one of the escapes `docs/user/spec.md` lists (N49) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0007` | `UNTERMINATED_COMMENT` | A block comment, `/* … */`, that the file ends inside; block comments nest (R1, 5b.17, `docs/user/spec.md`, *Comments*) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0006` | `INTERPOLATION` | An interpolation's hole that is not one: empty, unclosed on its line, a lone `}`, a format interpolation does not have, a precision on something not a float, or not one expression (R1a, `docs/user/spec.md`, *String interpolation*) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0005` | `STRING_LAYOUT` | A multi-line string with text after its opening `\"\"\"`, or a line not indented as its closing `\"\"\"` is (R1a, `docs/user/spec.md`, *Multi-line and raw strings*) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0100` | `UNEXPECTED_TOKEN` | Unexpected token |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0101` | `UNSUPPORTED_CONSTRUCT` | Unsupported construct — **the umbrella code** for a construct this implementation refuses; its message names the construct, and a more specific code replaces it where one exists (Q1-D-13) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0102` | `NESTING_TOO_DEEP` | An expression or block nested past the parser's limit |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0200` | `UNDEFINED_VARIABLE` | Undefined variable |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0201` | `UNDEFINED_FUNCTION` | Undefined function |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0202` | `ALREADY_DEFINED_IN_SCOPE` | Already defined in scope |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0203` | `DUPLICATE_FUNCTION` | Duplicate function |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0204` | `MISSING_MAIN` | Missing main |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0205` | `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` | `use \"path\";` named a file that could not be read |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0206` | `PRIVATE_DEFINITION` | A name that exists in an imported module, and is private there |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0207` | `AMBIGUOUS_IMPORT` | Two directly imported modules export the same name |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0208` | `IMPORT_COLLIDES_WITH_DEFINITION` | An import brings in a name this module also defines |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0209` | `ALIAS_COLLIDES` | `use \"PATH\" as NAME;` where `NAME` is already a function, a type or another import's name in the importing module (N49) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0210` | `UNKNOWN_QUALIFIED_NAME` | `NAME::item` where `NAME` is no alias, or the aliased module exports no `item` (N49) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0211` | `REEXPORT_UNKNOWN` | A `pub use` names something the module it re-exports from does not export (N103) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0212` | `REEXPORT_COLLIDES` | A module offers one name twice, its own or a re-export's (N103) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0213` | `REEXPORT_CYCLE` | Modules re-export from each other in a cycle (N103) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0300` | `TYPE_MISMATCH` | Type mismatch |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0301` | `CONDITION_NOT_BOOL` | Condition not bool |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0302` | `BRANCH_TYPES_DIFFER` | Branch types differ |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0303` | `WRONG_ARGUMENT_COUNT` | Wrong argument count |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0304` | `INVALID_OPERANDS` | Invalid operands |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0305` | `UNKNOWN_TYPE` | Unknown type |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0310` | `ASSIGN_TO_IMMUTABLE` | Assign to immutable |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0311` | `MUTABLE_PARAMETER` | Mutable parameter |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0312` | `NOT_IN_A_LOOP` | `break` or `continue` outside a loop |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0313` | `UNREACHABLE_STATEMENT` | A statement that provably cannot run |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0314` | `CONTROL_FLOW_AS_VALUE` | `break` or `continue` where a value is expected |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0320` | `SPAWN_OUTSIDE_SCOPE` | `spawn` outside a `scope` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0321` | `ILLEGAL_TASK_CAPTURE` | A value that may not cross into a task |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0330` | `DUPLICATE_TYPE` | Two types declared with one name in one module |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0331` | `BUILTIN_TYPE_REDEFINED` | A type declared with a built-in type's name |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0332` | `DUPLICATE_FIELD` | Two fields of one record, or of one variant's payload, with one name |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0333` | `UNKNOWN_FIELD` | A field named in a construction, a projection or a pattern that the record or variant does not have |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0334` | `MISSING_FIELD` | A construction that does not give every field a value, or a pattern that does not name every payload field |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0335` | `INVALID_PROJECTION` | `.field` on something that is not a record — including an enum, whose payload is reached by `match` and not by projection |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0336` | `RECURSIVE_RECORD` | A user-defined type that contains itself by value, directly or through others |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0337` | `PRIVATE_TYPE_EXPOSED` | A public function, record or enum whose signature, fields or payloads name a private type, which an importer could not resolve |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0338` | `TYPE_NESTING_TOO_DEEP` | User-defined types nested inside one another past the stated bound |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0339` | `EMPTY_ENUM` | An enum with no variants |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0340` | `DUPLICATE_VARIANT` | Two variants of one enum with one name |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0341` | `UNKNOWN_VARIANT` | A variant named in a construction or a pattern that the enum does not have |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0342` | `MATCH_ON_NON_ENUM` | `match` on a value that is not an enum |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0343` | `NON_EXHAUSTIVE_MATCH` | A `match` that does not name every variant of its enum |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0344` | `DUPLICATE_MATCH_ARM` | A `match` that names one variant twice |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0345` | `WRONG_ENUM_IN_PATTERN` | A pattern whose variant belongs to a different enum than the scrutinee |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0350` | `DUPLICATE_TYPE_PARAMETER` | Two type parameters of one declaration with one name |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0351` | `TYPE_ARGUMENTS_ON_NON_GENERIC` | Type arguments written on something that takes none |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0352` | `MISSING_TYPE_ARGUMENTS` | A generic definition, or `Vec`, written where a complete type is required but without its type arguments |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0353` | `WRONG_TYPE_ARGUMENT_COUNT` | A generic definition applied to the wrong number of type arguments |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0354` | `CANNOT_INFER_TYPE_ARGUMENT` | A generic call whose arguments do not determine every type parameter |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0355` | `CONFLICTING_TYPE_ARGUMENTS` | Two arguments of one call that give one type parameter different types |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0356` | `GENERIC_MAIN` | A generic `main` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0357` | `UNBOUNDED_SPECIALISATION` | A generic function whose native instances would never end — polymorphic recursion, `f[T]` calling `f[Vec[T]]` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0358` | `GENERIC_INSTANCE_LIMIT` | More native generic instances than one program may have, or one nested too deeply |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0359` | `OWNERSHIP_CYCLE` | A type that can own itself through a reference-counted container — `Node { children |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0360` | `PROPAGATE_NON_RESULT` | `?` applied to something that is not the core prelude's `Result` — an `Option`, a project enum shaped like one, anything else |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0361` | `PROPAGATE_OUTSIDE_RESULT` | `?` in a function whose return type is not the core prelude's `Result` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0362` | `PROPAGATE_ERROR_MISMATCH` | `?` whose operand's error type is not exactly the enclosing function's |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0363` | `PRELUDE_TYPE_REDECLARED` | A project type named like one of the core prelude's, which every module sees |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0364` | `UNSATISFIED_REQUIREMENT` | A type argument, written or inferred, that does not have a capability its parameter requires — a concrete type without equality, or a caller's own parameter whose … |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0365` | `UNKNOWN_REQUIREMENT` | A requirement naming something that is not a capability |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0366` | `UNDECLARED_EFFECT` | A function whose declared effect set lacks an effect its body requires |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0367` | `UNKNOWN_EFFECT` | A name in an effect set that is not an effect |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0368` | `DUPLICATE_EFFECT` | An effect written twice in one set |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0369` | `MISSING_AUTHORITY` | An operation whose authority the function does not hold (N37) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0370` | `CAPABILITY_CONSTRUCTED` | An attempt to build a capability |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0371` | `MAIN_PARAMETER` | A `main` parameter that is not a capability |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0372` | `RESTRICTED_FLOW` | A restricted flow (N38) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0380` | `FOREIGN_ABI` | A foreign declaration names an ABI other than `\"C\"` (N42) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0381` | `FOREIGN_TYPE` | A foreign declaration takes or returns a type that cannot cross the C boundary (N42) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0382` | `FOREIGN_SYMBOL` | A foreign declaration's symbol is not a C identifier a linker can be handed (N42) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0383` | `FOREIGN_CONFLICT` | Two foreign declarations of one symbol disagree about its signature (N42) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0384` | `FOREIGN_SHAPE` | A foreign declaration has type parameters or a written effect set (N42) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0385` | `FOREIGN_NOT_INTERPRETED` | `nazm run` was asked to run a program that calls a foreign function (N42) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0386` | `CAPTURE_REFUSED` | A closure captures a `let mut` binding whose type can hold a function value (N50; narrowed by N51 and R1b) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0387` | `NOT_A_FUNCTION_VALUE` | A function that cannot be a value — generic, foreign or built-in — is used as one (N50; narrowed by R1b) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0388` | `EFFECT_PARAMETER` | An effect parameter where none may be |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0389` | `CONFLICTING_EFFECT_ARGUMENT` | A call binds its callee's effect parameter to two different sets (N51) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0390` | `CHANNEL_ELEMENT` | A `Chan[T]` whose `T` may not cross into a task (N53) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0391` | `EXPORT_SHAPE` | An export (N55) that is not public, declares an effect, is generic, or takes or returns a type other than `Int` and `Bool` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0392` | `MACHINE_ONLY` | A device-register built-in (`mmio_read32`, `mmio_write32`) reached by something that has no device registers |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0393` | `COMPTIME_REFUSED` | A function `nazm comptime` will not evaluate |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0394` | `KERNEL_INELIGIBLE` | A function `nazm accel` will not run as a kernel |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0395` | `NOT_A_CONTRACT` | A module `nazm contract` was given that does not have a contract's shape |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0396` | `CONSERVATION_BROKEN` | A transaction that would change the contract's conserved quantity |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0397` | `CALLER_NOT_INT` | A sender whose address is not an `Int`, as the language's `caller` must be |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0398` | `BAD_CALLDATA` | Calldata that is not a known entrypoint's selector and `int64` arguments |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0399` | `EVM_UNSUPPORTED` | A contract construct the EVM backend does not emit, or a storage upgrade it refuses |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0400` | `INTEGER_OVERFLOW` | Integer overflow |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0401` | `DIVISION_BY_ZERO` | Division by zero |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0402` | `ITERATION_LIMIT` | The interpreter's iteration guard, not a language rule |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0403` | `CALL_DEPTH_LIMIT` | Runaway recursion, caught before the stack is exhausted |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0404` | `INTERPRETER_UNAVAILABLE` | The host refused what running needs |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0405` | `INDEX_OUT_OF_BOUNDS` | An index outside a value's bounds |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0406` | `ALLOCATION_FAILED` | The allocator refused |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0407` | `IO_FAILED` | A file could not be read or written |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0408` | `STACK_EXHAUSTED` | A compiled program's call would exhaust its thread's stack (N49) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0409` | `NULL_FROM_C` | A foreign function returned null where its declaration promised a value (N85) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0410` | `PRECONDITION_FAILED` | A precondition that did not hold as the function was entered (N87) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0411` | `POSTCONDITION_FAILED` | A postcondition that did not hold as the function returned (N87) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0412` | `SHIFT_OUT_OF_RANGE` | A shift or rotation by a negative amount, or a shift by the operand's width or more (Gate 2) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0413` | `NOT_UTF8` | Bytes that are not UTF-8 made into a `Text`, a `Text` cut or read away from a scalar boundary, or an `Int` that is not a Unicode scalar value made into one (Gate 2) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0414` | `TASK_DEADLINE` | A board's task released again before it had run |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0415` | `WATCHDOG_EXPIRED` | A board's watchdog expired |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0416` | `EXIT_STATUS` | `exit_with` given a status outside `0..=255`, the statuses every host reports unchanged (v1, Q1-B-05, `docs/user/spec.md`, *Ending*) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0500` | `MANIFEST_INVALID` | A manifest that cannot be read as `nazm.package/1` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0501` | `PACKAGE_NOT_FOUND` | A dependency's directory or manifest is not there |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0502` | `VERSION_MISMATCH` | A dependency's manifest states another version than the one declared for it |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0503` | `PACKAGE_CONFLICT` | Two packages of one name in one build |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0504` | `PACKAGE_CYCLE` | A package depends on itself, through its dependencies |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0505` | `LOCK_MISSING` | `--locked`, and there is no lockfile |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0506` | `LOCK_MISMATCH` | `--locked`, and the packages resolved are not the ones the lockfile records |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0507` | `DIGEST_MISMATCH` | A package's bytes no longer match the digest the lockfile records for it |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0508` | `UNKNOWN_DEPENDENCY` | An import names a package the importing package does not declare |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0509` | `NO_ENTRY` | A package built as a program has no `main` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0510` | `PROFILE_VIOLATION` | A program that breaks a rule of a profile in force |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0511` | `UNKNOWN_PROFILE` | A profile named on the command line or in a manifest that does not exist |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0512` | `REGISTRY_INVALID` | A registry index that is not `nazm.registry-index/1`, names another package, records a version twice or a digest of the wrong shape; or a publish of a version already … |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0513` | `VERSION_UNSATISFIABLE` | No version in the registry satisfies every requirement on a package |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0514` | `PACKAGE_UNSAFE` | A registry package holding a symbolic link or anything but files and directories |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0600` | `IMPL_CONFLICT` | Two impls of one trait for one type in one compilation |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0601` | `IMPL_ORPHAN` | An impl in a module that declares neither the trait nor the type |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0602` | `IMPL_MISSING_METHOD` | An impl that does not define every method of its trait that has no default body (narrowed by R1b) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0603` | `IMPL_METHOD_MISMATCH` | An impl method its trait does not declare, or one whose signature is not the trait's with `Self` replaced by the impl's type, effects included |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0604` | `IMPL_TYPE_REFUSED` | An impl for a type that cannot have one, or one with type parameters not written for a generic record or enum applied to exactly them (R1b) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0605` | `NO_METHOD` | A method call no trait in scope provides for the receiver's type |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0606` | `AMBIGUOUS_METHOD` | A method call more than one trait in scope provides |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0607` | `TRAIT_NOT_A_TYPE` | A trait written where a type is expected |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0608` | `METHOD_NOT_A_VALUE` | A method named without being called |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0609` | `TRAIT_METHOD_SELF` | A trait method whose first parameter is not `self |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0610` | `NOT_A_TRAIT` | A bound, an impl or a qualified call naming a type that is not a trait |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0611` | `OPAQUE_HANDLE` | An opaque handle (`extern \"C\" struct S;`) built or taken apart |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0612` | `CALLBACK_NOT_EXPORT` | A callback argument to C that is not an export's name |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0613` | `ERRNO_UNAVAILABLE` | `c_errno()` in a build for a target with no `errno` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0614` | `CONTRACT_SHAPE` | A contract clause that is not made only of literals, names, operators, field reads and calls of pure functions |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0615` | `PRECONDITION_REFUTED` | A call whose arguments are all literals and that breaks its callee's precondition |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0616` | `CAPTURE_CYCLE` | A closure capturing a value that can hold a function value behind a counted handle — a `Vec[fn() -> Int]`, a `Vec` of records with a function field, a record holding one |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0617` | `SHIFT_AMOUNT_REFUSED` | A shift whose amount is a constant outside `0..width` (Gate 2) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0618` | `ARRAY_TOO_LARGE` | An array over 64 KiB, or of no elements (Gate 2) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0619` | `ATTRIBUTE` | An attribute the language does not have, on a declaration it does not apply to, or with arguments it does not take (Gate 2, `docs/user/spec.md`, *Attributes*) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0620` | — | **reserved**, never assigned: kept for a warning at each use of a deprecated item, should a warning severity ever exist (Q1-D-14) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0621` | `ARRAY_ELEMENT` | An array whose element owns something — a `Str`, a handle, a function value — rather than plain data (Gate 2) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0622` | `NOT_A_CONSTANT` | A constant's value, or an array's length, that is not computed from literals, other constants, operators and numeric conversions (Gate 2) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0623` | `CONSTANT_FAILS` | A constant whose computation overflows, divides by zero or shifts out of range (Gate 2) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0624` | `ARRAY_INDEX` | An index that is not into an array, or a constant index outside it (Gate 2) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0625` | `STATIC_ASSIGNED` | An assignment to a static, which is read-only — changed, if an `Atomic`, only by the atomic operations (Gate 3, `docs/user/spec.md`, *Statics*) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0626` | `BOARD_MANIFEST` | A board's manifest the build cannot honour |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0627` | `INTERRUPT_HANDLER` | An interrupt handler of a shape the board cannot call, two handlers for one interrupt, or one for an interrupt the board does not have (Gate 3, `docs/user/spec.md`, *Boards*) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0628` | `NOT_ITERABLE` | A `for` loop over something that is not an `Ints`, `Strs`, `Vec[T]` or `Bytes` (R1a, `docs/user/spec.md`, *`for` loops*) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0629` | `OR_PATTERN_BINDINGS` | An or-pattern's alternatives that bind different names, or one name with different types (R1a, `docs/user/spec.md`, *Patterns*) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0630` | `LET_ELSE_COMPLETES` | A `let … else` whose `else` can finish (R1a, `docs/user/spec.md`, *Patterns*) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0631` | `DEFER_LEAVES` | A `defer` body that would leave it: `return`, `?`, or `break`/`continue` out of it (R1b, `docs/user/spec.md`, *`defer`*) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0632` | `WILDCARD_COVERS_VARIANTS` | A **warning**: a `_` or a name in a `match` of an enum covers variants no arm names (R1b, `docs/user/spec.md`, *Patterns*) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0635` | `CLOSURE_PARAMETER_UNTYPED` | A short closure's parameter without a type where no function type is expected to take it from (R1.5, `docs/user/spec.md`, *Shorter forms*) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0636` | `VARIANT_AMBIGUOUS` | A variant written without its enum where two enums in scope have a variant of that name (R1.5, `docs/user/spec.md`, *Shorter forms*) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0637` | `BUILTIN_RENAMED` | A call of one of R1a's `list_` built-ins, renamed `chain_` with their type, `Chain[T]` (R1.5, `docs/user/spec.md`, *Immutable indirection*) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0634` | `RESULT_TYPE_NOT_INFERRED` | A function written `= e` with no result type that must write one: a `pub` function, a method, or one whose body reaches itself (R1.5, `docs/user/spec.md`, *Shorter forms*) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0830` | `TLS_TARGET` | A program reaching `@std/tls` built for a target with no TLS binding: a board, WebAssembly (whose host terminates TLS), or one whose binding is not yet written (v1 track C1, `docs/user/spec.md`, *TLS*) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0850` | `BOARD_MEMORY` | An image, its data or its stack that does not fit a microcontroller board's flash or RAM, naming the region and the overflow (M1) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0851` | `BOARD_INIT` | A board manifest's `init` that names no function `fn NAME() -> Int ! {}` or `fn NAME(m: MmioCap) -> Int ! {}` of the program, or names more than one (M1) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0854` | `BOARD_FLOAT` | A floating-point value a microcontroller target cannot compute with: `Float64` on `thumbv8m.main-none-eabihf`, whose FPU is single-precision, and either float on `riscv32imc-unknown-none-elf`, which has none (M1) |")
    strs_push(l, "| `N0900` | `COMPILER_DEFECT` | The compiler contradicted itself (N39) |")
    strs_push(l, "<!-- registry:end -->")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Spans are byte offsets")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`start` is inclusive, `end` is exclusive, and both count **bytes** from the beginning of")
    strs_push(l, "the file — not characters, not UTF-16 units, not lines. `start == end` is an insertion")
    strs_push(l, "point rather than an empty range.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "For a program assembled from several files with `use`, a diagnostic's offsets are into")
    strs_push(l, "the concatenation of every file in load order.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**This did not change when source identity became internal (N1, 2026-09-21.)** The compiler")
    strs_push(l, "now carries a real file with every span and offsets that are local to it, and the human")
    strs_push(l, "rendering names the file directly rather than searching for it. The published shape is")
    strs_push(l, "deliberately unmoved: `nazm.diagnostic/1` has always reported concatenation offsets with no")
    strs_push(l, "`file` field, and improving the compiler's internals is not a reason to move every existing")
    strs_push(l, "consumer's numbers. A future schema version could publish `{ file, start, end }` directly;")
    strs_push(l, "that is a version decision, not a side effect. `nazm fix --json` resolves them: its `file`,")
    strs_push(l, "`start` and `end` name a real file and an offset inside it, which is what an editing tool")
    strs_push(l, "needs.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Where the conversion happens, corrected 2026-09-22.** N1 met the compatibility")
    strs_push(l, "requirement inside `Span` itself: a hand-written `Serialize` that dropped the file, and a")
    strs_push(l, "`Deserialize` that put `FileId::ROOT` back. The published bytes were right and the design")
    strs_push(l, "was wrong — *every* serialisation of a span was lossy, including future ones with no")
    strs_push(l, "connection to this schema, and a span read back named the wrong file with no error. The")
    strs_push(l, "conversion now belongs to `nazm-diag`, which owns this format: `Diagnostic::published`")
    strs_push(l, "converts through `SourceMap::global` at the moment of serialisation into `wire::Published*`")
    strs_push(l, "types that exist to be this schema and nothing else. `nazm-span` no longer depends on serde")
    strs_push(l, "at all, so a span cannot be serialised by accident; `cargo xtask check`'s **span identity**")
    strs_push(l, "gate fails if that changes. A test pins the exact bytes of a diagnostic in the second file")
    strs_push(l, "of a two-file program.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**An editor sees the same diagnostics, converted at its own boundary (N16, 2026-09-25).**")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm lsp` publishes diagnostics as the Language Server Protocol requires: per file, with")
    strs_push(l, "positions as lines and UTF-16 columns. That is the protocol's shape, not a new Nazm schema:")
    strs_push(l, "the code, message and severity are the diagnostic's own, the range is its primary span")
    strs_push(l, "converted from file-local byte offsets at the adapter, and nothing in `nazm.diagnostic/1`")
    strs_push(l, "changed. Standard LSP messages are not Nazm machine interfaces and carry no `schema` field.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Fixes, and when to apply one")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A fix is `replace these bytes with this text`. Two things make it usable unattended:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `applicability: \"automatic\"` | Correct whenever the diagnostic is correct, and changes nothing else. `nazm fix --apply` applies these |")
    strs_push(l, "| `applicability: \"needs_review\"` | Resolves the diagnostic and may not be what was meant. Never applied automatically; presented with its precondition |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**`precondition` is present on every fix, including the automatic ones.** On an automatic")
    strs_push(l, "fix it states what makes the edit unconditional; on one needing review it states the")
    strs_push(l, "assumption a person is being asked to confirm. A fix with nothing written there would be")
    strs_push(l, "a fix whose author never asked when it could be wrong, and the field exists to force the")
    strs_push(l, "question at the point the fix is written.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm fix --apply` also refuses to write a file that would no longer parse, applies edits")
    strs_push(l, "right-to-left so earlier offsets stay valid, and skips an edit that overlaps one it has")
    strs_push(l, "already made — reporting each skip and why. Overlapping repairs are two answers to what")
    strs_push(l, "may be one mistake, and applying both produces text neither suggested.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Every reason an edit is not applied is reported in `skipped`, and there are exactly seven:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| `skipped` | When |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `it needs review` | the fix is `needs_review`, which is never applied unattended |")
    strs_push(l, "| `the file could not be read` | the file to edit could not be read back |")
    strs_push(l, "| `it overlaps an edit already applied in this run` | a later edit in the file touched these bytes first |")
    strs_push(l, "| `the span does not name a range of this file` | the span is past the end of the file or inside a character |")
    strs_push(l, "| `the file changed since it was checked` | the bytes at the span are no longer the ones the checker saw |")
    strs_push(l, "| `applying it produced a file that does not parse` | the file's edits together left it unparsable; nothing in it is written |")
    strs_push(l, "| `the file could not be written` | writing failed; the edit is not reported applied |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### In an editor")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm lsp` offers the same fixes as quick fixes (`textDocument/codeAction`), from the")
    strs_push(l, "diagnostics of the document's current analysis and never from the diagnostics a client")
    strs_push(l, "sends:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- an **automatic** fix is a quick fix, marked preferred when it is its diagnostic's only")
    strs_push(l, "  fix;")
    strs_push(l, "- a **needs-review** fix is a quick fix the user chooses, titled with its precondition —")
    strs_push(l, "  `Review fix N0300: discard the value — right only if …` — and never preferred.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The two execution models differ, and neither pretends to be the other. `nazm fix --apply`")
    strs_push(l, "writes files, and can roll a file back when the result would not parse. The language server")
    strs_push(l, "writes nothing: it returns each fix as an edit tied to the open document's exact version, with")
    strs_push(l, "the bytes it replaces checked against the current text, and the editor applies it — so there")
    strs_push(l, "is no rollback after the fact. What stands in for one is that every fix the compiler attaches")
    strs_push(l, "is tested to parse and to remove its diagnostic when applied alone, and that a client whose")
    strs_push(l, "buffer has moved on cannot apply an edit tied to the old version.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## The capability inventory")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Not the language's capabilities. `IoCap` and `SpawnCap` are **authority**, values a program")
    strs_push(l, "holds (`docs/user/spec.md`, *Capabilities*); this inventory is a list of what the toolchain can")
    strs_push(l, "do, and the two share a word and nothing else.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm capabilities` reports what **this build** supports, read from the tables the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler dispatches on: `Intrinsic::ALL` for the front end, the backend's own `Builtin`")
    strs_push(l, "for `nazm build`, `Type::ALL` for the types. A built-in cannot be listed as interpreted")
    strs_push(l, "and be missing from the interpreter, because the interpreter's table is where the name")
    strs_push(l, "came from.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Constructs are the exception and say so. Whether `scope` or recursion compiles is decided")
    strs_push(l, "by code, not by a table, so each of those rows carries an `evidence` field naming the")
    strs_push(l, "test file or the document that establishes it. A row claiming `compiled: false` means the")
    strs_push(l, "construct is **refused by name** — never silently missing, and never approximated.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Running a corpus")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm test PATH…` runs every `NAME.nz` that has a `NAME.expected` beside it, under")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm run` **and** as a `nazm build` executable, and requires both to produce the")
    strs_push(l, "recorded output. That convention is not new — `compiler/bootstrap.sh` has compared the")
    strs_push(l, "conformance corpus that way since the bootstrap existed; the command makes it available")
    strs_push(l, "to anything that is not the bootstrap script.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The comparison is **stdout and stderr combined, trimmed**: a program's diagnostic is as")
    strs_push(l, "much of its behaviour as its value, and a trailing newline is a property of `printf`.")
    strs_push(l, "A `.nz` file with no `.expected` beside it is not a test case, and the number of them is")
    strs_push(l, "reported rather than passed over — a silently skipped file is how a renamed test stops")
    strs_push(l, "running and nobody notices.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A case whose program *fails* cannot match both legs**, and that is a real difference")
    strs_push(l, "rather than an oversight. `nazm run` renders a failure with the source line, a caret and")
    strs_push(l, "a help line; a compiled program writes one line — `nazm: error[N0401]: … at file:line:col`")
    strs_push(l, "— because the executable carries the message and the position and not the source. Both")
    strs_push(l, "name the same code and the same place, which is the part that is specified. A corpus")
    strs_push(l, "case that is meant to fail should therefore test one leg, with `--interpret-only`, or")
    strs_push(l, "assert on the code rather than the rendering.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## The exit statuses")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| 0 | Success — nothing to report |")
    strs_push(l, "| 1 | The source, program, package or request is invalid |")
    strs_push(l, "| 2 | The program ran and failed at run time |")
    strs_push(l, "| 3 | A file or resource the command needs could not be found or read |")
    strs_push(l, "| 4 | The compiler, a tool it runs, or the machine failed |")
    strs_push(l, "| 5 | The command line itself is wrong |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "4 is separate from 1 on purpose: one means the request is wrong, the other means the")
    strs_push(l, "machine could not carry out one that is fine. 5 is separate from 2: a mistyped option is not a")
    strs_push(l, "program that failed. The full definitions, and what moved when the contract was frozen (Q1-C1),")
    strs_push(l, "are `docs/user/stability.md`, *Diagnostics and exit statuses*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to Gate 3, requirements traceability.** No diagnostic code. `nazm.trace/1` is new, with")
    strs_push(l, "`schema/nazm.trace-1.json` checked against real output (`schemas.rs`): each requirement of a")
    strs_push(l, "`requirements.toml` (`schema = \"nazm.requirements/1\"`) to its definitions by durable identity and")
    strs_push(l, "digest, their obligations, and its tests' outcomes. A broken link — a definition renamed away, a test")
    strs_push(l, "missing or failing, a requirement naming nothing to verify it — is written to `broken` and to")
    strs_push(l, "standard error, and the command exits 1.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to the v1 fixes.** One code appeared, compatible: `N0416`, a run-time failure — `exit_with`")
    strs_push(l, "given a status outside `0..=255` (Q1-B-05). Until then such a status reached the host and was")
    strs_push(l, "truncated differently by each implementation; no program that ran with a status in range changes.")
    strs_push(l, "`N0381` gained a use, also compatible: on a 32-bit target, a foreign declaration whose crossing is a")
    strs_push(l, "C pointer (Q1-A1-05).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Applied to R3, Core IR for a lowering in Nazm (2026-10-15).** No code appeared. One debugging")
    strs_push(l, "schema moved: `nazm.core-ir/2` → `nazm.core-ir/3`, a new major because a field's values changed —")
    strs_push(l, "a function or array type is spelled (`fn(Int) -> Str`, `[Int; 4]`) where `/2` wrote `?`. It also")
    strs_push(l, "gains each function's `pub`, `closure`, `captures` and `attributes`, and the root's `modules`,")
    strs_push(l, "`types` (records and enums in the checker's id order), `statics`, `impls` and `derived_hash`")
    strs_push(l, "(`architecture.md` §7.41). Every `/2` field stays where it was; the digests are unchanged.")
    str_join(l, str_from_byte(10)) + str_from_byte(10)
}

fn dd_doc9() -> Str {
    let l = strs_new()
    strs_push(l, "(* The Nazm grammar.")
    strs_push(l, " *")
    strs_push(l, " * This file is an artefact, not a description: `crates/nazm-syntax/tests/grammar.rs`")
    strs_push(l, " * reads it and checks three things against the real implementation.")
    strs_push(l, " *")
    strs_push(l, " *   1. Every terminal written here is a real token, and every token the lexer has is")
    strs_push(l, " *      written here. A keyword added to the lexer and not to the grammar fails the test.")
    strs_push(l, " *   2. Every nonterminal referenced is defined, and every nonterminal defined is")
    strs_push(l, " *      reachable from `program`. A rule nobody uses is a rule nobody maintains.")
    strs_push(l, " *   3. Every rule carries at least one `@example`, and every example is fed to the real")
    strs_push(l, " *      parser and must parse with no diagnostics. A grammar whose examples the parser")
    strs_push(l, " *      rejects is describing a language that does not exist.")
    strs_push(l, " *")
    strs_push(l, " * What the test does *not* do is prove the parser accepts exactly this language. That")
    strs_push(l, " * would need a generated parser, and this one is written by hand — deliberately, for the")
    strs_push(l, " * diagnostics. So: the terminals are exact, the examples are executable, and the")
    strs_push(l, " * structure is a claim checked by review. `docs/user/guide.md` is generated from this file.")
    strs_push(l, " *")
    strs_push(l, " * Notation: `=` defines, `|` alternates, `{ x }` is zero or more, `[ x ]` is optional,")
    strs_push(l, " * `( )` groups, quoted text is a terminal, UPPERCASE is a token class.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example use \"other.nz\"; fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example struct Point { x: Int, } fn main() -> Int { Point(x: 1).x } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum State { Ready, } fn main() -> Int { match State.Ready() { State.Ready() => 0, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn identity[T](value: T) -> T { value } fn main() -> Int { identity(7) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example trait Show { fn show(self: Self) -> Str; } impl Show for Int { fn show(self: Int) -> Str { int_to_str(self) } } fn main() -> Int { str_len(7.show()) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example const SIZE: Int = 4; fn main() -> Int { SIZE } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example @cfg(os = \"linux\") fn f() -> Int { 1 } @cfg(not(os = \"linux\")) fn f() -> Int { 0 } fn main() -> Int { f() } *)")
    strs_push(l, "program = { use_item } , { { attribute } , ( function | foreign_function | record | foreign_struct | enumeration | trait_item | impl_item | constant ) } ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* An attribute (Gate 2): `@` and a name from a closed vocabulary — `cfg`, `test`, `bench`,")
    strs_push(l, " * `fuzz`, `deprecated` — before a top-level declaration, never before a `use`. Which names")
    strs_push(l, " * exist and what each takes is the checker's (`N0619`), not the grammar's. See")
    strs_push(l, " * `docs/user/spec.md`, *Attributes* and *Conditional compilation*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example @test fn checks() -> Int { 0 } fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example @cfg(all(os = \"macos\", any(arch = \"aarch64\", arch = \"x86_64\"))) fn f() -> Int { 0 } fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "attribute = \"@\" , IDENT , [ \"(\" , [ attribute_arg , { \",\" , attribute_arg } , [ \",\" ] ] , \")\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example @deprecated(\"use g\") fn f() -> Int { 0 } fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example @test(fails) fn f() -> Int { 0 } fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "attribute_arg = STRING")
    strs_push(l, "              | IDENT , [ \"=\" , STRING | \"(\" , [ attribute_arg , { \",\" , attribute_arg } , [ \",\" ] ] , \")\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* A constant (Gate 2): a value the checker computes from literals, other constants,")
    strs_push(l, " * operators and numeric conversions. `const` is a word only here, before a name and a `:`,")
    strs_push(l, " * so it remains an ordinary name everywhere else. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Constants*.")
    strs_push(l, " *")
    strs_push(l, " * A static (Gate 3) is written the same way with `static`: storage with one address, a")
    strs_push(l, " * number or a `Bool` read-only, or an `Atomic` started by `atomic_new` of a constant. `static`")
    strs_push(l, " * is a word only where `const` is. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Statics*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* R1a (L8): a constant may be a record, enum value, tuple or array built of constant parts, and")
    strs_push(l, " * `pub const` exports one; an importer under a name reads it as `m::NAME`. See `docs/user/spec.md`,")
    strs_push(l, " * *Constant tables and exported constants*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example const MASK: UInt8 = 0xF0; fn main() -> Int { Int(MASK) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example static TICKS: Atomic = atomic_new(0); fn main() -> Int { atomic_add(TICKS, 1) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example struct K { s: Str, n: Int, } pub const TABLE: [K; 2] = [K(s: \"a\", n: 1), K(s: \"b\", n: 2)]; fn main() -> Int { TABLE[1].n } *)")
    strs_push(l, "constant = [ visibility ] , ( \"const\" | \"static\" ) , IDENT , \":\" , type , \"=\" , expression , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* A trait (N78): a named set of methods a type may implement. Each method is a signature")
    strs_push(l, " * ended by `;`, or since R1b a default body an impl that writes none gets, whose first")
    strs_push(l, " * parameter is `self: Self`. A trait")
    strs_push(l, " * is in the type namespace and is not a type: it is written as a type parameter's bound,")
    strs_push(l, " * `[T: Show]`, and never as the type of a value. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Traits and methods*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example pub trait Show { fn show(self: Self) -> Str; fn shout(self: Self, n: Int) -> Str ! {}; } fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "trait_item = [ visibility ] , \"trait\" , IDENT , \"{\" , { trait_method } , \"}\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example trait Size { fn size(self: Self) -> Int; } fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example trait Size { fn size(self: Self) -> Int; fn big(self: Self) -> Bool { self.size() > 9 } } fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "trait_method = \"fn\" , IDENT , \"(\" , [ parameters ] , \")\" , result , [ effect_set ] , ( \";\" | block ) ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* `impl Trait for Type`: every method of the trait without a default body, once, with")
    strs_push(l, " * `Self` written as the type. `for` is a word here and nowhere else. At most one impl of a")
    strs_push(l, " * trait for a type, in the trait's module or the type's. Since R1b, `impl[T…] Trait for")
    strs_push(l, " * D[T…]` implements it for every instance of a generic record or enum. *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example trait Size { fn size(self: Self) -> Int; } struct P { x: Int, } impl Size for P { fn size(self: P) -> Int { 1 } } fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example trait Size { fn size(self: Self) -> Int; } struct W[T] { v: T, } impl[T] Size for W[T] { fn size(self: W[T]) -> Int { 1 } } fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "impl_item = \"impl\" , [ type_parameters ] , type , IDENT , type , \"{\" , { function } , \"}\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example use \"lib/helpers.nz\"; fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* `as NAME` imports the module under a name (N49): its exports are written `NAME::item`")
    strs_push(l, " * and are not brought into scope. `as` is a word here and nowhere else. See `docs/user/spec.md`,")
    strs_push(l, " * *Qualified names*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example use \"other.nz\" as other; fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* `pub use` re-exports (N103): every name the module offers, or the names in braces, each")
    strs_push(l, " * optionally offered under another name with the word `as`. A re-export is also an ordinary")
    strs_push(l, " * import, and is never under a name: `pub use \"PATH\" as m;` is refused. See `docs/user/spec.md`,")
    strs_push(l, " * *`pub use` offers another module's definitions*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example pub use \"shapes.nz\"; fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example pub use \"shapes.nz\" { double, Sq as Square }; fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "use_item = \"use\" , ( STRING | standard_path ) , [ IDENT , IDENT ] , \";\"")
    strs_push(l, "         | visibility , \"use\" , STRING , [ \"{\" , [ reexport_name , { \",\" , reexport_name } , [ \",\" ] ] , \"}\" ] , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* A standard module by its dotted path (R1.5, D7): `use std.json;` is `use \"@std/json\";`. *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example use std.hash; use std.hashmap; fn main() -> Int { hashmap_len(hashmap_single(\"a\", 1)) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "standard_path = \"std\" , \".\" , IDENT , { \".\" , IDENT } ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example pub use \"shapes.nz\" { Sq as Square }; fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "reexport_name = IDENT , [ IDENT , IDENT ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* `NAME ::` before the name of a definition: a function, a record, an enum. Nazm has no")
    strs_push(l, " * module-level values, so a qualified name is never a variable.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example use \"geometry.nz\" as g; fn main() -> Int { g::area(g::Point(x: 1, y: 2)) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example use \"shapes.nz\" as s; fn f(x: s::Shape) -> Int { match x { s::Shape.Dot() => 0, } } fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "qualifier = IDENT , \"::\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn add(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int { a + b } fn main() -> Int { add(1, 2) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example pub fn add(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int { a + b } fn main() -> Int { add(1, 2) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn first[A, B](a: A, b: B) -> A { a } fn main() -> Int { first(1, \"x\") } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn add(a: Int, b: Int): Int { a + b } fn main(): Int { add(1, 2) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn double(n: Int): Int = n * 2 fn add(a: Int, b: Int) = a + b fn main() -> Int { add(double(1), 2) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "function = [ visibility ] , \"fn\" , IDENT , [ type_parameters ] , \"(\" , [ parameters ] , \")\" ,")
    strs_push(l, "           [ result ] , [ effect_set ] , { contract } , ( block | expression_body ) ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* An expression body (R1.5, D2): the function's value is the expression. Written with no result")
    strs_push(l, "   type, the result type is the expression's — not for a `pub` function, a method, or one whose")
    strs_push(l, "   body reaches itself (`N0634`). *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn double(n: Int): Int = n * 2 fn main() -> Int { double(21) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "expression_body = \"=\" , expression , [ \";\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* A result type is written after `:` (R1.5, D1), as a parameter's is; `->` is still read until")
    strs_push(l, "   1.0. A function that writes none returns nothing (R1, 5b.2). *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn add(a: Int, b: Int): Int { a + b } fn main() -> Int { add(1, 2) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "result = ( \":\" | \"->\" ) , type ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* A contract clause (N87): `requires` is checked as the function is entered, `ensures` as it")
    strs_push(l, " * returns, on every path, with `result` the value returned. Both are IDENTs recognised only")
    strs_push(l, " * here, between the signature and the body; every `requires` comes before every `ensures`. A")
    strs_push(l, " * clause is a `Bool` of literals, names, operators, field reads and calls of pure functions.")
    strs_push(l, " * See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Contracts*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn half(n: Int) -> Int ! {} requires n >= 0 ensures result * 2 <= n { n / 2 } fn main() -> Int { half(8) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "contract = ( \"requires\" | \"ensures\" ) , expression ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* A foreign function (N42): a C function this program calls, declared by its signature and")
    strs_push(l, " * its C symbol, with no body. `extern` is not a keyword — it is recognised only where a")
    strs_push(l, " * declaration starts, before a string — so it is an IDENT here, and the string before `fn`")
    strs_push(l, " * is the ABI, which must be `\"C\"`. Only `Int` and `Bool` cross; no type parameters and no")
    strs_push(l, " * written effect set: calling one is always the effect `foreign`, and needs a `ForeignCap`.")
    strs_push(l, " * `nazm run --interpret` refuses a program that calls one; `nazm run` calls one from the system's libraries and `nazm build --link FILE` links any. See")
    strs_push(l, " * `docs/user/spec.md`, *Foreign functions*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example extern \"C\" fn c_add(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int = \"c_add\"; fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example pub extern \"C\" fn is_even(n: Int) -> Bool = \"c_is_even\"; fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "foreign_function = [ visibility ] , IDENT , STRING , \"fn\" , IDENT , \"(\" , [ parameters ] , \")\" ,")
    strs_push(l, "                   result , \"=\" , STRING , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* The effects a function declares it may exercise: after the return type, a `!` and a")
    strs_push(l, " * set in braces. `! {}` is the empty set — the function is pure, and its body may call")
    strs_push(l, " * nothing that is not. With no set written the checker infers one from the body, and")
    strs_push(l, " * another module calling the function must assume every effect — so `fn f() -> Int` and")
    strs_push(l, " * `fn f() -> Int ! {}` are not the same: only the second promises purity. A declared set")
    strs_push(l, " * says what a function does, not what allows it: its body holds only the authority of")
    strs_push(l, " * the capability values in its scope (`IoCap`, `SpawnCap`). The names live in their")
    strs_push(l, " * own namespace: `io`, `spawn` and `foreign` are the only effects, a name that is not one is refused,")
    strs_push(l, " * and so is one written twice. Order means nothing. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Effects*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn show(io: IoCap, s: Str) -> Int ! { io } { print(s) } fn main(io: IoCap) -> Int { show(io, \"hi\") } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn add(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int ! {} { a + b } fn main() -> Int { add(1, 2) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn w(c: Chan) -> Int { 0 } fn run(t: SpawnCap) -> Int ! { spawn } { let c = chan_new(1); scope { spawn w(c); } 0 } fn main(t: SpawnCap) -> Int { run(t) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "effect_set = \"!\" , \"{\" , [ effect_name , { \",\" , effect_name } ] , \"}\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* `spawn` is a keyword, and the effect of starting a task is named by it. *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn w(c: Chan) -> Int { 0 } fn run(io: IoCap, t: SpawnCap) -> Int ! { io, spawn } { let c = chan_new(1); scope { spawn w(c); } print(\"done\") } fn main(io: IoCap, t: SpawnCap) -> Int { run(io, t) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "effect_name = IDENT | \"spawn\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* A generic declaration's parameters: at least one, no trailing comma. A parameter")
    strs_push(l, " * is a **position** — renaming one changes nothing — and it is a type and nothing else.")
    strs_push(l, " * Which names may be one (not a built-in type, not `Vec`, not twice) is the checker's")
    strs_push(l, " * question. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Generics*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example struct Pair[A, B] { first: A, second: B, } fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum Maybe[T] { None, Some(value: T), } fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "type_parameters = \"[\" , type_parameter , { \",\" , type_parameter } , \"]\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* `effects E` declares the function's effect parameter (N51): `effects` is a word only")
    strs_push(l, " * here, before a name. At most one, only on a function that declares its effect set, and")
    strs_push(l, " * never on a record or an enum (`N0388`); its name may then be written in the function's")
    strs_push(l, " * effect sets. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Effect parameters and captured authority*.")
    strs_push(l, " *")
    strs_push(l, " * A parameter may require a capability of every type it stands for: one name after a")
    strs_push(l, " * `:`, and no list: `Equality`, which gives the parameter `==`, or a trait (N78), which")
    strs_push(l, " * gives it the trait's methods. Only a function's parameter may require one. `Equality` is")
    strs_push(l, " * not a type and nothing declares it. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *A type parameter may require")
    strs_push(l, " * equality* and *Traits and methods*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn same[T: Equality](a: T, b: T) -> Bool { a == b } fn main() -> Int { if same(1, 1) { 1 } else { 0 } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn apply[effects E](f: fn() -> Int ! { E }) -> Int ! { E } { f() } fn main() -> Int { apply(fn() -> Int { 1 }) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "type_parameter = IDENT , [ \":\" , IDENT ] | \"effects\" , IDENT ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* One bit, and one spelling for it. Absent means private to this module; `pub` exports")
    strs_push(l, " * it to the modules that directly import this one. There is no `private` keyword,")
    strs_push(l, " * because the default needs no word, and no package or friend visibility: a package offers")
    strs_push(l, " * what its modules export, and nothing sits between. See `docs/user/spec.md`.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example pub fn helper() -> Int { 1 } fn main() -> Int { helper() } *)")
    strs_push(l, "visibility = \"pub\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* A record: a nominal type whose fields are named. `struct` is the keyword; *record* is")
    strs_push(l, " * what the semantics call the category. One concept, one spelling in each place — see")
    strs_push(l, " * `docs/user/spec.md`, *Records*.")
    strs_push(l, " *")
    strs_push(l, " * Declaration order is written down and means nothing: construction names every field,")
    strs_push(l, " * and reordering two fields changes neither the type, nor its interface fingerprint, nor")
    strs_push(l, " * its native layout.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example struct Point { x: Int, y: Int, } fn main() -> Int { Point(x: 1, y: 2).x } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example pub struct User { name: Str, } fn main() -> Int { str_len(User(name: \"a\").name) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example struct Box[T] { value: T, } fn main() -> Int { Box[Int](value: 1).value } *)")
    strs_push(l, "record = [ visibility ] , \"struct\" , IDENT , [ type_parameters ] , \"{\" , [ fields ] , \"}\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* A struct C sees (N85): `extern \"C\" struct Name;` is an opaque handle — a C pointer only a")
    strs_push(l, " * foreign function returns, never built, read or compared — and `extern \"C\" struct Name { … }`")
    strs_push(l, " * a record laid out as C's struct, its fields in the order written, which here is meaning.")
    strs_push(l, " * `extern` is an IDENT recognised before a string, as for a foreign function. See `docs/user/spec.md`,")
    strs_push(l, " * *Foreign functions v3*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example extern \"C\" struct Db; fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example extern \"C\" struct Point { x: Int, flag: Bool, y: Int } fn main() -> Int { Point(x: 1, flag: true, y: 2).y } *)")
    strs_push(l, "foreign_struct = [ visibility ] , IDENT , STRING , \"struct\" , IDENT , ( \";\" | \"{\" , [ fields ] , \"}\" ) ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example struct P { x: Int, y: Int, } fn main() -> Int { P(x: 1, y: 2).y } *)")
    strs_push(l, "fields = field , { \",\" , field } , [ \",\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example struct P { x: Int, } fn main() -> Int { P(x: 7).x } *)")
    strs_push(l, "field = IDENT , \":\" , type ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* An enum: a closed set of named variants, exactly one of which is active in any value.")
    strs_push(l, " * `enum` is the keyword and *enum* is what the semantics call the category — unlike")
    strs_push(l, " * `struct`/record there is no second word, because none was needed.")
    strs_push(l, " *")
    strs_push(l, " * Variant order is written down and means nothing: the discriminant is derived from the")
    strs_push(l, " * names, so reordering two variants changes neither the type, nor its interface")
    strs_push(l, " * fingerprint, nor its native representation. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Enums*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum State { Ready, Done, } fn main() -> Int { match State.Ready() { State.Ready() => 1, State.Done() => 0, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example pub enum E { V(x: Int), } fn main() -> Int { match E.V(x: 1) { E.V(x: n) => n, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum Maybe[T] { None, Some(value: T), } fn main() -> Int { match Maybe[Int].Some(value: 1) { Maybe.None() => 0, Maybe.Some(value: v) => v, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "enumeration = [ visibility ] , \"enum\" , IDENT , [ type_parameters ] , \"{\" , [ variants ] , \"}\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum E { A, B, } fn main() -> Int { match E.A() { E.A() => 1, E.B() => 0, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "variants = variant , { \",\" , variant } , [ \",\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* A variant with no payload is written with **no parentheses**: there is no field list,")
    strs_push(l, " * exactly as a record with no fields has none. Construction and patterns always write")
    strs_push(l, " * them, because there the parentheses are what separates a variant from a projection.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum E { A, } fn main() -> Int { match E.A() { E.A() => 0, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum E { V(x: Int, y: Int), } fn main() -> Int { match E.V(x: 1, y: 2) { E.V(x: a, y: b) => a + b, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "variant = IDENT , [ \"(\" , payload , \")\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum E { V(x: Int,), } fn main() -> Int { match E.V(x: 1) { E.V(x: n) => n, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "payload = field , { \",\" , field } , [ \",\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn f(a: Int, b: Str) -> Int { str_len(b) + a } fn main() -> Int { f(1, \"x\") } *)")
    strs_push(l, "parameters = parameter , { \",\" , parameter } ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn f(n: Int) -> Int { n } fn main() -> Int { f(1) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "parameter = IDENT , \":\" , type ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* A name, applied to type arguments or not. Which names are types — `Int`, `Bool`,")
    strs_push(l, " * `Str`, `Ints`, `Strs`, `Chan` (and `Chan[T]`, N53), the seven capabilities (`IoCap`, `OutCap`, `SpawnCap`, `ForeignCap`, `VouchCap`, `TimeCap`, `MmioCap`), `Vec`, a")
    strs_push(l, " * declared record or enum, a type parameter in scope — is a *checking* question, not a grammatical one: the parser accepts any")
    strs_push(l, " * identifier here and the checker reports `N0305` for one that is not a type. A grammar")
    strs_push(l, " * that listed them would be claiming the parser rejects `fn f(x: Widget)`, which it does")
    strs_push(l, " * not — it parses it and then says what is wrong with it, which is how one mistake stays")
    strs_push(l, " * one error. How many arguments a name takes is the checker's too (`N0351` – `N0353`).")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn f(c: Chan) -> Int { 0 } fn main() -> Int { f(chan_new(1)) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn f(c: Chan[Str]) -> Bool { chan_send_of(c, \"hi\") } fn main() -> Int { if f(chan_new_of[Str](1)) { 0 } else { 1 } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn f(xs: Vec[Vec[Int]]) -> Int { vec_len(xs) } fn main() -> Int { f(vec_new[Vec[Int]]()) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn say(io: IoCap, s: Str) -> Int ! { io } { print(s) } fn main(io: IoCap) -> Int { say(io, \"hi\") } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn f(xs: [Int; 4]) -> Int { xs[0] } fn main() -> Int { f([1, 2, 3, 4]) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "type = function_type | array_type | tuple_type | [ qualifier ] , IDENT , [ type_arguments ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* R1a: a tuple type, two to eight elements; `(T)` is `T`, parenthesised, and `(T,)` or a ninth")
    strs_push(l, " * element is refused (`N0101`). See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Tuples*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn f(p: (Int, Str)) -> (Str, Int) { (p.1, p.0) } fn main() -> Int { f((1, \"a\")).1 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "tuple_type = \"(\" , type , \",\" , type , { \",\" , type } , [ \",\" ] , \")\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* A fixed-size array type (Gate 2): its element type and its length, an integer literal or a")
    strs_push(l, " * constant's name. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Arrays*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example const N: Int = 3; fn f(xs: [UInt8; N]) -> Int { Int(xs[2]) } fn main() -> Int { f([UInt8(1), 2, 3]) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "array_type = \"[\" , type , \";\" , ( INTEGER | IDENT ) , \"]\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* A function type (N50): its parameters' types, its result's, and the effects a call")
    strs_push(l, " * performs — none when unwritten. Structural: two are one type exactly when all three are")
    strs_push(l, " * equal. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Function values and closures*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn twice(f: fn(Int) -> Int, x: Int) -> Int { f(f(x)) } fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn run(c: IoCap, f: fn(IoCap) -> Int ! { io }) -> Int ! { io } { f(c) } fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "function_type = \"fn\" , \"(\" , [ type , { \",\" , type } ] , \")\" , result , [ effect_set ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* Square brackets, and one spelling: there are no angle brackets and no indexing, so")
    strs_push(l, " * `name[` can only begin type arguments. Empty brackets parse — `Vec[]` is a type written")
    strs_push(l, " * with the wrong number of arguments, which is `N0353` rather than a syntax error.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example struct Pair[A, B] { a: A, b: B, } fn f(p: Pair[Int, Str]) -> Int { p.a } fn main() -> Int { f(Pair[Int, Str](a: 1, b: \"x\")) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "type_arguments = \"[\" , [ type , { \",\" , type } ] , \"]\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let a = 1; a } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { 1 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "block = \"{\" , { statement } , [ expression ] , \"}\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let a = 1; a } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* R1, 5b.19: a statement's closing \";\" may be left out where a line break or its block's")
    strs_push(l, "   \"}\" follows it; see spec.md, \"else if, and a line break for ;\". *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let mut n = 0; while n < 5 { n = n + 1; if n == 3 { break } } n } *)")
    strs_push(l, "statement = let_statement")
    strs_push(l, "          | assignment")
    strs_push(l, "          | while_statement")
    strs_push(l, "          | for_statement")
    strs_push(l, "          | let_else_statement")
    strs_push(l, "          | return_statement")
    strs_push(l, "          | break_statement")
    strs_push(l, "          | continue_statement")
    strs_push(l, "          | scope_statement")
    strs_push(l, "          | defer_statement")
    strs_push(l, "          | spawn_statement")
    strs_push(l, "          | expression_statement ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let a = 1; a } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let mut a = 1; a = 2; a } *)")
    strs_push(l, "let_statement = \"let\" , [ \"mut\" ] , IDENT , \"=\" , expression , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* R1a: `let P = e else { … };` — the `else` must leave; `P`'s names are in scope after it.")
    strs_push(l, " * Without `else` (L5), `P` must match every value (`N0343`): `let (a, b) = pair;`.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn f(o: Option[Int]) -> Int { let Option.Some(value: x) = o else { return 0; }; x } fn main() -> Int { f(Option[Int].Some(value: 2)) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let (a, _) = (1, \"b\"); a } *)")
    strs_push(l, "let_else_statement = \"let\" , pattern , \"=\" , expression , [ \"else\" , block ] , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* The left-hand side is a **place**: a binding, then a path of fields through it.")
    strs_push(l, " * Mutability is checked at the binding, so `p.x = 2` needs `let mut p` — see")
    strs_push(l, " * `docs/user/spec.md`, *Binding mutability reaches every field*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let mut a = 1; a = 2; a } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example struct P { x: Int, } fn main() -> Int { let mut p = P(x: 1); p.x = 2; p.x } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* R1, 5b.12: `place op= e` is `place = place op e`; an index in the place is a name or a number. *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let mut n = 1; n += 2; n *= 3; n <<= 1; n } *)")
    strs_push(l, "assignment = place , ( \"=\" | compound_operator ) , expression , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let mut n = 100; n -= 1; n /= 3; n %= 7; n &= 6; n |= 1; n ^= 2; n >>= 1; n } *)")
    strs_push(l, "compound_operator = \"+=\" | \"-=\" | \"*=\" | \"/=\" | \"%=\" | \"&=\" | \"|=\" | \"^=\" | \"<<=\" | \">>=\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example struct I { n: Int, } struct O { i: I, } fn main() -> Int { let mut o = O(i: I(n: 1)); o.i.n = 2; o.i.n } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let mut g = [[0; 2]; 2]; g[1][0] = 5; g[1][0] } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let mut t = ((1, 2), 3); t.0.1 = 5; t.0.1 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "place = IDENT , { \".\" , ( IDENT | INTEGER ) | \"[\" , expression , \"]\" } ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let mut i = 0; while i < 3 { i = i + 1; } i } *)")
    strs_push(l, "while_statement = \"while\" , expression , block ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* R1a. `in` is a word only here; `..` only between a range's bounds. Each form means the")
    strs_push(l, " * `while` loop `docs/user/spec.md` (*`for` loops*) gives for it. *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let xs = ints_new(); ints_push(xs, 2); let mut t = 0; for x in xs { t = t + x; } for i in 0..3 { t = t + i; } t } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let ps = vec_new[(Int, Int)](); vec_push(ps, (2, 3)); let mut t = 0; for (a, b) in ps { t = t + a * b; } t } *)")
    strs_push(l, "for_statement = \"for\" , ( IDENT | tuple_pattern ) , \"in\" , ( expression , \"..\" , expression | expression ) , block ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn f() -> Int { return 1; } fn main() -> Int { f() } *)")
    strs_push(l, "return_statement = \"return\" , expression , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let mut i = 0; while true { break; } i } *)")
    strs_push(l, "break_statement = \"break\" , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let mut i = 0; while i < 3 { i = i + 1; continue; } i } *)")
    strs_push(l, "continue_statement = \"continue\" , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn w(c: Chan) -> Int { 0 } fn main(t: SpawnCap) -> Int { let c = chan_new(1); scope { spawn w(c); } 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "scope_statement = \"scope\" , block ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* R1b: a block run when the enclosing block is left — at its end, or by `return`, `?`,")
    strs_push(l, " * `break` or `continue` — the last registered first. `defer` is a word only here, before")
    strs_push(l, " * `{`. Its body leaves nothing: no value, and no `return`, `?`, `break` or `continue` out of")
    strs_push(l, " * it (`N0631`). *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let mut n = 0; { defer { n = n + 1; } n = 10; } n } *)")
    strs_push(l, "defer_statement = \"defer\" , block ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn w(c: Chan, n: Int) -> Int { 0 } fn main(t: SpawnCap) -> Int { let c = chan_new(1); scope { spawn w(c, 1); } 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "spawn_statement = \"spawn\" , IDENT , \"(\" , [ arguments ] , \")\" , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main(out: OutCap) -> Int { print(\"hi\"); 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "expression_statement = expression , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { 1 + 2 * 3 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "expression = disjunction ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* `||` and `&&` (N49): `Bool` operands, left-associative, and short-circuit — the right")
    strs_push(l, " * operand is evaluated only when the left does not decide. `||` binds loosest. Each is the")
    strs_push(l, " * `if` it lowers to; see `docs/user/spec.md`, *Logical operators*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { if 1 < 2 || 2 < 1 { 1 } else { 0 } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "disjunction = conjunction , { \"||\" , conjunction } ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { if 1 < 2 && 2 < 3 { 1 } else { 0 } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "conjunction = comparison , { \"&&\" , comparison } ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* Each operator gets an example. Listing six and demonstrating one would be a grammar")
    strs_push(l, " * that is right about the alternatives and silent about five of them, which the")
    strs_push(l, " * examples exist to prevent.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { if 1 < 2 { 1 } else { 0 } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { if 1 == 1 { 1 } else { 0 } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { if 1 != 2 { 1 } else { 0 } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { if 1 <= 2 { 1 } else { 0 } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { if 2 > 1 { 1 } else { 0 } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { if 2 >= 2 { 1 } else { 0 } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "comparison = bit_or , { ( \"==\" | \"!=\" | \"<\" | \"<=\" | \">\" | \">=\" ) , bit_or } ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* The bit operators (Gate 2): two integers of one type, or for a shift an integer and an")
    strs_push(l, " * `Int` amount. They bind tighter than comparison — `a & m == 0` is `(a & m) == 0`, not C's")
    strs_push(l, " * reading — and looser than arithmetic. See `docs/internal/general-purpose.md` §3.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { 6 | 1 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "bit_or = bit_xor , { \"|\" , bit_xor } ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { 6 ^ 3 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "bit_xor = bit_and , { \"^\" , bit_and } ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { 6 & 3 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "bit_and = shift , { \"&\" , shift } ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { 1 << 4 >> 2 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "shift = sum , { ( \"<<\" | \">>\" ) , sum } ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { 1 + 2 - 3 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "sum = product , { ( \"+\" | \"-\" ) , product } ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { 2 * 3 / 4 % 5 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "product = unary , { ( \"*\" | \"/\" | \"%\" ) , unary } ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* `!` is logical negation, as tight as `-`: `!a && b` is `(!a) && b`. It is never the `!` of")
    strs_push(l, " * an effect set, which follows a result type, where no expression is.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* `~` is the bit complement of an integer (Gate 2). *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { -1 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { if !false { 1 } else { 0 } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { ~0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "unary = [ \"-\" | \"!\" | \"~\" ] , primary ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { (1 + 2) * 3 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { if true { 1 } else { 0 } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { if false { 1 } else { 0 } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { str_len(\"a name\") } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example struct P { x: Int, } fn main() -> Int { P(x: 1).x } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* `?` is a postfix beside projection, in any order and any number: `r?`, `make()?.x`,")
    strs_push(l, " * `r??`. It binds tighter than negation, so `-r?` is `-(r?)`. Whether the operand is a")
    strs_push(l, " * `Result` — and the core prelude's one — is the checker's question, not the grammar's.")
    strs_push(l, " * See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Propagation*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn f(r: Result[Int, Str]) -> Result[Int, Str] { Result[Int, Str].Ok(value: r? + 1) } fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example struct P { x: Int, } fn f(r: Result[P, Str]) -> Result[Int, Str] { Result[Int, Str].Ok(value: -r?.x) } fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* `.name(…)` after an operand is a method call (N78): `p.show()`, `make().size()`. With a")
    strs_push(l, " * trait's name as the operand, `Show.show(p)`, the trait chooses the method and the first")
    strs_push(l, " * argument is the receiver. *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example trait Size { fn size(self: Self) -> Int; } fn f[T: Size](x: T) -> Int { x.size() + Size.size(x) } fn main() -> Int { 0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* `[index]` after an operand reads an array's element (Gate 2): `xs[i]`, `grid[r][c]`,")
    strs_push(l, " * `points[i].x`. After a name, a `[` followed by types and then `(` is type arguments instead,")
    strs_push(l, " * as it always was: `vec_new[Int]()`; a method call on an element is written `(xs[i]).m()`.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* `.0` after an operand is a tuple's element (R1a, L5); `t.0.1` is two of them.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let xs = [1, 2, 3]; xs[1] } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let t = ((1, 2), 3); t.0.1 + t.1 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "primary = atom , { \".\" , ( IDENT , [ \"(\" , [ arguments ] , \")\" ] | INTEGER ) | \"?\" | \"[\" , expression , \"]\" } ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* A `FLOAT` is digits, `.` and digits, and/or an exponent: `1.5`, `2e9` (Gate 2). An")
    strs_push(l, " * `INTEGER` may be written `0x`, `0o` or `0b`, with `_` between digits.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* A `STRING` is an ordinary literal, or since R1a a raw one — `r\"…\"`, `r#\"…\"#` — or a multi-line")
    strs_push(l, " * one between `\"\"\"` lines (`docs/user/spec.md`, *Multi-line and raw strings*): one token class, as the")
    strs_push(l, " * lexer reads them.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { 1 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { Int(2.5e1) + 0xff + 0b1_0 + 0o7 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { str_len(r#\"say \"hi\"\"#) + str_len(r\"C:\\path\") } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* An `FSTRING` (R1a, L4) is `f\"…\"` or `f\"\"\"…\"\"\"` whose `{expr}` and `{expr:spec}` holes are")
    strs_push(l, " * expressions (`docs/user/spec.md`, *String interpolation*).")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let n = 4; str_len(f\"n = {n:>3}, half = {Float64(n) / 2.0:.1}\") } *)")
    strs_push(l, "atom = INTEGER")
    strs_push(l, "     | FLOAT")
    strs_push(l, "     | STRING")
    strs_push(l, "     | FSTRING")
    strs_push(l, "     | \"true\"")
    strs_push(l, "     | \"false\"")
    strs_push(l, "     | IDENT")
    strs_push(l, "     | qualifier , IDENT")
    strs_push(l, "     | call")
    strs_push(l, "     | construction")
    strs_push(l, "     | variant_construction")
    strs_push(l, "     | if_expression")
    strs_push(l, "     | if_let_expression")
    strs_push(l, "     | match_expression")
    strs_push(l, "     | closure")
    strs_push(l, "     | short_closure")
    strs_push(l, "     | map_literal")
    strs_push(l, "     | array")
    strs_push(l, "     | tuple")
    strs_push(l, "     | \"(\" , expression , \")\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* R1a: a tuple, two to eight elements (`docs/user/spec.md`, *Tuples*). *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let t = (1, \"two\", true); t.0 } *)")
    strs_push(l, "tuple = \"(\" , expression , \",\" , expression , { \",\" , expression } , [ \",\" ] , \")\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* An array (Gate 2): its elements, or one value and a count. *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let a = [1, 2, 3]; let b = [0; 4]; a[2] + b[3] } *)")
    strs_push(l, "array = \"[\" , expression , ( { \",\" , expression } , [ \",\" ] | \";\" , expression ) , \"]\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* A closure (N50): a function written where a value is, its parameters and result in")
    strs_push(l, " * full, its effects declared or none. Its body may name the bindings around it, each")
    strs_push(l, " * copied in when the closure is made; a `let mut` binding is shared instead (R1b), unless")
    strs_push(l, " * it can hold a function value (`N0386`). A capability may be (N51): the closure holds")
    strs_push(l, " * it, and its type says what it does. One may be written in a generic function (R1b).")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let k = 2; let f = fn(x: Int) -> Int { x * k }; f(3) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "closure = \"fn\" , \"(\" , [ parameters ] , \")\" , result , [ effect_set ] , block ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* A short closure (R1.5, D3): its unwritten types are the function type's expected where it is")
    strs_push(l, "   written, its result type its body's; with nothing expected, a parameter writes its type")
    strs_push(l, "   (`N0635`). `||` at the start of an expression is a closure with no parameters. *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn twice(f: fn(Int) -> Int, x: Int) -> Int { f(f(x)) } fn main() -> Int { twice(|x| x * 3, 2) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let inc = |n: Int| n + 1; let z = || 0; inc(z()) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "short_closure = ( \"||\" | \"|\" , [ short_parameter , { \",\" , short_parameter } ] , \"|\" ) ,")
    strs_push(l, "                ( block | expression ) ;")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let add = |a: Int, b: Int| a + b; add(1, 2) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "short_parameter = IDENT , [ \":\" , type ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* A map literal (R1.5, D5): its first key a literal or a name, so `{` and that key and `:` tell")
    strs_push(l, "   it from a block. It builds `@std/hashmap`'s `HashMap`, which must be in scope. *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example use \"@std/hash\"; use \"@std/hashmap\"; fn main() -> Int { let m = {\"a\": 1, \"b\": 2}; hashmap_len(m) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "map_literal = \"{\" , map_entry , { \",\" , map_entry } , [ \",\" ] , \"}\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example use \"@std/hash\"; use \"@std/hashmap\"; fn main() -> Int { let k = \"b\"; let m = {\"a\": 1, k: 2}; hashmap_len(m) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "map_entry = expression , \":\" , expression ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* Type arguments are written where inference cannot find them from the arguments —")
    strs_push(l, " * `vec_new[Int]()` — or where a reader wants them visible. The expected result type")
    strs_push(l, " * never supplies one.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { str_len(\"abc\") } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn identity[T](v: T) -> T { v } fn main() -> Int { identity[Int](7) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "call = [ qualifier ] , IDENT , [ type_arguments ] , \"(\" , [ arguments ] , \")\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* Named, never positional, so field order is never an implicit API. Parenthesised rather")
    strs_push(l, " * than `Point { x: 1 }` because `IDENT \"{\"` is exactly what an `if` whose condition is a")
    strs_push(l, " * bare name looks like, and no amount of parser lookahead makes that a decision rather")
    strs_push(l, " * than a guess. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Why construction is parenthesised*.")
    strs_push(l, " *")
    strs_push(l, " * Told apart from `call` by two tokens: `IDENT \"(\" IDENT \":\"`. No argument expression can")
    strs_push(l, " * begin with a name followed by a colon, so the two forms cannot be confused.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example struct P { x: Int, y: Int, } fn main() -> Int { P(x: 1, y: 2).x } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example struct Box[T] { value: T, } fn main() -> Int { Box[Int](value: 7).value } *)")
    strs_push(l, "construction = [ qualifier ] , IDENT , [ type_arguments ] , \"(\" , initialisers , \")\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example struct P { x: Int, } fn main() -> Int { P(x: 1,).x } *)")
    strs_push(l, "initialisers = initialiser , { \",\" , initialiser } , [ \",\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example struct P { x: Int, } fn main() -> Int { P(x: 1 + 1).x } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* A field may be given by position (R1.5, D4): every field of the record or variant, in the")
    strs_push(l, "   order declared, none named — `Point(1, 2)`, `Shape.Rect(3, 4)`. *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example struct P { x: Int, y: Int, } fn main() -> Int { P(1, 2).y } *)")
    strs_push(l, "initialiser = IDENT , \":\" , expression | expression ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* Always qualified by the enum, and always parenthesised — including for a variant with")
    strs_push(l, " * no payload, because `E.V` alone is exactly the shape of a field projection. Told apart")
    strs_push(l, " * from one by three tokens, `IDENT \".\" IDENT \"(\"`. Since N78 a method call has that shape")
    strs_push(l, " * too: `x.m(…)` with an unlabelled argument is always a call, and `x.m()` is a call when the")
    strs_push(l, " * checker finds `x` names a value rather than an enum — an enum keeps every meaning it had.")
    strs_push(l, " * See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Variants are named by their enum* and *Traits and methods*.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum E { A, } fn main() -> Int { match E.A() { E.A() => 0, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum E { V(x: Int), } fn main() -> Int { match E.V(x: 1 + 1) { E.V(x: n) => n, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum Maybe[T] { None, Some(value: T), } fn main() -> Int { match Maybe[Int].None() { Maybe.None() => 0, Maybe.Some(value: v) => v, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "variant_construction = [ qualifier ] , IDENT , [ type_arguments ] , \".\" , IDENT , \"(\" , [ initialisers ] , \")\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { ints_set(ints_new(), 0, 1) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "arguments = expression , { \",\" , expression } ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { if true { 1 } else { 2 } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let mut n = 0; if true { n = 1; } n } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* R1, 5b.11: \"else if\" is \"else { if … }\". *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { let n = 50; if n < 10 { 1 } else if n < 100 { 2 } else { 3 } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "if_expression = \"if\" , expression , block , [ \"else\" , ( block | if_expression | if_let_expression ) ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* R1a: `if let P = e { … } else { … }` means `match e { P => …, _ => … }`. *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { if let 3 = 3 { 1 } else { 0 } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { if let 3 = 4 { 1 } else if true { 2 } else { 0 } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "if_let_expression = \"if\" , \"let\" , pattern , \"=\" , expression , block , [ \"else\" , ( block | if_expression | if_let_expression ) ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* The one elimination form for an enum. An expression, so it composes wherever one may")
    strs_push(l, " * appear, and its arms reuse the existing block and completion rules rather than")
    strs_push(l, " * introducing a second set.")
    strs_push(l, " *")
    strs_push(l, " * Every value is matched by some arm and no arm is unreachable (`docs/user/spec.md`, *Patterns*).")
    strs_push(l, " * Since R1a an arm's pattern may be `_`, a name, a literal or several alternatives; a `match`")
    strs_push(l, " * written variant by variant still breaks when a variant is added, as *Exhaustiveness* says.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum E { A, B(x: Int), } fn main() -> Int { match E.A() { E.A() => 1, E.B(x: n) => n, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum E { A(text: Str), } fn main() -> Int { match E.A(text: \"hi\") { E.A(text: s) => { let n = str_len(s); n }, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "match_expression = \"match\" , expression , \"{\" , [ match_arms ] , \"}\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum E { A, B, } fn main() -> Int { match E.A() { E.A() => 1, E.B() => 0, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* R1.5, 4.6: the \",\" between two arms may be left out where a line break follows the first, as")
    strs_push(l, "   a statement's \";\" may (5b.19); see spec.md, \"Shorter forms\". *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { match 2 { 1 => 10, _ => 0 } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "match_arms = match_arm , { \",\" , match_arm } , [ \",\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* A pattern names the enum and never its type arguments: the value being matched already")
    strs_push(l, " * has one concrete type, and `Maybe.Some(value: v)` matches a `Maybe[Int]` and a")
    strs_push(l, " * `Maybe[Str]` alike.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum E { V(x: Int), } fn main() -> Int { match E.V(x: 1) { E.V(x: n) => n, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* R1, 5b.17: a guard after the pattern; the arm is chosen only where it is true. *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { match 7 { n if n < 0 => 0, n if n % 2 == 1 => 1, _ => 2, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "match_arm = pattern , [ \"if\" , expression ] , \"=>\" , expression ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* R1a: a pattern is one alternative or several separated by `|`. *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { match 2 { 0 => 10, 1 | 2 => 20, n => n, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "pattern = pattern_one , { \"|\" , pattern_one } ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* `_`, a name, a literal (an integer, perhaps negated, a string, `true` or `false`), or a")
    strs_push(l, " * variant pattern.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum E { A, B(x: Int), } fn main() -> Int { match E.B(x: 3) { E.B(x: 3) => 1, E.B(x: _) => 2, _ => 0, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "pattern_one = \"_\" | IDENT | [ \"-\" ] , INT | STRING | \"true\" | \"false\" | variant_pattern | tuple_pattern ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* R1a: a tuple pattern, as many elements as the tuple; `(p)` is `p`, parenthesised. *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { match (1, true) { (0, _) => 0, (n, true) => n, (_, false) => 2, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "tuple_pattern = \"(\" , pattern , \",\" , pattern , { \",\" , pattern } , [ \",\" ] , \")\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum E { V(x: Int, y: Bool), } fn main() -> Int { match E.V(x: 1, y: true) { E.V(x: 1, y: _) => 1, E.V(x: n, y: _) => n, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* R1, 5b.14: a variant with no payload needs no `()`; `Some(p)`, `Ok(p)`, `Err(p)` and `None` name the")
    strs_push(l, "   prelude's variants. *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum C { R, G, } fn main() -> Int { match C.G { C.R => 1, C.G => 2, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example fn main() -> Int { match Some(3) { Some(n) => n, None => 0, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* A capitalised name alone (R1.5, D4) is a variant of the value's own enum, written without it:")
    strs_push(l, "   `Circle(r)`, `Dot`. *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum S { C(r: Int), D, } fn area(s: S) -> Int { match s { C(r) => r, D => 0, } } fn main() -> Int { area(S.C(r: 2)) } *)")
    strs_push(l, "variant_pattern = [ qualifier ] , IDENT , \".\" , IDENT , [ \"(\" , [ pattern_fields ] , \")\" ]")
    strs_push(l, "                | IDENT , [ \"(\" , [ pattern_fields ] , \")\" ]")
    strs_push(l, "                | ( \"Some\" | \"Ok\" | \"Err\" ) , \"(\" , pattern , \")\"")
    strs_push(l, "                | \"None\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum E { V(x: Int, y: Int), } fn main() -> Int { match E.V(x: 1, y: 2) { E.V(x: a, y: _) => a, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "pattern_fields = pattern_field , { \",\" , pattern_field } , [ \",\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "(* A payload field matches a pattern — a name binds it, `_` discards it. `_` declines to name")
    strs_push(l, " * the value; it does not mean the field is absent and does not mean it is not released.")
    strs_push(l, " *)")
    strs_push(l, "(* @example enum E { V(x: Int), } fn main() -> Int { match E.V(x: 1) { E.V(x: _) => 0, } } *)")
    strs_push(l, "pattern_field = IDENT , \":\" , pattern | pattern ;")
    str_join(l, str_from_byte(10)) + str_from_byte(10)
}

fn dd_doc10() -> Str {
    let l = strs_new()
    strs_push(l, "# The Nazm language guide")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm is small on purpose. This page is what a person — or an agent — needs to write a")
    strs_push(l, "program in it, and nothing more; `docs/user/spec.md` says what each construct *means* and why,")
    strs_push(l, "and is the document to read when two implementations could differ.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## A whole program")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn max(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int {")
    strs_push(l, "    if a > b { a } else { b }")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int {")
    strs_push(l, "    let x = 17;")
    strs_push(l, "    let y = 25;")
    strs_push(l, "    max(x, y)")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm run` compiles and runs `main` (`--interpret` evaluates it instead). `nazm build`")
    strs_push(l, "compiles the same program to a native executable that does the same. `nazm check` type-checks without")
    strs_push(l, "running anything, and `nazm test` runs a directory of programs against recorded outputs")
    strs_push(l, "— interpreted and compiled, requiring both to agree.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm build` has two code generators. The default, `--backend llvm`, writes LLVM IR as text and")
    strs_push(l, "has clang compile it; `--backend cranelift` compiles every function in process with Cranelift,")
    strs_push(l, "which built the compiler's own source at `-O0` in 0.74 s against LLVM's 1.21 s on the measured host")
    strs_push(l, "(`docs/internal/performance-log.md`, N41). They produce programs that behave identically — the same output,")
    strs_push(l, "the same failures, the same memory report — and neither ever stands in for the other: a program")
    strs_push(l, "one cannot compile is refused, never quietly built by the other. `--target` names the target")
    strs_push(l, "triple: one of nine (`docs/user/support.md`), built to an executable where this host can link it and to")
    strs_push(l, "objects with `--objects` elsewhere; an unknown triple is refused rather than built for this one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A native program can call C. `extern \"C\" fn c_add(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int = \"c_add\";` declares a")
    strs_push(l, "C function by its signature and its symbol, and `nazm build --link add.o` hands the object that")
    strs_push(l, "defines it to the linker. Only `Int` (`int64_t`) and `Bool` (`bool`) cross; every call needs a")
    strs_push(l, "`ForeignCap` in scope and is the effect `foreign`. `nazm run` compiles, so it calls C from the")
    strs_push(l, "system's libraries (since R1.5, D11); `nazm run --interpret` refuses such a program rather than")
    strs_push(l, "pretend to run C. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Foreign functions*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### Writing a program the way v1 prefers")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Declare what each function does and hand it the authority it needs, rather than relying on a")
    strs_push(l, "caller's: `fn save(io: IoCap, path: Str, data: Str) -> Int ! { io } { write_file(path, data) }`.")
    strs_push(l, "A function that declares `! {}` is pure, and a profile such as `critical` or `cyber` refuses any")
    strs_push(l, "function that declares nothing. Reach for the standard library before writing helpers —")
    strs_push(l, "`@std/text` gives `text_split`, `text_trim` and `text_parse_int`, which returns a `Result`")
    strs_push(l, "rather than failing; in your own program `@std/text`, `@std/hashmap`, `@std/hash`, `@std/ordmap`,")
    strs_push(l, "`@std/sort`, `@std/option` and `@std/result` need no `use` — naming one of their functions, or calling `s.split(\" \")`,")
    strs_push(l, "`counts.top(10)` or `r.unwrap_or(0)`, is enough (R1.5, D9, 4.5) — while a package's modules write theirs. A program that grows past one directory becomes a package: a `nazm.toml`")
    strs_push(l, "beside `src/`, dependencies as `use \"NAME:path.nz\";`, and `nazm lock` before a `--locked` build.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm build --debug` makes a program a debugger can stop in, `nazm build --release` a hardened macOS")
    strs_push(l, "executable (stack-protected, PIE, stripped, signed with the hardened runtime), `nazm build --timings` says where a")
    strs_push(l, "build's time went, and `nazm inspect` prints everything the compiler knows about a program.")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/limitations.md` lists what v1 does not do.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## The shape of the language, in six sentences")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **A file is a module.** `use \"other.nz\";` makes the definitions that file marked `pub`")
    strs_push(l, "  nameable here. Everything else in it stays private to it, and what *it* imports does not")
    strs_push(l, "  come with it.")
    strs_push(l, "- **`fn main() -> Int` is the entry point**, and every function writes its parameter and")
    strs_push(l, "  return types — there is no inference across a function boundary. `main` may take")
    strs_push(l, "  capabilities, `fn main(io: IoCap) -> Int`, and nothing else.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Bindings are immutable** unless written `let mut`, and a parameter is never mutable.")
    strs_push(l, "- **A block's last expression, with no `;`, is its value.** That is how `if` produces one.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Arithmetic is checked.** Overflow, division by zero and `Int::MIN / -1` fail with a")
    strs_push(l, "  diagnostic rather than wrapping or trapping silently; `Int::MIN % -1` is `0`.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Tasks are scoped.** `spawn f(args);` only appears inside `scope { … }`, and that block")
    strs_push(l, "  does not finish until every task started in it has.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## The types")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Int` | A 64-bit signed integer. Every operation on one is checked |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Bool` | `true` or `false`. Not a number, and not convertible to one |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Str` | Immutable **bytes**, by value. Not text: `str_len` counts bytes, and an embedded zero is an ordinary byte |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Ints` | A growable sequence of `Int`, **by reference** |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Strs` | The same, of `Str` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Chan` | A bounded queue of `Int`, by reference. The one type designed to be shared between tasks |")
    strs_push(l, "| a `struct` you declare | A **record**: a value with named fields, each keeping its own type's rules |")
    strs_push(l, "| an `enum` you declare | One of a fixed set of named **variants**, each with its own named fields |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Vec[T]` | A growable sequence of **any** type — records, enums, strings, other `Vec`s — by reference |")
    strs_push(l, "| `List[T]` | The same type as `Vec[T]`, under the name taught since R1.5 (D7): `List[Int]` is `Vec[Int]`, which is `Ints`. R1a's immutable sequence, which held the name before, is `Chain[T]` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `IoCap`, `OutCap`, `SpawnCap` | **Capabilities**: authority to reach the outside world, only its standard streams, and to start a task. Only `main` receives them; nothing constructs one, and an `IoCap` is accepted where an `OutCap` is expected. Four more — `ForeignCap`, `VouchCap`, `TimeCap`, `MmioCap` — authorise calling C, vouching for a string, reading the clock and device registers (`docs/user/spec.md`, *The capabilities*) |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`Ints`, `Strs`, `Vec[T]` and `Chan` are handles: two bindings of one sequence are the same storage,")
    strs_push(l, "and `==` is not offered on them, because it would have to mean either identity or")
    strs_push(l, "contents and the language has not chosen. A sequence may **not** be passed to a task; a")
    strs_push(l, "channel may, and its operations are the synchronisation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Records")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "pub struct Point {")
    strs_push(l, "    x: Int,")
    strs_push(l, "    label: Str,")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int {")
    strs_push(l, "    let mut p = Point(x: 1, label: \"here\");")
    strs_push(l, "    p.x = 41;")
    strs_push(l, "    p.x + str_len(p.label)")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Six things to know, and then you know records:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **Every field is named when you build one.** There is no positional form, no default")
    strs_push(l, "  value and no partial record. A field you forget is an error that names it.")
    strs_push(l, "- **A record is a value.** `let q = p;` gives you another record. Changing `q.x` does not")
    strs_push(l, "  change `p.x` — and if a field is an `Ints`, both records still point at the *same*")
    strs_push(l, "  sequence, because that is what an `Ints` is. Each field keeps its own rules; the record")
    strs_push(l, "  does not override them.")
    strs_push(l, "- **`p.x = 2` needs `let mut p`**, at any depth: `a.inner.count = 3` asks permission of")
    strs_push(l, "  `a`. Replacing part of what a binding holds is changing the binding.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Reading a field gives you a value you can keep.** `let s = make().label;` is valid")
    strs_push(l, "  after the record `make()` returned is gone.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Records are nominal.** Two records with the same fields are two types, and there is no")
    strs_push(l, "  conversion between them. A record and a function may share a name.")
    strs_push(l, "- **`a == b` compares fields**, when every field's type has equality — see *Equality*")
    strs_push(l, "  below. A record holding an `Ints` cannot be compared: that field would have to mean the")
    strs_push(l, "  same storage or the same contents.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Field order is presentation. Moving two field declarations changes nothing at all — not")
    strs_push(l, "the type, not what constructs it, not the compiled program. Construction is by name.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Whether a record can be passed to a task is **worked out from its fields**: one made of")
    strs_push(l, "`Int`, `Str` and `Chan` can, one holding an `Ints` anywhere inside it cannot, and the error")
    strs_push(l, "tells you which field decided it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A record cannot contain itself, directly or in a circle. That is refused as a layout with")
    strs_push(l, "no size rather than as a safety problem — there is nowhere for such a value to fit.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Enums, and `match`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A record has all of its fields at once. An enum has **one of its variants** at a time.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "pub enum State {")
    strs_push(l, "    Ready,")
    strs_push(l, "    Done(code: Int),")
    strs_push(l, "    Failed(why: Str, code: Int),")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "fn describe(s: State) -> Int {")
    strs_push(l, "    match s {")
    strs_push(l, "        State.Ready() => 0,")
    strs_push(l, "        State.Done(code: c) => c,")
    strs_push(l, "        State.Failed(why: w, code: c) => str_len(w) + c,")
    strs_push(l, "    }")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int {")
    strs_push(l, "    describe(State.Failed(why: \"disk\", code: 5))")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An arm that ends its line needs no `,` before the next, as a statement needs no `;` (R1.5, 4.6):")
    strs_push(l, "`Circle(r) => 3 * r * r` and `Dot => 0` on two lines are two arms. Two arms on one line still")
    strs_push(l, "take the `,`, and `nazm fmt` keeps whichever was written.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Six things to know, and then you know enums:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **A variant is always written with its enum, and always with brackets.** `State.Ready()`,")
    strs_push(l, "  not `Ready` and not `State.Ready`. That is why two enums may both have a `Ready`, and why")
    strs_push(l, "  importing a module brings in no new bare names.")
    strs_push(l, "- **`match` is the only way to get at a payload.** There is no `s.code`: which fields a")
    strs_push(l, "  value has depends on which variant it is, so the question only has an answer inside an")
    strs_push(l, "  arm that has established one.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Every variant gets exactly one arm.** Leave one out and the compiler names it; write")
    strs_push(l, "  one twice and it says so. There is no `_ => …` arm — deliberately, so that when somebody")
    strs_push(l, "  adds a variant, every `match` that thought it had handled the whole enum is told.")
    strs_push(l, "- **A pattern names every payload field**, binding it or discarding it with `_`. Same")
    strs_push(l, "  reason: add a field and the old patterns stop compiling instead of quietly ignoring it.")
    strs_push(l, "  `_` only declines to *name* the value — it is still there and still cleaned up.")
    strs_push(l, "- **A binding is a borrowed view that lives in its arm.** You can return it, store it or")
    strs_push(l, "  pass it on, and it stays valid after the value you matched is gone. If it names an `Ints`,")
    strs_push(l, "  you can still push to the sequence: the binding is immutable, the storage is not.")
    strs_push(l, "- **`a == b` compares the variant and then its payload**, when every payload field of")
    strs_push(l, "  every variant has equality — see *Equality* below.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Variant order and payload-field order are presentation, exactly as a record's field order")
    strs_push(l, "is. Moving two of either changes nothing at all.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Whether an enum can be passed to a task is worked out from **every** variant, not the one")
    strs_push(l, "it happens to hold: `enum Work { None, Values(xs: Ints), }` may not cross even while it is")
    strs_push(l, "`None`, because what a task is given is a value of a type.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An enum and a record can contain one another, and an enum can contain an enum. What is")
    strs_push(l, "refused is a circle — the same layout-with-no-size refusal a record gets.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Generics, and `Vec[T]`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A record, an enum or a function may take **type parameters**, written in square brackets")
    strs_push(l, "after its name, and a type is applied to arguments the same way.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "struct Pair[A, B] {")
    strs_push(l, "    first: A,")
    strs_push(l, "    second: B,")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "enum Maybe[T] {")
    strs_push(l, "    None,")
    strs_push(l, "    Some(value: T),")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "fn or_else[T](m: Maybe[T], fallback: T) -> T {")
    strs_push(l, "    match m {")
    strs_push(l, "        Maybe.None() => fallback,")
    strs_push(l, "        Maybe.Some(value: v) => v,")
    strs_push(l, "    }")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int {")
    strs_push(l, "    let pairs = vec_new[Pair[Int, Str]]();")
    strs_push(l, "    vec_push(pairs, Pair[Int, Str](first: 7, second: \"nazm\"));")
    strs_push(l, "    let p = vec_get(pairs, 0);")
    strs_push(l, "    p.first + or_else(Maybe[Int].Some(value: 35), 0)")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Six things to know, and then you know generics:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **A generic function is checked once, for every `T` at once.** So its body can only do")
    strs_push(l, "  what every type can: bind a `T`, pass it, return it, store it, push it into a `Vec[T]`.")
    strs_push(l, "  It cannot add two `T`s, read a field of one or pass one to a task. What a bound grants is")
    strs_push(l, "  the exception: `T: Equality` gives `==` (see *Equality*), and `T: Trait` gives that trait's")
    strs_push(l, "  methods (N78, `docs/user/spec.md` *Traits and methods*). Nothing can say \"`T` may be passed to a")
    strs_push(l, "  task\".")
    strs_push(l, "- **A call's type arguments come from its arguments, or you write them.** `or_else(m, 0)`")
    strs_push(l, "  works out `T` from `m`; `vec_new[Int]()` has no argument to work it out from, so it is")
    strs_push(l, "  written. What the result is *used for* never decides it.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Building a generic value names its arguments.** `Pair[Int, Str](first: …)` and")
    strs_push(l, "  `Maybe[Int].None()`, never `Pair(…)`. A **pattern** is the other way round —")
    strs_push(l, "  `Maybe.Some(value: v)` — because the value being matched already has one type.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Parameter order means something; parameter names do not.** `Pair[B, A]` is a different")
    strs_push(l, "  definition from `Pair[A, B]`, and renaming `T` to `Value` everywhere changes nothing at all.")
    strs_push(l, "- **`Vec[T]` is a sequence, like `Ints`.** `let b = a;` shares it, and `==` is not offered.")
    strs_push(l, "  `vec_get(xs, i)` gives you **your own copy** of an element; `vec_set(xs, i, v)` replaces")
    strs_push(l, "  one; `vec_push` appends and `vec_pop` removes the last. There is no `xs[i]` — to change a")
    strs_push(l, "  field of a record in a `Vec`, get it, change the copy, and set it back.")
    strs_push(l, "- **A type cannot own itself through a `Vec`.** `struct Node { children: Vec[Node], }` is")
    strs_push(l, "  refused: a value of it could hold itself, and nothing would ever reclaim it. `Vec[Vec[Int]]`")
    strs_push(l, "  and a record holding a `Vec[Str]` are fine — the refusal is only for a circle.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A `Vec` may not be passed to a task, whatever it holds, for the reason an `Ints` may not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Equality")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`==` and `!=` take two values of **one** type. `Int`, `Bool` and `Str` compare as they always")
    strs_push(l, "have — a `Str` by its bytes. For your own types equality is worked out from what they")
    strs_push(l, "contain; there is nothing to declare:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **A record** can be compared when every field's type can, and two records are equal when")
    strs_push(l, "  every field is. It compares values, never identity: two records built separately with")
    strs_push(l, "  equal fields are equal.")
    strs_push(l, "- **An enum** can be compared when every payload field of **every** variant can — decided")
    strs_push(l, "  for the whole type, not for the variant a value happens to hold. Different variants are")
    strs_push(l, "  unequal and their payloads are not looked at; the same variant compares its own payload")
    strs_push(l, "  and nothing else.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Two types of one shape** are still two types and cannot be compared.")
    strs_push(l, "- **A generic type** is answered after its arguments are filled in: `Box[Int]` compares,")
    strs_push(l, "  `Box[Vec[Int]]` does not. `Option[T]` and `Result[T, E]` are ordinary enums and follow the")
    strs_push(l, "  same rule.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Not comparable:** `Vec[T]`, `Ints`, `Strs` and `Chan`, anything that contains one, and an")
    strs_push(l, "  unconstrained `T` inside a generic function — `fn same[T](a: T, b: T) -> Bool { a == b }`")
    strs_push(l, "  is refused, because `T` might be any of those. Declaring the requirement is the way out.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A generic function that needs `==` on `T` **says so** where `T` is declared:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn same[T: Equality](a: T, b: T) -> Bool { a == b }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Inside it `T` can be compared, and so can `Box[T]` or `Option[T]`. Every caller must pass a")
    strs_push(l, "type that has equality — `same(1, 2)`, `same(Point(…), Point(…))` and `same(Box[Int](…), …)`")
    strs_push(l, "are fine, `same(v, v)` for a `Vec[Int]` is refused, and so is an `Option[Vec[Int]]` even when")
    strs_push(l, "it holds `None`. A generic caller can pass its own `T` on only if its `T` says")
    strs_push(l, "`: Equality` too. `Equality` is the one built-in requirement — a trait is the other kind — it adds nothing at run time —")
    strs_push(l, "the compiled `same` at `Int` is the same code as one written for `Int` — and it is not a way")
    strs_push(l, "to define your own `==`: what `==` means is still worked out from the type.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/spec.md`, *Equality is derived* and *A type parameter may require equality*, have the")
    strs_push(l, "full rules.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Errors as values: `Result`, `Option`, and `?`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Something that can fail says so in its return type. `Result[T, E]` is either a success")
    strs_push(l, "holding a `T` or a failure holding an `E` — a **typed error value**, which you return, pass")
    strs_push(l, "and store like any other value. There are no exceptions: nothing is thrown, nothing is")
    strs_push(l, "caught, and nothing leaves a function unless the function returns.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "struct ParseError {")
    strs_push(l, "    at: Int,")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "fn digit(s: Str, i: Int) -> Result[Int, ParseError] {")
    strs_push(l, "    let d = str_byte(s, i) - 48;")
    strs_push(l, "    if d < 0 {")
    strs_push(l, "        return Result[Int, ParseError].Err(error: ParseError(at: i));")
    strs_push(l, "    }")
    strs_push(l, "    if d > 9 {")
    strs_push(l, "        return Result[Int, ParseError].Err(error: ParseError(at: i));")
    strs_push(l, "    }")
    strs_push(l, "    Result[Int, ParseError].Ok(value: d)")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "fn parse(s: Str) -> Result[Int, ParseError] {")
    strs_push(l, "    let mut i = 0;")
    strs_push(l, "    let mut n = 0;")
    strs_push(l, "    while i < str_len(s) {")
    strs_push(l, "        n = n * 10 + digit(s, i)?;")
    strs_push(l, "        i = i + 1;")
    strs_push(l, "    }")
    strs_push(l, "    Result[Int, ParseError].Ok(value: n)")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int {")
    strs_push(l, "    match parse(\"4x2\") {")
    strs_push(l, "        Result.Ok(value: n) => n,")
    strs_push(l, "        Result.Err(error: e) => 100 + e.at,")
    strs_push(l, "    }")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "That prints `101`. Three separate things are going on, and each is worth knowing on its own:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **`Result` is an ordinary enum.** It and `Option` are declared by the **core prelude**,")
    strs_push(l, "  which every module sees without a `use`, so you build one as you build any generic enum —")
    strs_push(l, "  `Result[Int, ParseError].Ok(value: d)` — and you cannot declare your own type called")
    strs_push(l, "  `Result` or `Option`.")
    strs_push(l, "- **`match` handles one explicitly.** `main` above looks at both variants and decides what")
    strs_push(l, "  each means. That is always available, and it is how `main` handles errors: `main` still")
    strs_push(l, "  returns `Int`.")
    strs_push(l, "- **`?` passes a failure on.** `digit(s, i)?` is the digit when `digit` succeeded; when it")
    strs_push(l, "  failed, `parse` returns that same error at once, in its own `Result`. The rule is exact:")
    strs_push(l, "  `?` works on the core `Result` only, in a function that itself returns a `Result`, and")
    strs_push(l, "  the two **error types must be the same type** — `?` never converts one error into")
    strs_push(l, "  another. The success types may differ: `?` gives you the value, and only the error")
    strs_push(l, "  leaves.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "When `?` leaves, it leaves the way `return` does: anything later in the same expression is")
    strs_push(l, "not evaluated, every `scope` in between is joined, and everything the function was holding")
    strs_push(l, "is released. The error value arrives intact.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**`Option[T]`** is `None` or `Some(value: T)`, for a value that may be absent — there is no")
    strs_push(l, "null. In this version `?` does not work on an `Option`; take it apart with `match`:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn first_or(xs: Vec[Int], fallback: Int) -> Int {")
    strs_push(l, "    let o = if vec_len(xs) > 0 { Option[Int].Some(value: vec_get(xs, 0)) } else { Option[Int].None() };")
    strs_push(l, "    match o {")
    strs_push(l, "        Option.None() => fallback,")
    strs_push(l, "        Option.Some(value: n) => n,")
    strs_push(l, "    }")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The prelude gives neither an impl. `@std/option` and `@std/result` offer functions —")
    strs_push(l, "`option_unwrap_or`, `result_ok` and the like — which read as methods by name, `o.unwrap_or(0)`,")
    strs_push(l, "`r.ok()`, and in your own program need no `use` (R1.5, 4.5); there is no `map` on either. Runtime failures such as an index")
    strs_push(l, "out of bounds are still runtime failures, not `Err` values.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Effects and capabilities")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A function may say what it does — `! { io }` reaches the outside world, `! { spawn }` starts")
    strs_push(l, "tasks, `! {}` does neither — and the checker holds its body to that. Leaving the set out is")
    strs_push(l, "not the same as `! {}`: an undeclared function's effects are inferred, and to another module")
    strs_push(l, "it may do anything.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A function that declares a set must also **hold the authority** for what it does: an")
    strs_push(l, "`IoCap` to call `print`, `read_file` and the other outside-world built-ins, a `SpawnCap` to")
    strs_push(l, "`spawn`. Authority is a value. `main` is handed it, and passes it to what needs it:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn log(io: IoCap, n: Int) -> Int ! { io } {")
    strs_push(l, "    print(int_to_str(n));")
    strs_push(l, "    print(str_from_byte(10))")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "fn double(n: Int) -> Int ! {} { n * 2 }")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "fn main(io: IoCap) -> Int ! { io } {")
    strs_push(l, "    log(io, double(21));")
    strs_push(l, "    0")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Declaring `! { io }` without holding an `IoCap` is refused, and so is holding one while")
    strs_push(l, "declaring `! {}` — two different mistakes, two different errors. A function holds what")
    strs_push(l, "it uses, whether it declares a set or not: one that prints and is given nothing is refused, so")
    strs_push(l, "authority is threaded from `main`'s parameters to every function that needs it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Hand a function less than everything: an `OutCap` authorises `print` and `eprint` and nothing")
    strs_push(l, "else, and an `IoCap` is accepted wherever one is expected —")
    strs_push(l, "`fn log(o: OutCap, n: Int) -> Int ! { io }`, called as `log(io, 42)`, cannot read or write a file. The checking")
    strs_push(l, "is static: a capability costs nothing at runtime, and it does not sandbox the program.")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/spec.md`, *Effects* and *Capabilities*, is the law.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Where values come from")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The checker records where each value's contents came from: the command line (`arg`,")
    strs_push(l, "`args_count`), a file (`read_file`, `file_exists`), `main`'s capabilities, or storage it does")
    strs_push(l, "not follow (anything read out of a sequence, a `Vec` or a channel). Computing over input keeps its")
    strs_push(l, "origin, and needs no effect:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn shout(s: Str) -> Str ! {} { str_concat(s, \"!\") }")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "fn main(io: IoCap) -> Int ! { io } {")
    strs_push(l, "    let text = read_file(\"in.txt\");")
    strs_push(l, "    write_file(arg(0), shout(text));")
    strs_push(l, "    0")
    strs_push(l, "}")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`text`, and `shout(text)`, are from a file; `shout` is still pure. A function that returns a")
    strs_push(l, "constant passes nothing on, whatever it is given.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "One flow is refused: in a function that declares its effects, the path `write_file` writes to")
    strs_push(l, "may not come from a file's contents — nor from a sequence or channel — directly or through a")
    strs_push(l, "function that writes to a path it is handed. `write_file(read_file(\"manifest\"), \"x\")` is")
    strs_push(l, "`N0372`, with the chain from the read to the write. A path from the command line, or one the")
    strs_push(l, "program built, is fine. This is explicit data flow only: a value is not tainted by the condition")
    strs_push(l, "that chose it. `docs/user/spec.md`, *Provenance*, is the law.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Memory: what you do not have to do")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Nothing.** There is no `free`, no `new`, no ownership annotation and no lifetime to")
    strs_push(l, "write. Storage is reclaimed when the last reference to it dies — a binding going out of")
    strs_push(l, "scope, a value being replaced, a sequence being released along with everything in it — and")
    strs_push(l, "it happens on every way out of a function, including the one a runtime failure takes.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Four things follow, and they are worth knowing because they are what makes the rest")
    strs_push(l, "predictable:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- **`let b = a;` shares.** For `Ints`, `Strs` and `Chan` that is visible: a push through")
    strs_push(l, "  `b` is a push through `a`. For `Str` it is not visible at all — a `Str` is immutable, so")
    strs_push(l, "  whether the bytes were shared or copied is something no program can ask.")
    strs_push(l, "- **Passing a value to a function costs nothing.** The caller keeps it; the callee borrows")
    strs_push(l, "  it and cannot keep it after it returns. A value you pass in is still yours afterwards.")
    strs_push(l, "- **A slice does not copy.** `str_slice(s, 1, 3)` points into `s`'s bytes and keeps them")
    strs_push(l, "  alive for as long as the slice lives — so a function may build a string, slice it, and")
    strs_push(l, "  return the slice.")
    strs_push(l, "- **What you put into a `Strs` stays valid**, independently of the binding it came from,")
    strs_push(l, "  and what you read back out of one stays valid even if you then overwrite the element.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`str_concat` in a loop is still quadratic in **time**, and `str_join(parts, sep)` is one")
    strs_push(l, "pass and one allocation. That is now a performance note rather than the memory warning it")
    strs_push(l, "used to be.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Finding out what a build supports")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "nazm capabilities")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "reports the types, the built-ins and the constructs this build has, read from the")
    strs_push(l, "compiler's own tables — and for each one, whether `nazm run` has it and whether")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm build` compiles it. `--json` gives the same thing under a versioned schema; see")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/diagnostics.md`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Seeing what a program became")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "nazm core-ir prog.nz")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "prints the program's Core IR — what each function became after checking, and what both")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm run` and `nazm build` start from: every value with its type, every call naming the")
    strs_push(l, "definition or built-in it reaches, every `break` and `continue` naming the loop it leaves, and")
    strs_push(l, "each `?` written out as the `match` it means. Definitions and types are named by their durable")
    strs_push(l, "keys (`main.nz::fn helper`), so the output is the same from any checkout; `--no-spans` leaves")
    strs_push(l, "out source positions, and `--json` gives one line. A program that does not check prints")
    strs_push(l, "nothing but its diagnostics. It is a view for a person asking *what did this source become*,")
    strs_push(l, "not a syntax to write or a format to depend on: `docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.41 says what its")
    strs_push(l, "version, `nazm.core-ir/3`, promises and what it does not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "nazm mir prog.nz")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "goes one level down, to what `nazm build` compiles: each concrete function — every instance of a")
    strs_push(l, "generic one included — as MIR, a graph of basic blocks in which every copy, move and drop of a")
    strs_push(l, "string, sequence, channel, record or enum is written out, every `scope` is joined on every way")
    strs_push(l, "out, and every operation that can fail names the block its failure goes to. Each function comes")
    strs_push(l, "with its executable digest, which a comment, a renamed local or an effect annotation does not")
    strs_push(l, "change. `--spans` names each statement's source position and `--json` gives one line. The same")
    strs_push(l, "promise as Core IR's: a debugging view, `nazm.mir/1`, internal and unstable")
    strs_push(l, "(`docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.42).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "nazm lir --target wasm32-unknown-unknown prog.nz")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "goes one level further, to what both native backends read before they write any code: the")
    strs_push(l, "target's data layout, every record's and enum's byte layout on that target, and which types own")
    strs_push(l, "anything, and (since N105) every unit's instructions, the one lowering both backends translate —")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.lir/2`, validated as every build validates it (`docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.82, §7.106);")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm lir --ops` prints the instructions alone, and `nazm lir --run` runs them on LIR's interpreter.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## The syntax")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "<!-- generated from docs/user/grammar.ebnf: begin -->")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Every rule below is checked against the parser by")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-syntax/tests/grammar.rs`, and every example is a program that parser")
    strs_push(l, "accepts.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Rule | Definition |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `program` | `{ use_item } , { { attribute } , ( function \\| foreign_function \\| record \\| foreign_struct \\| enumeration \\| trait_item \\| impl_item \\| constant ) }` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `attribute` | `\"@\" , IDENT , [ \"(\" , [ attribute_arg , { \",\" , attribute_arg } , [ \",\" ] ] , \")\" ]` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `attribute_arg` | `STRING \\| IDENT , [ \"=\" , STRING \\| \"(\" , [ attribute_arg , { \",\" , attribute_arg } , [ \",\" ] ] , \")\" ]` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `constant` | `[ visibility ] , ( \"const\" \\| \"static\" ) , IDENT , \":\" , type , \"=\" , expression , \";\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `trait_item` | `[ visibility ] , \"trait\" , IDENT , \"{\" , { trait_method } , \"}\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `trait_method` | `\"fn\" , IDENT , \"(\" , [ parameters ] , \")\" , result , [ effect_set ] , ( \";\" \\| block )` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `impl_item` | `\"impl\" , [ type_parameters ] , type , IDENT , type , \"{\" , { function } , \"}\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `use_item` | `\"use\" , ( STRING \\| standard_path ) , [ IDENT , IDENT ] , \";\" \\| visibility , \"use\" , STRING , [ \"{\" , [ reexport_name , { \",\" , reexport_name } , [ \",\" ] ] , \"}\" ] , \";\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `standard_path` | `\"std\" , \".\" , IDENT , { \".\" , IDENT }` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `reexport_name` | `IDENT , [ IDENT , IDENT ]` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `qualifier` | `IDENT , \"::\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `function` | `[ visibility ] , \"fn\" , IDENT , [ type_parameters ] , \"(\" , [ parameters ] , \")\" , [ result ] , [ effect_set ] , { contract } , ( block \\| expression_body )` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `expression_body` | `\"=\" , expression , [ \";\" ]` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `result` | `( \":\" \\| \"->\" ) , type` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `contract` | `( \"requires\" \\| \"ensures\" ) , expression` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `foreign_function` | `[ visibility ] , IDENT , STRING , \"fn\" , IDENT , \"(\" , [ parameters ] , \")\" , result , \"=\" , STRING , \";\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `effect_set` | `\"!\" , \"{\" , [ effect_name , { \",\" , effect_name } ] , \"}\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `effect_name` | `IDENT \\| \"spawn\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `type_parameters` | `\"[\" , type_parameter , { \",\" , type_parameter } , \"]\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `type_parameter` | `IDENT , [ \":\" , IDENT ] \\| \"effects\" , IDENT` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `visibility` | `\"pub\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `record` | `[ visibility ] , \"struct\" , IDENT , [ type_parameters ] , \"{\" , [ fields ] , \"}\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `foreign_struct` | `[ visibility ] , IDENT , STRING , \"struct\" , IDENT , ( \";\" \\| \"{\" , [ fields ] , \"}\" )` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `fields` | `field , { \",\" , field } , [ \",\" ]` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `field` | `IDENT , \":\" , type` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `enumeration` | `[ visibility ] , \"enum\" , IDENT , [ type_parameters ] , \"{\" , [ variants ] , \"}\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `variants` | `variant , { \",\" , variant } , [ \",\" ]` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `variant` | `IDENT , [ \"(\" , payload , \")\" ]` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `payload` | `field , { \",\" , field } , [ \",\" ]` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `parameters` | `parameter , { \",\" , parameter }` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `parameter` | `IDENT , \":\" , type` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `type` | `function_type \\| array_type \\| tuple_type \\| [ qualifier ] , IDENT , [ type_arguments ]` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `tuple_type` | `\"(\" , type , \",\" , type , { \",\" , type } , [ \",\" ] , \")\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `array_type` | `\"[\" , type , \";\" , ( INTEGER \\| IDENT ) , \"]\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `function_type` | `\"fn\" , \"(\" , [ type , { \",\" , type } ] , \")\" , result , [ effect_set ]` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `type_arguments` | `\"[\" , [ type , { \",\" , type } ] , \"]\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `block` | `\"{\" , { statement } , [ expression ] , \"}\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `statement` | `let_statement \\| assignment \\| while_statement \\| for_statement \\| let_else_statement \\| return_statement \\| break_statement \\| continue_statement \\| scope_statement \\| defer_statement \\| spawn_statement \\| expression_statement` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `let_statement` | `\"let\" , [ \"mut\" ] , IDENT , \"=\" , expression , \";\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `let_else_statement` | `\"let\" , pattern , \"=\" , expression , [ \"else\" , block ] , \";\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `assignment` | `place , ( \"=\" \\| compound_operator ) , expression , \";\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `compound_operator` | `\"+=\" \\| \"-=\" \\| \"*=\" \\| \"/=\" \\| \"%=\" \\| \"&=\" \\| \"\\|=\" \\| \"^=\" \\| \"<<=\" \\| \">>=\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `place` | `IDENT , { \".\" , ( IDENT \\| INTEGER ) \\| \"[\" , expression , \"]\" }` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `while_statement` | `\"while\" , expression , block` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `for_statement` | `\"for\" , ( IDENT \\| tuple_pattern ) , \"in\" , ( expression , \"..\" , expression \\| expression ) , block` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `return_statement` | `\"return\" , expression , \";\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `break_statement` | `\"break\" , \";\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `continue_statement` | `\"continue\" , \";\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `scope_statement` | `\"scope\" , block` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `defer_statement` | `\"defer\" , block` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `spawn_statement` | `\"spawn\" , IDENT , \"(\" , [ arguments ] , \")\" , \";\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `expression_statement` | `expression , \";\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `expression` | `disjunction` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `disjunction` | `conjunction , { \"\\|\\|\" , conjunction }` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `conjunction` | `comparison , { \"&&\" , comparison }` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `comparison` | `bit_or , { ( \"==\" \\| \"!=\" \\| \"<\" \\| \"<=\" \\| \">\" \\| \">=\" ) , bit_or }` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `bit_or` | `bit_xor , { \"\\|\" , bit_xor }` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `bit_xor` | `bit_and , { \"^\" , bit_and }` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `bit_and` | `shift , { \"&\" , shift }` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `shift` | `sum , { ( \"<<\" \\| \">>\" ) , sum }` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `sum` | `product , { ( \"+\" \\| \"-\" ) , product }` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `product` | `unary , { ( \"*\" \\| \"/\" \\| \"%\" ) , unary }` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `unary` | `[ \"-\" \\| \"!\" \\| \"~\" ] , primary` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `primary` | `atom , { \".\" , ( IDENT , [ \"(\" , [ arguments ] , \")\" ] \\| INTEGER ) \\| \"?\" \\| \"[\" , expression , \"]\" }` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `atom` | `INTEGER \\| FLOAT \\| STRING \\| FSTRING \\| \"true\" \\| \"false\" \\| IDENT \\| qualifier , IDENT \\| call \\| construction \\| variant_construction \\| if_expression \\| if_let_expression \\| match_expression \\| closure \\| short_closure \\| map_literal \\| array \\| tuple \\| \"(\" , expression , \")\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `tuple` | `\"(\" , expression , \",\" , expression , { \",\" , expression } , [ \",\" ] , \")\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `array` | `\"[\" , expression , ( { \",\" , expression } , [ \",\" ] \\| \";\" , expression ) , \"]\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `closure` | `\"fn\" , \"(\" , [ parameters ] , \")\" , result , [ effect_set ] , block` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `short_closure` | `( \"\\|\\|\" \\| \"\\|\" , [ short_parameter , { \",\" , short_parameter } ] , \"\\|\" ) , ( block \\| expression )` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `short_parameter` | `IDENT , [ \":\" , type ]` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `map_literal` | `\"{\" , map_entry , { \",\" , map_entry } , [ \",\" ] , \"}\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `map_entry` | `expression , \":\" , expression` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `call` | `[ qualifier ] , IDENT , [ type_arguments ] , \"(\" , [ arguments ] , \")\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `construction` | `[ qualifier ] , IDENT , [ type_arguments ] , \"(\" , initialisers , \")\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `initialisers` | `initialiser , { \",\" , initialiser } , [ \",\" ]` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `initialiser` | `IDENT , \":\" , expression \\| expression` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `variant_construction` | `[ qualifier ] , IDENT , [ type_arguments ] , \".\" , IDENT , \"(\" , [ initialisers ] , \")\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `arguments` | `expression , { \",\" , expression }` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `if_expression` | `\"if\" , expression , block , [ \"else\" , ( block \\| if_expression \\| if_let_expression ) ]` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `if_let_expression` | `\"if\" , \"let\" , pattern , \"=\" , expression , block , [ \"else\" , ( block \\| if_expression \\| if_let_expression ) ]` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `match_expression` | `\"match\" , expression , \"{\" , [ match_arms ] , \"}\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `match_arms` | `match_arm , { \",\" , match_arm } , [ \",\" ]` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `match_arm` | `pattern , [ \"if\" , expression ] , \"=>\" , expression` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `pattern` | `pattern_one , { \"\\|\" , pattern_one }` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `pattern_one` | `\"_\" \\| IDENT \\| [ \"-\" ] , INT \\| STRING \\| \"true\" \\| \"false\" \\| variant_pattern \\| tuple_pattern` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `tuple_pattern` | `\"(\" , pattern , \",\" , pattern , { \",\" , pattern } , [ \",\" ] , \")\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `variant_pattern` | `[ qualifier ] , IDENT , \".\" , IDENT , [ \"(\" , [ pattern_fields ] , \")\" ] \\| IDENT , [ \"(\" , [ pattern_fields ] , \")\" ] \\| ( \"Some\" \\| \"Ok\" \\| \"Err\" ) , \"(\" , pattern , \")\" \\| \"None\"` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `pattern_fields` | `pattern_field , { \",\" , pattern_field } , [ \",\" ]` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `pattern_field` | `IDENT , \":\" , pattern \\| pattern` |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `program`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "program = { use_item } , { { attribute } , ( function | foreign_function | record | foreign_struct | enumeration | trait_item | impl_item | constant ) } ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "use \"other.nz\"; fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "struct Point { x: Int, } fn main() -> Int { Point(x: 1).x }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum State { Ready, } fn main() -> Int { match State.Ready() { State.Ready() => 0, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn identity[T](value: T) -> T { value } fn main() -> Int { identity(7) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "trait Show { fn show(self: Self) -> Str; } impl Show for Int { fn show(self: Int) -> Str { int_to_str(self) } } fn main() -> Int { str_len(7.show()) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "const SIZE: Int = 4; fn main() -> Int { SIZE }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "@cfg(os = \"linux\") fn f() -> Int { 1 } @cfg(not(os = \"linux\")) fn f() -> Int { 0 } fn main() -> Int { f() }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `attribute`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "attribute = \"@\" , IDENT , [ \"(\" , [ attribute_arg , { \",\" , attribute_arg } , [ \",\" ] ] , \")\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An attribute (Gate 2): `@` and a name from a closed vocabulary — `cfg`, `test`, `bench`,")
    strs_push(l, "`fuzz`, `deprecated` — before a top-level declaration, never before a `use`. Which names")
    strs_push(l, "exist and what each takes is the checker's (`N0619`), not the grammar's. See")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/spec.md`, *Attributes* and *Conditional compilation*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "@test fn checks() -> Int { 0 } fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "@cfg(all(os = \"macos\", any(arch = \"aarch64\", arch = \"x86_64\"))) fn f() -> Int { 0 } fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `attribute_arg`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "attribute_arg = STRING | IDENT , [ \"=\" , STRING | \"(\" , [ attribute_arg , { \",\" , attribute_arg } , [ \",\" ] ] , \")\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "@deprecated(\"use g\") fn f() -> Int { 0 } fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "@test(fails) fn f() -> Int { 0 } fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `constant`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "constant = [ visibility ] , ( \"const\" | \"static\" ) , IDENT , \":\" , type , \"=\" , expression , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A constant (Gate 2): a value the checker computes from literals, other constants,")
    strs_push(l, "operators and numeric conversions. `const` is a word only here, before a name and a `:`,")
    strs_push(l, "so it remains an ordinary name everywhere else. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Constants*.")
    strs_push(l, "A static (Gate 3) is written the same way with `static`: storage with one address, a")
    strs_push(l, "number or a `Bool` read-only, or an `Atomic` started by `atomic_new` of a constant. `static`")
    strs_push(l, "is a word only where `const` is. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Statics*.")
    strs_push(l, "R1a (L8): a constant may be a record, enum value, tuple or array built of constant parts, and")
    strs_push(l, "`pub const` exports one; an importer under a name reads it as `m::NAME`. See `docs/user/spec.md`,")
    strs_push(l, "*Constant tables and exported constants*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "const MASK: UInt8 = 0xF0; fn main() -> Int { Int(MASK) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "static TICKS: Atomic = atomic_new(0); fn main() -> Int { atomic_add(TICKS, 1) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "struct K { s: Str, n: Int, } pub const TABLE: [K; 2] = [K(s: \"a\", n: 1), K(s: \"b\", n: 2)]; fn main() -> Int { TABLE[1].n }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `trait_item`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "trait_item = [ visibility ] , \"trait\" , IDENT , \"{\" , { trait_method } , \"}\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A trait (N78): a named set of methods a type may implement. Each method is a signature")
    strs_push(l, "ended by `;`, or since R1b a default body an impl that writes none gets, whose first")
    strs_push(l, "parameter is `self: Self`. A trait")
    strs_push(l, "is in the type namespace and is not a type: it is written as a type parameter's bound,")
    strs_push(l, "`[T: Show]`, and never as the type of a value. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Traits and methods*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "pub trait Show { fn show(self: Self) -> Str; fn shout(self: Self, n: Int) -> Str ! {}; } fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `trait_method`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "trait_method = \"fn\" , IDENT , \"(\" , [ parameters ] , \")\" , result , [ effect_set ] , ( \";\" | block ) ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "trait Size { fn size(self: Self) -> Int; } fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "trait Size { fn size(self: Self) -> Int; fn big(self: Self) -> Bool { self.size() > 9 } } fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `impl_item`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "impl_item = \"impl\" , [ type_parameters ] , type , IDENT , type , \"{\" , { function } , \"}\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`impl Trait for Type`: every method of the trait without a default body, once, with")
    strs_push(l, "`Self` written as the type. `for` is a word here and nowhere else. At most one impl of a")
    strs_push(l, "trait for a type, in the trait's module or the type's. Since R1b, `impl[T…] Trait for")
    strs_push(l, "D[T…]` implements it for every instance of a generic record or enum.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "trait Size { fn size(self: Self) -> Int; } struct P { x: Int, } impl Size for P { fn size(self: P) -> Int { 1 } } fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "trait Size { fn size(self: Self) -> Int; } struct W[T] { v: T, } impl[T] Size for W[T] { fn size(self: W[T]) -> Int { 1 } } fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `use_item`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "use_item = \"use\" , ( STRING | standard_path ) , [ IDENT , IDENT ] , \";\" | visibility , \"use\" , STRING , [ \"{\" , [ reexport_name , { \",\" , reexport_name } , [ \",\" ] ] , \"}\" ] , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`as NAME` imports the module under a name (N49): its exports are written `NAME::item`")
    strs_push(l, "and are not brought into scope. `as` is a word here and nowhere else. See `docs/user/spec.md`,")
    strs_push(l, "*Qualified names*.")
    strs_push(l, "`pub use` re-exports (N103): every name the module offers, or the names in braces, each")
    strs_push(l, "optionally offered under another name with the word `as`. A re-export is also an ordinary")
    strs_push(l, "import, and is never under a name: `pub use \"PATH\" as m;` is refused. See `docs/user/spec.md`,")
    strs_push(l, "*`pub use` offers another module's definitions*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "use \"lib/helpers.nz\"; fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "use \"other.nz\" as other; fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "pub use \"shapes.nz\"; fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "pub use \"shapes.nz\" { double, Sq as Square }; fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `standard_path`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "standard_path = \"std\" , \".\" , IDENT , { \".\" , IDENT } ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A standard module by its dotted path (R1.5, D7): `use std.json;` is `use \"@std/json\";`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "use std.hash; use std.hashmap; fn main() -> Int { hashmap_len(hashmap_single(\"a\", 1)) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `reexport_name`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "reexport_name = IDENT , [ IDENT , IDENT ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "pub use \"shapes.nz\" { Sq as Square }; fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `qualifier`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "qualifier = IDENT , \"::\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`NAME ::` before the name of a definition: a function, a record, an enum. Nazm has no")
    strs_push(l, "module-level values, so a qualified name is never a variable.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "use \"geometry.nz\" as g; fn main() -> Int { g::area(g::Point(x: 1, y: 2)) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "use \"shapes.nz\" as s; fn f(x: s::Shape) -> Int { match x { s::Shape.Dot() => 0, } } fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `function`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "function = [ visibility ] , \"fn\" , IDENT , [ type_parameters ] , \"(\" , [ parameters ] , \")\" , [ result ] , [ effect_set ] , { contract } , ( block | expression_body ) ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn add(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int { a + b } fn main() -> Int { add(1, 2) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "pub fn add(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int { a + b } fn main() -> Int { add(1, 2) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn first[A, B](a: A, b: B) -> A { a } fn main() -> Int { first(1, \"x\") }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn add(a: Int, b: Int): Int { a + b } fn main(): Int { add(1, 2) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn double(n: Int): Int = n * 2 fn add(a: Int, b: Int) = a + b fn main() -> Int { add(double(1), 2) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `expression_body`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "expression_body = \"=\" , expression , [ \";\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An expression body (R1.5, D2): the function's value is the expression. Written with no result")
    strs_push(l, "type, the result type is the expression's — not for a `pub` function, a method, or one whose")
    strs_push(l, "body reaches itself (`N0634`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn double(n: Int): Int = n * 2 fn main() -> Int { double(21) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `result`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "result = ( \":\" | \"->\" ) , type ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A result type is written after `:` (R1.5, D1), as a parameter's is; `->` is still read until")
    strs_push(l, "1.0. A function that writes none returns nothing (R1, 5b.2).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn add(a: Int, b: Int): Int { a + b } fn main() -> Int { add(1, 2) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `contract`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "contract = ( \"requires\" | \"ensures\" ) , expression ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A contract clause (N87): `requires` is checked as the function is entered, `ensures` as it")
    strs_push(l, "returns, on every path, with `result` the value returned. Both are IDENTs recognised only")
    strs_push(l, "here, between the signature and the body; every `requires` comes before every `ensures`. A")
    strs_push(l, "clause is a `Bool` of literals, names, operators, field reads and calls of pure functions.")
    strs_push(l, "See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Contracts*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn half(n: Int) -> Int ! {} requires n >= 0 ensures result * 2 <= n { n / 2 } fn main() -> Int { half(8) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `foreign_function`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "foreign_function = [ visibility ] , IDENT , STRING , \"fn\" , IDENT , \"(\" , [ parameters ] , \")\" , result , \"=\" , STRING , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A foreign function (N42): a C function this program calls, declared by its signature and")
    strs_push(l, "its C symbol, with no body. `extern` is not a keyword — it is recognised only where a")
    strs_push(l, "declaration starts, before a string — so it is an IDENT here, and the string before `fn`")
    strs_push(l, "is the ABI, which must be `\"C\"`. Only `Int` and `Bool` cross; no type parameters and no")
    strs_push(l, "written effect set: calling one is always the effect `foreign`, and needs a `ForeignCap`.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm run --interpret` refuses a program that calls one; `nazm run` calls one from the system's libraries and `nazm build --link FILE` links any. See")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/spec.md`, *Foreign functions*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "extern \"C\" fn c_add(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int = \"c_add\"; fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "pub extern \"C\" fn is_even(n: Int) -> Bool = \"c_is_even\"; fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `effect_set`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "effect_set = \"!\" , \"{\" , [ effect_name , { \",\" , effect_name } ] , \"}\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The effects a function declares it may exercise: after the return type, a `!` and a")
    strs_push(l, "set in braces. `! {}` is the empty set — the function is pure, and its body may call")
    strs_push(l, "nothing that is not. With no set written the checker infers one from the body, and")
    strs_push(l, "another module calling the function must assume every effect — so `fn f() -> Int` and")
    strs_push(l, "`fn f() -> Int ! {}` are not the same: only the second promises purity. A declared set")
    strs_push(l, "says what a function does, not what allows it: its body holds only the authority of")
    strs_push(l, "the capability values in its scope (`IoCap`, `SpawnCap`). The names live in their")
    strs_push(l, "own namespace: `io`, `spawn` and `foreign` are the only effects, a name that is not one is refused,")
    strs_push(l, "and so is one written twice. Order means nothing. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Effects*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn show(io: IoCap, s: Str) -> Int ! { io } { print(s) } fn main(io: IoCap) -> Int { show(io, \"hi\") }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn add(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int ! {} { a + b } fn main() -> Int { add(1, 2) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn w(c: Chan) -> Int { 0 } fn run(t: SpawnCap) -> Int ! { spawn } { let c = chan_new(1); scope { spawn w(c); } 0 } fn main(t: SpawnCap) -> Int { run(t) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `effect_name`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "effect_name = IDENT | \"spawn\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`spawn` is a keyword, and the effect of starting a task is named by it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn w(c: Chan) -> Int { 0 } fn run(io: IoCap, t: SpawnCap) -> Int ! { io, spawn } { let c = chan_new(1); scope { spawn w(c); } print(\"done\") } fn main(io: IoCap, t: SpawnCap) -> Int { run(io, t) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `type_parameters`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "type_parameters = \"[\" , type_parameter , { \",\" , type_parameter } , \"]\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A generic declaration's parameters: at least one, no trailing comma. A parameter")
    strs_push(l, "is a **position** — renaming one changes nothing — and it is a type and nothing else.")
    strs_push(l, "Which names may be one (not a built-in type, not `Vec`, not twice) is the checker's")
    strs_push(l, "question. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Generics*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "struct Pair[A, B] { first: A, second: B, } fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum Maybe[T] { None, Some(value: T), } fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `type_parameter`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "type_parameter = IDENT , [ \":\" , IDENT ] | \"effects\" , IDENT ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`effects E` declares the function's effect parameter (N51): `effects` is a word only")
    strs_push(l, "here, before a name. At most one, only on a function that declares its effect set, and")
    strs_push(l, "never on a record or an enum (`N0388`); its name may then be written in the function's")
    strs_push(l, "effect sets. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Effect parameters and captured authority*.")
    strs_push(l, "A parameter may require a capability of every type it stands for: one name after a")
    strs_push(l, "`:`, and no list: `Equality`, which gives the parameter `==`, or a trait (N78), which")
    strs_push(l, "gives it the trait's methods. Only a function's parameter may require one. `Equality` is")
    strs_push(l, "not a type and nothing declares it. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *A type parameter may require")
    strs_push(l, "equality* and *Traits and methods*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn same[T: Equality](a: T, b: T) -> Bool { a == b } fn main() -> Int { if same(1, 1) { 1 } else { 0 } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn apply[effects E](f: fn() -> Int ! { E }) -> Int ! { E } { f() } fn main() -> Int { apply(fn() -> Int { 1 }) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `visibility`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "visibility = \"pub\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "One bit, and one spelling for it. Absent means private to this module; `pub` exports")
    strs_push(l, "it to the modules that directly import this one. There is no `private` keyword,")
    strs_push(l, "because the default needs no word, and no package or friend visibility: a package offers")
    strs_push(l, "what its modules export, and nothing sits between. See `docs/user/spec.md`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "pub fn helper() -> Int { 1 } fn main() -> Int { helper() }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `record`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "record = [ visibility ] , \"struct\" , IDENT , [ type_parameters ] , \"{\" , [ fields ] , \"}\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A record: a nominal type whose fields are named. `struct` is the keyword; *record* is")
    strs_push(l, "what the semantics call the category. One concept, one spelling in each place — see")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/spec.md`, *Records*.")
    strs_push(l, "Declaration order is written down and means nothing: construction names every field,")
    strs_push(l, "and reordering two fields changes neither the type, nor its interface fingerprint, nor")
    strs_push(l, "its native layout.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "struct Point { x: Int, y: Int, } fn main() -> Int { Point(x: 1, y: 2).x }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "pub struct User { name: Str, } fn main() -> Int { str_len(User(name: \"a\").name) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "struct Box[T] { value: T, } fn main() -> Int { Box[Int](value: 1).value }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `foreign_struct`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "foreign_struct = [ visibility ] , IDENT , STRING , \"struct\" , IDENT , ( \";\" | \"{\" , [ fields ] , \"}\" ) ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A struct C sees (N85): `extern \"C\" struct Name;` is an opaque handle — a C pointer only a")
    strs_push(l, "foreign function returns, never built, read or compared — and `extern \"C\" struct Name { … }`")
    strs_push(l, "a record laid out as C's struct, its fields in the order written, which here is meaning.")
    strs_push(l, "`extern` is an IDENT recognised before a string, as for a foreign function. See `docs/user/spec.md`,")
    strs_push(l, "*Foreign functions v3*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "extern \"C\" struct Db; fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "extern \"C\" struct Point { x: Int, flag: Bool, y: Int } fn main() -> Int { Point(x: 1, flag: true, y: 2).y }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `fields`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "fields = field , { \",\" , field } , [ \",\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "struct P { x: Int, y: Int, } fn main() -> Int { P(x: 1, y: 2).y }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `field`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "field = IDENT , \":\" , type ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "struct P { x: Int, } fn main() -> Int { P(x: 7).x }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `enumeration`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "enumeration = [ visibility ] , \"enum\" , IDENT , [ type_parameters ] , \"{\" , [ variants ] , \"}\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An enum: a closed set of named variants, exactly one of which is active in any value.")
    strs_push(l, "`enum` is the keyword and *enum* is what the semantics call the category — unlike")
    strs_push(l, "`struct`/record there is no second word, because none was needed.")
    strs_push(l, "Variant order is written down and means nothing: the discriminant is derived from the")
    strs_push(l, "names, so reordering two variants changes neither the type, nor its interface")
    strs_push(l, "fingerprint, nor its native representation. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Enums*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum State { Ready, Done, } fn main() -> Int { match State.Ready() { State.Ready() => 1, State.Done() => 0, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "pub enum E { V(x: Int), } fn main() -> Int { match E.V(x: 1) { E.V(x: n) => n, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum Maybe[T] { None, Some(value: T), } fn main() -> Int { match Maybe[Int].Some(value: 1) { Maybe.None() => 0, Maybe.Some(value: v) => v, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `variants`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "variants = variant , { \",\" , variant } , [ \",\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum E { A, B, } fn main() -> Int { match E.A() { E.A() => 1, E.B() => 0, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `variant`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "variant = IDENT , [ \"(\" , payload , \")\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A variant with no payload is written with **no parentheses**: there is no field list,")
    strs_push(l, "exactly as a record with no fields has none. Construction and patterns always write")
    strs_push(l, "them, because there the parentheses are what separates a variant from a projection.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum E { A, } fn main() -> Int { match E.A() { E.A() => 0, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum E { V(x: Int, y: Int), } fn main() -> Int { match E.V(x: 1, y: 2) { E.V(x: a, y: b) => a + b, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `payload`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "payload = field , { \",\" , field } , [ \",\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum E { V(x: Int,), } fn main() -> Int { match E.V(x: 1) { E.V(x: n) => n, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `parameters`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "parameters = parameter , { \",\" , parameter } ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn f(a: Int, b: Str) -> Int { str_len(b) + a } fn main() -> Int { f(1, \"x\") }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `parameter`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "parameter = IDENT , \":\" , type ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn f(n: Int) -> Int { n } fn main() -> Int { f(1) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `type`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "type = function_type | array_type | tuple_type | [ qualifier ] , IDENT , [ type_arguments ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A name, applied to type arguments or not. Which names are types — `Int`, `Bool`,")
    strs_push(l, "`Str`, `Ints`, `Strs`, `Chan` (and `Chan[T]`, N53), the seven capabilities (`IoCap`, `OutCap`, `SpawnCap`, `ForeignCap`, `VouchCap`, `TimeCap`, `MmioCap`), `Vec`, a")
    strs_push(l, "declared record or enum, a type parameter in scope — is a *checking* question, not a grammatical one: the parser accepts any")
    strs_push(l, "identifier here and the checker reports `N0305` for one that is not a type. A grammar")
    strs_push(l, "that listed them would be claiming the parser rejects `fn f(x: Widget)`, which it does")
    strs_push(l, "not — it parses it and then says what is wrong with it, which is how one mistake stays")
    strs_push(l, "one error. How many arguments a name takes is the checker's too (`N0351` – `N0353`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn f(c: Chan) -> Int { 0 } fn main() -> Int { f(chan_new(1)) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn f(c: Chan[Str]) -> Bool { chan_send_of(c, \"hi\") } fn main() -> Int { if f(chan_new_of[Str](1)) { 0 } else { 1 } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn f(xs: Vec[Vec[Int]]) -> Int { vec_len(xs) } fn main() -> Int { f(vec_new[Vec[Int]]()) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn say(io: IoCap, s: Str) -> Int ! { io } { print(s) } fn main(io: IoCap) -> Int { say(io, \"hi\") }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn f(xs: [Int; 4]) -> Int { xs[0] } fn main() -> Int { f([1, 2, 3, 4]) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `tuple_type`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "tuple_type = \"(\" , type , \",\" , type , { \",\" , type } , [ \",\" ] , \")\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "R1a: a tuple type, two to eight elements; `(T)` is `T`, parenthesised, and `(T,)` or a ninth")
    strs_push(l, "element is refused (`N0101`). See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Tuples*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn f(p: (Int, Str)) -> (Str, Int) { (p.1, p.0) } fn main() -> Int { f((1, \"a\")).1 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `array_type`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "array_type = \"[\" , type , \";\" , ( INTEGER | IDENT ) , \"]\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A fixed-size array type (Gate 2): its element type and its length, an integer literal or a")
    strs_push(l, "constant's name. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Arrays*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "const N: Int = 3; fn f(xs: [UInt8; N]) -> Int { Int(xs[2]) } fn main() -> Int { f([UInt8(1), 2, 3]) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `function_type`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "function_type = \"fn\" , \"(\" , [ type , { \",\" , type } ] , \")\" , result , [ effect_set ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A function type (N50): its parameters' types, its result's, and the effects a call")
    strs_push(l, "performs — none when unwritten. Structural: two are one type exactly when all three are")
    strs_push(l, "equal. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Function values and closures*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn twice(f: fn(Int) -> Int, x: Int) -> Int { f(f(x)) } fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn run(c: IoCap, f: fn(IoCap) -> Int ! { io }) -> Int ! { io } { f(c) } fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `type_arguments`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "type_arguments = \"[\" , [ type , { \",\" , type } ] , \"]\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Square brackets, and one spelling: there are no angle brackets and no indexing, so")
    strs_push(l, "`name[` can only begin type arguments. Empty brackets parse — `Vec[]` is a type written")
    strs_push(l, "with the wrong number of arguments, which is `N0353` rather than a syntax error.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "struct Pair[A, B] { a: A, b: B, } fn f(p: Pair[Int, Str]) -> Int { p.a } fn main() -> Int { f(Pair[Int, Str](a: 1, b: \"x\")) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `block`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "block = \"{\" , { statement } , [ expression ] , \"}\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let a = 1; a }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { 1 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `statement`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "statement = let_statement | assignment | while_statement | for_statement | let_else_statement | return_statement | break_statement | continue_statement | scope_statement | defer_statement | spawn_statement | expression_statement ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "R1, 5b.19: a statement's closing \";\" may be left out where a line break or its block's")
    strs_push(l, "\"}\" follows it; see spec.md, \"else if, and a line break for ;\".")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let a = 1; a }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let mut n = 0; while n < 5 { n = n + 1; if n == 3 { break } } n }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `let_statement`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "let_statement = \"let\" , [ \"mut\" ] , IDENT , \"=\" , expression , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let a = 1; a }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let mut a = 1; a = 2; a }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `let_else_statement`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "let_else_statement = \"let\" , pattern , \"=\" , expression , [ \"else\" , block ] , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "R1a: `let P = e else { … };` — the `else` must leave; `P`'s names are in scope after it.")
    strs_push(l, "Without `else` (L5), `P` must match every value (`N0343`): `let (a, b) = pair;`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn f(o: Option[Int]) -> Int { let Option.Some(value: x) = o else { return 0; }; x } fn main() -> Int { f(Option[Int].Some(value: 2)) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let (a, _) = (1, \"b\"); a }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `assignment`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "assignment = place , ( \"=\" | compound_operator ) , expression , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The left-hand side is a **place**: a binding, then a path of fields through it.")
    strs_push(l, "Mutability is checked at the binding, so `p.x = 2` needs `let mut p` — see")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/user/spec.md`, *Binding mutability reaches every field*.")
    strs_push(l, "R1, 5b.12: `place op= e` is `place = place op e`; an index in the place is a name or a number.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let mut a = 1; a = 2; a }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "struct P { x: Int, } fn main() -> Int { let mut p = P(x: 1); p.x = 2; p.x }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let mut n = 1; n += 2; n *= 3; n <<= 1; n }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `compound_operator`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "compound_operator = \"+=\" | \"-=\" | \"*=\" | \"/=\" | \"%=\" | \"&=\" | \"|=\" | \"^=\" | \"<<=\" | \">>=\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let mut n = 100; n -= 1; n /= 3; n %= 7; n &= 6; n |= 1; n ^= 2; n >>= 1; n }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `place`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "place = IDENT , { \".\" , ( IDENT | INTEGER ) | \"[\" , expression , \"]\" } ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "struct I { n: Int, } struct O { i: I, } fn main() -> Int { let mut o = O(i: I(n: 1)); o.i.n = 2; o.i.n }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let mut g = [[0; 2]; 2]; g[1][0] = 5; g[1][0] }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let mut t = ((1, 2), 3); t.0.1 = 5; t.0.1 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `while_statement`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "while_statement = \"while\" , expression , block ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let mut i = 0; while i < 3 { i = i + 1; } i }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `for_statement`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "for_statement = \"for\" , ( IDENT | tuple_pattern ) , \"in\" , ( expression , \"..\" , expression | expression ) , block ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "R1a. `in` is a word only here; `..` only between a range's bounds. Each form means the")
    strs_push(l, "`while` loop `docs/user/spec.md` (*`for` loops*) gives for it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let xs = ints_new(); ints_push(xs, 2); let mut t = 0; for x in xs { t = t + x; } for i in 0..3 { t = t + i; } t }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let ps = vec_new[(Int, Int)](); vec_push(ps, (2, 3)); let mut t = 0; for (a, b) in ps { t = t + a * b; } t }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `return_statement`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "return_statement = \"return\" , expression , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn f() -> Int { return 1; } fn main() -> Int { f() }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `break_statement`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "break_statement = \"break\" , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let mut i = 0; while true { break; } i }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `continue_statement`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "continue_statement = \"continue\" , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let mut i = 0; while i < 3 { i = i + 1; continue; } i }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `scope_statement`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "scope_statement = \"scope\" , block ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn w(c: Chan) -> Int { 0 } fn main(t: SpawnCap) -> Int { let c = chan_new(1); scope { spawn w(c); } 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `defer_statement`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "defer_statement = \"defer\" , block ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "R1b: a block run when the enclosing block is left — at its end, or by `return`, `?`,")
    strs_push(l, "`break` or `continue` — the last registered first. `defer` is a word only here, before")
    strs_push(l, "`{`. Its body leaves nothing: no value, and no `return`, `?`, `break` or `continue` out of")
    strs_push(l, "it (`N0631`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let mut n = 0; { defer { n = n + 1; } n = 10; } n }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `spawn_statement`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "spawn_statement = \"spawn\" , IDENT , \"(\" , [ arguments ] , \")\" , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn w(c: Chan, n: Int) -> Int { 0 } fn main(t: SpawnCap) -> Int { let c = chan_new(1); scope { spawn w(c, 1); } 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `expression_statement`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "expression_statement = expression , \";\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main(out: OutCap) -> Int { print(\"hi\"); 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `expression`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "expression = disjunction ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { 1 + 2 * 3 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `disjunction`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "disjunction = conjunction , { \"||\" , conjunction } ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`||` and `&&` (N49): `Bool` operands, left-associative, and short-circuit — the right")
    strs_push(l, "operand is evaluated only when the left does not decide. `||` binds loosest. Each is the")
    strs_push(l, "`if` it lowers to; see `docs/user/spec.md`, *Logical operators*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { if 1 < 2 || 2 < 1 { 1 } else { 0 } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `conjunction`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "conjunction = comparison , { \"&&\" , comparison } ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { if 1 < 2 && 2 < 3 { 1 } else { 0 } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `comparison`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "comparison = bit_or , { ( \"==\" | \"!=\" | \"<\" | \"<=\" | \">\" | \">=\" ) , bit_or } ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Each operator gets an example. Listing six and demonstrating one would be a grammar")
    strs_push(l, "that is right about the alternatives and silent about five of them, which the")
    strs_push(l, "examples exist to prevent.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { if 1 < 2 { 1 } else { 0 } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { if 1 == 1 { 1 } else { 0 } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { if 1 != 2 { 1 } else { 0 } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { if 1 <= 2 { 1 } else { 0 } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { if 2 > 1 { 1 } else { 0 } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { if 2 >= 2 { 1 } else { 0 } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `bit_or`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "bit_or = bit_xor , { \"|\" , bit_xor } ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The bit operators (Gate 2): two integers of one type, or for a shift an integer and an")
    strs_push(l, "`Int` amount. They bind tighter than comparison — `a & m == 0` is `(a & m) == 0`, not C's")
    strs_push(l, "reading — and looser than arithmetic. See `docs/internal/general-purpose.md` §3.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { 6 | 1 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `bit_xor`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "bit_xor = bit_and , { \"^\" , bit_and } ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { 6 ^ 3 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `bit_and`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "bit_and = shift , { \"&\" , shift } ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { 6 & 3 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `shift`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "shift = sum , { ( \"<<\" | \">>\" ) , sum } ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { 1 << 4 >> 2 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `sum`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "sum = product , { ( \"+\" | \"-\" ) , product } ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { 1 + 2 - 3 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `product`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "product = unary , { ( \"*\" | \"/\" | \"%\" ) , unary } ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { 2 * 3 / 4 % 5 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `unary`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "unary = [ \"-\" | \"!\" | \"~\" ] , primary ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`!` is logical negation, as tight as `-`: `!a && b` is `(!a) && b`. It is never the `!` of")
    strs_push(l, "an effect set, which follows a result type, where no expression is.")
    strs_push(l, "`~` is the bit complement of an integer (Gate 2).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { -1 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { if !false { 1 } else { 0 } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { ~0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `primary`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "primary = atom , { \".\" , ( IDENT , [ \"(\" , [ arguments ] , \")\" ] | INTEGER ) | \"?\" | \"[\" , expression , \"]\" } ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`?` is a postfix beside projection, in any order and any number: `r?`, `make()?.x`,")
    strs_push(l, "`r??`. It binds tighter than negation, so `-r?` is `-(r?)`. Whether the operand is a")
    strs_push(l, "`Result` — and the core prelude's one — is the checker's question, not the grammar's.")
    strs_push(l, "See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Propagation*.")
    strs_push(l, "`.name(…)` after an operand is a method call (N78): `p.show()`, `make().size()`. With a")
    strs_push(l, "trait's name as the operand, `Show.show(p)`, the trait chooses the method and the first")
    strs_push(l, "argument is the receiver.")
    strs_push(l, "`[index]` after an operand reads an array's element (Gate 2): `xs[i]`, `grid[r][c]`,")
    strs_push(l, "`points[i].x`. After a name, a `[` followed by types and then `(` is type arguments instead,")
    strs_push(l, "as it always was: `vec_new[Int]()`; a method call on an element is written `(xs[i]).m()`.")
    strs_push(l, "`.0` after an operand is a tuple's element (R1a, L5); `t.0.1` is two of them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { (1 + 2) * 3 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { if true { 1 } else { 0 } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { if false { 1 } else { 0 } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { str_len(\"a name\") }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "struct P { x: Int, } fn main() -> Int { P(x: 1).x }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn f(r: Result[Int, Str]) -> Result[Int, Str] { Result[Int, Str].Ok(value: r? + 1) } fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "struct P { x: Int, } fn f(r: Result[P, Str]) -> Result[Int, Str] { Result[Int, Str].Ok(value: -r?.x) } fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "trait Size { fn size(self: Self) -> Int; } fn f[T: Size](x: T) -> Int { x.size() + Size.size(x) } fn main() -> Int { 0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let xs = [1, 2, 3]; xs[1] }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let t = ((1, 2), 3); t.0.1 + t.1 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `atom`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "atom = INTEGER | FLOAT | STRING | FSTRING | \"true\" | \"false\" | IDENT | qualifier , IDENT | call | construction | variant_construction | if_expression | if_let_expression | match_expression | closure | short_closure | map_literal | array | tuple | \"(\" , expression , \")\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A `FLOAT` is digits, `.` and digits, and/or an exponent: `1.5`, `2e9` (Gate 2). An")
    strs_push(l, "`INTEGER` may be written `0x`, `0o` or `0b`, with `_` between digits.")
    strs_push(l, "A `STRING` is an ordinary literal, or since R1a a raw one — `r\"…\"`, `r#\"…\"#` — or a multi-line")
    strs_push(l, "one between `\"\"\"` lines (`docs/user/spec.md`, *Multi-line and raw strings*): one token class, as the")
    strs_push(l, "lexer reads them.")
    strs_push(l, "An `FSTRING` (R1a, L4) is `f\"…\"` or `f\"\"\"…\"\"\"` whose `{expr}` and `{expr:spec}` holes are")
    strs_push(l, "expressions (`docs/user/spec.md`, *String interpolation*).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { 1 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { Int(2.5e1) + 0xff + 0b1_0 + 0o7 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { str_len(r#\"say \"hi\"\"#) + str_len(r\"C:\\path\") }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let n = 4; str_len(f\"n = {n:>3}, half = {Float64(n) / 2.0:.1}\") }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `tuple`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "tuple = \"(\" , expression , \",\" , expression , { \",\" , expression } , [ \",\" ] , \")\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "R1a: a tuple, two to eight elements (`docs/user/spec.md`, *Tuples*).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let t = (1, \"two\", true); t.0 }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `array`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "array = \"[\" , expression , ( { \",\" , expression } , [ \",\" ] | \";\" , expression ) , \"]\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An array (Gate 2): its elements, or one value and a count.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let a = [1, 2, 3]; let b = [0; 4]; a[2] + b[3] }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `closure`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "closure = \"fn\" , \"(\" , [ parameters ] , \")\" , result , [ effect_set ] , block ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A closure (N50): a function written where a value is, its parameters and result in")
    strs_push(l, "full, its effects declared or none. Its body may name the bindings around it, each")
    strs_push(l, "copied in when the closure is made; a `let mut` binding is shared instead (R1b), unless")
    strs_push(l, "it can hold a function value (`N0386`). A capability may be (N51): the closure holds")
    strs_push(l, "it, and its type says what it does. One may be written in a generic function (R1b).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let k = 2; let f = fn(x: Int) -> Int { x * k }; f(3) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `short_closure`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "short_closure = ( \"||\" | \"|\" , [ short_parameter , { \",\" , short_parameter } ] , \"|\" ) , ( block | expression ) ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A short closure (R1.5, D3): its unwritten types are the function type's expected where it is")
    strs_push(l, "written, its result type its body's; with nothing expected, a parameter writes its type")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0635`). `||` at the start of an expression is a closure with no parameters.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn twice(f: fn(Int) -> Int, x: Int) -> Int { f(f(x)) } fn main() -> Int { twice(|x| x * 3, 2) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let inc = |n: Int| n + 1; let z = || 0; inc(z()) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `short_parameter`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "short_parameter = IDENT , [ \":\" , type ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let add = |a: Int, b: Int| a + b; add(1, 2) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `map_literal`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "map_literal = \"{\" , map_entry , { \",\" , map_entry } , [ \",\" ] , \"}\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A map literal (R1.5, D5): its first key a literal or a name, so `{` and that key and `:` tell")
    strs_push(l, "it from a block. It builds `@std/hashmap`'s `HashMap`, which must be in scope.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "use \"@std/hash\"; use \"@std/hashmap\"; fn main() -> Int { let m = {\"a\": 1, \"b\": 2}; hashmap_len(m) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `map_entry`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "map_entry = expression , \":\" , expression ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "use \"@std/hash\"; use \"@std/hashmap\"; fn main() -> Int { let k = \"b\"; let m = {\"a\": 1, k: 2}; hashmap_len(m) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `call`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "call = [ qualifier ] , IDENT , [ type_arguments ] , \"(\" , [ arguments ] , \")\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Type arguments are written where inference cannot find them from the arguments —")
    strs_push(l, "`vec_new[Int]()` — or where a reader wants them visible. The expected result type")
    strs_push(l, "never supplies one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { str_len(\"abc\") }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn identity[T](v: T) -> T { v } fn main() -> Int { identity[Int](7) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `construction`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "construction = [ qualifier ] , IDENT , [ type_arguments ] , \"(\" , initialisers , \")\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Named, never positional, so field order is never an implicit API. Parenthesised rather")
    strs_push(l, "than `Point { x: 1 }` because `IDENT \"{\"` is exactly what an `if` whose condition is a")
    strs_push(l, "bare name looks like, and no amount of parser lookahead makes that a decision rather")
    strs_push(l, "than a guess. See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Why construction is parenthesised*.")
    strs_push(l, "Told apart from `call` by two tokens: `IDENT \"(\" IDENT \":\"`. No argument expression can")
    strs_push(l, "begin with a name followed by a colon, so the two forms cannot be confused.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "struct P { x: Int, y: Int, } fn main() -> Int { P(x: 1, y: 2).x }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "struct Box[T] { value: T, } fn main() -> Int { Box[Int](value: 7).value }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `initialisers`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "initialisers = initialiser , { \",\" , initialiser } , [ \",\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "struct P { x: Int, } fn main() -> Int { P(x: 1,).x }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `initialiser`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "initialiser = IDENT , \":\" , expression | expression ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A field may be given by position (R1.5, D4): every field of the record or variant, in the")
    strs_push(l, "order declared, none named — `Point(1, 2)`, `Shape.Rect(3, 4)`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "struct P { x: Int, } fn main() -> Int { P(x: 1 + 1).x }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "struct P { x: Int, y: Int, } fn main() -> Int { P(1, 2).y }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `variant_construction`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "variant_construction = [ qualifier ] , IDENT , [ type_arguments ] , \".\" , IDENT , \"(\" , [ initialisers ] , \")\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Always qualified by the enum, and always parenthesised — including for a variant with")
    strs_push(l, "no payload, because `E.V` alone is exactly the shape of a field projection. Told apart")
    strs_push(l, "from one by three tokens, `IDENT \".\" IDENT \"(\"`. Since N78 a method call has that shape")
    strs_push(l, "too: `x.m(…)` with an unlabelled argument is always a call, and `x.m()` is a call when the")
    strs_push(l, "checker finds `x` names a value rather than an enum — an enum keeps every meaning it had.")
    strs_push(l, "See `docs/user/spec.md`, *Variants are named by their enum* and *Traits and methods*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum E { A, } fn main() -> Int { match E.A() { E.A() => 0, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum E { V(x: Int), } fn main() -> Int { match E.V(x: 1 + 1) { E.V(x: n) => n, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum Maybe[T] { None, Some(value: T), } fn main() -> Int { match Maybe[Int].None() { Maybe.None() => 0, Maybe.Some(value: v) => v, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `arguments`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "arguments = expression , { \",\" , expression } ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { ints_set(ints_new(), 0, 1) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `if_expression`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "if_expression = \"if\" , expression , block , [ \"else\" , ( block | if_expression | if_let_expression ) ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "R1, 5b.11: \"else if\" is \"else { if … }\".")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { if true { 1 } else { 2 } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let mut n = 0; if true { n = 1; } n }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { let n = 50; if n < 10 { 1 } else if n < 100 { 2 } else { 3 } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `if_let_expression`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "if_let_expression = \"if\" , \"let\" , pattern , \"=\" , expression , block , [ \"else\" , ( block | if_expression | if_let_expression ) ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "R1a: `if let P = e { … } else { … }` means `match e { P => …, _ => … }`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { if let 3 = 3 { 1 } else { 0 } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { if let 3 = 4 { 1 } else if true { 2 } else { 0 } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `match_expression`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "match_expression = \"match\" , expression , \"{\" , [ match_arms ] , \"}\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The one elimination form for an enum. An expression, so it composes wherever one may")
    strs_push(l, "appear, and its arms reuse the existing block and completion rules rather than")
    strs_push(l, "introducing a second set.")
    strs_push(l, "Every value is matched by some arm and no arm is unreachable (`docs/user/spec.md`, *Patterns*).")
    strs_push(l, "Since R1a an arm's pattern may be `_`, a name, a literal or several alternatives; a `match`")
    strs_push(l, "written variant by variant still breaks when a variant is added, as *Exhaustiveness* says.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum E { A, B(x: Int), } fn main() -> Int { match E.A() { E.A() => 1, E.B(x: n) => n, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum E { A(text: Str), } fn main() -> Int { match E.A(text: \"hi\") { E.A(text: s) => { let n = str_len(s); n }, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `match_arms`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "match_arms = match_arm , { \",\" , match_arm } , [ \",\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "R1.5, 4.6: the \",\" between two arms may be left out where a line break follows the first, as")
    strs_push(l, "a statement's \";\" may (5b.19); see spec.md, \"Shorter forms\".")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum E { A, B, } fn main() -> Int { match E.A() { E.A() => 1, E.B() => 0, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { match 2 { 1 => 10, _ => 0 } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `match_arm`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "match_arm = pattern , [ \"if\" , expression ] , \"=>\" , expression ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A pattern names the enum and never its type arguments: the value being matched already")
    strs_push(l, "has one concrete type, and `Maybe.Some(value: v)` matches a `Maybe[Int]` and a")
    strs_push(l, "`Maybe[Str]` alike.")
    strs_push(l, "R1, 5b.17: a guard after the pattern; the arm is chosen only where it is true.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum E { V(x: Int), } fn main() -> Int { match E.V(x: 1) { E.V(x: n) => n, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { match 7 { n if n < 0 => 0, n if n % 2 == 1 => 1, _ => 2, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `pattern`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "pattern = pattern_one , { \"|\" , pattern_one } ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "R1a: a pattern is one alternative or several separated by `|`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { match 2 { 0 => 10, 1 | 2 => 20, n => n, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `pattern_one`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "pattern_one = \"_\" | IDENT | [ \"-\" ] , INT | STRING | \"true\" | \"false\" | variant_pattern | tuple_pattern ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`_`, a name, a literal (an integer, perhaps negated, a string, `true` or `false`), or a")
    strs_push(l, "variant pattern.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum E { A, B(x: Int), } fn main() -> Int { match E.B(x: 3) { E.B(x: 3) => 1, E.B(x: _) => 2, _ => 0, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `tuple_pattern`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "tuple_pattern = \"(\" , pattern , \",\" , pattern , { \",\" , pattern } , [ \",\" ] , \")\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "R1a: a tuple pattern, as many elements as the tuple; `(p)` is `p`, parenthesised.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { match (1, true) { (0, _) => 0, (n, true) => n, (_, false) => 2, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `variant_pattern`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "variant_pattern = [ qualifier ] , IDENT , \".\" , IDENT , [ \"(\" , [ pattern_fields ] , \")\" ] | IDENT , [ \"(\" , [ pattern_fields ] , \")\" ] | ( \"Some\" | \"Ok\" | \"Err\" ) , \"(\" , pattern , \")\" | \"None\" ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "R1, 5b.14: a variant with no payload needs no `()`; `Some(p)`, `Ok(p)`, `Err(p)` and `None` name the")
    strs_push(l, "prelude's variants.")
    strs_push(l, "A capitalised name alone (R1.5, D4) is a variant of the value's own enum, written without it:")
    strs_push(l, "`Circle(r)`, `Dot`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum E { V(x: Int, y: Bool), } fn main() -> Int { match E.V(x: 1, y: true) { E.V(x: 1, y: _) => 1, E.V(x: n, y: _) => n, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum C { R, G, } fn main() -> Int { match C.G { C.R => 1, C.G => 2, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "fn main() -> Int { match Some(3) { Some(n) => n, None => 0, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum S { C(r: Int), D, } fn area(s: S) -> Int { match s { C(r) => r, D => 0, } } fn main() -> Int { area(S.C(r: 2)) }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `pattern_fields`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "pattern_fields = pattern_field , { \",\" , pattern_field } , [ \",\" ] ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum E { V(x: Int, y: Int), } fn main() -> Int { match E.V(x: 1, y: 2) { E.V(x: a, y: _) => a, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `pattern_field`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```ebnf")
    strs_push(l, "pattern_field = IDENT , \":\" , pattern | pattern ;")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A payload field matches a pattern — a name binds it, `_` discards it. `_` declines to name")
    strs_push(l, "the value; it does not mean the field is absent and does not mean it is not released.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```nazm")
    strs_push(l, "enum E { V(x: Int), } fn main() -> Int { match E.V(x: 1) { E.V(x: _) => 0, } }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "<!-- generated from docs/user/grammar.ebnf: end -->")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Where to go next")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `docs/user/spec.md` | What each construct means, and the decisions behind it |")
    strs_push(l, "| `docs/user/grammar.ebnf` | The grammar this page's syntax section is generated from |")
    strs_push(l, "| `docs/user/diagnostics.md` | The machine interface: diagnostics, fixes, capabilities, exit statuses |")
    strs_push(l, "| `docs/internal/bootstrap.md` | What the self-hosting claim does and does not establish |")
    str_join(l, str_from_byte(10)) + str_from_byte(10)
}

fn dd_doc11() -> Str {
    let l = strs_new()
    strs_push(l, "# `nazm-mcp`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A read-only [Model Context Protocol](https://modelcontextprotocol.io) server over stdio, built on")
    strs_push(l, "the official Rust SDK. It offers eleven tools: the compiler's semantic context packet for a")
    strs_push(l, "definition (N27), a semantic snapshot of the root's compilation and the delta against one kept")
    strs_push(l, "earlier (N28), a planned rename or diagnostic fix (N29), the current diagnostics compactly or")
    strs_push(l, "one in full (N30), a compact summary of the root's check (N31), Nazm's own documentation by")
    strs_push(l, "section (N32), and the Nazm repository's context map and the minimum context for a task (N33).")
    strs_push(l, "It is local compiler tooling — it answers questions about one program, about the language and")
    strs_push(l, "about its repository, and changes nothing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Running it")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```sh")
    strs_push(l, "cargo build --release -p nazm-mcp")
    strs_push(l, "nazm-mcp --root path/to/root.nz            # optionally --source-root DIR, --docs REPOSITORY")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An MCP client starts it as a stdio server. A client configuration is usually a command and its")
    strs_push(l, "arguments:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "```json")
    strs_push(l, "{ \"command\": \"nazm-mcp\", \"args\": [\"--root\", \"/absolute/path/to/root.nz\"] }")
    strs_push(l, "```")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## The root")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`--root` names the compilation every answer is about: that file and everything it imports, loaded")
    strs_push(l, "exactly as `nazm check` loads it. It is fixed for the server's lifetime; a tool call cannot name")
    strs_push(l, "another. Nothing outside that compilation is read — there is no directory scan — and nothing")
    strs_push(l, "claims to know every caller or importer in a project.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## The tools")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Tool | Arguments | Result |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.semantic_context` | `file`, `byte_offset` | `nazm.context/3` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.semantic_snapshot` | none | `nazm.snapshot/3` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.semantic_delta` | `baseline`, a `nazm.snapshot/3` object | `nazm.delta/3` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.semantic_patch` | `operation` (`rename` or `diagnostic_fix`) and its fields | `nazm.patch/1` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.diagnostics` | none | `nazm.diagnostic-index/1` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.diagnostic_detail` | `id`, `state` | `nazm.diagnostic-detail/1` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.command_summary` | `operation`: `check` | `nazm.command-summary/1` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.docs_index` | optionally `document` | `nazm.docs-index/1` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.docs_section` | `id`, `state` | `nazm.docs-section/1` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.repository_map` | none | `nazm.repository-map/1` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm.task_context` | `seeds`, `state`; optionally `intent`, `max_entities`, `max_source_bytes`, `max_doc_bytes` | `nazm.task-context/1` |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Each result is carried **once**, in the tool result's structured content, with an empty `content`,")
    strs_push(l, "and each tool's output schema is the published one in `schema/`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `nazm.semantic_context`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Two arguments:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Argument | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `file` | a file of the root's compilation, relative to its source root (as packets name files) or absolute |")
    strs_push(l, "| `byte_offset` | a UTF-8 byte offset into that file |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The position must be on the declaration of a function, record or enum, or on a use of one. The")
    strs_push(l, "result is a `nazm.context/3` object (`schema/nazm.context-3.json`, `docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.29) in")
    strs_push(l, "the tool result's structured content, **once**: `content` is an empty array, not a second copy of the")
    strs_push(l, "packet as text (which the specification only suggests, and which would double every response). A position with no such definition, a file the compilation did not load, or a")
    strs_push(l, "compilation that needed syntax recovery gives an `unavailable` object and `isError: true`; a")
    strs_push(l, "malformed call (an unknown tool, a missing or mistyped argument) is a protocol error.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A packet's links are **source-linked program dependencies only**: every link has a declaration in a")
    strs_push(l, "file of the compilation. Compiler-owned, built-in, interface-only or toolchain definitions with no")
    strs_push(l, "navigable declaration — the core prelude's `Option` and `Result`, `Int` — may affect checking but are")
    strs_push(l, "omitted from the link sections.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A packet holds the target's exact source and compact links — identity, kind, name, place — to what")
    strs_push(l, "it uses, the types it names, what uses it, what it calls and what calls it, and the diagnostics")
    strs_push(l, "inside it. To follow a link, call the tool again at the linked declaration.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `nazm.semantic_snapshot` and `nazm.semantic_delta`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A snapshot (`schema/nazm.snapshot-3.json`, `docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.30) lists every durable")
    strs_push(l, "function, record and enum of the root's compilation by its definition key, with one digest per")
    strs_push(l, "section the compiler records — source, shape, dependencies, related types, references, callers,")
    strs_push(l, "callees, diagnostics. **Keep it**: the server does not. To learn what changed, pass it back as")
    strs_push(l, "`baseline` to `nazm.semantic_delta`, which derives a snapshot from the disk at that call and")
    strs_push(l, "reports definitions added, removed, and changed, naming which sections changed. A rename is a")
    strs_push(l, "removal and an addition. A comment or a changed literal is `source` alone.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N28 reports changes in the semantic surfaces Nazm currently records. It is not a proof of")
    strs_push(l, "behavioural equivalence.** Effects, capabilities and tests are unsupported, not unchanged — each")
    strs_push(l, "result lists them in `unsupported`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The baseline is data, never a path: a string such as `\"/etc/passwd\"` is not a snapshot and is")
    strs_push(l, "refused as one, and no file is read for it. A baseline of another root module or another compiler")
    strs_push(l, "version, one with a field the schema does not define, a malformed identity, a duplicate or a bad")
    strs_push(l, "digest is refused with a reason and `isError: true` — never compared as well as it can be. A")
    strs_push(l, "compilation that needed syntax recovery has no snapshot and no delta.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `nazm.semantic_patch`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**N29 plans edits but never applies them.** A patch (`schema/nazm.patch-1.json`,")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.31) is a proposal bound to exact semantic and source state, not")
    strs_push(l, "permission to change a file. Two operations:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| `operation` | Fields | Plans |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `rename` | `file`, `byte_offset`, `new_name` | the compiler's validated rename of the entity there: locals and private definitions only |")
    strs_push(l, "| `diagnostic_fix` | `file`, `byte_offset`, `fix` | fix number `fix` among those the current diagnostics at that byte carry |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The result is minimal exact-byte edits — each renamed occurrence, or the compiler's one fix span —")
    strs_push(l, "with three freshness layers: `baseline.snapshot`, BLAKE3 of the root's `nazm.snapshot/3`; each")
    strs_push(l, "file's `digest`, BLAKE3 of its bytes; and each edit's `expected` bytes. A client that applies one")
    strs_push(l, "checks all three first. A fix's `applicability` (`automatic` or `needs_review`) and `precondition`")
    strs_push(l, "are structured fields: a `needs_review` patch is never safe to apply unread. An exported")
    strs_push(l, "definition's rename is refused, because one root compilation is not every module that may import")
    strs_push(l, "it; so is a fix at a position with no current diagnostic, whatever code a client expects there,")
    strs_push(l, "and any fix of a syntax diagnostic, whose compilation has no snapshot to bind to. The input is")
    strs_push(l, "typed: no root, no unknown argument, and no client-written replacement is accepted.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `nazm.diagnostics` and `nazm.diagnostic_detail`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Progressive disclosure. `nazm.diagnostics` lists every current diagnostic of the root's")
    strs_push(l, "compilation compactly (`schema/nazm.diagnostic-index-1.json`, `docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.32): each")
    strs_push(l, "one's `id`, code, severity, file and byte range, owning definition and fix counts — none of its")
    strs_push(l, "message, help or label text. Syntax errors are included. `nazm.diagnostic_detail`, with an `id`")
    strs_push(l, "and the index's `state.source`, returns that one diagnostic exactly as `nazm.diagnostic/1`")
    strs_push(l, "publishes it, with its places in their files, and for each fix the `nazm.semantic_patch` request")
    strs_push(l, "that plans it where N29 can — a compiler fix of a syntax diagnostic has none. If the sources have")
    strs_push(l, "changed since the index, the detail is refused as `stale_state`; ask for a fresh index. No fact is")
    strs_push(l, "read from prose, and `facts` is `unavailable`: the compiler records none.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `nazm.command_summary`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "What `nazm check` concludes for the root as it is on disk now (`schema/nazm.command-summary-1.json`,")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.33): its status and exit status, and a reference to every diagnostic it")
    strs_push(l, "reports — code, place, fix counts and, where `nazm.diagnostics` indexes it, its `id` — including a")
    strs_push(l, "program's missing `main`, which the index does not hold. No prose; `nazm.diagnostic_detail` answers")
    strs_push(l, "an `id`. The only `operation` is `check`, and it runs without the check cache, so nothing is")
    strs_push(l, "written. Building writes an executable and testing runs programs that may write files, so neither")
    strs_push(l, "is offered here; `nazm build --summary-json` and `nazm test --summary-json` are the command line's.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `nazm.docs_index` and `nazm.docs_section`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Nazm's own documentation by section, exactly as `nazm docs` gives it (`schema/nazm.docs-index-1.json`,")
    strs_push(l, "`schema/nazm.docs-section-1.json`, `docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.34). The corpus is a fixed list of the")
    strs_push(l, "repository's documents — the specification, the grammar, the architecture, the capability matrix,")
    strs_push(l, "the roadmap, the goals and the rest — under the repository given as `--docs` at startup, or the one")
    strs_push(l, "the server was built from. It is not the root's project and not a directory scan.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.docs_index` takes an optional `document` id and returns every document with its authority")
    strs_push(l, "and every section's stable id, title, parent and digest, with no body, and the corpus `state`.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.docs_section` takes a section's exact `id` and that `state`, and returns the section's own")
    strs_push(l, "canonical text byte for byte — not its subsections', and never a paraphrase — with its document's")
    strs_push(l, "authority: a `goal` section is aspiration and never evidence of what exists, a `planning` section")
    strs_push(l, "is never a rule of the language. A `state` the documentation no longer has is `stale_state`; an id")
    strs_push(l, "no section has is `not_found`, never the nearest one. There is no path argument: `../README.md` or")
    strs_push(l, "`/etc/passwd` is only an id no section has, and no file is opened for it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### `nazm.repository_map` and `nazm.task_context`")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The repository's context map and the minimum context for a task, exactly as `nazm repo` gives")
    strs_push(l, "them (`schema/nazm.repository-map-1.json`, `schema/nazm.task-context-1.json`,")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/internal/architecture.md` §7.35), over the same repository as the documentation tools — the one given")
    strs_push(l, "as `--docs`, or the one the server was built from — never the root's project.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.repository_map` takes nothing and returns every entity with a durable identity — packages")
    strs_push(l, "and targets, source roots, compilation roots, modules and durable definitions, documents, schemas,")
    strs_push(l, "mutation profiles — with its authority, parent, structural relationships and how to retrieve more,")
    strs_push(l, "and the repository `state`; no source body and no section text. `nazm.task_context` takes one to")
    strs_push(l, "eight `seeds`, ids from that map, and that `state`, and an optional `intent` — `understand`,")
    strs_push(l, "`edit` (the default, the widest), `diagnose` or `test` — and a structural budget. It returns the")
    strs_push(l, "smallest context the repository can justify, one relationship step from each seed: each item")
    strs_push(l, "with its reason, the seed it came from, its priority class, its authority and how to retrieve it")
    strs_push(l, "again; the seed's exact source, other definitions by shape, and sections by their exact text. What")
    strs_push(l, "a budget cuts is listed and makes the answer `partial`; a budget the seeds do not fit is")
    strs_push(l, "`insufficient_budget`. A `state` the repository no longer has is `stale_state`; a seed is an id and")
    strs_push(l, "never a path — `/etc/passwd` or `../x.nz` is `invalid_request`, and nothing is opened for it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## What it reads, and when")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Every call opens the root **from disk as it is then**, derives its answer and drops the analysis.")
    strs_push(l, "An edit written between two calls is seen by the second; a broken file gives no packet, snapshot or")
    strs_push(l, "delta, never a previous one. The documentation and repository tools read the repository at each")
    strs_push(l, "call in the same way.")
    strs_push(l, "No snapshot, history or index is kept between calls. It does not see an editor's unsaved buffers — for those, use `nazm lsp`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## What it does not do")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "- Write, rename or delete anything, or run a command. `nazm.semantic_patch` describes an edit")
    strs_push(l, "  and applies nothing; there is no tool that applies one, and no plan is kept to apply later.")
    strs_push(l, "- Read a file its root's compilation did not load, other than the fixed documentation corpus:")
    strs_push(l, "  `file` is matched against the compilation's own files and is otherwise refused unopened, a")
    strs_push(l, "  baseline is an object, never a path, and a documentation section is asked for by id.")
    strs_push(l, "- Search documentation or the repository: ids are exact, with no fuzzy, full-text or semantic")
    strs_push(l, "  matching, and no directory listing or glob.")
    strs_push(l, "- Keep a previous snapshot, watch the disk, or infer a rename.")
    strs_push(l, "- Serve resources, prompts, completions or sampling; only stdio — no HTTP, no authentication.")
    strs_push(l, "- Report effects, capabilities, tests, semantic history or behavioural equivalence: the compiler")
    strs_push(l, "  has no such facts, and a packet, snapshot or delta marks each `unsupported` rather than empty or")
    strs_push(l, "  unchanged.")
    str_join(l, str_from_byte(10)) + str_from_byte(10)
}

fn dd_doc12() -> Str {
    let l = strs_new()
    strs_push(l, "# Roadmap")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Status: Era 1 (M1–M3) is complete. This document answers one question — what comes next,")
    strs_push(l, "and why in this order.**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "It stopped being a build diary on 2026-09-21. Roughly 900 lines of completed M1a–M1f")
    strs_push(l, "increment narrative were removed: every accepted/rejected table, every status section, every")
    strs_push(l, "derivation of a rule that had already landed. Nothing was lost that is not preserved better")
    strs_push(l, "elsewhere — the semantics went to [`spec.md`](spec.md), the evidence to")
    strs_push(l, "[`bootstrap.md`](../internal/bootstrap.md) and [`releases/4fb1554.md`](../internal/releases/4fb1554.md), the current")
    strs_push(l, "status to [`capability-matrix.md`](../internal/capability-matrix.md), and the narrative to Git. Two")
    strs_push(l, "rules that other files were citing *this* file for — where a loop target binds, and why")
    strs_push(l, "native recursion is refused rather than counted — were normative, so they moved to")
    strs_push(l, "`spec.md` where a reader would look for them.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Ambition beyond the next few milestones is [`NAZM_LANGUAGE_GOALS.md`](../internal/NAZM_LANGUAGE_GOALS.md).")
    strs_push(l, "The invariants that constrain any ordering are [`master-architecture.md`](../internal/master-architecture.md).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## Where the line is today")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm run` | The interpreter. The widest subset |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm build` | Native, through Core IR, MIR and LIR, by LLVM or Cranelift |")
    strs_push(l, "| `compiler/*.nz` | A compiler for Nazm written in Nazm, reaching a C2 ≡ C3 fixpoint; all 21 parity probes as the reference builds them (N102), and narrower than the language — `limitations.md` |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Ask `nazm capabilities --json` for construct-level truth; it is read from the compiler's own")
    strs_push(l, "tables. Ask `capability-matrix.md` for architectural truth, area by area.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## The road to 1.0, since the 0.9.0 preview")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Decided by the copyright holder on 2026-10-11 (`openspec/changes/rewrite-in-nazm`): before 1.0,")
    strs_push(l, "the whole toolchain — compiler, interpreter, every command, the test harness and the tests — is")
    strs_push(l, "rewritten in Nazm, and Nazm's own code generator replaces Cranelift. The Rust implementation is")
    strs_push(l, "then frozen as the bootstrap seed. The language is made ready for that first. Releases come at")
    strs_push(l, "large boundaries only, not one per stage (`releases/0.9.0.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Stage | What | Status (2026-10-16) |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **R1** | The language the rewrite is written in: patterns, tuples, `for`, closures in generics, `defer`, 128-bit integers, serialisation, `@std/regex` and the other libraries, the platform built-ins, and the conveniences for a first program (`openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-14-r1-language-for-the-rewrite`) | **complete**, 2026-10-15; published as **0.10.0** |")
    strs_push(l, "| **R1.5** | Performance and ease: faster builds, `nazm run` compiled, word frequency and `fib` ahead in the cross-language comparison, `:` result types, `[…]` lists, `{…}` maps, short closures, hardened and signed reproducible releases (`openspec/changes/r1-5-performance-and-dx`) | in progress, 17 of 28 tasks: `fib` 55 → 44 ms (C's time with the same checks), word frequency 189 → about 125 ms, one pool worker per processor, `--release` hardening, Sigstore signing. Open: the size-class allocator, a native string hash, whole-program optimisation, streaming `file_lines`, map literals, the safety column, reproducibility checked in CI |")
    strs_push(l, "| **R2** | The Nazm-written compiler carries the whole language, with diagnostics identical to the reference's | nearly complete: the parser agrees on every input; the checker agrees on every compilation it carries (3,235); Core IR identical for all 96,572 functions, every one of the 1,885 documents byte for byte. Open: `@derive`'s JSON and TOML encodings (6 inputs), per-module output |")
    strs_push(l, "| **R3** | The native pipeline in Nazm: ownership and cleanup, LIR, the runtime, the object cache, debug info, every supported target | in progress: MIR (1,476), LIR (1,015), runtime units (990) and the object cache (4,610 units) identical to the reference on both Mac targets, runtime ABI 37. Open: the boards and Windows targets |")
    strs_push(l, "| **R4** | The interpreter in Nazm | in progress: its suite 229 of 229; 2,672 of 2,686 comparisons with the Rust tests' programs agree, the rest varying between runs of the Rust interpreter itself; about 1.7× faster than at first |")
    strs_push(l, "| **R5** | Every command in Nazm: `fmt`, `check`, `fix`, `test`, `doc`, `init`, `lsp`, the MCP server and the rest | in progress: `fmt`, `check` (packages too), `doc`, `fix`, `init`, `lsp`, the argument parser and the dispatcher, 0 differences; refusals being lifted |")
    strs_push(l, "| **R6** | Host qualification: the Nazm toolchain builds itself under a bounded heap | planned |")
    strs_push(l, "| **R7** | The harness and the tests in Nazm | nearly complete: 175 of 176 test files ported, 0 differences; 64 tests stay in Rust by design |")
    strs_push(l, "| **R9** | Nazm's own code generator: LIR to Mach-O and ELF objects for aarch64 and x86_64, checked against LLVM | in progress: 119 of 119 programs agree with LLVM on both Mac targets; `nazm build --backend nazm` |")
    strs_push(l, "| **R8** | Cut-over: the released `nazm` built by Nazm | after R6 |")
    strs_push(l, "| **P** | Performance in Nazm, between the cut-over and the 1.0 gate: the optimisation passes and the compiler's own speed, written once in Nazm rather than in the Rust compiler and ported. Target (2026-10-15): lead every compared language on every measured parameter, 10–30% faster than C, C++ and Rust, safety kept (`openspec/changes/performance-leadership`) | after R8; a research target, not a claim |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Domains** | 1.0 waits for every domain (2026-10-15, `openspec/changes/v1-every-domain`): C cloud, M microcontrollers, D drivers, H hardware (FPGA at 1.0), Q quantum | in progress: C — HTTP/1.1 server and client, TLS on macOS and Linux, calendar time, metrics, configuration, a drain with a deadline; Windows TLS written, not yet run. M1 — Cortex-M33 and RV32IMC, emulator-verified. D, H, Q designed |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Windows** | The toolchain on Windows x86_64 (`openspec/changes/windows-toolchain`, W1–W4) | W1 complete: programs agree on a real Windows host (68 of 68); `nazm.exe` runs, checks and formats (60 of 60). W2–W4 open |")
    strs_push(l, "| **0.11.0** | The stable release before 1.0 (the copyright holder, 2026-10-16): everything above — R1–R9, R1.5 to its last item, stage P's runtime and compiler halves, Windows W1–W4 and its TLS — except the domain tracks, through the full gate (the whole mutation catalogue, signed reproducible archives) on macOS and Windows x86_64 | after P and Windows |")
    strs_push(l, "| **1.0 gate** | 0.11.0 plus every domain track: the full mutation run again, real-board evidence, signed reproducible archives, the licence and CLA review | last |")
    strs_push(l, "| **After 1.0** | Zero dependence on LLVM: Nazm's own optimiser and code generator for optimised builds too, measured against the LLVM build before replacing it; then the ecosystem and Linux hosts | after 1.0 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### When 0.11.0 and 1.0")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Revised 2026-10-16, evening. Two releases remain (the copyright holder, 2026-10-16): **0.11.0**, the")
    strs_push(l, "stable, fast release of everything but the domains, and **1.0**, which adds every domain track.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Part | For | Paced by | Estimate |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| R5, then R6 and R8 — the cut-over | 0.11.0 | agent time | 1–2 weeks |")
    strs_push(l, "| Stage P — the runtime half (concurrency, now), the compiler's passes (after the cut-over) | 0.11.0 | agent time and quiet benchmark runs | weeks |")
    strs_push(l, "| Windows W2–W4 and Windows TLS | 0.11.0 | the Windows host; GitHub's Windows runner | days to weeks |")
    strs_push(l, "| R1.5's last items, R7's `bench`/`fuzz`, the contained runner in Nazm | 0.11.0 | agent and machine time | days |")
    strs_push(l, "| The full gate: the whole mutation catalogue, signed reproducible archives | 0.11.0 and 1.0 | machine time; the copyright holder signs | about a day each |")
    strs_push(l, "| The domains' code (C4 onward, M on real boards, D, H, Q) | 1.0 | agent time | 2–4 months |")
    strs_push(l, "| Real boards (Pico 2, ESP32-C3, iCEBreaker), an IBM Quantum account | 1.0 | purchases and accounts | when they arrive |")
    strs_push(l, "| The licence and CLA review | 1.0 (0.11.0 ships under the same terms as 0.10.0) | the copyright holder and counsel | outside the code |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "From the pace so far, **0.11.0 around the end of 2026** and **1.0 in early-to-mid 2027**, paced by")
    strs_push(l, "the domains, the boards and the review. Usage limits on the agents remain the largest variable.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The milestone tables below are the history that led here; the \"R1\" among them (2026-10-07) is the")
    strs_push(l, "earlier release-readiness milestone, not this programme's first stage.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## What Era 1 delivered")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Milestone | Outcome | Evidence |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **M1** — native vertical slice | `Int`/`Bool`/`Str`/`Ints`/`Strs`, all control flow, calls, one IR level, LLVM text → `clang` | `capability-matrix.md` areas 10–11; 127 two-oracle tests |")
    strs_push(l, "| **M2** — facilities for a compiler | Text, sequences, I/O, modules | `bootstrap.md` §1 |")
    strs_push(l, "| **M3** — bootstrap | C1 → C2 → C3, byte-identical in IR and executable | `bootstrap.md` §3 |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Concurrency C-1…C-3** | Specified first, then interpreted, then compiled, then compiled *by* the Nazm compiler | `capability-matrix.md` area 14 |")
    strs_push(l, "| **AI-native (a)** | Versioned schemas, a checked grammar, a generated guide, a canonical formatter, machine-applicable fixes | `capability-matrix.md` areas 22–24 |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Release** | One experimental candidate, contained, manifest-verified twice | `releases/4fb1554.md` |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### What M2 bypassed rather than delivered")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "This matters more than what it delivered, because it is where the next decisions come from.")
    strs_push(l, "M2's first, third and fourth rows — **value/copy/move semantics with cleanup, records and")
    strs_push(l, "tagged unions with exhaustive matching, and generics** — were never built. The compiler was")
    strs_push(l, "written around them, with parallel `Ints`/`Strs` arrays addressed by index. That was the")
    strs_push(l, "shortest sound path to a bootstrap and it worked; it also means the type system has never")
    strs_push(l, "been asked the questions that make type systems hard, and that the memory model is still")
    strs_push(l, "the one `bootstrap.md` §1 states: allocate, never free.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "---")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "## What comes next, and why in this order")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The ordering rule is [`master-architecture.md`](../internal/master-architecture.md) §3: **a layer earns")
    strs_push(l, "its existence by owning a semantic responsibility no existing layer owns.** Matching the")
    strs_push(l, "aspirational IR diagram is not such a reason. By that test the next step is not the next box")
    strs_push(l, "in the diagram — it is the one place where a responsibility is currently owned *twice*.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N1 — Source identity, and one resolution result · **complete, 2026-09-21**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Done, in four slices** (`0045ed9`, `26a52bd`, `ea016c3`):")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N1A** | `Span` is `{ file, start, end }` with file-local offsets; `SourceMap` replaces the merged buffer; each file is parsed on its own text. The published diagnostic shape is unchanged |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N1C** | One built-in inventory. `nazm-lir`'s 31-variant enum and its `by_name`/`name` tables are gone; `Builtin` is `nazm_syntax::Intrinsic`. `Type` and `Intrinsic` moved to `nazm-syntax` so the backend can see them without reaching the interpreter |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N1B** | `nazm_core::check` produces a `nazm_syntax::Resolution`; the backend reads it. Deleted from `nazm-lir`: `resolve`, `bind`, `scoped`, the scope stack, the name-keyed signature table, the declared-names set, `native_ty`, and the built-in-first rule at the call and spawn sites |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N1D** | A `cargo xtask check` rule fails if `nazm-lir` declares a name-keyed table; eleven tests run resolution-sensitive programs both ways and require one answer |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The acceptance test was met:** one of the two resolvers no longer exists.")
    strs_push(l, "`crates/nazm-lir/src` declares no symbol table keyed by a name and performs no name lookup.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**No new crate.** The shared vocabulary went into `nazm-syntax`, which both consumers")
    strs_push(l, "already depend on; the resolver did not move, the duplicate was deleted. `architecture.md`")
    strs_push(l, "§7.1 records why a `nazm-hir` holding a copy of the checker's answer would have been the")
    strs_push(l, "pass-through the ordering rule exists to prevent.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What N1 deliberately did not do:** no HIR, no Core IR, no MIR — a resolution is not an IR")
    strs_push(l, "— no ownership, effects, capabilities, generics, visibility, separate or incremental")
    strs_push(l, "compilation, and no content-addressed identity. Every id it produces is session-local.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N2 — Compilation units, visibility and module interfaces · **complete, 2026-09-22**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Done, in two commits** (`ae77034` the semantics, `871f09e` the implementation), after a")
    strs_push(l, "separate correction (`72019e2`) that removed a lossy `Serialize` from `Span`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N2A** | `spec.md` settles it: one module is one file; top-level definitions are private and `pub` exports; `use` makes a module's *exported interface* nameable, unqualified; imports are **not transitive**; every collision is a diagnostic naming both sides; cycles stay legal; the root module owns `main`. Grammar gains `[ visibility ]`, one bit, one spelling |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N2B** | `ModuleId` and a `ModuleGraph` the driver builds while loading — a graph, not an ordered bag of files. `nazm-sema` is created, and earns it: `nazm-syntax`'s lexer, parser, formatter and AST referred to `types`, `intrinsic` and `resolve` exactly zero times |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N2C/D/E** | `declare_unit` reads one module's declarations and returns its `UnitInterface`; `check_unit` checks its bodies against its own definitions and its dependencies' **interfaces**. `check` is a loop over the two and holds no resolution of its own |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N2F** | Deleted: the checker's program-wide name table, the evaluator's `HashMap<String, usize>` and its private copy of the built-in-first rule, and the backend's last two name lookups. 80 of the self-hosted compiler's 215 functions became `pub`; 135 stayed private |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The acceptance test was met.** `crates/nazm-core/tests/unit_checking.rs` checks a module")
    strs_push(l, "against an interface for a module whose **source does not exist** — no tree, no body,")
    strs_push(l, "nothing to parse — and refuses the same module when that interface is empty. A dependency's")
    strs_push(l, "bodies are not a parameter of `check_unit` and are not reachable from one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What N2 deliberately did not do:** nothing is separately *compiled*. Lowering still takes")
    strs_push(l, "the whole program and emits one LLVM module; there are no per-module artefacts, no cached")
    strs_push(l, "interfaces and no linker symbols. Every id remains session-local. No packages, no")
    strs_push(l, "re-export, no aliasing, no qualified paths, no HIR.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N3 — Durable identity and persisted interfaces · **complete, 2026-09-22**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Done, in one commit after a separate constitution commit** (`40b1c9a` the semantics).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N3A** | `spec.md` settles what makes this the same module and the same definition, before any representation. A **source root** — the root module's directory, derived not declared. `ModuleKey` is the normalised path relative to it; `DefKey` is that plus a kind and a name. A body edit, a signature edit, a visibility change and a move all keep the key; a rename does not |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N3B** | `ModuleKey`/`DefKey` in `nazm-sema`, beside the session ids rather than replacing them. The loader computes them and **withdraws** one where the two compiler implementations could disagree |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N3C** | `nazm-iface`: `nazm.interface/1`, deterministic, validated on read. serde lives there and not in `nazm-sema`, so a session-local id cannot be serialised by accident |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N3D** | `InterfaceHash` — BLAKE3 over the canonical bytes. Twelve invalidation rows measured rather than asserted |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N3E** | `nazm interface FILE`, so the boundary is real: two processes, two directories, and a dependent checked with its dependency's source **deleted** |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N3F** | A `sema purity` gate, verified to fire both ways; five identity mutations, all caught |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The symlink policy is the part that was settled rather than coded around.** The reference")
    strs_push(l, "loader keys by canonical path and the Nazm-written one by normalised text, so an aliased")
    strs_push(l, "file is one module to the first and two to the second. Durable identity **declines** where")
    strs_push(l, "they could disagree, and so does a path that escapes the source root. Both compile exactly")
    strs_push(l, "as before; they simply get no key, and everything built on one refuses rather than guesses.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What N3 is not.** No cache, no store, no query engine, no scheduler, no artefact reuse,")
    strs_push(l, "and no claim that anything is faster. `InterfaceHash` answers *must this module's dependents")
    strs_push(l, "be re-checked* and excludes bodies by design — using it as a codegen cache key would hand")
    strs_push(l, "back an object file compiled from a body that has since changed, which is why")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.3 names an implementation fingerprint and a `BuildKey` it is not.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N4 — Sound incremental semantic reuse · **complete, 2026-09-22**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Done, in two commits** (`2565419` the keys and the store, `7b44b4f` the root and the")
    strs_push(l, "reuse).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N4A** | A **declared** source root, which had to come first: under a derived one a module's key depends on which file the compilation began at, so two compilations of one project never share anything. `nazm.root` is an empty marker — enforced empty, because the first field it carried would make it a manifest — and `--source-root DIR` names one without writing a file. With neither, nothing changes |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N4B** | `nazm-cache`: `SourceFingerprint` over the exact source bytes with no normalisation at all, `CheckerIdentity` deriving the built-in table, the type set and both schemas with an explicit `SEMANTIC_EPOCH` for what cannot be derived, and `CheckKey` over both plus each direct import's `(ModuleKey, InterfaceHash)`. Every input tested by removing it |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N4C** | `nazm.check/1` and a local store. Content-addressed, so entries are immutable and two compilers need no lock; published by `rename`; validated on read by recomputing the key from the inputs the entry records. Sixteen ways of damaging one, every one a miss |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N4D** | One hook in `nazm-core`, `Reuse`. `check_unit` is still the only thing that decides what a body means; the driver only says which bodies it needs decided. Only a clean check is written, so no entry is ever a cached refusal |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N4E** | `--no-cache`, `--cache-report` (one `nazm.check-report/1` object, off by default), `NAZM_CACHE_DIR`. The store's location is not part of any identity |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N4F** | A **cache soundness** gate, proved by breaking it three ways; six mutations; twenty-nine end-to-end tests, all of them running the binary |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The acceptance test was met, three times.** A private body change re-checks its own module")
    strs_push(l, "and leaves its importer alone. An exported signature change re-checks the importer and finds")
    strs_push(l, "the error it now has. In `A → B → C`, a change to C that forces B to re-check but leaves B's")
    strs_push(l, "interface unchanged **stops at B** — which is the difference between interface-driven")
    strs_push(l, "invalidation and a reachability sweep, and the reason the design is worth the keys.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What N4 is not, and does not claim.** Incremental *native* compilation. What is reused is")
    strs_push(l, "the second stage of checking one module — its bodies. Every module is still read, parsed and")
    strs_push(l, "declared from source on every run, which is exactly what makes a skipped module invisible.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm run` and `nazm build` reuse nothing, because both need the resolution that only")
    strs_push(l, "checking a body produces, and lowering is still whole-program. There is no object, IR or LIR")
    strs_push(l, "cache, no query database, no scheduler and no eviction policy.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N5 — Separate code generation and internal linking · **complete, 2026-09-22**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Done, in three commits** (`0bf58be` a preflight correction, `41e0536` the symbol")
    strs_push(l, "constitution, `d303571` the split).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N5A** | A native symbol is a spelling of the definition's `DefKey`, not a position in a whole-program numbering. The encoding escapes every byte outside `[A-Za-z0-9]` including `_`, so it is injective and collisions are impossible **by construction** — no digest, no truncation, no probability. `pub` chooses linkage and never spelling |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N5B** | Lowering splits into a global `plan` — signature admissibility and the recursion refusal, both of which span modules — and `lower_module`, which reads one module's bodies and every function's *signature*. No new IR |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N5C** | `emit_unit` per module. A call across a boundary is a `declare` and a linker reference; a unit contains no other module's body and has no route to one |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N5D** | Runtime and platform entry in artefacts of their own, defined once. Constants needed no qualification: `private` linkage makes them local labels, established by linking two objects that both define `@.s0` |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N5E** | `clang -c` per artefact, then a link. Deterministic input order, a working directory this build created and removes, and nothing else touched |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N5F** | A `native identity` gate, proved by breaking it three ways; five mutations; sixteen end-to-end cases; clean-build cost measured against the previous commit |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**The acceptance tests were met.** Three modules each define a private `helper` and all")
    strs_push(l, "three compile; a diamond generates the shared module once; a legal import cycle links; a")
    strs_push(l, "cross-module *call* cycle is still refused; an imported `main` is not the process entry;")
    strs_push(l, "two checkouts and two entry points give one library identical symbols.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**A preflight found a live defect and fixed it first.** Every native runtime failure named")
    strs_push(l, "the file `nazm build` was invoked on, so a division by zero in `lib.nz` printed")
    strs_push(l, "`main.nz` with `lib.nz`'s line and column — a location that points somewhere real and")
    strs_push(l, "wrong. The interpreter had been right all along and no assertion compared the two.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What N5 answered that N4 had assumed.** A's object names B in one `declare` and one")
    strs_push(l, "`call`. Changing B's body, adding a private definition, or adding an export A does not call")
    strs_push(l, "leave A's artefact byte-identical — so an object depends on its dependencies' **symbol")
    strs_push(l, "identity and ABI signature**, not their implementations. N4's report said otherwise; it was")
    strs_push(l, "reasoning ahead of an architecture that did not exist yet.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What N5 is not.** A cache. Every module is regenerated on every build, and the clean build")
    strs_push(l, "is roughly twice as slow for a small program — almost entirely `clang` process startup,")
    strs_push(l, "which `performance.md` measures rather than hides.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### After N5, in dependency order")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Depends on | Why not before |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| A persistable unit interface | durable identity ✓ | done — N3 |")
    strs_push(l, "| A key independent of which file was named | a declared source root ✓ | done — N4 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Semantic check reuse | that, plus a key covering every checking input ✓ | done — N4 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Separate *code generation* | units ✓ + a linking model ✓ | done — N5 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Native artefact reuse | separate code generation ✓ + a key over the backend's input ✓ | done — N6 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Content-addressed compilation | reuse ✓ + a normalised form of a definition | nothing normalises or hashes a definition — `research-register.md` R2 |")
    strs_push(l, "| A language server | units ✓ + durable identity ✓ + reuse ✓ + a lossless CST | it would re-implement the semantic engine otherwise |")
    strs_push(l, "| Ownership / the surface memory model | — | the largest open design question; `research-register.md` R1 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Effects | a typed core IR | and *\"is divergence an effect?\"* is unanswered — `spec.md` *Open* |")
    strs_push(l, "| Capabilities, information flow | effects | `architecture.md` §5 keeps the three separate |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N6 — Content-addressed native object reuse · **complete, 2026-09-22**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An emitted LLVM unit whose object was compiled before is not compiled again.")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.6 owns the design; this is what shipped and in what order.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **preflight** | A generated artefact names a module by its durable identity. Two strings used to carry the path the command line spelled — the `source_filename` and every runtime failure's location — so one project built from two directories was two programs. Without this there is no reuse between checkouts and no honest failure message |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N6A** | `ObjectKey` over three things and nothing else: a digest of the exact bytes handed to the object compiler, that compiler's identity, and the configuration it resolves. A store beside the semantic one under a shared `.nazm/` root, one file per entry, validated six ways before it is believed |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N6B–D** | One `clang -###` per build reads what the driver says it will actually run, so the triple, the CPU features, the relocation model and the ABI are in the key without anyone enumerating them. The invocation is hermetic: an environment built from nothing plus ten named variables. Module, runtime and entry units all go through one key and one store. `--no-cache`, `--build-report`, `nazm.build-report/1` |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N6E** | An `object cache` gate, proved by breaking each of its rules; six mutations, three of which attack the key and three the validation; forty end-to-end and store-level cases |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N6F** | Measurement, and the authorities |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the key is, and what it is not.** Not a second dependency graph — not the module's")
    strs_push(l, "source, not each dependency's exported signatures, not an emitter epoch. Every one of those")
    strs_push(l, "is an approximation of what `clang -c` reads, and every approximation leaves something out.")
    strs_push(l, "The emitted IR **is** the input, so N5's measured precision falls out rather than being")
    strs_push(l, "encoded: a dependency's body change and an export the caller never calls each leave the")
    strs_push(l, "caller's object alone, and a called signature change does not, because it is written into")
    strs_push(l, "the caller's own `declare`.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What a warm store cannot do.** Bypass anything. A key is a digest of an artefact, so the")
    strs_push(l, "artefact must exist before the key does, so the reading, parsing, checking, backend")
    strs_push(l, "admissibility, lowering and emission have all already happened — including the whole-program")
    strs_push(l, "recursion refusal, which a fully warm store never reaches.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Measured.** On the five-module compiler: `-O0` 665.4 ms with `--no-cache`, 730.7 ms cold,")
    strs_push(l, "**157.6 ms** warm; `-O2` 1693.0 ms, 1755.4 ms, **157.6 ms**. A one-module edit costs")
    strs_push(l, "198–218 ms whether it is a private body, a called export's body or an export nobody calls —")
    strs_push(l, "the three are indistinguishable, which is the whole point. A warm build runs two external")
    strs_push(l, "processes where a cache-disabled one runs eight.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What N6 is not.** Incremental native compilation. Lowering and emission run every time and")
    strs_push(l, "so does the link; there is no executable cache, no `LinkKey`, no incremental linker, no")
    strs_push(l, "persistent LIR, no LTO. Nothing is evicted, so the store grows until it is deleted.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N7 — Memory constitution and the first reclamation — **complete, 2026-09-22**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The cache ladder stopped here on purpose. `architecture.md` §7.7 owns the design and the")
    strs_push(l, "evidence; `spec.md`'s *memory constitution* owns the law.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **preflight** | A mutation verdict is measured the way the suite is authoritative — one job, one test thread. `nproc` reports 10 inside a container limited to one CPU, and the suite has wall-clock deadlines, so verdicts were a function of scheduling. The dangerous direction was never the one that was noticed: a spurious failure while measuring a **mutant** counts as CAUGHT and is invisible |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N7A** | The audit. Every type across both implementations, every allocation site, the leak measured, and `compiler/*.nz` counted |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N7B–C** | Five models compared against real Nazm code; the constitution settled in `spec.md` before anything was implemented |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N7D** | Reference counting on the sequence header. Reclamation on the three exit edges of a generated function, and the same rule modelled in the interpreter rather than inherited from the host |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N7E** | Sixteen cases, each run twice and compared; six mutations |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N7F** | Measurement, and the authorities |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What the audit changed.** Two findings moved the design before a line was written. A")
    strs_push(l, "`Str` has four provenances and does not say which — a literal's constant, `argv`, a heap")
    strs_push(l, "buffer, or the **interior** of any of them, because `str_slice` is specified not to")
    strs_push(l, "allocate — so `free` is wrong for three of the four. And the specification's `Str` value")
    strs_push(l, "semantics are currently paid for *with the leak*. `Str` is therefore out of the slice, in")
    strs_push(l, "the specification's own words.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**What did not change.** Any program's meaning. `let b = a;` still aliases a sequence, a")
    strs_push(l, "push through one is still visible through the other, a parameter is still borrowed. A model")
    strs_push(l, "that had to break that to be implementable would have been the wrong model.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Measured.** 5,000 / 20,000 / 80,000 short-lived sequences: 4.38 / 12.28 / 43.52 MiB")
    strs_push(l, "before, **1.78 / 1.88 / 1.86 MiB** after. Flat in work where it was linear. A genuinely")
    strs_push(l, "live sequence and a string-heavy loop are both unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### After N7, in dependency order")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Depends on | Why not before |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Reclaiming `Ints` and `Strs` | a memory constitution ✓ | done — N7 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Reclaiming `Str` | a representation that records provenance | done — N8. Four provenances, one of them an interior pointer, answered by a third field naming the owner |")
    strs_push(l, "| Reclaiming `Chan` | a rule for a value whose lifetime is a `scope`'s and whose holders are tasks | done — N8. The count is atomic, because it does cross; a waiter implies a live reference, which is what makes `rc == 0` sufficient |")
    strs_push(l, "| Reclamation in the self-hosted backend | the above, and a migration | done — N8. No source change was needed; the runtime is derived from the Rust emitter's and a gate refuses drift |")
    strs_push(l, "| User-defined records | a decision this milestone deliberately did not make | `research-register.md` R1, re-scoped: value semantics are a live question for a kind of value with no existing meaning to break |")
    strs_push(l, "| Ownership cycles | a recursive type existing at all | impossible today: no value can refer to another that can refer back |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N8 — Complete current heap reclamation — **complete, 2026-09-22**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Every heap-backed type the language has is reclaimed, in the reference interpreter, in the")
    strs_push(l, "Rust compiler's output, and in the output of the compiler written in Nazm.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N8A–C** | The `Str` backing model — `{ pointer, length, owner }`, four origins classified rather than guessed at — string and channel reclamation, container element ownership, task-boundary ownership, and four runtime leaks that were nobody's feature |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N8D** | `compiler/emit.nz` migrated. Its runtime is **derived** from the Rust emitter's rather than transcribed, with a gate; its decisions are held by a differential memory test |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N8E** | Nine mutations, and the scaling measurements |")
    strs_push(l, "| **N8F** | The authorities |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The number that says what it was for: the accumulator shape from the 2026-09-21 incident,")
    strs_push(l, "at 8,000 iterations, fell from **70.66 MiB to 2.23 MiB**. 80,000 temporary strings against a")
    strs_push(l, "constant live set: 4.17 MiB → 1.77 MiB. 2,000 short-lived channels: 2.38 MiB → 1.80 MiB.")
    strs_push(l, "Sequences, a genuinely live sequence and a sieve are unchanged, which is the control. The")
    strs_push(l, "cost is about 13–16 ns per string operation and nothing measurable elsewhere.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/*.nz` needed **no source change**, which was the test of whether the constitution")
    strs_push(l, "is as ergonomic as it claims: memory semantics are transparent, and a milestone that had")
    strs_push(l, "required manual lifetime management in the compiler's own source would have been evidence")
    strs_push(l, "against the design rather than for it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### After N8, in dependency order")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Depends on | Why not before |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **User-defined records** | a decision about value semantics for a kind of value with no existing meaning to break | done — N9. Value semantics, composed field by field; cycles refused as an impossible layout rather than admitted with a policy |")
    strs_push(l, "| Variants, pattern matching, `Option`, `Result` | records ✓ | the shape of a payload is a record's question first, and it has been answered |")
    strs_push(l, "| Generics | records ✓ and variants | nothing to be generic over yet |")
    strs_push(l, "| A lossless CST | nothing in this list | the last AI-native item, and independent of all of it |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm explain-cost` | the cost table in `spec.md` ✓ | the model is documented; the tool is not written, and is not urgent |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### After N9, in dependency order")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Depends on | Why not before |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Variants and pattern matching** | records ✓ | done — N10. A discriminant, an exhaustiveness rule and a binding form, and copy and release that act on the active variant alone |")
    strs_push(l, "| Generic containers | records ✓ and variants | a `Vec<Record>` is where value semantics usually start to hurt, and it is also what would make a reference cycle expressible again — at which point `spec.md`'s *Cycles* has to be satisfied a second time |")
    strs_push(l, "| Copy elision, specified | records ✓ | `research-register.md` R1's original sharp question, still unanswered: a record copy costs one reference adjustment per owning field, and nothing says when the compiler may remove the pair |")
    strs_push(l, "| A lossless CST | nothing above | unchanged; still independent, still the last AI-native item |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### After N10, in dependency order")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Depends on | Why not before |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Generic containers** | records ✓ and variants ✓ | `Vec[T]` is now named by two findings rather than argued for: it is what the self-hosted compiler needs before an enum can replace a tagged integer, and it is where value semantics usually start to hurt. It is also what would make a reference cycle expressible again, at which point `spec.md`'s *Cycles* has to be satisfied a second time |")
    strs_push(l, "| `Option`, `Result`, typed errors | generics | expressible monomorphically today — `enum MaybeInt { None, Some(value: Int), }` — which is the evidence the kernel is ready and also the reason not to bless a built-in one before it can be written once |")
    strs_push(l, "| Copy elision, specified | records ✓ and variants ✓ | R1's original sharp question, still unanswered, and now slightly larger: a copy costs one reference adjustment per owning field and, for an enum, a branch as well. Nothing says when either may be removed |")
    strs_push(l, "| A wildcard arm and `non_exhaustive` | variants ✓ | deliberately absent. Adding a variant should break importers while the language is young; when it should stop doing that is a design decision, not an omission to fix |")
    strs_push(l, "| A lossless CST | nothing above | unchanged; still independent, still the last AI-native item |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### After N11, in dependency order")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Depends on | Why not before |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **`Result`, `Option` and typed error propagation** | generics ✓ | expressible now as ordinary generic enums, which is the evidence the kernel is ready. What is missing is not the type but the decisions around it: where a standard definition lives when there is no standard library, whether `?`-style propagation is syntax, and what a failure *is* when `N0405` already stops the program. N11 deliberately left all three alone |")
    strs_push(l, "| Traits, or any constraint on `T` | generics ✓ | a generic body can do only what every type can, which is the honest limit of N11. A constraint system is a large decision about dispatch, coherence and orphan rules and should be forced by a program that needs `==` or ordering on `T`, not by symmetry |")
    strs_push(l, "| Copy elision, specified | records ✓, variants ✓, generics ✓ | R1's sharp question is larger again: a `Vec` of records copies each element on `vec_get`, by `T`'s law, and nothing says when the pair may be removed |")
    strs_push(l, "| A compact enum representation | variants ✓, `Vec[T]` ✓ | an enum is one slot per variant, and a `Vec[Enum]` multiplies that by its length. `performance.md` measures the pressure; nothing here claims it is acceptable at scale |")
    strs_push(l, "| A lossless CST | nothing above | unchanged; still independent, still the last AI-native item |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### After N12, in dependency order")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Depends on | Why not before |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Blocks as values in `nazm build`, and derived equality on records and enums** | records ✓, variants ✓ | the two walls both dogfoods hit. N11 could not turn the compiler's integer tags into an enum because an enum has no `==`; N12 could not turn a single `-1` sentinel into an `Option` because a `match` arm cannot be a block in the native subset, so the only spelling converts straight back to the sentinel. The interpreter already has blocks as values; the native backends refuse them, which is also why an explicit early return from an arm is written `if true { return … } else { return … }` there |")
    strs_push(l, "| `?` on `Option`, and conversion between error types | traits | both need a protocol — a carrier `?` can dispatch on, a conversion it can call — and a protocol is a trait. N12 refused both rather than special-case them |")
    strs_push(l, "| Traits, or any constraint on `T` | generics ✓ | unchanged: a constraint system is a large decision and should be forced by a program that needs `==` or ordering on `T`. Derived equality on *concrete* types is the smaller step that does not need one |")
    strs_push(l, "| Mapping a typed error to a process status | `Result` ✓ | `main` still returns `Int`. Letting it return a `Result` is a contract with the operating system, not a type rule, and nothing has needed it yet |")
    strs_push(l, "| A compact enum representation | variants ✓, `Vec[T]` ✓ | `Option[Str]` and every `Result` are now common, and each is one slot per variant; `performance.md` measures them |")
    strs_push(l, "| Copy elision, specified | records ✓, variants ✓, generics ✓ | unchanged, and `?` adds one retain/release pair per success it passes through |")
    strs_push(l, "| A lossless CST | nothing above | unchanged; still independent |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "*N12.1 took the first half of the first row.* Blocks as values compile natively in both")
    strs_push(l, "compilers, and the `-1` sentinel became an `Option`. Derived equality is what is left of it.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### After N12.1, in dependency order")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Depends on | Why not before |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| **Derived equality on records and enums** | records ✓, variants ✓ | the wall N11's dogfood hit and N12.1's did not remove: the compiler's node kinds, token kinds and frame kinds are integers compared with `==` or `!=` at 463 sites in `compiler/*.nz` (`kind == n_block()`), and an enum cannot replace them while it has no `==`. Rewriting every comparison as a `match` would be the workaround this milestone refused. Needs no trait: equality on a *concrete* nominal type, derived from its fields as copy and release already are |")
    strs_push(l, "| `?` on `Option`, and conversion between error types | traits | unchanged |")
    strs_push(l, "| Traits, or any constraint on `T` | generics ✓ | unchanged |")
    strs_push(l, "| Mapping a typed error to a process status | `Result` ✓ | unchanged |")
    strs_push(l, "| A compact enum representation | variants ✓, `Vec[T]` ✓ | unchanged; `Option[Int]` now appears inside the compiler too |")
    strs_push(l, "| Copy elision, specified | records ✓, variants ✓, generics ✓ | unchanged |")
    strs_push(l, "| A lossless CST | nothing above | unchanged; still independent |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### After N48: the v1 foundation, and what is deliberately after it")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N40–N48 complete the v1 foundation; `docs/user/limitations.md` is the one list of what it does not do.")
    strs_push(l, "What follows is **not started** and is bounded here so it is not mistaken for v1 scope:")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Post-v1 work | Depends on | Why not in v1 |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Function values, closures, traits | a calling convention for captures | changes the language; every layer below would move — N50 |")
    strs_push(l, "| Effect polymorphism, attenuation and revocation of capabilities | function values; a capability with a type argument | the coarse kinds are what N37 settled |")
    strs_push(l, "| Richer information flow: more sinks, declassification | N38's framework | one sink was enough to make the framework real |")
    strs_push(l, "| More targets and cross-compilation | a foreign linker and runtime per target | the host is the only verified one |")
    strs_push(l, "| A suspendable-task scheduler (M:N) | stack switching or compiled continuations | a worker pool would deadlock blocking programs (§7.46) |")
    strs_push(l, "| A JIT, SIMD, GPU/HPC | a reason; area 21 | none proposed |")
    strs_push(l, "| Pointers, strings and structs across the FFI | a layout promise and a borrowed-string type | scalars were enough to make the boundary real |")
    strs_push(l, "| Debug variables, a live-debugger workflow, Cranelift DWARF | `DILocalVariable` from MIR locals | function and statement positions were the declared scope |")
    strs_push(l, "| A package registry and version ranges | a resolver that chooses | exact path dependencies choose nothing |")
    strs_push(l, "| Formal methods | a semantics to state them against | area 19's acceptance is an assessment, not a test count |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### After N75: N76–N100, closing what is PARTIAL or RESEARCH")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "One milestone at a time, each constitution first, each ending with its own evidence and the")
    strs_push(l, "capability row decided against that evidence rather than its title. The order is")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/nazm_N76_N100_FULL_prompts/MASTER_EXECUTION_ORDER.md`'s: the front end (N76–N80); execution,")
    strs_push(l, "runtime and interoperability (N81–N85); embedded, assurance and AI/HPC (N86–N88); tooling,")
    strs_push(l, "ecosystem, evidence, platforms and contracts (N89–N96); formal trust, the compiler written in Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "and the interactive tier (N97–N99); and N100, an audit of the whole catalogue that may fail")
    strs_push(l, "honestly. A row stays PARTIAL, RESEARCH or BLOCKED when that is what its evidence says.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### After N100: N101–N108, closing the core")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`docs/nazm_N101_N108_core_closure_prompts/MASTER_EXECUTION_ORDER.md`'s order: evidence closure (N101),")
    strs_push(l, "the compiler written in Nazm at parity (N102), re-exports (N103), authority (N104), one LIR contract")
    strs_push(l, "(N105), the default M:N runtime (N106), a core-scope audit (N107) and a release gate over the full")
    strs_push(l, "catalogue (N108).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### After v0.3.0: post-release tracks, not core defects")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The core is closed under its declared scope (N108), and v0.3.0 is its first public release (R1).")
    strs_push(l, "What follows is classified so that nothing reads as missing compiler-core correctness merely")
    strs_push(l, "because another language has it. Each is a later track or a research item, blocked outside this")
    strs_push(l, "repository, or a deliberate non-goal; none is promised, and none blocks the release.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Ambition | Class | Why |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Distributed runtime, supervision trees, durable actors | post-release track | a runtime layer over structured concurrency; nothing in v0.3 depends on it |")
    strs_push(l, "| Hard real-time and WCET bounds | research | `wcet` is always `null`; needs a timing model per target (area 18) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Macros and compile-time metaprogramming | research | `nazm comptime` is a command; a macro system is a language decision not yet made (`spec.md`, *Non-goals*) |")
    strs_push(l, "| A verified optimizer, more proof systems | blocked / research | no proof assistant here; formal evidence is bounded model checking (area 19) |")
    strs_push(l, "| New architectures and platform ports | post-release track | each needs a machine or emulator to run on; x86_64 Linux first (`support.md`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Database and HTTP frameworks, networking | post-release track | the standard library has no network authority yet (area 16) |")
    strs_push(l, "| A public package registry | post-release track | the registry is local; signatures and a remote source come first (area 26) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Multi-agent semantic collaboration, deterministic replay | research | the semantic tooling (snapshots, deltas, patches) is the substrate; neither is designed |")
    strs_push(l, "| A second GPU provider | blocked | no Metal or SPIR-V toolchain here (area 21) |")
    strs_push(l, "| sBPF / Solana execution | blocked | no sBPF toolchain or validator (area 34) |")
    strs_push(l, "| An in-process JIT | blocked | needs `unsafe`, which the workspace forbids (area 12) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Trait objects, effect handlers, user effects, implicit-flow tracking | research | N107 checked each and found none a defect or a requirement of the core (`audit-n107.md`) |")
    strs_push(l, "| Windows, 32-bit hosted, big-endian targets | non-goal | stated reasons in `support.md` |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### V1 Gate 1 — core stability and the 1.x constitution — **2026-10-07; awaiting review**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "The v1 programme's first gate (its brief is kept outside the tracked tree, and is a goal, not")
    strs_push(l, "evidence). Language 1.0, toolchain 1.0.0; the semantic epoch (29), `nazm.interface/11`, runtime")
    strs_push(l, "ABI 14 and every schema unchanged, each for its own reason (`stability.md`). `stability.md` is the")
    strs_push(l, "1.x compatibility constitution — the promise, the patch/minor/major lines, and a class for every")
    strs_push(l, "spec section, schema, command and option; `spec.md` classifies each of its sections and a test")
    strs_push(l, "holds it to that. `tests/compat/v1/` is the append-only compatibility corpus, pinned by digest.")
    strs_push(l, "Public outputs that described an earlier language were fixed: the refusal help, the built-in type")
    strs_push(l, "list in help text and `nazm capabilities`, `1.5` refused by name as floating point, and four")
    strs_push(l, "commands' help. Selfhost claims are scoped to the declared subset; `licensing.md` is the technical")
    strs_push(l, "audit, and **a licensing decision is required before public release**. **Found, not fixed:** a")
    strs_push(l, "closure stored into a `Vec` it captures forms a reference cycle that is never reclaimed — a defect")
    strs_push(l, "against `spec.md`'s *Cycles*, reported for decision (area 4 is PARTIAL). Nothing tagged, pushed or")
    strs_push(l, "published.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "**Gate 1-C1** — the reviewer chose cycle prevention, extended to closure environments, over a")
    strs_push(l, "collector or a narrowed claim. A closure may not capture a value that can hold a function value")
    strs_push(l, "behind a counted handle (`N0616`), decided by the captured type where the closure is written, in")
    strs_push(l, "both compilers; storing a function value is never refused. Semantic epoch 29 → 30. `Type::ALL`")
    strs_push(l, "holds all seven capability types, so completion offers them. `architecture.md` §7.111.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### R1 — public release readiness — **complete, 2026-10-07; candidate `996984f`**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`releases/996984f.md` the record. No language or runtime semantics changed intentionally. The")
    strs_push(l, "version is settled — language v0.3, toolchain 0.3.0, tag `v0.3.0` — and `docs/user/stability.md` keeps the")
    strs_push(l, "six identities apart; `docs/user/spec.md` opens as the v0.3 specification with each section's kind")
    strs_push(l, "stated. CI runs the host-safe subset and leaves the contained stages out by reading the guard; it is")
    strs_push(l, "not the release gate. N108's lifecycle \"timing flake\" was an inherited ignored SIGINT, and the test")
    strs_push(l, "now restores the default itself. A public README, a getting-started page and a tour the suite runs as")
    strs_push(l, "written, a support matrix checked against the compiler's table, `SECURITY.md` and `CONTRIBUTING.md`.")
    strs_push(l, "Dates inside a candidate are the commit's, and a build-input digest covers every tracked file. **R1-C1**")
    strs_push(l, "fixed the one defect R1 found — a function written as a value was missing from the reference index")
    strs_push(l, "(`architecture.md` §7.110) — and a claims audit brought the current documents to the compiler. Two")
    strs_push(l, "assemblies of the candidate were byte-identical; the manifest redigested independently, 220 of 220;")
    strs_push(l, "five catalogue entries added and caught in their own campaigns. Nothing tagged, pushed or published.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N108 — the core release gate — **complete, 2026-10-06; candidate `920a2a5`**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.109 first; `releases/920a2a5.md` the record. The whole catalogue, contained:")
    strs_push(l, "1,268 of 1,268 caught, after 34 entries the campaign could not decide were repaired — killers chosen on")
    strs_push(l, "macOS that Linux does not see, and nine whose code N90, N104 and N105 had moved. The platform runs")
    strs_push(l, "found a debugger regression from N105, fixed. Workspace, selfhost, bootstrap, lifecycle, fuzzing,")
    strs_push(l, "benchmark, platforms and the release assembly pass; the manifest redigested independently, 206 of 206.")
    strs_push(l, "No class-A row is PARTIAL. Nothing tagged, pushed or published.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N107 — the core's scope, audited — **complete, 2026-10-05; areas 2, 3, 5, 6, 7 VERIFIED**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.108 first; `audit-n107.md` the table. Every core candidate gap was checked for")
    strs_push(l, "being a defect first (none was) and then for being required (none is): trait objects, generic traits,")
    strs_push(l, "default methods, effect handlers, user effects, runtime or linear capabilities, implicit flow. The")
    strs_push(l, "rows now say what VERIFIED promises — areas 3, 5, 6 and 7 as scoped — and every absent construct is")
    strs_push(l, "still refused by name. Divergence and implicit flow stay registered research. Twenty-nine VERIFIED,")
    strs_push(l, "eight PARTIAL, all ecosystem or domain. No code; no version moves. Next: N108.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N106 — the pool by default; two regressions attributed — **complete, 2026-10-05; area 13 VERIFIED**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.107 first. N83's M:N pool is the default runtime on every hosted target with a")
    strs_push(l, "switch; `threads` by name, any other name refused (`N0404`), a program that calls C on threads unless")
    strs_push(l, "it asks; `nazm.cost/2` says which; runtime ABI 14. The `channels` build regression is the pool's")
    strs_push(l, "runtime text, accepted; the check regression is N76's lossless tree and N80's provenance, with a sort")
    strs_push(l, "and SipHash inside them removed (contained `compiler/check` 213.7 → 180.2 ms), the rest accepted; the")
    strs_push(l, "bench baseline re-saved. Next: N107.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N105 — one LIR both backends consume — **complete, 2026-10-05; area 10 VERIFIED (v2)**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.106 first. An instruction-level LIR in `nazm-lir/src/op/`, lowered from MIR once,")
    strs_push(l, "decides every failure, guard, offset, runtime call and retain or release; LLVM prints it and Cranelift")
    strs_push(l, "translates it, and Cranelift may no longer depend on MIR. A validator and an interpreter of LIR — the")
    strs_push(l, "oracle, for the sequential subset — with hand-written expectations and a fifth fuzz tier; `--layout")
    strs_push(l, "soa` on both backends; `nazm.lir/2`; the Cranelift object key is the LIR's digest. Epoch, interface")
    strs_push(l, "schema and runtime ABI unchanged. Next: N106.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N104 — authority is a parameter — **complete, 2026-10-05; area 6 stays PARTIAL**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.105 first. The authority bridge removed: no function exercises its caller's")
    strs_push(l, "capabilities; every program in the repository, and the compiler written in Nazm, migrated to take")
    strs_push(l, "them as parameters; `N0369` in both compilers; epoch 29, `nazm.inspect/2`. Next: N105.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N103 — re-exports — **complete, 2026-10-05; area 2 stays PARTIAL**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.104 first. `pub use`, with chosen names and `as`; one identity per definition")
    strs_push(l, "in every output; `N0211`–`N0213`; `nazm.interface/11`, `nazm.api-doc/2`, epoch 28; both compilers.")
    strs_push(l, "Not done: check reuse for `nazm build` and `nazm run`. Next: N104.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N102 — the compiler written in Nazm at parity — **complete, 2026-10-05: 21 of 21 probes**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.103 first. Effects, capabilities, recursion with the stack check, contracts,")
    strs_push(l, "foreign declarations, `@std`, traits, closures and function values, `&&`, `||` and `!` ported into")
    strs_push(l, "`compiler/*.nz`, each as the reference has it; the parity record 21 equal, 0 refused, none differs.")
    strs_push(l, "Selfhost and bootstrap passed contained (C2 = C3, `8cc750c6…`, 34 conformance cases, 29 refusals).")
    strs_push(l, "The cost: 3,400 more lines and about 30 % more check time for the compiler itself")
    strs_push(l, "(`performance.md`). Next: N103.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N101 — evidence closure — **complete, 2026-10-05**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.102 first. N100's survivor, `n79-a-held-io-cap-is-read-alone`, is reachable —")
    strs_push(l, "N100's probe read a warm check cache — and has a focused killer. The four without a verdict have")
    strs_push(l, "focused killers. Every other catalogue entry without one got a killer found by applying it: 175, all")
    strs_push(l, "caught. 1,254 of 1,255 entries declare a killer; the one that does not is a known survivor with its")
    strs_push(l, "reason. `cargo xtask check` refuses an entry with neither. Next: N102.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N100 — the grand audit — **complete; the zero-partial objective NOT MET**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.101 and `docs/internal/audits/audit-n100.md`. Every row audited against executed evidence;")
    strs_push(l, "twenty-two VERIFIED, fifteen PARTIAL. The combined gate: workspace, selfhost and bootstrap passed")
    strs_push(l, "contained; of 215 mutants, 210 caught (five after a finding was fixed), one survives, four without a")
    strs_push(l, "verdict; every container-backed run passed. A release candidate and a human procedure — nothing")
    strs_push(l, "tagged, pushed or published.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N99 — JIT and REPL v2 — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-04; the JIT stays BLOCKED**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.100 first. The REPL, the interpreter and both native backends held to one")
    strs_push(l, "answer; the JIT's blocker shown to need `unsafe` and an absent crate, and its isolated design written.")
    strs_push(l, "Next: N100, the grand audit.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N98 — the compiler written in Nazm at parity — **not accepted: parity measured, 13 of 21 probes**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.99 first. A per-feature parity record, measured contained and gated:")
    strs_push(l, "13 equal, 8 refused, none differs. Porting the refused features is the remaining work, and the")
    strs_push(l, "acceptance criterion is not met. Next: N99, JIT and REPL.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N97 — formal semantics v2 — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-04; proofs BLOCKED (no proof assistant)**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.98 first. The formal model extended to loops, mutation, early return and")
    strs_push(l, "recursion with fuel, and held to the interpreter and the checker over 12,900 programs. No proof:")
    strs_push(l, "none can be made without a proof assistant, and none is installed. Next: N98, the compiler written")
    strs_push(l, "in Nazm at full parity.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N96 — smart contracts v2 — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-04; area 34 stays PARTIAL, sBPF BLOCKED**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.97 first. The EVM and WebAssembly backends held to the simulator on generated")
    strs_push(l, "transaction sequences under their reference VMs: 750 transactions, every outcome, code and final state")
    strs_push(l, "equal, every gas bound held. No language change; events, external calls and sBPF remain out. Next:")
    strs_push(l, "N97, formal semantics v2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N95 — the platform matrix v2 — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-04; area 33 stays PARTIAL**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.96 first. Every target × backend cell is run-verified, compile-only or")
    strs_push(l, "unsupported, with its evidence and CPU identity, in one table `nazm inspect` prints and a test holds")
    strs_push(l, "the capability matrix to; Windows, 32-bit hosted and big-endian targets are decided non-goals. Not")
    strs_push(l, "here: an x86_64 Linux runner. Next: N96, smart contracts v2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N94 — reproducibility and provenance v2 — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-04; area 32 stays PARTIAL**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.95 first. A five-part reproducibility model, each part with its own evidence;")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm build --sbom` (CycloneDX 1.5); `nazm attest sign`/`verify` — in-toto statements signed and")
    strs_push(l, "verified with OpenSSH. Not here: a transparency log, keyless signing, independent rebuilders. Next:")
    strs_push(l, "N95, the platform and target matrix v2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N93 — coverage-guided fuzzing — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-04; area 30's fuzzing stays PARTIAL**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.94 first. A coverage-guided fuzzer of the compiler's own entry points, built")
    strs_push(l, "with SanitizerCoverage and run contained by `cargo xtask contained fuzz`; four targets, 3.9 million")
    strs_push(l, "executions, no crash; the minimised corpora replayed by the ordinary suite. Not here: sanitizers,")
    strs_push(l, "Miri, Loom, backend/FFI/registry fuzzing. Next: N94, reproducibility and provenance v2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N92 — performance evidence v2 — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-04; area 28 stays PARTIAL**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.93 first. Every measured section of `performance.md` is filed in")
    strs_push(l, "`bench/claims.toml` as reproducible, dated or unreproduced, held by a gate; `nazm.bench/2` records the")
    strs_push(l, "machine, the spread, sizes, the noise floor and why a reference was not measured; Rust and Go sieve")
    strs_push(l, "references. Eight current claims stay unreproduced. Next: N93, coverage-guided fuzzing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N91 — debugger and profiler v3 — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-04; area 27 stays PARTIAL**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.92 first. Bindings have lexical scopes under LLVM; Cranelift writes DWARF line")
    strs_push(l, "tables and subprograms, checked by lldb and a live gdb session; `nazm profile --sample` attributes a")
    strs_push(l, "run's samples to Nazm functions and lines, the runtime, foreign code and the system, with waits")
    strs_push(l, "counted as blocked (`nazm.profile/2`). Not here: Cranelift variables, the remaining types, DAP, a")
    strs_push(l, "Linux sampler. Next: N92, performance evidence v2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N90 — packages v3 — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-04; area 26 stays PARTIAL**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.91 first. The registry resolver backtracks: name order, newest first, the")
    strs_push(l, "lockfile's choice first, bounded at 10,000 candidates, and a refusal names the package and every")
    strs_push(l, "requirement on it with who placed it. `nazm update [NAME…]` re-resolves without the lockfile's")
    strs_push(l, "preference and prints each change. No language or lockfile change. Not here: signatures, a remote")
    strs_push(l, "registry, features, pre-releases, multi-root workspaces. Next: N91, debugger and profiler v3.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N89 — LSP and MCP workspace editing — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-04; area 25 stays PARTIAL**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.90 first. A declared source root is a workspace: an exported entity is renamed")
    strs_push(l, "in every module under it, validated whole, and a library package's API is refused; `nazm patch")
    strs_push(l, "apply` writes a plan only to the exact bytes it was made from, all or nothing. Not here: an MCP")
    strs_push(l, "apply, DAP, editor automation. Next: N90, packages v3.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N88 — AI/HPC v2 — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-04; area 21 stays PARTIAL**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.89 first. `nazm accel` runs maps and zips of `Int` kernels and folds them")
    strs_push(l, "(`--reduce add|min|max`) in index order, every run held to the interpreter; a numeric oracle of")
    strs_push(l, "generated kernels against 128-bit arithmetic on the GPU. `nazm.accel/2`. No language change. A")
    strs_push(l, "second provider is BLOCKED here (no Metal compiler, no Vulkan); vector operations in LIR DESIGNED.")
    strs_push(l, "Next: N89, LSP and MCP workspace editing.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N87 — assurance profiles v3 — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-04; areas 19 and 20 VERIFIED as scoped, as enforcement**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.88 first. Contracts — `requires` and `ensures`, checked on entry and on every")
    strs_push(l, "return path, identical on every tier, never compiled out — with calls of literals proved or refused")
    strs_push(l, "at compile time; `nazm obligations` and `nazm.obligations/1`, every obligation proved, checked or")
    strs_push(l, "unknown; `no-unknown-calls` in `critical` and `cyber`. Semantic epoch 27, `nazm.interface/10`. Not")
    strs_push(l, "here: loop invariants, a solver, constant time (RESEARCH), certification. Next: N88, AI/HPC v2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N86 — embedded v2 — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-04; area 18 VERIFIED as scoped**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.87 first. Boards are descriptions (`nazm_runtime::board::BOARDS`), from which")
    strs_push(l, "each linker script, runtime and entry is generated; a second architecture family,")
    strs_push(l, "`riscv64gc-unknown-none-elf` on QEMU's RISC-V `virt`, boots beside AArch64's with identical output,")
    strs_push(l, "failures and in-bound stacks at `-O0` and `-O2`, built and run in `nazm-qemu:n86`; device registers")
    strs_push(l, "at 8, 16 and 32 bits. Semantic epoch 26, runtime ABI 13. Not here, each DESIGNED with its reason:")
    strs_push(l, "atomics, interrupts, a heap; and no hardware. Next: N87, the critical and cyber profiles v3.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N85 — FFI and ABI v3 — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-04; area 17 VERIFIED as scoped**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.86 first. A practical C ABI subset: opaque handles (`extern \"C\" struct Db;`),")
    strs_push(l, "C-layout structs by borrowed pointer, nullability in the result type (`N0409` or `None`), `Str`")
    strs_push(l, "results copied, `c_errno()`, exports passed to C as callbacks, `nazm build --lib --shared`, and")
    strs_push(l, "`bindgen` reading all of it. The crossing is written as ordinary Core IR, so MIR, LIR and both")
    strs_push(l, "backends learned only the borrowed struct copy, the `errno` capture and an export's address. Semantic")
    strs_push(l, "epoch 25, `nazm.interface/9`, runtime ABI 12. Not here: floats, by-value structs, variadics, closures")
    strs_push(l, "as callbacks, `dlopen`, other ABIs, the compiler written in Nazm. Next: N86, embedded and bare metal")
    strs_push(l, "v2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N84 — the standard library 1.0 — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-04; area 16 VERIFIED as scoped**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.85 first. Seventeen modules and 126 public items, frozen by `library/std/API-1.0`")
    strs_push(l, "and a semver policy in `spec.md`; four representative programs (a CLI tool, a data tool, a concurrent")
    strs_push(l, "service, a package utility) written against it alone and run on every tier. Not here: networking,")
    strs_push(l, "cryptography, floats, a faster map, `@std` in the compiler written in Nazm. Next: N85, FFI and ABI v3.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N83 — the task pool — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-04; area 15 VERIFIED as scoped**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.84 first. `NAZM_SCHEDULER=pool`: tasks on bounded workers, each a guarded stack")
    strs_push(l, "pinned to its worker, a per-target switch, every wait parking the task; ten thousand tasks alive at")
    strs_push(l, "once on two workers; the whole CLI suite passes on the pool. Faster spawn (7.4 µs against 25.4 µs).")
    strs_push(l, "Not here: the default stays a thread per task, no work stealing or preemption, no hand-off for a")
    strs_push(l, "blocking foreign call, Linux unverified, the interpreter and the compiler written in Nazm unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "Runtime ABI 11. Next: N84, the standard library 1.0.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N82 — runtime v2: the runtime as an artifact — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-03; area 13 stays PARTIAL**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.83 first. `nazm runtime build` compiles the whole runtime for a target and")
    strs_push(l, "profile into `libnazmrt.a` with a `nazm.runtime/1` manifest; `nazm build --runtime` links it on both")
    strs_push(l, "backends after checking schema, ABI revision, runtime digest, target, profile, services and archive")
    strs_push(l, "bytes, and refuses by name otherwise; `nazm runtime verify`; provenance names the archive. Behaviour is")
    strs_push(l, "identical over the repository; a cold build is 34 ms faster with it. Not here: a runtime in Rust (one")
    strs_push(l, "implementation kept), an allocator, a scheduler (N83). Next: N83, the advanced scheduler.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N81 — the backend contract v2, stage one — **not accepted, 2026-10-03; area 10 stays PARTIAL**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.82 first, and it says why: LIR now owns a target's data layout, every byte")
    strs_push(l, "layout and the ownership table, both backends read them, every native build validates them, and")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm lir` prints them as `nazm.lir/1`; the fuzzer exercises layouts on every tier. Objects are")
    strs_push(l, "byte-identical on every program in the repository. Not done, by decision: one instruction-level LIR")
    strs_push(l, "that both backends consume, with an oracle interpreter — a rewrite of both code generators that this")
    strs_push(l, "programme does not risk the reference compiler for. Next: N82, runtime v2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N80 — provenance v3 — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-03; area 7 stays PARTIAL**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.81 first. Containers by type-keyed cell, calls through values and bounds by")
    strs_push(l, "type-based targets, closures' parameters and captures received, fields and variants within a body,")
    strs_push(l, "one policy engine with `checked-paths` in `cyber`, and a chain per origin at every sink")
    strs_push(l, "(`nazm.flow/2`). Epoch 24, `nazm.check/4`. No program in the repository changed verdict. Not here:")
    strs_push(l, "implicit flow, per-handle precision, labels a program writes. Next: N81, LIR and the backend")
    strs_push(l, "contract v2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N79 — effects and capabilities v3 — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-03; areas 5 and 6 stay PARTIAL**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.80 first, amended as built. The ambient bridge became a recorded contract: each")
    strs_push(l, "function's inherited authority is computed, recorded and shown by `nazm inspect`, and the")
    strs_push(l, "`authority` profile's `explicit-authority` refuses it by name. `OutCap` attenuates `IoCap` to the")
    strs_push(l, "standard streams, by passing; nothing widens it back. A function value with fewer effects than")
    strs_push(l, "expected is accepted where one is passed or returned. Revocation is declared outside the model.")
    strs_push(l, "Epoch 23. Not here: refusing the bridge by default (the corpus and the compiler written in Nazm")
    strs_push(l, "rely on it), per-resource capabilities, subsumption inside other types. Next: N80.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N78 — traits and methods — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-03; area 3 stays PARTIAL**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.79 first. Nominal traits, `impl Trait for Type`, `recv.m(…)`, `Trait.m(recv, …)`")
    strs_push(l, "and trait bounds; coherence over the compilation (one impl per trait and type, in the trait's or the")
    strs_push(l, "type's module); methods resolved before Core IR — a concrete call is the impl's function, a call")
    strs_push(l, "through a bound is `CallTrait`, resolved per instance by MIR and per value by the interpreter. The")
    strs_push(l, "same results in the interpreter, LLVM and Cranelift. `@std/show` is the first standard trait;")
    strs_push(l, "interfaces carry traits, impls and bounds (`/8`); epoch 22. Not here: trait objects, default")
    strs_push(l, "methods, associated items, generic traits, generic function values (`N0387` stays outside the")
    strs_push(l, "model), the compiler written in Nazm (N98). Next: N79, effects and capabilities v3.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N77 — resolution, persisted — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-03; area 2 stays PARTIAL**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.78 first. A module that checks cleanly leaves `nazm.resolved/1`, its names by")
    strs_push(l, "durable identity, stored with its check (`nazm.check/3`) so its invalidation is the check's; the")
    strs_push(l, "same bytes from two processes and two checkouts. `nazm references` and `nazm resolve` read reused")
    strs_push(l, "modules' units without checking their bodies, and agree with the language service. The compiler")
    strs_push(l, "written in Nazm refuses `@std/` and package imports by name. Not here: re-export and export under")
    strs_push(l, "another name (no design, so area 2 stays PARTIAL), a build that skips bodies, persisted locals. Next:")
    strs_push(l, "N78, traits and methods.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N76 — syntax completion: incremental reparse, finer recovery, `\\u{…}` — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-03**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.77 first. `nazm_syntax::Revision` and `Revision::edit`: a file's next parse from")
    strs_push(l, "its previous one, relexing and reparsing only from the first item an edit can reach to the first old")
    strs_push(l, "boundary it lands on, held **equal to a fresh parse** over every `.nz` file in the repository under")
    strs_push(l, "seeded edit sequences. Recovery inside record, enum, parameter, argument, initialiser and arm lists,")
    strs_push(l, "and at a broken `use`'s `;`; the abstract tree's contract unchanged. `\\u{…}` escapes, epoch 21.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm lsp` synchronises incrementally through the service's per-document revision. Not here: a")
    strs_push(l, "hole-tolerant checker, incremental parsing outside an editor's open document, the compiler written")
    strs_push(l, "in Nazm (N98). Next: N77, resolution and modules.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N75 — production-readiness audit and release gate — **complete: candidate `c3da8ca`, not released, 2026-10-03**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An audit, not a feature: every matrix status against its evidence, `limitations.md` line by line, the")
    strs_push(l, "security wording of every current document, the schemas against their documentation — four documentation")
    strs_push(l, "defects fixed. The gate at one commit, contained: the workspace suite, lifecycle, selfhost, bootstrap,")
    strs_push(l, "the benchmark and the **full mutation catalogue, 1,089 of 1,089 caught** (one timeout given a killer); nine")
    strs_push(l, "platform runs and the fuzzers and formal core at release scale on the host. The release assembly found")
    strs_push(l, "that its script could not copy the conformance corpus's directories, fixed in `c3da8ca`, which it then")
    strs_push(l, "assembled and verified; the artefact re-digested independently. `docs/internal/releases/c3da8ca.md` holds the")
    strs_push(l, "identities, the target table, the accounting, the evidence index and the human release procedure.")
    strs_push(l, "Nothing is tagged, pushed or published: that is a person's decision. N49–N75's programme ends here.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N74 — ecosystem, IDE and migration tooling — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.76 first. `nazm init` and six templates, each held by its own commands; a library")
    strs_push(l, "package checked as its modules; `nazm doc` from the checker's facts; `nazm bindgen` for the C subset")
    strs_push(l, "that crosses, refusing the rest; `nazm publish --dry-run`; the language service tested across packages;")
    strs_push(l, "an LSP client for one editor. Not here: a network registry, rename across packages, a debug adapter,")
    strs_push(l, "an agent-efficiency claim. Next: N75, the release-candidate audit.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N73 — compiler trust and supply chain — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.75 first. A front-end robustness fuzzer and a differential fuzzer across the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter and three native tiers, both seeded, with a replayed regression corpus; three injected")
    strs_push(l, "faults found by them alone. `nazm build --provenance` writes a deterministic record of a build's inputs,")
    strs_push(l, "toolchain and outputs, and `--attest-with` hands it to a local signer; `cargo xtask evidence` indexes an")
    strs_push(l, "evidence bundle with checksums and writes the compiler's bill of materials from `Cargo.lock`.")
    strs_push(l, "Cross-toolchain objects measured and classified. Not here: coverage-guided fuzzing, sanitizers, Miri, Loom. Next: N74, ecosystem.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N72 — sBPF account backend — **PARTIAL: analysis and metadata; execution BLOCKED, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.74 first. A `signed-writes` rule refuses a state write no signer decision guards,")
    strs_push(l, "and account metadata states each instruction's discriminator, arguments and account constraints. No")
    strs_push(l, "sBPF toolchain, validator or emulator exists here, and upstream eBPF is not sBPF: the backend is")
    strs_push(l, "designed by the metadata and not built. Next: N73, compiler trust and supply chain.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N71 — WASM contract adapter — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.73 first. The ordinary WebAssembly backend, unchanged, plus a generated adapter")
    strs_push(l, "appended to the contract's own unit: exports per entrypoint, the state across two typed host imports,")
    strs_push(l, "conservation in the module. The reference host's run equals the simulator's. Next: N72, an")
    strs_push(l, "account-oriented BPF backend.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N70 — EVM backend — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.72 first. Contracts compile directly from Core IR to EVM bytecode — `i64` held")
    strs_push(l, "exactly in 256-bit words, conservation enforced on-chain, selectors from the compiler's own keccak,")
    strs_push(l, "storage slots by field name so order and additions move nothing — and run in py-evm with the")
    strs_push(l, "simulator's outcomes, codes and storage, inside their stated gas bounds. Next: N71, a WASM contract")
    strs_push(l, "adapter.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N69 — The Web3 semantic contract model — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.71 first. A contract is ordinary Nazm under a `web3` profile of existing")
    strs_push(l, "rules; its read and write sets are facts, conservative where unseen; a deterministic simulator runs")
    strs_push(l, "transactions, reverting by code and rejecting any that changes a declared conserved quantity. Static")
    strs_push(l, "asset linearity is designed. Next: N70, an EVM backend.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N68 — Adaptive representation — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.70 and research register R4 first, with the prior art. A `Vec` of a record of")
    strs_push(l, "`Int`s and `Bool`s has an unobservable layout, so `--layout soa` stores it one array per field: the")
    strs_push(l, "same results and failures, the layout in every affected object's identity, 2.8× on a one-field scan")
    strs_push(l, "and 2× slower on an all-field one — which is why the compiler does not choose yet. Next: N69, the")
    strs_push(l, "Web3 semantic contract model.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N67 — GPU/HPC — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.69 first. A kernel is a pure `(Int) -> Int` function meeting a stated")
    strs_push(l, "eligibility, refused by name otherwise; `nazm accel` generates OpenCL C from Core IR carrying checked")
    strs_push(l, "arithmetic, runs it on the M1 Pro's GPU with every transfer and the synchronisation in its report,")
    strs_push(l, "recovers the sequential map's first failure from a parallel run, and holds every result to the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter's. About 6× one CPU core on a Collatz map. Next: N68, adaptive representation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N66 — Vectorisation — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.68 first. Checked arithmetic kept every loop scalar; `ints_sum_from` keeps the")
    strs_push(l, "ordered checked sum's meaning while adding a block unchecked only where every partial sum is provably")
    strs_push(l, "in range, and native builds replace the counted summation loop with it — 1.9× on an M1 Pro at `-O2`,")
    strs_push(l, "the same values and failures everywhere. Every other loop's reason is in `nazm explain-cost`.")
    strs_push(l, "Next: N67, GPU/HPC.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N65 — The interactive tier — **complete as scoped, JIT BLOCKED, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.67 first. A REPL that checks its session as one program on every edit and")
    strs_push(l, "refuses a redefinition that breaks a caller, by name; comptime for parameterless pure functions,")
    strs_push(l, "isolated by the authority model itself (not an OS sandbox); a reload check naming what a running image could take. The")
    strs_push(l, "JIT is blocked by the workspace's `unsafe_code = \"forbid\"`, which is the project's to lift, and is")
    strs_push(l, "designed. Next: N66, SIMD and vectorisation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N64 — WebAssembly — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.66 first. `wasm32-unknown-unknown` through the LLVM backend, carrying checked")
    strs_push(l, "arithmetic and failure unchanged, with every capability of the outside a `nazm_host` import present")
    strs_push(l, "only where used — a module with no `IoCap` has no `write`. A reference host grants exactly those.")
    strs_push(l, "Fourteen corpus programs run as WebAssembly with the interpreter's output; fifty are refused by")
    strs_push(l, "part, for want of a heap, which is designed and not built. Next: N65, a JIT and REPL tier.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N63 — Real-time bounds — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.65 first. A `realtime` profile — `embedded` plus no blocking, no clock and")
    strs_push(l, "bounded loops — and a bounds report: exact trip bounds for the counted loop form, call depth, site")
    strs_push(l, "counts, `wcet` null. A board build states its stack bound from the code generator's frames along the")
    strs_push(l, "deepest path; a painted stack on QEMU stays below it at `-O0` and `-O2`. Measurement is never the")
    strs_push(l, "bound. Next: N64, WebAssembly.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N62 — Embedded bare metal — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.64 first. `aarch64-unknown-none`: a board runtime without thread-local storage")
    strs_push(l, "or a C library, failure on the UART and semihosting's exit, `_start` and `link.ld`, a stack check")
    strs_push(l, "against the image's own stack; volatile `mmio_read32`/`mmio_write32` under an `MmioCap`, refused")
    strs_push(l, "where there is no device (`N0392`). A Nazm program boots on QEMU's `virt` board and prints through")
    strs_push(l, "its UART. Atomics, interrupts, a heap and `@std` designed, not built. Next: N63, real-time bounds.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N61 — Formal semantics — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.63 and `docs/internal/formal-core.md` first. A core's typing and evaluation rules,")
    strs_push(l, "transcribed with no compiler dependency, and five properties checked over all 94,352 programs up to")
    strs_push(l, "five nodes, holding Nazm's interpreter and checker to them. Its first run found the transcription")
    strs_push(l, "wrong against the spec (`i64::MIN % -1`). A model check, not a proof. Next: N62, embedded bare metal.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N60 — Restriction profiles v2 — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.62 first. `pass`/`fail`/`unknown` verdicts, `unknown` refused; `embedded`'s")
    strs_push(l, "`no-recursion` over MIR's direct call graph, `unknown` through a function value; `critical`'s")
    strs_push(l, "`no-select`; a dependency cannot weaken the root's profile. Constant-time RESEARCH; bounded loops,")
    strs_push(l, "queues and tasks to N63. Next: N61, formal semantics.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N59 — Backend performance — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.61 first. Scalar temporaries assigned once and read in their block have no")
    strs_push(l, "slot in the LLVM emitter: 54 % fewer `alloca`s in the compiler's own text, a 5 % faster `-O0`")
    strs_push(l, "build, a quarter faster `-O0` program, the same output. MIR's ownership model untouched; Cranelift")
    strs_push(l, "already SSA. The native build still needs clang for the runtime and the C driver for the link,")
    strs_push(l, "named by `nazm inspect`. Next: N60, advanced restriction profiles.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N58 — Debugger and profiler v2 — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.60 first. `Int`, `Bool` and `Str` parameters and bindings described in DWARF;")
    strs_push(l, "the prologue carries no line, so a breakpoint on a function stops after its slots are written; a")
    strs_push(l, "subprogram is named by its Nazm name. A live gdb session verified in the Linux container — names,")
    strs_push(l, "lines, backtraces, stepping and variables; lldb on macOS still blocked by developer mode. `nazm")
    strs_push(l, "profile` prints one run's memory and scheduler counts as `nazm.profile/1`. Cranelift's DWARF is")
    strs_push(l, "BLOCKED by name. Next: N59, backend performance.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N57 — Targets and cross-compilation — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.59 first. Four targets, both backends, from any host in the matrix; an")
    strs_push(l, "executable where the host links the target, objects and `link.txt` where it cannot; the triple in")
    strs_push(l, "every key; `nazm inspect` names each target's output. Run-verified on three (host, x86_64 macOS")
    strs_push(l, "under Rosetta, aarch64 Linux in the container), compile-only on x86_64 Linux. No language change:")
    strs_push(l, "semantic epoch unchanged. Next: N58, debugger and profiler v2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N56 — Packages v2: a local registry — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.58 first. A registry is a directory: an index per package and an immutable,")
    strs_push(l, "digest-checked copy per version. Four requirement forms, solved per name to the lockfile's version")
    strs_push(l, "while it satisfies or the highest non-yanked, one version per name, no backtracking. `nazm publish`")
    strs_push(l, "and `nazm yank`; tampering, links, malformed or equivocating indexes, double publishing and name")
    strs_push(l, "conflicts refused by code. No network, no signatures, no multi-root workspaces; the self-hosted")
    strs_push(l, "compiler's package support is DESIGNED. Semantic epoch unchanged: no checker rule moved. Next: N57,")
    strs_push(l, "cross-compilation.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N55 — FFI v2: C strings in, exports out — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.57 first. A `Str` argument to C is a borrowed NUL-terminated copy, freed after")
    strs_push(l, "the call; a NUL byte is refused before C runs. `pub extern \"C\" fn … ! {} = \"sym\" { … }` exports a")
    strs_push(l, "scalar Nazm function, and a failure inside one ends the process instead of unwinding into C.")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm build --lib -o OUT.a` writes a static archive and `OUT.h`, the same bytes on every build,")
    strs_push(l, "under both backends. Opaque handles, C structs, callbacks and `errno` are DESIGNED with their")
    strs_push(l, "reasons. Runtime ABI 7; semantic epoch 18. Next: N56, packages v2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N54 — Select, deadlines, cooperative cancellation and counters — **complete as scoped, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.56 first. One OS thread per task stays: the stackful pool is DESIGNED, its three")
    strs_push(l, "thread-local prerequisites named, and not built. Built: `chan_select_of` and `chan_select_until`")
    strs_push(l, "over `Vec[Chan[T]]` with the lowest ready index winning and a closed channel always ready — the")
    strs_push(l, "cancellation signal — on a runtime-wide event count that cannot lose a wake-up; `time_now_ms`;")
    strs_push(l, "`TimeCap`, held, and `critical`'s `no-ambient-time`; `NAZM_SCHED_REPORT` counters agreeing across the")
    strs_push(l, "interpreter and both backends. N44's failure rule unchanged. Runtime ABI 6; semantic epoch 17. Next:")
    strs_push(l, "N55, FFI v2.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N53 — Runtime crate and generic channels — **complete, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.55 first. The runtime is its own crate, `nazm-runtime` — text, inventory,")
    strs_push(l, "OS adapter and platform entry — depending on nothing of the compiler and consumed by both")
    strs_push(l, "backends; runtime ABI revision 5, and a digest of what the runtime emits enters every object key")
    strs_push(l, "beside it. `Chan[T]` for any `T` that may cross into a task (`N0390` otherwise), with")
    strs_push(l, "`chan_new_of`, `chan_send_of`, `chan_recv_of` and `chan_close_of`: one runtime (`nz.chanv_*`) whose")
    strs_push(l, "header extends the `Int` channel's with the element's stride and release, so retain and close are")
    strs_push(l, "shared; a queued value is released by the channel's last reference, a refused one by its sender.")
    strs_push(l, "The `Int`-only `Chan` and its built-ins are unchanged, and the Nazm-written compiler does not")
    strs_push(l, "carry the typed channel. Semantic epoch 16. Next: N54.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N52 — Resource cost and information flow v2 — **complete, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.54 first. Resource sites read off MIR with a count per call that is")
    strs_push(l, "`at-most-once` or `unknown` (`nazm explain-cost`, `nazm.cost/1`); a sink registry — `path`,")
    strs_push(l, "`output`, `file-data` — solved through helpers, closures and modules (`nazm explain-flow`,")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.flow/1`); `str_vouch` under a new `VouchCap`, recorded; three profile rules over the new")
    strs_push(l, "facts. Containers stay whole-container conservative, by statement. Semantic epoch 15. Next: N53,")
    strs_push(l, "the runtime crate.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N51 — Effects and capabilities v2 — **complete, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.53 first. One effect parameter per function, `effects E`, opaque in its body")
    strs_push(l, "and bound at each call from its function-typed arguments (`N0388`, `N0389`); `vec_map`,")
    strs_push(l, "`vec_filter` and `vec_fold` take it, so a caller is held to what the function it passes does, and")
    strs_push(l, "a profile sees it. A closure holds the capabilities visible where it is written, as captured")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0386` narrowed to `let mut`). Making a value of an undeclared function needs the authority its")
    strs_push(l, "type's effects need, which bounds the N37 bridge at the edge N50 opened. Attenuation and")
    strs_push(l, "revocation deferred with their cost. Semantic epoch 14; interface `/7` with `*` in effect lists.")
    strs_push(l, "Next: N52, resource cost and information flow.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N50 — First-class functions and closures — **complete, 2026-10-02**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.52 first, amended with the code where the code was simpler. Function types")
    strs_push(l, "`fn(T…) -> R ! {e}`, named functions as values, closures capturing by copy (`N0386` for a `let mut`")
    strs_push(l, "binding or a capability), indirect calls through a binding, and `N0387` for what cannot be a value.")
    strs_push(l, "One lowering: the checker declares each closure, Core IR lifts it, MIR adds the environment and a")
    strs_push(l, "thunk per named function used as a value, and the interpreter and both backends consume that. One")
    strs_push(l, "closure object, counted in the memory report's new `closures` class. `@std/seq` gained `vec_map`,")
    strs_push(l, "`vec_filter` and `vec_fold`, plain Nazm. Semantic epoch 13, runtime ABI 4, interface schema kept at")
    strs_push(l, "`/7` with a fifth type shape. Traits and methods are designed and deferred: function values met")
    strs_push(l, "every need in hand. The compiler written in Nazm has none of it. Next: N51, effects and")
    strs_push(l, "capabilities v2 — effect polymorphism is what keeps the higher-order library pure-only.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N49 — Language usability and native completeness — **complete, 2026-10-01**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.51 first. String escapes (`N0004`), `&&`, `||` and `!` (lowered to `if` in")
    strs_push(l, "Core IR), native recursion under both backends with a measured per-thread stack guard (`N0408`,")
    strs_push(l, "runtime ABI 3), and `use \"PATH\" as NAME;` with `NAME::item` (`N0209`, `N0210`). Semantic epoch")
    strs_push(l, "12. `nazm capabilities` now separates the two implementations only by the interpreter's iteration")
    strs_push(l, "budget and the native-only foreign call. The compiler written in Nazm refuses all of it by name.")
    strs_push(l, "Found on the way: an instance that calls itself was declared and defined by one unit, which")
    strs_push(l, "recursion through a generic function exposed. Next: N50, function values.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N48 — Inspector, debug information, timings, and the v1 release audit — **complete, 2026-10-01**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.50 first. `nazm inspect` prints `nazm.inspect/1`; `nazm build --debug` writes")
    strs_push(l, "DWARF through the LLVM backend, verified statically with lldb; `nazm build --timings` prints")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.timings/1`. The release audit added `docs/user/limitations.md`, release-candidate notes and the")
    strs_push(l, "human release procedure in `docs/internal/releases/`, and this section.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N47 — Restriction profiles — **complete, 2026-10-01**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.49. `general`, `embedded`, `critical` and `cyber`: rules with stable ids over")
    strs_push(l, "the checker's facts, `N0510`/`N0511`, and `nazm.profile-report/1`. A profile only refuses.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N46 — Packages, locking and reproducible builds — **complete, 2026-10-01**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.48. `nazm.toml`, `use \"NAME:path\"`, `nazm lock`, `--locked`, `N0500`–`N0509`,")
    strs_push(l, "and byte-identical executables from two directories.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N45 — The standard library — **complete, 2026-10-01**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.47. Seven `@std/…` modules of Nazm source, every function's contract declared.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N44 — Structured concurrency and the scheduler — **complete, 2026-10-01**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.46. The OS as scheduler, stated and stress-tested; no cancellation, by")
    strs_push(l, "decision.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N43 — The runtime constitution — **complete, 2026-10-01**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.45. One typed inventory of the runtime, an OS adapter, runtime ABI revision 2")
    strs_push(l, "in every object key, and the runtime tested directly.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N42 — The ABI and foreign functions — **complete, 2026-10-01**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.44. `extern \"C\"` declarations of `Int` and `Bool`, the effect `foreign` and")
    strs_push(l, "`ForeignCap`, `--link`, `nazm.interface/7`, semantic epoch 11.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N41 — The backend boundary and the Cranelift backend — **complete, 2026-10-01**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.43. A `Backend` trait, a typed runtime registry, and Cranelift 0.136.1")
    strs_push(l, "compiling every MIR function, identical to LLVM on all 104 buildable programs.")
    strs_push(l, "### N40 — MIR, the one lowering for the native backend — **complete, 2026-10-01**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`architecture.md` §7.42 was written first. `nazm-mir` holds MIR: each concrete function — every")
    strs_push(l, "generic instance included — as basic blocks with exactly one terminator each, typed locals, and")
    strs_push(l, "every copy, move, drop, scope join and failure edge written out; a validator proves, by a forward")
    strs_push(l, "dataflow over managed locals, no read of an empty local, no overwrite of an owned one, nothing")
    strs_push(l, "owned at a return or unwind, and every task list joined. `nazm-lir` reads MIR only — it no longer")
    strs_push(l, "depends on `nazm-cir` and cannot name a `Resolution` (a `cargo xtask check` rule) — and its LLVM")
    strs_push(l, "emitter was rewritten over it. `nazm mir` prints `nazm.mir/1`. Each function has an executable")
    strs_push(l, "digest that formatting, names and effects do not move. The interpreter stays on Core IR, by")
    strs_push(l, "decision. All 205 sources check, run and build byte-identically to N39, and all 104 buildable")
    strs_push(l, "programs behave identically. No language change: `SEMANTIC_EPOCH` stays 10.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Settled | Where |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| the constitution | `architecture.md` §7.42 |")
    strs_push(l, "| the representation, lowering, validator, printer, digest | `crates/nazm-mir/` |")
    strs_push(l, "| native lowering and emission from MIR | `crates/nazm-lir/src/lower.rs`, `emit.rs` |")
    strs_push(l, "| the boundary | `cargo xtask check` *core ir boundary*, `xtask/src/rules.rs` |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Mutation evidence: fifteen new mutations and 44 historical ones repointed to where their rule lives")
    strs_push(l, "now, each for a stated responsibility, seven retired; all 59 caught (`capability-matrix.md` §30).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### After N39, in dependency order")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "No item is chosen here; N39 left these standing, beside N38's below.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Depends on | Why not before |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| MIR: places, moves, drops, exclusivity | Core IR ✓, its region ownership ✓ | Core IR says what a region owns; nothing yet needs a place |")
    strs_push(l, "| Digests as cache keys (Core IR, MIR, objects) | per-function digests ✓ | nothing reuses work at this level yet, so nothing could key on them |")
    strs_push(l, "| Persisting Core IR across runs | a cache key that covers what lowering reads | built from each run's full check; cheap next to checking |")
    strs_push(l, "| An optimiser | a level to optimise, and a reason | no pass exists and none was added for a benchmark |")
    strs_push(l, "| The Nazm-written compiler reading Core IR | its own checker growing a lowering | the bootstrap compares what it emits, which did not move |")
    strs_push(l, "| Checking cost in one function's bindings | a scope structure that is not scanned | quadratic in bindings per function (`performance.md`, N39) — the checker's, predating Core IR |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N39 — Core IR constitution and typed lowering v1 — **complete, 2026-09-30**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "One lowering of a checked program, and both backends start from it. `architecture.md` §7.41 was")
    strs_push(l, "written first and says what Core IR represents and omits, when it is built, and the invariants a")
    strs_push(l, "consumer may assume. `nazm-cir` holds it: typed values — the checker's types, or *never* for an")
    strs_push(l, "`if`, `match` or block every path of which transfers — definitions and built-ins by identity,")
    strs_push(l, "structured regions with explicit completion and a named loop on every `break` and `continue`,")
    strs_push(l, "`?` as a `match` whose error arm returns, comparisons with their law, and each function's effect")
    strs_push(l, "contract and authority. `nazm-core` lowers only after checking succeeded, privately, and a")
    strs_push(l, "disagreement with the checker is `N0900`, a compiler defect; the verifier runs on every lowering.")
    strs_push(l, "The interpreter runs Core IR with slot frames and reads neither the tree nor the resolution;")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-lir` lowers Core IR and no longer depends on `nazm-syntax`; a `cargo xtask check` gate, run")
    strs_push(l, "by the suite too, refuses a position lookup below Core IR. `nazm core-ir` prints")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.core-ir/1`, deterministic and durable. Each function has a semantic and a body digest: an")
    strs_push(l, "effect-only change moves only the first, a capability parameter both, provenance neither.")
    strs_push(l, "Provenance stays a checker fact. All 205 sources check, run and emit IR byte-identically to N38;")
    strs_push(l, "the interpreter is 16–52 % faster on the bench programs on the host, and mixed — −12 % to +10 % —")
    strs_push(l, "in the Linux container. No language change: `SEMANTIC_EPOCH`")
    strs_push(l, "stays 10, `nazm.interface/6` and every tooling schema unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Settled | Where |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| the constitution | `architecture.md` §7.41 |")
    strs_push(l, "| the representation, verifier, printer, digests | `crates/nazm-cir/` |")
    strs_push(l, "| the one lowering | `crates/nazm-core/src/lower.rs` |")
    strs_push(l, "| the interpreter over Core IR | `crates/nazm-core/src/eval/` |")
    strs_push(l, "| native lowering from Core IR | `crates/nazm-lir/src/lower.rs` |")
    strs_push(l, "| the boundary | `cargo xtask check` *core ir boundary*, `xtask/src/rules.rs` |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Mutation evidence: nineteen new mutations, twelve repointed to where their rule lives now, one")
    strs_push(l, "retired; 37 selected with a stated link each, all caught (`capability-matrix.md` §30). The MILESTONE")
    strs_push(l, "gate ran offline and every stage passed; the campaign needed six sessions, 13,876 s. The interpreter")
    strs_push(l, "is faster on the host and mixed in the Linux container (`performance.md`, N39).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "N40 followed; see above.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### After N38, in dependency order")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "No item is chosen here; N38 left these standing, beside N37's and N36's below.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Depends on | Why not before |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Implicit flow (conditions, loop bounds) | a control-dependence model | explicit data flow is what v1 can state exactly |")
    strs_push(l, "| Field-, element- and alias-precise provenance | a MIR that tracks places | records are tracked whole and shared storage is `unknown` |")
    strs_push(l, "| More sinks, user labels, declassification, sanitisers | a policy design | one sink is what current semantics justify without an escape hatch |")
    strs_push(l, "| Provenance summaries for foreign code | an FFI | there is none |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N38 — Provenance and information flow v1 — **complete, 2026-09-30**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Where a value came from, statically. Four compiler-owned origins — `argument`, `file`, `authority`,")
    strs_push(l, "`unknown` — enter only through the built-ins that bring data in and `main`'s capabilities, and flow")
    strs_push(l, "by explicit data flow through bindings, operators, calls, records, variants, `Result` and `?`; a")
    strs_push(l, "condition contributes nothing, and a value read out of a sequence or channel is `unknown`. Each")
    strs_push(l, "module's bodies are reduced to facts kept in its check entry (`nazm.check/2`), and every run solves")
    strs_push(l, "the whole program's summaries from them to the least fixed point, so a callee's body change reaches")
    strs_push(l, "a caller the cache reused. One restricted flow: in a function with a declared effect set, the path")
    strs_push(l, "`write_file` writes to may not derive from a file's contents or from shared storage, directly or")
    strs_push(l, "through any function that writes to a path it is given (`N0372`). Tools carry it in")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.context/3`, `nazm.snapshot/3` and `nazm.delta/3`. Nothing reaches what runs: the IR is")
    strs_push(l, "byte-identical under N37 and N38. `SEMANTIC_EPOCH` 9 → 10; `nazm.interface/6` unchanged. All 203")
    strs_push(l, "existing sources check exactly as before.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Settled | Where |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| origins, flows, facts and summaries | `crates/nazm-sema/src/provenance.rs` |")
    strs_push(l, "| the walk, the solve and the restriction | `crates/nazm-core/src/provenance.rs` |")
    strs_push(l, "| facts across runs | `crates/nazm-iface/src/facts.rs`, `crates/nazm-cache/src/artifact.rs`, `crates/nazm-cli/src/checking.rs` |")
    strs_push(l, "| packets, snapshots, deltas | `crates/nazm-service/`, `schema/nazm.{context,snapshot,delta}-3.json` |")
    strs_push(l, "| the law | `spec.md` *Provenance: where a value came from*, `architecture.md` §7.40 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Mutation evidence: twenty-five new mutations and one retired; 34 selected with a stated link each,")
    strs_push(l, "all caught (`capability-matrix.md` §30). The MILESTONE gate ran offline in 7,217 s. Every stage passed but the MCP benchmark's memory")
    strs_push(l, "check, which a one-time glibc arena step failed; its law now samples the measured window and allows")
    strs_push(l, "one such step only with a plateau after it, and the release-benchmark stage passed when run again")
    strs_push(l, "alone (`performance.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### After N37, in dependency order")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "No item is chosen here; N37 left these standing, beside N36's below.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Depends on | Why not before |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| Attenuation and resource-specific capabilities (a read-only `IoCap`, one file, one directory) | a kind with a resource argument | v1 has no narrower kind to derive one into |")
    strs_push(l, "| Retiring the ambient bridge | declared sets on the compiler's own sources, and a migration story | 1,034 of 1,054 function checks in the tree still declare no set |")
    strs_push(l, "| Runtime or operating-system enforcement | a design for what crosses into foreign code | the check is static; nothing at runtime consults a capability |")
    strs_push(l, "| Linear or affine authority, revocation | move semantics, lifetimes | a capability copies freely today |")
    strs_push(l, "| Restriction profiles (no `IoCap` in embedded, no `SpawnCap` in critical) | capabilities ✓, a profile mechanism | nothing selects a profile yet |")
    strs_push(l, "| Foreign and unsafe authority | an FFI | there is none to authorise |")
    strs_push(l, "| The Nazm-written compiler reading capabilities | the same lexer and parser work as effect sets | no source it reads declares one |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N37 — Capabilities / authority v1 — **complete, 2026-09-30**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "An effect says what a function does; a capability says what allows it. Two compiler-owned kinds,")
    strs_push(l, "`IoCap` and `SpawnCap`, are built-in types: a function that declares an effect set holds exactly")
    strs_push(l, "the capability values its scope reaches, and every outside-world built-in, `spawn` and call of an")
    strs_push(l, "undeclared function needs the authority for what it does (`N0369`), checked apart from the effect")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0366`) and reported before it. `main` is the root: the runtime hands it one of each capability")
    strs_push(l, "it declares, it may take nothing else (`N0371`), and nothing constructs one (`N0370`). A function")
    strs_push(l, "that declares no set is the **compatibility bridge** — it exercises its caller's authority — and is")
    strs_push(l, "bounded so that code with a contract cannot reach authority it does not hold through it, in its")
    strs_push(l, "module or another. Authority crosses a module as parameter types, in `nazm.interface/6` unchanged.")
    strs_push(l, "The checking is static and a capability erases to a word nothing reads; there is no sandbox.")
    strs_push(l, "`SEMANTIC_EPOCH` 8 → 9. Of the 200 `.nz` sources at N36, 197 check exactly as before; the three")
    strs_push(l, "that do not are N36's `examples/effects/`, which declared effects without authority and now hold it.")
    strs_push(l, "N36's wording was corrected so that `fn f() -> Int` and `fn f() -> Int ! {}` cannot be read as one.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Settled | Where |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| capability kinds, sets and the built-in table | `crates/nazm-sema/src/capability.rs`, `types.rs` |")
    strs_push(l, "| possession, forging, `main`'s parameters | `crates/nazm-core/src/check/` |")
    strs_push(l, "| the authority check and its witness | `crates/nazm-core/src/effects.rs` |")
    strs_push(l, "| the root at runtime | `crates/nazm-core/src/eval/`, `crates/nazm-runtime/src/entry.rs` |")
    strs_push(l, "| the law | `spec.md` *Capabilities: what allows a function to act*, `architecture.md` §7.39 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Mutation evidence, under the new responsibility law: twenty new mutations and one retired; 33")
    strs_push(l, "selected — the twenty and thirteen N36 entries each with a stated link — all caught, 32 at tier 1")
    strs_push(l, "and 1 at tier 2 whose killer was then strengthened and verified alone (`capability-matrix.md` §30).")
    strs_push(l, "The MILESTONE gate ran offline: 5,737 s of wall time across its stages (`performance.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### After N36, in dependency order")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "No item is chosen here; N36 left these standing, beside N35's and N34's below.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Depends on | Why not before |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| ~~Capabilities: who may exercise an effect~~ | the effect sets N36 settled | **done in N37** |")
    strs_push(l, "| Profiles that forbid effects (critical: no `io`, no `spawn`; embedded) | effect sets ✓, a profile mechanism | nothing selects a profile yet |")
    strs_push(l, "| The Nazm-written compiler reading effect sets | a lexer token and a parser rule in `compiler/*.nz`, and a bootstrap | N36 avoided migrating the compiler's sources; none of them declares a set |")
    strs_push(l, "| Declared sets on the compiler's own exports | the item above | an undeclared import is every effect to its importer, so 152 of 1,044 function checks in the tree read `{ io, spawn }` |")
    strs_push(l, "| Effect polymorphism and handlers | function values | nothing a type argument brings can call anything yet |")
    strs_push(l, "| Divergence, panic and allocation as effects | answers to `spec.md` *Open — Effects* | each is a design question, not an omission |")
    strs_push(l, "| Completion of effect names | a completion site inside an effect set | two names; not worth a new site kind in N36 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N36 — Typed effects and the effect system constitution v1 — **complete, 2026-09-30**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "A function may declare the effects it exercises — `fn show(n: Int) -> Int ! { io }`, `! {}` for")
    strs_push(l, "pure — and every function's effects are inferred from its resolved calls to the least fixed point")
    strs_push(l, "over its module. Two effects, both the compiler's: `io`, the eight outside-world built-ins, and")
    strs_push(l, "`spawn`, a `spawn` statement and everything its task does. A declared set is a contract the body")
    strs_push(l, "is checked against (`N0366`, with a shortest witness); unknown and repeated names are refused")
    strs_push(l, "(`N0367`, `N0368`). Across modules only a declared set travels, persisted in `nazm.interface/6`, so")
    strs_push(l, "a caller never reads another module's body and an undeclared import is every effect. Tools show")
    strs_push(l, "it: signatures and hover, a packet's `effects` (`nazm.context/2`), an `effects` snapshot section")
    strs_push(l, "(`nazm.snapshot/2`, `nazm.delta/2`). Nothing reaches what runs: the IR is byte-identical with and")
    strs_push(l, "without declarations. `SEMANTIC_EPOCH` 7 → 8. Every one of the 116 existing sources checks exactly")
    strs_push(l, "as before; none needed a change.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Settled | Where |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| the syntax, CST node and formatting | `crates/nazm-syntax/`, `grammar.ebnf`, `guide.md` |")
    strs_push(l, "| effect identity and sets | `crates/nazm-sema/src/effect.rs` |")
    strs_push(l, "| inference, the contract and the witness | `crates/nazm-core/src/effects.rs` |")
    strs_push(l, "| the interface, `/6` | `crates/nazm-iface/src/wire.rs` |")
    strs_push(l, "| signatures, hover, packets, snapshots, deltas | `crates/nazm-service/`, `schema/nazm.{context,snapshot,delta}-3.json` (`-2` until N38) |")
    strs_push(l, "| the law | `spec.md` *Effects: what a function may do*, `architecture.md` §7.38 |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Mutation evidence: seventeen new mutations, two retired, two repointed; 85 selected, all caught,")
    strs_push(l, "78 at tier 1 with their killers verified and 7 at tier 2 (`capability-matrix.md` §30). The")
    strs_push(l, "MILESTONE gate ran offline: 7,242 s of wall time across its stages (`performance.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### After N35, in dependency order")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "No item is chosen here; N35 left these standing, beside N34's and N33's below.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Depends on | Why not before |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| The same benchmark on a second model family, through the direct adapters | a key a developer brings | none was supplied; the OpenAI and Anthropic adapters are tested against recorded responses only |")
    strs_push(l, "| A deterministic run (temperature 0) | a provider that takes one | the Claude Code client sets none; the model's default applied |")
    strs_push(l, "| More trials, and intervals rather than ranges | a budget for them | two trials show a spread, not a significance |")
    strs_push(l, "| Routing a tiny, self-contained task to raw source | evidence across models, and a rule to test | N35 observed one crossover, for one model, between 744 and 6,720 input tokens; it routes nothing |")
    strs_push(l, "| A task wording that keeps builtins out of \"definitions\" (T2) | a new suite version, compared from the start | the frozen suite is not edited after its results |")
    strs_push(l, "| Tool-using and multi-turn agents | a protocol for them | N35 measures whether the context alone suffices |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N35 — Agent task token, cost and correctness benchmark v1 — **complete, 2026-09-29**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-agent-bench` puts eight tasks over the seven N33 scenarios — understand, edit, diagnose,")
    strs_push(l, "documentation and test selection, the 123-byte diagnostic among them — to a real model, each with")
    strs_push(l, "the naive baseline and with `nazm repo --task`'s context, byte for byte and digest-addressed, one")
    strs_push(l, "prompt for both. Each answer is scored fact by fact by an offline oracle whose truths come from the")
    strs_push(l, "authorities; hallucinations are kept apart from misreadings; usage is kept raw and normalised, and")
    strs_push(l, "dated prices are applied in integer pico-USD, never in an identity. A spend cap is checked before")
    strs_push(l, "every attempt, transport failures are retried at most twice and never counted incorrect, the")
    strs_push(l, "journal resumes, and a dry run needs no provider. On `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` through the Claude")
    strs_push(l, "Code client, two trials: the N33 context solved 12 of 16 requests to 6, with 112 of 116 facts to")
    strs_push(l, "95, no hallucination in either arm, 94.36 % fewer input tokens and 95.39 % less cost as billed")
    strs_push(l, "(92.86 % uncached); correctness was preserved on 7 of 8 tasks, T2 the exception by the")
    strs_push(l, "pre-declared rule, and the diagnostic the one task where raw source was cheaper. Evaluation tooling")
    strs_push(l, "only: no crate depends on it, and no grammar, semantics, `SEMANTIC_EPOCH` (7), `nazm.interface/5`")
    strs_push(l, "or existing schema changed; one new schema.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Settled | Where |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| the suite, oracles, providers, runner and report | `crates/nazm-agent-bench/`, `architecture.md` §7.37 |")
    strs_push(l, "| the dated price list | `tools/agent-bench/pricing.toml` |")
    strs_push(l, "| the results | `tools/agent-bench/results/`, `performance.md` |")
    strs_push(l, "| how to run it, and bring a key | `runbook.md`, *The agent task benchmark* |")
    strs_push(l, "| nothing else on the network, nothing depending on it | `xtask/src/rules.rs`, the `network reach` and `tokenizer reach` gates |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Mutation evidence: sixteen new mutations and an `agent` profile, all caught at tier 1 with their")
    strs_push(l, "sixteen killers verified (`capability-matrix.md` §30). The MILESTONE gate ran offline after the")
    strs_push(l, "paid run, at `0419b25`: 2,977 s of wall time (`performance.md`). The benchmark spent $1.78 of a $2")
    strs_push(l, "cap, pilots included.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### After N34, in dependency order")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "No item is chosen here; N34 left these standing, beside N33's and N32's below.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Depends on | Why not before |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| An agent task benchmark with a real model: tokens, cost, success (G83–G85) | task contexts ✓, multi-tokenizer counts ✓ | nothing has been run against a model, and a model run is its own protocol |")
    strs_push(l, "| Framing and protocol overhead of a model conversation | a chosen protocol and model | N34 measures content only, by law |")
    strs_push(l, "| A compact transport for tiny contexts | evidence that the fixed overhead matters in a real task | it is 400–700 tokens, constant, and carries the retrieval and reasons the planner's law requires |")
    strs_push(l, "| An audit of syntax decisions against several tokenizers (the rest of G81) | a syntax change to decide | no syntax was changed or proposed here |")
    strs_push(l, "| More families (e.g. WordPiece), a model's own chat template | a reason and a permissive asset | three families are what G82 asks |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N34 — Tokenizer-independent context measurement and multi-tokenizer benchmark v1 — **complete, 2026-09-29**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm-tokens measure` counts the exact text on standard input under four pinned tokenizers of")
    strs_push(l, "three families — OpenAI byte-level BPE (`cl100k_base`, `o200k_base`), SentencePiece BPE")
    strs_push(l, "(Mistral-7B-v0.1) and SentencePiece Unigram (T5-small) — offline, with every identity carrying its")
    strs_push(l, "library, revision, licence, normalisation, special-token policy and asset digest, as")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.token-cost/1`. Content only; framing and unknown pieces beside the count; nothing normalised")
    strs_push(l, "first; an unknown tokenizer or an altered asset refused by name. The seven N33 tasks, with their")
    strs_push(l, "baselines unchanged, keep a 72.7–97.5 % reduction under every tokenizer, the one-function diagnostic")
    strs_push(l, "reported as a stress case. It is a tool beside the compiler: no crate depends on it, and `nazm` is")
    strs_push(l, "the same bytes as at N33. No grammar, semantics, `SEMANTIC_EPOCH` (7), `nazm.interface/5` or")
    strs_push(l, "existing schema changed; one new schema.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Settled | Where |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| the tokenizers, their identities and the measurement | `crates/nazm-tokens/`, `architecture.md` §7.36 |")
    strs_push(l, "| the pinned assets and their provenance | `tools/tokenizers/` |")
    strs_push(l, "| one definition of the N33 tasks for both benchmarks | `crates/nazm-repo/tests/scenarios/` |")
    strs_push(l, "| the benchmark | `crates/nazm-tokens/tests/benchmark.rs`, `performance.md` |")
    strs_push(l, "| no tokenizer outside `nazm-tokens`, nothing depending on it | `xtask/src/rules.rs`, the `tokenizer reach` gate |")
    strs_push(l, "| workloads with no network | `xtask/src/contained.rs` |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "Mutation evidence: eleven new mutations and a `tokens` profile, all caught at tier 1 with their")
    strs_push(l, "twelve killers verified (`capability-matrix.md` §30). The MILESTONE gate ran offline: 2,090 s of")
    strs_push(l, "stages, 40.6 minutes of wall time with one documentation fix and its re-run (`performance.md`).")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### After N33, in dependency order")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "No item is chosen here; N33 left these standing, beside N32's below.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| | Depends on | Why not before |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| An agent task benchmark with a real model: tokens, cost, success (G83–G85) | task contexts ✓, their byte measurements ✓ | nothing has been run against a model; bytes are not tokens |")
    strs_push(l, "| Multi-tokenizer measurement of contexts (G81, G82) | task contexts ✓ | tokenizer claims need several tokenizers |")
    strs_push(l, "| Rust semantic entities in the map | a compiler-owned Rust fact source | the compiler has no Rust semantics; packages and targets are all the map can own |")
    strs_push(l, "| Project-wide callers and importers of exported definitions | a project/importer boundary | callers are the manifest's compilations only, as rename's refusal already records |")
    strs_push(l, "| Transitive or ranked context | a justified bound | one step and sixteen members per relationship are the v1 law |")
    strs_push(l, "| A persistent or incremental repository index | measurement that forces one | a map takes about 0.4 s and a task 0.05–0.6 s in a release build |")
    strs_push(l, "| Documentation links from definitions and diagnostics | an authority that states them | no document names a definition or a code structurally today |")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "### N33 — Repository context map and minimum task context v1 — **complete, 2026-09-29**")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm repo --map` lists every entity of the repository with a durable identity — packages and")
    strs_push(l, "targets, source roots, compilation roots, modules and durable definitions, documents, schemas and")
    strs_push(l, "mutation profiles — with its authority, its structural relationships and where to retrieve more,")
    strs_push(l, "and never a body. `nazm repo --task` answers, for seed ids and an intent, the smallest context the")
    strs_push(l, "repository can justify: one step from each seed, each item with its reason, class, authority and")
    strs_push(l, "retrieval, the seed's exact source and the selected sections' exact text, under a structural budget")
    strs_push(l, "whose cut is `partial`. A goal or a plan never outranks the specification or the evidence; a stale")
    strs_push(l, "state is refused; a seed is an id and never a path. `nazm-mcp` adds `nazm.repository_map` and")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.task_context`. It composes N27, N28, N30 and N32: no grammar, semantics, `SEMANTIC_EPOCH` (7),")
    strs_push(l, "`nazm.interface/5` or existing schema changed; two new machine schemas.")
    strs_push(l, "")
    strs_push(l, "| Settled | Where |")
    strs_push(l, "| --- | --- |")
    strs_push(l, "| the map, the planner, the manifest, the Cargo and catalogue readers | `crates/nazm-repo/`, `architecture.md` §7.35 |")
    strs_push(l, "| a durable definition's name range, for asking its packet | `crates/nazm-service/src/durable.rs` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm repo` | `crates/nazm-cli/src/repo.rs`, `schema/nazm.repository-map-1.json`, `schema/nazm.task-context-1.json` |")
    strs_push(l, "| `nazm-mcp`: `nazm.repository_map`, `nazm.task_context` | `crates/nazm-mcp/src/main.rs`, `docs/user/mcp.md` |")
    strs_push(l, "| each package's documentation | `[package.metadata.nazm] docs` in its `Cargo.toml` |")
    strs_push(l, "| what it costs and saves | `performance.md` |")
